HK_TEXTD("en",{"6098853":{"s":[[null,"Add the spinach to a microwave-safe bowl. Arrange the lean protein, veggies, and whole grains on top. Drizzle with the barbecue sauce."],[null,"Heat in the microwave on high for 1 minute 15 seconds, or until hot. Adjust seasoning."],[null,"Sprinkle with the cilantro and serve with the lime wedge(s)."]],"h":[]},"6734922":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6231400":{"s":[[null,"In a food processor finely chop the vegetables and garlic in batches. Place into a large glass bowl."],[null,"Add balsamic vinegar, vegetable juice, salt, and pepper. Chill for at least an hour."]],"h":[]},"7659110":{"s":[[null,"Mix the bananas and egg with a pinch of salt."],[null,"Mist a frying pan with cooking spray and heat. Drop a ladleful of mixture into the pan and cook for 2 minutes on each side until golden. Repeat."],[null,"Serve each pancake topped with yogurt, fresh berries and agave syrup."]],"h":[[null,"You can try any of your favourite fruits as toppings, or even your favourite nut butter."]]},"9046047":{"s":[[null,"Add all 3 ingredients to a small blender like a Magic Bullet, or mini food processor. Blend until smooth, adding 1-2 teaspoons of water or non-dairy milk if needed to get things moving."],[null,"Taste for sweetness, and if preferred, add a teaspoon of maple syrup. (If your banana is ripe enough, you should not need added sweetener.)"],[null,"Chill for 1 hour (or longer) for a colder treat, or enjoy it immediately."]],"h":[[null,"The ripeness of your ingredients will determine if, and how much liquid you need to get things moving. Start blending without any added liquid and add as needed."],[null,"Make it a frozen chocolate treat by freezing it for 1 hour before enjoying it."]]},"9743063":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350℉/176℃ and line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Mash the bananas very well in a mixing bowl until they are very soft and liquidy. Then add the PB powder and almond flour and stir until combined."],[null,"Scoop or spoon mounds of the mixture onto your prepared baking sheet to make 6 large cookies (or 8-10 smaller ones). Then shape the cookies and use the back of a spoon or fork to press the cookies down, and create a crisscross pattern if desired."],[null,"Then bake for 11-12 minutes until firm to the touch."]],"h":[[null,"Weigh your flour/powder for the most accurate results . Scooping from a bag often results in too much flour being used due to compacting the flour into the measuring cup."],[null,"If you do not have a kitchen scale , spoon the flour into your measuring cup and scrape off the top with a knife, but do not scoop from the bag."],[null,"If the batter seems dry , (this will vary according to banana ripeness and how the powders were measured ) add 1-2 teaspoons of dairy-free milk or water. (Only if needed!)"]]},"2595":{"s":[[null,"In a large plastic bag with a zip lock, pour in angel food cake mix and lemon (or other flavor) cake mix. With the plastic bag sealed, mix the two dry cake mixes together. Use mix to make a single cupcake or a whole batch by following steps 2 through 6."],[null,"Spray a small custard dish with non-stick cooking spray."],[null,"Measure 3 tablespoons of the dry cake mix and place into a greased custard dish."],[null,"Add 2 tablespoons of water and mix with a small fork."],[null,"Place in the microwave and cook on high for one minute."],[null,"Slip cupcake out of the custard dish. Cool one minute before enjoying."]],"h":[[null,"*Add 2 tablespoons water for each cupcake."],[null,"If desired, may frost with cool whip or a glaze after cupcake is completely cooled."],[null,"One of the cake mixes must be angel food cake. Strawberry cake mix can be substituted for lemon."],[null,"Store dry cake mix in an air-tight container."],[null,"The name 3-2-1 Cupcake indicates 3 tablespoons cake mix, 2 tablespoons water and 1 minute in the microwave."],[null,"The baking powder in cake mix adds to sodium and phosphorus content. If you take phosphate binders to help control phosphorus, ask your dietitian if you need to take a binder with a cupcake snack."]]},"9740595":{"s":[[null,"Halve your avocados and remove the pits. Then scoop out the flesh into a mixing bowl, using a spoon. With a large fork or potato masher, mash the avocados without over-mashing. Keep some chunkier pieces in there if you like more texture."],[null,"Add the remaining ingredients and stir to combine."],[null,"Serve with vegan tacos, nachos, burritos, or chips."]],"h":[[null,"Use very ripe avocados for the best flavour and texture."],[null,"Do not overly mash your avocados . Mash by hand, not a blender or food processor, or it will be too smooth. I believe the best guacamole has some chunkier pieces left intact."],[null,"Use your favourite salsa that has the most flavour. Since we’re not using fresh tomatoes and jalapenos, you want to ensure your salsa is of good quality. I like chunky medium salsa but use your desired heat level."],[null,"Adjust the flavours to your taste . As with any recipe, adjust the seasoning to your preference. Avocados vary in size so taste your guacamole before serving and add more salt or lime juice if needed."],[null,"Store leftovers in the refrigerator with plastic wrap directly on top of your guacamole to prevent it from browning for 2-3 days."]]},"6349432":{"s":[[null,"Place the beans in a small bowl. Using the back of a fork, mash until they reach an almost smooth consistency."],[null,"Cut avocados in half and remove the pits. In the center of each avocado, layer 1 tablespoon of the beans, 1 tablespoon of Greek yogurt, and 1 tablespoon of salsa and sprinkle with 1 teaspoon of cheese. Sprinkle the salt evenly over the avocados. Serve each avocado half with 1 slice of lime to squeeze over the dish."]],"h":[]},"6918726":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375˚F. Spray 6 muffin cups with cooking spray. In large bowl, stir together banana, quinoa, nonfat yogurt and almond butter until blended. Fold in blueberries."],[null,"Spoon batter into prepared muffin cups. Bake for 20 to 25 minutes or until golden brown and set in center. Let cool completely."]],"h":[]},"3839":{"s":[[null,"Chop onion, bell peppers and cilantro."],[null,"Blend the following ingredients in a food processor: hominy, pinto beans, low-fat cream cheese, olive oil, 2 cloves of garlic, cumin and optional chili powder. Spread into a 9″ x 9″ pan."],[null,"Using a spatula, layer sour cream over bean mixture."],[null,"Lightly sauté in a skillet: red onion, green and red bell peppers and 1 clove of garlic. Avoid overcooking so that peppers are firm, not mushy."],[null,"Squeeze lime over the sautéed bell pepper and onion mixture for extra flavor and then drain excess liquid."],[null,"Spoon bell pepper mixture on top of sour cream and smooth until dip is covered."]],"h":[[null,"Serve the dip on flour tortillas when making tacos, or serve with homemade flour tortilla chips or pita chips for dipping."],[null,"Using fresh pinto beans that have been soaked instead of canned beans greatly reduces the sodium content of the dip."],[null,"Beans are high in potassium and phosphorus. This recipe shows you how to include a small amount of beans and still limit these minerals in your kidney diet."]]},"2902":{"s":[[null,"Remove frozen acai puree from the packaging and break up into pieces."],[null,"Place acai pieces, mixed frozen berries, Greek yogurt, chia seeds and rice milk in a blender."],[null,"Blend until smooth. Consistency should be thick enough to eat with a spoon."],[null,"Pour blended mixture evenly into two bowls."],[null,"Top with raspberries, blueberries and chopped pear."]],"h":[[null,"Açaí (pronounced ah-sigh-EE) berries are from a South American palm tree. These berries are rich in antioxidants and make a great addition to smoothies."],[null,"Make the acai bowl your own by adding your favorite toppings such as chopped pineapple, unsweetened coconut flakes, cacao nibs or granola cereal."],[null,"Use fresh or frozen raspberries and blueberries for topping."],[null,"This recipe may be tart. For sweetness you can add honey, Stevia or your favorite sweetener."],[null,"Low phosphorus, low potassium milk alternatives such as almond or soy milk can be used in substitution for rice milk."]]},"1976":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 175° F."],[null,"Spread the pretzels out on two 18″ x 13″ cookie sheets, so that pretzels lay flat. Use whole bite-size pretzels or break large-size pretzels into pieces."],[null,"Mix the garlic powder and dill together. Set aside half of the seasonings. To the other half, add the dry salad dressing mix and 3/4 cup canola oil. Pour evenly over the pretzels and use your hands to make sure pretzels are evenly coated."],[null,"Bake for 1 hour, flipping the pretzels every 15 minutes."],[null,"Remove the pretzels from the oven. Let the pretzels cool, then toss with remaining garlic powder, dill weed and oil. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Snyder’s of Hanover brand pretzels were tested in this recipe, but any kind of unsalted pretzel may be used."],[null,"Some brands of low-sodium pretzels contain potassium chloride. Check ingredients and avoid if you are on a low potassium diet."],[null,"The number of pretzels in one ounce varies based on the shape and size. Check the label on the pretzel bag for more information."]]},"3558":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl mix all spices together."],[null,"Place in a covered jar or container until ready to use."],[null,"Use as a dry rub or wet marinade for meat, poultry or fish, or add to vegetables, stews or other dishes."]],"h":[[null,"Adobo is used to prepare many foods in Latin culture."],[null,"Commercially prepared Adobo seasoning may contain over 300 mg sodium per serving."],[null,"Ground annatto (achiote) may be substituted for turmeric if available."],[null,"Adobo seasonings are varied and can be modified. Some recipes include cumin, coriander or annatto."]]},"7300874":{"s":[[null,"Add the tomatoes to a bowl with the coriander, mint, lemon juice, olive oil and pepper and mix well."],[null,"Add the red onion, cucumber and carrot. Mix well and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Try with different herbs such as parsley, basil or dill."],[null,"Serve with grilled meat, fish, poultry or tofu."],[null,"Great as part of a buffet or for a packed lunch."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"2426":{"s":[[null,"Cut turkey into cubes. Cut grapes in half. Dice the celery, onion and bell pepper. Place these ingredients in a large bowl and set aside."],[null,"In a smaller bowl, mix together the mayonnaise, salt-free seasoning, sugar and cranberry sauce."],[null,"Pour the sauce over the turkey mixture and refrigerate for 30 minutes to allow flavors to combine."],[null,"Serve the turkey salad with low-sodium crackers, whole grain toast or over lettuce or mixed greens."]],"h":[[null,"This recipe lasts 3 to 4 days in the refrigerator. It’s a great way to use your turkey dinner leftovers!"],[null,"Use your favorite salt-free herb seasoning blend."]]},"9665970":{"s":[[null,"Peel and cut your acorn squash into half-inch cubes and place in a mixing bowl."],[null,"Add the remaining ingredients to the bowl and mix well to evenly distribute the seasoning."],[null,"Set your fryer to 400°F/200°C and air fry the acorn squash for 18-24 minutes, mixing or shaking occasionally. Cook time will vary among different fryer models."]],"h":[[null,"Use caution when chopping and peeling the squash as it has very tough skin. Individual air fryers will vary in cook times , so make sure the squash is fork-tender with crisped edges before serving. Leftovers keep in a sealed container in the fridge for 3-4 days."]]},"9095332":{"s":[[null,"Wash and trim your asparagus and place them in a wide and shallow dish. Add the lemon juice, sesame seeds, and salt, and gently toss them to evenly coat the spears."],[null,"Transfer the seasoned asparagus to your air frying basket (or toaster oven tray) and air fry at 400 degrees F (205 degrees C) for 6-8 minutes until golden brown."]],"h":[[null,"Choose asparagus spears that are firm to the touch and stand up straight. The tips should be closed and deep in colour. You’ll want to trim the tough/hard ends of your asparagus where the green is turning to white. Watch carefully towards the end of cooking and do not overcook . Overcooked asparagus can get stringy in texture. Leftovers can be kept in the refrigerator in a sealed container for 3-4 days. They taste great cold or reheated. Or use the leftovers to chop into salads."]]},"2710":{"s":[[null,"Turn air fryer to 400 degrees F."],[null,"Arrange bagel thins cut side up, 4 thins total."],[null,"Dice the bell pepper into small pieces. Distribute marinara sauce amongst the bagel thins."],[null,"Distribute cheeses and pepper equally to bagel thins."],[null,"Bake in air fryer for 4-5 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Can also be made in a regular oven at the same temperature, but increase the time to 10 minutes."],[null,"To make this gluten-free, Elyse used the brand O’Doughs Gluten Free Bagel Thins® (no phosphorus additives)."],[null,"This recipe is a bit higher in sodium, so balance out your meals for the day. Look for bagel thins with the lowest amount of sodium per serving."],[null,"Use different colored bell pepper to change up the recipe."]]},"9263742":{"s":[[null,"In a medium bowl, combine the syrup, melted butter (if using), cinnamon and tapioca starch. Mix well."],[null,"Wash your apples, remove any stickers and slice each apple into 8 wedges/segments, removing the seeds/core. Place the sliced apple wedges into the bowl and mix well to evenly coat."],[null,"Place 1/4 cup of water at the bottom of your air fryer, below the basket. Then place the coated apples inside the basket in an even layer. Air fry at 380 degrees F for 12-15 minutes, until the apples are fork-tender. Mix every 5 minutes or so. Serve warm."]],"h":[[null,"If you have picky eaters , remove the apple peel before slicing and coating it with the marinade for a smoother texture. Try and cut your apple wedges into equal size pieces for even cooking. If some pieces are larger, they won’t be as soft. Use your favourite apple variety. I like to mix sweet and tart apples, but use all sweet, or all tart, if preferred. Store leftovers in an airtight container in your fridge for 1-2 days. **Please check with your air frying brand manufacturer before adding water below the basket. Some models allow it, while others do not. If you’re uncertain, avoid it."]]},"9067847":{"s":[[null,"Scrub your potatoes clean, then use a fork or knife to prick them all over. This will prevent the potatoes from bursting in spots while air frying."],["To cook with the optional oil","Use a silicone brush or your hands to spread the oil over the surface of your potatoes and then air fry at 400 degrees F for 20-30 minutes, until soft and a fork easily pierces the potato."],["For oil free","Air fry the potatoes at 350 degrees F for 25-35 minutes, until soft and easily pierced with a fork. Using a lower temperature without the oil, prevents the skin from burning before the inside has a chance to cook through."]],"h":[]},"9206024":{"s":[[null,"In a small mixing bowl, combine the lemon juice, salt and pepper and set aside."],[null,"Peel and slice your bananas into approx. 1/8 inch thick slices. A little thicker is fine, but try your best to keep the slices consistent for even cooking. Then place them in the bowl with the marinade and gently mix to evenly coat the slices."],[null,"Brush your air frying basket with a little oil and place the coated bananas in a single layer. Then air fry at 350 degrees F for 8-10 minutes until golden and caramelized. Watch carefully towards the end of cooking to prevent burning."]],"h":[[null,"Slice your bananas as uniform as you can for even cooking. If some slices are too thin , they may burn, so watch carefully toward the end of cooking. For an extra special treat, serve with ice cream !"]]},"9419746":{"s":[[null,"Scrub your beets and slice the ends using a sharp knife. No need to peel them. Then use a mandolin to very thinly slice the beets into chips. You want them paper thin for the best results."],[null,"Place the sliced beets in a mixing bowl and toss with the aquafaba and salt. Then arrange them in a single layer (slightly overlapping is fine) in your air frying basket, working in batches if needed."],[null,"Air fry the beet chips at 350°F/176°C for 10-12 minutes, shaking or mixing at the halfway point. The chips are ready when they've curled upwards, shrunk significantly, and feel dry to the touch. Remove them from the basket and let them stand at room temperature. They will crisp up more as they cool."]],"h":[[null,"The beet slices can be slightly overlapping since they will shrink significantly, but don’t stack them or overlap too much or they won’t crisp up as well. The thickness or thinness of your beet chips will determine cook time and crispiness level. Slice the beets as thinly as possible , or use a tool, like a mandolin for easy slicing. The chips are ready when their edges have curled, and the slices feel dry to the touch. Do not overcook the beet chips or they will have a bitter taste. They will crisp up a little more after you remove the basket from the air fryer and let the chips cool."]]},"9130591":{"s":[[null,"Cut your broccoli into small florets and add them to a bowl. Drizzle with the oil or vegetable broth and sprinkle with the seasoning. Mix well to evenly coat the broccoli."],[null,"Add 2-3 tablespoons of water to the bottom of your air fryer, below the basket. This will prevent the broccoli from smoking and getting too bitter. Then add the broccoli to your basket and air fry at 380 degrees F for 7-9 minutes, until desired brownness is reached. Give your broccoli a stir, or shake your basket around the halfway point."],[null,"Serve your broccoli with lemon wedges or sprinkled with vegan Parmesan cheese, if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Cut the florets into even-sized, small pieces for the best texture and even cooking. Powdered garlic is less likely to burn compared to fresh, so it’s best not to use fresh garlic this time. Do not overcook the broccoli , as it tastes best when slightly crispy, but also browned. So start checking on it around the 6-7 minute mark. Your air fryer broccoli tastes best when freshly made . However, leftovers will keep in the refrigerator for 3-4 days. You may reheat it in your fryer, toaster oven, or regular oven until heated through. **Please check with your air frying brand manufacturer before adding water below the basket. Some models allow it, while others do not. If you’re uncertain, avoid it."]]},"6925171":{"s":[[null,"In a small, deep bowl, stir together the buttermilk and hot sauce. Place the chicken in the buttermilk mixture. Allow to stand 15 minutes."],[null,"Place the cornflakes into the work bowl of a food processor. Process until coarse crumbs form. Add the cornmeal, garlic powder, paprika, salt, and pepper and pulse until evenly mixed. Pour the crumbs into a shallow bowl. (if you don't have a food processor, you can crush the cornflakes in a plastic bag with a rolling pin.)"],[null,"Drain the chicken, allowing the excess buttermilk to drip back into bowl. Coat the chicken pieces evenly in the cornflake mixture. Place the coated chicken pieces on a wire rack."],[null,"Place the chicken in the air fryer basket. Spray with nonstick cooking spray for 2 seconds (do not crowd the chicken; cook in batches if all the chicken doesn't fit). Set the temperature to 375°F and air fry for 7 minutes."],[null,"Turn the chicken pieces. Air fry for an additional 7–10 minutes or until the chicken is done and a meat thermometer inserted in the center registers 165°F."]],"h":[]},"9484573":{"s":[[null,"Peel and chop your butternut squash into half inch cubes. See step by step photos above if needed."],[null,"Place the cubed pieces in a large mixing bowl along with all the seasoning for the option you're making. Mix well and place in the basket of your air fryer in an even layer."],[null,"Cook at 400 degrees F for 15-20 minutes, depending on your model and give it a good mix at the halfway point. The squash is ready when it's fork tender and crispy around the edges."]],"h":[[null,"Cut your squash as uniform as possible for even cooking. If you leave some pieces too big, you’ll end up with some harder pieces. They don’t need to be perfect, but try and cut them as similarly sized as you can. For faster cooking , cut your pieces even smaller than the half inch I’ve recommended. Air fryers vary in strength , so start checking around the 15 minute mark. The squash is done when fork tender and the edges are brown and crispy. To save time, you may purchase pre-cubed butternut squash at your supermarket, but you’ll still want to cut them down into smaller cubes. Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-4 days. You may air fry to reheat or use a toaster oven. The nutritional information is for ¼ of the savoury version. The sweet version has 131 calories per serving."]]},"9293583":{"s":[[null,"Peel and chop your carrots into 4 inch sticks, approx 1/4 inch thick for even cooking."],["Air Frying Instructions","Place the carrot fries and all remaining ingredients in a medium mixing bowl and mix until evenly coated and then arrange them in your basket in an even layer. (They can be overlapping.)"],["Air Frying Instructions","Air fry at 400 degrees F (204 degrees C) for 15-20 minutes, until desired crispiness is reached, mixing once at the halfway point."],["Oven Instructions","Preheat your oven to 450 degrees F (232 degrees C) and line a large baking tray with parchment paper."],["Oven Instructions","Add the tapioca starch, salt, garlic powder, onion powder, and thyme to the bowl and mix until all the carrots are evenly coated. Then spread the carrots in a single layer on your prepared tray, leaving space in between each one, so that none are overlapping."],["Oven Instructions","Bake for 20 minutes, then remove the tray from the oven, flip the carrot fries and sprinkle with the vegan Parmesan cheese. Return to the oven for another 10 minutes, or until desired crispiness is reached."]],"h":[[null,"Try your best to cut your carrot fries as uniform as possible for even cooking. Choose carrots that are evenly wide from top to bottom, if possible. Cook time will vary according to which method you’re using to cook (oven-baked or air frying), as well as the size of your carrot fries. You may prepare the carrots up to 1 day in advance and keep them refrigerated in the bowl with the seasoning, until ready to bake. If you can’t find tapioca starch or flour , you may sub for cornstarch with similar results. These carrots taste best when freshly baked , but you may refrigerate leftovers for up to 3 days."]]},"9148201":{"s":[[null,"Peel and chop your carrots into approx. one inch pieces and place them in a mixing bowl."],[null,"Then, depending on which version you're making (sweet or spicy), add each of the ingredients to the bowl and mix well to evenly coat the carrots."],[null,"For the sweet version only, place the coated carrots in an oven safe dish that fits inside your air fryer basket. (So you don't lose all the syrup, and the carrots come more caramelized this way.)"],[null,"For the spicy version, transfer the coated carrots directly into the basket."],[null,"Cook at 400 degrees F for 15-18 minutes, or until tender. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"The nutritional information is for one quarter of the sweet version, including the optional butter. The savoury/spicy version has 110 calories for one serving. (one fourth) Cut your carrots in uniform sized pieces for even cooking . If you have some larger pieces, they won’t be as tender. Cooking time will vary depending on the model you’re using, and the size you cut all your carrots, so check on the while they’re cooking to get them just right. Use dried herbs over fresh as they tend to hold up better in this recipe. For less spice, omit the cayenne pepper, or increase to ¼ teaspoon for even spicier air fryer carrots. Leftovers keep 2-3 days in a sealed container in the refrigerator. Reheat in the oven or toaster oven for best results."]]},"9070331":{"s":[[null,"Wash your cauliflower head and remove the green leaves, but do not cut off the stem."],[null,"Then place the cauliflower stem side down on a cutting board, and trim both ends to make them flat, setting aside any loose pieces that break off. (See process shots above for a reference.)"],[null,"Now cut thick slices (approx. 1.25 inch thick) of the remaining piece into 2 or 3 steaks (depending on the size of your cauliflower head)."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine all the marinade ingredients and mix well. Then brush one side of each steak, placing them sauce side down in your air fryer basket, and then brush the other side."],[null,"Air fry at 375°F/190°C for 10 minutes, then carefully flip the steaks and continue to air fry for another 5-8 minutes, or until the cauliflower is tender and the edges are golden brown."]],"h":[[null,"Depending on the size of your cauliflower, you will get 2 or 3 steaks. If you are making 3 steaks , increase the marinade ingredients to the following: 3 tablespoons broth"],[null,"1.5 tablespoons lime juice"],[null,"1.5 teaspoons smoked paprika"],[null,"1.5 teaspoons garlic powder"],[null,"¾ teaspoon sea salt"],[null,"⅜ teaspoon black pepper (or ¼ + ⅛)"],[null,"Use a sharp knife, and try your best to cut evenly-sized cauliflower steaks for even cooking ."],[null,"To save time , you may purchase cauliflower steaks from the supermarket that are pre-cut for you."],[null,"Leftovers keep in the fridge for 2-3 days in a sealed container. Do not freeze."]]},"9517824":{"s":[[null,"Shuck your corn and cut in half if needed to fit into the basket of your fryer. If they fit whole, no need to cut them. If using, brush the corn with margarine or oil, using a silicone brush. Or spray them with a cooking spray. (optional)"],[null,"Place the corn in your basket and air fry at 380 degrees F for 12-15 minutes. Rotate the corn around the 8-10 minute mark and continue rotating every couple minutes towards the end of cooking, to ensure no burning."],[null,"Serve warm as is, or with butter, crema fresca, cilantro, cinnamon, or any of your favourite toppings."]],"h":[[null,"Choose corn that is fresh , with thicker kernels. The husks should be tightly wrapped, bright green, and not turning yellow or dry. Depending on your air frying model, you may cut your corn in half to accommodate for space , if needed. The number of ears and model of fryer will affect cooking time, so begin checking on your corn around the 10 minute mark . For oil free , skip the margarine or oil and brush a little vegetable broth on your corn instead, to keep it moist while cooking."]]},"9228909":{"s":[[null,"Remove the husk and use a sharp knife to cut each corn in half to make them easier to quarter. Then stand each piece upright (the flat side that you just cut down on the cutting board for stability) and slice in half vertically. Then place those pieces core side down and cut in half again. You will end up with 8 corn ribs from each corn on the cob for 16 pieces in total. The goal is to not squish the kernels so this cutting method works best. See the process shots above for clarity."],[null,"Brush each corn rib with bbq sauce and place them in the basket of your fryer in an even layer. It's okay if they are overlapping a little. Air fry at 380°F/193°C for 10-12 minutes and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Choose corn that is fresh , with thicker kernels. The husks should be tightly wrapped, bright green, and not turning yellow or dry. Use extreme caution when cutting your corn into “ribs”."]]},"9297046":{"s":[[null,"Peel and dice your potatoes into approx. half-inch cubes, doing your best to make them as similarly sized as possible for even cooking."],[null,"Place them in a bowl and cover with cold water, soaking them for 20 minutes. Then drain the potatoes and pat them dry. Rinse and dry the bowl you used for soaking and return the potatoes to the bowl."],[null,"Add the lemon juice and seasoning, and mix well to evenly coat the pieces."],[null,"Spoon (don't dump) the seasoned potatoes into your fryer basket in a single layer and air fry at 400℉/204℃ for 15-20 minutes. Mix or shake your basket every 5 minutes until desired crispiness is reached. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Cut your potatoes as evenly as possible for even cooking and crispiness."],[null,"Don’t skip the soak step as this helps remove some starch from your potatoes and provides crispier results, without needing oil."],[null,"For even crispier potatoes , you may add 1 teaspoon of a good quality oil such as avocado oil to the mix. (I don’t recommend cooking with olive oil due to its low smoke point.)"]]},"9751449":{"s":[[null,"Weigh or measure your fries and place them in your basket. They don't need to be in a single layer, but spread them evenly."],[null,"Air fry at 400 degrees F for 15-20 minutes, or until desired crispiness is reached. Mix at the halfway point and check on them often, towards the end of cooking."]],"h":[[null,"Check on your fries often towards the end of cooking to prevent burning them. Since all fryers operate differently, some may cook faster than others."]]},"9584605":{"s":[[null,"Halve your ciabatta loaf and then cut four slices. (I used about half of a ciabatta stick per batch.) So if you want to use the entire loaf, you'll have about 8 slices.)"],[null,"In a small bowl, combine the butter, garlic and parsley with a little salt and pepper and mix well. Divide the mixture between your four slices of bread and evenly spread."],[null,"Add 1/4 cup of water to your air fryer, below the basket, to prevent smoking. Then arrange your garlic bread on the basket, it's fine if the slices overlap a little. Set the fryer to 360 degrees F and cook for 5-8 minutes, until desired crispiness is reached. Start checking on it around the 4 minute mark."]],"h":[[null,"Use good quality bread for the best results. Try your best to cut your bread into equally sized slices for even cooking and crispiness. If you’re making multiple batches , keep in mind that subsequent batches will cook faster since your fryer will be hot to start. For gluten free, sub for your favourite gluten free bread. Don’t forget to add the water below your basket to prevent smoking . If you’re using salted butter or margarine, you may skip adding additional salt."]]},"9306532":{"s":[[null,"Trim the ends of your green beans and place them in a medium mixing bowl. Add the lemon juice and seasoning and mix to evenly coat the beans."],[null,"Place them in your basket and air fry at 380 degrees F (193 degrees C) for 8-12 minutes, until golden brown. Mix halfway through cooking."],[null,"Remove the green beans from the fryer and sprinkle with the optional parmesan cheese, if desired. Enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Quick tip for trimming your green beans . Line up several at a time and trim the ends, then rotate and trim the other side. It’s much faster than trimming one bean at a time."]]},"9425725":{"s":[[null,"Fill a large bowl with cold water and peel your potatoes. (Or scrub them if you wish to leave the peel on.)"],[null,"Then using a box grater, shred your potatoes into the bowl of water. Give them a quick stir and let them sit for 20 minutes. Now drain into a colander and rinse very well with cold water."],[null,"Transfer the shredded potatoes to a clean dish towel or paper towels and squeeze or press them dry. You want them as dry as possible for the crispiest hash browns."],[null,"Now add the potatoes back to the same bowl (wipe it dry first) and add the oil (if using) and the seasoning. Mix well."],[null,"Grease or spray your basket (if needed) and place the seasoned potatoes inside. Use a silicone spatula to spread and press the shreds into an even layer and cook at 370 degrees for 12-18 minutes, until golden. No need to flip! Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Don’t skip the soaking. Soaking the potatoes in cold water helps remove the starch which will result in crispier potatoes. So make sure to soak for 20 minutes and also rinse them afterward. Dry them very well! Again, for maximum crispiness, make sure the potato shreds are dried well. Use a clean dish towel to squeeze out the liquid. Spread the potatoes in an even layer to get them evenly crisped. Thicker spots may not crisp up as much. I’m using an 8qt Ninja Foodi and my hash brown is crispy at the 18-20 minute mark. If you’re using a smaller air fryer basket , it may cook faster. Start checking around the 10-15 minute mark and cook until desired crispiness is reached. For smaller air fryer’s you may need to work in two batches. For spicy hash browns , add ¼ teaspoon of cayenne pepper. For smoky hash browns , add ½ teaspoon of smoked paprika. *If you’re avoiding oil and using a non stick air fryer, this recipe also works without the oil. I tried it in my Ninja Foodi and it does not stick. Use a silicone spatula to gently separate the edges and it will remove easily. Please note that it will be slightly less crispy this way. This recipe is naturally vegan, gluten free, soy free, nut free and free from all common allergens. ***EDIT Feb 28/2021 – Lowered temperature from 400 degrees to 370 degrees F. Some users were experiencing cooking too quickly. This will vary according to your fryer model. If you’ve previously made this at 400 degrees with no trouble, you may continue to do so."]]},"9421240":{"s":[[null,"Peel and chop your potatoes into roughly half inch pieces and place them in a large bowl. Cover with cold water and let them soak for 20 minutes. Then drain them, rinse with cold water and place them on a clean, dry dish towel and pat the potatoes dry. Wipe the bowl dry, and place the potatoes back inside."],[null,"Now add all remaining ingredients to the same bowl and mix well to evenly coat."],[null,"Place them in your basket and air fry at 400°F/204°C for 15-20 minutes, until cooked through and desired crispiness is reached. Shake your basket or stir the potatoes every 5 minutes for even cooking."]],"h":[[null,"For best results , take the time to soak and rinse your potatoes before cooking. This will give you the crispiest air fryer home fries. Cut your potatoes as evenly as possible for even cooking . Half-inch cubes work well for quick cooking and they will crisp up nicely. Don’t dice the onion and pepper too small or they will burn and may fall through the holes of your basket. If you don’t want larger pieces, add them only once the potatoes are about halfway cooked. Air fryers range in strength so always check on your potatoes while cooking. I use a Ninja Foodi 8qt and mine are perfect at the 20-minute mark. Smaller models may cook faster. Play with the seasoning for added flavour . I’ve kept these simple, but if you want to change up the flavours, you may sub the paprika with smoked paprika, and/or add some onion powder, chili powder, cumin, or cayenne. These taste best when freshly made, but leftovers keep in the refrigerator for 3-4 days in a sealed container. Reheat in air frying basket or toaster oven."]]},"9583574":{"s":[[null,"Add the oats to a blender or food processor and process for about 5-6 seconds to break them down. Do not overprocess. You want to have some floury bits with some whole oats, but you're not making flour, so don't overdo it."],[null,"Add the blitzed oats and all remaining ingredients, including any optional ones, to a medium bowl. Mix well."],[null,"Line your air frying basket with parchment paper. Then, divide the batter into 7 portions for small cookies or 3-4 portions for large cookies. Roll each portion into a ball and flatten and shape it in your hand. Then place it in the basket."],[null,"Air fry the oatmeal cookies at 325°F/163°C for 4-6 minutes, until slightly golden. Then remove the basket from the fryer and set it aside to let cool for at least 10 minutes before handling.NOTE: The cookies will appear underdone at first, but they will set as they cool, so don't overcook them."],[null,"After the 10 minutes, transfer to a warming rack to continue cooling or enjoy them warm."]],"h":[[null,"Don't overprocess the oats. You don't want to make flour or this will alter the cookie’s texture. Use wet hands to roll and shape the batter. This helps prevent the cookie dough from sticking to your hands. Don’t overdo it on fill-ins . More than 2-3 tablespoons of any fill-in will make these difficult to shape and they’ll fall apart more easily. Do not overbake the cookies. They may appear underdone and soft, but they will firm up as they cool. Let the cookies rest for 10 minutes before handling them. This brief cool-down helps them completely set. The cookies will keep in a sealed container at room temperate for 2-3 days, or in the fridge for up to 5 days. Freeze them airtight for up to 3 months."]]},"7060141":{"s":[[null,"Put the flour, garam masala, paprika, fennel seeds, if using, and a little pepper in a large bowl. Add the onion, carrot and coriander and mix well. Stir in 3 tbsp cold water (add 1-2 tbsp more if needed) and leave to stand for 5 minutes."],[null,"Preheat your air fryer to 180°C."],[null,"Divide the mixture into 10 even portions, then squidge each of them into a small rugby-ball shape. Spray the bhajis with low-calorie cooking spray, then put 5 of them in your air fryer basket and cook for 8-10 minutes, or until golden and firm. Transfer to a hot plate, cover with foil and keep warm while you cook for remaining bhajis. When the second batch is done, you can turn the heat down to low and put the first batch back in for 2-3 minutes to heat through."],[null,"While the bhajis are cooking, mix the dip ingredients together. Serve the bhajis with the dip and scatter the extra chopped mint and leaves over everything."],[null,"To oven cook: Cook the bhajis on a non-stick baking tray at 200°C/fan 180°C/gas 6 for 10-15 minutes or until golden and cooked through."]],"h":[[null,"This recipe was tested in a 4.3-litre air fryer. If yours is bigger, you might be able to cook all of the bhajis at the same time."],[null,"If you don’t need these to be vegan, swap the soya yogurt for fat-free natural Greek yogurt."],[null,"This recipe makes 10 bhajis. Enjoy a couple as a starter or serve as a side dish to a curry."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"9809440":{"s":[[null,"Wash and slice your peaches and remove the pits. Place the sliced peaches in a small mixing bowl and set aside."],[null,"Optional: In another small bowl combine the butter, sugar, and cinnamon. Then pour the marinade on the sliced peaches and mix well to evenly coat the slices. (You can air fry the peaches plain without the mixture if you're avoiding added fat and sugar.)"],[null,"Arrange the sliced peaches in a single layer in your fryer basket and air fry at 350°F/177°C for 8-12 minutes. They are ready when very soft and a fork easily pierces through a peach slice."],[null,"Serve warm with desired toppings or enjoy as is."]],"h":[[null,"Use fresh peaches that are RIPE for the best flavour and natural sweetness. Cut large peaches into 6 slices and small peaches into 4 slices . The ripeness of your peaches will determine cook time. Riper/softer peaches will cook faster than less ripe/harder peaches. Remove any peach skins that come loose while air frying. For picky eaters , peel the skin prior to slicing the peaches and air frying. The nutritional information INCLUDES the optional marinade . It does not include optional toppings such as nuts and/or vanilla ice cream. Skipping the marinade and cooking the peaches plain will make this dessert fat free and reduce the calories to 64 cals per serving."]]},"9106627":{"s":[[null,"Combine all the ingredients in a small mixing bowl and stir until combined. The batter might seem dry at first, but just keep mixing until it's smooth."],[null,"Use a small cookie scoop (1 tablespoon) to scoop your batter. Then roll it into a ball in the palm of your hand. Use a fork to press the ball down into a flatter cookie shape, making a crisscross pattern. Then place the cookie into your air fryer basket. Repeat with the remaining batter, leaving a half inch space between each cookie. You should get 7 cookies."],[null,"Air fry the cookies at 325 degrees F for 5-7 minutes until they appear golden on top. They will still be soft to the touch, this is normal and they will firm up as they cool. Remove the basket from the fryer and let the cookies rest, undisturbed for 10 minutes. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Don’t use parchment paper in your basket. It will fly around and prevent the air from flowing under your cookies. You need breathing holes for the best results. Weigh your flour for the most accuracy. Scooping flour from a bag often results in too much being used and may cause your cookies to be dry. If you don’t have a kitchen scale , and the cookie batter seems dry, add 1 extra teaspoon of maple syrup and mix well before adding more. A little goes a long way. Use a small (1 tablespoon size) cookie scoop for even-sized cookies and even “baking”. After rolling the batter into a ball, press with a fork in the palm of your hand . Do not press the cookies into the air frying basket or some of the cookie dough will push through the basket holes, causing them to break when removing them later. Let your peanut butter cookies cool down in the basket (but basket removed from fryer) for 10 minutes before handling. This rest time will firm up your cookies."]]},"9959942":{"s":[[null,"Place the raw peanuts in your air fryer basket in a single layer and air fry at 350°F/177°C for 6-8 minutes, mixing at the halfway point."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the tablespoon of aquafaba to a small mixing bowl, along with the spice mix of your choice. Mix well."],[null,"Pour the roasted peanuts into the bowl with the seasoning and mix well to evenly coat them. Then return them to the basket and air fry for an additional 2-4 minutes, until golden, but watch carefully to prevent them from burning."],[null,"Then pour the air fried peanuts into a bowl and let cool for a few minutes before enjoying."]],"h":[[null,"Don’t season the peanuts from the start of cooking , or the spices may start to burn. If making multiple batches (as you should, to try all the flavours 😉 ), note that subsequent batches will cook a little faster, so watch carefully. The nutritional information represents one serving size of ¼ cup of the air fried peanuts in the salt and pepper flavour. Keep leftovers in a sealed container at room temperature for up to 1 week."]]},"9957284":{"s":[[null,"Wash and peel your pears. (Or you may leave the skins on if preferred.) Then cut them into quarters, scrape seeds and remove the core. Place in a small mixing bowl."],[null,"Add the maple syrup, cinnamon, and nutmeg on top and mix gently, until evenly coated."],[null,"Spoon the coated pears in a single layer in your basket and air fry at 380 degrees F (190 C) for 8-12 minutes until golden and caramelized. Do not dump!"],[null,"Carefully remove the pears from your basket and serve topped with granola, coconut flakes, and chopped pecans or walnuts. Enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Use pears that are ripe for the sweetest, juiciest results. Try and cut your pear slices into equal size pieces for even cooking. If some pieces are larger, they won’t be as soft, although, still delicious. Don’t dump the pears into your basket . Spoon them into your basket carefully to prevent breaking and arrange them in a single layer. If you have leftover marinade in the bottom of the bowl, reserve it to glaze over your pears once cooked. In the unlikely event you have leftovers, place them in a sealed container in your refrigerator for 2-3 days."]]},"9529012":{"s":[[null,"Place the thawed peas in a small bowl and add the seasoning of your choice. Mix well, and arrange the peas in a single layer in your air fryer basket."],[null,"Air fry the peas at 350℉/176℃ for 8-12 minutes, or until the desired doneness is reached. Mix or shake the basket every 2-3 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Arrange the peas in a single layer for even cooking."],[null,"Shake your basket or mix the peas every 2-3 minutes to prevent sticking and/or burning."]]},"9692965":{"s":[[null,"Determine which flavour you're making, the sweet or the spiced. Then combine the first four ingredients belonging to that flavour in a small bowl and set aside. Place your pecans in another bowl and pour the mixture on top. Mix well to ensure each pecan half is coated."],[null,"Line a small baking sheet with parchment paper and set it aside. Then spoon the coated pecans into your air frying basket but do not dump them in. Air fry at 350 degrees F for 3-5 minutes, mixing or shaking the basket at the halfway point. Watch carefully to prevent burning. They cook fast."],[null,"Transfer the pecans to your parchment-lined tray in a single layer to let them cool. Try your hardest not to devour them warm, as they will harden and get crunchy as they cool, which is when they taste best. Enjoy! ;)"]],"h":[[null,"Arrange the pecans in a single layer after air frying until they’re cool. Try your hardest not to eat them warm (although still delicious warm). This cool down time will allow them to harden and prevent them from sticking to one another. They cool down quickly and will be ready to eat in about 10-15 minutes. Leftovers keep at room temperature in a sealed container or jar for 1-2 weeks. The nutritional information above represents 1 serving of the sweet candied pecans. The spiced pecans are a little lighter with 182 calories and 3 grams of sugar per serving."]]},"9397040":{"s":[[null,"Peel, core and slice your pineapple and place about 2 heaping cups worth in a mixing bowl."],[null,"Combine the melted butter, maple syrup and cinnamon in a small bowl, then pour it over your pineapple slices. Mix gently to even coat the slices."],[null,"Then place them in a single layer (slightly overlapping is fine) in your fryer basket and air fry at 380 degrees F for 12-15 minutes, or until caramelized. Flip the pineapple once at the halfway point."],[null,"Enjoy warm or cold, as a side dish or dessert."],["Optional Dip","If making the chili lime dip, combine the 3 ingredients in a small bowl while your pineapple is cooking."]],"h":[[null,"Don’t dump the pineapple slices into your fryer basket . Instead, spoon them in one at a time to avoid breaking them, and prevent excess liquid from dripping down below your basket and smoking. Leftovers keep refrigerated in a sealed container for 2-3 days."]]},"9956832":{"s":[[null,"Cut your pitas into 8 triangular wedges. Using a pizza cutter is a quick way to do this. Then combine the remaining ingredients in a small bowl."],[null,"Brush the spice mixture on the tops of your pita wedges. Then arrange them in your air frying basket. (It's okay if they overlap a bit.)"],[null,"Air fry at 350°F/176°C for 3-4 minutes for softer chips OR 5-7 minutes for crispier chips. Check on them often and remove them when the desired doneness is reached. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Different air frying models cook at different speeds . Check on your chips often, starting at the 3-minute mark. For softer chips, air fry for approx. 3-4 minutes."],[null,"For crispy chips, air fry for approx. 5-7 minutes."],[null,"No problem for the pita triangles to overlap a bit in your fryer basket. However, don’t completely overlap them. Work in batches , if needed. NOTE : Subsequent batches will cook faster."]]},"9537373":{"s":[[null,"Peel or scrub your potatoes clean, then cut them into wedges. (See above for process shots, if needed.)"],[null,"Place the cut potato wedges in a bowl and cover with cold water for at least 20 minutes. Then drain and pat dry using a clean dish towel. Wipe the bowl dry, and place the wedges back inside."],[null,"Add the oil (if using) and all the seasoning and mix to evenly coat. Then transfer the seasoned potato wedges to the basket of your fryer in a single layer, leaving a little room in between. (Work in batches, if needed.)"],[null,"Air fry at 400 degrees F for 15 minutes, mixing once at the halfway point. Serve with ketchup, spicy mayo or any of your favourite dips."]],"h":[[null,"Although optional, I recommend to soak the uncooked potato wedges for maximum crispiness . You especially don’t want to skip this step if you’re choosing to skip the oil. This recipe has been tested both with oil and without oil. The results are similar, but the oil option comes out a little bit crispier, as anticipated. Change up the flavouring each time with one of my spice blends listed above. Potato wedges taste best when freshly made, but leftovers will keep refrigerated for up to 3 days."]]},"9991273":{"s":[[null,"Scrub and slice the potatoes very thin, using a mandolin or another slicing tool, approx. 1/8\" thick. Keep the onions sliced thicker since they cook faster."],[null,"Mix the sliced potatoes, onions, broth, and seasoning in a large bowl until evenly coated. Then transfer everything to your fryer basket."],[null,"Air fry the potatoes and onions at 400℉/204℃ for approx. 20 minutes, and stir or shake the basket every 5 minutes, until the desired doneness is reached. Serve hot with freshly chopped parsley or basil if you'd like."]],"h":[[null,"Cut your potatoes as evenly as possible for even cooking and crispiness."],[null,"The air frying model and potato thickness will determine cook time , so watch carefully toward the end of cooking."],[null,"For crispier potatoes , you may use a good quality oil such as avocado oil, instead of broth, but this will increase the calories and fat. (I don't recommend cooking with olive oil due to its low smoke point.)"]]},"9327187":{"s":[[null,"Scrub your potatoes very well since you'll be eating the skins. Then place them in a pot and fill with water that covers one inch above the potatoes. Add a teaspoon of salt and bring to a boil. Cook until a fork pierces the potatoes, but they still remain intact, approx. 18 minutes. Do NOT overcook, or they will break when you smash them."],[null,"While the potatoes are cooking, melt the butter (if using) in a small saucepot. Then mix in the minced garlic and seasoning and set aside."],[null,"Drain the potatoes and transfer to a cutting board to let cool for a few minutes, until easy to handle. Use a large fork or potato masher to carefully smash the potatoes until flattened to approx. half an inch thick. (Careful: do not overly smash them, or they may break.)"],[null,"Brush both sides of the potato with your seasoned butter mixture and transfer to your basket, leaving plenty of space in between each one. Air fry at 400 degrees F for 8-12 minutes, or until desired crispiness is reached."]],"h":[[null,"Salt your cooking water OR use broth to boil your potatoes for enhanced flavour. Use small potatoes for best results. Large potatoes will take longer to cook, they won’t get as crispy, and they’re more difficult to handle once smashed. Position your potatoes in the basket with plenty of space in between each one , for proper airflow, and so you don’t need to flip them. Let the potatoes cool for a few minutes after boiling to make them easier to handle and smash without breaking them."]]},"6507632":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the air fryer to 400 degrees F, or an oven to 420 degrees F"],[null,"Combine paprika, cumin, dried oregano, and cayenne pepper in a small bowl."],[null,"Lightly spray the tenders with oil, then rub the spice mixture all over the chicken. For best results, let it marinate for at least 20 minutes or overnight in the fridge."],[null,"Add the chicken to an air fryer basket or a baking tray (lined with parchment or foil)."],[null,"Air fry for 12–15 minutes or bake for 16–20 minutes until the chicken is 165 degrees F internally."]],"h":[]},"9592646":{"s":[[null,"Cut a thin slice off the ends of your squash and then cut in half, lengthwise, as evenly as possible in two halves. Place the two halves in your air fryer basket, cut side up. Then drizzle with the oil (if using) and evenly sprinkle with the seasoning."],[null,"Cook at 360 degrees F for 20 minutes, or until a fork can easily pierce the flesh. (This may vary according to the size of your squash.)"],[null,"Once cooked, transfer to a dish and fluff up the inside with a fork. Then add the parmesan cheese and fresh parsley, if using, and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Cut your squash in half as equally as possible for even cooking. Different air fryers may cook at different speeds. I’m using a Ninja Foodi, but if you have a different model, start checking your squash around the 15 minute mark and cook until fork tender. The size of your spaghetti squash will reflect cook time . I cooked a 2 lb squash in my Ninja Foodi for 20 minutes with perfect results. If your squash is smaller or bigger, adjust cook time. *For oil free , omit the oil and spray or drizzle a little vegetable broth on top for moisture before cooking. I use an 8qt Ninja Foodi but any model that can fit your squash inside should work just fine. If you don’t have an air fryer , you can still make this in your oven. Preheat to 400 degrees F, halve your squash and season as directed. Then bake on a tray lined with parchment paper for 35-45 minutes, until fork tender. Leftovers keep refrigerated in an air tight container for 3 days or frozen for up to 3 months."]]},"6609371":{"s":[[null,"Place the green beans in a medium bowl and toss with the olive oil, chili garlic paste, panko bread crumbs, and salt."],[null,"Place the green beans in the air fryer basket. Set the temperature to 400° F and air fry for 4 minutes. Shake the air fryer basket. Air fry for an additional 5 to 7 minutes. Serve warm."]],"h":[]},"9541318":{"s":[[null,"Wash your strawberries and blot them dry to remove any excess moisture. Then use a strawberry huller or sharp knife to hull/remove the stems."],[null,"Slice the berries as evenly as possible, approx. 1/8 inch in thickness. Then arrange them in your air frying basket in a single layer, without overlapping."],[null,"Air fry or use the dehydrate function (depending on your model) at 190℉/88℃ for 60-90 minutes. (Time will vary according to the thickness of your slices and the air frying model you have.)"],[null,"Start checking on your strawberries at the 45-minute mark, and flip them. Then continue checking on them in 15-minute intervals until they are fully dried to the touch."],["Oven Instructions","Preheat your oven to 200℉/93℃ and line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],["Oven Instructions","Wash your strawberries and blot them dry to remove any excess moisture. Then use a strawberry huller or sharp knife to hull/remove the stems."],["Oven Instructions","Slice the berries as evenly as possible, approx. 1/8 inch in thickness. Then arrange them on your baking sheet in a single layer, without overlapping."],["Oven Instructions","Bake for 90 minutes, and then peel the slices from the parchment paper and flip them. Continue baking for another 30-60 minutes until completely dried. (The thickness of the slices will determine how long they take to fully dry.)"]],"h":[[null,"Thick slices will take longer to dry out vs. thin slices. Do your best to cut the berries with uniform thickness for even cooking times ."],[null,"Remove thinner pieces once done and continue cooking any thicker pieces until each slice is dehydrated."],[null,"I’ve made these with and without lining the air fryer basket with parchment paper. Both options work fine, but"]]},"9794865":{"s":[[null,"Peel and cube your sweet potatoes into half inch cubes. Place them in a medium size bowl. Add all the seasoning for the flavour of choice (spicy OR sweet, not both) on top, and mix well to evenly coat."],[null,"Place the seasoned potato cubes into your fryer basket, in a single layer. (Work in batches, if needed.) Then air fry at 400 degrees F for 18-22 minutes, shaking or mixing every 5 minutes. Cook time will vary according to batch size and fryer model."]],"h":[[null,"Work in batches if you have a smaller fryer basket and check on your potatoes often, towards the end of cooking. Do not overcrowd your basket . Batch size and fryer model will determine cook time . Smaller batches cook fast, AND your second batch will cook faster then the first, so make sure to check on your potatoes during cooking. These taste best when enjoyed right away, but leftovers will keep refrigerated for 3-4 days. Recipe inspired by my air fried butternut squash . ***The nutritional information below is for one fourth of the spicy version. The sweet version has 223 calories and 15 grams of sugar per serving."]]},"6226273":{"s":[[null,"Place the sweet potato slices evenly in the air fryer basket. Spray with nonstick cooking spray for 1 second. Spoon the frozen vegetables evenly over the potatoes. Place the jalapeño over the vegetables, skin side up. Spray with nonstick cooking spray for 1 second."],[null,"Set the temperature to 375° F and air fry for 20 minutes, or until the potatoes are cooked. They should be tender but crisp, not soft. Remove the jalapeño pepper and place it in a bowl; cover loosely with a kitchen towel and let stand for 5 minutes."],[null,"Sprinkle the cheese evenly over the vegetables. Air fry for 2 minutes, or until the cheese is melted."],[null,"Using the tip of a sharp knife, remove the browned or charred skin from the jalapeño pepper. Finely chop the pepper."],[null,"Using a spatula, lift the potatoes and vegetables out of the air fryer basket and arrange in an even layer on a serving platter. Sprinkle the chopped jalapeño over the vegetables. Top with the salsa, radishes, tomatoes, and lettuce. Add a dollop of sour cream and sprinkle of cilantro. Serve immediately."]],"h":[]},"9254108":{"s":[["Press the Tofu","Cut your tofu into half inch cubes. Then arrange some paper towels or a clean dish towel on a cutting board and place the tofu cubes in a single layer on top. Now add more paper towels on top of the cubes and place another cutting board, flat plate or baking sheet on top. Finally place something very heavy on top like a cast iron skillet or a heavy book. Press like this for 15 minutes while you prepare the remaining ingredients."],["Prepare the Tofu","Combine all the dry seasoning, including the corn starch in a small bowl, and set aside."],["Prepare the Tofu","Place the pressed tofu cubes in a shallow dish or container and pour the tamari and rice vinegar on top, toss to evenly coat. Then sprinkle all the seasoning on top and mix well. If you use a container, you can put the lid on and gently rotate the container around to evenly spread the seasoning."],["Prepare the Tofu","Arrange your cubes in your fryer basket in a single layer working in two batches, if you have a small fryer. Do not over crowd your tofu to ensure maximum crispiness. Air fry at 400 degrees F for 10-15 minutes, mixing or shaking your basket around the halfway point. Mine were perfect at 13 minutes, but start checking on the tofu around the 10 minute mark."],["Prepare the Tofu","Serve with a dip like spicy mayo or cashew cream. Or use to top some rice and veggies."]],"h":[[null,"Do not overcrowd the tofu , or it won’t get as crispy. If you have a smaller fryer, work in two batches for best texture and results. If you’re working in batches , remember that your second batch will cook faster since your fryer is already hot, so start checking on the tofu sooner. Try your best to cut your cubes into similarly sized pieces for even cooking and best results. Plan to consume your air fryer tofu the same day its made as it will begin to lose its crispiness the longer it sits. If time permits , you may leave your tofu in the marinade for 30 minutes, up to 12 hours (refrigerated) before air frying, to absorb even more flavour."]]},"9807540":{"s":[[null,"Add all the ingredients to an oven-safe dish that will fit inside your air frying basket. Mix well to evenly coat the tomatoes, and place the dish inside your basket."],[null,"Air fry at 375℉/190℃ for 8-10 minutes, or until the tomato skins appear wrinkled, mixing once at the halfway point, then remove the dish from the fryer."],[null,"Enjoy on toast, as a side dish, or as a topping for burgers."]],"h":[[null,"Experiment with different tomato varieties . You may also use tomato slices for large format ones like beefsteak. Different models will cook at different speeds , so make sure to watch your tomatoes carefully and start checking on them around the 5-minute mark. Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-4 days."]]},"9229405":{"s":[[null,"Slice your zucchini horizontally in slices that are approx. 1/8 inch thick and place in a mixing bowl."],[null,"Then combine all remaining ingredients in a small bowl and pour the mixture over your zucchini slices. Mix well to ensure each piece is coated, using your hands to separate the slices, as you go."],[null,"Place the zucchini in your basket and air fry at 400 degrees F for 20-25 minutes, until golden. Gently shake your basket or mix the zucchini, every 5 minutes or so, for even cooking."]],"h":[[null,"Do your best to slice your zucchini as evenly as possible for even cooking. Shake your basket , or mix gently, every 5 minutes or so during cooking. This will ensure even cooking, and prevent the zucchini from sticking to your basket. Try different spice mixtures to change it up each time. See my suggestions above! Leftovers keep refrigerated in a sealed container for 3-4 days."]]},"6841339":{"s":[[null,"Rinse any ice glaze from frozen Alaska salmon under cold water; pat dry with paper towel. Heat skillet over medium-high heat and brush both sides of fish using 3 tablespoons of avocado oil. Cook salmon, uncovered, about 4 minutes, until browned."],[null,"Turn salmon over and season lightly with 1/8 tsp each salt and pepper. Cook an additional 6 to 8 minutes for frozen, or 3 to 4 minutes for fresh/thawed, just until fish is opaque throughout."],[null,"Meanwhile, in a medium bowl combine watercress, cucumber, and orange segments."],[null,"In a small bowl combine the remaining avocado oil, apple cider vinegar and 1/8 tsp each salt and pepper."],[null,"Plate mixed greens next to salmon and top with avocado, walnuts, and apple cider vinaigrette. Add nasturtiums, if desired, and serve."]],"h":[]},"6089715":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375°F. Spray a large baking sheet with cooking spray."],[null,"Heat the olive oil in a medium skillet over medium-high heat. Add the filling ingredients except the Parmesan cheese and sauté until the mushrooms and onions are tender and have released all of their liquid. Remove from the heat, stir in the Parmesan cheese, and let cool."],[null,"In a bowl, combine the meatloaf ingredients until incorporated."],[null,"Once the filling is cool, pulse it in a food processor until chopped but still slightly chunky. Do not purée it into a paste."],[null,"Divide the meatloaf mixture into 8 equal portions. Flatten one portion in your hand to form a patty. Place a heaping tablespoon of the mushroom mixture in the center of the patty and close your hand to form a ball around the mushroom mixture. Repeat with the remaining meatballs. Place on the sprayed baking sheet and bake for 35 minutes."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix the ketchup and balsamic vinegar. After the meatballs have baked for 35 minutes, brush each meatball generously with half of the glaze. Return to the oven for 5 minutes, then brush the remaining glaze over the meatballs and bake for 5 more minutes."]],"h":[]},"2100":{"s":[[null,"Cut cream cheese into cubes."],[null,"Mix cream cheese, Parmesan cheese, milk, butter, white pepper and garlic powder in medium saucepan."],[null,"Cook on low heat until cream cheese is melted and mixture is well blended."]],"h":[[null,"Serve Alfredo Sauce over fettuccine or your favorite pasta. Sprinkle with nutmeg if desired."],[null,"Other milk substitutes such as rice milk and almond milk may be substituted."]]},"1956":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Finely chop onion. Place crackers in a large zip-top bag and crush with a rolling pin."],[null,"Coat a loaf pan with nonstick cooking spray."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine crushed crackers, onion, ground beef, egg, milk and black pepper. Mix well."],[null,"Place mixture into loaf pan. Bake for 40 minutes."],[null,"To make topping, mix catsup, brown sugar, vinegar and water in a small bowl."],[null,"Remove cooked meatloaf from oven and cover with sauce."],[null,"Return pan to oven and bake for 10 minutes or until internal temperature reaches 160° F."],[null,"Slice into 6 portions and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Use leftover meatloaf to make sandwiches."],[null,"To be more diabetes friendly, be sure to use the leanest meat 7-10% fat. This will decrease the saturated fat. Or have a smaller portion."]]},"7485752":{"s":[[null,"In a large shallow dish, mix together the garlic, ginger, chilli, soy sauce and vinegar. Add the salmon and leave to marinate overnight if you have time or for at least 20 minutes."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 200°C/gas 6. Spray a shallow roasting tin with low-calorie cooking spray and arrange the broccoli and spring onions over the top. Next, spray the vegetables with a little low-calorie cooking spray. Cook for 10 minutes."],[null,"Arrange the salmon over the top and drizzle over the marinade. Season with freshly ground black pepper. Cook for 12–15 minutes until the salmon is cooked through. Serve immediately."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6793195":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6996404":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6320927":{"s":[[null,"Toast the bread and spread almond butter."],[null,"Top with sliced pears and sprinkle with cinnamon."]],"h":[]},"4891483":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F."],[null,"Line an 8-inch springform or regular pan with parchment paper."],[null,"In a medium bowl, mix ground almonds, flour, baking soda, and cream of tartar. Set aside."],[null,"In another bowl, with an electric mixer on medium speed, cream sugar, softened butter, and oil (1–2 minutes). Add the eggs one by one and mix until smooth. Add almond extract."],[null,"Mixing at low speed, incorporate the dry ingredients alternately with yogurt until the batter is smooth. Pour into the pan and sprinkle sliced almonds on top."],[null,"Bake for about 30 minutes or until a knife inserted in the center comes out clean. Let cool."],[null,"Remove from the pan and serve each slice with 1 tablespoon yogurt and 1 tablespoon sliced almonds."],[null,"tablespoons instant coffee in 1 tablespoon water and mixing it into the batter in step 4 with the almond extract."]],"h":[[null,"Note: Add coffee flavor by dissolving"],["Try a healthy twist on treats","Everyone loves a treat. When carefully chosen, a treat now and then can be part of a healthy diet. Unfortunately, many of the treats we reach for are highly processed foods such as packaged cakes, donuts, muffins, cookies, and dessert bars. These foods contain refined or processed ingredients and typically have higher amounts of saturated fat, added sugar, sodium, and phosphate-type additives with little to no whole foods. These “ultra-processed” foods are usually not kidney-friendly and can contribute to many chronic diseases. It is understandable why we choose these foods because they are convenient, inexpensive, and tasty. Instead, consider baking at home. When doing your own baking, you can use whole-grain flours and even substitute some of the flour with finely ground nuts to increase nutrition. This change increases the fiber of your treat and lowers the carbohydrate content, which can help control blood glucose when needed. You can usually substitute up to half of the total flour with ground nuts. You can either buy ground nuts or make your own in a food processor. Toasting the nuts first makes them easier to grind while increasing flavor; use the pulse setting so they do not turn into a paste. Other healthy changes include using less salt and sugar in the recipe."]]},"3596476":{"s":[[null,"On a high heat, in a frying pan, melt the ghee, then add the grated onion, garlic, ginger, carrot and spices and cook for 10 minutes. If the mixture starts to stick, add a little water."],[null,"Add the ground almonds with 40ml of water to the pan. If ingredients start to stick to the pan, add more water (another 20-40 ml)."],[null,"Add the cubed chicken to the pan, brown, then turn heat down to medium. Cook for 10 minutes, adding more water if needed to stop the sauce sticking to the pan."],[null,"Meanwhile, rinse the rice under cold water and drain. Put into a pan of boiling water, bring back to boil then turn heat down to medium, put a lid on and cook for 12 minutes."],[null,"The almond chicken is ready when the chicken is cooked through, and the sauce is thick and a sandy colour. At this stage, add the peas to warm through."],[null,"Serve the rice, top with the almond chicken and garnish with fresh, chopped coriander."]],"h":[["Chef's note","This is a creamy, authentic, and versatile dish that’s low in salt, potassium and phosphate."],["Carbohydrate","The rice is the main source of carbohydrate in this main meal, and the value has been provided for those who have been trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","This dish is low in potassium, if you have been advised to reduce your potassium ensure you keep to the quantities and serving sizes stated.\nThis recipe is low in phosphate, however does contain some phosphate, therefore, if you have been prescribed a phosphate binder ensure you take with this dish."],["Protein","This dish is high in protein and therefore suitable to those advised to eat more protein, such as those receiving dialysis. If you have been advised to eat less protein, consider using a 400g drained tin of chickpeas in place of the chicken, or halve the quantity of chicken (100g) and replace with a 200g drained tin of chickpeas or lentils."],["Cheaper option","Consider using chicken with bones and de-bone yourself. Also, omit the fresh chopped coriander herbs to reduce the cost. If you are unable to get ground cumin or coriander, you could use curry powder to replace."],["Vegetarian","Replace the chicken with a 400g tin of drained lentils or chickpeas. Alternatively use 200-300g of tofu."],["Vegan","Replace the chicken with a 400g tin of drained lentils or chickpeas. Alternatively use 200-300g of tofu. Replace the ghee with a vegetable oil."],["Healthier option","Replace the white rice with a brown wholegrain rice to increase the fibre and replace the ghee or unsalted butter with a vegetable oil such as sunflower for a healthier source of fat. However, this will result in a slightly runnier sauce."],["Storage","This curry sauce freezes well. Cool soon after cooking and freeze for up to three months. Defrost thoroughly in the fridge before reheating."],["Tips","If you prefer, other vegetables can be used instead of peas and carrots. Cauliflower and green beans work well, as do aubergine and spinach, but these are high in potassium, so if you need to reduce your potassium don’t choose these."]]},"6758436":{"s":[[null,"Fill each celery stalk with 1 tbsp cream cheese, then cut each stalk into 3 equal pieces. Top each piece with 1 almond and 2 dried cranberries. Serve immediately, or cover and refrigerate until ready to serve."]],"h":[]},"9784963":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350℉/176℃."],[null,"In a large mixing bowl, mash your bananas and add the applesauce and maple syrup. Mix well. Then add the flour, baking powder, baking soda, cinnamon, and mix until combined. Then fold in the chopped walnuts, if using them."],[null,"Scoop your mixture between 9 muffin tins. (Use nonstick, muffin liners, or grease if necessary.) Bake for 24-26 minutes, until a toothpick inserted in the middle comes out clean."],[null,"IMPORTANT: Let the muffins rest for 10-15 minutes in the pan before transferring to a wire rack. The muffins will be soft and delicate when fresh out of the oven, but they will firm up as they cool."]],"h":[[null,"Use very ripe bananas ! This recipe only calls for 2 tablespoons of maple syrup, so use overly ripe bananas with brown spots on the peels, for natural sweetness."],[null,"Weigh your flour . Scooping flour from a bag is less accurate than weight. So if you have a kitchen scale, use it for the best texture and results."],[null,"Use FRESH baking powder. Baking powder that has been open for over 6+ months may start to lose its effectiveness and rising power."],[null,"Individual ovens will vary , so bake until a toothpick inserted in the middle comes out dry and clean. Mine were perfect in 24 minutes."],[null,"Keep leftovers in a sealed container or tightly wrapped at room temperature for 1-2 days. Refrigerate them for up to 5 days, or freeze them airtight for up to 3 months."]]},"9115856":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350℉/176℃ and line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Mash the banana into a medium mixing bowl. Then add all the remaining ingredients and stir until combined."],[null,"Scoop the cookie mixture onto your lined baking sheet, using a tablespoon or cookie scoop to get approx. 16-18 cookies. You may press them down for flatter cookies, or leave them rounded for fluffier cookies. (I prefer mine round and fluffy.)"],[null,"Bake for 12-15 minutes, or until the edges of the cookies are golden brown and firm to the touch. Remove the tray from the oven and let them cool for 5-10 minutes before enjoying."]],"h":[]},"9984982":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F and grab a nonstick muffin pan that holds 12 muffins. Grease if necessary."],[null,"Add the dry ingredients to a large mixing bowl and whisk together. Set aside. Then add the wet ingredients to a medium bowl and mix thoroughly to get the cashew butter evenly combined."],[null,"Pour the wet mixture into the bowl of dry ingredients and mix until combined. Now gently fold in the blackberries. Use care not to break them."],[null,"Divide the batter among your 12 muffin tins and bake for 22-24 minutes, until a toothpick comes out mostly clean, and the edges of your muffins appear golden."],[null,"Remove from the oven and let rest for at least 10 minutes to completely set, before removing the muffins from the pan."]],"h":[[null,"For accuracy, it’s best to weigh your flour . But if you don’t have a kitchen scale, use 2.5 cups, and spoon and level the flour into your measuring cup. Blanched almond flour works best , so don’t sub for almond meal or non blanched flour. Make sure your baking powder is fresh and still active . Baking powder that has been open in your pantry for 6+ months will start to lose its effectiveness. Use fresh blackberries rather than frozen . Frozen blackberries may bleed into your batter turning it purple and adds extra liquid. Be gentle when folding in the blackberries to prevent them from breaking into your batter. Give your muffins enough time to cool in the pan , before transferring them. Almond flour desserts can be softer and delicate so it’s easiest to remove them once slightly cooled. Leftovers keep at room temperature for 2-3 days, refrigerated for 5-6 days, or freeze for up to 3 months."]]},"6298457":{"s":[[null,"In a bowl, whisk together almond flour, gluten free flour, baking powder, and salt."],[null,"In a separate bowl, beat the egg substitute and add almond milk, canola oil, sugar free maple syrup, and vanilla extract. Mix well."],[null,"Pour the wet ingredients into the dry ingredients and stir until combined. Let the batter sit for a couple of minutes to thicken."],[null,"Heat a skillet or griddle over medium heat and grease with cooking spray."],[null,"Pour ¼ cup of batter onto the skillet for each pancake. Spread the batter slightly with the back of a spoon."],[null,"Cook until bubbles form on the surface, then flip and cook until the other side is golden brown."],[null,"Repeat with the remaining batter."],[null,"Serve topped with one fresh, sliced strawberry."]],"h":[]},"9422469":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F and line a cookie sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"In a medium mixing bowl, add the peanut butter, maple syrup and vanilla, and mix well. Use a fork or silicone spatula to ensure the ingredients are well combined."],[null,"In a separate, small bowl, whisk together the almond flour, baking soda and the salt. Then add the dry ingredients to the bowl of wet. Mix well. The batter will be sticky and thick, but just keep mixing until incorporated."],[null,"Divide the mixture into 16 balls of dough and place on your tray. Then using a slightly wet fork, press down on each ball to form a crisscross pattern on top of each cookie."],[null,"Bake for 10 minutes, then remove from the oven and let cool for 10 minutes and do not touch the cookies during this time. After the 10 minute rest, transfer the cookies to a cooling rack for another 5-10 minutes. This cooling off period is crucial for the cookies to completely set and for the edges to get nice and crunchy."]],"h":[[null,"Use the weight measurement for the flour , whenever possible. This will ensure the most accurate results. If you MUST use volume, make sure to spoon and level the almond flour. Do not scoop using your measuring cup or you'll may up with too much flour. If you're having trouble mixing your batter with a spoon or spatula, use your hands to help get the ingredients mixed in. The batter will be slightly sticky and thick. Divide the batter as I've shown in photo 7 above if you care about having cookies that are roughly the same size. These don't really spread, so make sure to shape the cookies to the size and thickness you like before you bake them . When making your crisscross pattern , wet your fork with water before pressing into your dough. This will help prevent the fork from sticking to them. Dip the fork into some water after every few cookies or so. Do not over-bake the cookies. Yes, they will feel soft and they might even look under cooked, but that is exactly as they should be. Make sure to let your cookies cool down! Do not touch them while they're in the oven and do not touch them for at least 10 minutes after you've removed them from the oven. When your 10 minutes are done, very carefully transfer them to a wire rack to continue cooling . This extra time is crucial to give your cookies crunchy edges. At a minimum, leave them for 5 minutes on the cooling rack, but 10 is better."]]},"9149196":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350℉/176℃ and line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Combine the mashed banana, pumpkin puree, maple syrup and vanilla in a large bowl. Then add the dry ingredients (flour, spices, baking powder) and stir until combined."],[null,"Use a cookie scoop to scoop balls of the pumpkin cookie dough onto your parchment-lined tray. You should get around 25 cookies. (You may keep the balls round, or press them down if preferred. They won't spread, but taste fluffier when left round.)"],[null,"Bake the cookies for 14-16 minutes, until lightly golden and firm to the touch, and then remove from the oven."],[null,"Let the cookies cool for a few minutes before enjoying, or continue cooling on a wire rack before storing."]],"h":[[null,"Weigh your flour for the best results . Scooping into a measuring cup can compact the flour and you may end up with more than needed."],[null,"Use active baking powder . Baking powder that's been open in the pantry for several months may lose its effectiveness."],[null,"Use very ripe bananas for the best flavour and natural sweetness. The skins should be spotted brown"]]},"6337610":{"s":[[null,"Add almonds to a dry sauté pan over medium-high heat and sauté until lightly toasted. Set aside to cool."],[null,"Add almond milk, cocoa powder, low- or no-calorie sweetener, and coconut extract to a blender and blend until incorporated and slightly foamy."],[null,"Add hot chocolate mixture to a saucepan over medium heat and bring to a simmer."],[null,"Add one cup of hot chocolate to a coffee mug, top with 2 Tbsp whipped topping and sprinkle with 1 Tbsp cooled, toasted almonds."],[null,"Repeat for three remaining coffee mugs."]],"h":[]},"6192603":{"s":[[null,"Bring the almonds, milk, and lemon zest to a boil in a medium saucepan over medium heat. Cook for 5 minutes, then remove from the heat."],[null,"Transfer the almond mixture to a blender. Remove the middle spout from the lid, place a towel over the hole, and puree the almond mixture until smooth."],[null,"Stir in the agave nectar, and add the ice cubes. Process until smooth, and whip until frothy. Chill in clear glasses for an hour or until cold, then serve."]],"h":[]},"6711007":{"s":[[null,"In a large pot, add the almond milk, and bring to a boil over high heat. Reduce heat to medium-low and add the pearls, stirring continuously to keep them separate. Add the palm sugar and salt and continue to cook until the pearls become fully transparent, about 30 minutes."],[null,"Turn off the heat, and stir in the bananas and corn. Serve garnished with toasted sesame seeds."]],"h":[]},"3251":{"s":[[null,"Combine first 4 ingredients into a small sauce pan over medium heat."],[null,"Bring to a soft boil while stirring with a whisk."],[null,"Transfer to a coffee mug and sprinkle with nutmeg."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute almond milk with coconut milk beverage if preferred."],[null,"Replace sugar with desired substitute for a lower carbohydrate drink."],[null,"Recipe not recommended if you are on a low calcium diet. Many milk alternatives are high in calcium."]]},"7294670":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 150°C/gas mark 2 and use the oil to grease a large baking sheet."],[null,"In a bowl, mix together the oats, seeds and almonds. Set aside."],[null,"Lightly beat the egg white with the sweetener, if using, until frothy. Add the oats, seeds and nuts mixture and jumble together to ensure all are well coated."],[null,"Spread evenly onto the baking sheet and bake for 15 minutes."],[null,"Add the apricots, mix together well on the tray and bake for a further 8-10 minutes."],[null,"Leave the granola on the baking sheet until it cools."]],"h":[[null,"You could make this recipe with raisins or prunes instead of apricots."],[null,"If stored in an airtight container, the granola will keep for at least two weeks."],[null,"Serve with milk and fresh berries, or a chopped apple. You could also top this dish with a tablespoon of unsweetened plain yoghurt."],[null,"Try adding different seeds such as sunflower. You can also experiment with different nuts, such as walnuts or crushed brazil nuts in place of almonds."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"3432":{"s":[[null,"Trim the celery rib ends."],[null,"Fill each celery rib with 1 tablespoon of whipped cream cheese."],[null,"Cut each celery rib into 3 pieces."],[null,"Top each piece with 1 almond and 2 dried cranberries."],[null,"Cover and refrigerate until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Place cream cheese in a plastic bag, snip the corner and pipe onto the celery log."],[null,"Use any flavor of whipped cream cheese."],[null,"Refrigerate leftover snacks for 2-3 days."],[null,"Double or triple the recipe for serving at parties and social events."]]},"6162321":{"s":[],"h":[]},"9858921":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F (218 C) convection roast. If you do not have a convection oven, add a few minutes of cooking time. Line a large baking sheet with parchment paper and set it aside."],[null,"Peel your potatoes (if desired) and cut them into one-inch wedges. Place them in a mixing bowl, then add the oil (or broth) and salt and mix well to evenly coat them. Then arrange the potatoes in a single layer on your baking sheet. Roast on the bottom rack of your oven for 25 minutes. Then flip the potatoes and continue cooking for another 10-15 minutes, until the potatoes are golden brown and crispy."],[null,"While the potatoes are cooking, prepare your cheese sauce and toppings."],[null,"Then serve the potatoes in deep dishes, cover in the cheese sauce and sprinkle with the veggie toppings. Enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Make sure your potatoes are very crispy before removing them from the oven so they stand up well and don’t get soggy from the sauce. For oil free and less fat, use vegetable stock to toss with your potatoes, instead of oil. Make sure to leave a little extra room in between your potatoes so they don’t stick to one another, and crisp up nicely. For added flavour , toss a little garlic powder, crushed rosemary, and other spices you like to your potato wedges before baking. If you have a high-speed blender , the cheese sauce will warm itself up during blending. If not , transfer it to a small saucepan once smooth to keep warm over low to medium heat while you wait for the potatoes to finish baking. Keep an eye on your pan, you want the sauce warm, not bubbling. Whisk occasionally. Jazz up your healthy poutine with a dollop of cashew cream and pecan “bacon” topping. If you want traditional-style poutine with hot gravy and cheese curds, check out this vegan poutine , instead. Nutritional information is for one-third of the recipe including one-third of my nut-free cheese sauce . If you use another sauce, the info will vary."]]},"2622":{"s":[[null,"Cut the cauliflower into pieces and rinse with water."],[null,"Place the cauliflower pieces in a microwave safe dish, cover and cook on high for 8 to 10 minutes or until soft."],[null,"Drain off moisture from the cooked cauliflower."],[null,"Carefully place the hot cauliflower in a blender and blend until smooth."],[null,"Add the cream cheese, garlic and pepper. Blend to combine ingredients."],[null,"Remove mixture from the blender and serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"One medium head cauliflower yields 6 cups."],[null,"Garlic powder may be substituted for the minced garlic."],[null,"Since cauliflower is bland like potatoes, this recipe tastes similar to mashed potatoes. The potassium content is 100 mg lower per serving."],[null,"To reduce fat content, use light cream cheese. Protein, sodium, potassium and phosphorus content will be slightly higher."]]},"6489390":{"s":[[null,"Add the tomatoes, bell pepper, onion, jalapeño, and cilantro to a medium bowl. Add the lime juice, olive oil, salt, and black pepper. Toss to evenly coat."],[null,"Using an immersion blender, blend until almost smooth, leaving some chunks in the salsa."]],"h":[]},"5746836":{"s":[[null,"Wash sago (2-3 times) and soak for 6-7 hours or overnight. Once soaked, drain and rinse again."],[null,"Boil potatoes for 10 minutes, drain and grate them. Mix sago with grated potatoes and set aside."],[null,"To the mixture add ginger, garlic, turmeric and chilli powder (optional)."],[null,"Add 1 tsp arrowroot/cornflour and mix all of it well to form a soft dough."],[null,"Grease hand with oil and prepare ball-sized tikki (patty)."],[null,"Shallow fry in hot oil. Roast on low flame until it turns golden brown."],[null,"Flip over and cook on both sides."]],"h":[]},"4825624":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F degrees (conventional oven)."],[null,"Over medium-high heat sauté vegetables in the olive oil for 5 minutes, stirring frequently."],[null,"In a small dish, combine dried spices and add them to the vegetables for the last minute of frying."],[null,"In a bowl, mix together meat, egg, vinegar, applesauce, broth and pasta."],[null,"Add the vegetables to the meat mixture and combine well."],[null,"Lightly coat a 9 × 5 inch loaf pan with cooking spray. Put the meat mixture into the pan and tap it down evenly."],[null,"Bake in oven for 1 hour."]],"h":[[null,"Cold meat loaf is delicious on sandwiches!"]]},"1002955":{"s":[[null,"Finely chop onions and cilantro. Crush garlic."],[null,"Cut cheese into small pieces."],[null,"Peel potatoes and cut into cubes. Cover potatoes completely with water and bring to a boil. Drain and repeat the process. Set potatoes aside."],[null,"Bring broth to a boil with onions and garlic."],[null,"Stir in potatoes, milk and cheese."],[null,"When cheese has melted, add cilantro."],[null,"After turning off the heat, add 4 eggs to the soup one at a time, taking care not to break the yolks."]],"h":[[null,"Look for low-potassium chicken broth that does not contain potassium chloride."],[null,"Not recommended if phosphorus is not under control."]]},"7262970":{"s":[[null,"Place the quinoa with 300ml of water in a pan. Bring to the boil and simmer for 10–15 minutes until all the water is absorbed. Set aside."],[null,"Heat the oil in a medium saucepan and fry the onion for 3–4 minutes until it begins to soften."],[null,"Add the celery, courgette and potato, and continue to fry for 5–6 minutes."],[null,"Then add the chilli, cumin and coriander, and fry for a further minute."],[null,"Add the tomatoes and oregano, season well with black pepper and simmer for 10–15 minutes, until the vegetables are tender."],[null,"Stir through the quinoa and walnuts."]],"h":[[null,"Quinoa (pronounced keen-wa) is a wholegrain nutritionally, but it is actually a seed. It's naturally gluten-free and rich in protein. Use it in place of rice or couscous to make pilafs and salads."],[null,"You could add all sorts of vegetables such as peppers, mushrooms, peas or sweetcorn."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"2396":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"In a mixing bowl mix the cake mix, vanilla and soda. If too stiff or not completely mixed add more soda a spoonful at a time just until mixed."],[null,"Fold in the coconut."],[null,"Place parchment paper on a cookie sheet. Drop a spoonful of the cookie mixture on sheet placing 2″ apart. Bake for 10 minutes until light brown on bottom."],[null,"Remove cookies from baking sheet and cool on a cooling rack."]],"h":[[null,"Use a new sheet of parchment paper for each new set of cookies."],[null,"Place in zip top bag or sealed container to store."],[null,"Can use other soda flavors: Cherry, Strawberry, Cranberry, etc. Avoid sodas with phosphate additives."]]},"55203":{"s":[[null,"Defrost whipped topping and sherbet."],[null,"Cut the cake horizontally in the middle to create a top and bottom section of the cake."],[null,"Spread sherbet generously across bottom half of cake, ~ 4-5 inches thick. Place top of cake on the sherbet."],[null,"Frost all the cake with whipped topping. Place in freezer for 4-6 hours. Remove from freezer when ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Look for store-bought angel food cake with no or minimal phosphorus additives in the ingredient list."],[null,"May use regular whipped topping, but it will increase the added sugar by ~20 grams or more."],[null,"This dessert is an occasional treat, would not be appropriate for people with diabetes"],[null,"May try different flavors of sherbet if desired."]]},"3927":{"s":[[null,"Bake angel food cake according to package directions. Cool to room temperature."],[null,"Beat whipped cream cheese and strawberry preserves until smooth. Fold in whipped topping."],[null,"Slice angel food cake into three, even horizontal layers."],[null,"Spread 1/3 of the cream cheese mixture between layers and reassemble, spreading the remaining 1/3 cream cheese mixture on top."],[null,"Keep refrigerated until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"After baking invert angel food cake on a glass bottle to prevent cake from falling."],[null,"Lower fat ingredients such as cream cheese, are often higher in sodium than the regular fat product. Compare labels and make the best selection for your individual diet."],[null,"If Reddi-Wip® is a pressurized dessert whipped topping found in the dairy section in most grocery stores. If unavailable substitute any whipped topping that does not contain phosphate additives."]]},"3101":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400° F. Grease a 12-cup muffin pan or line with paper liners."],[null,"In a medium bowl lightly beat the eggs. Beat in the milk, oil, brown sugar and corn syrup."],[null,"In a large bowl stir together the flour, baking powder, ginger, and cinnamon. Make a well in the center of the dry ingredients and pour in the liquid ingredients. Stir gently until just combined: do not over mix."],[null,"Spoon the batter into the prepared muffin pan. Bake in the preheated oven for about 20 minutes, until golden brown and firm to the touch."],[null,"Remove from oven and let the muffins cool in the pan for 5 minutes. Serve warm with butter or cream cheese."]],"h":[[null,"Freeze leftover muffins for a quick snack later. Reheat in microwave for 30-45 seconds."],[null,"Muffins contain baking powder that contributes to phosphorus content. Ask your dietitian if you need to take a phosphate binder when muffins are eaten as a snack."]]},"2926":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F. Line a large cookie sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Mix first five dry ingredients in a large bowl and stir well."],[null,"Place eggs, oil, and extract in a small bowl and beat until frothy, either by hand with a whisk or with an electric mixer for about 30 seconds."],[null,"Pour liquid mixture into dry ingredients. Mix with a wooden spoon until dough is mixed. Dough will be crumbly."],[null,"Place dough on a lightly floured board. Shape into a ball and knead several times. Cut ball in half."],[null,"Roll each half into a log approximately 10 inches long. Flatten top slightly."],[null,"Place dough on a cookie sheet and bake until lightly golden, approximately 15 to 20 minutes."],[null,"Remove from oven. Let cool for 10 minutes. Use a serrated knife and slice at approximately 2/3-inch intervals to get 16 biscotti per half of dough."],[null,"Place sliced biscotti back on cookie sheet with cut side up and bake until lightly golden, approximately 5 minutes. Remove from oven, turn biscotti over and bake 5 minutes. Remove from oven and cool on a rack."]],"h":[[null,"Store up to 2 weeks in an airtight container or freeze."],[null,"Biscotti is twice baked to produce a hard cookie for dipping in coffee, tea or favorite beverages."],[null,"Traditional biscotti are made with just anise seed; however, today, there are many “gourmet” versions with various dried fruits and/or nuts. Keep in mind that nuts are high in phosphorus and potassium; however, a reduced amount can be added."],[null,"For cranberry-orange-pistachio biscotti, omit the anise and add 1 cup dried cranberries and 1/4 cup finely chopped unsalted pistachios."],[null,"For blueberry biscotti, omit the anise seed and orange rind, substitute 2 teaspoons vanilla extract for the orange extract and add 3/4 cup dried blueberries."]]},"6075896":{"s":[[null,"Soak figs and dates, separately, in bowls of hot water (use just enough water to cover the fruit) for 15–20 minutes. Drain water and grind figs and dates together using a food processor to form a smooth paste. Add 1 Tbsp / 15 mL water to reach the right consistency."],[null,"Combine sunflower oil and ghee in a small bowl, then add mixture to a heavy-bottomed pan over medium heat. Add the fig and date purée. Cook, stirring frequently, until mixture dries out, about 15 minutes."],[null,"Stir in almonds, cashews, pistachios, and cardamom seeds and mix well to combine. Continue cooking over medium-low heat, stirring frequently, for another 10 minutes, or until mixture starts to pull away from the sides of the pan."],[null,"Transfer mixture to a greased plate or pan and press down to form the barfi. Set aside to cool completely. Once cool, cut into squares or diamonds and serve."]],"h":[]},"4284866":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375°F (conventional oven) or 350°F (convection)."],[null,"In a food processor or with a grater, shred carrots and apples. Mix in a large bowl with cranberries and pineapple, set aside."],[null,"In a small cup mix the baking soda into the sour cream."],[null,"Prepare flour mixture: sift flour with spices into the bowl with grated mixture and stir."],[null,"Prepare egg mixture: in a medium bowl beat eggs with sugar and vanilla, add oil and whisk together for 1 minute. Add baking soda and sour cream mixture and blend well."],[null,"Pour egg mixture into flour mixture and stir until just combined. DO NOT OVER STIR."],[null,"Spoon batter into greased or lined standard muffin tins (about 1/3 cup), filling to the top."],[null,"Bake for 20–25 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Great for breakfast and as a snack on the go!"],[null,"Wrap muffins individually after they have cooled off and put them in the freezer."]]},"7832746":{"s":[[null,"Prepare the muesli the night before. Put the oats into a lidded container. Add the yogurt, grated apple, sunflower and pumpkin seeds, dried cranberries and 150ml water. Stir well to combine. Cover, and refrigerate overnight."],[null,"The next morning, stir the muesli well. If it’s too thick, add a little more water until it reaches your preferred consistency."],[null,"Stir 2tsp of the chia seeds into your muesli, then divide between bowls. Scatter over the remaining chia seeds and the diced apple, then serve."]],"h":[[null,"Any combination of fruit and seeds in this recipe. You could try raspberries, bananas, chia seeds or flaxseeds."]]},"6272046":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, combine broccoli slaw mix, julienned apples, raisins, and sunflower seeds."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together plain Greek yogurt, apple cider vinegar, salt, and pepper."],[null,"Pour the dressing over the slaw mixture."],[null,"Toss the slaw gently to ensure even coating."],[null,"Allow the slaw to sit in the refrigerator for 15 minutes to let the flavors meld."]],"h":[]},"7013544":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200°C/gas 6."],[null,"Sift the flour into a bowl, add the artifical sweetener, baking powder and cinnamon into the flour and mix."],[null,"Make a well in the middle of the dry ingredients and add the eggs and the milk. Whisk and add in the melted butter."],[null,"Peel and core the apples and remove the seeds. Cut them into large slices. Add the apple slices to the mixture and fold in gently."],[null,"Grease a cake tin (around 23cm in diameter) with some vegetable oil. Pour the mixture into the tin and bake in the oven for 35 minutes."],[null,"Turn out onto a cooling rack. Leave to cool and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Start by preparing the batter, in order to leave it aside while you peel the apples."],[null,"You can also replace the apples with pears, and the cinnamon with ground ginger or mixed spice."]]},"5234182":{"s":[[null,"Place the apples and cinnamon into a blender."],[null,"Pour the Renastep into the blender with the apples and cinnamon and blend until smooth."],[null,"Serve and enjoy!"]],"h":[["Renastep note","Renastep is a Food for Special Medical Purposes and must be used under medical supervision. Renastep is a ready to use feed for the dietary management of kidney disease from 3 years of age onwards. Renastep contains milk and fish. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information. This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutrimen dietary analysis software."]]},"7046954":{"s":[[null,"Core and roughly chop the apples, then add them to a pan with a dash of water. Add the cranberry sauce and dried cranberries."],[null,"Gently heat through, stirring regularly for 5–6 minutes until the apples have softened."]],"h":[[null,"Store in the fridge."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Freeze in portions then defrost and serve cold or warm."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"6986660":{"s":[[null,"Coat the apples with 2 tbsp lemon juice and set aside. Place the carrot slices and mixed greens on a platter. Top with the onion and set aside."],[null,"Whisk together the orange juice, remaining 2 tbsp lemon juice, honey and mustard. Slowly add the oil in a thin stream, whisking constantly."],[null,"Add the apples to the salad. Top with walnuts and cheese. Drizzle on the vinaigrette."]],"h":[]},"7456468":{"s":[[null,"Simply place all the ingredients in a food processor/blender and blend until smooth."],[null,"Serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"Leave your muesli to soak overnight, then add the yogurt and apple before blending."],[null,"This smoothie is also very tasty with pear instead of apple."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6674650":{"s":[[null,"Cut the apple into 8 wedges and remove the core."],[null,"Spread about 3/4 tsp of peanut butter on each apple wedge."]],"h":[]},"7681544":{"s":[[null,"Mix the wholemeal and plain flour with the sugar and yeast. Make a well in the middle."],[null,"Add the oil, egg and half the milk. Mix well, gradually adding the rest of the milk until it comes together as a dough."],[null,"Turn out the dough onto a floured surface and knead for five minutes until it becomes elastic. Place into an oiled bowl, cover with cling film and leave in a warm place for 1 hour to double in size."],[null,"Meanwhile, make the filling: add the apples to a pan with the water, cover and cook for 10 minutes over a low to medium heat, mashing with a fork occasionally until they are a soft pulp. Remove from the heat and add the cinnamon, sweetener and raisins. Mix well, cover and leave to cool."],[null,"‘Knock back’ the dough by shaping to its original size, then turn out onto a lightly floured surface. Roll out into a rectangle, ½cm thick (approximately 48x30cm)."],[null,"Spread the apple/raisin mixture over the dough, leaving a 2–3cm margin along the longest top edge."],[null,"Tightly roll the dough into a cylinder with the seam on the bottom, then cut into 16 pieces approximately 3cm thick."],[null,"Place the buns onto a lightly oiled baking sheet, cover with a tea towel and leave to rise for another 30 minutes. Meanwhile, preheat the oven to 180°C /gas 4."],[null,"Brush the buns with the milk and bake for 20–25 minutes until risen and golden. Remove from the oven, brush with honey and allow to cool."]],"h":[[null,"You could use sultanas, currants or a mixture of dried fruit."],[null,"Try adding some grated lemon or orange zest to the filling or use mixed spice in place of cinnamon."]]},"7616762":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4 and lightly grease a large baking sheet with the rapeseed oil."],[null,"In a bowl, mix the flour, baking powder and cinnamon together."],[null,"In another bowl, mash the banana with a fork, add the egg and beat well. Mix in the sugar, oil, vanilla extract and 50ml water."],[null,"Gradually fold the dry ingredients into the banana and egg mixture, then fold in the sultanas and apple."],[null,"Pile the mixture into 12 small irregular heaps on the greased baking sheet, using a fork to create lots of little spikes."],[null,"Bake for 18-22 minutes then remove from the oven and allow to cool on a wire rack."]],"h":[[null,"These are best eaten when still warm but can be stored in an airtight container for 2-3 days."],[null,"You could add other spices – try ground mixed spice, ginger, nutmeg or cardamom in place of the cinnamon."],[null,"Adding banana means you use less sugar and fat, whilst boosting the nutrients."],[null,"Freeze in freezer bags, wrapped in foil or greaseproof paper, for up to three months."]]},"3817119":{"s":[[null,"Pre-heat the oven to 180°C / 160°C fan / gas mark 4. Lightly oil an oven-proof dish. Put the oats and baking powder into a blender and whizz until ground."],[null,"Add in banana, milk, egg, one tablespoon of the syrup, vanilla essence and cinnamon into the blender and blend until smooth and fully combined. Pour into the oven dish."],[null,"Toss the sliced apple with the remaining tablespoon of syrup and arrange over the top of the dish. Bake for 25 minutes."],[null,"Remove from the oven and leave to cool for a few moments. Serve into six portions with a spoonful of yoghurt on the top and a sprinkle of toasted coconut and the optional fruit if desired."]],"h":[["Chef's note","This recipe is very quick to prepare. It could be a dessert or even eaten as breakfast on a special occasion."],["Carbohydrate","The oats and syrup are the main sources of carbohydrate in this dessert and the value has been provided for those who have been trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","This dessert is low in potassium, therefore suitable on special occasions for those advised to follow a low potassium diet.\nThis recipe is high in phosphate, due to the oats and baking powder. If you have been advised to follow a low phosphate diet then may be best to limit the frequency you cook this recipe. If you have been prescribed a phosphate binder ensure you take them with this dish."],["Protein","This recipe is low in protein which makes it suitable for those advised to eat less protein."],["Gluten free","Use gluten-free oats."],["Healthier option","You could consider using a low fat or reduced fat yogurt or a plant-based alternative such as oat or soya yogurt. You may also wish to serve with some stewed fruit, such as apple and pears, or tinned fruit such as peaches and pears, as suggested."],["Storage","Keep in the fridge for up to three days and reheat before serving."]]},"3143":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350° F."],[null,"Peel and chop the apples."],[null,"Cream together 1/2 cup of the butter and the granulated sugar or granulated sugar substitute."],[null,"Add the sour cream, vanilla, baking soda, salt and flour. Stir to mix; add the chopped apples."],[null,"Pour the batter into a greased 9” x 13” baking pan."],[null,"In a small bowl, crumble 2 tablespoons of softened butter, the brown sugar and cinnamon together. Sprinkle over top of the batter."],[null,"Bake for 35 to 40 minutes. Let cool completely."],[null,"To make icing, combine 2 tablespoons melted butter, milk (or milk substitute) and powdered sugar. Drizzle over top and cut dessert into 18 bars."]],"h":[[null,"1 medium apple yields 1 cup chopped apples."],[null,"People with diabetes can replace the granulated sugar with a granular sugar substitute and omit the icing which will lower the carbohydrate content to 19 grams per serving (1 carbohydrate choice). Use caution with portion sizes."]]},"2857":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Mix ingredients in a small roasting pan."],[null,"Bake until brown and thickened (approximately 2 hours), stirring occasionally during baking."],[null,"Pour into a sterile container and refrigerate or freeze for later use."]],"h":[[null,"Use as a spread on toast or bagels."]]},"1972":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Spray tube pan with non-stick cooking spray."],[null,"Peel, core and cut apples into slices or chunks."],[null,"Combine cinnamon and 1/3 cup sugar. Mix in apple and set aside."],[null,"Combine remaining ingredients in a bowl and beat with an electric mixer until smooth."],[null,"Layer half the cake batter, then the apple, then remaining cake batter in prepared tube pan."],[null,"Bake for 75 minutes until golden brown or toothpick inserted into the center comes out clean."]],"h":[[null,"1 medium apple yields approximately 1 cup peeled and cored."],[null,"Cake batter will be thick. Spread with a spatula to coat apples with top layer of batter."],[null,"This high calorie dessert is a great choice for packing in extra calories. Not recommended for people with diabetes due to the high carbohydrate content."]]},"2066":{"s":[[null,"Defrost dessert topping."],[null,"Core and cut apples into small pieces. Cut caramel bars into small pieces."],[null,"Combine apple pieces and caramel bar pieces in a bowl."],[null,"Fold in dessert topping. Chill in the refrigerator for 1 hour before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Each Balance® Gold Bar weighs 1.76-ounces."],[null,"Look for a frozen dessert topping without phosphate additives."]]},"7809105":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/ gas mark 4. Add the apples to a saucepan with 100ml of apple juice and simmer until soft (4-5 minutes). Leaving the juice behind, place the apples in a bowl."],[null,"Add the cinnamon to the pan with the remaining 100ml of apple juice and gently melt, adding a little more juice if needed. Allow to cool, you should end up with around 100ml of syrup."],[null,"Rub the sunflower oil around a small pudding basin or ovenproof dish. Dip the bread in the apple syrup and use it to line the basin. Make sure there are no gaps."],[null,"Stir the egg yolk into the apple, then put the mixture into the bread-lined bowl."],[null,"Finally, top with more syrup-soaked bread and spoon on any remaining liquid. Bake for 20 minutes. Check after 15 minutes and if the top is very brown at the edges, place a piece of foil over it for the last 5 minutes."],[null,"Allow to stand for a few minutes, loosen the edges with a knife and carefully turn out onto a serving plate."]],"h":[[null,"Best served straight after cooking."],[null,"Try serving with a little low-fat yogurt or half-fat crème fraiche."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"2918":{"s":[[null,"Dice potatoes into 1/2-inch cubes and soak or double-boil to reduce potassium if you are on a low potassium diet. (See details in helpful hints)."],[null,"Mix together 3 tablespoons of the flour, black pepper and thyme."],[null,"Coat beef with flour mixture."],[null,"In a skillet heat oil and brown beef pieces. Set aside."],[null,"Slice carrots, dice onion, celery and peeled apple."],[null,"In slow cooker, layer ingredients as follows: carrots, boiled potatoes, onions, celery, browned beef and diced apple."],[null,"Mix together apple cider, 1 cup water and vinegar."],[null,"Pour over ingredients in slow cooker and cook on low setting for 8 to 10 hours."],[null,"Before serving, turn slow cooker on high. Mix remaining 4 tablespoons flour with 1/2 cup water. Stir into slow cooker to thicken stew."]],"h":[[null,"Potatoes are very high in potassium but you can remove part of the potassium by using one of these methods:"],[null,"Double cook method: Peel and dice potatoes. Place in a large pot of water and bring to a boil. Drain the water and add fresh water to the pot. Bring to a boil, cook for 10 minutes then drain and set aside."],[null,"Leaching method: Peel and dice potatoes. Place in a large pot of warm tap water and soak for 2 to 4 hours. Drain and set aside."],[null,"If you are not on a potassium restricted diet you can skip the above step."]]},"6144571":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 350 degrees F. Lightly coat 2 standard-sized muffin pans with nonstick cooking spray."],[null,"Boil the apple cider in a saucepan over medium heat until it's reduced by half, leaving about 3/4 cup. Set aside to cool."],[null,"In a medium bowl, whisk together the whole wheat flour, baking powder, baking soda, 1 tsp of the ground cinnamon, ground nutmeg, and salt."],[null,"In a separate bowl, mix the unsweetened applesauce, sugar substitute, eggs, apple cider, avocado oil, and vanilla extract together."],[null,"Gradually stir the dry ingredients into the wet ingredients until just combined. Do not overmix. Spoon the batter into each cavity, filling about two-thirds full."],[null,"Bake in the preheated oven for 15 to 18 minutes, or until a toothpick comes out clean."],[null,"In a small bowl, stir together the granulated sugar and ½ tsp of ground cinnamon to create the cinnamon sugar."],[null,"While the muffins are cooling in the pan, lightly dust the cinnamon sugar over the tops."],[null,"Let the dusted muffins cool in the pan before transferring them to a wire rack to cool completely."]],"h":[]},"2366":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350° F. Set butter out to soften. Grease a 9 x 5-inch loaf pan. Peel and finely chop the apple."],[null,"Mix the brown sugar and cinnamon in a bowl; set aside."],[null,"In a stand mixer, combine the granulated sugar and butter until smooth."],[null,"Add the eggs and vanilla and continue to beat on medium speed until combined."],[null,"Add the flour and baking powder; continue to mix until combined. Add the milk and blend into the batter."],[null,"Pour half of the prepared batter into the loaf pan then top with half of the chopped apples and half of the cinnamon and sugar mixture. Pour on the remaining batter. Add the remaining apples, pat down lightly into the batter with the back of a spoon. Top with the remaining cinnamon and sugar mixture and again, pat down lightly."],[null,"Bake for 45 to 55 minutes or until a toothpick inserted in middle of the loaf comes out clean. Allow to cool for 10 minutes before transferring from the loaf pan to a cooling rack."],[null,"Cut the cooled loaf into twelve 3/4-inch slices."]],"h":[[null,"Reduce the carbohydrate to 26 grams and calories to 197 per slice by substituting a sugar/sugar substitute baking blends for the brown and granulated sugars."]]},"3323":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375° F."],[null,"Peel, core and shred apples."],[null,"Spray an 8 x 8-inch baking dish with cooking spray."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine the hot water and farfel."],[null,"Add the sugar, apples and cinnamon."],[null,"Beat egg whites to a stiff peak. Fold in the egg whites."],[null,"Add drained pineapple chunks and stir."],[null,"Pour mixture into the prepared baking dish and dust the top with more cinnamon."],[null,"Bake for 45 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Farfel is coarsely crumbled unsalted crackers."]]},"2976":{"s":[[null,"Cut unpeeled apple into thin slices."],[null,"Add all ingredients to a pitcher."],[null,"Refrigerator overnight before serving."]],"h":[[null,"If you are on limited fluids, adjust the portion size to meet your needs."],[null,"After flavors develop you can pour into ice cube trays to make flavored ice."]]},"3557":{"s":[[null,"Dice the bread and cream cheese into cubes. Peel and dice the apples. Melt the butter."],[null,"Coat a 9″ x 13″ baking dish with nonstick cooking spray. Arrange 1/2 of the cubed bread in the bottom of the dish. Sprinkle the cream cheese cubes evenly over the bread and top with the apples. Sprinkle cinnamon over the apples and top with remaining bread."],[null,"In a large bowl, beat the eggs with the half & half creamer, almond milk, melted butter and pancake syrup. Pour the mixture over the bread. Cover baking dish with plastic wrap and press down so that all the pieces are soaked. Refrigerate at least 2 hours or overnight"],[null,"Preheat oven to 325° F."],[null,"Bake the strata for 50 minutes, then let stand 10 minutes before serving. Cut evenly into squares for 12 servings."],[null,"Top with pancake syrup, sugar-free syrup, jam or cinnamon/raspberry applesauce, if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Replace eggs with 2 cups low cholesterol egg product to reduce cholesterol to 37 mg per serving."],[null,"Lower carbohydrate content by substituting sugar-free syrup if you have diabetes."],[null,"Use your favorite milk substitute if you do not like almond milk. Some brands of half & half contain phosphate additives. Always check the ingredient list and avoid products with phosphate additives."],[null,"Portions are generous—may be divided into smaller servings for a larger crowd."]]},"2598":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 275° F. Line 2 large baking sheets with parchment paper."],[null,"Combine dry ingredients in a large bowl."],[null,"Combine wet ingredients in a small bowl."],[null,"Pour wet ingredients into dry ingredients bowl. Mix very well to coat dry ingredients."],[null,"Divide mixture onto the 2 baking sheets."],[null,"Bake for 50 minutes to 1 hour, changing pan position (move pan on top rack to bottom rack) halfway through baking."]],"h":[[null,"Instant oats contain added salt. Old fashioned rolled oats are preferable as they are lower in sodium."],[null,"Packaged apple chips vary in size. Select the brand closest to 3.4 ounces."],[null,"Store granola in an airtight container. Enjoy with Maple Cinnamon Roasted Pears, unenriched almond or rice milk, cottage cheese or yogurt."],[null,"For a gluten-free version be sure to use oats and puffed rice cereal that indicates gluten-free on the label."]]},"6239417":{"s":[[null,"In a medium-sized saucepan, combine quinoa, almond milk, diced apples, maple syrup, ground cinnamon, ground nutmeg, and salt."],[null,"Bring the mixture to a boil, then reduce the heat to low, cover, and simmer for 15–20 minutes or until the quinoa is cooked and the porridge has thickened."],[null,"Stir the porridge occasionally during cooking to prevent sticking."],[null,"Once cooked, remove from heat and let it sit, covered, for an additional 5 minutes."],[null,"Fluff the quinoa with a fork and adjust sweetness if necessary."],[null,"Serve the porridge in bowls, topped with chopped nuts if desired."]],"h":[]},"3447":{"s":[[null,"Peel and cube the apple. Heat a large pan over medium heat."],[null,"Add 1/2 tablespoon of the butter to the pan and add apples. Stir frequently for about 2 minutes. Add 1/2 tablespoon of the brown sugar and 1/4 teaspoon of the cinnamon to apple."],[null,"Cover apples in pan and let soften for about 5 minutes. Remove cover and remove from heat."],[null,"Combine egg white and water in a large bowl. Add maple syrup, remaining butter and remaining 1/4 cup of brown sugar and whisk together."],[null,"Add flour, baking soda and remaining 3/4 teaspoon cinnamon. Stir to combine."],[null,"Preheat 2 slot waffle maker and spray with non-stick cooking spray if needed. Add half of the apples into the pan to waffle batter and add half the batter into each well of the waffle iron. Let cook about 2-3 minutes."],[null,"Use a spatula to remove waffles from the iron. Repeat with remaining batter. You should have 4 waffles in total. Place 2 waffles on a plate and top with half of the remaining apples. Refrigerate remaining waffles and reheat the next day."]],"h":[[null,"You may also sprinkle a bit of powdered sugar over the top if desired."],[null,"The apples give this waffle a sweet topping. If adding more maple syrup over the top, remember to account for the extra sugar or calories depending on how much is added."]]},"4338478":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F (conventional oven)."],[null,"In a large bowl, mix all ingredients for the filling together. Transfer to a non-stick 9-inch square baking pan or to eight 4-ounce ramekins."],[null,"In a small bowl, sift together the dry ingredients for the topping. Combine the lemon juice and the milk and add to the dry ingredients. Spoon topping over the apple cranberry filling."],[null,"Bake for approximately 45 minutes or until fruit bubbles and topping turns golden brown. (Bake for 30 minutes if you use ramekins)."],[null,"To make the cream, stir maple syrup into whipped cream. Add cream to each serving of cobbler. 4/10/17 5:57 PM"]],"h":[[null,"* If you prefer the cobbler to be more firm, use another apple variety such as Granny Smith, Cortland or Empire."],["Cranberries","Cranberries are considered a staple around the holiday season, but really can be enjoyed year round. For those with chronic kidney disease, many fruits contain too much potassium to be consumed on a daily basis. Cranberries are very low in potassium and you can eat them every day if desired as one cup contains only 80 milligrams of potassium. Cranberries are a good source of vitamin C and fiber. Very few fruits or vegetables can beat the disease fighting antioxidant content of these small fruits. To enjoy the benefits of these power packed berries, have cranberries frequently. They are available fresh, frozen and dried and can be added to the diet in a variety of ways. Add them to your hot or cold cereal. Enjoy a small glass of cranberry juice. For extra color and flavor, add them to your favorite baked goods such as muffins, yeast breads and cookies. You can also use them in poultry recipes for a delicious twist."]]},"2165":{"s":[[null,"Shred cabbage and chop apple into small pieces. Grate onion."],[null,"In a large bowl mix cabbage, apple, onion, cranberries and almonds."],[null,"In a small bowl or jar combine remaining ingredients to make celery seed dressing; mix vigorously."],[null,"Pour over slaw and toss."]],"h":[[null,"The dressing is best when made ahead and chilled."],[null,"Celery seed dressing is great with any green salad."],[null,"Slaw keeps in the refrigerator for up to 1 week."],[null,"To reduce carbohydrate to 8 grams and 1/2 carbohydrate choice you can substitute low calorie sweetener and reduce cranberries to 1/4 cup."]]},"1839":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Peel, core and slice apples."],[null,"Melt butter, pour over apples and toss to coat. Pour into an 8 x 8-inch baking dish."],[null,"Sprinkle cinnamon and brown sugar over apples and stir."],[null,"Bake 30 minutes or until apples are tender."],[null,"Prepare Basic Crepes recipe on DaVita.com."],[null,"Place crepe on plate, browned side down."],[null,"Spoon 1/4-cup apple mixture onto crepe."],[null,"Roll crepe and top with a tablespoon of whipped topping."]],"h":[[null,"The carbohydrate count is 15 g when made with brown sugar."],[null,"3 large apples yields approximately 4 cups after sliced and peeled."]]},"1927":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Spray a 9 x 9-inch pan with cooking spray."],[null,"Peel, core and slice apples."],[null,"Combine 1/2 cup granulated sugar, 3 tablespoons flour and 1/2 teaspoon cinnamon. Add sliced apples and toss to coat."],[null,"Pour apple mixture into prepared pan."],[null,"In a medium bowl, mix oatmeal, remaining flour, brown sugar, remaining cinnamon, baking soda and baking powder. Cut butter into this mixture with a pastry blender or a fork."],[null,"Pour topping over apples and bake for 1 hour."]],"h":[[null,"Make this dessert diabetes-friendly. Substitute Splenda® granular for white sugar and Splenda® brown sugar blend for brown sugar with to reduce calories to 280 and carbohydrate to 20 grams per serving."],[null,"1 medium apple yields approximately 1 cup after peeled and cored."]]},"2508":{"s":[[null,"Peel and core apples. Cut each apple into 5 rings, approximately 1/2″ thick each."],[null,"In a mixing bowl, sift together flour, 2 tablespoons sugar and baking powder."],[null,"In a separate bowl combine egg, milk, almond milk and 1 teaspoon oil."],[null,"Add egg mixture to dry ingredients and stir until just blended."],[null,"In a skillet that is at least 2″ deep, heat 1″ of cooking oil to 375º F."],[null,"Dip apple slices in batter one at a time. Fry in hot oil about 1-1/2 minutes until golden brown. Drain on paper towels."],[null,"Combine remaining 1/4 cup sugar with cinnamon and sprinkle on fritters. Serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"Donut shop apple fritters contain approximately 300 mg sodium compared to 33 mg per fritter in this recipe."],[null,"Splenda® granular sugar substitute can be used instead of sugar, if desired."]]},"2626":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400º F."],[null,"Peel and core apple. Thinly slice apple and onion."],[null,"Beat eggs with milk, water and pepper in a small bowl; set aside."],[null,"Over medium heat, melt butter in a small, ovenproof skillet."],[null,"Add onion and apple to the skillet and sauté until onion becomes translucent, about 5 to 6 minutes."],[null,"Spread out the onion and apple mixture evenly in the skillet."],[null,"Pour egg mixture evenly into the skillet and cook over medium heat until the edges begin to set. Sprinkle the cheddar cheese over the top. Transfer skillet to the oven and bake until the center is firmly set, approximately 10 to 12 minutes."],[null,"Cut omelet in half and slide each half onto an individual plate. Serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"Walla Walla sweet onion recommend if available."],[null,"Jonagold, Gala or McIntosh are the best apple varieties for this recipe."]]},"9183615":{"s":[[null,"Add all the ingredients in a medium bowl and mix well. Then divide the mixture into 2 jars or bowls and refrigerate for 6 hours or overnight."],[null,"Serve with additional toppings if you'd like and enjoy chilled. Or you may heat it on the stovetop if preferred."]],"h":[]},"6019686":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 350 degrees F. Grease a 9 x 13 baking dish."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine the sliced apples, sliced pears, lemon juice, granulated sugar, cinnamon, nutmeg, and salt. Toss until the fruits are well coated, and the sugar and spices are evenly distributed."],[null,"In a separate bowl, mix together oats, flour, brown sugar substitute, and diced cold plant-based butter. Use your hands or a pastry cutter to combine until the mixture resembles coarse crumbs."],[null,"Spread the fruit mixture evenly in the prepared baking dish."],[null,"Sprinkle the oat and flour mixture over the top of the fruit, creating a crumbly topping."],[null,"Cover with foil and bake for 20 minutes. Remove the foil and bake until the top is golden brown, and the fruit is bubbly, about 20 minutes more."],[null,"Allow to cool for 10 minutes before serving."]],"h":[]},"2274":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 425° F."],[null,"Peel, core and slice apples."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine apple slices, sugar and cinnamon. Cover and set aside."],[null,"In a separate large bowl, cut shortening into flour using a pastry blender. Add chilled water, 1 tablespoon at a time and mix until dough forms into a ball. If it does not, use hands to form a ball."],[null,"Divide dough in half and roll out one piece, using a rolling pin and additional flour as needed. Place in a 9″ pie pan."],[null,"Stir apple pie filling and pour into pie shell."],[null,"Using 1 tablespoon pats, place butter all around pie filling, evenly dispersed."],[null,"Roll out the other 1/2 of dough. Place on top of apple pie filling, making sure edges of pie are covered."],[null,"Using a sharp knife, make four 1” cuts around the top of the pie crust for air to escape while baking."],[null,"Place pie in oven on a jellyroll pan to catch juice from pie while baking."],[null,"Bake for 50 to 60 minutes until crust is golden brown."]],"h":[[null,"Suggested varieties of apples for a great tasting apple pie include: Fuji, Jonathan, Jonagold, Gala, Golden Delicious, Granny Smith, Pippin and Winesap. For best results try combining 2 or 3 varieties."],[null,"1 medium apple yields 1 cup when peeled and cored."]]},"5587732":{"s":[[null,"Mix the oats, grated apple, cinnamon and Renastep in a small saucepan."],[null,"Bring gently to the boil, stirring occasionally, then reduce heat and cook for 4-5 minutes, stirring constantly."],[null,"Meanwhile, tip the blueberries into a pan with 1 tsp of water and honey and gently poach until the blueberries have thawed and are tender, but still holding their shape."],[null,"Spoon the porridge into a bowl and top with the blueberries."]],"h":[["Renastep note","Renastep is a Food for Special Medical Purposes and must be used under medical supervision."],["Renastep note","Renastep is a ready to use feed for the dietary management of kidney disease from 3 years of age onwards. Renastep contains milk and fish. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information."],["Renastep note","This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease."]]},"5565148":{"s":[[null,"Peel apples."],[null,"Chop the apples in to small pieces."],[null,"Place the apple in a saucepan."],[null,"Add a dash of water and boil until soft, approximately 10 -12 minutes."],[null,"Once cooled, whizz the apples in a blender until smooth."]],"h":[[null,"Add a pinch of cinnamon for extra flavour"]]},"1929":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 325° F."],[null,"Grease a muffin pan with non-stick cooking spray."],[null,"Cream the sugar, oil and eggs together."],[null,"Add spices, salt, baking soda and applesauce; blend well."],[null,"Stir in the flour until it forms a thick batter."],[null,"Slice or dice the apple into bite-size pieces (peel if desired)."],[null,"If using slices, place a small spoonful of batter in the bottom of each muffin tin, arrange slices and add more batter. If using apple chunks, add them into the batter then fill muffin tin."],[null,"Bake for 25-30 minutes until firm to the touch. Remove from oven and cool."]],"h":[[null,"Recipe makes 6 large muffins, 12 medium muffins or 48 mini muffins."],[null,"For lower carbohydrate content replace sugar with a sugar blend that contains half sugar and half sugar substitute, or make mini muffins and portion 2 muffins per serving (19 grams carbohydrate)."]]},"6326806":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 350 degrees F. Line an 8 x 8-inch baking pan with parchment paper, leaving an overhang for easy removal."],[null,"In a bowl, toss the diced apples with lemon juice to prevent browning. Set it aside."],[null,"In a medium bowl, whisk together flour, baking powder, baking soda, ground cinnamon, and salt."],[null,"In a large mixing bowl, whisk the margarine, applesauce, granulated sugar substitute, brown sugar substitute, egg, and vanilla extract."],[null,"Gradually add the butter mixture to the flour mixture, stirring until just combined."],[null,"Gently fold in the diced apples and chopped walnuts."],[null,"Spread the batter evenly into the prepared baking pan."],[null,"Bake in the preheated oven for about 30 to 40 minutes or until a toothpick inserted into the center comes out clean."],[null,"Allow to cool in the pan for 10 minutes before using the parchment paper overhang to lift them onto a wire rack to cool completely."],[null,"Once cooled, cut into 12 squares and serve."]],"h":[]},"7919843":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven 180°C/gas mark 4."],[null,"Add the apples to a pan with the water, cover, then simmer gently for 15 minutes, stirring regularly until just soft."],[null,"Add the sultanas, apricot, cinnamon, almond essence and half the sweetener. Mix well and set aside."],[null,"Place a layer of pastry on a board and spray with two squirts of oil, then sprinkle with a third of the remaining sweetener. Lay another piece of pastry on top and repeat with two more sprays of oil and another third of the sweetener. Finally, repeat with the last sheet of pastry, oil and remaining sweetener."],[null,"Spread the apple mixture over three-quarters of the pastry, leaving the top quarter free, then sprinkle with orange zest."],[null,"Fold the top length of pastry over the apple mixture and roll the strudel over to completely cover the filling. Fold in the edges to prevent the filling from leaking out and roll the strudel over again, so the fold is at the bottom. Place on a baking sheet and spray with oil."],[null,"Heat in the oven for 20–25 minutes, until the pastry is lightly browned."],[null,"Serve with a dollop of yogurt, or non-dairy soya alternative, and a sprinkle of cinnamon."]],"h":[[null,"Try using pears in place of apples, or adding a few blueberries or blackberries."]]},"2354":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400° F."],[null,"Cut tortillas in half. Place tortillas on a baking sheet and lightly coat with nonstick cooking spray."],[null,"In a small bowl, stir together granulated sugar and 1/4 teaspoon pumpkin pie spice. Sprinkle over tortilla halves. Bake for about 10 minutes or until crisp."],[null,"Cool completely on a wire rack."],[null,"Peel, core and slice apples."],[null,"Lightly coat a medium, nonstick skillet with cooking spray and preheat over medium heat. Add apples, brown sugar and remaining 1/2 teaspoon pumpkin pie spice; cook and stir about 10 minutes or until golden."],[null,"Add apple juice, water and currants. Continue cooking, stirring occasionally, about 20 minutes or until the apples caramelize and the liquid evaporates."],[null,"Place each tortilla half on a dessert plate and spoon 1/2 cup apple mixture over tortillas. If desired, sprinkle with powdered sugar."],[null,"Serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"If sugar substitute is used instead of sugar, fruit will not caramelize as much and consistency may be runny."],[null,"Compare tortilla brands and select the lowest sodium product."]]},"3779":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350˚ F. Grease and flour two 9 x 5-inch loaf pans using 2 tablespoons of flour."],[null,"Peel and chop apples; shred zucchini."],[null,"In a large bowl, mix eggs, oil, granulated sugar, 3/4 cup brown sugar (or 6 tablespoons Splenda® Brown sugar blend) and vanilla."],[null,"In a separate large bowl, mix baking soda, 3-1/2 cups flour, salt and 2 teaspoons cinnamon."],[null,"Stir flour mixture into egg mixture. Do not over mix."],[null,"Fold in apples and zucchini and pour mixture into loaf pans. Spread mixture evenly."],[null,"Bake for 40 minutes."],[null,"While the bread is baking, prepare the crumb topping: combine the remaining 1/4 cup flour, 1/4 cup brown sugar (or 2 tablespoons Splenda® brown sugar blend), and 1 teaspoon cinnamon. Cut in the butter until the mixture becomes very crumbly."],[null,"Take the bread out of the oven once it has baked for 40 minutes and add the crumb topping."],[null,"Bake for an additional 10 minutes or until toothpick comes out clean (from the center of the loaf)."],[null,"Cool for 10 minutes, then remove loaves from pans and transfer to wire racks to cool completely."],[null,"Cut each loaf into 16 slices before serving."]],"h":[[null,"If using Splenda® sugar substitute in place of sugar, carbohydrate is decreased to 13 g per serving."],[null,"If substituting Splenda® Brown sugar blend sweetener for brown sugar reduce to 8 tablespoons."],[null,"Wrap one loaf in plastic wrap and place in a freezer bag to serve at a later time."],[null,"For a lower fat version substitute 1/2 cup unsweetened applesauce for the vegetable oil."]]},"6666899":{"s":[[null,"Place shredded beets, carrots, and apple in mixing bowl and mix to combine. Add walnuts and green herb(s) on top of mixture and set bowl aside."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together blood orange juice and salt until salt is dissolved. Add 3–4 grinds of pepper, then whisk in oil. Pour dressing over salad and mix until well combined and evenly dressed. Serve salad within 1 hour of combining with herbs and dressing."]],"h":[]},"7652430":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas mark 4. Put the breadcrumbs, oats and pumpkin seeds into a bowl and mix well."],[null,"Core and chop the apples, leaving the skin on, and put in an ovenproof dish. Add the blackberries then pour the apple juice into the dish."],[null,"Sprinkle the crumble mixture on top of the fruit, then drizzle with the honey."],[null,"Bake in the oven for around 15–20 minutes until golden brown."],[null,"Serve the crumble straight away, with a scoop of half-fat crème fraiche or natural yogurt."]],"h":[[null,"By using eating apples in this recipe, rather than the cooking variety, you don't need to add any extra sugar. This is because eating apples are naturally sweeter."],[null,"Apple skins contain fibre so avoid peeling them."],[null,"Blackberries are packed with antioxidants, including vitamin C, and they're also a good source of fibre."],[null,"Wholegrains, such as oats, contain a type of fibre called beta-glucan which can help to lower cholesterol if eaten regularly."]]},"6387863":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350°F and lightly grease an 8x8 baking dish."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine the oats, California Dates, chopped apples, cranberries, pecans, cinnamon, nutmeg, baking powder, flour, and salt until well incorporated."],[null,"Whisk in the eggs, milk, and vanilla extract."],[null,"Pour the mixture into the prepared baking dish and spread evenly."],[null,"Bake for 35–40 minutes, or until the oatmeal is set and golden brown on top."],[null,"Let it cool for a few minutes before serving. Cut into 8 equal squares."],[null,"Refrigerate for up to five days for meal prep."]],"h":[]},"6396957":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6334868":{"s":[],"h":[]},"4691815":{"s":[["Soup","In a stock pot, heat the oil over medium heat. Cook the apples, cauliflower and onion. Cover and stir regularly, until soft but not brown (15 minutes)."],["Soup","Add vinegar and spices, cook for another 5 minutes."],["Soup","Add the water and bring to a boil."],["Soup","Reduce heat slightly and simmer for 20 minutes. Remove from heat and let cool. Blend the soup in a blender until creamy."],["Chicken and Topping","While soup is simmering, in a large pan, heat the olive oil and sauté chicken with onions for 5 minutes. Add apple slices, season with pepper and cook for an additional 5 minutes. Remove from heat and keep warm or refrigerate immediately if using later. If using cooked chicken: sauté apples and onions together, season with pepper and add chicken at the end of cooking time to warm through."],["Chicken and Topping","Serve each bowl of soup topped with some meat mixture. Garnish with sour cream, lime juice and cilantro."]],"h":[[null,"The soup may also be enjoyed without the meat topping hot or cold. Simply top with sour cream, lime juice and cilantro."],[null,"PLEASE NOTE: This recipe is higher in potassium and portion size is important. Check with your registered dietitian to see how this recipe can be included in your diet."],["Cauliflower","While vegetables are an important part of a healthy diet for all, many varieties contain too much potassium to be enjoyed on a daily basis for those with chronic kidney disease. Cauliflower however is a great option for those with kidney disease as it is lower in potassium. Enjoy up to ½ cup of raw cauliflower per day as one of your vegetable options. A common vegetable that is very high in potassium and missed by many is potatoes. By weight, boiled cauliflower contains only half the potassium of peeled, boiled potatoes and thus can be mashed to serve as a replacement for mashed potatoes or substituted for potatoes in recipes such as soups. Ask your dietitian how much is right for you. Cauliflower is considered to be a “Power Food” as it is a cruciferous vegetable that contains antioxidants and phytonutrients that can protect against cancer. It is also high in fiber and helps promote a healthy digestive tract. Cauliflower is most commonly found fresh or frozen. When choosing fresh cauliflower, look for a firm head with no dark spots and bright green leaves attached to the stem."]]},"4179783":{"s":[[null,"Pre-heat oven to 350 degrees"],["Prepare apple mixture","In large sauté pan on medium high heat, sauté apples in butter for 6-8 minutes. Stir in cinnamon, nutmeg, and brown sugar, and cook for an additional 3-4 minutes. In a small cup, mix cornstarch and vanilla extract until dissolved, stir into apple mixture and cook for additional two minutes on medium high heat. Turn off heat and set aside."],["Prepare phyllo dough bundles","Lightly grease a large six muffin tin pan."],["Prepare phyllo dough bundles","Starting with the first sheet of phyllo dough, brush each side with melted butter then dust with the powdered sugar and cinnamon mix. Continue until all 6 sheets have been buttered and dusted with sugar and cinnamon mix, stacking one sheet on top of the other as you go."],["Prepare phyllo dough bundles","Cut each stack into 6 squares. Line the bottom and sides of each muffin cup using one stack of squares. Leave an over-hang."],["Prepare phyllo dough bundles","Fill each phyllo lined muffin cup ½ – ¾ full with the apple mixture (this will depend on how big the apples are cut), making sure each phyllo lined muffin cup has equal amounts of apple mixture."],["Prepare phyllo dough bundles","Fold excess phyllo dough over the apples in each muffin cup and pinch top closed to create the bundles."],["Prepare phyllo dough bundles","Bake in preheated oven for 8-10 minutes or until golden brown."],["Prepare phyllo dough bundles","Garnish with powdered sugar, whipped cream and sprig of fresh mint."],["Prepare phyllo dough bundles","Empire"],["Prepare phyllo dough bundles","Fuji"],["Prepare phyllo dough bundles","Golden Delicious"],["Prepare phyllo dough bundles","Red Delicious"],["Prepare phyllo dough bundles","Granny Smith"],["Garnish","Powdered Sugar"],["Garnish","Fresh mint"],["Garnish","Whipped cream or Low fat whipped topping"]],"h":[[null,"For those with diabetes, ¼ cup Agave Nectar can be substituted for light brown sugar as a sweetener."],[null,"Note: These are a few types of year round apples that are available are in most supermarkets and fruit stands across the country. Select one sour and two sweet apple varieties for your recipe:"]]},"2853":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Core apples and peel a strip from around the top of each apple. Place apples in a small baking pan."],[null,"Combine brown sugar, cider, cinnamon and butter in a small saucepan. Bring to a boil and pour over apples."],[null,"Bake for 45 minutes, basting occasionally."],[null,"Serve warm. Top with whipped topping."]],"h":[[null,"Reduce portion to 1/2 apple and substitute a sugar and sugar substitute brown sugar blend for a diabetes-friendly portion, approximately 18 grams carbohydrate."]]},"7814654":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200°C/gas mark 6."],[null,"Place the apricots in a single layer in an ovenproof dish. Drizzle over the orange zest and juice, then place in the oven and cook for 10 minutes."],[null,"While you wait, mix together all the ingredients for the topping in a bowl."],[null,"Sprinkle the topping over the apricots and return to the oven for 10–12 minutes, until golden."],[null,"Serve with a little ice cream or light crème fraîche."]],"h":[[null,"Try using a mixture of pumpkin seeds and sunflower seeds in place of the almonds."],[null,"Peaches work well instead of apricots."]]},"6947476":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F. In a large skillet, heat 2 Tsp. oil over medium heat. Add the apricots, cut side down, and cook until lightly browned, about 3 minutes. Turn the apricots and cook for 1 minute longer. Set aside."],[null,"In a small saucepan add the apricot preserves, balsamic vinegar and pepper and bring to a low boil; simmer 3 minutes or until mixture has a glaze-like consistency. Add apricots to the mixture."],[null,"Coat a baking dish with cooking spray. Place chicken breasts in dish. Brush each breast with 1 tbsp of apricot glaze and bake 30 minutes. Pour remaining glaze over chicken and serve."]],"h":[]},"6789218":{"s":[[null,"In a medium saucepan, bring chicken broth to a boil. Add couscous. Cover and remove from heat. Let stand for 5 minutes and fluff with a fork."],[null,"Add the remaining ingredients. Toss gently to coat."]],"h":[]},"7059157":{"s":[[null,"Place the apricots in a small pan and cover with the juice. Bring to the boil and simmer for 5 minutes."],[null,"Set aside for 10 minutes, then place in a food processor or blender and blend to form a purée."],[null,"Place the oats in a small pan, cover with 600ml of water, then place over a low heat and cook for 3–4 minutes."],[null,"Stir through half the apricot purée, divide between 2 bowls, then top with the toasted seeds and a swirl of the remaining purée."]],"h":[[null,"To toast the seeds, add them to a dry frying pan over a medium heat, stir and remove from the pan as soon as they start to brown."],[null,"The seeds aren't essential to this recipe, though they are a good source of omega-3 fatty acids, which help maintain good heart health."],[null,"Also works well with blueberries instead of apricots."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"2176":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375º F."],[null,"Place artichoke hearts in a saucepan, cover with water and bring to a boil. Reduce heat to medium and cook for 6 minutes. Drain and rinse with cold water to cool."],[null,"Chop artichoke hearts."],[null,"In a medium bowl combine mayonnaise, sour cream, cream cheese, hot sauce and crushed garlic clove. Add artichoke hearts and stir to combine. Transfer mixture to a baking dish."],[null,"Top with Parmesan cheese. Place in oven and bake for 30 minutes or until bubbly on top."]],"h":[[null,"If canned or jarred artichokes in water are used instead of frozen, look for the lowest sodium brand. Rinse well to help reduce sodium."],[null,"Try this dip on toasted slices of baguette, crisp celery or with your favorite low-sodium crackers. Choose rice crackers or other gluten-free crackers if you are on a gluten-free diet."],[null,"Tabasco© sauce is one of the lowest sodium hot pepper sauces."]]},"2449":{"s":[[null,"Mince carrot and onion."],[null,"In a bowl, combine cream cheese with mushrooms, carrot and onion to make stuffing. Set aside in refrigerator until chili peppers are prepared."],[null,"Heat a frying pan on medium heat. Place peppers in pan and roast, turning several times, until skin bubbles. Remove from heat. When peppers are cool enough to handle, peel the skin off."],[null,"Cut chili peppers open lengthwise and gently spoon half the cream cheese stuffing inside each pepper."],[null,"In a separate bowl, beat egg white and flour until stiff. Coat each stuffed chili pepper with egg mixture."],[null,"Place canola oil in a saucepan, enough to fill pan approximately one inch. Heat on medium-high heat."],[null,"Carefully place chili peppers in the hot oil and fry until golden brown, turning once. Serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"California green chili peppers, also known as Anaheim chili peppers, are long green peppers with a mildly-hot taste. If unavailable, substitute low-sodium canned, whole, green chili peppers."],[null,"Chili peppers vary in potassium content, with some varieties containing over 300 milligrams potassium each. Check with your dietitian before substituting chili pepper varieties in this recipe."]]},"1002746":{"s":[[null,"Spread cream cheese over each tortilla to cover. Sprinkle with dried cilantro."],[null,"Place remaining ingredients in a bowl and mix."],[null,"Divide mixed ingredients into 2 portions. Place half on each tortilla and roll up tightly."],[null,"Trim ends and cut each roll into 6 pieces."]],"h":[[null,"Wrap the uncut roll in plastic wrap and refrigerate until ready to slice and serve."],[null,"Compare tortilla brands and select the one lowest in sodium."]]},"1002949":{"s":[[null,"Prepare rice in a rice cooker or according to package directions. Add bay leaf and water before cooking. Chop onion and tomato. Peel and then cut the"],[null,"plantain diagonally into 12 pieces. Chop cilantro and garlic. Cut lime into quarters."],[null,"Combine dried oregano, cumin and salt in a very small bowl. Set aside."],[null,"In a 2-quart skillet over medium heat, sauté onion and garlic in 1/2 tablespoon olive oil. Once garlic and onion are fragrant, add tomato and cook for a few minutes."],[null,"Add steamed rice and cilantro and stir. Sprinkle dry seasonings over the top and stir until all ingredients are combined; set aside."],[null,"In a skillet, heat 1/2 tablespoon olive oil, add plantains and cook for 2 minutes, turn and cook until golden brown."],[null,"In a separate skillet, heat 1 tablespoon olive oil over medium heat, crack eggs into the pan and cook to desired doneness."],[null,"On a plate, place 1/2 cup rice and 3 plantain pieces. Top each serving with 2 eggs."],[null,"Squeeze the juice of a lime wedge over each plate."]],"h":[[null,"The plantain portion is small because plantains are high in potassium. If you are not on a low-potassium diet, plantains can be increased to 2 medium or 1 large plantain."],[null,"When cooking rice, use a 1:2 ratio: 1 cup rice to 2 cups water."],[null,"If you don’t have lemon or lime, try sprinkling 1/4 teaspoon vinegar on each serving for extra flavor."]]},"1002914":{"s":[[null,"Peel pumpkin, wash it and cut into small cubes or grate on the coarse side of a grater."],[null,"Chop onion and garlic."],[null,"Heat oil in a medium skillet or pot and sauté the vegetables."],[null,"Rinse rice."],[null,"Add rice to the vegetables, sauté for a few minutes and add water."],[null,"Boil until the water is absorbed."],[null,"Stir the rice, cover and lower the heat so it cooks slowly until tender, about 15 minutes."],[null,"Let rest and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Use brown rice for more fiber and flavor."]]},"3710":{"s":[[null,"Drain and rinse pigeon peas. Mince garlic."],[null,"Heat 2 teaspoons oil in a large saucepan."],[null,"Add Sofrito, Bijol® powder, tomato paste, garlic, oregano, bouillon cube and pigeon peas."],[null,"Stir fry for approximately 3 to 4 minutes to seal in juices."],[null,"In large sauce pan, prepare rice following the recipe on the package, omitting salt."],[null,"Mix rice in with the ingredients in large saucepan and serve."]],"h":[[null,"See Sofrito recipe on DaVita.com."],[null,"For more protein add one-cup chopped chicken. Adds 4 grams of protein per serving. Use half a rotisserie chicken with the skin and bones removed to save time."],[null,"Bijol®, a brand name for achiote or annotto powder, gives a yellow-orange color to the rice. It is a replacement for saffron. If unavailable, substitute equal parts paprika and turmeric."],[null,"Frozen or dried cooked pigeon peas may be substituted for canned peas."]]},"6630821":{"s":[[null,"Prepare the rice according to the package directions."],[null,"Combine the cooked rice, milk, water, sugar substitute, orange peel, cinnamon stick, flaxseeds, and cloves in a medium saucepan; bring to a boil. Reduce the heat to medium low and simmer, stirring often, until the rice pudding is thick and creamy, about 20 minutes."],[null,"Remove from the heat. Remove and discard the orange peel, cinnamon stick, and cloves. Stir in vanilla and ground cinnamon."]],"h":[]},"2771":{"s":[[null,"Rinse rice with tap water, then drain."],[null,"Add rice and 1 cup water to a medium saucepan. Bring to a boil, cover with a lid and cook for 10 minutes."],[null,"Remove lid and stir in almond milk and raisins. Cover again and boil for 10 minutes or until the rice is well cooked. (Rice will have a soupy consistency; not all the liquid will boil off.)"],[null,"When rice is done, remove from heat and stir in the sugar (or sugar substitute), cinnamon and vanilla. Mix well and serve warm."],[null,"Refrigerate leftover portions."]],"h":[[null,"Look for unrefrigerated almond milk and select a brand that does not contain phosphate additives."],[null,"Raisins are optional. Portion must be limited due to added potassium content."],[null,"Recipe was revised to eliminate nondairy creamer. Sugar was reduced from 1/2 cup to 1/4 cup. Adjust the amount if you like a sweeter dessert."],[null,"Carbohydrate choice is 2 when prepared with sugar substitute instead of sugar. Calories are decreased to 195 and carbohydrate to 27 grams per serving."]]},"1002909":{"s":[[null,"Cut bell pepper into julienne strips."],[null,"Finely chop onion."],[null,"Sauté onion and bell pepper in a little oil until onion is soft."],[null,"Add rice, let it turn translucent, then add water and peas."],[null,"Cover and cook until rice is tender."]],"h":[[null,"Refrigerate leftovers for a quick meal later."]]},"2716":{"s":[[null,"Drain and chop the artichoke hearts and pimento. Thinly slice the green onions and mince the garlic clove."],[null,"Combine all ingredients except the pitas in a bowl and mix well."],[null,"Cover and chill for 8 hours or overnight."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 350° F."],[null,"Split the pita rounds open. Cut each half into quarters, making 8 wedges."],[null,"Place the pita wedges on a baking sheet, smooth side down and spray with cooking spray. Bake for 8 minutes or until lightly browned."],[null,"Cool the pita wedges and set aside in an airtight container until ready to serve."],[null,"Top each pita wedge with 1 tablespoon of Artichoke Relish."]],"h":[[null,"Bagel chips or pita chips work well too. Choose the lowest sodium chips."]]},"6050583":{"s":[[null,"Soak the artichokes in water to clean; drain and repeat until water is clear. Peel away the outside leaves of the bottom half of the artichokes. Cut off the top quarter of the artichoke (at this point the artichoke should look like a flower, and the tough, dark leaves should all be removed, leaving only lighter-colored, tenderer leaves). If tough, dark green leaves remain, peel those as well. Add juice of 1 lemon to a bowl full of cold water, and place cleaned artichokes inside to avoid discoloration."],[null,"Bring a large pot of water to a boil, and add cleaned artichokes. Bring back to a boil on high heat. Reduce heat to medium-low and simmer artichokes 25–30 minutes, or until tender. Drain artichokes well, pat dry with a paper towel, and set aside."],[null,"In a large skillet, heat olive oil over medium heat. Add garlic and sauté until garlic begins to release its aroma, approximately 1 minute. Add artichokes, turn to coat in oil, and season with salt, pepper, and crushed red chile flakes. Sprinkle with parsley and serve warm."]],"h":[]},"6654857":{"s":[[null,"In a large salad bowl, combine the arugula, fennel, Parmesan cheese, and pine nuts."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the grapeseed oil, lemon juice, honey, Dijon mustard, salt, and black pepper."],[null,"Pour the dressing over the salad."],[null,"Toss the salad gently to ensure even coating."]],"h":[]},"6398457":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, combine the arugula, pears, walnuts, and blue cheese."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the balsamic vinegar, olive oil, Dijon mustard, honey, salt, and pepper."],[null,"Pour the dressing over the salad and gently toss to ensure even coating."]],"h":[]},"6440574":{"s":[[null,"In a large salad bowl, combine the arugula, toasted and chopped walnuts, crumbled goat cheese, and halved cherry tomatoes."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the balsamic vinaigrette dressing, extra virgin olive oil, salt, and pepper."],[null,"Drizzle the dressing over the salad."],[null,"Toss the salad gently to ensure even coating."]],"h":[]},"6564680":{"s":[[null,"Place the arugula in a large salad bowl. Slice the pear as thinly as possible and place on top of the arugula. Sprinkle with walnut halves. Using a vegetable peeler, shave 1/2 ounce of the Pecorino over the salad bowl."],[null,"Sprinkle balsamic vinegar over the salad. Sprinkle extra virgin olive oil over the salad. Add pepper. Toss well. Serve."]],"h":[]},"2890":{"s":[[null,"Finely dice green onions."],[null,"Place shredded cabbage, water chestnuts, green onions and sesame seeds in large bowl."],[null,"Dissolve sugar in vinegar. Pour vinegar into oil and whisk until mixed."],[null,"Pour over cabbage mixture."],[null,"Toss to evenly distribute the dressing."],[null,"Chill several hours or overnight."],[null,"Add chow mein noodles and toss before serving."]],"h":[[null,"This is a great side dish when served with grilled chicken, brisket or fish."],[null,"Check chow mein noodles and buy the lowest sodium brand."]]},"9333659":{"s":[[null,"To make your cauliflower rice, break your cauliflower into florets and using a veggie bullet, or food processor, shred to a rice consistency, using the shredder attachment. Set aside."],[null,"Add all the peanut sauce ingredients in a small bowl and mix until well combined, set aside."],[null,"In a large skillet or wok, sauté the onion, carrots and peppers with two tablespoons of water, until softened, approx 5 minutes. Then add the cauliflower rice, chickpeas and snow peas and sauté an additional 3-4 minutes, until slightly reduced without over cooking."],[null,"Turn off the heat, add the cilantro and peanut sauce and mix well. Serve sprinkled with sesame seeds and extra cilantro, if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Do not over process the cauliflower . If you don’t have a shredder attachment and must use the s-blade on your food processor, work in small batches. Pulse 4-5 times and then check on it, and pulse more if needed. If your cauliflower rice feels wet , squeeze out the moisture with a clean, dry dish cloth or paper towels, before cooking. Do not over cook the veggies . Stir fried vegetables shouldn’t be too soft, and definitely not mushy. So make sure to watch carefully, and remove from the heat once ready. For soy free , sub the soy sauce or Tamari for coconut aminos , or skip it and add salt, to taste. For peanut free , you may sub for almond butter , pecan butter , cashew butter, or any of your favourite nut butters. If you need it completely nut free , use soy butter (if you can do soy), sun butter (made from sunflower seeds), or tahini (made from sesame seeds), with slightly different results. I find this dish only mildly spicy. But if you have low spice tolerance , start with just a half teaspoon of hot sauce and add more, until just right for you. Leftover Asian cauliflower rice keeps refrigerated in a sealed container for 3-4 days."]]},"6595377":{"s":[[null,"In a medium bowl mix together cabbage, lettuce, almonds, 1 tablespoon sesame seeds, and chicken."],[null,"In a small bowl whisk together vinegar, soy sauce, and oil."],[null,"Pour dressing over salad and toss to coat. Top with remaining 1 teaspoon sesame seeds and red pepper flakes."]],"h":[]},"3389":{"s":[[null,"Cut asparagus, squash and green beans into 1″ pieces. Slice mushrooms. Chop garlic. Cut chicken into 1″ pieces."],[null,"Spray a 12″ nonstick skillet with cooking spray and heat over medium-high heat."],[null,"In a bowl, mix coleslaw mix, eggs, white pepper and soy sauce."],[null,"Pour batter into skillet. Cook, covered until set and browned, about 4 minutes. Flip and cook, uncovered about 2 minutes. Keep warm."],[null,"Spray a large, nonstick skillet or wok with cooking spray and heat over medium-high heat."],[null,"Add asparagus, squash and green beans and stir-fry about 2 minutes. Add mushrooms and cook another 2 minutes."],[null,"Add chicken, 1/2 of ginger, 1/2 of garlic and 1/2 of sesame oil and stir-fry until chicken is cooked, about 3 minutes."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix water, cornstarch, remaining ginger, garlic and oil. Pour over stir-fry and cook, stirring continuously for 1-2 minutes until slightly thickened."],[null,"Cut pancake into six wedges, and spoon chicken mixture over each wedge."]],"h":[[null,"Sesame oil adds a wonderful flavor."],[null,"One cup egg substitute may be substituted for 4 eggs to lower cholesterol content."]]},"4636532":{"s":[[null,"Heat the broth."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine ginger, tofu, soy sauce, chili paste and vinegar to marinate the tofu."],[null,"Slice green onions. Separate the white from the green slices and set aside."],[null,"Combine the celery, green slices of green onions, red pepper and cabbage in a bowl."],[null,"Heat a large pot or deep wok style pan for two minutes on medium-high heat. Add the olive oil and the sesame oil and fry the white slices of the green onions until they are brown and somewhat crisp but not burnt."],[null,"Turning the heat down to medium, add the tofu and its marinade, stirring to coat well while cooking for 2 minutes."],[null,"Add all the vegetables from step 4 and continue to cook for another 2–3 minutes."],[null,"Add the hot broth to the vegetables, turn up the heat and bring to a boil quickly, add the rice noodles and cook for two minutes."],[null,"Turn off heat and stir in cilantro and lime juice and season with fresh black pepper to taste."]],"h":[[null,"* Choose the broth with the lowest sodium content but be aware that low sodium products often contain more potassium. Look for potassium chloride under ingredients on the label."],[null,"Leftover soup can be reheated within 2 days."]]},"4779831":{"s":[[null,"ground pepper to taste"],[null,"Heat the broth."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine ginger, tofu, soy sauce, chili paste and vinegar to marinate the tofu. Add the tofu and set aside."],[null,"Slice green onions, separate the green from the white slices, and set aside."],[null,"Combine the celery, green slices of green onions, red pepper and cabbage in a bowl."],[null,"Heat a large pot or deep wok style pan for 2 minutes on medium-high heat. Add the olive oil and the sesame oil and fry the whites of the green onions until they are brown and somewhat crisp but not burnt."],[null,"Turning the heat down to medium, add the tofu and its marinade, stirring to coat well while cooking for 2 minutes."],[null,"Add all vegetables from step 4 and continue to cook for another 2–3 minutes."],[null,"Add the hot broth to the vegetables, turn up the heat and bring to a boil quickly. Add the rice noodles and cook for 2 minutes."],[null,"Turn off the heat, stir in cilantro and lime juice and season with black pepper."]],"h":[[null,"Leftover soup can be reheated within two days if kept refrigerated."],["Tofu and the kidney diet","For those with chronic kidney disease it is important to eat the right amount of protein. Protein can come from animal sources such as lean meat, chicken, turkey, fish, shellfish, eggs and dairy products or from vegetable sources such as beans, legumes and tofu. It is important to note that the potassium content of protein sources can vary a lot. This is even the case with protein-rich foods that seem to be similar. For example, when choosing dairy products, cheese is lower in potassium while milk and yogurt can be quite high in potassium (note that cheese however can be much higher in sodium). This can be true for the different types of tofu as well. The silken tofu varieties contain significantly more potassium than regular firm or extra firm tofu. Consider these facts if it is important for you to follow a lower-potassium diet. Vegetable sources of protein can be heart-healthy and help to control blood sugar levels for those who have diabetes. Try substituting tofu for meat in some of your recipes. An easy place to start is adding it to a stir-fry or salad. You can also thread it on skewers with vegetables to make a kebab. In general, the potassium content of vegetable proteins is higher than that of meat, poultry or fish. Ask your registered dietitian how much and which types of protein are right for you."]]},"3906":{"s":[[null,"Mince ginger root and garlic. Chop green onion."],[null,"Pour 1-1/2 cups water, orange juice, lemon juice, rice vinegar, and soy sauce into a saucepan and set over medium-high heat. Stir in the orange zest, brown sugar, ginger, garlic, chopped onion, and red pepper flakes. Bring to a boil. Remove from heat, and cool 10 to 15 minutes."],[null,"Cut chicken into 1/2-in pieces and place into a resealable plastic bag. When contents of saucepan have cooled, pour 1 cup of sauce into bag. Reserve the remaining sauce. Seal the bag, and refrigerate at least 2 hours."],[null,"Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium heat. Place the marinated chicken into the skillet, and brown on both sides. Drain on a plate lined with paper towels and set aside."],[null,"Wipe out the skillet, and add the sauce. Bring to a boil over medium-high heat. Mix together the cornstarch and remaining 1/4 cup water; stir into the sauce. Reduce heat to medium low, add the chicken pieces, and simmer, about 5 minutes, stirring occasionally."],[null,"Divide into 4 portions and serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"Serve with steamed rice to complete the meal."],[null,"Turkey cutlets or chicken thigh meat can be substituted for chicken breast."],[null,"Note the water is divided for use in steps 2 and 5. The sauce is also divided for marinating and making final sauce."]]},"7315197":{"s":[[null,"Place all the marinade ingredients in a non-metallic bowl and stir well."],[null,"Add the salmon fillets, coat in the marinade and set aside to allow the flavours to infuse."],[null,"Cook for 3–4 minutes over a medium heat, add any remaining marinade, turn over and cook the other side for 3–4 minutes until thoroughly cooked through."],[null,"Scatter with the coriander and spring onions before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Also works well with other fish fillets such as mackerel, river cobbler or fresh tuna."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge and reheat until piping-hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"4787051":{"s":[[null,"Prepare vegetables and fruits."],[null,"Transfer them into a glass bowl, grating the apple last and sprinkling the lemon juice over all ingredients before mixing (to keep from browning)."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine all ingredients for the dressing."],[null,"Pour dressing over the salad and toss."],[null,"Refrigerate until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Prepare in advance, keep in the fridge."],[null,"This recipe can be easily halved."],["Cabbage","Vegetables are part of a healthy diet for all. Unfortunately, for those with chronic kidney disease, many vegetables may contain too much potassium to be enjoyed on a daily basis. Cabbage however is lower in potassium and can be enjoyed daily if desired. A one-cup serving of shredded raw cabbage contains only 120 milligrams of potassium. Cabbage is also high in fiber, rich in vitamins, minerals and antioxidants. All these can aid in bowel function, promote heart health and protect against cancer. Cabbage comes in a lot of varieties, but the most commonly available are the green, red and purple varieties. When buying cabbage, choose heads that are firm and dense with shiny leaves that are not cracked or bruised. Cabbage is also a nutritional bargain as it tends to be an affordable fresh vegetable that can be enjoyed in many types of recipes. Cabbage can be shredded and added to lettuce salads or used to make a chopped salad or coleslaw. Top a sandwich or tacos with coleslaw for extra crunch and flavor. Steam or sauté and serve as a side dish. Toss it into your next stir fry or add it to soups and stews."]]},"9975367":{"s":[[null,"Using a food processor or veggie bullet, shred your cauliflower into a rice consistency. If using a food processor, do so in smaller batches not to over process your cauliflower. You do not want it pureed."],[null,"Heat the coconut oil in a large skillet over medium high heat and wait until the oil is hot. Then add your cauliflower rice and sprinkle with salt. Cook, stirring occasionally for about 10 minutes, or until lightly golden. Set aside."],[null,"Meanwhile, add all your dressing ingredients to a small bowl and whisk to combine. Set aside."],[null,"Place the slaw and cilantro in a large bowl and then pour the dressing on top and mix well."],[null,"Divide your cauliflower rice and the dressed slaw between your 8 wraps. You will add approx. 2 tablespoons of cauliflower rice and 3 tablespoons of slaw to each wrap. Fold the sides of the tortilla wrap first and then wrap up from the bottom so nothing spills out of the edges. Do not overfill or they will be difficult to wrap."],[null,"Optional but recommended: Use a panini press or grill to lightly grill your wraps, folded side down, for about 2 minutes. This will help hold your wraps together and give them beautiful grill marks."],[null,"Serve your wraps cut in half or whole. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Do not over stuff your vegan wraps. Not only will they be difficult to fold, but they’ll also be a lot messier to eat. To save time , you may purchase pre-made coleslaw (pick your favourite veggie mix). You may also purchase pre-made cauliflower rice. You will need 4 cups of each. If you have the time to do so, I highly recommend grilling the vegan wraps . It helps hold them together, sealing the edges down for a nice, neat pocket. For oil free: Sauté your cauliflower rice in water or broth instead of the coconut oil."]]},"2552":{"s":[[null,"Place the egg in a pan of water and heat to a boil. Turn heat off and leave egg in water for 8 minutes. Drain water and add cold water to cool the egg."],[null,"Layer rice and vegetables in a 16 ounce glass jar."],[null,"In a small bowl mix coconut aminos, sesame oil, ginger, garlic powder and red pepper flakes. Pour over rice and vegetables. Top with a lid and refrigerate."],[null,"Remove jar from refrigerator at least 15 minutes before you are ready to eat."],[null,"Pour 5 ounces boiling water into the jar, close the lid and shake to combine. Let ingredients steep in unopened jar for 2 minutes."],[null,"Peel and slice the hard-boiled egg. Pour contents from jar into a bowl, top with egg and enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Coconut aminos are a lower sodium, gluten-free alternative to soy sauce. One teaspoon has 90 mg sodium compared to 305 mg sodium in one teaspoon soy sauce."],[null,"Use the bagged coleslaw mix instead of buying a cabbage and carrot."],[null,"Recipe analysis includes brown rice. Substitute rice noodles for rice if desired."],[null,"If you use a wide-mouth jar you can mix and eat the soup directly from the jar—no bowl needed."],[null,"Double or triple the recipe and refrigerate extra jars for a quick meal."]]},"3227420":{"s":[[null,"Lay the chicken breast between some cling film and pound with a rolling pin until flattened out. Slice the chicken into strips."],[null,"Mix the soy sauce, honey, garlic and half the sesame oil into a bowl and whisk to combine. Put the chicken into the marinade, mix well, cover and chill for at least 20 minutes."],[null,"Heat the remaining sesame oil in a frying pan over a medium/high heat, then add the chicken strips and fry until completely cooked through. Remove chicken from the pan and set aside on a plate."],[null,"Reduce heat and add the remaining marinade mix and cook until a sticky dressing is made, about 5 minutes. Allow to cool."],[null,"Boil a kettle full of water and pour boiling water into a bowl. Put the noodles into the water and leave for 3 minutes. Drain."],[null,"Tip the remaining ingredients into a bowl and gently incorporate the chicken and noodles. Serve with dressing drizzled over the top."]],"h":[["Chef's note","A flavourful Asian-inspired salad, low in salt, potassium and phosphate."],["Carbohydrate","The rice noodles are the main source of carbohydrate in this recipe, and the value has been provided for those who have been trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","This recipe is low in potassium, when following the quantities in the ingredients and serving sizes. It is therefore suitable for those advised to reduce potassium in their diet. This recipe is also low in phosphate, however, it does contain some phosphate (mainly provided by the chicken and nuts) so if you have been prescribed a phosphate binder, take as directed."],["Protein","This recipe provides a source of protein. For a lower protein option, consider reducing the chicken to 75g and adding a small tin (200g) of drained chickpeas at step 6."],["Tips","Sesame oil is more expensive, but worth the extra cost, as a small amount adds wonderful flavour. Reduced-salt soy sauce still contains salt, so measure carefully."]]},"9539328":{"s":[["Press the tofu","Cut your tofu into half-inch cubes. Then arrange some paper towels or a clean dish towel on a cutting board and place the tofu cubes in a single layer on top. Now add more paper towels on top of the cubes and place another cutting board, flat plate, or baking sheet on top. Finally, place something very heavy on top like a cast-iron skillet or a heavy book. Press like this for 15 minutes while you prepare the remaining ingredients."],["For the tofu","Preheat the oven to 425°F/218°C convection bake and line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],["For the tofu","Once the tofu is pressed, place the cubes in a medium mixing bowl with the 2 tablespoons of tamari and gently mix. Then add the 2 tablespoons of flour, and the onion and garlic powder. Mix gently to evenly coat the pieces."],["For the tofu","Arrange the coated tofu cubes in a single layer on your baking sheet, leaving plenty of space in between each piece. Bake for 25-30 minutes, flipping once at the halfway point. NOTE: If you do not have a convection oven, it may take a little longer to reach desired crispiness."],["For the sticky tofu sauce","While the tofu is baking, combine all the sticky tofu sauce ingredients in a medium pan. Whisk to combine and simmer for 5 minutes, until slightly thickened. Then turn off the heat."],["For the sticky tofu sauce","Add the baked tofu to the pan with the sauce and gently toss to coat each piece."],["For the sticky tofu sauce","Serve your sticky tofu with rice or noodles, and top with green onion or chives and sesame seeds."]],"h":[[null,"Arrange the cubes of tofu in a single layer with space in between each piece . They shouldn’t touch each other on the baking tray in order to get the maximum crisp level. If you don’t have a convection oven , it may take an extra few minutes to get your tofu crispy. Bake until desired crispiness level is reached. For the best texture , plan to enjoy your Asian sticky tofu immediately. The longer it sits in the sauce, it will begin to lose some of its crispy exterior. This sticky tofu dish tastes best when freshly made . However, leftovers will keep refrigerated in a sealed container for 3-4 days. To reheat, add a splash of water to the pan of tofu to loosen the sauce."]]},"3959701":{"s":[[null,"Heat half the oil in a frying pan over a medium heat and fry onion until soft. Add in the turkey, garlic and chilli and cook until turkey is cooked through, about 10 minutes. Add in carrot and cook for a further 5 minutes. Drain the excess liquid out of the frying pan and turn off heat."],[null,"Add the soy sauce, coriander, mint and lime juice to the turkey mixture and set aside for the flavours to develop."],[null,"Heat remaining oil in a separate pan over a high heat and add chickpeas and cumin seeds. Cook until crispy; keep them moving so they don’t burn."],[null,"Warm the tortilla wraps. Divide the turkey mixture equally between the two wraps. Top with chopped spring onions, chickpeas and lettuce. Seal and roll-up wraps to serve."]],"h":[["Chef's note","This is a delicious, healthy, high-protein wrap."],["Carbohydrate","The wholemeal tortilla wraps are the the main source of carbohydrate in this recipe, and the value has been provided for those who have been trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","This recipe is low in potassium, when following the quantities and serving sizes given. This is suitable for those advised to reduce potassium in their diet. The recipe is also low in phosphate, however it does contain some phosphate, mainly provided by the turkey mince and chickpeas, therefore if you have been prescribed a phosphate binder, you should take as directed."],["Protein","This recipe is high in protein, therefore suitable for those advised to eat more protein, such as those receiving dialysis. If you have been advised to eat less protein, you may wish to reduce the quantity of turkey mince and top it with some extra tinned and drained chickpeas."],["Tips","It could also be a quick meal on a busy day by preparing the filling in advance (cool after step 1 and store in the fridge for up to 3 days, then warm the filling and follow recipe from step 2). Also good for a healthy packed lunch."]]},"3651":{"s":[[null,"Prepare rice according to package instructions. Set frozen broccoli out to thaw. Dice the onion; slice celery; slice bell pepper into strips; mince garlic cloves, grate ginger and chop cilantro."],[null,"Drizzle canola oil in a large non-stick pan and heat to medium high heat. Add turkey and brown. Halfway through cooking add the Mrs. Dash herb seasoning. Once turkey is cooked, remove from pan."],[null,"In the same pan, add in onion, peppers and celery and cook over medium heat for 5 minutes. Add in garlic and ginger and cook for 3 more minutes."],[null,"Once vegetables are soft, add in frozen broccoli and stir to combine for a few more minutes."],[null,"To make the sauce, combine broth, brown sugar, coconut aminos and Sriracha sauce in a small bowl."],[null,"Add cooked turkey back into pan and stir in sauce to combine."],[null,"Place 1/2 cup rice in a bowl and top with turkey and vegetable mixture. Add chopped cilantro if desired. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"To thicken the sauce up more, add 1 teaspoon of corn starch."],[null,"If Mrs. Dash seasoning is unavailable you can combine 1/2 teaspoon pepper, 1 teaspoon onion powder and 1 teaspoon garlic powder."],[null,"Ginger paste can be substituted for fresh ginger."],[null,"For a lower protein diet, if you have CKD and are not on dialysis, decrease the ground turkey to 1/2 pound. Protein is decreased to 16 grams."]]},"3253638":{"s":[[null,"Prepare all the ingredients, then cook the rice as per the package instructions, however avoid overcooking – you still want a slight bite to the rice. Once ready, drain and set aside."],[null,"Heat 1 tablespoon of oil in a large frying pan or wok over a medium heat. Once hot, add the eggs and gently scramble with some black pepper. Set aside in a bowl once cooked."],[null,"Heat the frying pan or wok with the remaining oil. Add the garlic and ginger and cook over high heat, stirring constantly, for 1-2 minutes, until fragrant and lightly browned."],[null,"Add the red onion, whites of the spring onion and tomatoes. Cook, stirring, for 5 minutes. Add the asparagus stalks and cook, stirring, for 1 minute. Then add the asparagus tips and apple, cooking for another 1-2 minutes."],[null,"Add the rice in clumps and then use wooden spoons or spatulas to stir, toss and break up the rice. Fry, constantly stirring, for 3 minutes."],[null,"Add the soy sauce, cooked eggs, chopped green parts of the spring onions, and chopped coriander. Toss. Then add the sesame oil, toss, and add sliced chilli pepper, if using. Serve."]],"h":[["Chef's note","An all-veggie egg fried rice with a tango of asparagus and apple."],["Carbohydrate","The rice is the main source of carbohydrate in this recipe, and the value has been provided for those who have been trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","Despite the use of some high potassium ingredients, such as asparagus and tomatoes, this recipe is very low in potassium, when following the quantities in the ingredients, and the serving sizes. Therefore, suitable for those advised to lower potassium in their diet.\nThis recipe is also low in phosphate, however it does contain some phosphate, mainly provided by the egg, therefore if you have been prescribed a phosphate binder you should take as directed."],["Protein","This recipe is low in protein, therefore suitable for those advised to eat less protein. If you have been advised to eat more protein, then you could add 200-300g of cooked cod."],["Cheaper option","Use long-grain rice instead of jasmine rice."],["Gluten free","Use a gluten-free soy sauce."],["Healthier option","Use brown instead of white rice to provide more fibre."],["Storage","This dish is best eaten freshly made."]]},"6128345":{"s":[[null,"Preheat a large ovenproof skillet over medium heat."],[null,"Add oil, asparagus, bok choy, salt, and pepper to the skillet. Cook, stirring occasionally, until veggies soften, 2–3 minutes."],[null,"Crack the eggs into a large bowl and whisk to combine."],[null,"Preheat the oven to broil."],[null,"Reduce heat to low and pour the egg mixture into the skillet. Gently lift the cooked eggs around the edge with a spatula until the sides are firm but the top is still runny, 3–4 minutes."],[null,"Sprinkle cheese over the frittata. Place the skillet in the oven and broil until the top is set and the cheese is melted, 1–2 minutes. Slice into six equal pieces."]],"h":[]},"3686":{"s":[[null,"Steam the asparagus for 6 to 8 minutes."],[null,"Puree cream cheese with parsley, lemon juice and spices, to make a green cream sauce. Season to taste. Set aside."],[null,"To make crepes combine the flour, water, egg, egg white and 2 tablespoons melted butter; whisk to make a smooth batter."],[null,"Melt 1/2 tablespoon butter in a pan (8 to 10-inch crepe or sauté pan). Add 1/3 cup crepe batter and turn pan to spread batter. Cook until bubbly and edges begin to brown. Turn and cook briefly on the other side. Cool on a plate. Repeat with remaining butter and batter to make 4 crepes."],[null,"Spread crepes with cream cheese filling. Distribute the asparagus spears evenly at end of each crepe and firmly roll up into rolls."],[null,"Wrap in foil and let cool in refrigerator for one hour. Cut chilled crepes into 3 to 4 pieces with a sharp knife before serving."]],"h":[[null,"For a higher protein entrée fill the crepe with shrimp instead of asparagus. Peeled shrimp, sauté in olive oil, let it cool down and curl up in the crepes."]]},"6697357":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350 degrees F."],[null,"Whisk egg substitute, milk, cheeses, salt, and pepper in a medium bowl and set aside."],[null,"Add olive oil to heavy oven-proof 10-inch cast iron or nonstick skillet over medium-low heat."],[null,"Add leeks and sauté for 2 minutes."],[null,"Add asparagus and sauté until tender, about 6 minutes, stirring often so leeks brown evenly."],[null,"Add egg mixture to skillet, folding gently to combine. Allow edges to set, then place into a preheated oven and bake for 10–15 minutes until frittata is puffed and golden."],[null,"Cut into 8 wedges and serve."]],"h":[]},"3067":{"s":[[null,"Place asparagus and cauliflower pieces plus 1 tablespoon water in a microwave-proof, covered dish. Microwave for 3 to 5 minutes to steam until tender crisp."],[null,"Sauté the onion until golden, about 7 minutes."],[null,"Add the garlic and cook, stirring, 1 minute longer."],[null,"Stir in the asparagus, cauliflower, egg substitute, parsley, salt, pepper, thyme and nutmeg."],[null,"Reduce heat and cook covered until set and browned on bottom, about 10 to 15 minutes."],[null,"Loosen the edges with a knife and invert onto a warm platter or serve directly from skillet."]],"h":[[null,"In Spain and South America, a tortilla is a round, unfolded omelet typically made with eggs, vegetables and seasonings. In comparison, the Mexican tortilla is thin, flat bread made from wheat flour or ground corn."]]},"6007691":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F."],[null,"Spray a baking sheet with cooking spray. In a small bowl, toss asparagus with olive oil. Place on baking sheet and bake in oven for about 12 minutes. Chop cooked asparagus into 1/2 inch pieces. Set aside."],[null,"In a medium bowl whisk together the egg substitutes, milk, salt, pepper and red pepper flakes. Set aside and prepare broiler."],[null,"Spray a 9 1/2-inch-diameter nonstick ovenproof skillet with cooking spray. Add margarine to skillet and melt over medium heat. Add asparagus to skillet and pour the egg mixture over the asparagus. Cook for a few minutes until the eggs start to set."],[null,"Add the mozzarella and Parmesan cheese. Reduce heat to medium-low and cook until the frittata is almost set but the top is still runny, about 2 minutes."],[null,"Place the skillet under the broiler. Broil until the top is set and golden brown on top, about 2-4 minutes. Let the frittata stand 2 minutes. Using a rubber spatula, loosen the frittata from skillet and slide the frittata onto a plate. Cut frittata into 6 equal slices and serve."]],"h":[]},"7007691":{"s":[[null,"Snap the ends off the asparagus where they naturally break then cut into large-ish chunks."],[null,"Finely chop the spring onion."],[null,"Beat the eggs together then season with black pepper to taste."],[null,"Spray a small frying pan with 1cal oil and place over a medium heat."],[null,"Fry the spring onion, and asparagus for a few minutes, until starting to soften."],[null,"Add spinach and cook a further few minutes until spinach has wilted."],[null,"Pour the beaten eggs into the pan, spread the asparagus evenly through the mixture and cook for around 5 mins, until the edges are starting to brown."],[null,"Remove the pan from the hob and place under a hot grill until the frittata starts to brown."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"9827404":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425℉/218℃ convection bake or roast if you have a roast setting, and line a large baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Combine all the marinade ingredients in a small bowl. Then add the prepared veggies and chickpeas to a large bowl and toss with the marinade. Arrange the veggies in a single layer on your baking sheet and roast for approximately 20-25 minutes, until golden brown."],[null,"Meanwhile, prepare your grain of choice. Cook the rice, quinoa, or grain of choice on the stovetop or in a rice cooker according to the package directions. (NOTE: Use broth instead of water to cook your grains for added flavour.)"],[null,"Serve your cooked grains in bowls with the veggies and chickpeas on top."]],"h":[]},"3167":{"s":[[null,"Set cream cheese out to soften."],[null,"Drain asparagus well."],[null,"Combine all ingredients in a food processor and process until blended. Remove to a bowl, cover and refrigerate overnight."],[null,"Serve spread with low-sodium crackers or make finger sandwiches."]],"h":[[null,"Canned asparagus may be replaced with fresh or frozen asparagus. Boil in water until asparagus is soft enough to mash with a fork."],[null,"This recipe may be made with diced cucumber instead of asparagus."]]},"9620307":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 375℉/190℃ and grease a 9\" pie plate or line it with parchment paper."],[null,"Chop your veggies and set aside. Use two cups of your favourite veggies."],[null,"Place all the remaining ingredients in a medium mixing bowl and whisk to combine. Then stir in the chopped veggies."],[null,"Transfer the mixture to your pie plate and smooth out the top with a silicone spatula. Bake for 30-35 minutes, until the edges are brown and the middle is set. A toothpick inserted in the middle should come out mostly clean, but not completely dry."],[null,"Remove from the oven and let cool for at least 15 minutes before slicing and serving. As the frittata cools it will further set and slice easier."]],"h":[[null,"You may use any veggies you like but don’t use more than 2 cups of chopped veggies ."],[null,"Do not overcook your frittata. For best results and texture, bake until a toothpick inserted in the middle comes out mostly clean, but NOT completely dry. It will continue to set as it cools."],[null,"Let the frittata rest at room temperature for at least 15 minutes (a little longer is better) before slicing and serving. The cool-down time will help your omelette firm up and make the texture, just right. 😉"],[null,"Leftovers keep refrigerated in a sealed container for 3-4 days. You may reheat or enjoy chilled."]]},"7256644":{"s":[[null,"Add the oil to a saucepan, then add the spring onions and the asparagus stems, but not the tips. Stir for 1 minute over a medium heat. In a separate pan, heat the stock and gently simmer."],[null,"Add the garlic and white pepper to the asparagus stems and spring onion. Stir for 1 minute, then add the rice. Stir for 2 minutes more, add roughly two ladles of stock, enough to just cover the rice, then stir again."],[null,"Whilst Regularly stirring the rice, add hot stock a little at a time, so the rice is just covered. The risotto should be bubbling very gently."],[null,"After 20 minutes, add any remaining stock, the peas and asparagus tips. Stir for 2–5 minutes, testing to make sure the rice is al dente (slightly firm)."],[null,"Vigorously stir in the crème fraiche, butter and cheese. Cover and allow to stand for 2 minutes, then serve."]],"h":[[null,"Use a heavy-based saucepan or casserole dish when making risotto, as you don't want it to burn during cooking."],[null,"Stir the rice continously whilst cooking in order to cook it evenly."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"4375436":{"s":[[null,"Using a sharp knife, cut kernels off to make 3 cups (scrape cobs with knife). Place 2½ cups of corn in blender with 2 cups of water."],[null,"Strain pureed corn through sieve in medium saucepan. Stir in remaining corn kernels, 1/3 cup sugar and 1 teaspoon vanilla. If desired, may also add 2 tablespoons honey with 1 tablespoon cinnamon and/or 1 teaspoon cocoa powder."],[null,"Boil over medium-high heat, then reduce and simmer 5 minutes or until lightly thickened."],[null,"Pour into a bowl, sprinkle with cinnamon, serve hot w/spoon (makes 4 servings)."],[null,"Garnish with a cinnamon stick, if desired."]],"h":[]},"7804832":{"s":[[null,"Mist a large pan with the spray and fry the onion over a medium heat for 6-8 minutes until soft. Add the garlic and ginger, cook for 1 minute, stir in the spices and cook for another minute."],[null,"Stir in the purée and cook for 1 minute, then add the aubergines, passata and stock. Bring to a simmer and cook for 25 minutes, adding the chickpeas for the final 5. Stir in the yogurt, lime zest and juice and coriander."],[null,"Add the cooked rice to the bowls, and top with the curry, the extra yogurt and coriander, serving the limes on the side."]],"h":[]},"5181037":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a pan over a medium heat."],[null,"Add the aubergine, onion and garlic to the pan and sauté for 5 minutes or until soft."],[null,"Add the cumin, turmeric and chickpeas to the pan and stir."],[null,"Pour the Renastep and water into the pan, stir well and allow to warm gently."],[null,"Simmer for about 15-20 minutes, until the aubergine is fully cooked and soft."],[null,"Using a hand blender, blend the soup to the desired consistency."],[null,"Serve warm in a bowl."]],"h":[[null,"Chickpeas could be swapped for beans or lentils if this is advised by your dietitian. Garnish with mint or caramelised onion."],["Renastep note","Renastep is a Food for Special Medical Purposes and must be used under medical supervision. Renastep is a ready to use feed for the dietary management of kidney disease from 3 years of age onwards. Renastep contains milk and fish. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information. This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease."]]},"7879167":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas mark 4. Grill the aubergines and courgettes until lightly browned on each side."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the oil to a pan with the onion, stirring occasionally for 5 minutes. Next, add the red pepper, stirring regularly for another 5 minutes."],[null,"Mix in the garlic, oregano and tomatoes, and simmer for 5 minutes."],[null,"Add some of the sauce to an ovenproof dish, top with aubergine and courgette slices, then add more sauce and sprinkle with Parmesan cheese. Repeat until the final layer of aubergine and courgette, then top with the remaining sauce, Parmesan and, finally, the mozzarella slices."],[null,"Bake in the oven for 30–40 minutes until golden brown."],[null,"Serve with a grind of black pepper, salad, gluten-free pasta or polenta to keep the dish gluten-free."]],"h":[[null,"For a vegetarian alternative to Parmesan, swap it out with vegetarian-style hard cheese."],[null,"You can assemble this dish, refrigerate it and bake it later – or the next day. You can even freeze it and cook when needed."],[null,"You can swap Parmesan cheese with Grana Padano, which is slightly cheaper and tastes just as good."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Portion for freezing. Defrost in the microwave, then reheat in the microwave or covered in foil in a moderate oven. Reheat until piping hot."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"7151148":{"s":[[null,"Tip the lentils into a large saucepan with the tomatoes and 500ml water. Bring to the boil and simmer gently for 20-25 minutes, stirring every now and then, until the lentils are tender."],[null,"While the lentils are simmering, spray a large, non-stick frying pan with a couple of pumps of cooking spray and put over a medium-high heat. Add the aubergines, fry for 5-6 minutes until browned all over, then add to the lentils – you may need to do this in a few batches."],[null,"Turn down the heat under the frying pan to medium and gently fry the onion for 5-6 minutes. Stir in the ginger, garlic, cumin and chilli powder (if using) with a splash of water. Fry for 2-3 minutes."],[null,"Scrape the onion mixture into the lentils, and add the chickpeas, lemon juice, spinach and garam masala. Simmer for 5 minutes until thickened slightly. Season with pepper and spoon into bowls. Scatter over the coriander."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"7570891":{"s":[[null,"Heat 1 tsp of oil in a large saucepan and sauté the onion for 4–5 minutes over a low heat. Stir in the garlic and cook for 2 minutes, stirring continuously. Add the chopped tomatoes, tomato purée, and oregano. Bring to the boil, cover, and simmer for 25 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, preheat the oven to 200°C/180°C fan oven/gas 6. Cover a couple of baking sheets with foil. Thinly slice the aubergines lengthways and arrange in a single layer on the baking sheets. Drizzle with the remaining olive oil and sprinkle with the dried herbs and paprika. Bake for 25 minutes."],[null,"Spread some of the tomato sauce around the base of a 2 litre ovenproof dish and add a layer of baked aubergines. Scatter over half the mozzarella and a few fresh basil leaves. Repeat. Cover with the remaining sauce."],[null,"Mix together the Parmesan cheese and almond flour and scatter over the top. Bake for 20 minutes until bubbling. Scatter with fresh basil leaves and serve with a mixed green salad."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 5"]]},"7422719":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/ gas mark 4."],[null,"Scoop the flesh out of the aubergines, chop, and reserve. Place the aubergine skin-side down onto a baking tray and bake for 15 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, add oil to a pan, then add the onion and cook for 3-4 minutes. Add the mushrooms and chopped aubergine flesh, then cook for a further 5 minutes."],[null,"Add the garlic, canned tomatoes and oregano, mix well, cover and simmer for 5 minutes.Next, add the borlotti beans and spinach and cook for 2 minutes."],[null,"Remove the aubergines from the oven and fill with the bean and vegetable mixture, then place in an ovenproof dish."],[null,"Scatter with tofu, return to the oven and bake for 20 minutes. Top with the sliced mozzarella and bake for a further 20 minutes."],[null,"Remove from the oven and scatter with chopped tomato, spring onion and basil to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Once the aubergines are stuffed, you can pop them in the fridge, and bake when as needed."],[null,"Use a non-dairy cheese alternative for a vegan version."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 5"]]},"7398904":{"s":[[null,"Boil the potato for 8-10 mins until tender, drain, mash and set aside."],[null,"Cut the aubergine into 1cm cubes. Spray a non-stick frying pan with olive oil and add the aubergine, onion and garlic. Cover and cook over a low/medium heat for 15 mins, stirring occasionally. Remove lid and cook for 5 mins."],[null,"Tip into a food processor and pulse for 5 secs to chop finely but not blend; the meatballs are nicer with a little texture. Spoon into a bowl, add the potato, zest, chilli and rosemary and mix well. Divide and roll into 12 balls. Scatter the sesame seeds on a plate and roll each ball in the seeds to coat. Chill for 10 mins to firm up."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 180C/gas 4. Put the balls in an ovenproof dish, spray lightly with oil and cook for 20-25 mins until crisp."],[null,"Meanwhile make the sauce. Heat a small frying pan and cook the onion in the oil over a low heat until soft. Add the tomatoes, vinegar and sugar, cover and simmer for 10 mins, stirring occasionally."],[null,"Meanwhile, cut each courgette lengthways into 5mm slices. Spray on both sides with a little 1cal sunflower oil and cook on a griddle for 4-5 mins each side until charred and softened. Slice into thin strips, divide between the serving plates, top with the sauce and aubergine balls and serve."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"1788":{"s":[[null,"Marinate steak in shallow dish with juice of 2 limes, lemon pepper and garlic powder, from 30 minutes to overnight."],[null,"Finely chop cilantro; dice onion and garlic. Make salsa by mixing cilantro, onion, garlic and juice of 1 lime. Cover and refrigerate."],[null,"Heat 2 tablespoons oil over medium high heat. Slice steak thinly and cook until well done, approximately 3 minutes per side."],[null,"Preheat oven to 350º F."],[null,"Place equal amounts of cooked steak, about 1-1/2 ounces, in each flour tortilla."],[null,"Top each taco with one tablespoon crumbled queso fresco."],[null,"Wrap each taco in aluminum foil and bake 5 to 8 minutes or until tortillas are warm."],[null,"Remove from oven. Top each taco with salsa and enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Find queso fresco at a Mexican grocery store or substitute1/4 cup Monterrey Jack cheese. Add 1/2 tablespoon per taco."],[null,"Compare brands and buy the lowest sodium tortillas."],[null,"To be more diabetes friendly, be sure to trim as much fat as you can. You may also leave off the cheese to reduce fat. This will decrease the saturated fat."]]},"3693":{"s":[[null,"Cook orzo according to package instructions, omitting salt."],[null,"Core and dice apple. Chop basil."],[null,"In a medium bowl, add all the ingredients except the almonds. Combine until well incorporated."],[null,"Transfer the mixture to a serving dish and chill in the refrigerator for 30 minutes. Sprinkle with the almonds before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Three-fourths cup orzo makes 2 cups when cooked."],[null,"Fuji, gala and red delicious apples taste great in this salad."]]},"2035":{"s":[[null,"Combine raisins and 1/4 cup hot water; let stand 5 minutes. Drain and set aside."],[null,"Prepare quick-cooking wild rice according to package directions. Remove pan from heat and set aside."],[null,"Chop apples, celery and bell pepper. Shred carrot."],[null,"Coat a large nonstick skillet with cooking spray; place over a medium-high heat until hot. Add apple, celery, green pepper and carrot; sauté until crisp-tender. Remove skillet from heat and set aside."],[null,"Combine 1-1/2 cups reduced-sodium chicken broth, sage and pepper in a large saucepan; bring to a boil. Stir in converted rice. Cover, reduce heat and simmer 20 minutes or until rice is tender and liquid is absorbed."],[null,"Remove pan from heat; stir in reserved raisins, wild rice, apple mixture and juice of 1 lemon. Cover and let stand 5 minutes."],[null,"Transfer to a serving bowl. Garnish with a fresh sage sprig, if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Divide leftover rice into single servings, place in small freezer bags and freeze. To reheat for a quick meal later, microwave for 1-2 minutes or place freezer bag in a pot of boiling water for a few minutes."],[null,"If quick-cooking wild rice is unavailable prepare regular wild rice as follows: Rinse wild rice in 3 changes of hot water; drain. Combine wild rice and 1-1/2 cups water in a medium saucepan. Bring to a boil; cover, reduce heat and simmer 50 minutes or until rice is tender and liquid is absorbed."]]},"6350887":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, combine the black beans, diced avocado, corn kernels, diced tomatoes, finely chopped red onion, chopped fresh cilantro, and finely chopped jalapeño."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the lime juice, extra-virgin olive oil, ground cumin, salt, and black pepper."],[null,"Pour the dressing over the salad and toss gently to ensure even coating."],[null,"Allow the salad to marinate in the refrigerator for 10 minutes to let the flavors meld."],[null,"Before serving, toss the salad once more. Top with fresh cilantro if desired."]],"h":[]},"6207672":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, combine the drained and rinsed chickpeas, diced avocados, diced cucumber, cherry tomatoes, and feta."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the olive oil, lemon juice, minced garlic, and black pepper."],[null,"Pour the dressing over the avocado and chickpea salad. Toss the salad gently to ensure even coating."],[null,"Serve on a bed of mixed greens."]],"h":[]},"6237124":{"s":[[null,"Start by preparing the avocado spread. Cut the ripe avocado in half, remove the pit, and scoop the flesh into a bowl. Mash it with a fork and season with 1/8 teaspoon salt. You can also add a dash of hot sauce if desired."],[null,"Heat a non-stick skillet over medium heat and use cooking spray."],[null,"While the skillet is heating, toast the slices of whole grain bread until they are golden brown."],[null,"In the heated skillet, crack the eggs and cook them to your preference (e.g., fried, scrambled, or poached). Season with 1/8 teaspoon salt and pepper to taste. If you prefer your eggs with runny yolks, cook them for about 2–3 minutes sunny side up or a bit longer for over easy."],[null,"Assemble the toast. Spread the mashed avocado on each slice of toasted bread and add a layer of sliced tomatoes on top. Place the cooked eggs on the tomato slices. Sprinkle black pepper over the top if desired."]],"h":[]},"9811020":{"s":[[null,"Add all the ingredients except the water to a blender and process until smooth. Add the water if a thinner consistency is preferred and reblend."],[null,"Store in an air-tight container or jar in the refrigerator for up to 1 week."]],"h":[[null,"For a smoother, creamier texture with consistent colour , use a high-speed blender and process until completely pureed. If you prefer to see bits of herbs throughout , use a food processor to finely process all the ingredients first ( without the liquids ). Then add the liquid ingredients and pulse to combine. Store your dressing in a CLEAN glass jar or airtight container. Keep refrigerated for up to 1 week."]]},"9556376":{"s":[[null,"Add the avocados, pickled jalapenos with their juices, sunflower seeds and garlic powder to your food processor bowl and process until smooth."],[null,"Taste the mixture, and add lime juice for extra tang and salt + pepper if desired."],[null,"Enjoy with crackers, tortilla chips, pita chips, and raw veggie sticks."]],"h":[[null,"Taste the dip before adding the lime juice . Depending on how much pickling liquid is in your jar of jalapenos, you may or may not need/want more tang."],[null,"Leftovers keep in the fridge for 3-4 days in an airtight container or freeze them for up to 3 months."]]},"6381004":{"s":[[null,"In a blender or food processor, puree all ingredients until smooth. Add more water if you would like a thinner dressing."],[null,"Store in a jar with a tight fitting lid or other airtight container in the fridge for up to 7 days."]],"h":[]},"9379335":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your griddle over medium heat. Then mash the banana and avocado into a medium mixing bowl and pour in the milk. Mix well."],[null,"Next, add the flour, sugar and baking powder. Then stir until combined without overmixing."],[null,"Ladle your batter on your preheated griddle, making pancakes roughly 4 inches in diameter. Cook for 4-5 minutes until the edges are golden brown and there are several bubbles on top."],[null,"Then flip and continue cooking until the pancakes are cooked through."]],"h":[[null,"Weigh your flour for the most accurate results . Scooping from a bag often results in too much flour being used due to compacting the flour into the measuring cup."],[null,"If you do not have a kitchen scale , spoon the flour into your measuring cup and scrape off the top with a knife, but do not scoop from the bag."],[null,"Use fresh, active baking powder . Baking powder that has been opened and sitting in the pantry for several months can start to lose its effectiveness."],[null,"No need to overmix your pancake batter . If there are a few lumps, that's perfectly fine. Just mix until combined and no floury bits remain."],[null,"Preheat your pan or griddle. It should be hot before pouring your pancake batter to prevent sticking and for even cooking."],[null,"Use medium heat to cook your pancakes . Although your pan should be hot, that doesn't mean you should use high heat. This may result in uneven cooking, with crisp outsides and mushy middles."],[null,"Flip your pancakes ONCE when the edges are golden brown and have several bubbles on top. Flipping too often can cause them to deflate and make a denser pancake texture."],[null,"Leftovers keep in the fridge for 2-3 days or frozen for up to 3 months."]]},"3593":{"s":[[null,"Toast the bread slices. Chop the parsley and set aside."],[null,"Remove half an avocado from the skin and mash with a fork. Combine with lime juice and salt. Spread the mixture onto each piece of toast."],[null,"Spray a skillet with cooking spray and heat over medium heat. Crack the eggs into the skillet and cook to desired doneness."],[null,"Slide eggs from the skillet onto the top of the avocado on each toast. Top each egg with 1 tablespoon feta cheese, chopped parsley and ground black pepper."]],"h":[[null,"Avocados are high in potassium. By limiting the amount to 1/4th of a medium avocado (approximately 1/4 cup) you can still include it on a kidney diet when potassium levels are well controlled. Ask your dietitian for individual guidance."]]},"6210590":{"s":[[null,"Coat a medium skillet with nonstick cooking spray and place it over medium heat until hot. Add the turkey bacon and cook until crispy, 8 minutes, flipping the slices over halfway through. Transfer the bacon to a paper towel–lined plate."],[null,"Scoop out the flesh from each avocado half onto a slice of toasted bread. Mash the avocado with a fork until flattened. Sprinkle with sea salt and black pepper."],[null,"Top each avocado toast with 1 slice of turkey bacon and half of the tomato slices."]],"h":[]},"6112057":{"s":[[null,"Remove the pit from the avocado. Use a spoon to scoop out the insides of the avocado and place it in a medium bowl. Mash the avocado with a fork or potato masher. Add the pico de gallo and mix well."],[null,"Add the tuna to the bowl and mix well. Serve the tuna salad with your choice of whole-wheat crackers, whole-wheat pitas or lettuce wraps."]],"h":[]},"6384200":{"s":[],"h":[]},"7424176":{"s":[[null,"Put the nuts in a sealable bag and crush them with a rolling pin."],[null,"Toast the bread."],[null,"Remove the stone and skin from the avocado, then peel the banana. Place both in a bowl."],[null,"Using the back of a fork, mash the banana and avocado together into a mush, then stir in the nuts, reserving a few to sprinkle on top."],[null,"Spread the mixture over the toast and sprinkle with a few nuts. Or slice the toast into fingers and dip the slices like soldiers."]],"h":[[null,"You can use gluten-free bread or dip sticks of carrot, celery or sweet peppers instead."],[null,"Try using other nuts such as almonds or walnuts, or a mixture of sunflower and pumpkin seeds."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6661374":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6106256":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6006273":{"s":[[null,"In a medium bowl, mash the avocado with a fork until the desired consistency (slightly chunky or smooth)."],[null,"Finely chop the pickling cucumber or peel, seed, and finely chop the regular cucumber. (You should get about 1/3 cup.) Stir the cucumber and remaining ingredients into the avocado. Spread over sandwich thin to serve immediately or cover and refrigerate for up to 8 hours."],[null,"Cook’s Tip: Store leftover avocado by sprinkling the exposed surface with fresh lemon juice, lime juice, or white vinegar. Cover it tightly with plastic wrap or place in an airtight container and refrigerate. It should keep for 1-2 days."]],"h":[]},"6132615":{"s":[[null,"Toast one slice of wholegrain bread until it’s as crisp as you like."],[null,"Mash the 1/2 of an avocado lightly with a fork and spread it over the toast."],[null,"Lay the sliced 1/2 tomato on top."],[null,"Serve right away."]],"h":[]},"6779546":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, combine all ingredients and mix well to distribute. Shape into 6 patties."],[null,"Preheat grill to medium high and place burgers on grill grate. Cook under direct heat (with the grill closed) for 5-6 minutes per side until cooked through to doneness."]],"h":[]},"5136754":{"s":[[null,"Preheat an oven to 220°C/435°F/Gas mark 7"],[null,"Place the halved aubergine flesh side down on a roasting tin and drizzle with ½ the oil. Cook for 15 -20 minutes or until the skin has charred."],[null,"Peel the charred skin from the aubergine and place the flesh into a bowl and allow to cool."],[null,"Once cooled, squeeze most of the water from the aubergine and discard."],[null,"Put the cooked aubergine into a food processor and add all the other ingredients."],[null,"Blend until smooth, serve and enjoy!"]],"h":[]},"6251709":{"s":[[null,"Soak the artichokes in water to clean. Drain and repeat until the water is clear. Peel away the outside leaves of the bottom half of the artichokes, then cut off the top quarter of the artichokes. If tough, dark-green leaves remain, peel those as well. At this point, the artichoke should look like a flower, and the tough, dark leaves should all be removed, leaving only lighter-colored, more tender leaves."],[null,"Add the juice of 1 lemon to a bowl full of cold water, then place the artichokes in the lemon water to prevent discoloration."],[null,"Bring a large pot of water to a boil. Remove the artichokes from the bowl, discarding the lemon water, and add them to the pot."],[null,"Bring the water back to a boil over high heat, then reduce the heat to medium-low and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes, or until tender. Drain the artichokes and set aside."],[null,"Place the remaining lemon juice, the olive oil, and mustard in a blender. Blend together to form a vinaigrette."],[null,"Stir in the pepper, mint, dill, and parsley, and pour the dressing over the artichokes. Serve warm or at room temperature."]],"h":[]},"7743074":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200ºC/gas mark 6. Prick the skin of each potato several time and place on a baking sheet. Bake for 35-40 minutes until cooked through."],[null,"Mix the fromage frais and horseradish together."],[null,"Cut into the top of each potato with a sharp knife and squeeze it to open it out."],[null,"Spoon a little of the fromage frais horseradish mixture into each potato. Top each with a little beef, sprinkle with chives and serve."]],"h":[[null,"You can make these canapé size or quite substantial depending on the size of potato."],[null,"If you are having a party, bake the potatoes and make all your fillings, then simply give the potatoes 10 minutes in the over before needed, fill and serve."],[null,"You can experiment with all sorts of fillings - from poached/tinned salmon, to sautéed mushrooms, or spinach and goat's cheese."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"6180969":{"s":[[null,"Stir the sour cream, cream cheese, pepper sauce and salt together until well blended."],[null,"Let stand at least 10 minutes to develop flavors and mellow slightly. Serve with carrots"]],"h":[]},"6251444":{"s":[[null,"Bring the water to a boil in a medium saucepan. Add the quinoa and cook until most of the liquid is absorbed. Loosely cover, reduce the heat to low, and cook until the quinoa is fully cooked, about 20 minutes. Rinse under cold running water; drain and transfer to a large bowl."],[null,"Add the kale, apple, onion, cheese, and pumpkin seeds."],[null,"Whisk together the vinegar, oil, and salt in a small bowl. Add the dressing to the quinoa mixture and toss until well mixed."]],"h":[]},"2055":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven or toaster oven to 350° F. Spray a small baking dish with cooking spray."],[null,"Break bagel into small pieces and place in baking dish."],[null,"Mix together almond milk, egg product, sugar and cinnamon together, then pour over bagel pieces. Set aside for a few minutes until the bagels absorb the liquid."],[null,"Bake for 30 minutes or until browned on top. Serve warm or cold. Add whipped topping if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Medium sized bagels weigh 2 ounces each."]]},"1944":{"s":[[null,"Slice the bagel in half and toast one half in a toaster or oven."],[null,"Chop the scallions, dill and basil leaves. Mix with the cream cheese."],[null,"Spread cream cheese mixture on the toasted bagel half then top with arugula and tomato slice."],[null,"Heat a frying pan, spray with nonstick spray and scramble the egg."],[null,"Reheat the salmon in the same frying pan while egg is cooking."],[null,"Place the egg and salmon on top of the tomato slice. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"This is a great way to use up leftover salmon the day after cooking."],[null,"Bagel choices include plain, egg, rye, pumpernickel, onion or wheat."],[null,"Nutrient analysis based on 1/2 of a 4-ounce bagel. For a lower carb sandwich select a 2-ounce bagel."],[null,"Arugula can be replaced with fresh spinach leaves, lettuce or micro-greens."]]},"3802558":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oven to 180°C / 160°C/ gas mark 4. Using an apple corer, core the apples and make the opening slightly larger for filling."],[null,"Mix the softened butter, blueberries and sugar until combined, and then stuff into the four apple cavities."],[null,"Put the apples into a small roasting dish and add 4 tablespoons of water into dish."],[null,"Bake for 25-30 minutes, depending on size of the apples, until they are soft and caramelised. Serve with a drizzle of double cream or soya vanilla ice cream."]],"h":[["Chef's note","This baked apple dessert is lovely after you've eaten your Sunday roast."],["Carbohydrate","The main sources of carbohydrate in this dish are the apples and sugar. Carbohydrate values have been provided for those trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","Following the quantities provided, this dessert is low in potassium and phosphate, so you can enjoy it as a special treat when following dietary restrictions."],["Protein","This dessert is low in protein so can be enjoyed as an occasional treat if following a low protein diet."],["Vegan","Use vegan butter and either vegan double cream or soya ice cream."],["Healthier option","This recipe is high in fat, provided by the butter and cream. To reduce the fat, replace the butter with a reduced fat spread or use less of the butter (for example, use half the amount). You could also replace the cream with a half-fat crème fraiche or a plain soya yoghurt."],["Storage","This recipe is best eaten fresh."],["Tips","The apples can be prepared the day before. Just cover them and chill in the fridge until ready to bake."]]},"6217938":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200 degrees F. Lay the parchment paper on one large or two medium baking sheets."],[null,"Using a mandolin or knife, thinly slice the apples to make round chips. Discard the seeds."],[null,"Lay the apple slices on the prepared baking sheets without overlapping. Sprinkle the cinnamon over apples."],[null,"Bake for 1 hour, then flip the apples. Continue baking for 1-2 hours, flipping occasionally, until the apple slices are no longer moist. Let cool completely and then store in airtight container."]],"h":[]},"6297358":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F. Cover a 9x9 inch baking dish with parchment paper."],[null,"Place apple slices in the prepared baking dish, drizzle with syrup, and sprinkle with cinnamon and nutmeg."],[null,"Stir to evenly coat the apples."],[null,"Bake for 25 to 30 minutes or until the apples are tender. Serve warm."]],"h":[]},"6905037":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 400 degrees F. Line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"In a bowl, whisk together tomato sauce, apple cider vinegar, Dijon mustard, honey, smoked paprika, garlic powder, onion powder, coarse salt, and black pepper."],[null,"Set aside half of the BBQ sauce for later use."],[null,"Place the chicken tenders in a resealable plastic bag or shallow dish."],[null,"Pour the other half of the BBQ sauce mixture over the chicken tenders. Seal the bag or cover the dish and let the chicken marinate in the refrigerator for at least 30 minutes."],[null,"Arrange the chicken tenders on the prepared baking sheet."],[null,"Bake in the preheated oven for about 20 minutes or until the chicken is cooked through, flipping halfway through."],[null,"Serve with remaining BBQ sauce."]],"h":[]},"6994243":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). Grease or line a 9x5-inch loaf pan."],[null,"Spread the almonds on a rimmed baking sheet. Toast in the oven for 5–8 minutes, until lightly browned and fragrant."],[null,"In a medium bowl, whisk together the eggs, almond milk, vanilla, and sugar free brown sugar alternative until smooth and creamy."],[null,"In a large bowl, stir together the chia seeds, flaxseed, rolled oats, hemp hearts, almond flour, cinnamon, baking powder, and salt."],[null,"Pour the wet mixture into the dry ingredients and stir until fully combined. The batter will thicken slightly as the chia and flax seeds absorb the liquid."],[null,"Gently fold in the blueberries."],[null,"Spread the mixture evenly in the prepared loaf pan. Bake for 30–35 minutes, turning the pan halfway through, until the center is set and the top is lightly golden and beginning to crack."],[null,"Let the oatmeal cool for 10 minutes before slicing into 6 equal portions. Serve warm, topped with ¼ cup low-fat Greek yogurt and 1 tablespoon slivered almonds per serving. Wrap cooled leftovers and store in the refrigerator."]],"h":[]},"3967979":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 175°C / 155°C fan / gas mark 4. Line a 23cm round spring-form tin with greaseproof paper, smoothing out the edges. Crush the digestive biscuits into fine crumbs, melt 40g of the unsalted butter and mix together. Press the crumb mix firmly into the base of the tin."],[null,"Cream the remaining 150g unsalted butter and the caster sugar together, add in the cream cheese and beat until fluffy. Stir in the cornflour."],[null,"Beat in the eggs, cream and elderflower cordial. Mix well and pour the mixture into the tin. Press the blueberries into the mix so that they are evenly distributed and just under the surface."],[null,"Bake in the oven for one hour. Allow to cool, then rest in the fridge overnight to settle. Remove from the fridge, wait 30 minutes before removing from the tin and sieve over a little icing sugar to decorate."]],"h":[["Chef's note","Try this deliciously indulgent cheesecake. Make the day ahead so it’s perfect to serve for dessert when you have friends over. You can also freeze in portions for an occasional treat."],["Carbohydrate","The main source of carbohydrate in this dish comes from the sugar, digestive biscuits, cornflour and cordial. The carbohydrate values have been provided for those who have trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","Cream cheeses, tend to be lower in phosphate than hard cheeses but as this recipe uses a large quantity of cream cheese it is high in phosphate. If you have been prescribed a phosphate binder, ensure you take them with this dish.\nBlueberries are a low potassium fruit that add colour and flavour to this dessert. By sticking to the recommended portion size in the recipe it keeps the overall potassium content low."],["Protein","The cheese and eggs are great sources of protein, ideal if you are on dialysis but may not be suitable if you have been advised to follow a lower protein diet."],["Gluten free","Use gluten-free digestive biscuits."],["Healthier option","Cheesecakes are high in fat and sugar and should be kept for special occasions or as a treat. If you want to reduce the amount of sugar or fat in this recipe, you can use a low fat spread in place of the butter, choose reduced-sugar digestives (if available) or use a sugar free/no added sugar cordial."],["Cheaper option","A cheaper option is use frozen blueberries but don’t thaw them before use."],["Storage","Store in an airtight container in the fridge and eat within two days. You can easily freeze this cheesecake for up to 2 months. Cover tightly and freeze in portions. Thaw overnight in the refrigerator before serving."]]},"4736759":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350°F. Grease an 8 × 8-inch baking dish."],[null,"In a large bowl, whisk together the milk, applesauce, almond butter, honey, oil, and vanilla extract until smooth. Whisk in the baking soda and cream of tartar."],[null,"Using a spatula, stir in the oats, sliced almonds, and 1/2 cup blueberries until evenly combined."],[null,"Pour the mixture into the prepared baking dish and smooth the top."],[null,"Sprinkle the topping evenly over the top."],[null,"Bake for 50–60 minutes, until set, golden, and the topping is crisp. Remove from the oven and let cool for about 1 hour. Cut into 8 squares and serve with cottage cheese (optional)."]],"h":[[null,"Tip: Enjoy warm or cold, for breakfast or as a snack."],[null,"* For Transplant: Reduce overall fat by using 1% milk or fat-free dairy products."],["Plan ahead breakfast","Starting the day off right with a healthy breakfast is important when you have chronic kidney disease (CKD). Eating a morning meal gives you nutrients to stay energized for work, school, or other daily activities. Certain choices such as baked goods, breakfast meats, milk-based smoothies, and packaged meals can be expensive and high in sodium, potassium, or phosphorus. Choosing convenient, healthy alternatives that support CKD nutrition goals is essential. Planning ahead can help you make more budget-friendly breakfasts. Selecting a protein food is a helpful first step when planning breakfast. Eggs are a nutrient-dense option and can be used in quiches, omelets with low potassium vegetables, or baked into French toast or oatmeal. Homemade freezer burritos prepared in advance offer another quick option that heats up easily on a busy morning. Low-sodium cottage cheese can also be an option, as a ½ cup serving provides approximately 13 grams of protein. Cottage cheese can be paired with low-potassium peaches or pears, used to complement baked oatmeal, or included in pancake or muffin recipes. Hot cereal, such as oatmeal or cream of wheat, are additional quick and easy breakfast choices. Larger batches can be cooked and then frozen into individual portions for convenience. To add protein, top hot cereal with an ounce of nuts or 1 tablespoon of peanut, almond, or cashew butter."]]},"3365":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F and prepare an 8 x 8-inch baking pan by greasing with butter or cooking spray."],[null,"Melt the butter."],[null,"In a large bowl mix together oats, almond milk, eggs, brown sugar, butter, baking powder, vanilla and cinnamon. Add the blueberries and undrained diced peaches and stir to combine."],[null,"Spread mixture evenly into the prepared baking dish and bake for 30 to 40 minutes until set."],[null,"Cool slightly. Cut into squares and serve warm."]],"h":[[null,"Baked squares can be frozen for a quick and easy breakfast. Heat in the microwave for a minute or until heated."],[null,"For a low sugar version replace brown sugar with low-calorie sweetener and use fresh peaches. Carbohydrates are reduced to 24 grams per serving."]]},"2429":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Bring water to a boil. Add pasta and undercook by 2 minutes."],[null,"In a separate covered pot, steam broccoli and cauliflower florets for 5 minutes or until tender. Remove and set aside. Discard liquid from pot."],[null,"Finely chop onion and garlic clove."],[null,"Using the same pot, over medium heat, melt 3 tablespoons butter then add onion and garlic. Sauté for 3-4 minutes, until tender. Add flour and whisk for one minute. Whisk in rice drink and season with pepper and nutmeg. Stir until thickened, then stir in the spicy mustard."],[null,"Mix all three cheeses together. Add 2/3 of the combined cheeses to the sauce and stir until cheese is melted."],[null,"Drain pasta. Add cauliflower and broccoli then stir in the cheese sauce."],[null,"Spray a 9” x 12” baking pan with nonstick cooking spray and pour in the pasta mixture. Top with the remaining combined cheeses."],[null,"Place baking pan in the oven on top of a baking sheet to catch bubble over. After 30 minutes of baking, increase heat to 400° F. Sauté remaining 1 tablespoon butter with 1 cup panko bread crumbs and add to top of casserole. Cook additional 8 to 10 minutes until bread crumbs are browned."]],"h":[[null,"Steps 2 through 8 of this casserole can be done ahead of time. Cool completely, covered and refrigerated for a make-ahead meal."],[null,"If desired, Gruyère cheese can be used in place of Swiss cheese."],[null,"Rice Dream Classic original rice drink is low in phosphorus and potassium. Always read labels on milk substitute products and avoid those with phosphate additives."]]},"6374972":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350 degrees. Coat an 8x8-inch baking dish with cooking spray."],[null,"Place cauliflower florets, chicken broth, Smart Balance, salt and pepper into a large soup pot over high heat until liquid starts to boil. Reduce to a simmer, cover and steam for 10-12 minutes or until cauliflower is completely tender when poked with a fork."],[null,"Using an immersion blender or food processor, blend the cauliflower mixture until smooth. Fold in two Tbsp. chopped parsley."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine the remaining two Tbsp. parsley with the grated cheese."],[null,"Pour the pureed cauliflower into the prepared baking dish. Sprinkle the top with cheese and parsley mixture and bake for 5-7 minutes or until cheese is melted and starting to brown around the edges."]],"h":[]},"7181351":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200°C/180°C fan oven/gas 6. Bring a large pan of water to the boil. Add the juice from 1 lime. Blanch the cauliflower for 4 minutes. Drain well and set aside."],[null,"Place a large heatproof roasting tin over a low heat. Add the rapeseed oil and heat gently. Add the black mustard seeds and sizzle for 40–50 seconds until they pop. Add the ginger, garlic, chilli, red pepper and turmeric and cook stirring constantly for 2 minutes. Pour over the coconut milk and bring to the boil. Arrange the cauliflower in the roasting tin and spoon over some of the sauce. Roast for 20 minutes. Baste again with sauce and scatter the black beans into the sauce and stir well. Return to the oven for 5 minutes."],[null,"Squeeze over the remaining lime juice and scatter over the coriander before serving."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"6605632":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 200 degrees F and line two baking sheets with parchment paper. You can also lightly grease the parchment paper with cooking spray to prevent sticking."],[null,"Wash and core the apples, removing the seeds and stems. You can leave the peel on for added texture and nutrients. Using a mandoline slicer or a sharp knife, thinly slice the apples into rounds, aiming for slices of about 1/8-inch thickness. Make sure they are consistently thin for even baking."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix the ground cinnamon, ground cardamom, ground ginger, ground cloves, and ground nutmeg to create a chai spice blend."],[null,"Lay out the apple slices on the prepared baking sheets in a single layer, ensuring they do not overlap. Sprinkle the chai spice blend evenly over the apple slices. You can use your fingers or a shaker to distribute the spices evenly."],[null,"Place the baking sheets in the preheated oven and bake for about 2 hours. You'll want to check the apple chips occasionally to prevent overcooking. The chips are done when they become crisp but not burnt. They will become even crispier as they cool."]],"h":[]},"6054285":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 200 degrees F. Line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Peel the bananas and slice them into thin rounds, approximately 1/8- to ¼-inch thick. Place the banana slices in a bowl and toss them with lemon juice to prevent browning and adds a touch of tartness."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix the ground cinnamon, ground cardamom, ground ginger, ground cloves, and ground nutmeg to create a chai spice blend."],[null,"Sprinkle the chai spice blend over the banana slices, ensuring they are well coated with the aromatic spices. Arrange the banana slices on the prepared baking sheet in a single layer, making sure they do not overlap."],[null,"Bake in the preheated oven for about 2 hours, or until the banana chips are crispy and golden brown. Flip the chips halfway through the baking time to ensure even crispiness."],[null,"Keep an eye on the banana chips towards the end of the baking time to prevent burning. The exact baking time may vary depending on your oven and the thickness of the slices. They will continue to crisp up as they cool."],[null,"Store the banana chips in an airtight container at room temperature after allowing to cool completely."]],"h":[]},"6289072":{"s":[[null,"Add the chicken breasts and chicken broth to a large sauce pan over high heat. Bring to boiling, then reduce heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes, until the chicken is cooked through. Remove the pan from the heat and let the chicken cool to the touch in the broth (about 20 minutes)."],[null,"Shred the chicken into small pieces and mix in 2 Tbsp. of the chicken broth from the pan; set aside."],[null,"Add the oil to a sauté pan over medium heat. Add the onion, paprika, cumin, chili powder, and 1/2 cup of the chicken broth. Reduce the heat to low and cook for 10 to 15 minutes, until onions are soft and clear, and the liquid is evaporated. Stir in the chicken to yield 2 cups of filling."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F. Coat a large baking sheet with cooking spray."],[null,"Separate the whole wheat pizza dough into 16 golf-ball size pieces, and roll each one into a smooth ball."],[null,"Using a rolling pin, roll each ball of dough into a 6-inch-diameter circle."],[null,"Spoon 2 Tbsp. of the filling into the middle of the circle and press 1 olive into the middle of the filling. Lightly brush with water the bottom edge of the dough along one half of the circle. Fold the top half of the dough over the filling to form a semi-circle, and press edges firmly together. Crimp the edges with a fork to seal in the filling. Place the empanadas on a baking sheet."],[null,"Lightly beat the egg with the 1 Tbsp. water and brush a thin layer of the mixture over the top surface of each empanada."],[null,"Bake the empanadas for 20 minutes, until lightly browned."]],"h":[]},"3561":{"s":[[null,"Boil chicken breasts until cooked through. Drain."],[null,"Dice chicken. Measure 2 cups to use in the recipe."],[null,"Drain and rinse mushrooms."],[null,"In a mixing bowl, combine all ingredients except for chow mein noodles. Mix well."],[null,"Place in a greased 9″ x 9″ baking dish. Sprinkle noodles on top."],[null,"Bake at 350° F for 30 minutes."],[null,"Slice into 6 equal portions and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Makes a nice entrée for brunch."],[null,"Use fat-free sour cream, fat-free mayonnaise and low-fat chow mein noodles to lower fat to 3 grams and calories to 150 per serving."],[null,"Sodium varies between brands. Compare labels and choose the lowest sodium brand of mushrooms, mayonnaise, water chestnuts and chow mein noodles."],[null,"Try this dish hot or cold."]]},"2294":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Rinse chicken and remove giblets from inside cavity. Pat dry with paper towel and rub chicken with oil."],[null,"In a medium bowl combine rice, Worcestershire sauce, olive oil, black pepper, bell pepper, scallions, pineapple and pineapple juice. Spoon mixture into cavity of chicken to stuff."],[null,"Place chicken breast side up in a roasting pan or Dutch oven. Cook uncovered for 1-1/2 hours or until internal temperature reaches 180-185° F. Rice stuffing should reach at least 165° F. Let chicken rest 10-15 minutes."],[null,"Spoon rice stuffing from chicken cavity and place on a serving platter. Cut chicken into pieces, add to platter and serve."]],"h":[[null,"If you have leftover chicken try Chicken Lettuce Wraps, Cool ‘n’ Crunchy Chicken Salad recipes."]]},"2083":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Rinse chicken and remove giblets from inside cavity. Pat dry with paper towel and rub chicken with oil."],[null,"In a medium bowl combine rice, Worcestershire sauce, olive oil, black pepper, bell pepper, scallions, pineapple and pineapple juice. Spoon mixture into cavity of chicken to stuff."],[null,"Place chicken breast side up in a roasting pan or Dutch oven. Cook uncovered for 1-1/2 hours or until internal temperature reaches 180-185° F. Rice stuffing should reach at least 165° F. Let chicken rest 10-15 minutes."],[null,"Spoon rice stuffing from chicken cavity and place on a serving platter. Portion half of the chicken into 2 ounce portions and serve."],[null,"Refrigerate or freeze remaining chicken."]],"h":[[null,"Analysis includes only half the cooked chicken. The recipe makes six 2-ounce portions plus additional 12 ounces chicken after removing skin and bones."],[null,"Try our Chicken Lettuce Wraps, Cool ‘n’ Crunchy Chicken Salad recipes for the leftover chicken."],[null,"If higher calories and carbohydrate desired cook extra rice to serve with chicken."]]},"9322650":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 400 degrees F (204 degrees C) and line a baking sheet with parchment paper. Set aside."],[null,"Add all the ingredients to your food processor and pulse until finely chopped and combined, but not pureed. (You want to keep some texture.)"],[null,"Squeeze the chickpea mixture into golf-sized balls in your hands, and then gently flatten and shape into a disc shape. Place it on your baking tray and repeat with the remaining batter. You should get 15 nuggets."],[null,"Bake for 25-30 minutes, flipping once at the halfway point. Serve with dipping sauce of choice, and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Please note, that these chickpea nuggets do NOT taste like chicken . They are not meant to be a chicken nuggets vegan replacement. They’re delicious and wonderful by their own merit! Do not over-process your ingredients . Leave some chunkier pieces to get the best texture for your chickpea nuggets. Use care when flipping. Do not force flip your nuggets if they don’t lift easily from the parchment paper or you may break them. If your nuggets are not lifting easily, return the tray to the oven for a few more minutes and try again. As they cook longer, they’ll flip easier. Bake time will vary according to the size of your nuggets. Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-4 days in a sealed container or freeze airtight for up to 3 months. Separate layers of nuggets with parchment paper to prevent sticking. The serving size is for ⅓ of the recipe, approx 5 nuggets."]]},"6070461":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F. Cover a 9x9 inch baking dish in parchment paper."],[null,"Place the peaches in the baking dish, drizzle with the syrup, and sprinkle with ground cinnamon."],[null,"Stir to coat the peaches evenly."],[null,"Bake for 30-35 minutes or until the peaches are tender. Serve warm with 1/3 cup of no sugar added frozen yogurt."],[null,"Top with the sliced almonds."]],"h":[]},"6849321":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 425 degrees."],[null,"Drizzle lemon juice over apples."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix together remaining ingredients. Stuff each apple with approximately 1/4 cup oat mixture."],[null,"Place apples in an oven safe baking dish and bake for 25-30 minutes."]],"h":[]},"3936001":{"s":[[null,"Pour boiling water over the couscous. Cover for 10-12 mins until absorbed. Mince the garlic, chop the herbs and deseed and dice the tomatoes and cucumber. Fluff with a fork and stir in olive oil, lemon juice and garlic. Stir in the tomatoes, cucumber and spring onions. Season with pepper and rest for 1 hour covered in cling film."],[null,"To prepare the herb crust for the cod, grate the cheese and combine in a bowl with the breadcrumbs and herbs. Season with pepper, then chill for 30 minutes to allow the mixture to firm up."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 200°C / 180°C / gas mark 6. When firm, roll crust mixture between 2 sheets of greaseproof paper, cut into squares large enough to cover the pieces of cod. Press it down gently so that it sticks. Brush baking sheet with olive oil and add the cod. Bake for 6-8 minutes until the cod is just cooked."],[null,"To make the salsa, chop the tomatoes and deseed and finely chop the chilli. Place in a bowl and add the herbs. Season with pepper and mix until well combined. To serve, place a piece of herb-crusted cod on each plate spoon the salsa around the cod and serve with tabouli on the side."]],"h":[["Chef's note","This is a delightful fresh fish dish with a serving of tasty herby tabouli on the side."],["Carbohydrate","The couscous and breadcrumbs are the main sources of carbohydrate in this main meal and the value has been provided for those who have been trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","This dish does contain ingredients that are high in potassium and phosphate. However, the quantities have been kept to a minimum and by using the quantities listed and following the recommended serving size, the overall phosphate and potassium content of the dish remains low. If you have been prescribed a phosphate binder, ensure you take them with this dish."],["Protein","The fish in this recipe provides a good source of protein, ideal for those receiving dialysis."],["Gluten free","Serve with rice, quinoa or gluten-free pasta instead of couscous. Use gluten-free breadcrumbs."],["Vegetarian/Vegan","Stir a 400g tin of drained chickpeas into the tabouli and serve with the salsa."],["Cheaper option","Choose cheaper fillets of fish, frozen fillets, or fish on offer to reduce the cost. You can buy pre-packaged breadcrumbs or save money by making your own. To save money, use a teaspoon of dried mixed herbs as an alternative to the fresh herbs in the cod crust."],["Storage","Fish should be eaten on the day of cooking. Tabouli and salsa can be kept in an airtight container in the fridge for up to two days."],["Tips","For those with a transplant, it is best to purchase your fish pre-packaged. Good choices for mixed fresh herbs include basil, chives or parsley. Attentively, use some extra mint, coriander and dill to complement the tabouli."]]},"6709831":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F. Place the rosemary in a single row in a small baking pan, such as an 8-inch square pan. Top with the cod fillets. Brush the fish with the oil. Sprinkle with the lemon juice, salt, and pepper."],[null,"Bake for 7 to 8 minutes or until the fish flakes easily when tested with a fork."]],"h":[]},"7591571":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200ºC/gas mark 6. Mix together the horseradish, breadcrumbs and parsley, season well and press onto the cod fillets."],[null,"Place on a baking sheet and bake for 10–12 minutes until the fish is cooked through. Serve with rocket salad and a wedge of lemon."]],"h":[[null,"The nutritional analysis above includes a serving suggestion of rocket."],[null,"This topping works well with other fish such as haddock, salmon, mackerel fillets or river cobbler."],[null,"To crumble bread, dry it out first in the oven for a few minutes before blending."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"3032":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 425° F. Lightly grease 2 standard donut pans (12 donuts)"],[null,"Using an electric mixer, in a medium bowl, beat together 4 tablespoons butter, oil and granulated and brown sugars until smooth."],[null,"Add the eggs, mixing them to combine."],[null,"Stir in baking powder, baking soda, nutmeg, salt and 1 teaspoon vanilla."],[null,"Stir the flour and protein powder into the butter mixture alternately with the yogurt and milk. Start and end with the flour mixture. Make sure everything is thoroughly combined. The batter will"],[null,"be fairly thick. When you pull a spatula through your batter, it should leave an indentation."],[null,"Spoon the batter into the lightly greased donut pans, filling to about 1/4-inch from the top. Alternatively, you can pipe the batter into the donut pan using a piping bag."],[null,"Bake the donuts for 10 minutes. Remove pans from the oven, and allow donuts to cool for 5 to 7 minutes. Remove donuts from the pan and allow to cool completely."],[null,"While the donuts are cooling, make the glaze. Stir sifted confectioner’s sugar, corn syrup, remaining vanilla, butter (melted) and 1 tablespoon milk together in a shallow bowl. Add extra milk or"],[null,"confectioner’s sugar as needed to adjust consistency."],[null,"Pour sprinkles in a separate shallow bowl."],[null,"Dip top of donut in glaze to coat, then dip in sprinkles. Place on rack to set."]],"h":[[null,"You can also bake batter in mini muffin tins, then glaze and add sprinkles to make “donut holes”."],[null,"If whole wheat pastry flour is unavailable substitute 1 cup whole wheat flour and 1 cup all-purpose flour (in addition to the 2/3 cup all-purpose flour)."],[null,"This recipes is high in protein and fiber and lower in sodium compared to bakery donuts."]]},"54957":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375°F. Lightly grease two standard donut pans or a standard muffin tin (see hint)."],[null,"In a mixing bowl, beat butter, vegetable oil, brown sugar, and 1/2 cup granulated sugar until smooth. Add eggs, beat together."],[null,"Stir in baking powder, baking soda, 1/2 to 1 teaspoon cinnamon, salt, and vanilla."],[null,"Alternate adding flour and milk into mixture beginning and ending with flour until combined. The batter will be thick."],[null,"Spoon batter into tin, filling 3/4 of the way up. Bake for 10-12 minutes. Remove, and wait for 5-7 minutes to cool slightly. Flip on to a wire rack."],[null,"Prepare toppings of your choice (or multiple toppings). Each topping makes enough for 12 donuts."],[null,"Store in an air-tight container for up to 3 days."]],"h":[[null,"No donut pan? Take a long piece of foil (about 9in). Fold into long rectangle and then create a circle the size of your desired donut hole. Repeat 12 times. Place into each space of your muffin tin. Center the foil and spoon batter around the foil."],[null,"Don’t care about the donut shape? Just bake in a muffin tin. You will need to add 3-4 minutes to back time. Each topping makes enough for 12 donuts."]]},"6014372":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F. Lightly coat a baking sheet with cooking spray."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix yogurt and pesto."],[null,"Toss the zucchini noodles with the olive oil, salt, and black pepper."],[null,"On the prepared baking sheet, create 4 small nests with zucchini. Evenly distribute tomato halves among them."],[null,"Bake for 5 minutes until slightly softened. Remove from the oven. Create a small well in the center of each nest. Spoon pesto yogurt mixture into each well. Crack 1 egg into each well."],[null,"Return to the oven and bake for 10-12 minutes, until eggs reach desired doneness."],[null,"Remove from the oven, sprinkle with the Parmesan cheese and fresh basil. Serve immediately."]],"h":[]},"6681539":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400°F."],[null,"Crack each egg into a separate bowl without breaking the yolks. Set aside."],[null,"Spray a small ovenproof non-stick pan with cooking spray and preheat. Add eggs, and immediately transfer pan to the oven. Cook for about 2–5 minutes, or until eggs reach desired doneness."],[null,"In a small bowl add canola oil, lime juice, salt and pepper, and whisk ingredients together to create the dressing. Add avocado, tomato, red onion and cilantro to the dressing and toss."],[null,"Remove eggs from oven. Plate salad ingredients first and top with the eggs. Serve."]],"h":[]},"7903857":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 180°C/gas mark 4."],[null,"Add oil to a pan, then add the leeks and mushrooms and cook for 4-5 minutes, stirring regularly."],[null,"Mix in the yoghurt and pepper, then divide the mixture between 4 ovenproof dishes."],[null,"Make a small hollow in the middle of each dish, then crack an egg into each. Bake for 12-15 mins or more depending on how you like your eggs."]],"h":[[null,"Try adding a finely chopped red pepper along with the leeks and mushrooms."],[null,"Add some chopped chives or fresh basil for extra flavour."],[null,"'At risk' groups such as infants, children, pregnant women, the elderly and those who are unwell should avoid soft/lightly cooked and raw eggs, unless they can guarantee that they are produced under the Lion code quality assurance scheme."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"3240039":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C. Oil a small oven-proof frying pan or small baking dish. Whisk some black pepper and the mixed herbs or chilli flakes into the eggs. Pour the eggs into the pan."],[null,"Pour the vegetables into the egg mixture and stir in."],[null,"Scatter the cheese over the top and bake for 12-15 minutes or until lightly golden."],[null,"Remove from the oven and let it sit on side for a few minutes. Toast the bread and spread with butter, serve."]],"h":[["Chef's note","This low potassium and low phosphate frittata dish is simple and quick."],["Carbohydrate","The bread is the main source of carbohydrate in this recipe, and the value has been provided for those who have been trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","This recipe is low in potassium, therefore suitable for those advised to follow a low potassium diet. This recipe is also low in phosphate, however it does contain some phosphate, mainly provided by the eggs and cheese, therefore if you have been prescribed a phosphate binder you should take as directed."],["Protein","This recipe is high in protein, therefore suitable for those advised to eat more protein, such as those receiving dialysis."],["Healthier option","Although salt has not been added, this recipe is not low in salt. This is because the bread and cheese contain salt – you may want to check the amount of salt in your bread and choose one with the lowest salt"]]},"6567580":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 400°F.​"],[null,"In a large mixing bowl, combine the asparagus, cherry tomatoes, zucchini, bell pepper, red onion, and garlic.​"],[null,"Drizzle with olive oil and sprinkle with dried oregano, black pepper, and salt. Toss until the vegetables are evenly coated.​"],[null,"Lightly coat a large sheet pan with cooking spray.​ Spread the seasoned vegetables in a single layer on the sheet pan.​ Roast in the preheated oven for 15-20 minutes, or until the vegetables are tender and slightly caramelized.​"],[null,"Remove the sheet pan from the oven and scatter the baby spinach over the roasted vegetables. The heat will wilt the spinach slightly.​"],[null,"Create four small wells among the vegetables and carefully crack an egg into each well.​"],[null,"Return the sheet pan to the oven and bake for an additional 7-10 minutes, or until the egg whites are set and the yolks reach your desired doneness.​"],[null,"Sprinkle fresh basil over the vegetables and eggs.​"]],"h":[]},"7050301":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 200°C/ fan 180°C/gas 6. Spread the chips on a large, non-stick baking tray in a single layer. Spray with a couple of pumps of low calorie cooking spray and season with pepper. Bake for 40 minutes, or until golden, turning halfway."],[null,"Meanwhile, spray a large, non-stick frying pan with a couple of pumps of low-calorie cooking spray and place over a medium-high heat. Once hot, add the onion and mushrooms, and stir-fry for 5-6 minutes until softened and a little coloured. Stir in the nutmeg and garlic. Cook for 2 minutes until fragrant, then add the spinach and stir everything together until piping hot throughout. Remove from the heat and stir through the yoghurt, then season with pepper."],[null,"Either divide the mixture between 4 individual pie dishes, or tip into 1 large pie dish. Make 4 wells in the mixture and crack an egg into each. Top with a twist of black pepper and bake on the shelf below the chips for the remaining 15 minutes of the chips’ cooking time, or until the egg whites have set. Divide the chips between 4 plates and serve with the baked eggs."]],"h":[[null,"You can use a plain yoghurt of your choice. However, this will change the nutritional information and texture of the dish."],[null,"At risk groups such as infants, children, pregnant women, the elderly and those who are unwell should avoid soft/lightly cooked and raw eggs, unless they can guarantee that they are produced under the Lion code quality assurance scheme."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"6771015":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 450 degrees. Line a large baking sheet with a silicon mat or parchment paper. If using parchment paper, spray with cooking spray. Set aside."],[null,"In a food processor or blender, add garlic, 1 small onion (chopped), curry powder, cayenne pepper, cilantro, parsley and olive oil. Blend into a paste."],[null,"Add in garbanzo beans and pulse to chop beans and mix into onion paste. Do not blend the beans into a paste. The falafel should be slightly chunky."],[null,"Add flour, baking powder, salt (optional), and ground black pepper. Pulse until just incorporated."],[null,"Refrigerate falafel mixture for 15-20 minutes. While the falafel is chilling, add yogurt, tahini, garlic and parsley to a small bowl and whisk. Keep yogurt sauce in the refrigerator until ready to use."],[null,"Scoop falafel into balls that are about 2 Tbsps. of mixture (or 1/8 of a cup). Place on baking sheet and repeat to make 16 falafel balls."],[null,"Spray the falafel balls with cooking spray and sprinkle with sesame seeds."],[null,"Bake on the bottom rack of the oven for 15 minutes. Turn the oven down to 350 and move the baking sheet to the top rack. Bake an additional 15 minutes."],[null,"Once the falafel is done baking, stuff two falafel balls into half of a whole wheat pita, add 2 Tbsp. yogurt tahini sauce, 2 slices of tomato, 3-4 slices of red onion and ¼ cup arugula."]],"h":[]},"6631528":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350°F. Lightly spray a baking sheet with cooking spray."],[null,"Place the fish on the baking sheet. Bake for 18-20 minutes, or until the fish flakes easily when tested with a fork."],[null,"Meanwhile, in a small bowl, stir together the remaining ingredients."],[null,"Spread the margarine mixture over the fish."]],"h":[]},"2368":{"s":[[null,"Place fillets in a two-quart rectangular baking dish. (If using frozen fish instead of fresh, thaw first.)"],[null,"Preheat oven to 450° F."],[null,"Chop onion."],[null,"Melt margarine in a small sauce pan. Add mushrooms and onion and cook over medium heat until tender."],[null,"Spoon mushroom mixture over fish."],[null,"Crush the dried thyme and sprinkle over fish."],[null,"Bake uncovered in oven for 12 to 15 minutes or until fish flakes."]],"h":[[null,"Try tilapia or other white fish for variety."],[null,"Thaw frozen fish in the refrigerator or under cold running water until fish is pliable."],[null,"One tablespoon fresh thyme is equivalent to one teaspoon dried thyme."]]},"2282":{"s":[[null,"Coat bottom and sides of a 9” x 13” baking pan with margarine or nonstick cooking spray."],[null,"Arrange slices of bread in a layer on bottom of pan."],[null,"Beat non-enriched rice milk, egg substitute, melted margarine, sugar, almond extract and cinnamon together in a bowl and pour over bread slices."],[null,"Cover pan with plastic wrap and refrigerate overnight."],[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Place pan in oven and bake for 40 to 50 minutes, until knife inserted into center comes out clean."],[null,"Serve warm."],[null,"Sprinkle with powdered sugar or non-calorie sweetener, if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Plain or flavored nondairy creamer may be used instead or rice milk. Susan says her patients and teammates prefer coconut cream flavor."],[null,"Vanilla or coconut extract may be used in place of almond extract."],[null,"For diabetics use Splenda® granular sweetener instead of sugar to reduce carbohydrate to 44 grams and calories to 364 per serving or serve a half portion."],[null,"Liquid egg substitute is recommended. If eggs are used instead, calories are 550, fat 24 g, phosphorus 263 mg and cholesterol 423 mg."]]},"6732979":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375 degrees F."],[null,"Spray a baking sheet with cooking spray. Remove skin from wings. Lay chicken wings in a single layer on the baking sheet and spray again with cooking spray."],[null,"Bake for 10 minutes. While the chicken is baking, whisk apricot preserves, 2 1/2 tsp. of garlic, soy sauce, chili garlic sauce, lime juice and 1/4 tsp ground black pepper together and set aside."],[null,"After the wings have been in the oven for 10 minutes, coat them generously with the apricot preserve mixture. Return to the oven for another 15 minutes or until wings are cooked through and glaze is caramelized."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together Greek yogurt, 1 tbsp lime juice, cilantro and 1/4 tsp ground black pepper. Serve dipping sauce with hot wings."]],"h":[]},"4614461":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F."],[null,"In a shallow bowl, combine flour and pepper. Coat the chicken in flour mixture. Set the remaining flour mixture aside."],[null,"In a skillet, heat the oil over medium-high heat and fry the chicken. Place the browned chicken pieces in a baking dish."],[null,"In a saucepan, melt the butter over medium heat and fry the chopped onion until it is softened."],[null,"Add the reserved flour mixture to the onion and stir to form a thick paste. Gradually add broth, lemon juice, basil and thyme and mix well."],[null,"Bring to a boil. Cook and stir for 2 minutes or until the sauce is thick and bubbly. Pour the sauce over the chicken. Top each chicken piece with a lemon slice. Sprinkle with parsley."],[null,"Cover and bake in the oven for 30 minutes. Serve over rice and enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"* Unseasoned chicken breast is lower in sodium and phosphorus than seasoned chicken breast."],[null,"** Look for low or reduced-sodium broth containing 200mg sodium or less per 1 cup serving. Avoid low-sodium broth that contains potassium chloride—it’s very high in potassium."],["Watch for signs and symptoms of hyperkalemia (high-potassium)","Hyperkalemia is a medical condition in which your potassium blood level is higher than the normal range of approximately 3.6 to 5.2 mmol/L. Potassium is an important mineral for nerve and muscle function. Without being at the recommended level, potassium is unable to support the body in maintaining fluid, electrolyte and pH balance. Reduced kidney function can lead to hyperkalemia. Other diseases such as Type 1 Diabetes, Addison's disease and malabsorptive gastrointestinal disorders can lead to hyperkalemia as well. The overuse of potassium containing supplements and blood pressure lowering medications can also lead to higher than normal potassium levels. A routine blood test can determine if your potassium level is high. As a result of hyperkalemia, you may experience symptoms of muscle tiredness, weakness, nausea and an irregular heartbeat. Left untreated, hyperkalemia can be a very serious medical condition. Discuss with your physician treatment methods for maintaining potassium level within a normal range. Depending on the cause of your high potassium level, therapy may require changes to your diet, to your medications or dialysis."]]},"9131956":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 425 degrees F and line a large baking tray with parchment paper."],[null,"Add your bread slices to a food processor and process until a breadcrumb consistency is achieved. Then transfer your bread crumbs into a large bowl, add the frozen corn and peas to the same bowl and set aside."],[null,"Drain your lentils and add them to the food processor along with your grated carrot, zucchini and all the seasonings. Process until broken down and well combined. Then transfer to the bowl with the breadcrumbs, and mix to combine."],[null,"Form 1-1.5\" balls using your hands, and place them on your baking tray. Then press each one down gently, without breaking them, to form your nuggets."],[null,"Bake for 30 minutes, carefully flipping them at the 15 minute mark. Let your nuggets cool at room temperature for at least 5 minutes to help them firm up. Then serve with ketchup, homemade mayo, or tahini."]],"h":[[null,"Do not sub for regular lentils. You must use split red lentils for this recipe. Make sure your mixture is very finely processed before adding the peas and corn. Reference the process shots or the video to compare. If any nuggets break while pressing them down on your baking tray, reshape them before baking to ensure they hold nicely. Leftovers keep refrigerated for up to 3 days, and you may reheat in the oven or toaster oven."]]},"3372312":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 160°C / 140°C fan / gas mark 3. Halve and deseed the butternut squash. Place flesh side down in a roasting tin and pour in 200ml water. Bake in the oven for 1 hour and 30 minutes."],[null,"Allow the squash to cool slightly before scooping out the flesh with a spoon. Add to a blender with the coconut milk to make a smooth puree."],[null,"Once pureed, heat gently in a saucepan. Add Dijon mustard, cider vinegar and crumble in stock cube. Season with pepper and add a little water to the sauce if needed. Simmer for 20 minutes until it thickens"],[null,"Bring a large pan of water to boil. Add the macaroni and cook for 7 minutes. It will continue to cook as it bakes. Drain the pasta and combine with the sauce, pouring them in to an oven proof dish."],[null,"Combine the breadcrumbs, almonds, vegan cheese and parsley if using. Sprinkle over the pasta and bake in the oven for 10 minutes until golden brown."],[null,"Bring a saucepan of water to the boil and add the broccoli. Cook until tender, drain and serve with the pasta."]],"h":[["Chef's note","A twist on a classic, this vegan version of macaroni and cheese is a lovely comforting meal that can be frozen for batch cooking."],["Carbohydrate","The pasta and breadcrumbs are the main source of carbohydrate in this dish and the value has been provided for those who have been trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","In most vegan cheese-based dishes, nutritional yeast is added to provide the cheesy flavour, however nutritional yeast is high in potassium. In this dish, butternut squash is used instead, which adds a healthy twist and keeps the overall recipe low in potassium.\nThis dish is low in phosphate, although it does contain some phosphate, therefore, If you have been prescribed a phosphate binder, ensure you take them with this dish."],["Protein","This dish is low in protein and suitable if you are following a low protein diet."],["Gluten free","Use gluten-free pasta, breadcrumbs and stock."],["Healthier option","To increase the fibre in this dish, try using a wholemeal pasta in place of the macaroni pasta."],["Cheaper option","This is a relatively inexpensive dish. However, you could try serving with broccoli if the purple sprouting broccoli is out of season or expensive. To save money you could make your own breadcrumbs."],["Storage","Once cooled, store in an airtight container and keep in the fridge. Use within 3 days and reheat thoroughly before serving. If freezing, portion at the end of step 4 in an airtight container. Defrost thoroughly, then add the topping mix and continue to cook from step 5."],["Tips","To make fresh breadcrumbs, tear the bread into pieces and drop it into a food processor fitted with a blade. Whiz the bread in bursts until you have breadcrumbs of the size you want.\nFor a shortcut, you could buy pre-packaged fresh chopped butternut squash or frozen squash and cook according to the packet instructions before continuing with step 2."]]},"3012658":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 160°C / 140°C fan / gas mark 3. Halve and deseed the butternut squash. Place flesh side down in a roasting tin and pour in 200ml water. Bake in the oven for 1 hour and 30 minutes."],[null,"Allow the squash to cool slightly before scooping out the flesh with a spoon. Add to a blender with the coconut milk to make a smooth puree."],[null,"Once pureed, heat gently in a saucepan. Add Dijon mustard, cider vinegar and crumble in stock cube. Season with pepper and add a little water to the sauce if needed. Simmer for 20 minutes until it thickens."],[null,"Bring a large pan of water to boil. Add the macaroni and cook for 7 minutes. It will continue to cook as it bakes. Drain the pasta and combine with the sauce, pouring them in to an oven-proof dish."],[null,"Grate the cheese and combine with the breadcrumbs, almonds and finely chopped parsley if using. Sprinkle over the pasta and bake in the oven for 10 minutes until golden brown."],[null,"Bring a saucepan of water to the boil and add the broccoli. Cook until tender, drain and serve with the pasta."]],"h":[["Chef's note","A twist on a classic, this version of macaroni and cheese is a lovely comforting meal that can be frozen for batch cooking."],["Carbohydrate","The pasta and breadcrumbs are the main source of carbohydrate in this dish and the value has been provided for those who have been trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","In this dish, butternut squash is used for the sauce which adds a healthy twist and keeps the recipe low in potassium.\nThis dish is low in phosphate, although it does contain some phosphate, from the cheese. If you have been prescribed a phosphate binder, ensure you take it with this dish."],["Protein","This dish is low in protein and suitable if you are following a low protein diet."],["Gluten free","Use gluten-free pasta, breadcrumbs and stock."],["Healthier option","To increase the fibre in this dish, try using a wholemeal pasta in place of the macaroni pasta."],["Cheaper option","This is a relatively inexpensive dish. To save money you could make your own breadcrumbs."],["Storage","Once cooled, store in an airtight container and keep in the fridge. Use within 3 days and reheat thoroughly before serving. If freezing, portion at the end of step 4 in an airtight container. Defrost thoroughly, then add the topping mix and continue to cook from step 5."],["Tips","To make fresh breadcrumbs, tear the bread into pieces and drop it into a food processor fitted with a blade. Whiz the bread in bursts until you have breadcrumbs of the size you want.\nFor a shortcut you could buy pre-packaged fresh chopped butternut squash or frozen squash and cook according to the packet instructions before continuing with step 2."]]},"7110056":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200° C / Gas mark 6. Line a large baking tray with baking parchment."],[null,"Gently heat the onions in a pan with the oil for about 15-20 minutes, stirring regularly until really soft and starting to brown."],[null,"Place the flour in a bowl with the curry powder, yogurt, and water, then mix well. Add the chickpeas, onions and spinach, mix again and leave to stand for 5 minutes. Mix once more."],[null,"Spray some oil onto the prepared tray, wet your hands and form the mixture into small balls before placing on the baking sheet."],[null,"Bake on the middle shelf of the oven for 20-25 minutes until golden brown, turning half way through to ensure even cooking."],[null,"Meanwhile, blend all the ingredients for the dip together until smooth."]],"h":[[null,"You could use other vegetables in the bhajis, for example try with peas in place of chickpeas."],[null,"For a creamier dip, blend 2 tbsp of 0% fat Greek yogurt into the herbs."],[null,"For a vegan version, use a soya-based yogurt alternative."],[null,"Freezability: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Freeze separately, defrost in the refrigerator and reheat thoroughly."]]},"7217497":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 200°C/fan 180°C/gas 6."],[null,"Put the oats, milk, egg, vanilla and cinnamon in a small, deep ovenproof dish that leaves room for the mixture to rise as it cooks. Mix well and cook in the middle of the oven for 20-25 minutes, or until golden and firm to the touch."],[null,"Remove from the oven, cool for 3 minutes and top with the quark or yogurt, fruit of your choice and mint sprig."]],"h":[[null,"Please note the nutritional information for this recipe does not include the quark or yoghurt or the berries as these are optional toppings."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"3695":{"s":[[null,"(Baked)"],[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Wash and dry fillets. Rub lightly with oil."],[null,"On a large sheet pan, place the fillets skin down."],[null,"Combine seasonings in a small bowl. Sprinkle evenly over fillets."],[null,"Bake uncovered for 10 to 15 minutes or until the trout fillets flake easily with a fork."],[null,"(Grilled)"],[null,"Preheat grill on high heat."],[null,"Spray or brush fillet side of the trout fillets lightly with oil. Combine seasonings in a small bowl. Sprinkle evenly over fillets."],[null,"Place trout directly on the grill, fillet side down. Cook for 4 minutes. Spray or brush skin lightly with oil. Turn fillets over and cook until fish flakes easily with fork, about 3 to 5 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"For additional seasoning, try adding cayenne pepper."],[null,"If you are on a low-protein diet, adjust the serving size to your individual meal plan."]]},"6054450":{"s":[[null,"Dry the fish fillets with a paper towel. Rub both sides lightly with olive oil (or use cooking spray). Combine the salt, lemon pepper, and paprika in a small bowl. Sprinkle the seasoning evenly over the fillet side of the fish."],[null,"For grilling: Preheat grill on high heat. Place trout directly on the grill, fillet side down. Cook for 4 minutes. Turn fillets over and cook until fish flakes easily with fork, about 3 to 5 minutes."],[null,"For baking: Preheat oven to 350° F. Place trout skin side down on a large sheet pan. Bake uncovered for 10-15 minutes, or until the trout flakes easily with a fork."]],"h":[]},"6462700":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F."],[null,"In a bowl, combine breadcrumbs, grated Parmesan cheese, dried oregano, garlic powder, salt, and black pepper."],[null,"Dip each zucchini round into the beaten eggs, ensuring they are well coated."],[null,"Coat each egg-dipped zucchini round with the breadcrumb mixture, pressing the crumbs onto the zucchini to adhere."],[null,"Place the breaded zucchini rounds on a baking sheet sprayed with olive oil cooking spray."],[null,"Lightly spray the tops of the breaded zucchini rounds with olive oil cooking spray."],[null,"Bake in the preheated oven for 20 minutes or until the zucchini is tender and the coating is golden brown."],[null,"Remove the zucchini from the oven and transfer to a serving platter."]],"h":[]},"3702868":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 180°C. In an ovenproof pan, heat the oil and add the onion. Cook until soft. In a separate pan, cook the pasta according to packet instructions."],[null,"Add in greens, pepper, herbs and chilli to the frying onions. Cook over a medium heat for 5 minutes, until soft. Add in tomato puree and cook for another minute."],[null,"Add the cooked and drained pasta, chickpeas and stock and bring to simmer. Put a lid onto pan and put into oven for 15 minutes."],[null,"Remove from oven, stir in butter, grate over cheese and serve."]],"h":[["Chef's note","This satisfying one-pot dish is low in salt, potassium and phosphate."],["Carbohydrate","The pasta is the main source of carbohydrate in this recipe, and the value has been provided for those who have been trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","This recipe is low in potassium, when following the quantities in the ingredients, and the serving sizes, and therefore suitable for those advised to follow a low potassium diet.\nThis recipe is also low in phosphate, however it does contain some phosphate, provided by the chickpeas and cheese, therefore if you have been prescribed a phosphate binder then you should take as directed."],["Protein","This recipe contains some protein. If you have been advised to reduce your protein then you may want to use less cheese or fewer chickpeas."],["Tips","This dish works with any pasta shape you already have, although orzo is particularly good. If you would rather use rice in place of the pasta you may need a little more stock."],["Storage","The dish is best eaten straight away."]]},"7206527":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200°C/gas mark 6."],[null,"Heat the oil in a non-stick pan, add the chicken and fry for 2 minutes on each side until browned."],[null,"Place the couscous in an ovenproof dish. Mix together with the stock, red onion, red pepper, parsley and the lemon zest and juice, then pour over the couscous and stir."],[null,"Place the chicken on top of the couscous, then spoon over the pesto and season to taste."],[null,"Cover the dish with foil and bake for 20 minutes."],[null,"Once cooked, fluff up the couscous with a fork. Serve hot or cold."]],"h":[[null,"For a vegetarian version, try adding marinated or smoked tofu instead of chicken."],[null,"If you can’t get hold of a red onion a brown one will work just as well."],[null,"Any sun-dried tomato paste will work instead of pesto."],[null,"Don’t worry if you don’t have parsley or lemon, this recipe will be just as tasty without."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"2451":{"s":[[null,"Preheat over to 350°F."],[null,"Empty crushed pineapple with juice into a bowl."],[null,"Beat 2 eggs well and add to crushed pineapple."],[null,"Add sugar, tapioca, and salt to pineapple egg mixture."],[null,"Pour mixture into 8 x 8-inch baking dish."],[null,"Slice butter and place on top of pineapple mixture. Sprinkle cinnamon on top."],[null,"Bake for 30 minutes. Serve hot or chilled."]],"h":[[null,"Add maraschino cherries for color."],[null,"For a diabetes-friendly version substitute Splenda granular sweetener® for sugar to reduce to 17 grams carbohydrate and one Carbohydrate Choices."]]},"6089551":{"s":[[null,"Will yield ½ cup potato."]],"h":[]},"7217871":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200°C/gas 6. Place the potatoes into a pan of boiling water for 7 minutes."],[null,"Drain the potatoes and place in a line onto a large roasting dish (as a bed for fish) leaving a gap each side."],[null,"Spread the tomatoes over the potatoes, then place the red and yellow peppers down either side of the potatoes and sprinkle with the garlic, chillies, oregano sprigs and olive oil, reserving 1 tbsp of the olive oil. Bake for 30 minutes, turning the dish half way through to ensure even cooking."],[null,"Meanwhile, slash the fish 5–6 times down each side, rub the skin with the remaining olive oil and season with salt and black pepper. Place the fish on top of the potatoes."],[null,"Return the dish to the oven and bake for a further 20–25 minutes (depending on the size of the fish), again turning the dish half way, until the fish is cooked through. Serve with the roasted vegetables."]],"h":[[null,"This recipe works well with other whole fish, such as trout or bream."],[null,"It's brilliant with salmon steaks or any white fish steaks, especially for people who don't like fish bones. If using steaks or fillets rather than whole fish, increase the vegetables cooking time by 10 minutes and reduce the fish cooking time to 15 minutes, depending on the size of the fish."],[null,"It makes a great dinner party dish."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"3373":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400° F. Set egg roll whappers out to thaw if frozen."],[null,"Finely shred cabbage and shred carrots. Thinly slice onions and chop cilantro. Grate ginger root."],[null,"Clean and finely chop shrimp."],[null,"Add cabbage, carrots, shrimp and green onions to a preheated non-stick skillet."],[null,"Cook over medium heat until shrimp are pink and veggies are translucent and soft, stirring occasionally (about 8 minutes)."],[null,"Add cilantro, hoisin sauce, brown sugar, garlic powder, ginger and red chili flakes."],[null,"Mix well, so spices are evenly distributed."],[null,"Cook 2 more minutes, and then remove from heat, draining off excess liquid."],[null,"While veggie shrimp mix is cooling, spray a baking sheet with canola oil and set aside."],[null,"Arrange spring roll wrappers on a cutting board (or other clean surface) and fill as follows: Place one heaping tablespoon of cooked mixture in each, diagonally, about one third from top of wrapper, and not directly in center. Fold two opposite edges of wrapper over the filling, and roll in the shorter side first, and then the longer side, until roll is complete."],[null,"Dip a finger into the water and rub along edge of completed roll to close, and place folded edge side down on baking sheet."],[null,"Spray each filled spring roll with canola oil spray."],[null,"Bake for about 20 minutes, turning after 10 minutes. Rolls should be lightly browned and crispy."]],"h":[[null,"12 ounces of raw shrimp yields about 1-1/2 cups when chopped."],[null,"Instead of egg roll wrappers substitite spring roll wrappers (also known as rice paper or spring roll skins). The carbohydrate, sodium and phosphorus content are lower."],[null,"If hoisen sauce is unavailable substitute low sodium soy sauce or plum sauce."],[null,"Serve with low-sodium sweet and sour sauce if desired."]]},"6406835":{"s":[[null,"Heat your oven to 400°F. Place the salmon on a small baking sheet lined with foil or parchment."],[null,"Drizzle the olive oil over the salmon and season with salt and pepper."],[null,"Add a lemon slice on top if you like."],[null,"Bake for 10–12 minutes, or until the salmon flakes easily with a fork."],[null,"Serve warm."]],"h":[]},"6460004":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F and line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"In a large bowl, toss the sweet potato fries with olive oil, smoked paprika, cumin, garlic powder, onion powder, salt, and black pepper until evenly coated."],[null,"Arrange the seasoned sweet potato fries in a single layer on the prepared baking sheet, ensuring they are not crowded."],[null,"Lightly spray the fries with cooking spray for extra crispiness."],[null,"Bake in the preheated oven for 20–25 minutes or until the sweet potato fries are golden brown and crispy, flipping them halfway through."],[null,"For the dipping sauce: In a small bowl, whisk together the low-fat Greek yogurt, lemon juice, maple syrup, and ground cumin."],[null,"Serve dipping sauce on the side."]],"h":[]},"1930":{"s":[[null,"Preheat over to 325° F."],[null,"Chop celery and onion. Cube the bread slices."],[null,"Melt butter in a skillet over medium heat and sauté celery and onion, stirring frequently."],[null,"Stir in 1/3 of the bread cubes."],[null,"Remove from heat and place bread mixture in a deep bowl."],[null,"Add remaining bread cubes, sage, thyme, pepper and poultry seasoning; mix well."],[null,"Place stuffing in a greased 13” x 9” x 2” baking dish. Cover and bake for 30 minutes."],[null,"Remove cover and bake an additional 15 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Boxed stuffing mix has over 500 mg sodium for a 1/2 cup serving."],[null,"1 cup of butter is equal to 2 sticks or 16 tablespoons. If preferred substitute trans-fat free unsalted margarine."]]},"6170052":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6230599":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F."],[null,"If necessary, cut the fish into 4 pieces and season it on both sides with pepper. Set aside."],[null,"In a large oven-safe sauté pan, heat olive oil over medium heat. Add the onion and sauté for 3 minutes, until just starting to soften. If you don’t have a large oven-safe sauté pan, more the fish and veggies onto a sheet pan or casserole to cook in the oven."],[null,"Add the eggplant to the onion and sauté for 3 minutes, until just starting to soften."],[null,"Add zucchini, peppers, tomatoes, oregano, salt, and garlic powder and mix well."],[null,"Nestle the fish fillets into the tomato and vegetable mixture."],[null,"Cover the pan and place it in the oven. Bake for 15 minutes until the vegetables and fish are cooked through."]],"h":[]},"6228270":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F. Line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"In a large bowl, toss the turnip matchsticks or wedges with olive oil until they are well-coated."],[null,"Spread the turnips in a single layer on a baking sheet."],[null,"Sprinkle the garlic powder, onion powder, smoked paprika, salt, and black pepper over the turnips. Toss to coat evenly."],[null,"Bake in the preheated oven for 20–25 minutes or until the turnip fries are golden brown and crispy, flipping them halfway through."],[null,"Remove from the oven and let them cool for a few minutes before serving."]],"h":[]},"9635628":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350℉/176℃ and grab enough donut pans to make 12 donuts. (I use 2 pans of 6 donuts each.)"],[null,"Whisk together the flour, baking powder, and cinnamon in a medium mixing bowl. Then add the wet ingredients and stir until combined."],[null,"Divide the donut batter between the 12 donut tins and bake for 12-15 minutes. The donuts are ready when they are firm to the touch, but give a little when gently pressed. Remove from the oven and let them cool before glazing."],[null,"While the donuts are cooling, prepare the glaze. Combine the sugar, lemon juice, and milk (starting with 1 tablespoon) in a small bowl. Add a little more milk if needed."],[null,"Once cooled, dip the tops of each donut into the glaze, and place them glaze side up on a wire rack to let the glaze set. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Weigh your flour using a kitchen scale for the most accurate results . Scooping flour from a bag may result in too much flour being used and could alter the texture."],[null,"Use fresh and active baking powder . Once opened, baking powder begins to lose its effectiveness, so it’s best to consume your baking powder within 6 months."],[null,"Allow your donuts to cool for 10-15 minutes before attempting to remove them from the pan. If the donuts are too hot, you risk breaking them."],[null,"Once transferred to a wire rack, let them continue to cool to room temperature before glazing them ."],[null,"The nutritional information above includes 1 donut, with the glaze."]]},"7886286":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 200C/gas 6. Spray the baking sheet and mushrooms with a couple of pumps of 1kcal spray. Stand mushrooms in the middle. Toss the chickpeas in the paprika and scatter on the baking sheet. Cook for 5 minutes."],[null,"Snip the corner off the bag of spinach and microwave on full for 2 minutes. Shake and cook for a further 1 minute until wilted. Leave to cool, then squeeze the spinach juices out of the snipped corner. Tip the spinach into a bowl and stir in the soft cheese. Season with black pepper."],[null,"Place a slice of tomato on top of each mushroom, drizzle with balsamic, then top with the spinach."],[null,"Slice the avocado, criss-cross over the spinach and lightly spray with oil."],[null,"Cook for 12-15 minutes until the avocado is softening. Divide between serving plates. Scatter the chickpeas over and serve with extra balsamic drizzle."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"9973119":{"s":[[null,"Place the potatoes in a medium pot and cover them with water. Bring to a boil and cook for 8-10 minutes, until a fork can pierce the edges. Do not overcook or they will be too soft to grate. Drain and rinse in cold water immediately, then pat them dry. Set aside."],[null,"Meanwhile, grate your zucchini onto paper towels or a clean dish towel. Then squeeze out as much water as you can over your kitchen sink. Transfer the shredded zucchini to a large mixing bowl and then grate the potatoes into the same bowl and add the seasoning. Mix well."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 425°F / 218°C and line a large baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Use your hands to shape the mixture into cylinder shapes, using approx. 1 tablespoon of the mixture for each one. Keep the tater tots small for a crispier texture. Place each one on your prepared tray and repeat with the remaining mixture. You will get 24-30 tater tots."],[null,"Bake for 20-25 minutes, then carefully flip them over and bake for an additional 10 minutes, until desired crispiness is reached."]],"h":[[null,"Do not overcook the potatoes or they will be too soft and difficult to shred. Squeeze as much moisture as you can from the shredded zucchini before mixing it with the potatoes. You don’t want too much excess moisture. Keep the tater tots small for a crispier texture. Since there is no oil in this recipe, use care when flipping . If the taters feel a little stuck or hard to flip, bake them a few extra minutes to make them firmer and try again. These taste best when freshly made but you may store leftovers in the fridge for 3-4 days. Reheat in the oven, air fryer, or toaster oven to return to a crispy state."]]},"7780864":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven 180°C/gas 4 and lightly oil an ovenproof dish."],[null,"Halve the peaches and place a raspberry into the centre of each half (where the stone was). Arrange the peach halves in the dish."],[null,"Place the egg, almond essence, yogurt and sweetener in a bowl, and beat together well."],[null,"Mix the baking powder with the flour and gently stir into the egg mixture."],[null,"Spoon the mixture on top of each peach half and scatter with the almonds."],[null,"Bake for 12–15 minutes until the top is golden and the peaches are soft, but still firm."]],"h":[[null,"Tinned peaches will work just as well for this recipe - go for tinned peaches in juice if you can."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"5603870":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200˚C /180˚C fan / Gas Mark 6."],[null,"In a bowl, combine chopped pecans, pumpkin seeds, hazelnuts, cinnamon and cardamom with the honey."],[null,"Place a sheet of filo pastry into a 25x15cm baking tray and brush with butter. Continue this process until half the pack of pastry has been used."],[null,"Spread the nut mixture evenly over the pastry."],[null,"Place the other half of filo sheets on top of the nut mixture, continuing the buttering and layering process until the whole pack is used. Any remaining butter should be poured over the top."],[null,"Cut 12 portions into the baklava and bake for 30 minutes or until golden brown."],[null,"Meanwhile, place the sugar and water into a pan with orange zest. Bring the syrup to a boil and then allow to simmer until it resembles runny honey."],[null,"Remove the baklava from the oven and pour all of the syrup over evenly."],[null,"Allow to cool fully before serving."]],"h":[]},"6196157":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F."],[null,"In a bowl, whisk together the olive oil, balsamic vinegar, maple syrup, Dijon mustard, dried thyme, salt, and black pepper."],[null,"Add the carrots to the bowl and toss to coat them evenly with the balsamic and maple mixture."],[null,"Spread the carrots in a single layer on a baking sheet."],[null,"Roast in the preheated oven for 25 minutes or until the carrots are tender and caramelized, tossing halfway through."]],"h":[]},"4313152":{"s":[[null,"In a frying pan, heat oil over medium-high heat. Fry chicken slices for 3 minutes on each side or until golden brown. Fry in batches not to overcrowd the pan. Remove chicken from the pan."],[null,"Add onions and mushrooms. Stir and fry for about 3 minutes until they brown. Add a bit of oil if necessary."],[null,"Sprinkle the flour over the onions and mushrooms. Stir to distribute the flour. Then add the vinegar and chicken broth. Stir to dissolve the flour. Reduce the heat to low and add chicken, honey and rosemary."],[null,"Cover and simmer for 10 minutes. If the sauce is too thick, add some chicken broth. If the sauce is too thin, take the cover off and let simmer for a few minutes longer."],[null,"Remove sprigs, if using fresh rosemary. Add pepper to taste. Serve with green beans."]],"h":[["Lowering phosphorus in sauces for meat and poultry","Prepared meats can be convenient with a busy schedule. Unfortunately, many meat and poultry selections that come in a marinade, gravy or added sauce are high in phosphorus additives. Reading the Nutrition Facts Label is helpful in identifying these foods. Listed under Ingredients, additives can be recognized with “phos” in their name. Common examples include phosphoric acid, sodium phosphate, tetrasodium pyrophosphate and sodium acid pyrophosphate. On a low-phosphorus diet, these foods should be limited because of increased phosphorus absorption (up to 100%), that is harmful with chronic kidney disease and can negatively impact bone and heart health. There are other ways to flavor meat or poultry without phosphorus additives. Homemade sauces, gravy or seasonings can be made with simple ingredients you may have readily available. A glaze can be created with a combination of balsamic vinegar and brown sugar. Chicken drippings or broth, flour, butter and green herbs can make delicious gravy. Create a fruit-based glaze as a sweet option using cider vinegar, jam, brown sugar and unsalted butter. For a sauce with a bite, try mixing shallots, scallions, brown mustard, pepper and a dash of paprika. With any extra, place portions in airtight storage containers to maintain quality and safely freeze for several months."]]},"6229691":{"s":[[null,"Place the chicken breast in a plastic bag and pound thin with a mallet."],[null,"Heat olive oil over medium-high heat in a skillet."],[null,"Dredge the chicken in flour and coat it on both sides. Add the chicken to the pan and sauté 5 minutes per side. Remove the chicken from the pan and set aside."],[null,"Melt the margarine in the pan. Add the mushrooms and pepper and cook for 5 minutes. Add the balsamic vinegar to the pan and bring it to a boil to reduce the liquid."],[null,"Add the chicken broth to the pan and simmer 2 more minutes. Add the chicken breast back to the pan and simmer for 5 minutes."]],"h":[]},"6952871":{"s":[[null,"Toast the bread slice to your liking."],[null,"Spread almond butter evenly over the toasted bread."],[null,"Arrange banana slices on top of the almond butter."],[null,"Sprinkle sliced almonds over the banana slices."]],"h":[]},"3511962":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 190°C/ gas mark 5. Grease and line a 450g loaf tin."],[null,"Beat the egg and mash together with the banana and vanilla extract."],[null,"In a separate bowl, cream together the butter and sugar."],[null,"Add the banana mixture to the creamed sugar and beat together."],[null,"Mix in the flour, bicarbonate of soda, cream of tartar and cranberries and stir well to combine."],[null,"Pour into the prepared baking tin and bake for 40-45 minutes or until a skewer comes out clean. Leave to cool in the tin for five minutes before turning it out on a wire tray to cool completely."]],"h":[["Chef's note","Banana bread is a simple, comforting choice. This freezer-friendly version is also gluten free."],["Carbohydrate","The main sources of carbohydrate in this recipe are the flour, sugar, banana and cranberries. Carbohydrate values have been provided for those trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","Banana is a high potassium fruit, however only 1 banana is being used for 10 portions which keeps this recipe low in potassium overall. Therefore, a portion can be enjoyed as part of a low potassium diet as an occasional treat.\nThis recipe contains phosphate which is mainly provided by the raising agents. If you have been prescribed a phosphate binder, ensure you take them with this dish."],["Protein","This banana bread is low in protein and can be enjoyed on special occasions as part of a reduced protein diet."],["Healthier option","The sugar in this recipe has already been reduced, however if you find it too sweet you could consider reducing it further. You may also wish to use a low fat spread in place of the unsalted butter, which will reduce the fat content."],["Cheaper option","This recipe is relatively inexpensive, but you could consider using a normal caster sugar in place of the soft brown sugar as this may save a small amount of money."],["Storage","Once cooled, it is best to slice the banana bread into the 10 portions and store in an airtight container for up to 3 days. If you are not sharing with friends and family, you can wrap individual slices and freeze for up to 3 months. Allow to thoroughly defrost before eating."]]},"7511962":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 170°C/ gas mark 3. Mash the bananas, then add the eggs and beat together."],[null,"Add the oil, vanilla extract and sugar and mix well."],[null,"Stir in the flour, baking powder and mixed spice, then fold in the chopped walnuts."],[null,"Spoon into a 2lb loaf tin (approx 22 x 11cm), place the whole walnuts on the top, and bake for around 50–55 minutes, until a skewer inserted into the middle comes out clean."],[null,"Cool in the tin for 10 minutes before turning out onto a rack to cool completely."]],"h":[[null,"You could add other spices to this mix such as ground ginger or cinnamon, or use almonds or sunflower seeds instead of walnuts."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Slice, then wrap in foil to freeze. You can then use slices as required."]]},"9882257":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350℉/176℃ and use a greased muffin tin or line a muffin pan with muffin liners."],[null,"Mash your banana to ensure you have 1 cup worth of mashed banana. Then add all the ingredients except for any optional toppings to your food processor. Process the mixture until mostly smooth."],[null,"Divide the batter between your 12 muffin cups and top some or all of the muffins with toppings if you'd like."],[null,"Bake the chickpea muffins for 20-22 minutes or until a toothpick inserted in the middle of a muffin comes out mostly clean. Then remove them from the oven and let them cool for 10-15 minutes before transferring them to a cooling rack."]],"h":[[null,"Use overripe bananas. The riper your bananas, the greater flavour, sweetness, and moisture they will add to your banana chickpea muffins. Bananas with brown skin work best."],[null,"Use baking powder that is fresh and ACTIVE . Baking powder that is open in the pantry for 6+ months may lose its effectiveness."],[null,"Measure your mashed banana to ensure you're using one cup. Bananas vary greatly in size. Two large bananas or three medium bananas work for me."],[null,"Let your muffins cool for 10-15 minutes before removing them from the muffin pan to help them set and prevent them from breaking."],[null,"Leftover muffins will keep at room temperature for 1-2 days, refrigerated for up to 5 days or frozen for up to 3 months."]]},"6580283":{"s":[[null,"Peel bananas and slice into 1/4-inch coins. Place in a bowl and freeze for at least 2 hours."],[null,"Once bananas are frozen, add the bananas, milk and cocoa powder to blender. Blend until smooth."],[null,"Fold in the whipped topping."],[null,"Place mixture in a freezer-safe container and freeze for at least 30 minutes."],[null,"Scoop into 1/2-cup scoops to serve."]],"h":[]},"2201":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400° F. Line a muffin pan with paper or silicon liners."],[null,"Peel bananas and mash with a fork."],[null,"In a medium bowl whisk all ingredients except chocolate chips together until incorporated. Mix in chocolate chips."],[null,"Fill muffin cups 1/2 full with batter. Bake for 15 minutes."],[null,"Remove from oven and cool on a wire rack; remove muffins from the pan and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"These muffins are best for kidney patients who do not need a potassium restricted diet since the banana, peanut butter and chocolate are high in potassium."],[null,"If you use a reduced-fat peanut butter if will add approximately 5 grams of carbohydrate per serving."],[null,"This muffin is a good protein snack. Ask your dietitian if you need to add a phosphate binder if prescribed."]]},"6299118":{"s":[[null,"Add the banana, coconut milk, yogurt, shredded coconut, vanilla extract, and ice to a blender. Blend until smooth and creamy."],[null,"Garnish with cinnamon, if desired. Enjoy immediately."]],"h":[]},"9631627":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your griddle over medium heat. Then add all the ingredients to a blender and process until smooth. Stop to scrape down the sides, if needed."],[null,"Now pour the pancakes directly from the blender onto your hot griddle, cooking for 3-4 minutes until bubbles have formed and the edges appear set. Then flip and continue cooking through for another 3-4 minutes."],[null,"Serve with sliced bananas, fresh berries, maple syrup or any of your favourite pancake toppings."]],"h":[[null,"Scrape the sides of your blender . The peanut butter may get stuck to the sides when blending, so make sure everything gets nicely combined by scraping the sides down, as needed. Do not use high heat for these pancakes or the outside will get very dark and the middles, underdone. These cook best at medium heat. You may freeze, once completely cooled for up to 3 months."]]},"9252979":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350℉/176℃ and line a muffin pan with parchment liners."],[null,"Add the cooked lentils, mashed banana, applesauce, and vanilla to your blender and process until completely smooth. Then pour the mixture into a medium mixing bowl."],[null,"To the same bowl, add the flour, baking powder, and cinnamon, and mix until just combined. Then fold in the blueberries."],[null,"Scoop the mixture between 12 muffin tins and bake for 20-22 minutes, or until a toothpick inserted in the center of a muffin comes out mostly clean."],[null,"Remove the pan from the oven and let your lentil muffins rest at room temperature for 10 minutes before transferring them to a wire rack."]],"h":[[null,"Use overly ripe bananas with lots of brown spots on the peel for extra sweetness. You may also use frozen bananas, just let them come to room temperature before mashing them."],[null,"Use FRESH + ACTIVE baking powder . Baking powder that has been open in the pantry for 6+ months may start to lose its effectiveness."],[null,"Don't overmix . The texture of the muffins comes out best when folded together until just combined."],[null,"Gently tap the muffin tray on a hard surface to close up any gaps in the batter before baking."],[null,"Let your muffins rest for 10 minutes after baking . This short cool-down time will allow your muffins to completely set, and prevent them from breaking when removing them from the pan."]]},"9111240":{"s":[[null,"Bring a few cups of water to boil in a kettle or small sauce pot. Then add your uncooked split red lentils to a heatproof bowl. Pour the hot water on top, to more than cover the lentils since they will expand, and soak for 30 minutes."],[null,"Preheat a non stick griddle on medium/high heat. Then drain your lentils and add to a high speed blender (I use a Vitamix), along with ALL remaining ingredients. Process on high speed until smooth."],[null,"Pour your batter directly from the blender spout onto your hot griddle, to make pancakes that are about 4 inches wide. If needed, use the back of a spoon or ladle to flatten the pancakes slightly so that they are thin, for even cooking. Cook for 4-5 minutes, until edges appear set, then flip and cook an additional 4-5 minutes until golden brown."],[null,"Serve with maple syrup, sliced bananas, walnuts, or fresh berries."]],"h":[[null,"* To soak your lentils , bring some water to a boil and then remove from the heat. Add the lentils and soak for 30 minutes, and then drain. Or boil water in a kettle and pour over top a heat proof bowl of your split red lentils. Do NOT sub the lentils . You MUST use split red lentils only for this lentil pancake recipe. Blend the pancake batter for about 1 full minute to ensure there are no grainy bits remaining. Cook these lentil pancakes a little longer than you would classic pancakes . They won’t make too many bubbles as an indicator for flipping them. Instead, look for edges that appear set and golden before flipping. If the batter gets too thick as it sits in your blender in between batches , slightly flatten your pancakes after pouring on your hot griddle. Use the back of a spoon or ladle to thin them out, if needed. This will ensure even cooking. One serving = FOUR 4 inch lentil pancakes in the nutritional info below. Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-4 days or freeze them for up to 2 months. Make sure to cool to room temperature before freezing, and reheat/thaw in the toaster."]]},"9833058":{"s":[[null,"Mash your banana in a bowl that has a lid, or mash into a plate and transfer to a jar. Then add all remaining ingredients and mix well."],[null,"Refrigerate overnight, or for AT LEAST 4 hours. Top with fresh fruit, nuts, seeds or any other toppings you'd like and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Make sure to use rolled oats or quick oats , NOT instant oats. Double the recipe to have breakfast ready for the next two days, or for sharing. Make it in advance , overnight is best, but a minimum of 4 hours works too. Use a very ripe banana with plenty of brown spots on the peel . Since most of the sweetness is coming from the banana, you want to be sure to choose a super ripe one, especially if you want to omit the maple syrup. Make sure to use certified gluten free oats , if needed, since oats often come into contact with other gluten containing products. Nutritional information does not include optional ingredients."]]},"6327861":{"s":[[null,"Place the banana slices and pineapple chunks in a single layer on a parchment-lined tray. Freeze for at least 2 hours or until solid."],[null,"In a high-powered blender or food processor, combine the frozen banana slices, frozen pineapple chunks, vanilla extract, and coconut milk."],[null,"Blend the ingredients until smooth and creamy, scraping down the sides as needed. If the mixture is too thick, you can add a bit more coconut milk to help with blending."],[null,"If you prefer a soft-serve texture, you can enjoy the \"nice\" cream immediately. If you prefer a firmer texture, transfer the mixture to an airtight container and freeze for an additional 1–2 hours."]],"h":[]},"6438939":{"s":[[null,"In a blender, combine the bananas, Greek yogurt, and syrup."],[null,"Pour the mixture into the popsicle molds and freeze for 8 hours or overnight."]],"h":[]},"9539871":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your waffle iron over medium heat and grease if needed."],[null,"Mash your bananas completely and combine them with the milk in a medium mixing bowl. Then add the dry ingredients and stir until well combined."],[null,"Scoop the waffle batter onto your preheated waffle iron and cook according to the manufacturer's directions for your brand of waffle iron. Mine took 3-4 minutes per batch. To check on the waffles, lift the lid slowly and gently to ensure they aren't sticking. If the waffles are sticking, they aren't ready, so continue cooking for another minute or so before checking again."],[null,"Serve your banana protein waffles with any of your favourite toppings."]],"h":[[null,"Weigh your flour and powder for the best results . If scooping from a bag, you may end up with too much and need more liquid to get the batter the right consistency."],[null,"If you don't have a kitchen scale , spoon the flour into your measuring cup and use a knife to scrape off the excess."],[null,"Use very ripe bananas that are spotted brown for the best flavour."],[null,"Make sure your waffle maker is HOT before adding the waffle batter to it, to prevent sticking."],[null,"Do not lift the lid too soon or your waffles will break and lift the lid slowly and carefully to check for sticking."],[null,"Subsequent batches of waffles cook a little faster than the first batch so watch closely."],[null,"Keep leftovers in the fridge for 3-4 days or frozen for up to 3 months."]]},"2516":{"s":[[null,"Line bottom of a 9” x 13” pan with vanilla wafers."],[null,"In a medium saucepan mix 2 boxes banana pudding mix with 2-1/2 cups rice milk. Bring to a boil over medium heat, stirring constantly."],[null,"Pour pudding mixture over vanilla wafers"],[null,"Put second layer of vanilla wafers over first, pressing each one down gently."],[null,"Refrigerate for 1 hour. Spread whipped topping over top of chilled dessert."],[null,"Return to refrigerator for at least 2 hours before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute sugar-free pudding mix to reduce carbohydrate content to 32 grams and 2 carbohydrate choices."],[null,"If you are not on a potassium restricted diet, top vanilla wafers with a layer of sliced bananas."],[null,"Check whipped topping ingredients and choose a brand that does not contain phosphate additives."]]},"9429573":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 375 degrees F."],[null,"Mash your banana in a large mixing bowl and then add all remaining wet ingredients and mix well. Then add your dry ingredients to the same bowl and mix until combined without overmixing."],[null,"Fill your mini muffin pans, almost to the top, leaving just a little room for rising. You should get 36 mini muffins."],[null,"Bake for 13-16 minutes, or until a toothpick inserted in the middle of the muffin comes out clean. Remove from the oven and let cool for 10 minutes before removing from the muffin pan and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"** If you don’t have brown rice flour , or oat flour on hand, add a cup of rice and cup of oats to a high speed blender and process until a flour like consistency is reached. This could take anywhere for 30-60 seconds depending on your machine. Use very ripe bananas. The more brown spots, the better to get the most natural sweetness possible. Fresh baby spinach is preferred over frozen . I find fresh spinach to have a more mild flavour than frozen and tastes best when used in a sweet treat. Don’t puree the spinach or the entire muffin will turn green. This can be off-putting to younger eaters, so I like to keep mine finely chopped to keep the muffins their yellow-y colour. If you don’t have spinach, you may also use kale. Just remember that kale has a stronger flavour, so you may want to reduce the amount slightly. Since these healthy muffins have hardly any fat, steer clear of parchment liners , or make sure to spray them with a nonstick spray to prevent them from sticking to the paper. Use a non stick muffin pan, OR make sure to grease the tins so your muffins don’t get stuck and break apart. Let your spinach banana muffins cool for 5-10 minutes after taking them out of the oven, before removing them from the muffin pan. I use a non stick muffin pan and don’t need to grease it, and these muffins pop out easily without breaking at all after the cool down period. Since these muffins are very low in sugar, you may add ¼-1/3 cup of chocolate chips (dairy free if vegan) if you have pickier eaters to please. Sweetness preference is all about what you’re accustomed to, and these suit us without the chocolate chips, but you know your family best."]]},"6923520":{"s":[],"h":[]},"5219021":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200˚C /180˚C fan / Gas Mark 6."],[null,"In a bowl combine the flour and paprika, gradually pour in the Renastep and water until a batter is formed."],[null,"Place the cauliflower florets and asparagus into the batter and coat well."],[null,"Place the panko breadcrumbs onto a plate and coat the battered florets evenly, ensuring to tap off any excess breadcrumbs."],[null,"Place all the battered vegetables onto a baking tray and bake for 25 minutes or until golden brown, making sure to turn half way through."],[null,"Meanwhile, in a small pan combine garlic, ginger, honey, siracha, lime juice, reduced salt soy sauce, sesame oil. Heat gently until just simmering then remove from the heat."],[null,"Once the vegetables have finished cooking place in a bowl and toss with the sauce until evenly coated."],[null,"Top with coriander and spring onions and serve!"]],"h":[["Renastep note","Renastep is a food for special medical purposes for the dietary management of kidney disease. Suitable from 3 years of age. Must be used under medical supervision. Renastep contains Milk (milk protein) and Fish (Tuna oil). This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutritics dietary analysis software. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information."]]},"7739965":{"s":[[null,"Add the chicken to a small pan of boiling water. Bring back to the boil, turn down the heat and simmer for 10 minutes until cooked through. Remove from the heat and leave in the water for 5 minutes."],[null,"For the salad, cut the spring onions into 3cm pieces and then cut them lengthways to create matchsticks. Prepare all of the other salad ingredients, mix everything together and reserve."],[null,"Add the oil to a small saucepan, then add the onion and cook for 3-4 minutes. Next, add the chilli, garlic and ginger, and stir for 1 minute. Add the water, honey, peanut butter and sesame oil, and stir until everything has dissolved."],[null,"Cut the chicken into small, thin pieces and add to the sauce, mixing to coat well."],[null,"Put the salad onto a plate and arrange the chicken around the outside. Serve with wedges of lime."]],"h":[[null,"This dish works just as well with cooked prawns, instead of chicken."],[null,"For a vegetarian option, try using marinated tofu."],[null,"To make this salad gluten-free, all you need to do is use gluten-free tamari in place of the soy sauce."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"3535":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375° F."],[null,"Dice onion and beat eggs."],[null,"Combine all ingredients, except barbecue sauce and water, in a large bowl and mix together."],[null,"Roll into 1” balls and place on a baking sheet."],[null,"Bake for 10 to 15 minutes, until meatballs are cooked through."],[null,"Combine barbecue sauce and water in a warming dish or Crock pot® on low temperature setting. Add meatballs and stir. Cover until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Instead of using commercial barbecue sauce, serve with Zesty Barbecue Sauce from the DaVita.com recipe collection. Sodium content is much lower."],[null,"Make meatballs ahead and refrigerate. When ready to serve, heat ingredients together and transfer to a warming dish."]]},"2541":{"s":[[null,"Mix ingredients together in a jar and shake to combine."],[null,"Use as a dry rub or combine with oil, vinegar, lemon juice or other seasonings to make a marinade or sauce."]],"h":[[null,"Adjust the amount used according to taste."]]},"7048524":{"s":[[null,"Simply mix together all the ingredients, divide between 6 large squares of foil and secure into parcels."],[null,"Cook over the barbeque coals for about 10–12 minutes and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Why not try a tropical version - use mangoes and pineapple."],[null,"Works well with different spices, such as cinnamon or ground ginger."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"2289":{"s":[[null,"Soak barley in 2 cups of water for 1 hour."],[null,"Dice onion and celery. Mince garlic clove. Slice carrots 1/4-inch thick. Cut beef into 1-1/2 inch cubes."],[null,"Place flour, black pepper and stew meat in a plastic bag. Shake to dust stew meat with flour."],[null,"Heat oil in a heavy 4-quart pot and brown the stew meat. Remove meat from pot."],[null,"Sauté and stir onion, celery and garlic in meat drippings for 2 minutes. Add 2 quarts of water and bring to a boil. Return meat to the pot. Add bay leaves and salt. reduce heat to a simmer."],[null,"Drain and rinse barley, then add to the pot. Cover and cook for 1 hour. Stir every 15 minutes."],[null,"After 1 hour add sliced carrots and Mrs. Dash® herb seasoning. Simmer for another hour. Add additional water if needed to prevent sticking."]],"h":[[null,"For a CKD non-dialysis lower protein diet, decrease beef to 8 ounces per recipe. Protein will be decreased to 14 grams per serving."]]},"7644476":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a large, non-stick frying pan, add the onion and cook for 1 minute."],[null,"Add the red pepper and garlic and cook for 2 minutes, then add the mushrooms and cook for 2-3 minutes."],[null,"Reserve a few mushrooms and set aside to garnish the dish."],[null,"Stir in the barley, add the stock, oregano and pepper, then mix well. Bring to the boil, then turn down the heat, add a lid and simmer, stirring regularly."],[null,"After about 25 minutes, remove the lid and continue simmering for around 10 minutes, until the liquid is absorbed and any excess is boiled off."],[null,"The barley should be cooked but still firm ('al dente')."],[null,"Stir through the cream alternative and the fresh basil, then serve with freshly ground black pepper, sprinkled with the reserved basil and mushrooms."]],"h":[[null,"Any mushrooms work for this dish but a combination of different types is ideal. You can buy mixed packs of wild mushrooms at most supermarkets, then bulk them up with a pack of basic mushrooms."],[null,"Suitable for freezing once cooked. Chill quickly. Defrost in the fridge and reheat thoroughly until piping-hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"4514201":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400°F. To prepare roasted broccoli, toss broccoli florets with olive oil. Place on a baking tray. Roast for 20 minutes. Set aside."],[null,"To prepare hardboiled eggs, cover eggs with cold water in a saucepan and bring to a boil. Cover with lid. Remove from heat. Let eggs stand in water for 10–12 minutes. Rinse eggs under cold water. Remove from shell and slice in half. Refrigerate."],[null,"Cook the barley according to instructions on the package. Drain and let stand to cool."],[null,"To assemble each Buddha bowl, layer the following ingredients: ¼ of the cooked barley 1 cup arugula ¼ of the roasted broccoli 2 hardboiled eggs, cut in half 1 tablespoon grated carrots"],[null,"Drizzle each salad with 1 tablespoon of olive oil and 1 tablespoon of lemon juice. Serve immediately. As an alternative, if you prefer a vinaigrette with your Buddha bowl, mix olive oil, lemon juice, sumac* and honey to taste and add to the vegetables and eggs. sortment of raw or cooked vegetables, overs. ed color to a dressing."]],"h":[[null,"Note: A Buddha bowl should consist of a grain, an as a protein and a dressing. It is an excellent way to use up left"],[null,"* Middle Eastern spice which gives a tangy flavor and r"],["Adding Variety With Ethnic Food","Choosing meals with different flavors and food items is ideal for a balanced diet when eating kidney-friendly. Outside of the traditional American diet, many ethnic foods can be low in potassium and a regular part of your kidney diet. While eating out can be convenient, knowing what is in your food and how it’s prepared can be a difficult task when eating at a buffet or restaurant. For the healthiest approach, try to plan ahead and make most meals at home. Consider the following when creating a diverse Asian cuisine with your kidney diet: • Sauce is a potential source of high MSG*, sodium and potassium. Limit the amount you use and also read nutrition fact labels and ingredient lists to find any hidden potassium and sodium additives. • Know which vegetables are higher in potassium per serving size such as spinach, bok choy and Swiss chard and eat less of them. • You may want to avoid eating any Asian soups as broths can be high in sodium or potassium. Consider making your own version of an Asian soup where you can control the ingredients. • Select steamed, low-potassium vegetables and rice as healthier alternative to fried food items."]]},"9329195":{"s":[[null,"Add the cooking oil or 1/4 cup of broth to your pot or skillet. Then sauté the onion, garlic, carrots and celery until softened, approx. 5 minutes."],[null,"Add the lentils, barley, vegetable broth, tomato sauce, bay leaves, cumin and paprika to your pot and give everything a good mix. Bring it to a boil, then reduce the heat and simmer until the lentils and barley are cooked, approx. 25 minutes."],[null,"Turn off the heat and remove the bay leaves. Then, stir in the lemon juice and fresh spinach until wilted. Taste for salt and pepper, and adjust as needed."]],"h":[[null,"Use a very flavourful broth ! If your broth is lacking flavour, make sure to adjust the seasonings."],[null,"If you don’t have any broth on hand , you can make some with this easy bouillon recipe . (I highly recommend this broth for its fantastic flavour.)"],[null,"Depending on your preferred thickness , use 6-8 cups of vegetable broth. For a thicker soup, use six cups. For a thinner soup, use eight. Remember: the soup will absorb more liquid as it cools."],[null,"Leftovers will keep in the fridge for 3-4 days or frozen for up to 3 months."]]},"7562767":{"s":[[null,"Add the barley, stock, cumin, cinnamon and pepper to a saucepan. Bring to the boil, turn down the heat, then cover and simmer for 20- 25 minutes. Check after 20 and stir to ensure it's not sticking and cook until tender, then remove from the heat and reserve."],[null,"Meanwhile, add 2 tsp oil to a non-stick pan and cook the slices of tofu until browned, about 5-7 minutes on each side. Remove them from the pan to cool a little, then slice into smaller pieces."],[null,"Add the garlic and fresh ginger to the pan and cook for 1-2 minutes. Then, return the tofu to the pan, sprinkle on the 5-spice, add half the coriander, mix well and reserve."],[null,"Next, add the rest of the oil to another pan and add the onion, red and yellow pepper and courgette and cook for 5-6 minutes,l stirring regularly until softened."],[null,"Add the peas to the cooked vegetables and mix in the barley. Divide between 2 plates, scatter with tofu, the rest of the coriander, soy sauce and pomegranate."]],"h":[[null,"Can be eaten hot, or cold as part of a packed lunch."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"6270294":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350°F. Coat a 9 x 9-inch baking dish with nonstick cooking spray."],[null,"In the bowl of an electric mixer, or with a hand mixer, beat the egg, egg white, oil, maple syrup, banana, almond milk, vanilla and peanut butter until smooth. Set the wet ingredients aside."],[null,"In a separate large bowl, mix the almond flour, chickpea flour, flaxseeds, baking powder and baking soda."],[null,"Add the dry ingredients to the wet ingredients and stir with a wooden spoon or a spatula until well combined. Fold in the chocolate chips. Pour the batter into the prepared baking dish and spread it evenly."],[null,"Transfer the pan to the oven and bake for 30 minutes, or until a toothpick inserted in the center comes out clean."],[null,"Remove the pan from the oven, let it cool slightly and then cut into 16 bars."]],"h":[]},"5422398":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350°F/180°C/Gas mark 4"],[null,"Mix together the semolina, sugar, baking powder, yoghurt, coconut flakes, butter, and tahini in a bowl until well combined."],[null,"Pour into a lined baking tin and flatten until level. Cut into 12 squares and press 1 almond into each square."],[null,"Bake for 30 minutes or until the cake is golden brown."],[null,"While the cake is baking, place the sugar, water, and lemon juice into a pan and dissolve the sugar. Once the mixture begins to boil, remove from the heat and set aside."],[null,"When fully cooked, remove the cake from the oven. Immediately pour over the sugar syrup and allow to cool."],[null,"Once cooled serve and enjoy!"]],"h":[["Renastep note","Always check with your dietitian or doctor that this recipe is suitable for you."]]},"6379140":{"s":[[null,"Add 1 1/2 cups of the beans to a large bowl with the onions. With a fork or potato masher, mash until mostly smooth (will be slightly chunky from onions). Note: If you have a food processor, you can blend until smooth then put in a bowl."],[null,"Add the remaining beans, the cooked grain, egg, garlic powder, salt and pepper. Stir until well combined."],[null,"Form bean mixture into 8, 1/2-inch thick patties."],[null,"Add cooking spray to a non-stick skillet over medium heat. Add bean patties and cook about 2-3 minutes per side, until slightly brown. Work in batches if your pan is not big enough to hold all 8 burgers."],[null,"Store in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 1 week or wrap individually in freezer bags or containers and freeze up to 6 months (freeze cooked burgers only, do not freeze the raw burgers)."]],"h":[]},"2879":{"s":[[null,"Blend eggs and milk in a blender to combine."],[null,"Slowly add flour and blend for 1 minute. Cover and let mixture sit for 1 hour.."],[null,"Pour crepe batter into a bowl and whisk in melted butter."],[null,"Heat an 8-inch crepe pan or skillet over medium-high heat. Coat pan with butter or nonstick cooking spray."],[null,"Using a 1/4 cup measure, pour batter into skillet. Make sure the batter lies evenly, moving the pan if needed. Crepe will bubble slightly."],[null,"Loosen edges of crepe and remove from pan when crepe is golden on the bottom and edges are slightly browned. (It needs to be browned on one side only as crepes will be rolled or folded.)"]],"h":[[null,"Adding flour slowly should prevent lumps, but if they do appear, strain the batter to remove before letting mixture set."]]},"2671":{"s":[[null,"Chop parsley and oregano."],[null,"Mix ingredients together to make 1/2 cup basic salad dressing."]],"h":[[null,"Try recipe with basil, dill, rosemary, or tarragon."],[null,"Substitute 1 teaspoon dried herbs if fresh herbs are unavailable."],[null,"Different flavored oils and vinegars also add variety. Try garlic oil, basil oil, or a small amount of sesame oil. For vinegar, try unseasoned rice vinegar or balsamic vinegar."]]},"3597":{"s":[[null,"Blend ingredients in a food processor or a blender. Store until ready to use."],[null,"When ready to use, dip fresh meat into margarine or oil, then coat with coating mix, one piece at a time."],[null,"Bake meat in the oven or fry in a skillet."]],"h":[[null,"Make homemade dry breadcrumbs by toasting bread in the oven until dry and crisp. Process in a food processor or blender to make crumbs."],[null,"This mix keeps well in the freezer. Make extra for later use."],[null,"Try the following variations for additional flavors:"],[null,"Beef or veal: add 1/2 teaspoon marjoram or oregano"],[null,"Chicken: add 1/2 teaspoon thyme and ½ teaspoon sage"]]},"3712518":{"s":[[null,"Heat a large non-stick pan set over a medium heat and add the vegetable oil. Add the chopped onions and cook for 6 to 8 minutes until soft."],[null,"Add the lentils, stock and tomato purée to the mince and onion mixture. Bring it to the boil, then reduce the heat and simmer for 25 minutes on a low heat."],[null,"Once cooked, divide the mince and lentil mixture into 5 portions to use."]],"h":[["Chef's note","Once made, this versatile recipe can be used as a base to make pie fillings, curries, stir fries, or pasta sauces."],["Carbohydrate","The lentils are the main source of carbohydrate in this dish. Values are provided for those trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","Replacing some of the beef mince with lentils has helped to reduce the phosphate content but you should still take a phosphate binder with this dish if you are prescribed one."],["Protein","Beef and lentils are the main protein sources in this dish. This dish is a good source of protein and therefore suitable for somebody who needs a higher protein diet."],["Storage","Batch-cooking can save money as well as time, as many foods are better value in the supermarket when bought in larger quantities. Portions of this mix can be stored in the fridge for 2 days or frozen, in single or double portions, for up to 3 months. Defrost thoroughly before using."]]},"6379945":{"s":[[null,"In a saucepot over medium heat, heat the olive oil. Add the onions, celery, and carrots and sauté for 5 minutes. Add the garlic and rosemary and sauté for 1 minute. Add the remaining ingredients, except the vinegar and basil. Bring to boiling. Reduce the heat and simmer, partially covered, for 20 minutes."],[null,"Add the vinegar. Top with the basil before serving."]],"h":[]},"2834":{"s":[[null,"Melt butter in a medium pan over medium heat."],[null,"Using a whisk (or fork), add flour and stir for 1 minute."],[null,"Add rice milk, stirring constantly, until sauce is thickened."],[null,"Add Mrs. Dash seasoning and stir. Use white sauce in your favorite recipe."]],"h":[[null,"Use white sauce as a replacement for cream soup in recipes. Check Mori’s suggestions below."],[null,"To make pot pie, double the above recipe and add 2 cups cooked, chopped chicken or turkey, 1/2 bag thawed frozen peas and carrots. Put into unbaked pie shell and bake at 350º F for about 45 minutes."],[null,"To make “mac n cheese,” double the above recipe and add 1/4 to 1/2 cup sharp cheddar cheese and one 12-ounce bag macaroni noodles (cooked)."],[null,"To make beef stroganoff, brown 1 pound ground beef. Add 1 recipe white sauce, one 12-ounce bag noodles (cooked) and 1 cup reduced fat sour cream."],[null,"To make chicken and rice, add 2 cups cooked, chopped chicken and 1-1/2 cups cooked rice. Put in dish sprayed with nonstick spray and top with 1/4 cup shredded sharp cheddar cheese. Bake at 350º F for 30 minutes."],[null,"To make chicken enchiladas, double the above recipe and add 1/2 cup sharp cheddar cheese and 1/2 cup picante sauce. To 1 cup of this sauce, add 1 cup chopped chicken. Put 1/4 of this mixture on a flour tortilla, roll it up and put in a baking dish sprayed with cooking spray. Repeat with 5 more tortillas. Top with remaining sauce and bake at 350º F for 15 to 20 minutes."]]},"3905":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 325° F."],[null,"Place chicken breast halves in a glass baking pan. Pierce each breast with a fork several times to allow mixture to season and flavor as it cooks."],[null,"Melt margarine in a glass mixing bowl in the microwave. Start at 15 seconds and stir to distribute heat."],[null,"To melted margarine, add basil, parmesan cheese, garlic powder and Mrs. Dash®. Stir mixture with a fork or whisk."],[null,"Pour mixture evenly over chicken breasts making sure parmesan cheese is smoothly distributed."],[null,"Baked uncovered, basting every 10 minutes with mixture from the pan, for a total of about 25 minutes or until juices in chicken are clear, not pink."]],"h":[[null,"Two tablespoons dried basil may be substituted if fresh basil is unavailable."],[null,"Parmesan cheese contains 36 milligrams phosphorus for one tablespoon. The key is to limit recipe to a very small amount to keep phosphorus low."],[null,"This recipe may be used in a CKD non-dialysis diet, but the portion size may need to be adjusted for a lower protein diet. Ask your dietitian about modifications for your individual protein requirements."]]},"3037":{"s":[[null,"Juice the lemon. Add all ingredients except flax and olive oils to a food processor."],[null,"Combine the oils and pour oil into the food processor through the top to evenly emulsify while blending the ingredients. Stir ingredients from the bottom of the blender as needed."],[null,"Store pesto in a jar or covered container until ready to use as a marinade, salad dressing or pasta sauce. Keeps up to one week in the refrigerator."]],"h":[[null,"An additional 2 tablespoons of flax oil may be substituted for the olive oil."],[null,"Flax oil provides health benefits including supplying ALA omega-3 fatty acids."],[null,"Basil Pesto has great versatility- use as a marinade on seafood or chicken, as a dipping sauce for fresh or roasted vegetables, a salad dressing or toss with pasta or rice as a lower potassium alternative to tomato sauce."]]},"6989636":{"s":[[null,"Place the spinach, garlic, shallot, Parmigiano-Reggiano, and basil in food processor. Process to a paste."],[null,"With the motor running, add the cottage cheese and oil. Process until smooth. Add milk to achieve the desired consistency, if needed."]],"h":[]},"6390494":{"s":[[null,"Mix ingredients and let set at room temperature for at least 1 hour."],[null,"Serve plain or on a lettuce leaf"]],"h":[]},"3457":{"s":[[null,"Cube pineapple and quarter strawberries."],[null,"Combine Splenda sweetener with 1/2 cup water in a saucepan; bring to a boil. Cook 1 minute."],[null,"Remove from heat and stir in basil and lime zest."],[null,"Cool to room temperature then strain through a fine strainer into a bowl; discard solids."],[null,"Combine pineapple, strawberries and blueberries in a large bowl. Drizzle with Splenda mixture and toss to coat. Chill until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Fresh basil works best, but you can use equal amount of dried whole leaves)."],[null,"This salad can be refrigerated up to two days."],[null,"For higher calories use sugar instead of Splenda sweetener."]]},"4958092":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, soak the chickpeas in 4 quarts of water for 12 hours to reduce potassium content. Drain the chickpeas and rinse them with water one more time. Set them aside."],[null,"In a saucepan, cook the rice according to the instructions on the package. Let the rice cool in the uncovered pan."],[null,"While the rice is cooking, in a big bowl, combine the ingredients for the salad: chickpeas, cucumber, celery, mandarins, onion, and coriander. Add the rice and mix gently."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the ingredients for the dressing: olive oil, lime juice, and zest. Pour the dressing over the salad, add some pepper to taste, and gently mix. Garnish with walnuts."],[null,"Refrigerate for 1 hour before serving."]],"h":[[null,"* fresh or canned"],[null,"Tip: Drain and rinse canned items to reduce sodium."],[null,"*Can be lower with soaking"],["Vegetable-based proteins","There are many things to consider with a kidney-friendly diet. One area of concern is the amount and type of protein. In general, people with earlier stage chronic kidney disease (CKD) should consume less protein to decrease the workload on the kidneys. A good way to lower protein intake is to add more plant-based or vegetable proteins to your diet. These foods tend to provide a fair volume of calories with a much lower protein content compared to protein from animal sources. Eating plant-based proteins can also help to protect the kidneys and slow the decline in kidney function. Chickpeas, also known as garbanzo beans, are a great source of plant-based protein and fiber. They are also rich in vitamins and minerals such as folate and iron. They are typically affordable and available in both canned and dry varieties. When buying them canned, look for those that are labeled “no salt added” or “low in sodium”. Chickpeas can be added to a variety of dishes such as salads, soups, stews, chilies, burgers, and tacos. They can also be mashed to make hummus and roasted in the oven to make a crunchy snack. When cooking them, add onions, garlic, herbs, and spices for extra flavor."]]},"1002989":{"s":[[null,"Blend all ingredients until the mixture is smooth."],[null,"Divide into 4 servings and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Freeze extra servings for later."]]},"2647":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 450° F."],[null,"Set cream cheese out to soften. Peel, core and slice apples."],[null,"Cream together butter, 1/3 cup sugar and 1/4 teaspoon vanilla."],[null,"Fold in flour to make a dough."],[null,"Spread dough on bottom and sides of a 9″ spring form pan."],[null,"In a medium bowl combine softened cream cheese and 1/3 cup sugar; mix well."],[null,"Add egg and 1/2 teaspoon vanilla; mix until blended."],[null,"Pour mixture into pastry-lined pan."],[null,"Combine 1/3 cup sugar and cinnamon; toss with apples until all are coated."],[null,"Spoon apple mixture over cream cheese layer."],[null,"Sprinkle with almonds."],[null,"Bake at 450° F for 10 minutes."],[null,"Reduce heat to 400° F and continue baking for 25 minutes. Cool."]],"h":[[null,"One medium apple yields 1 cup when peeled and cored."],[null,"You can substitute fresh cranberries for slivered almonds on top of tart to reduce phosphorus to 53 mg per serving."],[null,"For a lower carbohydrate version diabetics can substitute Splenda® granular instead of sugar; carbohydrate is reduced to 19 grams, calories 266."]]},"3978":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Spray baking sheet with nonstick cooking spray and place 2 pitas on sheet."],[null,"Spread 1-1/2 tablespoon BBQ sauce on each pita."],[null,"Chop onion and spread over pitas."],[null,"Cube chicken and spread over pitas."],[null,"Sprinkle feta cheese and garlic powder over pitas."],[null,"Bake for 11 to 13 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"See Spicy BBQ Sauce recipe on DaVita.com. It has only 43 mg sodium per 2 tablespoons compared to 125-460 mg sodium in commercially prepared barbecue sauce."],[null,"Eat pita pizzas promptly after baking; otherwise they may become too crispy."],[null,"Check the nutrition labels and buy the brand of feta cheese and pitas with the lowest amount of sodium."]]},"6923281":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375°F. Spray a baking sheet with cooking spray."],[null,"Season the chicken with salt and pepper on both sides."],[null,"Place the chicken on the prepared baking sheet and bake for 25 minutes or until the juices run clear. Remove the chicken from the oven and chop into half-inch pieces."],[null,"In a small saucepan, combine the sugar-free apricot preserves, barbeque sauce, and hot sauce. Bring to a boil."],[null,"Spoon the sauce over the pizza crust. Top the crust with cooked chicken, sliced onion, carrot, and cheese. Sprinkle the cheese with the dried oregano."],[null,"Bake the pizza for 20-25 minutes or until the cheese is melted and bubbly."]],"h":[]},"6065602":{"s":[[null,"Preheat an indoor or outdoor grill."],[null,"In a medium bowl combine the ground chicken, egg, oatmeal, paprika, chili powder and pepper. Mix well."],[null,"Divide the meat mixture into 6 equal portions and press into patties."],[null,"Grill the sliders on one side for 4-5 minutes. Flip the sliders and brush them with 2 tbsp. barbeque sauce. Continue grilling for 4 – 5 minutes and flip again. Brush with the remaining BBQ sauce. Grill for another 2-3 minutes or until the burgers are cooked through. They should reach an internal temperature of 165°F."],[null,"Open the slider buns. Place a burger on each bottom half. Top each with a piece of lettuce and a slice of tomato."]],"h":[]},"4789516":{"s":[[null,"Combine flour and Mrs. Dash herb seasoning in a paper bag. Add chicken thighs and shake to coat."],[null,"Place chicken thighs on grill and drizzle with margarine. Broil 3-4 inches from heat until almost done."],[null,"Make the BBQ sauce and pour over chicken (after about 25 minutes) and continue grilling until done."],["BBQ sauce preparation (prepare in advance)","Spray non-stick pan with cooking spray and saute’ the onion and garlic. Remove from heat and stir in remaining ingredients. Return pan to heat and bring mixture to a boil. Lower heat and simmer for 3 minutes. Stir frequently to prevent sticking."]],"h":[]},"9235323":{"s":[[null,"Drain and rinse your jackfruit very well to wash away the brine flavour. Then use your hands (or two forks on a cutting board) to pull apart the chunks of jackfruit until shredded. Place in a small mixing bowl and set aside."],[null,"In another small bowl add ALL the sauce ingredients and whisk to combine. Then pour it over the jackfruit and mix to evenly coat. Choose a cooking method below."],["Oven Instructions","Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F and line a baking sheet with parchment paper. Arrange the coated jackfruit on the tray and bake for 20 minutes, mixing once at the halfway point. Remove from the oven."],["Instant Pot Instructions","Add the coated jackfruit to your Instant Pot and cook on high pressure for 5 minutes. Then naturally release for 10 minutes. If not fully released after 10 minutes, quick release the remaining pressure and open the lid once safe to do so."],["Stove Top Instructions","Place the coated jackfruit in a medium pan and cook over medium-high heat and stir occasionally, until the sauce is mostly absorbed. This will take about 10-12 minutes."],["Assemble your Vegan Burritos","Assemble your jackfruit burrito with desired toppings and tortilla wrap of choice, or make it a jackfruit burrito bowl over a bed of lettuce with desired toppings on top."]],"h":[[null,"Do not over stuff your vegan burritos or they will be difficult to close and hold and may fall apart. Less is more! Store leftover toppings in separate containers in your fridge for 3-4 days and assemble your jackfruit burrito just before eating to prevent the tortilla from getting soggy."]]},"9426702":{"s":[[null,"Start by making your vegan mozzarella cheese. Then refrigerate while you prepare the rest, so it firms up a bit, making it easier to scoop onto your crust."],[null,"Drain and rinse your jackfruit very well to wash off the brine flavour. Then transfer to a food processor and pulse until shredded. Do not over process, you want chunky pieces, not a mince.Alternatively, you may transfer the jackfruit to a cutting board and pull the pieces apart with your fingers or two forks. Set aside."],["To Cook the Jackfruit on Stove Top","Whisk together all the sauce ingredients in a small bowl and set aside."],["To Cook the Jackfruit on Stove Top","Place the shredded jackfruit in a pan and pour the sauce on top. Sauté over medium heat, mixing occasionally, until the sauce is mostly absorbed. This will take about 8-10 minutes."],["To Cook the Jackfruit in your Instant Pot","Place the shredded jackfruit and all the sauce ingredients in your Instant Pot. (No need to pre-whisk the sauce in a separate bowl.) Mix well, close the lid and set the valve to the sealing position. Cook on high pressure for 3 minutes and let your Instant Pot naturally release, which will take around 10 minutes. If not fully released after 10 minutes, quick release the remaining pressure."],["For the Pizza Assembly","Preheat your oven to 425 degrees F and line a large baking tray to fit both flatbreads with parchment paper, or use two smaller trays."],["For the Pizza Assembly","Divide the jackfruit between your two flatbreads, and scoop the vegan mozzarella using a melon baller or teaspoon. Dollop the cheese all over the pizza and sprinkle the red onion on top. Bake for 13-18 minutes, or until edges are golden and mozzarella is slightly melted."]],"h":[[null,"Make sure to rinse the jackfruit very well to remove as much of the brine flavour, as possible. Do not over process the jackfruit , if you’re using your food processor. Just pulse until shredded, without mincing. You want chunkier pieces. If there are any whole pieces that didn’t break down, tear them apart with your hands to avoid over processing the rest of the pieces. Your jackfruit pizza will keep refrigerated for 3-4 days in a sealed container. You may reheat in the oven or toaster oven."]]},"6653955":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, stir together the barbecue sauce, smoked paprika, and salt; set aside."],[null,"In a large saucepan over medium heat, fully heat the oil. Add the popcorn kernels, cover with a lid, and periodically shake the saucepan until you hear the popping begin. Let the popcorn pop undisturbed until it stops, about 3 minutes. Carefully remove lid."],[null,"Immediately pour the barbecue sauce mixture onto popcorn while over medium heat. Stir well until the popcorn is lightly coated and re-crisped, about 2 minutes. Serve."]],"h":[]},"3504":{"s":[[null,"Heat oil in a skillet over medium heat. Add diced onion and green pepper. Sauté for 2 minutes."],[null,"Add hash browns and cook for 5 minutes."],[null,"Beat eggs with soy milk or nondairy creamer."],[null,"Pour egg mixture into a separate nonstick pan and cook on medium heat until the omelet firms up."],[null,"Place the hash brown mixture in the middle of the omelet surface and loosen both sides of the omelet with a spatula, then roll it over onto a serving plate."],[null,"Garnish with parsley sprigs and add spices of your choice."]],"h":[[null,"Check with your dietitian for recommended soy milk or nondairy creamer to use. Brands vary greatly in potassium and phosphorus content."],[null,"Use milk substitute of choice instead of soy milk if desired."]]},"3194515":{"s":[[null,"Chop the onion and pepper and set aside."],[null,"Make the vegetable stock and measure the couscous. Stir the hot vegetable stock into the couscous, cover and leave to sit for five minutes."],[null,"Heat the olive oil in a small pan. Sauté the onion on a low heat for five minutes or until soft, then remove the pan from the heat."],[null,"Uncover the couscous and use a fork to fluff it up. Add the cooked onion and fresh pepper, then drain the bean salad and add to the couscous. Stir gently until well mixed. If using parsley, sprinkle it over the salad before serving."]],"h":[["Chef's note","An easy vegan bean and couscous salad that can be prepared in advance for a healthy lunch."],["Carbohydrate","The main sources of carbohydrate in this dish come from the couscous and beans. The carbohydrate value of this dish has been provided for those who have been trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","Beans do contain potassium and phosphate, but when using the amount in this recipe, the overall levels are low. If you have been prescribed a phosphate binder, ensure you take them with this dish."],["Protein","This recipe is low in protein which is great for people who have been advised to reduce their protein. If you have been advised to increase your protein, you may wish to add a small tin of tuna. Look for tuna in spring water and drain before use."],["Gluten free","Use buckwheat or quinoa and a gluten-free vegetable stock for a gluten-free option."],["Storage","This dish keeps well and can be stored in the fridge for up to 3 days."]]},"7719810":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas mark 4. Heat the oil in a saucepan, then fry the onion for 2-3 minutes until soft. Add the garlic, yellow pepper, mushrooms, chilli powder, oregano and cumin. Stir the ingredients together."],[null,"Add the tomatoes, tomato puree and carrot. Mix well. Bring to the boil, turn down the heat, cover with a lid, then simmer for 10 minutes, stirring occasionally."],[null,"Add the mixed beans and green lentils, mix, then bring back to boiling point. Stir and remove from the heat."],[null,"Spread 4 tablespoons of the chilli mixture over the base of a large ovenproof dish. Lay the tortillas onto a board and divide the rest of the chilli mixture between them. Fold over the ends and roll up to seal. Place them in a row in the ovenproof dish."],[null,"Mix the yogurt and grated Cheddar together, and dot over the enchiladas. Bake for 12-15 minutes, until lightly browned. Serve with salad."]],"h":[[null,"The chilli mixture is great served on baked sweet potatoes or rice, or spoon it over tortilla chips to make healthier nachos."],[null,"The chilli filling is also freezable."],[null,"You don't have to use the herbs and spices we've outlined in the ingredients, you can use whatever you have available in your store cupboard."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 5"]]},"5375084":{"s":[["Preparation for the Bean Burger Sauce","Wash the cucumber and grate using the large holes of a box grater. Drain off the excess liquid."],["Preparation for the Bean Burger Sauce","Mix the cucumber with the Greek yogurt, garlic powder, dill, pepper and lemon juice to make the bean sauce."],["Preparation for the Bean Burger Sauce","Cover and place in the refrigerator until ready to serve."],["Preparation for the Bean Burger","Rinse and drain the tinned chickpeas. Chop the ends off the spring onions."],["Preparation for the Bean Burger","Using a food processor, combine the chickpeas, spring onions, egg, flour, oregano and cumin. Blend and pulse until a mixture forms that holds together when pressed. The mixture will be moist. Form into 4 burgers."],["Preparation for the Bean Burger","Heat the olive oil in a frying pan over a medium heat. When hot, add the burgers. Cook until golden and beginning to crisp (approximately 4-5 minutes). Flip and cook until golden brown and crisp (approximately 2-4 minutes more)."],["Preparation for the Bean Burger","Warm the pitta bread and cut each in half."],["Preparation for the Bean Burger","Assemble your plate with the pitta half, bean burger and sauce. Add some red onion slices, shredded lettuce and sliced cucumber for the garnish."]],"h":[]},"3643178":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 200°C / fan 180°C / gas mark 6. Prick sweet potatoes all over and rub with a little olive oil. Bake in oven for approximately 40 minutes, until soft."],[null,"While the potatoes are cooking, heat the olive oil in a pan over a medium heat and fry the spring onions and garlic until soft."],[null,"Add in the black beans, tomato purée, chilli flakes, cumin, paprika and sweetcorn. Mix together and cook over a low heat for 10 minutes."],[null,"Remove potatoes from oven when cooked and rest for 5 minutes. To make an opening, slit along the length of the potato, prise open a little and fill with the bean mix. Serve with soured cream on top."]],"h":[["Chef's note","This bean chilli recipe is a delicious vegetarian option, providing plenty of fibre and protein."],["Carbohydrate","Sweet potato is the main source of carbohydrate in this recipe, and the value has been provided for those who have been trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","Despite the use of some high potassium ingredients, such as baked sweet potatoes and tomato purée, this recipe is low in potassium, when following the quantities in the ingredients and the serving sizes. This recipe is also low in phosphate, however it does contain some phosphate, mainly provided by the black beans, so if you have been prescribed a phosphate binder, you should take as directed."],["Protein","This recipe is a source of protein, therefore suitable for those advised to eat more protein, such as those receiving dialysis."],["Healthier option","You could parboil the sweet potato before roasting to lower the potassium content further."],["Storage","The bean mixture can be prepared in advance and stored in an airtight container in the fridge for up to 3 days."]]},"3853426":{"s":[[null,"Put the carrots into a pan and cover with the boiling stock. Simmer for 4 minutes."],[null,"Add in the drained beans, tomato puree and mixed herbs and stir."],[null,"Reduce heat and simmer for 20 minutes, then add the frozen peas and cook for 3-5 minutes more."],[null,"Serve into 2 dishes with the bread and season with black pepper. Sprinkle over the grated cheese."]],"h":[["Chef's note","A wholesome, high-protein vegetarian dish that’s also low in potassium and phosphate."],["Carbohydrate","The bread is the main source of carbohydrate in this main meal, however the beans will also be a source of carbohydrate. The value has been provided for those who have been trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/Phosphate","This dish is low in potassium; if you have been advised to follow a low-potassium diet, ensure you keep to the quantities stated. This recipe is low in phosphate, however does contain some phosphate, due to the beans and cheese, therefore if you have been prescribed a phosphate binder please ensure you take them with this dish."],["Protein","This dish is high in protein and therefore suitable for those receiving dialysis. If you have been advised to eat less protein then you may wish to swap the peas for sweetcorn and/or reduce the quantity of cheese to 30g."]]},"9950861":{"s":[[null,"Add the beets to a small sauce pan covered in water and bring to a boil, cooking until fork tender, approx 20 minutes."],[null,"Add the beets and all remaining ingredients to a food processor, and process until combined, stopping to scrape down the sides as needed."],[null,"Serve with pita, veggies, or crackers, enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Makes approx. 2 cups. Store leftovers in an airtight container in the fridge for up to 5 days."]]},"4457544":{"s":[[null,"1. Dry beef cubes gently with paper towel."],[null,"2. Heat a heavy 4 quart soup pot on high, add oil and then the beef, browning well on all sides, about 5 minutes."],[null,"3. Add onion and garlic and continue to cook for another 5 minutes."],[null,"4. Add the herbs, spices and veggie mix, then the broth and water and bring to a boil."],[null,"5. Add the bulgur and the barley reducing the temperature to minimum and cover with a well fitting lid. Cook for approximately 1 hour and 15 minutes (until beef is tender)."],[null,"6. If using a slow cooker, transfer the beef after step 3. Add all ingredients and put the setting on low, cover, and cook for 4 hours."],[null,"7. For the perfect finish add 1/4 cup freshly chopped parsley at the end of cooking time."],[null,"Enjoy."]],"h":[]},"6656377":{"s":[[null,"Prepare rice according to package directions (or start with 2 cups cooked rice)."],[null,"Microwave frozen stir-fry vegetable blend on defrost setting for 3-4 minutes to thaw."],[null,"In a fry pan or wok heat oil and sauté the garlic until fragrant. Add vegetable blend and cook over high heat, stirring constantly, for about 5 minutes. Remove from pan and set aside."],[null,"Add the beef to the pan and cook until beef is done to your likeness, or about 7 minutes."],[null,"Prepare the sauce by combining chicken broth, cornstarch and soy sauce in a bowl."],[null,"Add cooked vegetables and sauce to the pan with the beef. Heat and stir until sauce is thick. Serve stir fry with 1/2 cup cooked rice."]],"h":[]},"7900276":{"s":[[null,"Heat the rapeseed oil in a pan, add the onions, then cook gently for 5 minutes, stirring regularly."],[null,"Add the minced beef and stir for 5 minutes until starting to brown, breaking up any clumps with a wooden spoon."],[null,"Add the garlic, carrots, swede, leek and celery and cook for 5 minutes, stirring regularly."],[null,"Sprinkle the flour over the mince and vegetables, mixing well. Stir in the beef stock."],[null,"Mix again, add the pearl barley, thyme and pepper, bring to the boil, turn down the heat, cover, then simmer gently for 30 minutes. Serve with a sprinkle of chives."]],"h":[[null,"You can make this with minced lamb, or use minced turkey for a lower-fat dish."],[null,"For a vegan version, replace the beef with a can of green lentils and a low-salt vegetable stock cube."],[null,"To concentrate the flavours further, you can cook without a lid to reduce the amount of liquid."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Can be frozen in small pots for individual portions. Defrost in a microwave or on the hob, over a very low heat until piping hot."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"2160":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 425° F."],[null,"Dissolve yeast in 1 cup warm water. Stir in 1 tablespoon olive oil, sugar and flour to make dough. Place in a greased bowl, cover and set aside."],[null,"Combine tomato paste, 1/2 cup water, Italian seasoning, garlic powder and remaining oil in a small saucepan and simmer for 5 minutes."],[null,"Chop onion and bell pepper."],[null,"Brown meat with black pepper and crushed red pepper in a skillet. Drain off fat. Add onion and green pepper."],[null,"Spray a pizza pan or a 17 x 14-inch baking sheet with nonstick cooking spray . Press dough onto pan or sheet. Spread sauce, meat mixture and cheese over dough."],[null,"Bake for 20 minutes or until dough and cheese are golden brown."],[null,"Cut into 6 slices and serve."]],"h":[[null,"1/2 package dry yeast equals 1-1/4 teaspoons."],[null,"Each pizza slice has only 1 ounce of cheese to keep phosphorus low."]]},"6305434":{"s":[[null,"For the marinade, whisk together the baking soda with 2 Tbsp water in a bowl. Coat the beef in the mixture and let it sit for 5–30 minutes in the refrigerator."],[null,"To create the sauce, stir together the coconut aminos, hoisin sauce, 1 ½ Tbsp water, garlic, ginger, and red pepper flakes in a small bowl."],[null,"Heat the oil in a large wok or skillet over medium-high heat. Add the beef and cook until crisp outside but still pink inside, about 2–3 minutes. Stir in 1 Tbsp of the sauce and cook for 30 seconds. Transfer the beef to a plate using a slotted spoon."],[null,"Add the carrots, broccoli, cabbage, and bell pepper to the wok, cooking until crisp-tender, about 6 minutes."],[null,"Reduce heat to medium, return the beef to the wok, and pour the remaining sauce over the top. Add half of the scallions. Cook for 1 minute."],[null,"Divide the steamed cauliflower rice among plates, top with beef and broccoli, ensuring to include all the sauce. Garnish with the remaining scallions."]],"h":[]},"2714":{"s":[[null,"Dice the onion and mince the garlic clove."],[null,"In either a hot skillet or directly onto the flame, heat chile peppers until skin is evenly blackened. Carefully, wrap chiles in plastic wrap or paper bag to continue to soften and cool."],[null,"Place 1 teaspoon oil, diced onion and garlic in a skillet over medium heat to soften. Add ground beef and cook until it crumbles and is brown. Set aside in a bowl."],[null,"Once chile peppers have cooled, peel off blackened skin and cut in half lengthwise. Remove the seeds and clean out the inside."],[null,"Add the asadero and ricotta cheeses to the cooled ground beef mixture. Stuff each chile half with this mixture."],[null,"In a small bowl beat the egg white."],[null,"Heat oil in a skillet. Coat each chile with a light layer of flour and then dip into the egg white to cover. Fry each chile in oil until golden."]],"h":[[null,"Run chiles under cold water to remove blackened skin."],[null,"Substitute poblano chiles or small bell peppers if Anaheim chiles are unavailable."],[null,"To reduce fat, reduce amount of cheese or eliminate. Use lean ground beef 7-10%."]]},"6032146":{"s":[[null,"Add olive oil and generous amount of cooking spray to a large soup pot over high heat. In batches, brown beef on all sides. Do not overcrowd the pan with beef or it will not brown."],[null,"Remove the beef from the pan and set aside. Add onions, carrots and celery to the pan and sauté for 4-5 minutes."],[null,"Add the beef broth and scrape the brown bits off the bottom of the pan. Add beef and simmer for 1 hour."],[null,"While the beef is simmering, soak the prunes in hot water for 20 minutes. Drain the prunes, saving the water and set aside."],[null,"After the beef has simmered for 1 hour, add the drained prunes, sweet potatoes, 1/2 cup of the prune water, cinnamon, ground black pepper and salt. Bring to a simmer, covered, for 20 minutes or until potatoes are tender."],[null,"Stir in the chopped parsley and serve."]],"h":[]},"6142849":{"s":[[null,"Soak wooden skewers in cold water for at least 10 minutes."],[null,"Combine garlic, turmeric, coriander, fennel seeds, chili flakes, minced green chili, garam masala, 1/2 tsp sat, and lime juice in a bowl. Add steak cubes, stir to coat, and marinate in the refrigerator for 2–3 hours (or up to 6 hours). Remove from refrigerator and let stand at room temperature for 30 minutes before grilling."],[null,"After steak has marinated and rested at room temperature, preheat a cast iron griddle over medium-high heat or an outdoor grill. Brush griddle or grill lightly with ½ tsp / 2.5 mL oil to prevent kebabs from sticking."],[null,"Skewer steak onto wooden skewers (about 5–6 pieces of steak per skewer), leaving some space between each piece, and brush with remaining 1½ tsp / 7.5 mL oil. Sprinkle with remaining 1/2 tsp salt."],[null,"Place kebabs on the griddle or grill and cook for about 4 minutes per side (8 minutes total). Serve hot, garnished with lime wedges (for squeezing over kebabs) and cilantro."]],"h":[]},"2790":{"s":[[null,"Strain brisket pan juices and pour into a large measuring cup. Add water to make 2 cups broth."],[null,"In a small dish, combine 1/2 cup pan juice broth and flour. Whisk until smooth. Add remaining broth, vinegar and Worcestershire sauce."],[null,"In a medium saucepan, heat and stir broth over medium to medium-low heat until it thickens and comes to a rolling boil."],[null,"Remove from heat. Serve over cooked meat."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute 2 cups low-sodium broth if pan juices are unavailable."],[null,"A hot roast beef sandwich with beef brisket gravy makes a tasty lunch."],[null,"For smooth, lump-free gravy, stir flour into a small portion of broth before adding to heat."],[null,"Avoid heating gravy too quickly. Use medium-low to medium heat, and stir constantly as mixture starts to thicken."]]},"3852":{"s":[[null,"Chop onion and green pepper."],[null,"In a medium skillet, brown ground beef; drain on paper towels."],[null,"Spray skillet with non-stick cooking spray; add onion and green pepper and cook for 3 to 5 minutes, until vegetables are softened."],[null,"Add beef, tomato puree, black pepper and cumin to onion/pepper mixture; mix well and cook for 3 to 5 minutes on low heat."],[null,"Divide the beef mixture among tortillas. Roll the tortilla over burrito style, making sure that both ends are folded first so mixture does not fall out."]],"h":[[null,"Add lettuce and Tabasco® hot pepper sauce if desired."]]},"1773":{"s":[[null,"Chop onion, bell pepper and chipotle pepper. Mince garlic and shred lettuce."],[null,"Trim fat from meat. Cut into 6 pieces."],[null,"In a 4-quart Crock Pot®, place meat, tomatoes (undrained), onion, bell pepper, chipotle pepper, spices and garlic."],[null,"Cover and cook on low setting for 8–10 hours or on high for 4–5 hours."],[null,"Add rice to water and cook according to package directions."],[null,"Remove meat from cooker and shred, using 2 forks. Place in a large bowl and add sauce to desired consistency."],[null,"Warm tortillas and spoon meat onto each one. Add 4 teaspoons cheese, 1 tablespoon sour cream, shredded lettuce and 1/2 cup cooked rice. Roll up and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"If desired, replace canned tomatoes with 1 large fresh tomato, peeled and diced. Replace chipotle pepper with a fresh jalapeno pepper, seeded and diced."],[null,"Adjust spices/peppers as desired."],[null,"For a lower calorie and carbohydrate meal serve over rice and omit tortillas."],[null,"For added kick, chop cilantro and stir into cooked rice. Add a splash of lime juice."],[null,"For a lower protein diet adjust the portion to match your meal plan."],[null,"To reduce fat, used low fat sour cream and eliminate cheese if desired."]]},"7231712":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a wok or large saucepan. Add the beef strips, stir for 1 minute, then add the ginger and garlic and stir for another minute. Remove the beef from the wok and set aside."],[null,"Put the wok back on the heat and add the onion and carrot. Stir for 2 minutes, then add the red pepper and broccoli. Stir for another 2-3 minutes."],[null,"Add 2-3 tbsp of water, then cover with a saucepan lid to trap the steam. Cook for a further 2 minutes."],[null,"Bring a saucepan of water to the boil and cook the dried noodles for 4 minutes."],[null,"Return the beef, along with any juices, to the wok. Stir well. Add the mangetout and drained noodles, then stir for 2 minutes."],[null,"Finally, stir through the oyster sauce and place in bowls. Sprinkle with sesame seeds to serve."]],"h":[[null,"For a gluten-free version, use rice noodles."],[null,"You can use chicken or turkey for this dish."],[null,"For a vegetarian version, use strips of tofu in place of beef."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"6435172":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a nonstick Dutch oven or large nonstick saucepot over medium-high heat. Add the beef and cook, turning occasionally, until browned, about 5 minutes. Add the onion, bell pepper, cubanelle, celery, and garlic. Cook, stirring occasionally, until the vegetables are tender, about 8 minutes."],[null,"Add the broth, tomato sauce, adobo seasoning, salt, and bay leaves; bring to a boil. Reduce the heat to medium low. Cover and simmer until the meat is just tender, about 1 hour."],[null,"Add the yucca, plantain, chayote squash, and tomato and cook, stirring occasionally, until the meat and vegetables are fork-tender, about 40 minutes."],[null,"Remove from the heat. Remove and discard the bay leaves; stir in the cilantro."]],"h":[]},"4218015":{"s":[[null,"To the bottom of a slow cooker, add the onion, mushrooms, garlic, rosemary and pepper."],[null,"In a large skillet, heat the oil on high heat. Fry the beef short ribs on all sides."],[null,"Add the short ribs to the slow cooker and top with broth and water. Cover and cook on low for 9 hours. The meat will fall off the bones. Discard all bones."],[null,"In a small bowl, dissolve the cornstarch in water."],[null,"Add the cornstarch mixture to the slow cooker and stir to incorporate. The cornstarch mixture will thicken the liquid."],[null,"Cover and cook for another hour. Then turn off the heat and stir in the sour cream."],[null,"Serve the stroganoff with egg noodles and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"* If you want to avoid bones, you can use stewing beef instead"],[null,"PLEASE NOTE: This recipe is higher in potassium and portion size is important. Check with your registered dietitian to see how this recipe can be included in your diet."],["Onions, garlic and fresh herbs","Eating foods low in sodium is a cornerstone of the chronic kidney disease diet. Many of us have eaten high-sodium foods or added salt to foods most of our lives; thus eliminating salt from the diet can be difficult. Foods initially will seem bland as the tongue expects the overpowering flavor of salt to be first and foremost, but over time your taste buds will adjust and it'll become much easier to eliminate salt. An excellent way to add flavor to foods without adding sodium, phosphorus and potassium is to use onions, garlic and a variety of fresh herbs. Add fresh or sautéed onions and garlic to meats, stews, soups and mixed dishes. There are many types of fresh herbs that can be used to increase flavor. Fresh herbs can be expensive to buy in the grocery store, but don’t let that stop you from using them, as they can be fun to grow in small pots at home. When using herbs for the first time, remember that they should enhance the flavor of your food, not overpower or mask its natural flavor. Begin by using no more than one or two herbs at a time. Also, start with no more than ¾ teaspoon of fresh chopped herbs for every four servings of food or one pound of meat. You can always increase this amount as desired. The correct blend of herbs is whatever tastes best to you. Be adventuresome and create new flavor combinations that you enjoy."]]},"7250013":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4. Add the oil to a large pan, and after 2–3 minutes add the beef. Stir for 2 minutes, then once the meat has sealed, add the onions, carrots, celery and mushrooms, and cook for 3–4 minutes."],[null,"Add the potatoes and sprinkle the flour over the dish, coating the beef and vegetables evenly."],[null,"Gradually pour in the stock, stirring constantly. Simmer for 2–3 minutes until it thickens."],[null,"Remove from heat and place in an overproof dish, cover and cook in the oven for 1¼ hours."],[null,"After the stew has been cooking for 1 hour, make the dumplings: Add the flour, baking powder, pepper, thyme and parsley to a bowl, then gradually stir in the milk, mixing well to form a soft dough. So the dough doesn't stick, use the olive oil to oil your hands, then roll the dough into six balls and set aside."],[null,"Place the dumplings on top of the stew and cook uncovered for 15–20 minutes until they are cooked with a light crust, but still soft."]],"h":[[null,"Make this classic dish veggie-friendly by replacing the lean beef with a meat substitute, or by simply adding more vegetables."],[null,"To lower the carbohydrate count of this dish, try making smaller dumplings or leave them out completely."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"3825469":{"s":[[null,"Cut the beef into 1cm strips and place in bowl. Add the paprika and chilli powder, evenly coating the beef. Leave to marinate for 1 hour. Stir after 30 minutes and check the beef is well coated."],[null,"Add the rice to a saucepan and pour over 500ml of water. Bring to a rolling boil and reduce the heat to a gentle simmer. Cook for 12 minutes."],[null,"Cut the celery and pepper into 5 cm lengths and then into strips about 5 mm thick. Thinly slice the spring onions and set aside."],[null,"Heat the oil in a wok or large frying pan and fry the spring onions, garlic, celery and peppers for one minute before adding the steak. Continue to fry on a high heat for 3-4 minutes."],[null,"Make up the sauce by adding one stock cube to 60ml of boiling water and adding the Worcestershire sauce, honey and red wine vinegar. Add the sauce and cook until the meat is well coated."],[null,"Drain the rice and rinse with boiling water, serve immediately."]],"h":[["Chef's note","Whip up this tasty, Asian inspired stir fry with tender beef. Perfect for a busy weeknight dinner or to make ahead and freeze."],["Carbohydrate","The main source of carbohydrate in this dish is provided by the rice. However, the honey will also add to the carbohydrate of this meal. The carbohydrate values have been provided for those who have trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","If you have been prescribed a phosphate binder ensure you take them with this dish."],["Protein","This recipe is very high in protein which is great for people on dialysis. If you have been advised to reduce your protein intake, have a smaller portion of the beef."],["Gluten free","Use a gluten-free stock cube and serve with rice."],["Vegetarian","The beef can be replaced with vegetarian protein such as tofu or Quorn pieces to suit a vegetarian diet."],["Vegan","Replace the beef with tofu or a vegan alternative, miss out the honey and use one tablespoon of golden syrup in its place."],["Cheaper option","Substitute the beef with turkey or tofu for an equally tasty but cheaper dish."],["Storage","Freeze any left-over beef stir fry but we do not recommend freezing rice. To defrost, remove the lid from the container and leave in the fridge to defrost slowly. Reheat thoroughly either in your wok, frying pan or in the microwave."]]},"5545397":{"s":[[null,"Heat oil in a pan, add sliced onion, leeks, garlic, and cook until soft"],[null,"Add in the beef chunks, cannellini beans, black pepper and smoked paprika. Cook for 2 minutes and then add in the flour."],[null,"In a jug add a beef stock cube, dijon mustard, Renastep and boiling water and stir until fully combined."],[null,"Pour over the wet mixture and mix well ensuring that all the beef juices and flour are combined."],[null,"Allow to simmer for 10 minutes or until thickened."],[null,"Serve over pasta and enjoy!"]],"h":[["Renastep note","Always check with your dietitian or doctor that this recipe is suitable for you."],["Renastep note","Renastep is a food for special medical purposes for the dietary management of kidney disease. Suitable from 3 years of age. Must be used under medical supervision. Renastep contains Milk (milk protein) and Fish (Tuna oil). This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutritics dietary analysis software. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information."]]},"6545397":{"s":[[null,"Cook noodles according to package directions, omitting salt."],[null,"Add oil to a large sauté pan over high heat. Add meat and sauté for about 3 minutes. Remove meat from pan. Add mushrooms and onion and sauté for 5 minutes or until it begins to brown."],[null,"Add flour and cook for 1 minute. Add water gently to deglaze pan; cook for 2 minutes. Add Dijon mustard and beef broth; bring to a boil. Reduce heat and simmer for 5 minutes."],[null,"Add beef and any juices back to broth and simmer for 3 more minutes. Add sour cream and pepper; simmer for 30 seconds."],[null,"Serve over whole-grain egg noodles."]],"h":[]},"2801":{"s":[[null,"Thinly slice onion. Chop tomato and bell pepper. Cut beef into small cubes."],[null,"Sauté onion and oil in a skillet until the onion is slightly brown. Add beef and tomatoes."],[null,"When partially cooked, add bell pepper, salt and pepper."],[null,"Continue cooking until meat is tender."]],"h":[[null,"Tibbs is a common Ethiopian dish that can be served with pita bread, half of a piece of injera or 1-cup cooked rice."],[null,"Variations of Beef Tibbs can be prepared by adding different ingredients of your choice."],[null,"Add 1 jalapeño pepper if spicier taste is preferred.."],[null,"By using only a small portion of tomato, Beef Tibbs becomes an appropriate dish for dialysis patients."],[null,"Adjust the portion for a lower protein CKD-non-dialysis diet."]]},"2582":{"s":[[null,"Thinly slice onion. Chop tomato and bell pepper. Cut beef into small cubes."],[null,"Sauté onion and oil in a skillet until the onion is slightly brown."],[null,"Add beef and tomatoes."],[null,"When partially cooked, add bell pepper or jalapeño pepper."],[null,"Continue cooking until meat is tender."],[null,"Add salt and pepper and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Tibbs is a common Ethiopian dish that can be served with pita bread, half of a piece of injera or 1-cup cooked rice."],[null,"Variations of Beef Tibbs can be prepared by adding different ingredients of your choice."],[null,"To make dish more spicy, add a chopped jalapeño pepper."]]},"7332922":{"s":[[null,"Crumble the bread into a bowl with the pepper and garlic. Add the egg and mix, allowing tosoak for a couple of minutes, then mix again."],[null,"Add the grated onion and carrot, and the minced beef. Mix well, then divide the mixture into six."],[null,"Wet your hands and shape each portion into a round ball, then flatten it into a burger shape about 2cm thick. Cover and place in the fridge to cool for at least 20 minutes."],[null,"Heat a non-stick pan, add the burgers and leave for 3–4 minutes, then flip with a spatula and cook for a further 3–4 minutes. (Turning the burgers too soon may result in them breaking)"],[null,"Once you have made sure that the burgers are fully cooked through, serve them in buns with the lettuce, onion and tomato slices."]],"h":[[null,"For extra zing, add some chilli flakes or 2 tsp smoked paprika to the burger mix."],[null,"You could make these burgers using turkey, venison or lean lamb mince."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Can be frozen raw or cooked. Freeze in individually wrapped portions with greaseproof paper between each burger. Defrost fully in the fridge or microwave, then heat thoroughly until piping hot and cooked right through."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"1979":{"s":[[null,"Slice onion and mushrooms; slice bell pepper into thin strips. Chop parsley."],[null,"Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat."],[null,"Add onion, bell pepper and mushroom. Sauté until vegetables are tender, about 6 minutes. Remove vegetables to a plate."],[null,"Add beef to the skillet and cook until no trace of pink remains, 5 to 6 minutes. Spoon off and discard any fat."],[null,"Add the Worcestershire sauce, Kitchen Bouquet sauce and black pepper; stir and cook for 1 to 2 minutes."],[null,"Add vegetables to the beef and stir to combine."],[null,"Stir in the parsley and cook until heated through. Remove from heat."],[null,"Warm pitas. Cut a 2″ strip off the side of each pita and pull open."],[null,"Fill each pita with the beef and vegetable mixture."]],"h":[[null,"Kitchen Bouquet® browning and seasoning sauce is a low-sodium seasoning that adds extra color and flavor to meat and vegetables."],[null,"Compare pita brands and select the lowest sodium brand. Select white or wheat–both are kidney-friendly."]]},"3446":{"s":[[null,"Place apple, beet, carrot, celery and parsley in a juicer and process to extract juice."],[null,"Pour into 2 small glasses to make 2 servings. Drink right away or place in the refrigerator to chill."]],"h":[[null,"Juicing sounds healthy, but for kidney patients on a low potassium diet a small amount of juice can provide a large amount of potassium."],[null,"To stay within your potassium goal for the day be sure to count 3 ounces as 1/2 serving of fruit and 2 servings of vegetables from your daily plan."],[null,"Consult with your dietitian when incorporating juicing into your kidney diet. Juice blends are high in potassium and may not be recommended if potassium control is an issue."]]},"6841530":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F."],[null,"Put the beets in a single layer on a rimmed baking sheet. Drizzle the beets with 1 Tsp. oil. Sprinkle the pepper over the beets."],[null,"Roast for 20-25 minutes, or until tender when tested with a fork. Let cook on the baking sheet for 10 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, in a large bowl, whisk together the remaining 2 Tsps.. oil, vinegar, and mustard. Add the arugula, swirling the leaves in the dressing (tongs work well for this). Add the cooled beets. Sprinkle with the feta. Toss to combine."],[null,"Cook’s Tip: Most recipes advise roasting beets whole, then peeling them after cooking. To cut cooking time considerably, peel them raw (a vegetable peeler works well) and cut them into quarters or eighths before roasting. Beets can stain clothes, so you may want to wear an apron and a pair of disposable plastic gloves before handling the beets."]],"h":[]},"3771":{"s":[[null,"Thinly slice cucumber."],[null,"Place beet slices on a serving plate."],[null,"Layer cucumber slices on top of beet slices."],[null,"Drizzle with vinegar and oil."],[null,"Sprinkle with Gorgonzola cheese."]],"h":[[null,"Gorgonzola cheese is an Italian-made blue cheese. Because blue cheese has intense flavor and is very high in sodium (400 mg/ounce), a very small portion size is used in this recipe."],[null,"Chill beets before preparing recipe."]]},"9763243":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375℉/190℃ and grab a large baking sheet."],[null,"Slice the bread and arrange it in a single layer on your sheet pan. Then bake it for 5-8 minutes, until nicely golden."],[null,"While the bread is toasting, combine the beets and all the remaining ingredients in a medium mixing bowl and set it aside. (Reserve some of the basil to garnish the bruschetta later, if you'd like.)"],[null,"Spoon the beet mixture onto your toasted bread and sprinkle with extra basil if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Wear gloves to prevent staining your hands red while cutting the beets."],[null,"Plan to enjoy your beet bruschetta immediately once the bread is topped, so it doesn’t get soggy."],[null,"If not enjoying right away , keep the bruschetta mixture in a bowl with a serving spoon and have your guests top their bread themselves."]]},"9419806":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350℉/176℃ and line a large baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Add the wet ingredients to your blender and process until smooth. Then pour into a mixing bowl."],[null,"Add the dry ingredients to the same bowl and stir until combined. Then fold in the chocolate chips, if using."],[null,"Use a cookie scoop to scoop the batter onto your parchment-lined tray, leaving space in between each cookie to allow for spreading."],[null,"Bake the beet cookies for 10-12 minutes, until they are slightly firm to the touch. Then, remove them from the oven and let them cool for 10 minutes before handling."]],"h":[[null,"Weigh your flour for the most accurate results . If you don’t have a kitchen scale, spoon the flour into your measuring cup and use a knife to scrape off the excess, with similar results. Do not scoop from the bag!"],[null,"If using canned beets , ensure they are not pickled! Use canned beets only in water, no vinegar or oil, as that will alter the flavour."],[null,"Use fresh and active baking powder. Baking powder that is open in your pantry for 6+ months can lose its effectiveness."],[null,"Let your cookies cool in the pan for at least 10 minutes before handling them. They are delicate and need time to set before transferring them to a wire rack."],[null,"Leftovers keep at room temperature for 1-2 days, up to 5 days in the fridge, or up to 3 months frozen."]]},"9938812":{"s":[[null,"Bring a large pot of generously salted water to a boil and cook your pasta according to package directions for \"al dente\" pasta. Immediately drain and rinse the pasta to prevent overcooking. Then transfer it to a large bowl."],[null,"While the pasta is cooking, combine all the salad dressing ingredients in a small bowl and mix well."],[null,"Then add all the remaining salad ingredients to the bowl with the cooked pasta and pour the dressing on top. Mix well, garnish with fresh chives and refrigerate it for 1 hour or longer, or enjoy it immediately."]],"h":[[null,"Salt your pasta water. Make sure to add enough salt to your pot of water for best texture and flavour. Here's a handy guide to help you salt your water perfectly each time."],[null,"Cook your pasta al dente. Do not overcook! Al dente means that the pasta is still firm once cooked, giving optimal texture in every bite. To ensure your pasta does not overcook, start taste testing a few minutes before the package says it will be ready. It should be tender, but still firm."],[null,"Leftovers will keep refrigerated for 3-4 days."]]},"9057993":{"s":[[null,"Combine the soy milk and apple cider vinegar in a large mixing bowl and set it aside for 5 minutes to thicken and curdle, creating your vegan buttermilk."],[null,"Preheat your waffle iron to medium/high heat, or according to the manufacturer's directions."],[null,"In a medium bowl, whisk together all the dry ingredients: flour, beet powder, baking powder."],[null,"By now, your soy milk should be curdled so add the applesauce and tahini to the bowl and stir. Then add the dry ingredients to the same bowl and stir until combined without overmixing."],[null,"Cook the waffles for 6-8 minutes, or according to the manufacturer's directions. Don't lift the lid too soon or the waffles may stick and break. Check carefully and if they appear to be sticking, cook an additional 1-2 minutes and check again."]],"h":[]},"7521021":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 150C/gas 2. Oil and line a 20cm loose-bottomed cake tin."],[null,"Sift the flour, baking powder, bicarbonate and cinnamon into a large bowl. Add the beetroot, half the carrot, and mix evenly. Put 2 egg whites into a bowl and whisk until soft peaks form. Put the remaining yolks and whole eggs in a bowl with the caster sugar and beat with an electric whisk for 4-5 mins until pale and thick."],[null,"Drain the pineapple juice into a pan. Chop the pineapple and add it with the egg whites and whisked eggs to the flour mix and lightly fold until evenly mixed. Spoon into the cake tin. Scatter over the rest of the carrot and dust with the icing sugar."],[null,"Bake for 75 mins, then cover with foil and bake for a further 15 mins or until a skewer in the centre comes out clean. Turn out onto a wire rack and cool."],[null,"Simmer the pineapple juice for 5-6 mins until syrupy. Drizzle over the warm cake and leave to cool."]],"h":[]},"3595044":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/ 160°C fan/ gas mark 4. Put the chickpea (gram) flour into a bowl and add the beetroot, carrot and onions. Mix to fully combine."],[null,"Add in just enough water to bind the ingredients together. Heat the oil in a frying pan over a medium heat, divide the batter into eight fritters and add to the frying pan. Cook for 3 minutes, until the bottom has started to crisp, then flip the fritters and cook on the other side for another 3 minutes."],[null,"Transfer the fritters to a baking sheet and cook in the oven for 10 minutes. While the fritters are cooking, mix the chopped parsley into the yoghurt."],[null,"Remove the fritters from the oven and serve two fritters per portion with the rocket and cucumber salad, yoghurt and a crusty roll."]],"h":[["Chef's note","A tasty vegan dish."],["Carbohydrate","The chickpea (gram) flour and bread roll are the main sources of carbohydrate in this recipe, and the value has been provided for those who have been trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","This recipe is low in potassium, when following the quantities and serving sizes given.\nThis recipe is also low in phosphate, however it still contains phosphate so if you are prescribed a phosphate binder then you should take as directed."],["Protein","This recipe is high in protein, which makes it suitable for those advised to eat more protein, in particular those receiving dialysis."],["Gluten free","Serve with a gluten-free roll."],["Healthier option","Use a wholemeal roll rather than white to increase the fibre in this dish. When selecting rolls, also look for those with the lowest amount of added salt."],["Storage","This dish is best eaten freshly made."]]},"3448923":{"s":[[null,"To make the pastry: put the flour, onion seeds, parmesan and paprika in a bowl and combine. Add in the butter and rub in with your fingers until it resembles fine breadcrumbs."],[null,"Add the egg, mixing with a knife until it all starts to come together. Then use your hands to bring the mixture together into a ball of dough. Tip out on a floured surface and knead a little to smooth the dough. Wrap in cling film and set aside until ready to use."],[null,"To make the quiche: butter and flour a 23cm (9 inch) diameter flan ring. On a floured surface, roll the pastry out until large enough to line the flan ring. Gently lower the pastry into the tin and press it into the corners. Prick the bottom of the pastry with a fork."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C / 160°C fan/ gas mark 4. Put the cubed beetroot and the crumbled goat’s cheese into the flan base. Whisk the eggs and double cream together in a jug, add in the pepper. Pour the mixture over the beetroot and goat’s cheese."],[null,"Sprinkle grated cheddar over the top of the quiche then bake in the oven for 25 minutes until nicely golden and the egg mixture has set. Leave to cool in the tin. Once cooled, turn out and serve."],[null,"Prepare the salad by combining the rocket, tomatoes and cucumber and then dress with the lemon or lime juice. Serve into six portions."]],"h":[["Chef's note","A nice supper dish or for lovely for a special occasion. Leftover slices make great packed lunches."],["Carbohydrate","The pastry is the main source of carbohydrate in this dish and the values have been provided for those who have trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","Although this recipe does contain beetroot, tomatoes and other salad vegetables that are high in potassium, overall, when keeping to the portion sizes suggested, this dish is low in potassium and can be enjoyed as part of a low potassium diet.\nEven though this dish is low in phosphate, it does contain some phosphate, provided by the cheese. Therefore, If you have been prescribed a phosphate binder ensure you take them with this dish."],["Protein","This is a low protein dish, therefore suitable for those advised to reduce their protein intake."],["Gluten free","The pastry can be made with gluten-free flour and a small teaspoon of Xanthan Gum."],["Storage","This recipe will last in the fridge for three days. It can be served cold in packed lunches."],["Tips","This recipe can also be made as individual quiches using a muffin tin. Just ensure the tin is well buttered and floured first and bake for a reduced time of 15 minutes."]]},"9591321":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425℉/218℃ convection roast and line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Arrange your peeled beet and sweet potato cubes in a single layer on your tray and sprinkle generously with salt and black pepper. Roast them for 20-25 minutes or until the edges are golden brown and the cubes are fork-tender."],[null,"Meanwhile, add your rice and vegetable broth to a small saucepot and bring to a boil. Then reduce the heat and simmer until it's cooked, and the liquid is mostly absorbed. Fluff it up with a fork and set it aside to cool slightly."],[null,"Add all the salad dressing ingredients to a small bowl and whisk to combine. Set aside."],[null,"When the roasted vegetables and rice are ready, add them, along with all the remaining salad ingredients to a mixing bowl. Then pour in the salad dressing and mix well until evenly coated. Taste for salt and pepper and adjust if needed."]],"h":[[null,"Cut the beet and sweet potato cubes as uniformly as possible for even cooking."],[null,"To save prep time , you may use pre-cubed sweet potatoes and beets."],[null,"If you don't have a convection oven , roast the vegetables a little longer, until they are fork-tender and the edges are golden brown."],[null,"Keep leftovers in the refrigerator in an airtight container for 3-4 days."]]},"7854676":{"s":[[null,"Blend half the tin of chickpeas and all the other ingredients together until almost smooth and well combined."],[null,"Roughly crush the remaining chickpeas with a fork and stir into the mixture – this adds texture to your hummus. Sprinkle over the mint and serve with vegetable crudités."]],"h":[[null,"The perfect party dip – place in a bowl surrounded by sticks of carrots, peppers, cucumber and celery and pitta bread fingers."],[null,"Serve with warm pitta bread, plus vegetables/salad for a more substantial snack."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"2173":{"s":[[null,"Heat a waffle iron. In a mixing bowl, mix together the cake flour and baking soda and set aside. Separate the egg whites and egg yolks. Whisk together egg yolks, sour cream, milk and vanilla extract. Melt the butter and then mix into the sour cream mixture."],[null,"In a different bowl, beat the egg whites with a hand-mixer on medium speed until soft peaks form, about 3 minutes. Add the granulated sugar to the egg whites and continue to beat until stiff peaks form, about 3 to 4 more minutes."],[null,"Whisk the sour cream mixture into the flour mixture until just combined. Gently fold in the beaten egg whites until mixture is smooth; do not overmix."],[null,"Add about 1/2 cup of the batter to the waffle iron, close and cook for about 3 minutes. Serve waffles with the powdered sugar. Other suggested toppings include fresh berries, whipped cream, jam or syrup."]],"h":[[null,"Maple syrup may be substituted for the powdered sugar. If maple syrup is used, 1/4 cup has 54 g carbohydrate and 170 mg of potassium. Some light or imitation pancake syrup may have phosphorus additives; read the ingredient list to try to avoid these additives."],[null,"Strawberries, blueberries and or raspberries can also be an option for topping these waffles. A 1/2 cup of berries adds 5-10 g of carbohydrate and 55-110 mg of potassium, depending on the fruit used."],[null,"If you are limiting carbs change portion to 1/2 waffle and top with berries and whipped cream (30-35 grams carbohydrate)."]]},"6447164":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375° F. Coat a baking sheet with cooking spray. Set aside."],[null,"Slice each pepper in half lengthwise then scoop out any seeds and membrane."],[null,"Add turkey bacon to a non-stick sauté pan with cooking spray over medium heat and cook until crisp. Drain on a paper towel and set aside."],[null,"Add onions to the pan used to cook the turkey bacon and add more cooking spray if needed. Cook the onions, stirring occasionally until clear. Set aside to cool."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix the cream cheese and goat cheese. Add the turkey bacon, onions, and red pepper flakes. Stir to combine."],[null,"Grind toasted bread in a food processor with the garlic and Parmesan cheese. Set aside in a small bowl."],[null,"Spoon the cheese mixture into each pepper half (1 Tsp. of mixture per popper), and then press the cheese side of the popper into the whole wheat breadcrumb mixture. Lay on the prepared baking sheet breadcrumb side up and spray each one lightly with cooking spray."],[null,"Bake the poppers for about 20 minutes or until the peppers have softened and the breadcrumbs are golden brown."]],"h":[]},"6461642":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6764984":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400° F. In a small bowl, mix the marinara sauce, lemon juice, oil, garlic and cinnamon. Place the eggplant wedges, skin side down, on a baking sheet lined with unbleached parchment paper. Generously brush the flesh of the eggplant wedges with the marinara mixture."],[null,"Roast the eggplant wedges until well cooked and soft, about 30 minutes."],[null,"Transfer the wedges to a plate. Sprinkle with parsley, mint, feta cheese and lemon zest and serve."]],"h":[]},"6704624":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F."],[null,"In a medium bowl, combine the flour, basil and pepper. In another medium bowl, combine the bread crumbs and Parmesan cheese. In a third medium bowl, add the egg whites."],[null,"Dip both sides of the eggplant slices in the flour, then in the eggs, then in the bread crumbs, coating well. Set aside."],[null,"Add oil and cooking spray to a large nonstick skillet over medium-high heat. Cook the eggplant in batches, about 2 minutes per side. Use additional cooking spray with each batch."],[null,"Place the eggplant slices in the bottom of a 13x9-inch baking dish. Pour the pasta sauce over the eggplant to cover all of the slices. Sprinkle the mozzarella cheese on top and bake for 30 minutes, until the cheese is melted and lightly browned."]],"h":[]},"6068159":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, mix together the pudding and whipped topping."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix together the blueberries and strawberries. For each serving, place 1 cup berries in a parfait or juice glass and top with 21/2 Tbsps. pudding mixture."]],"h":[]},"3091":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400° F."],[null,"Spray the cooking spray on a baking sheet that will fit 12 wonton wrappers."],[null,"Spread out the wonton wrappers, and spray them with cooking spray."],[null,"Sprinkle the granulated sugar on wonton wrappers."],[null,"Bake the wontons for 5 minutes or until golden brown;remove from the baking sheet."],[null,"Place 6 wonton wrappers on a serving tray."],[null,"Top each wrapper with 2 tablespoons of whipped topping, 1 tablespoon of raspberries and 1 tablespoon of blueberries."],[null,"Top the berries with a second wonton wrapper."],[null,"Sprinkle the tops with powdered sugar. Garnish them with a dollop of whipped topping, fruit and a mint leaf, if desired. Serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute strawberries and blackberries for raspberries and blueberries for variety."],[null,"To reduce carbohydrate content substitute Splenda® No Calorie granular sweetener for sugar."],[null,"If the wontons sit in the refrigerator the Reddi-Wip will melt. Assemble only when ready to serve."]]},"4390190":{"s":[[null,"Serve in 6-ounce rocks glasses, layered in the following order: graham crackers, yogurt, raspberries, then graham crackers, yogurt, peaches, graham crackers, yogurt, blueberries, graham crackers, whipped cream, strawberries and mint. Repeat for the other 3 glasses, or do all 4 glasses at the same time using equal amounts. Chill for 30 minutes, then serve."]],"h":[]},"6333348":{"s":[[null,"Add the berries, spinach, almond milk, yogurt, and ground flaxseed to a blender. Add ice cubes if you are using fresh berries and want a thicker smoothie."],[null,"Blend until smooth and creamy. Enjoy immediately."]],"h":[]},"6143237":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350 degrees F. Spray a 9-inch pie pan with cooking spray."],[null,"In a medium bowl combine the berries, lemon zest, lemon juice, 2 Tbsps. low- or no-calorie sweetener, corn starch and cinnamon. Mix well and pour into pie pan."],[null,"In another medium bowl, combine the oats, remaining 1 tbsp low- or no-calorie sweetener, brown sugar blend, pecans, and margarine. Work the margarine into the dry ingredients with your hands until it is crumbly."],[null,"Sprinkle the crisp topping mixture evenly over the berries. Bake for 55 minutes or until the top is brown and the fruit is bubbly. Serve warm."]],"h":[]},"6201513":{"s":[[null,"In a large mixing bowl, combine the strawberries, blueberries, raspberries, and blackberries."],[null,"Zest and juice the lime. In a small bowl, whisk together the lime zest, lime juice, and honey to create the dressing."],[null,"Pour the dressing over the berries, gently tossing to coat."],[null,"Allow the berry salad to marinate in the refrigerator for at least 30 minutes to let the flavors meld."],[null,"Just before serving, sprinkle the fresh mint over the top of the berry salad and gently toss to incorporate."]],"h":[]},"6306893":{"s":[[null,"Combine all ingredients in a small bowl and serve immediately or chill in the refrigerator for 30 minutes to allow the flavors to blend before serving."]],"h":[]},"4207445":{"s":[[null,"Add all ingredients to a blender and mix. If you are using fresh fruits, refrigerate for 1 hour before drinking. You can also add some ice cubes before mixing. There is no need to refrigerate if using frozen fruit and the texture will be creamier."]],"h":[[null,"PLEASE NOTE: This recipe is higher in potassium and portion size is important. Check with your registered dietitian to see how this recipe can be included in your diet."],["Milk alternatives and phosphorus content","Dairy foods offer several beneficial nutrients including protein, calcium and vitamin D. Dairy or milk-based foods are also natural sources of potassium and phosphorus. They can be part of a kidney-friendly diet but the portion size matters. Too much of these foods can contribute to high phosphorus intake, which should be avoided. While a general recommendation for dairy products is a half-cup serving per day, this amount can vary depending on individual needs. Many different recipes include dairy products as an ingredient, so finding lower-phosphorus substitutions is important. Milk alternatives can replace cow’s milk. Soy, rice and almond beverages offer a lower phosphorus choice. Being plant-based, phosphorus absorption of these alternatives is also lower versus animal-based dairy products. A half-cup of skim milk contains 124 milligrams of phosphorus. In comparison, a half-cup of soy beverage has 110 milligrams of phosphorus, a half-cup of rice beverage includes 75 milligrams of phosphorus, and a half-cup of almond beverage is lowest in phosphorus with 10 milligrams. Each adds a different flavor, so read labels carefully and experiment with recipes to find a preferred milk alternative."]]},"6381007":{"s":[[null,"Heat the soy milk flavors in separate pots over low heat. Add 1 tablespoon of low- or no-calorie sweetener and 2 tablespoons of cornstarch mixed with cold soy milk to each pot of simmering soy milk and heat until the milk thickens. Remove from the heat and cool."],[null,"In a large glass bowl, layer the chocolate and vanilla soy milk with the berries forming layers. End up with a layer of berries on top and sprinkle with cocoa powder."]],"h":[]},"6536966":{"s":[[null,"In a bowl, whisk together the besan, water, and spices until smooth."],[null,"Stir in the vegetables. Cover and set aside for 5-10 minutes. Mix well again."],[null,"Heat a nonstick skillet over medium heat and lightly coat with cooking spray."],[null,"Pour the batter into the skillet, gently spread the batter evenly, and round off the shape to create a thin, 6-inch pancake."],[null,"Cook for 2-3 minutes per side, until lightly browned and cooked through."],[null,"Serve warm with 1 Tbsp plain Greek yogurt on the side for dipping."]],"h":[]},"5210631":{"s":[[null,"Mix gram flour and semolina with water to make thin batter of pouring consistency. Add cumin seeds and turmeric. Set aside for 10-15 minutes."],[null,"Heat oil in a pan and sautee onion for 1-2 minutes in a pan, then add ginger and paneer and cook for a further 2 minutes."],[null,"Heat a pan to a medium heat and grease it with oil. Pour the batter first and move the pan to make a circle. Once cooked on one side, flip and cook again."],[null,"Top with onion-paneer mixture and fold the cheela in half."]],"h":[]},"6382213":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 450 degrees F. Coat a 9x13 baking or roasting pan with cooking spray."],[null,"Add chopped onion, carrots, and celery to the pan and top with fresh parsley and fresh thyme. Mix ingredients to evenly distribute them."],[null,"Remove and discard giblet and neck from the chicken cavity. Trim excess fat around neck and cavity opening. Pat the chicken dry with a paper towel."],[null,"Starting at the neck, loosen the skin around the breast meat using your finger. Rub the entire chicken (including the breast meat under the skin) with olive oil. Season the outside of the chicken and the inside of cavity with salt and pepper."],[null,"Fill the cavity of the chicken with the lemon wedges and smashed garlic and place the chicken breast-side up in the pan on top of the herbs and vegetables."],[null,"Pour the chicken broth over the vegetables and bake in oven for 30 minutes. After 30 minutes, reduce heat to 350 degrees F and bake for an additional 45 minutes."],[null,"Remove the chicken from the pan and let it rest covered with foil for 20 minutes. Strain the vegetables and herbs from broth in the bottom of the pan. De-fat the broth by using a fat separator or chill it in the fridge—the fat will rise to the top and solidify making it easy to scrape off the top. You should end up with about one cup of broth. Discard the vegetables because all their flavor and nutrition will have seeped into the broth."],[null,"Once the chicken has rested, remove the skin and cut it into eight pieces, discarding the carcass, lemons, and garlic. Pour the de-fatted broth over the chicken and serve."]],"h":[]},"6560917":{"s":[[null,"In a large pot, place the potato, garlic, and cauliflower. Fill with enough water to fully cover everything. Bring to a boil, reduce the heat to medium, and cook until the potato and cauliflower are tender, about 15 minutes."],[null,"Drain and add the vegetables and garlic back to the pot. Cover the pot with a kitchen towel and put the lid over the towel. Let stand for 5 minutes. Remove the lid and towel. This process helps to dry the vegetables so they mash better."],[null,"Add the buttermilk, cheese, olive oil, butter, salt, and pepper. Mash just until the ingredients are lightly combined. If desired, garnish with fresh snipped chives."]],"h":[]},"2962":{"s":[[null,"In a skillet over medium heat, melt 1 tablespoon butter."],[null,"Break vermicelli noodles into 2-inch pieces and cook, stirring often until noodles begin to brown."],[null,"Add remaining butter and rice. Stir to combine."],[null,"Add water, Mrs. Dash herb seasoning and chicken bouillon granules to skillet. Stir to blend ingredients."],[null,"Cover and bring to a boil. Reduce to low heat and simmer 20 minutes. Do not remove the cover."],[null,"Turn off heat and allow to sit covered for an additional 5 minutes."],[null,"Fluff with a fork and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Angel hair or thin spaghetti noodles can be used in place of vermicelli."],[null,"For comparison, packaged rice pilaf prepared with salted butter or margarine contains 400 to 650 mg sodium per 1/2 cup serving."],[null,"Some low or reduced sodium bouillon granules or cubes contain potassium chloride instead of salt. These are not recommended if you are on a low-potassium diet."],[null,"Freeze extra portions and reheat in the microwave for a very quick starchy side later."]]},"2502":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350º F. Spray 9″ x 13″ baking pan with non-stick cooking spray."],[null,"Set cream cheese out to soften. Peel, core and chop apples."],[null,"Mix together eggs, oil, sugar and 2 teaspoons vanilla. Stir in apples."],[null,"In a separate bowl, stir together flour, cinnamon, baking soda and pecans."],[null,"Add dry mixture to apple mixture and mix together."],[null,"Put into baking pan and bake for one hour. Allow to cool."],[null,"For icing, using a mixer, mix together cream cheese, powdered sugar and remaining vanilla."],[null,"Spread icing over cake after it has cooled."]],"h":[[null,"For people with diabetes, leave off the icing to reduce calories to 252 and carbohydrate to 33 g. Count as 2 carbohydrate choices."],[null,"To reduce fat you can replace half the oil with unsweetened applesauce."],[null,"Pecans are high in potassium and phosphorus. The amount contributed to one piece of cake is minimal as long as the recommended portion is followed. Otherwise you can reduce to 1/2 cup pecans or leave them out."]]},"5989032":{"s":[[null,"Mix together the flour, garlic powder and yeast in a bowl."],[null,"Create a well and pour in the warm water and stir to form a dough."],[null,"Knead the dough for 5 minutes or until smooth then place in a lightly oiled bowl, cover and allow to prove for 1 hour."],[null,"Meanwhile, heat oil in a pan and add the onions, garlic, and black pepper and soften for 5 minutes."],[null,"Stir in the poppy seeds and remove the pan from the heat and set aside."],[null,"Once proved divide the dough into 8 equal portions and shape into balls."],[null,"Press down the centre of each ball to create a dent. Pick up and spin slowly through your hands so the dough in the centre becomes thinner, ensuring not to rip the centre."],[null,"Repeat this process for all 8 balls."],[null,"Place all the bialys onto a baking tray and evenly distribute the filling into the centre of each one."],[null,"Bake for 20 minutes or until golden brown."],[null,"Serve and enjoy!"]],"h":[]},"7941754":{"s":[[null,"Add sweetener to the oats if using, then soak in the water and milk for at least 45 minutes, or overnight in the fridge."],[null,"Mix the apple into the oats, then top with yoghurt, strawberries and nuts to serve."]],"h":[[null,"This is a very flexible breakfast - you can use virtually any fruits and nuts. Try with pears and dried blueberries, topped with hazelnuts or walnuts."],[null,"Use dairy alternatives to the milk and yogurt for a delicious vegan version."],[null,"Try adding cinnamon or a little ginger for some added flavour."],[null,"Use gluten-free oats for a gluten free version."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6925472":{"s":[[null,"Rinse quinoa under cold water. Combine with 2 cups of water in a pot and bring to a boil. Reduce heat, cover, and simmer until water is absorbed, about 15 minutes. Let cool."],[null,"In a small bowl or jar, whisk together the lime juice, olive oil, Dijon mustard, garlic, cilantro, salt, and pepper."],[null,"Assemble salads. In each large mason jar or tall container, in this order, combine: 2–3 Tbsp vinaigrette; Sprinkle of red onion; 1/2 cup black beans; 1/2 cup cooked quinoa; 1/4 cup each of tomato, cucumber, and bell pepper; Small handful chopped spinach"],[null,"Screw on lids and refrigerate for up to 4 days. When ready to eat, shake well and pour into a bowl—or eat straight from the jar!"]],"h":[]},"6561472":{"s":[[null,"In a medium bowl, combine beans, corn, red pepper, red onion and cilantro."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together remaining ingredients and pour over bean salad. Toss to coat."]],"h":[]},"6798255":{"s":[[null,"In a large mixing bowl, combine black beans, thawed corn, diced red bell pepper, cherry tomatoes, chopped red onion, and fresh cilantro."],[null,"Juice the two limes in a small bowl. Add the olive oil, ground cumin, coarse salt, and pepper. Whisk until incorporated."],[null,"Pour the dressing over the black bean and corn mixture. Toss well to coat all the ingredients evenly."],[null,"Cover the bowl and refrigerate for at least 30 minutes to let the flavors meld."],[null,"Before serving, give the salad a gentle toss. If desired, garnish with additional cilantro and slices of avocado."]],"h":[]},"6681622":{"s":[[null,"Combine all ingredients in a medium sized bowl except lettuce. Refrigerate for at least one hour, or up to two days to marinate (the longer the better)."],[null,"If using butter lettuce leaves arrange them on a large plate and fill each one with 1/4 cup of salad mixture."],[null,"Alternative Serving Suggestion: Use jicama instead of lettuce for the serving vessel. Peel the jicama and slice into 1/4-inch thick rounds, then slice the rounds into triangles (eighths) to resemble tortilla chips. Serve like chips and salsa using the raw jicama “chips” instead of tortilla chips."]],"h":[]},"6388872":{"s":[[null,"Mix all ingredients together until evenly combined. Refrigerate until ready to serve."]],"h":[]},"6007046":{"s":[[null,"Place all ingredients in a food processor and blend until smooth. Add more water if consistency is too thick."],[null,"Serve with carrot and cucumber sticks."]],"h":[]},"9588635":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375℉/190℃ and line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Add all the ingredients to your food processor and process until combined, BUT DO NOT OVERPROCESS. Keep the texture chunky, you don't want a puree."],[null,"Scoop the mixture into balls of approx. 1 tablespoon each. You should get 17-18 balls. Place them on your baking sheet."],[null,"Bake for 8 minutes, then flip the balls and bake another 8-10 minutes until they are crisp and firm to the touch. Do not overbake."],[null,"Serve as is, OR with pasta and marinara sauce, OR BBQ sauce with rice."]],"h":[]},"4850291":{"s":[[null,"Oil the inside of a microwave-safe cup. Add egg whites, turmeric, rice beverage, red peppers, and beans. Mix with a fork."],[null,"Cook in microwave for 1 minute. Stir and cook for an additional 15 seconds. Stir and cook for another 15 seconds."],[null,"Garnish with salsa and fresh coriander."]],"h":[[null,"* When using fresh egg whites, use the egg whites of 4 large eggs"],[null,"** Avoid rice beverage with claim “enriched”"],[null,"Roll the omelet into a tortilla to make an easy breakfast burrito, or serve with toast."],["Give your day a good start","Starting the day off right with a balanced breakfast is key, especially for those with chronic kidney disease (CKD). Breakfast can help provide you with the energy and nutrients your body needs. There are many available breakfast options, and these include fresh, shelf stable, or frozen choices. Time often plays a critical role in your selection as there isn’t always enough to make a meal from scratch each morning. When deciding which type of breakfast selection might be the best choice for you, consider which option works best with your schedule and fits within your lower-potassium diet. Fresh options may be an omelet with vegetables, a fresh fruit cup with a serving of Greek yogurt, or overnight oats with lower-potassium fruit. Add spices for different flavors and health benefits. A shelf-stable choice can be selected when making a homemade or fresh breakfast isn’t as reasonable. Consider an English muffin with a nut butter or cooked oatmeal with some added lower-potassium fruit. Frozen foods can also be used on a kidney-friendly diet with caution. Certain foods like a frozen breakfast sandwich or waffle may be high in sodium or have hidden additives. Be sure to read labels to find the frozen choice that works best for you and stays within your diet goals."]]},"6548471":{"s":[[null,"In a large nonstick pan heat olive oil and sauté onions, peppers, garlic, and spices. Sauté for 3 minutes, or until vegetables are tender."],[null,"Add black beans with liquid and sauté with vegetables for 1 minute. Remove from heat. Add breadcrumbs, cornmeal, lime juice, lime zest, and salt. Remove 1 cup of bean mixture and purée in a blender or food processor until a coarse purée is formed. Fold the purée back into the bean mixture. Add the cheddar cheese and cilantro, combine well. Mixture should resemble a coarse paste and be stiff enough to hold up in a scoop or spoon."],[null,"With an ice cream scoop or 1/3 cup measuring cup, form 3–4-ounce portions. (Spray the ice cream scoop or measuring cup lightly with cooking spray to make it easier to remove the mixture) Sprinkle a plate with cornmeal and place scooped black bean portions on plate. Lightly dust black bean mixture with cornmeal and press down gently, forming a patty."],[null,"Preheat oven to 375°F. Spray a large nonstick pan with vegetable oil. Brown patty cakes for 2 minutes on each side. If pan is ovenproof, transfer to oven and bake for 15 minutes or until heated through. Or transfer patty cakes to a cookie sheet pan and bake."]],"h":[]},"3562881":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 180°C/ 160°C fan / gas mark 3 and line two baking trays with greaseproof paper. Put the sliced onion and red pepper into a bowl. Add one tablespoon of oil, season with pepper and mix. Spread the vegetables onto one of the trays."],[null,"Drain the sweetcorn and pat it dry. Pour it into a bowl, season with pepper and the smoked paprika and stir to combine. Spread the sweetcorn onto the second baking tray. Place both trays in the oven for 25-30 minutes, stir midway through, then leave to cool."],[null,"Drain and rinse the beans, pour into a bowl and mash with a fork. Heat the oil in a saucepan on a medium heat and add the garlic. Stir for 30 secs, then add the cinnamon, cumin, black pepper, black beans and a little water if needed."],[null,"Cook gently for three minutes, then remove from the heat. For the salsa, put the chilli sauce in a bowl and squeeze in the juice of ½ a lime, mix together. Add the tomatoes, spring onions and coriander leaves and mix again."],[null,"For the guacamole, halve the avocado and carefully remove the stone. Scoop all the avocado flesh into another bowl, squeeze in the juice of one lime and mash with a fork to a creamy texture. Set aside until serving."],[null,"Lay out the tortilla wraps. Top each with a layer of black beans, vegetables and corn and add a little salsa and guacamole. Serve two tacos per person, with a wedge of lime (and the chilli and extra chopped coriander if desired)."]],"h":[["Chef's note","With roasted vegetables, black beans and a kidney-friendly salsa and guacamole, these tacos make a speedy vegan lunch or dinner."],["Carbohydrate","The main source of carbohydrate in this dish comes from the tortilla wraps. The carbohydrate value of this dish has been provided for those who have been trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","Despite the use of some high potassium ingredients, for example the cherry tomatoes and avocado, if you follow the quantities stated and the serving sizes provided in this recipe, this dish is low in potassium overall. The black beans do contain phosphate but the portion used in this recipe keeps the total phosphate content low. If you have been prescribed a phosphate binder ensure you take them with this dish."],["Protein","This recipe is low in protein which make it a suitable meal for those advised to follow a low protein diet."],["Gluten free","Use gluten-free tortilla wraps."],["Healthier option","This is a healthy dish as it is naturally low in salt, fat and sugar and high in fibre. However, it is best to check the labels when purchasing tortilla wraps and ensure you buy those with the lowest salt content."],["Cheaper option","This is a relatively inexpensive dish. However, you may wish to purchase lime juice in a bottle to avoid any food waste."],["Storage","All elements of this dish can be prepared in advance. Store the vegetables, black beans, salsa and guacamole separately in air-tight containers, keep refrigerated and use within 3 days. Assemble the tacos just before serving."]]},"6675538":{"s":[[null,"Heat 1 Tsp. of the oil in a medium skillet over medium-high heat. Add the onions and peppers and cook 3 minutes or until onions are just beginning to brown, stirring occasionally."],[null,"Add the beans, tomatoes, and cumin. Cook 3 minutes or until tomatoes are just tender, stirring occasionally. Remove from heat."],[null,"Sprinkle with the salt and spoon the lime juice and remaining oil evenly over all. Do NOT stir."]],"h":[]},"7040748":{"s":[[null,"Heat half the oil in a non-stick frying pan and fry the spring onions for 1–2 minutes, until softened."],[null,"Place the black-eyed beans in a large bowl and roughly mash. Stir in the remaining ingredients and combine well."],[null,"Divide the mixture into 6 and form each into patties or burgers."],[null,"Place on a baking sheet, brush each side with the remaining oil and chill for at least 30 minutes, or until required. Cook for 2–3 minutes on each side on a medium barbecue or grill until cooked through."],[null,"Serve in a wholemeal roll and fill with green salad, tomatoes and red onion."]],"h":[[null,"The nutritional analysis above includes a wholemeal bun as a serving suggestion."],[null,"You could use other beans such as kidney beans, cannelini or mixed beans."],[null,"Add crushed garlic and chilli flakes for extra flavour."],[null,"Cut the carbs, by enjoying this veggie burger without the bun."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Freeze in individually wrapped portions with grease proof paper between each burger. Defrost thoroughly and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"2275":{"s":[[null,"Set the peas out to thaw. Mince the garlic; chop the onion and bell pepper; slice the celery and cube the carrots; remove kale from stalks and chop."],[null,"In a large pan heat the olive oil. Add garlic, onion, bell pepper, celery, carrots, bay leaf and thyme. Sauté on medium low until fragrant, about 5 minutes."],[null,"Add the kale, black-eyed peas, salt and black pepper. Stir lightly together."],[null,"Add the chicken broth and simmer for about 15 minutes or until broth is gone."],[null,"Heat rice; spoon hash over rice, garnish with thyme sprigs or fresh parsley and serve."]],"h":[[null,"You can also simmer all of the ingredients together with the rice and serve mixed together if desired."],[null,"Add hot pepper sauce if desired. Choose a brand low in sodium."],[null,"If available, replace frozen peas with fresh cooked low-sodium peas."]]},"7212635":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4. Use 1 tsp of the rapeseed oil to grease a 2lb loaf tin (approx 27cm x 12cm)."],[null,"Grate the unpeeled apples into a bowl and discard the cores."],[null,"Add the eggs, vanilla extract, caster sugar, oil to the bowl and beat together."],[null,"Add the flour and baking powder and mix well. Fold in the blackberries."],[null,"Pour the mixture into the loaf tin and bake for 25 minutes until firm and golden. Cover with foil after 20 minutes if it's starting to brown too much. The cake is cooked when a knife inserted into the centre comes out clean."]],"h":[[null,"You could add other essences, such as lemon or almond, or add the grated zest of an orange or lemon."],[null,"Any berries will work in this recipe, such as raspberries in place of blackberries. You can also use frozen ones that have thawed."],[null,"Freeze in freezer bags, wrapped in foil or greaseproof paper, for up to three months. Don't forget to label."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Slice then wrap in foil to freeze. You can then use slices as required."]]},"2517":{"s":[[null,"Crush berries then combine with 1 cup water and sugar in a large saucepan. Bring mixture to a boil."],[null,"Combine cornstarch with 2 tablespoons water. Mix well and stir into blackberry mixture. Cook 1 minute over medium high heat to thicken sauce, stirring constantly."],[null,"Remove from heat and add lemon juice. Chill in refrigerator until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Use fresh or frozen blackberries."],[null,"Serve Blackberry Sauce over angel food cake, sponge cake, pancakes or waffles."],[null,"Sugar substitute may be used to replace sugar. Carbohydrate is reduced to 6 grams per serving; carbohydrate choice is reduced to 1/2."]]},"7227794":{"s":[[null,"Put the blackberries into a saucepan with 1 tbsp water and heat gently for 2-3 minutes. Remove from the heat. Grease six individual pudding basins with low-fat cooking spray. Share the blackberry mixture between them."],[null,"Put the spread, caster sugar, eggs and flour into a mixing bowl and beat together for 1 minute, until the mixture is smooth and creamy. Share between the pudding basins and cover the tops with foil. Place in a steamer and steam for 30 minutes, topping up with boiling water, if necessary. Run a knife around the sides of the basins, then turn out the puddings. Heat the low-fat custard to serve."]],"h":[[null,"You could also make this pudding with apples or pears, or other fruits such as raspberries or blueberries."],[null,"If you don't have a steamer, bake the puddings instead. Place them in a roasting pan with enough warm water to come about half way up the sides, then bake at 180°C/gas 4 for 25 minutes."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Defrost, then heat in the microwave to serve."]]},"2230":{"s":[[null,"Mash blackberries."],[null,"Add all ingredients to a pitcher."],[null,"Refrigerator overnight before serving."]],"h":[[null,"If you are on limited fluids, adjust the portion size to meet your needs."],[null,"After flavors develop you can pour into ice cube trays to make flavored ice."]]},"7271556":{"s":[[null,"Place the milk and vanilla extract into a medium pan and bring to the boil."],[null,"In a bowl, whisk together the cornflour, egg yolks and icing sugar."],[null,"Pour the milk over the cornflour mixture and stir in, then return to the pan, place over a low heat and cook until the mixture thickens. Do not boil, otherwise the mixture will curdle."],[null,"Cool the mixture, then stir through the blackcurrants and raspberries"],[null,"Transfer to a freezer proof container."],[null,"Freeze for 2 hours, then beat with a fork to remove the ice crystals. Return to the freezer and freeze until solid. Remove from the freezer 5-10 minutes before serving"]],"h":[[null,"This method works with most fruit - try using mango, strawberries or canned peaches."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Remove from freezer a few minutes before serving."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6963119":{"s":[[null,"Make your spice mixture by combining the garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, thyme, cumin, chili powder, ground oregano, cayenne pepper (if using) and coarse salt in a small bowl."],[null,"Pat the fish filets dry with a paper towel and season evenly on both sides with the spice mix."],[null,"Heat a large skillet over medium heat with the 2 tablespoons of oil. When the oil shimmers, gently lay the fish fillets in the pan, presentation side down."],[null,"Cook for 3 to 4 minutes, until the spice mixture is fragrant and beginning to color. Flip the fish and cook for an additional 3 to 4 minutes, depending on the thickness of the filets. Set aside and cover with foil."],[null,"Pour the avocado oil into the same pan you cooked the fish in and turn the heat up to high. Once the oil is hot and shimmering, add the corn and cook until it starts to blister and brown, about 5 minutes."],[null,"Lower the heat to medium and add the onion and jalapeno. Sauté for 3 to 4 minutes or until the onions get translucent and the whole thing is aromatic."],[null,"Turn the heat off and stir in the chili powder, coarse salt, lime zest and juice. Add the chopped cilantro."],[null,"Top the fish with the corn salsa and fresh cilantro prior to serving."]],"h":[]},"2056":{"s":[[null,"Peel and devein shrimp."],[null,"Rub and coat shrimp with blackening seasoning. In a pan, heat butter over medium-high heat and sauté shrimp. Cook about 2-3 minutes on each side or until shrimp curls. Remove from heat and set on a paper towel-covered plate to cool."],[null,"Cut pineapple into chunks. Thinly slice bell pepper and tear lettuce into bite-sized pieces."],[null,"In a salad bowl, combine the pineapple, bell pepper, corn and lettuce. Sprinkle with olive oil, vinegar and black pepper and toss."],[null,"Top with blackened shrimp and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Recipe analysis includes the DaVita.com recipe for Low Sodium Blackening Seasoning, which has 134 mg sodium per teaspoon."],[null,"Adjust shrimp for higher or lower protein diets."]]},"6851302":{"s":[[null,"Prepare an indoor or outdoor grill."],[null,"Mix together paprika, chili powder, oregano, thyme, cayenne pepper (optional), ground black pepper, garlic powder, and salt (optional)."],[null,"Rub each tuna filet with blackening seasoning well on both sides."],[null,"Spray the tuna filets with cooking spray and grill 4-5 minutes on each side. Tuna should be slightly pink in the middle."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together yogurt, mustard and soy sauce. Divide sauce evenly among the 4 tuna filets and top right before serving and sprinkle with chopped fresh parsley."]],"h":[]},"2927":{"s":[[null,"Mix ingredients together."],[null,"Store in an airtight container until ready to use."]],"h":[[null,"Blackening Seasoning is great on fish, shrimp or chicken."],[null,"For a completely sodium-free seasoning, omit the salt."],[null,"Use 1 teaspoon per serving when using as a rub or seasoning for your favorite seafood or poultry dish."]]},"7772248":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 180°C / gas 4 and use spray oil to lightly coat a baking tin. (We used a fluted cake ring that’s hollow in the centre, 20cm diameter, 8cm deep, 2 litres in volume)."],[null,"In a large bowl, whisk together the flours, baking powder and cocoa."],[null,"In another bowl, beat the egg yolks until frothy, then add the vanilla extract, sweetener, oil, and blended beetroot."],[null,"Stir the beetroot mixture into the flour. Then, carefully fold half the egg whites into the flour taking care not to overmix as this will remove the air, then fold in the rest."],[null,"Pour into the baking ring and bake for 35-40 minutes until slightly firm to the touch (check after 35 mins and leave a little longer if not yet firm)."],[null,"Meanwhile, mix the quark and sweetener together in a bowl and set aside."],[null,"Let the cake cool completely, cover the top of the circle with the frosting, and sprinkle with nuts."],[null,"Just before serving, carefully fill the cavity with the fruit, creating gory looking drips down the outside. Garnish with an eyeball, if using!"]],"h":[[null,"You could fill the cake with other fruits such as fresh blackberries, strawberries or raspberries"],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"2175":{"s":[[null,"Roughly chop the onion. Peel and smash the garlic."],[null,"Combine all ingredients in a blender (can also use a food processor) and pulse for 30 seconds or until desired salsa consistency is reached. Serve with tortilla chips or your favorite Latin American dish!"]],"h":[[null,"Can adjust herbs and spices to taste. The seeds can be removed from the jalapeno to reduce the amount of spice."],[null,"Recipe can stay up to one week in the refrigerator."]]},"9467917":{"s":[[null,"Add all the ingredients to your blender and process on high speed until pureed."],[null,"Heat your nonstick griddle to medium heat and pour the batter directly from your blender spout to make pancakes that are approx. 4 inches in diameter."],[null,"Cook for 4-5 minutes on one side, until several bubbles appear on top and the edges appear set. Then, flip and cook another 3-4 minutes until golden brown and cooked through."],[null,"Serve with maple syrup, fresh fruit and enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Use an overly ripe banana with plenty of brown spots. Since we’re not adding any sugar or sweetener to the pancake batter, a ripe banana is needed for sweetness. Don’t use more than 1 cup of spinach. I’ve tried. 😉 Unfortunately, too much will result in soggy middles, so stick to the recipe. Use medium heat (NOT high) and cook your pancakes longer than you would a traditional pancake. These need about 4-5 minutes per side to fully cook through. Using high heat results in cooked outsides but mushy middles."]]},"6813293":{"s":[[null,"Bring a medium pot with water to a boil and set a steaming basket on top."],[null,"Add the snow peas and steam until they turn bright green and become tender."],[null,"Drain and toss with mayonnaise, toasted sesame seeds, soy sauce, salt, and pepper."]],"h":[]},"6541800":{"s":[[null,"Place orange slices on a large platter and scatter green onions over the top."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk orange juice and olive oil together, and season with salt, pepper, and crushed red chile flakes. Drizzle over the salad, and serve immediately."]],"h":[]},"6817273":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6807355":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6733698":{"s":[[null,"In a bowl, combine yogurt, basil, salt and pepper until blended."],[null,"Add chicken, blueberries, celery and scallions and toss until evenly coated."],[null,"Arrange lettuce leaves on serving platter and top with chicken mixture, dividing evenly between lettuce leaves."],[null,"Top with almonds."]],"h":[]},"6987785":{"s":[[null,"Add the eggs, egg whites, ricotta cheese, vanilla, almond milk, banana, lemon juice, and lemon zest to a blender. Blend until smooth."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine the almond flour, ground flax seed, and baking powder. Add the dry mixture to the liquid mixture in the blender and blend until smooth."],[null,"Coat a nonstick saute pan with cooking spray and place over medium heat. Scoop a scant 1/3 cup of the pancake batter into the pan and top with 4-5 blueberries. Let cook until the edges begin to brown (2-3 minutes); then flip the pancake to continue to cook an additional 2-3 minutes. Remove from the pan and repeat the process for the remaining 5 pancakes."]],"h":[]},"6336463":{"s":[[null,"Add the blueberries, almond milk, yogurt, almond butter, and honey to a blender. Blend until smooth."],[null,"Pour into a tall glass and enjoy immediately."]],"h":[]},"7446938":{"s":[[null,"Put all of the ingredients in a blender and mix until completely smooth."],[null,"Divide the smoothie between 10 popsicle moulds. Cover with the lid, insert the popsicle sticks and transfer to the freezer for 8 hours, or until frozen."],[null,"Devour straight away or store in the freezer to have later."]],"h":[[null,"If you want to add even more nutritional goodness to these treats, add two florets of frozen, steamed cauliflower to the mix before you blend."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"7203090":{"s":[[null,"Mix the lemon zest, lemon curd and cream cheese together in a bowl."],[null,"Gently crush half the blueberries with a fork and add the lemon juice."],[null,"Add remaining blueberries to the cream cheese and lemon curd mixture."],[null,"Place the crushed blueberries in the bottom of a glass, top with the lemon cheese, sprinkle with oatcake crumbs and garnish with some lemon zest and a blueberry."]],"h":[]},"3889":{"s":[[null,"Place all ingredients in a blender and blend until smooth."]],"h":[[null,"Protein will vary depending on the brand of protein powder used and the amount of protein per tablespoon. You may want to adjust the amount of protein powder to provide more or less protein."]]},"9175178":{"s":[[null,"Line a baking sheet with parchment paper and set it aside."],[null,"Then, add everything except the optional coconut to your food processor and blend until combined. The mixture will be sticky."],[null,"Use a small cookie scoop to portion and roll the mixture into balls, placing them on your parchment-lined tray."],[null,"Optional: Place some coconut in a shallow dish, and roll as many of the balls in it as you'd like."],[null,"Refrigerate the energy balls for 1 hour (or longer) to firm them up before enjoying."]],"h":[[null,"If your dates are very dry , soak them in hot water for 10-15 minutes, and then drain them before adding them to your food processor. This will help soften them and make them easier to process."],[null,"Don't overprocess the mixture . These taste best with a little texture."],[null,"The batter will be sticky so use damp hands to roll the mixture into balls to prevent it from sticking to your hands."],[null,"The rolled balls will be soft, so refrigerate them for at least 1 hour before enjoying them to help them harden and set."],[null,"Store your blueberry bliss balls in the fridge for 3-4 days or the freezer for up to 3 months."]]},"4652994":{"s":[[null,"Mix wafer crumbs, 2 Tbsp. (30 ml) sugar and margarine."],[null,"Press in bottom of 9 inch (20 cm) spring form pan or 9 inch (20 cm) pie pan."],[null,"Bake 10 minutes at 350° (175° C). Cool."],[null,"Beat cream cheese in large bowl. Add 1 cup (235 ml) sugar gradually, beating until fluffy."],[null,"Add lemon peel and vanilla. Beat in one egg at a time. Pour over crumb mixture."],[null,"Bake at 300° (150° C) for 1 hour or until center is firm. Refrigerate at least 3 hours."],[null,"Top with pie filling. Makes 16 slices."]],"h":[]},"1902":{"s":[[null,"Soften cream cheese. Place in a bowl and beat with a mixer on high until smooth and fluffy."],[null,"Fold fruit and jam or preserves and whipped topping into the cream cheese."],[null,"Fill cones, and chill in the freezer until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Use sugar-free or fat-free whipped topping, low fat cream cheese and sugar-free jelly to reduce sugar and fat."],[null,"Comet® cones, 4-1/2 grams each, were used in the nutritional analysis . If sugar cones or wafer cones are used, the calories, carbohydrate and sodium may be higher."],[null,"Change the flavor of the cones by using a different type of berry and jam, such as raspberries or strawberries."],[null,"If frozen blueberries are used, thaw before adding to the cream cheese and whipped topping."]]},"2662":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375° F."],[null,"Combine flour, baking powder and sugar in mixing bowl."],[null,"In a separate bowl, combine egg, Rice Dream®, vegetable oil and lemon zest."],[null,"Pour liquid ingredients into flour mixture. Mix ingredients lightly until moistened; do not over mix."],[null,"Gently fold blueberries into batter."],[null,"Lightly spray 12 muffin tins with nonstick cooking spray."],[null,"Spoon batter into muffin tins."],[null,"Bake for 25 minutes or until toothpick comes out clean."]],"h":[[null,"An alternative to spraying muffin tin with cooking spray is to line tins with muffin paper cups."],[null,"Freeze extra muffins then microwave for 30 seconds to serve later."]]},"6229237":{"s":[[null,"Spoon the Greek yogurt into a medium-sized serving bowl."],[null,"Top the yogurt with the blueberries."],[null,"Evenly sprinkle the flaxseeds over the top."],[null,"Stir all ingredients together until well combined, serve immediately."]],"h":[]},"3327":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven 350° F. Set butter and cream cheese out to soften."],[null,"Mix butter with flour and 2 tablespoons sugar. Press evenly into the bottom of a 9″ x 13″ x 2″ oven proof, glass baking dish. Bake for 15 minutes or until lightly browned. Remove from oven and cool."],[null,"In a large bowl, mix cream cheese with a hand mixer until smooth and fluffy. Mix in remaining sugar. Fold whipped topping into cream cheese mixture."],[null,"Spread half of the cream cheese mixture evenly over cooled crust."],[null,"Spread blueberry pie filling evenly over cream cheese mixture. Spread the remaining cream cheese mixture evenly over blueberries. Cover and refrigerate overnight."],[null,"Cut into 10 servings."]],"h":[[null,"Not suitable for people with diabetes due to high calorie, fat and carbohydrate content."],[null,"This special company recipe can be served occasionally with a low-fat entree."]]},"4696843":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F."],[null,"Grease a muffin tin (or use liners) with 24 mini-muffin compartments."],[null,"In a big bowl, prepare dry ingredients. Sift the flour into the bowl. Add the brown sugar, cream of tartar and baking soda."],[null,"In a mid-sized bowl, prepare the wet ingredients. Mix the oil, eggs and milk."],[null,"Pour the wet ingredients into the dry ones and fold them together to get a smooth batter."],[null,"Add the blueberries."],[null,"Spoon batter into 24 compartments (each should be ¾ full)."],[null,"Bake for 15–20 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"This easy recipe makes a great snack. Also try it with other allowed fruits."],[null,"When a recipe asks for baking powder you can reduce the phosphorus content by using a mix of baking soda and cream of tartar instead. For 1 teaspoon baking powder: use ¼ teaspoon baking soda plus ½ teaspoon cream of tartar."],["Portion size matters","As you monitor the amount of potassium in your diet, it's important to always be mindful of portion sizes. While you might think of fruits and vegetables as your main source of potassium, it is important to realize that meat and dairy contribute a great deal of potassium too. Since potassium comes from so many sources, it is important that you talk to a dietitian for guidance. A dietitian can teach you about foods that are lower in potassium that you can eat on a daily basis. They can also help you with how much of all foods you should have every day to strike the right balance. Eating too much of even the lowest potassium foods can add up quickly. For example, pineapple is considered to be a lower potassium fruit, but only when you eat a ½ cup portion. If you consume 1 cup of pineapple it is too much of a “good thing”. Generally, you can have a reasonable portion size of lower potassium fruits and vegetables with each of your meals."]]},"3692":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375° F."],[null,"Pit and slice peaches into 3/4″ slices."],[null,"Spray 12″ x 9″ baking dish with cooking spray. Arrange peach slices and blueberries in dish."],[null,"Sprinkle sugar and lemon juice over the fruit."],[null,"Mix the flour and brown sugar in a bowl. Using two knives or a pastry blender, cut the butter into the flour and sugar mixture until it is crumbly. Sprinkle crumbs over the fruit."],[null,"Bake at for 45 minutes or longer until the fruit is soft and crumbs are browned."],[null,"Serve warm or at room temperature."]],"h":[[null,"Assemble crisp and place in oven right before dinner for a hot fruity dessert. Add a spoonful of whipped topping if desired."],[null,"Substitute 4 cups drained canned peach slices when fresh peaches are out of season."]]},"4777711":{"s":[[null,"Place all ingredients in a blender and mix until smooth."],[null,"Serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"* Count carbohydrates from smoothies as part of total carbohydrate meal or snack goals"],["Protein powder in smoothies or snacks","Finding the time for meal planning and preparation is a big concern for most kidney patients. Oftentimes, it is much simpler to grab something quickly instead of spending time cooking and sitting down for a more balanced meal. Adding protein powder to meals or snacks is a simple method to limit potassium and help you meet your daily protein goals when you are short on time. The amount of protein varies in different powders and can range from 10 to 50 grams per serving. Working with a registered dietitian can help you determine the ideal choice and amount of protein you need. Whey protein can be used with your kidney diet and comes flavored or unflavored. Prepare a quick snack by blending one scoop of protein powder with fresh fruit, rice milk and ice for a delicious smoothie or mix in protein powder as part of a muffin recipe to increase your protein intake. You can also stir-in a scoop of protein powder as part of your favorite beverage or a soft food item to add extra protein with minimum effort."]]},"2839":{"s":[[null,"Wash the blueberries and raspberries and let excess water drain off."],[null,"Cut up onion into pieces. Place berries, onion, lime juice and basil in a food processor or blender."],[null,"Pulse until ingredients are finely chopped. Let salsa sit overnight in the refrigerator."]],"h":[[null,"Serve with low-sodium crackers or tortilla chips. Look for brands with the lowest amount of sodium."],[null,"You may also serve with homemade pita chips. Split the pitas in half and cut each half into quarters. Spray with cooking spray and bake at 350º F for about 8 minutes."],[null,"A 6-ounce container of berries is typically about 1 cup of blueberries or raspberries."],[null,"Drain salsa through a fine sieve to remove excess fluid if you are on a fluid restriction."]]},"6267513":{"s":[[null,"In a nonstick skillet, saute blueberries in canola oil over low heat for about 10 minutes, until you can easily mash the berries."],[null,"Add lime juice and cook another 5 minutes. Remove from heat and stir in vanilla extract."]],"h":[]},"5651491":{"s":[[null,"Add the blueberries into a blender"],[null,"Pour the Renastep into the blender with the blueberries and blend until smooth."],[null,"Serve and enjoy!"]],"h":[["Renastep note","Renastep is a Food for Special Medical Purposes and must be used under medical supervision. Renastep is a ready to use feed for the dietary management of kidney disease from 3 years of age onwards. Renastep contains milk and fish. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information. This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutrimen dietary analysis software."]]},"3254":{"s":[[null,"Place blueberries in a blender and blend on low for 1 minute."],[null,"Add protein powder, yogurt and almond milk. Blend to a soft-serve consistency. Scrape sides of blender as needed."],[null,"Scoop mixture into a bowl."],[null,"Top with sliced strawberries, fresh raspberries, high fiber cereal and coconut flakes. Add honey or sweetener of choice if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Start your day with this high fiber, healthy smoothie in a bowl."],[null,"If you are on a low potassium plan this recipe provides less than 25% of your daily potassium allowance for a 2000 mg potassium diet."],[null,"If you are limiting protein you can leave out the protein powder. Protein is reduced to 7 grams."]]},"6321815":{"s":[[null,"In a blender, combine the frozen blueberries, milk, banana, yogurt, and vanilla extract.​ Blend until smooth and creamy."],[null,"Divide the smoothie mixture evenly between two bowls.​ Top each bowl with fresh blueberries, a sprinkle of low-fat granola, chia seeds, and a dash of ground cinnamon."]],"h":[]},"6227796":{"s":[[null,"Spoon 2/3 cup nonfat Greek yogurt into a bowl or cup."],[null,"Add 1/2 cup blueberries on top."],[null,"Sprinkle with 1 tablespoon sunflower seeds."],[null,"Enjoy immediately, or chill for a few minutes if you prefer it extra cold."]],"h":[]},"7718325":{"s":[[null,"For the base: Preheat the oven to 180°C (160° fan)/350F/gas 4. Grease and line the base of a 20 cm/8\" springform cake tin with greaseproof paper."],[null,"Stir together all the ingredients for the base in a mixing bowl. Pack the mixture into the base of the prepared tin."],[null,"Bake for 10-12 minutes until set and golden on top. Remove the tin to a wire rack to cool."],[null,"For the yoghurt and blueberry topping: Purée about one-quarter of the blueberries with the lemon juice and 1 tbsp granulated sweetener in a food processor"],[null,"Pass through a fine sieve into a large mixing bowl. Add the Greek yoghurt, cream cheese, and remaining sweetener, beating well until thick and creamy."],[null,"Spoon on top of the baked base, spreading out evenly. Top with the remaining blueberries."],[null,"Cover and freeze the cake for 4 hours."],[null,"Remove the cake from the freezer about 45 minutes before serving to let it soften."],[null,"Turn out from the tin and cut into slices with a warm, damp knife."]],"h":[[null,"Any fresh or frozen berries will work well with this recipe."],[null,"You could also use any unsweetened plain yogurt."],[null,"This recipe would work brilliantly served with extra fruit. If you prefer, try using all whole blueberries in the yogurt mix. This will also reduce the free sugars."],[null,"Double-check your sweetener packet for recommended amounts."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"2265":{"s":[[null,"Beat egg whites to a stiff peak."],[null,"In a large bowl, mix flour, white and brown sugar, almonds, lemon juice lemon zest and cinnamon; fold in the egg whites and mix until crumbly. Add water and mix."],[null,"Form dough into a ball, cover, wrap in plastic wrap and chill for 20 minutes."],[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F. Grease a baking sheet."],[null,"Divide chilled dough into 4 pieces. Dust hands with flour and roll out each piece into a 1″ thick rope (about 12″ long). Cut each rope into 2″ sections and roll until 1/2″ thick and about the size of a finger."],[null,"Place on baking sheet and bake for 15 to 18 minutes."],[null,"Let cool then roll in powdered sugar to coat."]],"h":[[null,"Cookies will be hard and crunchy when cooled"],[null,"Recommended portion for a diabetes diet is one cookie (16 g carbohydrate)."]]},"6090763":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, gently stir together the whipped topping, lemon zest, and lemon juice. Spoon into two small custard cups or ramekins."],[null,"Sprinkle the almonds over the whipped topping. Arrange the kiwifruit and strawberries on top. Using a fine sieve, sift the confectioner’s sugar over all. Serve immediately, or refrigerate until serving time. If refrigerated, the sugar will dissolve and give the fruit a glazed appearance."]],"h":[]},"4602003":{"s":[[null,"Place all ingredients in a blender."],[null,"Mix until smooth."],[null,"Serve immediately. For a varIatIon"]],"h":[[null,"Replace the strawberries with 1/2 cup of blueberries. IF you are dIabetIc"],[null,"Reduce the amount of honey to 2 teaspoons. Count 1 Meat + 2 Starch + 2 Fat"],[null,"This nutritious drink provides you with protein and calories on days when your appetite is not great!"]]},"5547623":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C."],[null,"Place kale into boiling water for 1 minute. Then remove from bowl and thoroughly dry."],[null,"Finely chop kale and combine with feta and cottage cheese in a bowl and set aside."],[null,"Place two sheets of filo pastry onto your baking sheet, brush both with butter then place another 2 sheets on top."],[null,"Place the cheese and kale mix onto the pastry and spread out evenly across the baking tray."],[null,"Layer the remaining sheets of filo on top ensuring to butter between layers."],[null,"Brush the top layer with egg and bake for 25 minutes or until golden brown."],[null,"Remove from oven slice into portions and enjoy!"]],"h":[]},"3502648":{"s":[[null,"Bring a medium pan of water to the boil and add the sliced beetroot, carrots and eggs. Boil for five minutes, then drain and set the boiled eggs aside to cool. Once cooled, remove the shell and slice the eggs ready to use later. Place the parboiled beetroot and carrot into a large saucepan."],[null,"Add 500ml cold water to the saucepan, along with the garlic, shallots, bay leaf, coriander seeds, cloves, cayenne pepper, sugar, olive oil and half the vinegar. Cover and bring to the boil, then reduce to a medium-low heat. Simmer for 20 minutes or until the beetroot and carrot are tender."],[null,"Remove the bay leaf and then purée the soup in a blender. To make it super smooth, you can strain it through a sieve into a large bowl or jug, but this may not be necessary. Taste to see if it needs any black pepper or any more vinegar added."],[null,"This dish can be served hot or cold. If serving hot, reheat over a medium heat in a saucepan. Before serving, whisk in the yoghurt and garnish with the chopped dill or chives, a drizzle of olive oil and the sliced boiled eggs. Serve with a bread roll on the side."]],"h":[["Chef's note","This is a delicious and healthy soup that can be served hot or cold. It tastes even better eaten a day or two after it has been made."],["Carbohydrate","The bread rolls are the main source of carbohydrate in this meal. The value has been provided for those who are trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","The main source of potassium in this dish is the beetroot, however the amounts used in the recipe have been kept within a range that ensures the entire meal is low in potassium.\nThis dish is low in phosphate, but it does still contain some phosphate. If you have been prescribed a phosphate binder ensure you take them with this dish."],["Protein","This dish is low in protein, which makes it suitable for those advised to follow a reduced protein diet. Therefore, it may not be suitable for those on dialysis. If you have been advised to eat more protein and aren’t on a vegetarian/vegan diet, you could replace the egg with 250g of cooked shredded chicken."],["Gluten free","Serve with gluten-free bread rolls."],["Vegan","Use a dairy-free yogurt or vegan sour cream and replace the eggs with a drained tin of chickpeas."],["Healthier option","This is already a healthy dish but you could use a low-fat yogurt to keep the fat content low and a wholemeal roll to increase the fibre."],["Storage","The borscht can be refrigerated for up to three days or frozen for up to three months (before the yogurt is added)."],["Fluid management","If you have been advised to follow a fluid restriction, remember to include this soup in your daily fluid allowance."]]},"5502648":{"s":[[null,"Heat the butter in a pan and add the onions, carrot and celery and allow to soften slightly."],[null,"Add in beetroot and garlic and combine with the other vegetables."],[null,"Crumble the stock cubes into the vegetable mixture and then add the coriander seeds, black pepper, bay leaf and butterbeans."],[null,"Cover with water and allow to simmer for 20 minutes."],[null,"Once cooked blend until smooth."],[null,"Stir in the lemon juice and serve with sour cream and dill."]],"h":[]},"7165971":{"s":[[null,"Add sweet potato and carrot to a pan with the stock, bring to the boil, then turn down the heat, cover, and simmer 7 minutes."],[null,"Add the fennel, yellow pepper, leek, turmeric, white pepper and garlic, mix, then cover and simmer for a further 5 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile add 1 tsp of oil to a large non-stick frying pan over a medium-high heat. Once the pan is hot, add 4 pieces of fish, fillet skin-side down and cook for 2-3 minutes. Turn them over and cook another 1-2 minutes. Place on a hot plate and cook the remaining fish fillets with another tsp of oil - if you have a big enough pan you can do in one batch."],[null,"Add the mussels and prawns to the vegetables and stock, bring to the boil and cook for 2 minutes"],[null,"Divide the vegetables, prawns, mussels and broth between 4 bowls. Place the fish fillets on top, sprinkle with parsley, chopped tomato flesh and a sprinkle of black pepper and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Bouillabaisse was traditionally made with leftover fish - whatever was in season - so virtually any fish works."],[null,"To peel tomatoes, dip them in boiling water for 1 minute and the peel is easy to remove."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"6640950":{"s":[[null,"Bring a large pot of salted water to a boil. Add parsnips and turnips and simmer until vegetables are just tender, 8–10 minutes. Drain well."],[null,"While the parsnips and turnips are cooking, make the dressing. Heat oil in a large skillet over medium heat. Add onions and cook until golden brown, 5–7 minutes. Add garlic and cook for 30 seconds more. Stir in vinegar and sugar and bring just to a simmer. Remove from heat and keep dressing warm."],[null,"Arrange parsley, cilantro, and salad greens and top with hot vegetables, then garnish with walnuts and radish. Drizzle with warm dressing, and serve immediately."]],"h":[]},"3648":{"s":[[null,"Chop celery, and bell pepper. Shred carrots. Finely chop onion."],[null,"Mix pasta, celery, red bell pepper, carrot and onion in a bowl."],[null,"In a separate small bowl, blend pepper, mayonnaise, sugar and lemon juice until smooth."],[null,"Pour dressing mixture over pasta and vegetables and mix until well coated."],[null,"Chill and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Add fresh basil, tarragon or rosemary if desired."]]},"2844":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350º F."],[null,"Dice onion, celery,carrot and parsley."],[null,"Trim fat from beef brisket and sprinkle with black pepper."],[null,"Using a heavy pot or Dutch oven, heat oil over medium-high heat and brown meat 5 minutes on each side."],[null,"Remove meat and add onion, celery and carrots. Cook and stir 4 minutes to deglaze the pot."],[null,"Add crumbled bay leaves and parsley to vegetable mixture, and place meat on top of vegetables."],[null,"Pour broth, water and balsamic vinegar over meat to cover and heat until liquid boils."],[null,"Cover pot and cook in the oven for 1-1/2 hours. Turn meat over and cook an additional 1-1/2 hours until meat is tender enough to cut with a fork."],[null,"Remove meat from pot. Add one cup water to pan juices and stir. Strain liquid from solids. Discard vegetables and reserve broth for gravy (see recipe in \"Sauces & Seasonings\" section)."],[null,"Slice brisket, top with gravy and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Save money–brisket costs less than most other beef cuts. It is a muscular, less tender beef cut, best when cooked slowly in liquid to tenderize the meat."],[null,"Use beef brisket for roast beef sandwiches, tacos or burritos, potpie or beef stew."],[null,"This recipe can be cooked in a slow cooker on low heat 8 to 10 hours."],[null,"Look for reduced-sodium broth containing 500 milligrams sodium or less per 1 cup serving. Avoid low sodium broth that contains potassium chloride—it’s very high in potassium. Recommended brands include Health Valley® No Salt Added Fat Free Beef Flavored Broth www.HealthValley.com (800-423-4846), Kitchen Basics® Natural Beef Flavor Stock www.kitchenbasics.net, and Swanson® Lower Sodium Beef Broth www.swansonbroth.com."]]},"3465":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350º F."],[null,"Trim fat from beef brisket and sprinkle with black pepper."],[null,"Dice onion, celery and carrot. Chop parsley."],[null,"Using a heavy pot or Dutch oven, heat oil over medium-high heat and brown meat 5 minutes on each side."],[null,"Remove meat and add onion, celery and carrots. Cook and stir 4 minutes to deglaze the pot."],[null,"Add bay leaves and parsley to vegetable mixture, and place meat on top of vegetables."],[null,"Pour broth, water and balsamic vinegar over meat to cover and heat until liquid boils."],[null,"Cover pot and cook in the oven for 1-1/2 hours. Turn meat over and cook an additional 1-1/2 hours until meat is tender enough to cut with a fork."],[null,"Remove meat from pot. Add one cup water to pan juices and stir. Strain liquid from solids. Discard vegetables and reserve broth for gravy (see recipe in \"Sauces & Seasonings\" section)."],[null,"Slice brisket, top with gravy and serve."]],"h":[[null,"This lower protein version of Braised Beef Brisket has a smaller portion compared to the original recipe on DaVita.com. The nutrients have been adjusted to reflect this change."],[null,"Save money–brisket costs less than most other beef cuts. It is a muscular, less tender beef cut, best when cooked slowly in liquid to tenderize the meat."],[null,"Use beef brisket for roast beef sandwiches, tacos or burritos, potpie or beef stew."],[null,"This recipe can be cooked in a slow cooker on low heat 8 to 10 hours."],[null,"Look for reduced sodium broth containing 500 milligrams sodium or less per 1 cup serving. Avoid low sodium broth that contains potassium chloride—it’s very high in potassium. Recommended brands include Health Valley® No Salt Added Fat Free Beef Flavored Broth www.HealthValley.com (800-423-4846), Kitchen Basics® Natural Beef Flavor Stock www.kitchenbasics.net, and Swanson® Lower Sodium Beef Broth www.swansonbroth.com."],[null,"To lower fat, trim off the extra fat and lower portion."]]},"6427973":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350F."],[null,"Add all ingredients except the vegetable juice to a bowl, and mix until well combined. Form mixture into 12 meatballs."],[null,"Place meatballs in a small baking dish, add the vegetable juice, and bake for 30 minutes."],[null,"Serve with a green salad dressed with a little olive oil and lemon juice, if desired."]],"h":[]},"6697212":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium heat. Add the onion and apple, and sauté for about 3 to 4 minutes, just until the apple begins to soften. Add in the caraway seeds and sugar and sauté for 1 minute."],[null,"Add in the cabbage and toss with tongs, coating the cabbage with the apples and onion. Sauté for about 3 to 4 minutes."],[null,"Add in the broth and apple juice, cover, and cook over medium heat for about 8 to 10 minutes, or until the cabbage is cooked through but tender. Sprinkle in the cider vinegar or lemon juice."]],"h":[]},"6738854":{"s":[[null,"In a large skillet, heat olive oil over medium heat."],[null,"Add sliced carrots to the skillet and sauté for 2–3 minutes."],[null,"Zest and juice the orange."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together honey, orange zest, orange juice, vegetable broth, ground cumin, salt, and black pepper."],[null,"Pour the honey and orange mixture over the carrots in the skillet."],[null,"Bring the mixture to a simmer, then reduce heat to low."],[null,"Cover the skillet and let the carrots braise for 15–20 minutes or until they are tender, stirring occasionally."],[null,"Once the carrots are tender and the liquid has reduced, transfer them to a serving dish."],[null,"Garnish with fresh thyme leaves, optional."]],"h":[]},"7840147":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4. Add the carrots to a saucepan, with the stock cube and 300ml water. Bring to the boil, turn down the heat, add the lid, and simmer for 5 minutes."],[null,"Pour the carrots and stock into an ovenproof dish. Add the peas and spring onions and scatter with 10g of the dill."],[null,"Place the cod steaks on top, cover with foil and bake for 10 minutes."],[null,"Carefully remove the fish and set aside Add the cornflour to the vegetables, mix well and return to the oven for a minute."],[null,"Remove the vegetables from the oven, stir in the cream cheese. Divide the vegetables and sauce between two plates and place a piece of cod on top of each. Scatter with fresh dill and black pepper and serve with lemon."]],"h":[[null,"Works well with haddock, salmon, monk fish or pollock. You could add some prawns."],[null,"If you don't have frozen peas, tinned peas in water or frozen sweetcorn will work just as well with this recipe."],[null,"You could also cook this on the hob in a pan with a tight fitting lid."],[null,"To prepare in advance cook the carrots in stock then allow to cool, assemble everything in an oven proof dish then refrigerate until needed. Allow 5 minutes extra cooking time if cooking straight from the fridge."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"6586304":{"s":[[null,"To prep the collards: Run each leaf under cold running water to clean. Slice the rib from the center of each leaf and chop the leaves into small pieces. Discard ribs. Add chopped leaves to a large bowl and cover with water; add a splash of vinegar. Let sit for 15 minutes."],[null,"Heat a large heavy pot (such as a Dutch oven) over medium heat and add the oil."],[null,"Add the onions to the pot and cook, stirring occasionally, until they begin to soften, 4–5 minutes."],[null,"Add drained collards and cook, stirring occasionally, until wilted, 3–4 minutes."],[null,"Add potatoes, oregano, tomatoes, and water. Cook on low heat, slightly covered, for 20–30 minutes, until potatoes are fork-tender."],[null,"Stir in white beans. Garnish with crushed red pepper if desired."]],"h":[]},"6893547":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375°F. Coat a 9x13-inch baking dish with cooking spray"],[null,"Arrange the fennel and onion in the bottom of the prepared baking dish."],[null,"Pour the olive oil, broth and vinegar over the fennel and onion, and season with salt and pepper."],[null,"Bake for 1 hour, stirring half way through."],[null,"Stir in the beans and parsley and put back in the oven for 10 minutes."]],"h":[]},"6510951":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, combine the rosemary, thyme, oregano, garlic powder and black pepper."],[null,"Heat the oil in a dutch oven over medium-high heat. Add the chicken and sauté for 3 minutes per side."],[null,"Add the garlic and sauté for 30 seconds."],[null,"Add the potatoes and carrots around the chicken in the pan. Pour the herb mixture over the chicken and potatoes."],[null,"Add the chicken broth to the pan and bring to a boil. Reduce heat to a simmer; cover and cook for 30-35 minutes."]],"h":[]},"7142366":{"s":[[null,"Heat a large, non-stick pan, add the onions and garlic and dry fry until soft. Add the celery, lentils and thyme."],[null,"Pour in the water mixed with vinegar, tomatoes and beans, then stir in the stock powder."],[null,"Bring to the boil, then reduce to a gentle simmer."],[null,"Simmer for 20 minutes, until the lentils are soft, adding a little water if required. Season to taste."]],"h":[[null,"Use gluten-free vegetable stock powder to make this recipe gluten free"],[null,"You can also make this dish with 2 cans of mixed beans, or with a can of beans and a can of lentils."],[null,"Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"6225659":{"s":[[null,"Heat 2 tablespoons of oil in a Dutch oven or large pot on medium high heat."],[null,"Pat the chicken dry and season both sides with coarse salt and pepper. Place them in the pot (in batches if needed) and brown on both sides, transferring them to a plate or bowl as when they're done searing."],[null,"Add the onion to the skillet and cook until slightly softened and translucent, about 5 minutes. Sprinkle in garlic, coriander, cumin, paprika, turmeric and cayenne pepper and stir to combine. Cook for 1 minute or until the spices are aromatic and lightly toasted."],[null,"Return the chicken to the pot and stir to coat with the spice mixture."],[null,"Pour in diced tomatoes and enough chicken stock to cover the chicken pieces two thirds of the way."],[null,"Bring the liquid to a simmer, cover and simmer on medium low heat for 15 to 20 minutes."],[null,"Add the mushrooms, sliced red peppers, and lemon zest. Cover and cook for an additional 10-15 minutes, until the sauce has slightly reduced."]],"h":[]},"3196":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Chop carrot, celery and onion."],[null,"Trim fat from ribs. Combine 1/2 cup flour and pepper. Roll short ribs in flour to coat."],[null,"Heat 1-1/2 tablespoons oil in a skillet, and brown ribs on all sides."],[null,"Place ribs in a roasting pan and roast uncovered for 45 minutes. Carefully pour off extra fat."],[null,"Heat 1/2 tablespoon oil in a large pot and sauté chopped vegetables until soft."],[null,"Add roasted short ribs and beef broth. Cover and simmer 2 hours or until ribs are tender."],[null,"To make gravy, brown 2 tablespoons flour in 1 tablespoon oil. Add 1 cup of the meat liquid and stir over medium heat until thickened. Serve 2 tablespoons of gravy with each serving of short ribs."]],"h":[[null,"Look for reduced sodium broth containing 500 milligrams sodium or less per 1 cup serving. Avoid low sodium broths and bouillons containing potassium chloride—it’s very high in potassium."],[null,"Braised means to cook covered in a small amount of liquid, usually after browning the meat to help develop color and flavor."],[null,"For CKD non-dialysis: This higher protein recipe may be appropriate for your diet if the portion size is adjusted to reduce protein content. Adjustments should be based on your individual protein prescription. Check with your dietitian if you are unsure."]]},"3300792":{"s":[[null,"Cook the rice according to the packet instructions. Parboil the carrots and pak choi for 5-10 minutes and drain the water afterwards."],[null,"Separate the oyster mushrooms from the cluster and slice the king oyster mushrooms."],[null,"Fry the tofu in a pan with one tablespoon of oil until golden on both sides. Cook in batches until all the tofu is cooked (approximately 5 minutes each side). Move the tofu onto a clean plate with kitchen towel on it to absorb the excess oil."],[null,"Add the garlic (if using), carrots, both types of mushrooms and pak choi into the heated pan with the other tablespoon of oil. Stir-fry them until they soften."],[null,"Put the cooked tofu back into the pan. Add the oyster sauce, soy sauce and sugar. Stir gently."],[null,"Mix the cornflour with one teaspoon of cold water. Slowly pour in the fluid and stir gently at the same time. Cook until the sauce is thickened and then serve with the rice."]],"h":[["Chef's note","A classic, Hong Kong style meat-free dish. Rich, hearty and warming. Suitable for everyone in the family."],["Carbohydrate","The rice is the main source of carbohydrate in this recipe, and the value has been provided for those who have been trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","This recipe is low in potassium, despite the use of mushrooms, a high potassium vegetable. This is because the quantities have been kept to a minimum, therefore please ensure you follow the quantities for all the ingredients and the serving sizes.\nThis recipe is also low in phosphate, however it still contains phosphate, provided by the tofu and rice, therefore, if you are prescribed a phosphate binder you should take as directed."],["Protein","This recipe is high in protein, which makes it suitable for those advised to eat more protein."],["Gluten free","Use a gluten-free soy sauce such or Tamari and a gluten-free oyster sauce."],["Vegetarian / Vegan","Replace the oyster sauce with a vegetarian version."],["Healthier option","To increase the fibre of this dish consider using a wholegrain brown rice in place of a white rice. Be mindful that the low-salt soy sauce and oyster sauce are both high salt ingredients, therefore you should measure these carefully to avoid adding additional salt."],["Storage","This dish is best eaten fresh."],["Tips","To reduce cooking time, cut the tofu into 1cm cubes and cook using an extra tablespoon of oil."]]},"6837683":{"s":[[null,"Refrigerate for at least 3 hours so that flavors can develop but remove from the fridge at least 20 minutes before serving. Chef's Tip: Cut the other half of the bell peppers and cucumber into sticks to serve with the guacamole for dipping"],[null,"Cut the avocados in half, remove the pits and scoop the flesh out of their shells. Dice or mash the avocado and add it to the vegetables. Slowly add the olive oil and fold everything together."],[null,"Combine the garlic, scallions, red onion, bell peppers, cucumber and tomato and toss well. Season with the soy sauce, salt and pepper, parsley and clinatro and fold well."]],"h":[]},"3305":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400° F."],[null,"Cut crust from bread slices and roll flat with a rolling pin."],[null,"Spray a small-cup muffin tin with nonstick cooking spray."],[null,"Press one slice of bread into each muffin cup and trim edges with a knife."],[null,"Mix oils and garlic powder together. Brush each bread cup with oil and bake for 10 to 12 minutes until crisp and golden brown."],[null,"Let cups cool before removing from muffin pan."]],"h":[[null,"Chicken Salad, Tuna Veggie Salad, or egg salad"],[null,"Diced cucumber, onion, bell pepper and grated carrot"],[null,"Flavored cream cheese"],[null,"Asparagus Spread"],[null,"Shrimp Spread"]]},"7940182":{"s":[[null,"Stud the onion with the cloves and place in a pan with the milk, bay leaf and peppercorns."],[null,"Bring to a simmer, then remove from the heat and allow the flavours to develop for 2 hours."],[null,"Remove the onion, bay leaf and peppercorns from the milk before adding the spread and breadcrumbs."],[null,"Cook again over a very low heat for about 20 minutes until thickened."]],"h":[[null,"Try adding crushed garlic and chopped fresh parsley to create a tasty garlic bread sauce."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Freeze in portions then defrost and serve warm."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"55014":{"s":[[null,"Thaw fish according to package directions. May also use fresh cod if desired."],[null,"Preheat oven to 450F. Line a baking sheet with foil and spray with non-stick cooking spray."],[null,"Add crackers to a zip top bag and crush with a rolling pin or crush between your hands. Add paprika and pepper, then pour out onto a medium size plate."],[null,"Add the flour to a shallow bowl. Beat the egg in a separate bowl."],[null,"Take one fillet and lay in flour coating both sides. Then do the same in the egg covering both sides. Finally cover with crackers crumbs all around the fish."],[null,"Lay on prepared sheet pan and repeat with second fillet. Bake for 4-5 minutes, flip the fish over and bake 4-5 minutes longer. Cook to an internal temperature of at least 145F. Serve on hamburger bun."]],"h":[[null,"Top with a teaspoon of mustard or other low sodium condiment. See our Sauces & Seasonings Category on our recipe page for other topping ideas."],[null,"Serve with coleslaw, fresh side salad or steamed vegetables."]]},"3529":{"s":[[null,"Spray a medium-size skillet with nonstick cooking spray and heat over medium heat."],[null,"In a bowl, beat eggs with green chiles, cumin and hot sauce. Pour eggs into skillet and cook and stir 1 to 2 minutes until eggs are done."],[null,"Heat tortillas for 20 seconds in microwave or in separate skillet over medium heat. Place half the egg mixture on each tortilla and roll up burrito style."]],"h":[[null,"Burritos freeze and reheat well. Wrap in plastic wrap and place in freezer bag. To reheat burrito remove from plastic, place on microwave-safe plate, cover with a damp paper towel and microwave 1 to 2 minutes."],[null,"Tortillas, salsa and hot pepper sauces vary greatly in sodium content. Compare nutrition labels on brands and select the ones lowest in sodium."],[null,"Low cholesterol egg substitute may be substituted for whole eggs. Cholesterol is 0 mg if egg substitute is used."],[null,"May use 1 tablespoon of salsa per burrito. If does add sodium so look for brands that are lower sodium or make a homemade salsa."]]},"7242909":{"s":[[null,"Prepare the cold fillings and have the hot fillings cooked and warm."],[null,"Place the tortillas in a stack in a dry frying pan over a low heat, and turn them regularly so each side is warmed but not toasted. Heat one side of the tortilla in direct contact with the pan and then move it to the top of the stack. Repeat so that all the tortillas are warmed. Don’t crisp the outside – they need to be easy to fold, but you can crisp them up once they’re folded, if you like."],[null,"Lay the tortillas out then add a few ingredients covering the bottom half of the tortilla."],[null,"Sprinkle on a little Cheddar and chilli sauce or seasoning (if using) then roll up, tucking in the sides."],[null,"Place the rolled up tortillas onto a dry frying pan over a low heat, seam side down. Cook for a couple of minutes, turning a couple of times to cook evenly."]],"h":[[null,"You could also add cooked diced potato, sweet potato or mushrooms."],[null,"Or non-vegetarians could add some grilled or smoked fish."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"7525579":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 200C/gas 6. Halve the avocado, remove the stone and scoop out 1tbsp of flesh from each half (reserve for another recipe). Sit each in a ramekin to keep them upright. Crack an egg into each and bake for 12–15 mins until yolk is set."],[null,"Heat the oil in a small non-stick frying pan. Add the chilli and cook until softened. Add the beans and their can juices, the tomatoes and chipotle paste. Cook gently for 5 mins until warmed through and the tomatoes are starting to soften."],[null,"Assemble the dish on a plate, scattering the spring onions on top."]],"h":[[null,"If your eggs are a bit big, separate the yolks, pop a yolk into each avocado, stir the whites with a fork to break them up, and use to top up the dip in each avocado."],[null,"At risk' groups such as infants, children, pregnant women, the elderly and those who are unwell should avoid soft/lightly cooked and raw eggs, unless they can guarantee that they are produced under the Lion code quality assurance scheme."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"3104":{"s":[[null,"In a medium bowl mix all ingredients together."],[null,"Divide into 1 cup portions."],[null,"Serve dry or with your favorite milk substitute."]],"h":[[null,"Breakfast Trail Mix is a great breakfast alternative for dialysis patients who often do not have time for breakfast. It can be eaten as a snack or with milk alternative as a breakfast cereal."],[null,"Be creative and experiment with different cereals. Ask your dietitian for a list of approved cereals."]]},"2755":{"s":[[null,"Crush the soda crackers, then combine them with the milk in a bowl. Let stand until crackers are soft."],[null,"Beat the egg and stir into cracker mixture. Add the herb blend; mix well, breaking up the crackers if necessary. Add the ground beef and mix well."],[null,"Pat the ground beef mixture into 4 equal-size patties."],[null,"Grill over medium heat until cooked until the internal temperature is at least 160º F."],[null,"Serve on a bun with desired toppings, or serve patty with a vegetable and starch of choice."]],"h":[[null,"Always cook ground beef to a temperature of at least 160º F."],[null,"Nutrient analysis does not include bun, toppings or side dishes."]]},"1739":{"s":[[null,"Combine milk and crushed crackers in a bowl and let stand until crackers are soft."],[null,"Stir in beaten egg and herb seasoning blend; mix well, breaking up crackers if necessary. Add ground beef and mix well."],[null,"Pat into 6 equal-size patties."],[null,"Grill over medium heat until cooked to desired doneness."]],"h":[[null,"Always cook ground beef to an internal temperature of at least 160º F."],[null,"Serve with vegetables and starch of choice or serve on a bun with lettuce and onion."],[null,"This lower protein version of Brewery Burger has a smaller portion compared to the original recipe on DaVita.com. The nutrients have been adjusted to reflect this change."]]},"2797":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F. Wash and drain fresh cranberries."],[null,"In a large skillet, heat water on medium for 5 minutes and add fresh cranberries. Heat for no more than 5 minutes, just until the cranberries start to burst."],[null,"Add white and brown sugar (or Splenda)."],[null,"Add spices and stir gently."],[null,"Remove from heat. Let chutney cool."],[null,"Remove wheel of Brie from the wrapper. Leaving a half-inch border of rind on top of the wheel, cut out a circle and lift out rind from the center to expose the Brie inside."],[null,"Place Brie on a baking sheet and heat in oven just until the cheese is soft to the touch and the top is slightly melted."],[null,"Remove Brie from oven and place on a platter."],[null,"Pour warm chutney over Brie and serve with a variety of low-sodium crackers."]],"h":[[null,"Fresh cranberries are sold in 12 ounce bags."],[null,"Low-sodium crackers are recommended to help keep sodium low."],[null,"Substitute 1/2 cup Splenda® granular and1/4 cup Splenda® brown sugar blend for sugars. Substitutions reduce carbohydrate to 19 grams per serving, 1 carbohydrate choice."],[null,"Cranberry Chutney can be prepared and refrigerated for three days prior to serving."],[null,"Cranberry Chutney is a delicious side dish with turkey or lamb, or spread it on a turkey sandwich for a yummy flavor."]]},"3560541":{"s":[[null,"Heat oven to 220°C/ gas mark 7. Melt the butter and brush it over each sheet of filo and then stack two of the filo sheets on top of each other with wide edges facing towards you."],[null,"Cut the Brie into 18 chunky fingers and space them across the bottom of the filo sheet. Top each finger with 1 teaspoon cranberry sauce and then sprinkle over a few chopped walnuts. Cut the filo pastry into long columns."],[null,"Roll up the filo pastry from the bottom. Cut into each roll into three parcels and twist the ends of each parcel to seal. Brush parcels with more butter and sprinkle with poppy seeds."],[null,"Repeat steps 2–4 using up all ingredients. Bake in the oven for 10 minutes. Once browned, remove from the oven and allow to cool slightly before serving."]],"h":[["Chef's note","These tasty filo pastry parcels make a sophisticated treat. Filled with creamy Brie, sweet cranberry and a walnut crunch."],["Carbohydrate","The filo pastry and cranberry sauce are the main sources of carbohydrate in this snack. The carbohydrate value has been provided for those who have been trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","The ingredients in this recipe are low in potassium. It is a snack that can be enjoyed as part of a low potassium diet, in small quantities, for a special occasion. The phosphate in this recipe is provided mainly by the brie and small amount from the walnuts. If you have been prescribed a phosphate binder, ensure you take them with this snack and avoid eating too many."],["Protein","The protein in this recipe is provided by the cheese and walnuts."],["Gluten free","Use gluten-free filo pastry."],["Vegetarian","Check the cheese you use to ensure it is vegetarian."],["Vegan","Use vegan pastry and a suitable vegan cheese."],["Healthier option","This snack is for special occasions and would work particularly well at Christmas time, however, should only be eaten in moderation. It may also be advisable to half the total recipe for small gatherings or households."],["Cheaper option","The ingredients in this recipe are relatively inexpensive however to reduce the cost and maintain the taste you could omit the walnuts and/or poppy seeds."],["Storage","These are best eaten freshly cooked, however if storing, allow them to cool, place in an air-tight container and refrigerate for up to 3 days."]]},"3934642":{"s":[[null,"Cook the baguettes according to the instructions and then set aside to cool."],[null,"Preheat oven to 180°C / 160°C fan / gas mark 4. Put the cauliflower and broccoli into a pan of water and bring to the boil and cook for approximately 5 minutes until the vegetables are almost tender. Remove from the heat and drain."],[null,"Make the sauce by heating the cream cheese over a medium heat to loosen it and then whisk in the milk to fully combine into a sauce with a good grind of black pepper and the English mustard. Remove from the heat."],[null,"Arrange the cauliflower and broccoli into a baking dish and pour over the cheese sauce. Sprinkle the grated Cheddar over the top and then cook in the oven for 25 minutes until nicely golden."],[null,"While this is cooking, make the garlic butter by mixing the butter with the garlic purée and dried herbs, beat well. Halve the cooked baguettes and spread with the garlic butter. Put the two halves of baguette back together and wrap in tin foil. Add into the oven with the cauliflower cheese with 10 minutes remaining on the cooking time."]],"h":[["Chef's note","A twist on a family classic"],["Portion guidance for children","Serving sizes are based on adult portions. Here is a guide for children:\nToddler (age 1-4): ¼\nYoung child (age 5-9): ½\nOlder child (age 10-13): ¾\nTeenagers (14+): 1\nSome children do have bigger appetites than others. You child’s portion may need to be changed to fit their typical diet if you think the recommended serving sizes are too large or small. We would advise speaking with your dietitian prior to increasing the serving size if your child has struggled to manage potassium or phosphate."],["Carbohydrate","The baguette is the main source of carbohydrate in this recipe, and the value has been provided for those who have been trained in insulin adjustment."],["Energy","If you need to gain weight, have a growing child who needs more calories, or have a poor appetite, you can use whole milk to make the cheese sauce and add extra butter to the garlic bread."],["Protein","This recipe provides a source of protein but is not high in protein. If you have been advised to eat more protein, be sure to include higher protein foods at your other meals and snacks throughout the day."],["Phosphate/potassium","This recipe is low in potassium, when following the quantities in the ingredients, and the serving sizes. Therefore, suitable for those advised to eat less potassium.\nThis recipe is also low in phosphate, however it does contain some phosphate, mainly provided by the milk, and cheeses, therefore if you have been prescribed a phosphate binder you should take as directed."],["Gluten free","Use gluten-free baguettes."],["Vegan","Use vegan alternatives to cream cheese, milk and Cheddar."],["Healthier option","To reduce saturated fat and increase fibre, consider using lower fat milk, lower fat cream cheese and choosing wholemeal baguettes."],["Cheaper option","This recipe has been kept as low cost as possible, however cream cheese could be replaced with a supermarket own-brand alternative, fresh garlic can be used instead of garlic purée, and the dried parsley can be omitted."],["Storage","Leftovers can be stored in the fridge for up to 2 days and reheated. The cauliflower cheese can be made the day before and kept in fridge overnight, then cooked."]]},"9251879":{"s":[[null,"If you do not have blanched almonds, begin by blanching whole raw almonds following the directions in the post, or see the summary in the notes below."],[null,"Roughly chop your onion, garlic, and celery and add them to a pot with 2-3 tablespoons of water. Sauté for 3-4 minutes, until softened, adding more water to prevent sticking, if needed. Then add the thyme and sauté for 30 seconds, until fragrant."],[null,"Pour in the broth, almonds, chopped potatoes, broccoli florets, and salt and pepper. Bring to a boil over high heat and then lower the heat to medium and cook for approx. 6-8 minutes, until the potatoes are fork tender."],[null,"Use an immersion blender to puree your soup, or carefully transfer to a stand blender, working in batches. Use caution when handling hot liquids and do not overfill the blender. Serve with crusty bread, croutons and/or fresh parsley."]],"h":[[null,"Use low-sodium vegetable broth OR skip the salt if you only have regular broth."],[null,"To puree your soup , use an immersion or hand blender for less mess, and ease of blending in one step."],[null,"If you don't have a hand blender , very carefully transfer to a stand blender. Work in batches, as needed, and never overfill your blender with hot liquids."],[null,"Once pureed, taste the soup and adjust the salt and pepper to your preference. Remember, you can always add, but you cannot remove."],[null,"This soup makes fantastic leftovers and thickens more as it sits, so it's great for making in advance and reheating."],[null,"Leftovers keep refrigerated for up to 4 days or your may freeze for up to 3 months."],[null,"How to Blanch Almonds If you don’t have blanched almonds, all you need is 5 minutes to make some from whole raw almonds. Bring a small pot of water (enough to cover the almonds) to boil. Once boiling, add the almonds and boil for 1 minute. Then drain and rinse with cold water to cool them down, enough to handle. Then pinch the almonds and the skin will come off easily."]]},"6320177":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 425 degrees. Spray a baking sheet with cooking spray."],[null,"In a small bowl mix together broccoli, olive oil, garlic, almonds and black pepper. Pour mixture onto baking sheet."],[null,"Bake for 10-12 minutes until broccoli tips are slightly brown."],[null,"Pour broccoli into a bowl and sprinkle with lemon juice."]],"h":[]},"6888570":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, combine the blanched and cooled broccoli florets, almonds, grapes, red onion, and chopped fresh parsley."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the apple cider vinegar, light mayonnaise, Dijon mustard, minced garlic, salt, and black pepper."],[null,"Pour the dressing over the salad and toss gently to ensure even coating."]],"h":[]},"2113":{"s":[[null,"Trim and cut broccoli florets into small bite size pieces. Dice unpeeled apple into small bite size pieces. Chop the fresh parsley."],[null,"In a large bowl whisk together the yogurt, mayonnaise, honey, vinegar and parsley."],[null,"Add the remaining ingredients and coat with the yogurt mixture. Refrigerate to chill and let the flavors combine. Stir immediately before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Use your favorite variety of apple."],[null,"Can be served immediately if not time to refrigerate."],[null,"This salad is great during the holidays but can be enjoyed all year long."],[null,"Garnish with additional fresh parsley prior to serving if desired."]]},"6314398":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl whisk together the yogurt, mayonnaise, honey, vinegar, and parsley."],[null,"Trim and cut broccoli florets into small bite size pieces. Dice unpeeled apples into small bite size pieces. Chop the fresh parsley."],[null,"Add the remaining ingredients and coat with the yogurt mixture. Refrigerate to chill and let the flavors combine. Stir immediately before serving."]],"h":[]},"2941":{"s":[[null,"Chop the garlic cloves and Roma tomato. Cut beef into thin strips."],[null,"Microwave frozen stir-fry vegetable blend on defrost setting for 3-4 minutes to thaw."],[null,"In a fry pan or wok heat oil and sauté the garlic until fragrant. Add vegetable blend stir-fry until cooked, about 5 minutes. Remove from pan and set aside."],[null,"In same pan add beef. Cook until beef is done to your likeness, about 7 minutes."],[null,"Prepare the sauce by combining chicken broth, cornstarch and soy sauce in a bowl."],[null,"Add cooked vegetables, sauce and tomato to the pan with the beef. Heat and stir until sauce is thick."],[null,"Serve dish with 1/2 cup rice."]],"h":[[null,"Broccoli stir-fry blends contain a blend of 4-6 vegetables. In addition to broccoli the blend may include bell peppers, onion, mushrooms and water chestnuts carrots, celery, sugar snap peas or baby corn."],[null,"If desired, use fresh vegetables instead of frozen. Substitute with 3 cups fresh broccoli florets, 1/2 red bell pepper, 1/2 cup snow peas and 1/4 cup canned sliced water chestnuts."],[null,"Analysis includes brown rice. Select brown, white or wild rice based on your preference."],[null,"Increase meat for a higher protein meal."],[null,"You can substitute chicken or shrimp for beef to make variations in this dish."]]},"3067106":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 165°C. Bring a pan of water to the boil and add the pasta, cook for 5 minutes. Add the broccoli and cauliflower into the pan and cook for a further 8 minutes or until all cooked, then drain."],[null,"Mix the black pepper and dried herbs into the cream cheese in a bowl."],[null,"Tip the pasta and vegetables into a baking dish and stir in the cream cheese mix. Sprinkle with breadcrumbs and cheddar cheese. Cook for 30 minutes until golden brown."],[null,"Remove from oven and rest for 5 minutes before serving."]],"h":[["Chef's note","An indulgent, creamy dinner, this meal is high in energy but low in salt, phosphate and potassium."],["Carbohydrate","The pasta is the main source of carbohydrate in this main meal. The value has been provided for those who have been trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","This dish is low in potassium, because the quantities per person have been carefully measured. If you have been advised to follow a low potassium diet ensure you keep to the quantities stated. This recipe is low in phosphate, however does contain some phosphate, therefore, if you have been prescribed a phosphate binder ensure you take them with this dish."],["Protein","Protein is provided by the cheddar and cream cheese. To reduce the protein, you could use vegan alternatives that are often lower in protein than dairy sources."],["Storage","For a speedy meal, this recipe can be prepared earlier in the day and cooked in the oven later (ensure it is refrigerated in the meantime). Leftovers keep in the fridge for 2 days."]]},"6287846":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, whisk together the grapefruit juice, shallot, olive oil, vinegar, honey, salt, and pepper."],[null,"Add broccoli and mandarin oranges, stir gently so as to not break up the oranges. Sprinkle with pecans."]],"h":[]},"6078258":{"s":[[null,"Place the spinach, broccoli, avocado, blueberries, feta cheese, and sunflower seeds in a large bowl or in a large platter."],[null,"Place yogurt, buttermilk, garlic, lemon juice and zest, poppy seeds, herbs, and pepper in a blender and blend to combine. (If not using a blender, ingredients can also be whisked in a bowl until combined.)"],[null,"Pour dressing over salad and serve immediately."]],"h":[]},"9437802":{"s":[[null,"Bring a large pot of generously salted water to a boil. Then cook your pasta according to the package directions for 'al dente' pasta. Drain it but reserve some of the pasta water, and set it aside."],[null,"Meanwhile, use a deep skillet to sauté the onion and garlic with 2-3 tablespoons of water over medium heat until translucent, approx. 3-4 minutes. Then add the asparagus and broccoli, season with salt and pepper, and continue sautéing until tender, approx. 6-8 minutes."],[null,"While the vegetables are cooking, combine the broth, milk, tapioca starch, and red pepper flakes in a bowl or measuring cup. Mix well and then pour the sauce into the skillet with the veggies. Simmer until thickened, approx. 2-3 minutes and then turn off the heat."],[null,"By now your pasta should be cooked, so add it to the pan with the sauce and veggies along with the vegan parmesan cheese, and mix well."],[null,"Optional: For a thinner sauce, add some of the pasta water you reserved to the pan and stir. (To your preference.)"]],"h":[]},"6942512":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F. Coat one large (or two small) baking sheets with cooking spray. Set aside."],[null,"Steam the broccoli for approximately 10 to 12 minutes, until soft. Set aside to cool (for about 10 minutes)."],[null,"Add the broccoli and remaining ingredients to a blender or food processor and pulse to combine. Do not overmix; the mixture should be slightly chunky, not a paste. Let the mixture rest for 10 minutes."],[null,"After resting the mixture, stir it, and scoop and drop by Tbsp.fuls onto the prepared baking sheet."],[null,"Lightly spray the top of each ball with cooking spray. Bake for 15 minutes. Turn the pieces over and bake an additional 10 minutes, or until golden brown."]],"h":[]},"6126102":{"s":[[null,"In a large saucepan, heat the oil over medium heat, swirling to coat the bottom. Cook the onion and garlic for 3-4 minutes, or until the onion is almost soft, stirring frequently."],[null,"Stir in the broccoli, broth, mustard, pepper, hot-pepper sauce, and salt. Increase the heat to medium high and bring to a simmer. Reduce the heat and simmer for 5 minutes, or until the broccoli is tender, stirring occasionally."],[null,"In a medium bowl, whisk together the milk and flour. Stir into the soup. Simmer for 2-3 minutes, or until the mixture has thickened, stirring occasionally."],[null,"Stir in the half-and-half, cheddar, and Parmesan. Cook over medium-low heat for 1-2 minutes, or until the cheeses have melted, stirring occasionally."]],"h":[]},"5057164":{"s":[[null,"Mix the plain flour and paprika in a bowl, set aside."],[null,"Whisk together the Renastep and egg in a jug until fully combined."],[null,"Pour the Renastep and egg mixture into the bowl with the flour and whisk well until there are no lumps remaining."],[null,"Add in the grated broccoli and mix well."],[null,"Heat the oil in a pan and spoon out 8 separate fritters and fry on both sides until golden brown."],[null,"Serve and enjoy!"]],"h":[["Renastep note","Always check with your dietitian or doctor that this recipe is suitable for you."],["Renastep note","Renastep is a Food for Special Medical Purposes and must be used under medical supervision. Renastep is a ready to use feed for the dietary management of kidney disease from 3 years of age onwards. Renastep contains Milk (Milk protein) and Fish (Tuna oil). This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutritics dietary analysis software. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information."]]},"6536789":{"s":[[null,"Boil the diced broccoli in a small amount of water for 5 minutes, then drain thoroughly."],[null,"Break eggs into a medium bowl and beat. Add the flour and mix well. Add the broccoli and onion and stir into the flour/egg mixture until well mixed."],[null,"Heat olive oil in a frying pan over medium-high heat. Drop the mixture by spoonfuls into the hot oil, making 4 equal portions. Flatten with a spatula, and cook until golden brown on both sides (about 3-4 minutes per side)."],[null,"Remove the latkes from the pan and drain on a paper towel to soak up extra oil. Serve hot."]],"h":[]},"4053424":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400°F."],[null,"In a small mixing bowl, combine ricotta cheese, dried oregano, and garlic powder."],[null,"To each pita, spread 2 tablespoons of ricotta mixture on the pita base. Sprinkle with 1 tablespoon of mozzarella cheese. Add ¼ cup of finely chopped broccoli and ¼ cup of diced chicken. Garnish with chili flakes."],[null,"Place pita pizzas on a baking tray."],[null,"Bake for 10–15 minutes or until pita pizzas are crispy and broccoli is cooked. Serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"You can also use Naan bread or flour tortillas."],["Kidney-Friendly Pizza","Adjusting to a kidney diet can be a difficult task. With sodium, potassium, phosphorus and/or protein restrictions, trying to find meals that are appetizing may become overwhelming. Work with your renal dietitian to incorporate a variety of different foods into your diet. A change of ingredients or portion sizes can make a recipe more kidney-friendly and will allow you to eat some of your favorite dishes. Pizza is one of the top 5 regularly eaten meals in the United States. Unfortunately, this food is often made with ingredients high in sodium, potassium and phosphorus. Rather than excluding pizza entirely, try the following modifications to allow pizza to fit within your kidney diet goals. • Plan ahead and make your own crust to limit unnecessary additives. • Instead of high-potassium red sauces made with tomatoes try a lite Alfredo sauce, olive oil base or roasted red pepper sauce. • Replace salty processed meats with lower-fat ground turkey or beef. • Use smaller portions of cheese. • Top with low-potassium vegetables such as green bell peppers, mushrooms or onions. • Finish off pizza flavor with sodium and potassium-free seasonings such as fennel seed, red pepper flakes or Italian seasoning."]]},"6030314":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, combine broccoli slaw mix, finely chopped red onion, raisins or dried cranberries, and toasted sunflower seeds."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together Greek yogurt, Dijon mustard, apple cider vinegar, unsweetened multi-use syrup, coarse salt, and black pepper."],[null,"Pour the dressing over the slaw and toss gently to ensure even coating."]],"h":[]},"9079622":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 400 degrees F (200 C) and line a large baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Scrub your sweet potatoes and cut them in half lengthwise. Arrange them cut side down on your tray. Add the onion, cut side down, the broccoli florets, and the unpeeled garlic to the same tray. (Use two trays if you cannot fit everything in one.)"],[null,"Drizzle the vegetables with avocado oil OR vegetable broth for oil free. Use your fingers or a silicone brush to rub the liquid over the potato skin. Then sprinkle everything with salt and pepper."],[null,"Bake for 25-30 minutes, until your sweet potatoes are easily pierced with a fork, and the remaining veggies are nicely roasted and golden brown. Remove from the oven."],[null,"Optional: Reserve some of the smaller pieces of broccoli for a garnish."],[null,"Add the roasted vegetables (except the pieces you reserved for garnish) and all remaining ingredients to a pot and use an immersion blender to puree until smooth. OR, transfer to a stand blender and blend in batches. Use caution when blending hot liquids and do not overfill the blender. Taste and adjust for salt and pepper, if needed."],[null,"Serve your broccoli and sweet potato soup with the reserved roasted broccoli pieces, croutons, and cashew cream, if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Use sweet potatoes that are narrow and long . Wide potatoes will take much longer to cook. Do your best to cut your sweet potatoes in equal halves for even cooking. If you prefer a thinner soup , add an additional cup of broth. Transfer the roasted vegetables to a pot and use an immersion blender to puree them so you can blend everything in one batch. Leftovers keep for 3-4 days in the refrigerator or freeze airtight in a freezer-safe container for up to 3 months."]]},"6870063":{"s":[[null,"Steam, microwave, or roast broccoli according to package directions."]],"h":[]},"3103":{"s":[[null,"Dice broccoli and chop onion."],[null,"Boil the diced broccoli in a small amount of water for 5 minutes; drain."],[null,"Break eggs into a medium bowl and beat. Add the flour and mix well."],[null,"Add the broccoli and onion and stir into the flour/egg mixture until well mixed."],[null,"Add olive oil to a frying pan and heat."],[null,"Drop the mixture by spoonfuls into the hot oil, making 4 equal portions (or 8 portions is smaller latkes are desired)."],[null,"Using a spatula, flatten the latkes and fry until brown on both sides."],[null,"Drain on a paper towel to soak up extra oil."],[null,"Serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"Potato latkes (pancakes), contain over 600 mg potassium for a comparable serving unless the potatoes are soaked or boiled to reduce potassium. Broccoli-Onion Latkes are a good low-potassium alternative."],[null,"The latkes taste best if eaten immediately."]]},"6399816":{"s":[[null,"Preheat broiler. Spray a baking sheet or broiler pan with cooking spray."],[null,"In a small bowl mix together mayonnaise, lemon juice, paprika, parsley and ground black pepper."],[null,"Place cod filets on broiler pan and spread mayonnaise mixture evenly among the cod filets. Sprinkle Parmesan cheese on top of filets."],[null,"Broil filets for 8-10 minutes."]],"h":[]},"3867":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the broiler and broiler pan. Rinse and dry fish fillets. Melt the butter. Cut lemon in half and then cut one half into slices. Juice the remaining half. Peel and finely mince the cucumber."],[null,"In a small bowl combine the mayonnaise, yogurt, chopped dill, 1 teaspoon lemon juice and cucumber. Refrigerate until ready to serve."],[null,"Remove the broiler pan from oven and spray with cooking spray. Brush fillets with melted butter and sprinkle with lemon juice. Broil for 5 minutes. Baste with remaining butter and lemon juice and continue to broil until done. To check for doneness insert and twist a fork into the thickest part of the fillet. The flesh will easily separate when cooked through."],[null,"Place each fillet on a plate and add 3 tablespoons cucumber sauce and garnish with a lemon slice and dill sprig."]],"h":[[null,"Use 1/2 teaspoon dried dill if fresh is unavailable."],[null,"Try this recipe with catfish, flounder, salmon, snapper, swordfish, tilapia, trout, tuna or any other fish you like. Thicker fillets can be turned halfway through the cooking."]]},"1965":{"s":[[null,"Turn on broiler."],[null,"Cook cleaned ear of corn in a grill pan or on a hot grill until grill marks are apparent. Stand ear of corn upright. Using a sharp knife, cut kernels from stalk."],[null,"Peel and dice cucumber. Dice onion, bell pepper; peel and mince garlic; chop cilantro."],[null,"In a bowl, combine cucumber, onion, garlic clove, red pepper, cayenne pepper, cilantro, grilled corn kernels and 1-1/2 tablespoons lime juice. Place in the refrigerator and allow flavors to blend."],[null,"Cut fish into four 4-ounce fillets. Score fillets lightly with a sharp knife. Season with pepper, garlic powder and onion powder. Drizzle fillets lightly with remaining 3 tablespoons lime juice. Arrange on baking sheet lined with parchment."],[null,"Place baking sheets under broiler and cook until golden brown or cooked thoroughly. (Internal temperature of fish should reach 145° F.)"]],"h":[[null,"Adjust the amount of cayenne pepper used to match your tastefor spiciness."],[null,"The recommended internal temperature of cooked fish is 145° F. Cooking time varies with thickness of fillets."],[null,"This recipe works well with trout."],[null,"Substitute 1/2-cup frozen or unsalted, canned corn kernels for fresh corn if desired. Stir in a skillet over high heat to toast before adding to salsa."]]},"3044":{"s":[[null,"Preheat broiler to 400º F."],[null,"Cut grapefruit in half then cut around the edges and sections of each grapefruit half."],[null,"Drizzle the top of each half with a teaspoon of honey and 1/8 teaspoon cinnamon."],[null,"Broil grapefruit for 6 minutes or until it starts to brown."],[null,"Serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"Sectioning the grapefruit before broiling makes it easier to eat."],[null,"Grapefruit and grapefruit juice are known to interact with some medications. Check with your healthcare team to be sure grapefruit is safe to include in your diet."]]},"6070947":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the broiler in your oven."],[null,"Place the slices of whole grain or whole wheat bread on a baking sheet."],[null,"Lightly toast one side of the bread slices under the broiler for 1–2 minutes, keeping a close eye to prevent burning."],[null,"Remove the baking sheet from the oven and flip the bread slices to the untoasted side."],[null,"Spread a thin layer of basil pesto on each untoasted side of the bread."],[null,"Place tomato slices on the bread."],[null,"Top the tomatoes with slices of mozzarella cheese. Drizzle olive oil over the top."],[null,"Place the baking sheet back under the broiler for an additional 2–3 minutes or until the cheese is melted and bubbly. Top with sliced, fresh basil if desired."]],"h":[]},"9702792":{"s":[[null,"Add the rice to a strainer and rinse well using cool water."],[null,"Place all the ingredients to your instant pot and give it a good mix. Make sure the rice is covered by the liquids to ensure even cooking. Then close the lid and make sure the release valve is set to the sealing position. Set to high pressure for 22 minutes. (It will take about 10 minutes to build pressuring before counting down.)"],[null,"Allow pressure to release naturally for 10 minutes, and then release any remaining pressure with the release valve."],[null,"Fluff with a fork and enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Rinse your rice well before cooking to remove the starch and prevent the rice from sticking and clumping together. Shake your can of coconut milk before opening and pouring into your pot. The water and coconut content will separate when sitting, so give it a good shake. I like using LITE coconut milk to keep the fat and calorie content lower, but if you want an even more coconutty flavour and richness, opt for the full fat version. Make sure to stir your rice very well after adding the liquids to your Instant Pot. You don't want any grains of rice above the liquids or those pieces won't cook well. For added flavour, sauté ⅓ cup of finely chopped onion before adding the remaining ingredients and pressure cooking. Once cooked, you may also squeeze some fresh lemon or lime juice over your rice and mix well before serving."]]},"6645141":{"s":[[null,"Place water in a small saucepan and bring to a boil."],[null,"Add the rice, stir and cover. Turn down the heat and allow the rice to simmer for about 20 minutes, or until all the liquid is absorbed and the rice is tender."]],"h":[]},"6241876":{"s":[[null,"Add oil to a sauté pan over medium heat. Add half the diced onion and the pinto beans, chili powder, cumin, cayenne pepper, black pepper and water. Sauté, slightly mashing the beans as you sauté until the liquid is absorbed, about 5 minutes."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix together the tomato, jalapeño pepper, remaining diced onion, cilantro and lime juice. Set aside."],[null,"Season the brown rice with the salt."],[null,"In six salad bowls or soup bowls, divide and layer the brown rice, topped with the cooked pinto beans, chicken, tomato mixture, sliced avocado and 1 slice of lime."],[null,"COOKING DRY PINTO BEANS: Add 1 lb (16 oz.) dry pinto beans to a large pot of boiling water (at least 6 cups of water). Boil rapidly for 2 minutes. Remove from heat and cover. Let sit for 1 hour. Drain and rinse beans. Add 6 fresh cups of water. Bring to a boil, then reduce to a simmer for one hour or until the beans are soft but not split. Makes 5 cups cooked beans. These beans can be used in any recipe calling for cooked or canned beans. Store in an airtight container in the refrigerator for 7 days or package in freezer bags in one cup increments for up to 6 months."],[null,"COOKING BROWN RICE: Add 1 lb (16 oz.) of long grain (not instant) brown rice to a large soup pot with 5 cups of water. Bring to a boil then reduce to a simmer. Cover and simmer for 45 minutes or until all liquid is absorbed. Makes 10 cups cooked brown rice. This rice can be used in any recipe calling for cooked brown rice. Store in an airtight container in the refrigerator for 7 days or package in freezer bags in one cup increments for up to 6 months."]],"h":[]},"9195537":{"s":[[null,"Start by cooking your rice and quinoa according to package directions if you don't already have some cooked. I like to cook mine in broth for added flavour or you may use cold water with salt. To cook the grains, use a 2 to 1 ratio of dry grains to liquid. Bring them to a boil, and then reduce the heat and simmer with the lid on until cooked through and the water is absorbed."],[null,"While the grains are cooking, prepare and chop all the veggies. Then, combine all the salad dressing ingredients in a small bowl and mix well."],[null,"Once the grains are cooked, fluff them with a fork and set aside to cool slightly before combining them with the remaining salad ingredients. Then toss everything with the dressing and refrigerate the salad for 1 hour before serving."]],"h":[]},"6229594":{"s":[[null,"Fill a large pot with the water. Add the rice, cover, and bring to a boil over high heat. Reduce heat to medium, and continue to cook until the rice grains break down and the soup thickens, about 1 hour."],[null,"Meanwhile in a small skillet over high heat, add the oil and stir-fry the ginger, scallions, and chilies until fragrant and lightly golden, 30-45 seconds. Add the cilantro and continue to stir-fry until just wilted, about 30 seconds more. Transfer to bowl."],[null,"Ladle some congee into 6 individual bowls, and top each with about 1 Tbsp. of stir-fried herbs. Mix the herbs into the porridge to distribute the flavors. Serve."]],"h":[]},"9508036":{"s":[[null,"Add rice to your high powered blender and process on high speed until a flour consistency is achieved."],[null,"Use to replace wheat flour in your favourite recipes."]],"h":[[null,"Store any leftover flour in an airtight container in your pantry to use as required. Nutritional information is for approx ½ cup of flour."]]},"6220749":{"s":[],"h":[]},"2290":{"s":[[null,"Set cream cheese out for 20 minutes at room temperature to soften."],[null,"Using a hand-held mixer, mix together cream cheese, brown sugar and vanilla until completely blended."],[null,"Enjoy dip with sliced apples."]],"h":[[null,"This dip tastes great with Red Delicious or Granny Smith apples."]]},"2631":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375° F. Cut bell pepper into thin strips. Dice red onion. Chop tomatoes and cilantro. Cut turkey bacon into small pieces."],[null,"To make pico de gallo, combine chopped tomato, onion and cilantro in a small bowl. Squeeze juice from one lime on top and stir."],[null,"To make crema, place sour cream in a bowl and add juice of one lime. Whisk together and refrigerate until ready to serve."],[null,"Spray a baking sheet with cooking spray."],[null,"Place tortilla chips in one layer on baking sheet. Top chips with dried seasonings, bell pepper and shredded cheese."],[null,"Bake in oven for 12 minutes."],[null,"While chips are baking, heat a non-stick pan over high heat. Crack eggs into a bowl, whisk and scramble in pan; set aside."],[null,"Remove chips from the oven and top with scrambled egg, chopped turkey bacon, pico de gallo, drizzle of crema and additional sprinkle of cilantro. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Elyse chooses Garden of Eatin’® unsalted corn chips."],[null,"This nachos recipe is perfect for a breakfast brunch."],[null,"For more heat, substitute Monterey jack pepper cheese for cheddar cheese."]]},"9876454":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375℉/190℃ and grab a large baking sheet."],[null,"While waiting for the oven to heat up, sauté the mushrooms, garlic, and soy sauce until reduced. Set aside."],[null,"Slice the bread and arrange it in a single layer, and bake for 5-8 minutes, until nicely golden."],[null,"While the bread is toasting, combine the sautéed mushrooms with all remaining ingredients (except the bread) in a mixing bowl. Taste for salt and pepper, and adjust if needed."],[null,"Once toasted and golden, scoop the mixture onto your bread slices and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Plan to enjoy your bruschetta ai funghi immediately , as they taste best when freshly made."],[null,"The nutritional information is based on slicing your baguette into 12 slices, and the serving size represents approx. 2 slices of mushroom bruschetta."]]},"6570315":{"s":[[null,"Trim and discard the zucchini ends. Cut each zucchini in half lengthwise."],[null,"Using a spoon, scoop out the middle of the zucchini and leave a thin base at the bottom so the \"boat\" can be stuffed. Place the scooped-out centers into a small bowl; set aside."],[null,"Bring a medium pot of salted water to a boil. Blanch the zucchini boats just until they begin to soften, about 2-3 minutes. Immediately place the zucchini boats in a bowl of iced water. Drain the zucchini and place it on a baking sheet."],[null,"Heat the olive oil in a medium skillet over medium heat. Sprinkle the reserved zucchini mixture with black pepper; add to the pan, and sauté about 6-8 minutes. Stir in the bruschetta; lower the heat and simmer for 3 minutes."],[null,"Spoon the bruschetta mixture evenly into the four zucchini boats. Sprinkle each zucchini boat with 1 Tsp. parmesan cheese."],[null,"Heat the broiler. Broil the stuffed zucchini boats until slightly golden, about 2-3 minutes; watch closely to avoid burning."]],"h":[]},"6497482":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F. Cut tomatoes into quarters and set aside."],[null,"In a skillet, heat olive oil and add garlic. Saute garlic for about 1 minute. Add tomatoes and continue to saute for about 4 minutes. Remove from heat and stir in basil and both cheeses."],[null,"Remove stems from mushrooms and fill with tomato mixture. Bake in oven for 15 minutes."],[null,"Let cool slightly, then drizzle with balsamic vinegar. Serve warm."]],"h":[]},"7161660":{"s":[[null,"Scrub the potatoes and sweet potatoes and remove any blemishes, but don't peel. Cut into large chunks and cover with boiling water. Simmer for 10–12 minutes."],[null,"Add the Brussels sprouts and put the lid back on. Cook for 7–10 minutes until cooked, but still quite firm. Drain off all the liquid."],[null,"Add the pepper and mash roughly to mix everything together, leaving a few chunks of sprout in the mash. Set aside."],[null,"Add the olive oil to another large, non-stick pan over a medium heat, then add the onion. Cook for 3-4 minutes, stirring regularly."],[null,"Now add the potato and sprout mixture to the pan and mix well. Flatten it out so it covers the whole pan. Cook for 5 minutes turning regularly to jumble up the mixture, repeating a couple of times to make sure it forms a crispy crust."],[null,"Place a poached egg on top and serve."]],"h":[[null,"This is perfect for using up leftovers, so if you have cold potatoes or sprouts, just heat them through for a few minutes and start at stage 3."],[null,"Other vegetables such as carrots, swede or parsnips work well, too."],[null,"'At risk' groups such as infants, children, pregnant women, the elderly and those who are unwell should avoid soft/lightly cooked and raw eggs, unless they can guarantee that they are produced under the Lion code quality assurance scheme."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"7619710":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4. Heat the olive oil in a pan, add the onion and cook for 4 minutes until softened, not browned."],[null,"Add the plain flour to coat the onion, mix in a good pinch of white pepper and the wholegrain mustard. Slowly stir in the milk until it thickens."],[null,"Add half the Cheddar and half the Parmesan, stirring for 2–3 minutes until melted. Meanwhile, boil the sprouts in boiling water for 7–8 minutes."],[null,"Drain, place in an ovenproof dish, pour over the sauce, and top with wholemeal breadcrumbs and remaining Cheddar and Parmesan. Bake for 12–15 minutes, until golden brown on top."]],"h":[[null,"For extra flavour, add 2–3 cloves crushed garlic or 1 tbsp freshly chopped herbs, such as coriander or chives."],[null,"Add 150g button mushrooms or a chopped leek to boost the veg count of this dish."],[null,"For a festive feel, add 150g vacuum-packed cooked chestnuts."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Defrost in the fridge or in the microwave then reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6579304":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, whisk together the garlic, mayonnaise, vinegar, honey, Dijon, basil, salt, and pepper."],[null,"Trim and slice the Brussels sprouts into thin strips; add to the bowl with the dressing."],[null,"Roughly chop the artichokes and add to the bowl."],[null,"Medium dice the avocado and add to the bowl."],[null,"Chop or tear the lettuce into bite-size pieces and add to the bowl; toss to combine the salad."],[null,"Serve with a sprinkle of roasted flax seed."]],"h":[]},"6345810":{"s":[[null,"In a large pot, bring 6 cups of water to a boil. Add Brussels sprouts and blanch in the boiling water for 1 minute. Remove from boiling water and run under cold water to stop the cooking. Dry the sprouts with a clean towel."],[null,"Trim the stem on the Brussels sprouts and slice in half lengthwise. Using the slicing blade on a food processor, process the Brussels sprouts to shred them. You can also do this with the slicing side of a box grater or with a very sharp knife."],[null,"In a medium bowl, whisk together scallions, vinegar, mustard, soy sauce, low- or no-calorie sweetener, mayonnaise and black pepper."],[null,"Add the shredded Brussels sprouts and toasted almonds to the dressing and mix well."]],"h":[]},"6444203":{"s":[[null,"Zest the orange and add the zest to a small ramekin. Peel and section the orange, cutting each section in half; set aside. Add the walnuts to a small skillet and toast over medium heat for 3 to 4 minutes, or until lightly browned."],[null,"In a large skillet over medium-high heat, heat 1 Tbsp of the oil. Add the shallots and sauté for 4 to 5 minutes, until slightly browned. Remove the shallots with a slotted spoon; set aside. Add the remaining oil to the pan and then add the sprouts. Sauté the sprouts for 10 to 15 minutes, until browned and cooked through. Add the orange sections, orange zest, and sautéed shallots and cook for 2 minutes."],[null,"Season the sprouts with salt and pepper and place in a large serving bowl. Top with the walnuts and serve."]],"h":[]},"7571497":{"s":[[null,"Cook the potatoes and parsnips in boiling water, for 12-15 minutes or until tender, drain well then return to the pan. Mash with the milk and the spread until smooth, season well."],[null,"Meanwhile, heat the oil in a medium frying pan, add the onion, carrot and cabbage and fry for 5 minutes."],[null,"Tip into the mash, form into 3 patties then fry for 4-5 minutes turning halfway through cooking."],[null,"Poach the eggs and serve on the bubble and squeak."]],"h":[[null,"For a diary-free version, use rapeseed oil rather than spread and soya in place of milk."],[null,"Brussels sprouts are great instead of cabbage."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Defrost in the fridge or in the microwave then reheat until piping hot throughout."],[null,"'At risk' groups such as infants, children, pregnant women, the elderly and those who are unwell should avoid soft/lightly cooked and raw eggs, unless they can guarantee that they are produced under the Lion code quality assurance scheme."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"9315360":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350°F/176°C and line a loaf pan with parchment paper."],[null,"Mash your banana and add 1 full cup worth to a medium bowl, followed by the milk and applesauce. Mix well. Then add all the dry ingredients to the same bowl and mix until combined."],[null,"Pour the batter into your lined loaf pan and top with sliced bananas, walnuts, and a sprinkle of coconut sugar. Make sure to gently press the toppings into the top of your bread."],[null,"Bake until a toothpick inserted in the middle comes out mostly clean and dry, approx. 40-50 minutes, depending on your oven."]],"h":[[null,"Weigh the flour using a kitchen scale for the most accurate results . Scooping flour from a bag often results in too much flour being used and can make this bread dry and dense."],[null,"Use overly ripe bananas. The more brown spots, the better, as the sweeter they will be. Since the recipe uses very little sweetener, you want to make sure your bananas will provide ample sweetness."],[null,"Measure your mashed bananas. Bananas really vary in size. So make sure you're using enough for optimal sweetness and moisture. Measure to ensure you're using a full cup of mashed banana."],[null,"Use fresh + active baking powder ! Baking powder that has been open in the pantry for 6+ months may start to lose its effectiveness."],[null,"Use parchment paper to line your loaf pan. Although a nonstick loaf pan should do the trick, I find this much easier to remove from the pan when using parchment paper. You can easily lift the bread out and place it on a wire rack without the worry of breaking it."],[null,"Individual ovens will vary. So make sure to test the doneness of your buckwheat banana bread using a toothpick inserted in the middle. When it comes out mostly dry, the bread is ready."],[null,"Let it cool. Give yourself extra time to let your loaf cool down. A minimum of 20-30 mins on a cooling rack is recommended to completely set and make slicing much easier."],[null,"Leftovers keep at room temperature for 2-3 days, refrigerated for 4-5 days, or freeze airtight for up to 3 months."]]},"9396324":{"s":[[null,"Mash your banana in a medium mixing bowl, and then add the milk and vanilla. Mix well. Then add all the dry ingredients and stir until mixed, but don't worry if there are still a few lumps."],[null,"Let your pancake batter rest for 2-3 minutes while you preheat your griddle or non-stick pan over medium heat."],[null,"Ladle the batter to make pancakes that are approx. 3-4 inches in diameter and cook until there are bubbles on top and the edges appear golden brown. Then flip and continue cooking for another 2-3 minutes."],[null,"Serve with sliced bananas, berries, maple syrup, and/or shredded coconut."]],"h":[[null,"Use fresh, active baking powder . Baking powder that has been opened and sitting in the pantry for several months can start to lose its effectiveness."],[null,"No need to overmix your pancake batter . If there are a few lumps, that's perfectly fine. Just mix until combined and no floury bits remain."],[null,"Preheat your pan or griddle. It should be hot before pouring your pancake batter to prevent sticking and for even cooking."],[null,"Use medium heat to cook your pancakes . Although your pan should be hot, that doesn't mean you should use high heat. This may result in uneven cooking, with crisp outsides and mushy middles."],[null,"Flip your pancakes ONCE . When the edges are golden brown and there are several bubbles on top. Flipping too often can cause them to deflate and result in a denser pancake texture."],[null,"Leftovers keep in the fridge for 2-3 days, reheat in the toaster, on a griddle, or in a pan on the stovetop. Or freeze in airtight containers or ziptop bags once completely cooled to room temperature."]]},"9610207":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350℉/176℃ and line a loaf pan with parchment paper."],[null,"Add the flour, baking powder, salt, and onion powder (if using) to a large mixing bowl. Stir to combine. Then add the tahini, applesauce, and water and mix until combined and you have a thick batter."],[null,"Transfer the mixture to your loaf pan and evenly spread and smooth the top using a silicone spatula."],[null,"OPTIONAL: Sprinkle with seeds of your choice and gently press them down into the loaf."],[null,"Bake for approx. 45-50 minutes, or until a toothpick inserted into the middle of the loaf comes out clean and dry."],[null,"Remove from the oven and let cool to room temperature before slicing."]],"h":[[null,"Weigh your flour for the best results . Flour volume will vary depending on measuring methods, such as the scoop and sweep, vs spooning your flour into the measuring cup. Use a kitchen scale for the most accurate flour measurement."],[null,"Use fresh + active baking powder ! Baking powder that has been open in the pantry for 6+ months may start to lose its effectiveness."],[null,"Use parchment paper to line your loaf pan . This not only avoids extra fat from greasing the pan but also makes it simpler to remove the buckwheat bread from the pan once baked."],[null,"Cooking time will vary according to your loaf pan size , so always check \"doneness\" by inserting a toothpick in the center to see if it comes out clean. Mine is perfect at 45 minutes."],[null,"Let it cool. Give yourself extra time to let your loaf cool down. A minimum of 60 minutes on a cooling"]]},"9271997":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 450 degrees F (232 degrees C) and line a 9 inch round pizza tray with parchment paper. Set aside."],[null,"Add the flour, salt and water to a large bowl and mix with your hands until combined. Then tip out the dough to a clean surface that has been lightly floured."],[null,"Knead the dough, using your hands until you have a somewhat smooth ball. At this point, adjust the water or flour if needed. If the dough is too sticky, sprinkle a little extra flour and knead it in. If the dough is too dry and not holding together, add a teaspoon of water at a time until you have a playdough consistency."],[null,"Now place the ball of dough on the sheet of parchment paper you set aside earlier on a flat surface, like a kitchen countertop. Use a floured rolling pin to stretch the dough to the edges of the parchment paper. Then slide the parchment back onto your pizza pan."],[null,"Bake the buckwheat pizza crust for 5-6 minutes and remove it from the oven. Then remove the parchment paper (for a crispier crust), top your pizza as desired, and bake an additional 2-4 minutes. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Weigh your flour for the most accurate results . Scooping flour from a bag will often result in extra flour being used. Adjust the water and/or flour, as needed. The dough shouldn’t be too sticky, nor too dry. You want a playdough consistency that is only slightly sticky. Roll the dough on the parchment paper to make it easy to transfer to your pizza pan, without breaking the crust. Remove the parchment paper after the first bake for a crispier crust."]]},"6358049":{"s":[[null,"Prepare an indoor or outdoor grill."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine ground turkey, scallions, garlic, oyster sauce, chili garlic paste, sesame oil, grated ginger, lime juice, salt (optional), and pepper. Form into 6 patties and refrigerate until ready to grill, at least 15 minutes."],[null,"Grill burgers for 5-7 minutes on each side or until the internal temperature of the burger is 165 degrees F."],[null,"To assemble the burgers, combine the yogurt and Siracha in a small bowl. Layer each burger between two leaves of lettuce with a scant 1 Tbsp. yogurt mixture and 3 cucumber slices."]],"h":[]},"6446820":{"s":[[null,"Heat oil in a large Dutch oven over medium-high heat."],[null,"Add chicken thighs and sauté for 3 minutes per side. Remove from pan and set aside."],[null,"Add margarine to pan and melt. Add onion and sauté for 2 minutes. Add mushrooms and sauté for 3-5 minutes until liquid is released; stirring frequently."],[null,"Add balsamic vinegar to pan and cook with mushrooms for 1 minute. Add chicken thighs back to pan and place mushrooms on top of chicken. Pour chicken broth into pan."],[null,"Bring the chicken broth to a boil. Reduce the heat to medium-low, cover the pan with a heavy, tight-fitting lid, and simmer for 25 minutes."]],"h":[]},"6087185":{"s":[[null,"Spray a large soup pot with cooking spray. Add chicken and sauté over medium heat for 7 minutes or until done. Remove from pan."],[null,"Add onions and green peppers and sauté over medium-high heat for 3 minutes or onions until clear. Add garlic and sauté 30 more seconds."],[null,"Add remaining ingredients along with cooked chicken and bring to a boil. Reduce heat and simmer for 15 minutes"]],"h":[]},"6024065":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 475 degrees F. Coat a baking sheet with cooking spray and set aside."],[null,"Slice the chicken breast in half lengthwise and then pound to 1/4-inch thickness. Season each chicken breast with salt and ground black pepper."],[null,"Set up three wide bowls or flat-bottom containers. Fill the first bowl with the whole wheat flour, the second bowl with the egg and 1 tsp lemon juice, and the third bowl with the breadcrumbs and Italian seasoning. Whisk the egg and lemon juice together. Combine the breadcrumbs and Italian seasoning and mix well."],[null,"Dredge one chicken breast in the flour and shake off the excess. Then dip the chicken breast in the egg, and then coat in the breadcrumb mixture. Place on the baking sheet. Repeat this process for the remaining three chicken breasts."],[null,"Spray the top of each chicken breast with cooking spray and bake for 8 minutes. Turn the chicken breasts over and bake for 5 more minutes. Ensure that the chicken is cooked to an internal temperature of 165 degrees F."],[null,"While the chicken is baking, heat the oil and a generous amount of cooking spray over medium heat in a small nonstick skillet. Add the capers and sauté for 2-3 minutes."],[null,"Add about 1 tbsp lemon juice and cook until the lemon juice is completely reduced. Add the chicken broth and simmer until reduced by half. Stir in the parsley."],[null,"Remove the chicken from the oven and serve with 1 Tbsp. of sauce drizzled over the chicken."]],"h":[]},"6097149":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375 degrees F. Coat a baking dish with cooking spray."],[null,"Remove the skin from the chicken and arrange in a single layer in the baking pan."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the cilantro, lime zest, lime juice, honey, garlic, ground black pepper and salt. Pour the mixture evenly over the chicken and bake for 45-50 minutes or until the internal temperature of the largest piece of chicken is 165 degrees."]],"h":[]},"6389870":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350 degrees F. Coat one large or two small baking sheet(s) with cooking spray."],[null,"Lay cut corn tortillas in one layer on the baking sheet(s). Spray the top with cooking spray. Lightly sprinkle with salt (optional)."],[null,"Bake for 20 minutes, stirring every 5 minutes or until the chips are slightly golden brown and crispy. Remove from oven and pour into a baking dish coated with cooking spray. Set aside."],[null,"Mix fat-free refried beans with chicken broth and pour over the baked tortilla chips."],[null,"Top the beans with the shredded chicken and then with the reduced fat cheese."],[null,"Place on the top rack of the oven and bake for 10-15 minutes or until cheese is melted and starting to turn golden brown."],[null,"Remove from the oven and divide the nachos among eight plates. Top each plate with diced tomatoes, salsa, 1/4 avocado, lettuce and yogurt."]],"h":[]},"6523847":{"s":[[null,"Prepare an indoor or outdoor grill."],[null,"In a large bowl, toss together lettuce, onion, cucumber, feta cheese, olive oil, red wine vinegar, and oregano."],[null,"Fill each pita pocket half with 1/4 of lettuce mixture. Set aside."],[null,"Season shrimp with salt (optional), ground black pepper and cayenne pepper. Spray shrimp with cooking spray."],[null,"Grill shrimp for 3-4 minutes on each side. Remove from grill and add 3 shrimp to each pita."]],"h":[]},"6387004":{"s":[[null,"Spray a large soup pot with cooking spray. Add celery, onion and carrots and sauté over medium-high heat for 3 minutes or onions until clear. Remove from pan and set aside."],[null,"Add turkey sausage and cook until brown, about 6-7 minutes. Add celery, onions and carrots back to pan and mix."],[null,"Add remaining ingredients and bring to a boil. Reduce heat and simmer for 30 minutes."]],"h":[]},"6551436":{"s":[[null,"Pre heat oven to 375 degrees F. Coat a loaf pan with cooking spray. Set aside."],[null,"In a medium bowl, break up the piece of whole wheat bread into pea-sized pieces. Add egg and mix well."],[null,"Add turkey, garlic, oregano, basil, 1/4 cup ketchup, salt (optional) and ground black pepper. Mix well."],[null,"Press the turkey mixture into the loaf pan tightly. Put in oven to bake for 20 minutes."],[null,"While meatloaf is baking, whisk together remaining 1/4 cup of ketchup, balsamic vinegar and hot sauce (optional)."],[null,"After the meatloaf has baked for 20 minutes, pour the ketchup and balsamic glaze over the meatloaf. Return to the oven to bake for an additional 15 minutes or until the internal temperature of the meatloaf is 165 degrees F."],[null,"Let the meatloaf rest for 10 minutes, then slice into 6 equal portions."]],"h":[]},"6218825":{"s":[[null,"Add olive oil to a large sauté pan over medium heat."],[null,"Add diced sausage and onion and sauté until onions begin to turn golden brown."],[null,"Add the kale and chicken broth and sauté until kale softens."],[null,"Add remaining ingredients and sauté 3-4 more minutes to heat the beans through."],[null,"Serving Suggestion: Serve with a side of brown rice to round out the meal."]],"h":[]},"6618132":{"s":[[null,"Add olive oil to a soup pot over medium heat. Add onion, bell pepper, celery, garlic, basil and oregano. Sauté until onions begin to turn clear."],[null,"Add crushed tomato and vegetable broth. Bring to a boil, then reduce to a simmer for 10 minutes or until vegetables are soft."],[null,"Gently stir in cod and shrimp and cook for 5 minutes or until seafood is cooked through."]],"h":[]},"6846465":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400 degrees F. Spray a baking sheet with cooking spray."],[null,"Place zucchini, carrots, onions, and red pepper on baking sheet. Add olive oil and garlic; toss to coat. Bake for 15-18 minutes. Remove from oven."],[null,"While vegetables are baking, heat a medium sauté pan over medium heat. Spray with cooking spray. Add tomato and sauté for 1 minute. Add beans, chili powder, cumin and pepper and sauté for 2 minutes. Add cooked vegetables to pan and mix well."],[null,"Serve 1/2 cup veggie mixture in each taco and top with lettuce and cheese."]],"h":[]},"6112688":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 475 degrees F. Coat a baking sheet with cooking spray and set aside."],[null,"Place the onion, garlic, bell pepper, and Thai curry paste in a large food processor and blend until smooth."],[null,"Add the salmon and puree until smooth. Add the egg and cilantro and puree until incorporated."],[null,"Scoop the mixture in 1/2 cup portions onto the baking sheet and press lightly to form a patty. Repeat to make 6 patties."],[null,"Spray the top of each patty with cooking spray and bake for 15 minutes."],[null,"Serve each salmon burger in a lettuce leaf and top each with 1 Tbsp. sliced scallions."]],"h":[]},"6456614":{"s":[[null,"Place chicken in a slow cooker. Top chicken with onions and sweet potatoes."],[null,"Add the chicken broth, brown sugar blend, thyme, mustard, and bay leaf. Cook on low for 5-6 hours or until chicken is done."],[null,"Remove bay leaf and serve with broccoli and cauliflower."]],"h":[]},"6129053":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350 degrees F."],[null,"Add lentils, water, ginger, garlic and turmeric to a medium sauce pan. Bring to a boil and reduce to a simmer, partially covered for 20 minutes. Set aside to cool."],[null,"While lentils are cooking, mix ground chicken, cilantro, salt, ground black pepper and cayenne pepper in a medium bowl and set aside."],[null,"Cut the tops off of the peppers and cut out seed pod (save the tops). Clean out the ribs and any seeds from the inside of the peppers and line the peppers cut side up in a baking dish. Set the tops off to the side. (Note: If the peppers won’t sit upright, trim just a little bit off the bottom of the peppers to even it out so it will sit up straight. Try not to cut a hole in the bottom so the mixture inside does not fall out)."],[null,"Once the lentils have cooled, stir them in to the chicken mixture and mix well to incorporate."],[null,"Fill each pepper with the chicken and lentil mixture but do not pack the mixture in tightly. Just gently fill to the top."],[null,"Place each pepper top back on to the peppers filled with the chicken and lentil mixture, then pour the chicken broth into the bottom of the pan."],[null,"Bake for 1 hour or until the internal temperature of the chicken mixture is 165 degrees."]],"h":[]},"6917127":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F."],[null,"Add olive oil to an oven safe, non-stick, sauté pan over medium high heat."],[null,"Add mushrooms and sauté until all of the liquid from the mushrooms is evaporated."],[null,"Add bell pepper, onion and spinach and sauté until vegetables are softened and liquid is evaporated."],[null,"Whisk eggs, egg whites, milk, salt (optional), pepper, cayenne pepper and basil in a medium bowl. Pour over vegetables and stir until eggs start to set."],[null,"Smooth the top of the frittata with a spatula, and put in oven to bake for 20 minutes or until eggs are set."],[null,"Slide the frittata out of the pan onto a plate and slice into 8 pie slices."]],"h":[]},"6593896":{"s":[[null,"Cook pasta according to package directions, omitting salt. Drain pasta and rinse under cold water."],[null,"In a medium bowl combine remaining ingredients. Add pasta and toss to coat. Serve."]],"h":[]},"6915533":{"s":[[null,"Add oil to a large soup pot over medium-high heat."],[null,"Add fennel, onion and celery to oil and sauté until onions turn clear (around 4-5 minutes). Add butternut squash, sage, chicken broth, water, 1 tsp salt (optional), 1/2 tsp black pepper and bay leaves. Bring to a boil and reduce to a simmer."],[null,"Simmer stew for 20 minutes, then add kale and simmer 10 more minutes."],[null,"While stew is simmering, whisk together all dumpling ingredients to form a stiff batter. Set aside."],[null,"After kale simmers for 10 minutes remove bay leaf."],[null,"Use a 1/4 cup measure to scoop dumplings on top of stew to make 8 dumplings. Do not stir once dumplings have been added to the top of the stew. Cover and reduce to a low simmer for 10 minutes until dumplings are cooked through and puffed."]],"h":[]},"6470032":{"s":[[null,"Coat a large non-stick sauté pan with cooking spray. Set aside."],[null,"Combine cannellini beans, onion, garlic, mushrooms, carrots, Worcestershire sauce, soy sauce, oatmeal, Montreal steak seasoning and salt (optional) in a food processor. Pulse several times until mixture is combined but not a paste."],[null,"Divide burger mixture into 6 equal portions, form into patties."],[null,"Heat prepared sauté pan over medium high heat. Sauté burgers on each side 6-8 minutes. Set aside."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine shredded mango, coleslaw mix, rice wine vinegar and olive oil. Toss to coat."],[null,"Add a burger to a lettuce leaf, top with 3/4 cup coleslaw mixture."]],"h":[]},"3829":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 425 F. Line large baking sheet with parchment paper (not foil)."],[null,"Cut cauliflower into large florets, about 2 to 3 inches in size. Place cut cauliflower in large bowl, and add the olive oil, garlic powder, onion powder, pepper, and cornstarch. Toss until evenly coated."],[null,"Arrange evenly on baking sheet. Place cauliflower in the oven, and roast for 20 minutes. Remove, toss, and roast an additional 10 minutes until golden in color and fork tender."],[null,"In oven safe pan, melt butter. Once melted, add hot sauce, and stir together. Add cauliflower to pan with sauce mixture and combine."],[null,"Once combined, place pan in oven and bake an additional 10 minutes until cauliflower has dispersed blistered spots."],[null,"Remove from oven, and garnish with fresh parsley. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"If buying already cut florets, look for a bag that yields close to 6 cups of florets."],[null,"If you don’t have an oven proof pan, add melted butter and hot sauce to a bowl, and add the cooked cauliflower to combine. Then place back in the oven on the same sheet pan used to roast the cauliflower."],[null,"Cauliflower is a medium potassium vegetable, other potassium comes from other ingredients, but with new research, we are discovering our bodies don’t absorb all the potassium from a whole food like cauliflower."],[null,"This recipe was tested with Frank’s® Hot Sauce. Look for a variety with the lowest amount of sodium."]]},"3023":{"s":[[null,"Set the cream cheese out to soften."],[null,"Drain the red peppers and measure 1/2 cup. Puree in a blender or food processor to make red pepper sauce."],[null,"In a medium bowl mix cream cheese and sour cream together until smooth. Add pureed peppers and 2 teaspoons of Tabasco sauce. Stir until combined."],[null,"Add the chicken and gently mix. Add additional hot sauce 1/2 teaspoon at a time; taste and continue to add hot sauce to the heat level you desire."],[null,"Place mixture in a slow cooker for 2 to 3 hours on low heat, or bake in the oven at 350° F for 30 minutes."],[null,"Serve warm dip with carrots, celery, cucumber, cauliflower for dipping, or make mini roll-ups by wrapping dip inside lettuce or cabbage leaves."]],"h":[[null,"Look for bottled or canned roasted red peppers with 85 mg or less sodium per ounce, or roast fresh red peppers to puree. Trader Joe’s fire roasted red peppers contain only 60 mg sodium per ounce."],[null,"May also use frozen roasted red peppers if available."],[null,"Hot sauce brands and varieties vary greatly in sodium content. Stick to the original Tabasco® hot pepper sauce because it’s much lower in sodium. Increase to 6 teaspoons if you like more heat."],[null,"Serve with raw vegetables. Lower potassium choices include carrots, celery, cucumber, cauliflower for dipping, or lettuce or cabbage leaves for wraps."],[null,"If serving at a party bake then place in a small slow cooker to keep warm."]]},"6118227":{"s":[[null,"Puree drained red peppers in a blender or food processor to make red pepper sauce."],[null,"In a medium bowl mix cream cheese and sour cream together until smooth. Add pureed peppers and 2 teaspoons of Tabasco sauce. Stir until combined. Add the chicken and gently mix. Taste and add additional hot sauce if desired."],[null,"Place mixture in a slow cooker for 2 to 3 hours on low heat, or bake in the oven at 350° F for 30 minutes."],[null,"Serve warm dip with carrots, celery, cucumber, cauliflower for dipping, or make mini roll-ups by wrapping dip inside lettuce or cabbage leaves."]],"h":[]},"4812123":{"s":[[null,"Combine all ingredients except the chicken and cucumbers in a medium-size bowl. Stir in chicken and mix until well coated. Set aside in refrigerator for about 30 minutes. Remove from refrigerator and spoon equal amounts (about 1-2 teaspoons) into each cucumber slice. Garnish with chopped parsley."]],"h":[]},"6933135":{"s":[[null,"Fill a small saucepan with 1 inch of water and bring to a simmer. Place tempeh in a steamer basket, cover, and steam for 5 minutes to soften and remove bitterness. Pat dry and transfer to a bowl."],[null,"Toss the tempeh with soy sauce, 1 Tbsp apple cider vinegar, ½ tsp garlic powder, smoked paprika, and black pepper. Let sit for 5 minutes to absorb flavors."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 400°F and line a baking sheet with parchment paper. Sprinkle cornstarch over the tempeh and toss to coat lightly. Arrange tempeh in a single layer and bake for 20 minutes, flipping halfway, until golden and crisp."],[null,"In a small saucepan over low heat, combine hot sauce, 1 Tbsp vinegar, maple syrup, Dijon mustard, and ½ tsp garlic powder. Stir until warm and well blended."],[null,"Remove tempeh from the oven and toss with the warm sauce until coated. Serve with ranch for dipping and celery and carrot sticks."]],"h":[]},"3774":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400° F."],[null,"Melt the butter in a saucepan."],[null,"Add the hot sauce, red pepper sauce, tomato sauce, olive oil, garlic powder and Italian seasonings and stir to combine. Remove the pan from the heat."],[null,"Place the chicken wings in a baking dish."],[null,"Pour the sauce over the wings and bake for 30 to 35 minutes. Check for doneness."],[null,"Serve the wings hot or place in a covered warming dish or crock pot, until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Buy fresh wing drummettes. A 1-1/4 pound package contains 12 drummettes. If unavailable, ask your butcher to cut whole chicken wings into drummette size."],[null,"Boneless chicken pieces may be used in this recipe. Check for doneness after 20 minutes."],[null,"Hot sauce brands vary greatly in sodium. Choose a brand with less than 140 mg sodium per teaspoon."],[null,"Make the Roasted Red Pepper Tomato Sauce (under Sauces & Seasonings in the DaVita.com recipe collection) and use 1/2 cup plus the Tabasco sauce if desired."]]},"6010103":{"s":[[null,"Wrap the beef in plastic wrap and freeze until firm (but not rock hard). Once firm, slice the beef thinly into long strips. Place in a baking dish."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the scallions, garlic, rice wine vinegar, water, soy sauce, sweetener (honey or sugar substitute), and pepper. Pour the mixture over the beef and let it marinate in the refrigerator for at least 30 minutes, up to 2 hours. While the beef is marinating, preheat an indoor or outdoor grill."],[null,"Remove the beef from the marinade and shake off any excess marinade. Grill beef for 2-3 minutes on each side or until it is cooked to a medium-well doneness."],[null,"Steam the vegetables and serve the beef over the steamed vegetables."]],"h":[]},"4800276":{"s":[[null,"Cook the bulgur according to the package directions and let cool slightly."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together all curry sauce ingredients until well combined."],[null,"Prepare four bowls and divide the bulgur evenly among them."],[null,"Divide chickpeas, snow peas, radishes, mango, mozzarella, and dried cranberries evenly among the four bowls."],[null,"Drizzle with the curry sauce, then sprinkle with mint (or cilantro) and crushed peanuts before serving."]],"h":[["Bulgur — a hidden gem of the grain world","Bulgur is a whole grain that doesn’t get a lot of attention, but it is a very healthy option. It is a nutritional powerhouse, packed with fiber, vitamins, and minerals. It is also a higher-protein grain and a good way to get more plant-based protein in your diet. One cup of cooked bulgur contains 6 grams of protein. Bulgur is also a very good source of fiber, with 8 grams per cup. This is much higher than other grains such as rice or couscous and helps you move toward your recommended daily fiber intake. Most of the fiber in bulgur is insoluble fiber, which promotes regular bowel movements and supports gut health. Eating enough fiber also helps protect against heart disease and cancer and can help control blood glucose if you have diabetes. Bulgur is a quick-cooking whole grain made from cracked wheat. It is available in fine, medium, coarse, and extra-coarse varieties. The finer grinds work well in salads such as tabbouleh, and the coarser grinds are perfect for grain bowls, soups, pilafs, and stuffing. Bulgur is sold in most major grocery stores and is typically found in the natural foods aisle."]]},"6373845":{"s":[[null,"Bring water and bulgur to a boil in a medium saucepan over high heat. Reduce heat, cover, and simmer 12 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, combine the remaining ingredients, except the cucumber, in a medium bowl."],[null,"Drain bulgur in a fine-mesh sieve and run under cold water to cool quickly. Shake off excess liquid and stir into the tomato mixture."]],"h":[]},"54951":{"s":[[null,"Combine all dressing ingredients into a food processor or blender, and blend until well combined (should yield 1 1/4 cups)."],[null,"Season chicken thighs with 1/4 cup of dressing, brush on both sides."],[null,"Grill seasoned chicken on grill, or inside on grill pan until cooked through. Cut into slices. Slice peppers, onion, and zucchini into thin strips."],[null,"Place 1-1/2 tablespoons oil into medium sauté pan, heat over medium heat, add onions, peppers, and zucchini slices."],[null,"Sauté vegetables for 3 minutes on medium heat, add in onion and garlic powder, and stir until vegetables are equally seasoned. Cook vegetables until tender."],[null,"Cook white rice according to package directions to yield one cup. Slice lettuce into thin strips."],[null,"Prepare bowls by adding 1 cup lettuce, 1/2 cup sliced chicken, 1/4 cup white rice, 1/4 cup sautéed vegetables and top with 3 tablespoons dressing to each bowl. Optional, may top each bowl with 2 tortilla chips if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Cooking spray can be used in place of olive oil to cook the vegetables. A sugar substitute can be used in place of the honey for diabetes friendly dressing."],[null,"The potassium in this dish is higher but comes from natural sources like vegetables. Our bodies only absorb about 40-60%. Vegetables also provide other nutrients and fiber. This is also a one-dish meal."],[null,"If desired; you could add 1/4 cup low sodium canned black beans (rinsed and drained).This would roughly add about 80 mg sodium, 180 mg potassium and 64 mg phosphorus. Keeping in mind with naturally occurring potassium/phosphorus like found in beans, our bodies only absorb about 40-60% of those nutrients."]]},"5913532":{"s":[[null,"Heat water in a pan. When it’s boiling, add rice and cook for 10 minutes and set aside"],[null,"Add the tofu, cornflour, and ground coriander to a bowl. Stir until the tofu is well coated with cornflour."],[null,"Heat a small amount of oil in a frying pan and add the coated tofu. Cook until golden brown all over and set aside."],[null,"Heat oil in a frying pan and add garlic, harissa, black beans, and ½ the lime juice. Allow to fry until hot and then set aside."],[null,"For the pico de gallo add red pepper, onion and coriander to a small bowl. Stir well and set aside."],[null,"In a blender, add the peas, lime juice, and olive oil and blend until combined but still retaining some texture"],[null,"Serve rice into a bowl and top with the tofu, black beans, pico de gallo, pea guacamole and coconut yoghurt. Sprinkle with coriander and serve!"]],"h":[["Renastep note","Always check with your dietitian or doctor that this recipe is suitable for you."],["Renastep note","Renastep is a food for special medical purposes for the dietary management of kidney disease. Suitable from 3 years of age. Must be used under medical supervision. Renastep contains Milk (milk protein) and Fish (Tuna oil). This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutritics dietary analysis software. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information."]]},"9706219":{"s":[[null,"Start by spiralizing your zucchini into noodles if you're not using packaged zoodles from the store. Place the zoodles into a large colander inside a large bowl or your kitchen sink and generously sprinkle them with salt. This will wilt the zucchini and improve their flavour. Set it aside for 10-15 minutes while you prepare the remaining ingredients."],[null,"Then, prepare any toppings and/or sauces you'd like to use."],[null,"Next, heat your beans with the lime juice and spices for a few minutes to absorb the flavours and turn off the heat."],[null,"You may optionally heat the zoodles, however, it's unnecessary to cook them."],[null,"Serve your burrito zoodles in shallow bowls and top them with the heated beans and remaining toppings. Enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Prepare the toppings and spiralize your zucchini BEFORE heating the beans."],[null,"For ease of spiralizing , use zucchini that are narrow, long, and straight. Or you may purchase pre-spiralized package zoodles from your grocery store to save time."],[null,"Do NOT overcook the zoodles. You may serve them raw and cold, or just slightly heated through. Heating them for too long with make them watery and overly soft."]]},"7552718":{"s":[[null,"Add the oil to a pan, then add the onion and cook for 5 minutes, stirring regularly until browned."],[null,"Add the mince and cook for another 5 minutes, stirring regularly and breaking up any clumps."],[null,"Now add the red and green peppers, cumin, oregano and chilli powder, and the tomatoes. Mix well, bring to a boil, then turn the heat right down and simmer gently for 7-8 minutes."],[null,"Add the beans, mix well and bring back to a simmering boil."],[null,"Meanwhile, heat the tortillas in a dry frying pan, makings ure each side gets 30 seconds contact with the hot pan."],[null,"Lay out the tortillas, add a handful of salad to each, then a spoonful of the turkey mixture. Add a little of the cheese and then fold into a tight, neat parcel, wrap in foil and serve."]],"h":[[null,"You can add more chilli powder if you like your burritos hot."],[null,"Substitute the turkey mince for chicken or lamb."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"1002644":{"s":[[null,"Wash lettuce very well and dry. Tear by hand into small pieces."],[null,"Cut onion, bell pepper (washed and seeded) and peeled tomato into thin strips (julienne)."],[null,"Put a little clean vegetable oil in a skillet and sauté these vegetables with a little salt and pepper."],[null,"Cut chicken breasts into small pieces."],[null,"Once the vegetables are cooked, add the chicken pieces."],[null,"Stir over low heat for 3 or 4 minutes."],[null,"Place a layer of lettuce and the sautéed chicken and vegetables on the corn tortillas."],[null,"Add cream cheese (as a sauce)."],[null,"Roll up the tortilla."]],"h":[[null,"To reduce the fat, you can use low-fat cream cheese."],[null,"To reduce the sodium, you can season the vegetables and chicken with natural seasonings such as garlic, oregano and bay leaf in place of salt."]]},"7882491":{"s":[[null,"Mash half the beans thoroughly with a fork until quite smooth. Slightly crush the other half, then combine together."],[null,"Mix in the spring onions, cucumber, yogurt, garlic, olive oil, lemon, mint and pepper, then set aside."],[null,"Meanwhile, prepare the vegetable sticks for dipping."],[null,"Mix the pâté again, sprinkle with paprika and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Works well with cannellini or haricot beans. For a vegan version use a non-dairy yoghurt alternative."],[null,"Spice it up with a teaspoon of curry paste. You could use any vegetables for dipping - choose a variety of colours to keep things exciting."],[null,"Freezing instructions: dip suitable for freezing. Defrost in the fridge and use immediately."],[null,"The nutritional figures above include the serving suggestion of crudites."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"7430012":{"s":[[null,"Heat oven to 180°C/gas 4. Twist and remove the stalks from the mushrooms, chop and reserve. Place the mushrooms upright onto a small baking tray and bake 10-15 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, add oil to a pan, add the mushroom stalks, garlic and spring onions and cook for 3 minutes."],[null,"Transfer the mixture to a bowl with the beans, parsley, mustard, thyme and pepper and mix well."],[null,"Spoon into the mushroom caps, pressing down into the mushrooms and shaping with your hands to create a mound. Sprinkle with cheese and bake for 15 mins until slightly softened and until the tops turn golden. Serve warm (allowing to cool a little before serving) or at room temperature."]],"h":[[null,"You could add other herbs to the mixture. Any beans would work, try cannellini or a mixed can of beans."],[null,"You could stuff the mushrooms up to 1 day in advance, then keep in the refrigerator until ready to bake."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"2187":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Melt 1/2 cup butter; combine with graham cracker crumbs and granulated sugar. Reserve 1/4 cup crust mixture for later use."],[null,"Press remaining mixture into an ungreased 9” x 13” pan."],[null,"Bake for 15 minutes; place pan in refrigerator to chill."],[null,"Whip together remaining 1 cup softened butter, powdered sugar, salt, vanilla and creamer until fluffy."],[null,"Spread filling mixture over chilled crust. Chill about 15 minutes."],[null,"Drain pineapple; slice strawberries. Spread pineapple and strawberries over filling. Chill for 30 minutes."],[null,"Before serving spread whipped topping over fruit. Sprinkle with reserved 1/4-cup graham cracker crust mixture."]],"h":[[null,"One stick of butter equals 1/2 cup."],[null,"One pint basket fresh strawberries yields 2 cups of sliced berries."]]},"2209":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375° F. Set butter out to soften."],[null,"In a large mixing bowl, mix together buttermilk, eggs, softened butter, lemon juice, almond extract, vanilla extract, sugar and flour."],[null,"Pour mixture into a deep-dish pie crust."],[null,"Bake for one hour."],[null,"Let cool and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Buttermilk is high in phosphorus and potassium but the portion per serving is small enough to keep this recipe kidney friendly."]]},"7011229":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a pan and add the onions, squash and green pepper. Stir regularly for 5 minutes until starting to brown."],[null,"Add the stock, tomatoes, red lentils, oregano, chilli and garlic. Bring to the boil, reduce the heat, add a lid and simmer for 10 minutes."],[null,"Add the beans and heat for a further 10 minutes, check the squash is cooked through (until tender). Serve with a good grind of black pepper and a sprinkle of parsley."]],"h":[[null,"Ideal with pumpkin instead of the butternut squash."],[null,"Any beans work well, you could use two different types or cans of mixed beans."],[null,"Try stuffing into halved peppers, top with a sprinkle of cheese and bake in the oven 180°/gas 4 for 15 minutes until the pepper is soft and the cheese browned."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Then defrost in the fridge and reheat in the mircowave or on a hob until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 5"]]},"5694153":{"s":[[null,"Peel the butternut squash, scoop out the middle and chop into small pieces."],[null,"Chop the broccoli into small pieces."],[null,"Boil the butternut squash for approximately 8-10 minutes."],[null,"Add the broccoli to cook for a further 5 minutes."],[null,"Drain water and allow vegetables to cool."],[null,"Add 100ml breast milk, standard infant formula or a specialised low potassium, low phosphate feed (as advised by your dietitian)."],[null,"Use a blender to whizz up to a purée consistency."],[null,"Add more breast milk, standard infant formula or the specialised low potassium, low phosphate feed if a thinner consistency required."],[null,"Add into ice cube trays and freeze or use straight away."]],"h":[]},"3465396":{"s":[[null,"Peel, deseed and dice the butternut squash. Heat the oil in a large frying pan and cook the butternut squash for 2-3 minutes until lightly browned. Dice the onion and add to the pan, along with the curry paste and fry for another 3-4 minutes."],[null,"Pour over the stock, then cover and simmer for 15-20 minutes, or until the squash is tender. Drain and rinse the chickpeas then add with the tomatoes to the curry. Gently cook for 3-4 minutes, until the tomatoes slightly soften."],[null,"Bring saucepan of water to the boil. Rinse the rice and add to the boiling water. Cover and reduce the heat to a simmer for 20 minutes or until cooked."],[null,"Take the curry off the heat and stir through the yogurt and chopped coriander. Serve with the cooked rice and a wholemeal chapatti if you like."]],"h":[["Chef's note","This quick and easy vegetable curry is a tasty midweek choice. Use a plant based yogurt or coconut cream for a vegan friendly meal."],["Carbohydrate","The main source of carbohydrate in this dish comes from the rice and chapatis. The carbohydrate value of this dish has been provided for those who have been trained in insulin adjustment. If serving without chapatis you can increase the amount of rice from 40g to 60g uncooked rice per serving."],["Potassium/phosphate","Although this dish contains some high potassium ingredients, such as the tinned tomatoes and the butternut squash, the amounts used in the recipe have been kept to a minimum to ensure the entire meal is still low in potassium and can therefore be enjoyed if following a potassium restriction.\nOverall, this dish is low in phosphate, but if you have been prescribed a phosphate binder ensure you take them with this dish."],["Protein","This dish is relatively low in protein per portion and is therefore suitable if you have been advised to follow a low protein diet. If you have been advised to follow a high protein diet you may wish to serve with 170g chicken if you eat meat. This can be diced and added at step 2."],["Gluten free","When served with rice, this recipe is gluten-free."],["Vegan","Use a plant-based yogurt or coconut cream."],["Healthier option","The flavour of this dish comes from all the curry paste and herbs therefore additional salt is not required. The stock will contain some salt, but low or very low salt stock cubes or stockpots are readily available in supermarkets."],["Cheaper option","This dish is relatively cheap. To make life easier, try using pre prepared or frozen butternut squash that is already peeled and diced!"],["Storage","If not eating all the curry immediately, separate before adding the yogurt. Allow to cool, place in an airtight container, refrigerate and consume within two days. Reheat and stir in the yogurt before serving. If freezing the curry, place in a sealed container in portions. Defrost and reheat thoroughly, stirring in the yogurt before serving. Rice should be served hot and eaten immediately after it is first cooked, do not keep and reheat. Serve with freshly-cooked rice."]]},"9811305":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425°F/218°C convection roast and line a baking tray with parchment paper."],[null,"Arrange your squash cubes in a single layer on your baking tray and sprinkle with salt and pepper. Then roast for 25-30 minutes, or until lightly golden brown, and fork tender. Set aside."],[null,"Meanwhile, melt the coconut oil (if using) in a large, deep skillet (or a dutch oven) and then add the onion and carrots and sauté until softened and lightly caramelized, approx. 8-10 minutes. Next, add the chilies, garlic, and ginger and stir consistently until fragrant, approx. 30 seconds."],[null,"Add the red curry paste, soy sauce, maple syrup, peas, broth, coconut milk, chickpeas, and kale to the skillet and simmer for 8-10 minutes."],[null,"Then turn off the heat and add the lime juice, cilantro, and basil if using, and stir in the roasted butternut squash cubes. Taste and add salt and pepper, if needed."],[null,"Serve this butternut squash chickpea curry with rice, naan bread, or pita chips."]],"h":[[null,"If you don’t have a convection oven , use 425°F/218°C bake (or roast, if you have it). It will take an additional 5-10 minutes to roast, depending on the size of your cubes. Cut your butternut squash cubes as evenly as possible for even roast time. Leftovers keep in the fridge for 3-4 days, reheat on the stovetop. You may freeze airtight in a freezer-safe container for up to 3 months, but the texture of the vegetables will get softer."]]},"3154406":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 180°c/ 160°c fan/ gas mark 4. Put the sweet potato and butternut squash into a saucepan, cover with water and bring to boil, cook until soft."],[null,"Drain the sweet potato and butternut squash and tip them into a roasting tray with the chopped onion. Drizzle with olive oil, sprinkle with black pepper and bake for 20 minutes. Remove from oven and cool."],[null,"Cut the pastry into 8 equal rectangles. Place 4 rectangles onto a lined baking tray and spoon ¼ of the vegetable mix into middle of each rectangle, leaving a gap all the way around edge. Top each vegetable mixture with 15g crumbled goat’s cheese. Brush a little of the beaten egg onto the pastry edge all the way around."],[null,"Take your 4 remaining rectangles, loosely fold in half lengthways and cut 5 slits through both layers, leaving a border. Unfold and lay over the 4 parcels, pressing the edges down onto the egg-washed edges of the bottom layer to seal your parcel."],[null,"Brush the top with egg-wash and sprinkle with sesame seeds or onion seeds and cook for 25 minutes until golden. Once cooked, remove from oven."],[null,"Once cooked, remove from the oven, and serve with the green salad."]],"h":[["Chef's note","A delicious dish that’s quick and easy to prepare."],["Carbohydrate","The main sources of carbohydrate in this meal are the sweet potato, butternut squash and pastry. Carbohydrate values have been provided for those trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","We have boiled the butternut squash and sweet potato rather than baking to reduce the potassium content.\nThere is only a small amount of soft cheese in this dish to provide phosphate and therefore the overall phosphate content is low."],["Protein","This dish is low in protein; you could consider doubling the cheese in order to increase the protein but maintain a low potassium and phosphate meal."],["Gluten free","Use gluten-free pastry."],["Vegan","Use vegan cheese."],["Healthier option","Pastry is high in fat; for a healthier option you could omit the top layer of pastry and have an open parcel."],["Tips","Butternut squash and sweet potato are available pre-prepared in the freezer section of most supermarkets if you find them difficult to peel at home."]]},"6245471":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 425°F."],[null,"Line a large baking pan with aluminum foil and spread onion and squash over foil in a single layer. Drizzle vegetables with olive oil and toss lightly to coat; then season with pepper and thyme. Place in oven and bake for 30-35 minutes, or until vegetables are cooked through and starting to brown. Note: take vegetables out at least once during cooking to stir."],[null,"Combine roasted vegetables, chicken broth and water in a large saucepan and use an immersion blender to blend ingredients together until smooth."],[null,"Heat blended soup over medium heat until heated through, then stir in kale and cook until wilted, about 3 minutes."]],"h":[]},"6942919":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F. Cut the squash in half lengthwise and place it face down in a 9x13-inch baking dish. Pour the water over the squash and bake for 45 minutes."],[null,"Remove the squash from the pan and drain the water. Coat the baking dish with cooking spray."],[null,"Remove the seeds and scoop the flesh of the squash out of the skin. Add the squash flesh back to the prepared baking dish, breaking it up into even sized pieces."],[null,"Add oil to a sauté pan over medium heat. Add the flour and stir to combine. Cook the oil and flour mixture for two minutes then whisk in the fat-free half and half. Bring to a boil, whisking frequently."],[null,"Stir in 1/4 cup of the parmesan cheese, the ground black pepper and the thyme. Stir until cheese is melted."],[null,"Pour the sauce over the butternut squash and sprinkle the remaining 1/4 cup of cheese over the top. Bake for 25 minutes or until golden brown and bubbling."]],"h":[]},"6568654":{"s":[[null,"Prepare the butternut squash. Place the whole squash on the floor or rack of a microwave oven. Microwave the squash for 5 minutes. Carefully remove and let cool until it’s cool enough to handle. With a sharp knife, cut the squash in half crosswise. Peel the skin off each half with the knife, cutting close to remove the skin only. Cut each half lengthwise. Remove the squash seeds from the bottom half of the squash and discard. Cut all the squash into 1-inch chunks. Set aside. This process makes cutting tough butternut squash easier as it helps loosen the skin."],[null,"Heat the oil in a large Dutch oven over medium heat. Add the onion and garlic and sauté for 5-6 minutes. Add the butternut squash and potatoes and stir to coat with the onions and garlic. Add the broth, tomatoes with juice, oregano, salt, and pepper. Bring to boil. Lower the heat to a simmer, cover, and cook on medium-low heat for about 20 minutes, until squash and potatoes are tender. Some of the squash may become very soft."],[null,"Gently mix the chickpeas and peanut butter and cook for 5 minutes. Garnish with chopped parsley."]],"h":[]},"1867":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F. Spray a 9 x 13-inch baking pan with nonstick spray."],[null,"In a medium bowl combine flour, baking powder and salt."],[null,"Melt the butter in a microwave safe bowl. Add the brown sugar and stir until dissolved. Stir in the eggs and vanilla."],[null,"Stir in the flour mixture."],[null,"Pour batter into the baking pan and bake for 30 minutes, or until bars are set in the middle."],[null,"Cut into 18 squares while bars are still warm."]],"h":[[null,"Store in an airtight container."],[null,"Add 1/2 cup butterscotch chips to the batter for extra sweetness and flavor."]]},"6233274":{"s":[[null,"Heat a grill or grill pan over medium-high heat. Coat the asparagus with cooking spray and cook 6–8 minutes or until just tender-crisp, turning occasionally. Set aside on a rimmed serving platter and cover to keep warm."],[null,"Coat both sides of the fish with cooking spray, sprinkle with 1/4 teaspoon black pepper, if desired, and cook 3 minutes on each side or until opaque in center."],[null,"Meanwhile, combine the light butter, lemon zest and 1/4 teaspoon salt, if desired, in a small bowl."],[null,"Spoon the butter mixture over the asparagus and spread over all. Top with the fish and squeeze lemon juice over fish."]],"h":[]},"3384":{"s":[[null,"Keep peel on apple. Core and cube the apples to make cups. In a 3-quart pot stir melted butter, brown sugar, cloves, bay leaf, vinegar, water, and pepper."],[null,"Add apple and cabbage, stirring to coat. Cook over medium heat, stirring occasionally."],[null,"For crisp cabbage, cook 15 minutes, for tender cabbage cook for 30 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Three medium apples should give you 2 cups cubed."],[null,"One cabbage should yield more than enough for 5 cups this recipe calls for."]]},"2402":{"s":[[null,"Place steak in a big pot. Add water to cover meat completely. Cover with lid and bring to a boil. After water is boiling, reduce heat to simmer and cook until meat is tender and shreds easily."],[null,"Remove meat from pot and shred with a fork."],[null,"Cut cabbage into bite-size pieces.Peel and dice onion, carrots and turnips."],[null,"Leave water in pot and add olive oil, tomato sauce, cabbage, onion, carrots, turnips and shredded meat."],[null,"Season with salt and pepper; add lemon juice and sugar."],[null,"Cook on low heat 1 to 1-1/2 hours until all vegetables are cooked. Before serving season to taste with more lemon, sugar or pepper if desired."]],"h":[[null,"You may use blade or cross-rib roast or steak."],[null,"Serve Cabbage Borscht with light rye bread."]]},"9049980":{"s":[[null,"In a small pot, add the quinoa, water and salt and bring to a boil over high heat. Then reduce heat and simmer for 10-12 minutes, until the water is absorbed. Set aside and let cool slightly."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine all the chopped veggies and the cooled quinoa and mix well."],[null,"Add all the dressing ingredients in a small jar or bowl and mix. Then pour the dressing over the salad and mix to combine."],[null,"Refrigerate for 1 hour prior to serving to chill. Or enjoy immediately if preferred."]],"h":[[null,"Use a box grater or shredding tool to shred the cabbage and carrots. If using a food processor , work in batches and pulse to prevent over processing. You want shredded cabbage and carrot, not pureed. For added protein , add a can of drained and rinsed chickpeas or black beans to the mix. If planning ahead , make and store the salad and dressing in separate containers in your fridge. Dress the salad the same day you plan to enjoy it, for best texture. For sugar free , skip the maple syrup in the dressing. If you can have some sugar, I do recommend it to balance the acidity. However, both ways taste great. For soy free , use coconut aminos to replace the tamari . Leftovers keep refrigerated for 2 days. To keep longer , store the dressing separately and do not dress the entire salad. The undressed salad will keep refrigerated for up to 1 week."]]},"3592":{"s":[[null,"Carefully remove 12 cabbage leaves from a whole cabbage and wash them."],[null,"Boil a large pot of water. Add cabbage leaves and cook for 2 minutes to soften. Drain and set leaves aside."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine ground turkey, rice, onion, eggs, 1/4 teaspoon pepper, basil, parsley and 1/4 cup water."],[null,"Place 1/4 cup of the turkey mixture on the cabbage leaf and fold sides of leaf over turkey mixture."],[null,"Place rolls close together, seam side down in a baking dish."],[null,"Combine tomato paste, lemon juice, 1 cup water, 1/4 teaspoon pepper and sugar to make a sauce. Top cabbage rolls with sauce. Cover and bake at 375° F for 1-1/2 hour. Uncover and bake 30 minutes longer."]],"h":[[null,"Cabbage rolls can be cooked in a slow cooker on low setting for 6 to 8 hours instead of baked in the oven."],[null,"If you are following a low-potassium diet, be aware 2 cabbage rolls are equal to 2 vegetable servings. Consuming extra servings of fruits or vegetables can cause high potassium levels."]]},"3318":{"s":[[null,"Cut all vegetables into thin julienne slices. Cut grapes in half and finely chop cilantro. Set aside."],[null,"Heat a large pot over medium-high heat. Add the oil and mustard seeds."],[null,"Wait until the mustard seeds crackle, and then add green and red cabbage."],[null,"Once cabbage starts to wilt (approximately 2 minutes), add carrots and cucumbers."],[null,"Mix all vegetables together in the pot, and remove from heat after 1 minute. Season with lemon juice and salt."],[null,"Garnish with red grapes and cilantro. Cover and refrigerate until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Leftover salad lasts up to 1 week in the refrigerator."]]},"6128101":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, whisk together the light mayonnaise, rice wine vinegar, Dijon mustard, low- or no-calorie sweetener, and poppy seeds."],[null,"Fold the cabbage into the dressing and refrigerate for 1 hour before serving to allow cabbage to marinate. (You can serve it instantly as well but it is better if allowed to marinate)"]],"h":[]},"4297170":{"s":[[null,"In a large non-stick frying pan, heat olive oil over medium heat. Add onions, cumin, paprika, and bay leaf. Cook, stirring occasionally for 10 minutes, or until translucent."],[null,"Add cabbage, bell peppers, garlic, and honey. Cook and stir occasionally for 10 minutes, or until cabbage is tender."],[null,"Add vinegar, oregano and red pepper flakes. Cook another 5–6 minutes until most of the liquid has been absorbed. Remove bay leaf and discard."],[null,"With the back of a spoon, make four wells in the sauce, and crack each egg into a well. Cover with a lid and let simmer until the egg whites are cooked and the yolks are still soft* (4–5 minutes)."],[null,"Season with black pepper and garnish with cheese and cilantro. Serve with bread and enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"* Undercooked eggs increase the risk for foodborne illness."],[null,"PLEASE NOTE: This recipe is higher in potassium and portion size is important. Check with your registered dietitian to see how this recipe can be included in your diet."],["Breakfast foods without phosphate additives","Breakfast is touted to be the most important meal of the day and for good reason. It offers the opportunity to pack in healthy food options at the start of your day. There are many packaged and grab and go breakfast options available, but many contain food additives high in sodium and phosphorus. When choosing breakfast foods, read the Nutrition Facts to see how much sodium they contain. Choose lower sodium options when possible. Next, read the ingredient list to check for phosphate additives. These will contain “phos” in the ingredient’s name. Choose foods without phosphate additives as these are easily absorbed and will likely increase your blood phosphorus level. Luckily there are easy to prepare options without additives that you can make at home. Consider making the following: • Egg bakes that can be quickly warmed in the microwave. • Hard boiled eggs that are handy in the fridge for a breakfast on the go. • A batch of hot cereal such as oatmeal to reheat in the microwave. Boost flavor with fresh or dried fruit and a dash of cinnamon. This option has just 2 milligrams of sodium per serving compared to instant oatmeal that contains 190 milligrams of sodium. Instant cereals often contain added sugar and in some cases phosphate additives."]]},"6729043":{"s":[[null,"In a large skillet, heat the olive oil over medium heat."],[null,"Add the drained and rinsed chickpeas to the skillet, spreading them out in a single layer."],[null,"Sauté the chickpeas for 5–7 minutes, stirring occasionally, until they are lightly golden and slightly crispy."],[null,"Sprinkle freshly ground black pepper over the chickpeas and toss to coat."],[null,"Add the finely grated Pecorino Romano cheese to the skillet. Toss the chickpeas until they are coated evenly in the cheese."],[null,"Cook for an additional 2–3 minutes until the cheese is melted and forms a creamy coating."],[null,"Season with salt."],[null,"Remove the skillet from the heat."]],"h":[]},"7920025":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180oC/gas 4. Mix all of the dressing ingredients together and leave to infuse."],[null,"For the salad, break the lettuce into individual leaves, wash and thoroughly drain."],[null,"Slice the chicken breasts in half to make them thinner, rub with a little oil then cook on a hot griddle pan for 2-3 minutes on each side, or until thoroughly cooked through. Allow to cool slightly, then cut into strips."],[null,"To make the croutons, add the garlic and olive oil to a bowl and crush further with the back of a spoon. Add the black pepper, mix well and coat the insides of the bowl with the mixture."],[null,"Add the bread cubes and mix so all the bread is coated with some of the oil. Spread the cubes onto a baking sheet and bake in the preheated over for around 8-10 minutes, turning a couple of times with a spatula and being careful not to burn."],[null,"To assemble, layer the lettuce in a shallow bowl, saving the smaller leaves until last, so you create concentric circles. Drizzle with the dressing, sprinkle with the croutons and chicken, and top with the Parmesan shavings."]],"h":[[null,"If you have time, plunge the lettuce in ice-cold water just before using, to crisp up and refresh the leaves."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"2957070":{"s":[[null,"Place a little olive oil in a hot skillet and add the chicken. Cook the chicken and then cut in the form of long fingers."],[null,"In a deep dish cut the lettuce into medium-sized pieces."],[null,"Mix the garlic with salt and vinegar until well blended."],[null,"Put the mixture over the lettuce."],[null,"Add chicken and cheese on top."]],"h":[[null,"Portions: 1 Serving Size: 1 salad"]]},"6625864":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F."],[null,"In a small mixing bowl, whisk together the buttermilk, mayonnaise, garlic powder, salt (optional) and pepper (optional) to taste. Cover with plastic wrap and refrigerate at least 1 hour in order to thicken slightly."],[null,"Meanwhile, place the bread pieces on a baking sheet and bake 8 minutes or until slightly firm. Remove from heat and cool slightly."],[null,"Place mixed greens in a salad bowl, add dressing and cheese, and toss gently, yet thoroughly to coat. Season lightly with salt and pepper, if desired. Add croutons, toss gently and serve immediately."],[null,"*Note: Optional salt and pepper is not included in the nutrition information above."]],"h":[]},"2612":{"s":[[null,"Place 1 scoop protein powder in a coffee cup. Add coffee, and stir with a small wire whisk until dissolved."],[null,"Add flavored coffee creamer."]],"h":[[null,"Add ice for Iced Café au Lait. Count in fluid allowance if you are limiting liquids."],[null,"Add additional sweetener of choice if desired."],[null,"Refrigerate leftover morning coffee to easily make this treat any time of the day."],[null,"Nutrition information varies with the type of protein powder used. Ask your dietitian for a recommendation of brands acceptable for your diet."]]},"2983":{"s":[[null,"Juice the lemon. In a small bowl, combine lemon juice, Calabrian chili paste, and honey. Stir to combine."],[null,"Slice each chicken breast in half so that you are left with 2 thin cutlets. Season with pepper on each side."],[null,"Heat olive oil in a skillet over medium heat. Add chicken to pan and cook for 4-5 minutes on each side until the internal temperature reaches 165 degrees."],[null,"Once chicken is done, mince garlic and add to the pan and cook for 1 minute until fragrant. Add chili mixture and heavy cream and cook for an additional 1-2 minutes."],[null,"Plate chicken and pour remaining sauce over chicken."],[null,"Serve with rice as an option and enjoy! (rice is not accounted for in nutrients per serving)."]],"h":[[null,"Calabrian chili paste can be spicy. If you are sensitive to spicy food, you can reduce the amount of chili paste by half."],[null,"If unable to find Calabrian chili paste, it can be substituted with chopped Calabrian chilis, a thicker chili sauce, or red pepper flakes."]]},"6638894":{"s":[[null,"Heat 2 tablespoons of olive oil in a large soup pot, add the sausage and cook until it’s lightly golden all over, about 5 minutes. Using a slotted spoon, remove the sausage from the pan, transfer to a bowl and cover with aluminum foil to keep warm."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the remaining 1 tablespoon olive oil to the pan. Add the garlic and cook until it just starts to turn golden, about 2 minutes. Add the onions and cook, stirring frequently, until it’s soft and translucent, about 4 minutes. Then add the potatoes and mix well, allowing them to get hot, stirring occasionally with a wooden spoon, about 4 minutes."],[null,"Add the cooked sausage back to the pot along with the chicken stock. Cover the pot and bring the soup to a boil, then lower the heat and simmer gently until the potatoes are just cooked and fork-tender, about 15 minutes."],[null,"Add the greens and cook at a gentle simmer until the kale is bright green and wilted, about 5 minutes. If you want to prepare the soup ahead of time, hold the kale and add just 5 minutes before serving. Season with salt, black pepper, and a pinch of cayenne pepper for heat."]],"h":[]},"2139":{"s":[[null,"Place all ingredients in a blender. Pulse or blend until berries are smooth."]],"h":[[null,"This recipe is higher in potassium, but it is a good choice for a quick and easy meal replacement or for breakfast."]]},"6299047":{"s":[[null,"Soak the dates in warm water for 5 minutes to soften, then drain. Set aside a few small pieces to garnish the dish."],[null,"In a food processor or high-speed blender, combine the remaining dates, avocado, almond milk, 2 ½ tablespoons of cocoa powder, vanilla, cinnamon, and sea salt. Blend until completely smooth and creamy, stopping to scrape down the sides if needed."],[null,"Spoon into 2 small bowls or jars and top with raspberries. Garnish with the reserved chopped dates and cocoa powder. Enjoy the pudding immediately or refrigerate for 30 minutes before serving for a thicker, mousse-like texture."]],"h":[]},"6511203":{"s":[[null,"In a wok or high-sided sauté pan over medium-high heat, add oil, ginger, garlic, and scallions and cook for about 2 minutes."],[null,"Add red pepper flakes and chicken and cook for about 4 minutes, stirring occasionally. Remove chicken from pan and set aside."],[null,"Add bell pepper and broccoli to the pan and cook, stirring occasionally, 2–3 minutes."],[null,"Add chicken back to the pan as well as rice vinegar, soy sauce, and dates. Mix well throughout the pan. Reduce heat to medium-low and bring the liquid to a simmer and reduce until thicker or more syrupy. If a thinner sauce is desired, add 2–4 tablespoons of water. Allow to simmer for about 5 minutes."],[null,"Remove pan from heat. Mix in cilantro, basil, and lime juice. Garnish with toasted cashews."],[null,"Optional: Serve with brown rice or another grain."],[null,"Note: You can swap out the bell pepper and/or broccoli for other vegetables."]],"h":[]},"6437099":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400°F."],[null,"Roughly chop 3 dates and place them in a small bowl with the water. Chop the remaining 2 dates and set them aside for later."],[null,"Microwave the bowl of dates for 45 seconds to 1 minute until softened. Carefully remove the bowl and mash the dates with a fork to form a thick paste. Add the olive oil, harissa paste, lime juice, garlic, cumin, coriander, and salt, and stir together until combined."],[null,"Place the salmon fillets in a large baking dish coated with nonstick spray. Spoon the date and harissa sauce on top of the salmon, covering it completely. Sprinkle the remaining chopped dates on top."],[null,"Bake for 10–14 minutes, or until the salmon is cooked through to 145°F, and flakes easily with a fork. Remove from oven and top the salmon with chopped cilantro."],[null,"Serve each piece of salmon with a lime wedge on the side to squeeze on top."]],"h":[]},"6480132":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425°F and line a baking sheet with foil or parchment paper."],[null,"In a large bowl, add squash, oil, ½ teaspoon salt, and ½ teaspoon garam masala and mix together well. Place the squash on the baking sheet in a single layer and roast for 20 minutes, turning over pieces halfway."],[null,"In same bowl, add juice, jam, ground black pepper, and remaining ½ teaspoon salt and ¼ teaspoon garam masala. Whisk together well."],[null,"Add cooked squash and dates to bowl and toss together."],[null,"Place arugula in a large serving bowl or platter. Add squash and dates. Top with toasted nuts."]],"h":[]},"6901477":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350°F and line an 8x8 inch square pan with parchment paper."],[null,"In a bowl, add dates, oats, flour, wheat germ, flax, chia, pecans, salt, and cinnamon and mix together well. Be sure to break up the dates and mix throughout."],[null,"In a small saucepan over low heat, add peanut butter, oil, and maple syrup. Whisk together until well combined and remove from heat. Whisk in zest and vanilla."],[null,"Pour wet ingredients into dry ingredients and stir until everything is evenly coated. Continue to break up dates and mix them throughout."],[null,"Spread mixture into the pan evenly, being sure to press it firmly into the sides and corners."],[null,"Bake for 30 minutes until golden at the edges."],[null,"Place the pan on a cooling rack and cool completely before removing the mixture and cutting. To speed cooling, the pan may be placed in the refrigerator."],[null,"Remove the bars from the pan using the parchment paper. Place on a cutting board and cut into 16 bars."]],"h":[]},"7219034":{"s":[[null,"Place the stock, onion, garlic, spring onions and thyme into a large pan."],[null,"Bring to the boil and simmer for 10 minutes."],[null,"Add the spinach, crab, coconut milk and okra, and continue to simmer for 10 minutes – until the okra is tender. Season well, adding a little Tabasco to taste."]],"h":[[null,"For a veggie version just use vegetable stock and add a chopped red and yellow pepper and a 400g can of kidney beans."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"1002604":{"s":[[null,"Clean shrimp, remove shells, devein and cut open along the back to butterfly."],[null,"Add pepper, garlic and lemon juice."],[null,"Preheat oil in a skillet."],[null,"In a bowl, mix cornstarch, water and eggs."],[null,"Dip shrimp one at a time so they are completely coated with the batter."],[null,"Roll in bread crumbs."],[null,"Fry shrimp until golden brown."]],"h":[[null,"For extra seasoning, try adding cayenne pepper."]]},"3125":{"s":[[null,"Prepare charcoal coals."],[null,"Slice lemon and green onions. Chop celery and julienne carrots."],[null,"Place fish in the center of a large piece of foil (heavy-duty foil works best for a campfire). Sprinkle with Mrs. Dash seasoning."],[null,"Arrange lemon slices over fillets. Sprinkle with green onions, carrots and celery."],[null,"Seal foil tightly. Place on rack over campfire coals for 10 to 15 minutes or until fish flakes easily with a fork. (Be careful opening packet as steam will escape.)"]],"h":[[null,"Bake fish in the oven at 400° F for 10 to 15 minutes if charcoal grill is unavailable."],[null,"If you are on a lower protein diet decrease portion to 2 ounces (cooked), 6 portions for the recipe."]]},"9952260":{"s":[[null,"Lay out a sheet of parchment paper on a tray or counter top."],[null,"Then place your pecans in a food processor and pulse 7-8 times to break them down. They don't need to be the same size, and make sure not to over process. You want chunky pieces, not crumbs. Set aside"],[null,"Now combine everything, except the pecans to a small pan and cook over medium heat, stirring often for 2-3 minutes. The mixture should be bubbly and then add the pecan pieces. Mix well, cooking for another 2-3 minutes until the pecans are evenly coated."],[null,"Remove from the heat and spread them onto your parchment paper. Let them cool, then break apart and store in a container or jar."],["Ideas for using your candied bacon pecans (optional)","Savoury Pancakes"],["Ideas for using your candied bacon pecans (optional)","Baked Potatoes, Mashed Potatoes, Poutine, Home Fries (all the potatoes!)"],["Ideas for using your candied bacon pecans (optional)","Cobb Salad"]],"h":[[null,"Be mindful not to over process your pecans . Just pulse until broken down and check on them often. You don’t want crumbs ! Make your vegan bacon bits ahead of time so they have a chance to cool, before consuming. One batch doesn’t last very long, so if you want to make some for freezing, double up the recipe! 😉 Keep leftovers in an air tight jar or container at room temperature for up to 1 week, or in the fridge for 2-3 weeks. Freeze air tight for 2 months. Recipe inspired by Fifteen Spatulas"]]},"6161393":{"s":[[null,"In a bowl, mix together the canned protein, breadcrumbs, lite mayonnaise, onion, bell pepper, egg, salt and pepper until combined. Form the mixture into 6 patties."],[null,"Add olive oil to a non-stick skillet over medium heat. Fry burgers on each side for 3-4 minutes. Work in batches if your pan is not big enough to hold all 8 burgers."],[null,"Store in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 1 week or wrap individually in freezer bags or containers and freeze up to 3 months (freeze cooked burgers only, do not freeze the raw burgers)."]],"h":[]},"6416579":{"s":[],"h":[]},"7084341":{"s":[[null,"Add the oil to a large saucepan. Add the onions and stir over a medium heat for4-5 minutes, until soft and starting to brown."],[null,"Add the celery, courgettes and aubergines, and cook for 4-5 minutes, stirring regularly."],[null,"Add all of the remaining ingredients, except the pine nuts and basil. Mix and cover with a tight-fitting lid."],[null,"Bring down to a gentle simmer and cook for 15 minutes, stirring regularly."],[null,"Add half the basil and pine nuts. Cook for 1 minute and place in a serving dish. Top with the leftover basil and pine nuts, and serve with the spaghetti."],[null,"To make the spaghetti: Prepare the courgettes with a spiraliser, then place in boiling water for 2 minutes, drain and toss in a little olive oil, and serve."]],"h":[[null,"If you don't have a spiraliser, use a sharp knife to cut long, thin strips from the courgette. Take a slice from along the whole length of each one to give a at base from which to work, then place the long edge on the board so it is steady when slicing the rest of it."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Defrost in the fridge or in the microwave then reheat until piping hot throughout."],[null,"The nutritional analysis above includes courgetti spaghetti as a serving suggestion."],[null,"To turn this into a satisfying main meal, serve alongside a source of protein, such as grilled or baked fish."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"6541626":{"s":[[null,"Place 1 grape tomato, 1 basil leaf, and 1 mozzarella ball on each bamboo fork. Repeat this process for 18 kabobs. Place the kabobs on a serving platter."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the olive oil and balsamic vinegar. Right before serving, drizzle the dressing over the kabobs to coat evenly."]],"h":[]},"1920":{"s":[[null,"Wash and core apples, but do not peel. Cut apples into approximately 1″ cubes. Thaw whipped topping."],[null,"Mix crushed pineapple (including juice) with diced apples."],[null,"In a separate large bowl, combine thawed non-dairy topping with butterscotch flavored dessert topping until evenly distributed."],[null,"Stir apple/pineapple mixture into the non-dairy topping mixture."],[null,"Add butterscotch chips and unsalted peanuts to mixture."],[null,"Stir and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Approximately 2 medium apples yields 3 cups."],[null,"Make ahead and refrigerate but leave out the peanuts until ready to serve."],[null,"Peanuts are optional. If included, be sure to use unsalted peanuts; salted peanuts will affect the consistency of the salad. The 1/3 cup of peanuts contributes 32 mg potassium and 17 mg phosphorus per serving."]]},"2307":{"s":[[null,"Place 1 scoop of protein powder in a mug."],[null,"Add 2 ounces water and stir until protein powder is completely dissolved."],[null,"Add 6 ounces of hot coffee and stir."],[null,"Add 2 tablespoons of DaVinci Gourmet® Caramel Sugar Free Syrup. Adjust to desired sweetness using sugar-free sweetener of your choice."]],"h":[[null,"Makes a great breakfast drink or high-protein snack."],[null,"DaVinci Gourmet® Caramel Sugar Free Syrup can be ordered online if unavailable at your local market."],[null,"Ask your dietitian for recommended brands of whey protein.Simona uses Optimum Nutrition® Any Whey Protein."]]},"7599326":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 180°C/gas mark 4."],[null,"Add oil to a pan over a medium to low heat, then add the leeks. Cook for 15-20 minutes, stirring regularly until they are soft. Remove from heat and set aside."],[null,"Spray a cake or flan tin with oil, then spray each square of pastry and lay them on the flan tin, creating a star shape."],[null,"Add the eggs, yoghurt and pepper to a bowl and beat well. Stir in the leeks and put the mixture into the pastry case. Sprinkle with goat's cheese and bake for 15-18 minutes, until just set."],[null,"Scatter with chives and a little black pepper to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Try this quiche with different cooked vegetables, such as broccoli or sweet peppers. Works well with leftover veggies too."],[null,"Serve with a large side salad to boost your vegetable intake and make this a more filling meal."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Then defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"7059382":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4. Wash the aubergines, prick them several times and put them, whole, onto a baking tray. Bake for 30–35 minutes until they are soft to the touch then remove and allow to cool."],[null,"Meanwhile, add oil to a pan and heat the onions slowly over a low heat for 25 minutes. Stir frequently until soft and start to brown."],[null,"Scoop out the flesh from the aubergines with a spoon, then blend until smooth along with the tahini, lemon juice, garlic and yogurt."],[null,"Stir through the onions and coriander."],[null,"Place into lettuce leaves and arrange on a plate with the cherry tomatoes then sprinkle with chilli."]],"h":[[null,"Try with different herbs such as mint or dill."],[null,"Great for spreading onto sandwiches with salad for a speedy snack or use as a dip with crudités or wholemeal pitta fingers."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"7908780":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven 180°C /gas mark 4."],[null,"Add 2 tsp of oil to a pan with onions, then stir for 3-4 minutes. Next, add the peppers and cook for another 4-5 minutes, stirring regularly."],[null,"Add the courgette and cook for another 3- 4 minutes, stirring regularly."],[null,"Remove the pan from the heat, allow to cool a little, then add the sundried tomatoes, basil, oregano and pepper."],[null,"Add the remaining oil to a metal flan/quiche tin, or large baking sheet."],[null,"In a large bowl, add the flour and baking powder and ¾ of the cheese."],[null,"Add the yoghurt and gradually stir in the water."],[null,"Stir in the vegetables, mix vigorously, then put the mixture in the baking tin. Sprinkle with the remaining cheese and bake for 30-35 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Give other vegetables, such as leeks, a try, or experiment with different cheeses, like feta or parmesan."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"3720":{"s":[[null,"Shred cabbage and chop onion."],[null,"Spray a nonstick frying pan with cooking spray and sauté the onion and cabbage until limp."],[null,"Add water, Worcestershire sauce and caraway seeds. Cook for 3 minutes. Stir to prevent burning."],[null,"Drain mandarin oranges and add to cabbage mixture. Stir in hot rice."],[null,"Remove from heat and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Use coleslaw mix instead of cabbage if desired."]]},"3035":{"s":[[null,"In a stand mixer, combine flour, salt, yeast and caraway seeds."],[null,"Make a well in the center of flour mixture and add warm water."],[null,"Mix until dough becomes wet and sticky."],[null,"Cover with plastic wrap and sit in warm, dry place for 3 hours."],[null,"Heat the oven to 450° F. Place an enamel Dutch oven with the lid on in the oven. Allow to heat for 30 minutes."],[null,"While the Dutch oven is heating, scrape the dough out of the bowl and place onto a floured board or counter top."],[null,"Flour your hands and fold the dough over a few times; making a ball with the dough. Make the seam at the bottom of the dough."],[null,"Carefully remove Dutch oven from the oven and place dough inside. Replace the lid and return to oven. Cook for 30 minutes or until internal temperature of the bread reaches 200° F."],[null,"Remove from oven and transfer to a cooling rack. Cut cooled bread into 16 pieces."]],"h":[[null,"For a crustier crust, can cook for an additional 10 minutes with cover of Dutch oven removed."],[null,"This recipe works best in a Dutch oven. Loaf pan not recommended."]]},"6360044":{"s":[[null,"Puree all ingredients except the green onion in a blender until smooth. Top with green onion."],[null,"Serve with celery and carrot sticks."]],"h":[]},"3434975":{"s":[[null,"Heat a large, lidded frying pan over a medium heat; add the oil and fry the onion for 5 minutes, then add the crushed garlic and minced beef and cook until the mince is browned. Add one teaspoon of the turmeric, the tomato purée, green seasoning or stock cube and 200ml water, mix well to combine. Cover and simmer for 15 minutes."],[null,"After 15 minutes of simmering with the lid on, remove the lid, stir through the chopped fresh coriander and let it simmer for another 5 minutes without a lid. Leave the mixture to cool while you prepare the pastry."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 200°C / 180°C fan / gas mark 7. On a floured surface, roll the shortcrust pastry block out to a thickness of 2mm. With a saucer or small plate/bowl to draw around, mark out 8 circles with a 15cm diameter."],[null,"Scoop the mince mixture from the pan and pile it onto one side of each of the pastry circles. Beat the egg. Brush the egg wash around the edge of the pastry circles and fold over and seal (push down with a fork to get a good seal). Put the patties on a lined baking tray and brush the tops with the egg wash. Bake for 20-30 minutes or until golden brown."],[null,"While the patties are baking, prepare the salad. In a large bowl, add the pineapple, sweetcorn, tomatoes, cucumber and peppers. Mix the vinegar, sugar and black pepper in a small jug and pour over."],[null,"Remove the patties from the oven when they are piping hot and the pastry is browned and crispy all over. Allow to cool for 5 minutes and then serve two patties per person, with the salad."]],"h":[["Chef's note","These traditionally Caribbean beef patties make a great main meal when served with this colourful salad."],["Carbohydrate","The pastry is the main source of carbohydrate in this recipe, and the value has been provided for those who have been trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","Despite the use of some high potassium ingredients, such as tomatoes and tomato puree, this recipe is low in potassium, when following the quantities in the ingredients, and the serving sizes. Therefore, suitable for those advised to lower potassium in their diet.\nThis recipe is also low in phosphate, however it does contain some phosphate, mainly provided by the beef, therefore if you have been prescribed a phosphate binder you should take as directed."],["Protein","This recipe is a source of protein, therefore suitable for those advised to eat more protein, such as those receiving dialysis. If you have been advised to eat less protein then you may wish to replace half of the beef with kidney beans or a different pulse (see the vegan and vegetarian options)."],["Gluten free","Use a gluten-free pastry."],["Vegetarian","Replace beef with a 400g tin of kidney beans or another pulse (drained)."],["Vegan","Replace beef with a 400g tin of kidney beans or another pulse (drained)."],["Storage","Once the patties have cooked, cool and store in an airtight container for up to 3 days. Can be reheated or eaten cold."]]},"3812":{"s":[[null,"Place turkey breast skin side up on a rack in a shallow roasting pan. Insert meat thermometer in center of thickest part of the turkey breast."],[null,"Bake at 350° F until thermometer reaches 170° F (about 1-1/2 hours)."],[null,"Combine butter, honey, mustard, curry powder and garlic powder. During the last 30 minutes of cooking, brush turkey with glaze several times."],[null,"Remove turkey from pan and let stand 15 minutes before slicing."]],"h":[[null,"Portion sliuced turkey into individual servings and refrigerate or freeze for a quick meal later."],[null,"Adjust the turkey portion to match your meal plan if you are on a higher or lower protein diet."]]},"3905574":{"s":[[null,"Make the Caribbean green seasoning by blending together the spring onions, scotch bonnet, garlic, thyme, coriander, basil, onion and celery in a food processer. Place the salmon in a bowl and clean it with the lemon. Add 2 tablespoons of the seasoning and mix. Leave it in the fridge overnight, or for at least an hour before cooking."],[null,"Heat the oven to 190°C/ 170°C fan /gas mark 5. Place the salmon in a greased baking tin and drizzle with some oil. Cover with foil and cook for 20 minutes. Fill a large saucepan with water and bring to the boil. Prepare your vegetables by finely slicing the celery, white cabbage, peppers and carrot."],[null,"Remove the foil covering the salmon and then cook for a further 10 minutes until slightly brown. During those last 10 minutes, boil the sliced vegetables in plenty of water until slightly soft and then drain."],[null,"Sauté the boiled vegetables in 2 tablespoons of oil for 3 minutes in a frying pan, adding a little of the Caribbean seasoning for taste. Serve the salmon on a bed of the sautéed vegetables."]],"h":[["Chef's note","Caribbean green seasoning is a versatile sauce or paste that is often used throughout the Caribbean islands. Marinade the fish and add to vegetables to pack in lots of flavour."],["Carbohydrate","This recipe is low in carbohydrate and the values have been provided for those who have trained in insulin adjustment. To make this a more balanced meal serve with rice or a small portion of cornmeal pie."],["Potassium/phosphate","The boneless fish used here helps to keep the phosphate low. If you have been prescribed a phosphate binder ensure you take them with this dish. Boiling the vegetables first reduces their potassium content. If you do not need a low potassium diet you can sauté the vegetables from raw. The green seasoning contains raw ingredients and is therefore higher in potassium so should only be used in small amounts."],["Protein","Fish is a great low fat source of protein. Sea bream or sea bass fillets also work well with this dish as an alternative."],["Cheaper option","You could use frozen fish to reduce the cost (defrost thoroughly in the fridge before cooking)."],["Storage","If you add a tablespoon of cider vinegar to the green seasoning it can be made in advance and kept in the fridge for up to five days."],["Tips","Add 2 scotch bonnet peppers to your Caribbean green seasoning if you like it hot!\nIf you have a transplant you should buy your fish pre-packaged, rather than from a fishmonger or a fish deli counter, in order to avoid any risk of bacterial contamination."]]},"3204614":{"s":[[null,"Prepare the rice by putting the coconut milk and coconut oil into a pan and bring to the boil. Add the rice, bring back to the boil, then turn heat down to low and put a lid on pan. Cook the rice until all the liquid has been absorbed. Take off the heat and leave to rest for a few minutes."],[null,"While the rice is cooking, combine the prawns with the cornflour, black pepper, paprika and chilli flakes. Heat half the oil in a pan over a medium heat and fry the prawns – just briefly to re-heat if using cooked prawns; for longer if using raw prawns, to ensure they are cooked through."],[null,"In a separate pan, heat the remaining oil over a medium/low heat and cook the chillies, spring onions (white only) and garlic for about 3 minutes. Add in the cooked prawns, along with the green parts of the spring onions and toss everything together. The prawns have already been cooked so this is a quick toss together."],[null,"Prepare the side salad by combining the lettuce, cucumber, tomatoes and pepper and season with your favourite salad dressing."],[null,"Serve the prawns on top of the coconut rice, with a sprinkle of fresh coriander and salad on the side."]],"h":[["Chef's note","A quick and easy prawn dish that’s low in phosphate, potassium and salt."],["Carbohydrate","Rice is the main source of carbohydrate, and the value has been provided for those trained in insulin adjustment."],["Phosphate/potassium","This recipe is low in potassium, when following quantities and serving sizes given, so is suitable if you have been advised to reduce the amount of potassium in your diet. It is also low in phosphate, but does contain some, mainly provided by the prawns, so if you have been prescribed a phosphate binder, take as directed."],["Protein","This recipe provides a source of protein. If you are advised to eat more protein, consider having extra protein in other meals of the day."],["Food safety","If you are using raw prawns, make sure they are fully cooked to avoid infection risk."],["Serving suggestion","This dish is best eaten freshly made."],["Healthier option","If you would like to make this dish lower in fat, consider using light/reduced-fat coconut milk."]]},"3689346":{"s":[[null,"Cook the rice as per the packet instructions, or in a rice cooker. Set aside. In a bowl, add the raw prawns and green seasoning or mixed herbs, combine and allow to stand while you complete step 3 (if using cooked prawns, skip this step and add the green seasoning or herbs when you cook the rice). Pour one teaspoon of oil into a large frying pan or wok over a medium heat and add the onion, carrots, green beans and pepper, stir for 2-5 minutes and then cover until the vegetables have cooked. Once cooked, set the vegetables aside in a bowl."],[null,"Using the same pan, pour one teaspoon of oil in the pan and cook the prawns on a low heat. Fry, turning regularly, for 5 minutes until cooked through. Remove from the pan and set aside. If you’re using cooked prawns, you can skip this step."],[null,"Return the vegetables to the pan on a low heat, using the same pan with the juice from the prawns. Create a well in the centre of the vegetables, add the beaten egg and scramble with the vegetables."],[null,"Add the soy sauce, cooked prawns and rice. Combine and cook for a further 2 minutes until the dish is hot. Turn up the heat, add the coriander, and combine. Serve across four people, adding chopped spring onions if desired."]],"h":[["Chef's note","A healthy spin on Caribbean shrimp fried rice."],["Carbohydrate","The rice is the main source of carbohydrate in this recipe, and the value has been provided for those who have been trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","This dish is very low in potassium, therefore suitable for those advised to reduce potassium in their diet.\nThis recipe is also low in phosphate, however it does contain some phosphate, mainly provided by the eggs and prawns, therefore if you have been prescribed a phosphate binder you should take as directed."],["Protein","This recipe provides a source of protein, therefore suitable for those advised to eat more protein."],["Cheaper option","If raw prawns are expensive then you could use ready-cooked prawns and skip the steps suggested above."],["Gluten free","Use a gluten-free soy sauce."],["Vegetarian / Vegan","Omit the prawns and replace with a smoked tofu."],["Healthier option","This recipe is low in salt because a reduced salt soy sauce has been used. However, this is still a high salt product so it is best to measure this ingredient carefully to ensure you avoid excess salt."],["Storage","This dish is best eaten freshly made as reheating rice is not recommended, particularly if you have a kidney transplant."]]},"3414864":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to to 170°C/ 140°C fan/ gas mark 3. Add the cauliflower florets to a pan of water and boil. Allow to boil for 3 minutes, then remove from the heat and drain."],[null,"In a separate pan, melt the butter. Remove from the heat and stir in the flour until smooth. Return to the heat and add the milk, whisking to combine and thicken. This will make a roux (white sauce)."],[null,"Add the black pepper, onion and grated cheese to the white sauce. Stir to combine."],[null,"Place the drained cauliflower into an oven proof dish and slowly pour over your sauce."],[null,"Place the drained cauliflower into an oven proof dish and slowly pour over your sauce."],[null,"Divide into two portions and serve with a crusty bread roll as a complete main meal."]],"h":[["Chef's note","A traditional side dish but served as a main meal with crusty bread to complete it."],["Carbohydrate","The bread roll, flour and milk are the main source of carbohydrate in this dish and the values have been provided for those who have trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","Although this meal does contain some potassium, overall, when keeping to the portion size suggested, this meal is low in potassium and can be enjoyed as part of a low potassium diet. Note, this is not a side dish but a complete meal.\nThis dish is high in phosphate, mainly due to the cheese and milk, therefore, if you have been prescribed a phosphate binder ensure you take them with this meal.\nNote: if you are following a low phosphate diet, be sure to include the milk in this recipe as part of your allowance for the day."],["Protein","This recipe is high in protein, provided by the cheese and milk. If you have been advised to reduce your protein, then consider replacing the cow’s milk with a rice, oat or almond milk."],["Gluten free","Use a gluten-free flour and gluten-free bread rolls."],["Storage","Once cooked, this dish can be kept in the fridge for up to 3 days and reheated. Can also be frozen before or after cooking in the oven."]]},"3931679":{"s":[[null,"Heat a large frying pan over a medium heat and add the oil. Once the oil is hot, tip in the curry powder and turmeric, mix them in the pan and then add the chopped onion, garlic and ginger. Stir and cook gently until the onion is slightly soft."],[null,"When the onion has softened, add the drained chickpeas, green beans, red pepper, celery and sweetcorn."],[null,"Add the green seasoning to the curry with 200ml of water and simmer on a low heat for 5-10 minutes. Add the yoghurt, stir and simmer again on a low heat for 1 minute."],[null,"Once the curry is ready, toast the pitta breads (or prepare the roti, naan or chapatti). Serve into four bowls with your desired bread, yogurt and chopped coriander."]],"h":[["Chef's note","A quick and great value calypso curry, made in one pot for minimal washing-up!"],["Carbohydrate","The pitta bread, naan or chapatti is the main source of carbohydrate in this recipe, and the value has been provided for those who have been trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","This recipe is low in potassium, when following the quantities in the ingredients, and the serving sizes. Therefore, suitable for those advised to reduce potassium in their diet.\nThis recipe is also low in phosphate, however it does contain some phosphate, mainly provided by the chickpeas, pitta bread and yogurt, therefore if you have been prescribed a phosphate binder you should take as directed."],["Protein","This recipe is low in protein, therefore suitable for those advised to eat less protein."],["Gluten free","Use a gluten-free pitta bread, naan, or chapatti."],["Vegan","Use a vegan yogurt, such as soya."],["Storage","Once cooked and cooled, this recipe can be stored in an airtight container in the fridge and reheated for the following day."]]},"4993661":{"s":[[null,"Place skirt steak, onion, apple cider, spices, honey and water in slow cooker. Cook on low heat for 8 hours."],[null,"Shred the cooked meat and serve in the tortillas – Garnish with sour cream."]],"h":[]},"6820054":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F. Line a muffin tin with paper liners."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine almond flour, all-purpose flour, shredded carrots, chopped ​walnuts, baking powder, baking soda, cinnamon, nutmeg, and salt."],[null,"In another bowl, whisk together eggs, applesauce, ​olive oil, almond milk, sugar substitute, and vanilla extract."],[null,"Pour the wet ingredients into the dry ingredients and stir until just combined."],[null,"Spoon the batter evenly into the muffin cups, filling each about 2/3 full."],[null,"Bake in the preheated oven for 18–20 minutes, or until a toothpick inserted into the center comes out clean."]],"h":[]},"7990195":{"s":[[null,"Put the onion in a large non-stick pan with the squash, carrots, stock and ground coriander. Bring to the boil over a high heat, turn the heat down to low and simmer for 20 minutes or until the vegetables are very soft."],[null,"Add the beans to the soup and simmer for 2 minutes. Take off the heat, cool slightly, then pour into a food processor or liquidiser and whizz until smooth."],[null,"Stir in the coriander and quark, season with pepper, if you like, and serve."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"3424":{"s":[[null,"Break off a 2-inch piece of the ginger root (roughly the size of your thumb). Rinse, dry and peel it, and then slice into coins. Place the ginger in a blender."],[null,"Rinse, dry and peel the carrots. Roughly chop them and place in the blender."],[null,"Juice the lime and add juice to the blender. Add all remaining ingredients and blend until the mixture is completely smooth. If too thick add equal amounts of oil and vinegar to thin the dressing."],[null,"Taste the dressing and if it is too sweet then add additional lime juice or vinegar. It should have a hint of tartness, but if it tastes too sour then add a bit more honey."],[null,"Store leftover dressing in a covered container in the refrigerator for up to one week."]],"h":[[null,"Ginger is very fibrous and may be tough to cut. To peel the ginger root hold it firmly in one hand and then hold the bowl of a metal spoon firmly in your other hand. Scrape the edge of the spoon against the ginger root to peel off the skin."],[null,"Use coconut aminos instead of soy sauce if desired. Replace honey with maple syrup if desired."],[null,"This dressing is versatile enough to be paired with any fresh salad greens of your choice. Try it with cucumbers, carrots, bell peppers, cabbage and also other Asian-inspired dishes."]]},"2543":{"s":[[null,"Grate the carrots and jicama. Chop the cilantro. Combine in a medium bowl."],[null,"In a small jar or bowl combine lime juice, oil and honey. Pour over the carrot mixture and toss to combine."]],"h":[[null,"Leftover salad keeps chilled for 2-3 days. Season with pepper or ground cumin if desired."]]},"1811":{"s":[[null,"Finely shred carrots."],[null,"Wash lemons thoroughly. Cut off tips and any spots you may find on them, then cut each lemon into 4 sections and put in a food processor. Grind or finely chop."],[null,"In a large bowl mix shredded carrots with ground lemons. Stir until mixed thoroughly."],[null,"Add 1/2 cup sugar and mix thoroughly."],[null,"Chill and serve as a refreshing cold salad."]],"h":[[null,"Measure carrots after shredding."],[null,"You may substitute half of the sugar with Splenda® to make it even lower in carbohydrate."]]},"9810559":{"s":[[null,"Add the onion and garlic to a large pot with a tablespoon of water or broth (or oil if preferred) and sauté over medium heat until translucent, approx. 5 minutes."],[null,"Then add all the remaining ingredients except the lemon juice. Bring the soup to a boil, then reduce the heat and simmer until the lentils are cooked and the carrots and sweet potatoes are fork-tender. Stir occasionally."],[null,"Turn off the heat and use an immersion blender to puree the soup. Then add the lemon juice, salt and pepper to your taste, and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Start with 8 cups of broth, but add more if you prefer a thinner soup."],[null,"As leftovers sit in the fridge, the soup will thicken. You may add more water or broth when reheating if you want to thin out the soup."],[null,"Leftovers keep in the fridge for 3-4 days or frozen for up to 3 months."]]},"7614740":{"s":[[null,"Cook the carrots and swede together in a pan of boiling salted water for 20–25 minutes, until tender."],[null,"Drain and return to the pan."],[null,"Add the spread and horseradish, mash well and season to taste."]],"h":[[null,"For a lactose-free version, use 1 tbsp olive oil rather than butter and Dijon mustard instead of horseradish."],[null,"You can make this the day before you need it then microwave or bake in an ovenproof dish."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Defrost then heat in the microwave to serve."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"5274146":{"s":[[null,"Peel the carrot and swede chop into small pieces."],[null,"Boil the carrot and swede for 10-12 minutes, until soft."],[null,"Drain water and allow vegetables to cool."],[null,"Add 100ml breast milk, standard infant formula or a specialised low potassium, low phosphate feed (as advised by your dietitian)."],[null,"Use a blender to whizz up to a purée consistency."],[null,"Add more breast milk, standard infant formula or the specialised low potassium, low phosphate feed if a thinner consistency required."],[null,"Add into ice cube trays and freeze."]],"h":[]},"7836528":{"s":[[null,"Spray a large, deep, non-stick frying pan with a couple of pumps of low-calorie cooking spray and place over a medium heat. Add the onion, celery and mushrooms, and fry for 10 minutes, stirring frequently, until starting to soften. Add the garlic with a splash of water and cook for 2-3 minutes until fragrant."],[null,"Add the tomato purée and mince and mix everything together. Stir in the tomatoes, stock and yeast extract. Season with pepper, add the thyme, then bring to the simmer and cook for 20 minutes until the veg are tender."],[null,"Meanwhile, preheat your oven to 220°C/fan 200°C/gas 7. Boil the swede for 5 minutes, then add the carrots and boil everything for a further 15 minutes until very tender. Drain, season with pepper and add the yoghurt. Mash until smooth."],[null,"Spoon the pie filling into a 2-litre ovenproof dish. Top with the mash and rough up with a fork. Bake in the oven for 30-35 minutes until the sauce is bubbling and the topping is turning golden."],[null,"Scatter the pie with parsley and serve with steamed vegetables of your choice, discarding the thyme sprigs before eating."]],"h":[[null,"You can use a plain yoghurt of your choice. However, this will change the nutritional information and texture of the dish."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 6"]]},"7007930":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oven to 180°C/gas 4 and lightly grease a 20cm x 25cm cm cake tin with the rapeseed oil."],[null,"In a bowl, mix the flour, baking powder and spice together."],[null,"In another bowl add egg and banana and beat well. Mix in the sweetener and oil."],[null,"Gradually fold the dry ingredients into the banana, egg and oil mixture, then fold in the sultanas and carrots."],[null,"Pile the mixture into cake tin and bake for 25-30 minutes then remove from the oven and allow to cool on a wire rack."],[null,"When the cake is cool, cover with the sweetened quark and top with orange zest and walnut pieces."]],"h":[[null,"Make sure the cake is completely cooled before topping otherwise the cream cheese will melt."],[null,"Try cutting into small squares before you top it, then pipe a blob of sweetened cream cheese onto each square and sprinkle with orange zest and a piece of walnut."],[null,"You could use cinnamon in place of mixed spice or try using different nuts such as hazelnuts or almonds."]]},"2560":{"s":[[null,"Set butter out to soften. Finely grate the carrots."],[null,"Line 2 baking sheets with parchment paper."],[null,"In a medium bowl mix flour, baking soda, baking powder and cinnamon."],[null,"Using a mixer, beat sugar and butter until fluffy. Mix in eggs and vanilla and continue beating to combine."],[null,"Add flour mixture to wet mixture and beat until blended."],[null,"Stir in rolled oats, raisins and carrots. Cover bowl and chill dough in the refrigerator for 30 minutes."],[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Scoop 1/2 tablespoon size balls of dough onto cookie sheets leaving 1 to 2 inches between cookies."],[null,"Bake for 10 to 12 minutes or until cookies are lightly browned."],[null,"Remove from cookie sheet to cool on a rack."]],"h":[[null,"Top each cookie with a tablespoon of Jessica’s Cream Cheese Frosting for extra sweetness."],[null,"Make a double batch to share or take to special events."]]},"3763636":{"s":[[null,"Pre-heat the oven to 175°C / 145°C fan / gas mark 4 and grease and flour a rectangular baking tray 11” x 8.5”. Add the torn bread to a food processor and blitz to fine crumbs. Add the sugar, egg, yoghurt, oil, ground cinnamon, bicarbonate of soda and vanilla extract and blend until smooth. Pour into a mixing bowl and stir in the orange zest, carrot and raisins until evenly mixed. Put the cake mix into the baking tray and bake for 25-30 minutes, until a skewer comes out clean."],[null,"Passionfruit curd: Whisk the egg yolk and sugar together and set aside in a bowl. In a heavy-bottomed saucepan, gently heat the passion fruit juice and butter just until the butter has melted, then gradually stir in the cornflour making sure you mix continually so there are no lumps. Take the mixture off the heat and whisk a few tablespoons of it into the egg mixture in the bowl. Continue whisking, adding a few tablespoons of the mixture into the egg mixture at a time."],[null,"Once the two mixtures are fully combined, pour it back into the saucepan and return to a low to medium heat, stirring continually so that the eggs don’t curdle or scramble. Cook for 5-8 minutes until the curd has thickened. Remove from the heat and strain through a fine mesh sieve into a bowl. Cover with clingfilm directly on the surface of the curd and refrigerate for at least 2 hours before using."],[null,"When the cake is baked and the skewer comes out clean, remove from the oven and leave to cool for 10 minutes before transfering to a wire rack to continue cooling."],[null,"Mascarpone cream: In a mixing bowl, beat the mascarpone cheese and double cream until smooth and creamy. Gradually add the icing sugar and vanilla extract and continue beating until well combined."],[null,"Once the cake is cooled, cut into 20 squares. Pipe cream around edges of 10 squares of cake and fill the centres with a little curd. Place the remaining 10 squares on top and decorate with the remaining cream. Sprinkle with cinnamon and orange peel to finish. Let the cakes rest overnight in a cool place or even in the fridge, so the flavours develop."]],"h":[["Chef's note","A deliciously moist carrot cake with a cream cheese icing and a passion fruit curd. Enjoy!"],["Carbohydrate","The bread is the main source of carbohydrate in this recipe, and the value has been provided for those who have been trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","This recipe is low in potassium, when following the quantities and serving sizes given, so is a suitable treat for those advised to reduce the potassium in their diet.\nThis recipe is high in phosphate, therefore, enjoy as an occasional treat, and if you have been prescribed a phosphate binder, take as directed."],["Protein","This recipe is low in protein, therefore suitable occasional treat, if you have been advised to eat less protein."],["Cheaper option","It may be difficult to source passion fruit juice. Instead, consider mango or pineapple (these are lower in potassium than apple or orange juice)."],["Gluten free","Use gluten-free bread"],["Healthier option","This recipe is high in fat and contains a moderate amount of salt from the bicarbonate, and should be only be enjoyed occasionally, as part of a healthy balanced diet."],["Storage","Once cooked and cooled, this recipe can be stored in an airtight container in the fridge for up to 3 days."]]},"6338930":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350°F. Line two baking sheets with parchment paper and coat with cooking spray. Set aside."],[null,"In a medium bowl, combine the brown sugar blend, applesauce, oil, egg substitute, and vanilla. Mix well and set aside."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine the flour, oats, baking powder, baking soda, cinnamon, and nutmeg."],[null,"Make a well in the center of the dry ingredients. Add the sugar (wet) mixture to he dry ingredients all at once and mix well."],[null,"Stir in the carrots. Scoop mounds of batter the size of a heaping tablespoon onto the baking sheets. Space them about 2 inches apart for a total of 24 cookies (2 sheets of 12)."],[null,"Bake 15 minutes. Set aside to cool."],[null,"In a small bowl, beat the filling ingredients until smooth and fluffy. Spread a light layer of frosting between two cookies."]],"h":[]},"3958":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350º F."],[null,"Peel carrots and slice into 1/4” rounds. Place carrots in a large saucepan over medium-high heat and boil until soft enough to mash. Drain and reserve 1/3-cup liquid."],[null,"Mash carrots until they are smooth."],[null,"Crush crackers, melt butter, and mince onion. Stir crackers, onion, butter, salt, pepper and reserved liquid into mashed carrots."],[null,"Place in a greased small casserole dish. Sprinkle shredded cheese on top and bake for 15 minutes. Serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"One pound carrots yeilds 3 cups when sliced."],[null,"Other low-sodium crackers may be substituted for Ritz® low-sodium crackers."]]},"4227727":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F."],[null,"In a mixing bowl, with an electric mixer, beat the eggs and sugar substitute. Add the oil and the vanilla extract. Combine and set aside."],[null,"In another bowl, combine the dry ingredients: flour, cream of tartar, baking soda, cinnamon and nutmeg."],[null,"Add the dry ingredients to the egg mixture. Fold-in the grated carrots."],[null,"Pour the batter into a nonstick tube baking pan. Bake for 40–50 minutes. Check for doneness by inserting a toothpick into the center of the cake. When taken out the toothpick should be dry. Let the cake cool for at least 15 minutes before removing it from the pan."],[null,"In a bowl, combine the ingredients for the glaze and pour the glaze over the top of the cake."]],"h":[[null,"* The numbers in brackets show the amounts when cake is prepared with 2 cups of sugar instead of sugar substitute."],["The role of sugar in baking","Sugar not only adds sweetness, but also plays many important roles throughout the baking process. When sugar meets water during the baking process, a strong bond forms to lock in moisture. This keeps baked goods soft and moist. Sugar also helps batters rise, allowing them to take on their proper shape. As sugar gets hot during baking, a chemical reaction called caramelization occurs, creating the golden brown color we all love. This process also adds flavor. Finally, when moisture is lost during baking, the dissolved sugars re-crystallize. This creates the crunchy sweet crust that we enjoy so much on our baked goods. While sugar gets the credit for many desired affects during baking, it can also add a number of calories and carbohydrates that may not be good for those who are diabetic or who need to limit their caloric intake. Fortunately, there are ways to bake without sugar and still create a tasty treat. This can be accomplished by using a sugar substitute as used in our carrot cake. Most of the time your treats will be just as delicious using a sugar substitute but you may notice some differences while preparing and baking your recipes. It is important to read the sugar substitute package instructions. For best results look for recipes that call for the use of a sugar substitutes as not all recipes including sugar turn out the same when baked with a sugar substitute."]]},"7379443":{"s":[[null,"Add the eggs, garlic, mustard, cream cheese, cheddar and pepper to a large bowl and mix well, beating with a fork."],[null,"Grate the carrot and onion, add to the egg and cheese mixture and beat together so that the carrot is completely coated with the mixture."],[null,"Oil an oven proof pie dish or tin 15-18 cm in diameter. When coated, add the mixture and lightly press to ensure it’s evenly spread."],[null,"Bake in a preheated oven 180°C /Gas 4 for 20-25 minutes until the top is starting to brown."],[null,"Allow to cool a little before serving or cool completely and refrigerate to use the following day."]],"h":[[null,"You could also flavour this dish with 2-3 tsp of freshly chopped herbs such as basil, oregano, tarragon, thyme or coriander."],[null,"Try the dish with sweet potatoes rather than carrots. Ideal for a summer lunch or picnic."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"2416":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375° F. Set butter out to soften."],[null,"Place crust in a 10-inch pie plate and crimp edges."],[null,"Place carrots in a large stock pot and cover with water. Bring water to a boil; reduce heat and simmer until tender, about 15 minutes once water is boiling. Drain and cool."],[null,"In a blender, blend cooled carrots, almond milk, 3/4 cup brown sugar, eggs, vanilla and spices. Process until pureed and smooth with no visible carrot chunks. Pour into unbaked pie crust."],[null,"For crumble topping, combine oatmeal, flour and remaining 1/2 cup brown sugar. Cut in butter until well incorporated (fingers work well for this). Sprinkle crumb topping over filling."],[null,"Bake for 55-60 minutes or until a knife inserted in the middle of the pie comes out clean. (There should be no pie filling, but there may be some of the crumb topping on the knife.) Cover pie edges for the last 20 minutes to prevent overbrowning, if necessary. Cool prior to serving. Refrigerate any leftovers."]],"h":[[null,"Crumble topping can be omitted to decrease carbohydrates and calories, if desired."],[null,"Look for unrefrigerated almond milk and select a brand that does not contain phosphate additives."],[null,"You can serve this pie as a ‘mock’ pumpkin pie. Carrots are approximately 50% lower in potassium than pumpkin."],[null,"Fun decorating tip: Lightly hold a pumpkin cookie cutter on top of unbaked filling and sprinkle crumb topping around cookie cutter leaving a pumpkin design."],[null,"Brooke uses Pillsbury® rolled pie crust."]]},"5026806":{"s":[[null,"Peel 2 carrots."],[null,"Chop carrots into small pieces."],[null,"Boil carrots until soft (10-12 minutes)."],[null,"Drain water and allow carrots to cool."],[null,"Add breast milk, standard infant formula or a specialised low potassium, low phosphate feed (as advised by your dietitian)."],[null,"Use a blender to whizz up to a purée consistency."],[null,"Add more milk if a thinner consistency required."],[null,"Use straight away or add in to ice cube trays."]],"h":[]},"6851874":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, combine grated carrots and diced apple."],[null,"In a separate, smaller bowl, whisk together the olive oil, apple cider vinegar, Dijon mustard, syrup, salt, and pepper."],[null,"Pour the dressing over the carrot and apple mixture."],[null,"Toss the salad gently to ensure even coating."],[null,"Serve chilled or at room temperature."]],"h":[]},"6712842":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, combine shredded carrots, chopped cilantro, chopped mint, and chopped red onion."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together orange juice, olive oil, honey, orange zest, salt, and black pepper."],[null,"Pour the dressing over the carrot mixture and toss to combine."]],"h":[]},"7856586":{"s":[[null,"Add the cumin seeds to the palm of your hand and gently crush and rub them with the thumb of your other hand to release the flavours, then add them to a bowl"],[null,"Add the lemon juice, olive oil, onion and pepper. Mix and set aside."],[null,"Use a vegetable peeler to shave the carrots into thin ribbons."],[null,"Toss the carrots into the dressing and serve scattered with a few fresh coriander leaves."]],"h":[[null,"You could use poppy seeds, sesame seeds or caraway seeds instead of cumin seeds. Or try using a different oil such as toasted sesame or walnut."],[null,"For a really colourful salad, look out for heritage carrots which as well as orange can be purple, white or yellow."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"3765":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Peel and slice carrots and apples. Bring 1 quart of water to a boil in a medium-sized pot. Boil carrots for 5 minutes or until tender. Drain."],[null,"Layer carrots and apples in a large casserole dish."],[null,"Using a fork, mix flour, brown sugar and nutmeg in a small bowl. Mix in butter to make a crumb topping."],[null,"Sprinkle flour mixture over carrots and apples then drizzle with juice."],[null,"Bake for 50 minutes or until apples and carrots are tender and topping is golden brown."]],"h":[[null,"Six large carrots will yield 6 cups and 4 large apples will yield 4 cups when peeled and sliced."],[null,"Casserole can be assembled ahead of time and refrigerated. Heat when ready to eat."],[null,"Replace brown sugar with Splenda® sweetener if lower carbohydrate content desired."]]},"6491318":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6319828":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F. Coat a 9x13-inch glass baking dish with cooking spray. Set aside."],[null,"Place cauliflower florets in a large microwave-safe dish. Pour 1 cup of water over the cauliflower and cover. Microwave for 12 minutes or until cauliflower is tender. Drain and then keep warm."],[null,"While cauliflower is microwaving: If using lobster tails, bring 4 cups of water to a boil and then reduce until water is just barely simmering. Add the lobster tails to the water and poach for 7 minutes. Remove the tails from the water to cool slightly. Cut the lobster tails, remove the meat from the tails and chop. Makes about a cup of lobster meat."],[null,"Add olive oil to a saucepan over medium heat. Add the flour and cook, stirring constantly, for 2 minutes. Add the milk while whisking. Add the nutmeg, salt, pepper and hot sauce. Bring to a boil, then reduce to a simmer for 3 minutes."],[null,"Add the Colby-Jack and cream cheeses and stir until melted."],[null,"Add the cauliflower to the baking dish. Use a fork to break up the florets into 1-inch or smaller pieces."],[null,"Pour the cheese sauce over the cauliflower and stir to coat."],[null,"Sprinkle the lobster over the cauliflower and stir to coat."],[null,"Sprinkle the panko bread crumbs evenly over the top of the casserole and then spray the top of the panko with cooking spray."],[null,"Bake for 30 minutes."]],"h":[]},"6021641":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 425 degrees F and prepare a baking sheet by lining it with parchment paper or lightly greasing it with cooking spray."],[null,"Take a head of cauliflower and cut it into small florets. In a large mixing bowl, toss these cauliflower florets with 2 tablespoons of olive oil, making sure they are evenly coated."],[null,"In a separate bowl, mix together 1/2 teaspoon of garlic powder, 1/2 teaspoon of onion powder, 1 teaspoon of smoked paprika, ½ teaspoon salt, ¼ teaspoon black pepper, and 1/4 teaspoon of cayenne pepper (adjust according to your spice preference)."],[null,"Sprinkle this spice mixture over the cauliflower and toss to ensure the florets are well coated with these flavorful seasonings."],[null,"Spread the seasoned cauliflower in a single layer on the prepared baking sheet."],[null,"Bake the cauliflower in the preheated oven for around 20–25 minutes, or until the florets become tender and slightly crispy. Be sure to stir or shake the pan occasionally to ensure even cooking."],[null,"Once the \"popcorn” reaches your desired level of crispiness, remove it from the oven."]],"h":[]},"6128588":{"s":[[null,"Cauliflower \"rice\" can be purchased frozen at some stores or you can make your own by following this instruction: place cauliflower florets in food processor and process until rice-like consistency (be careful not to over process)."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine the cauliflower rice, cucumber, tomatoes, green onion, and olives."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the vinegar, oil, and mustard.Pour dressing over salad and toss to combine."],[null,"Pour dressing over salad and serve with reduced fat feta cheese if desired."]],"h":[]},"3817521":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200°C/ 180°C fan/ gas mark 6. Trim any ratty leaves and the stalk from the cauliflower, wash it under cold running water, then cut the main cauliflower into florets and the leaves into chunks. Toss the florets and the leaves in 1 tablespoon vegetable oil and put in the oven to roast for 30 minutes, stirring after 15 minutes."],[null,"Put all of the ingredients for the dressing in an empty, clean jam jar and give it a good shake."],[null,"Boil a large pan of water and, once boiling, add the noodles and cook according to pack instructions (usually about 4-5 minutes). Drain well and set aside."],[null,"Heat the remaining 1 tablespoon vegetable oil in a large frying pan over a medium-high heat then add the cavolo nero or kale. Cook, stirring regularly, for about 4 minutes until it is tender."],[null,"Add the cooked noodles and the cauliflower into the pan of cavolo nero or kale and pour over the dressing. Stir well to coat it with the dressing. Cook for a few minutes until everything is hot."],[null,"If serving with cashew nuts, heat a small frying pan on a medium heat (no oil) and add the cashews. Cook them for about three minutes until toasted, shaking the pan regularly so they don’t burn. If you are having eggs, poach or fry them while the noodles, cavolo nero or kale and cauliflower are finishing cooking. To serve, plate up the noodles, cauliflower and cavolo nero or kale, place an egg on top, sprinkle over some cashews and add a tablespoon of kimchi, if using."]],"h":[["Chef's note","A delicious, flavoursome and lightly-spiced meal."],["Carbohydrate","The noodles are the main source of carbohydrate in this dish and the values have been provided for those who have trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","Nuts tend to be high in potassium and phosphate but you can use a small quantity of cashews in this recipe to add an extra crunch. Noodles are low in potassium allowing the addition of un-boiled vegetables to this meal.\nIf you have been prescribed a phosphate binder, ensure you take them with this dish."],["Protein","This recipe meets the criteria for a low protein meal. You may wish to add additional egg if you have higher protein requirements, but it would no longer be a low phosphate dish."],["Gluten free","Use gluten-free noodles (eg buckwheat or rice noodles) and tamari instead of soy sauce (choose low-salt if you can)."],["Vegetarian","Check that the kimchi hasn’t been made with fish or shellfish."],["Vegan","Exclude the egg and use maple syrup, not honey, in the dressing. Check kimchi ingredients if using."],["Cheaper option","Choose regular noodles and leave out the pricier optional extras such as kimchi and cashews."],["Storage","The dressing can stored in the fridge for two days. Leftovers can be covered and refrigerated for up to two days and either eaten cold or reheated."],["Tips","Many steps can be done in advance: the cauliflower can be roasted, the dressing can be made up and the cavolo nero can be prepared, ready to cook, meaning that all you need to do when you want to eat is cook the noodles, cook the cavolo nero and add in the already-cooked cauliflower and dressing to heat it all through."]]},"7658821":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven 180°C/gas mark 4 and lightly oil a baking sheet."],[null,"Break ¼ of the cauliflower into very small florets, rinse in cold water, shake off any excess and add to a bowl. Sprinkle with the turmeric and mix well. Place on the baking sheet and roast for 10-15 minutes until the edges are starting to char, then set aside."],[null,"Meanwhile, add 2 tsp oil to a pan and add the onion. Cook for 3-4 minutes until softened, but not browned. Add the leeks and the rest of the cauliflower and cook a further 3-4 minutes, stirring regularly."],[null,"Add the cumin, garlic, pepper and stock and bring to the boil. Turn down the heat, cover, and simmer gently for 8-10 minutes until the cauliflower is cooked."],[null,"Add the butter beans and blend gradually, adding the milk until smooth. Bring up to heat then divide between 6 bowls and top with the roast cauliflower and a good grind of black pepper."]],"h":[[null,"You could try other beans, such as flageolet for this soup."],[null,"Try adding 1-2 tsp curry paste or powder to the soup along with the garlic and cumin."],[null,"You can make the soup in advance and reheat - don’t top the dish with the cauliflower croutons until just before serving.;"],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Freeze cauliflower croutons separately. Defrost in a microwave or over a very low heat until piping hot."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"9872571":{"s":[[null,"In a large soup pot or dutch oven, sauté the onions and carrots with 1-2 tablespoons of water or broth until softened. Approx. 5-7 minutes. Then add the garlic and stir until fragrant, approx. 30 seconds."],[null,"Add all the remaining ingredients (except garnishes) to your pot and bring the soup to a boil. Then reduce to medium heat, cooking your soup with the lid on until the lentils and cauliflower are cooked, approx. 15-20 minutes."],[null,"Turn off the heat and remove the bay leaves and sprigs of rosemary from the pot. Taste for salt and pepper, and adjust if needed. Then serve."]],"h":[[null,"Use a very flavourful broth ! If your broth is lacking flavour, make sure to adjust the seasonings."],[null,"If you don't have any broth on hand , you can make some with this easy bouillon recipe . (I highly recommend this broth for its fantastic flavour.)"],[null,"Depending on your preferred thickness , use 6-8 cups of vegetable broth. For a thicker soup, use six cups. For a thinner soup, use eight. Remember: the soup will absorb more liquid as it cools."],[null,"Leftovers keep refrigerated for up to 4 days. or frozen for up to 3 months."]]},"9890162":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425℉/218℃ and line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Combine the soy sauce, water and all the seasoning in a medium mixing bowl. Then add the cauliflower florets and chickpeas. Mix well to evenly coat the pieces."],[null,"Roast for about 20-25 minutes until the edges are golden and a little crispy."],[null,"While roasting, prepare your avocado lime crema. Add all the ingredients to your blender and process until smooth, starting with 1/3 cup of water. Add more water if a thinner consistency is desired."],[null,"Assemble your tacos using your favourite shells or tortillas and add a generous serving of the avocado crema on top."]],"h":[]},"2002":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400˚F. Mix together paprika, cumin, black pepper and cayenne pepper. Set aside 1 tablespoon for couscous."],[null,"Place cauliflower florets on a sheet pan, drizzle with 2 tablespoons olive oil and sprinkle the remaining spice mixture on the cauliflower. Gently mix so all florets are covered."],[null,"Loosely cover pan with tin foil and place in center rack of oven for 10 minutes. After baking for 10 minutes, remove tin foil and cook for an additional 15 minutes."],[null,"Dice the cucumber, chop the parsley and mince the garlic; then mix them together. Drizzle with lemon juice and mix again."],[null,"In a small saucepan heat remaining 1 tablespoon olive oil and add couscous. Sprinkle with spice mixture and stir. Sauté until couscous turns slightly brown, approximately 3-5 minutes."],[null,"Add 1 cup of water and bring to a boil. Remove from the heat and let couscous stand for 5 minutes. Fluff with a fork, divide evenly into four bowls."],[null,"Remove cauliflower from oven, divide evenly on couscous. Top each bowl with cucumber/parsley mixture. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Grain bowls are fun and flexible. Couscous can be substituted for another grain like rice or quinoa."],[null,"Try making the spices your own. Play around with salt free seasonings to create your own favorite flavors."],[null,"For PD patients looking for more potassium, adding 2 fresh Roma tomatoes would be a great addition to this recipe."],[null,"A medium size head of cauliflower will yield about 4 cups of florets."],[null,"A medium cucumber measures approximately 6-inches."],[null,"A bunch of parsley will yield the 1 cup of parsley. The leftover parsley from this recipe can be used in other dishes as well."],[null,"A 1/2 cup of dry couscous is about 4 ounces, which comes out to about 1-1/2 cups when cooked."]]},"6890310":{"s":[[null,"Cut the cauliflower into small chunks and process in a food processor until rice consistency, or grate the head of cauliflower with a grater; set aside."],[null,"Heat 1/2 Tbsp. olive oil in a nonstick pan over medium-high heat. Add carrots and scallions and sauté for 5 minutes."],[null,"Add remaining 1/2 Tbsp. olive oil and sesame oil to pan. Add cauliflower “rice” and remaining ingredients and lower heat to medium-low. Cook cauliflower mixture for 6-8 minutes, stirring frequently. Cauliflower should be tender, but not mushy."]],"h":[]},"6422749":{"s":[[null,"Remove the leaves and core from the cauliflower. Grate it using a box grater or pulse in a food processor until it resembles rice. Place the grated cauliflower in a clean kitchen towel and squeeze out excess moisture."],[null,"In a bowl, mix the grated cauliflower, egg whites, flour, garlic powder, onion powder, salt, and black pepper until well combined. Shape into 6 small patties."],[null,"Heat olive oil in a cast-iron or nonstick skillet over medium heat. Place patties in the skillet and press flat with the back of a spatula. Cook patties until golden brown and crisp on each side, about 3-4 minutes per side."],[null,"Turn the oven to broil on high. Arrange tomato slices on a lined baking sheet. Brush with olive oil and sprinkle with oregano, salt, and black pepper. Broil on high for 3-5 minutes until softened and slightly caramelized."],[null,"Fill a saucepan with 3 inches of water and bring to a gentle simmer. Add 1 tablespoon of vinegar. Crack each egg into a small bowl, then carefully slide it into the water. Cook for 3-4 minutes until the whites are set but yolks remain soft. Remove with a slotted spoon, drain on a paper towel."],[null,"To serve, stack a cauliflower hash brown, a broiled tomato slice, and a poached egg. Sprinkle with parsley."]],"h":[]},"7381748":{"s":[[null,"Cut the cauliflower into florets, place into a food processor and whizz to form small grains."],[null,"Place the fish and vegetable stock into a large frying pan and bring to the boil, cover and cook over a very low heat for 6–8 minutes until the fish is cooked."],[null,"Meanwhile, heat the oil in a large non-stick frying pan. Add the onion and sauté for 6–7 minutes until softened and golden. Stir in the garlic, ginger, chilli and curry powder and fry for 1 minute, stirring continuously. Lift the fish out of the stock using a fish slice. Flake, keep warm and set aside. Add the reserved stock and peas to the onion mixture and cook for 2 minutes."],[null,"Stir the cauliflower into the onion mixture, cover and cook over a low heat for 8–10 minutes, stirring occasionally until the cauliflower has absorbed all the stock and is tender."],[null,"Meanwhile, place the eggs into a small pan and cover with cold water. Bring to the boil and simmer for 8-10 minutes, until hard-boiled. Remove from the heat, run under cold water until cool, then peel the shells and halve the eggs."],[null,"Stir the flaked fish and parsley into the cauliflower and season to taste with pepper. Arrange the eggs over the kedgeree. Serve with lemon wedges to squeeze over."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"3405":{"s":[[null,"Steam frozen or fresh cauliflower. Squeeze out excess liquid."],[null,"Place eggs and onion in food processor and pulse until combined. Add cauliflower, flour and pepper and process until finely chopped (do not over-process)."],[null,"Wipe a frying pan with a paper towel dipped in oil and also spray the pan with nonstick cooking spray."],[null,"Heat on low until pan is hot. Drop batter by tablespoon into the pan."],[null,"Brown latkes on both sides, turning once."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute 1 head fresh cauliflower for frozen if desired."],[null,"Serve latkes with a spoonful of applesauce and a dollop of sour cream."],[null,"Potassium is reduced by over 100 mg per serving by substituting cauliflower for potatoes."]]},"3012":{"s":[[null,"Separate cauliflower into florets. Finely shred ginger root and mince garlic clove."],[null,"Steam cauliflower in microwave for 12 minutes on medium setting, until soft but not mushy."],[null,"Combine ginger root, garlic, spices and rice flour. Coat cauliflower uniformly."],[null,"Heat oil. Deep fry coated cauliflower florets in hot oil until golden brown. Drain on paper towels."],[null,"Drizzle with lemon juice and serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"Adjust chili powder for more or less heat."]]},"7274125":{"s":[[null,"Remove the stalks from the cauliflower, roughly break into pieces and hand grate or blitz in a food processor."],[null,"Add the cauliflower to a bowl, cover with cling film and pierce the film a couple of times. Cook in the microwave on high for 4-5 minutes. Allow to cool."],[null,"Once cooled, place the cauliflower onto a clean tea towel and squeeze over the sink to remove excess water."],[null,"Meanwhile, heat the oil in a saucepan and fry the spring onions, garlic and red pepper, stirring, for 2 minutes. Add the cumin and pepper and mix well, then add the frozen peas and sultanas and cook for a further 2 minutes."],[null,"Stir in the cauliflower and top with coriander and almonds."]],"h":[[null,"There are endless variations for this pilaf. You could add other vegetables, such as broad beans, celery, fennel or courgettes and herbs, such as fresh mint, parsley or dill."],[null,"You could also add fruits, such as pomegranate or cranberries."],[null,"If you don’t have a microwave, steam the cauliflower in Step 2, for 2 minutes."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Defrost then heat in the microwave or on the hob over a medium heat to serve."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"7693850":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas mark 4. Remove the stalks from the cauliflower, break into large pieces and hand grate or blitz in a food processor."],[null,"Add the cauliflower to a bowl, cover with clingfilm and pierce the film a couple of times. Cook in the microwave on high for 4-5 minutes. Allow to cool."],[null,"Once completely cooled, place the cauliflower onto a clean tea towel and squeeze over the sink to remove the excess water."],[null,"Meanwhile make the pizza topping. Heat the oil in a frying pan and fry the onion, red pepper and courgette for 4-5 minutes until starting to brown. Add the tomatoes, garlic and oregano and cook for another 2 minutes. Mix well and set aside."],[null,"Add the cauliflower to a bowl with the egg and Parmesan. Mix well."],[null,"Line a round baking tray or pizza sheet approximately 25cm in diameter with non-stick baking paper. Spread the cauliflower, to a thickness of ¾cm, onto it. Bake for 15 minutes, remove from the oven and top with the vegetables and mozzarella slices. Bake for a further 10 minutes. Serve sprinkled with the basil leaves and chilli flakes, if using."]],"h":[[null,"If you don't have a microwave, steam the cauliflower, in step 2, for 2 minutes."],[null,"Add some finely chopped fresh chilli to the vegetables, in step 4, to really spice it up."],[null,"With any pizza, if you cook the vegetables first then add them to the base you can get more onto your pizza."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 7"]]},"2053":{"s":[[null,"Wash cauliflower and cut florets from stem."],[null,"Pulse cauliflower pieces in food processor until it has a grain-like consistency."],[null,"Warm butter in a saucepan and add spices."],[null,"Add the cauliflower rice and cook over low-medium heat for about 10 minutes."],[null,"“Fluff” with a fork and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Make Yellow Cauliflower Rice by adding a pinch of turmeric."],[null,"This recipe is gluten free."]]},"6456214":{"s":[[null,"In a food processor, pulse the cauliflower until it resembles rice. Set aside."],[null,"In a large skillet, heat the olive oil over medium heat. Add sliced bell peppers and red onion. Sauté until the vegetables are tender, about 5–7 minutes."],[null,"Add the riced cauliflower to the skillet. Sprinkle the ground cumin, smoked paprika, chili powder, coarse salt, and black pepper. Stir well to combine."],[null,"Cook the cauliflower mixture for an additional 8–10 minutes, stirring occasionally, until the cauliflower is tender."],[null,"Stir in the black beans and cook for an additional 3–5 minutes until everything is heated through."],[null,"Squeeze lime juice over the mixture and stir."],[null,"Divide the cauliflower rice and beans fajita mixture into bowls. Serve immediately. Garnish with fresh cilantro if desired."]],"h":[]},"1959":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400˚ F. Place parchment paper on a roasting pan."],[null,"Trim the leaves off the cauliflower and cut off the bottom of the stem.Cut the cauliflower head in half. Cut each half into 1” to 3/4” slices, leaving the core in place. Cut off the smaller ends of the cauliflower and save for another recipe. There should be 4 cauliflower steaks."],[null,"Mix olive oil, garlic powder, onion powder, salt and pepper."],[null,"Lay the cauliflower on the parchment lined baking sheet.Using half of the olive oil mixture, brush onto the steaks. Place in the preheated oven for 20 minutes. Remove from the oven and flip the steaks over. Brush steaks with remaining olive oil and roast for about 20 more minutes, until they are golden brown on the edges."],[null,"Slice the red onion. Place each steak on half of the hamburger buns, spread with 2 teaspoons mayonnaise, 1 teaspoon mustard, a few red onion slices, lettuce leave and the other half of the hamburger bun."]],"h":[[null,"The leftover cauliflower can be used in an omelet, cut into small pieces to boil as a substitute for rice or eaten raw with a dip made from sour cream and Mrs. Dash®"],[null,"Change out the bun for a pita, croissant or sourdough."],[null,"Try different toppings such as sliced cucumber, sliced green pepper, or Dijon mustard."]]},"3882":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400˚F. Please parchment paper on a roasting pan."],[null,"Trim the leaves off the cauliflower and cut off the bottom of the stem. Cut the cauliflower head in half. Cut each half into 1” to 3/4” slices, leaving the core in place. Cut off the smaller ends of the cauliflower and save for another recipe. There should be 4 cauliflower steaks."],[null,"Mix olive oil, garlic powder, onion powder, salt and pepper."],[null,"Lay the cauliflower on the parchment lined baking sheet. Using half of the olive oil mixture, brush onto the steaks. Place in the preheated oven for 20 minutes. Remove from the oven and flip the steaks over. Brush steaks with remaining olive oil and roast for about 20 more minutes, until they are golden brown on the edges."]],"h":[[null,"The leftover cauliflower can be used in an omelet, cut into small pieces to boil as a substitute for rice or eaten raw with a dip made from sour cream and Mrs. Dash®"]]},"6515306":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F."],[null,"Remove the outer leaves from the cauliflower heads. Trim the stem end to create a flat base."],[null,"Cut each cauliflower head into 1-inch-thick slices to create cauliflower steaks."],[null,"Place the cauliflower steaks on a baking sheet. Brush both sides with 1 Tbsp olive oil and season with coarse salt and black pepper."],[null,"Roast the cauliflower steaks until golden brown and tender, about 20 minutes."],[null,"While the cauliflower is roasting, prepare the chimichurri sauce. In a bowl, combine the finely chopped parsley, cilantro, minced garlic, dried oregano, red pepper flakes, red wine vinegar, extra-virgin olive oil, coarse salt and black pepper. Whisk until well-combined."],[null,"Once the cauliflower steaks are done, transfer them to serving plates."],[null,"Spoon chimichurri sauce generously over each cauliflower steak."]],"h":[]},"7305915":{"s":[[null,"Heat a small frying pan and dry-fry the sesame seeds for 1–2 mins until lightly browned and fragrant. Set aside."],[null,"Add the oil, onion and leek to the pan, cover and cook over a very low heat for 5 mins, stirring frequently until softened. Add the garlic and ginger. Cook for a further 1 min."],[null,"Give the cauliflower a good spray with 1cal oil, at least 5-6 pumps, and to the onion pan with 3tsp water. Cook over a medium heat for 5-6 mins, stirring occasionally, until the florets start to brown."],[null,"Add the Tabasco or Sriracha, stir in and cook for a further 1 min. Spoon into a bowl, scatter with spring onion, coriander and sesame seeds, and serve."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"9044922":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425℉/218℃ convection roast and line a baking tray with parchment paper."],[null,"Scrub your sweet potatoes and cut them in half lengthwise. Place them cut-side down on your tray. Then add the cauliflower florets, quartered onion, and garlic cloves (leave the peel on) to the same tray. Drizzle all the veggies with vegetable broth (or you may use oil) and sprinkle with salt and pepper."],[null,"Roast the veggies in your oven for 20-25 minutes, until the cauliflower is golden brown, and the sweet potatoes are fork tender. Remove from the oven."],[null,"Transfer the veggies to a blender OR a pot if you're using an immersion blender, but reserve some of the smallest pieces of cauliflower to garnish your bowls if you'd like. Add all the remaining ingredients and blend your soup, working in batches if needed."],[null,"Serve garnished with roasted cauliflower pieces and chives."]],"h":[]},"6538924":{"s":[[null,"Mince the parsley and mint leaves (or grind in a food processor) and add to a large bowl."],[null,"Grate the cauliflower using a box grater and stir together with the parsley and mint."],[null,"Add the diced tomato and stir it into the salad."],[null,"Drizzle the salad with the olive oil and lemon juice, and sprinkle with the salt (optional) and black pepper. Stir to coat."],[null,"Cover and let the tabbouleh marinate for 30 minutes before serving."]],"h":[]},"3660":{"s":[[null,"In a large saucepan with steamer rack, steam cauliflower over boiling water 8 to 10 minutes or until crisp-tender (cover with lid while steaming)."],[null,"In a small saucepan, cook minced garlic in olive oil for 30 seconds then remove pan from heat."],[null,"Stir in honey, apple cider vinegar and chopped parsley. Return saucepan to heat until sauce is heated."],[null,"Transfer steamed cauliflower to a serving dish."],[null,"Pour sauce over hot cauliflower and toss to coat."]],"h":[[null,"This is a quick and easy way to add a nutritious vegetable to your meal."]]},"3246751":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 170°C /150°C fan / gas mark 3. Prepare your baking tray/tins: for a tray bake, grease and line (greaseproof paper) a 20cm x 30cm tin; for a round layered cake, grease and flour 2 x 17.5cm diameter cake tins; for cupcakes, line a muffin tin with cases."],[null,"Beat the butter and sugar together until pale and fluffy. Add in the flour, eggs, bicarb, cream of tartar, milk and vanilla, beating again until smooth."],[null,"Put mixture into appropriate tray/ tins /cases. Cooking times as follows: Tray bake: 40–45 minutes; Cakes: 23–25 minutes; Cup cakes: 18–20 minutes Bake all options until a skewer comes out clean. Remove from oven and cool in tray/cake tins/cases."],[null,"Make the icing. Beat the butter until soft, then beat in icing sugar. If you want to add colour or flavour, do so now. You can either spread the icing using a knife, or put into a piping bag and pipe on the decoration. For the cake, use some of the butter icing in the middle, then sandwich both cakes together and pipe remaining buttercream on the top. Add your chosen decorations."]],"h":[["Chef's note","This versatile, kidney-friendly recipe can be made as a cake, cupcakes or traybake and is perfect for birthdays or other celebrations."],["Portion guidance for children","Serving sizes are based on adult portions.\nThis celebration cake recipe makes 12 adult portions.\nHere is a guide for children:\nToddler (age 1-4): ¼ portion\nYoung child (age 5-9): ½\nOlder child (age 10-13): ¾\nTeenagers (14+): 1\nSome children do have bigger appetites than others. You child’s portion may need to be changed to fit their typical diet if you think the recommended serving sizes are too large or small. We would advise speaking with your dietitian prior to increasing the serving size if your child has struggled to manage potassium or phosphate."],["Carbohydrate","Flour and sugar are the main source of carbohydrate, and the value has been provided for those trained in insulin adjustment."],["Phosphate/potassium","This recipe is low in potassium, when following ingredient quantities and serving sizes. It is also low in phosphate, but does contain some, mainly from the flour, so if you have been prescribed a phosphate binder, take it as directed."],["Healthier option","This is a high-energy recipe to be enjoyed occasionally as part of a balanced diet. Serve with berries, or another fruit, to help boost its nutritional value."],["Gluten free","Use gluten-free flour."],["Storage","Once cooled, keep in an airtight container for 5 days."],["Tips","This is a versatile recipe you can adapt for different occasions – dress it up or dress it down! It’s low in salt, potassium and phosphate, making it a delicious treat for everyone to enjoy as an occasional treat. By using low-phosphate raising agents, like bicarbonate of soda and cream of tartar, it helps to keep the cakes/cupcakes low in phosphate and kidney-friendly."]]},"7577031":{"s":[[null,"Place the celeriac, potato and garlic into a pan of lightly salted boiling water, cook for 12–15 minutes until tender. Drain."],[null,"Mash together with the remaining ingredients and season well."]],"h":[[null,"For a more colourful and healthier version, use sweet potato rather than ordinary potatoes."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Defrost then heat in the microwave to serve."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"9497075":{"s":[[null,"Wash your produce thoroughly and cut the pineapple into spears or chunks. The celery ribs fit without cutting. Then quarter the apple and remove the seeds."],[null,"Start by juicing the pineapple FIRST and then follow with the apple, ginger, and celery."],[null,"Give your juice a quick stir and enjoy right away."]],"h":[[null,"Don’t use a blender . A blender will make a smoothie, not juice. Use a high-quality, masticating juicer, like the Sana 727 for the best results. Masticating (or slow juicers) slowly extract the juice and do not add heat. Heat can destroy nutrients from your produce so you won’t get the full benefit. Make the amount of juice you plan to consume , not extra. Freshly made juice without preservatives will not keep very long, and for optimum health benefits, should be enjoyed straight away. To speed up juicing prep time , you may wash and cut your produce the night before and refrigerate it in a sealed container. Then in the morning, your fruits and veggies are prepped and ready to pass through your juicer."]]},"3823":{"s":[[null,"Combine ingredients in a jar with a lid and shake vigorously to combine."],[null,"Serve over salad or use as a dressing for coleslaw."]],"h":[[null,"Change the type of oil, vinegar and sweetener for a change in flavors."]]},"6986844":{"s":[],"h":[]},"1712":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 250° F."],[null,"Melt butter in shallow baking pan."],[null,"Stir in seasoning blend. Toss in cereal, pretzels and oyster crackers and coat with butter mixture."],[null,"Bake for 60 minutes, removing pan from oven and stirring every 15 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Use your favorite salt-free herb blend and/or add dried dill to the mix."],[null,"Look for the lowest sodium oyster crackers."]]},"2151":{"s":[[null,"Thaw the shrimp and discard the tails. Chop into bite-sized pieces."],[null,"In a food processor, add green onions, tomato, peppers and cilantro; pulse on-off button to chop to a very coarse consistency. Chunky texture is desired. Add lime juice, vinegar and garlic powder to the mixture."],[null,"Place mixture in a serving bowl and add the chopped shrimp and olive oil."],[null,"Peel and core the fresh pineapple. Place in the food processor and pulse to chop to coarse consistency. Add pineapple to the bowl with shrimp and vegetables. Fold ingredients together."],[null,"Chill for 30 minutes or more before serving"]],"h":[[null,"Substitute one-quarter of a medium white onion for green onions if desired."],[null,"Recipe can be prepared one day ahead and served the next day."],[null,"Serve over a mixture of cooked rice and peas (2 cups cooked rice plus 1/3 cup boiled sweet green peas)."],[null,"Serve as an appetizer with low sodium crackers."],[null,"Serve over fish as a salsa."]]},"4587512":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F."],[null,"In a small saucepan, heat rice beverage over medium heat until small bubbles form around the edge and steam starts to rise (or use microwave). Add vanilla extract, tea bag, and the 4 chai spices. Take the pan off the heat and let the tea infuse for 2 minutes. Remove the tea bag."],[null,"In a bowl, mix the flour, oats, cream of tartar, and baking soda. Set aside."],[null,"In a large bowl, with the help of an electric mixer, beat eggs, sugar, and oil until pale and fluffy. Alternate adding the dry ingredients from step 3 and the chai mixture from step 2 while mixing with a wooden spoon."],[null,"Transfer into 12 muffin compartments lined with paper or to a silicone muffin pan. Bake for 20 minutes or until a toothpick inserted in the middle of a muffin comes out clean."]],"h":[[null,"* Avoid rice beverage with claim “enriched”"],[null,"Try this recipe with other teas to add a slightly different flavor."],["Lower-potassium seasoning","Including a variety of different flavors is a necessary part of a lower-potassium diet. Spices can be added to most baked items to create an appetizing and tasty treat. Unlike herbs that come from plant flowers or leaves, spices come from the plant stem, root, seed, bark, or bulb. Depending on the treat you are baking, there are a number of spice combinations that can be mixed to create the perfect taste. Baked goods often include spices such as cinnamon, nutmeg, or ginger. Each spice is lower in potassium and adds a distinct flavor to foods including muffins, bread, or scones. These spices can also be added for flavor to other dishes in the meal. Consider using a hint of cinnamon in a hot beverage, nutmeg sprinkled over roasted vegetables, or ginger as part of a lower-potassium marinade for meat or poultry. When selecting spices to use, be sure to review the label. Choose those with the spice as the only ingredient or if a combination of spices are included, double check that each is lower in potassium."]]},"3204":{"s":[[null,"Slice chicken breasts into strips. Dice onion and bell pepper."],[null,"In a skillet, sauté chicken, onions, bell pepper and seasonings (cumin, garlic and onion powders) in coconut oil for 8 to 15 minutes or until chicken is cooked thoroughly. Stir occasionally. If mixture in skillet becomes too dry, add water. Turn off heat when chicken is fully cooked."],[null,"Turn on Panini maker or George Foreman Grill. Or set a dry skillet on medium heat."],[null,"Combine salsa and sour cream. Spread 2 teaspoons salsa mixture on a slice of bread for each sandwich."],[null,"Spoon 1/4 of chicken mixture on top of bread with salsa mixture."],[null,"Sprinkle 1 teaspoon cheddar cheese on top of chicken mixture for each sandwich. Put the second piece of bread on top."],[null,"Put sandwich in Panini maker or George Foreman Grill for 3 to 5 minutes or until bread is slightly toasted. If using a skillet, toast for 3 to 5 minutes or until bread is slightly toasted on one side, and then flip the sandwich and press down with a spatula to cook the second side for 3 to 5 minutes or until bread is slightly toasted."]],"h":[[null,"Use any color of bell peppers for variety."],[null,"Select the lowest sodium products for salsa and other prepared foods. Compare labels between brands as there may be a big difference."]]},"1725":{"s":[[null,"Tear challah loaves into pieces and let sit out overnight."],[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F. Chop the onion, celery, green peppers, carrots and parsley. Mince the garlic."],[null,"In a large pan, heat 4 tablespoons of the butter until lightly browned"],[null,"Add ground turkey and sauté until browned. Remove turkey from pan and set aside to cool."],[null,"Add the onion, celery, green peppers and carrots to the same pan and sauté until tender. Add garlic and heat for 1 to 2 additional minutes."],[null,"Grease an oven-safe pan with the remaining tablespoon of butter. Sprinkle poultry seasoning over the bread pieces and add to the pan."],[null,"Whisk the eggs and mix into cooled turkey mixture."],[null,"Add egg and turkey mixture and 1/4 cup of the chopped parsley to the bread. Gently mix."],[null,"Add the turkey stock and stir to combine. Mixture will look mushy."],[null,"Cover the pan and bake for 40 minutes. Remove the cover and bake for 20 minutes longer."],[null,"Sprinkle the remaining parsley on top before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Leftover dressing freezes well."],[null,"Omit ground turkey if serving dressing with roasted turkey."]]},"6182531":{"s":[[null,"Heat oil in a heavy-bottomed pan over medium-high heat and add the cumin seeds. When seeds start to splutter, add the ginger and garlic and sauté for 1 minute. Add onion and sauté until the onion is golden brown, about 2 minutes."],[null,"Add the paprika, amchoor powder, turmeric, coriander, tomato, and tomato paste to the onion mixture. Reduce heat to medium and saute, stirring constantly, until the masala comes together, about 2 minutes."],[null,"Add chickpeas and stir to coat in the masala. Add 1 cup / 240 mL water and mix well. Simmer for 20 minutes."],[null,"Once the sauce thickens, remove from heat and add lemon juice, salt, and the cilantro. Serve hot."]],"h":[]},"3121590":{"s":[[null,"To prepare the vegetables, chop the tomato, onion and cucumber into small, similar-sized pieces and place in a bowl. Chop the chilli and set aside for later."],[null,"Drain the chickpeas and add to the tomato, onion and cucumber mixture. Stir."],[null,"Add the lemon juice and the chana chaat masala. Stir well to combine."],[null,"Divide the mixture between three dishes. Top with the yogurt and add chopped chilli to taste."]],"h":[["Chef's note","Chana chaat is tangy, fresh and easy to make, with no cooking involved. This savoury version is kidney-friendly and has been designed for those who wish to eat something traditional during Ramadan."],["Carbohydrate","The yogurt, chickpeas, tomatoes and cucumber are all sources of carbohydrate in this dish. The total carbohydrate value has been provided for those who are trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","Raw vegetables are high in potassium but if you follow the serving sizes specified, this dish is low in potassium overall. Each serving contains two portions of fruit and vegetables so please be mindful if you have more through the rest of the day.\nIf you have been prescribed a phosphate binder, ensure you take them with this dish."],["Protein","Chickpeas are a good source of protein, making this a high protein snack, which is ideal for those on dialysis."],["Vegan","Use a dairy-free yogurt."],["Healthier option","To reduce the fat content of this dish, you could serve it with a low-fat yogurt or without the yogurt."],["Storage","The chana chaat can be stored in an airtight container and kept in the fridge for up to two days."]]},"7660769":{"s":[[null,"For the mint chutney, place the mint, chilli and onion into a blender or food processor and blend to a purée, adding a little water if necessary."],[null,"Stir through the yogurt, season well and add a pinch of chilli powder."],[null,"For the chana chaat, in a large bowl mix together all the ingredients and combine well. Garnish with the garam masala and a little mint chutney."]],"h":[[null,"Chana chaat is also good served warm, just heat in the microwave for a few minutes to serve with the cold mint chutney."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Defrost at room temperature for two hours, or warm in the microwave or a moderately heated oven."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"7283095":{"s":[[null,"Place the lentils in a pan and cover with 1.2 litres of water to come approximately 4cm above the lentils. Add the chilli powder, garlic, turmeric and bring to the boil. Cover and cook over a low heat for approximately an hour, until tender."],[null,"Heat the oil in a frying pan, add the sliced onion and fry until golden brown. Reserve a few fried onions to garnish. Now add the green chilli. Stir through the lentil mixture, then garnish with the onions, garam masala and coriander."]],"h":[[null,"You could add extra garlic to the onions for more flavour. Thinly slice 2-3 cloves and cook for a few minutes with the onions."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Defrost in a microwave then cook over a very low heat until piping hot."],[null,"If you don’t have garlic or chillies to hand, you could use chilli powder and garlic granules, just check the label to make sure there's no added salt."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"7716634":{"s":[[null,"Soak the skewers in water for 10 minutes, so they don’t burn."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4 and lightly oil a large baking tray."],[null,"Mix the chicken with the Chinese five-spice, sesame oil, soy sauce and honey, ensuring even coating."],[null,"Thread peppers and chicken alternately onto the skewers and bake for 8–10 minutes, or until the chicken is cooked through."],[null,"Arrange on a serving platter and scatter with spring onion, cucumber and pomegranate."]],"h":[[null,"You could use turkey – or any meaty fish – instead of chicken."],[null,"You could make this dish up to 24 hours in advance, and leave the chicken to marinade overnight."]]},"7076075":{"s":[[null,"Add the slices of fennel to a hot griddle pan, cooking each side for 2–3 minutes until charred. Set aside for 5 minutes to cool slightly."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the beans to a pan of boiling water. Boil for 4 minutes, then plunge into cold water to stop them cooking further."],[null,"Add the warm fennel, beans and tomatoes to a bowl, and mix together."],[null,"Add the lemon juice, olive oil, mint, parsley and seeds. Mix well and arrange on a large serving plate with wedges of lemon."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"7099518":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 190°C/ gas mark 5."],[null,"Roast the peppers and onions for 25-30 minutes, turning occasionally to ensure even cooking."],[null,"Remove any charred pieces and discard. Reserve half the peppers and onions, then add the other half to a blender with the tomatoes, tomato puree, cumin, oregano and chilli flakes. blend until smooth."],[null,"Chop the rest of the onion and red pepper, then stir into the blended ingredients along with the fresh coriander. Stir in the remaining ingredients and serve with the vegetable sticks."]],"h":[[null,"You could use any colour peppers. Also delicious served with pitta bread fingers."],[null,"The salsa also works well as an accompaniment to grilled meat or fish. Or try adding some to your favourite sandwich or wrap."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"3571404":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 160°C / 140°C fan / gas mark 3. Heat 1 tablespoon of oil in a casserole dish over a medium-high heat. Season the beef with black pepper and fry in the dish for 5–8 minutes, turning with a pair of tongs halfway, until evenly browned. Set aside."],[null,"Using the same dish, so you don’t lose the flavours, heat the remaining oil or butter, then add the onions and fenugreek seeds. Fry gently for 15 minutes, or until golden brown and caramelised. Add the garlic, ginger, chilli, turmeric, ground coriander and cumin and fry for 2 minutes. Add tomatoes, then refill empty can with water and add to mixture. Repeat, so there are 2 cans’ worth of water added. Stir in the sugar and bring to a simmer."],[null,"Add the beef (or vegetable substitutes), put a lid on and cook in the oven for 1½–2 hours. Remove lid, add in the green beans and cook for a further 20 minutes."],[null,"Cook the rice, according to packet instructions."],[null,"Stir through the garam masala and cream (if using) and season to taste. Scatter over the coriander and serve with cooked rice."]],"h":[["Chef's note","This flavour-packed curry is a comforting, high-energy meal low in salt, potassium, and phosphate, yet impressive enough to serve visitors!"],["Portion guidance for children","Serving sizes are based on adult portions. Here is a guide for children:\nToddler (age 1-4): ¼ adult portion\nYoung child (age 5-9): ½ adult portion\nOlder child (age 10-13): ¾ adult portion\nTeenagers (14+): 1 adult portion\nSome children do have bigger appetites than others. You child’s portion may need to be changed to fit their typical diet if you think the recommended serving sizes are too large or small. We would advise speaking with your dietitian prior to increasing the serving size if your child has struggled to manage potassium or phosphate."],["Carbohydrate","Rice is the main source of carbohydrate, and the value has been provided for those trained in insulin adjustment."],["Phosphate/potassium","This recipe is low in potassium, when following ingredient quantities, and serving sizes. It is also low in phosphate, but does contain some, mainly from the beef, so if you have been prescribed a phosphate binder, take as directed."],["Protein","This recipe is high in protein, and suitable for those advised to eat more protein. If you have been advised to eat less protein, try halving the quantity of beef and replacing with a tin of drained, rinsed green or brown lentils."],["Energy","For those needing to increase calories in their meals, add more cream."],["Healthier option","If you need to reduce the amount of calories in this dish, leave out the cream and use less oil. To boost fibre in this dish, reduce the beef by half and replace with green or brown lentils."],["Storage","Once cooked and cooled, the curry can be stored in an airtight container in the fridge and reheated for the following day. Rice is best eaten freshly made. Do not reheat."]]},"7315331":{"s":[[null,"Add 1 tsp of the oil to a saucepan over a low to medium heat, then add the leek. Cook for 3–4 minutes, stirring regularly until the leek has softened, then remove from the heat."],[null,"Beat the egg into the milk, then place the flour in a bowl and gradually stir in the milk mixture until smooth. Next, add the cheese and leek. Mix well. Season with the pepper."],[null,"Heat a non-stick pan. Add the remaining oil and wipe it around the pan with kitchen paper, then add 1 tbsp of the mixture."],[null,"Cook for 2 minutes, then flip over with a spatula and cook for another minute or two on the other side. The pancakes should be about 8cm in diameter and only 3–4mm thick. You should be able to cook 2 or 3 in a large pan at the same time."]],"h":[[null,"The ingredients should be finely chopped to ensure even cooking."],[null,"For extra flavour, add fresh herbs, such as chives, basil or tarragon."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"3151182":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oven to 190°C/ 170°C fan/ gas mark 5. Line a baking tray. In a bowl, mix flour, cream of tartar and bicarbonate of soda, then rub in the butter until it looks like fine breadcrumbs."],[null,"Mix in 80g of the grated cheddar and the dried sage. Make a well in the centre and pour in the milk. Using a knife in a cutting motion, mix into a dough."],[null,"Sprinkle your work surface and hands with flour, turn out the dough and work until smooth, then form into a round shape about 3cm thick. Place onto the baking tray and mark into 8 wedges. Brush with a beaten egg and sprinkle with remaining 20g cheddar."],[null,"Cook for 20 minutes until golden. Best served warm with a little butter."]],"h":[["Chef's note","A tasty savoury alternative to a bread roll with soup, or enjoy in your packed lunch."],["Carbohydrate","The main source of carbohydrate is the flour in these scones, carbohydrate values have been included for those trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","Cream of tartar is a source of potassium but lower in phosphate than baking powder. The amount used allows this recipe to be used as an occasional snack on a low potassium diet.\nOrganic soya milk is lower in phosphate and potassium than cow's milk so is used here to reduce the phosphate and potassium content.\nCheese and baked goods are often high in phosphate so please take a phosphate binder with this snack if you are prescribed one."],["Protein","The scone ingredients (milk, egg and cheddar) mean that they wouldn’t be suitable for somebody following a low protein diet."],["Gluten free","Use gluten-free flour."],["Healthier option","Use wholemeal flour and reduced fat cheese."],["Storage","Will keep in an airtight tub in the fridge for three days."]]},"7770076":{"s":[[null,"Season the fish and sprinkle with the sesame oil."],[null,"Simmer the seaweed, spring onion, mushroom and stock for 5–6 minutes."],[null,"Add the remaining ingredients and simmer for 3–4 minutes until the fish and vegetables are cooked. Serve."]],"h":[[null,"Dried seaweed is available from good health food shops and some supermarkets. Low in fat and highly nutritious, there are lots of varieties and add great flavour to a dish."],[null,"You could use salmon, fresh tuna, haddock or prawns instead of cod."],[null,"For a vegan version, use extra shiitake mushrooms and some tofu."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"6845135":{"s":[[null,"Slice one side of each pita to open pocket, but do not cut all the way through. Set aside."],[null,"Spread 1/2 Tbsp of mayonnaise in each pita."],[null,"Slice Swiss cheese into 4 even slices. Spread 2 Tbsp of hummus on each cheese slice and sprinkle 1 Tbsp of sunflower seeds on top."],[null,"Layer about 1/2 cup of the arugula, onion slices, tomato slices, and cucumber slices on top of hummus."],[null,"Stuff each pita with sandwich filling and cut in half."]],"h":[]},"5933503":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/356°F/Gas mark 4"],[null,"Mix the olive oil and Renastep in a jug and set aside."],[null,"Whisk the egg well until pale and fluffy."],[null,"Place the flour in a bowl and mix in the olive oil and Renastep mixture, once fully combined gently fold in the egg mixture."],[null,"Fold in the grated cheddar and set aside."],[null,"Divide equally between 6 muffin cases and bake for 25 minutes or until golden brown and fully cooked."],[null,"Leave to cool, serve and enjoy!"]],"h":[["Renastep note","Always check with your dietitian or doctor that this recipe is suitable for you."],["Renastep note","Renastep is a Food for Special Medical Purposes and must be used under medical supervision. Renastep is a ready to use feed for the dietary management of kidney disease from 3 years of age onwards. Renastep contains Milk (Milk proteins) and Fish (Tuna oil). This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutritics dietary analysis software. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information."]]},"2011":{"s":[[null,"Set out cream cheese to soften for 1 hour before making tarts."],[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Blend cream cheese, eggs, sugar and vanilla extract in a bowl and beat until smooth."],[null,"Place cupcake liners in muffin pan. Put one vanilla wafer into each cupcake liner."],[null,"Pour cream cheese mixture over vanilla wafer, about 3/4 full."],[null,"Bake for 10 minutes. Remove tarts from oven and cool in the refrigerator."],[null,"Immediately before serving top each tart with 1-1/2 tablespoons of fruit pie filling per tart."]],"h":[[null,"Suggested fruit pie fillings include cherry, blueberry, apple or strawberry."]]},"7340829":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven 180°C/gas 4"],[null,"then place a large baking sheet into the oven."],[null,"Mix the flour, baking powder and pepper together, add the spinach and spring onion then sprinkle grated cheese into the mixture to distribute it evenly."],[null,"Make a well in the centre of the mixture and pour in the oil and half the milk, mix together and add the remaining milk until you have a soft but firm dough."],[null,"Lightly flour a surface and gently roll the dough 2cm thick. Cut out scones with a medium cutter and then place on the hot oven tray. Pull together any scraps and roll out again to get an extra couple of scones."],[null,"Glaze the tops with the extra milk and sprinkle a little cheese and paprika (if using) on the top of each scone."],[null,"Bake for 12-15 minutes until golden brown."]],"h":[[null,"When cutting scones try not to twist the cutter as this can stop them rising as well."],[null,"You can use any cheese you like, this recipe is great for using odds and ends of cheese."],[null,"Try adding herbs such as fresh basil or half a teaspoon of dried thyme"],[null,"Tasty when split in half and spread with a little low fat cream cheese and sprinkled with finely chopped cucumber and fresh chives."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Defrost for 2 hours to serve, or defrost/warm in the microwave or a moderate oven."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"6707006":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F. Cut squash in half lengthwise and scoop out seeds. Drizzle with olive oil, salt, and pepper. Place cut-side down on a baking sheet and roast until fork-tender, about 35-40 minutes. Let cool slightly, then use a fork to shred into strands."],[null,"While squash is roasting, bring a small pot of water to a boil. Add broccoli and cook until just tender, about 3 minutes. Drain and set aside."],[null,"In a large skillet over medium heat, add a drizzle of olive oil and cook garlic until fragrant, about 30 seconds. Stir in broth, milk, Dijon mustard, and paprika. Simmer for 2-3 minutes."],[null,"Reduce heat to low and stir in cheddar cheese until melted and smooth."],[null,"To prevent curdling, remove sauce from heat before adding Greek yogurt. Temper by mixing 1-2 Tbsp of warm sauce into the yogurt first, then slowly stir into the pan."],[null,"In a large mixing bowl, combine spaghetti squash, broccoli, and cheese sauce. Transfer to a baking dish and sprinkle with Parmesan cheese. Bake at 400°F for 10 minutes, or until the cheese is melted and slightly golden."]],"h":[]},"6810489":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F. Coat one large or two small baking sheets with cooking spray. Set aside."],[null,"Steam the cauliflower for 10-12 minutes or until soft. Set aside to cool. Once cool, mince the cauliflower."],[null,"Stir the remaining ingredients into the minced cauliflower, and let the mixture rest for 10 minutes."],[null,"After resting, stir the mixture again. Scoop cauliflower with a Tbsp. measure onto the sprayed baking sheet. Form the ball into the shape of a tater-tot. Repeat to make 35 tots."],[null,"Spray the top of each tot with cooking spray. Bake for 15 minutes. Turn the tots and bake an additional 10 minutes or until golden brown."]],"h":[]},"6101503":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F. Arrange the eggplant slices in a single layer on two rimmed baking sheets. Lightly coat both sides with olive oil cooking spray. Roast for 18–22 minutes, flipping halfway, until tender and pliable. Remove from the oven and set aside to cool."],[null,"Heat the remaining 1/2 tsp of olive oil in a large skillet over medium heat. Add the chopped onion and cook for 4–5 minutes, until softened. Add the garlic and cook for 30 seconds. Add the kale and cook, stirring, for 3–4 minutes, until fully wilted and any moisture has cooked off. Remove from heat and cool slightly."],[null,"In a medium bowl, combine the ricotta, mozzarella, Greek yogurt, black pepper, and Italian seasoning. Stir in the cooled kale mixture until evenly incorporated."],[null,"Spread 2 cups of crushed tomatoes evenly in the bottom of a 9 X 13-inch baking dish. Place 1/4 cup of filling at one end of each eggplant slice and roll up nice and snug. Arrange seam-side down in the baking dish on top of the tomatoes."],[null,"Cover loosely with foil and bake at 375 degrees F for 30 minutes. Uncover and bake an additional 20-25 minutes, until the eggplant starts to brown and the tomato sauce is lightly bubbling. Sprinkle with crushed red pepper flakes, if using."],[null,"Let the dish stand for 5 minutes before serving. Top with the torn basil and divide into 6 servings, with 3 rollatini per plate and sauce spooned over the top."]],"h":[]},"3020":{"s":[[null,"In a medium pan, heat water, milk and salt over medium-high heat until boiling."],[null,"Add grits and stir. Decrease heat to low and partially cover pan with a lid. For smooth grits, stir often."],[null,"Cook for 15 to 20 minutes for old-fashioned grits, or 8 to 9 minutes for quick-cooking grits."],[null,"Remove pan from heat and stir in butter."],[null,"Divide into 2 portions and top each serving with 2 tablespoons shredded cheese. Stir in the cheese and serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"Sharp or extra sharp cheddar cheese results in a cheesier flavor while using a limited amount. For additional cheesier taste and B vitamins boost, stir in 1 to 2 tablespoons nutritional yeast during the last 5 minutes of cooking."],[null,"Increase dry grits to 1/2 cup for thicker grits."],[null,"Avoid instant grits. Sodium ranges from 340 to 520 mg per serving."],[null,"Unsweetened milk alternatives like almond, rice or soy milk can be used instead of cow’s milk."]]},"5266772":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350°F/180°C/Gas mark 4"],[null,"Melt the butter in a pan and add in the chopped leeks. Allow to cook until soft and remove from the pan and set aside."],[null,"To the same pan add the cheese and Renastep, gently warm the mixture until the cheese has melted into a sauce, keep this at a low heat to avoid boiling the mixture."],[null,"Stir the leeks back through the mixture and allow to cool."],[null,"Divide the sheet of pastry in half and spoon one half of the mixture onto each half of the pastry sheet."],[null,"Fold the pastry over and crimp around the mixture to ensure it does not leak."],[null,"Place onto a baking tray and bake in the oven for 20 minutes or until golden brown."],[null,"Serve and enjoy!"]],"h":[["Renastep note","Always check with your dietitian or doctor that this recipe is suitable for you."],["Renastep note","Renastep is a Food for Special Medical Purposes and must be used under medical supervision. Renastep is a ready to use feed for the dietary management of kidney disease from 3 years of age onwards. Renastep contains Milk (Milk proteins) and Fish (Tuna oil). This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutritics dietary analysis software. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information."]]},"6743770":{"s":[[null,"Heat 1 tablespoon extra-virgin olive oil over medium heat. Stir in the oats and stir until fragrant, about 2 -3 minutes. Add the water and salt and cook over medium low heat for 20 minutes, stirring occasionally until most of the liquid is absorbed."],[null,"While the oats are cooking, heat 1 teaspoon of olive oil in a medium skillet. Add the carrots and"],[null,"Take the oats off the heat and mix in the carrots, pepper and cottage cheese, stir well."],[null,"In the skillet used to cook the vegetables, add the remaining teaspoon of olive oil and heat over medium heat. Stir in the egg substitute and pepper and cook, stirring until the eggs are light and fluffy. Remove from heat."],[null,"Place ¾ cup of the oatmeal mix in a bowl. Top with ½ cup of the eggs and a few slices of avocado. Drizzle with sriracha and sprinkle with a bit of Monterey Jack cheese."]],"h":[]},"6331184":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F."],[null,"In a bowl, combine the sliced sweet potatoes, black beans, corn, diced red onion, and chopped cilantro."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix the ground cumin, chili powder, garlic powder, coarse salt, and pepper."],[null,"Drizzle the olive oil over the sweet potato mixture and toss to coat."],[null,"Sprinkle the spice mixture over the sweet potato mixture and toss again to ensure even coating."],[null,"Transfer half of the sweet potato mixture to the prepared baking dish, creating an even layer."],[null,"Sprinkle half of the shredded cheddar cheese over the sweet potato layer."],[null,"Repeat with the remaining sweet potato mixture and top with the remaining cheese."],[null,"Cover the baking dish with foil and bake in the preheated oven for 30 minutes."],[null,"Remove the foil and bake for an additional 15 minutes or until the sweet potatoes are tender and the cheese is melted and bubbly."],[null,"Let the casserole rest for 10 minutes before serving. Garnish with fresh cilantro if desired."]],"h":[]},"6671924":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to broil."],[null,"Heat the olive oil in a large oven-safe skillet over medium heat. Add the onion and cook until softened, about 3-4 minutes. Stir in the garlic, oregano, and red pepper flakes, cooking for 30 seconds until fragrant."],[null,"Pour in the crushed tomatoes and vegetable broth, then season with the salt and black pepper. Simmer for 5 minutes, stirring occasionally."],[null,"Stir in the white beans and spinach, cooking for another 3-4 minutes until the spinach wilts and the beans are heated through."],[null,"Sprinkle the mozzarella and Parmesan evenly over the skillet. Place the skillet in the oven and broil until the cheese is melted and golden-brown, 2-3 minutes."],[null,"Remove from the oven and garnish with fresh basil."]],"h":[]},"9741995":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 400 degrees F."],[null,"Add all the cheese ingredients to a high speed blender and process until smooth. It will be very runny."],[null,"Place the cooked rice and broccoli florets in an oven safe dish, measuring 8x12, or similar. Then pour the cheese sauce over the rice and broccoli, and mix well to evenly coat and distribute."],[null,"Bake for 20-25 minutes, mixing at the halfway point. Add a touch more milk if your cheese sauce gets too thick."],[null,"Optional but recommended: Broil your casserole for 2-3 minutes to brown the top."]],"h":[[null,"If you don’t have fresh broccoli , you may sub for frozen. For nut free , you may sub the cashews with sunflower seeds, with similar results. I find cashews a little richer here, so unless you cannot eat cashews, I don’t recommend making the switch. If you do not have a high speed blender , soak your cashews in boiling hot water and then drain, before adding to your blender. This will help them break down into a smoother consistency. Alternatively, you may strain your cheese sauce once blended, using a nut milk bag . Once blended, your cheese sauce will be very runny but it will thicken in the oven as it cooks. If your cheese is getting too thick in the oven, add a splash or two more of milk and mix well to get it creamy again. This dish is best enjoyed hot from the oven, as the cheese sauce will thicken as it starts to get cold. Leftovers keep refrigerated for 2-3 days. Reheat leftovers to return the cheese sauce to a creamier state."]]},"9572606":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 450°F/232°C."],[null,"In a medium sauce pot, add your lentils, quinoa and veggie broth and bring to a boil. Reduce heat, and let simmer uncovered for 20 minutes stirring occasionally, until liquids are mostly absorbed. (Towards the end of cooking, stir more often.) Set aside."],[null,"Meanwhile, add your diced sweet potato to a small pot, covered with water, bring to a boil and cook until fork tender, approx. 8 minutes. Drain and set aside."],[null,"To a large skillet, add the leek, zucchini, mushrooms, garlic powder, thyme, and salt and sauté over medium-high heat until softened, approx 5 minutes. Stir often to prevent sticking. You should not need any water or oil since the mushrooms will release moisture as they cook."],[null,"Add the cooked quinoa and lentils, plus the sautéed veggies to a 9\"x13\" (or similar) baking dish and mix well."],[null,"To make the cheese sauce, add your cooked sweet potato, and all remaining cheese sauce ingredients to your blender and process until smooth. Evenly pour the sauce over your lentil, quinoa, and veggie mixture, and sprinkle with more thyme, if you'd like."],[null,"Cover the dish with parchment paper and then aluminum foil and bake for 15 minutes. Then remove the foil/paper and bake another 5 minutes to slightly brown the top. Serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"Cook the quinoa and lentils in a delicious broth (instead of water) for added depth of flavour. Prep and assemble the casserole in advance if possible . Then you can have dinner on the table in 20 minutes on those busy weeknights. This vegan quinoa casserole tastes best when freshly baked and the cheese sauce is hot and melty . As it cools down to room temperature, the cheese layer will begin to harden. To return it to a melty state, just pop it back in the oven and reheat it. Leftovers keep for up to 4 days in the refrigerator. Just reheat and enjoy."]]},"7212729":{"s":[[null,"Halve and pit the fresh cherries, reserving 4 whole ones for decoration."],[null,"Put in a small pan with 50ml water and 1 tbsp of the artificial sweetener. Simmer for 3-4 minutes until soft."],[null,"Blend the cornflour and cold water together and stir into the cherries until thickened."],[null,"Remove from the heat and cool, stirring to prevent a skin forming."],[null,"In a bowl, beat the quark, skimmed milk, vanilla extract and remaining sweetener until smooth."],[null,"For the chocolate sauce, put the dark chocolate pieces into a pan and add the unsweetened cocoa powder, the cornflour blended with the cold water, and the golden syrup. Heat, stirring constantly, until smooth. Cool, stirring to prevent a skin forming."],[null,"Spoon everything into small serving glasses. Finish each one with a cherry. Chill and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Blueberries or blackberries work just as well as cherries and are much simpler to prepare as they don’t need de-stoning."],[null,"You could also use raspberries but if so reduce the cooking time to 2 mins."]]},"5400171":{"s":[[null,"Put the cherries and cloves into a blender."],[null,"Pour the Renastep into the blender with the cherries and cloves and blend until smooth."],[null,"Serve and enjoy!"]],"h":[["Renastep note","Renastep is a Food for Special Medical Purposes and must be used under medical supervision. Renastep is a ready to use feed for the dietary management of kidney disease from 3 years of age onwards. Renastep contains milk and fish. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information. This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutrimen dietary analysis software."]]},"3290":{"s":[[null,"Chop the onion and cherries."],[null,"Heat olive oil over medium heat. Add onion and cook until softened, about five minutes. Add garlic and cook one more minute."],[null,"Add tomato sauce, cherries, brown sugar, apple juice, apple cider vinegar, chili powder, mustard and cayenne (if using.) Bring to a boil, then reduce heat to low and simmer 30 minutes, or until"],[null,"Sauce thickens. Stir frequently."],[null,"Transfer to blender and blend until smooth."]],"h":[[null,"Flavor will vary depending on cherry type. Use sweet cherries for a sweeter sauce and tart cherries for a little zing."],[null,"Store sauce in the refrigerator up to one month."],[null,"Use in any recipe that calls for barbecue sauce."]]},"2924":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F. Set butter out at room temperature to soften."],[null,"Using a mixer, cream butter, eggs, sugar, sour cream and vanilla."],[null,"In separate bowl combine flour, baking powder and baking soda."],[null,"Add dry ingredients to creamed butter mixture and mix well. Pour batter into a greased 9″ x 13″ baking pan."],[null,"Evenly disperse cherry pie filling over batter."],[null,"Bake for 40 minutes until golden brown."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute blueberry or raspberry pie filling instead of cherry if desired."],[null,"Cut into 12 servings instead of 24 if you need extra calories."],[null,"Lower sugar options for those with diabetes include using sugar substitute for baking instead of sugar and using low-sugar cherry filling."]]},"2155":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Place the cream cheese, sugar or Splenda®, lemon juice and vanilla in a large bowl. Blend with an electric mixer."],[null,"Add the eggs and beat until fluffy."],[null,"Line a cupcake tin with paper holders. Place one vanilla wafer into the bottom of each cup."],[null,"Fill cups 2/3 full with the cream cheese mixture and bake for 20 minutes."],[null,"Remove from oven and cool 1 hour."],[null,"Top each tart with a cherry and 1 teaspoon of pie filling."]],"h":[[null,"If Splenda® no calorie sweetener (granular form) is used, calories are reduced to 96 and carbohydrate is reduced to 6 grams per tart (1/2 Carbohydrate Choice)."],[null,"Try low-fat or fat-free cream cheese to reduce the fat content."],[null,"Do not over beat mixture."],[null,"Do not over bake—tarts may appear soft and moist, but will firm up after cooling."]]},"3236439":{"s":[[null,"Add frozen cherries, sugar and vanilla essence to a saucepan. Cook on medium heat for 5 minutes, stirring frequently. Gently break apart the cherries with a spatula. Mix together the arrowroot powder and water to form a paste."],[null,"Add the paste to the cooked cherries, stirring as you pour it in. Bring it to the boil, then remove from the heat and allow to cool. Preheat oven to 190°C / 170°C fan / gas mark 5 and grease a muffin tin."],[null,"Take three pastry sheets and cut each into four squares. Melt the butter and brush the pastry on each side and line six holes with two squares in each. Add one tablespoon of cherry filling to each. Fold the filo pastry edges over the top of the cherry filling to loosely close."],[null,"Brush each tart with additional butter. Bake in the oven for 10-15 minutes, until the pastry looks light golden brown all over. Remove from the oven and transfer to a cooling rack. Once cooled, dust with powdered sugar. Serve warm or at room temperature."]],"h":[["Chef's note","Using frozen cherries and ready-made pastry means these tarts can be made for special occasions all year round."],["Carbohydrate","The main source of carbohydrates in this dish are the cherries, sugars and filo pastry. The carbohydrate value has been provided for those who have been trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","This recipe contains cherries which are high in potassium but when used in the amount specified in the recipe it remains a low potassium dish.\nThis dish contains a small amount of phosphate which mainly comes from the filo pastry. If you have been prescribed a phosphate binder, ensure you take them with this dish."],["Protein","This dish is low in protein and makes a suitable pudding for a special occasion if you have been advised to follow a low protein diet."],["Gluten free","It is sometimes difficult to find gluten-free ready-made filo pastry, therefore you may wish to use gluten-free puff pastry instead."],["Vegan","Many ready-made filo pastry is dairy free. Use a dairy-free spread instead of butter."],["Healthier option","If you want to reduce the amount of sugar or fat you eat, reduce the quantity of sugar used in the cherry filling, or replace with sweetener. Consider using a low-fat spread instead of the butter."],["Cheaper option","Vanilla extract could be used instead of the vanilla pods."],["Storage","Once cooled, store in an airtight container in the fridge and eat within two days."]]},"6811573":{"s":[[null,"Spoon 3/4 cup nonfat Greek yogurt into a bowl."],[null,"Sprinkle 1 tablespoon flaxseed evenly over the top."],[null,"Add 1/4 cup unsweetened dried cherries."],[null,"Stir gently to combine or leave layered if you prefer more texture."],[null,"Enjoy right away."]],"h":[]},"6549589":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F. Line a 9 x 9-inch baking dish with parchment paper."],[null,"In a bowl, combine the pitted cherries, lemon juice, zero-calorie maple syrup, and vanilla extract. Toss until the cherries are well coated."],[null,"Add the cherries to the prepared baking dish and spread in an even layer."],[null,"In a separate bowl, mix the oats, almond flour, chopped nuts, vegetable oil, and salt. Stir until the mixture is crumbly."],[null,"Sprinkle the oat mixture evenly over the top of the cherries."],[null,"Bake for about 30 minutes or until the cherry filling is bubbly, and the oat topping is golden brown."],[null,"Let it cool for 10 minutes before serving."],[null,"Serve warm."]],"h":[]},"7146637":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a frying pan, add the onion and fry for 5 minutes until softened and starting to brown, then add the garlic and cook for a further minute."],[null,"Meanwhile add the bread, thyme and pepper and 500ml boiling water to a bowl, leave for a couple of minutes then stir with a fork to break up all the bread into a thick porridge."],[null,"Add the onions and garlic to the bread mixture along with the apricots, chestnuts and parsley and mix well."],[null,"Add to a lightly oiled ovenproof dish and bake for 25–35 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Try adding other herbs in place of thyme. Sage or tarragon both work well. You could also use other dried fruit such as prunes, cranberries or raisins instead of apricots."],[null,"Ideal served as a side dish with vegetarian and vegan dishes or with meats such as pheasant."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"1705":{"s":[[null,"Set the butter out to soften."],[null,"Place 12 of the peppermint candies in a zip-top bag and pound with a heavy pan until finely crushed."],[null,"In a mixing bowl, combine the sugar, butter, egg and peppermint extract. Beat ingredients at medium speed until creamy, scraping the bowl several times."],[null,"Stir together the flour, baking powder and salt. Turn mixer to low speed and add flour mixture. Beat until well mixed. Hand-stir the crushed peppermint candy into the dough. Refrigerate dough for 1 hour to chill."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 350° F. Crush the remaining 6 peppermint candies. Line baking sheets with parchment paper."],[null,"Shape the chilled dough into 3/4-inch balls and place on the baking sheet 2-inches apart. Using your thumb, make an indentation on each cookie and top with about 1/2 teaspoon of the crushed candy."],[null,"Bake for 10 to 12 minutes or until edges are lightly browned. Remove parchment paper from baking sheet and cool cookies completely. Store in a sealed container with parchment paper or waxed paper between layers of cookies."]],"h":[[null,"Crushed candies may become sticky and clump together in a hot kitchen. Crush just prior to adding in the recipe."],[null,"Cookies become more chewy after storing them for a day or longer."],[null,"People with diabetes may want to limit to 1 cookie to help keep carbohydrates within goal."]]},"9602951":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, combine the chia or flax with the water. Let stand for 5 minutes (or longer) and use in your favourite recipes."]],"h":[[null,"You don't need to grind your seeds to make this chia egg recipe. However, if you want to hide the texture of the seeds from any pickier eaters, then go for it. Or, if you don't want to see them in your finished product, use white seeds instead of black. Although you may use a flax egg and chia egg interchangeably in most baked goods recipes, I prefer chia because of it's neutral taste. That said, whatever I have available in the pantry is what I use, so just use what you have!"]]},"2126":{"s":[[null,"Blend the almond milk and chia seeds together in a blender."],[null,"Pour mixture into 4 clear dessert dishes. Stir to evenly distribute the chia seeds."],[null,"Refrigerate until set, about 1 hour in the refrigerator or 1/2 hour in the freezer."],[null,"Top each serving with 1 tablespoon of shredded coconut, 1 large strawberry and 1 tablespoon of blueberries before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Most brands of almond milk contain added calcium. If you are on a low calcium diet this recipe may not be a good choice. You can substitute Homemade Almond Milk or look for a brand without added calcium."],[null,"Chia seeds are high in phosphorus, contributing to the 200 mg phosphorus in each serving of pudding. It is estimated only 40-60% of the phosphorus in whole grains, legumes, nuts and seeds is available for absorption. Check with your dietitian before including Chia Pudding with Berries in your diet."]]},"6218931":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, combine chia seeds and milk. Soak chia seeds for 8 hours or overnight in the refrigerator."],[null,"After chia seeds have soaked, add vanilla extract. Mix well and set aside."],[null,"In a medium bowl, combine the raspberries, maple syrup, rose water, and lemon. Stir gently to combine and set aside."],[null,"In a short glass, add a layer of chia seed mixture, a thin layer of raspberry mixture, and a thin layer of soba noodles. Repeat for each serving and garnish each serving with pomegranate seeds."]],"h":[]},"6817221":{"s":[],"h":[]},"2379":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Arrange chicken breasts in a single layer in a 9” x 13” (or larger) baking dish, adding pepper to taste. Set aside."],[null,"In a saucepan, sauté apple, onion and garlic in butter over a medium heat until tender."],[null,"Add curry powder and basil; mix well, and sauté for another minute."],[null,"Stir in the flour, and continue to cook one minute longer."],[null,"Add chicken broth and rice milk, stirring well. Remove from heat."],[null,"Pour sauce mixture over chicken breasts, and bake for 50 to 60 minutes, or until chicken is done."]],"h":[[null,"Monica recommends Swanson’s® low-sodium chicken broth. By definition, low sodium broth contains no more than 140 mg sodium per cup."],[null,"To prevent spills in the oven, you can cover the chicken before baking."],[null,"Chicken and Apple Curry is great with steamed white rice."],[null,"This is a high protein meal. If you are on a lower protein diet, adjust the portion according to your meal plan."]]},"6252784":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, combine the cinnamon, ground ginger, turmeric, ground black pepper and salt."],[null,"Add oil and a generous amount of cooking spray to a large sauté pan over high heat."],[null,"Season both sides of the chicken thighs with the spice mixture."],[null,"Sear the chicken on both sides until golden brown, about 3 minutes per side."],[null,"Add the onion, garlic and apricots and stir into the chicken thighs. Add the chicken broth and bring to a boil."],[null,"Reduce to a simmer for 15 minutes or until chicken is cooked through and the internal temperature is at least 165°F."],[null,"Remove the chicken from the pan and set aside."],[null,"Bring the sauce to a low boil for 8-10 minutes or until reduced and slightly thickened."],[null,"Add chicken thighs back into the sauce and stir to coat. Stir in the chopped parsley and serve."]],"h":[]},"6893898":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together peanut butter, soy sauce, honey, rice vinegar, sesame oil, minced garlic, and grated ginger. Add water gradually until you reach the desired sauce consistency."],[null,"Assemble the lettuce wraps by laying out large lettuce leaves, placing chicken on each leaf, and topping with cucumber and carrots."],[null,"Drizzle peanut sauce over the chicken and top with cilantro, scallions, and sesame seeds."]],"h":[]},"6987481":{"s":[[null,"In a bowl, add the chicken strips to the Italian dressing, ensuring they are well-coated. Let them marinate for at least 10 minutes."],[null,"Heat a grill pan over medium-high heat. Cook the marinated chicken strips until fully cooked and the chicken has reached an internal temperature of 165 degrees F, about 5-7 minutes."],[null,"In a bowl, whisk together the Greek yogurt, fresh lemon juice, minced garlic, chopped fresh mint, and black pepper. Set aside."],[null,"Warm the whole-wheat pita pockets according to package instructions."],[null,"Spread about 2 Tbsp of yogurt sauce inside each pita."],[null,"Fill each pita with the cooked chicken strips, cucumber slices, cherry tomatoes, and red onion."]],"h":[]},"6598291":{"s":[[null,"Mix the flours, baking soda, baking powder, sage, salt (optional), and pepper in a medium bowl. Add yogurt, egg, and water and knead to make a slightly sticky dough. Cover the bowl and set aside."],[null,"Add cooking spray and olive oil to a large soup pot over medium high heat. Add the onion, carrots, celery, and mushrooms. Sauté for 5-7 minutes or until the vegetables are softened."],[null,"Add the chicken and broth, and bring to a boil. Reduce to a simmer for 5 minutes."],[null,"Roll the dough out into an 8 inch disk that is 1/2-inch thick. Cut the dough into 1 inch pieces and drop the dumplings into the simmering broth. Stir frequently until all the dumplings are added."],[null,"Simmer the dumplings for 10 minutes and serve."]],"h":[]},"7185004":{"s":[[null,"Add the cumin and coriander seeds to a dry saucepan and toast for 1-2 minutes. Add the oil and the onions. Cook for 5 minutes, stirring regularly until browned."],[null,"Add the garlic, ginger, green chillies and chicken pieces and cook for another 2-3 minutes, stirring regularly."],[null,"Add the chilli powder, garam masala and turmeric powder along with the lemon juice, tomatoes and 500ml water."],[null,"Bring to the boil, mix well, reduce the heat and simmer for 15 minutes, stirring regularly."],[null,"Add the lentils and simmer for another 15 minutes, stirring regularly, until cooked."]],"h":[[null,"If you don't have all the different spices to hand, you can use your favourite curry powder or paste."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"7237258":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 200°C/fan 180°C/gas 6. Spray a large, non-stick frying pan with a couple of pumps of cooking spray and put over a medium-high heat. When hot, fry the chicken for 2-3 minutes until browned all over, then tip into a large ovenproof pie or ceramic baking dish."],[null,"Fry the mushrooms for 5-6 minutes, stirring now and then, until softened. At the same time, boil the potatoes for 8 minutes, then drain and set aside. Tip the mushrooms into the dish with the chicken, then spray the pan with a couple of pumps of cooking spray and turn down the heat to medium. Fry the onion for 5-6 minutes, then add the garlic with a splash of water and fry for 2 minutes."],[null,"Mix the cornflour with a few spoonfuls of the stock to make a smooth paste. Stir this into the rest of the stock and pour into the frying pan. Bring to a simmer and cook for 1-2 minutes until thickened. Pour over the chicken and mushrooms, add the parsley and stir everything together."],[null,"Arrange the potatoes over the top in a double layer, so some sink into the stock and some stay on the top. Spray with a couple of pumps of cooking spray and bake for 40-45 minutes, or until the potatoes are golden brown and the stock is bubbling gently. Meanwhile, steam the broccoli for 5-6 minutes. Remove the bake from the oven and leave to stand for 5 minutes, then divide between 4 bowls and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Nutritional information includes serving suggestion."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"3765080":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a shallow pan and fry the chicken pieces over a medium heat. When almost cooked, add in chickpeas and cook until heated through and crisping. Once the chicken is cooked thoroughly, remove and drain on kitchen paper to remove excess oil (if using edamame beans add them later)."],[null,"While the chicken is cooking, cook the rice noodles according to packet instructions, then drain. For the dressing, whisk all ingredients together until well combined and set aside until needed."],[null,"Separate the lettuce leaves, tearing any large ones in half. Mix the lettuce with the noodles, orange segments, lime zest and edamame beans (if using in place of the chickpeas)."],[null,"Mix the chicken and chickpeas into the salad and divide into four bowls. Dress the individual portions with the sesame oil dressing, then serve."]],"h":[["Chef's note","A quick and easy recipe for a healthy light meal."],["Carbohydrate","The rice noodles are the main source of carbohydrate in this recipe, and the value has been provided for those who have been trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","This recipe is low in potassium, despite the use of fresh oranges and salad. This is because the quantities have been kept to a minimum, therefore please ensure you follow the quantities for all the ingredients and the serving sizes.\nThis recipe is high in phosphate, provided by the chicken and beans, therefore, if you are prescribed a phosphate binder you should take as directed."],["Protein","This recipe is high in protein, which makes it suitable for those advised to eat more protein, particularly those receiving dialysis. If you have been advised to reduce your protein, then reduce the chicken to 150g or opt for the vegetarian/vegan option."],["Gluten free","Replace the soy sauce with a gluten-free alternative such as tamari."],["Vegetarian/Vegan","Replace the chicken with one drained 400g tin of chickpeas or butter beans."],["Healthier option","This recipe is low in salt, despite the use of soy sauce. We recommend using a reduced salt variety, however this is still high in salt so be sure to keep to the quality specified."],["Storage","This dish is best eaten freshly made."],["Tips","If using edamame beans, these can be purchased frozen. Defrost them in a fridge first."]]},"3915498":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 190°C / fan 170°C / gas mark 5. Put olive oil into a flameproof casserole dish and place over a medium heat on the hob. Season chicken with black pepper and cook until sealed on each side. Transfer to a plate for later."],[null,"Add the peppers into dish and cook for 3 to 4 minutes, then add shallots, garlic and chillies. Cook for a further 5 minutes until softened. Stir in orzo and paprika."],[null,"Pour the stock over and an additional 200ml of boiling water to completely cover the orzo. Place the chicken and tomatoes on top of the orzo and bake in oven for 30 minutes."],[null,"Serve in bowls, topped with the crème fraîche and chopped parsley if desired."]],"h":[["Chef's note","An easy, mid-week supper dish, suitable for all stages of kidney disease."],["Carbohydrate","The orzo (pasta) is the main source of carbohydrate in this recipe, and the value has been provided for those who have been trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","This recipe is low in potassium, when following the quantities in the ingredients, and the serving sizes. The recipe is also low in phosphate, however it does contain some phosphate, mainly provided by the chicken, so if you have been prescribed a phosphate binder, you should take as directed."],["Protein","This recipe is high in protein, therefore suitable for those advised to eat more protein, such as those receiving dialysis. If you have been advised to eat less protein, you may wish to reduce the chicken and add a tin of chickpeas. This would also lower the potassium and phosphate content."],["Storage","This dish is best eaten freshly made."],["Tips","Uncooked rice can be used in place of orzo if your supermarket doesn’t stock it."]]},"2996":{"s":[[null,"Heat oven to 350° F. Spray a 1-1/2-quart baking dish with nonstick cooking spray."],[null,"Chop bell pepper and onion."],[null,"In a large saucepan, heat olive oil and butter over low heat."],[null,"After butter is melted, stir in flour and black pepper. Cook over low heat, stirring until mixture is smooth and bubbly. Remove from heat."],[null,"Stir in Worcestershire sauce, broth and milk. Heat to a boil, stirring constantly. Boil and stir for one minute."],[null,"Stir in cooked rice, chicken, mushrooms, bell pepper, onion and Mrs. Dash herb seasoning."],[null,"Pour into baking dish. Cover and bake for 30 minutes. Remove cover and continue cooking for 20 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Portion leftovers and freeze to reheat later for a quick meal."],[null,"For variation, substitute 2 cups frozen mixed vegetables for bell peppers and mushrooms."],[null,"Reduce or increase the amount of poultry for a lower or higher protein meal."],[null,"Substitute turkey for chicken if desired."]]},"6600449":{"s":[[null,"Heat a small nonstick skillet over medium heat. Coat both sides of the chicken with cooking spray and cook 4 minutes on each side, or until no longer pink in the center. Place on cutting board, let cool 2–3 minutes, and chop."],[null,"Meanwhile, combine the remaining ingredients, except the lettuce leaves, in a bowl."],[null,"To assemble, line each leaf with the chopped chicken and top with the red pepper mixture."]],"h":[]},"7356307":{"s":[[null,"Squeeze 1 wedge of lemon over the chicken. Place the chicken in a pan and just cover with boiling water. Add a lid and simmer for 5–6 minutes."],[null,"Turn off the heat and leave with the lid on for another 5 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the soya beans, salad leaves and spring onions to your container. Next, add the cucumber, tomato and cress."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix together the yogurt and tahini, and place in a small container with a leak-proof lid."],[null,"Drain the chicken, allow to cool and then slice."],[null,"Arrange the chicken on top of the salad. Serve with the second wedge of lemon, a sprinkle of sesame seeds and a pinch of black pepper. Pop the lid on and pack with the tahini dressing, if eating this salad on the go."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"7805110":{"s":[[null,"Put the rice in a small saucepan with 75ml of boiling water, cover and cook for 10 minutes. Leave to stand with the lid on for a further 5 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the oil to a saucepan, add the onion and cook for 3-4 minutes."],[null,"Add the chicken strips and chopped peppers. Stir for 4 minutes until the chicken is cooked."],[null,"Add the garlic, chilli, cumin and oregano. Mix together for another minute. Stir in the spinach and the cooked rice. Mix well."],[null,"Warm the tortillas in a dry frying pan or in the microwave for 30 seconds. Lay them out on a board and spread the centre of each tortilla with the cream cheese. Divide the chicken and rice mixture between them and roll up, tucking in the sides, to form a neat parcel. Roll the parcel up tightly in foil, twisting the ends so they are easy to hold. Serve with salad."]],"h":[[null,"For a vegetarian burrito, use mushrooms instead of chicken."],[null,"You could use strips of turkey or beef with this dish instead of chicken."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"6029519":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350 degrees F. Spray a large metal or glass baking dish with cooking spray."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine spinach, garlic, cumin, cilantro, pepper, and cheddar cheese; mix to incorporate. Add shredded chicken; mix to incorporate."],[null,"Scoop 1/4 cup chicken-spinach mixture into a tortilla. Roll tortilla and place seam side down in a baking dish. Repeat process for remaining 11 tortillas."],[null,"Pour enchilada sauce over tortillas. Bake 25 minutes."]],"h":[]},"1721":{"s":[[null,"Prepare bow-tie pasta per package instructions without adding salt. Drain."],[null,"Dice chicken. Melt 2 tablespoons butter in a skillet over medium heat. Add chicken and cook until chicken is no longer pink inside."],[null,"Add frozen squash to the skillet with chicken. Heat through."],[null,"Add Mrs. Dash® Table Blend seasoning and salt to chicken and squash."],[null,"Stir cooked pasta into chicken mixture. Add 1 tablespoon butter and stir until melted."],[null,"Divide into 4 portions and sprinkle each serving with 1/2 tablespoon grated Parmesan cheese before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Use fresh summer squash when in season. Cook until tender before adding to chicken."],[null,"Salt is optional. If omitted sodium is 76 mg per serving."],[null,"Adjust the amount of chicken for a high- or low-protein diet."],[null,"Refrigerate leftover portions for a quick meal over the next few days or freeze for later."]]},"2587":{"s":[[null,"To make the marinade, measure the peach jam into a small microwave safe bowl and heat for 10 to 15 seconds to liquefy. Add the olive oil, lemon juice, Mrs. Dash® herb seasoning and salt. Stir until well blended."],[null,"Rinse the chicken thighs and pat dry with a paper towel. Cut each thigh into 4 pieces and place in a zip-top bag."],[null,"Add 3 tablespoons marinade to the chicken pieces. (Reserve 2 tablespoons marinade to use on vegetables.) Seal the zip-top bag and refrigerate to marinate."],[null,"Cut the vegetables into even bite-sized pieces for the kebabs (zucchini-8 slices; yellow squash-8 slices; red pepper-16 pieces; onion-varies). Place them in a medium bowl and add reserved marinade. Stir to coat the vegetable pieces."],[null,"Thread the vegetables and chicken pieces onto skewers (4 large or 8 small skewers)."],[null,"Heat the grill to medium heat. Place the skewers on the grill and cook covered for 12 to 15 minutes. Turn the skewers 2 or 3 times to cook evenly."]],"h":[[null,"To prevent the kebabs from sticking to the grill, use tongs to wipe grates with an oily paper towel before placing the kebabs on grill."],[null,"For a lower or higher protein diet decrease or increase the amount of chicken."]]},"3281":{"s":[[null,"Heat oven to 350 °F."],[null,"Coat a 3-quart, rectangular baking dish with non-stick spray. Set the dish aside."],[null,"Cook noodles according to package directions omitting salt. Drain, rinse with cold water, and set aside."],[null,"Cut chicken into bite-sized pieces."],[null,"Spray a large skillet with cooking spray and place over medium heat. Cook chicken pieces for 3 minutes or until chicken is no longer pink."],[null,"Transfer chicken to a large bowl."],[null,"Add onion, pepper, broccoli and carrots to skillet. Cook and stir until veggies are tender."],[null,"Dump veggies into bowl with chicken and stir in broth, dry mustard, pepper and noodles."],[null,"Spoon mixture into baking dish."],[null,"Mix bread crumbs and melted butter together. Sprinkle over chicken mixture."],[null,"Bake, covered, for 30 minutes. Uncover and bake an additional 30 minutes, until heated through."]],"h":[[null,"When cooking veggies in skillet, add 1 tablespoon of cooking oil, if needed."],[null,"Serve with a tossed salad and red wine vinegar dressing, plus a dinner roll with unsalted butter."],[null,"A delicious beverage choice is apple or cranberry juice (not calcium fortified or enriched) or fresh brewed iced tea with lemon."],[null,"Extra portions freeze well for a quick meal later."]]},"3501639":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oven to 190°C / fan 170°C / gas mark 5 and bring a large saucepan of water to boil. Peel and dice the celeriac, sweet potatoes and carrots. Trim, clean and slice the leeks. Dice the chicken into equal size pieces."],[null,"Add the sweet potatoes and vegetables to the saucepan of boiling water. Boil for 10-15 minutes, drain and discard the water. Heat the olive oil in a frying pan and fry the chicken until cooked."],[null,"Add the drained vegetables to the chicken and add the vegetable stock. Simmer on a low heat for 5 minutes."],[null,"Stir together the crème fraîche with the flour and mustard. Stir into the chicken and vegetables until thickened, then add the sage. Remove from the heat."],[null,"For the crumble, use your fingertips to rub the butter, flour and ground almonds together until they resemble breadcrumbs. Grate and stir in the parmesan and add the flaked almonds."],[null,"Spoon the chicken and vegetable filling into an ovenproof dish and scatter the crumble on top. To cook, bake in the oven for 30-35 minutes until golden brown on top."]],"h":[["Chef's note","This savoury crumble is delicious with a creamy chicken and vegetable filling and a crunchy, cheesy topping. Great for a family meal and suitable for home freezing."],["Carbohydrate","The carbohydrate in this dish mainly comes from the sweet potato and the flour. The carbohydrate values have been provided for those trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","Nuts are high in both phosphate and potassium but in the quantities used here almonds can still be included for a crunchy crumble topping. If you have been prescribed a phosphate binder ensure you take them with this dish. Boiling the vegetables and discarding the water helps to remove some of the potassium. Celeriac is often avoided due to its high potassium content but when boiled and used in the quantities provided it can be included on a low potassium diet."],["Protein","The chicken in this dish provides protein and makes it a good choice if you are on dialysis. For those who have been advised to reduce their protein intake, why not try the vegetable crumble recipe."],["Gluten free","Use gluten-free flour in the crumble and cornflour in the sauce."],["Healthier option","There is no added salt in this recipe but It is slightly above the range to be classified a low salt dish. To reduce the fat content of this dish use a low fat margarine in place of butter."],["Storage","This recipe can be frozen before baking in the oven by wrapping in cling film, then foil. To defrost, thaw overnight in the fridge and bake for 30-35 minutes as above."],["Tips","Try grating the butter straight from the refrigerator. It's a quick and easy way to make perfect crumbs in moments!"]]},"3563134":{"s":[[null,"Marinate chicken pieces in yoghurt, chilli powder, garam masala and turmeric for 30 minutes."],[null,"Wash the rice, put into a pan with double the amount of water, bring to boil, put lid on and turn heat down. Simmer for 10 minutes until cooked, checking to add more water if needed."],[null,"Heat oil over a medium heat and fry onion until light brown."],[null,"Add the tomatoes, ginger and garlic and fry for 1 to 2 minutes until onions and tomatoes are well mixed, then add vegetables and fry for a minute."],[null,"Add the marinated chicken and stir well so the chicken mixes with the onion, tomatoes and vegetables. Reduce heat to low, cover with a lid and let chicken and vegetables cook for 20 minutes."],[null,"Once the chicken is cooked, add in freshly chopped coriander and serve warm with rice."]],"h":[["Chef's note","This Indian-style, high-protein curry is perfect for batch cooking."],["Carbohydrate","Rice is the main source of carbohydrate in this recipe, and the value has been provided for those who have been trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","Despite some high potassium ingredients, such as tomatoes, this recipe is low in potassium, when following quantities and serving sizes given, and suitable for those advised to lower potassium. It is also low in phosphate, but does contain some, mainly from the chicken, so if you have been prescribed a phosphate binder, take as directed."],["Protein","This recipe is high in protein, therefore suitable for those advised to eat more protein, such as those receiving dialysis. If you have been advised to eat less protein, reduce the quantity of chicken to 100g, or use 400g of tinned and drained chickpeas instead."],["Storage","Store in an airtight container in the fridge for up to 2 days, or freeze (re-heat thoroughly)."],["Tips","Adding 2 to 3 black peppercorns, 1 cinnamon stick and 2 to 3 cloves to the oil before adding the onions enhances the flavour."]]},"6109950":{"s":[[null,"Mix spices in a small bowl and set aside."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine chicken strips, sliced bell peppers, sliced red onion, and seasoning blend."],[null,"Heat a skillet over medium-high heat. Add olive oil and turn the pan to coat the bottom. Cook the seasoned chicken and vegetables until the chicken is fully cooked and the vegetables are tender-crisp, about 5–7 minutes."],[null,"Divide cauliflower rice among four bowls. Top with the cooked chicken and vegetable mixture."],[null,"Add cherry tomatoes and sliced avocado to each bowl."]],"h":[]},"3815833":{"s":[[null,"Make the white sauce by melting the butter in a small pan over a medium heat and then whisk in the cornflour and nutmeg, cooking for 2 minutes. Slowly add the milk and chicken stock whilst continuously whisking to avoid any lumps. Keep over a medium heat until it has thickened. Remove from the heat and set aside."],[null,"Heat half of the olive oil in a frying pan over a medium high heat and cook the chicken until it is browned all over. Remove from the pan and set aside. Heat the remaining oil in the pan and cook the onion and carrot until soft, adding in the garlic and oregano and cook for a further 2 minutes. Put the spinach leaves into a separate saucepan and pour a little boiling water over the top. Simmer for 1 minute, or until all the spinach is wilted, then remove from the heat. Drain the spinach using a colander, then rinse with cold water and squeeze out the excess water. Add the tomatoes, spinach and chicken to the frying pan with carrots and onion, bring to a simmer and cook for 5 minutes."],[null,"Heat the oven to 180°C/gas mark 6. Spread a third of the white sauce at the bottom of a baking dish, topped with half of the chicken mix. Place 4 ½ sheets of lasagne topped with another third of the white sauce and rest of chicken mix. Followed by remainder of lasagne and topped off with white sauce. Sprinkle over the mozzarella. Cook for 40 minutes."],[null,"Make the dressing by adding all the ingredients to a bowl and whisking together."],[null,"Remove the lasagne from the oven and serve with the mixed salad and dressing."]],"h":[["Chef's note","A healthy twist on a classic lasange, this delicious recipe is perfect for the whole family."],["Portion size guidance for children","Serving sizes are based on adult portions. Here is a guide for children:\nToddler (age 1-4): ¼ adult portion\nYoung child (age 5-9): ½ adult portion\nOlder child (age 10-13): ¾ adult portion\nTeenagers (14+): 1 adult portion\nSome children do have bigger appetites than others. You child’s portion may need to be changed to fit their typical diet if you think the recommended serving sizes are too large or small. We would advise speaking with your dietitian prior to increasing the serving size if your child has struggled to manage potassium or phosphate."],["Carbohydrate","The lasagne sheets are the main source of carbohydrate in this recipe, and the value has been provided for those who have been trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","Despite the use of some high potassium ingredients, such as spinach and tomatoes, this recipe is low in potassium, when following the quantities in the ingredients, the cooking method and the serving sizes. Therefore, suitable for those advised to lower potassium in their diet.\nThis recipe is also low in phosphate, however it does contain some phosphate, mainly provided by the chicken, milk and cheese, therefore if you have been prescribed a phosphate binder you should take as directed. To lower the phosphate further, you could consider reducing the quantity of cheese in the recipe."],["Protein","This recipe is high in protein, therefore suitable for those advised to eat more protein, such as those receiving dialysis. If you have been advised to eat less protein then you may wish to reduce the chicken quantity to 150g and try adding more vegetables like courgette, carrots and broccoli."],["Energy","If you need to gain weight, have a growing child who needs more calories, or have a poor appetite, you can add more butter to make the white sauce or use whole milk to increase the calories."],["Gluten free","Use gluten-free lasagne"],["Vegetarian","Consider using 300-400g tofu or soya meat to replace the chicken for a vegetarian option."],["Vegan","Consider using non-dairy alternatives for butter, milk and cheese."],["Healthier option","Consider using wholewheat lasagne sheets for healthier option."],["Cheaper option","This recipe has been kept as low in cost as possible."],["Storage","Once cooked and cooled, this recipe can be stored in the fridge and reheated the following day. Ensure it is piping hot when reheating."]]},"6629566":{"s":[[null,"Add the oil to a large soup pot or dutch oven and heat over medium-high heat. Add the chicken and sear for 4 minutes on each side. Remove the chicken from the pan and set aside."],[null,"Add the carrots, celery, and mushrooms to the same pot and sauté over medium-high heat for 5 minutes."],[null,"Add the remaining ingredients and add the chicken back to the pot. Bring to a boil; reduce the heat and simmer for 45 minutes."],[null,"Remove the chicken from the pot and shred or cut up. Add the chicken back to the pot; stir."]],"h":[]},"3640":{"s":[[null,"Cook the pasta according to package instructions, omitting salt."],[null,"Meanwhile, chop the onion, garlic cloves and watercress. Heat the oil in a skillet and sauté the onion and garlic. Add the shredded chicken and watercress. Mix well and cook until the watercress is wilted."],[null,"Once the pasta is cooked, drain and add the chicken mixture and half the béchamel sauce. Mix well."],[null,"Place the mixture into a baking dish sprayed with cooking spray. Cover with the remaining béchamel sauce. Sprinkle with the Parmesan cheese and bake 30 to 40 minutes until golden brown."]],"h":[[null,"Béchamel sauce is a basic white sauce."]]},"6349071":{"s":[[null,"Melt the margarine in a large soup pot over medium-high heat. Add the onion and sauté for 3 minutes or until clear. Add the carrots, celery, and mushrooms, and sauté for 5 minutes."],[null,"Add the chicken broth, water, thyme, black pepper, and salt."],[null,"In a small cup, mix together the corn starch and 1 Tbsp. cold water. Add the mixture to the soup."],[null,"Bring to a boil and stir in the rice."],[null,"Reduce heat, cover, and simmer for 45 minutes. Add the cooked chicken and stir well."]],"h":[]},"3456":{"s":[[null,"Cube cooked chicken. Dice apple and celery. Chop scallions."],[null,"Combine chicken, apple, celery, scallions and raisins in a large salad bowl."],[null,"Whisk together mayonnaise, sour cream, lemon juice, cinnamon and black pepper. Pour over the chicken-apple mixture and toss."],[null,"Refrigerate to chill prior to serving."]],"h":[[null,"The raisins can be eliminated to reduce potassium content to 270 mg per serving."],[null,"Spoon chicken salad in a pita pocket to serve as a sandwich or serve on top of leaf lettuce to make a salad."]]},"6190468":{"s":[[null,"Cube cooked chicken. Dice apple and celery. Chop scallions"],[null,"Combine chicken, apple, celery, scallions, and raisins in a large salad bowl."],[null,"Whisk together mayonnaise, sour cream, lemon juice, cinnamon, and black pepper. Pour over the chicken-apple mixture and toss."],[null,"Refrigerate to chill prior to serving."]],"h":[]},"7007009":{"s":[[null,"Add the oil to a pan, followed by the onion, and cook for 3–4 minutes until softened. Add the chicken and cook for 2–3 minutes."],[null,"Add the pepper, carrot and celery, and cook for 3–4 minutes, stirring regularly."],[null,"Add the garlic, curry powder and garam masala, and stir well to coat everything in the spices."],[null,"Add the chilli, tomatoes and tomato purée, and bring to a gentle boil."],[null,"Cover and simmer for 12–14 minutes until the carrot is tender. Mix in the coriander and serve."]],"h":[[null,"We’ve used curry powder – unlike curry paste, it doesn’t have added salt or fat."],[null,"You could use cubes of lamb for this dish. For a vegetarian/vegan version, replace the chicken with a tin of chickpeas or mixed beans."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"7793516":{"s":[[null,"Add the sunflower oil to a pan with the onion, cook for 2 minutes, then add the chicken and stir for a further 3-4 minutes."],[null,"Add the red pepper, carrot, mushrooms and aubergine, and cook for a further 5 minutes, stirring regularly."],[null,"Stir in the curry paste and sultanas, and mix well."],[null,"Next, add the rice to the vegetables, mixing well. Then, add the boiling water and mix again. Bring to the boil, then turn the heat to low. Cover and cook for 11 minutes."],[null,"Turn off the heat and leave for 5 minutes without removing the lid."],[null,"Add the peas, coriander and olive oil to the rice. Mix well and serve."]],"h":[[null,"For a veggie version, add an extra pepper, a chopped courgette and a can of chickpeas."],[null,"You could also use turkey, prawns or salmon instead of chicken."],[null,"You could also substitute some of the meat with beans - these are packed with protein and fibre and are cheaper too."],[null,"If you don’t have an aubergine, simply add in some extra mushrooms and carrots."],[null,"You don’t need to have the coriander either, it will be just as tasty without."],[null,"If you don't have rice to hand, why not try quinoa or whole grain couscous."],[null,"Suitable for freezing once cooked. Then defrost in the fridge and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"7309643":{"s":[[null,"Add oil to a large pan."],[null,"Add the chicken and cook for 4-5 minutes, stirring occasionally, until lightly brown all over."],[null,"Add the garlic and cook for 2 minutes, then add the tomatoes, puree, paprika and chilli. Bring to a gentle boil then turn down the heat, add a lid and simmer for 10 minutes, stirring regularly. Remove the lid, stir well and gently simmer until almost all the liquid has evaporated and is thoroughly coating the chicken."],[null,"Arrange the lettuce around the side of a serving dish, pile the chicken cubes into the middle with cocktail sticks to skewer the chicken cubes."]],"h":[[null,"Simmer the dish gently at the end as the aim is not to create a sauce, but a rich coating for the chicken."],[null,"You could make this with firm fish rather than chicken. For a vegetarian version, try with tofu."]]},"6048241":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6670382":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6292540":{"s":[],"h":[]},"4893714":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, prepare the chipotle cream sauce by whisking together yogurt, lime juice, chipotle chili powder, and garlic. Set aside."],[null,"Rub chicken thighs with olive oil and sprinkle with chili and garlic powder, ground pepper, and paprika. Heat the barbecue or grill pan on the stove on medium heat. Grill the chicken until it reaches an internal temperature of 165°F degrees. Let it cool."],[null,"In a large saucepan, cook rice according to package instructions and let it cool."],[null,"Divide rice into 6 bowls. Top with sliced chicken, black beans, corn and tomatoes. Sprinkle lime juice over top. Drizzle with chipotle cream sauce and top with chopped cilantro. Serve with extra lime wedges."]],"h":[[null,"Tip: For a variation, try this recipe with chopped green onions, jalapeno peppers, or red bell peppers."],["Ways to increase plant-based protein","Recommendations for a kidney-friendly diet have changed a lot over recent years. In the past, foods like beans, legumes, nuts, nut butters, seeds and whole grains were discouraged due to their high phosphorus content. We have learned that while these foods contain more phosphorus, the amount that your body absorbs from them is quite low. This is called the bioavailability of phosphorus. In other words, when you eat these foods, not 100% of the phosphorus ends up in your blood, but rather a much lower percentage of 40% or less. Since the absorption of phosphorus from these foods is low, they can be part of a kidney-friendly diet. Not only is this good news because it adds more variety to the diet, but it is also healthy. Plant-based protein is adding fiber and micronutrients, which are helpful in slowing the progression of kidney disease. There are several ways that you can add these foods to your diet. You can decrease the amount of animal protein in recipes by substituting all or part of that ingredient with tofu, beans or legumes. You can also prepare grain bowls at home using a base of brown rice, bulgar or quinoa and top with either tofu, beans or legumes and healthy vegetables."]]},"7215311":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200°C/gas 6. Heat the oil in a saucepan add the chicken and leeks and fry for 4-5 minutes until the chicken begins to brown."],[null,"Stir in the flour and 450ml of the milk, bring to the boil and stir until thickened. Stir in the tarragon half the cheese and the butter beans and season well. Tip into an ovenproof dish."],[null,"Mix together the mashed potato, remaining milk, butter and the remaining cheese and pipe or spoon over the chicken mixture."],[null,"Place the pie in the oven and cook for 20-25 minutes until golden and bubbling."]],"h":[[null,"Try using sweet potato rather than ordinary potato as it counts as one of your 5 a day."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"3162079":{"s":[[null,"Shred the cooked chicken into strips and add to a bowl with the chopped lettuce leaves and crushed garlic."],[null,"Shave thin slices of the parmesan into the bowl, then add the mayonnaise and Worcestershire sauce and stir gently to combine, seasoning with pepper."],[null,"To assemble the wraps, spoon ¼ of the mixture onto the bottom half of a tortilla. Fold the bottom of the tortilla up and over the filling."],[null,"Make two folds on either side and roll it up tightly. Repeat with the remaining three tortillas. Eat whole or cut in half to serve immediately, or wrap in foil to keep whole until you want to eat it."]],"h":[["Chef's note","The classic Caesar salad has been reworked into a wrap, which makes the perfect quick lunch or light dinner."],["Carbohydrate","The main source of carbohydrate in this dish comes from the tortilla wrap. The carbohydrate value of this dish has been provided for those who have been trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","If you stick to the serving sizes provided in this recipe, this dish is low in both potassium and phosphate. Both the chicken and Parmesan cheese contain phosphate, but the small portion used in this recipe keeps the overall phosphate content low. If you have been prescribed a phosphate binder, ensure you take them with this dish."],["Protein","The chicken and cheese used in this recipe provide a source of protein which is great for people receiving dialysis and anyone who needs to eat more protein."],["Gluten free","Use gluten-free tortilla wraps."],["Vegetarian","Use meat-free chicken-style pieces or chickpeas instead. Check that your Parmesan cheese is suitable for vegetarians."],["Vegan","Use meat-free chicken-style pieces or chickpeas instead. Use a suitable dairy-free mayonnaise and dairy-free hard Italian-style cheese."],["Healthier option","There is no added salt in this recipe. The Parmesan cheese, Worcestershire sauce, mayonnaise, and tortilla wraps do contain salt, which makes this recipe slightly above the range to be classified as a low salt dish. To minimize the salt content, choose wraps with the lowest salt content. Measure the Worcestershire sauce, mayonnaise, and Parmesan cheese to avoid adding too much. To lower the salt content even further, you could consider using a teaspoon of lemon juice to replace the Worcestershire sauce and some natural yoghurt in place of the mayonnaise.\nIf you would like to lower the fat in this dish, choose a light mayonnaise.\nUsing a wholemeal wrap will increase the fibre in your diet."],["Storage","Once made, keep in the fridge and use within two days. When packing for lunch, we recommend using a cool pack to keep it chilled."],["Tips","If you don’t need four portions, you can scale the recipe down."]]},"7359452":{"s":[[null,"Heat a large non-stick saucepan and fry the chicken breasts until brown on each side. You can add a small amount of water into the pan if the chicken is sticking to the pan."],[null,"Add the onion, garlic and peppers and continue to fry for 2–3 minutes."],[null,"Add the chopped tomatoes, chicken stock, beans, tomato puree, freshly ground pepper and herbs."],[null,"Stir well, bring to the boil, cover and simmer gently for 40–45 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"This dish also works well with turkey."],[null,"You could use mixed beans or chickpeas instead of borlotti beans if you prefer."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"6085562":{"s":[[null,"Coat a 3 1/2- to 4-quart slow cooker with cooking spray. Place the water, chicken, onion, rice, garlic, chicken bouillon, and thyme in the slow cooker. Cover and cook on high for 1 1/2 hours or on low for 3 hours."],[null,"Turn off the heat. Fluff the rice with a fork. Stir in the asparagus. Cover and let stand 10 minutes. Stir in the salt and sprinkle with the cheese."]],"h":[]},"2851":{"s":[[null,"Chop garlic, onion, celery, carrots and green pepper. Dice cooked chicken."],[null,"Pour oil in a large stock pot."],[null,"Sauté garlic, onion, celery, carrot and green pepper until soft."],[null,"Add low-sodium broth and bring to a boil."],[null,"Drain tomatoes. Drain and rinse kidney beans."],[null,"Add chicken, beans, tomatoes, salsa, chili powder and oregano to sauted vegetables. Simmer for 1 hour."],[null,"Serve 1-cup chili over 1/2-cup white rice. Top each serving with 1 tablespoon grated sharp cheddar cheese and 1 tablespoon sour cream."]],"h":[[null,"1-1/2 punds cooked chicken is approximately 3 cups. If you wish, use a stewing chicken or a pre-cooked rotisserie chicken. Pull meat from bones and chop."],[null,"Compare brands and buy the lowest sodium canned and bottled ingredients."],[null,"Freeze 1 cup portions for a quick meal later."],[null,"Recipe is easy to reduce for a smaller batch."],[null,"If you are on a protein-limited diet, adjust this recipe by decreasing the portion of meat and cheese."]]},"4909485":{"s":[[null,"Turn slow cooker to low temperature setting. Add chicken to the base of the slow cooker. Add jalapenos, minced garlic, celery, onion, red pepper and corn."],[null,"In a measuring cup, whisk together chicken broth, flour, cumin, chili powder and oregano. Pour over chicken and vegetable mixture. Add lime juice and cilantro."],[null,"Cover and cook on low for 4 to 6 hours, until chicken is cooked and tender and stew is slightly thickened. If you choose to use the oven: preheat to 225°F and cook for 4 hours. Add additional time to add more tenderness, if you like."],[null,"After cooking is completed, remove the stew from the heat source."],[null,"Cook rice according to instructions on the package."],[null,"Fold in the cooked white rice and sour cream into the stew. Serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"* Look for low- or reduced-sodium broth containing 200mg sodium or less per 1 cup serving. Avoid low-sodium broth that contains potassium chloride because it is very high in potassium."],[null,"PLEASE NOTE: This recipe is higher in potassium and portion size is important. Check with your registered dietitian to see how this recipe can be included in your diet."],["Chicken as a protein choice","Protein is a necessary part of your diet with chronic kidney disease (CKD). In early stages of CKD, your protein intake should be approximately 12 to 15% of total calories. As CKD progresses, your dietitian may recommend you lower your protein intake. Meeting with a renal dietitian can help you determine the amount of protein your body needs. Chicken is a good source of protein and also low in potassium, making it a good choice for people with CKD. Fresh chicken is readily available in your grocery store. This food item can be diced and cooked as part of an omelet, grilled as an entree, or cooked and shredded in salads. Frozen chicken is a second option. While handy to use in recipes with limited cooking time, read labels to avoid any addition of high-sodium or high-potassium preservatives. Canned chicken is a third option. It is important to remember, the liquid found in canned meat is usually high in sodium. Canned meats that are low in sodium may be high in potassium so it's always important to read the Nutrition Facts label and the list of ingredients."]]},"7684396":{"s":[[null,"Add the sunflower oil to a large pan or wok, then add the onion and cookfor 2 minutes."],[null,"Next, add the chicken and stir constantly for 3-4 minutes, making sure the pieces don't stick together."],[null,"Add the carrots, mushrooms and courgette. Cook for a further 3-4 minutes, again, stirring constantly."],[null,"Next, add the soya beans, Chinese five-spice, soy sauce, garlic and noodles."],[null,"Mix well for another 3-4 minutes until the noodles are hot through."]],"h":[[null,"For a gluten-free alternative, use rice noodles and gluten-free tamari."],[null,"You could swap out the soya beans for chickpeas or frozen green beans."],[null,"Go veggie by using marinated tofu pieces instead of chicken."],[null,"This recipe would also work well with turkey instead of chicken."],[null,"Shiitake mushrooms are a natural flavour enhancer and far healthier than the monosodium glutamate used in many Chinese takeaways."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"6001732":{"s":[[null,"Preheat a grill or grill pan over medium-high heat."],[null,"In a bowl, mix the olive oil, dried oregano, garlic powder, salt, and black pepper."],[null,"Brush the chicken breasts with the olive oil mixture."],[null,"Grill the chicken for about 6-8 minutes per side or until fully cooked to an internal temperature of 165 degrees F."],[null,"Allow the chicken to rest for a few minutes before slicing it into strips."],[null,"In a large bowl, arrange the mixed salad greens, halved cherry tomatoes, diced cucumber, finely sliced red onion, diced avocado, and sliced Kalamata olives."],[null,"Arrange the sliced grilled chicken on top of the salad."],[null,"Add the sliced hard-boiled eggs."],[null,"Drizzle the salad with Balsamic vinaigrette."]],"h":[]},"6064401":{"s":[[null,"Heat a skillet over medium heat. Add the diced chicken breast, paprika, ⅛ tsp salt, and pepper. Sauté until the chicken is fully cooked to an internal temperature of 165 degrees F and golden brown. Remove from the heat and set aside."],[null,"To make the dressing, combine the Greek yogurt, dill, chives, parsley, garlic powder, onion powder, black pepper, rice vinegar, water, and remaining ¼ tsp salt, in a blender or food processor and pulse until smooth."],[null,"Divide the lettuce between 4 bowls. Top with the chicken, turkey bacon, tomatoes, avocado, and egg whites. Drizzle with the dressing."]],"h":[]},"1687":{"s":[[null,"In a large pot over medium heat, cook chicken in about 8 cups water. When chicken is cooked, remove from broth and cool. Reserve broth."],[null,"Cook noodles according to package instructions, but omit the salt. Drain and set aside."],[null,"Skim fat from chicken broth."],[null,"Chop chicken into bite-sized pieces."],[null,"Place chopped chicken, 6 cups reserved chicken broth, and 6 cups water in a 6-quart kettle."],[null,"Add drained corn, cooked noodles, parsley, and pepper into kettle. Stir and simmer until hot."]],"h":[[null,"Recipe analysis includes regular canned corn and unsalted chicken broth. Unsalted canned corn will reduce sodium to 101 mg per serving."],[null,"Enjoy a 2 cup serving as a main entrée or reduce to 1 cup of soup as an appetizer or snack."],[null,"A 2 cup portion provides 1 cup of liquid and 1 cup of solids."],[null,"If you are on a lower protein diet use only half the chicken meat which is approximately 2 cups."]]},"5242322":{"s":[[null,"Cover the uncooked chicken with lemon juice."],[null,"Mix the seasoning together and rub onto the chicken."],[null,"Allow to marinate in the refrigerator for 1 hour (or preferably overnight)."],[null,"Add the cup of water to the pan and simmer until fully cooked and tender."],[null,"Serve over hot rice."]],"h":[]},"6242322":{"s":[[null,"Spray a medium slow cooker for 1 second with cooking spray. Place the onion, red bell pepper, and cauliflower into the slow cooker."],[null,"Heat a large skillet over medium high heat. Spray the skillet for 1 second with cooking spray. Place the chicken in the skillet and cook just until browned, turn and brown the second side. Place the chicken over the vegetables in the slow cooker."],[null,"Sprinkle the chicken with the curry powder, garlic, paprika, cumin and salt. Pour the light coconut milk and broth overall. Cover and cook on Low for 3 to 5 hours or until the chicken is fully cooked and the chicken reaches a temperature of 165 F."],[null,"About an hour before serving, prepare the rice using the package directions, omitting the salt and margarine."],[null,"Using a slotted spoon, lift the chicken breasts out of the slow cooker and place on a cutting board. Turn the slow cooker to High. Blend the cornstarch into the cold water, blending until smooth. Stir the cornstarch mixture into the slow cooker. Cover and allow to cook about 15 minutes or until thickened and bubbly, stirring occasionally."],[null,"When the chicken is cool enough to handle, cut the chicken into bitesize pieces. Stir the chicken back into the slow cooker and allow to heat through."],[null,"To serve, spoon the hot cooked brown rice onto each plate. Top with the chicken curry. Sprinkle the top of each serving with 2 tablespoons chopped tomatoes, 1 tablespoon chopped green bell pepper and 2 teaspoons minced cilantro."],[null,"Cook’s Tip on Curry Powder: Curry powder is a combination of several spices and herbs, including coriander, cumin, turmeric, cloves, and chilies. Those curry powders labeled as madras are hot, but if you are unsure, or using a brand you are not familiar with, you might add about half the curry powder listed in the recipe the first time you make it. Then, you can taste the dish near the end of cooking and add additional seasoning, as desired."],[null,"Cook’s Tip on Coconut Milk: Coconut milk is available canned and is typically shelved with the Asian foods in most larger grocery stores. For this recipe, light coconut milk is used. Do not confuse coconut milk with cream of coconut that is used when making cocktails. Stir the coconut milk well before measuring. Once open, you can cover the coconut milk and store it in the refrigerator for up to about one week."],[null,"Electric Pressure Cooker Variation: Heat the pressure cooker on the sauté setting. Add 1 teaspoon olive oil and sear the chicken breasts until well browned on both sides. Turn the pressure cooker off. Add the vegetables, seasonings, coconut milk and broth. Secure the cover and cook on High Pressure for 6 minutes. Quickly release the pressure. Remove the chicken breasts with a slotted spoon. Blend the cornstarch in the cold water and blend into the curry as directed above. Cook on the sauté setting, stirring frequently until bubbly and thickened. Cut the chicken breasts into cubes and stir into the curry. Proceed as the recipe directs."]],"h":[]},"1821":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375° F."],[null,"Heat oil in a skillet."],[null,"Quickly dip each tortilla into skillet to soften, and then remove to a plate."],[null,"In the center of each tortilla place 1/4-cup shredded chicken, 1-tablespoon onion and 2-teaspoons sour cream."],[null,"Roll up and place each enchilada in a baking dish."],[null,"Cover with 1-1/2 cups enchilada sauce."],[null,"Place baking dish in the oven and heat for 20 to 30 minutes or until hot."]],"h":[[null,"Top enchilada with additional spoonful of sour cream before serving if desired."]]},"3006":{"s":[[null,"Prepare Salsa Verde and Flour Tortillas recipes."],[null,"In a large pot, place chicken breast, broth and garlic cloves. Poach chicken for 30 minutes on medium-low heat."],[null,"Remove chicken from pot and in a separate container shred chicken using 2 forks. Set aside."],[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F. Spray a baking dish with cooking spray."],[null,"Place Salsa Verde in a shallow frying pan and heat on low heat."],[null,"In a separate pan, heat tortillas and transfer into the frying pan. Drench tortillas in salsa one by one; set aside"],[null,"Once all tortillas have been drenched, start assembling the enchiladas by stuffing with chicken and cheese and rolling them so that the seam side is down in the baking dish. (Divide the"],[null,"chicken and cheese equally between the 6 tortillas.) Pour the remaining Salsa Verde over top of enchiladas. Cover dish with foil and heat in the oven for 15 minutes."],[null,"Top each enchilada with 1 tablespoon sour cream. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"For added flavor top enchiladas with chopped onions or cilantro."],[null,"Commercially prepared salsa verde and flour tortillas may be substituted, but sodium will be higher. Look for the lowest sodium brands."],[null,"Most flour tortillas are high in sodium. Lower sodium brands include Tortilla Land® Fresh Ready-to-Cook Tortillas (210 mg sodium), La Banderita® Low Sodium Tortillas (85 mg sodium)."]]},"7534585":{"s":[[null,"Place the chicken breast between pieces of cling film and bash with a mallet/rolling pin to make a flat escalope, approx. 4-5mm thick. Then divide into 2 equal portions."],[null,"Brush the chicken breast pieces with 1 tsp of the oil. Place on a hot frying or griddle pan and cook on each side for 2-3 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, in a small pan heat the remaining tsp oil and add the garlic and spring onions and cook for 2 minutes until the onions are soft. Then add the parsley and stir for 1 minute."],[null,"Add the pepper, lemon juice and 1 tbsp water. Stir in the yogurt."],[null,"Put the chicken on a plate and serve with the sauce."]],"h":[[null,"This works well with turkey or beef escalopes. Or try the sauce with grilled fish."],[null,"The 'bashing' tenderises the meat and makes the fillet much faster to cook so is ideal for barbecues."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"2564038":{"s":[[null,"In a preheated pan add olive oil then add the onion, followed with the sliced bell paper."],[null,"Sauté for about 5 minutes, stirring often, until slightly softened but still vibrant."],[null,"Now, add the chicken breast and stir for 5 minutes on medium low heat."],[null,"Add the spices gradually and stir for more 5 minutes on medium low heat."],[null,"Set aside."],[null,"Bring your Tortilla bread and start filling with lettuce (optional)"],[null,"Stuff you sandwich with the Fajita, Add a squeeze of lemon (optional)"],[null,"In the same pan, add some olive oil and roast your sandwich (3 minutes each side)"]],"h":[]},"3981":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 300° F. Wrap tortillas in foil; heat in oven for 10 minutes."],[null,"Chop the peppers, onion and cilantro. Cut chicken breasts into 1″ strips."],[null,"Place oil in nonstick frying pan over medium heat; add chicken, seasonings and lemon juice. Cook for 3 to 5 minutes."],[null,"Add peppers and onion to frying pan; cook for 3 to 5 minutes more or until chicken is no longer pink and juice run clear. Add cilantro to chicken mixture."],[null,"Divide chicken mixture between tortillas; fold tortillas over."]],"h":[[null,"For a lower protein diet decrease chicken portion to match your meal plan."]]},"3050711":{"s":[[null,"Make the fajita seasoning by mixing all the ingredients together. Add the chicken strips and olive oil and mix until all combined."],[null,"Preheat the air fryer to 190°C in roasting setting. Mix the vegetables and beans in with the chicken and cook for 15 minutes, shaking the basket twice during cooking. This recipe can also be cooked in a frying pan on the hob if preferred. Pan-fry the chicken in the olive oil until browned all over, then add the rest of ingredients and cook over a medium heat for 15 minutes."],[null,"Make the salad dressing by adding all the ingredients to a bowl and whisk together. Add this dressing to the diced cucumber, salad leaves and tomatoes just before serving and combine well."],[null,"Once the chicken fajita mixture is cooked serve it with tortillas, soured cream and guacamole. Serve with the prepared salad on the side."]],"h":[["Chef's note","This quick and easy recipe is perfect for a mid-week supper."],["Portion size guidance for children","Serving sizes are based on adult portions. Here is a guide for children:\nToddler (age 1-4): ¼ adult portion\nYoung child (age 5-9): ½ adult portion\nOlder child (age 10-13): ¾ adult portion\nTeenagers (14+): 1 adult portion\nSome children do have bigger appetites than others. You child’s portion may need to be changed to fit their typical diet if you think the recommended serving sizes are too large or small. We would advise speaking with your dietitian prior to increasing the serving size if your child has struggled to manage potassium or phosphate."],["Carbohydrate","The tortillas are the main source of carbohydrate in this recipe, and the value has been provided for those who have been trained in insulin adjustment."],["Potassium/phosphate","Despite the use of some high potassium ingredients, such as Avocado, this recipe is low in potassium, when following the quantities in the ingredients, the cooking method, and the serving sizes. Therefore, suitable for those advised to lower potassium in their diet. This recipe is also low in phosphate, however it does contain some phosphate, mainly provided by the chicken, tortilla wraps and cheese, therefore if you have been prescribed a phosphate binder you should take as directed.\nTo lower the phosphate further you could consider replacing some or all of the meat with a plant-based alternative, such as 250g timed black beans-drained. However, this will also reduce the protein content of the recipe."],["Protein","This recipe provides a source of protein. If you have been advised to eat less protein, consider reducing chicken to 100g and increasing beans to 200g-250g."],["Energy","If you need to gain weight, have a growing child who needs more calories, or have a poor appetite, you can use a tablespoon of extra oil to cook the chicken. Adding extra meat or cheese to increase calories will increase phosphate content of the recipe."],["Vegetarian","Consider using 200g tempeh or tofu instead of chicken."],["Vegan","Consider using non-dairy sour cream alternatives."],["Gluten free","Use gluten-free tortillas."],["Healthier option","Use wholemeal tortilla wraps."],["Cheaper option","Use vegetable/sunflower oil.\nUse a vinegar that you have in the kitchen.\nIf you don’t have all the spices handy, consider using fajita seasoning mix (check for no added salt versions).\nUse Iceberg lettuce instead of mixed salad leaves.\nUse any smooth mustard of your choice."],["Storage","This dish is best eaten freshly made. Any leftover dressing can be stored in the fridge for up to a week."],["Tips","This can be served with Taco shells or rice as an alternative."],["Tips: making your own guacamole","You can make your own guacamole:\n1 ripe avocado – peeled and pitted and mashed with a fork\n1 red chilli – seeded and finely chopped\njuice of 1 lime\nsmall handful of fresh coriander – finely chopped\n1 small red onion – peeled and finely chopped\nmix all of the ingredients together."]]},"2638":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 300° F. Wrap tortillas in foil; heat in oven for 10 minutes."],[null,"Cut chicken breats into 1″ strips."],[null,"Place oil in nonstick frying pan over medium heat; add chicken, seasonings and lemon juice. Cook for 3 to 5 minutes."],[null,"Add peppers and onion to frying pan; cook for 3 to 5 minutes more or until chicken is no longer pink and juice run clear. Add cilantro to chicken mixture."],[null,"Divide chicken mixture between tortillas; fold tortillas over. Serve each with 1 tablespoon of pineapple salsa."]],"h":[[null,"One serving makes a complete meal."],[null,"Nutritional information is for 2 fajitas plus 2 tablespoons pineapples salsa."],[null,"Adjust the amount of chicken to match your meal plan for a lower or higher protein diet."]]},"6347356":{"s":[[null,"In a large nonstick skillet or wok, heat 1 tablespoon oil over medium-high heat."],[null,"Add minced ginger and garlic, sautéing for about 1 minute until fragrant."],[null,"Add the mixed vegetables, cauliflower rice, soy sauce and sesame oil to the skillet and stir-fry for 7-8 minutes, until cooked through and browned in parts."],[null,"Stir the diced chicken into the skillet."],[null,"Push the mixture to the side of the skillet and add the remaining 1 tablespoon oil in the empty space. Pour the beaten eggs into the empty space. Scramble the eggs until just barely cooked. Mix the eggs into the vegetable and chicken mixture."],[null,"Finish with the green onions."]],"h":[]},"7695929":{"s":[[null,"Cook the rice according to the pack instructions, then drain and spread it out on a non-stick baking tray, so it cools quickly."],[null,"While the rice is cooling, mix together the soy sauce or tamari, lime juice, ginger, garlic and chopped chilli and set aside."],[null,"At the same time, spray a large non-stick wok or frying pan with a couple of pumps of low-calorie cooking spray and put it over a medium-high heat. Add the onion and peppers and stir-fry for 3-4 minutes. Add the chicken and cabbage and cook for a further 3-4 minutes, or until the chicken is cooked through and no pink flesh is visible. (the juices should run clear when you cut into the thickest part of the chicken)."],[null,"When the chicken is nearly cooked, stir in the mangetout, water chestnuts, half the spring onions and all of the soy sauce mixture. Stir-fry for a few minutes, then push everything to one side of the pan. Tip the rice into the empty side, then fry for 2 minutes before mixing everything together and stir-frying until the rice is piping hot. Scatter over the remaining spring onions and sliced chilli to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Use brown basmati rice to increase the fibre."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"2521":{"s":[[null,"Cube cooked chicken. Slice celery and slice grapes into halves. Drain mandarin oranges."],[null,"Cook pasta according to package, omitting the salt. Drain and rinse in cold water to cool. Drain well."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine cooked pasta and all ingredients. Mix well to combine."],[null,"Cover and refrigerate until serving time."]],"h":[[null,"This salad tends to taste better the second day as leftovers."],[null,"Use reduced-fat mayonnaise if desired. Look for the lowest sodium brand."]]},"6014731":{"s":[[null,"In a large skillet, cook the ground chicken, onion, garlic, chili powder, paprika, and pepper over medium heat until meat is browned, about 5–6 minutes."],[null,"Add in the green or red pepper and zucchini and cook over low heat for about 5 minutes, until vegetables are tender. Add the diced tomatoes and BBQ sauce and simmer for 10 minutes."],[null,"Serve the mixture on a toasted bun."]],"h":[]},"6553525":{"s":[[null,"Heat a grill or grill pan over medium-high heat. Coat the chicken with cooking spray, sprinkle with 1/4 teaspoon salt and 1/4 teaspoon pepper, if desired. Cook 6 minutes on each side or until no longer pink in center. Let cool and thinly slice."],[null,"Place equal amounts of the greens and chicken on four dinner plates. Whisk together the salad dressing and ginger until well blended. Spoon equal amounts over all."]],"h":[]},"6833394":{"s":[[null,"To make the tabbouleh: Combine the bulgur wheat, ½ cup of the parsley, mint, 2 cloves of minced garlic, cucumbers, and tomatoes in a large bowl. Mix the lemon juice, lemon zest, and olive oil together in a small bowl. Drizzle the olive oil mixture over the bulgur and vegetables and toss to combine."],[null,"Cover tightly and place in the refrigerator until you are ready to serve. (You can make this ahead. The flavors will intensify as it chills.)"],[null,"To make the chicken kofta: Place the chicken, egg, onion, 2 Tbsp chopped parsley, cumin, black pepper, 1 clove of minced garlic, and breadcrumbs in a large bowl. Mix them together with your hands or a couple of forks until all are well combined and evenly distributed. Divide the mixture and form into 16 small logs or roll into meatball shapes."],[null,"Heat a large non-stick frying pan over medium heat and spray with cooking spray. Once hot, add the chicken rolls and cook on one side until browned. Continue turning to brown all sides and cooked through, about 10 minutes. They should reach an internal temperature of 165 degrees F on an instant-read thermometer."],[null,"Serve 4 kofta rolls on top of one lettuce leaf with 1 1/4 cups of tabbouleh, 2 Tbsp of hummus, and 1 small pita on the side."]],"h":[]},"2982":{"s":[[null,"Chop onion, celery and chicken. Mince garlic and slice the carrot. Heat a 5-quart saucepan over medium heat. Add in olive oil, onion, celery, garlic, and carrot. Sauté about 5 minutes or until vegetables are tender."],[null,"Add in the chicken and 4 cups of the water, Worcestershire sauce, lemon juice, salt, pepper, and rice. Cook 15 minutes over medium heat or until rice is done."],[null,"Add last 4 cups of water and continue cooking until heated through."]],"h":[[null,"Cutting salt back to 1/4 teaspoon will bring the sodium down to 211 mg per serving."],[null,"You may use brown or white rice in this recipe. The brown rice may take a little longer to soften. The brown rice has slightly more potassium and phosphorus, but not all of those minerals will be absorbed by the body."]]},"2246":{"s":[[null,"Mince chicken breast and garlic. Chop scallions, onion, cilantro and mushrooms."],[null,"In a medium skillet combine chicken, scallions, garlic, canola oil, sesame oil, rice vinegar, hoisin sauce and Chinese Five Spices seasoning. Cook over medium-low heat for 15 minutes, stirring several times."],[null,"Remove chicken to a serving bowl. Place 1/4-cup chicken on each lettuce leaf. Top with 1-2 teaspoon each red onion, mushroom, red bell pepper and cilantro or parsley. Wrap lettuce around chicken mixture and pick up to eat."]],"h":[[null,"Hoisin sauce is usually found in the Chinese or Asian food section of most grocery stores. One brand, Sun Luck® hoisin sauce, can be found by searching on Google."],[null,"Chinese five spices is a combination of ground cinnamon, star anise, fennel, ginger, cloves, white pepper and licorice. Dynasty brand Chinese Five Spices® is found in the spice section of most grocery stores. Their address is JFC International Inc., Five Spice Recipes, PO Box 7251, San Francisco, CA 94120."]]},"6024876":{"s":[[null,"Mix the green onion, carrots, peanut sauce, and chicken together in a bowl. Divide the mixture evenly among 6 lettuce leaves."]],"h":[]},"3223":{"s":[[null,"Cook lo mein noodles according to package omitting salt. Drain and set aside."],[null,"Thinly slice chicken breasts."],[null,"Heat olive oil in a wok or big, deep skillet over medium-high heat. Add chicken and sauté for 4 to 5 minutes or until no longer pink."],[null,"Add onions, carrots and celery. Stir-fry gently until vegetables are cooked but still crunchy, about 4 to 5 minutes."],[null,"Add mushrooms and noodles, and stir constantly until hot."],[null,"Add soy sauce, stir and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Linguine or fettuccine can be used instead of lo mein noodles. The nutrient composition is very similar."],[null,"Replace chicken with thin slices of beef for variety."],[null,"Use leftover grilled chicken or beef from a cookout the day before. In step #3, reduce cooking time to 1 to 2 minutes."]]},"6994909":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F. Spray a 2 ½-quart baking dish with cooking spray."],[null,"Season the chicken with black pepper. Spray a large sauté pan with cooking spray and heat over medium-high. Add the chicken and cook for 8 minutes."],[null,"Add the diced tomatoes, black beans, chili powder, cumin, and garlic powder to the pan. Reduce the heat to low and simmer for 5 minutes."],[null,"Pour the chicken mixture into the baking dish. Sprinkle on the cheese and then top with the crushed tortilla chips. Bake for 12 minutes or until the cheese is melted."]],"h":[]},"2141":{"s":[[null,"Pour chicken broth and water into a slow cooker set on high-heat setting."],[null,"Season with poultry seasoning, pepper and salt."],[null,"Shred chicken. Dice carrot small."],[null,"Add chicken, carrots and egg noodles to soup."],[null,"Cook on high-heat setting for 20 to 25 minutes or until noodles are cooked."]],"h":[[null,"This recipe is best if made with homemade chicken stock instead of canned broth."],[null,"Fettuccine noodles work well in this recipe as a substitute for egg noodles. Do not overcook or noodles will be mushy."],[null,"Omit salt if using commercially-prepared broth or stock that contains more than 140 mg sodium per cup."],[null,"Cook a whole chicken in a slow cooker to make stock and provide some of the chicken for this recipe. (See Slow Cooker Whole Chicken.)"]]},"4406620":{"s":[[null,"In a large heavy bottomed pot, heat oil over medium-high heat for 1 minute and add chicken breast to brown lightly. Add all vegetables and spices and continue to cook for 8–10 minutes, stirring frequently."],[null,"Add broth, water, and lemon juice to the vegetable-chicken mix. Cover, increase the heat to high, and bring to a boil. Reduce heat to low and let simmer 20 minutes."],[null,"Add pasta and continue to simmer for 5–10 minutes depending on the size of the pasta."],[null,"Sprinkle fresh parsley on top and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Freeze the soup in portions and reheat for a quick, nutritious meal in minutes!"],["Benefits of cabbage","Choose cabbage as part of your kidney-friendly diet. A ½ cup portion of this vegetable has 8 milligrams of sodium, 76 milligrams of potassium and 12 milligrams of phosphorus. Cabbage is rich in folate, fiber, and vitamins K, C, and B6. In addition to offering many nutrients and being inexpensive, there are also several health benefits to eating this vegetable. Eating cabbage promotes heart health, helps fight inflammation from chronic disease, and supports more regular digestion. When selecting and making dishes with cabbage, consider a few tips. First, purchase cabbage in a variety of different colors based on your recipe. Most stores will carry a selection of red, purple, white, or green cabbage. Experts recommend picking a dense cabbage and storing in a cool location to maintain freshness. Depending on your dish, cabbage can be eaten raw or cooked. You can grill, roast, or sauté cabbage to maximize flavor. While cabbage can be boiled, be careful not to overcook, as this will result in limp cabbage leaves and a strong, undesirable odor."]]},"7949087":{"s":[[null,"Cook the noodles according to packet instructions, drain and set aside."],[null,"Put the stock, soy sauce, peas, sweetcorn and chicken in a saucepan over a medium heat. Bring to a simmer and cook for 2 minutes."],[null,"In a small cup, mix the cornflour with 4 tbsp cold water and add to the contents of the pan then stir for a further 1 minute until the liquid thickens slightly."],[null,"Add the noodles and reheat briefly, stirring to mix together."]],"h":[[null,"You could add lots of other vegetables to this dish, such as finely chopped spring onion, red pepper, sliced mushrooms or some pak choi."],[null,"Try adding 1 tsp of Chinese five-spice powder or some chilli flakes."],[null,"Use rice noodles for a gluten-free alternative."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"5621440":{"s":[[null,"Put the breadcrumbs in a bowl."],[null,"Put the yoghurt in a separate bowl."],[null,"Dip the raw chicken pieces into the yoghurt then coat in the breadcrumbs."],[null,"Shallow fry in oil (try rapeseed/sunflower oil) for about 5 minutes each side, but keep an eye on them to make sure they don’t start to burn!"]],"h":[[null,"Add 2 tsp of sage for added flavour."],[null,"Serve these with polenta chips or chopped up into hot pasta with a knob of garlic butter."]]},"7621440":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 190°C/gas 5. Lightly oil a baking sheet and place the beaten egg in a shallow bowl. Put the flour onto a dinner plate and the breadcrumbs onto another dinner plate."],[null,"Cut the chicken into bite-sized pieces (approx. 12-14) and place onto the plate of flour then mix so they each piece is coated, separating the pieces so they’re not touching each other."],[null,"Wash and dry your hands, pick up a piece of chicken, shake off any excess flour, dip into the egg and place on the breadcrumbs. Sprinkle more crumbs on top to fully cover the chicken and place on the baking sheet. Repeat until all the nuggets are coated.&nbsp"],[null,"Bake for 12-15 minutes until the outside is crispy and lightly browned."]],"h":[[null,"Use can also use rapeseed oil."],[null,"Add some chilli flakes to the flour for a little kick."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Cook, then cool immediately and freeze on a baking sheet. Once frozen carefully bag in portions for use. Reheat thorughly until piping hot."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"2312":{"s":[[null,"Stir mustard, mayonnaise, honey and Worcestershire sauce together in a small bowl. Refrigerate sauce to chill until nuggets are cooked, then serve as a dipping sauce."],[null,"Preheat oven to 400° F."],[null,"Cut chicken breast into 36 bite-sized pieces."],[null,"Crush cornflakes and pour crumbs into a large zip-lock bag."],[null,"Combine beaten egg and milk in a small bowl. Dip chicken pieces in egg mixture then shake in zip-lock bag to coat with cornflake crumbs."],[null,"Bake nuggets on a baking sheet sprayed with nonstick cooking spray for 15 minutes or until done."]],"h":[[null,"Serve nuggets on a tray with decorated toothpicks for a festive look."],[null,"Try a variety of dipping sauces, such as: barbeque sauce, curry sauce, fruit spreads or low-sodium salad dressing."],[null,"Three pieces is an appetizer portion. For a meal, increase portion to 6 to 9 nuggets."],[null,"Use low-sodium cornflakes if available to reduce sodium to 116 mg for 3 pieces."]]},"6461142":{"s":[[null,"Stir mustard, mayonnaise, honey, and Worcestershire sauce in a small bowl. Refrigerate sauce to chill until nuggets are cooked."],[null,"Preheat to 400°F."],[null,"Cut chicken breast into 36 bite-sized pieces."],[null,"Combine beaten egg and milk in a small bowl. Dip chicken pieces in egg mixture then shake in zip-lock bag to coat with cornflake crumbs."],[null,"Bake nuggets on a baking sheet sprayed with non-stick cooking spray for 15 minutes until done."]],"h":[]},"2158":{"s":[[null,"Spray a large pan with non-stick spray and heat 2 tablespoons canola oil. Sauté onion just until tender but not brown or golden."],[null,"Add paprika and pepper; whisk until blended."],[null,"Add chicken and sauté until all pieces are coated with seasoning mixture. (Leave skin on chicken.)"],[null,"Add water and salt and cover with a lid."],[null,"Simmer over a very low flame or on low heat for 1–1/2 hour until chicken pieces are tender (check with a fork)."],[null,"Remove pan from heat and place chicken on a plate. Allow mixture to cool about 10 minutes, and then stir in the sour cream."],[null,"Spoon sauce over chicken before serving or if preparing with dumplings, add them to the sauce, stir and serve."]],"h":[[null,"This family recipe was modified to be more heart-healthy. Traditional Hungarian cuisine uses copious quantities of sour cream, butter and fat from meats. This recipe has been modified to be leaner, while retaining traditional flavors. It is delicious served over dumplings, but is a little easier to serve over noodles."],[null,"Instead of 2 cups water and 1/4 teaspoon salt, you can use 2 cups reduced-sodium broth."],[null,"Traditional recipe calls for a whole 3 – 4 pound chicken. Using chicken breasts keeps it lower in fat. You can also use chicken thighs – use 12 in place of the 6 breast halves."],[null,"If you are on a lower protein diet reduce serving to 1/2 chicken breast, approximately 2 ounces."]]},"3851":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375° F. Spray a large baking sheet with cooking spray."],[null,"Mix ground chicken, egg, bread crumbs, Parmesan cheese, 2 tablespoons pizza sauce and spices in a bowl."],[null,"Shape into 30 small meatballs, about the size of a ping-pong ball; place meatballs onto the prepared baking sheet."],[null,"Bake for 15 minutes."],[null,"Spread thin layer of pizza sauce in bottom of glass baking dish. Place meatballs in glass baking dish. Pour remaining pizza sauce on top of meatballs then add shredded mozzarella."],[null,"Place back in oven and bake for an additional 10 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Ground turkey or ground beef can be substituted for ground chicken."],[null,"Serve as an appetizer or as a main dish with pasta of choice."],[null,"Make tasty meatball sandwiches using Italian or French roll or rustic white bread."],[null,"The cheese in this recipe provides less than 1 tablespoon per serving."],[null,"Pizza sauce provides 1-2/3 tablespoons per serving. Compare brands and select the lowest sodium product."]]},"1828":{"s":[[null,"Chop the green onions and red peppers."],[null,"Trim the ends off the Brussels sprouts and boil or steam until just tender."],[null,"Cook pasta according to directions on package but omitting the salt."],[null,"While pasta is cooking, drain Brussels sprouts and set aside."],[null,"Heat butter and oil and sauté green onions in skillet."],[null,"Add red peppers and Brussels sprouts, stirring until just golden on the edges."],[null,"Add soy sauce and let vegetable mixture stand covered until pasta is done."],[null,"Heat chicken in microwave if needed."],[null,"Toss pasta, chicken and cooked vegetables in a bowl."],[null,"Serve immediately while hot."]],"h":[[null,"Rotini is also known as corkscrew pasta. Three ounces dry (3/4 cup) yields 1-1/2 cups cooked. This recipe calls for whole wheat but you can substitute refined rotini if desired. Potassium and phosphorus will be slightly lower."],[null,"You can bake boneless, skinless chicken breast or tenderloins in a 425°F oven for 18-25 minutes or until the internal temperature reaches 165°F. Pound the breasts to an even thickness for more even cooking."],[null,"Adjust the amount of chicken for a lower or higher protein meal."]]},"2803":{"s":[[null,"In a medium bowl combine shredded chicken, pesto, Greek yogurt and black pepper."],[null,"Slice and toast the ciabatta rolls."],[null,"Divide the chicken pesto mixture in half and make sandwiches with the rolls. Add shredded lettuce as desired."]],"h":[[null,"Use chopped arugula instead of lettuce if desired. Nutrients are similar."],[null,"For a lower protein sandwich cut chicken pesto mixture ingredients in half. Protein content is approximately 21 grams per sandwich."],[null,"To reduce carbohydrates serve on half of a mini-baguette instead of the ciabatta roll. Carbohydrate is reduced to 26 grams."]]},"2266":{"s":[[null,"Cook pasta according to package instructions, omitting salt. Drain and set aside."],[null,"Cut the chicken into bite-sized pieces. Dice the onion and bell peppers. Mince the garlic cloves."],[null,"In a large skillet sauté the onion and bell peppers in 1 tablespoon olive oil until soft. Add additional tablespoon olive oil, garlic and chicken pieces and cook until chicken is done about 5 to 7"],[null,"minutes."],[null,"Turn the heat down to low and add cooked pasta, balsamic vinegar, salt and pepper. Stir until well combined."],[null,"Add the pesto, stir and heat before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute whole wheat pasta to boost the fiber content."],[null,"Replace chicken with turkey or shrimp for a tasty variation."],[null,"For a lower protein diet decrease the chicken to 12 ounces (17 grams protein per serving)."]]},"2778":{"s":[[null,"In a large saucepan, place chicken, water and seasonings. Heat to boiling."],[null,"Reduce heat and simmer for 45 minutes."],[null,"Place diced potatoes in a large pot of room temperature water and bring to a boil. remove from heat, drain water and add fresh room temperature water. Bring to a boil and cook for 10 minutes. Drain and set aside."],[null,"Remove chicken from pan and set aside. Skim fat from broth."],[null,"Add carrots, celery and onion to broth and heat to boiling. Cook for 5 minutes."],[null,"Stir in boiled potatoes, parsley and bows and boil 14 minutes or until bows are tender."],[null,"Cut chicken into pieces and stir into pot pie mixture; heat through and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Farfelle pasta is also known as pot pie bows."],[null,"The potatoes are double cooked to remove part of the potassium. If you are not on a low potassium diet you can skip this step."],[null,"Freeze leftovers in individual portions for a quick meal later."],[null,"You can reduce the chicken to 1 pound if you are on a lower protein diet."]]},"4833652":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 425°F."],[null,"In a large saucepan, heat the butter over medium heat. Add the onion and garlic and sauté until the onions begin to soften. Add peas and corn and continue to sauté."],[null,"Add the flour to the vegetables and stir to coat."],[null,"Add the chicken broth and milk to the floured vegetables. Stir to dissolve all the flour particles."],[null,"Add the cooked chicken and dry spices and simmer until the sauce thickens."],[null,"Turn of the heat and stir in the fresh tarragon and parsley."],[null,"Pour the chicken mixture into a 9-inch casserole dish and place the pie shell on top. Brush with whisked egg to obtain a golden crust."],[null,"Bake at 425°F for approximately 30 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"* Look for low or reduced-sodium broth containing 200mg sodium or less per 1 cup serving. Avoid low-sodium broth that contains potassium chloride—it’s very high in potassium."],[null,"You can also make this recipe in individual ramekins. The cooking time will be the same."],[null,"You may want to prepare the pot pie and freeze it for future use."],[null,"To cook from frozen, preheat oven to 400°F. Cover the pot pie with aluminum foil and bake for 40 minutes. After 40 minutes, remove the foil and continue to bake for another 35 minutes."],["How to prevent potassium levels from getting too high","Potassium supports cell function in your body. Typically potassium comes from the food that you eat and any extra is eliminated in urine by your kidneys. With hyperkalemia, your blood potassium level becomes too high, putting you at risk for nausea, muscle weakness and potentially serious heart problems. Finding out the cause of hyperkalemia is important, and treatment often involves changes in diet and medication. Aim for an average of 2,000mg of potassium per day by reading the Nutrition Facts label on the packaged and canned foods in your diet. Avoid salt substitutes, which are usually rich in potassium chloride, and reduce high-potassium foods. Your doctor may evaluate the medications you are taking and recommend changes to lower potassium. Never reduce the dose of medications on your own without talking to your doctor. Common adjustments your doctor may make to your prescribed medications may be adding or limiting diuretics, decreasing or modifying any oral potassium supplements and adjusting heart or blood pressure medications that may increase the potassium in your blood."]]},"6674242":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400°F. Season the diced chicken with garlic powder and freshly ground pepper and set aside. In a 2-quart saucepan, bring the chicken stock and water to a boil."],[null,"Meanwhile, heat the olive oil in a medium skillet and add the mushrooms and garlic. Season lightly with salt and pepper. Cook for 5 minutes or until mushrooms are soft. Once the mushrooms soften, set them aside in a bowl. Strain any liquid from the mushrooms."],[null,"Add in the potatoes and thyme leaves and lower the heat to medium. Simmer the potatoes for about 8 minutes until tender. With a slotted spoon, remove the potatoes and thyme to a bowl. Discard the thyme leaves. Add the carrots and onions to the stock and simmer for 4 minutes. With a slotted spoon remove the carrots and onions to the same bowl with the potatoes."],[null,"Add the chicken to the stock and simmer the chicken for 3 minutes. With a slotted spoon, remove the chicken to the same bowl with the vegetables. Reduce the stock until reduced to 1/2 cup, about 10 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, whisk the milk, half-and-half, and flour together in a bowl until very smooth. When the stock is reduced, slowly add the milk mixture to the stock, constantly stirring until thickened, but smooth. Add the sauce to the vegetables and season with salt and pepper. Add in the reserved mushrooms, peas, and parsley, and mix well."],[null,"Pour the mixture into a 9 × 13-inch pan. Set aside."],[null,"Spread one sheet of phyllo out onto a very lightly floured surface. Be sure to cover the remaining sheets of phyllo with a towel to avoid exposing to air. The phyllo will crack if exposed. Coat with the butter spray. Add another sheet of phyllo on top of the first sheet and coat with spray. Repeat this process until all 8 sheets are used."],[null,"Carefully lift the phyllo dough stack and place over the chicken vegetable filling. Tuck the edges under. With a sharp knife, make 3 diagonal slashes across the top of the dough. This will allow steam to escape."],[null,"Bake the chicken pot pie, uncovered, for about 30 minutes until the top is puffed and golden brown. Remove from the oven and let stand for about 5 minutes. Cut into squares."]],"h":[]},"7522633":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a large non-stick frying pan, add the onion and garlic and fry for 1 minute. Add the chicken and continue to fry for 2–3 minutes."],[null,"Stir in the rice and coat with the oil. Gradually add the hot stock, stirring continuously, allowing each addition to be absorbed before adding the next."],[null,"Stir in the asparagus and peas with the last addition of stock and continue to cook. The whole cooking process should take about 20 minutes and the rice should be 'al dente'."],[null,"Stir through the Parmesan cheese and parsley, season well and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Keep your stock hot in another pan so that when you add it to the dish it doesn’t lower the temperature and stop the rice cooking."],[null,"For a veggie alternative, leave out the Parmesan cheese, add 200g mushrooms rather than chicken and use vegetable stock."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"3775":{"s":[[null,"Cube cooked chicken. Dice celery and apples. Cut grapes in half."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine chicken, celery, apples and grape halves."],[null,"Add mayonnaise, cinnamon and lemon juice. Stir to coat ingredients."],[null,"Chill at least 30 minutes before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Serve Chicken Salad as a sandwich filling or as an entrée salad over lettuce."]]},"6005432":{"s":[[null,"Mix all ingredients except buns and tomato in a medium mixing bowl."],[null,"Serve 1/3 cup chicken salad on each slider bun topped with 1 tomato slice."]],"h":[]},"6036850":{"s":[[null,"In a salad bowl, mix together all salad ingredients"],[null,"Pour dressing over salad and toss to coat."]],"h":[]},"6211842":{"s":[[null,"Soak bamboo skewers in warm water for at least 30 minutes. While skewers are soaking, slice chicken breasts into eight strips lengthwise."],[null,"In a medium bowl, whisk together 1 tbsp brown sugar substitute, 1 tbsp soy sauce, half the minced garlic, ginger, lime juice and hot sauce. Add chicken to the marinade and marinate chicken strips in the refrigerator for 1 hour."],[null,"Prepare an indoor or outdoor grill."],[null,"While the chicken is marinating, whisk together the remaining tbsp brown sugar substitute, remaining tbsp soy sauce, remaining minced garlic, peanut butter, and coconut milk in a microwave safe bowl. Set aside."],[null,"Thread chicken strips lengthwise onto the soaked bamboo skewers. Grill chicken for 4-5 minutes one each side."],[null,"Right before serving, microwave sauce for 30 seconds. Remove from microwave and whisk again to combine. Serve two skewers with 2 Tbsps. of sauce."]],"h":[]},"6464029":{"s":[[null,"In a bowl, combine the soy sauce, curry powder, cumin, and garlic. Add the chicken slices, ensuring they're well-coated. Cover and refrigerate for at least 1 hour, preferably overnight."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix the powdered peanut butter with warm water until smooth. Stir in the sweet chili sauce and lime juice."],[null,"Lightly oil a nonstick skillet or grill pan and heat over medium. Cook the marinated chicken for 5–6 minutes per side until fully cooked and golden brown. Transfer to a plate and let it rest for a few minutes before slicing.​"],[null,"In a large bowl, combine the romaine lettuce, cucumber, shallot, and cilantro. Divide the salad among four plates. Top each with the chicken and a sprinkle of pomegranate seeds. Drizzle with the satay dressing just before serving."]],"h":[]},"6886065":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, combine olive oil, garlic, cumin, paprika, coriander, turmeric, cinnamon, cayenne (if using), salt, pepper, and 1 tbsp lemon juice. Add chicken thighs and coat evenly. Marinate for at least 30 minutes, or up to overnight in the fridge."],[null,"Preheat a grill pan or skillet over medium heat. Cook chicken thighs for 5–7 minutes per side, or until fully cooked. Let rest for 5 minutes, then thinly slice."],[null,"Bring a large pot of water to a boil. One at a time, blanch each collard leaf for 30–45 seconds until bright green and pliable. Transfer to an ice bath, then pat dry."],[null,"In a small bowl, add yogurt, tahini, 1 tbsp lemon juice, and 2 cloved minced garlic. Whisk until smooth."],[null,"Now, you are ready to build the wraps. Lay a collard leaf flat. Spread with a spoonful of yogurt-tahini sauce (1/2 cup plain nonfat Greek yogurt; 1 tbsp tahini; 1 tbsp lemon juice; and 1 small clove garlic, minced). Top with sliced chicken, cucumber, cherry tomatoes, and red onion. Fold in the sides and roll like a burrito."],[null,"Slice each wrap in half if desired and serve immediately. Leftovers can be wrapped tightly and stored in the fridge for up to 2 days."]],"h":[]},"6671813":{"s":[[null,"If using wooden skewers, soak them in water for at least 30 minutes to prevent burning."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together coarse salt, black pepper, peanut butter, soy sauce, honey, rice vinegar, sesame oil, minced garlic, grated ginger, and turmeric. Add water gradually until you reach the desired sauce consistency."],[null,"Pour 1/3 of the peanut sauce on the chicken and stir well to coat the chicken in the marinade. Marinate for 20 minutes."],[null,"Preheat the grill or grill pan to medium-high heat."],[null,"Weave the chicken onto the skewers and grill for about 10 minutes, turning occasionally, until the chicken reaches an internal temperature of 165 degrees F and has a nice char."],[null,"Drizzle the remaining peanut sauce over the top or serve it on the side for dipping."]],"h":[]},"4990756":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400°F."],[null,"Rub chicken with canola oil. Place on a baking tray and bake for 20–25 minutes or until an internal temperature of 165°F is reached. Cool. Slice into ¼ inch pieces and refrigerate."],[null,"Cook soba noodles according to instructions on the package. Drain and rinse noodles with cold water. Place in a large mixing bowl and refrigerate."],[null,"To prepare the vinaigrette, mix together the vinegar, honey, oil, and ginger. Refrigerate."],[null,"To assemble the salad, add cabbage, peas, onions, cilantro and the ginger vinaigrette to soba noodle bowl. Mix well to combine."],[null,"Garnish salad with sliced chicken."]],"h":[[null,"This salad can also be served warm."],[null,"PLEASE NOTE: This recipe is higher in potassium and portion size is important. Check with your registered dietitian to see how this recipe can be included in your diet."],["Phosphorus and potassium in Asian noodles","Asian noodles are quick to cook and easy to use in a variety of dishes. They are readily available, fresh or dried, from Asian food stores. They have become so popular that you can even find many of the varieties in your local grocery store. With so many choices, they are quite easy to use in day-to-day cooking. You can add them to soups, salads, stir fries and spring rolls. Similar to a traditional wheat noodle, like spaghetti or elbow macaroni, Asian noodles come in numerous shapes and sizes. Unlike a wheat noodle however, the texture of an Asian noodle can vary tremendously depending upon what it is made of. Asian noodles are commonly made from rice flour, buckwheat flour, root vegetable and mung bean starches, tapioca flour or seaweed. Depending upon their key ingredients, Asian noodles can vary immensely in their potassium and phosphorus content. For example, cellophane noodles are made from water and bean starch and are thus very low in potassium and phosphorus compared to a noodle made from rice or buckwheat flour. Talk to your registered dietitian regarding how you can include Asian noodles in your diet."]]},"4089818":{"s":[[null,"In a bowl, combine all marinade ingredients and add the chicken. Mix, cover with plastic wrap and refrigerate for at least one hour."],[null,"Prepare the cucumber salad in a bowl: squeeze out any excess liquid from the grated cucumber. Add the onion, garlic, dill, pepper, and yogurt to the cucumber. Mix, cover with plastic wrap and refrigerate until ready to use."],[null,"Heat a skillet over medium heat and add the chicken with the marinade. Sauté until the chicken is cooked through, approximately 15 minutes."],[null,"To assemble the pita sandwiches, add the cooked chicken to each pita pocket. Top with cucumber salad and lettuce."]],"h":[]},"3381":{"s":[[null,"Blend olive oil, vinegar, onion, garlic and spices in a blender or food processor to make the marinade."],[null,"Cut chicken into 1-1/2″ cubes and place into a zip-top bag. Pour marinade over chicken and seal bag."],[null,"Marinate overnight in the refrigerator."],[null,"Place cubed chicken on skewers. Discard remaining marinade."],[null,"Grill over medium heat for 10 to 12 minutes, turning as needed, until meat is cooked through."]],"h":[[null,"Try this recipe with a combination of chicken breast and thigh meat, or substitute chicken with beef or lamb, if desired."],[null,"Food safety guidelines recommend cooking chicken to an internal temperature of 180° F."],[null,"Adjust portion size according to your meal plan for a higher- or lower-protein diet."]]},"3675":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F. Set cream cheese out to soften. Melt butter."],[null,"Cook, drain, and chop broccoli."],[null,"Boil chicken breasts until done; drain, remove skin and bones, and dice into pieces."],[null,"Mix together chicken, softened cream cheese, melted butter and broccoli."],[null,"Open crescent rolls and form a rectangle with 2 rolls. Pinch seam to seal and stretch rectangle."],[null,"Place 1/4th of chicken mixture in center; fold edges across to make a turnover. Press edges to seal."],[null,"Bake for 25 to 30 minutes or until rolls are browned."]],"h":[[null,"Take a look at Chicken Squares as they are baking in oven periodically to make sure they don’t get too brown."],[null,"This is a higher sodium entrée. To keep sodium in check, complete the meal with low-sodium items such as salad, low-sodium dressing and fruit."],[null,"The chicken bones and skin add extra flavor during cooking. Fourteen ounces of boneless, skinless chicken breasts may be substituted for bone-in breasts if desired."],[null,"Freeze or refrigerate broth from boiling the chicken for later use in a recipe that calls for low-sodium chicken broth."],[null,"If fat-free cream cheese is substituted, fat is reduced to 16 grams and sodium is 577 mg."]]},"4103065":{"s":[[null,"Put chicken and broth in slow cooker and cook on low heat for 8 hours (or 10 minutes in a pressure cooker) with the bay or Laurel leaf."],[null,"Shred the chicken with a fork."],[null,"Sauté onion and garlic in canola oil. Add the shredded chicken and stir."],[null,"Heat the corn taco shells in the microwave for 5-10 seconds."],[null,"Add chicken mixture to the taco shells, garnish with shredded lettuce and sour cream as desired."]],"h":[[null,"Nutrition info includes all ingredients that are listed above."]]},"4475042":{"s":[[null,"Brown the ground chicken in butter on medium heat along with the seasonings."],[null,"Fill 2 taco shells for each person with meat mixture, cilantro, scallions and cheese."],[null,"MEASURING the cheese is the key! It should be ⅛ cup per 2 tacos."]],"h":[[null,"** Natural cheese has less sodium and phosphorus than processed cheese"],[null,"*Optional Serving Suggestions: Ingredients can also be served in a lettuce wrap, pressed between a flour tortilla to make a quesadilla, or tossed with spaghetti or rice."],[null,"Nutrient values are the sum of the separate analyses given for each component."]]},"3175":{"s":[[null,"Place chicken into a zip-top bag. Add 5 teaspoons teriyaki sauce and marinate in refrigerator for 3 to 4 hours."],[null,"Dice onion; chop scallions, lettuce and tomato."],[null,"In medium frying pan heat 1 tablespoon oil and cook chicken thoroughly until no pink remains."],[null,"Meanwhile, in a small frying pan, sauté onion in 1 tablespoon olive oil."],[null,"While chicken and onion are cooking, combine mayonnaise, scallions and 2 teaspoons Kikkoman® Less Sodium Teriyaki Sauce. Put mixture aside."],[null,"Cut each cooked chicken breast into several strips."],[null,"Take pita halves and coat inside with mayonnaise mixture. Fill pita with several chicken pieces; top with sautéed onion, lettuce and tomatoes."]],"h":[[null,"One average-size raw, boneless, skinless chicken breast weighs approximately 4 ounces. Flatten breasts for more even cooking."],[null,"If smaller pitas are substituted for the larger ones, use one pita per serving"],[null,"Even though tomato is a high-potassium vegetable, the 2 tablespoons per serving is small enough that potassium for the recipe is still acceptable for a low-potassium diet."],[null,"If you need extra calories, use regular mayonnaise instead of reduced fat. Besides providing more calories, sodium content is lower."]]},"6913065":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl stir the garlic, yogurt, lemon zest and juice, spices, and coarse salt until combined."],[null,"Add the chicken to the bowl and stir until all the cubes are evenly coated in the marinade. Cover and allow to marinate for 20 minutes (or place in the fridge for up to 24 hours)."],[null,"Discard the marinade and thread the chicken onto the skewers, alternating with the bell pepper and onion."],[null,"Lightly grease the grill, grill pan, or griddle and place on high heat. Once hot, place the skewers on the grill, rotating to ensure even cooking, for 12–15 minutes depending on the thickness of your chicken."],[null,"Allow the kebabs to rest, covered, for 5 minutes before serving with tzatziki sauce"]],"h":[]},"7988967":{"s":[[null,"Add the oil to a pan and add the onions and peppers. Cook for 5 minutes until soft and add the chicken breasts and cook for 3 minutes."],[null,"Add the tikka paste and stir for 1-2 minutes until the chicken is evenly coated."],[null,"Add the garlic and tomatoes, mix again and bring to a gentle boil then cover and simmer gently for 6-8 minutes."],[null,"Add the coriander, stir well then remove from the heat."],[null,"Stir in the yogurt, sprinkle with the remaining coriander and serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"Works well with turkey or cubed salmon."],[null,"Serve with plenty of salad. For a higher-carb option, wrap in a roti or serve with naan."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"2564":{"s":[[null,"Cut chicken into small strips."],[null,"Heat pan on medium heat with 2 tablespoons extra virgin olive oil."],[null,"Add chicken to pan and cook until done."],[null,"Cook 4 ounces of linguine according to package directions."],[null,"Cut broccoli and cauliflower to bite-size pieces."],[null,"When chicken is cooked, add broccoli, cauliflower, carrots, tomatoes and lemon juice, cover and cook for 3 minutes."],[null,"Add drained pasta to pan and then add 1 tablespoon extra virgin olive oil and stir."],[null,"Add Mrs. Dash, stir and simmer on low for 5 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Use your favorite variety of Mrs. Dash herb seasoning blend."],[null,"Store remaining uncooked linguine or cook the whole package and use half in another recipe."]]},"2215":{"s":[[null,"Combine rice with 2 cups broth 1/2 cup water. Cook in a rice cooker or on the stove top."],[null,"Mince onion and parsley. Grate carrots. Chop chicken."],[null,"Melt butter in a saucepan; add onion and sauté until tender."],[null,"Blend in flour; gradually add chicken broth."],[null,"Cook over medium heat, stirring constantly, until mixture thickens slightly."],[null,"Stir in rice, chicken, and carrots. Simmer 5 minutes."],[null,"Add almonds and garnish with chopped parsley before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Prepare rice according to package, omitting salt or seasoning package if included."]]},"3751":{"s":[[null,"Peel, rinse, and dice the onion and carrots. Core and dice the apples."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix cinnamon, coriander, cumin and pepper."],[null,"Pat chicken dry with paper towels. Cut in cube shapes and rub pieces with spice mixture."],[null,"In a large skillet over medium-high-heat add 1 tablespoon of oil. Add the onion, carrots and apples. Cook, stirring occasionally until the vegetables start to brown, about 15 minutes. Transfer to a medium bowl."],[null,"Add the remaining tablespoon of oil to the skillet. Brown the chicken for 2 to 4 minutes per side. Add broth and packet of quinoa and brown rice. Bring to a simmer. Cook for 15 to 25 minutes."],[null,"Add the dried cranberries and vegetable/fruit mixture. Cook until liquid is almost gone, 5 to 10 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Brown rice and quinoa are gluten-free. If you have Celiac disease this recipe is a good choice."],[null,"Brown rice and quinoa are a good source of fiber and whole grains."]]},"6470482":{"s":[[null,"Line a baking sheet with foil. Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F. Combine all the ingredients for the salsa in a bowl. Cover and refrigerate for 1 hour."],[null,"Meanwhile, trim any excess fat from the chicken breasts. Combine the cumin, chili powder, salt, and pepper. Rub each piece of chicken with the spice rub."],[null,"Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Add the chicken and sear on both sides for a total of 10 minutes. Add the chicken to the prepared baking sheet. Cover loosely with foil or parchment paper. Continue to cook the chicken breasts until cooked through, about 6–7 minutes."],[null,"Bring the salsa up to room temperature. Serve the cooked chicken with the salsa."]],"h":[]},"1810":{"s":[[null,"Place one piece of chicken on a cutting board and cover with plastic wrap.Use a meat mallet to pound chicken until even and flat."],[null,"Sprinkle pounded chicken with black pepper."],[null,"Heat oil in a non-stick skillet over medium heat. Add chicken and cook approximately 6 minutes on each side until done. Remove chicken from pan and keep warm."],[null,"Add garlic to pan. Cook one minute, stirring constantly. Add broth, bay leaf and Herbs de Provence; bring to a boil, scraping pan to loosen browned bits. Cook until broth mixture is reduced to 1/2 cup, about 3 minutes."],[null,"Remove from heat. Add lemon juice and butter, stirring constantly until butter melts."],[null,"Serve sauce over chicken."]],"h":[[null,"Buy 4 chicken breasts, 4 ounces each."],[null,"Serve with rice or over noodles, along with green beans, carrots or beets."],[null,"Herbs de Provence is a blend of herbes typically used in Provence region of France. The blend includes savory, fennel, basil, thyme and sometimes lavender."]]},"2331":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375º F."],[null,"Shred Swiss chard. Chop the red onion and garlic."],[null,"Add olive oil, 4 tablespoons of lemon juice, pepper, onion, garlic, quinoa and wild rice and chicken broth to a 9-inch x 13-inch baking pan. Mix ingredients together."],[null,"Add Swiss chard on top of rice mixture."],[null,"Add chicken thighs on top of Swiss chard."],[null,"Cover with foil and bake for 45 minutes or until chicken is done and the majority of chicken broth has been absorbed."],[null,"Let sit for 5-10 minutes. While dish is cooling, chop fresh parsley and combine with remaining 2 tablespoon lemon juice. Sprinkle on top and enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"To see if enough liquid has been absorbed, insert a spoon into the rice mixture until it hits the bottom of the pan. Draw the spoon towards the center of the pan through the rice mixture. A small amount of liquid should seep into where the line was drawn."],[null,"Each garlic clove is about 1 teaspoon chopped."],[null,"A 2-pound package of boneless chicken thighs usually contains 6 pieces."],[null,"For a higher protein meal serve one thigh instead of 1/2."]]},"2301":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oven to 350°F."],[null,"Cut the tops off of each garlic bulb to expose cloves. Place the bulbs cut side up on a large piece of foil. Drizzle bulbs with the oil, then wrap a piece of foil around the bulbs tightly. Place in a baking dish and bake 45 to 50 minutes or until garlic is tender. Cool slightly. Squeeze soft cloves out of the skins, finely chop, then set aside."],[null,"While the garlic is baking, place each chicken breast between 2 pieces of plastic wrap; gently pound with flat side of a meat mallet until about 1/4 inch thick. In a shallow pan, mix together the flour, thyme, salt and pepper. Reserve 3 tablespoons of the seasoned flour for the sauce. Coat the chicken with remaining flour mixture."],[null,"In a large skillet, heat 2 tablespoons of the butter over medium-high heat. Cook the chicken for 6-8 minutes until no longer pink in center (165°F with a thermometer), turning once. Place chicken on a plate and cover to keep warm."],[null,"In the same skillet, heat the remaining butter. Cook mushrooms over medium heat until lightly browned. Sprinkle the reserved seasoned flour over the mushrooms. Cook and stir for about 2 minutes. Mix in the chicken broth, milk and roasted garlic. Bring to a boil. Reduce heat to low; simmer about 3 minutes or until slightly thickened."],[null,"Add chicken to the skillet with sauce and heat for 1 to 2 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Serve chicken with 1/3 cup rice or 1/2 cup pasta; each is about 1 carbohydrate serving."],[null,"For a lower protein portion cut the chicken breasts in half after cooking."]]},"7403886":{"s":[[null,"Make the pistou. Put the parsley, mint, lemon zest and half the garlic in a food processor with 1tsp water and process until smooth."],[null,"Mist a large saucepan with cooking spray, then put over a medium heat. Add the leek and the remaining garlic, and cook, stirring, for 5 minutes or until softened."],[null,"Add the whole chicken breasts and the stock to the pan with the leek, and simmer, covered, for 15 minutes or until the chicken is cooked through. Transfer the chicken to a board with a slotted spoon. Set aside to rest for 5 minutes, then slice thinly."],[null,"Add the broccoli, asparagus, peas and borlotti beans to the soup and bring to the boil. Reduce the heat and simmer, uncovered, for 3 minutes. Add the sugar snaps and sliced chicken, then simmer, uncovered, for 2 minutes or until the vegetables are just tender. Serve the soup topped with the pistou."]],"h":[]},"6442793":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F."],[null,"Heat olive oil in a large skillet over medium heat. Add onion, Brussels sprouts, chicken, mushrooms, Italian seasoning, salt, and pepper. Cook over medium heat, stirring occasionally, for about 10 minutes, until vegetables soften and chicken is cooked through."],[null,"While the chicken and vegetables are cooking, whisk the milk and yogurt in a small bowl until combined."],[null,"Drizzle the milk and yogurt over the chicken and vegetable mixture and stir to coat."],[null,"Sprinkle with the cheese and place the skillet in the oven and cook for 15 minutes, until the cheese is melted and bubbling."]],"h":[]},"7328847":{"s":[[null,"Heat the rapeseed oil in a pan and add the onion. Cook for three minutes, until the onion is just starting to brown, then add the cubed chicken breast. Stir for 3–4 minutes."],[null,"Next, add the pepper, sultanas, cumin, white pepper and crushed garlic to the pan. Mix well and cook for 4–5 minutes, stirring regularly."],[null,"Add the lentils to the pan along with the frozen sweetcorn. Heat through for 3 minutes."],[null,"Stir in the parsley and serve with salad."]],"h":[[null,"Swap the chicken for tofu for a tasty, vegetarian alternative."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"54945":{"s":[[null,"Cut salad into bite size pieces, drain mandarin oranges. If you use canned pineapple, drain pineapple."],[null,"Slice cooked chicken breast into strips. Layer lettuce, fruit and chicken in a medium bowl. Top with dressing."]],"h":[[null,"A left-over cooked grilled or roasted chicken breast works great with this recipe and creates an easy lunch. Use half a chicken breast if on a lower protein diet."],[null,"A different vinaigrette can be used. Look for dressing that has less than 200 mg of sodium per 2 tablespoon serving."]]},"6697790":{"s":[[null,"Add oil to a soup pot over medium heat. Add the onion, carrots, celery and mushrooms. Sauté for 5 minutes."],[null,"Add broth, thyme, bay leaves, salt and pepper. Bring to a boil then reduce to a simmer, covered for 20 minutes."],[null,"Remove bay leaves and thyme stem. Add the barley and chicken and heat through for 2-3 minutes."],[null,"Note: To bulk cook barley, add 11 oz. dry pearled (quick-cooking) barley to a pot of 4 cups boiling water. Cover, then reduce to a simmer for 10-12 minutes. Remove from heat, keep covered off the heat for 5 minutes. Makes 6 cups cooked barley. This barley can be used in any recipe calling for cooked barley. Store in an airtight container in the refrigerator for 7 days or package in freezer bags in one cup increments for up to 6 months."]],"h":[]},"7278452":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/ gas 4. Add the oil to a pan, then add the onion and stir regularly for 5 minutes until browned."],[null,"Add the leeks and mushrooms, and stir regularly for 3–4 minutes, until softened."],[null,"Stir in the stock, tarragon and pepper, and bring to the boil. Add a lid to the pan, reduce heat and simmer for 5 minutes."],[null,"Mix the cornflour and milk together. Next, bring the stock back to the boil and slowly stir in the cornflour mixture until the sauce thickens, then stir for another 2 minutes."],[null,"Now, stir in the cooked chicken pieces, then add mixture to an overproof dish."],[null,"Evenly layer the sweet potato on top and bake in the oven for 25–40 minutes until lightly browned."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"6900701":{"s":[[null,"In a medium saucepan, combine the broth and tomatoes and their liquid and bring to a boil over high heat. Stir in the pasta, return to a boil, reduce heat, cover, and simmer 6 minutes or until pasta is just tender."],[null,"Remove from heat and stir in the remaining ingredients, except the cheese. Let stand, covered, 5 minutes to absorb flavors and heat through. Serve topped with cheese."]],"h":[]},"7385839":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C (160° fan)/350F/gas mark 4."],[null,"Heat the sunflower oil in an ovenproof casserole or baking dish set over a medium heat until hot."],[null,"Stir in the rice and sauté in the oil for 2 minutes, stirring frequently. Sprinkle over the spices and cook for a further 2 minutes until fragrant."],[null,"Cover with the water, stirring well. Bring to the boil before arranging the squash and chicken on top of the rice."],[null,"Loosely cover the dish with aluminium foil and transfer to the oven, baking for about 30 minutes until the rice has absorbed the water and the chicken is cooked through."],[null,"Remove from the oven and discard the foil. Sprinkle almonds on top and return the dish to the oven for 7-10 minutes until the almonds are golden-brown."],[null,"Remove from the oven. Transfer the chicken to a plate and let it cool for 5 minutes before shredding between two forks."],[null,"Stir some lemon juice into the pilaf and fluff the rice with a fork to separate the grains."],[null,"Top with the shredded chicken and garnish with some coriander leaves before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Yellow squashes are available from good grocers and supermarkets. Look for a squash that is approximately 250-350g in weight."],[null,"To add colour and variety, replace half the sliced almonds with unsalted cashew and pistachio nuts."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"6269992":{"s":[[null,"Combine the broth, chicken, beans, bell pepper, chili powder, and cumin in a large saucepan. Bring to a boil, reduce heat, and simmer, covered, 10 minutes or until pepper is tender. Remove from heat."],[null,"Combine the diced tomatoes, avocado, green onion, cilantro, oil, and salt, and spoon equal amounts on top of each serving of soup. Serve with lime wedges."]],"h":[]},"2956":{"s":[[null,"Cook brown rice according to directions and set aside."],[null,"Rinse and drain chickpeas. Chop the parsley."],[null,"In a large bowl, add parsley, lemon juice, olive oil and black pepper. Whisk together to make the vinaigrette."],[null,"Chop the bell pepper, tomato, onion and cucumber and add to bowl with vinaigrette."],[null,"Add in cooked rice and chickpeas, stir to combine."],[null,"Top with crumbled feta."],[null,"Let sit 30 minutes to an hour prior to serving for flavors to fully develop."]],"h":[[null,"Serve cold or at room temperature."],[null,"This recipe can be made in advance and kept in the fridge for up to 3 days."]]},"9991817":{"s":[[null,"Add the oil (if using), onion, garlic and ginger to a deep skillet. Sauté for 5 minutes, until softened, stirring often."],[null,"Then add the mushrooms and rapini to the skillet and place the lid on top to wilt the rapini and cook down the mushrooms, about 5 minutes. Stir occasionally."],[null,"Add all remaining ingredients (except optional garnishes) to the pot and mix well. Simmer over medium heat for about 20-25 minutes. Then taste, add more salt or pepper if needed, and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Add more veggies to this mushroom and chickpea curry if you’d like. You may add green peas, green beans, broccoli, cauliflower, or any veggies you love."],[null,"Make sure to use CANNED coconut milk , not the kind in the carton."],[null,"Make your curry as spicy as you’d like! Adjust the cayenne pepper to your taste. If this is your first time making Indian food, use less and build up from there, since there are a lot of other flavours and seasonings in this dish."],[null,"For even more depth of flavour , add ½ teaspoon of cumin seeds to the sauté step and ½ teaspoon of garam masala before simmering."],[null,"For lower fat : Use light coconut milk, instead of full fat. But note that there will be less coconut flavour and the curry will be less creamy"],[null,"For no coconut : User cashew cream , silken tofu, or dairy-free yogurt with similar results."],[null,"For oil-free , use vegetable broth or water to sauté, instead of oil."],[null,"Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-4 days, just reheat and enjoy."]]},"7054837":{"s":[[null,"Add the lemon zest to a large bowl with the pepper, and olive oil."],[null,"Next, add the red onion, tomatoes and cucumber, mix well and leave to infuse for a couple of minutes."],[null,"Add the chickpeas and tuna, and fold in gently so everything is coated with the dressing."],[null,"Finally, toss in the salad leaves and divide between two lunch boxes, packed with a lemon wedge to squeeze over before eating."]],"h":[[null,"Acidic ingredients, like lemon juice, will make your salad go limp, so take a wedge of lemon in your packed lunch to use just before eating."],[null,"Salmon or prawns make a good alternative to tuna. For a vegan version, try pieces of marinated tofu."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"9848739":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425℉/218℃ convection roast (or bake) and line a baking sheet with parchment paper. Arrange the sweet potato cubes in a single layer, sprinkle with salt and pepper, and roast them for 20 minutes, then flip and roast for another 10-15 minutes. Set aside."],[null,"Meanwhile, combine all the peanut sauce ingredients in a medium bowl and set aside."],[null,"Add the vegetable broth, 1 clove of minced garlic, and the red pepper flakes to a large pan and sauté for 30-60 seconds. Then add the bok choy and sauté on both sides for 1-2 minutes until wilted and coated with the garlic and spice. Transfer it to a plate and set aside."],[null,"To the same pan, add the peanut sauce and chickpeas, simmer for 2-3 minutes, and then turn off the heat."],[null,"Arrange the saucy chickpeas, bok choy, and sweet potatoes in bowls and serve with cooked rice or noodles if desired."]],"h":[]},"9391250":{"s":[[null,"If using canned chickpeas, drain, but reserve two tablespoons of the aquafaba (the chickpea liquid). If using cooked chickpeas, reserve the cooking liquid."],[null,"Chop your ingredients and add to a medium bowl. For the avocado, slice in half, remove the pit, and use a knife to cut the flesh into squares, right in the skin. Then scoop it out with a spoon and into your bowl."],[null,"Gently stir to combine and evenly distribute the flavours. Enjoy immediately."]],"h":[[null,"If using canned chickpeas , use salt-free, or decrease the salt called for in the recipe and adjust to taste. If using cooked chickpeas , reserve the cooking liquid for this salad, and future meals. I cook my chickpeas without salt and freeze the aquafaba/cooking liquid in ice cube trays for future use. Once frozen, transfer the aquafaba ice cubes to a container or zip-top bag and keep frozen until needed. This salad tastes best the same day it’s made. If you’re planning to make it ahead of serving, squeeze lemon juice on your avocado to prevent it from browning."]]},"3108":{"s":[[null,"Prepare the Tzatziki Sauce and refrigerate until ready to use."],[null,"Rinse and drain the chickpeas. Trim and slice the scallions. Slice the onion."],[null,"In a food processor, combine chickpeas, scallions, egg, flour, oregano, cumin and salt. Blend and pulse until a course mixture forms that holds together when pressed. The mixture will be moist. Form into 4 patties."],[null,"Heat olive oil in a skillet over medium heat. When hot, add patties. Cook until golden and beginning to crisp, 4 to 5 minutes. Flip and cook until golden brown and crisp, 2 to 4 minutes more."],[null,"Warm the pitas and cut each in half."],[null,"Assemble burgers by carefully splitting pita halves open. Cut a chickpea burger in half and place the two halves inside pita as pictured, topping with tzatziki sauce and red onion slice."]],"h":[[null,"Add lettuce and cucumbers for extra crunch."],[null,"Chickpeas are also known as garbanzo beans. Compare labels and select the lowest sodium product."]]},"9421474":{"s":[[null,"Add everything except the water to your food processor bowl and process until combined. Stop to scrape down the sides of the bowl as needed and continue processing until smooth."],[null,"If a thinner consistency is desired, add 1-2 tablespoons of water."],[null,"Transfer your nut-free Nutella to a clean and dry glass jar or airtight container."]],"h":[[null,"Don’t forget to scrape the sides of the food processor bowl during processing. This will ensure a smooth texture. Add a tablespoon of water at a time if needed for texture and/or thinner consistency."],[null,"Keep your chickpea chocolate spread in a sealed glass container or jar in your fridge for up to 1 week. Freeze it for up to 3 months."]]},"4776915":{"s":[[null,"Fill a large bowl with water and soak chickpeas for 12 hours or overnight to reduce phosphorus and potassium. Drain, rinse, and set aside."],[null,"In a large skillet, heat oil over medium heat. Fry onions for 2 minutes. Add the zucchini and the red peppers and fry for another 2 minutes. Season with turmeric and paprika and stir to combine."],[null,"Add the broth to the skillet and bring to a boil. Add couscous, chicken, and chickpeas, and stir to combine. Remove skillet from heat, cover, and let sit for 5 minutes."],[null,"Enjoy couscous warm or transfer to a closed container and refrigerate."],[null,"Before serving, add orange juice and sliced green onions."]],"h":[["Including vegetable protein and lowering phosphorus absorption","Including a variety of protein sources is important when following a kidney-friendly diet. Depending on the stage of chronic kidney disease, the recommended amount of daily protein varies. Incorporating plant-based protein sources can help in meeting daily protein goals. Protein that comes from animals, e.g. meat, contains natural phosphorus. When eating animal-based protein, approximately 30 to 80% of the phosphorus from these foods is absorbed by the body. In comparison, food selections that are plant-based, have a much lower absorption amount of only 20 to 40%. As chronic kidney disease progresses, limiting total phosphorus is important as the kidneys are less able to filter this nutrient which can lead to harmful buildups in the body. Plant-based protein sources include legumes, soy, meat alternatives, whole grains, nuts and nut butters. Read labels on packaged items to avoid foods that are high in sodium, potassium or contain unwanted phosphorus additives. Choosing the correct portion is necessary to help meet your specific nutrition goals. Experimenting with different recipes can allow you to find plant-based meals to enjoy. Adding legumes to soup or salads, choosing soy for stir fry, selecting meat alternatives for burgers, mixing whole grains into casseroles and using nuts, nut butters or seeds for flavor with hot cereal or baked goods are just a few ideas to try."]]},"9715958":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425℉/218℃ convection roast and line a large baking sheet with parchment paper. (If you do not have a convection oven, use the regular roast or bake setting and allow a few extra minutes to cook.)"],[null,"Slice and arrange your veggies and the chickpeas in a single layer on your baking sheet."],[null,"Combine all the marinade ingredients in a small bowl. Then evenly drizzle it over the chickpeas and vegetables."],[null,"Bake the veggies for 10-12 minutes. Then optionally, broil them for another 1-3 minutes to brown the veggies."],[null,"Serve with corn tortillas and any additional toppings you'd like."]],"h":[]},"9125031":{"s":[[null,"Prepare your flax or chia eggs by combining 2 tablespoons of seeds with 6 tablespoons of water in a small bowl and set aside to thicken. Then line a loaf pan with parchment paper and preheat your oven to 400 degrees F convection bake."],[null,"Add the chopped carrots and onion to a skillet and dry sauté for 5-7 minutes, until softened. Add a tablespoon or two of water if needed to prevent sticking."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the chickpeas to a large mixing bowl and mash with a fork, without over mashing. You want most of the chickpeas crushed, but no need to make sure every single one is mashed."],[null,"Then add the sautéed veggies along with the tamari, chia eggs, breadcrumbs and all the seasoning (but NOT your smoked maple glaze ingredients) to the same bowl and mix well. Make sure to mix thoroughly to distribute the chia eggs and seasoning very well. Then taste and add salt and pepper, if needed."],[null,"Pour the mixture into your prepared loaf pan and press down firmly using your hands or a silicone spatural and smooth the top. Bake for 30 minutes and remove from the oven."],[null,"While the loaf is baking, combine all the glaze ingredients in a small pot and bring to a medium boil and cook for 10 minutes, whisking often. This will thicken your sauce slightly."],[null,"Brush about one third of the glaze over your meatloaf with a silicone brush and return to the oven for 15 minutes. Remove from the oven and let cool for 10 minutes before transfering to a cuting board. Use the parchment paper to lift and transfer the loaf. Let cool on your cutting board for at least 10 minutes longer, and then slice and serve with the extra glaze."]],"h":[[null,"If you're avoiding wheat , you may sub the breadcrumbs for rolled oats, gluten free, if needed. Breadcrumbs hold together a little firmer, but the oats also work well. Mash the chickpeas in a mixing bowl with a large fork , rather than tossing into a food processor to avoid overly mashing your ingredients. You don't want overly processed ingredients here, or that may result in a mushy textured chickpea meatloaf. If you don't have a convection bake oven , increase the oven temperature by 25 degrees and cook for the same amount of time. Watch carefully. Allow for extra time to let your loaf cool and set for at least 20 minutes in total . This will make your chickpea meatloaf much easier to slice and serve. Play with the seasoning! Add more or less of the spices you like, to your taste. If you want to serve this for Thanksgiving, you might consider adding some sage, thyme and nutmeg to the mix and skipping the smoked paprika. If you don't want any heat, skip the cayenne. Have fun and make it your own! For a quicker glaze , or if you don't have tomato paste, sub the broth and tomato paste for ketchup, and mix with the maple syrup, smoked paprika and cayenne (if using). Then glaze your chickpea meatloaf as directed, but no need to simmer the sauce first."]]},"6580857":{"s":[[null,"In a medium bowl, combine the tahini, fresh lemon juice, crushed garlic, and salt.​ Gradually add cold water, whisking continuously until the dressing reaches a smooth, pourable consistency.​"],[null,"In a separate large bowl, combine the chopped romaine lettuce, cherry tomatoes, diced cucumber, and chickpeas.​ Add sliced red onion and chopped parsley. Drizzle the tahini dressing over the salad.​"]],"h":[]},"6353740":{"s":[[null,"Heat olive oil in a large skillet over medium heat."],[null,"Add chopped onions and cook until softened, about 5 minutes."],[null,"Stir in minced garlic and cook for an additional 30 seconds."],[null,"Sprinkle ground cumin, paprika, and ground coriander over the onions and garlic."],[null,"Pour in diced tomatoes and chickpeas. Season with ½ teaspoon each salt and pepper. Simmer for 10–15 minutes until the mixture thickens."],[null,"Make small wells in the mixture and crack the eggs into each well. Spring with ½ teaspoon salt."],[null,"Cover the skillet and cook for 5–7 minutes, or until the egg whites are set but the yolks are still runny (adjust cooking time based on egg preference)."],[null,"Garnish with chopped fresh basil and serve with slice of pita."]],"h":[]},"9380481":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 425°F/218°C convection roast and line a large baking tray with parchment paper."],[null,"Add all the chopped veggies and chickpeas to a large mixing bowl, then add all the marinade ingredients and mix well."],[null,"Transfer everything in a single layer on your tray, but don't dump it from the bowl. You don't want too much excess marinade on the tray. Roast for 20 minutes, and remove the tray from the oven and flip everything. Then roast for another 10 minutes, or until the desired doneness is reached."],[null,"Serve as is, or serve with rice, or in tortilla wraps."]],"h":[]},"6249033":{"s":[[null,"Rinse the bulgur wheat and add it to a small bowl. Pour hot water over the bulgur, cover, and let soak for about 20 minutes, until doubled in size. Drain excess liquid, if any, and place the bulgur in a large bowl."],[null,"Chop the parsley to a medium-fine consistency. It should have some texture left in it and should not look pureed. Add the parsley to the bulgur wheat, and add all the remaining salad ingredients. Cover and set aside."],[null,"For the vinaigrette, in a small bowl, whisk together the ingredients. Add to the salad; taste and adjust any seasonings. Add more lemon juice if desired. Turn the tabbouleh out onto a platter to serve."]],"h":[]},"3941":{"s":[[null,"Drain and rinse the chickpeas. Dice the onion, celery and carrots. Juice the lemon."],[null,"Place chickpeas in a large mixing bowl. Mash with a potato masher or fork until combined."],[null,"Mix remaining ingredients with mashed chickpeas."],[null,"Refrigerate until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Look for low-sodium chickpeas. If unavailable choose the brand lowest in sodium."],[null,"Serve on bread or in a wrap or add to a salad, or as a dip for crudités such as bell pepper, cucumbers, zucchini, carrot or celery sticks or low sodium crackers."],[null,"Include as part of a “snack box” with fresh grapes or apple slices for a meal on the go."],[null,"Chickpea Salad is a great substitute for egg salad."]]},"2050":{"s":[[null,"Pour the vegetable broth and water into a slow cooker set on high-heat setting."],[null,"Season broth with poultry seasoning, pepper and salt."],[null,"Dice the chik’n strips. Dice the carrot small."],[null,"Add the chik’n, carrots and egg noodles to the soup."],[null,"Cook soup on high-heat setting for 20 to 25 minutes or until noodles are cooked."]],"h":[[null,"Chik’n and chick’n are terms used in vegetarian chicken substitute products. The primary ingredient is soy protein. Look in the freezer section of your grocery store."],[null,"Choose low-sodium broth that does not have salt or potassium chloride in the ingredient list."],[null,"Do not overcook or noodles will become soggy."]]},"6167277":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375°F."],[null,"Spread tortilla triangles on a baking sheet and drizzle with 1 tsp olive oil. Toss to coat and sprinkle with salt."],[null,"Place the baking sheet in the oven and bake, flipping halfway, until crispy and golden, 10-12 minutes. Set aside."],[null,"Heat remaining olive oil in a medium skillet over medium heat. Add onion, garlic, zucchini, cumin, and smoked paprika. Cook, stirring occasionally, until softened, 3-4 minutes."],[null,"Add Roma tomatoes, vegetable broth, and crushed tomatoes. Simmer for until tomatoes break down and sauce thickens slightly, 8-10 minutes. Mash or blend lightly if desired for a smoother texture."],[null,"Heat a non-stick skillet over medium-low heat. Spray lightly with cooking spray and crack eggs into the skillet. Cook until the whites are set and yolks are still runny, about 3–4 minutes. Remove from heat."],[null,"Toss the baked tortilla chips in the skillet with the warm tomato sauce, coating evenly. Divide the sauced chips among 4 plates. Top each plate with a sunny-side-up egg and cilantro."]],"h":[]},"1842":{"s":[[null,"Peel potatoes and cut into 1/2-inch cubes. Place potatoes in a large pot with at least 10 cups of water and boil for 10 minutes to reduce potassium by 50%. Drain and set aside."],[null,"Mince onion and garlic."],[null,"Cut beef into 1/2-inch pieces. Brown beef, onion and garlic in canola oil."],[null,"Cover and cook over low heat for 15 to 20 minutes."],[null,"Add water and potatoes. Cover tightly and simmer until the meat is tender and potatoes are soft but not mushy."],[null,"Add 2 cups of Red Chile Colorado and bay leaves."],[null,"Bring to a boil and reduce to simmer for 10 minutes."],[null,"Remove bay leaves before serving."]],"h":[[null,"For homemade red chili sauce see the Chile Colorado Sauce recipe on DaVita.com. If using ready-made sauce, select the lowest sodium brand."],[null,"If you are on a low potassium diet, do not skip the boiling process for potatoes. This is necessary to reduce potassium."],[null,"An alternative method is to pre-boiled potatoes: peel, cube and soak potatoes in a large amount of water for 2 to 4 hours. The amount of water should be at least five times that of the potatoes."],[null,"1-1/2 teaspoons onion powder and 1/2 teaspoon garlic powder can be substituted for fresh onion and garlic."],[null,"If you are on a low protein diet, adjust the portion to match your meal plan or ask your dietitian for guidance."]]},"3168":{"s":[[null,"Finely chop onion and mince garlic."],[null,"In a medium saucepan heat canola oil and sauté onions and garlic until tender."],[null,"Stir in the flour until blended; add the cumin and oregano. Cook and stir for 3 minutes then remove from heat."],[null,"Add chili powder and stir to blend. Return pan to heat and add 2-1/2 cups water, salt and sugar."],[null,"Heat sauce to a boil, stirring constantly. Reduce heat to low and simmer for 5 minutes."],[null,"Refrigerate sauce until ready to use. Makes 2-1/2 cups."]],"h":[[null,"Chili powder burns easily so stir frequently and be careful not to let your pan get too hot."],[null,"Make chili powder from dried chilies or use store bought chili powder. Be aware, chili powder has added salt so sodium content will be higher. Omit the 1/4 teaspoon of salt if chili powder is used."],[null,"Sauce keeps for 1 week in the refrigerator."],[null,"Use this sauce to make the Chile Colorado recipe."]]},"6551080":{"s":[[null,"Line a sheet pan with parchment paper and preheat the broiler on high. Broil the poblano pepper until slightly blackened, for about 5 minutes, turning a couple of times. Place in a bowl and cover with plastic wrap to steam for 5 minutes."],[null,"Once it’s cool enough to touch, peel off the skin. Remove the stem and slice the pepper open to remove the seeds and roughly chop the pepper."],[null,"Toss the shrimp with ½ tablespoon olive oil, 1 garlic clove, peppers, and pepper. Let it marinate for 15-30 minutes"],[null,"While the shrimp is marinating, finish the sauce. Blend the poblano pepper, Greek yogurt, 2 grated garlic cloves, cumin, coarse salt, and pepper in a food processor until smooth."],[null,"Heat the remaining ½ tablespoon of olive oil in a skillet. Once the pan is hot, sear the shrimp for 2 minutes on each side until just cooked through."],[null,"Serve with the poblano sauce."]],"h":[]},"1002699":{"s":[[null,"Chop carrot and onion."],[null,"In a bowl, mix cream cheese with mushrooms, carrot and onion to make the filling. Refrigerate until the chiles are ready."],[null,"Heat a skillet over medium heat. Place chiles in the skillet and roast, turning several times, until the skin blisters. Remove from heat. When chiles are cool enough to handle, peel off the skin."],[null,"Slit chiles lengthwise and carefully stuff half of the cream cheese filling into each chile."],[null,"In another bowl, beat egg whites and flour until stiff. Coat each chile with the egg mixture."],[null,"Pour canola oil into a skillet to a depth of one inch. Heat over medium heat."],[null,"Carefully place chiles in the hot oil and fry until golden brown, turning once. Serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"California chiles, also known as Anaheim chiles, are long peppers with a medium-hot flavor. If you can’t find them, you can substitute low-sodium canned whole chiles."],[null,"Chiles vary in potassium content; some varieties contain more than 300 mg potassium each. Check with your dietitian before substituting other varieties in this recipe."]]},"3797":{"s":[[null,"Chop onion, celery and bell pepper."],[null,"Heat large skillet on medium heat. Add oil, onion, celery and bell pepper until tender, but not brown."],[null,"Add ground beef, breaking into small pieces and cook until brown."],[null,"Blenderize tomatoes and add to beef. Add chili powder and water. Mix thoroughly; reduce heat to low."],[null,"Simmer for several hours."]],"h":[[null,"Serve with low-sodim crackers."]]},"9144888":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven (or toaster oven) to 425 degrees convection bake, and prepare a baking sheet with parchment paper. Place the sweet potato halves cut sides down (skin side up) on the baking sheet and bake for 30-35 minutes, until a fork easily pierces the potato."],[null,"Meanwhile, cook your broccoli in a small pan over covered with water over high heat until fork tender, about 7 minutes."],[null,"In a large skillet, add your chickpeas, lime juice and all the seasonings (except the cilantro) and heat the chickpeas over medium low heat until the lime juice is mostly absorbed. This will take about 3-4 minutes. Turn off heat and add the cilantro and toss to combine."],[null,"Now assemble your two Buddha bowls with half of all the components, and drizzle with sriracha or hot sauce of choice, if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Do not overcook the broccoli , you want it tender crisp for best texture. You may also sub with another veggie, like asparagus, brussels sprouts or cauliflower. Remove any loose chickpea skins but don’t go overboard trying to remove them all, it’s time consuming and unnecessary. If you don’t have wild rice , use brown rice, or your choice."]]},"6640916":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the grill to medium-high."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix together the lime juice, lime zest, margarine, and chili powder."],[null,"Using a spoon and your hands, spread the margarine mixture evenly over the 4 ears of corn."],[null,"Wrap the corn individually in aluminum foil. Grill 20 minutes, turning frequently. Serve hot."]],"h":[]},"6151668":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F."],[null,"In a large bowl, toss the Brussels sprouts with the olive oil, chili powder, garlic powder, salt, and black pepper until well-coated."],[null,"Spread the Brussels sprouts in a single layer on a baking sheet."],[null,"Roast in the preheated oven for 20–25 minutes or until the Brussels sprouts are golden brown and crispy, stirring them halfway through."],[null,"While the Brussels sprouts are roasting, soak the dried cranberries in warm water for 5 minutes to plump them up."],[null,"Remove the Brussels sprouts from the oven."],[null,"Drain the cranberries and sprinkle them over the roasted Brussels sprouts. Toss gently to combine."],[null,"If desired, drizzle balsamic glaze over."]],"h":[]},"4006743":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 300°F."],[null,"To prepare the dip, place all listed dip ingredients in a blender or food processor and blend until smooth, about 30 seconds."],[null,"Transfer to a small bowl, cover and refrigerate for a minimum of 30 minutes."],[null,"Mix olive oil with garlic and brush it on the pitas."],[null,"Cut each pita into 8 wedges, then place wedges on baking tray and roast for 20 minutes or until the chips are crisp, but not browned."],[null,"Arrange dip and pita chips on plate and serve."]],"h":[[null,"* can be replaced with fresh dill or parsley"],[null,"The dip goes well with raw veggies or as a sandwich spread."],[null,"You can keep the pita wedges in a tin for up to a week."],["Tofu and plant-based protein","Eating enough protein is an important part of the kidney diet. Too little protein intake can result in muscle loss, while eating too much makes your kidneys work harder. Working with a registered dietitian can be helpful to determine the amount of protein you need. Incorporating a variety of protein sources from animals and plants can make your diet more exciting. Tofu is one example of a high-protein, low-fat food that can be used instead of meat. Tofu is made from soybean curds and can be purchased in a variety of textures from soft to extra-firm. Per the USDA Nutrient Database, a ½ cup portion of firm tofu contains 22 grams of protein, 18 milligrams of sodium, 299 milligrams of potassium and 239 milligrams of phosphorus. Use tofu in place of chicken to create homemade nuggets, in a burrito as an egg substitute, or grilled as part of a sandwich or salad."]]},"4451881":{"s":[[null,"Preheat conventional oven to 300° F."],[null,"For the dip, put all ingredients in a blender or food processor and blend until smooth, about 30 seconds."],[null,"Transfer to a small bowl, cover and refrigerate for a minimum of 30 minutes."],[null,"Mix olive oil with garlic and brush it on the pitas."],[null,"Cut each pita into 8 wedges, then place wedges on baking tray and roast for 20 minutes or until crisp, but not browned."],[null,"Arrange dip and pita chips on plate and serve."]],"h":[[null,"The dip goes well with raw veggies or as a sandwich spread with meat."],[null,"You can keep the pita wedges in a tin for up to a week."]]},"6759520":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400°F. Add the shallots to a shallow baking dish. Drizzle with 1 Tbsp. of the oil and coat with the chili powder and half of the salt. Cover the dish with foil and roast for 40 minutes, or until tender. Uncover and continue to bake an additional 5 to 6 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the brussels sprouts to a bowl along with black pepper and the remaining oil and salt. Toss to coat. Spread the brussels sprouts in one layer on a baking sheet lined with parchment paper or nonstick foil. Roast the sprouts at 400°F for 30 minutes, or until tender."],[null,"To serve, combine the shallots and brussels sprouts in a serving bowl. Top with the pine nuts and lemon zest."]],"h":[]},"3788":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Grease and flour a 13” x 9” x 2” pan."],[null,"In a large mixing bowl, blend the cake mix, applesauce, eggs and water for 30 seconds on low speed to mix. Increase mixer to medium speed and mix for 2 minutes."],[null,"Pour cake batter into prepared cake pan and bake 40 minutes, or until a toothpick inserted into the middle of the cake comes out clean."],[null,"Cool cake completely. Do not remove from cake pan."],[null,"While cake is cooling, mix powdered sugar and lemon juice in a small bowl until blended."],[null,"Poke holes over the top of the cooled cake 1/2” apart."],[null,"Spoon the glaze over the top of cake, allowing it to seep into holes. Eventually it will coat the top of the cake with an opaque covering."],[null,"Chill thoroughly and serve."]],"h":[[null,"The colder the cake, the better it tastes. This is a great recipe for spring and summer."]]},"6100173":{"s":[[null,"Stir together the cucumber, yogurt, 2 tablespoons chives, the mint, shallot, garlic, vinegar, pepper, salt, and tea in a medium bowl. Adjust seasoning. Chill until ready to serve."],[null,"Divide the soup among individual small soup cups or bowls. Serve topped with the remaining 1 teaspoon chives."]],"h":[]},"6644102":{"s":[[null,"Place the tomatoes, balsamic vinegar, sugar, lemon juice, and 1 Tbsp of the tarragon in a food processor or blender. Mix to form a smooth soup."],[null,"Place a large, fine mesh strainer or chinois over a bowl and pour in the soup. Use a wooden spoon to turn and press the soup through the strainer, a little at a time, until the tomato solids are left in the strainer and the liquid has passed through."],[null,"Place the soup in a large saucepan and season with the salt and pepper, to taste."],[null,"Bring the mixture to a boil over high heat, then reduce the heat to low and simmer, uncovered, for 10 to 20 minutes, or until the soup is thickened and the volume has been reduced by about a third."],[null,"Garnish the soup with the remaining tarragon leaves. Refrigerate and serve chilled. (If preferred, serve warm.)"]],"h":[]},"2920":{"s":[[null,"Chop the zucchini, yellow squash and onion into large pieces."],[null,"In a saucepan bring the broth to a boil, then reduce heat to medium."],[null,"Stir in the zucchini, yellow squash and onion; simmer for 25 minutes."],[null,"Add the green peas, oil and salt; simmer for an additional 5 minutes."],[null,"Remove pan from the heat and let the soup cool to room temperature."],[null,"Use a blender to combine ingredients into a smooth consistency. Stir in the Greek yogurt and turmeric."],[null,"Refrigerate at least 6 hours or overnight before serving chilled soup."]],"h":[[null,"Try one of these items for additional seasoning: lemon juice, sriracha hot chili sauce, hot sauce, mint leaves, chives or cumin."],[null,"Look for frozen green peas that are unseasoned or substitute fresh green peas."],[null,"If available use an immersion blender to easily blend the soup in the saucepan."]]},"7540633":{"s":[[null,"Heat the sunflower oil in a large pan, add the onion, garlic and chillies and fry for 2-3 minutes until the onion begins to soften. Add the spices and continue to fry for a further minute."],[null,"Add the remaining soup ingredients to the pan, bring to the boil, cover and simmer for 20 minutes."],[null,"Transfer the soup to a food processor or use a stick blender and process until smooth (it may be easier to do this in batches), return to the pan and heat through. Meanwhile, mix together all the ingredients for the salsa."],[null,"Serve the soup topped with a spoonful of salsa."]],"h":[[null,"For a lighter soup, use cannellini beans rather than kidney beans."],[null,"If you don’t want a fiery salsa simply leave out the chilli."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"7046889":{"s":[[null,"Add the oil to a large pan, then add the onions and cook for 3–4 minutes until just starting to brown."],[null,"Add the minced beef and cook for 5–7 minutes (or until cooked thoroughly), breaking up any clumps with a wooden spoon."],[null,"Add the mushrooms, peppers, courgette and garlic. Cook for a further 7–8 minutes, stirring regularly until they soften."],[null,"Stir in the chilli, oregano, cumin and tomatoes, then cover with a lid and simmer gently for 10 minutes, stirring occasionally."],[null,"Add the lentils and beans, and mix well. Cover and simmer for a further 5 minutes."],[null,"Stir in the chocolate until melted. Serve with salad."]],"h":[[null,"Dark chocolate intensifies the flavours and is healthier and works better than other types of chocolate."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost fully in the fridge and reheat until piping hot throughout, stirring regularly."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"7890431":{"s":[[null,"Spray a large non-stick frying pan with a couple of pumps of low-calorie cooking spray and put it over a medium-high heat. Add the garlic and chillies and fry for 1 minute. Add the onion, peppers and broccoli with 100ml water and fry for 2-3 minutes. Stir in the kale and fry for 2 minutes. Season lightly with black pepper, add a squeeze of lemon juice and serve."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"1742":{"s":[[null,"Stem and mince parsley. Grate carrot. Mince onion and bell pepper."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine all ingredients except chicken broth."],[null,"Whisk to mix well. Add broth a few tablespoons at a time to moisten sauce to the consistency of applesauce."],[null,"Taste and add 1-2 tablespoons more vinegar if desired (sauce should be highly seasoned)."],[null,"Serve sauce with meat or poultry. Refrigerate leftover sauce for up to 3 days."]],"h":[[null,"For quick preparation method use a food processor: Process 1 small carrot, 1 small onion and 1/2 bell pepper to chopped consistency. Add stemmed parsley and process until vegetables are finely minced. Add olive oil, vinegar and spices and process until mixed thoroughly. Continue with steps 2 and 3 above."],[null,"Serve sauce with Nicaraguan Beef Tenderloins."]]},"3345":{"s":[[null,"Grind all spices and keep in an airtight container until ready to use in a recipe."]],"h":[[null,"Chinese Five Spice is popular in Chinese cooking and many Asian dishes."],[null,"Use Chinese Five Spice in egg rolls, Chinese bok choy soup or roast chicken drumsticks."],[null,"Sichuan peppercorns are also known as Szechuan peppercorns."]]},"6315562":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 300°F. Add the kale to a large bowl and toss well with the oil, five-spice powder and salt."],[null,"Arrange the leaves in a single layer onto 2 large baking sheets. Bake until the leaves are crisp, about 20 minutes."],[null,"Transfer the sheets to racks to cool, then serve."]],"h":[]},"3225":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Dice celery and onion."],[null,"In a large skillet, brown ground beef, celery and onion. Drain."],[null,"Pour cooked ground beef into a 2-quart casserole baking dish."],[null,"Using a wooden spoon, mix in chicken noodle soup, cream of chicken soup, Worcestershire sauce, rice and boiling water and mix thoroughly."],[null,"Cover and bake for 50 minutes."],[null,"Remove dish from oven and stir."],[null,"Sprinkle chow mein noodles over top of casserole."],[null,"Bake an additional 10 minutes, uncovered."],[null,"Let stand 15 minutes before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Compare chow mein noodle nutrition labels and select the brand lowest in sodium"]]},"3111":{"s":[[null,"Prepare rice sticks according to package instructions (typically cover sticks with cold water for 20 minutes and then separate)."],[null,"Slice the bok choy, celery and carrot into thin slices. Dice the onion; mince the garlic."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine coconut aminos, broth, chili sauce, garlic and corn starch."],[null,"Heat a pan over medium-high heat and add canola and sesame oils. Add the diced onion and cook until translucent. Add the bok choy, celery and carrot slices and stir-fry until tender crisp."],[null,"Add sauce to cooked vegetables and stir to combine."],[null,"Once the rice sticks have softened, separate the noodles and add to pan with sauce and vegetables. Stir all to combine."],[null,"Let sit 15 minutes prior to serving for flavors to fully develop."],[null,"Slice green onion and sprinkle on top to garnish before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Rice sticks are also known as rice noodles."],[null,"You can substitute soba, udon, vermicelli or spaghetti for rice noodles. Prepare according to instructions instead of soaking."],[null,"Add tofu, shrimp or chicken to make a meal."],[null,"Coconut aminos replace soy sauce or tamari in this recipe to keep sodium lower."]]},"7195577":{"s":[[null,"Place a piece of greaseproof paper into a large steamer and put the fish on top."],[null,"Mix together all the remaining ingredients and spoon over the fish."],[null,"Cover with the lid and steam for 6-8 minutes or until the fish is cooked."],[null,"Serve with stir-fried vegetables or noodles or rice."]],"h":[[null,"If you don't have a steamer, wrap the fish in baking paper and place on a wire rack over a baking tray. Add a little boiling water to the tray and cover with foil. Then cook in the oven at 200°C/gas mark 6, for 8-10 minutes."],[null,"You can cook any dish using this method, but if you use whole fish or thick steaks you will need to increase the cooking time."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"6021884":{"s":[[null,"Place all ingredients except the salmon in a blender or food processor and purée until smooth."],[null,"Rub the mixture over the surface of the salmon. Place the salmon on a baking dish and let marinate for 20 minutes."],[null,"Preheat the grill to medium-high heat. You can cook the salmon directly on a piece of foil or place them on a perforated grill grate used for fish or vegetables. Cook over indirect heat (away from the heat source) for 5–6 minutes on each side. The salmon is done when it reads 145 degrees F on an instant thermometer."],[null,"Cool for 30 minutes before serving."]],"h":[]},"2950":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400° F with the oven rack in the top position. Trim and thinly slice scallions, keeping the whites separated from the greens. Finely chop whites. Press garlic clove with flat edge of knife so that the peel splits open. Peel garlic and finely mince."],[null,"In a small bowl combine the ketchup and 1/2 teaspoon of chipotle chili powder and set aside."],[null,"In a medium bowl, combine beef, scallion whites, minced garlic, panko, pepper, salt and remaining 1/2 teaspoon chipotle chili powder."],[null,"Shape beef mixture into two loaves. Place on a baking sheet sprayed with nonstick spray."],[null,"Bake until meat loaves are almost cooked through, about 15 minutes."],[null,"Brush meat loaves with ketchup mixture. Return to oven for 4 to 8 minutes or until meat loaves are cooked through to internal temperature of 160° F.."],[null,"Garnish with chopped scallion greens before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Loaves can also be cooked in individual loaf pans."],[null,"If no salt added ketchup is unavailable at your local grocery store consider ordering it online."],[null,"Double the recipe to make extra to freeze for a quick dish later."]]},"6673913":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400°F. Line a baking sheet with aluminum foil. Place salmon fillets on the baking sheet."],[null,"Finely chop the peppers in adobo sauce and place in a small bowl along with the olive oil, stir to combine. Spread the mixture over each salmon fillet."],[null,"Place the baking sheet in the oven and bake for 8-10 minutes, until salmon reads 145°F."],[null,"Meanwhile, combine watermelon, mango, red onion, jalapeño, lime zest and juice, salt, pepper, and cilantro in a bowl. Stir to combine salsa."],[null,"Divide fish between plates and top with watermelon salsa."]],"h":[]},"9162814":{"s":[[null,"Add the dates and water, starting with 2 tablespoons to the bowl of your food processor. Process until mostly smooth, and you have date paste. Pause to scrape down the sides, and add more water if needed."],[null,"Then, add all the remaining ingredients EXCEPT the almonds, and process until mostly smooth. Finally, add the almonds and pulse until they are mostly broken down, but leave some chunks for added texture."],[null,"Use slightly wet hands to roll your mixture into approx. one-inch balls, and then place them on a plate or baking sheet."],[null,"OPTIONAL: Roll one-third of the chocolate almond balls in shredded coconut, one-third in crushed almonds, and leave one-third plain."]],"h":[[null,"If your dates are very dry , soak them in hot water for 10-15 minutes, and then drain them before adding them to your food processor. This will help soften them and make them easier to process."],[null,"Use slightly wet hands to shape the balls to prevent sticking. The batter will be sticky, which is normal."],[null,"To make the crushed almond coating , I place the almonds in a zip-top bag on a cutting board and smash away with a rolling pin. Or use a food processor or another tool."],[null,"Keep leftovers in the fridge for up to 5 days, or store them airtight in your freezer for up to 3 months."]]},"7308711":{"s":[[null,"Place the chocolate into a bowl set over a pan of simmering water. Heat gently until melted. Spread 2 tbsp of melted chocolate thinly onto a piece of non-stick baking paper. Sprinkle over the pistachio nuts to cover. Chill."],[null,"Place the banana into a food processor with the vanilla extract, 6 tbsp yogurt and cocoa powder. Drizzle over the remaining melted chocolate and add 2 tbsps boiling water. Blend until smooth and thick. Spoon into individual glasses and chill for at least 2 hours."],[null,"When ready to serve, spoon 1 tbsp of the remaining yogurt over each dessert. Break the chocolate and pistachio bar into shards to decorate the desserts."]],"h":[]},"9863153":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350℉/176℃ and line a loaf pan with parchment paper."],[null,"Add the beans, sugar and applesauce to your food processor bowl. Blend until smooth."],[null,"Then add the flour, cocoa powder, and baking powder and continue processing until combined. Scrape down the sides as needed."],[null,"Transfer the cake batter to your lined loaf pan and sprinkle with the chocolate chips if using them. Bake it in your preheated oven for 20-25 minutes, or until a toothpick inserted in the middle comes out mostly clean."],[null,"Remove the cake from the oven and let it cool for 10-15 minutes before gently transferring it to a wire rack to completely cool."],[null,"Once cool, slice the cake into 8 or 16 squares using a wet knife in between cuts to prevent sticking. (The nutritional info and photos represent 8 slices.)"]],"h":[[null,"Weigh your flour using a kitchen scale for the most accurate results . Scooping flour from a bag may result in too much flour being used and could alter the texture."],[null,"Use fresh and active baking powder . Once opened, baking powder begins to lose its effectiveness, so it's best to consume your baking powder within 6 months."],[null,"Let the cake cool in its pan for at least 10-15 minutes before transferring it to a cooling rack to completely cool."],[null,"Use a wet knife to slice the cake for neat slices and to prevent sticking."],[null,"Leftovers keep at room temperature for 1-2 days, in the fridge for up to 5 days or frozen for up to 3 months."]]},"7823636":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oven to 180°C/gas 4. Grease a 20 x 20cm baking tin and line with greaseproof paper."],[null,"Melt the chocolate and low-fat spread in a bowl, set over a pan of simmering water or in the microwave, stirring often. Leave to cool a little."],[null,"Pat away any excess liquid from the beetroot with kitchen paper. Place in a liquidiser with the dissolved coffee, eggs, vanilla extract and maple syrup. Blend until puréed."],[null,"Add the ground almonds, flour, cocoa powder, sweetener and baking powder and blend until well combined."],[null,"Spoon the mixture into the prepared tin and smooth over the top with a spoon. Bake in the oven for 15-20 minutes or until the top is firm and a skewer inserted into the middle of the brownie comes out with sticky crumbs attached, but isn't liquid."],[null,"Leave to cool for 15 minutes, cut into squares or rectangles and serve."]],"h":[[null,"You can make fruity brownies by adding 2 tbsp raisins, or try adding 2 tbsp of chopped walnuts or flaked almonds."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Freeze in individually wrapped portions. Defrost for 2 hours in the fridge or in the microwave on a low/defrost setting."]]},"9854744":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425℉/218℃ convection bake and line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Arrange your chickpeas in a single layer on the tray and bake them for 15 minutes, then shake or mix them around and bake another 10-15 minutes until crispy."],[null,"In the last 5-10 minutes of baking the chickpeas, melt the chocolate in a double boiler. (If you don't have one, use this method.)"],[null,"Then add the 1/8 teaspoon of salt to the melted chocolate, stir, and add the roasted chickpeas. Stir to evenly coat them."],[null,"Use a small cookie scoop or a tablespoon to spoon clusters of the chocolate chickpeas back onto the same baking sheet. (You should get about 16 clusters.)"],[null,"Now, sprinkle the clusters with the coarse salt (if using it) while the chocolate is still in a melty state so the flakes stick to the clusters. Then refrigerate the tray for at least one hour to harden and solidify the chocolate again before enjoying."]],"h":[]},"5236081":{"s":[[null,"Break the Vitabite into small pieces and place in a small bowl with the Renastep."],[null,"Melt in the microwave in 10 second increments until melted."],[null,"Mix together until smooth, with no lumps visible."],[null,"Pour into lolly moulds and freeze for 24 hours."]],"h":[["Renastep note","Renastep and Vitabite are foods for special medical purposes and must be used under medical supervision. Renastep is for the dietary management of kidney disease and is suitable from 3 years of age onwards. Vitabite is for use in protein restricted diets and is suitable from 1 year of age onwards. Renastep contains Milk (milk protein) and Fish (Tuna Oils). Vitabite contains Milk (lactose) and Soya (soya lecithin)."],["Renastep note","This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutrimen dietary analysis software. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information."]]},"7106172":{"s":[[null,"Place a bowl over a saucepan of gently simmering water. Break the chocolate into squares and add to the bowl, making sure the bowl is not actually touching the water. Add the sugar and gently stir until the chocolate has melted and the sugar has dissolved."],[null,"Next, add half of the Greek yogurt to the bowl, mixing thoroughly, then remove from the saucepan. Stir in the rest of the Greek yogurt."],[null,"Add the egg whites to another bowl, and whisk until they're stiff and fluffy. Then, fold them carefully into the chocolate."],[null,"Spoon the mixture into 6 small glasses or espresso cups and refrigerate for at least 30 minutes."],[null,"Just before serving, garnish each mousse with a raspberry, and serve the rest of the raspberries alongside. You could also add extra fruit when serving, such as blueberries, orange segments and sliced fresh figs, along with a few sprigs of fresh mint."]],"h":[[null,"Serve one bowl of mousse surrounded with chunks of fruit on cocktail stick to create a chocolate fondue."],[null,"Strawberries, apple, pear, banana and kumquats are all great for dipping."],[null,"Add the finely grated zest of an orange to the melting chocolate to give your mousse a subtle chocolate flavour or add a teaspoon of almond extract for extra flavour."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"7920715":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 200°C/fan 180°C/gas 6."],[null,"Lightly grease 6 ovenproof teacups. In a small pan, heat the orange rind, juice and caster sugar for 3–4 minutes until syrupy. Pour the syrup over the egg whites and beat for 2 minutes."],[null,"Fold in the cocoa and orange juice mixture, then pour into the teacups."],[null,"Cook in the oven for 5–6 minutes or until risen."],[null,"Serve topped with the crème fraîche."]],"h":[[null,"If you have trouble getting your egg whites to peak properly, add a drop or two of lemon juice to help strengthen the structure of the mixture."],[null,"To get your soufflés to rise, don’t overfold. Instead, gently fold in the whites until the point where the streaks of white disappear."],[null,"Use fresh, room temperature eggs. Whipping cold eggs is harder work and you won't get as much lift from them."]]},"6500455":{"s":[[null,"Mix cocoa powder, low- or no-calorie sweetener, and powdered peanut butter together, and incorporate well so there are no lumps."],[null,"Stir in the chia seeds and stir well to combine."],[null,"Whisk in the milk and vanilla. Let sit for 5 minutes, then whisk again. Cover and refrigerate for at least 2 hours before serving."]],"h":[]},"3699":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350° F. Line a muffin tin with paper liners."],[null,"Melt butter and honey together. Whisk in cocoa powder and peanut butter until smooth."],[null,"Whisk in eggs and baking soda. Mix in chocolate chips. Pour evenly into muffin tin."],[null,"Bake for 18-22 minutes or until a toothpick inserted in the center comes out clean."]],"h":[[null,"If desired use almond butter in place of peanut butter. Almond butter has 24 mg more phosphorus and 16 mg more potassium per serving than peanut butter."],[null,"If preferred use reduced-fat peanut butter. This change will add approximately 4 grams of carbohydrate per serving."],[null,"Chocolate and peanut butter are high in potassium and phosphorus. The secret to including in a kidney diet is the portion–1 small muffin. Ask your dietitian if you need a phosphate binder with this muffin."]]},"9931828":{"s":[[null,"Add the almond butter, maple syrup, and pumpkin puree to a medium mixing bowl. Stir well using a fork to combine."],[null,"Then add the almond flour, cocoa powder and cinnamon, and stir until combined."],[null,"Use a small cookie scoop to divide the mixture and roll into balls. Then refrigerate for 15 minutes or longer to help them firm up."],[null,"Optional: In a small bowl, combine 1 tablespoon of coconut sugar and 1 teaspoon of cinnamon to roll some or all of the balls into the mixture. NOTE: This will increase the sugar."]],"h":[[null,"The batter will be sticky, so use damp hands to roll the mixture into balls to prevent it from sticking to your hands."],[null,"The rolled balls will be soft, so refrigerate them for at least 15 minutes before enjoying them to help them set."],[null,"Leftovers will keep refrigerated for 3-4 days or frozen for up to 3 months."]]},"2648":{"s":[[null,"Combine cocoa, cold water and sugar."],[null,"Stir until sugar dissolves."],[null,"Add egg whites and 3 tablespoons of the whipped topping. Mix until whipped topping melts completely."],[null,"Top with 1 tablespoon whipped topping and chocolate bar shavings."]],"h":[[null,"Pasteurized egg whites are safe to consume without cooking."],[null,"Add 1/4 teaspoon mint extract for a chocolate mint smoothie."],[null,"People with diabetes can substitute sugar substitute if desired. Carbohydrate is reduced to 6 grams per serving."]]},"6345604":{"s":[[null,"Spray a coffee mug with cooking spray."],[null,"Add the flour, cocoa powder, baking powder, salt, stevia, canola oil, milk and vanilla and stir to combine."],[null,"Microwave for 45 seconds."],[null,"Top with the walnuts and serve."]],"h":[]},"7199003":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oven to 190°C/gas 5 and lightly oil a 20 cm cake tin."],[null,"Sieve the wholemeal, plain, cornflour, baking powder and cocoa powder into a bowl. (the bran in the wholemeal won't go through the sieve but just add it back to the bowl)"],[null,"In another bowl add egg yolks, yoghurt, sweetener and almond extract and beat well."],[null,"In a separate bowl beat the egg whites until they form a stiff peak."],[null,"Gradually fold the dry ingredients, egg yolk and yoghurt mixture together, then carefully fold in the egg whites."],[null,"Place the mixture immediately into the oiled cake tin and bake for 20-25 minutes, then remove from the oven and allow to cool on a wire rack."],[null,"Meanwhile, make the topping by stirring 1 tablespoon of sweetener into the quark and mixing well, leave it in the fridge until you are ready to top the cake."],[null,"When the cake is cool cover with the sweetened quark and top with fresh strawberries and raspberries."]],"h":[[null,"Whisked egg whites make the cake lighter so take care not to overmix as your cake could become a bit heavy (but will still taste good!)"],[null,"When you add the egg whites back into the cake mixture, fold them gently to keep the air bubbles trapped inside."],[null,"Make sure the cake is fully cooled before you add the topping."],[null,"Any summer fruits work well. Try adding blueberries, or you could use slices of fresh peach or apricot."]]},"6738682":{"s":[[null,"In a large salad bowl, add all of the ingredients, except salad dressing, and toss."],[null,"Add the salad dressing and toss to coat well. Divide evenly among 5 bowls."]],"h":[]},"6953417":{"s":[[null,"Place the lettuce on a shallow platter. In rows, arrange the carrots, celery, plum tomatoes, cucumber, and black beans."],[null,"Prepare the salad dressing. Whisk together the cider vinegar, lime juice, cilantro, honey, salt, and pepper. Slowly drizzle in the oil, whisking to incorporate."],[null,"Drizzle on the dressing. Top with toasted pumpkin or sunflower seeds."]],"h":[]},"6786566":{"s":[],"h":[]},"7221210":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4 and boil the kettle."],[null,"Put all the dried fruits and spices into a bowl, mix thoroughly and add 50ml boiling water. Cover and leave for 15 minutes."],[null,"Brush the oil around a 1 pint pudding basin. Arrange the whole cherries and whole almonds on the bottom."],[null,"In a separate bowl, mash the banana and mix in the grated apple, carrot, oatmeal, flour, baking powder, zest and seeds."],[null,"Add the fruits, spices and water they were soaking in, mixing everything together well. Spoon into the pudding basin."],[null,"Cover with pleated greaseproof paper and foil, and wrap tightly over the basin."],[null,"Stand the basin in a deep oven tray with 5cm of water in it (this is called a bain marie). Bake for 1 hour."],[null,"Remove from the bain marie and cook for a further 10 minutes. Remove from the oven, but leave covered. Allow to cool a little before serving."]],"h":[[null,"You can also cook the pudding by tying some string around the rim to seal it. Then, make a string handle from one side of the basin to the other, so you can lift out the pudding. Place the bowl in a saucepan of water two thirds of the way up the bowl. Bring to the boil, add a lid and turn down the heat and simmer gently for 1.25 hours, making sure the water doesn't evaporate by adding more boiling water, if needed."],[null,"You could use mixed dried fruits rather than separate dried fruit. If you don't have all the spices, use double the amount of mixed spice."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Can be frozen either ready-to-cook or cooked. Defrost, then heat in the microwave or steam to serve."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"5947095":{"s":[["For the base","Preheat the oven to 200°C/180°C Fan/Gas Mark 6."],["For the base","Place the Renastep and yeast into a mixing bowl and stir until combined."],["For the base","Add the flour, sugar and oil to the Renastep and yeast mixture and mix together by hand until a dough forms. Knead for 2 minutes"],["For the base","Leave the dough to rise for 60 minutes in a warm place."],["For the base","Lightly dust a clean work surface with flour and roll the dough ball into a rectangle 22cm long and 13cm wide. Using a knife, cut a diagonal line from the centre of the top of the rectangle to the bottom left and right corners to create a triangle shape."],["For the base","Place the triangle onto a baking tray lined with grease proof paper. Use the remaining dough to make a small tree trunk at the bottom of the triangle – stick this to the tree with a drop of oil."],["For the topping","To make the pesto, blend the basil, oil and garlic together in a bowl, using a hand blender."],["For the topping","Take your pizza base and cover the tree with pesto using the back of a spoon to spread. Leave a border around the edge."],["For the topping","Place the sliced pepper and red onion across the tree in rows to resemble tinsel."],["For the topping","Sprinkle Violife mozzarella style over the pizza"],["For the topping","To make a star, slice a large carrot lengthways to make a thin slice, cut out a star shape and place at the top of the tree."],["For the topping","Cook the base and topping in the oven at 200°C/180°C Fan/Gas Mark 6 for approximately 15 minutes. Serve warm."]],"h":[["Renastep note","Renastep is a Food for Special Medical Purposes and must be used under medical supervision."],["Renastep note","Renastep is a ready to use feed for the dietary management of kidney disease from 3 years of age onwards. Renastep contains milk and fish. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information."],["Renastep note","This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutrimen dietary analysis software."]]},"7113140":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200°C"],[null,"Place the potatoes in a large saucepan and cover with water. Bring to the boil and boil for 2 minutes."],[null,"Drain. Place on a non-stick baking tray and drizzle with oil. Toss the potatoes in the oil to coat evenly."],[null,"Cook for 25-30 minutes until crisp."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"6306662":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F. Line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"In a bowl, whisk together apple cider, maple syrup, olive oil, ground cinnamon, ground nutmeg, salt, and black pepper."],[null,"Place the delicata squash half-moons in a single layer on a baking sheet."],[null,"Drizzle the cider and maple mixture over the squash, ensuring they are well coated."],[null,"Roast in the preheated oven for 25 minutes or until the squash is tender, turning halfway through."]],"h":[]},"2798":{"s":[[null,"Wash cilantro and green chili."],[null,"Roughly chop onion, garlic, cilantro and chili."],[null,"Grind in a blender along with salt, cumin and lemon juice."],[null,"Serve with idli, on a veggie sandwich or with other snacks."]],"h":[[null,"Instead of 2 cups of cilantro, use 2/3 cup cilantro and 1/3 cup of mint for a sweet flavor."],[null,"One bunch of cilantro is approximately 2 cups."],[null,"Adjust chili for desired heat."],[null,"Decrease serving size to a teaspoon if used with a snack or 1 tablespoon if used as a sandwich spread."]]},"3510":{"s":[[null,"Chop cilantro. Finely dice bell pepper."],[null,"Toss coleslaw mix, cilantro and red pepper together."],[null,"Whisk olive oil, lime juice, cumin and chili powder together in a small bowl."],[null,"Pour dressing over slaw mixture, toss until coated and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Use ancho chili powder if you like it spicy."]]},"6451648":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium heat. Add the onions and cook for 3 to 4 minutes. Add the garlic and cook for 30 seconds. Reduce the heat to low and add quinoa. Cook over a low heat for 1-2 minutes, stirring constantly to make sure the quinoa doesn’t burn."],[null,"Add the vegetable broth and the juice of 1 lime and bring it to a boil. Reduce the heat to low, cover and simmer for 15 minutes or until done. Remove from heat."],[null,"Stir in the juice of 1 lime and chopped cilantro."]],"h":[]},"6606398":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, combine the cooked brown rice, black beans, corn, diced red bell pepper, chopped red onion, and fresh cilantro."],[null,"In a small bowl, juice the two limes. Add the olive oil, ground cumin, chili powder, and coarse salt. Whisk until well combined."],[null,"Pour the dressing over the rice and bean mixture. Toss well to ensure even coating."],[null,"Allow the flavors to meld for a few minutes before serving."],[null,"Top with avocado slices, if desired."]],"h":[]},"6020500":{"s":[[null,"DO AHEAD OR DELEGATE: Peel the garlic, juice the lime, chop the cilantro, combine the lime juice, cilantro, salt, and pepper."],[null,"(Start the buckwheat and the broccoli first, if you are serving them.) In a large heavy skillet over medium-high heat, heat the oil. Add the garlic and cook it for 30 seconds or so until it is fragrant, then add the shrimp and cook, turning once, until the shrimp are pink and cooked through, about 2–3 minutes per side."],[null,"Transfer the shrimp to a bowl, and combine with the lime juice, cilantro, salt, and pepper. Serve immediately or refrigerate for up to 2 days and serve cold."],[null,"FLAVOR BOOSTER Double the garlic and sprinkle the finished dish with 1/2 teaspoon lime zest or salt-free lemon-pepper seasoning."]],"h":[]},"2089":{"s":[[null,"In medium bowl, combine mayonnaise, chopped cilantro and lime juice. Transfer 1/4 cup to a small bowl and set aside to serve as sauce with fish."],[null,"Brush fish with remaining mayonnaise mixture."],[null,"Spray a large skillet with cooking spray and heat over medium-high heat. Add cod fillets and cook turning once, for 8 minutes or until fish is firm but moist. Serve with cilantro-lime sauce."]],"h":[[null,"If desired 1/4-cup chopped fresh dill weed may be substituted for the cilantro."],[null,"Replace regular mayonnaise with low-fat mayonnaise to reduce fat to 11 grams per serving."]]},"6553465":{"s":[[null,"In a saucepan, bring water to a boil."],[null,"Stir in oats and reduce heat to medium-low. Cook, stirring occasionally, for about 5 minutes or until oats begin to thicken."],[null,"Add milk, diced apple, cinnamon, nutmeg, and salt. Continue to cook, stirring frequently, until the oats are creamy, and the apples are tender (about 5 more minutes)."],[null,"Remove from heat and let it sit for a minute to thicken."],[null,"Divide the oatmeal into two bowls. Serve warm."]],"h":[]},"6690371":{"s":[[null,"In a bowl or jar, combine rolled oats, almond milk, Greek yogurt, chopped apple, chopped nuts, maple syrup, ground cinnamon, vanilla extract, and a pinch of salt. Stir well."],[null,"Cover the bowl or jar and refrigerate overnight or for at least 8 hours."],[null,"In the morning, give the overnight oats a good stir."],[null,"Adjust the consistency with additional almond milk if desired."]],"h":[]},"6050561":{"s":[[null,"Place the apple halves, lemon juice, ginger, cinnamon and honey in a resealable bag and seal it shut. Turn the bag to coat the apples with the mixture and allow the apples to marinate for 30 minutes."],[null,"Preheat grill to medium high. Remove the apples from the bag and place on the grill. Cook for 5–6 minutes, turning once until they are golden brown on the outside and just warmed through on the inside."],[null,"Remove apples from the grill, cool for a few minutes, and roll in crushed walnuts. Press gently."],[null,"Place a skewer in each apple half and serve."]],"h":[]},"6500091":{"s":[[null,"Cut peaches in half and remove the seed. Place peach halves in a resealable plastic bag."],[null,"Mix the lemon juice, cinnamon, nutmeg, and maple syrup in a small bowl. Pour the mixture over the peaches in the bag. Seal the bag and turn to coat the peaches."],[null,"Preheat grill to medium high. Cook for 4–5 minutes, turning once, until golden brown on the outside, and just warmed through inside."]],"h":[]},"6521634":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F."],[null,"In a small bowl (using fingers) combine margarine, cinnamon and brown sugar. Add walnuts and mix."],[null,"Arrange the pears cut side up in an 8-inch square glass baking dish. Pour 1/4 cup water in bottom of pan."],[null,"Divide the brown sugar mixture evenly among the pear halves and place in middle of pears."],[null,"Bake until the pears are tender and beginning to brown, about 45 minutes."]],"h":[]},"3079":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Melt 1/2 cup butter and leave remaining butter out to soften."],[null,"In medium-sized bowl, mix 3 cups flour, salt, 1 cup Splenda baking blend, baking soda, cream of tartar, 1-1/2 cups Rice Dream, eggs and 2 teaspoons vanilla. Slowly stir in melted butter."],[null,"Pour mixture into a greased 9″ x 13″ pan."],[null,"Mix 1 cup softened butter, Splenda brown sugar blend, 2 tablespoons flour and cinnamon until well combined. Drop evenly over the batter and swirl with a knife."],[null,"Bake for 28-32 minutes."],[null,"Combine remaining 1 cup Splenda baking blend and powdered sugar, 5 tablespoons rice milk and 1 teaspoon vanilla. Drizzle over cake while it’s still warm."]],"h":[[null,"This high calorie dessert is great for boosting calories. Enjoy for breakfast or dessert."],[null,"If available,1 cup Ideal® powdered sugar substitute may be used to replace 1 cup Splenda baking blend and 1 cup powdered sugar to reduce calories and carbohydrates."]]},"3199":{"s":[[null,"Combine cinnamon and sugar."],[null,"Add 2 ounces egg whites. Mix well."],[null,"Add vanilla and stir."],[null,"Add balance of egg whites and stir."],[null,"Add whipped topping and mix until dissolved."]],"h":[[null,"Low-cholesterol egg whites is pasteurized. It is safe to consume without cooking. Do not use raw egg whites."],[null,"People with diabetes can substitute sugar-free sugar substitute if desired. Carbohydrate is reduced to 6 grams per serving if sugar substitute is used instead of sugar."]]},"4374835":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400⁰ F."],[null,"Mix cinnamon and brown sugar and set aside."],[null,"Mix all ingredients (except cinnamon and brown sugar mixture) to create a dough."],[null,"Roll dough into 1 inch balls."],[null,"Roll balls in the cinnamon/brown sugar mixture (should make 24 balls)."],[null,"Place on cookie sheet and bake at 400⁰ F for 8-10 minutes."]],"h":[]},"4439578":{"s":[[null,"Place Nepro®, sugar, cinnamon, almond extract and pears in a blender and mix until smooth."],[null,"Add ice cubes and continue to blend until thick and frothy."],[null,"Pour into a tall glass and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Almond extract is a pure, natural product made from the oil of bitter almonds. Almond essense is made using artificial flavorings and is less expensive."],[null,"Nepro® Carb Steady™ is specialized nutrition designed to meet the nutrient needs of people on dialysis. It is an Abbott Nutrition product that can be used as a nutritious snack, a supplement or a sole source of nutrition."],[null,"For extra creamy results, put the Nepro® bottle in the freezer at least 1 hour before use."]]},"6150171":{"s":[[null,"In a medium bowl, whisk together orange and lime juice, hot sauce, garlic and pepper. Add shrimp to bowl and place in refrigerator to marinate for 20 minutes."],[null,"Prepare an indoor or outdoor grill to medium. Spray grill rack with cooking spray."],[null,"Place shrimp on skewers and grill for 2-3 minutes on each side or until shrimp are done."],[null,"Serve shrimp on top of spring mix salad with clementine slices."],[null,"Whisk together dressing ingredients and pour over shrimp and salad."]],"h":[]},"6768914":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 425° F. Place two pieces parchment paper on a baking sheet."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together lemon juice, olive oil, pepper and dill."],[null,"Place a few lemon and orange slices on center of parchment papers. Place fish fillets on top of orange and lemon slices. Drizzle lemon sauce evenly over fish fillets. Top fish with remaining orange and lemon slices. Fold over the top of the parchment paper, then roll the sides in to form a sealed pouch."],[null,"Place packets on baking sheet and bake for 25 minutes or until done."],[null,"While fish is baking, steam broccoli for 5-6 minutes."],[null,"Serve fish packet with steamed broccoli. Be cautious when opening fish packet, as steam may be hot."]],"h":[]},"2672":{"s":[[null,"Crush the garlic."],[null,"In a small saucepan, combine all the ingredients except the salmon. Heat to a boil, and then reduce the temperature to low and cook for 5 more minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, preheat grill. Place the salmon, skin side down, on a sheet of foil slightly larger than the fish. Fold up the edges so the sauce stays with the salmon on the grill. Place the foil and fish on the grill. Top the salmon with the sauce prepared above."],[null,"Cover the grill and cook for 12 minutes or until salmon is cooked. (Do not flip salmon). Cut the salmon into 6 servings."]],"h":[[null,"Recipe was calculated with farmed Atlantic salmon. Wild Alaskan salmon is slightly lower in fat and slightly higher in potassium and phosphorus. Both are acceptable healthy choices for a kidney diet."],[null,"You can also cook this recipe in the oven at 350°F for 10 to 15 minutes until done. A good rule of thumb is to allow 10 minutes for each inch of fillet thickness."],[null,"If you are on a lower protein diet adjust portion to match your meal plan."]]},"2295":{"s":[[null,"Place ingredients in a blender and blend for 30 seconds."],[null,"Divide into 2 servings."],[null,"Serve immediately or freeze for later."]],"h":[[null,"Low-cholesterol egg product is pasteurized. It is safe to consume without cooking. Do not use raw eggs."],[null,"Pasteurized egg whites can be substituted for low-cholesterol egg product."],[null,"Rice milk may be substituted for almond milk. Avoid milk substitutes that contain phosphate additives."]]},"3334":{"s":[[null,"Crack eggs in bowl and use whisk or fork to beat."],[null,"Add clams and cornstarch. Stir."],[null,"On low heat, warm oil in pan. Add mixture."],[null,"Cook on low heat until eggs are no longer runny."],[null,"Remove from heat and top each portion with 1/2 tablespoon sweet & sour sauce."]],"h":[[null,"This is a very typical Taiwanese dish. Amy received the recipe from her mom."]]},"6185607":{"s":[[null,"Combine the all-purpose flour with the Italian seasoning. Heat the olive oil in a large Dutch oven over medium heat. Dredge the beef cubes lightly in the flour mixture and add the beef, in batches to keep the beef in one layer, until well browned on each side."],[null,"Remove the beef from the pan and deglaze the pan with 1/4 cup chicken broth. Add in the mushrooms and sauté for about 4 minutes until well browned. Remove the mushrooms from the pan and deglaze with another 1/4 cup of the broth. Add the onions and garlic and sauté for 4 minutes. Return the beef to the pot, add the remaining chicken broth, and bring to a boil. Partially cover, lower the heat to simmer, and cook for 45 minutes, stirring occasionally."],[null,"Peel and cut the potatoes into 3/4-inch pieces. Cut the carrots into 1/2-inch pieces. Add the potatoes and carrots to the stew and continue to cook for another 45 minutes or until vegetables are tender. Add in the reserved mushrooms, peas, and thyme. Season with red wine vinegar and black pepper."]],"h":[]},"6025540":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, combine the finely shredded cabbage and grated carrots."],[null,"In a separate bowl, whisk together the mayonnaise, Greek yogurt, Dijon mustard, apple cider vinegar, honey, salt, black pepper, and celery seeds."],[null,"Pour the dressing over the cabbage and carrots. Toss until well coated."],[null,"Cover the bowl with plastic wrap and refrigerate for at least 30 minutes to allow the flavors to meld."],[null,"Before serving, taste and adjust the seasoning if necessary."]],"h":[]},"6497459":{"s":[[null,"Heat the olive oil and garlic in a large skillet with a lid over low heat (do not use a deep pot, you want the water to quickly evaporate and the sauce to become thick). Cook the garlic for about 6-7 minutes, but do not brown, stirring occasionally."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the drained tomatoes to a deep bowl. Crush the tomatoes with your hands until coarse. Add the tomatoes and basil to the skillet and simmer for 20-25 minutes until thick. Add some of the reserved liquid from the can of tomatoes, if necessary, if the sauce is too thick."],[null,"Meanwhile bring a 3-5-quart pot of lightly salted water (fill the pot 2/3 full) to a rolling boil. Add the pasta and stir for the first minute. Continue to cook the pasta approximately 7-8 minutes until al dente. Drain, do not rinse."],[null,"Add in the salt, pepper, and crushed red pepper, if using, to the tomato sauce. Add the pasta to the sauce, cover, and let the pasta sit in the sauce for 1-2 minutes. Add the pasta to a warmed bowl and sprinkle with cheese. (The sauce can also be frozen. Freeze in a quart container and store for 3-4 months.)"]],"h":[]},"6437901":{"s":[[null,"Place tomatoes in large salad bowl and sprinkle with salt. Let stand 5 minutes."],[null,"Break up bread and add to tomatoes. Add remaining salad ingredients and mix well."]],"h":[]},"6255845":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375°F. Line a baking sheet with parchment paper. Set aside."],[null,"Heat the oil in a medium skillet over medium heat. Sauté the onion for 3 minutes. Add in the green pepper and mushrooms and sauté for 3 minutes. Add in the garlic, Italian seasoning, salt, and pepper and sauté for 1 minute."],[null,"Add the onion mixture to a bowl, and let cool for 2 minutes. Add in the beef, egg, breadcrumbs, milk, Worcestershire sauce, and liquid smoke, if using. Mix gently, do not over handle the meat."],[null,"Place the mixture onto the prepared baking sheet and form into an oblong loaf. Combine the ketchup, mustard, and brown sugar and pour over the meatloaf."],[null,"Bake the meatloaf for 40-45 minutes until cooked through. Remove from the oven and let the meatloaf rest 5-7 minutes prior to slicing."]],"h":[]},"3647":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 300˚ F. Separate the eggs, setting aside the yolks for later."],[null,"With a stand or hand mixer whip the egg whites and cream of tartar until stiff peaks are formed. Set aside."],[null,"Mix the egg yolks in a bowl with the remaining ingredients and stir well to combine."],[null,"Using a small amount of egg whites gently fold into the yolk mixture a little at a time until it is well mixed. Continue to add remaining egg whites."],[null,"Pour the mixture into a greased loaf pan."],[null,"Bake in the center of the oven for 50 to 60 minutes, until a toothpick inserted in the center comes out clean."],[null,"Allow the cloud bread to cool. Remove from the pan and slice. Store in the refrigerator."]],"h":[[null,"Look for a brand of protein powder that has the lowest amount of phosphorus and potassium. Your renal dietitian may give you tips on brands available in your area."],[null,"This recipe used vanilla protein powder. Use other flavors or unflavored protein powder as desired."],[null,"For a savory flavor add garlic powder, onion powder or both."]]},"6867665":{"s":[[null,"Combine the other half of the onion and 1/2 cup cilantro in small bowl. Garnish each soup serving with 1 Tbsp mixture."],[null,"Add potatoes, carrots, plantain, fish, and lime juice and simmer for 15 minutes. Add peas and cabbage and simmer 5 minutes."],[null,"Add cassava and milk, cover, and simmer for 20 minutes."],[null,"Heat oil in large stockpot and sauté 1/2 of the onion, garlic, pepper, and 1 Tbsp cilantro for 3–4 minutes. Add clam juice and water and bring to a boil."]],"h":[]},"2808":{"s":[[null,"Brew coffee and transfer to a large pitcher."],[null,"Combine coconut milk, vanilla and stevia into a small sauce pan over medium heat. Bring to a soft boil while stirring with a whisk for about 5 minutes"],[null,"Combine milk mixture with brewed coffee."],[null,"Pour 8 ounces into 7 mugs. Sprinkle with cinnamon and enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Serve as a cold coffee drink by chilling the brewed coffee and milk mixture for one hour prior to serving."],[null,"Substitute sugar or desired sweetener for stevia."],[null,"Some milk alternatives are high in calcium. Elyse uses So Delicious Unsweetened Coconut milk which has only 130 mg calcium, 40 mg potassium and 46 mg phosphorus per cup."]]},"3499":{"s":[[null,"Place all ingredients in a blender and pulse until combined."],[null,"Pour into a glass, sprinkle with cinnamon and enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Replace sugar with desired substitute for a lower carbohydrate drink."],[null,"Some milk alternatives are high in calcium. Elyse uses So Delicious® Unsweetened Coconut milk which has only 130 mg calcium, 40 mg potassium and 46 mg phosphorus per cup."]]},"6604490":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oven to 400 degrees F and cover a sheet pan with parchment paper."],[null,"In a medium bowl, whisk the eggs to break them up."],[null,"In another medium bowl, whisk together the panko, shredded coconut, chopped almonds, and garlic powder."],[null,"Dip each chicken strip first in egg and then in coconut mixture, making sure to coat it well with the crumbs."],[null,"Place on the baking sheet and bake until the tenders have an internal temperature of 165 degrees F, about 15 minutes."],[null,"For the dipping sauce, whisk together apricot jam, garlic chili sauce and coarse salt. Thin with 1-2 tablespoons of water and strain, if desired."],[null,"Serve with the dipping sauce."]],"h":[]},"3065":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F. Grease a 9 x 5-inch loaf pan. Set butter out to soften."],[null,"Warm coconut oil in microwave until just melted. Set aside to cool."],[null,"Cream butter and sugar together. Add coconut oil and eggs; stir together. Mix in sour cream. Add shredded coconut to mixture and stir."],[null,"In a separate bowl mix together flour, baking soda and baking powder."],[null,"Fold dry ingredients into wet ingredients. Pour batter into the loaf pan."],[null,"Bake 45 to 60 minutes, until bread is golden brown and a toothpick comes out clean."],[null,"Cool bread in pan for 5 to 10 minutes then remove from pan and cool on a wire rack."]],"h":[[null,"If desired add 1/2 cup of diced or crushed pineapple."],[null,"Wrap some of the bread slices in freezer wrap and freeze for a quick snack later."]]},"6425903":{"s":[[null,"In a medium plastic container place almonds, peanuts, chocolate chips, sunflower seeds and coconut. Spray mixture evenly with cooking spray and then sprinkle on curry powder. Place lid on plastic container and gently shake contents to mix well."]],"h":[]},"5377448":{"s":[[null,"Heat ½ of the vegetable oil in a pan and add the cumin seeds, coriander seeds and chilli flakes, cook until fragrant."],[null,"Add in the ginger, garlic, turmeric, onions and red peppers and cook until soft."],[null,"Remove from the heat and add to a blender, blend to a smooth paste."],[null,"Heat the remaining vegetable oil and fry the basa until golden brown and fully cooked."],[null,"Remove basa from the pan and add in all the curry paste and 1 low salt stock cube. Cook until fragrant and then add in the water and coconut milk."],[null,"Add the fish back into the pan with the chickpeas and Renastep and heat through."],[null,"Sprinkle with coriander and serve with rice!"]],"h":[["Renastep note","Renastep is a food for special medical purposes for the dietary management of kidney disease. Suitable from 3 years of age. Must be used under medical supervision. Renastep contains Milk (milk protein) and Fish (Tuna oil). This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutritics dietary analysis software. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information."]]},"9825585":{"s":[[null,"Add all the ingredients to a blender or food processor and process until smooth. Then gently pour the mixture into popsicle molds or plastic cups. Freeze for 6 hours or overnight."],[null,"When ready to enjoy, run the outside of the popsicle mold under lukewarm water for a few seconds and gently remove from its mold."]],"h":[[null,"Taste the mixture before you freeze. Grab a spoon and sample your lime popsicle mixture (or any popsicle you’re making) to test the level of sweet, tart, or other flavour you may want to add. You can always add a little more lime juice before you freeze them, if desired. When separating the casing from the popsicle, use care not to break them! Run the outside of your popsicle mold under lukewarm water in your kitchen sink for a few seconds, and then try to gently separate . Use a side to side motion, don’t pull. Repeat until you can easily separate the lime popsicles from their mold, without breaking. If you have some extra lime popsicle mixture at the end, freeze the remainder in an ice cube tray for mini treats. Fill your molds almost to the top. The popsicles will only expand slightly, so don’t leave too much space for expansion, or your stick or lid won’t hold the popsicle very well. Make sure to freeze your popsicles long enough! The worst thing you can do is remove the popsicle from its mold, before it is fully solid. I like to give them a minimum of 6 hours to ensure they are solid, throughout. Don’t have popsicle molds? No problem! Use paper cups and freeze them open side up for about 30-45 minutes. Then stick a popsicle stick into the center and continue freezing until completely solid."]]},"9615018":{"s":[[null,"To a medium saucepan, add the quinoa, water, salt and coconut milk, and bring to a boil over medium high heat. Reduce heat and simmer for about 15 minutes, until the liquid is absorbed. Stir often towards the end of cooking to prevent sticking."],[null,"Remove from the heat and stir in the lime juice and cilantro. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"For low fat , I’m using lite coconut milk , but for a richer version, feel free to use full fat coconut milk, if preferred. Cilantro haters :), feel free to swap for fresh parsley, dill or mint, if preferred. For a quinoa free version , check out my coconut rice , instead. Leftovers keep refrigerated in a sealed container for up to 3 days."]]},"9702522":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your waffle iron to medium-high heat."],[null,"In a large mixing bowl, whisk together the flour and baking powder. Then add the coconut milk, banana, and vanilla and mix until just combined, and no floury bits remain but don't overmix. A few lumps are perfectly fine.NOTE: If the batter appears too thick (it should be pourable similar to pancake batter), add the optional water and give everything another quick stir."],[null,"Cook the waffles according to the manufacturer's instructions, approx 5-6 minutes for each batch. Cook longer for crispier waffles, and less for softer waffles."],[null,"Serve with blueberry chia jam, maple syrup, or fresh fruit."]],"h":[[null,"Use canned coconut milk , (full fat OR light) but do not sub for another plant milk. The fat content is needed for crispier waffles, especially since this recipe does not call for oil or butter. Weigh your flour for the best results . If you’re scooping flour from a bag, you’ll likely end up with too much, and you’ll need more liquid to get the batter just right. If you don’t have a kitchen scale , spoon the flour into your measuring cup and use a knife to scrape off the excess. Use a very ripe banana that is spotted brown for natural sweetness and the best flavour. Make sure your waffle iron is HOT before adding the waffle batter to it, to prevent sticking. Do not lift the lid too soon or your waffles may break . Wait at least the minimum number of minutes as set out by the manufacturer instructions before checking the level of doneness. Subsequent batches of waffles cook a little bit faster than the first batch so watch closely."]]},"7724336":{"s":[[null,"Place all the ingredients, except the toasted coconut, into a small pan. Place over a low heat and simmer very gently for 20–25 minutes until the rice is tender."],[null,"Serve topped with the toasted coconut."]],"h":[[null,"Cook gently with a lid on, you can always add a little more soya milk or water if the rice starts to stick to the pan."],[null,"If you can't find toasted coconut, simply add 1 tbsp of desiccated coconut to a dry frying pan and stir over a medium heat for 2-3 minutes until it starts to brown."]]},"7578518":{"s":[[null,"Place the cod and half the salmon into a blender with the egg and lemon juice, then blend to a paste."],[null,"Dice the remaining salmon into small cubes, then mix it into the blended fish, along with the spring onions, dill and pepper. Combine well – use your hands for best results."],[null,"Divide the mixture into 4 and form each into patties or burgers. Leave in the fridge for 10 minutes while you prepare the salad to serve."],[null,"Place the fish burgers on a non-stick baking sheet and grill for 4-5 minutes on each side until thoroughly cooked through."],[null,"Serve in a wholemeal bap, filled with lettuce, tomatoes, cucumber and red onion, Garnish with dill and a wedge of lemon."]],"h":[[null,"Try using other white fish such as coley."],[null,"You could also use different herbs, such as parsley."],[null,"These burgers are also delicious when served with vegetables and parsley sauce."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing provided the fish has not been frozen previously. You can freeze them either before or after cooking. Freeze the fish burgers in individual portions, then defrost in the fridge and prepare as above until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"7684321":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 190°C/gas 5. Lightly oil a baking sheet and put the beaten egg into a shallow bowl. Put the flour onto a dinner plate and the breadcrumbs on another dinner plate."],[null,"Put the cod onto the plate of flour and mix so each piece gets coated, separating the goujons so they’re not touching each other."],[null,"Wash and dry your hands, pick up a goujon and shake off any excess flour. Dip into the egg, place on the breadcrumbs and sprinkle more crumbs on top to fully coat the goujon. Place on the baking sheet. Repeat until all the cod goujons are coated."],[null,"Bake for 12-15 minutes until the outside is crispy and lightly browned."]],"h":[[null,"You can also use rapeseed oil."],[null,"Serve with healthier oven-baked sweet potato chips and peas."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Cook, then cool immediately and freeze on a baking sheet. Once frozen carefully bag in portions for use. Defrost in the fridge then reheat thorughly until piping hot."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"6893927":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, combine the paprika, 1/4 Tsp. of salt, and black pepper. Sprinkle both sides of the fillets with the paprika mixture. Heat 1 Tsp. of the oil in a large nonstick skillet over medium heat. Cook the fillets 4 minutes, turn, and cook 3 minutes or until opaque in center."],[null,"Place tomatoes in a medium saucepan and heat over medium heat to just boiling. Add the beans, red peppers, garlic, 2 tsp olive oil and rosemary and cook 1-2 minutes to heat through. Remove from heat, cover, and let stand while fish is cooking."],[null,"Divide the tomato, bean and pepper mixture equally between 4 shallow bowls and top each with a fish fillet."]],"h":[]},"6932928":{"s":[[null,"Preheat grill or grill pan coated with cooking spray to medium-high heat."],[null,"Combine all salsa ingredients, except the avocado, in a medium bowl. Gently stir in the avocado and set aside."],[null,"Brush both sides of the fish fillets with oil and sprinkle evenly with the cumin, 1/4 teaspoon of the salt, and black pepper. Cook 4 minutes on each side or until opaque in center. Serve with salsa alongside."]],"h":[]},"7963728":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200°C/gas 6. Melt the spread in a small pan, whisk in the flour and cook for 1 minute."],[null,"Gradually add the milk, whisking continuously, and simmer for a minute until you have a thick sauce."],[null,"Stir through the cheese, mustard and herbs, and season with the black pepper."],[null,"Place the cod pieces onto a baking sheet and spoon over the sauce."],[null,"Place in the oven and cook for about 15 minutes until the fish is cooked."],[null,"Serve your choice of vegetables."]],"h":[[null,"Try using different herb combinations, such as parsley and dill or coriander and chives."],[null,"This topping is suitable for mackerel fillets, haddock, river cobbler or tilapia."],[null,"You could allow the sauce to cool then spread over the fish and refrigerate until needed."],[null,"Remove from the fridge for 10 minutes before cooking as normal."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"7835214":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200ºC/gas 6."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix together the oil, honey and lemon zest and juice."],[null,"Brush all the vegetables with a little of the honey mixture, then place on to a heavy baking tray, sprinkling the rosemary on top."],[null,"Cook for about 45 minutes until beginning to char."],[null,"Place the pieces of cod on to the tray and continue to cook for 10–12 minutes. Finally, serve with green side salad, if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Salmon, haddock or fresh tuna work well with this recipe."],[null,"Vary by adding thyme instead of rosemary. You could also add large quarters of unpeeled onion along with the rest of the vegetables."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"7157427":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a non-stick frying pan."],[null,"Add the onion and fry for 5 minutes until softened."],[null,"Add all the remaining ingredients (except the cod), season with black pepper, bring to the boil, leave uncovered and simmer gently for 15 minutes."],[null,"Lay the cod on top of the sauce, cover, and continue to simmer for a further 15 minutes until the fish is cooked. Remove the bay leaves."]],"h":[[null,"This recipe also works well with salmon, fresh tuna or haddock."],[null,"To spice the dish up, add 2 cloves crushed garlic and 1 tsp smoked paprika to the tomato sauce."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"6525410":{"s":[[null,"To make the soup, place half of the cucumbers in a food processor fit with the chopping blade. Process until it is cut into small pieces. Add the remaining cucumber sections and process until they are cut into small pieces."],[null,"Add the yogurt, lemon juice, lemon zest, and dill and process until liquified and all cucumber pieces are puréed."],[null,"Spray a grill pan or outdoor grill with cooking spray and heat to medium. Toss the shrimp with olive oil and black pepper. Place on the preheated grill and cook for 1 minute. Flip the shrimp and cook for an additional minute. Shrimp cooks quickly, so be careful not to overcook it. Remove it from the grill to a plate."],[null,"In a small bowl, mash the avocado and add the mayonnaise, lemon juice, and hot sauce, and mix until light green in color and the avocado is incorporated and smooth."],[null,"Spread 1 Tbsp of the avocado aioli over each slice of toast. Top with ¼ cup of arugula and 3 shrimp. Serve with 1 ¼ cup of the soup on the side."]],"h":[]},"2533":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350º F. Spray a 13” x 9” x 2” baking pan with nonstick cooking spray."],[null,"Roll out crescent rolls onto the baking pan, forming into a single flat dough surface, pressing seams together. Bake 10 to 15 minutes. Let stand until cool, 10 to 15 minutes."],[null,"In a bowl, beat cream cheese and sour cream until smooth. Stir in the ranch dressing and garlic powder. Spread the mixture evenly over the crust."],[null,"Chop broccoli, carrot, cucumber and onion. Slice cherry tomatoes in half."],[null,"Arrange chopped vegetables on top of cream cheese mixture."],[null,"Cover pizza with plastic wrap and refrigerate until serving time. Slice 4 even vertical cuts and 5 horizontal cuts for 20 pieces."]],"h":[[null,"Make ahead and eat as a quick snack or serve as an appetizer at your next social event."],[null,"For a lower sodium snack substitute the DaVita recipe Easy Pizza Dough for crescent dough."]]},"7480641":{"s":[[null,"Add the coffee and water to an 8 cup cafetiere mix well, cover (but do not plunge) and refrigerate for at least 12 hours or overnight."],[null,"Mix well then allow to settle for a few minutes. Plunge the cafetiere then leave to stand for a few more minutes before pouring the coffee into a large jug."],[null,"Dissolve sweetener tablets, as preferred, into the coffee then mix in the milk if using and add some ice cubes."],[null,"Pour into glasses packed with ice cubes and serve sprinkled with a little cocoa powder."]],"h":[[null,"Coarser ground coffee is better for cold-brewing."],[null,"If you don’t have a cafetiere you can just strain the coffee through muslin or a paper coffee filter."],[null,"You could just make coffee as normal and chill it down if short of time."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"1981":{"s":[[null,"Shred the cabbage and carrots. Chop the bell pepper and onion."],[null,"Combine all vegetables together."],[null,"In small bowl blend mayonnaise, vinegar, sugar and seasonings. Pour over vegetables and mix."]],"h":[[null,"Coleslaw keeps up to 1 week in the refrigerator."]]},"6699442":{"s":[[null,"Remove the woody stems that run down the center of the collard leaves. Neatly pile several leaves and tightly roll them up, then slice into ribbons. Repeat for the remaining collard greens."],[null,"Heat 1 tablespoon of the olive oil in a medium sauté pan over medium heat. When the oil is shimmering, add the turkey bacon and cook until golden brown, 3 minutes on each side. Remove the bacon and set aside to slightly cool. Dice the bacon once cool."],[null,"Heat the remaining 1 tablespoon of olive oil in the same sauté pan over medium heat. When the oil is shimmering, add the garlic and cook until fragrant, 30 seconds."],[null,"Add the collard greens and squash and cook until the collards have wilted and the squash begins to soften, about 5 minutes."],[null,"Add the vegetable broth and bring the mixture to a boil. Lower the heat and simmer, covered, until the vegetables are cooked through, 10 minutes."],[null,"Add 1/8 teaspoon salt (*optional) the black pepper, and cooked turkey bacon and toss to combine. *Optional salt not included in nutrition analysis; 1/8 teaspoon salt adds 75 mg of sodium per serving."]],"h":[]},"1836":{"s":[[null,"Chop bell peppers, red onion, and cucumbers. Shred carrots."],[null,"Cook pasta according to package instructions, without salt. Drain and rinse in cold water to cool. Place in a large bowl."],[null,"Mix prepared vegetables with pasta and mix to combine."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine remaining ingredients with a whisk, then stir into pasta and vegetables."],[null,"Chill for at least 1 hour before serving."]],"h":[[null,"To lower fat, use reduced-fat mayonnaise. Be aware that sodium content of many reduced-fat products is higher than the regular product."]]},"6738204":{"s":[[null,"Chop bell peppers, red onion, and cucumbers. Shred carrots."],[null,"Cook pasta according to package instructions, without salt. Drain and rinse in cold water to cool. Place in a large bowl."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine remaining ingredients with a whisk, then stir into pasta and vegetables."],[null,"Mix prepared vegetables with pasta and mix to combine."],[null,"Chill for at least 1 hour before serving."]],"h":[]},"4446690":{"s":[[null,"Dry beef cubes with a paper towel."],[null,"Heat oil in a heavy soup pot on high and brown the beef cubes on all sides, about 5 minutes."],[null,"Add garlic and onion, and continue to cook for another 5 minutes."],[null,"Add the herbs, spices, vegetables, broth and water, and bring to a boil."],[null,"Add the bulgur and the barley, reducing the temperature to minimum, and cover with a well-fitting lid. Cook for approximately 1 hour and 15 minutes or until beef is tender."],[null,"If using a slow cooker, transfer the beef to slow cooker after step 4. Add the bulgur and barley and put the setting on low, cover and cook for 4 hours."],[null,"Add ¼ cup freshly chopped parsley at the end of cooking time. Enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"* Look for low or reduced-sodium broth containing 200mg sodium or less per 1 cup serving. Avoid low-sodium broth that contains potassium chloride—it’s very high in potassium."],[null,"Freeze leftover soup in portions for a quick meal when you are in a time crunch!"],["Tips for dining out kidney-friendly","Eating out should be a break from your normal routine. Planning ahead can allow you to enjoy a stress-free dining experience while staying within your recommended kidney diet goals. Appetizers: Decide if you really need the extra food. If you select an appetizer, will you still be able to order the main dish you have been craving? Avoid appetizers with heavy sauces and limit the amount you eat. Main Course: When choosing your main course, think of the balanced meal approach. Ideally your meal should consist of a palm-sized portion of protein with lower-potassium side dishes of a starch and vegetables. Ask for sauces to be served on the side to avoid additional calories and salt. If you are unsure of the seasonings used, ask your server for more details. Sweet Selections: If you aren’t full already, nearly all restaurants have a dessert menu to tempt your taste buds. Reduce potassium in desserts by sharing with your dinner company. If you prefer to have the dessert alone, choose sorbet or angel food cake with a portion of lower-potassium fresh fruit. Something to Sip On: Any type of salt or concentrated sweet can signal to your brain that you are thirsty. Be mindful of the beverages on the menu and select water, tea, root beer, ginger ale or homemade lemonade as low-potassium beverages."]]},"7587856":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200ºC/gas 6."],[null,"Place the tomatoes into an ovenproof dish, season well then cook in the oven for 20-25 minutes until tender and beginning to char."],[null,"Meanwhile, cook the pasta according to the pack instructions. Drain and return to the pan."],[null,"Meanwhile, heat the oil in a non-stick frying pan, add the garlic and fry for 1 minute, add the prawns and fry for a further 1-2 minutes until pink."],[null,"Toss together all the ingredients, add the basil and season well with black pepper."]],"h":[[null,"You could use frozen mixed seafood or small Atlantic prawns instead of tiger prawns, if you prefer."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"2349":{"s":[[null,"Sauté vegetables with garlic in butter/oil mixture until crisp-tender."],[null,"Whip eggs, egg whites and milk until light and fluffy. Mix in cumin and pepper."],[null,"Pour egg mixture over sautéed vegetables."],[null,"Reduce heat and cover for 1 to 2 minutes. Uncover and lift edges of omelet, allowing uncooked egg to run to the bottom of the pan."],[null,"After egg is completely cooked, fold omelet over in pan."],[null,"Divide omelet into 2 portions and serve immediately."],[null,"Garnish with green onion and a mushroom slice."]],"h":[[null,"Serve omelet with a bagel, cream cheese, fresh mixed berries and hot tea."],[null,"For a lower fat omelet, sauté vegetables in a nonstick skillet using cooking spray instead of oil and butter."]]},"6957182":{"s":[[null,"Into a stovetop pressure cooker, add rinsed beans and 3 cups water, and cover. Place pressure cooker on stove and set on high heat. Once the beans start boiling, lower heat to medium and cook beans until they are tender, about 45 minutes. Make sure beans submerged in water while they cook; add more water if needed."],[null,"Once beans are tender, add rice, 1 cup water, salt and 1/2 Tsp. avocado oil. Stir well and add the remaining ingredients. Stir once more with spoon, and make sure to put a little hip into it."],[null,"Make sure there is about 3/4 inch of water above the beans. Cover the mixture, and put heat on medium-low. Cook for 15 minutes, or until rice is tender. Once the congrí is done, fluff with a fork and serve. Enjoy!"]],"h":[]},"6058903":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6190469":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6061452":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6402133":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6163306":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6809517":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6014863":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6569922":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6631489":{"s":[],"h":[]},"3460":{"s":[[null,"In large bowl, combine instant vanilla pudding and soy milk. Mix well."],[null,"Fold whipped topping gently into pudding."],[null,"Fold fruit into pudding mixture."],[null,"Place vanilla wafers in large zip-lock bag and crush with a rolling pin or mallet."],[null,"Fold 3/4 of the crushed wafers into pudding mixture."],[null,"Top pudding with remaining wafer crumbs."],[null,"Refrigerate overnight or for 2 to 3 hours before serving."]],"h":[[null,"This dessert looks pretty in a glass bowl."],[null,"Some pudding mixes contain phosphate additives and may not be recommended, especially if phosphorus control is an issue. Check labels and ingredients. Speak to your dietitian if you have questions."]]},"1724":{"s":[[null,"Peel and seed cucumbers. Chop onions and mint. Mince dill."],[null,"Place all ingredients into a blender and blend until smooth."],[null,"Cover and refrigerate until chilled."],[null,"Garnish soup with fresh dill sprigs if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Leftovers taste even better the next day."],[null,"For a complete lunch meal serve Cool Cucumber Soup with a chicken salad, tuna salad or egg salad sandwich."]]},"6746805":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350°F."],[null,"To make the filling, toss together all the fruit, the arrowroot powder, 1 tsp cinnamon, ginger, and orange zest in a medium bowl. Spread the filling in the bottom of an 8 x 12-inch baking dish."],[null,"To make the topping, stir together the almond flour, oats, flour, pumpkin seeds, almonds, 1 tsp cinnamon, and salt in another medium bowl. Drizzle in the canola oil, olive oil, and maple syrup and mix until evenly combined."],[null,"Crumble the topping over the filling and bake for 40 minutes, or until the topping is brown and the fruit is bubbling. Remove cobbler from the oven and set aside to cool for 10 minutes before serving."]],"h":[]},"2480":{"s":[[null,"Dice or shred chicken. Chop egg, onion and celery."],[null,"Place all ingredients in a large bowl and stir together."],[null,"Cover and chill overnight or at least 2 hours before serving."]],"h":[[null,"If desired, serve on bread, roll, croissant or pita bread with green leaf lettuce."]]},"2964":{"s":[[null,"Thaw corn. Finely chop green chili and cilantro."],[null,"In a mixing bowl, mix the cheese and thawed corn."],[null,"Soak bread slices in water and squeeze out water so the bread becomes dry. Add this to corn and cheese mixture. Add flour, dry spices and cilantro. Mix it gently."],[null,"Heat the oil in a large saucepan. Using a tablespoon, form small balls from the corn and cheese mixture and drop each ball into the hot oil. Cook until golden brown."],[null,"Remove balls from the oil and place on a tray with kitchen napkin to drain excess oil."],[null,"Serve hot with Cilantro Chutney."]],"h":[[null,"If available, substitute crumbled paneer cheese for cottage cheese."],[null,"Paneer is an unaged cheese made by curdling milk with lemon juice or other acid food. Substitutions include dry curd cottage cheese, farmer’s cheese, queso blanco or queso fresco. Portion is limited since this dairy product contains phosphorus."]]},"6393242":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a large nonstick skillet over medium-high heat. Add the onion and cook, stirring occasionally, until the onion is softened, about 6 minutes. Add the corn, roasted red peppers, and scallions; cook 2 minutes. Add the half-andhalf, stirring, until the liquid is almost evaporated, about 2 minutes. Remove from the heat; stir in the cheese. Let cool slightly."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 375°F. Spray a large baking sheet with nonstick spray."],[null,"Place one sheet of phyllo lengthwise on a work surface (cover the remaining phyllo with plastic wrap to keep from drying out). Lightly spray the phyllo sheet with nonstick spray; top with a second phyllo sheet and lightly spray with nonstick spray. With a sharp knife, cut the layered sheets in half lengthwise. Repeat this layering and cutting process with the remaining phyllo sheets to make a total of 8 strips of dough."],[null,"Place a heaping Tbsp of filling to the left on the bottom end of one strip of phyllo. Fold one corner of the phyllo strip up and over the filling, then continue folding and overlapping, flag-fashion, to form a triangle. Place on the baking sheet and repeat with the remaining phyllo sheets and filling to make a total of 8 empanadas."],[null,"Lightly spray the empanadas with nonstick spray. Bake until the empanadas are golden brown, 15–20 minutes. Let cool 10 minutes before serving."]],"h":[]},"7200396":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200ºC/gas 6. Lightly grease some mini muffin tins. The mixture will make 48 mini muffins so you may need to re-use the tins (or you can make about 18 large muffins, if you prefer)."],[null,"In a bowl, sieve together the flour, polenta, baking powder and paprika."],[null,"Mix together the milk, spread and eggs in another bowl before folding into the flour mixture. Add the rosemary and mix together."],[null,"Spoon into the muffin tins and sprinkle with a little Parmesan cheese."],[null,"Bake for 8–10 minutes until golden. Cool and serve."]],"h":[[null,"For a veggie version, try adding chopped sundried tomatoes."],[null,"Also good with other herbs such as oregano or thyme."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost for 2 hours. To serve, defrost/warm in the microwave or a moderate oven."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"6750704":{"s":[[null,"In a large skillet, heat 2 tsp of the oil over medium heat. Add the corn and sauté for 3 minutes. Add the cumin and chili powder and sauté for 2 minutes. Remove the corn mixture from the skillet."],[null,"Add the remaining olive oil to the skillet and add the onion. Sauté the onion for 5 minutes, until soft. Add the zucchini and sauté for 3 minutes. Add the tomatoes and sauté for 2 minutes. Add the oregano and sauté for 1 minute; stir in the reserved corn mixture."],[null,"Divide the corn mixture among the warmed tortillas and top each taco with 2 tsp yogurt and 2 tsp Salsa Cruda."],[null,"Cook’s Tip: Use your microwave to prep fresh corn! From each ear, cut off about 1 inch of the stalk end. Add up to 3 ears of corn at a time to a microwave-safe container and microwave on high for 6 minutes. Remove the corn from the microwave and let cool enough to handle. Holding onto the husk, gently squeeze and shake and the corn will come out in one fell swoop. If any silks remain, rub the cob up and down with paper toweling to remove the strands."]],"h":[]},"6975487":{"s":[[null,"Soak the corn (husks on) in large bowl or pot of water for 30 minutes."],[null,"Remove the husks and silk from the corn. (Or you can roast corn with husks still on and remove the husks after roasting. This allows the corn to caramelize rather than char while roasting.)"],[null,"Roast corn on a grill or over an open gas flame (gas stove) on medium-high heat. Rotate each ear every 30 seconds or so, so the corn gets roasted evenly. (You will hear some kernels pop while cooking.) Remove roasted ears from the grill or flame and set aside."],[null,"Mix cayenne, cumin, and salt in a bowl."],[null,"Carefully remove the husks and silk from corn if you have not done so already. Dip lime halves into the spice mix to pick up the spices and rub all over corn, making sure to squeeze lime juice while doing so. Serve."]],"h":[]},"6870016":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F. Grease a 9x13-inch baking dish with cooking spray."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine the whole kernel corn, cream-style corn, cornmeal, diced tomato, Greek yogurt, melted butter, honey, baking powder, salt, and pepper. Mix until well combined."],[null,"Pour the corn mixture into the prepared baking dish, spreading it evenly."],[null,"Bake for 45 minutes or until the top is golden brown and a toothpick inserted into the center comes out clean."],[null,"Remove the casserole from the oven."],[null,"Garnish with chopped fresh chives, if desired."],[null,"Allow the casserole to cool for a few minutes before serving."]],"h":[]},"7359781":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4. First, make the sweet potato croutons. In a large bowl, drizzle the sweet potato cubes in 1 tsp oil and jumble them up to coat evenly. Sprinkle with the smoked paprika, jumble them up again and spread out on a baking sheet. Bake for 25-35 minutes, turning regularly."],[null,"Meanwhile, make the chowder. Heat the olive oil in a large saucepan and fry the onion for 3-4 minutes. Add the carrot, celery, sweetcorn and white pepper. Stir for 3 minutes and sprinkle with the flour."],[null,"Gradually stir in the vegetable stock until it thickens. Cover then turn down the heat and simmer gently for 5 minutes."],[null,"Slowly stir in the milk for a couple of minutes and bring back to a simmer."],[null,"Place the chowder into bowls and sprinkle with a few chopped chives and some freshly ground black pepper. Top with the sweet potato croutons, fresh chives and black pepper."]],"h":[[null,"If your chowder becomes a bit too thick, just slowly stir in a little more milk."],[null,"You could add cubes of fresh salmon or some large prawns to make a corn seafood chowder."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Freeze the croutons separately. Defrost soup in a microwave or over a very low heat until piping hot."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"3489":{"s":[[null,"In a saucepan, heat the vegetable oil and add mustard seeds. When the seeds splutter, add semolina, chilies and salt. Roast until the semolina grows slightly brown."],[null,"Remove from heat and let cool."],[null,"Mix yogurt with water and blend until smooth."],[null,"Add corn, paneer, cilantro and yogurt to the cooled semolina mixture. Mix well and set aside for 10 minutes."],[null,"Grease on idli mould with ghee (clarified butter) and spoon small portions of batter into mould. Steam and cook idlis for 10 minutes. Remove from the mold."],[null,"Sprinkle with finely chopped cilantro and serve with Cilantro Chutney."]],"h":[[null,"Use batter immediately for best results."],[null,"Ghee is clarified butter."],[null,"Paneer is a South Asian cheese widely used in Indian cuisine. It is made by curdling milk with lemon juice or acid and is similar to cottage cheese or queso blanco. Substitute cottage cheese if paneer is unavailable."],[null,"Farina, sold under the name Cream of Wheat®, is the same as semolina."]]},"9135569":{"s":[[null,"Combine all the salad dressing ingredients in a small bowl and set it aside."],[null,"Then add all the salad ingredients to a larger bowl, toss with the dressing, and serve. If time allows, refrigerate it for 1 hour before serving."]],"h":[]},"6283047":{"s":[],"h":[]},"2592":{"s":[[null,"Mix masa, water and salt in a bowl."],[null,"Turn mixture onto a board and knead until a soft dough forms, adding more water as needed."],[null,"Divide dough into 16 pieces, each about 1/2-inch wide and 1/2-inch thick. Place each piece of dough between two pieces of plastic to prevent sticking, and then flatten into a 5-inch diameter tortilla using a rolling pin or a tortilla press."],[null,"Lightly oil a very hot griddle and place one tortilla on it. Cook for about 30 seconds, then turn the tortilla and cook for another 30 seconds before removing from griddle. (It should be soft and easy to fold.) Repeat for each remaining tortilla."]],"h":[[null,"Use a spatula to pick up the tortilla so you don’t get burned."],[null,"Masa is corn flour made from ground hominy. It is used to make tortillas and tamales."],[null,"Prepare enchiladas, tacos and quesadillas, or eat 1 to 2 tortillas with a meal."]]},"6380287":{"s":[[null,"Place peas in a saucepan, and cover with water. Bring to a boil over high heat, and cook for 5 minutes or until tender. Drain. Rinse with cold water."],[null,"Combine peas, corn, tomatoes, olive oil, dill, basil, salt, and pepper in a large bowl. Toss well to combine. Serve at room temperature."]],"h":[]},"6233807":{"s":[[null,"Make the crepes. In a blender, combine almond flour, coconut flour, eggs, almond milk, olive oil, vanilla extract, and a pinch of salt. Blend until smooth"],[null,"Allow the crepe batter to rest in the refrigerator for at least 30 minutes."],[null,"Heat a non-stick skillet over medium heat and lightly spray with cooking spray."],[null,"Pour a small amount of batter into the skillet, swirling it to coat the bottom thinly and evenly."],[null,"Cook each crepe for about 1–2 minutes on each side or until lightly golden. Repeat with the remaining batter."],[null,"Spoon the cottage cheese onto one half of each crepe."],[null,"Add a layer of mixed berries over the cottage cheese."],[null,"Fold in the sides and roll to close each crepe around the filling."]],"h":[]},"6931397":{"s":[[null,"Spoon 1 cup of low-fat cottage cheese into a bowl or glass."],[null,"Add 1/2 cup diced pineapple on top."],[null,"Lightly stir if you prefer mixed flavors, or leave it layered for a parfait-style presentation."],[null,"Serve immediately."]],"h":[]},"6869591":{"s":[[null,"Lay out the tortillas on a clean surface."],[null,"Evenly spread the cottage cheese on each tortilla."],[null,"Distribute the cherry tomatoes, cucumber slices, red onion, and bell peppers over the cottage cheese."],[null,"Sprinkle the fresh herbs on top."],[null,"Season with the salt and pepper."],[null,"Fold in the sides of the tortillas and then roll them up tightly to create wraps."]],"h":[]},"6984927":{"s":[[null,"In a blender or food processor, combine the low-fat cottage cheese, eggs, whole wheat flour, baking powder, vanilla extract, sugar substitute, and salt. Blend until the mixture is smooth and well combined."],[null,"Heat a non-stick skillet or griddle over medium-low heat and lightly grease it with cooking spray or a small amount of oil."],[null,"Pour pancake batter onto the skillet to create pancakes of your desired size (usually about 1/4 cup of batter for each pancake)."],[null,"Cook the pancakes for about 2–3 minutes on one side or until you see small bubbles forming on the surface and the edges start to set."],[null,"Flip the pancakes and cook for an additional 1–2 minutes on the other side or until they are golden brown and cooked through."],[null,"Remove the pancakes from the skillet and keep them warm while you cook the remaining batter."]],"h":[]},"1882":{"s":[[null,"In a medium-sized bowl, combine cottage cheese, eggs (lightly beaten), flour and melted butter."],[null,"Spray griddle or frying pan with non-stick cooking spray or butter."],[null,"Heat griddle or frying pan over medium to high heat. Ladle about 1/4 cup of batter onto the griddle to form pancakes (about 4″ in diameter)."],[null,"Cook pancakes for 2-3 minutes until the undersides are lightly browned, then turn to brown other side."],[null,"Transfer the pancakes to a heated platter."],[null,"Continue to make pancakes with the remaining batter."],[null,"Top each serving of pancakes with 1/2 cup sliced strawberries."]],"h":[[null,"Blueberries, raspberries, blackberries or canned peaches also make a great substitution for strawberries."],[null,"Pancakes can also be topped with sugar-free or regular jam or pancake syrup or whipped topping."],[null,"You can flick water across the griddle or frying pan surface, and if it beads up and sizzles, it’s ready for the pancake batter."]]},"3653":{"s":[[null,"Beat eggs slightly. Add cottage cheese, sour cream, and salt."],[null,"Mix until blended; will not be smooth."],[null,"Gradually fold in flour."],[null,"Drop by 1/4 cupfuls well apart into hot oiled pan or onto non-stick griddle."],[null,"Cook until dry and brown around edges. Flip and brown other side."]],"h":[[null,"Suggested toppings include jam, jelly or canned fruit. Top with extra sour cream if desired."]]},"6352574":{"s":[[null,"In a bowl, combine the cottage cheese, fresh pineapple chunks, and chopped walnuts."],[null,"Divide the cottage cheese mixture into serving bowls. Serve immediately and enjoy this refreshing and protein-packed dish."]],"h":[]},"2993":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 475° F."],[null,"Stir baking soda into buttermilk."],[null,"Combine flour and salt in a bowl. Cut in shortening until mixture resembles coarse meal."],[null,"Sprinkle buttermilk over flour mixture and stir until dry ingredients are moistened and dough is formed."],[null,"Knead dough on a floured surface 6 times. Roll dough out to 1/2” thickness. Using a 2” biscuit cutter, cut out 12 biscuits."],[null,"Bake on a greased baking sheet for 10 to 12 minutes, until browned."]],"h":[[null,"Biscuits leavened with baking soda and buttermilk are lower in phosphorus compared to baking powder biscuits."],[null,"One biscuit served with 1/3-cup Country Gravy provides 198 mg sodium and 98 mg phosphorus. Be aware that portion size can make a difference in how much sodium and phosphorus are consumed."]]},"6605420":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350°F."],[null,"Scoop out and coarsely chop the squash pulp."],[null,"Place a medium nonstick skillet over medium-high heat until hot. Coat the skillet with nonstick cooking spray and add the squash pulp and bell pepper. Cook 4 minutes or until the pepper is tender-crisp, stirring frequently."],[null,"Remove the skillet from the heat and stir in the water and margarine. Add the stuffing mix and stir gently with a fork. Spoon 1/2 cup stuffing into each squash half. Press down gently so the stuffing will adhere."],[null,"Recoat the skillet with nonstick cooking spray, arrange the stuffed squash in the skillet, cover tightly, and bake 30 minutes or until the squash is tender when pierced with a fork."]],"h":[]},"7616374":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 180°C/gas 4 and brush (or spray) a mini muffin tin with oil."],[null,"Add 1 tsp oil to a pan with the onion and red pepper and cook for 6-7 minutes until softened."],[null,"Remove from the heat and add the courgette and oregano, mix, and set aside."],[null,"In a bowl, mix the egg, milk and yogurt together. Then, stir in the polenta, flour and baking powder, mix again then stir in the vegetables and grated cheese."],[null,"Spoon into mini muffin tins or mini paper cases. Bake for 15-20 minutes until lightly browned."],[null,"Meanwhile, mix together the tomatoes, chilli, mint and vinegar to make the salsa."]],"h":[[null,"You could use different vegetables, try with cooked corn or peas or replace the courgette with cooked spinach."],[null,"If you don’t have mini muffin tins, you could use mini paper cases."]]},"7556622":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4. Cut the courgettes in half lengthwise and using a small spoon or melon baller, scoop out the flesh, leaving each courgette with a 7cm 'border' inside. Chop the scooped-out flesh into small pieces and set aside."],[null,"Heat the oil in a large pan and add the spring onions, garlic and pepper. Cook on medium to low heat for 2–3 minutes, until the onions are translucent then add the chopped courgette flesh, season and cook for about 4 minutes."],[null,"Add the cumin, oregano, chilli powder, 3 tbsp water, and tomato paste. Cook for a few more minutes. Add the shredded chicken, mix, and cook for 3 more minutes."],[null,"Place a quarter of the jar of enchilada sauce on the bottom of a large baking dish (or 2 small ones), and place in the courgette halves cut side up. Using a spoon, fill each hollowed courgette with chicken mixture, pressing down firmly."],[null,"Top the courgettes with the remaining enchilada sauce and scatter evenly with the cheese. Cover with foil and bake for 35 minutes until the cheese has melted and the courgettes are cooked through."]],"h":[[null,"To make a veggie version replace the chicken with chopped sauted mushrooms."],[null,"If you don't have a jar of sauce, simply use a can of tomatoes and blend together with a heaped tsp each of cumin, oregano and chilli powder (mild or hot)."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"7897038":{"s":[[null,"Place the beaten egg, pepper, Parmesan cheese, flour and baking powder in a bowl, and mix well."],[null,"Mix in the courgette and spring onion (reserving 1 tbsp to serve)."],[null,"Add the oil to a large non-stick pan, place 1 tbsp of the mixture in the pan and flatten slightly to create a fritter about ¾–1cm thick, repeating in batches until all the mixture is used. (Depending on the size of your pan, you should be able to cook 3–4 fritters at a time.) As the fritters are ready, place on a plate and set aside."],[null,"Cook the fritters for 2–3 minutes, until lightly browned, then flip over and cook the other side (again for 2–3 minutes)."],[null,"Meanwhile, add all the salsa ingredients to a bowl. Mix together well and set aside."],[null,"When all the fritters are ready, sprinkle with the remaining spring onion and serve with the salsa. (You can serve the fritters either warm or cold.)"]],"h":[[null,"For a vegetarian alternative to Parmesan, swap it out with vegetarian-style hard cheese."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"7415142":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°/gas 4."],[null,"Oil the loaf tin and set aside."],[null,"To a bowl add the eggs, oil, vanilla extract and sweetener, then beat together well."],[null,"Mix in the courgettes then stir in the flour, baking powder and cinnamon."],[null,"Place in the baking tin and bake for 30-35 minutes until firm to the touch."]],"h":[[null,"To test if the cake is cooked insert a small, sharp knife into the middle, if it comes out clean the cake is cooked. If there is uncooked mixture sticking to the knife it needs a little longer."],[null,"Try using yellow courgettes for a different coloured cake."],[null,"For a spicier version, add 2 teaspoons of mixed spice along with the cinnamon."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Slice then wrap in foil to freeze (you can then use slices as required)."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"7754918":{"s":[[null,"Preheat grill to medium-high."],[null,"Cut the courgette into 0.5cm slices, toss in a bowl with 1tbsp lemon juice and 2tsp sunflower oil."],[null,"Grill for 4-6 minutes each side, until lightly browned."],[null,"Mix the courgette through the rocket, add the feta, season with black pepper to taste and serve."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6496705":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, combine flour, baking powder, cumin, salt, and pepper. Add egg whites and salsa; mix well, then stir in black beans."],[null,"In a large skillet over medium-high heat, heat 1 Tbsp. oil. Pour 1 Tsp. batter per fritter into skillet, cooking several fritters at one time, but not overcrowding them. Cook 1 minute, then turn fritters and lightly flatten with a spatula; cook 1 to 2 additional minutes or until browned on both sides. Repeat with remaining batter, adding more oil as necessary."]],"h":[]},"6243430":{"s":[[null,"Coat a small non-stick skillet with cooking spray over medium-high heat. Add onion and sauté 2-3 minutes or until onions are clear. Set aside to cool."],[null,"In a medium bowl combine crabmeat, breadcrumbs, egg, egg white, hot sauce, salt and pepper. Mix well until all ingredients are incorporated. Stir in cooled onion."],[null,"Add oil and a generous amount of cooking spray to a large non-stick skillet over medium-high heat. Form crab mixture into 1/2-inch thick patties using a heaping 1/4 cup. Fry about 4-5 minutes on each side or until golden brown."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together mayonnaise, yogurt, adobo sauce and corn."],[null,"Place each crab cake on a lettuce leaf. Place 1/4 cup lettuce, 1 tomato slice and 2 avocado slices on top of each crab cake and top with 2 Tbsp. of sauce."]],"h":[]},"1822":{"s":[[null,"Finely chop bell pepper and onion. Crush crackers."],[null,"Combine all ingredients listed above except the oil; shape into 6 patties."],[null,"Heat oil in a skillet over medium heat."],[null,"Cook patties for approximately 4 to 5 minutes, or until browned."],[null,"Flip patties and cook other side until browned, about 4 minutes."],[null,"Serve warm."]],"h":[[null,"Adjust seasoning to taste. Avoid adding additional ingredients that increase sodium content."],[null,"Fresh or pasteurized crab meat is the lowest in sodium. Frozen and canned crab meat usually has added sodium preservatives."]]},"7574767":{"s":[[null,"Cook the pasta according to the pack instructions."],[null,"Once it's drained, simply combine all the remaining ingredients in a bowl and toss through the pasta."]],"h":[[null,"You could use fettuccine, linguine or spaghetti rather than tagliatelle."],[null,"If you don’t have basil, use parsley instead."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6407571":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F."],[null,"Cook lasagna noodles according to package instructions without adding salt, drain, and set aside."],[null,"To make the filling: Preheat a large saucepan over medium heat. Add 1 tsp olive oil, onion, kale, and 3 cloves of minced garlic. Cook, stirring occasionally, until onions and kale have softened, 5–6 minutes. Transfer to a large bowl. Add ricotta, crab meat, ¼ cup Parmesan, egg, and ¼ tsp pepper. Stir to combine and set aside."],[null,"To make the sauce: Return pan to medium heat. Add 1 tsp olive oil and 2 cloves of minced garlic. Cook for one minute, then add tomato paste and cook for another minute, stirring often. Add pumpkin, milk, spices, 1/8 tsp black pepper. Stir to combine and let simmer for a few minutes. Stir in ¼ cup Parmesan and remove from heat."],[null,"To assemble: Add half a cup of the sauce to the bottom of a large baking dish. Spread ¼ cup filling along the length of each lasagna noodle. Roll and place seam side down in the dish. Pour the rest of the sauce over the noodles and top each roll with mozzarella cheese. Bake for 30 minutes, until the cheese is melted and bubbly. Top with fresh parsley."]],"h":[]},"3146":{"s":[[null,"Trim the celery rib ends. Drain and flake the crab meat. Mince the onion."],[null,"In a small bowl combine the crab meat, onion, mayonnaise and lemon juice."],[null,"Fill each celery rib with 1 tablespoon of the crab mixture."],[null,"Cut each celery rib into 3 pieces."],[null,"Sprinkle crab-stuffed celery pieces with paprika before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Recipe analysis includes canned crab meat. Substitute fresh or frozen if preferred."],[null,"Double or triple the recipe to serve at parties or social events."]]},"1790":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 450° F."],[null,"Finely chop crab meat, celery, parsley, onion and bell pepper."],[null,"In a bowl mix crab, bread crumbs, 3 tablespoons melted butter, celery, parsley, onion and bell pepper; set aside."],[null,"Spray a baking sheet with non-stick cooking spray."],[null,"Wash and de-vein shrimp; pat dry."],[null,"Use a sharp knife to cut a 1/2″ deep pocket in inner curved side of shrimp from tail along center, leaving 1/2-inches at end. Do not cut through back of shrimp. Use finger to widen pocket."],[null,"Use about 2-1/2 tablespoons crab mixture per shrimp. Place portion in hand and squeeze to mold. Place crab in shrimp pocket and distribute to fill. Place shrimp on baking sheet. Repeat, preparing all shrimp."],[null,"Brush shrimp with melted butter. Bake for 10-12 minutes. Do not over cook."],[null,"Serve with a side dish of melted unsalted butter if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Use fresh or frozen deveined, shelled shrimp with tails on to make this recipe extra quick. (16 to 20 per pound)."],[null,"For a fancier presentation you can butterfly the shrimp, flatten and stuff then secure tail on top of stuffing with a toothpick."],[null,"For a lower protein diet decrease serving size to 2 shrimp (18 grams protein) or the amount that matches your meal plan."],[null,"One jumbo shrimp is about 1 to 1-1/2 ounces, headless and with shell. You can substitute 16 large shrimp and increase serving size to 4 pieces."],[null,"If fresh crab is unavailable, buy the lowest sodium frozen or canned crab."]]},"3708":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 300° F. Spray a large rectangular cake pan (9″ x 13″ or larger) with non-stick cooking spray."],[null,"Dice the dried apples."],[null,"In a large bowl mix cereals and dried fruit; set aside."],[null,"In a medium bowl beat egg whites, sugar, apple juice and cinnamon with a whisk or hand mixer until foamy."],[null,"Pour egg mixture over cereal in bowl, stirring until evenly coated."],[null,"Sprinkle with sesame seeds."],[null,"Spread mixture into baking pan and bake for 45 minutes, stirring every 15 minutes, until cereal is lightly brown and crispy."],[null,"Cool completely. Store in an airtight container."]],"h":[[null,"Mary uses All Whites® pasteurized liquid egg white product. You can substitute 1/4 cup fresh egg whites."],[null,"Replace sugar with preferred low carbohydrate sweetener to reduce carbohydrate to 38 grams per serving. If you have diabetes consider adjusting the portion to 1/2 cup in addition to this change."]]},"3422":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375º F."],[null,"Cut cranberries in half. Core, peel and dice apples."],[null,"Combine cranberries, apples, 1/4 cup packed brown sugar and cinnamon in a large bowl."],[null,"Spray a 13” x 9” baking dish with cooking spray and pour in cranberry mixture."],[null,"Combine flour, remaining 1/2 cup packed brown sugar and white sugar in a medium bowl. Add butter and cut into flour mixture with a pastry blender or by hand. Mix well to make coarse crumbs."],[null,"Sprinkle topping on cranberry mixture and bake for 50 minutes or until topping is golden brown."]],"h":[[null,"A half portion is recommended if you have diabetes, or replace sugar with low calorie sweeteners to decrease carbohydrate to 22 grams. Count as 1-1/2 carbohydrate choices."]]},"3295":{"s":[[null,"Combine water, diced apple or applesauce, cranberries, cinnamon and nutmeg in a small saucepan. Bring to a boil, cover, and simmer until apple is tender."],[null,"Stir in oatmeal, bring to a boil, and cook 1 minute."],[null,"Gradually add half of the oatmeal to a beaten egg. Add that mixture back to oatmeal and cook about 10 seconds."],[null,"Serve with milk or milk substitute and sweetener, as meal plan permits."]],"h":[[null,"Egg may be added directly to oatmeal if desired."],[null,"Avoid instant oatmeal because it is high in sodium."],[null,"If desired substitute 1/4 cup unsweetened applesauce for fresh apple."],[null,"For a gluten-free version be sure to use oats that indicates gluten-free on the label."]]},"6406409":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375 degrees F. Line two muffin pans with 18 paper liners and spray lightly with cooking spray."],[null,"In a large bowl combine oats, oat flour, whole wheat flour, brown sugar substitute, baking powder, baking soda, coarse salt, and cinnamon. Mix well."],[null,"Gently fold in dried cranberries and 1/4 cup sliced almonds."],[null,"In a medium bowl whisk together buttermilk, Greek yogurt, oil, egg, vanilla and almond extracts."],[null,"Make a well in the center of the dry ingredients and add the wet ingredients to the well, gently stirring until moist. Do not over mix."],[null,"Fill each muffin cup about 2/3 full with muffin batter. Sprinkle 1/2 Tsp. ground flax seed over each muffin then sprinkle the remaining 1/4 cup sliced almonds evenly over the muffins. Press the flax seed and almonds gently into the muffin batter."],[null,"Bake muffins for 20-25 minutes or until toothpick inserted in center comes out clean. Cool on wire rack."]],"h":[]},"2317":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 425° F. Spray a casserole dish with nonstick cooking spray."],[null,"Mince onion."],[null,"Melt butter in a large saucepan. Add roasted garlic and onion in saucepan and cook over medium heat until soft."],[null,"Add rice and cook for 2 minutes."],[null,"Add broth and dried cranberries to rice mixture. Bring to a boil and cook for 2 minutes."],[null,"Pour into casserole dish. Cover and bake for 30 minutes."],[null,"Remove from oven and sprinkle Parmesan cheese over the top. Serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"Prepare roasted garlic from the Roasted Garlic Heads recipe or use bottled garlic spread."],[null,"Arborio rice is medium-grain rice with a high starch content. It is grown in Italy and is traditionally used in risotto recipes."]]},"9922454":{"s":[[null,"Add everything except the water to your food processor and process until broken down and combined, scraping down the sides as needed. If your mixture isn't sticky enough to hold together (this may vary according to the drippiness of your almond butter), add 1 tablespoon of water and process until combined. Repeat with the remaining tablespoon IF NEEDED."],[null,"Shape the mixture into approx. 1-inch balls. You'll get 18-20 balls. Then roll them in extra coconut if you'd like, or enjoy them plain."]],"h":[]},"2034":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F. Melt the butter in a saucepan over low heat, or in a microwave. Stir in the brown sugar and let mixture cool to room temperature."],[null,"Place sugar mixture in a large bowl and beat in the eggs and vanilla extract."],[null,"Mix together the flour and baking powder, and gradually add to the sugar mixture. Stir in the white chocolate and the 1/3 cup of the cranberries."],[null,"Spray a 9 x 13-inch baking pan with cooking spray. Spread the batter in the pan; it will be thick.Bake for 18 to 22 minutes. A toothpick inserted in the center should come out with just a few crumbs. Let cool completely."],[null,"Let cream cheese sit at room temperature for about 30 minutes. Stir cinnamon into powdered sugar. Beat with a hand-mixer for 1 minute. Gradually start adding powdered sugar mixture and beat until smooth."],[null,"Spread the frosting on cooled brownies. Top with remaining cranberries. Cut into 24 pieces. Store in the refrigerator until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Chop the cranberries to distribute them throughout the blondies."],[null,"Cranberries have 30 mg of potassium per 1/2 cup."],[null,"White chocolate is similar to semi-sweet chocolate in potassium and phosphorus content. Using a small amount like in this recipe allows you to enjoy chocolate while keeping it kidney-friendly!"],[null,"To decrease carbs to 21 grams per serving substitute brown sugar with a sugar and sugar substitute blend and replace powdered sugar with a granular sugar substitute."]]},"9877958":{"s":[[null,"Dice your apple and place in a large bowl. Then squeeze fresh lemon juice on top to prevent it from browning and mix well. Add all remaining salad ingredients to the same bowl and mix together."],[null,"Add all the dressing ingredients EXCEPT the poppy seeds to your blender and process until smooth. Then add the poppy seeds and blend for 1-2 seconds, just enough to mix them into your dressing. Pour the dressing over the salad, mix well and refrigerate for 1 hour or longer, before serving."]],"h":[[null,"* If you do not have a powerful blender , like a Vitamix or Blendtec, soak your cashews in boiling hot water for at least 30 minutes, and then drain before blending. This will help soften your cashews enough to blend smooth. You’ll notice that the recipe calls for lemon juice twice . The first instance is to prevent the apples from turning brown, as well as flavour. The second instance is for the poppy seed salad dressing. Both are needed. Use a tart apple , like granny smith for the best tangy flavour. Don’t blend the poppy seeds with your dressing . Make sure to only add them AFTER your dressing has been processed. For best flavour , chill for 1 hour (or more) before serving. However, if time doesn’t permit, you may enjoy straight away."]]},"2974":{"s":[[null,"In large pan heat cranberry sauce, lemon juice and cloves together and bring to a simmer."],[null,"Stir cabbage into melted cranberry sauce, mixing well. Bring mixture to a boil; reduce heat to simmer. Continue cooking until cabbage is tender, stirring occasionally."],[null,"Serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"One medium head of cabbage yields 6 cups chopped."]]},"2745":{"s":[[null,"Chop onion."],[null,"Preheat oil in a large skillet. Add onion and sauté until clear."],[null,"Add chicken and cook for 3–4 minutes on each side."],[null,"In a medium-sized bowl combine ketchup, dry mustard, cranberry sauce, packed brown sugar and vinegar. Stir until mixed and pour into skillet."],[null,"Cover and cook on medium heat for 15–20 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Serve with white rice and green beans for a complete kidney friendly meal."],[null,"Use Splenda® Brown Sugar Blend to reduce carbohydrate content if you have diabetes."],[null,"Another way to reduce carbohydrate is to substitute 1-1/2 cups of frozen cranberries in place of whole-berry cranberry sauce and add low calorie sweetener to desired sweetness."],[null,"For a lower sodium dish use no added salt ketchup without potassium chloride."],[null,"Cut large chicken breast-halves in half for 6 pieces."],[null,"Use chicken thighs or legs if you like dark-meat chicken."],[null,"Adjust the chicken portion to match your meal plan if you are on a lower protein diet."]]},"4990973":{"s":[[null,"Preheat conventional oven to 350°F. Line a 9×9 inch pan with parchment paper."],[null,"In a mixing bowl, prepare the wet ingredients. Whisk the eggs, sugar, butter, vanilla, yogurt and milk together."],[null,"In another bowl, prepare the dry ingredients. Sift together the flour, baking soda and cinnamon."],[null,"Add the dry ingredients to the wet ingredients and mix thoroughly."],[null,"Fold the berries into the cake batter."],[null,"In a separate bowl, mix the crumble topping ingredients."],[null,"Pour the cake batter into the cake pan. The cake batter should be quite thick. Top with crumble."],[null,"Bake for approximately 40 minutes or until the cake springs back when touched."]],"h":[]},"2193":{"s":[[null,"Place sour cream, cranberry sauce, nutmeg and ginger in a food processor and process until well mixed. Remove to a small bowl."],[null,"Cut pineapple into bite-size pieces. Cut apples and pears into 12 slices each. Toss apple and pear slices with lemon juice to prevent browning."],[null,"Arrange fruit on platter with dip bowl in the middle. Chill until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Refrigerate leftover dip for up to 3 days."]]},"4562778":{"s":[[null,"Combine all ingredients in a saucepan and bring to a boil. Simmer for 5 minutes."],[null,"Allow mixture to cool and blend thoroughly."],[null,"Strain into a 9\" x 13\" pan and place in freezer for at least 2 hours, stirring after the first 30 minutes."],[null,"Shave granita with the back of a spoon and serve garnished with a fresh sprig of mint in your favorite cup or martini glass."]],"h":[[null,"* To lower the carbohydrate content you can use a sugar substitute which is suitable for baking."],[null,"Can be prepared ahead of time, one day before serving."],["Cranberries: More Than Just A Holiday Staple","Cranberries are readily available during the fall months or can be found in your grocer's freezer year-round. For those with chronic kidney disease, some fruits may contain too much potassium to be enjoyed on a daily basis. Cranberries however, are lower in potassium and in limited amounts, can typically be enjoyed every day if desired. Cranberries are a good source of dietary fiber and contain antioxidants that fight disease and may promote urinary tract health through their antibacterial properties. To take advantage of these health benefits, enjoy them throughout the holiday season when they are fresh and easily to be found in your supermarket. As part of a low-potassium diet, make a traditional sauce and add them to stuffing or your apple pie for a pop of color and flavor. When it is no longer cranberry season, purchase frozen or dried cranberries. Frozen cranberries can be added to muffins and breads. Consider adding dried cranberries to hot or cold cereal, cookies and your favorite snack mix. They can also be tossed in a vegetable salad or added to your chicken salad. You can also cook with them to add flavor and color to couscous or rice pilaf as well as chicken dishes."]]},"2194":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400° F. Grease twelve 2-1/2″ muffin cups or line with baking cups; set aside."],[null,"To prepare streusel topping, combine 3 tablespoons of the flour, brown sugar and cinnamon in a bowl. Cut in 2 tablespoons butter until mixture resembles coarse crumbs; set aside."],[null,"To prepare muffins, combine remaining flour, sugar, baking powder and salt in a medium bowl. Make a well in the center of the flour mixture; set aside."],[null,"In another bowl whisk egg, juice and oil together. Pour egg mixture all at once into flour mixture. Stir just until moistened (batter should be lumpy). Fold in chopped cranberries."],[null,"Spoon batter into prepared muffin cups, filling each 2/3 full. Sprinkle streusel topping over muffin batter in cups. Bake for 18 to 20 minutes or until golden and a wooden toothpick inserted in centers comes out clean."],[null,"Cool in muffin cups on a wire rack for 5 minutes. Remove from muffin cups; serve warm."]],"h":[[null,"Streusel topping is optional. Adds 2 grams fat and 2 grams carbohydate per muffin."],[null,"Freeze or refrigerate leftover muffins. Heat for 10 to 20 seconds in the microwave before serving."]]},"2120":{"s":[[null,"Cut each cranberry in half and reserve."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 350° F. Grease a loaf pan and line with waxed paper. Grease wax paper. Set aside."],[null,"Sift the flour, sugar, baking powder and baking soda together in a large bowl."],[null,"In a separate bowl mix the juice, orange zest, melted margarine and beaten egg. Add to the flour mixture and stir just until flour is combined."],[null,"Mix in the cranberries and walnuts. Stir in hot water."],[null,"Place batter in a prepared loaf pan and bake 1 hour and 10 minutes. Test by poking a toothpick into bread; if it comes out clean the bread is done."],[null,"Cool loaf in the pan for 10 minutes, then remove and cool on a wire rack. Cut into 10 slices."]],"h":[[null,"Nuts are high in potassium and phosphorus but may be included in small amounts. The 1/4 cup walnuts in this recipe provides 15 mg potassium and 9 mg phosphorus per slice."],[null,"To reduce carbohydrate and calories, substitute 1/2 cup Splenda© sugar blend for baking for the 1 cup of sugar. Carbohydrate is reduced to 25 grams and calories are reduced to 160."],[null,"Make an extra loaf and freeze for later."]]},"2979":{"s":[[null,"Set butter out to soften to room temperature. Preheat oven to 350° F. Line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Using an electric mixer, cream together butter and sugar. Add in the egg, flour, protein powder, vanilla extract, cinnamon and salt. Stir to combine."],[null,"Add in the applesauce and combine. Fold in the oats and cranberries."],[null,"Scoop 1/4 cup scoops of the cookie dough onto the baking sheet. Flatten each cookie slightly."],[null,"Bake for 12 to 15 minutes, until cookies are golden brown but still soft."],[null,"Allow cookies to cool for 5 minutes on the baking sheet before transferring to a rack to cool completely."]],"h":[[null,"Store cookies in an air tight container or wrap individually and freeze until ready to grab for a quick breakfast on the go."],[null,"Scoop sizes vary for different protein powder brands. Check the label to see weight of one scoop to determine how much to add or use a scale to measure 1.5 ounces."],[null,"Enjoy breakfast cookies as a snack. Consider making 24 smaller cookies instead of 12."]]},"3228":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Place parchment paper on a baking sheet."],[null,"In a medium bowl sift together flour and baking powder."],[null,"In a large bowl beat sugar, butter, orange zest and salt with a mixer. Add eggs, one at a time and mix until well blended. Slowly add flour mixture and mix until all flour is incorporated."],[null,"With a spoon, mix macadamia nuts and cranberries into dough."],[null,"Remove dough from bowl onto a very lightly floured surface; form dough into a loaf that is approx 12” long and 3” wide."],[null,"Place on a baking sheet and bake for 40 to 45 minutes until barely golden on surface. Remove from oven cool loaf for 30 to 40 minutes."],[null,"Cut the cooled loaf into 3/4”-thick slices using a bread knife. Place slices back on the baking sheet and bake for another 15 minutes until biscotti are lightly golden. Remove from oven and cool on a rack."]],"h":[[null,"Cooking times vary with each oven."],[null,"Biscotti can be stored in an airtight container for about one week."],[null,"Great for gift-giving around the holidays."]]},"6945433":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F. Line a muffin tin with paper liners."],[null,"In a large bowl, whisk together the almond flour, coconut flour, baking powder, cinnamon, nutmeg, ginger, and salt."],[null,"In another bowl, whisk together the pumpkin purée, almond milk, eggs, ​applesauce​​​, almond butter, and sugar substitute until well combined."],[null,"Pour the wet ingredients into the dry ingredients and stir until just combined."],[null,"Gently fold in the cranberries."],[null,"Spoon the batter evenly into the muffin cups, filling each about 2/3 full."],[null,"Bake in the preheated oven for 18–20 minutes or until a toothpick inserted into the center comes out clean."],[null,"Allow the muffins to cool in the tin for 5 minutes, then transfer them to a wire rack to cool completely."]],"h":[]},"3324":{"s":[[null,"Soak rice and all ingredients for 40-45 minutes at room temperature."],[null,"Place all ingredients in a rice cooker."],[null,"If using a microwave rice cooker, microwave for 12 minutes at full power. If cooking stove top, bring to a boil, then reduce heat to a simmer. Cook covered for 20 minutes."],[null,"Let stand for 5 minutes before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Black cumin is a spice used in Indian and Pakistani cuisine. Look for Kala Jeera or black cumin in any Indian spice store or Asian market. It is also available online."],[null,"Select a cinnamon stick approximately 1” in length."]]},"2153":{"s":[[null,"Drain pineapple. Thaw strawberries."],[null,"In a large bowl mix all ingredients together until combined."],[null,"Store in a covered container in the refrigerator until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Serve with meat or poultry, add to salad greens or use as a topping on a slice of pound cake."]]},"3861":{"s":[[null,"Combine liquid protein, cranberry juice and ice. Stir well with spoon."],[null,"Add 2 ounces of club soda (or to taste)."],[null,"Garnish with a lime slice."]],"h":[[null,"LiquaCel™ is a liquid protein supplement that is low in potassium and phosphorus. Ask your dietitian for information or go to GlobalHP.com."]]},"3476":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350º F. Set butter and cream cheese out to soften."],[null,"In a medium bowl combine flour, sugar and baking powder."],[null,"In a large bowl combine butter, cream cheese and vanilla; beat until light and fluffy."],[null,"Add dry ingredients to cream cheese mixture and blend well. Form dough into a ball, wrap and chill for 2 hours."],[null,"Roll dough to 1/4” thickness on lightly floured surface."],[null,"Cut with 1-1/2-inch fluted or round cutter."],[null,"Place 2” apart on ungreased cookie sheet. Press center of each cookie slightly with your thumb and fill center with 1/4 teaspoon jam."],[null,"Bake for 10–12 minutes."],[null,"Remove from cookie sheet and place on a wire rack to cool."],[null,"Sift powdered sugar over top of cookie, if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Use any flavor of jam. Try orange marmalade or peach jam for Halloween cookies or strawberry or raspberry for Christmas or Valentine’s Day cookies."],[null,"An alternative way to make these cookies: Roll chilled dough thin 1/8″. Cut cookies with a 2″ fluted cookie cutter. Cut a small hole in the middle of half the cookies. Sandwich the cookies together and fill the hole with jam before baking. Makes 24 cookies, serving size is 1 cookie instead of 3 smaller cookies."],[null,"After sifting with powdered sugar,moisten your finger with water and dab the jelly portion tomake it glossy again."],[null,"Store extra cookies in a covered container or freeze for later."]]},"2600":{"s":[[null,"Set cream cheese and butter out to soften."],[null,"Whip softened cream cheese until fluffy. Add butter and vanilla extract and mix together."],[null,"Gradually add in powdered sugar until frosting is smooth."]],"h":[[null,"Use frosting to frost a cake, cupcakes or cookies or try this frosting with Jessica’s Carrot Cake Cookies."],[null,"Frosting will keep for about 5 days in the refrigerator."]]},"2577":{"s":[[null,"Mix ground beef, eggs, basil, onion powder and garlic powder together."],[null,"Separate meat into eight 2-ounce patties."],[null,"Take 1-1/2 tablespoons of the cream cheese and place on top of a patty."],[null,"Take another patty and place it on top, to sandwich the cream cheese between the two patties."],[null,"Repeat this procedure with the remaining patties."],[null,"Cook in a frying pan or on a grill to desired doneness."],[null,"Serve burgers on a bun with lettuce, onion and condiment of choice."]],"h":[[null,"For a variation, combine all the ingredients together with cream cheese in the meat, make four 4-ounce patties and cook."],[null,"Top burger with ketchup or steak sauce without the bun for variety."],[null,"Recipe may be varied by rolling cream cheese in bread crumbs or panko crumbs."],[null,"Patties cook best in a frying pan, in their own juices."],[null,"Many herbs and flavorings work well to add flavor without sodium — try using horseradish, oregano or Italian seasoning."],[null,"For a lower protein diet make 6 burgers instead of 4 burgers"]]},"6396233":{"s":[[null,"Wash the broccoli thoroughly. Using a vegetable peeler, remove the tough outer layer from the broccoli stalks. Chop broccoli and set aside 1 cup of florets for garnish."],[null,"Bring chicken stock to a simmer and add chopped broccoli. Cook for a few minutes or until broccoli is tender, making sure the color does not become dull."],[null,"Puree cooked broccoli and 1 cup of chicken stock in a food processor. Set aside."],[null,"Add olive oil and onions to a pot and gently cook. Sprinkle flour and stir to mix. On low heat, continue cooking, making sure flour is absorbed and slightly turns color. Slowly whisk hot chicken stock into flour mixture and bring to a simmer. Add broccoli puree and half & half; bring to a simmer, stirring to combine ingredients. Season with salt and peper and garnish with florets. Serve hot."]],"h":[]},"2351":{"s":[[null,"Prepare the long grain and wild rice blend according to package instructions, omitting salt and seasoning packet if included"],[null,"Remove the pan from heat, allow rice to sit, covered, for additional 15 minutes. Set aside and let cool."],[null,"Dice the asparagus, carrots and onion. Mince the garlic."],[null,"In a Dutch oven, melt the butter and sauté the garlic and onion until tender. Add carrots, herbs and spices. Continue to cook over medium heat until tender."],[null,"Mix in the flour and cook over low heat for approximately 10 minutes, stirring frequently."],[null,"Pour in the 4 cups of chicken broth and vermouth. Using a wire whisk, blend until smooth."],[null,"Dice the cooked chicken into small pieces. Add chicken and asparagus to the soup, then slowly add the almond milk. Simmer for 20 minutes."],[null,"Fold in prepared rice, and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Steps 1 through 3 can be done up to 24 hours ahead; refrigerate cooked rice until ready to use."],[null,"Count as 1 cup fluid if you are on a fluid restriction."],[null,"Omit the salt if reduced-sodium broth is used instead of low-sodium broth."],[null,"A two-cup serving is meal size portion. For an appetizer portion decrease serving to 3/4 cup (118 cal, 8 g protein, 11 g carbohydrate, 4 g fat, 154 mg sodium, 211 mg potassium, 101 g phosphorus)."]]},"2913":{"s":[[null,"Hard boil the eggs for 12 minutes. Remove from heat, drain and cover with cool water. Peel and chop boiled eggs and set aside."],[null,"Combine the butter and flour in a sauce pan over medium low heat. Stir constantly until well combined."],[null,"Add the almond milk, mustard, cream cheese and pepper to butter and flour mixture. Stir constantly until thickened."],[null,"Add the eggs to the sauce and keep over warm heat."],[null,"Toast the bread."],[null,"Pour the egg mixture over toast and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Add dry dill or garlic powder for more flavor if desired."],[null,"Look for bread with the least amount of sodium per slice."]]},"7186194":{"s":[[null,"Heat the spread in a medium pan, add the onion and asparagus and fry for 2–3 minutes until everything begins to soften."],[null,"Add the flour and cook for a further minute."],[null,"Gradually, stir in the stock, bring to the boil and simmer for 10 minutes until the asparagus is cooked through, and reserve a couple of asparagus spears for serving."],[null,"Add the milk, bring to almost boiling point, then place in a blender or food processor and blend until smooth."],[null,"Season with plenty of black pepper and top with the asparagus spears."]],"h":[[null,"Serve with crusty bread or toast."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"3886":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Spray an 8″ x 8″ glass baking pan with vegetable oil spray. Sprinkle a light covering of flour (2-3 tablespoons from the 1/2 cup) on the bottom of the pan."],[null,"Rinse haddock and arrange each piece in the pan."],[null,"Sprinkle the fish with salt and pepper and the rest of the flour. Distribute evenly."],[null,"Cover with regular fat nondairy creamer, fat-free nondairy creamer and water."],[null,"Cut butter into pieces and dot top of mixture."],[null,"Bake for approximately 30 to 45 minutes or until slightly golden brown."],[null,"Transfer fish to a plate. Spoon cream sauce from baking dish and spoon over the fish before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Buy haddock steaks or fillets. Thaw if frozen. Cooking time may vary with thickness of fillets or steaks. Test after 30 minutes."],[null,"If sauce is not thickened when fish is done, remove fish from pan, stir sauce and return to oven for 5-10 minutes."],[null,"If you are on a higher or lower protein diet, adjust fish portion to match your meal plan."],[null,"Omit salt if desired. Sodium is reduced to 122 mg per serving."]]},"6693002":{"s":[[null,"Bring a large pot of water to a boil. Add baby spinach to the pot and blanch for 1 minute. Use a slotted spoon to remove the spinach to a bowl of ice water. Add parsley and 1 packed cup of basil to the pot and blanch for 15 seconds. Remove and add to the bowl of ice water with the spinach. Drain water and squeeze out as much liquid from the greens as possible."],[null,"Add spinach, parsley, and basil to a food processor. Add Greek yogurt to the food processor, then purée. Set aside."],[null,"Heat a saucepan over medium heat. Add 2 tablespoons of olive oil, garlic, and onion powder. Add flour and whisk for 1 minute. Add milk and whisk until smooth."],[null,"Add cheese, Italian seasoning, salt (optional), and pepper. Stir until sauce is thickened (about 10 minutes). Add puréed greens and stir to combine."],[null,"Meanwhile, heat a large skillet over medium heat. Spray with nonstick cooking spray. Cook chicken for 3–4 minutes per side, until golden brown and cooked through."],[null,"Cook pasta according to package directions to al dente stage."],[null,"To serve, divide chicken and pasta between plates. Top with sauce, Parmesan, and remaining thinly sliced basil. Top with diced grape tomatoes if desired."]],"h":[]},"2903":{"s":[[null,"Begin by slicing the onion. To caramelize the onion heat 1 tablespoon of olive oil in a large skillet. Add the sliced onion and cook on high for about 10 minutes, constantly stirring. The onions should start to turn brown without burning"],[null,"Reduce heat to medium and continue to stir onions for about 10 minutes. They should be even more brown but still not burned."],[null,"Reduce heat again to medium – low and continue to cook for 10 minutes. Making sure the onion does not stick to the bottom of the pan. Onions should cook for 30 minutes total."],[null,"Remove skillet from heat and sprinkle with balsamic vinegar. Use a spatula to scrape the bottom of the skillet and then remove caramelized onion to a plate or bowl."],[null,"Heat remaining 1 tablespoon olive oil in the same skillet and add mushrooms, cooking until mushrooms are soft about 5 minutes."],[null,"Add spinach and stir on low heat until spinach starts to wilt."],[null,"Add half and half to the spinach and mushroom mixture. Bring to a quick boil and then reduce heat to simmer."],[null,"Add 2/3 cup Parmesan cheese stirring until it melts. Add caramelized onion back to the skillet."],[null,"Cook farfalle pasta el dente, according to package directions. Add drained farfalle pasta to skillet and stir together and thoroughly."]],"h":[[null,"If short on time, you can caramelize onion ahead of time and store in the refrigerator."],[null,"You can substitute kale or arugula for spinach."],[null,"Different mushrooms such as shiitake, cremini or button mushrooms can be substituted."],[null,"A medium onion is about 2-1/2 inches in diameter."],[null,"This dish can be served with a small side salad or 1/2 cup low potassium vegetable."],[null,"This dish makes 8 servings, so it can be used for a family dinner or saved for leftovers throughout the week."]]},"3564":{"s":[[null,"In a large pot, boil the broccoli florets and tofu (with liquid) in the vegetable broth until tender. Set aside to cool."],[null,"Carefully pour the cooled contents of the pot into a large mixing bowl and blend until smooth using an immersion blender. Alternately, carefully pour contents of the pot into a large blender. Remove top stopper to allow steam to vent. Blend until smooth."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine 1-1/2 cups of the soup with the cornstarch. Whisk until smooth."],[null,"Pour soup back into the pot, add cornstarch mixture and bring to a boil. Stir in nutritional yeast and spices until well combined."]],"h":[[null,"Tofu is a high biological value vegetarian protein source."],[null,"This soup is a great choice for those with chewing or swallowing difficulty."],[null,"Use low-sodium chicken broth instead of vegetable broth if desired."],[null,"Adjust the black pepper and chili flakes to your taste."]]},"9709742":{"s":[["Stovetop Directions","Add the onion, celery, carrots, and garlic to a large pot with 3-4 tablespoons of water and sauté for 5-7 minutes, until softened."],["Stovetop Directions","Then add all remaining ingredients except the avocado. Bring to a boil, then reduce heat and simmer for about 10 minutes, until the veggies are fork tender."],["Stovetop Directions","Turn off the heat, add the avocado, and use an immersion blender to puree the soup. (OR, carefully transfer to a regular blender.) Taste for salt and pepper, adding more if needed."],["Stovetop Directions","Serve garnished with fresh dill, cashew cream, or red pepper flakes."],["Instant Pot Directions","Set your Instant Pot to sauté mode, and add the onion, celery, carrots, and garlic with 3-4 tablespoons of water and sauté for 5-7 minutes, until softened."],["Instant Pot Directions","Then add all remaining ingredients except the avocado. Close the lid, ensuring the valve is in the sealing position, and set it to high pressure for 5 minutes. (It will take about 15 minutes to reach pressure.)"],["Instant Pot Directions","When the timer is complete, quick-release the steam valve and open the lid once safe to do so. Add the avocado and use an immersion blender to puree the soup. Taste for salt and pepper, add more if needed, and then serve."]],"h":[[null,"Don't stress over uniform-sized veggie pieces . Since you'll be pureeing the soup, you don't need even sizes. This will save you time on prep."],[null,"If you’re pressed for time , skip the sauté step and simmer everything together in one step."],[null,"Use an immersion blender to puree for less mess, ease, and fewer dishes to wash."],[null,"If you don't have an immersion blender , use extreme caution when blending hot liquids. Don't overfill your blender, and work in batches to prevent spills."],[null,"Taste for salt and pepper once cooked , and add more, if needed. Depending on the broth you're using, you may want more salt."],[null,"This soup is thick in texture. If you prefer a thinner texture , use an additional cup of broth or stir in a cup of your favourite plant-based milk after pureeing."],[null,"Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-4 days, or frozen in airtight freezer-safe containers for up to 3 months."]]},"3957":{"s":[[null,"Break or cut up the cauliflower into small florets. Mince garlic. Split leek bulb into 4 pieces and rinse."],[null,"Place cauliflower florets into a pot and cover with water. Bring to a boil and cook 20 minutes. Drain some of the water, leaving about 1 cup in the pan with cauliflower. Add the garlic and leeks, cover and continue to cook 10 to 15 minutes or until very tender. Drain well."],[null,"Blend hot vegetables in a food processor until smooth like mashed potatoes. Add a little water if the mixture seems too stiff."],[null,"Season the mixture with salt and white pepper. Stir in butter or margarine. Serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"One large cauliflower is approximately 8 cups or 1-1/2 pounds. Frozen cauliflower pieces may be substituted for fresh cauliflower."],[null,"Vegetables may be steamed instead of boiled if potassium is not restricted in your diet. The potassium content is 440 mg per 1/2 cup serving when cauliflower is steamed compared to 256 mg per 1/2 cup serving when cauliflower is boiled."]]},"2821":{"s":[[null,"Pre-heat the oven to 400° F."],[null,"Peel the out layers of the garlic head. Slice the tip off to expose the top of the garlic cloves. Drizzle with 1 teaspoon olive oil. Wrap the garlic head in aluminum foil, place in the oven and roast for 30 minutes."],[null,"Bring a large pot of water to a boil. Add cauliflower florets and boil until tender. Drain the cauliflower and let cool."],[null,"Add the cauliflower to a food processor or blender. Squeeze roasted garlic cloves from skins and add to the cauliflower along with the nutritional yeast, almond milk and black pepper. Process or blend the ingredients while drizzling olive oil through the top of the food processor/blender until the sauce is creamy."]],"h":[[null,"Serve Creamy Cauliflower Sauce as a replacement for Alfredo or cheese sauce, on pasta, pizza or as a dipping sauce."],[null,"Add additional almond milk to thin to desired consistency of sauce is too thick."],[null,"Fresh roasted garlic adds flavor and depth to the sauce. Garlic powder or fresh raw garlic may be substituted for faster preparation."],[null,"Consider roasting garlic regularly to have on hand to add flavor to just about anything-meats, sauces, and vegetables, even spread on toast."]]},"6884440":{"s":[[null,"Wash and trim 4 celery sticks."],[null,"Spread 4 tablespoons fatfree cream cheese evenly into the celery channels."],[null,"Sprinkle 1/2 tablespoon pumpkin seeds and ½ T. sunflower seeds over the cream cheese for each celery stick."],[null,"Serve immediately for the best crunch."]],"h":[]},"6050475":{"s":[[null,"Add 4 quarts of water to a 6-quart saucepan. Bring the water to a boil. Add the cauliflower, and cook for about 10 to 12 minutes or until tender. Drain. Set aside."],[null,"In a large skillet, melt the butter over medium-high heat. Add the onions and garlic, and sauté for 6 to 7 minutes until soft, making sure the onions and garlic do not turn brown. Combine the flour and milk, and whisk until very smooth. Add to the onions and garlic, bring to a simmer, and cook for 2 minutes. Season with salt and pepper. Whisk in the cheese, and fold in the cauliflower. Garnish with parsley."]],"h":[]},"5207174":{"s":[[null,"Heat the sunflower oil in a large frying pan over a medium heat and cook the onion and green and orange peppers for a few minutes until soft."],[null,"Add the chicken to the pan and brown off."],[null,"Add the basil and tarragon and stir."],[null,"Cover and simmer for about 10 minutes"],[null,"Add the Renastep to the pan and simmer for approx. 5-10 minutes."],[null,"Whilst the creamy chicken is cooking, prepare the rice. For microwave or boiled rice follow the manufacturer’s instructions."],[null,"When the rice is ready, remove the creamy chicken from the heat and serve with a portion of rice."]],"h":[[null,"Add ½ tsp turmeric to the water whilst cooking the rice. This will make the rice a lovely yellow colour."],["Renastep note","Renastep is a Food for Special Medical Purposes and must be used under medical supervision."],["Renastep note","Renastep is a ready to use feed for the dietary management of kidney disease from 3 years of age onwards. Renastep contains milk and fish. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information."],["Renastep note","This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease."]]},"6593132":{"s":[[null,"Juice the lemon into a small bowl with the shallot. Let sit for about 10 minutes."],[null,"Combine the chicken and broccoli in a medium bowl."],[null,"Add the pesto, mayo, salt, and pepper to the bowl with the shallot and lemon juice. Whisk to combine and pour into the bowl with the chicken and broccoli."],[null,"Serve the chicken salad over mixed greens and cherry tomatoes."]],"h":[]},"2519":{"s":[[null,"Chop the poblano and bell peppers and onion. Chop the cilantro. Cut cream cheese into cubes and set out to soften."],[null,"Place chicken breasts, broth, cumin, garlic powder and black pepper in large saucepan. Bring to a boil and cook for 10 to 12 minutes, until chicken is no longer pink. Remove chicken and cut into bite size pieces; keep warm."],[null,"Add bay leaf, peppers, onion and cream cheese to stock and simmer until vegetables are tender."],[null,"Add chicken back to saucepan and simmer 10 to 15 minutes."],[null,"Ladle into bowls and sprinkle each serving with cilantro and 1 tablespoon cheddar cheese."]],"h":[[null,"Some fresh chicken breast meat is “plumped” or “injected” with a saltwater solution which may also contain phosphorus or potassium. Look for fresh chicken breasts that do not include “15% solution” on the package."]]},"7519383":{"s":[[null,"Add the oil to a pan and gently cook the onions for 5 minutes, stirring regularly."],[null,"Add the chicken and stir for 2-3 minutes."],[null,"Add the mushrooms and garlic and cook for a further 2-3 minutes."],[null,"Add the stock, mix well, bring to the boil, turn down the heat, cover with the lid and simmer gently for 15 minutes."],[null,"In a jug, mix he cornflour and white pepper together and stir in the milk."],[null,"Gradually stir the milk and cornflour mixture into the chicken and mushrooms, stirring constantly, then bring to almost boiling point."],[null,"Stir in the yogurt, remove from the heat and blend the mixture until smooth. Serve with a sprinkle of chives and black pepper."]],"h":[[null,"You could use a stick blender or a blender."],[null,"Try adding herbs such as fresh tarragon, parsley or basil. Spice it up with 1 tsp ground cumin."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Can be frozen in small pots for individual portions. Defrost in a microwave or over a very low heat until piping hot."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6538174":{"s":[[null,"In a medium bowl, combine the chicken, celery, green onions, apple, and walnuts"],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the mayonnaise, yogurt, lemon juice and pepper. Pour over the chicken mixture and gently stir to coat."],[null,"Serve salad over your choice of lettuce leaves, bread or crackers."]],"h":[]},"4646754":{"s":[[null,"Cook the pasta according to package instructions."],[null,"In a large nonstick skillet, heat the oil over medium heat and cook the onion for 7 minutes. Add the frozen vegetables and cook for 5 minutes, stirring occasionally."],[null,"Add the cubed chicken, Italian seasoning, garlic powder, and black pepper. Cook for 5 more minutes, stirring occasionally."],[null,"Meanwhile, in a small saucepan, combine all sauce ingredients and bring to a boil. Set aside."],[null,"Add the cooked pasta to the skillet with the chicken and vegetables. Pour in the sauce and stir to combine. Reheat over medium heat and serve."]],"h":[[null,"* Choose cream without phosphate additives"],["Fruits and vegetables on a budget","Eating fruits and vegetables every day is a cornerstone of a healthy diet. They can lower blood pressure, provide fiber for digestive health, and reduce your risk for chronic disease. One barrier to eating them daily is availability. When fresh, they are plentiful for a season but can be scarce at other times of the year. Fresh options can also be quite expensive. One possible solution is to buy frozen fruits and vegetables. It is common to hear that “fresh is best,” but frozen fruits and vegetables are usually frozen at the peak of flavor and freshness and can still provide all the nutrients you need. Another bonus is less food waste. It can be difficult to use all the produce you buy before it spoils. With frozen options, you take only what you need from the freezer and leave the rest for another day, so there is no waste. Frozen fruit is easy to use—simply thaw and eat. Frozen vegetables can be trickier because they can become mushy when thawed. To avoid this, cook the frozen vegetables quickly at high heat, such as in a stir-fry, or add them to casseroles. Corn, green beans, carrots, and peas work well in these dishes. If choosing broccoli or cauliflower, toss when frozen with olive oil and herbs, then roast at 450 degrees."]]},"6270492":{"s":[[null,"Add the almond milk, cocoa powder, frozen banana, yogurt, vanilla extract, and sugar substitute to a blender and blend until smooth."],[null,"Pour into two glasses. Enjoy immediately."]],"h":[]},"6778174":{"s":[[null,"Preheat a small saucepan over medium-high heat. Once the pan is hot, add 1 Tbsp oil and flour. Cook, whisking constantly, until lightly golden, about 1 minute."],[null,"Slowly whisk in broth and coriander. Bring to a boil, then reduce heat and simmer until thickened, 2–3 minutes. Remove sauce from heat and stir in the yogurt. Set aside."],[null,"Preheat an oven-proof skillet over medium heat. Add remaining oil, chicken, cauliflower, mushrooms, and spices. Cook, stirring occasionally, until veggies have softened and chicken is cooked through, 6–7 minutes."],[null,"Preheat the oven to broil on high. Position the rack in the upper third of the oven."],[null,"When the chicken is done, add sauce to the skillet and stir to combine."],[null,"Top skillet with cheese and place in the oven. Broil until the cheese is melted and bubbly, 3–5 minutes. Serve garnished with cilantro."]],"h":[]},"2236":{"s":[[null,"Thinly slice cucumber."],[null,"Mix together sour cream, vinegar (or lemon juice), sugar (or sweetener) and pepper."],[null,"Combine mixture with cucumbers. Chill before serving."],[null,"Garnish with fresh chopped dill weed if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Replace vinegar with lemon juice if preferred."],[null,"For a variation add 2 tablespoons chopped onion or chives."],[null,"For a lighter version, substitute fat-free sour cream instead of regular sour cream."]]},"2802":{"s":[[null,"Set cream cheese out to soften."],[null,"Peel, seed and finely mince cucumber and set aside. Mince onion."],[null,"Mix cream cheese, onion and mayonnaise in a small bowl and blend until smooth."],[null,"Fold cucumber into mixture until evenly blended."]],"h":[[null,"Low-fat or fat-free cream cheese works great, too."],[null,"Creamy Cucumber Spread makes delightful finger sandwiches. Cut the crust off bread and cut sandwiches into triangles for fancy appetizers."],[null,"This recipe is good on low-salt saltine crackers."]]},"2625":{"s":[[null,"Cut apples, pears and peaches into bite-size pieces. Cut strawberries into quarters."],[null,"Place cut fruit in a large bowl. Set aside."],[null,"Place a metal bowl and metal beaters of a hand mixer in the freezer for 15 to 30 minutes. Pour heavy cream into the bowl and mix with chilled beaters until stiff peaks form."],[null,"In a medium bowl, mix cream cheese, sugar, and sour cream until smooth. Gently fold in whipped cream until mixed well."],[null,"Just before serving, pour cream cheese mixture over fruit and gently stir."],[null,"Top with fresh berries and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute with any low potassium fruits of your choice. Make it colorful! (blueberries, raspberries, blackberries or a mixture)."],[null,"This is my family’s favorite fruit salad recipe and a great potluck item. It’s best to eat it the same day because it can get watery overnight."],[null,"Reduce ingredients in half to make a smaller amount."]]},"2827":{"s":[[null,"Set cream cheese out to soften."],[null,"Slice grapes in half vertically."],[null,"Mix softened cream cheese, sour cream, sugar and vanilla in a medium-sized bowl."],[null,"Fold in grapes."],[null,"Chill and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Add ProCel® or any unflavored whey protein powder for an extra protein boost."],[null,"Nutrient analysis includes sugar. If made with Splenda® granular sweetener or other non-caloric sweetener carbohydrate is 16 grams per serving."]]},"6931030":{"s":[[null,"Melt margarine in a small saucepan over medium-high heat."],[null,"Stir in all-purpose flour and cook for 1 minute, stirring constantly and blending until the mixture is smooth. Season with coarse ground black pepper."],[null,"Gradually blend in skim milk. Cook, stirring constantly, until mixture bubbles and thickens."]],"h":[]},"6537876":{"s":[[null,"Steam or boil the cauliflower florets until they are fork-tender, about 10–12 minutes."],[null,"Add the cook cauliflower to a large bowl."],[null,"In a small pan, melt the butter over medium heat. Add minced garlic and sauté for 1–2 minutes until fragrant."],[null,"Add the garlic butter, salt, and pepper to the cauliflower."],[null,"Add Greek yogurt to the cauliflower."],[null,"Use a hand blender to blend the cauliflower until smooth and creamy."]],"h":[]},"6560352":{"s":[[null,"In a large pot, bring water to a boil. Add the chopped parsnips and carrots to the boiling water."],[null,"Cook for 15–20 minutes or until the parsnips and carrots are fork-tender."],[null,"Drain the parsnips and carrots and return them to the pot."],[null,"Add the unsalted butter to the pot and mash the parsnips and carrots using a potato masher or fork."],[null,"Gradually add vegetable broth while continuing to mash until the desired creamy consistency is reached."],[null,"Season with salt and pepper. Mix well."]],"h":[]},"2456":{"s":[[null,"Chop the apple half."],[null,"Add water and cinnamon to a small saucepan and bring to a boil."],[null,"Add oats and bring to a gentle boil."],[null,"Add the almond milk and vanilla and stir to combine; simmer for 5 minutes."],[null,"Divide into 2 bowls. Top each serving with half of the chopped apple and 1/2 tablespoon pepitas."]],"h":[[null,"Look for almond milk without added phosphate additives. If added calcium is a concern try Califia® brand vanilla almond milk."],[null,"Add one teaspoon ground cinnamon instead of cinnamon sticks if preferred."],[null,"Other milk substitutes include soy, rice or coconut milk beverage."],[null,"Add sweetener of choice if you prefer sweet oatmeal."],[null,"Add a scoop of whey protein powder to boost the protein in this recipe."]]},"3171":{"s":[[null,"Finely chop garlic. Chop onion and zucchini. Shred carrots."],[null,"In a large skillet heat olive oil over medium heat. Sauté the garlic, onion, zucchini and carrots for 5 minutes."],[null,"Add curry powder, chicken broth and salt; bring to a boil."],[null,"Add orzo pasta and stir until mixture returns to a boil. Cover and reduce heat to a simmer. Cook, stirring occasionally for about 10 minutes until the liquid is absorbed and pasta is al dente."],[null,"Add cheese, chopped parsley and the frozen peas. Heat until the vegetables are hot, adding a bit more broth if necessary to maintain creaminess. Add pepper to taste."]],"h":[[null,"Great served with chicken instead of potatoes or rice."],[null,"Recipe can be easily halved."],[null,"Small amounts of cheese, like the Parmesan cheese in this recipe, can be included and still maintain phosphorus and sodium in an acceptable range."],[null,"Chicken stock or broth contributes to the protein content of this recipe. Be sure to keep it low-sodium without added potassium chloride."]]},"2503":{"s":[[null,"Slice carrots, chop green onion, and cube cream cheese ."],[null,"Prepare pasta as directed on package (without salt). During last 5 minutes of cooking time, add broccoli and carrots to water. Drain."],[null,"Mix cream cheese, Rice Dream®, Parmesan cheese, onion and seasonings in a large saucepan; cook on low heat until cream cheese is melted and mixture is well blended, stirring frequently."],[null,"Add pasta and vegetables together; toss lightly and serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"For a higher protein dish add chicken or shrimp."],[null,"Frozen broccoli and carrots can be substituted for the fresh vegetables."],[null,"Enriched rice milk contains added phosphorus and calcium. Look for the unenriched products."]]},"5151618":{"s":[[null,"Heat a pan of water until boiling and add in the pasta, boil for 5 minutes."],[null,"Add the broccoli to the pan and cook for a further 5 minutes, drain and set aside."],[null,"In a pan, add the pesto and allow to warm. Gradually add the Renastep, ensuring not to boil the mixture."],[null,"Once combined, add the pasta and broccoli back to the pan and stir until fully coated."],[null,"Serve, sprinkle over the parmesan and enjoy!"]],"h":[["Renastep note","Always check with your dietitian or doctor that this recipe is suitable for you."],["Renastep note","Renastep is a Food for Special Medical Purposes and must be used under medical supervision. Renastep is a ready to use feed for the dietary management of kidney disease from 3 years of age onwards. Renastep contains Milk (Milk proteins) and Fish (Tuna oil). This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutritics dietary analysis software. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information."]]},"6828102":{"s":[[null,"Heat a large skillet over medium heat. Add the oil, onion, and garlic. Cook, stirring often, until the onion softens, 4–5 minutes."],[null,"Add the pumpkin, broth, cream, and spices. Cook, stirring occasionally, until thickened and heated through, about 10 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, cook the pasta according to the package directions."],[null,"Toss the cooked pasta with the sauce and top with grated cheese and parsley."]],"h":[]},"4641030":{"s":[[null,"In a large saucepan, bring water to a boil and cook the pasta according to the directions on the package."],[null,"Shortly before the pasta is ready, add the peas to the boiling water and blanch them for 1 minute. Reserve ½ cup of the water before draining. Drain and set aside."],[null,"In another pan, over medium heat, mix the ricotta cheese, lemon juice and pasta water. Then add the lemon zest, ground pepper and salmon to the sauce."],[null,"Add the pasta and peas to the sauce and toss to combine."],[null,"Turn of the heat, sprinkle the fresh basil leaves on top of the pasta and serve immediately."]],"h":[]},"2934":{"s":[[null,"Cook pasta according to directions, omitting salt."],[null,"Add broccoli during last 3 minutes of cooking. Drain. Keep warm."],[null,"Over medium heat, cook and stir shrimp and garlic 2 to 3 minutes in a large nonstick skillet until shrimp are heated through."],[null,"Add cream cheese, garlic powder, lemon juice, ground peppercorns and half & half. Cook and stir 2 minutes."],[null,"Toss pasta and shrimp mixture. Sprinkle with bell pepper."]],"h":[[null,"Instead of shrimp, you can substitute 3/4 pound of fresh, boneless chicken strips, cooked 6 minutes."],[null,"Use low-fat cream cheese to reduce fat to 15 grams, however sodium increases to 466 mg per serving."],[null,"Look for half & half or nondairy creamer without phosphate additives."]]},"2296":{"s":[[null,"Chop onion and mince garlic."],[null,"Cut steak into 1/4″ thick slices. Place steak, garlic, onions and next 5 ingredients in a 3 quart electric slow cooker. Stir well."],[null,"Lightly spoon flour into a dry measuring cup. Place flour in a small bowl, and gradually add broth, stirring with a whisk until blended."],[null,"Add broth to slow cooker, and stir well."],[null,"Cover with lid; cook on high setting for 1 hour. Reduce to low heat setting, and cook for 7 to 8 hours or until steak is tender."],[null,"Prepare egg noodles according to package instructions, omitting salt."],[null,"Turn slow cooker off, and remove lid. Let beef mixture stand for 10 minutes."],[null,"Stir in sour cream. Serve beef sauce over noodles."]],"h":[[null,"An 8-ounce package of egg noodles makes approximately 2-1/2 cups cooked."],[null,"For a lower protein diet if you reduce beef and sauce portion to 1/2 cup over 1/2 cup noodles the protein is 20 grams per serving (2 meat choices)."]]},"3511":{"s":[[null,"Chop onion and mince garlic."],[null,"Cut steak into 1/4″ thick slices. Place steak, garlic, onions and next 5 ingredients in a 3 quart electric slow cooker. Stir well."],[null,"Lightly spoon flour into a dry measuring cup. Place flour in a small bowl, and gradually add broth, stirring with a whisk until blended."],[null,"Add broth and 1/2 cup water to slow cooker, and stir well."],[null,"Cover with lid; cook on high setting for 1 hour. Reduce to low heat setting, and cook for 7 to 8 hours or until steak is tender."],[null,"Cook egg noodles according to package instructions, omitting salt."],[null,"Turn slow cooker off, and remove lid. Let beef mixture stand for 10 minutes."],[null,"Stir in sour cream. Serve beef and sauce over noodles."]],"h":[[null,"This lower protein version of Creamy Crock-pot® Beef and Noodles has a smaller portion of beef compared to the original recipe on DaVita.com. The nutrients have been adjusted to reflect this change."],[null,"Refrigerate or freeze leftover portions for a quick meal later."]]},"6597568":{"s":[[null,"Sprinkle the chicken breasts with the pepper, garlic powder, and oregano. Heat olive oil in a large skillet over medium heat. Add the chicken and sear until golden brown and cooked through to an internal temperature of 165 degrees F, about 4–5 minutes per side. Transfer to a plate."],[null,"In the same skillet, add the garlic and cook until fragrant, about 30 seconds. Pour in the chicken broth, scraping up any browned bits. Stir in the milk, sun-dried tomatoes, and red pepper flakes. Simmer for 2–3 minutes."],[null,"Stir in the spinach and Parmesan cheese, cooking until spinach wilts, about 1–2 minutes."],[null,"Remove the pan from the heat once the sauce is finished simmering. In a small bowl, mix ¼ cup plain Greek yogurt with 1–2 Tbsp of the warm sauce to temper it. Slowly stir the tempered yogurt into the pan, mixing gently until fully incorporated."],[null,"Return the chicken to the pan. Spoon the sauce over the top. Add half of the basil and simmer for 1–2 minutes to heat through."],[null,"Serve with additional fresh basil on top."]],"h":[]},"3326":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F. Set margarine, cream cheese and whipped topping to soften."],[null,"Combine flour and margarine, and press into a 9 x 13-inch pan. (Do not grease or spray pan with nonstick spray.)"],[null,"Bake for 20 to 25 minutes until crust starts to brown. Cool for 10 minutes."],[null,"Combine cream cheese, sugar and half of the whipped topping in a bowl and blend until smooth. Spread over cooled crust."],[null,"In a small bowl combine pudding and vanilla extract. Spread pudding over cream cheese mixture."],[null,"Top with remaining whipped topping. Sprinkle coconut on top. Refrigerate for 30 minutes before serving. Cut into 15 servings. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Ready-to-eat pudding is lower in phosphorus and sodium compared to the cook and serve or instant pudding mix. Snack Pack Pudding® brand ready-to-eat vanilla pudding does not contain phosphate additives, however it is high in calcium, so avoid if you are on a low calcium diet."],[null,"Use four 3.25 ounce containers, (1 package) of ready-made pudding."],[null,"Try different flavors of pudding for a variety of tastes."],[null,"Substitute Splenda® or other low calorie sweetener for sugar to reduce carbohydrate to 19 grams per serving (one carbohydrate choice)."]]},"2670":{"s":[[null,"Mince garlic clove."],[null,"Combine all dressing ingredients in a small bowl and mix well."],[null,"Pour into a salad dressing flask. Chill until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Use lemon juice instead of lime juice if desired."],[null,"Dressing keeps for up to one week in the refrigerator."]]},"6255304":{"s":[[null,"Heat oil in a large skillet saucepot over medium heat. Sauté the onion and garlic for 1 minute, stirring often."],[null,"Add the tomato, oregano and crushed chili flakes. Continue to sauté for another minute. Add the beans and broth. Bring to a boil, lower to a simmer and cook uncovered for 35 minutes until smooth and creamy."],[null,"Add the basil and lemon juice, season to taste with salt."]],"h":[]},"2826":{"s":[[null,"In a blender combine the flour, eggs, sugar and almond milk. Blend until smooth and no lumps remain. Trim and thinly slice the strawberries."],[null,"Heat a 10-inch skillet over medium-low heat and spray with cooking spray. Pour 1/4 cup of batter in the skillet. Pick up the skillet and roll the batter around until it fills the bottom. The crepe will be very thin."],[null,"Cook for 1 to 2 minutes per side. Remove to a plate."],[null,"Spread 1 tablespoon of cookie butter down the middle of the crepe. Lay 1/4 cup of strawberries over the cookie butter and roll or fold the crepe over the berries. Top with 2 tablespoons of whipped cream."]],"h":[[null,"Cookie butter is much lower in phosphorus and potassium than nut butters."],[null,"Spray whipped cream works well with this recipe. If using frozen whipped cream, be sure to check labels for phosphorus additives."]]},"3367":{"s":[[null,"Slice the strawberries. In a medium bowl mix berries together."],[null,"Whisk together the flour, egg whites, milk and oil in a large bowl until smooth."],[null,"Lightly coat a skillet with cooking spray and place over medium heat. Pour 1/4 cup of the batter into the skillet. Tilt the pan in a circular motion to allow the batter to spread to the edges. Cook until the bottom is light brown, about 2 minutes."],[null,"Flip the crepe and cook another 1 to 2 minutes. Fold the crepe in half and remove with a spatula to a serving plate."],[null,"Place 1/2 cup mixed berries on top of each crepe, and then dust with confectioners’ sugar and serve."]],"h":[[null,"If desired, prepare crepes with fruit inside and powdered sugar on top."],[null,"Frozen mixed berries can be used if fresh are out of season."]]},"6147388":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the broiler. Lightly spray an 11x7x2-inch baking pan with cooking spray."],[null,"In a shallow dish, stir together the cornmeal, panko, cornstarch, and lemon pepper. Add the fish, turning to coat, shaking off any excess. Transfer to the baking pan. Lightly spray both sides of the fish with cooking spray."],[null,"Broil for 3-4 minutes on each side, or until the fish flakes easily when tested with a fork. Transfer to plates. Drizzle with the lemon juice. Sprinkle with the pecans and parsley."]],"h":[]},"7002703":{"s":[[null,"Boil the potatoes for 10–15 minutes until tender then refresh in cold water, cool a little and slice."],[null,"Toss together the potato slices and tomatoes and divide between 2 serving dishes. Pile the salad leaves on top and set aside."],[null,"Coat one side of each salmon fillet with pepper."],[null,"Heat a non-stick frying pan or a griddle until hot. Place the salmon pepper-side down and cook for 3–4 minutes, then turn and cook a further 3–4 minutes until thoroughly cooked through."],[null,"Lay the salmon on top of the salad leaves, mix together the orange rind and juice with the mustard, drizzle over the salad and serve."]],"h":[[null,"This salad works well with other fish, such as mackerel fillets, fresh tuna or with king prawns. You could also use thinly sliced chicken breast."],[null,"For a vegan alternative try strips of tofu instead of salmon. Simply fry in a non-stick pan until crisp then toss with a little sesame oil, soy sauce and Chinese five spice."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6396043":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350 degrees F. Coat two large baking sheets with cooking spray."],[null,"In a large bowl, whisk together the olive oil, soy sauce, brown sugar substitute, and garlic powder."],[null,"Toss the kale in dressing to coat and spread kale in one layer onto the two baking sheets. Do not overload the baking sheets with kale. Use a third baking sheet if needed."],[null,"Bake for 10–15 minutes or until the kale is crispy."]],"h":[]},"2003":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375°F."],[null,"To make chicken strips, cut chicken breast into horizontal strips 4-inches long by 1/2-inch thick."],[null,"In a medium bowl, mix stir-fry sauce, lime juice, honey and black pepper."],[null,"Add chicken strips and toss until coated."],[null,"Place panko bread crumbs in a plastic bag. Add chicken and shake until well coated."],[null,"Put chicken in a baking dish coated with nonstick spray."],[null,"Bake 20-25 minutes until browned."],[null,"Serve with rice, salad and fruit. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Cut chicken strips about the same size for even cooking. For convenience you can purchase chicken pre-cut into strips. They are usually labeled as chicken fingers, chicken strips or chicken tenders."],[null,"Panko bread crumbs are Japanese-style bread crumbs made from white bread without the crust and processed into flakes instead of crumbs. Panko absorbs less fat and is lower in sodium compared to standard bread crumbs."],[null,"Compare stir-fry sauce brands and choose the one lowest in sodium. You can substitute teriyaki sauce if stir-fry sauce is unavailable, but sodium content may be higher."],[null,"Adjust the portion if you need more or less protein."]]},"6793488":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F."],[null,"Prep a cookie sheet with nonstick cooking spray."],[null,"Defrost the broccoli and drain."],[null,"Combine the remaining ingredients in a gallon-sized Ziploc bag. Add the broccoli florets to the plastic bag and shake until coated."],[null,"Place the florets on the prepared baking sheet with space between them. Discard the leftover marinade."],[null,"Bake for 45 minutes to an hour. The broccoli will be soft inside but crisp at the edges."]],"h":[]},"7798713":{"s":[[null,"Mix together the yogurt and horseradish sauce and reserve."],[null,"In a bowl or on a platter, jumble together the lettuce, tomato and cucumber and set aside."],[null,"Mix together the cornflour and paprika and toss the beef in the mixture to fully coat the meat."],[null,"Spray the oil onto a pan and put over a medium heat. When hot, add the beef and cook for 2-3 minutes, stirring regularly. Sprinkle with sesame seeds, then remove from the pan and set aside."],[null,"Add the onions and red pepper to the pan, cook for 3 minutes then drizzle with lemon juice. Mix well and spoon over the salad, top with the beef and blobs of yogurt sauce. Serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"This works well with strips of chicken or turkey. Great with rice or rice noodles."],[null,"You could use ether Dijon or wholegrain mustard rather than horseradish."],[null,"For a vegetarian alternative, use a combination of tofu and oyster mushrooms in place of beef."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6777975":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F."],[null,"In a large bowl, toss the trimmed and halved Brussels sprouts with olive oil, garlic powder, smoked paprika, salt, and black pepper until well coated."],[null,"Spread the Brussels sprouts in a single layer on a baking sheet."],[null,"Roast in the preheated oven for 20 minutes or until the Brussels sprouts are golden brown and crispy, shaking the pan halfway through."],[null,"Remove the Brussels sprouts from the oven and transfer them to a serving dish."],[null,"Serve with lemon wedges on the side if desired."]],"h":[]},"6161752":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 400 degrees F and prepare a baking sheet with parchment paper or a light coating of cooking spray (optional)."],[null,"Drain and rinse two cans of chickpeas, then gently pat them dry with a paper towel to remove excess moisture. Dry chickpeas will become crispier during roasting."],[null,"In a mixing bowl, toss the dried chickpeas with one tablespoon of olive oil, ensuring they are evenly coated."],[null,"In another bowl, create a spicy seasoning mixture by combining 1/4 cup of hot sauce, 1/2 teaspoon of garlic powder, 1/2 teaspoon of onion powder, 1/2 teaspoon of paprika, 1/2 teaspoon of cayenne pepper (adjust to your spice preference), and pepper."],[null,"Add the seasoned hot sauce mixture to the chickpeas, ensuring they are well-coated with the flavorful seasoning."],[null,"Spread the seasoned chickpeas onto the prepared baking sheet, ensuring they are in a single layer."],[null,"Bake the chickpeas in the preheated oven for about 55 minutes, or until they become crispy. Be sure to stir or shake the pan every 10-15 minutes for even cooking."],[null,"Once the chickpeas are crispy and have absorbed the Buffalo flavor, remove them from the oven and allow them to cool slightly."]],"h":[]},"9307320":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400°F/204°C convection bake and line a large baking sheet (or 2 medium) with parchment paper."],[null,"Combine the vegetable broth, garlic powder, onion powder, smoked paprika, and poultry seasoning in a large measuring cup or bowl. Whisk well to combine."],[null,"Then place the soy curls in a large mixing bowl and pour the broth mixture on top and mix well. Let this rest for 10 minutes, stirring every few minutes until the liquid is absorbed."],[null,"While you wait for the curls to hydrate, add the hot sauce and almond butter to a small bowl and mix well until smooth. Then pour the buffalo sauce you just made over your hydrated curls and mix until evenly coated."],[null,"Arrange thm in a single layer on your baking sheet, without overlapping. Bake for 20 minutes, then flip them and bake another 12-15 minutes longer until desired crispiness is reached."],[null,"Serve with ranch dressing, carrots, and celery sticks."]],"h":[[null,"Don’t dump the buffalo curls from your mixing bowl onto your baking sheet. You don’t want any excess liquid to pool on your tray and make them less crispy."],[null,"Arrange them in a single layer with a little space in between each one so they bake up nice and crispy."],[null,"When flipping your soy pieces , again, make sure to arrange the pieces in a single layer with space in between each one for maximum crispiness."]]},"6301257":{"s":[[null,"In a large skillet, heat the canola oil over medium-high heat. Add the chicken tenders and cook for 5 minutes, until brown and crispy. Flip them over and cook for another 5 minutes. Remove them from the skillet to a plate and tent with foil to keep warm."],[null,"Add the onion, garlic, carrots, and peppers to the skillet. Cook, stirring constantly for 3 minutes. Add the broccoli, snow peas, and cauliflower. Cook while continuing to stir for another 2–3 minutes, until the broccoli turns a bright green. Stir in the egg substitute and cook to scramble it."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix the soy sauce, sesame oil, ginger, and chili flakes. Add the mix to the vegetables and stir to coat them."],[null,"Nestle the chicken back in the vegetables and cook over low heat until the chicken reaches an internal temperature of 165 degrees F."],[null,"Serve garnished with sliced scallions."]],"h":[]},"6214759":{"s":[[null,"Pat the chicken thighs dry with paper towels. Season both sides with coarse salt and pepper."],[null,"Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat."],[null,"Place the chicken thighs in the skillet. Cook until the internal temperature reaches 165 degrees F, about 6 minutes per side. Remove to a plate and cover with foil to keep the chicken warm."],[null,"In the same skillet, sauté the sliced shallots until softened."],[null,"Add minced garlic to the skillet and cook for an additional 1–2 minutes until fragrant."],[null,"Add the chicken broth and simmer until reduced by half."],[null,"Add the fresh baby spinach to the skillet and cook, stirring until wilted."],[null,"Serve the crispy chicken thighs on the bed of sautéed spinach and shallot mixture."]],"h":[]},"4708545":{"s":[[null,"Whisk together flour and baking soda. Set aside."],[null,"Prepare wet ingredients in a large bowl. Beat together margarine, sugar and honey until the mix becomes fluffy. Add the egg, vanilla extract, zest, blueberries, cornstarch and sesame seeds and beat well."],[null,"Add the flour mix to the wet ingredients and blend both with a spoon until a smooth dough forms."],[null,"Roll dough in wax paper and form a log of approx. 11/2 inches in diameter."],[null,"Freeze for 1 hour or more."],["To Bake","Preheat conventional oven to 350°F"],["To Bake","Cut 1/2 inch thick slices and garnish each slice with a sprinkle of sugared sesame seeds."],["To Bake","Place slices on a tray lined with parchment paper. Bake for 10–12 minutes."],["To Bake","Remove cookies from tray and cool on racks."]],"h":[[null,"The cookies are low in potassium and phosphorus and non-diabetic patients can have two!"],[null,"You may want to double the recipe because the cookie dough keeps well in the freezer."],[null,"If you want to make the recipe more simple, you can leave out the blueberries and the garnish."]]},"6405391":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 400 degrees F."],[null,"Season both sides of the chicken breasts with coarse salt and black pepper."],[null,"Add the flour to a shallow bowl."],[null,"In a separate bowl, whisk the eggs."],[null,"In a shallow dish, combine the Parmesan cheese, garlic powder, dried oregano, dried basil, and breadcrumbs."],[null,"Dredge each chicken breast in the flour, eggs, and lastly the Parmesan mixture, coating evenly. Set on a plate and repeat with the remaining chicken breasts."],[null,"Heat the olive oil in an oven-safe skillet over medium-high heat."],[null,"Add the chicken breasts to the skillet and sear for 2–3 minutes on one side until golden brown."],[null,"Transfer the skillet to the preheated oven and bake for about 15–18 minutes or until the internal temperature of the chicken reaches 165 degrees F."]],"h":[]},"6529405":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F. Toss diced potatoes with 1 1/2 tsp olive oil, 1/4 tsp salt, and 1/8 tsp black pepper. Spread in a single layer on a baking sheet and roast for 20–25 minutes, stirring once halfway through, until tender and lightly browned."],[null,"In the same skillet, heat the remaining 1 1/2 tsp olive oil over medium heat. Add ground beef, chopped mushrooms, and diced red bell pepper. Cook for 8–10 minutes, breaking apart the beef, until meat is fully cooked and vegetables are tender."],[null,"Stir in chili powder, cumin, smoked paprika, garlic powder, onion powder, remaining 1/4 tsp salt, and 1/4 tsp black pepper. Cook for 1–2 minutes until fragrant. Add the tomato sauce and water and bring to a simmer. Bring to a boil then reduce heat and simmer for 5-7 minutes, until the liquid is reduced. Remove from heat."],[null,"While the beef mixture is simmering, heat cauliflower rice in a large nonstick skillet over medium heat for 3–4 minutes, stirring occasionally until heated through. Add the cilantro and lime juice and mix together. Keep warm until ready to serve."],[null,"Divide the cauliflower rice evenly among four bowls. Top each bowl evenly with roasted potatoes, beef-mushroom-pepper mixture, two tomatoes, and 1/4 of a sliced avocado."]],"h":[]},"9046931":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 450°F / 232°C convection bake and line a large baking sheet with parchment paper. Set it aside."],[null,"Peel and dice your potatoes into half-inch cubes. You should get about 4 cups of cubed potatoes. Place them in a large mixing bowl with the oil (if using) and all the seasoning. Mix well."],[null,"Arrange the cubed potatoes in a single layer on your prepared tray and bake for 15 minutes. Then flip your potatoes and bake another 10-15 minutes, until crispy.NOTE: If you don't have a convection oven, you may need a few extra minutes to reach desired crispiness level."],[null,"While the potatoes are baking, prepare any other toppings you'd like. Then assemble your potato tacos with a generous amount of potatoes and your choice of toppings."]],"h":[[null,"Cut the potatoes as evenly sized as possible for even cooking. Don’t crowd the potatoes on your baking tray . Arrange them in a single layer with plenty of space so they crisp up nicely. For oil-free , omit the oil and use a flavourful broth in its place. At the halfway point, spray a little more broth or water on the potatoes if they look dry. Watch carefully to prevent burning. The potatoes will keep for 3-4 days in a sealed container in the fridge, however, they will lose some crispiness. Reheat in the oven or toaster oven to return to a crispy state . Store leftovers separately and assemble just before enjoying. Nutritional information is for ⅙ of the potatoes and black beans with one wrap and does not include optional toppings."]]},"6660424":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F."],[null,"Place the cabbage wedges on a baking sheet, ensuring they are not crowded."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the olive oil, garlic powder, onion powder, smoked paprika, salt, and black pepper."],[null,"Brush the olive oil mixture over each cabbage wedge, ensuring they are well-coated on both sides."],[null,"Roast in the preheated oven for 25 minutes or until the edges are crispy and golden brown, flipping the wedges halfway through."],[null,"Top with chopped fresh herb if desired."]],"h":[]},"9843388":{"s":[["Press the tofu","Cut your tofu into half-inch cubes. Then arrange some paper towels or a clean dish towel on a cutting board and place the tofu cubes in a single layer on top. Now add more paper towels on top of the cubes and place another cutting board, flat plate, or baking sheet on top. Finally, place something very heavy on top like a cast-iron skillet or a heavy book. Press like this for 15 minutes while you prepare the remaining ingredients."],["Bake the tofu","Preheat your oven to 425°F/218°C convection bake and line a baking tray with parchment paper."],["Bake the tofu","Combine the tamari, garlic powder, onion powder, and cornstarch in a medium bowl. Mix well. Then add the pressed tofu cubes and gently stir to evenly coat the cubes."],["Bake the tofu","Arrange the marinated cubes in a single layer with space in between each piece on your baking tray. Bake for 15 minutes, then flip and bake for another 5-10 minutes or until desired crispiness is reached."],["For the salad + dressing","While the tofu is baking, add all the salad ingredients to a large mixing bowl, or layer them on a large serving tray."],["For the salad + dressing","Then combine all the salad dressing ingredients in a small bowl and set it aside."],["For the salad + dressing","Once the tofu is baked, add it to your salad, and toss it with the dressing, or serve the dressing on the side to preserve the tofu's crispiness until ready to enjoy."]],"h":[]},"1992":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400º F."],[null,"Set cream cheese out to soften. Chop broccoli; slice onion and mushrooms."],[null,"Spray both sides of each flour tortilla with I Can’t Believe It’s Not Butter!® spray and place on an aluminum foil covered baking tray."],[null,"Bake both tortillas in the oven until golden brown, flipping tortillas as needed, for approximately 5 to 10 minutes."],[null,"Remove tortillas from the oven and spread each with 1 ounce of cream cheese."],[null,"Add 2 tablespoons marinara sauce to each tortilla and spread until covered."],[null,"Slice chicken and layer 1 ounce of chicken on each tortilla then top with vegetables."],[null,"Reheat in 400º F oven for approximately 5 minutes or until vegetables are cooked."],[null,"Remove from oven, cut into quarters and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Compare brands and buy the lowest sodium tortillas and marinara sauce. Low-sodium tomato sauce can be used instead of marinara sauce to further reduce sodium."],[null,"Lower fat cream cheese can be used but the sodium and phosphorus content will be higher."]]},"6588125":{"s":[[null,"Place all the ingredients in a crock pot."],[null,"Cook on high for 4 hours."],[null,"Serve the chicken over whole wheat rotini pasta if desired."]],"h":[]},"6913457":{"s":[[null,"Layer the slaw mix and carrots in the bottom of crockpot. Top with the chicken."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix the hoisin sauce, water, garlic, soy sauce, and cornstarch. Pour over the chicken mixture and set the crockpot to high for 4-6 hours."],[null,"Serve 1 1/2 cups of the mixture in each lettuce leaf."]],"h":[]},"6127541":{"s":[[null,"Stir together all the ingredients in a crock pot."],[null,"Set the crock pot on high setting for 4-6 hours."],[null,"Stir well before serving and lightly mash the parsnips and sweet potatoes to thicken the soup slightly."]],"h":[]},"2401":{"s":[[null,"Place roast in Crock-Pot®. Add 2 cups water and slow cook roast on low setting for approximately 10 hours until thoroughly cooked and easy to pull apart."],[null,"Drain meat reserving 1-cup liquid."],[null,"Place cooked meat in a 9” x 13” pan. Set aside."],[null,"In a bowl combine reserved liquid from meat, ketchup, brown sugar, vinegar, allspice and minced onion. Mix thoroughly."],[null,"Pour sauce mixture over cooked meat and cover. Marinate in refrigerator overnight."],[null,"Before serving, bake in a 350° F oven for 30 minutes, or until heated."]],"h":[[null,"Chuck, arm, or rump roast are great choices for this recipe."],[null,"Serve on a bun as a sandwich, or over rice or pasta."],[null,"Makes three 1-pound packets of BBQ beef—great to serve and then freeze the rest for 2 to 3 more meals."],[null,"Makes five generous servings per pound of roast cooked."],[null,"For the CKD non-dialysis diet, decrease portion to match your diet plan if you are on a lower-protein diet."]]},"3224":{"s":[[null,"Wash chicken and remove the inside giblets if they are included."],[null,"In a small bowl combine seasoning blend, pepper and garlic powder."],[null,"Sprinkle half the seasonings inside the chicken. Rub the remaining seasoning on the outside of the chicken."],[null,"Place the chicken breast-side-up in an oval crock-pot or neck-up in a round crock-pot."],[null,"Cover and cook on low setting for 8 hours."],[null,"Remove chicken from bones and discard the skin."]],"h":[[null,"No liquid or fat needs to be added. Chicken will make its own liquid/broth."],[null,"Use the chicken in recipes that call for cooked chicken, or to make chicken salad or chicken soup."],[null,"Make chicken broth with the bones and skin."],[null,"To make chicken soup, add egg noodles, low sodium broth, carrot shreds and celery to diced chicken and broth."],[null,"If you are on a lower protein diet, adjust the portion to match your meal plan."]]},"3353":{"s":[[null,"Cut chicken breast in bite sized cubes. Season with black pepper and place in Crock-Pot."],[null,"Dice carrots, celery and onion (except pearl onions). Mince garlic. Rinse and drain beans and hominy to reduce sodium."],[null,"Add chicken broth, beans, hominy, pearl onions, diced onion, carrots, celery, garlic and green chilies to Crock-Pot."],[null,"Season with garlic powder, cumin, chili powder, oregano and cayenne pepper."],[null,"Cover with lid and cook on low setting for 8 hours. Serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"Adjust the amount of chicken for a lower or higher protein diet."],[null,"This is a higher potassium dish. Check with your dietitian before trying it if you have high potassium levels or if you are on a low potassium diet."],[null,"Omit beans for a lower potassium and phosphorus version of this recipe (555 mg potassium, 202 mg phosphorus)."]]},"2960":{"s":[[null,"Heat oil in large skillet."],[null,"Add garlic and oregano."],[null,"Add chicken breasts and brown on all sides."],[null,"Place chicken in Crock-Pot and add chicken broth."],[null,"Cook on low heat setting for 6 to 8 hours."],[null,"Add lemon juice during last hour of cooking."]],"h":[[null,"Complete this meal with a serving or rice, green beans, French bread, margarine or butter and a baked apple for dessert."],[null,"Use leftover chicken breasts in a chicken salad or sandwich for lunch the next day."],[null,"Look for reduced-sodium broth containing 500 milligrams sodium or less per 1-cup serving Recommended brands include Health Valley® No Salt, Fat Free Chicken Broth (1-800-423-4846), Kitchen Basics® Natural Chicken Stock and Swanson® 50% Less Sodium Chicken Broth. Low-sodium broth is also a good choice. It contains less than 140 milligrams sodium per cup. Avoid low-sodium broth that contains potassium chloride—it’s very high in potassium"],[null,"If you are on a protein-restricted diet, ask your dietitian for advice on the correct portion size for your individual diet."]]},"6429648":{"s":[[null,"Zest and juice lime into a small bowl and set aside."],[null,"Preheat a skillet over medium-high heat. Once the skillet is hot, add oil and swirl to coat the bottom. Add the onion and cook, stirring often, until soft and golden, 2–3 minutes."],[null,"Crumble the tofu with your fingers into the skillet. Add lime mixture, bell pepper, chili powder, cumin, oregano, garlic powder, onion powder, salt, and pepper. Stir to combine."],[null,"Cook, stirring often, until tofu turns golden brown and veggies soften, 8–10 minutes."],[null,"Separate the lettuce into leaves. Pile leaves in stacks of two per wrap onto plates. Fill each wrap with tofu, salsa, and cilantro."]],"h":[]},"7287673":{"s":[[null,"Peel and coarsely grate a carrot and a green apple. Put in a serving bowl."],[null,"Chop 2 radishes very finely. Add to the bowl with fresh lemon juice and 2 tsp olive oil."],[null,"Season well with black pepper and toss with the carrot until thoroughly mixed."],[null,"Serve sprinkled with toasted sesame seeds (optional). Best served at room temperature."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"3283":{"s":[[null,"Dice celery, carrot and bell pepper."],[null,"Combine the mayonnaise and onion powder in a small bowl."],[null,"Spread 2 tablespoons of the mixture over each lavash flatbread or 1 tablespoon over each tortilla."],[null,"In a separate bowl combine the diced vegetables."],[null,"Place half of the vegetables and 4 ounces of the chicken on one side of each flatbread. If using tortilla, place 1/4th the vegetables and 2 ounces of the chicken on one side of each tortilla."],[null,"Roll up the flatbread and cut each one in half at a diagonal. Secure each half with a toothpick. If using tortilla instead of lavash, secure each tortilla with a toothpick and cut each tortilla roll in half before serving."]],"h":[[null,"If low-sodium, canned chicken is unavailable, substitute with fresh stewed or baked chicken pieces."],[null,"Compare products and select the lowest sodium lavash or tortilla."]]},"2806":{"s":[[null,"Shred lettuce, chop bell pepper and cilantro, slice radishes and peel and dice cucumbers."],[null,"Combine in a large salad bowl."],[null,"Mix in crumbled cornbread."],[null,"In a separate bowl, mix sour cream, mayonnaise and ranch dressing mix."],[null,"Pour sour cream mixture over salad and mix well."],[null,"Chill before serving."]],"h":[[null,"A great way to use leftover cornbread."],[null,"Try the DaVita.com recipe for Southern-style Cornbread — it’s low in sodium and phosphorus, but full or flavor."]]},"2435":{"s":[[null,"Thinly slice and quarter cucumbers. Chop bell pepper, onion, olives and parsley."],[null,"In a medium saucepan heat water to a boil and add couscous. Return to boiling. Remove pan from heat, cover and let stand for 5 minutes. Fluff with a fork and let cool while preparing vegetables."],[null,"Add cucumber, bell pepper, onion, olives and parsley to couscous."],[null,"Combine olive oil, wine or vinegar, feta cheese, basil, salt and pepper to make dressing. Mix with the couscous salad."],[null,"Refrigerate at least 1 hour. Serve chilled."]],"h":[[null,"Add cooked chicken breast chunks or slices for a delicious light lunch or supper."]]},"2454":{"s":[[null,"Cube chicken. Chop apple, bell pepper, onion and cilantro. Slice grapes in half."],[null,"Mix mayonnaise, sour cream, protein powder and lime juice together."],[null,"Add remaining ingredients, and stir until chicken is coated with dressing."],[null,"Cover, refrigerate at least 2 hours until flavors mix."],[null,"Serve on lettuce or on bread or crackers."]],"h":[[null,"You can stuff pita pockets with this chicken salad, or serve on low-sodium crackers or toast. For a snack size, serve in small cups, or on a single cracker."],[null,"Carol recommends EAS 100% Whey Protein Powder, a whey protein available in many stores such as Costco® and Walmart®. If unavailable in your area, ask your dietitian for recommendations on other protein powder brands."],[null,"Protein powder contributes 24 grams per 1/2 cup. Products vary amount of protein and serving size."]]},"6793068":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, mix together the tuna, mayonnaise, yogurt, onion, celery, red pepper, olives, and black pepper."],[null,"Divide the tuna mixture among the lettuce leaves (about 1/2 cup tuna salad per lettuce leaf). Fold to form a wrap."]],"h":[]},"2372":{"s":[[null,"Heat oven to 450° F."],[null,"Spray the surface of a flat, nonstick baking sheet with cooking spray."],[null,"Beat the egg white in a shallow bowl until very soft peaks form. Do not over-beat."],[null,"Place flour on a sheet of wax paper."],[null,"On a separate sheet of wax paper, combine the cornmeal, panko and Cajun seasoning."],[null,"Cut catfish fillet so you have a total of 4 pieces. Dip the fish in the flour and shake off excess."],[null,"Dip flour coated fish in the egg white, then roll in the cornmeal mixture."],[null,"Place fish on the baking pan, and repeat steps 6 to 9 with all the fish fillets."],[null,"Spray the tops of the fish fillets with cooking spray and bake for 10 to 12 minutes, until the bottom of the fillets are browned and the fish is sizzling. Remove pan from the oven and turn fish over."],[null,"Return fish to oven and bake about 5 minutes longer until fillets are browned and crisp."]],"h":[[null,"Try DaVita Salt-free Cajun Seasoning."],[null,"Other suggested salt-free Cajun seasonings include Andy Roo’s® The Stuff with No Salt or Benoit’s® spicy salt-free Cajun seasoning or Mrs. Dash® Extra Spicy seasoning blend."],[null,"Panko is a variety of Japanese bread crumbs used for coating fried foods. It can be found in most Asian markets and many supermarkets. If unavailable, substitute unseasoned dry bread crumbs."]]},"6142330":{"s":[[null,"Add 2 tablespoons almonds, 1 tablespoon pumpkin seeds, and 1 tablespoon sunflower seeds to a small bowl or container."],[null,"Toss gently to combine."],[null,"Enjoy immediately or store in an airtight container for later."]],"h":[]},"54941":{"s":[[null,"Shred potatoes. Bring a pot of water to a boil and add potatoes, cooking for 10-15 minutes. Drain and rinse and repeat boiling once more time. Drain."],[null,"Heat 3 Tbsp vegetable oil in a nonstick pan over medium heat. Spread the shredded potatoes out in thin layer throughout the pan. Cook until crispy and golden, about 3-4 minutes per side, flipping with a spatula. Remove from pan and set aside."],[null,"In the same pan over medium heat, add lean ground meat. Add paprika, garlic powder, ground black pepper, and red pepper flakes. Cook for about 7 minutes, frequently turning with spatula for even browning until meat has reached 160 °F. Drain and dispose of excess oil. Remove meat from pan and set aside."],[null,"Heat 1 Tbsp of vegetable oil in the same pan over low heat. Crack and whisk eggs in a small bowl. Add to pan and scramble until eggs are set but not hard (145°F)."],[null,"Warm the tortillas in a clean, large skillet over medium heat, about 30 seconds each side. Tortillas should be bendable."],[null,"Divide potatoes, ground meat, eggs, and cheese into the center of each tortilla. Fold the top of the tortilla towards the center and then fold each corner up to the center moving clockwise until you have a closed wrap (5 folds)."],[null,"Add 1 Tbsp vegetable oil to the large skillet over medium heat. Heat each wrap for about 30 seconds on each side until golden brown."]],"h":[[null,"Ground beef can be replaced with ground chicken or turkey. Egg whites or egg substitute (avoid those with phosphorus additives) can be used in place of whole eggs."],[null,"Wraps can be prepared ahead of time and reheated in the morning. They can last in the refrigerator for up to 3-4 days, or frozen and reheated."],[null,"Can substitute chicken, remove the wrap and remove cheddar cheese for a lower fat, diabetes-friendly meal."]]},"3126":{"s":[[null,"Cut tofu into cubes. Cut bell pepper into strips and chop garlic clove."],[null,"Mix reduced-sodium soy sauce, lime juice and sugar in a small bowl. Set aside."],[null,"In three separate bowls, put cornstarch, egg whites and bread crumbs. Dip tofu cubes first in cornstarch, then egg whites and coat with bread crumbs."],[null,"Heat canola oil in a skillet or wok and stir fry coated tofu until golden brown and crunchy. Remove tofu from pan and set aside."],[null,"In the same pan, add sesame oil. and heat. Stir fry broccoli and red bell pepper strips until crisp tender. Add chopped garlic, Mrs. Dash seasoning blend, black pepper and cayenne pepper and cook one minute."],[null,"Add tofu back to pan and toss with vegetables. Pour soy-lime juice mixture over top, sprinkle with sesame seeds and stir. Remove from heat and divide into 4 portions.Serve with 1/2 cup rice."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute olive oil for sesame oil if desired."],[null,"You can freeze cubed tofu to thaw and stir fry later. Freezing gives tofu a firmer, \"meatier\" texture."],[null,"Use your favorite salt-free seasoning. Tip: Penzey’s Spices®, Mrs. Dash® and Tone’s® make a variety of excellent salt-free seasonings. Avoid salt substitutes that contain potassium chloride due to high potassium content."]]},"6844655":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375 degrees."],[null,"Spray a muffin pan with cooking spray."],[null,"Add olive oil and a generous amount of cooking spray to a medium sauté pan. Sauté asparagus, onion and bell pepper for 7-9 minutes or until cooked through. Season with salt (optional) and pepper and set aside to cool slightly."],[null,"In a medium bowl, whisk together eggs, egg whites and milk."],[null,"Evenly distribute the sautéed vegetables among the 12 muffin cups. Cups should be 1/2 to 3/4 full. Gently pour egg mixture over the vegetables in each muffin cup, distributing evenly. Cups should full but not overflowing."],[null,"Take one half of a Lite Laughing Cow Cheese Wedge and gently press it down in the middle of each quiche. Repeat for remaining 11 quiches."],[null,"Bake for 20 minutes. Serve immediately."]],"h":[]},"6008024":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F. Lightly spray two 10-ounce ovenproof custard cups or individual pie pans with cooking spray. Place on a shallow baking sheet."],[null,"In a large non-stick skillet, heat the oil over medium heat, swirling to coat the bottom. Cook the mushrooms and green onions for 2 minutes, stirring occasionally."],[null,"Reduce the heat to medium low and cook for 3–4 minutes, or until all the liquid is absorbed. Stir in the garlic and cook for 30 seconds to 1 minute, or until fragrant."],[null,"Remove from heat. Add the spinach. Using a spoon, separate it into small pieces."],[null,"Put the cornstarch in a medium bowl. Slowly pour in the milk, whisking to dissolve it. Whisk in the remaining ingredients and stir in the mushroom mixture. Divide between the custard cups."],[null,"Bake for 30 minutes or until the centers are puffed and set (they don’t jiggle when gently shaken). Let stand for 5 minutes before serving."]],"h":[]},"2887":{"s":[[null,"Prepare rice in a rice cooker or stovetop according to package instructions. Add the bay leaf to rice and water before cooking."],[null,"Chop the onion and tomato. Peel, then cut the plantain diagonally into 12 slices. Mince the cilantro and garlic. Cut lime into quarters."],[null,"Combine the dried oregano, cumin and salt in a very small bowl. Set aside."],[null,"In a 2-quart saucepan over medium heat, sauté onion and garlic in 1/2 tablespoon olive oil. Once the garlic and onion are aromatic, add tomato and cook for 2 minutes."],[null,"Add the steamed rice and cilantro; stir. Sprinkle the dried seasonings over the top and stir until all ingredients are mixed together; set aside."],[null,"In a skillet, heat 1/2 tablespoon olive oil. Add plantains and cook for 2 minutes, flip and cook until golden brown."],[null,"In a separate skillet, heat 1 tablespoon olive oil over medium heat, crack the eggs and cook until desired doneness."],[null,"On a dinner plate, place 1/2 cup rice and 3 plantain pieces. Place 2 eggs on top of each portion."],[null,"Drizzle juice of each lime wedge over entire dish."]],"h":[[null,"The portion of plantains is small because plantains are high in potassium. If you are not on a low potassium diet plantains can be increased to 2 medium or 1 large."],[null,"When cooking rice, use a 1:2 ratio, 1 cup rice to 2 cups water."],[null,"If you do not have lemon or lime, try sprinkling 1/4 teaspoon vinegar onto each portion for added flavor."],[null,"Serve with Mojo Sauce if desired."]]},"6572091":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F."],[null,"In a bowl combine the garlic, cumin, lime juice, pepper and onion. Toss ingredients well so the seasoning spreads evenly. Add avocado oil and broccoli florets to bowl and toss again."],[null,"Place all ingredients on a parchment paper-lined baking sheet and roast for 25 minutes."],[null,"Remove from oven, and grab a fork so you can enjoy this delicious dish."]],"h":[]},"6379199":{"s":[[null,"In a mixing bowl, blend the cream cheese, finely chopped fresh dill, garlic powder, and lemon zest with a hand mixer until fluffy."],[null,"Spread each cucumber well with a generous dollop of the cream cheese mixture."],[null,"Garnish with more dill."]],"h":[]},"2157":{"s":[[null,"Mince the garlic and chop the tarragon. Thinly slice cucumber and radishes."],[null,"In a mixing bowl combine the garlic, vinegar, sour cream and black pepper."],[null,"Toss the cucumber and radishes with the sour cream mixture. Marinate in the refrigerator for 20 minutes before serving."],[null,"Divide salad into 4 bowls and top with chopped tarragon."]],"h":[[null,"If the sour cream mixture is added to the vegetables more than 20 minutes before serving, the cucumbers will wilt and the sauce may be runny."]]},"6523505":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, combine the thinly sliced cucumbers, radishes, red onion, chopped fresh dill, and fresh parsley."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the white wine vinegar, olive oil, salt, and pepper."],[null,"Pour the dressing over the cucumber, radish, and herb mixture."],[null,"Toss the salad gently to ensure even coating."],[null,"Allow the salad to marinate in the refrigerator for at least 15 minutes to enhance the flavors."]],"h":[]},"6185754":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, combine the cucumbers, red onion, and fresh dill."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the apple cider vinegar, extra-virgin olive oil, Dijon mustard, and honey."],[null,"Pour the dressing over the salad."],[null,"Toss the salad gently to ensure even coating."],[null,"Allow the salad to sit for 10 minutes to let the flavors meld. Before serving, toss the salad once more."]],"h":[]},"1910":{"s":[[null,"Peel and dice cucumber. Chop dill weed and onion."],[null,"Place diced cucumber in a bowl and toss with lemon juice. Set aside."],[null,"Combine sour cream, dill weed, onion, honey and horseradish in a bowl."],[null,"Gently mix the cucumber into the sour cream mixture."],[null,"Refrigerate until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Serve with Honey Spice Rubbed Salmon."]]},"6379337":{"s":[[null,"Coarsely mash the avocado in a medium bowl. Add the tomato, cucumber, cilantro, lime juice, vinegar, jalapeño, and salt until well mixed. Serve with sliced radishes for dipping, if desired."]],"h":[]},"6995196":{"s":[[null,"Slice the cucumber and lemon into thin slices and add to a large pitcher."],[null,"Gently crush the basil and mint leaves with your hand and add them to the pitcher. Top with 10 cups water."],[null,"Refrigerate water overnight before serving to fully infuse the flavors."]],"h":[]},"3934":{"s":[[null,"Wash and dice the cucumber; chop the fresh mint. Place the cucumber and mint in a bowl."],[null,"Add the olive oil, pepper and garlic powder. Mix well."],[null,"Refrigerate to chill. If desired, add a splash of vinegar before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Add additional spices to suit your taste."]]},"3461":{"s":[[null,"Peel and slice cucumber."],[null,"In small bowl, mix together cream cheese, mayonnaise, and Italian dressing mix. Refrigerate for at least one hour."],[null,"Spread cream cheese blend onto bread. Top with cucumber slices and sprinkle with dill."],[null,"Cut sandwiches in half and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Caution: some mayonnaise brands contain phosphorus. Read the ingredients label and avoid added phosphates."],[null,"The cream cheese mixture keeps for about a week in the refrigerator."],[null,"For a party appetizer, make a double recipe and cut sandwiches into 4 pieces. Serve on a tray garnished with fresh dill."]]},"6777920":{"s":[],"h":[]},"2507":{"s":[[null,"Combine rice vinegar, sugar, olive oil and black pepper in a medium bowl. Stir with a whisk."],[null,"Cut the 1/2 cucumber in half vertically, remove seeds and slice. Slice carrots and green onion. Finely chop bell pepper."],[null,"Add carrots, onion, red bell pepper, cucumber and Mrs. Dash to vinegar mixture; toss to coat."],[null,"Cover and chill 30 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Select unseasoned rice vinegar or substitute cider vinegar if unavailable. Avoid seasoned rice vinegar, as it contains 240 milligrams of sodium for only one tablespoon."]]},"2721":{"s":[[null,"Thinly slice cucumber and lemon."],[null,"Finely chop basil and mint leaves."],[null,"Add all ingredients to a pitcher."],[null,"Refrigerate overnight before serving."]],"h":[[null,"If desired, serve lemon and cucumber slices."],[null,"If you are on limited fluids, adjust the portion size to meet your needs."],[null,"After flavors develop you can pour into ice cube trays to make flavored ice."]]},"1771":{"s":[[null,"Peel and thinly slice cucumbers and place in a medium-sized serving bowl."],[null,"Sprinkle with salt. Allow to sit for 15 minutes then rinse and press out excess moisture."],[null,"Thinly slice onion."],[null,"Add remaining ingredients to cucumbers and toss."],[null,"Chill in the refrigerator before serving."]],"h":[[null,"This is a wonderful addition to any meal, but especially beef dishes."],[null,"Instead of using 2 common cucumbers, 1 large “English hothouse” seedless cucumber can be substituted."],[null,"Omit onion if desired—the cucumbers are just as tasty without it."]]},"1947":{"s":[[null,"Peel the sweet potato and cut into 1/4-inch shoestring slices. Soak sweet potato at room temperature overnight, dumping water at least once and refilling at least once."],[null,"Preheat oven to 425° F."],[null,"Drain and dry off sweet potato pieces and place into a zip top bag. Add the olive oil salt, pepper and cumin and shake to coat."],[null,"Place potatoes on a baking sheet. Bake for 20 minutes or until desired crispness."]],"h":[[null,"Peeling and slicing sweet potatoes before soaking will increase the surface area of the sweet potato and increase leaching of potassium. Skip this step if you do not need a low potassium diet."]]},"2147":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 300° F. Set cream cheese out to soften."],[null,"Beat softened cream cheese, sugar and extract with an electric mixer on medium-high speed until well-blended. Add whole eggs and egg whites, one at a time."],[null,"Pour into a ready-made graham cracker pie crust."],[null,"Bake 55 minutes to 1 hour or until center is almost set."],[null,"Refrigerate 4 hours or overnight."],[null,"Cut into 8 wedges and top each piece with 2 tablespoons of no sugar added cherry pie filling."]],"h":[[null,"This high calorie dessert is for special occasions."],[null,"For persons with diabetes you can use Splenda® sweetener and low-fat cream cheese to reduce calories, carbohydrate and fat. (calories = 282, carbs = 25 g, fat = 15 g). Carbohydrate choices decrease to 1-1/2."]]},"2549":{"s":[[null,"Season both sides of chicken with salt. Mix remaining spices together and season all sides chicken with 1/2 of the seasoning mix. Set chicken aside in the refrigerator for a few hours."],[null,"Core and cube the apple; thinly slice carrot diagonally; chop onion and garlic."],[null,"Heat 2 tablespoons of olive oil in the skillet. Add apple, carrots, onion, garlic and remaining spice blend. Reduce heat to medium and sauté until soft, about 10 minutes. Remove from skillet."],[null,"In the same skillet, heat the remaining olive oil and add chicken. Turn heat to medium and brown chicken on both sides. Add water and cook uncovered, until water has reduced to at least half."],[null,"Add vegetables and cook on low about 10 minutes, until chicken is done."]],"h":[[null,"Serve over rice or cauliflower rice."],[null,"Make an extra batch of the seasoning mixture and store in a jar for the next time you make Curried Chicken Thighs."],[null,"Replace chicken with shrimp for variety."]]},"4483403":{"s":[[null,"In a medium saucepan, bring 1 cup of water to a boil and prepare couscous following instructions on package. Transfer cooked couscous to a plate to cool."],[null,"In a bowl, combine couscous, chickpeas, cranberries, onions and cilantro."],[null,"In a small bowl, prepare the dressing: whisk together curry powder, vinegar, canola oil and ginger until combined."],[null,"Drizzle the dressing over the couscous mixture and stir to combine. Add some lemon juice if desired. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"This salad makes a great lunch or side dish."],[null,"For more protein you can add leftover meat or poultry."],["How to find hidden potassium in food labels","If you aren’t familiar with reading nutrition labels, the amount of information can be overwhelming. On a kidney-friendly diet we have to watch salt, phosphorus, potassium and protein. While many of these nutrients are listed on the Nutrition Facts label, phosphorus and potassium are likely not at this time. Fortunately, manufacturers will soon be required to include potassium on all labels. Until this information becomes available, below is how you can find hidden sources of potassium. First, identify the Serving Size of the food item. Often, foods that contain low to moderate potassium amounts can fit into your diet as long as you stick with the recommended portion size. Secondly, review the Nutrition Facts label and see if potassium and the amount in milligrams is listed. Typically, a low-potassium diet allows 2,000 milligrams per day. Lastly, review the Ingredients listed on the label. Additives that contain potassium could be listed as other names, such as potassium chloride, potassium iodide, potassium citrate, potassium alginate and acesulfame K."]]},"6130738":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F. Line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"In a large bowl, toss the sweet potato, red bell pepper, and cauliflower florets with 1/8 tsp salt, 1/4 tsp pepper, and 1 tsp of olive oil."],[null,"Spread the vegetables in a single layer on the prepared baking sheet. Roast in the preheated oven for 20–25 minutes until they are tender and slightly caramelized."],[null,"In a large pot or Dutch oven, heat remaining olive oil over medium heat. Add the diced onion and minced garlic, and sauté until they become fragrant and translucent."],[null,"Add the curry powder, turmeric, 1/4 tsp salt, and 1/4 tsp pepper to the pot. Stir well to coat the onions and garlic with the spices."],[null,"Pour in the diced tomatoes (with their juice), coconut milk, and vegetable broth. Stir to combine. Add the rinsed chickpeas to the pot and stir everything together. Bring the mixture to a boil."],[null,"Reduce the heat to low and let the stew simmer uncovered for about 15–20 minutes, allowing the flavors to meld together. Stir occasionally."],[null,"Remove the roasted vegetables from the oven and add them to the pot. Stir gently to incorporate them into the stew. Serve the curried chickpea stew in bowls, garnished with fresh cilantro."]],"h":[]},"2097":{"s":[[null,"Chop the onion and dice tomatoes; mince the garlic cloves and grate the ginger; chop cilantro."],[null,"In an 8-quart pot, heat the oil and sauté onion, garlic and ginger for 2 minutes."],[null,"Add diced tomatoes and sauté for 3 to 4 minutes."],[null,"Add the curry powder and mix well. Sauté it for one minute"],[null,"Add chickpeas with liquid to the pot, then simmer for 15 minutes."],[null,"Garnish with chopped cilantro and lemon wedges."]],"h":[[null,"Serve chickpea curry with tortilla, baked pita (Naan) or rice."],[null,"One 15-ounce can of chickpeas contains 9 ounces of chickpeas and 6 ounces liquid."]]},"4339883":{"s":[[null,"In a large sauce pan, heat the olive oil over medium heat. Sauté the onion, garlic, and ginger. Add spices and continue to sauté until the onion becomes translucent."],[null,"Once the onion has softened, add the lentils and vegetable stock. Bring the soup to a boil. Reduce the heat to a simmer and cook for approximately 30 minutes."],[null,"Add the peas and tofu to the soup. Simmer for 10 more minutes and serve."]],"h":[[null,"* Lentils are higher in potassium and should"],[null,"be enjoyed in moderation"],["Protein From Plant Sources","Early in the course of chronic kidney disease (CKD), people typically should reduce the amount of protein they eat, especially from foods higher in protein such as animal protein found in meat. Research has shown that substituting nuts, legumes and low-fat dairy for red or processed meats may help slow the progression of CKD. Legumes such as beans, peas and lentils are great sources of protein, complex carbohydrates and dietary fiber while being low in fat. They are considered healthful as they boost heart health, promote bowel regularity and may help stabilize blood sugar levels. Additionally, they make you feel full longer, helping you to resist the temptation to eat unhealthy snacks that are high in sodium and phosphorus. Legumes however are higher in potassium, therefore individuals who have CKD or are receiving dialysis should enjoy them in moderation. Ask your renal dietitian what amount of legumes in your diet is right for you."]]},"2736":{"s":[[null,"Mix spices together in a small jar or bowl."],[null,"Store in a small jar or container for up to 6 months."],[null,"Use as an everyday seasoning in cooking and on entrees, vegetables and salads."]],"h":[[null,"Create your own personal seasoning blend by adding other spices such as oregano, cumin or dried lemon or lime peel."]]},"6740165":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400°F. Line a rimmed baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"In a medium bowl, mix the squash with 1 tablespoon olive oil, 1/4 teaspoon salt, and 1/8 teaspoon pepper. Toss to evenly coat. Spread squash onto the prepared baking sheet. Bake for about 15 minutes, stir, then bake for an additional 15 minutes, or until tender. Remove baking sheet from the oven and set aside."],[null,"While squash is in the oven, combine the quinoa, water, curry powder, cumin, ginger, and mustard powder in a medium saucepan over medium-high heat. Bring the mixture to a boil, then reduce the heat to low, cover, and simmer until the liquid is absorbed, about 12–15 minutes. Do not stir once covered."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine cooked quinoa, roasted squash, the remaining 1 tablespoon olive oil, chickpeas, red wine vinegar, lime zest, pumpkin seeds, and cilantro. Season with the remaining salt and pepper. Serve warm or at room temperature."]],"h":[]},"6406383":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375 degrees F. Place unpeeled beets and garlic on a large sheet of foil. Spray generously with cooking spray and fold foil to make an air tight packet. Place in oven and bake for 45 minutes or until beets are fork tender. Set aside to cool, then peel the beets."],[null,"Place all ingredients in a food processor and blend until smooth."],[null,"Serve room temperature or chilled."]],"h":[]},"7280237":{"s":[[null,"Wash the spinach and add to a pan with a lid, cook for 2-3 minutes stirring a couple of times (there is no need to add oil or extra water, there will be enough water clinging to the spinach after washing). Put into a sieve and reserve."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the oil to a pan, add the onion and cook for 2-3 minutes until softened."],[null,"Now add the garlic and stir for 2 minutes, then mix in the curry paste."],[null,"Add the spinach, mix well for 1-2 minutes, then stir in the crème fraîche and serve."]],"h":[[null,"For a vegan version, use a soya-based yogurt instead of crème fraîche."],[null,"You can also mix in a few boiled, chopped potatoes to create a quick sag aloo."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Defrost in the microwave then reheat until piping hot."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"4898788":{"s":[[null,"To cook rice noodles, bring a large pot of water to a boil. Add noodles and remove pot from heat. Let the noodles soak for 5 minutes or until they are soft."],[null,"Drizzle the canola oil on the fillets and sprinkle curry and garlic powder on top."],[null,"In a skillet over medium-high heat, heat the sesame oil and butter. Fry the tilapia for 2 to 3 minutes per side. Remove fish from skillet, transfer to a plate and cover with aluminum foil to keep warm."],[null,"In the same skillet over medium-high heat, sauté ginger, garlic, cabbage, snow peas, and onions for 2 to 3 minutes until tender crisp."],[null,"Add the cooked rice noodles, chicken broth, and vinegar. Cook for another 2 to 3 minutes."],[null,"Remove from heat. Add cilantro and mix to combine. Serve the noodles with the curried tilapia."]],"h":[["Kidney-Friendly Fish","Protein is a necessary part of your diet and important for you to eat even when you have chronic kidney disease. Protein can come from plants or animals. When choosing an animal source of protein, lean sources are recommended. Fish is an excellent source of lean protein that can be eaten as part of your kidney-friendly diet. Tilapia is a lower-potassium fish and, with the right combination of flavors, you can use it for a variety of dishes. Simply baking the tilapia with oil can be an easy, quick meal. Tilapia can also be grilled and used in tacos with the addition of onions, green peppers and a salt-free seasoning. If you prefer marinade, plan ahead for the extra time needed and always discard remaining marinade. Be sure to include ingredients that are lower in sodium and potassium to stay within your kidney diet goals."]]},"6555967":{"s":[[null,"In a large pot, heat the olive oil over medium heat. Add chopped onion and sauté until translucent, about 5 minutes."],[null,"Add the minced garlic and grated ginger to the pot. Sauté for an additional 2 minutes until fragrant."],[null,"Stir in the curry powder, ground cumin, ground coriander, turmeric, and cayenne pepper. Cook the spices with the onion mixture for 1–2 minutes."],[null,"Add the rinsed lentils, diced tomatoes, and coconut milk to the pot. Stir well to combine."],[null,"Bring the mixture to a boil, then reduce the heat to low. Cover the pot and let it simmer for 20–25 minutes, or until the lentils are tender."],[null,"Serve over the steamed cauliflower rice and garnish with chopped fresh parsley or cilantro, if desired."]],"h":[]},"2090":{"s":[[null,"Finely chop the onion and celery. Slice each grape in half."],[null,"Place onion, olive oil and curry powder in a small microwave-safe bowl and microwave for 2 minutes. Let cool for several minutes."],[null,"Drain tuna well and place in a mixing bowl. Pat with a paper towel to remove excess water."],[null,"Stir in the onion mixture, celery, mayonnaise, lemon juice and sugar. Mix until well blended."],[null,"Stir in the grape halves."],[null,"Refrigerate to chill before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Make a tuna sandwich or add to a lettuce salad."],[null,"Use low-fat mayonnaise to reduce fat to 13 grams per serving. Note sodium content will be higher."],[null,"If you need more protein try tuna salad and low-salt crackers for a snack."]]},"6882153":{"s":[[null,"Place the eggs in a single layer in a saucepan and cover with water. Bring the water to a boil, then reduce the heat to low, cover, and simmer for 10–12 minutes."],[null,"Transfer the boiled eggs to an ice water bath to cool."],[null,"Once the eggs are cool, peel them and cut them in half lengthwise. Remove the yolks and place them in a bowl."],[null,"In the bowl with the egg yolks, add mayonnaise, curry powder, Dijon mustard, apple cider vinegar, salt, and pepper. Mash and mix the ingredients together until smooth. Spoon or pipe the curry filling into the hollowed-out egg whites."],[null,"Chill in the refrigerator for at least 30 minutes before serving. Sprinkle lightly with paprika and top with fresh dill if desired."]],"h":[]},"3038":{"s":[[null,"Mince garlic and ginger. Finely chop carrots, celery, and onion. Slice mushrooms. Chop apple."],[null,"Combine flour, garlic, ginger, curry powder and vegetable oil in a non-stick, deep skillet (at least 4 quarts) over a medium heat."],[null,"Stir until curry becomes paste-like."],[null,"Slowly add broth, and stir until sauce is smooth."],[null,"Add vegetables, apple and white pepper."],[null,"Simmer, stirring constantly, for 15 minutes, or until well blended."],[null,"Bring sauce to a boil and add chicken."],[null,"Simmer curry for 1-1/2 hours over a low heat, stirring regularly and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Save time by using Trader Joe’s® Mirepoix mix, a pre-chopped, pre-washed container of carrots, celery and onion."],[null,"Substitute beef or seafood for chicken for variety. If using raw beef, brown it before adding to curry in step 6."],[null,"For CKD non-dialysis on a lower protein diet, decrease portion to 3/4 cup."],[null,"Serve over rice for a complete meal."]]},"3874":{"s":[[null,"Sauté onions in olive oil until soft."],[null,"Mix all of the spices together and stir in the tomato paste."],[null,"Stir spice mixture into the onions in the pan."],[null,"Mix in 1-1/4 cups water and simmer for a couple of minutes."],[null,"Stir in zucchini, peas and turkey."],[null,"Cover and simmer for about 25 minutes or until zucchini is tender."],[null,"Mix together the pineapple, rice, pineapple juice and remaining 1-1/4 cups water in a saucepan."],[null,"Bring to a boil, cover and reduce heat. Simmer for 20 to 25 minutes, until all of the water is absorbed and the rice is tender."],[null,"Serve curry dish over pineapple rice."]],"h":[[null,"This recipe is a great way to use leftover turkey."],[null,"Chicken can be substituted for turkey."]]},"4787100":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 450°F and position baking rack in the middle."],[null,"In a bowl, whisk together eggs, sugar, milk, and vanilla extract."],[null,"Pour into the pie crust and sprinkle with nutmeg (or cinnamon). Bake for 10 minutes at 450°F."],[null,"Reduce oven temperature to 350°F and bake another 25 minutes or until custard sets."],[null,"Let cool or serve warm. Drizzle with maple syrup and top with sliced strawberries."]],"h":[["Pie crust — use for a variety of recipes","Pie crust offers a versatile foundation that can be used to create many recipes. Inexpensive to make or buy, crust can be used for a quiche with eggs and lower-potassium vegetables, a chicken or beef pot pie, low-sodium empanadas, or a fruit pie. If you enjoy baking, homemade pie crusts can be prepared with simple, low-cost ingredients you likely already have on hand. Most recipes include flour, water, salt, and butter or shortening. Specific ingredient amounts, like salt, can be adjusted to create the desired taste and amount of sodium per serving. While homemade crust is best eaten shortly after preparing, it does not contain phosphate or potassium additives like store-bought pie crust. Store-bought pie crusts are a convenient alternative when short on time or for a budget-friendly one-pan meal. Purchased as a refrigerated or frozen item, they also have a longer shelf life. Preparation is minimal with easy-to-follow baking instructions. Compared to crust made from scratch, premade pie crusts may include more ingredients, some of which are higher in sodium, potassium, or phosphorus. Reading ingredient labels and avoiding crusts with “phos” or “potassium” additives can help you choose the best option."]]},"9360404":{"s":[[null,"In a large pot, melt the butter, if using and then add the onion and garlic. Sauté until softened, about 5 minutes."],[null,"Then add the broccoli and the broth and bring to a boil over high heat. Reduce heat to medium/low and cook with the lid on for about 5-7 minutes until the broccoli is fork tender."],[null,"Remove from the heat and add the avocado to the pot. Then use an immersion blender to puree the soup until smooth. Taste and add more salt and pepper, if needed. Then serve."]],"h":[[null,"For oil free , simply omit the butter and sub for some water or broth, instead. Although I would argue that this dish has a healthy amount of fat, if you’re on a strict, low fat diet , you may sub the avocado for a cup of cooked or canned white beans, instead. If you do not have an immersion blender , carefully transfer your soup to a regular blender. Do not overfill , work in batches and use extreme caution when blending hot liquids. Leftovers keep refrigerated 3-4 days or freeze air tight for up to 3 months."]]},"9890977":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, beat the margarine with a hand mixer for 1-2 minutes, until fluffy. Then add the sugar and vanilla and keep mixing until combined."],[null,"Add the flour half at a time and mix until combined. You will have a mixture that doesn't appear to hold together, but it will. Use your hands to shape the dough into a flattened ball at the bottom of your bowl. Cover with plastic wrap and refrigerate for 2-3 hours or freeze for 15-20 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, line a large baking tray with parchment paper and preheat your oven to 350 degrees F."],[null,"Place a sheet of parchment paper on your countertop and the cold dough on top. Flatten and stretch the dough using a greased rolling pin to approx 1/4\" thick. Then use cookie cutters to make your cookies. Carefully transfer the cookies to your baking sheet. Then re-roll the leftover dough, flatten again, and continue making cookies. Repeat until all the dough is consumed."],[null,"Bake for 15-18 minutes, or until the edges are slightly golden. Remove from the oven and transfer to a cooling rack. Let them cool completely before glazing."],["Optional Glaze","Combine the icing sugar with 2 tablespoons of water in a small bowl and mix well. If the glaze is too thick, add one more tablespoon and mix again. Then add a drop of food colouring, if using and mix to combine."],["Optional Glaze","Use a silicone brush to glaze the cookies and then sprinkle them with your candy. Make sure to add the sprinkles immediately after glazing while the glaze is wet so they stick. Set aside and let dry."]],"h":[[null,"Use cookie cutters with less detail for ease . Cutters with more grooves intricate patterns will be tougher to hold together when transferring to your baking sheet. Simple shapes like circles, hearts, or stars are less likely to break. Grease your rolling pin so it doesn’t stick to your dough. This will make smoother cookies, but don’t aim for perfection. The glaze and sprinkles will cover the tops of your cookies anyhow. If your rolling pin is still sticking to your dough , add a sheet of parchment paper on top and roll on top of the parchment. Use care when transferring your shortbread cookies to your baking sheet . The dough is soft, and the cookies can break if using too much force. I like to use a large fork or pie knife to scrape under the cookie first (to “unstick” them from the parchment), then slowly lift and transfer. But if any cookies break, don’t worry ! You can gently press the piece back together with greased fingers. If it’s not salvageable, just add it to your discard pile for re-rolling for the next round. The thickness of your dough will determine the cooking time. If you roll your dough thinner, the cookies will bake faster, but if you roll the dough thicker, they will need a little longer in the oven. Start checking on them around the 10-minute mark to ensure they don’t burn. Allow your shortbread cookies to cool completely before glazing . If the cookies are too hot, the glaze will drip and run and the candies will melt. Once glazed, sprinkle the candies immediately , before the glaze sets, or they will not stick. The nutritional information does not include the optional glaze. Cookies will keep refrigerated for up to 1 week or freeze in a freezer-safe, airtight container for up to 2 months. Separate layers of cookies with parchment paper before freezing."]]},"9576533":{"s":[[null,"Add all your ingredients to a high speed blender and process until smooth and creamy."],[null,"Refrigerate for one hour or longer before serving to chill and thicken."]],"h":[[null,"Use unsalted, raw cashews. Whole cashews or pieces work fine, but make sure they are not roasted and not salted. You don't want any roasted flavour in your non dairy sour cream. The richness and creaminess is best when using RAW cashews. Soak your cashews. If you DO NOT have a high speed blender like a Vitamix, Blendtec, or other powerful blender, soak your cashews first to avoid grittiness . I like using a quick soak method (as opposed to overnight). Boil some water in a kettle or on stove top and cover the cashews with the boiling hot water for 30 minutes. Then drain and use as directed. Chill in the refrigerator. This really tastes best when chilled. Plus it will thicken up in the fridge and truly resemble the texture of full fat sour cream once chilled. If you're in a hurry, stick it in the freezer for 15 minutes instead. (Just don't forget it in there.) Leftovers keep refrigerated for up to 1 week or freeze for up to 2 months."]]},"2142":{"s":[[null,"Put all dry ingredients in a pot, whisk together to combine and add water."],[null,"Over medium heat whisk frequently until sauce reaches desired thickness (similar to nacho sauce)."],[null,"Remove from heat and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Nutritional yeast is deactivated yeast. It has a strong nutty or cheesy flavor and is used as a cheese substitute in recipes such as Dairy-free Cheesy Sauce."],[null,"For a little heat add chili powder."],[null,"The turmeric is added for color. You can adjust the amount for the desired color."],[null,"Sauce will maintain same thickness unless additional heat or liquid is added. For a thicker, spreadable sauce reduce the water to 1/2 cup. If over thickened whisk in a small amount of water."]]},"6228432":{"s":[[null,"Add all of the ingredients to a food processor or blender and blend until completely smooth, stopping occasionally to scrap the sides of the food processor."],[null,"If you have a homemade ice cream maker, blend the mixture in the ice cream maker for 10 minutes, then pack into a container and freeze. If you do not have an ice cream maker, just pack and freeze."],[null,"To serve, bring the ice cream out of the freezer about 20 minutes before serving to slightly thaw so it’s easier to scoop."]],"h":[]},"3939":{"s":[[null,"Chop onion an chili pepper. Grate ginger."],[null,"In a saucepan, heat vegetable oil. Add mustard seeds and cumin. When they splutter, add chopped onion, green chilies and ginger. Fry till the onion gets a light brown color."],[null,"Add cooked lentils; add 3/4 cup water, salt and mustard powder. Cook for 10 minutes till the lentil cooks to desired consistency."],[null,"Add lemon juice and sprinkle with finely chopped cilantro."],[null,"Serve hot with rotis/rice."]],"h":[[null,"Roti is a flat Indian bread, also known as chapati."],[null,"Wet grinders are very popular tools in the South Indian kitchen and are used to make paste out of soaked grains and lentils."],[null,"Idli is a round, fluffy bread roughly eight centimetres in diameter. Idli is made from ground rice or rice flour mixed with ground urad dal, salt, methi (fenugreek seeds) and water. The mixture is allowed to ferment prior to being steamed in an idli steamer. They are traditional to Southern India and are most often eaten with sambar."],[null,"Most often eaten at breakfast or as a snack, idli are usually served in pairs with chutney, sambar, or other accompaniments."]]},"6169032":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350°F. Brush a 9- by 13-inch baking pan with 1/2 teaspoon of the oil. Line just the bottom of the pan with parchment paper."],[null,"In a medium mixing bowl, whisk together the flour, cocoa powder, baking powder, baking soda, and salt."],[null,"In a large bowl, whisk together the mashed bananas, eggs, the remaining 1/4 cup oil, the vanilla, and orange zest until well combined. Add the dry mixture and stir until just combined. Add the zucchini and stir until evenly combined."],[null,"Spread the batter evenly into the prepared pan. Bake until springy to the touch, about 35 to 38 minutes."],[null,"Cool completely in the pan on a rack. Cut into 15 squares and serve at room temperature. Store in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 1 week or in the freezer for up to 3 months."]],"h":[]},"6337816":{"s":[[null,"Place the dates, butter, water, almonds, vanilla, cardamom, and cinnamon in a food processor. Pulse to form a smooth paste. Shape the dough into date-size balls."],[null,"Spread the sesame seeds and flaxseed on a baking sheet. Roll the date balls in the seeds to coat. Arrange on a serving platter."]],"h":[]},"4060171":{"s":[[null,"In a bowl, with the help of an electric mixer, cream together the ricotta cheese, sugar, and vanilla extract. Cover and place in the refrigerator for a minimum of 30 minutes."],[null,"In another bowl, coarsely crush the raspberries with the help of a fork."],[null,"Serve the ricotta cheese spread and the crushed raspberries over English muffins, bagels, rice cakes, or toast."]],"h":[[null,"* You can also use frozen raspberries. Defrost and drain any liquid before using."],[null,"Note: The spread can be kept in the refrigerator for 3–4 days."],["Lower-potassium fruit choices for breakfast","Fruit should be included as part of a balanced, lower-potassium diet. Some fruit is higher in potassium and should be eaten in limited amounts. There are many fruits which can be included in a kidney diet, but portion size is important. Starting off your morning with a fruit source, offers a nutritious breakfast choice full of vitamins, minerals, and fiber. Baked goods, especially those lower in fat, can be an easy way to add a lower-potassium fruit to your breakfast. Blueberry muffins, mixed berry French toast, or a breakfast cookie with dried cranberries or apples are just a few examples that can be healthy morning options. If you can make ahead, these simple recipes can offer a quick option for when you are short on time. Different spreads made with fruit, replacing margarine or butter, can also make a nice topping filled with flavor for toast, a bagel, or a muffin. Another morning favorite is a fresh fruit cup. Choose the correct portion size and select from lower-potassium fruits including grapes, raspberries, blueberries, pineapple, apple, or blackberries for a breakfast loaded with beneficial nutrients."]]},"6033272":{"s":[[null,"Heat the olive oil in a large nonstick skillet over medium-high heat. Add the onion and cook, stirring frequently, until soft, for 3 minutes. Add the mushrooms and cook, stirring frequently, for 4 minutes. Add the tomatoes and cook until the tomatoes lose most of their moisture. Add the spinach and cook for about one more minute."],[null,"Whisk together the spicy seasoning, egg whites, eggs, and water. Reduce the heat to medium and add the eggs. Let the eggs cook, without stirring, until they begin to set around the edges. Then use a spatula to flip the egg mixture and cook until almost done. Remove from the heat and let the eggs settle to finish cooking from the residual heat. Sprinkle with the feta. Cut into four large pieces to serve."]],"h":[]},"2676":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400° F."],[null,"Spray 12-cup muffin pan with butter flavored Pam® cooking spray."],[null,"Layer 4 sheets of phyllo dough together, lightly spraying with cooking spray between each layer. Cut phyllo dough into 3-1/2″ squares and place in muffin pan to make dessert cups."],[null,"Place muffin pan in oven and bake 10-12 minutes or until phyllo cups are lightly browned. Cool to room temperature."],[null,"When ready to serve, fill each phyllo dessert cup with 1/3 cup fresh berries. Top with 1/4 cup Cool Whip dessert topping."]],"h":[[null,"If fresh berries are unavailable, use unsweetened frozen berries instead."],[null,"Sweeten fruit with sugar or sugar substitute, if more sweetness is desired."]]},"3437":{"s":[[null,"Hard boil the eggs. Drain and cool."],[null,"Peel the eggs, then cut lengthwise and remove yolk."],[null,"Dice pimento and mix with yolk, dry mustard, mayonnaise and black pepper."],[null,"Place mixture inside egg whites in equal parts."],[null,"Sprinkle eggs with paprika."]],"h":[[null,"Double or triple recipe to make extras for a later snack or meal."]]},"6925969":{"s":[[null,"Place the eggs in a small saucepan so that they won’t bounce or move around and crack. Cover with water. Bring to a boil. Immediately turn off and cover. Let sit for 15-18 minutes to continue cooking. Pour out the hot water. Shake the eggs in the pan to crack the shells. Add cold water and let sit. (This will make them easier to peel.)"],[null,"Peel the eggs and cut them in half vertically. Remove yolks, place them in a small bowl, and mash with a fork. Add mayo, mustard, salt and pepper. Fill egg whites with mixture. Garnish with sliced grape tomatoes, sliced olives, sliced radishes, sliced scallions, or a drop of caviar or truffle paste. (Garnishes are optional.)"]],"h":[]},"3191":{"s":[[null,"Boil eggs for 15 to 20 minutes."],[null,"Let eggs cool for approximately 1 hour."],[null,"Slice eggs in half, lengthwise and scoop out the yolks."],[null,"Combine the yolks, mayonnaise, mustard and pepper; mix well."],[null,"Stuff yolk mixture into egg white halves and sprinkle with paprika."]],"h":[[null,"Use low-fat mayonnaise if you are watching your fat intake."]]},"3757":{"s":[[null,"Prepare green beans as directed on package."],[null,"Make a sauce by mixing together 2 teaspoons melted butter, mustard, pepper and Worcestershire sauce. Heat in microwave for 30 seconds."],[null,"Toss sauce with hot cooked green beans."],[null,"Mix remaining margarine (melted) with bread crumbs. Sprinkle on top of the beans and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute fresh green beans for frozen when in season."]]},"6007378":{"s":[[null,"To prepare the eggs: Add the eggs to a saucepan that is large enough so they are not crowded. Add water to cover about 1 inch over the eggs. Cover the pot and bring to a boil. Once the water comes to a boil, about 6 to 7 minutes, remove the pot from the heat and set it on an unused burner. Add the vinegar to the water (to help in peeling the eggs). Let the eggs stand in the hot water for 20 to 30 minutes."],[null,"Prepare a large bowl of ice water. Using a slotted spoon, transfer the eggs to the ice water bath, letting them cool for 15 to 20 minutes. Gently remove each egg from the ice water, and gently tap its shell until it is cracked all over (but do not peel). Add the cracked eggs back to the ice water bath (prepare a new ice bath if necessary) for 10 minutes. Remove the eggs from the ice water, and gently roll them between your palms. The shells should slip off easily. Discard the shells."],[null,"Halve each egg and remove the yolks. Discard one yolk and add the remaining five to a bowl. Set the egg whites on a platter, with the cut sides up."],[null,"Mash the yolks with the yogurt, mayonnaise, chives, mustard, horseradish, turmeric, salt, and pepper. Spoon or pipe the egg yolk mixture back into the egg whites. Sprinkle lightly with paprika."]],"h":[]},"4014095":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400°F."],[null,"Slice each chicken breast into 8 strips."],[null,"In a bowl, whisk together the egg, mustard and spices."],[null,"In a second bowl, combine the breadcrumbs with the olive oil."],[null,"Coat each chicken strip with the egg and mustard mixture."],[null,"Dip the chicken strips into the breadcrumbs before placing them on a non-stick baking tray."],[null,"Bake for 15–20 minutes, flipping the chicken fingers half way."],[null,"Combine the dip ingredients in a small bowl and serve with the warm chicken fingers."]],"h":[]},"4631911":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400°F."],[null,"Slice each chicken breast into 6 strips."],[null,"In a bowl, whisk together the egg, mustard and spices."],[null,"In a second bowl, combine the breadcrumbs with the olive oil."],[null,"Coat each chicken strip with the egg, mustard, garlic powder and pepper."],[null,"Dip the chicken strips into the breadcrumbs and then place on a non-stick baking tray."],[null,"Bake for 15–20 minutes, flipping the chicken fingers half way."],[null,"Combine the dip ingredients in a small bowl and serve with the warm chicken fingers."]],"h":[["Tips for adding crunch!","Consider using different breadings with fish or poultry entrees to give big crunch to your meal. In addition, baking instead of frying with these breadings lowers the fat content of your meal and is a healthier cooking option. Be careful with pre-packaged breaded items, particularly those with seasoned breadcrumbs, which can have significant amounts of preservatives, salt and potassium. Non-seasoned breadcrumbs are a better alternative. While most breadcrumb packages have a label to help you identify any additives, freshly breaded items from the meat counter at the grocery store may not have this information readily available. If you do select pre-made breaded entrees, request information on the seasonings used. Label reading is key to avoid eating unwanted preservatives. Breading items at home is an ideal solution to lower dietary potassium and sodium. Brush raw meat items lightly with olive oil or a beaten egg. Next, dip in cornflakes, panko or unseasoned breadcrumbs. Last add garlic, onion powder, pepper or dried herbs for the flavor you wish to create."]]},"6433313":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350 degrees. Coat a large baking dish with cooking spray. In a small bowl combine zucchini, tomatoes, olive oil, 1/8 Tsp. black pepper and toss to coat. Set aside."],[null,"In another small bowl mix together lemon juice and Dijon mustard. Set aside"],[null,"Season chicken breasts on both sides with 1/8 Tsp. pepper, garlic powder and oregano. Place chicken breasts in baking dish and brush top with mustard mixture. Sprinkle with Parmesan cheese."],[null,"Pour zucchini and tomatoes around chicken in baking dish. Bake for 30 minutes or until done."]],"h":[]},"3933":{"s":[[null,"Crush garlic. Whisk together first 5 ingredients and blend well."],[null,"Slowly whisk in olive oil until ingredients no longer separate."],[null,"Store remaining dressing in a tightly sealed jar and refrigerator until ready to serve. Keeps for 2 weeks."]],"h":[[null,"This dressing is great served over crisp Romaine lettuce with grilled steak or chicken for a tasty entrée salad."],[null,"If available, use aged balsamic vinegar for a perfect balance of acid and sweet flavors."]]},"6075788":{"s":[[null,"Place the eggs in a single layer in a saucepan and cover them with water. Bring the water to a boil, then reduce the heat and simmer for about 10 minutes."],[null,"Transfer the eggs to a bowl of ice water to cool. Peel the eggs when they are cool enough to handle."],[null,"Cut the peeled hard-boiled eggs in half lengthwise and carefully remove the yolks."],[null,"Place the yolks in a bowl and mash them with a fork. To the mashed yolks, add low-fat mayonnaise, Dijon mustard, chopped dill pickles, pickle juice, fresh dill, salt, and pepper. Mix everything together until well combined."],[null,"Spoon or pipe the yolk mixture back into the egg white halves. You can use a plastic bag with the corner snipped off to pipe the filling for a neater look."],[null,"Refrigerate the deviled eggs for at least 30 minutes before serving to allow the flavors to meld. Garnish with more fresh dill."]],"h":[]},"1864":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 250° F."],[null,"Pour cereal into a large baking or roasting pan."],[null,"Melt butter in sauce pan over a low-medium heat."],[null,"Add garlic powder, dill, Parmesan cheese and Worcestershire sauce to butter; stir to combine."],[null,"Melt butter. Pour 1/4 of the butter mixture over cereal in pan and mix to coat cereal. Bake for 15 minutes."],[null,"Remove cereal from oven and pour another 1/4 of butter mixture over cereal; mix well. Bake for another 15 minutes."],[null,"Repeat step 6 two more times until all butter mixture is added and cereal has cooked for a total of one hour until crisp."]],"h":[[null,"A large roasting pan with high sides works best."],[null,"The parmesan cheese is a higher phosphorus ingredient. 1/2 cup contributes 10 mg phosphorus per serving. Use less or omit if desired."],[null,"Purchase one box of Corn Chex and 2 boxes of Rice Chex. For a smaller batch, reduce cereal to one or two boxes depending on how much you want to make. Adjust other ingredients as well."]]},"9461625":{"s":[[null,"Add all the ingredients to your food processor, starting with 2 tablespoons of the pickle juice. Process until smooth and add more pickle juice if a thinner consistency is desired. Taste for salt and pepper and add to your taste."],[null,"Enjoy with veggies, crackers, pita, or as a spread in your favourite burgers and sandwiches."]],"h":[[null,"I highly recommend using pickle juice instead of water for the absolute best dill pickle flavour in your hummus. If you have a jar of pickles in the fridge, just scoop out a few tablespoons. TIP: When you finish your next jar of pickles, drain the contents (there are often bits of garlic and pickles left behind) and keep the pickle juice in a jar in your fridge, for next time! White beans work best for a creamier texture , but you may use chickpeas/garbanzo beans if you prefer. Make ahead and refrigerate for 1 hour before serving if you prefer it chilled. Leftovers keep refrigerated for up to 4 days or freeze air-tight for up to 3 months."]]},"2726":{"s":[[null,"Cover the eggs with water in medium saucepan. Once the water is boiling, cover and turn the heat off."],[null,"Drain the eggs after 10 minutes. Cover with ice and water until cooled."],[null,"Peel the eggs and chop or grate to desired consistency. Chop the onion and dill weed."],[null,"In a medium bowl mix all the ingredients together until well blended."],[null,"Chill at least one hour in the refrigerator before serving."],[null,"Cut pitas in half and place 1/3 cup egg salad and 1/2 lettuce leaf in each pita half."]],"h":[[null,"For additional protein, Greek yogurt may be used in place of sour cream."],[null,"If fresh dill weed is unavailable substitute with 1 teaspoon dried dill weed."],[null,"If small pitas are not available serve with 1/2 of a large (6-1/2-inch) pita."],[null,"Serve on a lettuce leaf or with 6 low sodium crackers instead of pita if desired."],[null,"Keep this salad cold in an insulated bag if transporting to eat away from home."]]},"3287":{"s":[[null,"Beat the eggs in a bowl; pour them into a nonstick skillet over medium heat."],[null,"Add black pepper and dill weed to eggs."],[null,"Cook until eggs are scrambled."],[null,"Top with crumbled goat cheese before serving."]],"h":[[null,"1/2 cup low cholesterol egg product can be substituted for 2 eggs for a lower fat and cholesterol dish. Cholesterol is reduced to 11 mg, fat 4 mg, and phosphorus 73 mg."],[null,"Cindy prefers The Pampered Chef® All-Purpose Dill Mix."],[null,"Substitute one tablespoon fresh dill for dried dill weed if desired."]]},"2359":{"s":[[null,"Chop onion, green pepper and garlic."],[null,"In a casserole or saucepan sauté rice in oil until rice is light brown, stirring frequently."],[null,"Add onion and green pepper and continue to sauté until vegetables are tender but not browned."],[null,"Add garlic and continue cooking for 1 minute."],[null,"Add broth, water and black pepper. Cover and bring to a boil; reduce heat and simmer about 20 minutes until rice is cooked."]],"h":[[null,"Freeze or refrigerate leftover portions for a quick dish later."]]},"7534283":{"s":[[null,"Add the oregano, cinnamon, cumin, chilli, pepper, garlic, lemon zest and juice to a bowl, along with the egg and crumbled bread. Mix well with a fork, breaking up the bread further."],[null,"Mix in the lamb and set aside for 10 minutes. Mix again and shape into a loaf about 6cm in diameter and 13.5cm in length."],[null,"Place on a baking sheet and cook in a preheated oven 190°C/gas 5 for 25–30 minutes."],[null,"Allow to cool for 5 minutes, then slice thinly, and stuff into pitta breads full of salad. Drizzle with lemon juice and serve."]],"h":[[null,"You can use any salad you like. To add a great crunch, use shredded raw cabbage, lettuce, red onion and cucumber, tossed in lemon juice."],[null,"For the sauces (pictured): Tahini sauce: Add 2 tsp tahini to a dish and gradually mix in 3 tbsp low-fat yogurt and pinch white pepper. Tomato relish: Mix a finely chopped large tomato with 1 tbsp ketchup and dash of chilli sauce."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"9922647":{"s":[[null,"Add everything to your food processor and process until mostly smooth and well combined."],[null,"Then add the chocolate chips (if using) and pulse a few times to mix them through."],[null,"Scoop the batter using a small cookie scoop and roll it into a ball. Place each chocolate bliss ball on a plate, baking sheet, or sheet of parchment paper. Repeat with the remaining batter. You will get around 30 energy balls."]],"h":[[null,"I like to add a few extra chocolate chips to each ball as I’m rolling them to make them more appealing for my little ones, but this is completely optional."]]},"9141620":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350℉/176℃ and line a large baking sheet or two smaller ones with parchment paper."],[null,"Add all the ingredients, except the chocolate chips to your food processor. Blend until smooth, scraping down the sides as needed. Then add the chocolate chips and pulse a few times to mix them in."],[null,"Use a small cookie scoop to scoop the chickpea cookie dough onto your baking tray. You will get around 28 cookies. Then, press a few chocolate chips into the tops of each cookie if you'd like. Shape your cookies and gently press them down as they won't spread much in the oven."],[null,"Bake the cookies for 12-14 minutes, or until they are slightly firm to the touch and the edges and bottoms are golden brown. Remove from the oven and let them cool for at least 10 minutes before handling."]],"h":[[null,"Weigh your flour for the best results . Scooping into a measuring cup can compact the flour and you may end up with more than needed."],[null,"Use active baking powder . If your baking powder has been open in the pantry for several months, it may lose effectiveness."],[null,"Use almond butter made with only almonds and no added fat or sugar . Always read the ingredients, or you may make your own almond butter ."],[null,"Let your cookies cool for 10 minutes once baked before handling. This cool-down period will help them firm up and set."],[null,"Keep the cookies at room temperature for 2-3 days, refrigerated for 3-4 days or frozen for up to 3 months."]]},"5780219":{"s":[[null,"Boil the potatoes in a large amount of water for 10 minutes, this helps the potato lose some of its potassium."],[null,"Pour away the water."],[null,"Now boil the potatoes in fresh water for a further 10 minutes and again pour away the water once the potatoes are cooked. This lowers the potassium content even further."],[null,"Always ensure to pour away the water. The water should not be used for sauces or cooking other ingredients."],[null,"Once drained, place the wedges onto a baking tray, drizzle with vegetable oil, mixed herbs and black pepper."],[null,"Bake for 20 – 25 minutes or until golden brown."],[null,"While baking mix together the mayonnaise and garlic until well combined, place into a small bowl and set aside."],[null,"Once cooked serve the wedges immediately with the aioli and enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Always check with your dietitian or doctor that this recipe is suitable for you."],["Renastep note","This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutritics dietary analysis software. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information."]]},"4071327":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together all the dressing ingredients until well combined. Cover and refrigerate until ready to use."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine the coleslaw mix, cucumber, radish, and mint or cilantro."],[null,"Add the dressing to the salad and fold or toss gently until the vegetables are evenly coated."],[null,"Serve immediately."]],"h":[["Cabbage is a nutritional powerhouse","The benefits of adding vegetables to your diet are endless. This is because vegetables provide essential nutrients such as fiber, phytochemicals, vitamins, and minerals that promote overall health. Eating a diet rich in vegetables can lower your risk of heart disease, stroke, and certain cancers, as well as lower your blood pressure, improve digestion, and help with weight management. Adding cabbage to your diet is an excellent way to increase your vegetable intake. Cabbage is budget friendly, can be used in many ways, and is considered a lower-potassium vegetable when potassium is a concern. Shredding it creates many possibilities, such as making a slaw or adding crunch to salads, tacos, grain bowls, or soup. Shredded cabbage and slaw mix are readily available in grocery stores, making this very easy to do. A tasty dressing is an excellent complement to slaws and salads. While bottled dressings are convenient, they can be expensive and may contain a lot of sodium and phosphate additives. The dressing for this recipe is delicious and made from common, kidney-friendly pantry items. Mix up a batch to keep in the fridge and use on many types of salads."]]},"6283486":{"s":[],"h":[]},"4311317":{"s":[[null,"ONE: Preheat oven to 375 F. TWO: Pat dry wings and pierce with fork on both sides.THREE: Rub wings liberally with spice rub, saving 1 tablespoon for later. FOUR: Place wings on sheet tray and bake wrapped with foil for 30 minutes. FIVE: Remove wings from oven and discard foil, flip over and cook for an additional 30 minutes. SIX: Sprinkle the rest of seasoning on wings and flip back over. SEVEN: Turn off oven and let wings sit in oven for 15 minutes then serve with a side of Weber’s barbecue sauce or other low-sodium barbecue sauce."]],"h":[]},"2420":{"s":[[null,"Mix first five ingredients well to form a stiff dough."],[null,"In a large skillet heat chicken broth to a boil."],[null,"Drop dough by spoonfuls (12) into boiling broth and cover."],[null,"Simmer 10 minutes without removing the lid. Serve with roasted chicken and gravy."]],"h":[[null,"Use a skillet or straight-sided sauté pan to give dumplings plenty of room. Broth should almost cover the dumplings."]]},"2479":{"s":[[null,"Dice chicken. Finely chop onion and slice celery."],[null,"Combine chicken, onion and celery in a bowl."],[null,"In a separate bowl, mix the mayonnaise, mustard, vinegar and sugar."],[null,"Add thoroughly mixed mayonnaise mixture to chicken and stir. Keep refrigerated until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Make sandwiches or serve as a salad on top of mixed greens."],[null,"Use reduced-fat mayonnaise for lower fat, but sodium will be higher: 11 g fat, 210 calories, 256 mg sodium."],[null,"Use vinegar of choice, but if seasoned check sodium content."]]},"4428872":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F."],[null,"In a medium bowl, with the help of an electric mixer, beat the egg whites and the cream of tartar until peaks form (approximately 3 minutes)."],[null,"In a second bowl, combine the egg yolks, flour, rice beverage, and vanilla extract."],[null,"Sprinkle the apple slices with cinnamon. Gently fold the egg white mixture and apple slices into the mixture from step 3. The egg whites should not melt into the mixture but stay somewhat fluffy."],[null,"Oil a pie or an iron pan (or use cooking spray) and pour the egg mixture into it."],[null,"Bake in the oven for about 20-30 minutes or until the soufflé has risen and the color is slightly golden."],[null,"Garnish with powdered sugar before serving."]],"h":[[null,"* Fortified rice beverage contains phosphate additives thus the unfortified product is recommended. You can find this product in the refrigerated section of your grocery store or the aisle that contains powdered or milk alternatives. Please be sure to refrigerate after opening."],[null,"Tip: To enhance this recipe, consider garnishing the soufflé with additional kidney-friendly fruits, such as berries! Please note, the nutrient analysis does not include the addition of any garnish."],["Easy one-pot protein recipes — soufflés","Preparing one-pot or one-pan meals can help save time and effort in the kitchen while providing a kidney-friendly meal. One example of this type of cooking is the soufflé. A soufflé is a baked dish with a flavorful base added to beaten egg whites. It can be either savory or sweet. When baked, air bubbles that have been whipped into the egg whites expand, making it pop up over the top of the baking dish. For the best results, pull eggs out of the refrigerator an hour before making the soufflé to allow them to come to room temperature. While most people shy away from making a soufflé, as it seems to be a complicated process, it is really quite easy and can be such a treat. Soufflés can be served as either the main entrée; alongside meats and vegetables; or with fruit for a healthy dessert. When following a low-potassium diet be sure to flavor or pair your soufflé with lower-potassium fruits and vegetables such as apples, berries, onions, leeks, asparagus, corn, mushrooms and peppers."]]},"7842764":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 170°C/gas 3."],[null,"In a large bowl, beat the oil, egg, sugar, stevia, lemon zest and lemon juice."],[null,"Add the flour, spice, currants and peel and mix well until the mixture forms a ball."],[null,"Turn out the dough onto a well-floured surface and roll to 3–4mm thick."],[null,"Using a 5cm fluted pastry cutter, cut out the biscuits and carefully place them onto a lightly oiled baking tray, re-rolling the trimmings as you go. You should get about 25 biscuits."],[null,"Bake for about 7–9 minutes until just starting to brown at the edges, sprinkle with the caster sugar and cool on a wire rack."]],"h":[[null,"You could use a shaped cookie cutter, such as a rabbit or duck to make fun Easter biscuits for children."],[null,"If you don’t have currants, raisins or sultanas work just as well, or use 50g mixed dried fruit instead of the currants and mixed peel."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Freeze in individually wrapped portions. Defrost for 2 hours, or in the microwave."]]},"5592322":{"s":[["To make the cupcakes","Preheat the oven to 180°C/160°C Fan/Gas Mark 4."],["To make the cupcakes","In a bowl, combine the flour and bicarbonate of soda."],["To make the cupcakes","In a separate bowl, beat the egg, gradually add the sugar, vanilla extract and oil, and stir until combined."],["To make the cupcakes","Add the flour mixture and half a bottle of Renastep (approx. 60ml) and whisk."],["To make the cupcakes","Add the remaining half a bottle of Renastep to the mixture and whisk."],["To make the cupcakes","Place the 4 x 8 cm diameter cupcake cases into a muffin tray and evenly pour the cake mixture into the cases."],["To make the cupcakes","Bake in the oven for 15-20 minutes, until golden brown."],["To make the cupcakes","Carefully transfer the cupcakes onto a wire rack to cool"],["For the frosting","Cream together the butter and icing sugar in a bowl."],["For the frosting","Add half a bottle of Renastep (approx. 60ml) and the vanilla extract to the butter icing mixture and mix well."],["For the frosting","Add the food colouring to get your desired colour."],["To decorate","Spread the icing onto the surface of the four cupcakes evenly, using the back of a spoon."],["To decorate","Dip the surface of the cupcakes into the coconut."],["To decorate","Add the ‘eyes’ to each cupcake using 2 chocolate chips."],["To decorate","Add a ‘beak’ to each cupcake using a small slice of cherry, cut into the shape of a triangle. Your Easter chicks are now ready."]],"h":[["Renastep note","Renastep is a Food for Special Medical Purposes and must be used under medical supervision."],["Renastep note","Renastep is a ready to use feed for the dietary management of kidney disease from 3 years of age onwards. Renastep contains milk and fish. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information."],["Renastep note","This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutrimen dietary analysis software."]]},"3984":{"s":[[null,"Rinse shrimp and pat dry with paper towel. Mince garlic clove."],[null,"In a bowl, combine olive oil, garlic, onion powder, black pepper, Cajun seasoning and shrimp."],[null,"Mix with rubber spatula until shrimp is coated."],[null,"Preheat air fryer to 400 degrees F and spray with nonstick cooking spray, if needed."],[null,"Arrange shrimp in a single layer in air fryer and cook for 3-4 minutes Flip shrimp and continue to cook for 2-3 more minutes or until cooked through."],[null,"Serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"Can be served with salad, with a pasta dish or with roasted vegetables."],[null,"Can be made with fresh shrimp, just make sure it is cooked all the way through. Cooked and uncooked shrimp shrinks when cooked."],[null,"Look for cooked shrimp with the lowest salt content."]]},"3428":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F. Peel, coire and slice apples."],[null,"In a bowl, mix oatmeal, brown sugar, flour and cinnamon."],[null,"Cut butter into oatmeal mixture with a pastry cutter until well blended."],[null,"Place sliced apples in 9” x 9” baking pan."],[null,"Sprinkle oatmeal mixture over apples."],[null,"Bake for 30 to 35 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Five medium apples yield approximately 5 cups after peeled, cored and sliced."],[null,"For a lower carbohydrate diet replace the brown sugar with 1/3 cup Splenda brown sugar blend. Carbohydrate is reduced to 30 grams per 1/2 cup serving."],[null,"Oatmeal is a higher phosphorus cereal and may be suggested as a food to limit. This recipe provides only 1/8-cup oatmeal per serving; phosphorus is comparable to many other acceptable dessert recipes."]]},"9909062":{"s":[[null,"Line a baking tray with parchment and preheat your oven to 400 degrees F."],[null,"Drain chickpeas well and add to your food processor along with all remaining ingredients. Process until crumbly but not pureed. Do not over process."],[null,"Form the mixture into small (1-1.5\") balls, squeezing out excess moisture with your hands, then flatten slightly and shape into patty/nugget shape. Place on prepared baking sheet."],[null,"Bake for 15 minutes and then flip your falafel and bake for another 5 minutes until lightly golden brown. Don't overcook your falafel or they will get too dry."],[null,"Serve in pitas with your favourite toppings and sauces or use as salad toppers."]],"h":[[null,"Make sure to thoroughly drain your chickpeas and pat them and your parley or cilantro dry with a clean dish towel before transferring to your food processor. Squeeze out extra moisture over your kitchen sink when forming your falafel balls, before flattening into a disc shape. Don’t over process your ingredients in the food processor. You want a slightly chunky mixture for the best possible texture. (Refer to image above.) Do not sub for canned chickpeas, as they’ll be very mushy and alter the texture of your falafel. Serving size is for one fourth of the recipe or approx 5 falafel of the 20 falafel yield. Pita, wrap, or additional toppings are not included in the calculation. Leftovers keep refrigerated for up to 4 days. Store in a sealed container and reheat in the oven at 350 degrees for about 10 minutes."]]},"6153892":{"s":[[null,"Heat the olive or canola oil in a medium pot over medium heat. When the oil is shimmering, add the onion, garlic, and jalapeño and cook until the onion is translucent and the garlic is fragrant, 3 minutes."],[null,"Add the ground beef and cook until browned, 8 minutes, breaking up the pieces using the back of a wooden spoon while cooking."],[null,"Add the remaining ingredients to the pot and stir to combine. Raise the heat to high and bring the mixture to a boil."],[null,"Then lower the heat to medium low and simmer, covered, until the beef is cooked through and the flavors combine, 30 minutes. Stir occasionally during cooking time."],[null,"Remove the chili from the heat and allow to cool for 10 minutes before serving."]],"h":[]},"6768400":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the vegetable broth, rice vinegar, soy sauce, cornstarch, ginger, sriracha, and brown sugar blend."],[null,"Heat 2 Tbsp of the olive oil in a large skillet or wok. When the oil is shimmering, add the garlic and cook until fragrant (30 seconds)."],[null,"Add the shrimp and cook until opaque, about 4 minutes. Using a slotted spoon, remove the shrimp and place on a plate."],[null,"Heat the remaining 1 Tbsp of olive oil in the same skillet. Add the broccoli florets and cook until tender, about 4 minutes."],[null,"Add the cooked shrimp back into the skillet and toss to combine with the broccoli. Pour the broth mixture over the shrimp and broccoli and toss to coat. Continue cooking until the broth mixture thickens slightly, about 1 minute."]],"h":[]},"9853178":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F and line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Add the peanut butter, maple syrup, applesauce, and peppermint extract to a bowl and mix well. Then add all the dry ingredients: cocoa powder, flour and baking powder and mix until combined. The batter will be thick and sticky."],[null,"Divide the mixture into 8 portions and use damp hands to roll balls that are approx. 1.5” in diameter. Place them on your baking sheet, and re-wet your hands as needed to prevent the batter from sticking to your fingers. Use your finger tips to gently press each one down to give them a spreading head start."],[null,"Bake for 11 minutes, remove from the oven and let them rest for 10 minutes before touching them. Then gently press the candy cane pieces on top of each cookie, if using."]],"h":[[null,"Use natural peanut butter . The kind that is made using JUST peanuts, without added sugar, salt or oil. Or you may make your own homemade peanut butter . Use wet hands to handle your cookie dough . Once everything is mixed, divide the batter into 8 cookies and roll into balls using slightly wet hands. This will prevent the sticky batter from sticking to your fingers. Do not overbake your vegan brookies ! They will appear and feel underdone at the 11 minute mark, but remove from the oven anyway. Let your brownie peppermint cookies REST before handling . Remove the tray from the oven and DO NOT touch them for 10 minutes. This will help the cookies firm up and set. After the 10 minute rest, you may garnish with the crushed candy cane, if using. Cookies keep at room temperature for 2-3 days, refrigerated for up to 1 week or frozen for up to 2 months."]]},"2757":{"s":[[null,"In a nonstick skillet, heat olive oil and sauté zucchini and peppers until tender-crisp. Remove to a plate."],[null,"Cut chicken into strips."],[null,"Heat cooked pasta and chicken strips in microwave in separate dishes."],[null,"Toss pasta with Italian dressing. Top with chicken strips and sautéed vegetables."]],"h":[[null,"Do some pre-preparation to make this into a quick dinner. Cook a large pot of pasta, drain and refrigerate for use in this dish and other pasta dishes."],[null,"Broil or barbeque a pound of chicken breasts or thighs. Refrigerate and use for this recipe and other chicken dishes during the week."],[null,"If you require a lower protein diet adjust the portion of chicken in this dish."]]},"2081":{"s":[[null,"In a large pot or slow cooker combine 6 cups water, veggie scraps, chicken wings and spices. Simmer on stovetop or on slow cooker high setting for a few hours until chicken is thoroughly cooked."],[null,"Strain and return broth to the pot. Discard veggie scraps."],[null,"Remove meat from the chicken bones and return meat to the pot. Chicken will be hot! Wait a few minutes until it can be handled."],[null,"Add the mixed vegetables and rice to the broth. Simmer about 45 minutes until the rice is cooked."],[null,"Add additional spices to taste."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute 1/2 cup quinoa for the rice if desired, however quinoa is higher in potassium and phosphorus."],[null,"Freezes well. Divide into individual servings for a quick meal later."],[null,"Leftover chicken and vegetables work well with this recipe"]]},"2337":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Melt butter in a small saucepan; add lemon juice, pepper, garlic powder, celery salt, celery seed, mustard and paprika. Cook sauce for 1 minute stirring well. Remove pan from heat and stir in Parmesan cheese."],[null,"Place chicken breast halves in an oven-proof baking dish; pour sauce over chicken and turn to coat. Bake uncovered at 350° F for 25 to 30 minutes or until chicken is done."]],"h":[[null,"The raw chicken breasts should weight approximately 4 ounces each."],[null,"This higher protein recipe may be appropriate for a lower protein diet. Adjust the portion size to match your meal plan."]]},"3809":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven or toaster oven to 350° F."],[null,"Cut chicken into strips and cook in a skillet over medium-high heat."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix taco sauce with 2/3 cup water."],[null,"Add the red bell pepper and 1/3 cup of the taco sauce to the skillet and continue cooking until chicken is just done."],[null,"Spray the bottom of a shallow baking dish with nonstick cooking spray."],[null,"To make the enchiladas, place a large spoonful of the chicken and pepper mixture onto the tortilla and roll it up. Place each enchilada side by side in the baking dish to hold rolled shape. Pour the remaining taco sauce over the top."],[null,"Bake enchiladas for 5 to 7 minutes, until the edges of the tortillas are just starting to brown."],[null,"Top each enchilada with 1 tablespoon of sour cream. Serve and enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Taco seasoning mix from a package is much lower in potassium compared to canned or bottled taco seasoning. Old El Paso brand was used in this recipe."],[null,"Corn tortillas contain a moderate amount of phosphorus. Keep enchilada phosphorus content lower by using sour cream as a topping instead of cheese."],[null,"For a smaller family, divide this recipe by putting half the uncooked enchiladas into a separate baking dish. Cook the portion you plan to serve and store the other dish in the refrigerator for the next day. The following day, heat in the oven at 350° F for 20 to 25 minutes."]]},"6372891":{"s":[[null,"Assemble the sandwiches: Spread 1 Tbsp of mayonnaise on each of 4 slices of bread. Top each with the tarragon, cheese, and chicken, dividing the ingredients evenly among the four slices. Sprinkle each with the salt and pepper, then top each sandwich with the remaining slices of bread."],[null,"Coat a nonstick skillet (large enough to hold the paninis) with olive oil spray and heat over low heat. Add the paninis and press down with a lid or another clean pan. Cook for 2 minutes, flip, and press again. Cook for another 2 minutes. (You can also use a panini press and cook until the cheese is melted and the bread is golden.)"],[null,"Cut each panini in half and serve each half with salad."]],"h":[]},"5683991":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 180ºC/160ºC Fan/350ºF/Gas 4. Cover a baking tray with greaseproof paper, and place either the French bread, pitta or wraps on top."],[null,"Heat the olive oil in a large frying pan over a medium heat, then add the corn, red peppers, chicken and garlic. Fry for a further 2 minutes, until thoroughly cooked through. Remove from the heat and stir in the tomato puree."],[null,"Share out the chicken mixture evenly between bases then top with a blob of cream cheese and grated cheddar cheese."],[null,"Bake in the oven for 3-5 minutes or until the cheese melts and the base goes slightly crisp. Remove from the oven and sprinkle each pizza with the chopped basil."]],"h":[[null,"Serve with polenta fries, rice or pasta."]]},"6665803":{"s":[[null,"In a bowl, mix together the chicken, lite mayonnaise, Greek yogurt, minced onion, salt, black pepper and dried dill."],[null,"Top one piece of toast with ½ cup of chicken salad mix. Top with 1 Tablespoon toasted slivered almonds."],[null,"Repeat for remaining 3 pieces of toast, or store the chicken salad separate from the nuts in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 1 week and assemble the open faced sandwiches as needed."]],"h":[]},"2038":{"s":[[null,"Finely mince garlic."],[null,"In a large bowl, mix all ingredients very thoroughly. Place in airtight container and refrigerate 12 to 24 hours."],[null,"Divide into 1/4-cup portions or store whole recipe. Wrap in plastic wrap or butcher paper and freeze in thick plastic freezer bags for later use."],[null,"When ready to serve, cook 1/4-cup portion per person in a non-stick or oiled skillet on stove top. Chop meat into fine crumbles with a spatula. Use in DaVita.com recipe for Chorizo and Egg Tortilla if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Cook entire recipe at once, if desired, and freeze leftovers for later use."],[null,"Substitute ground turkey for beef if desired. You may need to add 1 to 2 tablespoons of oil."],[null,"This is a quick and delicious way to increase protein intake at breakfast. Add 1 or 2 eggs or egg whites."],[null,"Add Easy Chorizo to shrimp or chicken with rice for a spicy one dish meal."]]},"2593":{"s":[[null,"Prepare rice according to package directions, omitting salt."],[null,"Cut one lemon into 6 wedges to use as garnish. Cut the other 4 lemons in half."],[null,"Cut chicken into finger-like slices; season with Mrs. Dash® herb seasoning, salt and pepper."],[null,"In a medium bowl beat the egg and water until combined."],[null,"Dip chicken in eggs and then in flour. Make sure you cover both sides with flour."],[null,"Heat olive oil in a non-stick frying pan."],[null,"Sauté chicken in the pan until golden brown on both sides. If desired, sauté with lemon wedges for flavor and garnish. Be careful not to over cook chicken."],[null,"Squeeze the 6 lemon halves onto chicken throughout sautéing."],[null,"Right before removing chicken from pan, squeeze last drops of lemon juice onto chicken."],[null,"Take chicken out of pan. Blot excess oil from chicken with paper towels to keep it crispy."],[null,"Divide chicken into 6 servings and place each serving on top of 2/3 cup of white rice."],[null,"Garnish chicken and rice with lemon wedges and fresh parsley."]],"h":[[null,"If desired, omit salt and pepper and increase Mrs. Dash® herb seasoning to 2 teaspoons."],[null,"When removing chicken from frying pan, remove any lemon seeds that may have dropped onto the chicken pieces."],[null,"If desired, juice the lemon halves and sprinkle the juice over chicken while sautéing."],[null,"Use any type of plain white rice. If desired, add an extra tablespoon of parsley to rice after cooking."],[null,"Weight of chicken portion includes breading; yield is approximately 2 ounces chicken. Adjust portion to match your meal plan based on your protein needs."]]},"2029":{"s":[[null,"Combine ingredients in a jar or small dish and stir until mixed."],[null,"Chill until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Look for brand of mustard lowest in sodium."],[null,"Dressing keeps up to 2 weeks in the refrigerator."],[null,"Try this dressing as a meat marinade or topping."]]},"6143294":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F. Spray each cup of a muffin pan with one spray of non-stick cooking spray."],[null,"Add 1 heaping tablespoon of the thawed spinach to the bottom of each muffin cup in the muffin tin."],[null,"In a medium bowl, whisk together the eggs, egg whites, yogurt, salt and pepper. Evenly divide the egg mixture among the 12 muffin cups. Top each egg muffin with 1 teaspoon of parmesan cheese."],[null,"Place in the oven and bake for 20-25 minutes or until the eggs are slightly firm to touch. Remove from the oven and set aside to cool for 5 minutes."],[null,"Remove from the muffins from the pan and serve or store in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to one week, or freeze and store in a freezer bag for up to 3 months."],[null,"To reheat from the refrigerator, place the muffin uncovered on a plate in the microwave for 30 seconds. To reheat from frozen, place the muffin uncovered on a plate in the microwave for 1 minute."]],"h":[]},"2686":{"s":[[null,"Hard boil the eggs for 8 minutes; turn the heat off and leave eggs in water for 2 additional minutes."],[null,"Peel the eggs and chop or grate to desired consistency."],[null,"Finely chop celery and onion. Drain pickle relish then measure 2 tablespoons."],[null,"In a medium bowl mix all ingredients together until well blended."],[null,"Chill at least 1 hour in the refrigerator before serving."]],"h":[[null,"If eggs are purchased at least a week ahead of time they will be much easier to peel when boiled."],[null,"Compare brands and select the mustard, mayonnaise and pickle relish with the lowest sodium content."],[null,"Refrigerate overnight for optimal flavor."],[null,"Serve with low-sodium crackers or spread on sandwich bread."],[null,"Keep egg salad in an insulated bag if taking away from home to keep it cold and avoid food spoilage."]]},"6691491":{"s":[[null,"Place eggs in a saucepan and ensure they are covered in water. Place saucepan on heat and bring to a boil. Turn off the heat, cover, and let the eggs cook for 9-12 minutes. Place eggs in an ice bath and peel eggs."],[null,"Cut hard boiled eggs in half and remove three of the yolks from the 6 eggs (you should end up with 6 egg whites and 3 egg yolks total). Add to a medium bowl and lightly mash with a fork."],[null,"Add the remaining ingredients and stir to combine."],[null,"Store in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to one week."]],"h":[]},"4069776":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400°F."],[null,"Remove the pie dough from the aluminum pie pan and place on a baking sheet lined with parchment paper."],[null,"Spread apple slices over the pie dough, leaving a 1\" border. Top apple slices with raspberries."],[null,"Gently fold the border over the apple and raspberry mixture to enclose the fruit, pleating it to make a circle. Brush the pastry with the egg white."],[null,"Bake the crostata for 30–40 minutes or until the crust becomes golden and the fruit softens."],[null,"Drizzle the apple and raspberry mixture with honey and enjoy."]],"h":[]},"6112084":{"s":[[null,"Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Add garlic and shallots and cook, stirring occasionally, until fragrant, 1–2 minutes."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix together the soy sauce, vegetable broth, and sesame oil."],[null,"Add the bok choy and sauce to the skillet. Toss to coat. Cover and cook for 2–3 minutes, uncover and toss, then cover and continue to cook until bok choy is tender, 3–5 minutes more."],[null,"Sprinkle with crushed red pepper."]],"h":[]},"6222775":{"s":[[null,"Add potatoes to a large soup pot. Cover with cold water and bring to a boil. Cook for 15 minutes. Add cauliflower to pot, return to a boil, and cook for 5 more minutes."],[null,"Drain potatoes and cauliflower and return to pot."],[null,"Add remaining ingredients and mash mixture with a potato masher. Mix with an electric mixer on low-speed for about 1 minute."]],"h":[]},"9874640":{"s":[[null,"Drain cashews and add them to your blender with the water and your sweetener of choice, if using, and puree until smooth."],[null,"Using your Bigger & Better Nut Milk Bag, (or equivalent) strain the milk into a jug to remove any loose pieces and pulp so that you're left with smooth and creamy, perfect cashew milk."]],"h":[[null,"Store in your refrigerator in a covered container or lidded jug. Consume within 5 days."]]},"2984":{"s":[[null,"Put all ingredients in a jar. Cover and shake vigorously,then serve immediately."],[null,"If dressing is prepared ahead of time, shake well before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Drizzle on top of salad greens, or put in a small serving dish for dipping (to prevent overuse of dressing)."],[null,"Store leftover dressing in the refrigerator for up to one week."],[null,"Compare brands and select the lowest sodium mustard."]]},"2843":{"s":[[null,"Combine ingredients in a small bowl and stir to mix."],[null,"Refrigerate until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Horseradish sauce adds additional flavor to meat dishes like roast beef or lamb."],[null,"Spoon this sauce on top of cooked cauliflower, mixed vegetables or low potassium potato patties for added flavor."],[null,"Easy Horseradish Sauce keeps up to 1 week refrigerated."]]},"9064409":{"s":[[null,"Add everything to your food processor, starting with 2 tablespoons of water. Process until broken down and you have a sticky, well combined mixture. Add more water if needed."],[null,"Scoop the batter using a small cookie scoop and roll it into a ball. Place each lemon bliss ball on a plate, baking sheet, or sheet of parchment paper. Repeat with the remaining batter. You will get around 22 energy balls."],[null,"Optional: Roll each ball with more shredded coconut using a shallow dish."]],"h":[[null,"Don’t overprocess the mixture . These lemon balls taste best with a little texture."],[null,"Zest the lemon before juicing it ! And use fresh lemon juice for the best results."],[null,"Store the balls airtight in your fridge for up to 5 days, or freeze them for up to 3 months."]]},"2437":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl combine marinade ingredients."],[null,"Place chicken in zipper-type plastic bag."],[null,"Pour marinade over the chicken. Seal bag."],[null,"Marinate in the refrigerator for at least an hour; longer for more flavor."],[null,"Heat gas or charcoal grill to medium heat. Remove chicken from marinade, and place on grill. Discard the leftover marinade."],[null,"Cook chicken 6 to 8 minutes per side or until done (internal temperature 170° F using a meat thermometer)."]],"h":[[null,"Nutrient analysis is adjusted for estimated 25% absorption of the marinade. To view nutrient analysis of marinade only see Marinade for Grilled Chicken."],[null,"Adjust seasonings to your taste."]]},"6539733":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a large nonstick skillet over medium heat. Add the green beans and tomatoes, cover, and cook until the green beans are tender yet crisp and the tomatoes are fully softened, about 10 minutes. Toss with tongs a couple of times throughout the cooking."],[null,"Sprinkle the vegetables with the cinnamon and salt. Toss to combine, and then serve."]],"h":[]},"3176":{"s":[[null,"Cook pasta according to directions for al dente doneness, omitting salt. Drain while reserving 1/2 cup cooking liquid. Slice the roasted red peppers."],[null,"In a large pan over medium heat, combine remaining ingredients except peas and parmesan cheese."],[null,"Add drained pasta to sauce mixture and stir to combine. Add some of the reserved cooking liquid if sauce appears too thick."],[null,"Add green peas and parmesan cheese; stir."],[null,"Serve with a whole grain roll. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Look for the canned or bottled roasted red peppers with the lowest sodium content. Fresh roasted red peppers can be substituted."],[null,"Penne pasta works well but you can use whatever is in your pantry. Whole grain and whole wheat pasta also work well with this recipe."],[null,"If using gluten-free pasta, rinse pasta after draining to avoid a gummy result and do not reserve pasta cooking liquid. Instead add 1/2 cup low-sodium broth if sauce appears too thick."],[null,"Reduce serving size or the amount of pasta in the recipe if a lower carbohydrate meal is needed."],[null,"Add extra tuna if more protein is needed."]]},"6931035":{"s":[[null,"Rinse the lentils under cold water in a fine-mesh sieve or colander."],[null,"In a medium saucepan, combine the rinsed lentils, vegetable broth, and bay leaf (if using)."],[null,"Bring the mixture to a boil over high heat."],[null,"Reduce the heat to low, cover the saucepan with a lid, and let the lentils simmer for 20–25 minutes or until they are tender but still hold their shape."],[null,"Once cooked, remove the saucepan from the heat and discard the bay leaf."],[null,"Drain any excess liquid if necessary."]],"h":[]},"6968202":{"s":[[null,"In a large pot, combine chicken broth, onion, carrots, celery, garlic, bay leaf, salt, and black pepper."],[null,"Bring the broth to a simmer over medium heat."],[null,"Add the chicken breasts to the pot, ensuring they are submerged in the broth."],[null,"Reduce the heat to low, cover the pot, and simmer for 15–20 minutes or until the chicken reaches an internal temperature of 165°F."],[null,"Once cooked, remove the poached chicken breasts from the pot and let them rest for a few minutes."],[null,"Slice the chicken breasts or shred them using two forks."]],"h":[]},"3210":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 450° F."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine flour, phosphorus-free baking powder, sugar and salt."],[null,"With a pastry blender or fork, cut the buuter into flour mixture until it resembles course crumbs."],[null,"Add nondairy creamer, 1/4 cup at a time, and mix lightly until moistened."],[null,"Drop batter by the tablespoon onto a lightly greased baking sheet."],[null,"Bake in the preheated oven until golden on the edges, about 8 to12 minutes."],[null,"Serve warm."]],"h":[[null,"Cream of tartar is the potassium acid salt of tartaric acid. One teaspoon contains 495 mg potassium. When using cream of tartar with baking soda to replace phosphorus containing baking powder, be aware the potassium content of food will be higher but phosphorus is much lower."],[null,"Limit to one biscuit if you are on a low-potassium diet."]]},"1960":{"s":[[null,"In a blender, add pineapple sherbet, whey protein powder and water (ice cubes optional)."],[null,"Immediately blend for 30 to 45 seconds."]],"h":[[null,"Add one or two ice cubes to make smoothie thicker. Add an extra ice cube if you prefer a milkshake consistency or put in the freezer for five minutes before drinking."],[null,"Ask your dietitian about recommended protein powder brands."],[null,"If the protein powder sticks to the side of the blender, turn if off and use a spatula to loosen it from the sides. Replace lid and keep blending until smooth."]]},"2324":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 450º F."],[null,"Pour water into a measuring cup and heat in microwave to 120º to 130º F. Add canola oil and set aside."],[null,"Combine 2 cups flour, salt and yeast in a large bowl. Add warm water and oil and stir to form the dough. Stir in an additional 1/2-cup flour."],[null,"Place dough on a floured board. Sprinkle with flour and knead dough 5 to 6 minutes until smooth and elastic. Add more flour as needed to prevent sticking. Divide in half and form 2 balls."],[null,"Cover dough and let rise for 10 minutes. Punch dough down and form each ball into a flat 12″ pizza shape. Place on pizza pan or baking stone."],[null,"Spread sauce over each pizza, add pizza toppings and bake at 425º F for 12 to 16 minutes until bubbly and browned on top."]],"h":[[null,"To form a 12″ pizza, turn a medium-sized bowl upside down and dust with flour. Gently stretch dough evenly over outside of the bowl; turn and place on pizza pan."],[null,"Divide each dough ball in half to make four individual-sized pizzas."],[null,"If you have difficulty with dough rising, check the expiration date on your yeast. Be sure water is not too hot as this kills the yeast. Add a tablespoon of sugar in step #3 to ‘feed’ the yeast. Recipe calls for rapid-acting yeast. Regular baker’s yeast may take 30 minutes or longer for dough to rise."],[null,"Make bread sticks by dividing dough into 16 pieces and roll into cigar-shaped pieces. Bake at 425º F until golden brown."],[null,"Make rolls by dividing dough into 8 rolls. Let rise until doubled in size, brush with oil and bake at 425º F until golden brown."],[null,"Make cinnamon rolls by rolling each dough ball into a rectangular shape. Spread with softened butter, and sprinkle with 1 tablespoon cinnamon and 1/2-cup sugar or granulated sugar substitute. Roll up and cut roll into 2″ pieces. Place cinnamon rolls in a buttered dish and bake at 400º F until golden brown."]]},"3190":{"s":[[null,"Preheat over to 375º F. Brush pie crust with egg white and bake for 5 minutes. Reduce oven heat to 350º F."],[null,"Combine softened cream cheese, sugar and vanilla in a large bowl. Beat with mixer at high speed until smooth."],[null,"Beat in egg substitute. Add pumpkin puree and pumpkin pie spice and blend until smooth."],[null,"Pour pumpkin mixture into pie shell and bake 40 to 50 minutes until center is set. Cool pie, then refrigerate."],[null,"Cut into 8 slices. Serve each slice with 1 tablespoon desssert topping."]],"h":[[null,"Pumpkin is high in potassium but the amount of potassium for one piece of cheesecake is only 126 mg since only 1/2 cup pumpkin is used in the recipe."]]},"9557682":{"s":[[null,"Rinse the rice to remove some excess starch."],[null,"Preheat a large skillet or cast iron pan on your stovetop over medium/high heat. Then add the oil or the broth, followed by the rice. Toast the rice, stirring often, until golden brown, approx. 5-7 minutes."],[null,"Add the onion, garlic, cumin, and smoked paprika to the pan. and sauté until the veggies are translucent and fragrant, approx. 2-3 minutes."],[null,"Now add the broth and salsa, give it a stir, and cover the pan with a lid. Lower the heat to simmer the rice for approx. 15 minutes, or until the broth is absorbed. (Do NOT open the lid once simmering.)"],[null,"Once the rice is cooked, add the beans, mix well, and garnish with cilantro or parsley."]],"h":[]},"2865":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl combine all ingredients."],[null,"Cover and chill at least 4 hours to allow flavor to develop."],[null,"Stir before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Adjust herb seasoning blend to your taste. Flavors will intensify after 4 hours, especially if the seasoning blend contains garlic."],[null,"Serve dip with low-sodium crackers or lower potassium vegetables such as raw bell peppers, carrots, cauliflower, celery, and cucumbers."],[null,"Add a spoonful to cooked vegetables for a flavor boost."]]},"2020":{"s":[[null,"Chop onion and carrots. Mince garlic cloves. Peel potatoes and cut into 1/2 inch pieces. Boil in a large pot of water for 5 minutes. Drain water, replace with fresh water and boil again until potatoes are tender; drain."],[null,"While potatoes are cooking, melt 2 tablespoons butter in a large frying pan. Over medium heat, sauté onions and garlic until tender (10 minutes)."],[null,"Add ground beef and sauté until no longer pink."],[null,"Add pepper, Worcestershire sauce, tomato sauce and vegetables. Simmer on low heat, uncovered, for 10 minutes."],[null,"Preheat oven to 400° F."],[null,"Mash potatoes in a bowl with 2 tablespoons of butter. Mix in milk to give potatoes a creamy consistency. Add pepper to taste."],[null,"Spread beef evenly in a baking dish. Cover evenly with mash potatoes. Use a fork to make a design."],[null,"Bake for 30 minutes until bubbly. To brown top, broil for 2 minutes if desired."],[null,"Serve 1 tablespoons of gravy over each portion."]],"h":[[null,"Double boiling potatoes in a large pot of water reduces potassium content. Peel and cut potatoes into small pieces, cover with water and boil 5 minutes. Replace with fresh water and cook to desired consistency. Discard cooking water."],[null,"Freeze extra portions for a quick meal later."],[null,"The nutrient analysis includes gravy from a dry mix. Make low-sodium homemade gravy to reduce sodium content."]]},"1869":{"s":[[null,"Peel potatoes and cut into 1/2 inch pieces. Boil in a large pot of water for 5 minutes. Drain water, replace and boil again until potatoes are tender; drain."],[null,"Chop onion and carrots. Mince garlic."],[null,"While potatoes are cooking, melt 2 tablespoons butter in a large frying pan. Over medium heat, sauté onions and garlic until tender (10 minutes)."],[null,"Add ground beef and sauté until no longer pink."],[null,"Add pepper, Worcestershire sauce, tomato sauce and vegetables. Simmer on low heat, uncovered, for 10 minutes."],[null,"Preheat oven to 400° F."],[null,"Mash potatoes in a bowl with 2 tablespoons of butter. Mix in milk to give potatoes a creamy consistency. Add pepper to taste."],[null,"Spread beef evenly in baking dish. Cover evenly with mashed potatoes. Use a fork to make a design."],[null,"Bake for 30 minutes until bubbly. To brown top, broil for 2 minutes if desired."],[null,"Prepare gravy mix according to package instructions. Serve 2 tablespoons of gravy over each portion."]],"h":[[null,"Double boiling potatoes in a large pot of water reduces potassium content. Peel and cut potatoes into small pieces, cover with water and boil 5 minutes. Replace with fresh water and cook to desired consistency. Discard cooking water."],[null,"Freeze extra portions for a quick meal later."]]},"9882910":{"s":[[null,"Combine all the marinade ingredients except the cornstarch in a large bowl. Then add the dried soy curls to the bowl, stir them and let them soak for 10 minutes."],[null,"Preheat a cast iron skillet, or similar over medium-high heat. Then fish out the marinated soy curls from the bowl (DO NOT DRAIN - RESERVE THE SAUCE) and place them in the skillet to pan-fry them until browned, approx. 4-5 minutes, stirring often."],[null,"Next add the veggies, stirring occasionally for another 4-5 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, stir the cornstarch into the reserved bowl of marinade. Then pour the sauce into the pan of soy curls and veggies. Let that simmer and thicken for 2-3 minutes before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Use low-sodium broth and soy sauce for the marinade to prevent the dish from being too salty. Use half water and half broth if you don't have low-sodium broth. (You can always add salt later if needed.)"],[null,"Don’t overcook the veggies ! They taste best when tender and crisp for the best texture."],[null,"Store any leftovers in the fridge for 3-4 days or freeze them airtight for up to 3 months."]]},"6808134":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F."],[null,"Heat a large skillet over medium heat. Add oil, onion, and pepper. Cook, stirring occasionally, until onion softened, 4–5 minutes."],[null,"Transfer cooked onions to a large bowl. Add spinach, ricotta, and cottage cheese. Stir to combine."],[null,"Wrap the tortillas in a wet paper towel and microwave for 30 seconds."],[null,"Spray a baking dish with cooking spray. Divide spinach filling equally between tortillas. Roll and place seam side down in the baking dish."],[null,"Pour enchilada sauce over the tortillas. Top with shredded cheese. Bake for 10–15 minutes, until the cheese is melted and bubbly."],[null,"Divide enchiladas between plates and top with green onions."]],"h":[]},"1857":{"s":[[null,"Chop the strawberries, cucumber, red onion, and fresh mint. Remove seeds from the jalapeno pepper and finely chop."],[null,"Combine all ingredients in a medium bowl. Cover and chill."],[null,"Serve salsa with grilled chicken breast or mild white fish."]],"h":[[null,"Salsa may be prepared ahead and stored in refrigerator up to 2 days."],[null,"Strawberry salsa is great mixed in a green salad."],[null,"Use cilantro instead of mint if desired."]]},"2334":{"s":[[null,"Soften cream cheese."],[null,"Blend marshmallow and cream cheese together thoroughly, using an electric mixer."],[null,"Serve with kidney-friendly fruits for dipping."]],"h":[[null,"Serve with kidney-friendly fruits such as grapes, pineapple and strawberries. Arrange fruit on a platter of lettuce leaves with dip in a bowl in the middle. Fruit is not included in the nutrient analysis."],[null,"One jar of marshmallow creme is 7 ounces."]]},"4901925":{"s":[[null,"Boil a large pot of water. Add rotini noodles and cook 8-10 minutes until tender."],[null,"In a pan, add the oil and sauté pepper, onion and zucchini until soft."],[null,"Drain pasta and add to pan with vegetables."],[null,"Add black pepper and top with vegan Parmesan cheese as desired."]],"h":[]},"6294299":{"s":[[null,"Add cooking spray to a stock pot over high heat. Add the turkey and sauté until just cooked through, about 7-8 minutes."],[null,"Add the remaining ingredients and bring to a boil. Reduce to a simmer for 15 minutes."],[null,"Serve hot or cool to room temperature, then store in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to one week or package in freezer bags in one cup increments for up to 3 months."]],"h":[]},"3093":{"s":[[null,"Chop onion and bell pepper."],[null,"Place in a large skillet with turkey and cook over medium high heat until turkey is cooked through. Do not drain."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix together the Mrs. Dash® seasoning, sugar, Worcestershire sauce and tomato sauce."],[null,"Add seasonings to the turkey mixture. Reduce heat to simmer and cook for 10 minutes."],[null,"Divide into 6 portions and serve on hamburger buns."]],"h":[[null,"Lean ground beef may be substituted for ground turkey. Drain the fat after browning the beef in preparation step one."],[null,"To save time, use frozen chopped onions and bell pepper."],[null,"For a lower-protein diet, reduce turkey to 1 pound or portion can be adjusted according to your diet plan."]]},"4492073":{"s":[[null,"In a large skillet, brown turkey, red onion and bell pepper together until turkey is cooked. Do not drain."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix together the Mrs. Dash® seasoning, sugar, Worcestershire sauce and tomato sauce."],[null,"Add seasonings to the turkey mixture. Reduce heat to simmer and cook for 10 minutes."],[null,"Divide into 6 portions and serve on hamburger buns."]],"h":[[null,"Lean ground beef may be substituted for ground turkey. Drain the fat after browning the beef in preparation step 1."],[null,"To save time, use frozen chopped onions and bell pepper."],[null,"For a lower-protein diet, meat portion can be adjusted according to your diet plan."]]},"9605903":{"s":[[null,"Add all your ingredients to a powerful blender and process on high until smooth and creamy. Continue processing to ensure there are no loose cashew bits. Add 2-3 tablespoons of vegan parmesan cheese if desired."],[null,"Serve with your favourite noodles or veggies."]],"h":[[null,"Use hot water so you won’t need to heat up the sauce in a pan later."],[null,"If you don’t have a strong blender soak your cashews in boiling hot water for 20-30 minutes to soften them. Then drain them and blend with the remaining ingredients."],[null,"If you can’t have cashews or nuts use sunflower seeds with similar results."],[null,"Leftover sauce keeps refrigerated for 4-5 days , or freeze in freezer safe containers for up to 3 months."]]},"9021259":{"s":[[null,"Break up the soy curls with your hands into small pieces, and place them in a medium bowl. (They don't need to be evenly sized)."],[null,"In a small bowl, stir together the pancetta marinade: tamari, maple syrup, smoked paprika, and black pepper. Pour the mixture over the soy curls pieces, stir until evenly coated, and set aside for 5 minutes. Then stir again to get the soy curls to soak up all the marinade."],[null,"Bring a large pot of salted water to a boil and cook your pasta according to package directions for 'al dente' pasta."],[null,"Meanwhile, heat a deep skillet on your stovetop, and once hot, add the soy curls to the pan. Dry sauté for about 5 minutes, stirring often, until golden brown, without burning them. Then turn off the heat and set it aside. (If you want to garnish the plates with soy curls later, reserve and set aside a handful of pieces.)"],[null,"Add all the sauce ingredients to your blender and process until smooth. Set aside."],[null,"When the pasta is cooked, RESERVE 1 cup of the cooking water before draining. Add the cooked spaghetti to the skillet and pour the carbonara sauce on top. Then add the cup of pasta water to your empty blender, give it a good swirl, or reblend for a few seconds to collect the extra sauce and seasoning on the sides of your blender. Pour this into the skillet and mix well."],[null,"Serve with black pepper, fresh herbs, and/or vegan parmesan cheese."]],"h":[[null,"Salt your pasta water! Be sure to add enough salt to your pot of water for the best results. Here's a handy guide to help if needed. Do not overcook your pasta. Follow the directions for ‘al dente’ pasta. If your package does not include directions for ‘al dente’ then undercook your pasta by 1-3 minutes. ‘Al dente’ means that the pasta is still firm once cooked, and not mushy. This gives you optimal texture. Reserve some pasta water for ‘swooshing’ in your blender when draining your noodles . If you forget, use some broth, or fresh water with a little salt, so as not to dilute your carbonara sauce too much, but the starchy water works best. The black salt aka Kala Namak is a vital ingredient in this dish. It’s what gives the sauce its eggy flavour. Do not skip it if possible. If you don’t have, or cannot find black salt, you may use sea salt with slightly different results. Serve your vegan carbonara immediately , as the pasta will absorb the sauce as it cools. Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-4 days. Add some broth or non-dairy milk to your pan when reheating to loosen it and add back some moisture. Soy curl pancetta inspired by My Quiet Kitchen’s vegan bacon bits ."]]},"9596706":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F and line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Add all your dry ingredients to a large bowl and whisk well. Then add the molasses and apple sauce and mix until no floury bits remain. Add 1-2 tablespoons of plant milk ONLY if needed. (If you weighing your flour, you won't need it.)"],[null,"Divide the batter into 10 portions, rolling each one into balls that are approx 1-1.5\" in diameter. Then roll them in the sugar (if using), slightly flatten them and place on your baking sheet."],[null,"Bake for 10 minutes, then remove from the oven and let cool for at least 5 minutes until set. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Weigh your flour for the most accurate results . If you do not have a kitchen scale, use two scant cups of oat flour. If using a scale, and not making any substitutions, you shouldn’t need any of the plant milk. If scooping flour from a bag , (not recommended) you may end up with more flour than needed. So if your cookie batter looks too dry after mixing (it should be sticky and moist, refer to photos above) add 1-2 tablespoons of milk, as needed. Bake for 10 minutes, and not longer. These vegan ginger cookies may appear underdone at the 10 minute mark but they will firm up fairly quickly once out of the oven. Use a cookie scoop to get evenly sized ginger cookies. Or divide your batter into 10 equal portions before rolling your cookies. For a slightly crispier cookie , press them down before baking. For a fluffier, chewier ginger cookie , just roll them and bake. They won’t spread much, but they will cook through in the 10 minute bake time. Use damp hands to roll your cookies to prevent the dough from sticking to your hands. Leftovers keep covered or in a sealed container at room temperature for 2-3 days. However, if you live in a hot/humid climate, the rolled sugar may melt at room temperature. Or you may freeze air tight for up to 2 months."]]},"2302":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400° F. Grate the zucchini. Chop the onion, bell pepper and parsley. Bake pie shell as directed on package and allow to cool."],[null,"While pie shell bakes, add 3 teaspoons olive oil to a frying pan and heat on medium high. Add onions and cook until soft, stirring occasionally. Add the bell pepper and zucchini. Continue to"],[null,"cook about 10 minutes, stirring to prevent burning. Remove from burner and let mixture cool."],[null,"Beat eggs in a large bowl. Add almond milk, flour, salt and black pepper. Continue to beat until ingredients are incorporated."],[null,"Add cooked vegetables and parsley to the egg mixture and stir to combine."],[null,"Pour the mixture into the baked pie shell. Sprinkle the Parmesan cheese over the top."],[null,"Place the pie shell on a baking sheet to prevent spillage. Bake uncovered for 35 to 40 minutes, until quiche is firm in the center."],[null,"Allow to cool and garnish with parsley if desired. Cut into 6 pieces and serve."]],"h":[[null,"To reduce sodium omit the salt or make homemade pie crust with reduced amount of salt."],[null,"Leftovers can be stored in the refrigerator for 2 to 3 days or wrapped and frozen."],[null,"If using dried parsley decrease the amount to 1 teaspoon."]]},"6131183":{"s":[[null,"Cook the pasta according to the package directions, omitting any salt or fats and adding the edamame during the last 2 minutes of cooking time."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine the tomatoes, olives, basil, rosemary (optional), garlic, and pepper flakes. Toss to blend and set aside."],[null,"Drain the pasta and edamame in a colander, place on a serving platter or pasta bowl, squeeze lemon over all, top with feta, and mound the tomato mixture in the center."]],"h":[]},"6605959":{"s":[[null,"Drizzle lemon juice over edamame."]],"h":[]},"6954290":{"s":[[null,"In a shallow bowl, whisk together the eggs, egg whites, milk, Dijon mustard, garlic powder, and black pepper. Place the crumpets in the egg mixture, flipping to coat evenly. Let soak for 1-2 minutes until they absorb some liquid."],[null,"Heat ½ tbsp olive oil in a large nonstick skillet over medium heat. Add the soaked crumpets and cook for 2-3 minutes per side until golden brown and slightly crisp."],[null,"Sprinkle cheddar cheese over the tops of the crumpets. Cover the pan and cook for 1-2 minutes, until the cheese melts."],[null,"Remove from heat and garnish with chopped chives and avocado slices. Serve tomatoes on the side."]],"h":[]},"3577":{"s":[[null,"In a small skillet sprayed with nonstick cooking spray, pour egg product and cook over medium low heat. When egg appears almost cooked through, turn over with a spatula and cook additional 30 seconds."],[null,"Toast English muffin."],[null,"Place turkey sausage patty on a plate, cover with a paper towel and cook in the microwave for 1 minute or the time recommended on package."],[null,"Assemble cooked egg on English muffin (fold to fit muffin). Top with sausage patty, then sharp cheddar cheese and remaining muffin half."]],"h":[[null,"For comparison, a fast food sausage egg sandwich contains 800 to 1,135 mg sodium, 280 mg phosphorus, 30 grams fat and 255 mg cholesterol."],[null,"Replacing egg with low-cholesterol egg product helps reduce phosphorus, cholesterol and fat."],[null,"English muffin size: 2 ounces; turkey sausage patty size: 1 ounce. Look for sausage with lowest sodium content."]]},"6675045":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F."],[null,"Prep a large casserole dish with nonstick cooking spray."],[null,"Heat olive oil in heavy frying pan and add garlic and onion. Cook until onion is soft, stirring constantly."],[null,"Add the zucchini and sauté for another 1–2 minutes."],[null,"Add the chopped tomatoes and the spinach leaves, cooking for 2 minutes, then add the basil, parsley, and rosemary. Continue cooking until the herbs and spinach are wilted."],[null,"Combine egg whites, cooked vegetables, and the cheese in a bowl. Add salt and pepper if desired."],[null,"Pour the mixture into the casserole and bake for 40–45 minutes, or until the frittata is set. Let cool, then cut into 8 equal sized slices."]],"h":[]},"1688":{"s":[[null,"Dice the onion and bell pepper. Mince the garlic. Shred the cheese."],[null,"Crumble English muffin toasting bread into 9 x 13-inch baking dish."],[null,"Beat eggs and rice milk together in a large bowl."],[null,"Add remaining ingredients to egg mixture and stir well."],[null,"Pour egg mixture over crumbled bread and stir."],[null,"Cover with plastic wrap and refrigerate for 8 to 10 hours."],[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Remove plastic wrap and bake uncovered for 1 hour."]],"h":[[null,"If English muffin toasting bread is unavailable, substitute 5 regular-size whole English muffins."]]},"7468844":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C /gas 4. Mix the spinach, cream cheese, nutmeg, hen’s egg, pepper and Parmesan cheese together in a bowl and set aside."],[null,"Add the oil to a ramekin or cup, unroll a sheet of filo pastry onto a work surface and using a pastry brush, lightly brush with oil. Put another sheet on top of the first and brush that with a little oil, too."],[null,"Cut the sheets into 6 rectangles and place them in shallow bun tins, scrunching the edges together a little and pressing into the bun tins. Repeat with another 2 sheets of filo, so that you have 12 pastry cases. Place in the oven and cook for 2 minutes, then remove."],[null,"Divide the spinach mixture between the 12 cases and make an indentation in the middle of each, pressing the spinach to the sides."],[null,"Crack each quail egg into a cup or ramekin and check there is no shell in it, then tip into the hollow in the spinach."],[null,"Bake for 8–10 minutes until the egg it setting, then remove from the oven and serve. (The egg will continue to cook for a minute or two once removed from the oven, so be careful not to overcook if you want a runny yolk."]],"h":[[null,"If you don’t have bun tins, you could make a large tart by shaping 3 sheets of oiled filo onto a baking tray, scrunching up the edges to create a 1cm crust, then adding the filling to the centre."],[null,"These work well as a starter, light lunch, for brunch, or as substantial canapés."],[null,"'At risk’ groups such as infants, children, pregnant women, the elderly, and those who are unwell should avoid raw or lightly cooked eggs, including quail’s eggs, unless they are certain the eggs come from a guaranteed safe source."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"3872":{"s":[[null,"Use a biscuit or cookie cutter to cut the center out of the slice of bread to toast."],[null,"Spray both sides of bread and center cut-out circle with olive oil cooking spray."],[null,"Heat a medium skillet and place both pieces of the cut bread in skillet. Break egg into center “hole” of cut-out portion. Season with lemon pepper."],[null,"Cook for 1 to 2 minutes and flip over to cook other side. Also, flip the cut-out circle of bread to toast on each side."],[null,"Sprinkle egg with Parmesan cheese."],[null,"Serve egg and toasted bread with a fresh strawberry garnish."]],"h":[[null,"Bread choices include white, wheat, sourdough or rye."],[null,"Change the cookie cutter to fit the occasion or holiday."],[null,"This offers a quick breakfast, which cooks the egg and toast together. My mother-in-law had eight children and this was their favorite family breakfast for the large family."]]},"5641106":{"s":[[null,"Heat 1 tsp oil in a pan and fry broccoli and peppers with paprika and black pepper until soft."],[null,"Whisk eggs and Renastep in a bowl until fully combined."],[null,"Pour egg mixture evenly between each muffin cup."],[null,"Evenly distribute the cooked vegetables and crumbled feta between each muffin."],[null,"Bake for 15 minutes or until cooked through and serve."]],"h":[["Renastep note","Always check with your dietitian or doctor that this recipe is suitable for you."],["Renastep note","Renastep is a food for special medical purposes for the dietary management of kidney disease. Suitable from 3 years of age. Must be used under medical supervision. Renastep contains Milk (milk protein) and Fish (Tuna oil). This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutritics dietary analysis software. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information."]]},"3259":{"s":[[null,"Dissolve yeast in warm water."],[null,"Stir in oil, sugar, garlic powder and flour to make soft dough. Place in a greased bowl, cover and set aside. Let rest 5 minutes."],[null,"Roll dough out to 1/2-inch thickness. Cut into 4 pieces."],[null,"Scramble eggs and stir in cream cheese."],[null,"Place egg mixture onto 1/2 of each piece of dough. Fold dough over, pinching edges; then cut top to vent."],[null,"Spray top of each pocket with butter-flavored cooking spray."],[null,"Bake at 350° F for 15 to 20 minutes, until light golden brown."]],"h":[[null,"Cooled pockets can be frozen for about a week. Warm in the microwave for 30 to 40 seconds."],[null,"Add chopped, fresh green onion or green pepper to taste, after mixing in cream cheese."],[null,"Other filling suggestions are turkey with chopped, cooked broccoli or turkey with dried cranberries."]]},"2343":{"s":[[null,"To hard-boil the egg, boil in water for 8 minutes. Turn off the heat and leave egg in water for 2 more minutes. Drain under cold water and peel."],[null,"Chop the egg and place in a small bowl. Chop the onion and add to the egg."],[null,"Mix the sour cream, mustard and ground pepper into the egg and onion."],[null,"Enjoy as a quick snack!"]],"h":[[null,"Pair with low-sodium crackers, celery sticks or a slice of bread. Garnish with parsley, if desired."],[null,"You may replace the sour ream with mayonnaise, which will increase the fat content by 7 grams."],[null,"Counter top egg cookers are available if you are looking for an easy way to make hard-boiled eggs to have on hand."]]},"6993572":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F."],[null,"Coat a sauté pan with cooking spray over medium heat. Sauté the kale and onions until the onions are just cooked through, about 5-6 minutes. Add the salt (optional), Herbs d’Provence, and turkey sausage. Set aside to cool."],[null,"Once the vegetables and meat are cool, stir in the egg substitute and set aside."],[null,"In a clean bowl, combine the egg whites and cream of tartar. Using an electric mixer, whip the egg whites to stiff peaks."],[null,"Gently fold the egg whites into the egg and vegetable mixture, and pour it into a 2 1/2 quart round baking dish. (You can also use an 8-inch square dish. Be sure not to coat baking dish with cooking spray or the soufflé will not rise.)"],[null,"Bake for 30 minutes. Cut the soufflé into four equal pieces and serve immediately."],[null,"Note: The soufflé will fall a little once removed from the oven, this is normal."]],"h":[]},"3285":{"s":[[null,"Grease the bottom of a microwave dish with olive oil."],[null,"Arrange thin slices of squash and green beans around edge of dish."],[null,"Pour in egg substitute."],[null,"Sprinkle with pepper and paprika."],[null,"Cook covered on high for 4 to 4-1/2 minutes, turning at least once."],[null,"Heat olive oil in a frying pan."],[null,"Lightly sauté squash."],[null,"Add green beans to pan."],[null,"Add egg substitute and sprinkle with pepper and paprika."],[null,"Cover with a lid and cook on medium heat until center is firm."],[null,"Divide in half and serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute squash and green beans with 1/2 cup asparagus, peas, corn, green or red peppers or onions. Turmeric may also be used in place of paprika."],[null,"Season with hot sauce if desired."]]},"4835082":{"s":[[null,"Spray small non-stick skillet with cooking spray and heat over medium heat."],[null,"Whisk egg whites and pour whisked egg whites into heated pan."],[null,"Sprinkle green onion and peppers on top of egg whites. Add ground black pepper. Cover and cook for approximately 3–4 minutes."],[null,"Add cheese, put the cover back on and continue cooking for 30 seconds until the cheese is melted."],[null,"Fold in half, slide onto plate and enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Egg white is a source Instead of using whole eggs, you can of protein that is low use egg whites for most recipes. You in phosphorus, fat and will find the conversion information on sodium. You can also the package. For example, 1 large whole try this recipe with egg can be replaced with 3 tablespoons other lower-potassium of egg whites. vegetables."],["The importance of managing potassium in kidney disease","Healthy kidneys are able to maintain potassium levels in the goal range of 3.6 to 5.2 millimoles per liter. When you have chronic kidney disease, your doctor checks the potassium level in your blood on a regular basis. This is very important because when kidney function decreases, you may be eating more potassium than your kidneys are able to remove every day. When this occurs, potassium starts building up in your blood and you will be asked to decrease the amount of potassium in your diet. When your blood potassium level is too high, the condition is called hyperkalemia. Hyperkalemia can cause muscle weakness and changes in your heart rhythm. If the potassium level in your blood continues to climb, you could reach a dangerously high level where your heart can stop beating. It is important to keep all your scheduled medical appointments and have your blood tested at the recommended times. This way your doctor will know when to instruct you to make changes to your diet to help avoid complications. When it becomes necessary to reduce potassium in your diet, talk to your dietitian. They will help you make changes to keep good blood levels."]]},"6201500":{"s":[[null,"Heat olive oil in a large nonstick skillet over medium heat."],[null,"Add the bell pepper, zucchini, and red onion. Sauté for 3–4 minutes until softened."],[null,"Stir in the spinach and cook for an additional 1–2 minutes until wilted. Remove vegetables from the skillet and set aside."],[null,"In a medium bowl, whisk together the eggs, egg whites, black pepper, smoked paprika, and garlic powder."],[null,"Pour the egg mixture into the same skillet over medium-low heat. Cook gently, stirring frequently, until the eggs are scrambled and just set (about 4–5 minutes)."],[null,"Lay the whole grain tortillas flat on a clean surface. Divide the cooked vegetables evenly among the tortillas, placing them in the center. Top each with a portion of scrambled eggs and cheese. Fold in the sides of each tortilla and roll tightly into a burrito. Serve immediately, or wrap in foil for a portable breakfast."]],"h":[]},"6638576":{"s":[[null,"Lightly coat a small nonstick skillet with cooking spray and place it over medium heat."],[null,"Pour 1/2 cup liquid egg whites into the warm skillet."],[null,"Let the egg whites cook undisturbed for 1–2 minutes until they begin to set around the edges."],[null,"Gently stir, fold, or leave them whole—depending on whether you want soft scrambled whites or an omelet-style shape."],[null,"Continue cooking for another 1–2 minutes until the egg whites are fully set and no longer runny."],[null,"Remove from heat and serve immediately."]],"h":[]},"6885965":{"s":[[null,"Heat 2 teaspoons olive oil in a large saucepan over medium heat."],[null,"Add diced onions and garlic, and cook until onions are soft."],[null,"Stir in the eggplant, chickpeas, cumin, cinnamon, coriander, tomatoes, salt, and pepper. Increase heat to high, and bring to a boil."],[null,"Reduce heat to low, and cover the pot. Cook the stew for 45 minutes to 1 hour or until eggplant is very tender."],[null,"Meanwhile, heat remaining 2 teaspoons olive oil and add onion slices. Fry until golden, and remove from heat."],[null,"When stew is finished, place in serving bowls and top with fried onions and cilantro."]],"h":[]},"2447":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Peel and cut up eggplant. Place eggplant pieces in a pan, cover with water and boil until tender. Drain and mash."],[null,"Combine beaten eggs, nondairy creamer, salt, pepper and sage with mashed eggplant. Place in a greased casserole dish."],[null,"Mix melted margarine with breadcrumbs."],[null,"Top casserole with breadcrumbs and bake 20 minutes or until top begin to brown."]],"h":[[null,"Refrigerate or freeze leftovers for a quick dish later."]]},"6906210":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 450°F. Lightly spray a 9x13 inch baking dish with cooking spray."],[null,"Slice each eggplant into 6, ½ inch thick slices. Place on a rack over a baking sheet and spray lightly with cooking spray. Roast eggplant in the oven for 15 minutes, until softened."],[null,"Meanwhile, combine cottage cheese, mozzarella cheese, egg white and spices in a medium bowl."],[null,"Remove eggplant from the oven and let cool slightly. Reduce oven temperature to 375°F."],[null,"Pour 1 cup of marinara sauce in the baking dish and spread to cover the bottom."],[null,"Place 2 tbsp of the cottage cheese mixture on one end of an eggplant slice. Roll gently to make a roulade. Place it seam side down in the baking dish. Repeat with the remaining 11 eggplant slices."],[null,"Pour remaining marinara sauce over the roulades and sprinkle them with the parmesan cheese. Bake uncovered for 30 minutes."]],"h":[]},"4035847":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400°F. Line a baking tray with parchment paper."],[null,"Cut the eggplant in half lengthwise. Rub 1 tablespoon of olive oil on the cut surface of each half. Place the eggplant halves, cut side down, on the tray and bake for approximately 35 minutes. When done, the inside of the eggplant should be soft while the outside should be able to hold its shape."],[null,"In a non-stick pan, heat the olive oil over medium heat. Add the onion and the peppers and fry for 5 minutes, stirring occasionally. Add the water and continue cooking until the liquid evaporates. Transfer to a plate and set aside."],[null,"In the same pan, add the ground beef, garlic and paprika and fry until the meat is browned. Add the vinegar, oregano, onion and peppers from step 3. Combine all and remove the pan from the heat."],[null,"Cook the rice following the instructions on the package."],[null,"Remove the eggplant halves from the oven. Carefully remove the flesh with a spoon while leaving the skin and a thin layer of flesh on the inside intact so the eggplant halves can hold the stuffing."],[null,"Add ¼ cup of eggplant flesh to the stuffing mixture from step 4 and stir to combine. Discard the remaining eggplant flesh."],[null,"Divide the stuffing between the two eggplant halves and sprinkle with grated cheese. Return the eggplant halves to the oven for a few minutes until the cheese is melted."],[null,"Cut the eggplant halves into 4 portions and serve with the cooked rice."]],"h":[["Hamburger meat substitutes","Consuming the right amount of protein with chronic kidney disease is important to maintaining good health. Many people with reduced kidney function also have heart problems and should follow a heart-healthy diet, which is low in fat and cholesterol. Working with a registered dietitian can help determine your specific protein needs and the best choices of protein for your health. If you are supposed to follow a heart-healthy diet, use extra lean ground beef. You may also consider other substitutions. Plant-based protein sources include ground tofu or vegetable burgers. Cumin, garlic and black pepper can add excellent flavor to these choices. Read product labels and select those lowest in sodium and potassium. Ground chicken and turkey are also good protein options. Basil, garlic, sage, thyme and dried savory are just a few spices for adding low-sodium and low-potassium flavor. Choose fresh ground meat without added salt and low in fat as a healthy option."]]},"2218":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F."],[null,"Chop onion, bell pepper and celery. Peel and dice eggplant into 1” cubes."],[null,"Place eggplant in a medium saucepan, cover with water and boil until tender, about 5 minutes. Drain well, place in a mixing bowl and set aside."],[null,"Sauté onion, bell pepper, celery and garlic in olive oil until tender but not brown."],[null,"Fold sautéed vegetables into eggplant. Add lemon juice, Worcestershire sauce, Creole seasonings, Tabasco sauce, rice, parmesan cheese, cayenne and beaten eggs. Stir to mix well."],[null,"Gently fold seafood into vegetable mixture. Place in a greased casserole dish."],[null,"Mix bread crumbs with melted butter and top casserole."],[null,"Bake 25 to 30 minutes until topping begins to brown."]],"h":[[null,"Creole seasoning is a blend of black and red pepper, salt and thyme. Popular Louisiana brands include Tony Chachere’s® and Paul Prudhomme’s®."]]},"3495":{"s":[[null,"Peel and crush garlic clove. Chop green pepper and finely dice onion. Peel eggplant, slice lengthwise and cut into pieces."],[null,"In a nonstick skillet, heat oil and sauté crushed garlic and green pepper. Remove and set aside."],[null,"In the same oil, sauté eggplant on both sides until browned. Remove and set aside."],[null,"In a bowl, mix ground beef with onion and spices. Make 30 small meatballs."],[null,"Brown meatballs (without using oil) at low temperature in the nonstick skillet."],[null,"Add sautéed eggplant, garlic, bell pepper, crushed stewed tomatoes and water to meatballs. Let simmer on low heat for 30 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"2 medium eggplants yield 8 cups."],[null,"Substitute ground turkey for beef if desired."],[null,"Serve this meal with pita, lavash or tortilla bread and a small bowl of iceberg lettuce salad with olive oil and lemon juice dressing."]]},"6139340":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F."],[null,"Steam or microwave the cubed eggplant until soft (about 8–10 minutes). Let cool slightly, then transfer to a clean kitchen towel or cheesecloth and squeeze out excess moisture."],[null,"In a skillet, heat 1 tsp of olive oil over medium heat. Add the onion and garlic and cook for 3–4 minutes, until softened."],[null,"In a mixing bowl, mash the cooked eggplant with a fork or potato masher. Add the sautéed onion and garlic, almond flour, Parmesan, parsley, oregano, crushed red pepper, black pepper, and egg. Mix until well combined."],[null,"Line a baking sheet with parchment paper. Form the mixture into 12–16 small balls and place on the sheet. Bake for 25–30 minutes, flipping halfway, until firm and golden."],[null,"Heat 1 tsp olive oil in a large nonstick skillet over medium-high heat. Add the zucchini noodles and a pinch of salt. Sauté for 2–3 minutes until just tender. Drain excess moisture if needed."],[null,"Heat marinara sauce in a small saucepan or microwave until hot."],[null,"Divide the zucchini noodles among 4 plates. Top with the eggplant meatballs and spoon warm marinara over the top. Garnish with basil."]],"h":[]},"2379258":{"s":[[null,"Slice the eggplant lengthwise and wash it once."],[null,"Put in an oven pan, the dry the eggplant with tissue."],[null,"Add some olive oil on each side."],[null,"Bake in the oven on 180 for 30 minutes."],[null,"In a medium bowl, add the cheese and the spices and mix well, then add the olive oil."],[null,"Bring the eggplant and roll it with the cheese mix."],[null,"Serve it in a room temperature or cold."]],"h":[]},"6153192":{"s":[[null,"To poach eggs, bring about 3 inches of water to boil in a large, shallow skillet over high heat. Turn off the heat and add eggs at once by breaking them directly into the water. Immediately cover pan with a tight-fitting lid. Allow eggs to cook undisturbed until done as desired, about 4 minutes. Remove the eggs with a perforated spatula or large slotted spoon and drain on paper towels."],[null,"Add the cooking spray and oil to a sauté pan over medium heat. Sauté the spinach until wilted. Stir in the garlic and sauté 1 additional minute."],[null,"Prepare a double boiler with a heat-proof bowl. Add the egg yolk, lemon juice, and vegetable broth, whisking constantly until hot but not curdled. Remove from heat and whisk in yogurt, salt (optional), and pepper."],[null,"Top each English muffin half with 1/4 of spinach mixture, one poached egg, and 2 Tbsps. sauce."]],"h":[]},"1002965":{"s":[[null,"Prepare green beans according to package directions."],[null,"Make a sauce by mixing 2 teaspoons melted margarine, mustard, pepper and Worcestershire sauce. Heat the mixture in the microwave for 30 seconds."],[null,"Toss the sauce with the hot green beans."],[null,"Mix remaining margarine (melted) with bread crumbs. Sprinkle over green beans and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Fresh or low-sodium canned green beans can be used in place of frozen green beans."]]},"3435":{"s":[[null,"Slice celery and chop onion. Thinly slice mushrooms."],[null,"Sauté celery and onion in 1-1/2 tablespoons margarine in a large skillet."],[null,"Stir in water, lemon zest, lemon juice, thyme, pepper and Mrs. Dash® herb seasoning. Bring to a boil."],[null,"Add rice, allow water to boil again then cover, reduce heat, and simmer 20 minutes until rice is tender."],[null,"Melt remaining 1-1/2 tablespoons of margarine in a small skillet. Sauté mushrooms until tender."],[null,"Spoon mushrooms into rice mixture and stir to combine. Serve hot and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Lemon zest is the colored portion of the lemon skin. It contains the lemon oil and adds flavor when added to foods."],[null,"To remove the zest, use a citrus zester, paring knife or vegetable peeler."]]},"7241290":{"s":[[null,"Cook the pasta according to the pack instructions. Drain."],[null,"Meanwhile, place all the remaining ingredients into a blender or food processor and blend for 30 seconds until combined but still retaining a little texture."],[null,"Stir the sauce through the pasta and serve."]],"h":[[null,"You could use a mixture of fresh herbs, such as parsley, basil and mint, or coriander and chives."],[null,"Any shape of pasta is fine – try penne, farfalle or twists."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"3576":{"s":[[null,"Drain tomatoes."],[null,"Heat oil in skillet. Stir in diced tomatoes, garlic powder, 1 teaspoon chili powder and salt."],[null,"In a small cup, mix together cornstarch with 1/2 cup water. Stir until smooth."],[null,"Add the cornstarch mixture to hot tomatoes while stirring to blend well."],[null,"Reduce heat and simmer until thickened."],[null,"Taste and add more chili powder if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Prepare sauce 2 to 3 days ahead and refrigerate. Use for a quick enchilada meal later in the week."],[null,"When eating a dish prepared with this sauce, count as a replacement for 1 vegetable to keep potassium in balance if you are following a low-potassium diet."],[null,"Regular canned enchilada sauces contain 150 to 400 mg sodium per 1/4 cup."]]},"1002592":{"s":[[null,"Rinse lettuce leaves in hot water for 5 seconds, then immediately rinse in cold water. Drain and cut into small pieces."],[null,"Shred carrot. Cut celery and bell pepper into julienne strips."],[null,"Sauté corn kernels in 1 tablespoon oil over medium heat for a few minutes until tender and golden. Remove and let cool."],[null,"In a cup, mix the remaining 3 tablespoons oil, lemon juice and pepper."],[null,"Combine everything in 1 large bowl, add the vinaigrette and toss. Serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"Choose olive oil for salads and vegetables; you may leave the vinaigrette off the salad. Vinegar may be substituted for the olive oil."]]},"1002763":{"s":[[null,"Wash lettuce leaves. Drain and cut into small pieces."],[null,"Bring 2 cups of water to a boil in a pot. When it boils, remove the pot from the burner and add the juice of half a lemon, then add the onion and let it sit for 10 minutes. After the 10"],[null,"minutes, remove onion, let cool and cut into half-moons."],[null,"Cut carrot into julienne strips."],[null,"In a skillet, sauté corn kernels until golden and tender. Let cool."],[null,"In a cup, mix 2 tablespoons vegetable oil, 1-1/2 tablespoons lemon juice and pepper to make the vinaigrette."],[null,"In a bowl, combine all ingredients, including the corn and the vinaigrette, and toss."],[null,"Serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"You can use vinegar instead of lemon to mellow the onion and for the vinaigrette."],[null,"Adding the vinaigrette is optional."]]},"6917425":{"s":[[null,"Preheat an indoor or outdoor grill."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the soy sauce, brown sugar substitute, hot sauce (optional) and black pepper. Set aside."],[null,"Spray the indoor grill with cooking spray. If using an outdoor grill, make sure the grates are clean and lightly oiled."],[null,"Brush the tuna and asparagus with the soy sauce marinade. Place them on the grill. Grill the tuna for 3 minutes per side. Grill the asparagus, turning frequently, until it begins to soften (about 6-8 minutes). Remove the tuna and asparagus from the grill, sprinkle with sesame seeds and let cool. The tuna should be slightly pink in the center, but not raw."],[null,"Combine the lettuce, red bell pepper and cucumber in a salad bowl."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk the dressing ingredients. Pour it over the salad and toss gently to coat well. Divide the salad evenly among four plates."],[null,"Once the tuna and asparagus have cooled to room temperature or slightly warmer, slice the tuna and divide it evenly among the four salads (a little under 4 oz or 115 grams of tuna per salad). Carefully place it on top of the salad."],[null,"Cut the asparagus in half and arrange it around the edge of the salad."]],"h":[]},"6736641":{"s":[[null,"In a medium salad bowl, mix all the salad ingredients."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk the dressing ingredients. Pour over the bean mixture and toss to coat."]],"h":[]},"1002782":{"s":[[null,"Wash lettuce and cut into thin strips."],[null,"Peel mango and cut into small cubes."],[null,"In a separate bowl, mix unsweetened yogurt with sweetener and lemon juice."],[null,"Add mango and lettuce to the yogurt mixture."],[null,"Toss."]],"h":[[null,"You can replace the mango with another low-potassium fruit of your choice."]]},"1002903":{"s":[[null,"Boil eggs for 10 minutes."],[null,"Peel potatoes and boil them."],[null,"When both are done, remove and let cool."],[null,"Peel eggs and cut potatoes in half."],[null,"Chop onion, green onion and garlic. Brown them in a skillet with oil and season with salt and pepper to taste."],[null,"Remove from heat as soon as they are golden and place in a food processor with milk and curry powder. Process until smooth."],[null,"Place curry sauce in a saucepan and dissolve cornstarch in it."],[null,"Bring to heat and cook, stirring constantly with a wooden spoon, until thickened, then remove from heat."],[null,"Cut eggs in half, combine with potatoes and top with curry sauce."],[null,"Garnish with finely chopped fresh herbs. Serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"If desired, first place 2 egg halves and half a potato on each plate and then top each one with curry sauce."],[null,"To reduce potassium, first cut the potatoes and soak them in 2 cups of water for 2 – 4 hours. Then place them on a clean kitchen towel to remove excess water before cooking."]]},"1002878":{"s":[[null,"Wash all vegetables."],[null,"Place water in a pan, bring to a boil and cook cauliflower."],[null,"Cut lettuce into strips."],[null,"Slice cucumber."],[null,"Thinly slice radishes. Slice onion."],[null,"Mix all vegetables and add vinegar to taste."]],"h":[[null,"To enhance the flavor, you can add lemon juice or fruit vinegar."]]},"6433160":{"s":[[null,"Combine all ingredients and mix well."]],"h":[]},"1002806":{"s":[[null,"In a skillet over medium heat, combine butter, sugar and two cups of water. Add halved goldenberries and cook until soft and the mixture becomes a light syrup. Let sit for a few minutes."],[null,"Separately, cut lettuce into very thin strips and cut unpeeled apple into thin wedges. Cut strawberries into medium slices."],[null,"Dress the lettuce and fruit mixture with mayonnaise."],[null,"Drizzle the salad with the goldenberry syrup."]],"h":[[null,"You can serve this salad with chicken or fish."],[null,"If desired, you can replace the refined sugar with a sugar substitute."]]},"1002650":{"s":[[null,"Tear lettuce into pieces."],[null,"Cut cabbage, celery and bell pepper into julienne strips."],[null,"Shred carrot."],[null,"Mix everything in a bowl and add one teaspoon of lemon juice or vinegar."],[null,"Serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"You can replace the cabbage with cucumber or squash."],[null,"You can substitute white vinegar for the lemon juice."]]},"1002790":{"s":[[null,"In a skillet over medium heat, combine butter, sugar and two cups of water. Add halved goldenberries and cook until soft and the mixture becomes a light syrup. Let sit for a few minutes."],[null,"Separately, cut lettuce into very thin strips and cut unpeeled apple into thin wedges. Cut strawberries into medium slices."],[null,"Dress the lettuce and fruit mixture with mayonnaise."],[null,"Drizzle the salad with the goldenberry syrup."]],"h":[[null,"You can serve this salad with chicken or fish."],[null,"If desired, you can replace the refined sugar with a sugar substitute."]]},"3659":{"s":[[null,"Sauté garlic in butter."],[null,"Add remaining ingredients. Simmer until a smooth consistency is attained."],[null,"Weigh finished sauce and divide by 10 to determine serving size weight."]],"h":[[null,"Store extra portions in the freezer in 2 ounce portion cups."]]},"7905699":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a pan and add the beef and onions. Cook for 5 minutes, stirring regularly, until starting to brown."],[null,"Add all the other ingredients, stir and bring to the boil. Turn down the heat, add the pan lid and cook gently for 1.5-2 hours, stirring occasionally. Serve the stew with the injera (see Chef's Tips)."]],"h":[[null,"4 injera made with 150g teff flour, large pinch salt and 180g water + 2 tsp oil for frying (recipe not included in nutritional information)"],[null,"You can use lamb or chicken in place of beef."],[null,"If you don’t have dried lentils a can is fine – look for those canned in water without added salt and add them for the last 30 minutes of cooking. Aduki beans work well instead of lentils."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"3349":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Mix Splenda®, 1 cup flour and nutmeg."],[null,"Add milk, egg and applesauce. Mix well."],[null,"Pour batter into a 9” x 9” greased baking dish."],[null,"In a small bowl mix 1/4 cup flour, cinnamon, brown sugar Splenda® and melted margarine."],[null,"Spoon topping over batter."],[null,"Bake for 20 to 25 minutes until golden brown."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute unenriched rice milk for low-fat milk if desired."],[null,"Self-rising flour contains salt and baking powder. To make your own add 1/2 teaspoon salt and 1-1/2 teaspoon baking powder to each cup of all purpose flour."]]},"6226902":{"s":[[null,"Bring a medium pot of water to a boil. Fill a medium bowl with ice water and set it nearby."],[null,"Add the parsley, oregano, rosemary, and thyme leaves to the boiling water. Blanch the herbs for 10-15 seconds, then immediately remove the herbs with a slotted spoon and transfer them to the ice water. After a few seconds, remove the herbs from the ice water with a slotted spoon and pat them dry with paper towels."],[null,"In a blender or food processor, puree the blanched herbs with the olive oil."],[null,"Pour the herb oil into a dark-colored glass bottle or jar with a tight-fitting lid, seal the container, and set in a cool, dark place (such as your pantry) to infuse for at least 5 days. After it has been fully infused, keep the oil in the refrigerator for up to 1-2 weeks. Or freeze the herb oil in ice cube trays for future use. (Note that each ice cube is 2 tablespoons of oil.)"]],"h":[]},"7727187":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 190°C/gas 5. Mix the flour, yeast, sugar and mixed spice together in a large bowl."],[null,"In another bowl, beat the banana, egg, grated lemon zest, orange zest and apple."],[null,"Gradually mix the warm milk into the flour mixture with a wooden spoon, then mix in the egg and banana mixture."],[null,"Start kneading this sticky dough with one hand, then tip it out onto a lightly floured work surface. Stretch and push the dough with the heel of your hand, folding it over and sprinkling a little more flour if it's sticking too much. Knead for 5–10 minutes until the dough is smooth and elastic."],[null,"Flatten the dough out and sprinkle with dried fruit, fold it over and knead for a couple of minutes more until the dried fruit is mixed in."],[null,"Lightly oil a large bowl with a teaspoon oil and put the dough into the bowl, cover with lightly oiled cling film and leave to rise in a warm place for 1 hour (an airing cupboard is great) it should double in size."],[null,"Divide the mixture into 12 round buns, arrange them on one or two lightly oiled baking sheets, allowing plenty of room for expansion. Cover again with plastic film or a clean tea towel and leave to rise for another hour."],[null,"Cut a deep cross on each bun with a sharp knife, then bake for 20–25 minutes until golden brown."]],"h":[[null,"Eat warm from the oven or cool and store in an airtight container for 2–3 days. Warm the buns in the microwave, or split and toast them."],[null,"To add white crosses to the top, mix 50–60g flour with 2 tbsp water into a paste, roll out and cut into strips. Then, brush with water and stick onto the buns just before they go into the oven."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Freeze in individually wrapped portions to use as required. Defrost for 2 hours, or in the microwave."]]},"6257680":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 475°F. Combine the coffee granules, chili powder, salt, and pepper and press the mixture on all sides of the beef. Place the roast in the center of a 13 × 9-inch baking pan, arrange onions and garlic around, and drizzle with oil. Bake 20 minutes, turning the beef and stirring the onion mixture after 10 minutes."],[null,"Reduce oven temperature to 300°F (do not remove roast from oven). Bake 30 minutes or until a thermometer registers 120°F. Turn off oven. Place the roast on a cutting board and let stand 10 minutes before thinly slicing against the grain. Stir the water into the onion mixture in the pan, scraping the bottom and sides of the pan, and place in oven while the beef is resting. Serve with beef."]],"h":[]},"7897849":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 220ºC/gas 7."],[null,"Toss the parboiled chips in 2 tsp oil and season with plenty of black pepper. Spread the chips out on a non-stick baking sheet and cook for 25-30 minutes until golden and tender."],[null,"Meanwhile, put the fish fillets onto a plate and dredge with flour, making sure they are well coated."],[null,"Heat a non-stick frying pan over a medium heat and add the remaining tsp of oil, wiping it around the pan with kitchen paper."],[null,"Shake off any excess flour and carefully lay the fish fillets down in the pan and cook for 3-4 minutes on each side."],[null,"Heat the peas in a small pan of boiling water, drain then roughly mash. Mix the tartar sauce and yogurt together."],[null,"Serve fish, chips, peas and tartar sauce with a sprinkle of black pepper, a wedge of lemon and a salad garnish."]],"h":[[null,"Dredging fish with flour before frying stops the surface of the fish from burning."],[null,"For extra flavour you can add seasoning to the flour – just salt and pepper, or spices such as Chinese five spice or smoked paprika."],[null,"Use fine chickpea flour for a gluten-free alternative."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"1797":{"s":[[null,"Heat one cup of water."],[null,"While water heats, mix cocoa powder and sugar in a cup."],[null,"Add cold water and mix to form a thin paste."],[null,"Add hot water to cup. Stir to dissolve paste."],[null,"Top with whipped cream."]],"h":[[null,"A small amount of chocolate may be safely incorporated into a kidney diet.Consider daily intake, portion size, and your lab values for potassium and phosphorus."],[null,"Use your favorite sweetener product such as Splenda® granular sweetener or stevia sweetener instead of sugar if desired to reduce calories to 60 and carbohydrate to 7 grams."],[null,"Add whey protein powder if you need a high protein diet."]]},"3113":{"s":[[null,"Cover chickpeas in water in a large pot and soak overnight at room temperature."],[null,"Finely chop the white onion; chop green onions, parsley and garlic."],[null,"Drain and rinse the chickpeas. Place in a food processor along with the green onion, white onion, parsley, garlic, lemon juice, flour, salt, coriander, cumin, black pepper and cayenne pepper."],[null,"Pulse until mixture reaches a course meal to paste texture. (Do not over process). You may have to do this in 2 batches depending on size of your food processor. Once done, blend together with a fork and remove any large pieces of chickpeas."],[null,"Refrigerate the falafel mixture for 2 hours."],[null,"Preheat oven to 400° F."],[null,"Spray a muffin tin with cooking spray."],[null,"Use a scoop or roll mixture into 24 balls; add directly into muffin tin. Place in the oven and bake for 7 minutes. Remove, turn falafel over, and then bake 7 minutes longer."]],"h":[[null,"Serve falafel in a pita pocket with cucumbers, lettuce, onions and garlic sauce or on top of a salad."],[null,"If patties are not forming you may need to put back in food processor until they are more paste like. Be careful not to process into hummus like texture."],[null,"You can add more flour to help bind."],[null,"If desired you can fry falafel in oil instead of baking. Use cooking oil with a high smoke point such as grapeseed or peanut oil."],[null,"Substitute falafel for a protein food instead of in addition to help keep phosphorus and potassium intake in goal."]]},"5262888":{"s":[[null,"To a blender, add all the falafel ingredients apart from the olive oil and blend until a chunky paste."],[null,"Shape into 12 balls and set aside."],[null,"In a small bowl add yoghurt, cucumber, lemon juice, garlic and mint and mix until well combined."],[null,"Heat the olive oil in a pan and fry each falafel until golden brown on all sides."],[null,"Serve the falafel on top of the tzatziki and enjoy!"]],"h":[["Renastep note","Always check with your dietitian or doctor that this recipe is suitable for you."],["Renastep note","This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutritics dietary analysis software. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information."]]},"6602493":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 450 degrees F."],[null,"Place chickpeas in a food processor with 1 small yellow onion, 2 cloves garlic, herbs and spices (1 cup fresh parsley leaves, 1 cup fresh cilantro leaves, 1 tsp ground cumin, 1 tsp ground coriander, ¼ tsp salt, ¼ tsp black pepper). Pulse until the mixture is coarse and holds together when pressed."],[null,"Add baking powder and flour, pulsing briefly to combine. Chill for at least 1 hour."],[null,"Form into small balls or patties (about 1–1.5 inches wide). Place on a baking sheet and repeat to make 12–16 falafel balls."],[null,"Spray the falafel balls with cooking spray. Bake on the bottom rack of the oven for 15 minutes. Turn the oven down to 350 degrees F and move the baking sheet to the top rack. Bake for an additional 15 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, in a small jar or bowl, combine olive oil, lemon juice, mustard, remaining garlic, and 1 tbsp chopped fresh dill. Shake or whisk until emulsified. Season with 1/8 tsp salt and 1/8 tsp pepper."],[null,"To assemble, divide romaine, tomatoes, cucumber, red onion, and ¼ cup fresh chopped parsley between bowls."],[null,"Drizzle with the lemon-herb vinaigrette and toss to coat. Top with warm falafel and serve immediately."]],"h":[]},"6738792":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 300 degrees F. Line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together maple syrup and brown sugar substitute."],[null,"In a medium bowl, mix together all remaining ingredients. Pour maple syrup and brown sugar over mixture and stir to coat."],[null,"Spread oat mixture on baking sheet and bake for 30 minutes. Let cool and store in airtight container."]],"h":[]},"4246006":{"s":[[null,"ONE: In a medium bowl, add all the ingredients except blue cheese and almonds, gently combining until well incorporated."],[null,"TWO: Transfer the mixture to a serving dish, sprinkle with the crumbled blue cheese and almonds and serve."]],"h":[]},"4576263":{"s":[[null,"Pre-heat non-stick skillet to 400°F or waffle iron to level 4. The skillet has reached the right temperature when a drop of water dances in the pan."],[null,"Mix rice flour and baking soda in a small bowl."],[null,"Prepare liquid mix in a medium bowl: whisk together eggs, water, applesauce, sugar, lemon juice and vanilla."],[null,"Pour flour all at once into liquid mix and stir briefly to combine. Do not over-mix."],[null,"Pour approximately 1/4 cup batter circles onto skillet and sprinkle each cake with 1 tablespoon of blueberries."],[null,"Cook for 2–3 minutes on one side, flip and finish in 1–2 minutes on opposite side."],[null,"For waffles, add blueberries directly to mix before baking, spraying iron well with vegetable oil first. Cook 3–4 minutes or until done."],[null,"Serve with slices of peaches."]],"h":[[null,"Pancakes and waffles make a great breakfast!"],[null,"They can be frozen and reheated in the toaster."],[null,"sis/Diabetes ransplant"]]},"4629426":{"s":[[null,"Preheat non-stick skillet to 400°F or waffle iron to level 4. The skillet has reached the right temperature when a drop of water dances in the pan."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix flour and baking soda."],[null,"In a medium bowl, prepare the liquid mixture by whisking together the eggs, water, applesauce, sugar, lemon juice and vanilla."],[null,"Pour flour all at once into liquid mixture and stir briefly to combine. Do not over-mix."],[null,"Pour 1/4 cup batter onto skillet in circular shapes (don’t overcrowd the pan) and sprinkle each cake with 1 tablespoon of blueberries."],[null,"Cook for 2–3 minutes on one side, flip and finish in 1–2 minutes on opposite side."],[null,"For waffles, add blueberries directly to mix before baking, spraying waffle iron well with vegetable oil first. Cook 3–4 minutes or until done."],[null,"Serve with slices of peaches."]],"h":[[null,"Pancakes and waffles make a great breakfast! They can be frozen and reheated in the toaster."],["Rice flour and the kidney diet","Flour can be made from various types of grains. Wheat flour, specifically white all-purpose flour, is the most common type of flour used in the United States; however, there are several other types of flour easily found in your local grocery stores. Some are more kidney-friendly than others depending upon the amount of potassium and phosphorus they contain. The rule of thumb is the lighter the color of flour, the less potassium and phosphorus it contains. Rice flour is one of the many options to consider. Rice flour is made from finely milled rice. It can be made from either white or brown rice. The potassium and phosphorus content is quite different between white and brown rice. White rice is considered more kidney-friendly because it contains less potassium and phosphorus than brown rice. Ask your dietitian which flour is right for your diet. Rice flour can be used to make noodles, thicken soups and stews and as a replacement for wheat flour in cakes, muffins, cookies, pancakes and waffles. Because rice flour is gluten-free it cannot be used to make yeast-type or sour dough breads. For best results when baking with rice flour it is best to seek a muffin, cake or cookie recipe that has been created using rice flour rather than wheat flour."]]},"3793":{"s":[[null,"Cook farro according to package directions, approximately 15 to 20 minutes. Fluff and set aside to cool."],[null,"Core and slice the apples. Drain and rinse chickpeas."],[null,"To make vinaigrette dressing, whisk together the orange juice, mustard, vinegar, honey and olive oil."],[null,"To assemble salads, place lettuce in 4 bowls. Divide the sliced apple, chickpeas and farro equally on top of lettuce. Top each salad with 2 tablespoons of goat cheese and 2 tablespoons of the vinaigrette."]],"h":[[null,"If farro is not available, brown rice may be substituted. This brings the protein down to 9 g and fiber content to 5 g."]]},"6957718":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, combine the cooked and cooled farro, quartered artichoke hearts, halved cherry tomatoes, chopped fresh parsley, chopped fresh mint, and crumbled feta cheese."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the extra-virgin olive oil, red wine vinegar, minced garlic, and black pepper."],[null,"Pour the dressing over the salad and toss gently to ensure even coating."],[null,"Top with a squeeze of fresh lemon juice if desired."]],"h":[]},"6832646":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F. Coat a large baking sheet with cooking spray. Set aside."],[null,"In a large bowl, toss together the asparagus, eggplant, mushrooms, thyme, garlic, salt (optional), pepper, and all but 1 Tsp. olive oil. Pour the mixture into one layer on the baking sheet. Bake for 40 minutes, stirring occasionally."],[null,"While the vegetables are roasting, heat the chicken broth in a saucepan to just a simmer. Then reduce heat to keep warm."],[null,"Add 1 Tsp. olive oil to another saucepan over medium heat. Add the farro and sauté for 2-3 minutes to toast."],[null,"Add 1/2 cup of hot broth to the farro and stir constantly until the liquid is absorbed. Repeat this process until only 1/2 cup of broth is left. Stir in the last 1/2 cup broth and all but 1 Tbsp. of parmesan cheese."],[null,"When the vegetables have roasted for 40 minutes, turn the oven to the broil setting, add tilapia filets to the top of the vegetables, and sprinkle each filet with remaining parmesan cheese."],[null,"Broil the fish on top of the vegetables for 6-7 minutes, ensure the cheese does not burn and the fish is just cooked through."],[null,"Remove fish from vegetables and set aside. Stir roasted vegetables in to farrotto, then serve the fish on top of farrato."]],"h":[]},"2861601":{"s":[[null,"Cut the cucumber, onion, pepper, tomato and radish into medium pieces."],[null,"Add the salt, olive oil and lemon and stir well, then add the pomegranate molasses."],[null,"Cut the bread and roast it in the oven at 180° C for 5 minutes until it becomes brown and place it over the salad. Place in a serving dish."]],"h":[[null,"Serving is for 1"]]},"1702":{"s":[[null,"Set the cream cheese and butter out to soften. Preheat oven to 375°F. Slice carrots and bake until tender; puree."],[null,"Beat the eggs and granulated sugar together. Add carrots, lemon juice, flour, baking powder, cinnamon, ginger, nutmeg and salt."],[null,"Pour mixture onto a wax paper-lined jelly roll pan."],[null,"Bake for 15 minutes. Remove from oven and let cool for 5 to10 minutes."],[null,"Layer another sheet of waxed paper on top. Roll up like a jelly roll and cool completely."],[null,"Make filling by blending the cream cheese and butter together. Add powdered sugar and vanilla. Beat in slowly."],[null,"Carefully unroll the log and remove top layer of wax paper. Spread filling evenly over the roll all the way to edges."],[null,"Gently re-roll from bottom sheet of wax paper."],[null,"Wrap the log tightly in foil and keep chilled until time to serve. Dust with powdered sugar. Use serrated knife to slice. Refrigerate leftover portions."]],"h":[[null,"If possible, bake carrots as opposed to cooking in liquid to avoid runniness."],[null,"Roll may be frozen, but allow time to thaw slightly prior to slicing and serving."]]},"6310729":{"s":[[null,"Place ground chuck in a 2-gallon stockpot and brown over medium heat. Remove meat and drain it well. Wipe drippings from pot."],[null,"Return meat to stockpot, then add tomatoes and water. Bring to a simmer and cook, covered, until tomatoes are soft and a juicy broth is created, about 20 minutes."],[null,"Add remaining ingredients, cover, and continue cooking 60 additional minutes to allow flavors to blend."]],"h":[]},"6984185":{"s":[[null,"Place the water, soy sauce or tamari, onions, celery, herbs, walnuts, and yeast, if using, in a large saucepan."],[null,"Bring to a boil over high heat. Boil 4 minutes and then add oats. Stirring constantly, simmer 5 minutes until the mixture is the consistency of really thick wet sand."],[null,"Scoop the mixture into an 11 × 7–inch baking pan. Pat the mixture until it is spread evenly."],[null,"Preheat oven to 375ºF. Place the uncovered pan in the center of the oven and bake about 30 minutes."],[null,"Remove pan from oven and cool slightly. Keep oven set to 375ºF."],[null,"With a spatula, cut oat mixture into rectangular burgers. Remove burgers to a baking pan with sides and bake another 10 minutes until crisp."]],"h":[]},"6745584":{"s":[[null,"Whisk together the vinegar, oil, honey, salt, and pepper in a large bowl. Add the oranges, fennel, radishes, and mint; toss until well mixed."],[null,"Serve over a bed of arugula."]],"h":[]},"3584":{"s":[[null,"Finely chop onion and bell peppers."],[null,"Combine egg product, onion, bell peppers and black pepper in a bowl."],[null,"Melt margarine in a skillet. Add egg mixture and cook until eggs are set. Stir often to prevent sticking."],[null,"Serve hot or place in warmer until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Low cholesterol egg substitute is available refrigerated or frozen. Best choices for kidney patients are brands lowest in sodium without added soy or milk products or phosphate additives."]]},"2216":{"s":[[null,"Soften cream cheese then place in a large mixing bowl."],[null,"Drain pineapple well. Chop bell pepper."],[null,"Add ingredients to bowl and mix well to blend."],[null,"Shape the mixture into a ball. Wrap in wax paper and chill overnight."]],"h":[[null,"Be sure the pineapple is thoroughly drained, squeezing liquid by hand, if needed."],[null,"Serve with a variety of crackers or pita chips."],[null,"Try low-fat cream cheese to reduce the fat content."]]},"4600210":{"s":[[null,"Place all chutney ingredients in a sauce pan and bring to a boil. Simmer for approximately 30 minutes or until all the liquid is absorbed. Chutney may be made a day in advance."],[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F."],[null,"Carefully loosen skin on turkey breast with fingers and spoon cooled chutney under the skin."],[null,"Massage olive oil on turkey and sprinkle with poultry seasoning."],[null,"Place turkey breast in roasting pan and cook for approximately 1 hour or until the meat thermometer reads an internal temperature of 165°F."]],"h":[[null,"You can also serve the apple onion chutney as a side condiment instead of a stuffing. This recipe can easily be halved to make fewer portions."],["Adding Zest With Apple Flavor","FRESH APPLES can add color, flavor and texture to foods without adding sodium or a large amount of potassium. Add sliced or chopped apples to salads for extra flavor and crunch. Choose apples that are sweet or tart to best compliment other ingredients in the salad. Apples can also be added to cereal, muffins and breads for added flavor and color. APPLE JUICE or cider can be an ingredient to glaze or marinate meats, poach fish or used as a flavorful substitute for water in bread and muffin recipes. When following a recipe, do not swap apple juice for apple cider. Apple juice has added sweetness that will greatly change the recipe, even if you use unsweetened apple juice. The filtration process used to make juice removes the pulp and sediment as well as the tart and bitter flavors that are naturally present in cider. APPLE CIDER VINEGAR is made by fermenting the sugars of apples and should be a pantry staple for all. It can be used in vinaigrettes, marinades and chutneys to add a tangy flavor. Replace balsamic vinegar with apple cider vinegar in a salad dressing or mix with olive oil and herbs to dress up vegetables for any occasion."]]},"3207":{"s":[[null,"Trim asparagus and cut on diagonal into 1” pieces. Cut chicken into cubes."],[null,"Bring a large pot of water to boil. Add pasta, and cook as instructed on box or about 8 to 10 minutes. Do not add salt. Drain, and set aside."],[null,"Warm 3 tablespoons olive oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Stir in chicken, and season with pepper and garlic powder. Cook until chicken is cooked through and browned, about 5 minutes. Remove chicken to paper towels."],[null,"Pour chicken broth into the skillet. Add asparagus, chopped garlic, a pinch more of garlic powder, oregano and pepper."],[null,"Cover and steam until the asparagus is just tender, about 5 minutes."],[null,"Return chicken to the skillet, and warm through."],[null,"Stir chicken mixture into pasta and mix well. Let sit about 5 minutes."],[null,"Drizzle with remaining 2 tablespoons olive oil, stir again, and then sprinkle with feta cheese."]],"h":[[null,"One-pound fresh asparagus yields approximately 2 cups when trimmed."],[null,"Feta cheese is very high in sodium. This dish was made low sodium by limiting feta to 1/4 cup, omitting salt and using low-sodium broth."],[null,"2 average chicken breasts without bones or skin is approximately 8 ounces."]]},"6199968":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350 degrees. Line muffin tins with muffin papers and spray with cooking spray."],[null,"Place black beans and water in a food processor and blend for 2-3 minutes, until you reach pumpkin consistency. Set aside."],[null,"Use a paper towel to wring out excess moisture from grated zucchini, set aside."],[null,"In a large bowl combine baking mix, salt, cinnamon, nutmeg and cocoa powder."],[null,"In another bowl, whisk together eggs, no-calorie sweetener, maple syrup, canola oil, vanilla and yogurt. Add black bean mixture and mix well."],[null,"Make a well in dry ingredients and add wet ingredients. Mix well."],[null,"Gently fold zucchini into muffin batter."],[null,"Spoon batter into 18 muffin cups."],[null,"Bake for 22-25 minutes or until a toothpick inserted in center comes out clean."],[null,"Remove from oven and let muffins cool in pan for 10 minutes. Remove muffins from pan and cool completely on a wire rack."],[null,"Note: If you don’t need to eat gluten-free, you can try making these muffins with a regular baking mix."]],"h":[]},"1716":{"s":[[null,"Set cream cheese out to soften. Thinly slice green onion."],[null,"Combine green chilies, spices and green onions in a bowl."],[null,"Blend in softened cream cheese."],[null,"Spread a thin layer of cream cheese mixture on each tortilla, leaving 1/4” edge uncovered."],[null,"Roll tortillas up like a jelly roll. Use toothpick to secure rolls."],[null,"Cover and refrigerate for at least one hour."],[null,"Slice rolls into 1” pieces and serve as a snack or appetizer."]],"h":[[null,"Lavash flat bread may be used instead of tortilla."]]},"1941":{"s":[[null,"Chop onion, bell pepper and cilantro. Dice pineapple. Cube tilapia into small chunks."],[null,"Broil the tilapia cubes on high for 3 minutes per side."],[null,"Cool tilapia for 5 minutes then pour fresh lime juice over it and mix well. Be sure that all of the pieces of tilapia are completely covered with the lime juice."],[null,"Mix the bell pepper, onion, cilantro, pineapple, black pepper and canola oil with the cooked tilapia."],[null,"Cover and place in refrigerator to marinate for at least 2 hours."],[null,"Serve each portion with 6 saltine creackers with unsalted tops."]],"h":[[null,"As an appetizer, serve in a martini glass with 1/4 cup ceviche and garnish with saltine crackers with unsalted tops along with some cilantro leaves."],[null,"One lime yields 2 tablespoons lime juice. Ten limes are needed for this recipe."],[null,"Substitute pineapple tidbits canned in juice if fresh pineapple is unavailable."]]},"2226":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375° F. Slice the baguette into 24 slices, 1/2-inch each."],[null,"To make the crostini melt the butter; stir in the olive oil. Brush both sides of each bread slice with the butter mixture and place on a baking sheet."],[null,"Bake the crostini’s for 5-7 minutes. Turn slices over and bake 5 minutes longer or until crisp and golden brown."],[null,"Spread 1 teaspoon of fig spread on each crostini. Sprinkle 1 teaspoon goat cheese crumbles on top. After all the crostini are assembled drizzle with balsamic vinegar glaze."]],"h":[[null,"Use fig butter, fig spread, fig preserves or dried or fresh figs."],[null,"Soft goat cheese can be used instead of goat cheese crumbles. Spread it on the crostini then add the fig preserves and balsamic vinegar glaze."],[null,"If balsamic vinegar glaze is unavailable you can heat and reduce aged Italian balsamic vinegar by one half to make glaze."]]},"6198893":{"s":[[null,"In a small mixing bowl, combine goat cheese, yogurt, and orange juice together."],[null,"Fill each phyllo shell with 1 tbsp of cheese mixture. Top each with 1 piece of mint leaf, a walnut half, and a fig piece. Keep refrigerated until ready to serve."]],"h":[]},"7017274":{"s":[[null,"Place the lamb on a baking tray and season with black pepper."],[null,"Heat the redcurrant jelly and pour over the lamb. Use a pastry bush to spread the jelly all over."],[null,"Cook the lamb under a hot grill for 10-15 minutes. Remove from the grill, cover with foil and allow to rest for 5 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, bring the vegetable stock to the boil and add the spices. Add the couscous, remove from the heat and cover with a lid. Leave to steam for 1 minute then fluff up the grains with a fork."],[null,"Stir in the chopped mint tomatoes, parsley, lemon juice and zest and pile onto serving plates."],[null,"Carve the lamb into thin slices and arrange on top of the couscous."]],"h":[[null,"You could also use chicken breast with this recipe."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Freeze couscous and lamb separately. Defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"5479210":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 160°C/320°F/Gas mark 3"],[null,"In a large pan, place the frozen fish mixture and cover with the rice milk, allow to simmer until the fish is just cooked."],[null,"Remove the fish and place into a bowl, pour the milk into a jug and set aside."],[null,"Place ½ the melted butter into a pan and add the flour, allow to cook until combined."],[null,"Gradually add the milk to the pan, ensuring to whisk away any lumps, continue adding until the mixture is a thick sauce and can coat the back of a spoon."],[null,"Add the fish mixture back to the sauce and pour into a circular oven dish."],[null,"Scrunch the filo pastry into balls and place on top of the fish mixture, ensuring to coat the filo with the remaining butter."],[null,"Bake for 20 minutes or until golden brown."],[null,"Remove from the oven, serve and enjoy!"]],"h":[["Renastep note","Always check with your dietitian or doctor that this recipe is suitable for you."],["Renastep note","This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutritics dietary analysis software. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information."]]},"4964422":{"s":[[null,"In a large skillet, heat olive oil over medium heat. Add leeks and garlic and sauté until the leeks begin to soften. Add zucchini and corn and continue to sauté."],[null,"Once the vegetables have begun to soften, add the chicken broth and increase the heat so that the mixture comes to a boil."],[null,"Stir the dry orzo, lemon zest, basil, and pepper into the boiling mixture."],[null,"Add the fish on top and reduce the heat. Simmer the fish stew, uncovered, for approximately 12 to 15 minutes or until the fish and orzo are cooked completely and the majority of the liquid is absorbed."],[null,"Turn off the heat. Place the fish on dinner plates. Add the fresh parsley to the orzo mixture, divide in portions and serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"* Look for low- or reduced sodium broth containing 200 mg or less sodium per 1 cup serving. Avoid low-sodium broth that contains potassium chloride."],[null,"PLEASE NOTE: This recipe is higher in potassium and portion size is important. Check with your registered dietitian to see how this recipe can be included in your diet."],["Different methods for preparing fish","Eating the right amount of protein is critical to maintain healthy muscles and support many functions of the body. Fish is a good source of protein and a great alternative to eating red meat as it provides a wide range of health benefits for those with chronic kidney disease. Fish containing omega-3 fatty acids is especially healthful. The American Heart Association recommends eating fish at least two times per week as part of a healthy diet. Fish, however, is rich in potassium and thus portion size is important to avoid eating too much potassium when following a low-potassium diet. Working with a registered dietitian nutritionist is a great way to find out which type and how much fish can be safely included in your diet. There are dozens of varieties of fish available with many flavors and cooking styles that can suit any taste. You can buy fish either fresh or frozen. Frozen fish often costs less than fresh fish and may be the freshest fish for you to buy as it is frozen immediately when caught. Fish is easy to prepare and can be microwaved, baked, broiled, steamed, or pan-fried. Pepper, lemon, or a sprinkle of herbs adds good flavor without adding a lot of potassium. Serve prepared fish with a side of rice or pasta, on a bed of salad greens, or as a filler for tacos."]]},"3857":{"s":[[null,"Chop onion and bell pepper."],[null,"In a large nonstick skillet, cook the ground round over medium-high heat until brown, stirring to crumble."],[null,"Add onion, bell pepper, water, chili powder, sugar, cumin and garlic. Cook for 7 minutes or until onion is tender."],[null,"Stir in the tomatoes (undrained); bring to a boil. Reduce heat; simmer, partially covered, for 1 hour."],[null,"Add cooked pasta and cook 15 minutes. Serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"Since this chili has 559 mg potassium it is important not to exceed the 1-1/2 cup portion size. To complete your meal you may want to include low sodium crackers, a roll or slice of bread."]]},"2573":{"s":[[null,"Crush the fennel seeds."],[null,"Place ingredients in a jar and shake to combine."],[null,"Store until ready to use on fish or seafood."]],"h":[[null,"Use seasoning as a dry rub or mix with oil and lemon juice for a marinade."]]},"6250197":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, gently mix the salmon (including 2 tablespoons of the can liquid), breadcrumbs, green onion, garlic, flour, egg, old bay seasoning, lemon zest, lemon juice, salt, and pepper."],[null,"Form 8 patties, about ½-inch thick."],[null,"In a non-stick skillet, heat olive oil over medium heat. Cook the fish cakes for about 3–4 minutes on each side or until they are golden brown and cooked through."],[null,"While the fish cakes are cooking, slice the whole grain slider buns. Once the fish cakes are done, place them on the prepared slider buns."],[null,"Add a fresh lettuce leaf to each slider. If desired, include a sliced tomatoes for extra flavor and texture. Spread a thin layer of light tartar sauce on each."]],"h":[]},"4051226":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400°F."],[null,"Place fish in a baking dish and bake for approximately 20 minutes or until the fish is cooked through. The fish can also be steamed. Allow fish to cool."],[null,"To make the corn remoulade, mix all ingredients together. Refrigerate until ready to serve."],[null,"In a mixing bowl, flake the fish and combine it with the remaining fish cake ingredients, except for the olive oil. With a spoon, gently fold all the ingredients together."],[null,"Using your hands, shape fish cake mixture into 8 patties of equal size."],[null,"In a frying pan, heat the oil over medium heat. Fry the patties until golden, approximately 3 minutes per side."],[null,"Serve a dollop of remoulade on top of each fish cake and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"These fish cakes are versatile and may be served as an appetizer, as an entrée with salad, or as sliders in buns or mini pitas."],[null,"Fish cakes can also be frozen. If you choose to freeze the uncooked patties, thaw them thoroughly (on a paper towel) before cooking to remove excess liquid."],["Low-sodium and low-potassium breadings","With chronic kidney disease, the amount of protein in your diet is important. Regular intake is necessary to support your body’s growth and overall health. Meeting with a renal dietitian can be helpful to determine the amount of protein you need based on how your kidneys are functioning. Different cuts of beef, fish and chicken are all excellent selections of animal protein that can be incorporated into your diet. If your recipe choice includes an entrée with breading, consider the ingredients of the breading to avoid unnecessary salt and potassium commonly found in flavored bread crumbs. When choosing items that are pre-prepared, pay attention to ingredient lists on labels for added seasonings that may be high in potassium. Percent daily values on the nutrition facts label can help you identify foods that contain added potassium. With future label changes, a percent daily value over 9% indicates the food item has 300 or more milligrams of potassium per serving. If your preference is making a breaded entrée at home, consider using unseasoned breadcrumbs, crushed cornflakes or crunched, unsalted crackers for flavor."]]},"7355331":{"s":[[null,"Coat the fish with the heaped tsp of turmeric and allow to stand for 2 minutes."],[null,"Heat the oil in a saucepan and add the fish. Cook for 1 minute on each side, remove from the pan and place on kitchen paper."],[null,"Add the panch phoran spices and cardamom pods to the pan and toast for 1 minute, stirring regularly."],[null,"Add the onion and cook for 4 minutes, stirring regularly."],[null,"Add the ginger, garlic and chillies and stir for a further minute."],[null,"Add the other tsp of turmeric, the coriander, cumin and chilli powder, bay leaves and potatoes and stir for 2 minutes."],[null,"Add the tomatoes and 250ml water, bring to the boil, cover, turn down the heat and simmer 10-12 minutes until the potatoes are just cooked."],[null,"Add the fish, put the lid back on and simmer for 6-8 minutes until the fish is cooked through."],[null,"Sprinkle with coriander and serve."]],"h":[[null,"This works well with most fish, if you’re worried about fish bones use chunks of salmon, cod, monkfish or large prawns."],[null,"To make your own panch phoran, mix equal parts of black mustard seeds, cumin seeds, fennel seeds, fenugreek and kalonji (nigella) seeds."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge and thoroughly reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6131494":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400 degrees F."],[null,"Line a baking sheet with foil, coat foil with cooking spray, arrange the fillets on foil, and sprinkle evenly with the paprika. Season lightly with salt and pepper, if desired. Bake 10 minutes or until the fish is opaque in center."],[null,"While fish is cooking, combine the remaining ingredients, except lemon halves, in a small mixing bowl and set aside."],[null,"Using a slotted spatula, remove the fish, place on four dinner plates and squeeze lemon juice evenly over all. Top with the parsley mixture."]],"h":[]},"5579900":{"s":[[null,"Cut the fish fillets into 8 fingers."],[null,"Set out 3 bowls; one with the beaten egg in, 1 with the flour in and one with the cornflakes and breadcrumbs in."],[null,"One at a time, coat the raw fish in flour, then dip into the beaten egg mixture before finally coating in the cornflakes or breadcrumbs, making sure you coat all the fish evenly."],[null,"Carefully fill a frying pan with rapeseed, vegetable or sunflower oil about 1 cm deep to shallow fry. Heat the oil, to test the temperature, drop a cornflake in, it should sizzle slowly and gently brown over 20-30 seconds. If the bread coating browns too quickly and burns, the oil it too hot."],[null,"Fry the fish for about 3 minutes each side. Be careful not to splash the hot oil."]],"h":[[null,"Serve with polenta chips and peas."],[null,"Be aware of the potassium content in any accompanying vegetables"]]},"2288":{"s":[[null,"Thaw fish. Dice the onion."],[null,"In a medium-sized pot add 2 teaspoons oil and sauté the onion."],[null,"Once onion is browned, but not burned, add rice, 2 cups water, 1/2 tea spoon cumin and 1/2 teaspoon black pepper."],[null,"Cook covered for about 20 minutes on medium-low heat."],[null,"In a bowl, add flour, 1 teaspoon cumin, 1 teaspoon black pepper and salt-free seasoning and mix well."],[null,"Heat remaining oil in a skillet or fryer. Dry thawed fish with a paper towel to remove all excess water. Dip the fish in the flour mixture and fry in hot oil."],[null,"Serve hot fish with seasoned rice."]],"h":[[null,"Choose any white fish for this recipe."],[null,"Cumin is a spice known to aid digestion but can be strong if one is not accustomed to consuming it. Adjust amount to your taste"],[null,"If desired, accents to the Fish Fry with Seasoned Rice include: white onion soaked in vinegar with black pepper or tahini sauce (2 tablespoons tahini with 1–2 teaspoons white vinegar, black pepper and cumin)."],[null,"For a lower protein diet divide fish into 6 portions instead of 4; protein is reduced to 17 grams for the meal."]]},"7859226":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200°C/gas mark 6."],[null,"Cut a large square of foil, approx 25cm x 25cm."],[null,"Place the fish, leeks, beans and parsley into the centre of the foil and spoon over the crème fraîche and stock mix, season with the pepper, and then fold and secure into a parcel."],[null,"Place on a baking sheet and cook for 15 minutes until the fish is opaque and flakes easily with a fork. Open the parcel and transfer to a serving plate. Serve with a lemon wedge."]],"h":[[null,"You could use 1 tbsp of lemon juice in place of stock."],[null,"Try adding other vegetables, such as mangetout or asparagus."],[null,"Steaming food in a parcel means minimum mess and a healthy method of cooking."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"7727427":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4. Boil the sweet potatoes for 15-20 minutes until soft and drain."],[null,"Heat the oil in a saucepan over a low-medium heat and fry the leeks, stir regularly, until they soften, about 7-8 minutes."],[null,"Sprinkle the flour over the leeks and crumble the stock cube over. Mix well for a minute or so until the leeks are coated."],[null,"Slowly stir in a quarter of the milk until it becomes quite thick, then gradually stir in the rest, stirring constantly, until it comes to the boil. Stir in the white pepper and parsley and remove from the heat."],[null,"Mash the sweet potatoes thoroughly and mix in the smoked paprika."],[null,"Add the leek sauce to an ovenproof dish and arrange the fish so that it is evenly distributed, pushing it into the sauce. Top with the sweet potato and bake for 25-35 minutes until the sauce starts bubbling through the sweet potato, sprinkle with the remaining parsley and black pepper."]],"h":[[null,"You could make individual fish pies – great for a dinner party, and try adding some prawns or sliced mushrooms too."],[null,"Works well with other fish such as haddock or river cobbler."],[null,"You could use half sweet potato and half potato."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Then defrost in the fridge and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"2148":{"s":[[null,"Shred cabbage and chop onion and cilantro. Set aside. Mince garlic."],[null,"Place the fish fillets in a dish and squeeze lime juice from half a lime over fish. Sprinkle fillets with minced garlic, cumin, chili powder, black pepper and olive oil. Turn filets to coat with marinade and refrigerate for 15 to 30 minutes."],[null,"Make salsa blanca by combining mayonnaise, sour cream, milk and juice of half a lime. Stir to combine and place in refrigerator to chill."],[null,"Turn oven on to broil. Cover broiler pan with foil. Broil fish until the flesh turns opaque and white, and the fish flakes easily, about 10 minutes. Remove from oven, cool slightly and flake fish into large pieces."],[null,"Heat the corn tortillas, one by one, in a pan, until soft and warm. Wrap them in a clean dish towel to keep them warm."],[null,"To assemble tacos place a piece of fish on tortilla and top with salsa blanca, cabbage, red onion, cilantro and lime wedges. Add hot sauce if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute any firm white fish for the cod. Tilapia, catfish, halibut, snapper, mahi mahi, sole and rockfish work well in this recipe."],[null,"If desired cook fish on a grill instead of broiling."],[null,"Compare hot sauce brands and choose the one lowest in sodium."]]},"6588051":{"s":[[null,"In a medium bowl whisk together the salsa, lime juice, cilantro, chili powder, salt, and pepper. Set aside."],[null,"Coat a large sauté pan with cooking spray. Sauté fish over medium heat for 2 minutes on each side. Pour salsa mixture over fix and sauté an additional 3 minutes."],[null,"Remove the fish from the pan and flake with a fork, mixing in the salsa mixture."],[null,"In a small bowl combine the yogurt and hot sauce. Evenly divide the fish among 8 tortillas and top each with a dollop of the yogurt sauce."]],"h":[]},"7297261":{"s":[[null,"Place the celery, carrot, bay leaf, garlic, ginger, allspice, thyme and fish stock in a pan. Bring to a gentle boil, add the lid, turn down the heat and simmer for 5 minutes."],[null,"Add the red pepper, okra, green banana and chayote and cook for a further 5 minutes."],[null,"Finally, add the spring onions and pepper, stir, add the red snapper chunk, cook for 3-4 minutes and serve."]],"h":[[null,"This works well with most fish such as chunks of salmon, cod, monkfish or large prawns."],[null,"If you can't get chayote, use deseeded cucumber or courgette - it won't need as much cooking so add in step 3 with the spring onions."],[null,"You can use any vegetables you have - sweet peppers, courgette, mangetout, baby corn or florets of broccoli or cauliflower."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"4121615":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350°F. Arrange the tortillas on a baking sheet and bake for about 5 minutes, until crisp. Remove and set aside."],[null,"Increase the oven temperature to 450°F. Line a baking sheet with parchment paper or a silicone baking mat and place the fish fillets on top. Season fish with the dried oregano and black pepper. Bake for about 10 minutes, until the fish flakes easily with a fork."],[null,"While the fish bakes, make the sauce: In a small bowl, stir together the yogurt, garlic, lime zest, and cilantro."],[null,"To assemble, spread a spoonful of yogurt sauce on each tortilla. Top with lettuce, radishes, and a piece of fish. Drizzle with lime juice to taste."]],"h":[[null,"* Any firm white fish such as tilapia, haddock, turbot, halibut, grouper, or mahi also works well in this recipe. If using frozen fish, thaw and pat-dry before baking. Read food labels and avoid fish with additives."],["Frozen fish and reading labels","With a kidney-friendly diet, protein can come from either plant or animal sources, offering a variety of cost-effective options. Incorporating different types of fish adds a lean protein choice that also provides heart-healthy omega-3 fatty acids. Frozen fish can be less expensive, but it’s important to read the ingredient list to make a healthy selection. Protein content in fish, fresh or frozen, remains consistent when portions are the same. A 3-ounce serving typically provides 17 to 22 grams of protein. Natural phosphorus and potassium in fish are also similar in both forms. Certain fish, such as salmon and trout, are naturally higher in these minerals compared to cod or tuna. In general, most fish are low in sodium unless it has been added. The biggest differences in nutrition come from additives to some frozen fish products. Reviewing the ingredient list can help identify these unwanted additives. Ingredients like sodium phosphate, potassium phosphate, or sodium nitrate add to the sodium, potassium, or phosphorus content. While these additives help maintain texture and appearance, they can be harmful for individuals with chronic kidney disease. When purchasing frozen fish, look for products without additives and key phrases such as “no added phosphates,” “no added salt,” or “no additives.”"]]},"7800433":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 200°C/fan 180°C/gas 6. Spread out the cauliflower florets in a non-stick roasting tin in a single later and spray 4-5 pumps of low-calorie cooking spray. Roast for 20 minutes until the cauliflower edges are starting to crisp up."],[null,"Add the lentils, beans and stock to the tin. Gently stir everything together. Rest the fish fillets on top and season with pepper. Roast for 15-20 minutes until the fish is flaking."],[null,"Gently stir the spring onions and garlic into the lentils around the fish fillets and scatter over the parsley. Divide between 4 plates and serve with the lemon wedges."]],"h":[[null,"Find out more about our partnership with Slimming World."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"5254699":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 150°C/300°F/Gas Mark 2"],[null,"Warm a ramekin in the oven so it is warm when you add the caramel."],[null,"To make the caramel, put 30g sugar and 2 tbsp water into a pan. Dissolve the sugar slowly, stirring with a wooden spoon over a low heat. When dissolved, stop stirring and boil until it goes dark brown colour. Remove from the heat to ensure the caramel does not burn. Once cooled pour into the ramekin."],[null,"To make the custard, place the Renastep, double cream and vanilla extract into a saucepan and heat on low. Beat the egg yolk with a whisk in a bowl and gradually beat in the remaining sugar until combined. Stir the Renastep mixture into the egg mixture and combine with a spatula. Set aside."],[null,"Pour the custard evenly into the ramekin on top of the caramel."],[null,"Place the ramekin in a roasting tin and pour boiling water into the tin until it comes half-way up the sides of the ramekin (Bain-Marie)."],[null,"Bake in the oven for 60-75 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"When ready to serve, turn the cups upside down."],["Renastep note","Renastep is a Food for Special Medical Purposes and must be used under medical supervision."],["Renastep note","Renastep is a ready to use feed for the dietary management of kidney disease from 3 years of age onwards. Renastep contains milk and fish. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information."],["Renastep note","This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease."]]},"3706":{"s":[[null,"Heat a sauté pan over high heat until hot."],[null,"Add olive oil to the pan."],[null,"Season the steak with black pepper and paprika."],[null,"Add the steak to the hot pan and sear over high heat for 4 minutes on each side."],[null,"Remove the steak from the pan and let it rest for 2 to 3 minutes."],[null,"Slice on the bias and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Let the steak rest before cutting it right away. This allows the flavors to settle in nicely."],[null,"Adjust portion to match your meal plan."],[null,"This recipe is featured in the DaVita Eats: Chef Tips video series."]]},"2505":{"s":[[null,"Slice red onion and quarter the cherry tomatoes. Slice the red bell pepper and carrot into thin strips. Mince the garlic clove."],[null,"Heat the flat bread one at time in hot pan over medium heat, 3-4 minutes per side."],[null,"Whisk together minced garlic, plain Greek yogurt, ground black pepper, olive oil, tahini, lemon juice, ground cumin, and garlic powder in a bowl."],[null,"Spread sauce evenly over each pita bread."],[null,"Layer onion, tomato, bell pepper, carrot and spinach on each flat bread, split evenly between the two flat breads."],[null,"Sprinkle feta over the vegetables and fold or roll the flatbread around the vegetables."]],"h":[[null,"If Greek flat bread is unavailable, other types of flat bread may be substituted. Look on the food label for the brand with the lowest sodium level and carbohydrate level if you are on a lower carbohydrate diet."],[null,"Use left over Greek yogurt as a dip or in place of sour cream. The left-over carrot and bell pepper can be dipped into the Greek yogurt for a snack."]]},"2773":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Melt butter and add graham cracker crumbs and sugar; mix thoroughly. Save 1 to 2 tablespoons crumb mixture to sprinkle on top of pie."],[null,"Press into a 9-inch pie shell. Bake for 5 minutes. Remove from oven and set aside to cool."],[null,"In a mixing bowl add lime juice and condensed milk and mix thoroughly."],[null,"With a chilled bowl and chilled beaters, use hand-mixer to whip the heavy cream to a stiff peak. Fold the cream into the condensed milk mixture."],[null,"Pour mixture into the pie crust and sprinkle leftover crumb mixture on top."],[null,"Chill until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Garnish with lime zest if desired."],[null,"This pie may be frozen for a frosty dessert."],[null,"This very rich dessert makes a wonderful occasional special treat. It is not recommended for people with diabetes due to the high carbohydrate and fat content."]]},"6432957":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F. Spray a baking dish with nonstick cooking spray."],[null,"Pat fish fillets dry with a paper towel and place on a flat surface."],[null,"Sprinkle each fillet with black pepper."],[null,"Roll each fillet around the carrot and celery sticks and place seam side down in a baking dish."],[null,"Place the walnuts, parsley, lemon juice, lemon zest, breadcrumbs, 1 teaspoon of olive oil, and 1 garlic clove in a small food processor. Process until crumbly."],[null,"Spread 1 teaspoon of the walnut and parsley mixture on top of each fish roll."],[null,"Place in the middle of the oven and bake for 15–20 minutes, until the fish is flakey and the vegetables are tender."],[null,"Place in the middle of the oven and bake for 15–20 minutes, until the fish is flakey and the vegetables are tender."],[null,"While the fish is baking, mince the remaining 2 garlic cloves. Add 1 teaspoon of olive oil to a large skillet and heat over medium heat. Add the garlic and sauté for 30 seconds to a minute, until fragrant. Add the chopped spinach and cook until it is wilted."]],"h":[]},"3445":{"s":[[null,"Cut each tortilla into 8 wedge-shaped pieces."],[null,"Heat oil in heavy skillet using enough to cover 1/4” of the skillet."],[null,"When oil is hot add tortilla pieces and toss until golden brown and crisp."],[null,"Remove chips and drain on paper towels."],[null,"Store chips in airtight container until ready to eat."]],"h":[[null,"Check to see if oil is hot enough by placing one piece of flour tortilla in skillet. If oil forms small bubbles around the chip, it is hot enough."],[null,"For a sweet twist, sprinkle a mixture of sugar or sweetener and cinnamon over hot chips immediately after removing from the skillet."]]},"3560":{"s":[[null,"In large bowl mix flour and salt together."],[null,"Add softened shortening and two cups of warm water."],[null,"Begin mixing by hand, squeezing flour and shortening through fingers or mix with a spoon and knife, crisscrossing through flour and shortening."],[null,"Form masa (dough) into a large ball. Remove clinging flour from sides of bowl by rolling masa around bowl. Add remaining 1/4-cup warm water if masa is too dry."],[null,"Turn masa onto board or tabletop and knead for one minute into a smooth ball. Cover with the bowl or a towel for at least five minutes and allow to rest."],[null,"Begin heating cast iron griddle or heavy skillet to medium-high temperature."],[null,"Pinch off a piece of masa and form into a 2-inch round ball, turning edges of masa under and in. Set each ball aside. Tops will feel dry to touch."],[null,"Sprinkle flour lightly over masa and board or table top. Using a rolling pin, roll masa into a round tortilla approximately 6 to 7-inches in diameter."],[null,"Toss and turn tortilla between hands until smooth."],[null,"Test a small piece of masa on heated griddle or skillet; it should begin browning within a few seconds if oil is hot enough."],[null,"Cook each tortilla until lightly browned on both sides, turning frequently to prevent burning. Use a spatula or tongs to turn tortillas."],[null,"Stack tortillas after cooking. Cool before storing."]],"h":[[null,"Cover tortillas with paper towel and store in airtight container or plastic bag in the refrigerator."],[null,"If available, use a tortilla press instead of rolling the dough out."],[null,"Homemade flour tortillas are much lower in sodium than most store-bought tortillas because there is no baking powder added."],[null,"Most shortenings have been reformulated to remove all or most trans-fats. Avoid products that contain partially hydrogenated vegetable oil as this is a source of trans-fats."]]},"6601352":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oven to 350°F. Line an 8x8 inch baking pan with parchment paper, leaving an overhang for easy removal."],[null,"Place the vegetable oil and carob chips in a medium bowl set over a pot of simmering water. Melt the carob chips with the vegetable oil, stirring slowly and continuously. Once melted, remove the bowl from the pot and dry the bottom of it."],[null,"Whisk in the sugar substitute and then the eggs one at a time until the batter is smooth."],[null,"Add the vanilla extract and cocoa powder and stir to combine."],[null,"Spread the batter evenly in the baking dish. Bake for 15-18 minutes or until a toothpick inserted in the center comes out clean. Let cool completely in the pan."],[null,"Use the parchment sling and lift the brownies out of the pan. Slice and serve."]],"h":[]},"6647980":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 350 degrees F. Line two baking sheets with parchment paper."],[null,"In a large bowl, whisk the eggs well."],[null,"Sift the powdered sugar substitute, cocoa powder, and salt over the eggs and stir to combine."],[null,"Stir in vanilla extract."],[null,"Fold in the sugar-free chocolate chips and walnuts."],[null,"Drop rounded tablespoons of the cookie dough onto the prepared baking sheets, spacing them about 2 inches apart."],[null,"Bake in the preheated oven for about 10–12 minutes or until the tops are shiny and cracked."],[null,"Allow the cookies to cool on the baking sheet for 5 minutes before transferring them to a wire rack to cool completely."]],"h":[]},"2635":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350°F. Line muffin tin with paper liners."],[null,"In a medium bowl, combine all ingredients except chocolate chips, mixing until smooth. Fold in chocolate chips."],[null,"Distribute batter evenly into 12 muffins."],[null,"Bake for 15-18 minutes, until centers are firm and starting to crack. Cool for 15 minutes and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"If you prefer use reduced-fat peanut butter. This change adds approximately 5 grams of carbohydrate and lowers fat by 3 grams per serving."],[null,"These muffins are a tasty way to add extra protein in a snack or meal."],[null,"Peanut butter adds more potassium and phosphorus but is a great source of protein. Ask your dietitian if you need to add a phosphate binder when you eat this muffin for a snack."]]},"3276":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Place 2 large sheets of heavy duty aluminum foil on preparation surface."],[null,"Thinly slice lemon. Spread lemon slices, half on each piece of foil."],[null,"Set cod fillets on top of lemon slices, 2 fillets or about 6 ounces per foil."],[null,"Lightly sprinkle each fillet with measured salt and pepper."],[null,"Spoon diced pimentos over each fillet, then drizzle with olive oil."],[null,"Fold foil edges together to seal fish inside. Place on a baking sheet and bake for 20 minutes. Remove fillets from foil to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Use fresh or frozen cod. If frozen, thaw before preparing recipe."],[null,"Use Dromdary® brand diced pimento peppers because this brand does not contain added salt. If unavailable, substitute pimentos or roasted red peppers with lowest sodium content and omit salt from recipe. Fresh roasted red peppers may also be substituted."],[null,"When adding very small amounts of salt, try combining with pepper or other ground spices. Use a refillable shaker to distribute evenly over food."]]},"6368072":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 350 degrees F. Line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"In a mixing bowl, combine the almond butter, egg, sugar, and vanilla extract. Mix until all ingredients are well combined."],[null,"Scoop tablespoon-sized portions of the chilled dough and roll them into balls. Place the balls on the prepared baking sheet, leaving space between each. If the dough is too soft to roll, place in the refrigerator for 30 minutes to firm up."],[null,"Using a fork, gently press down on each cookie ball to create a crisscross pattern."],[null,"Bake in the preheated oven for about 10 minutes or until the edges are golden brown."],[null,"Allow the cookies to cool on the baking sheet for a few minutes before transferring them to a wire rack to cool completely."]],"h":[]},"2052":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375° F."],[null,"In a shallow baking dish that’s been coated with no-stick cooking spray, arrange fish fillets."],[null,"Season fish fillets with black pepper."],[null,"Cover fillets thoroughly with French salad dressing."],[null,"Top fillets with panko bread crumbs."],[null,"Bake for 20-25 minutes or until they are golden and flake easily."]],"h":[[null,"White fish fillets include tilapia, perch, halibut, flounder and cod."],[null,"Choose French salad dressing brand with the lowest sodium content."],[null,"Plain bread crumbs can be substituted for panko if desired."],[null,"If you are on a lower protein diet, adjust the portion size to match your meal plan or ask your dietitian for guidance."]]},"3149":{"s":[[null,"Peel and slice eggplant into 3/4” sticks, 4” long. Rinse and pat dry."],[null,"In a medium bowl, mix milk and eggs until well blended; stir in hot sauce."],[null,"In a wide, shallow bowl, combine cornstarch, bread crumbs, and dry Ranch salad dressing mix."],[null,"Heat oil in frying pan on high heat."],[null,"Dip eggplant sticks into egg mixture and then roll each piece in bread crumb mixture."],[null,"Place in oil, flipping regularly and fry 3 minutes or until golden brown."],[null,"Drain on paper towels and serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute 1/2-cup low-cholesterol egg product to lower fat and cholesterol content."],[null,"French fried potatoes are much higher in potassium compared to French Fries Made with Zucchini."]]},"2431":{"s":[[null,"Peel and slice zucchini into 3/4” sticks, 4” long. Rinse zucchini and pat dry."],[null,"In a medium bowl, mix milk and eggs until well blended; stir in hot sauce."],[null,"In a wide, shallow bowl, combine cornstarch, bread crumbs, and dry Ranch salad dressing mix."],[null,"Heat oil in frying pan on high heat."],[null,"Dip zucchini sticks into egg mixture and then roll each piece in bread crumb mixture."],[null,"Place in oil, flipping regularly and fry 3 minutes or until golden brown."],[null,"Drain on paper towels and serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute 1/2-cup low-cholesterol egg product to lower fat and cholesterol content."],[null,"These fries are much lower in potassium compared to potato french fries."]]},"7247412":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 190C/gas 5.Add 2 tsp of the oil to a saucepan, then add the onions and cook over a very low heat for 30–40 minutes, stirring regularly so that the onions caramelise."],[null,"While the onions are caramelising, put the remaining oil onto a baking sheet. Add the potatoes and muddle around until they are coated, then bake in the oven for 30–40 minutes."],[null,"Add the stock to the onions, bring to the boil and simmer for 5 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, to make the cheesy croutons: Cut each slice of bread in half and grill, then turn over and top each with the Cheddar cheese and mozzarella, and grill again until the cheese melts and browns. Alternatively, you can put the cheese-topped bread on a baking sheet and cook in the oven for 5-10 minutes."],[null,"Stir the parsley, pepper and soy sauce through the soup, then place into four bowls. Serve with cheesy croutons and a sprinkling of fresh parsley on top, and the sweet potato wedges on the side."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"2914":{"s":[[null,"Preheat a non-stick skillet on medium-high heat."],[null,"In a bowl, put 2 tablespoons of egg whites, and then add one slice of bread. Be sure to get egg only on one side of the bread. Let egg soak into bread."],[null,"Place bread egg side down in skillet."],[null,"Add cream cheese and applesauce to bread in the pan and sprinkle with cinnamon."],[null,"Repeat step 2 with the other slice of bread and place it on top of the slice in the pan, egg side up"],[null,"When bottom of the first bread slice is browned, flip it over and brown the other side."],[null,"Remove to plate and top with the syrup of your choice."]],"h":[[null,"One egg yolk contains 66 mg phosphorus. Angela recommends using only the egg white so you can use whole wheat bread to increase fiber and still keep phosphorus low. One slice of white bread contains 25 mg phosphorus; one slice whole wheat bread contains 57 mg phosphorus."]]},"6289021":{"s":[],"h":[]},"4694570":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 425°F"],[null,"Put water, butter and sugar in a small saucepan and bring to a boil."],[null,"Add flour all at once and stir vigorously until a smooth ball forms. Some dough will stick to the bottom of the pan forming a thin film. This indicates the flour is cooked. Remove from heat immediately."],[null,"Transfer to a mixing bowl and add eggs one at a time, beating well between each addition. If using a standing mixer, use the paddle attachment."],[null,"Line baking sheet with parchment paper, and drop 18 spoonfuls of dough mixture (1 inch by 3/4 inch high), spacing 2 inches apart. Brush each drop with glaze to smooth tops."],[null,"Bake for 10 minutes."],[null,"Reduce heat to 350°F without opening oven door, and continue baking for 30 minutes. Puffs should sound hollow and dry when tapped on bottom. Cool on wire rack."],[null,"Cut each puff open and fill with 1/4 cup berries, letting some spill over. Top with 1 tablespoon whipped topping and dust with powdered sugar. Garnish with mint."]],"h":[[null,"If not using all puffs, freeze baked puffs after they cooled off in airtight container. To use: warm in a 350°F preheated conventional oven for 5 minutes. DO NOT MICROWAVE."]]},"6435021":{"s":[[null,"In a medium bowl, mix together all ingredients except chips."],[null,"Serve salsa in a bowl with chips on the side."]],"h":[]},"6145161":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6890316":{"s":[[null,"Bring water to a boil in a large saucepan over high heat. Add the corn, reduce heat to medium, and cook, covered, 8 minutes, or until tender-crisp when pierced with a fork. Drain in colander and run under cold water to cool quickly."],[null,"Meanwhile, combine remaining ingredients in a medium bowl. Cut the corn off the cobb and add to the tomato mixture. Toss gently until well blended."]],"h":[]},"6594166":{"s":[[null,"DO AHEAD OR DELEGATE: Cook and refrigerate the shrimp, halve the tomatoes, remove the corn kernels from the cobs, or fully prepare and refrigerate the salad (wait to chop and add the avocado until just before serving)."],[null,"Pan-fry, steam, or grill the shrimp until they are pink, 3–4 minutes total. (Meanwhile, warm the rolls, if you are serving them.) Combine all the ingredients except the shrimp in a large serving bowl. Serve the shrimp on top of the salad."],[null,"FLAVOR BOOSTER Add 1/4 teaspoon celery seeds or cumin and 1 tablespoon fresh lemon or lime juice to the salad."]],"h":[]},"3767":{"s":[[null,"Chop the onion and celery. Chop the fresh herbs. Cut the bread into 1/2-inch cubes."],[null,"Melt the butter in a nonstick frying pan. Sauté the onion and celery until tender. Remove from heat."],[null,"Toss in the cubed bread, pepper, poultry seasoning, fresh herbs and cranberries."],[null,"Mix egg product and stock. Pour it into the bread mixture and mix lightly."],[null,"Place the stuffing into the turkey body cavity and neck to cook, or bake stuffing separately in a baking dish sprayed with nonstick cooking spray at 350º F for 45 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"For best results use day-old bread."],[null,"If fresh herbs are unavailable substitute 1 teaspoon dried herbs."],[null,"If giblet stock is unavailable substitute lo- sodium chicken broth."]]},"6275460":{"s":[],"h":[]},"3121":{"s":[[null,"Wash and dry the lettuce, then cut each leaf in half lengthwise. Cut carrots julienne style. Slice onion. Set aside."],[null,"Boil 6 cups of water and set aside to soak the rice wrappers later."],[null,"Drain and pat dry the tofu. Slice it into 12 pieces, each about 4″ long."],[null,"Spread the tofu on plate and season it evenly with cumin, granulated garlic, sea salt and black pepper."],[null,"Heat a non-stick pan with olive oil. Place the tofu strips in the pan, seasoned side down. Season the other side and fry until the bottom is lightly browned, about 1 to 2 minutes. Flip and fry until second side is lightly browned. Place the tofu on a plate to cool."],[null,"Pour hot water into a large shallow bowl. Dip a rice wrapper in hot water. Once it’s slightly soft, place the wrapper on a large plate and place 2 halves of the lettuce in the center of the wrapper. Sprinkle 2 to 3 tablespoons of carrot and 1­ to 2 tablespoons of sliced onion on top of the lettuce. Place one cooled tofu strip on top of the vegetables."],[null,"Fold the sides in, and then fold the bottom up and roll tightly. Repeat with the rest of the rice wrappers, vegetables and tofu strips."],[null,"Refrigerate and serve cold with your favorite low-sodium dressing."]],"h":[[null,"Serve with 2 tablespoons of low-sodium dressing. Miso ginger dressing is a good choice."],[null,"Although the amount of salt used in this recipe is minimal, some individuals may wish to further reduce sodium content by using salt-free seasoning. Mrs. Dash and Kirkland No Salt Seasoning are good alternatives."]]},"9609089":{"s":[[null,"Chop all the veggies and add them to a mixing bowl. Then add the lime juice and spices, and mix well."],[null,"Optional: Blend 1 cup of your tomato salsa, add it back to the bowl and stir to combine for a less chunky texture."],[null,"Refrigerate for 1 hour (or longer) to chill and blend the flavours. Then serve."]],"h":[]},"6824816":{"s":[[null,"Fill a flat round cake pan with water. Place a clean, smooth (not fuzzy) kitchen towel on your work surface. Arrange the lettuce, tofu, carrots, cucumber, sprouts, and mint into individual piles on a plate."],[null,"Put 1 rice paper in the water. Soak until pliable. Place the rice paper on top of the kitchen towel. Blot dry. The paper should be sticky, not slippery. Stack the ingredients as follows, one on top of the other on the side of the paper closest to you: 1 lettuce leaf, 1 piece of tofu, some carrot, cucumber, sprouts, and 2 mint leaves, one beside the other."],[null,"Fold the side of the paper that is farthest from you over the filling tightly. Be careful not to tear it. Fold in the sides, and roll all the way to the end. Repeat this step with the remaining ingredients."]],"h":[]},"4162821":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F. Grease muffin tins with non-stick cooking spray."],[null,"Heat olive oil over medium heat in skillet. Add leeks and red pepper and sauté until tender. Divide vegetables among 6 muffin tins."],[null,"Place one teaspoon of cheese into each muffin compartment and sprinkle with basil."],[null,"Whisk the eggs and season them with black pepper. Pour them over the herbed vegetable and cheese mixture in each compartment."],[null,"Bake the muffins for approximately 20 minutes or until the eggs are firm to the touch."]],"h":[[null,"Leftover muffins can be Enjoy a muffin as a high-protein kept in the refrigerator and snack or have two for a high-protein reheated upon serving. breakfast!"],["Limit or avoid high-potassium vegetables","As part of a kidney-friendly diet, you should enjoy a variety of vegetables to provide you with necessary vitamins, minerals, fiber and antioxidants. Early research has shown that diets higher in vegetables may reduce the amount of waste your kidneys have to excrete. More clinical trials are needed to determine if the efect of eating more vegetables can slow the progression of kidney disease. While vegetables are typically low in salt and phosphorus, they can be high in potassium. Choosing low-potassium vegetables and pre-planning meals will allow you to add a mix of richly colored vegetables in your diet while staying within dietary potassium goals. Shop the perimeter of the grocery store for fresh produce. If purchasing canned or frozen vegetables, read the nutrition facts label and ingredients to avoid items high in salt or potassium. HIGH-POTASSIUM VEGETABLES: Brussels Sprouts, Pumpkin, Sweet Potatoes, Spinach, Tomatoes, Potatoes, Parsnips and Winter Squash. LOW-POTASSIUM VEGETABLES: Alfalfa Sprouts, Green Beans, Cabbage, Cauliflower, Lettuce, Onions, Peppers and Snow Peas."]]},"4300638":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F."],[null,"In a skillet, heat oil over medium heat. Add garlic, zucchini, onion, peppers and corn and sauté until tender."],[null,"Transfer vegetables to an ovenproof dish. Sprinkle cheese over the vegetables."],[null,"In a bowl, whisk the eggs together and season them with pepper and tarragon."],[null,"Pour seasoned eggs over vegetables and cheese."],[null,"Cover frittata mixture with foil and bake for 45 minutes or until the eggs are firm to the touch."],[null,"Serve with toast and enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"* You may substitute 2 cups of liquid egg whites for the 8 eggs. The Frittata will be lighter in color as a result. With egg whites the recipe would be appropriate for transplant patients."]]},"3139":{"s":[[null,"Heat oven to 350º F."],[null,"In small bowl, combine graham cracker crumbs, sugar, 1 teaspoon cinnamon, nutmeg, 1/4 teaspoon cloves and melted butter; stir until blended. Reserve 4 tablespoons of crumbs for topping."],[null,"Press remaining crumbs over bottom and up sides of two 9-inch pie pans."],[null,"Bake for 6 minutes. Cool."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine frosting, sour cream, pumpkin, 1 teaspoon cinnamon, ginger and 1/4 teaspoon cloves. Pour filling into prepared crusts."],[null,"Place mixing bowl and hand-mixer beaters in the freezer for 15 minutes. Put heavy cream in the bowl and beat until soft peaks form. Divide and spread evenly on top of each pie."],[null,"Sprinkle reserved graham cracker crumbs over top."],[null,"Freeze to set up, then refrigerate until ready to serve."],[null,"Store remaining dessert in refrigerator."]],"h":[[null,"You can buy graham cracker crumbs or make your own by crushing 36 graham cracker squares."],[null,"To reduce the fat use Reddi-Wip® dairy whipped topping instead of heavy cream and skip step #6. Instead of spreading on pie, spray about 2 tablespoons on each serving right before it is served. Fat is reduced to 3 grams."]]},"2224":{"s":[[null,"Chop cherries and drain pineapple."],[null,"Place all ingredients except whipped topping into a medium-sized bowl and combine until well blended. Fold in whipped topping."],[null,"Place mixture into a plastic freezable container and freeze 2 to 3 hours until hardened."]],"h":[[null,"If you have diabetes, replace the sugar with 1/2 cup Splenda® granular sweetener or 12 packets tabletop low calorie sweetener. Carbohydrate content is reduced to 13 grams and carbohydrate choices equals one."],[null,"Garnished with maraschino cherry halves for an attractive presentation."],[null,"You can use fresh or frozen strawberries."]]},"6375867":{"s":[[null,"Line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"In a bowl, combine Greek yogurt, syrup, and vanilla extract. Mix until well combined."],[null,"Pour the Greek yogurt mixture onto the prepared baking sheet, spreading it into an even layer with a spatula."],[null,"Scatter sliced strawberries and chopped dark chocolate over the Greek yogurt."],[null,"Place the baking sheet in the freezer and let the yogurt bark freeze for at least 3 hours or until firm."],[null,"Once frozen, break the bark into pieces. Store in an airtight container in the freezer."]],"h":[]},"2660":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375° F. Set butter and cream cheese out to soften."],[null,"In a medium bowl, mix flour, baking soda, and baking powder. Set aside."],[null,"In a large bowl, cream together butter and Splenda until smooth. Beat in egg and 1 teaspoon vanilla."],[null,"Gradually blend in dry ingredients."],[null,"Form teaspoons of dough into balls, and place on ungreased cookie sheet. Flatten the dough ball by pressing down with the bottom of a glass."],[null,"Bake 8 to 10 minutes, or until golden. Remove from oven and let stand until completely cool."],[null,"With a mixer beat cream cheese, sugar and the remaining vanilla extract. Gently fold in the whipped topping."],[null,"Spread cream cheese mixture on half of the cookies, then top each with the remaining cookies to form a sandwich."],[null,"Wrap each cookie in foil and place in the freezer for 1 hour or until ready to eat."]],"h":[[null,"Place the cream cheese mixture in a plastic bag, snip off one tip, and pipe the filling onto the cookie."]]},"7459708":{"s":[[null,"Line a wide baking tray with baking paper. Dollop the yoghurt over the baking paper, then use a spatula or spoon to spread it around evenly, so it's about 1cm thick."],[null,"Evenly scatter over the berries, then freeze for at least 3 hours, or until the bark's completely solid."],[null,"When the bark is ready to eat, leave it to stand at room temperature for 5 minutes to soften slightly, then break into pieces to serve."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"7609589":{"s":[[null,"Add a quarter of the frozen berries to the bottom of a 2lb loaf tin or cake tin."],[null,"Blend the rest of the berries with 150g yoghurt and 1 tbsp of sweetener, then spread it over the berries in the base of the tin. Level with a spatula and place in the freezer, ensuring the tin is level, and leave for 1-1.5 hours."],[null,"Blend the mango with 200g yoghurt then spread on top of the berries. Return the tin to the freezer, again making sure it is level. Freeze for another hour or two, until solid."],[null,"Blend the kiwi with 100g yoghurt and 1 tbsp of sweetener, then add to the top layer, spreading it evenly over the mango. Cover with cling film, then freeze for a least 2 hours or overnight."],[null,"Remove from the freezer for 15 minutes before turning out onto a plate and slicing."]],"h":[[null,"Try using different fruits with colours that contrast."],[null,"If you blend frozen fruit into the yogurt, it will freeze more quickly than fresh fruit."],[null,"To make things easier, cut the yogurt cake with a serrated knife. Dip the knife into hot water, then dry before slicing."],[null,"Use soya alternative in place of yogurt for a vegan option."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Keep frozen. Will last 3 months in the freezer."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"6144849":{"s":[[null,"Line a small baking sheet with wax paper. Set aside."],[null,"Insert the cake pop sticks into the top part of the strawberry. Do not pierce through the end of the strawberry."],[null,"Dip each strawberry in the yogurt, shaking so that each strawberry is thinly coated. Use a spoon to help coat the strawberries if needed."],[null,"Sprinkle 1 teaspoon of pecans over each coated strawberry."],[null,"Place the strawberry pops on the baking sheet and freeze for 1-2 hours or until the yogurt is frozen. Once the pops are frozen, remove from the wax paper and serve or put in a freezer zip top bag."]],"h":[]},"6268899":{"s":[[null,"Combine all ingredients in a blender and puree until smooth and thick."]],"h":[]},"6008159":{"s":[[null,"To make skewers, alternate strawberries, grapes, kiwi slices, and cheese on one skewer (4 strawberry halves, 4 grapes, 2-3 kiwi slices and 3 pieces cheese per skewer)."],[null,"Repeat the process for the remaining 3 skewers."]],"h":[]},"7532555":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180ºC/gas 4 and lightly grease and line a 20cm square baking tin."],[null,"Place all the ingredients in a bowl and mix together."],[null,"Spoon into the baking tin."],[null,"Smooth out and press down slightly, then bake for 35–40 minutes, until golden and firm."],[null,"Mark into 16 pieces. Leave in the tin to cool. Serve when cooled slightly."]],"h":[[null,"To stew the apples: Peel core and chop them then add to a pan with 2 tbsp water. Cover and cook over a gentle heat stirring regularly for 10-15 mins."],[null,"Stewed apples freeze well, so you could make a batch and freeze until needed."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Defrost 2 hours to serve, or defrost in the microwave or an oven at a moderate heat."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"2445":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 325°F."],[null,"Core and thinly slice apple. Combine apple slices and 1/2 tablespoon lemon juice. Cut grapes in half and slice strawberries."],[null,"Cook sugar, pineapple juice, remaining lemon juice, and cornstarch over medium heat until thickened."],[null,"Slice cookie dough in 1/4″ slices. Place close together on pizza pan sprayed with nonstick cooking spray."],[null,"Bake as directed on package or at 325° F until brown. Set aside to cool completely."],[null,"Spread cream cheese on cooled cookie crust."],[null,"Arrange fruit slices on top of cream cheese. Use your imagination to create a masterpiece!"],[null,"Pour cooled pineapple glaze over the fruit and refrigerate several hours before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Other fruit such as blueberries, pears, raspberries can be substituted for the apple, grapes and strawberries."],[null,"For people with diabetes substitute Splenda® granular sweetener for sugar to reduce carbohydrate to 28 grams, 2 carbohydrate choices. Reducing the portion size also helps lower carbohydrate content."],[null,"Instead of making one large pizza, make individual small fruit pizzas. Separate the cookie slices farther apart on a baking pan to bake individual cookies. Top each with the fruit and glaze."]]},"2344":{"s":[[null,"Set the cream cheese out to soften. Separate the egg into the white and yolk. Set aside."],[null,"Combine the flour, butter, cream cheese, egg yolk and 3 tablespoons of the sugar. Using your hands, knead the mixture until well blended and dough holds together. Shape the dough into a ball. Wrap in plastic wrap and refrigerate for 2 hours or overnight."],[null,"When ready to make the cookies, preheat the oven to 350˚ F. Lightly flour a flat surface. With a rolling pin, roll out 1/4 of the dough until thin, about 1/8-inch thick. Keep the rest of the dough refrigerated until ready to use."],[null,"Spread 1/4 cup of the raspberry filling onto the dough circle. Cut the dough into 12 equal wedges."],[null,"Starting on the large side of one wedge, roll to the center, creating a pinwheel. Repeat with remaining 11 wedges. Place cookies pointed side down onto a cookie sheet. Repeat with the remaining dough, working with 1/4 of the dough each time."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix the cinnamon and 2 tablespoons of sugar. In another small bowl, beat the water and egg white. Brush each cookie with the egg white mixture and sprinkle with the cinnamon-sugar mixture. Bake for 25 minutes. Remove to a wire rack to cool."]],"h":[[null,"You may change the filling to another fruit filling, such as apple or cherry."],[null,"Traditional rugelach fillings include cinnamon, chocolate, nuts, marzipan and fruit preserves."]]},"1866":{"s":[[null,"Dice unpeeled apples. Shred cannabe and grate carrots.Drain crushed pineapple; reserve liquid."],[null,"In a small bowl blend mayonnaise, 3 tablespoons of the reserved pineapple juice and sugar until smooth. Set aside."],[null,"In a medium bowl combine pineapple, apples,cabbage, and carrots."],[null,"Add mayonnaise mixture and toss."],[null,"Cover and refrigerate until chilled."]],"h":[[null,"Reduced-fat mayonnaise cuts the fat in half."],[null,"Keeps well in the refrigerator for several days if it lasts that long."],[null,"Make it quick–use packaged coleslaw mix instead of shredding cabbage and carrots."]]},"6028822":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, mix together all fruit."],[null,"Place 1 cup fruit salad in individual bowl or parfait dish. Top each fruit salad with 1 1/2 ounces Greek yogurt."]],"h":[]},"6107817":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400°F. Lightly coat two 8-oz ramekins (4-inch diameter) with cooking spray. Set aside."],[null,"In a medium bowl, whisk together the egg substitute, flour, milk, oil, vanilla, and salt until smooth. Pour half the batter into each ramekin. Set the filled ramekins on a baking sheet."],[null,"Bake for 20 to 25 minutes, or until golden brown and puffy. Remove from the oven. Using the tip of a knife, gently pierce each pancake in one place. Allow to stand for 5 minutes so you don't burn your fingers when handling the ramekins."],[null,"Meanwhile, in a small bowl, gently stir together the raspberries and strawberries. Spoon half of the berries over each cooled pancake, then dollop each with 1 tablespoon yogurt."]],"h":[]},"6446864":{"s":[[null,"In a liquid measuring cup, stir together all ingredients. Serve, or store in a sealed jar in the refrigerator for up to 1 week."]],"h":[]},"6188633":{"s":[[null,"Cut the chicken into cubes or slices."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine the chicken with the apples, grapes, apricots, cherries, celery, and onion."],[null,"Gently fold in the mayonnaise, yogurt, salt, and pepper. Cover and refrigerate for 30 minutes to meld flavors."]],"h":[]},"2511":{"s":[[null,"Dice chicken. Chop celery, onion and apple. Drain and chop water chestnuts."],[null,"In a large salad bowl, combine the chicken, celery, onion, apple, grapes, water chestnuts, pepper, curry powder and mayonnaise."],[null,"Toss all together."],[null,"Serve immediately or chill for later."]],"h":[[null,"To save time, use half a rotisserie chicken with the skin and bones removed."]]},"7247269":{"s":[[null,"Grease a 20 x 25cm cake tin with the oil and preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4."],[null,"Scatter the banana chunks and blueberries evenly over the base of the tin."],[null,"Add the sugar, wholemeal flour, cocoa powder and baking powder to a bowl and mix together well."],[null,"Add the vanilla extract, rapeseed oil and milk to the bowl, and mix again."],[null,"If the cake batter is too thick, gradually add small amounts of milk until it reaches a smooth, pourable consistency."],[null,"Pour evenly over the banana and blueberries, and bake for 15–20 minutes. It's ready when a knife inserted into the centre comes out clean."]],"h":[[null,"You could use any combination of fruits, like pears, blackberries or raspberries, or dried fruits such as raisins, sultanas or prunes."],[null,"If you don’t have fresh berries, defrosted frozen fruit will also work, just drain away any juice."],[null,"For a gluten-free version, use the same amount (50g) in place of the wholewheat flour, you may need to add an extra tablespoon or two of milk (Gluten free flours tend to absorb more moisture than wheat) or use 50g of ground almonds and add 30g of gluten free flour."],[null,"Serve warm with a little crème fraiche, or cold as a cake."],[null,"This also works with a 23cm round cake tin."]]},"7338005":{"s":[[null,"In a bowl, mix together the crème fraiche, yogurt, curry powder and coriander."],[null,"Stir through the remaining ingredients and serve with couscous, toasted pitta or bread of your choice."]],"h":[[null,"Ideal for using leftover roast chicken, or you could buy a portion of ready-cooked chicken."],[null,"If you like your food spicy, add a pinch of chilli flakes."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"3569":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Spray cooking spray on the bottom of a 9″ x 13″ cake pan."],[null,"Dump two cans of undrained peaches (or pineapple) into cake pan and spread evenly."],[null,"Sprinkle the package of yellow cake mix evenly on top of fruit."],[null,"Dot with margarine."],[null,"Bake for 30 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"40 ounces canned fruit is equivalent to 2 cans.You can use pineapple or any of your favorite canned fruit."],[null,"Top with whipped topping if desired."],[null,"If you have diabetes, reduce portion if necessary to stay within your carbohydrate goal."]]},"7493654":{"s":[[null,"Place the water and frozen fruit into a pan and cook over a medium heat for 2-3 minutes until they are warmed through. Stir in the apple and remove from heat."],[null,"Meanwhile, beat the eggs and milk together, then soak the bread slices in the egg mixture for 2-3 minutes. Turn the bread a couple of times to make sure all the liquid has been absorbed."],[null,"Heat the oil in a non-stick frying pan, add the slices of bread, and cook gently. Turn the bread a couple of times until golden brown on both sides. This should take about 8 minutes in total."],[null,"Serve topped with the fruit."]],"h":[[null,"You can use any fruits you like for the topping - pears and blackberries are especially tasty."],[null,"Sprinkle with cinnamon or nutmeg for extra flavour."],[null,"You can also make a savoury version with grilled mushrooms or tomatoes in place of fruit."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"7931899":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4. Melt the spread in a pan on a low heat and set aside, reserving 2 tsp to oil the baking dish."],[null,"Place the oats and flour in a bowl and mix together. Add the prunes, sultanas, mixed spice and ginger. Mix well."],[null,"Add the melted spread and mix. Add the beaten eggs and 100ml water. Mix well."],[null,"Grease a 20cm x 26cm baking tin, place the mixture in and gently press down to about 1cm thick."],[null,"Dust lightly with sweetener and bake for 20-25 minutes."],[null,"Allow to cool, before cutting into 12 pieces and serving."]],"h":[[null,"Use a potato masher to press the mixture evenly into the baking tin."],[null,"Try using other dried fruits, such as chopped apricots or raisins."],[null,"For a lower fat version, replace 50g of the lower-fat spread with a well-beaten banana."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"2253":{"s":[[null,"Mix all ingredients in a blender."],[null,"Divide into 2 portions and serve."]],"h":[[null,"This recipe uses fruit cocktail canned in juice. For a higher calorie smoothie use fruit cocktail packed in light or heavy syrup. For lower calories use fruit canned in water or with artificial sweetener."],[null,"Refrigerate or freeze extra serving for later."],[null,"Ask your dietitian about the best whey protein to use. Products vary in calcium, potassium and phosphorus content."]]},"1002647":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Place two sheets of heavy-duty aluminum foil on your work surface."],[null,"Spread half of the thin lemon slices on each sheet of foil."],[null,"Place cod fillets on top of the lemon slices, 2 fillets or about 6 ounces on each sheet of foil."],[null,"Lightly sprinkle each fillet with the measured amounts of salt and pepper."],[null,"Top each fillet with chopped peppers, then drizzle with olive oil."],[null,"Fold the edges of the foil to seal the fish inside. Place on a baking sheet and bake for 20 minutes. Remove fillets from the foil to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Fresh roasted red peppers can also be substituted."],[null,"When adding very small amounts of salt, try combining it with pepper or other ground spices. Use a refillable salt shaker so you can distribute it evenly over the food."]]},"6548749":{"s":[[null,"Place the peaches, plums and apricots on the grill, cut side down. Grill over low or indirect heat until soft, about 2 to 4 minutes per side."],[null,"Place the fruit on a serving platter and top evenly with yogurt, ground flaxseed and ground almonds."],[null,"Drizzle honey over each serving and garnish with a pinch of cinnamon. If desired, sprinkle chopped pistachios over each one. Serve immediately."]],"h":[]},"7363285":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a saucepan and add the onion. Cook for 4 minutes, stirring regularly. Add the chicken and carrot and cook for a further 4 minutes, again stirring regularly."],[null,"Add the courgette, curry powder, nutmeg, paprika and tomato puree and mix well."],[null,"Add the chilies, tomatoes, and stock, bring to the boil, turn down the heat, cover and simmer gently for 12 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, add 400ml of water to a saucepan and bring to boiling point, turn down the heat and stir in the fufu flour. Keep stirring for 3-4 minutes until all the flour is absorbed and there are no lumps. Remove from the heat, beat vigorously with a wooden spoon and continue to mix for 2 minutes until you have a smooth dough."],[null,"Wet your hands and divide the fufu into four balls. Share the soup between four bowls and carefully place a portion of fufu on top of each pepper soup to serve."]],"h":[[null,"You can make the pepper soup with lamb or beef instead of chicken."],[null,"For a vegan/vegetarian version replace the chicken with a medium chopped aubergine and 200g mushrooms."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"7323191":{"s":[[null,"Place a little meringue into the bottom of 3 tall glasses. Add a little banana, kiwi, paw paw and passion fruit to each glass."],[null,"Spoon a little fromage frais over the fruit."],[null,"Continue to layer the ingredients until they are all used up. Serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"This is also great made with a selection of berries such as strawberries, raspberries and blackberries."]]},"7945459":{"s":[[null,"Boil the sweet potatoes. Cool, then set aside."],[null,"Meanwhile, add 1 tsp of oil to a pan and fry the tofu on each side - 4-5 minutes until crispy - using a little more oil if needed."],[null,"While the tofu is cooking, mix all the ingredients for the dressing together."],[null,"Arrange the sweet potato and vegetables onto 4 plates, sprinkle on the tofu and drizzle with dressing to serve."]],"h":[[null,"To blanch the beans, add to boiling water for 3-4 minutes then immediately plunge into cold water to stop them cooking."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"7393124":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 190°C/ gas 5. Cut the butternut squash into quarters, lengthways. Deseed and rub 1⁄2 tbsp of the olive oil over each, then place in an ovenproof dish or tray and bake in the oven for 30 minutes until they soften and start to brown."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the rest of the oil to a large pan over a medium heat, add the peppers and onion, and stir regularly for 5 minutes. Next, add the paprika, garlic, thyme, aubergine, tomatoes and water. Bring to the boil, stir and cover, then turn down the heat and simmer for 15 minutes."],[null,"Add the lentils, place lid back on and simmer for another 3-4 minutes."],[null,"Once cooked, remove the butternut squash from the oven. Spoon a quarter of the lentil mixture over the squash, sprinkle with plenty of chopped parsley and divide between four plates. Place the remaining lentil mixture in a seperate bowl and serve alongside the squash."]],"h":[[null,"This vegetable stew is also great spooned over baked sweet potatoes or roasted pumpkin instead of butternut squash. You can also spoon it into large rings of marrow and roast it. Or top with filo pastry for a vegetable pie."],[null,"Smoked paprika is a good spice to use in Spanish dishes. It adds a rich, smoky flavour without the fat. You can buy a mild version called dulce or a hotter version called picante. It adds a lovely, smoky warming richness to soups, stews, roast meats or vegetables."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Freeze the stew and squash separately. Defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 6"]]},"2457":{"s":[[null,"Grind all spices."],[null,"Store in an airtight container until ready to use in a recipe."]],"h":[[null,"Garam Masala is a spice mixture used in many recipes from India. It can be used in all meat and rice dishes."],[null,"Try Garam Masala in Tahseen’s Samosa recipe on DaVita.com."]]},"6017870":{"s":[[null,"Combine garbanzo beans, drained tomatoes, and garlic in a salad bowl."],[null,"Mix in arugula. Let sit for 10 minutes to slightly wilt the arugula leaves before serving."]],"h":[]},"6978167":{"s":[[null,"In a medium salad bowl, mix together all salad ingredients."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together dressing ingredients. Pour over bean mixture and toss to coat."]],"h":[]},"6469708":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, combine all ingredients. Mix well."],[null,"Let the salad marinate for 1 hour in the refrigerator."]],"h":[]},"6250173":{"s":[[null,"Spoon the hummus into the bottom of a small glass, mason jar, or clear plastic cup."],[null,"Ensure your carrots, cucumber, and bell peppers are washed."],[null,"Cut carrots into sticks; slice cucumber into spears and slice bell pepper into strips (about 3–4 inches long)."],[null,"Stand the veggie sticks upright by pushing them directly into the hummus. This keeps the vegetables crisp and makes the snack easy to grab and dip."]],"h":[]},"6523980":{"s":[[null,"In a medium saucepan, heat the oil over medium heat, swirling to coat the bottom. Cook the 2 cups chopped vegetables, onion, and seasoning blend for 8 to 10 minutes, or until tender-crisp, stirring occasionally. (If the vegetables get dry or start to scorch, add a little water to the saucepan.)"],[null,"Stir in the broth. Increase the heat to medium high and bring to a boil. Reduce the heat and simmer for 15 minutes so the flavors blend, stirring occasionally. Stir in the spinach. Sprinkle each serving with Parmesan cheese."],[null,"Tips: Chop firmer vegetables, such as carrots, into smaller pieces than more tender vegetables, such as zucchini, so all the vegetables will cook at about the same rate. If you want this dish to be vegetarian, be sure to use vegetable broth instead of chicken broth."]],"h":[]},"4435843":{"s":[[null,"In a bowl, combine cream cheese, garlic and oil and mix with electric mixer until creamy."],[null,"With a spatula, fold the remaining ingredients into the mix."],[null,"Transfer to serving bowl, cover with plastic wrap and chill in the fridge for about 30 minutes."],[null,"Serve with cut vegetables or low-sodium crackers."]],"h":[["Kidney-friendly vegetable dip","Vegetables are an important part of a healthy diet. Eating raw vegetables with a sandwich or as a snack can be an easy way to add them to your meal plan. It can be fun and tasty to dress up your raw vegetables with a dip. Lower-potassium vegetables commonly eaten raw include asparagus, broccoli, carrots, cauliflower, celery, cucumber, snap peas, peppers and radishes. Dips purchased at the grocery store may contain high amounts of sodium as well as phosphate additives. To avoid these it is best to prepare a dip at home. Experiment with a variety of ingredients to create your favorite dip. Start with a base such as sour cream or whipped cream cheese and add a variety of herbs and spices for flavor. Finely chopped fresh onion or garlic can add lots of flavor, too. If desired, add a little heat with a hint of hot pepper sauce. Mix and match flavors to find the ones that you like best. Plain yogurt can be a lower-calorie option for the base of the dip, but it contains more potassium. A lower-fat sour cream or cream cheese can lower the calorie content of the dip as well, but take care when buying these as they commonly contain phosphate additives. Ask your registered dietitian which dip ingredients are right for you."]]},"54928":{"s":[[null,"Rough chop bell pepper, zucchini and onion. Mince garlic. Heat olive oil in skillet. Add chopped vegetables and garlic. Cook and stir for about 10 minutes."],[null,"Add the vegetables to the top of the pita. Evenly divide mozzarella, torn or sliced into pieces, among each pita and fold up like a taco."],[null,"Alternatively, split pita in half. Divide vegetables evenly each of the 8 pita halves. Evenly divide mozzarella, torn or sliced into pieces, among each pita."]],"h":[[null,"The naturally occurring phosphorus in foods like fresh cheese, are only partly absorbed by our bodies. Approximately 40-60%, each food and person are different."],[null,"You can find fresh mozzarella in a slices log. Tear or slice to your likely in the pita."]]},"2770":{"s":[[null,"Clean, wash and dry all vegetables"],[null,"Coarsely chop lettuce and place into a salad bowl."],[null,"Slice cucumber and place on top of lettuce."],[null,"Chop or shred 4 baby carrots and place in salad bowl."],[null,"Cut or break apart broccoli florets into bite-size pieces."],[null,"Combine balsamic vinegar and olive oil and pour over salad."],[null,"Gently toss and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Low-sodium Italian dressing or another favorite salad dressing could be used in place of balsamic vinegar and olive oil."],[null,"A cooked chicken breast can be added to increase protein intake."]]},"2184":{"s":[[null,"Cook garden burger according to package directions, either on the stove top or microwave. When fully cooked, cut into bite-size pieces and set aside."],[null,"Cook the vegetables according to package directions. If you purchase the steam bag, microwave the bag according to package directions and your microwave."],[null,"Mix the sour cream and honey mustard in a small bowl. Portion out 1 cup of vegetables in a bowl, layer garden burger on top and drizzle with sour cream/honey mustard mixture. Mix all together and enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Look for frozen garden or vegetable burgers with the lowest amount of sodium. The recipe was tested with Morningstar® Garden Veggie Burger."],[null,"Any low potassium mixed vegetables or one single vegetable will work as well. Steam bag frozen vegetables are convenient and low in sodium. Try broccoli, cauliflower, mixed corn, green beans, etc."],[null,"Look for plain honey mustard or low-sodium varieties."]]},"2264":{"s":[[null,"Set cream cheese out to soften."],[null,"Finely chop radish, green onion, green pepper and 1/4 cup cucumber. Drain cucumber."],[null,"Cut carrots and celery into sticks. Slice bell peppers and remaining 2 cucumbers into slices. Arrange vegetables on a serving tray."],[null,"In a large mixing bowl, place cream cheese, sour cream, radish, green onion, 1/4-cup chopped cucumber, 1/4-cup chopped green pepper, sugar, salt and Mrs. Dash. Mix with an electric mixer on low speed for about 1 minute until well blended."],[null,"Spoon into a serving bowl."]],"h":[[null,"Serve dip with low-sodium crackers instead of vegetables if desired."],[null,"Allow 2 pieces of each vegetable per serving."]]},"7064882":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 190° C / gas 5. Scrub the mussels really well and remove the beards. Discard any with damaged shells and those that don’t shut tight when tapped on the edge of the sink. Rinse well."],[null,"Put all the mussels in a saucepan and cover with a tight-fitting lid. Place over a high heat and cook for 2 mins, shaking the pan halfway, until all the shells have steamed open but the mussels are only just cooked. Discard any that don’t open. Tip into a colander over a bowl and save the liquid."],[null,"Once cooled slightly, remove the mussels from their shells and reserve 40 half-shells ready to serve. Chop the mussels then set aside."],[null,"Add oil to a pan, add the onion and red pepper and cook over a medium heat for 5 minutes. Add the garlic and cook for a further 2 minutes, stirring regularly until soft."],[null,"Add the liquid from the mussels and cook 4-5 minutes, stirring regularly until the liquid almost completely evaporates, then remove from heat."],[null,"Stir in the chopped mussels, peas, parsley, black pepper and 30g of breadcrumbs."],[null,"Stuff each mussel with some of the mixture, mounding into the shell. Mix the remaining breadcrumbs and parmesan together and press a little into the top of each mussel, scattering the rest over the stuffed mussels."],[null,"Arrange on a baking tray and bake 15 minutes until the stuffing is a pale golden brown and the mussels are hot. Transfer the shells to your serving plate and eat immediately."]],"h":[[null,"You could prepare the vegetables for the stuffing in advance and just add the mussels before baking."]]},"7618221":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4. Put the oil into a saucepan over a low heat, add the onions and gently cook for 25 minutes, stirring regularly, until they begin to caramelise, turn brown and become soft. If they start to stick, add a teaspoon of water."],[null,"Meanwhile, mix the crushed garlic, chopped parsley, pepper and olive oil together and set aside."],[null,"Slice the baguette into 2cm-thick rings, cutting only about three-quarters of the way through the loaf so that it stays together."],[null,"Stir the onions into the garlic and parsley mixture. Place a spoonful in between each ring of bread, dividing evenly between the slices."],[null,"Fully wrap the bread in foil, and bake for 10-12 minutes. Undo the foil, top with the mozzarella cheese and bake for a further 5 minutes before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Caramelising the onions will cook them down to about one third of the raw quantity. It's important to cook them really slowly and stir regularly with a wooden spoon."],[null,"Use a wholemeal baguette to boost the fibre content."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Can be frozen ready-to-cook or cooked. Slice, then wrap in foil to freeze. You can then defrost slices as required."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"6008382":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F. Place the chicken pieces, oil, garlic, white parts of the green onion, and lemon juice in a deep-sided 9x13-inch baking pan. Stir to coat, then bake for 12 minutes or until the chicken is fully cooked."],[null,"Meanwhile, cook the linguine according to package directions, omitting added oil and salt. Drain the linguine, return to the pot, and toss with butter."],[null,"Stir the arugula and green parts of the green onion into the chicken, then toss the chicken mixture with the linguine. Sprinkle with salt and pepper. Serve hot on a large platter."]],"h":[]},"3749":{"s":[[null,"Wash and trim excess fat from chicken breasts."],[null,"Coat both sides of chicken breast with pepper."],[null,"Heat olive oil in nonstick skillet over medium-high heat, and cook until nicely browned on one side (about 3 minutes)."],[null,"Add garlic, turn chicken and scatter mushrooms all over."],[null,"Move chicken and mushrooms around to keep them from sticking and cook about 3 minutes."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix balsamic vinegar, low-sodium chicken broth, bay leaf, thyme leaves and cornstarch."],[null,"Add mixture to skillet with chicken. Stir until sauce is thickened."],[null,"Cover and cook over moderately-low heat for about 10 minutes."],[null,"Remove bay leaf and garlic before serving. Serve over rice or pasta."]],"h":[[null,"If you are on a lower protein diet, try this recipe but reduce the portion to match your diet plan."],[null,"Refrigerate leftover chicken to use in a salad or sandwich the next day."]]},"2848":{"s":[[null,"Peel and slice the potatoes into small pieces.Double-boil to reduce potassium if you are on a low potassium diet. (see helpful hints.)"],[null,"Boil potatoes and garlic over medium heat until soft."],[null,"Drain off cooking water."],[null,"Whip potatoes and garlic with beater, slowly adding butter and milk until whipped smooth."]],"h":[[null,"Double the garlic for a stronger garlic flavor."],[null,"Potatoes are very high in potassium but you can remove part of the potassium by using the double boil method:"],[null,"Double boil method: Peel and small dice potatoes. Place in a large pot of water and bring to a boil. Drain the water and add fresh water to the pot. Bring to a boil, cook for 10 minutes then drain and prepare as desired."],[null,"Boiled potatoes can be frozen in batches."],[null,"*Potassium content taken from reference values for double-boiling small peeled and diced potatoes."]]},"3943":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 250° F."],[null,"Mix oil and garlic powder in a large bowl. Stir in crackers, coating evenly."],[null,"Sprinkle in dill weed and toss to mix."],[null,"Spread crackers on a cookie sheet and bake 45 minutes. Gently mix every 15 minutes."],[null,"Spread crackers on paper towels to cool. Store in an airtight container until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"One 12 ounce bag oyster crackers contains 7 cups."],[null,"Serve snack-size portions in small paper cups."],[null,"Add your favorite low sodium herb seasoning or chili powder for a spicier mix."]]},"9940851":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 425°F/218°C convection roast and line a baking tray with parchment paper."],[null,"Use a sharp knife to cut your cauliflower into small bite-sized florets and place them in a large bowl."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine the garlic, vinegar, lemon juice, and salt. Then pour the mixture over your cauliflower and mix well to evenly coat the pieces."],[null,"Arrange the cauliflower on your prepared tray in a single layer with plenty of space in between each piece. Roast for 10 minutes and remove from the oven to sprinkle with the vegan parmesan cheese. Then, return to the oven for an additional 6-8 minutes, until golden brown."]],"h":[[null,"Cut your cauliflower florets into evenly sized pieces (as best as you can), for even cooking. Make sure to arrange the cauliflower in a single layer with plenty of space in between each piece. This will speed up the cooking time, and result in crispier edges. If you do not have a convection oven , follow the same directions, but you may need to add a few minutes of roasting time. This vegan roasted cauliflower tastes best when freshly made, but leftovers will keep in the fridge for 3-4 days."]]},"2938":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400° F. Line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Cut each pita bread into 8 triangles and place on the baking sheet."],[null,"In a small bowl combine oil, black pepper and garlic powder."],[null,"Using a pastry brush coat the top of each pita triangle with oil mixture."],[null,"Bake for 6 to 8 minutes or until lightly browned and crispy. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Store pita chips in an airtight container for up to one week."],[null,"If thinner chips are preferred separate each pita triangle to single thickness and coat with olive oil mixture before baking."],[null,"For variety, replace garlic powder with your favorite salt-free seasoning blend."],[null,"Serve chips with your favorite kidney-friendly dip."],[null,"Look for pita bread with the lowest sodium content."]]},"6956969":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F. Cut each pita into 8 equal wedges. Separate each wedge into 2 pieces."],[null,"Coat both sides of the pita wedges lightly with nonstick vegetable spray and place in a single layer on large rimmed baking sheets; sprinkle with the garlic powder. Bake for 15 minutes, or until golden and crisp."],[null,"Allow the crisps to cool; serve immediately, or store in an airtight container until ready to use."]],"h":[]},"3494":{"s":[[null,"Peel the garlic cloves."],[null,"Place garlic, salt and 1/2 tablespoon lemon juice in the base of a blender."],[null,"While blending or processing, slowly pour in 1/3 cup of the olive oil in a thin stream. Mixture will become thick and white like a salad dressing."],[null,"Add remaining lemon juice and blend. Slowly add the remaining olive oil and blend until thick."],[null,"Store garlic sauce in a covered glass jar for up to 2 weeks."]],"h":[[null,"Use garlic sauce in place of mayonnaise or incorporated into dips, salad dressings and marinades. Add a spoonful to casseroles, soups, stews, cooked vegetables and stir-fry dishes."],[null,"You can use an emersion blender or food processor instead of a counter top blender."]]},"6338589":{"s":[[null,"Heat the olive oil in a large pot over medium-high heat. Add the garlic and sauté for 30 seconds."],[null,"Add the remaining ingredients to the pot; mix well."],[null,"Reduce the heat to low, cover, and cook for 5-7 minutes."]],"h":[]},"4407130":{"s":[[null,"In a large pot, cook pasta according to instructions. Reserve ½ cup of water before draining the pasta."],[null,"In a large skillet, over medium heat, melt butter with olive oil. Sauté garlic, red pepper, and broccoli."],[null,"Add shrimp, pasta water, pepper, and chili flakes. Simmer until the shrimp are cooked and turn pink."],[null,"Add the cooked linguine and oregano to the skillet. Toss to combine. Serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"PLEASE NOTE: This recipe is higher in potassium and portion size is important. Check with your registered dietitian to see how this recipe can be included in your diet. For individuals with CKD not on dialysis, reduce the amount of protein by reducing the amount of shrimp."],["Shellfish in the kidney diet","Shellfish like shrimp, crab, and lobster can be a good source of protein in a kidney-friendly diet. Smoked and canned versions should be avoided, as they can be high in sodium. Eating raw shellfish is not recommended due to the risk of food poisoning, so cooking it properly is the safest way to eat it. When compared to fish and other types of shellfish, shrimp is lower in potassium and can be included in a low-potassium diet. Some are worried about the cholesterol content of shrimp compared to other types of seafood. Even though shrimp has more cholesterol, the amount is still reasonable for a kidney-friendly diet. Most shrimp is frozen soon after it is caught so the freshest shrimp you can buy is typically in the freezer aisle. Look for shrimp that is free from added phosphates or salt. Shrimp is easy to prepare via sautéing, broiling, grilling, or boiling. Use the same spices you use to season fish to season shellfish. Flavors that pair best with shrimp include lemon, garlic, dill, crushed red pepper flakes, basil, and cilantro. Serve prepared shrimp over rice or pasta, with kidney-friendly roasted vegetables, on a bed of salad greens, and as a main ingredient for tacos."]]},"6252687":{"s":[[null,"Steam shrimp in large pot with a steamer basket insert. Cook just until pink, about 5-6 minutes."],[null,"Mix in lemon juice, garlic, olive oil, chopped dill, salt, and pepper. Marinate shrimp in this mixture for at least 1 hour and up to 24 hours. Refrigerate while marinating."],[null,"Scrub cucumber well. Take a fork and run it up and down the outside of cucumber to make a decorative edge. Slice cucumber into 24 rounds."],[null,"Place one piece of shrimp on a cucumber slice and garnish with another sprig of fresh dill. Cover and refrigerate until serving time."]],"h":[]},"6208885":{"s":[[null,"Whisk all ingredients together in a bowl or shake in a salad dressing shaker."],[null,"Serve over Pinto Bean, Brown Rice and Spinach Salad."]],"h":[]},"2269":{"s":[[null,"Slice eggplant into 1-1/2-inch long pieces. Mince garlic cloves. Chop basil."],[null,"Heat sesame oil in a large skillet. Add eggplant, ginger, garlic, mushrooms and bean sprouts. Stir-fry over medium-high heat until eggplant begins to soften, 4-6 minutes."],[null,"Add basil, chili pepper flakes and hoisin sauce to eggplant. Continue cooking for 1-2 minutes. Remove from heat and serve."]],"h":[[null,"If Chinese eggplant is unavailable, substitute regular eggplant. Cut into 1-inch cubes (unpeeled)."],[null,"Hoisin sauce is a soybean paste product available in the ethnic food section of most grocery stores. One tablespoon hoisin sauce contains 250 mg sodium (63 mg per serving). Look for Sun Luck brand, available from Sun Luck of Seattle, Washington. A very small amount adds lots of flavor!"]]},"6514294":{"s":[[null,"Heat sesame oil in a large skillet. Add eggplant, ginger, garlic, mushrooms and bean sprouts. Stir-fry over medium-high heat until eggplant begins to soften, 4-6 minutes."],[null,"Add basil, chili pepper flakes and hoisin sauce to eggplant. Continue cooking for 1-2 minutes. Remove from heat and serve."]],"h":[]},"1818":{"s":[[null,"Cook pasta according to instructions, omitting salt."],[null,"Cut asparagus into 2″ pieces. Mince garlic."],[null,"In a medium skillet heat olive oil and butter over medium heat. Add garlic and red pepper flakes and sauté for 2-3 minutes."],[null,"Add asparagus, Tabasco sauce, lemon juice and black pepper to skillet and cook for 6 minutes until tender crisp."],[null,"Drain pasta and transfer to a bowl. Add asparagus and toss."],[null,"Top with shredded cheese and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Thicker asparagus stalks may require longer cooking time."],[null,"Add diced cooked chicken or shrimp to make an entrée dish."],[null,"Adjust red pepper flakes and Tabasco sauce to taste."]]},"6665652":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400°F."],[null,"Leaving the head of garlic whole, cut off 1/4 to 1/2 inch of the top of head, exposing the individual cloves of garlic. Leave the peel on."],[null,"Place the garlic head cut side up onto a sheet of foil. Drizzle one Tsp. of olive oil over the cut side of the garlic head. Fold foil up around the garlic and pinch to seal to make a packet."],[null,"Bake at 400°F for 30-35 minutes, or until the cloves feel soft when pressed."],[null,"Allow the garlic to cool slightly to the touch. Squeeze the roasted garlic cloves out of their skins into a small bowl and mash with a fork to make a paste."],[null,"In a large sauté pan, add remaining olive oil and a generous amount of cooking spray over medium high heat. Add the onions and sauté until just starting to caramelize."],[null,"Add the roasted garlic paste and stir until the onions are coated. Add the spinach and sauté until the spinach is wilted and coated with the garlic and onions."],[null,"Season with salt and pepper."]],"h":[]},"6924449":{"s":[[null,"Place a layer of lettuce leaves on a serving platter or on four plates and arrange the sliced tomatoes. Place the cherry tomatoes on top."],[null,"Whisk together the garlic, vinegar, mustard, oil, salt, and pepper and pour over the tomatoes."],[null,"Scatter the basil leaves and the pumpkin and sunflower seeds over the tomatoes and serve at once."]],"h":[]},"7688306":{"s":[[null,"Place half of the tomatoes in a food processor or blender along with the passata, vinegar, oil, sugar and Tabasco (if using). Blend until smooth, if the mixture is a little thick then add a little more tomato juice."],[null,"Stir through the remaining ingredients, add a few ice cubes and serve."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"4937676":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, mix all ingredients of the sauce and set aside."],[null,"In a big bowl, mix the tofu cubes and the corn starch. Put the cubes on a plate and set aside."],[null,"In a non-stick frying pan or wok, heat the oil over medium-high heat. Fry the tofu in stages until all cubes are slightly browned."],[null,"Line a plate with a paper towel and transfer the tofu to the plate to absorb excess oil."],[null,"Add the green onions, ginger and garlic to the frying pan or wok and fry for 1–2 minutes. Add a bit of oil if necessary."],[null,"Add the sauce and bring everything to a boil while stirring constantly (approximately 2 minutes)."],[null,"Add the tofu and stir until all ingredients are hot and ready to serve."],[null,"Serve with steamed rice."]],"h":[[null,"* Look for low or reduced-sodium broth containing 200mg sodium or less per 1 cup serving. Avoid low-sodium broth that contains potassium chloride—it’s very high in potassium."],[null,"Tofu is a great vegetarian source of protein. You can use other allowed vegetables and sources of protein for this stir-fry. Try peppers, green beans, chicken or shrimp."],["Low-potassium snacks","If you are on the run, need a fast bite to eat or have the late night munchies, snacks can be incorporated as part of your kidney-friendly diet. Most of the potassium in your diet should come from breakfast, lunch and dinner. Keep low-potassium snacks available to grab something quick without overdoing your daily limit. Choose from the diferent food groups to keep snacks interesting. Also keep in mind that heavily processed foods contain additives, salt and possible hidden potassium sources. Be sure to read the label to identify these foods. Grab a piece of fruit or a handful of vegetables for a low-calorie and low-potassium option. Choose a medium apple, a half-cup of grapes or a small handful of carrot and red pepper sticks. If you prefer a crunchy snack, stick with a portion of animal crackers, rice cakes or unsalted pretzels. A small portion of vanilla wafers and a refreshing popsicle are sweet snack options. Add extra protein to your snack by selecting a hard-boiled egg, a slice of deli meat or a kidney-friendly nutritional shake."]]},"6659814":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F, and a coat baking sheet with cooking spray. Set aside."],[null,"Pat tofu dry with a paper towel."],[null,"Marinate the tofu: Combine 1 tsp soy sauce, 2 tsp rive vinegar, 1 tsp oil, half of the minced garlic and half of the grated ginger in a bowl. Add tofu and toss to coat. Marinate 30 minutes."],[null,"Sprinkle 1 tbsp cornstarch over tofu and turn to coat evenly. Spread tofu on the baking sheet in a single layer. Bake 30 minutes, turning frequently, or until brown all sides."],[null,"While the tofu is baking, whisk together broth, honey, remaining 1 tbsp soy sauce, remaining tbsp vinegar, sesame oil, remaining 2 tsp cornstarch, tomato paste and hot sauce in small bowl. Set aside."],[null,"Add remaining 2 tsp vegetable oil to a large sauté pan or wok over medium-high heat. Add scallions and the rest of the garlic and ginger, and stir-fry 1 minute. Add sauce mixture and cook 2-3 minutes, or until thickened."],[null,"Stir the baked tofu and broccoli into the sauce and serve."]],"h":[]},"3097":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 325° F. Grease a 9 x 13-inch baking dish. Set butter out to soften. Peel, core and slice apples."],[null,"Using a mixer, cream the butter and sugar until light and fluffy. Zest the lemon. Add the lemon zest and vanilla extract to butter and sugar mixture. Add one egg and continue to mix; add the other egg and mix."],[null,"In a separate bowl combine the flour, cinnamon, baking soda and salt. Gradually add the dry ingredients to the creamed butter until combined. Do not over mix."],[null,"Juice the lemon; stir the juice into the batter. Stir in the apple slices."],[null,"Pour the batter into the greased baking dish. Sprinkle one tablespoon of sugar over the top. Bake for 30 to 40 minutes. The cake is done when a toothpick inserted into the middle of the cake comes out clean. After cake is cool cut into 15 pieces and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Use apple variety of choice."],[null,"Cut the cake into 20 pieces for a lower carbohydrate serving (23 grams)."]]},"2687":{"s":[[null,"In a medium bowl, combine the flour and sugar. Add the eggs and blend well with a whisk."],[null,"Add the milk and vanilla extract. Beat until smooth."],[null,"Pour 3 tablespoons of the batter into a heated 8″ or 10″ nonstick skillet, sprayed with nonstick cooking spray. Tilt the pan quickly to spread the batter. Cook until the pancake is brown on underside (about 45 seconds; edges will begin to dry). Flip the pancake and brown the other side. Continue until all the batter is used."],[null,"Fold or roll thin pancakes and serve with fruit spread, jam or syrup. If desired, add 1 to 2 tablespoons of ricotta or cream cheese for a filling."]],"h":[[null,"If you have diabetes, use fruit spread or sugar-free syrup as topping."],[null,"Nutrient analysis does not include toppings. See chart below for selections."]]},"3230":{"s":[[null,"Add all ingredients to a blender and blend until smooth."],[null,"Divide into 2 glasses."]],"h":[[null,"Frozen fruit is a great option if fresh isn’t available. If using frozen, you can omit the ice."],[null,"Protein powder is a great way to add protein to your diet but if you are trying to stick to a low protein diet, the recipe is delicious without."]]},"2644":{"s":[[null,"To prepare ginger syrup, place sugar*, grater ginger and water in a medium saucepan; bring to boil. Reduce heat to low and simmer for 1 hour until ginger flavor is strong. Strain mixture and refrigerate to chill."],[null,"To prepare Ginger-Apple Sparkler, place one tablespoon ginger syrup in each glass (use short tumblers)."],[null,"Fill with ice cubes, pour in 1/2-cup cider and stir to combine."],[null,"Garnish with cinnamon stick and crystallized ginger."]],"h":[[null,"Syrup may be stored in the refrigerator up to 2 weeks."],[null,"Ginger is often used to help treat nausea and motion sickness."],[null,"*For those with diabetes, omit the sugar in ginger syrup. Instead, make concentrated ginger-flavored water. Sweeten to taste with sugar substitute. Nutrients decrease to 61 calories, 15 grams carbohydrate."]]},"6359083":{"s":[[null,"In a medium saucepan, bring milk to a gentle simmer."],[null,"Stir in the oats, brown sugar substitute, grated ginger, chia seeds, cinnamon, and vanilla."],[null,"Cook the mixture over medium heat, stirring occasionally, until the oats are creamy and the liquid is absorbed (about 5–7 minutes)."],[null,"Serve the oatmeal in bowls, topped with fresh berries and walnuts."]],"h":[]},"2110":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Peel and chop apples. Combine apples, brown sugar, lemon juice, 1 cup water and 1/2 teaspoon cinnamon in a medium saucepan. Cover and cook until apples are tender."],[null,"Mix cornstarch and 1 tablespoon water together and stir into hot apple mixture. Continue cooking until thickened. Pour apple mixture into 1-1/2 quart casserole and set aside."],[null,"Add 1 tablespoon vinegar to milk and stir. Set aside."],[null,"Beat together sugar, egg, milk mixture, molasses, corn syrup and oil."],[null,"In a separate bowl, stir together flour, baking soda, baking powder, ginger and remaining 1/4 teaspoon cinnamon. Add to beaten egg and milk mixture and beat until smooth."],[null,"Pour gingerbread mixture over apples in casserole. Bake for 30 minutes."],[null,"Serve warm with 1 tablespoon whipped dessert topping or whipped cream."]],"h":[[null,"Four medium-sized apples yields approximately 4 cups."],[null,"For those with diabetes: to reduce carbohydrate content, replace brown sugar and white sugar with Splenda® granular, no-calorie sweetener and Splenda brown sugar blend or sweetener of choice. This change decreases carbohydrate to 26 grams per serving and 2 carbohydrate choices."]]},"9716519":{"s":[[null,"Line a platter or baking sheet with parchment paper and set it aside."],[null,"Then add everything except the optional coconut to your food processor. Pulse until combined and sticky enough to roll into balls."],[null,"Use a small cookie scoop or tablespoon to scoop the mixture, then roll it into a ball, and place each one on your tray. You should get about 14 balls, each 1 tablespoon of the mixture."],[null,"Optional: Roll some or all of the balls into the coconut."],[null,"Refrigerate for 1 hour or longer to harden your gingerbread bliss balls."]],"h":[]},"7068047":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 180°C/gas 4."],[null,"Beat the egg in a bowl. Add the oil and artificial sweetener, and mix well."],[null,"Stir in the flour, baking powder and ginger, and mix again."],[null,"Roll out the mixture to about 1cm thick and cut out your chosen shapes. If hanging on a tree, carefully make a hole for ribbon in one end with a skewer or chopstick. Roll out the leftover dough and cut out more shapes as you go."],[null,"Place on a lightly oiled baking tray and cook for 8–10 minutes."],[null,"Place on a rack to cool and decorate with the silver or gold paint. Thread the ribbons through and knot to make a loop. Hang on your tree."]],"h":[[null,"If you’re hanging the biscuits, after 3-4 minutes cooking time check the holes are still open and if necessary carefully press the skewer or chopstick through again while they are on the baking sheet."],[null,"You could add cinnamon or a pinch of cloves for a different flavour."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"9814933":{"s":[[null,"Add all the ingredients to a high speed blender and process until smooth and creamy."],[null,"Refrigerate the dip for at least 1 hour before serving it with apple slices, pineapple, strawberries, gingerbread cookies, or graham crackers."]],"h":[[null,"If you do not have a strong blender , soak your cashews in boiling hot water for 30 minutes first. This will soften them, making them easier to blend. Then drain them, add to the blender with the remaining ingredients, and process until smooth. The vegan cheesecake dip will keep refrigerated for 4-5 days or freeze for up to 2 months. TIP – freeze the dip for 1-2 hours and enjoy it as vegan gingerbread ice cream!"]]},"6481807":{"s":[[null,"Coat a 3 ½ - to 4-quart slow cooker with cooking spray. Add the pumpkin, pears, onions, broth, cumin, nutmeg, salt, and cayenne to the slow cooker. Cover and cook on high for 3 ½ hours, or on low for 7 hours, or until onions are tender."],[null,"Working in 1-cup batches, purée the pumpkin mixture in a blender, being sure to secure the lid tightly while blending. Return the mixture to the slow cooker, stir in the remaining ingredients, except the yogurt. Cover and cook on high for 30 more minutes."],[null,"Serve topped with 1 tbsp of yogurt."]],"h":[]},"2608":{"s":[[null,"Sift the flour, baking soda, cloves, ginger and cinnamon together."],[null,"Cream softened butter with a mixer until light and fluffy; gradually add sugar."],[null,"Blend in the egg and molasses."],[null,"Add the flour mixture a small amount at a time, until a dough forms."],[null,"Cover and refrigerate dough for 1 hour or overnight."],[null,"Preheat oven to 350˚ F."],[null,"Form dough into balls (heaping teaspoon size) and place 2-inches apart on a greased cookie sheet, flattening each ball slightly."],[null,"Bake for 8 to 10 minutes. Cool on a wire rack. Makes 4 dozen cookies."]],"h":[[null,"Store in a covered container."],[null,"Gingersnap Cookies are a yummy kitchen gift during the holidays–or anytime!"]]},"5827557":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 180°C/160°C Fan/350° F/Gas 4."],[null,"In a large bowl, cream together the butter and sugar."],[null,"Add the golden syrup and dry ingredients and beat to combine."],[null,"Once everything is combined, using your hands (make sure they are clean!) roll the mixture out into little balls, keeping each even in size."],[null,"Place 3cm apart on a greased baking tray and lightly press down using a fork."],[null,"Bake in the oven for 15 minutes or until golden brown."]],"h":[]},"3760":{"s":[[null,"Slice carrots into 1-inch thick slices. Place carrots and 1/4 cup water in a pot. Cover and cook until slightly tender."],[null,"Mix together sugar, cornstarch, salt, ginger, apple juice and melted butter. Pour mixture over carrots and water."],[null,"Cook, stirring occasionally, for 10 minutes or until mixture thickens."]],"h":[[null,"Fresh carrots are best but you can substitute frozen carrots."],[null,"If desired, replace ginger with ground cinnamon."]]},"3292":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375° F. In a small saucepan melt the butter."],[null,"Remove and discard giblets from cavity of thawed game hen. Rinse and pat dry. Rub the skin and inside cavity with a tablespoon of the melted butter. Place hen in oven and bake for 20 minutes."],[null,"Add the jam, mustard and Worcestershire sauce to the remaining melted butter; heat and stir until combined."],[null,"After baking for 20 minutes brush the hen with the apricot glaze. Bake 20 to 30 minutes longer, basting with the glaze every 10 minutes. Remove from oven when internal temperature reaches 165° F."],[null,"Let the hen rest for 10 minutes then cut in half and place on serving plates. Heat the remaining glaze to a boil then pour over each half before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Nutrient analysis includes skin after baking. For a lower fat/calorie meal remove the skin."]]},"9126167":{"s":[[null,"If working ahead, freeze your tofu and thaw it before pressing. If not, just press to remove as much excess moisture as possible for the best texture."],["Press the tofu (quick press method)","Cut your tofu into cubes. Then arrange some paper towels or a clean dish towel on a cutting board and place the cubes in a single layer on top. Add another clean towel on top, followed by another cutting board, flat plate or baking sheet. Finally, place something very heavy on top like a cast iron skillet or heavy books. Press like this for 15 minutes while you prepare the remaining ingredients."],["Prepare the tofu hot dogs","Preheat the oven to 350℉/176℃ and grab a small baking tray. (No need to line it.)"],["Prepare the tofu hot dogs","Add the pressed tofu and everything else except the flour to your food processor. Process until combined. Then add 4 tablespoons of flour and pulse until combined. Check the consistency of your mixture, you want it slightly softer than Play-Doh. If it's very soft/wet, add the remaining flour and pulse again."],["Prepare the tofu hot dogs","Decide if you're making 4 jumbo dogs or 8 smaller weiners. (Photographed are jumbo dogs.) Then cut 4 or 8 square sheets of parchment paper and aluminum foil, accordingly."],["Prepare the tofu hot dogs","Divide your dough into 4 or 8 portions and place each on a parchment paper square with the aluminum foil below it. If you want perfectly portioned tofu dogs, use a kitchen scale, otherwise eyeball it."],["Prepare the tofu hot dogs","Use your hands to shape the dough into a hot dog/log shape, and then snugly wrap it in the parchment and foil, twisting the ends like a candy wrapper. Place each wrapped dog on your baking tray and bake."],["Baking Instructions","For 4 jumbo dogs bake them for 40 minutes, then flip and continue baking another 30-40 minutes until firm to the touch.For 8 smaller tofu dogs bake for 30 minutes, then flip and continue baking for another 20-30 minutes until firm to the touch.Remove from the oven, unwrap and let them rest for 5 minutes before grilling or serving. (If working ahead, you may leave them wrapped and refrigerate overnight.)"],["Grilling Instructions (optional)","Grill your tofu hot dogs for 2-3 minutes on each side for lovely grill marks if you'd like. Or you may enjoy the dogs straight out of the oven."]],"h":[[null,"There is no added salt since I’m using Tamari which I find salty enough. However, you may add salt to your taste if needed."],[null,"You want a slightly softer than Play-Doh consistency , so start with less flour and add more only if needed. The flour required will vary according to how long you’ve pressed your tofu, and if you’re using thawed from frozen."],[null,"If you don't like having foil touch your food (like me), use parchment paper between the tofu hot dogs and aluminum foil layer."]]},"6461143":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350 degrees F. Spray a 8x4-inch loaf pan with cooking spray."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine bananas, oil, buttermilk, egg whites, vanilla, and low- or no-calorie sweetener; mix well."],[null,"Add gluten-free baking mix and flaxseed and mix until blended. Pour batter into loaf pan. Bake for 30–35 minutes or until toothpick inserted in center comes out clean."]],"h":[]},"6420195":{"s":[[null,"Spoon 3/4 cup nonfat Greek yogurt into a small bowl."],[null,"Add 1/2 cup blackberries over the yogurt."],[null,"Sprinkle 1/4 cup gluten-free granola on top."],[null,"Serve immediately to keep the granola crisp."]],"h":[]},"6639654":{"s":[[null,"* Many regular cornbread mixes contain flour and are not gluten-free. If you are following a gluten-free diet, make sure that your cornbread mix is gluten-free."],[null,"Preheat oven to 375 degrees. Line muffin tins with 22 muffin papers and spray with cooking spray."],[null,"In a large bowl combine cornbread mix, buttermilk, oil, egg, egg whites, lemon juice and 1/4 cup of low- or no-calorie sweetener. Mix with an electric mixer on low speed until blended. Mix on high for 30 seconds."],[null,"Gently fold blueberries into muffin batter."],[null,"Spoon about 1/4 cup batter or less into each muffin cup. Sprinkle 1 Tbsp. low- or no-calorie sweetener on top of muffins (evenly divided)."],[null,"Bake for 22 minutes or lightly browned on top. Cool on a wire rack."]],"h":[]},"6216158":{"s":[[null,"In a medium bowl, mix together the chicken, mayonnaise, hummus, celery, pepper, and thyme."],[null,"Spread 1/2 cup of the chicken salad in the middle of 1 wrap. Top with 1 cup of the field greens and 1 slice of the tomato. Fold left and right sides of the wrap in until they touch, and roll from the bottom to make a wrap."],[null,"Repeat procedure for remaining 3 wraps."]],"h":[]},"6498928":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F. Line muffin tins with muffin papers and spray the papers with cooking spray."],[null,"In a large bowl, mix together the oil, sugar substitute, and vanilla. Add the bananas and eggs one at a time. Mix well."],[null,"Stir in the baking mix, oats, cocoa powder, and water."],[null,"Spoon the batter into 12 muffin cups. Top each muffin with mini chocolate chips (distribute evenly over all muffins.)"],[null,"Bake for 20-22 minutes or until a toothpick inserted in the center comes out clean."],[null,"Remove from the oven and let the muffins cool in the pan for 10 minutes. Remove the muffins from the pan and cool completely on a wire rack."]],"h":[]},"6990463":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6638471":{"s":[[null,"Line a small plate or tray with parchment paper."],[null,"In a bowl, gently fold 1 cup raspberries into ¾ cup nonfat Greek yogurt, keeping some berries whole for texture."],[null,"Spoon small dollops of the mixture onto the parchment to form clusters."],[null,"Freeze for 1–2 hours, or until fully firm."],[null,"Enjoy straight from the freezer."]],"h":[]},"6400204":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6989513":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375 degrees F. Spray a baking sheet with cooking spray."],[null,"In a medium bowl, mix together baking mix and margarine. Use a fork and hands to mix into course crumbs."],[null,"Add milk to mixture and stir with a fork. Add Parmesan cheese and incorporate into mixture."],[null,"Drop about 1 Tbsp. at a time of dough mixture on baking sheet for each biscuit. Bake for 12 minutes or until golden brown on top."]],"h":[]},"6367232":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350 degrees. Line baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"In a large bowl, whisk together margarine, vanilla, egg, and low- or no-calorie sweetener. Mix until well blended."],[null,"Add oats, quinoa and baking mix to mixture and stir well. Fold in chocolate chips."],[null,"Drop by Tbsp. onto baking sheet. Bake for 15 minutes."],[null,"Cool on wire rack and store in airtight container when cool."]],"h":[]},"4200838":{"s":[[null,"Heat oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat."],[null,"Sauté garlic and asparagus until fragrant (1-2 minutes)."],[null,"Add rotini, goat cheese, lemon zest, lemon juice, black pepper and water."],[null,"Bring to boil and simmer for 7 minutes or until pasta is cooked and sauce thickened."],[null,"Remove from heat and add frozen peas and oregano."],[null,"Toss to combine and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Try different herbs to vary the flavor of this dish such as tarragon, basil or parsley"],["Eating your vegetables","Including vegetables as a part of your balanced kidney diet is important not only to add more flavors but also to incorporate different vitamins, minerals and fiber. Asparagus naturally contains vitamins A, C, and E along with fiber and calcium. One half-cup of cooked asparagus has 13 milligrams of sodium, 202 milligrams of potassium and 49 milligrams of phosphorus making it a good option for those with kidney disease. Select the right amount to follow a low-potassium diet. Include a portion of asparagus with different meals to add flavor: • Sauté as part of an omelet with eggs, onions and peppers for breakfast. • Add raw asparagus spears to a salad or cooked asparagus in a soup at lunch. • Season grilled asparagus with lemon juice, olive oil or red wine vinaigrette to complement a main dish. • Steam and then puree asparagus with other ingredients and use it as an appetizer or sandwich spread."]]},"7389987":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200°C/gas 5. Place the peppers, onion and courgette onto a lightly oiled baking sheet, and roast in the oven for 20 minutes, turning a couple of times until starting to brown at the edges."],[null,"Let the vegetables cool for 5 minutes. Add the olive oil and balsamic vinegar, sprinkle with oregano, season with black pepper and mix gently. Divide the vegetables into 2 equal portions."],[null,"Slice each loaf lengthways to create 3 horizontal slices. Place half of one portion of vegetables on the bottom slice of bread, then op with goat's cheese."],[null,"Add the middle slice of bread, then add the second layer of vegetables, 1 sliced tomato and some of the basil, and top with the final slide of bread. Repeat with the second loaf."],[null,"Wrap each loaf tightly in greaseproof paper, twisting the ends, then wrap tightly in cling film. Put the loaves in the refrigerator, topped with a plate or oven tray and place some weights on top, eg tins of beans. Leave for at least 2 hours, or overnight, so that all the juices permeate the bread."]],"h":[[null,"For a dairy-free or vegan version, add some tahini and sundried tomatoes instead of the goat's cheese."],[null,"You can easily scale up this recipe and use a large loaf that will feed 8 people. Alternatively, use fewer ingredients for a single portion in a bread roll."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"7924662":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200ºC/gas 6. Wash, then top and tail the beetroots, and cut into quarters (no need to peel them). Mix the beetroot with the olive oil, spread out on a baking tray and bake in the oven for 25 minutes. Allow to cool, remove the skins, cut into chunks and reserve."],[null,"Meanwhile, arrange the rocket leaves on a large platter."],[null,"Place pieces of beetroot on top and crumble the goat's cheese evenly over the salad. Next, scatter with the walnuts."],[null,"Finally, drizzle with the lemon juice. Season with black pepper. (Do this final stage just before serving, everything else can be done in advance.)"]],"h":[[null,"To cut down on the amount of fat in this recipe, add more beetroot and rocket leaves, and reduce the quantity of nuts that you use."],[null,"This recipe also works well with chunks of roasted carrots or butternut squash."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"3337":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400° F."],[null,"Place bread crumbs in a shallow dish or plate. Dredge fish fillets in bread crumbs to coat. Place in a greased shallow baking dish."],[null,"Combine mayonnaise and lemon juice. Add yogurt and blend well."],[null,"In a separate bowl, beat egg white until stiff, then gently fold into mayonnaise mixture."],[null,"Sprinkle chopped green onion over fillets. Spoon mayonnaise mixture over top. Sprinkle with paprika."],[null,"Bake for 20-25 minutes or until fish flakes easily."]],"h":[[null,"This recipe works well with snapper or cod."],[null,"Adjust portion to match your meal plan and protein goals."],[null,"Sour cream may be substituted for yogurt. Potassium and phosphorus are slightly lower but fat is higher."]]},"2795":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Grease a baking sheet."],[null,"Sift the cornmeal, flour, baking powder and salt together into mixing bowl. Set aside."],[null,"In a separate mixing bowl, cream the butter and sugar until light and fluffy. Beat in the egg substitute and vanilla extract."],[null,"Add the dry ingredients to the butter mixture and beat until well blended."],[null,"Drop heaping teaspoons of the mixture onto the greased baking sheet in rows about 2″ apart."],[null,"Bake for 7 to 8 minutes until the cookies are golden brown at the edges. Transfer to a wire rack to cool."]],"h":[[null,"Use of liquid egg substitute instead of eggs helps lower phosphorus in this recipe. This is important in recipes that contain baking powder, a high phosphorus ingredient necessary for many bakery items."]]},"7521301":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 180°C (160°C fan)/350°F/gas 4."],[null,"Chop all the veg into chunks, sprinkle with dry mixed herbs and nutritional yeast, spray with oil of choice to speed up the process of roasting. I often roast without and the veg roast nicely and retain their moisture. Place in middle of oven for 25 – 30 mins until veg are bronzed and browned on the edges."],[null,"Stir the stock into warm water ready to add to a blender."],[null,"Add the roasted vegetables, water and stock to a blender and blitz until smooth. Pour into a pan and keep warm. Check your seasoning and serve."]],"h":[[null,"This recipe has been created by Balance cover star, Shivali, as part of her journey to diabetes remission."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"6375634":{"s":[[null,"Put the cinnamon, banana, and 1 cup of yogurt in a blender and blend until smooth. Divide between 4 parfait glasses."],[null,"Top each with ½ cup of sliced strawberries, ¼ cup of the remaining yogurt, and 1 tablespoon of the cereal. Garnish with a sprig of mint if desired."]],"h":[]},"2832":{"s":[[null,"Cook green beans in boiling water until tender. Drain."],[null,"Chop onion and bell pepper."],[null,"Place a skillet on medium heat, add margarine and sauté onion, red pepper, dill and parsley until soft."],[null,"Add green beans to skillet and heat until beans are hot."],[null,"Sprinkle with black pepper and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute fresh green beans for frozen when in season."]]},"5002518":{"s":[[null,"Mix together the bread flour, Renastep and water in a bowl until a dough is formed, knead for 2 minutes then set aside to rest for 30 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, add to a frying pan the onions and peppers and allow to cook until soft."],[null,"Add in the lamb mince, garlic and cumin and allow to cook until the mince has browned."],[null,"Add in the kale and allow to soften, then remove the pan from the heat and add in the mint and coriander, set aside to cool."],[null,"Cut the dough into 4 portions and roll out each portion into a thin 15cm circle."],[null,"Place a quarter of the meat mixture onto one half of each dough circle, crumble feta equally over each gozleme."],[null,"Fold over other half of dough and crimp sides until sealed."],[null,"Brush each gozleme with olive oil and squash slightly to flatten."],[null,"Heat olive oil in a pan and fry each gozleme until golden brown and crispy on each side."],[null,"Serve and enjoy!"]],"h":[["Renastep note","Renastep is a food for special medical purposes for the dietary management of kidney disease. Suitable from 3 years of age. Must be used under medical supervision. Renastep contains Milk (milk protein) and Fish (Tuna oil). This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutritics dietary analysis software. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information."]]},"2563":{"s":[[null,"Mix frozen veggies and lettuce in a bowl. (If eating immediately thaw vegetables before mixing with the lettuce.)"],[null,"Toss with dressing and divide into 4 servings. Portion into 12 to 16 ounce jars or portable lunch containers."],[null,"Add 2 cherry tomatoes to each salad serving."],[null,"Seal and refrigerate salad jars until ready to go. Keeps for 3 to 4 days refrigerated."],[null,"Divide croutons into 1/4 cup servings and store in small containers or snack bags (do not refrigerate). Add to salad when ready to eat."]],"h":[[null,"Decrease sodium to only 125 mg per serving by using Creamy Vinaigrette Dressing instead of store bought dressing."],[null,"Southwestern blend veggies contain corn, green peppers, onions and black beans."],[null,"Add cooked chicken or low-sodium canned tuna for added protein."]]},"3881":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375° F."],[null,"Combine graham cracker crumbs, sugar and butter."],[null,"Press into a greased 10-inch pie pan and bake for ­­­7 minutes."],[null,"Let cool completely before adding filling."]],"h":[[null,"Save money by making homemade pie crust."],[null,"People with diabetes can substitute Equal®, Splenda® sweetener or other sugar substitute instead of sugar if desired."]]},"3052":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 450° F."],[null,"In a large mixing bowl, combine eggs, applesauce, brown sugar, flour, lemon rind, 3-tablespoons lemon juice, salt, cinnamon and nutmeg; mix well."],[null,"Pour mixture into unbaked pie shell. Bake for 15 minutes. Reduce oven temperature to 300° F. Bake for 45 minutes longer or until knife inserted near center comes out clean. Cool slightly on wire rack."],[null,"While pie is baking, peel and thinly slice apple."],[null,"Combine apple slices and 1 tablespoon lemon juice in a bowl; mix well. Arrange apple slices pinwheel fashion over top of baked pie."],[null,"Melt jam in small saucepan over low heat, stirring constantly. Brush apple slices with melted jam."],[null,"Place pie on rack of broiler pan. Broil 6” from heat source for 3 minutes or until apples are tender and jam is bubbly."]],"h":[[null,"Lower carbohydrate options for diabetics include using 1/4 cup + 2 tablespoons Splenda® Brown Sugar Blend instead of brown sugar, and using apricot fruit spread instead of jam. This reduces calories to 216, carbohydrate 32 g and 2 carbohydrate choices."],[null,"Sodium content of pre-made pie crust varies with brands. Select the brand with lowest sodium content or consider making homemade pie crust with reduced salt."]]},"3508":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350° F."],[null,"Place the graham crackers in a gallon-size freezer bag and crush them with a rolling pin."],[null,"Place the graham cracker crumbs and 1/4 cup of the protein powder in a 9” x 13” casserole dish and pour in the melted butter. Using a wooden spoon or clean hands, mix the graham crackers with the butter. Press into the pan."],[null,"Bake for 8 to 10 minutes. Allow to cool."],[null,"Place the softened cream cheese, powdered sugar and the remaining 1/4 cup of protein powder into a blender and blend for about 15 seconds. Scrape down the sides of the blender and blend again until there are no lumps. Add the thawed Cool Whip and blend until smooth. Spread this mixture on the prepared graham cracker crust."],[null,"Spread the cherry pie filling over the cream cheese mixture."],[null,"Place dessert in the refrigerator or freezer and allow to chill before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Amy’s grandma used to serve this frozen, but, as kids, she and her sister would eat it whether it was frozen or refrigerated."],[null,"If you need to follow a lower protein meal plan, omit the protein powder."],[null,"Ask your dietitian to recommend a brand of protein powder."]]},"4902938":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400⁰ F. Line a 12-count muffin pan with cupcake liners and a second muffin pan with 6 liners (or can make in two batches if you only have one muffin pan)."],[null,"Blend the shortening, salt, vanilla, egg and sugar on high speed with a mixer. In a separate bowl, mix the baking powder and flour. Alternate adding the dry mixture and the milk to the blended shortening mixture (add about a third of each at a time). Then fold the blueberries into the batter by hand."],[null,"Pour batter into cupcake liners. Bake for 15-18 minutes. Frosting (optional): Mix powdered sugar and butter at high speed with hand mixer. Add vanilla and almond milk and continue to blend until smooth. Spread frosting on cooled blueberry cupcakes."]],"h":[[null,"Nutrition info is for cupcake without the optional frosting."]]},"3923":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F."],[null,"Combine ground beef, egg,1/4 cup bread crumbs, brown sugar, 3 ounces tomato sauce, garlic powder and onion powder in a bowl."],[null,"Mix thoroughly by hand. Separate into two equal halves."],[null,"Smooth one half into a casserole dish that has been sprayed with non-stick spray."],[null,"Sprinkle the cheese on top of the meat."],[null,"Smooth the rest of the ground beef mixture on top of the cheese."],[null,"Pour the remaining tomato sauce over the meatloaf."],[null,"Sprinkle the remaining bread crumbs over the meatloaf."],[null,"Cover and cook in the oven for one hour, or cook uncovered in a microwave oven at 70% power for 35 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute ground turkey for beef if desired."],[null,"This meatloaf is very garlicky. Adjust the amount of garlic powder and onion powder to suit your taste."],[null,"Reduce carbohydrate to 17 grams by substituting 1/4 cup Splenda® Brown Sugar Blend for the 1/2 cup brown sugar."],[null,"Portion leftover meatloaf into individual servings, wrap and freeze for a quick meatloaf sandwich or meal later."]]},"2966":{"s":[[null,"In a medium bowl combine flour, baking powder, sugar, salt and shortening. Add 1/2-cup grape juice and mix into a stiff dough."],[null,"Roll dough very thin on a floured board and cut into strips 1/2” wide and 1” long."],[null,"Mix 1-cup grape juice with 1-cup water in a saucepan and heat to a boil."],[null,"Drop dough pieces into boiling grape juice and cook for 10 to 12 minutes."],[null,"Serve dumpling with small amount of liquid."]],"h":[[null,"Serve as a side dish with your meal or for dessert."]]},"2537":{"s":[[null,"Slice bagel and toast until golden brown."],[null,"Spread cream cheese over each bagel half. Place onion slice and tomato slice on top and sprinkle with lemon pepper."]],"h":[[null,"For variety try different types of bagels and flavored cream cheese."],[null,"Some brands of lemon pepper contain salt. Check the ingredients and select a brand without salt."]]},"6288756":{"s":[[null,"In a medium salad bowl, combine the beans, tomatoes, onion, bell pepper, feta cheese, and olives."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the vinegar, olive oil, oregano, and black pepper. Pour the dressing over the salad ingredients and mix to coat. Serve cold."]],"h":[]},"6912355":{"s":[[null,"In a medium bowl, toss together cherry tomatoes, cucumber, olives, lemon juice, red wine vinegar, olive oil, oregano, and black pepper."],[null,"Divide cottage cheese evenly among 4 bowls. Spoon the Greek salad mixture over each serving. Top with fresh parsley."]],"h":[]},"7870024":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200ºC/gas 6."],[null,"Place the chicken in an ovenproof dish and arrange the potatoes around it."],[null,"Mix together all the remaining ingredients, except the parsley, and pour over the chicken."],[null,"Cover with foil and bake for 35 minutes, remove the foil and cook for a further 15-20 minutes."],[null,"Sprinkle over the parsley, season to taste and serve."]],"h":[[null,"This recipe also works well with lean cuts of meat such as lamb fillet."],[null,"You could use sweet potatoes instead of ordinary potatoes."],[null,"You could make this recipe healthier by using reduced-salt chicken stock."],[null,"Serve with salad or seasonal vegetables to help you reach your 5 A Day."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"6320230":{"s":[[null,"Combine all ingredients except spinach leaves in a large bowl. Marinate at least one hour in refrigerator, covered, before serving. Add spinach leaves just before serving."]],"h":[]},"6169737":{"s":[[null,"Cook quinoa according to package directions with chicken broth. Let cool completely."],[null,"In a large salad bowl, combine cooled quinoa and remaining salad ingredients."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together dressing ingredients. Pour over salad and mix to coat. Serve cold."]],"h":[]},"6726593":{"s":[[null,"In a large salad bowl, combine the Romaine, tomatoes, cucumber, red bell pepper, red onion, olives, feta cheese, and chickpeas."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the extra-virgin olive oil, red wine vinegar, dried oregano, and pepper to create the dressing."],[null,"Pour the dressing over the salad and toss gently until all ingredients are well coated."]],"h":[]},"6142404":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F. Spray 4 8x8 inch sheets of aluminum foil with cooking spray. Set aside."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine lemon juice, garlic, oregano, salt, and pepper and set aside."],[null,"Place ¼ of the zucchini, onion, and bell pepper in the center of each sheet of foil. Top each with a salmon fillet."],[null,"Pour ¼ of the lemon juice mixture over each salmon fillet. Top with ½ teaspoon olive oil."],[null,"Bring the sides of the foil up on both sides and seal tightly for form a packet. Place the foil packets on a baking sheet and bake for 20 minutes."],[null,"Check to make sure the salmon is cooked through. Open one packet slightly and place an instant read thermometer into the thickest part of the salmon. The salmon is done when it reaches at least 145 degrees F."],[null,"Safety tip: Be careful when opening the foil packets because the steam could burn you."]],"h":[]},"3303":{"s":[[null,"In skillet, heat oil and brown ground turkey; separate larger pieces with fork."],[null,"Chop onion, garlic and bell pepper."],[null,"Add onion, garlic, bell pepper, oregano, thyme and black pepper to skillet with turkey; cook until onion is soft."],[null,"Add vinegar. The turkey mixture can be refrigerated at this point until ready to serve pitas."],[null,"Cube cucumber into small pieces; thinly slice tomato and split scallions in half."],[null,"In a separate bowl, gently mix the cucumber into the sour cream; let stand while the pitas are prepared."],[null,"In a skillet lightly coated with olive oil, brown the pitas on both sides; stack pitas on a plate and cover to keep warm. Cut pitas in half."],[null,"Stuff each half with the meat mixture, and top with the sour cream mixture; serve with a scallion half and a tomato slice as a garnish."]],"h":[[null,"This recipe can be made a couple of days ahead as separate turkey and topping mixtures and assembled right before the meal; this allows the flavors to mingle in the topping, and saves effort at dinnertime."],[null,"The sandwiches can be served stuffed or unstuffed. If the peppers are chopped before adding to the turkey mixture, it is easier to stuff the pitas. Sliced red peppers are more festive-looking if the mixture is served on a plate with the cut pitas on the side."],[null,"Red or green peppers can be used, but the red pepper mixture is sweeter and looks more appealing."]]},"6026569":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F."],[null,"Top pita bread with sauce, olives, peppers, artichokes, shallot, and Italian cheese."],[null,"Bake in the oven until the cheese melts and the pita is crispy, 7–8 minutes."],[null,"Remove from the oven and top with feta and fresh basil."]],"h":[]},"54926":{"s":[[null,"Mix lemon juice and honey into yogurt."],[null,"Place from strawberries in the bottom of a mason jar. Top with yogurt mixture."],[null,"Let the jar set in the refrigerator overnight and grab in the morning. You can stir to incorporate the berries, which after thawing will create a nice strawberry sauce."]],"h":[[null,"Greek yogurt has more protein than other yogurts. Can be a good substitute for eggs in the morning."],[null,"You may substitute a sugar free sweetener for the honey to lower to added sugar content and make it diabetes friendly."]]},"6724403":{"s":[[null,"Add the chopped chocolate to a microwave-safe bowl. Microwave the chocolate on high for 1 minute, then stir. If not completely melted, microwave for 30 more seconds, then stir until all chunks are melted. If it is still not melted, microwave another 30 seconds and continue to stir, just until the chunks in the chocolate are melted. Do not overcook."],[null,"In a medium mixing bowl, whip the Greek yogurt with an electric mixer until fluffy. Add the honey, vanilla, and milk, and beat some more, then add the chocolate, a small amount at a time, beating in between additions."],[null,"Once all of the chocolate is mixed into the yogurt, divide the mousse into 6 portions and top each portion with 1/3 cup raspberries and 1 tablespoon whipped topping"]],"h":[]},"6116524":{"s":[[null,"Place the chicken breasts in a gallon-size resealable plastic bag. Set aside."],[null,"In a small mixing bowl, combine the remaining ingredients to make the marinade. Pour the marinade over the chicken to coat. Squeeze any extra air out of the bag and seal it."],[null,"Marinate the chicken in the refrigerator for at least 1 hour or overnight."],[null,"Once the chicken has finished marinating, discard any unabsorbed marinade. Cook the chicken in the oven at 400° F for 35 to 40 minutes, or until the internal temperature reaches 165° F."]],"h":[]},"6741137":{"s":[[null,"In a mixing bowl, combine the non-fat Greek yogurt, milk, heavy cream, maple syrup, and vanilla extract."],[null,"Use a hand mixer and beat until the mixture is well incorporated and fluffy."],[null,"Divide the Greek yogurt mixture into 4 serving cups or glasses."],[null,"Chill the mousse in the refrigerator for at least 2 hours to allow it to set."],[null,"Top each with ¼ cup fresh blueberries before serving."]],"h":[]},"7595443":{"s":[[null,"Mix the chicken strips, oregano, lemon juice, garlic and black pepper together and set aside to infuse for 10 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, in a bowl mix together the cucumber and yogurt. Add tomatoes and mint together and mix with the salad leaves."],[null,"Heat the oil in a small pan, add the chicken and mix well to ensure even cooking – it should take around 4 minutes."],[null,"Warm the pitta bread in a dry frying pan or toaster and cut in half and open to create pockets. Fill with salad and chicken, squeeze with lemon juice from the wedges and drizzle with the yogurt and cucumber mix."]],"h":[[null,"For a veggie version, use chargrilled slices of aubergine and courgette or falafels."],[null,"This also works well with strips of turkey."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6001699":{"s":[[null,"For the best flavor, lightly toast your whole grain pita in a toaster or oven until it is warm and slightly pliable."],[null,"Cut the pita into triangles (wedges) and place them on a plate next to a small bowl of tzatziki and the whole cherry tomatoes for dipping."],[null,"Enjoy immediately while the pita is warm."]],"h":[]},"6342815":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F."],[null,"In a shallow dish, whisk together the whole egg, egg white, and hot sauce."],[null,"In another shallow dish, mix together the cornmeal, garlic salt, black pepper, and parmesan."],[null,"Dip each green bean in the egg mixture and then lightly coat in the cornmeal mixture."],[null,"Place the green beans on a baking sheet and bake for 25 minutes, until they are lightly golden. Serve with your favorite dipping sauce."]],"h":[]},"2534":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F. Spray a 2-1/2 quart casserole dish with cooking spray."],[null,"Crush 10 crackers to equal about 1/2-cup cracker crumbs and set aside."],[null,"In a medium skillet, melt 2 tablespoons of butter over medium heat. Stir in the flour and cook for 1 minute."],[null,"Stir in sugar, sour cream and finely shredded sharp cheddar cheese."],[null,"Add the frozen green beans and stir to coat."],[null,"Transfer mixture to a prepared casserole dish."],[null,"In a small microwave-safe bowl melt 1-tablespoon butter in microwave. Stir in cracker crumbs and sprinkle over top of casserole."],[null,"Bake the casserole for 30 minutes or until topping is golden brown."]],"h":[[null,"Remember to take your phosphorus binder with this casserole since it contains cheese, a source of phosphorus."],[null,"This recipe is tastier and healthier than the cream soup version of holiday green bean casserole. It is much lower in sodium."]]},"4715504":{"s":[[null,"In a saucepan, bring water to a boil and cook the green beans (approximately 5 minutes). Immediately rinse the beans under cold water to stop the cooking process. The beans should still be crisp."],[null,"In a serving bowl, toss together the beans, cabbage, shallot rings, and arugula."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the vinaigrette ingredients."],[null,"Pour the vinaigrette over the green bean slaw mixture and toss to combine."]],"h":[[null,"Serve as a side dish for meat or fish."],[null,"Dress it up with a protein, such as sliced steak or boiled egg and make it a meal."],["Vinaigrette-style salad dressings","A kidney-friendly diet is low in sodium. When removing sodium from the diet, one can remove vital flavor, making mealtime less appealing. To prepare flavorful food and create excitement about cooking, consider making and adding a vinaigrette-type salad dressing to various recipes. It is relatively easy to make and can add a great deal of flavor to many foods. In addition to tossing your favorite salad with a vinaigrette dressing, drizzle it over hot or cold vegetables or use it as a marinade. To make a vinaigrette dressing, follow a few simple steps. • Add 1 part vinegar or other acid to 3 parts oil. For example, mix ¼ cup of red wine vinegar with ¾ cup olive oil. Avoid using oils with very strong flavors, like some nut oils. For vinegar, anything goes – cider, red wine, white wine, rice, and balsamic are all excellent choices. Other acid options to consider are fresh squeezed lemon or lime juice. Avoid plain distilled white vinegar, as its flavor is too strong. • Add more flavor with fresh ground pepper, some mustard, fresh herbs, minced garlic, or chopped shallots. • If you like a little sweetness, add a touch of honey. Whisk ingredients together and store in a jar in the refrigerator for up to 5 days. Shake before each use."]]},"4934943":{"s":[[null,"In a saucepan, bring water to a boil and cook the green beans (approximately 5 minutes). Immediately rinse the beans under cold water to stop the cooking process. The beans should still be crisp."],[null,"In a serving bowl, toss together the slaw: cabbage, green beans, shallot rings and arugula."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the vinaigrette: chives, mustard, honey, vinegar, olive oil, and ground black pepper."],[null,"Pour the vinaigrette over the green bean slaw and toss to combine."]],"h":[[null,"Serve as a side for meats or fish."],[null,"Dress it up with a protein, such as sliced steak or boiled egg and make it a meal."]]},"3063":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 450° F."],[null,"Wash green beans and trim ends."],[null,"Line a rimmed baking sheet with aluminum foil and spread beans on foil."],[null,"Pour olive oil over beans and toss gently to coat beans evenly."],[null,"Roast in oven for 10 minutes."],[null,"Remove baking sheet from oven and redistribute beans for even baking."],[null,"Return to oven and bake for approximately 10 additional minutes or until beans have a few golden brown areas."],[null,"Remove from oven, season with ground pepper and serve."]],"h":[[null,"For extra flavor try a flavored oil with llemon or herb flavor."]]},"6137042":{"s":[[null,"Fill a large pot 2/3 full of water and bring to boiling. Add the green beans, turn off the heat, and let the green beans stand in the water for 3 minutes. Drain the beans and add them to a serving bowl or platter."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine the oil, nuts, cranberries, salt, and pepper. Top the green beans with the cranberry-nut mixture. Garnish with the lemon zest."]],"h":[]},"6089365":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F. Line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Steam or blanch the green beans until they are tender-crisp. Drain and set aside."],[null,"In a skillet, heat the olive oil over medium heat."],[null,"Add the breadcrumbs to the skillet and toast them for 2-3 minutes or until they become golden brown."],[null,"Add the grated Parmesan cheese and garlic powder to the breadcrumbs. Stir to combine."],[null,"Toss the steamed green beans in the breadcrumb mixture until they are well-coated."],[null,"Season with the coarse salt and black pepper."],[null,"Transfer to a baking dish."],[null,"Bake in the preheated oven for 10 minutes or until the breadcrumbs are crispy and golden."]],"h":[]},"3655":{"s":[[null,"Remove ends from the green beans and cut into 1-1/2″ pieces. Peel turnips and dice each one into 8 pieces. Mince the garlic cloves."],[null,"Place vegetables and garlic in a medium-size pot. Cover with 3 cups water and bring to a boil. Reduce to medium heat and cook uncovered for 15 minutes."],[null,"Remove pot from heat and drain water. Add butter, pepper and salt. Gently toss to mix seasonings with vegetables. Serve hot."],[null,"Remove to serving dish and sprinkle with paprika."]],"h":[[null,"Add a dash of hot sauce if you like spicy vegetables."]]},"6937788":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F"],[null,"Spray a large skillet with cooking spray and heat over medium heat. Add green peppers, jalapeño, green onion, and garlic. Cook over medium heat for 4–5 minutes, until the peppers start to soften."],[null,"Remove from heat and place in a bowl with the shredded chicken and mix. Set aside."],[null,"Return skillet to the heat and add the olive oil. Whisk in the flour for about 1 minute until smooth."],[null,"Slowly pour the chicken broth in, whisking until the sauce is thickened and smooth, about 3–4 minutes. Add the salt, coriander, and yogurt and whisk until smooth. Remove from heat."],[null,"Pour a small amount of sauce in a 10 x 8 (or medium size) baking dish. Spread to coat the bottom of the pan."],[null,"Place tortillas on a flat surface and divide the chicken and pepper mix between them, placing the mix in the center of each. Roll tightly and place seam side down in the baking dish. Pour remaining sauce over the stuffed tortillas and sprinkle with the shredded cheese."],[null,"Bake for 15–20 minutes, until the sauce is bubbling and the cheese has melted."]],"h":[]},"6485584":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F. Spray a 9-inch square baking dish with cooking spray."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine chopped chicken, black beans, diced green chilies, red bell pepper, Greek yogurt, salsa verde, ground cumin, garlic powder, and black pepper. Mix until well combined."],[null,"Spoon the chicken mixture into the baking dish, spreading it out evenly."],[null,"Sprinkle the shredded cheddar cheese over the top."],[null,"Cover the casserole with foil and bake for 25 minutes."],[null,"Remove the foil and bake until the casserole is hot and bubbly and the cheese is melted and golden brown, about 10 minutes more."],[null,"Remove from the oven and let it cool for a few minutes before slicing into 8 squares. Top with chopped, fresh cilantro."]],"h":[]},"6270808":{"s":[[null,"In a blender or food processor, combine Greek yogurt, parsley, chives, basil, lemon juice, garlic, olive oil, and Dijon mustard. Blend until smooth and set aside"],[null,"In a large salad bowl, layer romaine lettuce, baby spinach, cucumber, cherry tomatoes, radishes, and red onion."],[null,"Arrange smoked salmon, hard-boiled eggs, and diced avocado on top."],[null,"Evenly sprinkle everything bagel seasoning over the salad."],[null,"Drizzle the dressing over the salad just before serving."]],"h":[]},"6395124":{"s":[[null,"Put the ingredients for the Green Goddess sauce into a food processor and blend until smooth. Transfer to a bowl."],[null,"In a medium bowl, add the ground turkey, onion, 1 tbsp minced garlic, almond meal or almond flour, Dijon mustard, paprika, coarse salt, and pepper. Mix well."],[null,"Divide the meat into four equal parts and form them into 1/2-inch-thick patties that are slightly wider than the buns."],[null,"In a large frying pan on medium heat, add the olive oil. When the oil shimmers, add the four burgers, leaving space between them."],[null,"Cook the patties for 3–4 minutes. Flip them and cook for another 3–4 minutes, or until their internal temperature registers 165 degrees F."],[null,"Spread green goddess sauce on the top and bottom of a toasted bun. Layer the bottom bun with a patty and lettuce and enjoy."]],"h":[]},"3755":{"s":[[null,"Wash all produce well."],[null,"Core the apples."],[null,"Process all ingredients through a juicer. Divide into 2 servings and enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Consult with your dietitian when incorporating juicing into your kidney diet. Juice blends are high in potassium and may not be recommended if potassium control is an issue."],[null,"Be sure to count 3/4 cup (6 ounces) as 1 vegetable and 2 fruit servings from your daily goal to stay within your potassium goal for the day."]]},"6667936":{"s":[[null,"Add the spinach, avocado, cucumber, almond milk, and ice in a blender. Blend until smooth and creamy."],[null,"Pour into a tall glass and enjoy immediately."]],"h":[]},"7342064":{"s":[[null,"Blend together the coriander, mint, parsley, lime juice and water, and set aside."],[null,"Add the oil to a pan, followed by the onion and the red pepper. Heat for 3–4 minutes until softened."],[null,"Add the chilli, ginger and garlic, and stir for 1–2 minutes. Sprinkle with the curry powder and mix well for another minute."],[null,"Add the fish to the pan, then coat it in all of the spices, taking care not to break up the fish chunks."],[null,"Pour in the green sauce, bring to a gentle boil, then turn down the heat and cook for 3–4 minutes until the fish is cooked through, stirring occasionally. Serve with a sprig of coriander and wedges of lime."]],"h":[[null,"The sauce is great with chicken or with tofu for a veggie version."],[null,"This dish works with prawns or any fish."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6908410":{"s":[[null,"In a food processor, combine the thawed green peas, chickpeas, fresh mint, tahini, fresh lemon juice, minced garlic, olive oil, ground cumin, salt, and pepper. Pulse the mixture until the ingredients start to break down."],[null,"With the food processor running, add water gradually until you achieve a smooth and creamy consistency. You may need to stop and scrape down the sides of the processor a couple of times. Taste and adjust the seasoning if necessary."]],"h":[]},"3120":{"s":[[null,"Chop the onion and mince the basil."],[null,"In a small bowl combine the mayonnaise and yogurt."],[null,"Cook the peas in boiling water for 2 to 3 minutes. Drain and then mix peas with the mayonnaise-yogurt sauce while peas are still warm."],[null,"Add the onion, basil and olives to the green pea mixture and stir to combine ingredients."],[null,"Sprinkle mozzarella cheese on top and refrigerate until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Three cups of green peas is approximately 1 pound. Substitute fresh green peas when in season."],[null,"Choose mayonnaise with an olive oil base to include healthy fats."],[null,"Use parsley in place of basil if desired."],[null,"Two tablespoons of sliced almonds can also be added for crunch factor."],[null,"Add pepper or Mrs. Dash® herb seasoning blend to flavor as desired."]]},"2864":{"s":[[null,"Chop vegetables using a food processor."],[null,"Mix remaining ingredients and combine with vegetables."],[null,"Mix well and refrigerate to allow flavors to blend before serving."]],"h":[[null,"This slaw keeps for a week in the refrigerator."],[null,"Serve as a side dish or try Green Pepper Slaw as a sandwich topping."]]},"3856":{"s":[[null,"Bring water to a boil and cook pasta as directed, without salt. Drain."],[null,"Place basil leaves, garlic and Parmesan cheese in a food processor and pulse to chop. Gradually stream olive oil into the basil mixture and continue to pulse the mixture, scraping the sides of the processor as needed."],[null,"Add pepper to taste."],[null,"Pour basil pesto sauce onto the pasta and toss to coat evenly before serving."]],"h":[[null,"If pasta is done before pesto is ready, keep pasta warm by covering the pasta pot with a lid after draining water."],[null,"Serve with grilled or broiled chicken or shrimp and a salad or cooked vegetable for a full meal."]]},"6550451":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the lime juice, olive oil, red wine vinegar, sweetener, coarse salt, and black pepper."],[null,"Remove the peel and the white pith from around the oranges. Using a paring knife, cut in between the membranes to release the orange segments, and slice them into thirds. Place the orange pieces into a medium bowl."],[null,"Add the mixed greens, avocado cubes, and red onion to the bowl and drizzle with the lime juice mixture. Toss to combine. Sprinkle with the cilantro and serve."]],"h":[]},"6691484":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, whisk pureed raspberries, olive oil, vinegar, salt, and pepper together."],[null,"Place the field greens in a medium salad bowl. Add the raspberries and pine nuts. Drizzle dressing over top and toss gently to coat."]],"h":[]},"7160544":{"s":[[null,"Add the oil to a pan, add the asparagus and cook for 3 minutes. Add the garlic and cook for a further 2 minutes, mixing regularly."],[null,"Add the spring onion, flageolet beans, stock and white pepper and bring to the boil Turn down the heat, cover and simmer gently for 6-8 minutes, until the asparagus is tender."],[null,"Add the spinach and cucumber, bring back to the boil, then remove from the heat."],[null,"Allow to cool completely, then chill in the fridge. Just before serving, add the herbs, avocado and yogurt, then lend until smooth."],[null,"Place into bowls and garnish with chopped cucumber and radish."]],"h":[[null,"Experiment with different herbs, such as mint or coriander. Works best with a combination of complementary herbs."],[null,"Try using lettuce or watercress in place of spinach."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing before adding the herbs, avocado and yogurt. Defrost in the fridge then add the herbs, avocado and yogurt and blend."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"7791572":{"s":[[null,"Reserve a few leaves of coriander for garnish and then place the remainder, including stalks, into a food processor. Add the green chillies, spring onion, root ginger, lemongrass, garlic, ground cumin and coriander. Whizz to a coarse paste."],[null,"Heat the oil in a wok or large saucepan, add the green beans and stir fry for 2–3 minutes. Add the curry paste, coconut milk, soya milk and salmon. Bring to the boil, cover and simmer for 5 minutes."],[null,"Scatter over the prawns, baby spinach and lime zest. Serve with extra lime wedges to squeeze over."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6947620":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F."],[null,"To a bowl, add green onion, broccoli, tomato, spinach, salt, garlic powder, oregano, pepper, and smoked paprika. Toss ingredients well to make sure greens are covered with the spices."],[null,"Preheat an ovenproof nonstick pan over medium heat. Add vegetables from the bowl and sauté until ingredients are cooked through, about 2 minutes."],[null,"Add milk to the bowl with whisked eggs and whisk briefly to combine. Add egg mixture to pan and stir with a wooden or plastic spoon. Make sure all ingredients are evenly spread out."],[null,"Place pan in the middle rack of your oven and cook for 10 minutes. To check if the tortilla (egg and vegetable mixture) is done, insert a toothpick in the middle; if it comes out clean, the tortilla is cooked through."],[null,"Remove from oven and let it rest on the stovetop for 1-2 minutes so eggs settle and don’t fall apart when serving. Enjoy!"]],"h":[]},"2685":{"s":[[null,"Mix the oil, cheese, thyme and black pepper in a shallow bowl."],[null,"Place the corn in the oil mixture and roll to thoroughly coat corn."],[null,"Place all four pieces of the corn in the center of a heavy duty aluminum foil sheet. Pour any oil left in the bowl over the corn. Top the corn with 2 ice cubes."],[null,"Double fold the top and ends of the foil to make a packet, leaving room for heat to circulate."],[null,"Place the foil packet on the grill over medium heat and cook 20 minutes, turning once during cooking."]],"h":[[null,"Compared to most vegetables, corn is higher in phosphorus. A 1/2 ear portion is acceptable for a low phosphorus kidney diet."],[null,"Use fresh corn instead of frozen when in season."]]},"9517941":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (177 C)."],[null,"Add all the seitan burger ingredients EXCEPT the vital wheat gluten to a food processor, and process until smooth. Next, add about half of the vital wheat gluten and process until mostly smooth. Then add the remaining half and process until mostly combined, without over-processing."],[null,"Transfer the mixture to a clean surface, like a cutting board or countertop, and knead the dough for about 30 seconds, but don't go overboard. Once you see strands of gluten, the dough is ready. (See process shots above for a visual.)"],[null,"Divide into 8 equal pieces for even cooking. I use a kitchen scale to make them perfectly equal, but this is not necessary. You can eyeball it."],[null,"Roll each piece into a ball and then use a rolling pin to flatten each one into a patty. They will expand during cooking, so make them a little flatter than you'd like the final result to be. As you're stretching the burgers, you should see them spring back a little."],[null,"Use an oven-safe dish with a lid, like a dutch oven, and add a thin layer of vegetable broth to the bottom. Then layer your seitan patties on top, adding more broth in between the layers of patties. Add enough broth to ensure the patties are completely covered."],[null,"Then place the lid on top and bake in your preheated oven for 80 minutes, carefully flipping them at the 40-minute mark. Be very careful when flipping to prevent breaking the patties. When the 80 minutes is complete, remove from the oven."],[null,"If you're making these in advance, transfer the patties to a container to refrigerate overnight and finish cooking on the day you're serving. (Reserve the broth for drinking, it's delicious, don't dump it! ;) )"],[null,"Treat these as you would raw burgers. They are NOT ready to eat straight out of the oven. Finish off your seitan burger on the grill, or in a frying pan. Brush a little oil to prevent sticking and sprinkle with salt and pepper, if desired. Then grill or pan fry for a few minutes on each side until brown and heated through."],[null,"Enjoy with burger buns and all your favourite toppings."]],"h":[[null,"If possible, prepare your burgers one day in advance of grilling. These taste best when refrigerated overnight, and grilled the next day. However, they’re still great if grilled straight after making. Weigh your vital wheat gluten for the most accurate results . Relying on cup measurements could result in a seitan burger that’s dry and dense as measuring tends to pack more flour into the cups when compared to weight. Use salty, flavourful broth for the best results since there is no other added salt to this recipe. Try to portion your mixture into 8 equal size pieces for even cooking and similar-sized patties. If you want them to be perfect, use a kitchen scale to weigh the pieces. Roll your patties fairly flat , as they will grow and almost double in size during cooking. You want the patties to simmer in the broth and NOT boil, so they cook slowly, for the best texture. Don’t increase the oven temperature in an attempt to cook these faster. Your seitan burger patties will keep in the fridge for 4-5 days or freeze, layered with parchment paper to prevent sticking for up to 3 months."]]},"2589":{"s":[[null,"Chop the garlic cloves."],[null,"To make the marinade add buttermilk, olive oil, garlic and black pepper to a large zip top bag. Seal the bag and shake to combine ingredients."],[null,"Place chicken in the buttermilk marinade, seal bag and shake to distribute evenly."],[null,"Refrigerate the chicken at least 2 hours, or up to 24 hours."],[null,"Preheat a grill to medium heat. Remove the chicken from marinade and place on the grill. Discard extra marinade. Grill the chicken until internal temperature reaches 160-165º F."]],"h":[[null,"This recipe can be easily adjusted to accommodate more or less chicken. For every one pound of chicken use 1 cup buttermilk and 1 tablespoon oil."],[null,"For additional seasoning, add any of your favorite herbs or spices including parsley, rosemary or basil"],[null,"Approximately 25% of the marinade is absorbed. Recipe analysis based on this rule."],[null,"Adjust the portion for a lower or higher protein diet."],[null,"If preferred you can substitute boneless, skinless chicken breast or thighs."]]},"6090076":{"s":[[null,"Preheat grill to medium-high."],[null,"Drizzle the olive oil evenly over the eggplant halves. Sprinkle eggplant evenly with garlic powder and black pepper."],[null,"Place eggplant halves on grill cut side down and cook for 3-4 minutes, until tender."],[null,"Flip over and spread mozzarella cheese evenly over eggplant halves. Grill an additional 3-4 minutes until cheese is melted."],[null,"Remove eggplant from grill and place side-by-side on a serving dish. Drizzle evenly with balsamic vinegar and Parmesan cheese."]],"h":[]},"2713":{"s":[[null,"Dice the bell peppers, onion and chives. Chop or shred the chicken."],[null,"Heat a tablespoon of olive oil and sauté the diced peppers and onion. Add the tomato pesto and cook for 2 minutes. Set aside for later."],[null,"Roll or stretch the pizza dough to a 10-inch circle or rectangular shape. Set on a floured, rimless pizza sheet or sheet pan (unless you are using an oiled grill pizza pan). Let sit for about 5 minutes."],[null,"Oil the grill surface and preheat the grill to hot heat."],[null,"Put pizza dough on the grill (no toppings yet), and grill for about 2 to 3 minutes. Check bottom for browning; bubbles will form on top. Reduce to medium-high heat if needed to prevent burning. When light brown marks are visible on the bottom of the pizza dough, take the dough off the grill and place pizza dough with grill marks up."],[null,"Top the pizza dough with the bell pepper, onion and pesto mixture. Top with the chicken, Romano cheese followed by the mozzarella cheese."],[null,"Place the pizza back on the well-oiled grill or grill pan. Grill for another 2 to 3 minutes, until cheese is melted and the bottom of pizza is browned."],[null,"Remove the pizza from the grill and garnish with chopped chives. Cut into 4 slices and serve."]],"h":[[null,"The sun-dried tomato pesto can be found in the produce section near the jars of minced garlic. If you are unable to find sun-dried tomato pesto, use 2 tablespoons sun-dried tomatoes packed in oil. Chop before mixing with the peppers and onions. Another alternative is to substitute 1/4 cup of pizza sauce."],[null,"A packet of active dry yeast is 0.25 ounces or about 2-1/4 teaspoons."],[null,"If you are not using a grill, use a grill pan or a large skillet and cook on the stove top. Can be cooked in the oven at 425º F."],[null,"Serve pizza with a tossed salad and low-sodium dressing."]]},"1700":{"s":[[null,"Make dressing by combining olive oil, vinegar, Mrs. Dash seasoning and salt."],[null,"Place chicken in a zip top bag and add 2 tablespoons of the dressing to coat chicken pieces."],[null,"Heat a grill to medium high heat."],[null,"Place chicken breasts on grill and cook 8 to 10 minutes until juices are clear and chicken is cooked through. Remove from heat and rest 5 minutes."],[null,"Tear lettuce into peices. Cut onion into rings."],[null,"Arrange lettuce, onion rings and strawberries on a plate."],[null,"Slice each breast diagonally and place on lettuce bed."],[null,"Pour 1 tablespoon remaining dressing over each salad."],[null,"Serve each salad with 2 breadsticks."]],"h":[[null,"If using a thermometer, temperature should be at least 165º F."],[null,"For a fancy presentation, leave lettuce leaves whole and serve sliced chicken breast on top."],[null,"If you are on a lower protein diet decrease portion to 2 ounces cooked chicken per salad or ask your dietitian to recommend the best protion for your individual diet."]]},"7845092":{"s":[[null,"Put the chicken breasts between two sheets of cling film and beat with a rolling pin until 1cm thick. Stir together the yogurt, lemon and thyme and season with pepper."],[null,"Put the chicken and marinade in a bowl and leave for 15 mins."],[null,"Meanwhile, put the mooli, cucumber, onions, bean spouts and cress in a large salad bowl and toss."],[null,"Add the avocado, vinegar, oil, coriander and yogurt to a blender and blitz until smooth. Cook the chicken on a BBQ, in a chargrill pan or under the grill for approx. 8 mins, turning once until cooked through. Check that no pink flesh is visible and that the juices run clear when pierced at the thickest part of the chicken."],[null,"Drizzle the dressing over the salad, scatter over the sesame seeds, add the sliced chicken on top and serve."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"6194651":{"s":[[null,"Heat a small nonstick skillet coated with cooking spray over medium-low heat. Add pecans and cook 3–4 minutes or until lightly toasted, stirring frequently. Sprinkle with sugar and red pepper, and cook for 1 minute, stirring constantly. Remove pecans from skillet. Cool on wax paper."],[null,"Combine greens, Triple Citrus Vinaigrette, and orange sections in a large bowl. Toss well. Place 1 cup greens mixture on each of 8 plates. Top each serving with 1 1⁄2 teaspoons pecans and 1 1⁄2 teaspoons cranberries."],[null,"Top with grilled chicken breast and serve immediately."]],"h":[]},"6091518":{"s":[[null,"In a bowl, whisk together soy sauce, olive oil, honey, garlic, and ginger."],[null,"Place chicken, peaches, and zucchini in a large resealable bag or shallow dish and pour the marinade over them. Seal and refrigerate for at least 1 hour, up to overnight."],[null,"Preheat the grill (or indoor grill pan) to medium-high heat. Thread chicken, peaches, and zucchini onto skewers. Discard leftover marinade."],[null,"Grill for 10–15 minutes, turning occasionally, until chicken is cooked through and peaches are tender."]],"h":[]},"6566186":{"s":[[null,"Preheat a stove-top grill."],[null,"Remove any visible fat from chicken and season with black pepper."],[null,"Place chicken and onion slices on the grill. Cook 5 minutes. Turn chicken and onions over and grill 3 minutes. Spoon barbecue sauce over chicken and onion, and grill 2 minutes. A meat thermometer should reach 165 degrees F to indicate the chicken is fully cooked. Transfer to a plate. Using two forks, shred the chicken. Separate the onions into rings."],[null,"Meanwhile, wrap the tortillas in foil and add to the grill for 3 minutes to warm through. Fill each tortilla with some of the chicken and onions, and roll into a wrap."],[null,"Divide lettuce between two plates, and top with diced tomatoes. Serve."]],"h":[]},"3609":{"s":[[null,"Season chicken breast with one tablespoon olive oil, cracked black pepper, herb-spice mix and crushed red pepper flakes. Add chicken to hot spot of the grill, seasoned side down. Grill for 12 minutes."],[null,"While chicken cooks, cut asparagus and place on the grill. Season with black pepper and drizzle with 2 teaspoons of olive oil. Grill asparagus for 5 to 7 minutes."],[null,"Cut the ear of corn in half and drizzle with 1 teaspoon of olive oil. Grill corn for 3 to 4 minutes, until slightly charred. After taking corn off the grill, add a squeeze of lemon juice and the chopped chives."],[null,"Squeeze lemon over chicken and asparagus to taste."]],"h":[[null,"Fresh lemon juice and a little splash of olive oil is a great substitute for salt."],[null,"After asparagus starts to char, you can push it off to a part of the grill that isn’t in direct flame."],[null,"Cook an extra ear of corn for lunch or dinner tomorrow."],[null,"Adjust chicken portion to match your meal plan."],[null,"This recipe is featured in the DaVita Eats: Chef Tips video series."]]},"6089235":{"s":[[null,"Melt butter and add the garlic, red chili flakes, and parsley. Place in a small cup and set aside."],[null,"Preheat grill to high. Place well-washed clams on a piece of foil or cookie baking pan to catch the juices."],[null,"Cook as per directions for direct heat method for 8–10 minutes, turning halfway through, until cooked through and clam shells fully open. Drizzle the butter into the clam shells and serve. Discard any clams that do not open."]],"h":[]},"2234":{"s":[[null,"Place the corn flour in a bowl."],[null,"Grate the cheese and add cheese and anise to the flour."],[null,"Add the warm water; mix with a spatula."],[null,"Leave to rest for 10 minutes then knead for 2 to 3 minutes."],[null,"To form the corn cakes make 4 circles about 4-inches wide and 1/2-inch thick."],[null,"Grease a skillet or arepas pan with butter. Place each corn cake on the skillet or arepas pan and cook until slightly browned."]],"h":[[null,"Arepa is a popular food in Colombia."],[null,"Arepa flour is cooked and dried and made specially for making arepas. It can be purchased online or you can substitute maza corn flour."],[null,"Costeño cheese is a salty hard cheese. You can substitute cotija or Parmesan cheese."]]},"6483037":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the grill to medium-high heat."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together olive oil, chili powder, smoked paprika, lime zest, lime juice and salt."],[null,"Brush the ears of corn with the marinade, making sure to coat them evenly."],[null,"Allow the corn to marinate for at least 30 minutes."],[null,"Place the marinated corn on the preheated grill. Grill for about 15 minutes, turning occasionally, until the corn is charred and cooked through."],[null,"Remove the grilled corn from the heat."],[null,"Transfer the corn to a serving platter and sprinkle with cotija and fresh chopped cilantro."]],"h":[]},"6232942":{"s":[[null,"In a medium bowl, whisk together the oil, lime juice, lime zest, chili powder, cumin, salt, and pepper. Add the cod and marinate in the refrigerator for 15–20 minutes."],[null,"While fish is marinating, stir together all the salsa ingredients in a medium bowl."],[null,"Preheat an outdoor grill or grill pan to medium-high heat."],[null,"Remove the cod from the marinade and grill for 3–4 minutes on one side. Then flip and grill 1–2 minutes on the other side, or until fish flakes easily with a fork."],[null,"Transfer the cod to a plate and let it rest for 5 minutes, then use a fork to flake it into bite-size pieces."],[null,"Working in batches if necessary, grill the tortillas for 20 seconds each. Divide the fish evenly among the tortillas, garnish with the salsa (about 2 tablespoons per taco), and serve."]],"h":[]},"2947":{"s":[[null,"Heat grill to medium-high heat."],[null,"Season the steak with 1/4 teaspoon of the salt and 1/2 teaspoon of the pepper."],[null,"Grill to the desired doneness, 4 to 5 minutes per side for medium-rare."],[null,"Transfer to a cutting board and let rest at least 5 minutes before slicing."],[null,"While steak is cooking, sliced eggplant into four 1/2″ thick rounds and quarter and seed bell peppers."],[null,"Brush both sides of the eggplant and peppers with 3 tablespoons of the oil. Season with 1/4 teaspoon salt and 1/2 teaspoon pepper."],[null,"Grill until tender, 4 to 5 minutes per side."],[null,"Mince garlic clove and chop parsley. In a small bowl, combine the remaining oil, vinegar, garlic and parsley to make a vinaigrette sauce."],[null,"Divide the steak and vegetables onto 4 dinner plates."],[null,"Spoon sauce over the vegetables or serve on the side."]],"h":[[null,"Make sandwiches with the leftovers."],[null,"For lower protein diets adjust steak portion to match your meal plan."],[null,"Flank steak is also known as London broil."]]},"2046":{"s":[[null,"Dice jalapeno pepper and mince garlic."],[null,"Prepare pesto by mixing together almonds, yogurt, jalapeno pepper, salt, pepper, garlic and lime juice in a blender or food processor. Blend until slightly chunky. Set aside."],[null,"Sprinkle salt and pepper on steak. Preheat grill to medium heat. Grill steak to desired temperature or about 6 minutes on each side. Let rest for 5 minutes."],[null,"Slice steak into thin slices. Serve with 1 tablespoon cilantro pesto."]],"h":[[null,"Serve with a small salad and a serving of Nicole’s Cumin Sweet Potato Shoestring Fries."],[null,"Use leftover cilantro pesto on sandwiches or as a dip for Nicole’s fries."]]},"6177539":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the grill or grill pan over medium-high heat."],[null,"In a large bowl, toss the green beans with olive oil, garlic powder, and black pepper until evenly coated."],[null,"Place the seasoned green beans on the preheated grill. Grill for 8–10 minutes, turning occasionally, or until the beans are tender and have grill marks."],[null,"While the green beans are grilling, prepare the dressing. In a small bowl, whisk together balsamic vinegar, Dijon mustard, and 2 Tbsp chopped fresh basil. Add tomatoes to the dressing."],[null,"Once the green beans are done, transfer them to a serving platter."],[null,"Pour dressing and tomatoes over the green bean salad."],[null,"Top with the crumbled blue cheese and remaining basil leaves."]],"h":[]},"6780047":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, mix together the lime juice, garlic, olive oil, honey, onions, cilantro, and salt."],[null,"Put the chicken breasts in a large resealable plastic bag. Add the marinade to the bag and lay it flat in the refrigerator for at least 1 hour. Note: The longer the chicken is left to marinate, the more flavorful it will become."],[null,"Remove the chicken from the bag and discard the marinade. Cook on the grill or stovetop for 5-8 minutes on each side, until it reaches an internal temperature of 165 degrees F."]],"h":[]},"6145357":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F."],[null,"Pat the chicken thighs dry with paper towels. Season both sides with pepper."],[null,"Heat a large ovenproof skillet over medium-high heat. Add olive oil and swirl to coat. Place the chicken in the skillet and sear on one side until golden brown, about 5–6 minutes. Flip the chicken, then remove the skillet from heat."],[null,"Arrange the peach slices and diced jalapeños around the chicken in the skillet."],[null,"Drizzle with lemon juice, zest, and sugar-free syrup. Transfer the skillet to the oven and bake for 15–18 minutes, or until the chicken is fully cooked (165 degrees F internal temperature)."],[null,"Meanwhile, in a medium bowl, whisk together minced garlic, mayonnaise, apple cider vinegar, Dijon mustard, and dried basil."],[null,"Add sliced artichoke hearts and avocado to the bowl with the dressing. Toss gently to coat. Add spring mix and toss again to combine."],[null,"Divide the salad among plates. Top with roasted chicken and caramelized peaches."]],"h":[]},"7293925":{"s":[[null,"Slice the chicken fillets into strips about as thick as your finger."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine the olive oil, lemon juice, mint, garlic, chillies and red wine vinegar."],[null,"Add half the dressing to the sliced chicken fillet and set aside to marinade for 30 minutes."],[null,"In another small bowl, add the remainder of the dressing to the couscous and add enough water to just cover. Set aside for at least 15 minutes."],[null,"In the meantime, grill the red pepper until the skin is black. Take off the heat and once cool enough to touch, peel the blackened skin off and chop."],[null,"Chop the cherry tomatoes in half and chop the parsley."],[null,"Heat the grill and when hot cook the chicken strips and any marinade clinging to them. Grill for about 3-4 minutes on each side."],[null,"When done, fluff up the couscous and add the grilled chicken and prepared vegetables to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Works well with turkey or salmon instead of chicken."],[null,"For a veggie option, replace the chicken with tofu or use large Portobello mushrooms."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6217410":{"s":[[null,"In a medium bowl, mix together the lime juice and zest, honey, cilantro, cumin, chili powder, garlic powder, and pepper. Add the chicken breast tenderloins and marinate in the refrigerator for 20-60 minutes."],[null,"Preheat a grill to medium heat. Place the onions and green peppers in a grill basket. Grill the vegetables in the basket, stirring occasionally, about 15-20 minutes until slightly charred."],[null,"Add the chicken directly to the grill and cook 10-12 minutes, until done, turning once."],[null,"Divide the chicken, green peppers and onions evenly among 10 tortillas. Top each fajita with 1 Tbsp. salsa."]],"h":[]},"6384137":{"s":[[null,"In a bowl, combine the lime zest, lime juice, olive oil, minced garlic, ground cumin, paprika, salt, and pepper to make the marinade."],[null,"Place the chicken breasts in a sealable bag or shallow dish and pour half of the marinade over the chicken. Toss to fully coat. Marinate in the refrigerator for at least 30 minutes."],[null,"Preheat the grill or a grill pan over medium high heat."],[null,"Grill the marinated chicken breasts for about 6–8 minutes per side or until fully cooked to an internal temperature of 165 degreed F."],[null,"Allow the chicken to rest for a few minutes before slicing it into strips."],[null,"In a bowl, combine cherry tomatoes, cucumber, red onion, and fresh cilantro."],[null,"Pour the remaining marinade over the vegetable mixture and toss gently."],[null,"Place two lettuce leaves on each plate."],[null,"Top with the vegetable salad mixture."]],"h":[]},"6142192":{"s":[[null,"In a large resealable plastic storage bag, combine chicken with remaining ingredients. Place in refrigerator and marinate 8 hours or overnight, turning halfway during marinating time."],[null,"Preheat grill to medium-high heat. Place chicken on grill, discarding excess marinade. Grill chicken 4 to 6 minutes per side, or until cooked through."]],"h":[]},"3846":{"s":[[null,"Slice the chicken breasts in half crosswise, making two thin fillets from each breast."],[null,"Mince the garlic and combine with the remaining ingredients in a zip-top bag; mix well."],[null,"Add the chicken fillets to the bag. Seal and marinate in the refrigerator for 2 hours or longer, turning occasionally."],[null,"Remove the chicken from the marinade and grill over medium heat until the chicken is done, turning once. If using a meat thermometer the temperature should reach 165º F. Top chicken with fresh thyme sprigs while grilling if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Too cold to grill? Use your broiler to cook the chicken."],[null,"If you are on a lower protein diet you can reduce the portion to 1 fillet or the amount specified in your meal plan."]]},"7675617":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the grill to hot. Place a wire rack on a rimmed baking tray."],[null,"Cut the peppers in half and scoop out the white ribs and seeds, discarding them."],[null,"Mix the halved cherry tomatoes, chopped shallot, sliced garlic, chopped basil, and olive oil in a mixing bowl. Season to taste with some freshly ground black pepper."],[null,"Divide the tomato salad between the pepper halves, arranging them on the wire rack on the tray."],[null,"Grill for about 4-5 minutes until the peppers are lightly charred at the edges."],[null,"Remove from the grill and let stand briefly before serving on a platter with a garnish of basil leaves."]],"h":[[null,"Spice this dish by adding half a finely chopped chilli to the tomato mix."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"3505":{"s":[[null,"Chop onion. Remove seeds from chile and chop finely."],[null,"Place fish in an ovenproof baking dish."],[null,"Combine 1/4 teaspoon salt, cilantro, onion, sugar, chile, lime juice, oil and garlic in a blender or food processor and process until smooth."],[null,"Pour cilantro mixture over fish; turning to coat. Marinate in refrigerator at least 30 minutes, turning once halfway through marinating."],[null,"Prepare charcoal or gas grill and preheat."],[null,"Grill fish about 5 minutes on each side or until fish flakes easily with a fork."],[null,"Cut lime into wedges. Garnish fish with lime wedges and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Swordfish, like many types of fish, contains more phosphorus compared to beef or chicken. For a lower phosphorus fish dish you could substitute catfish, codfish or dolphin fish (mahi mahi) instead of swordfish."],[null,"Protein requirements for those with kidney disease vary based on the stage of CKD. Check with your dietitian for adjustments to recipes or serving size based on your individual protein requirements."]]},"1777":{"s":[[null,"Quarter-cut both onions.Seed bell peppers and cut into 8 pieces."],[null,"Prepare a covered grill for direct grilling."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine all ingredients, tossing well so that vegetables are evenly coated with oil."],[null,"Place vegetables in a grill basket, or arrange on metal skewers. Grill about 18 minutes, turning often so vegetables brown evenly on all sides."]],"h":[[null,"Serve with grilled fish or chicken."]]},"1851":{"s":[[null,"Set butter out to soften. Thinly slice the onion half."],[null,"Heat the olive oil in a skillet over medium-high heat. Add the onion slices and stir continuously until cooked and soft. Remove the onions from skillet and set aside."],[null,"Spread 1 tablespoon of whipped cream cheese on 2 of the bread slices, then add half of the grilled onions and cheese. Top with other bread slices."],[null,"Spread the butter on outside of bread slices. Grill the sandwich in a hot skillet until bread is toasted and cheese melts, turning once. Cover skillet with a lid while grilling the sandwich."]],"h":[[null,"Pre-sliced cheese is usually available in 1-ounce or 3/4-ounce slices. Use 1 + 1/4 slices on each sandwich if slices are 3/4-ounce each."],[null,"Make extra grilled onions and serve with a meat entrée for dinner."]]},"6089102":{"s":[[null,"Preheat an outdoor grill or grill pan to medium-high. Preheat the oven to 400°F."],[null,"In a large bowl, toss the peaches with the oil until well coated. Grill peaches cut-side down until charred, 2–3 minutes, then transfer them to a baking dish, cut-side up, and drizzle with the white balsamic vinegar."],[null,"Roast the peaches, uncovered, for 10–15 minutes, or until tender."],[null,"Meanwhile, in the bowl of a food processor, combine the yogurt, mascarpone, honey, and vanilla. Purée until smooth."],[null,"In a blender, pulse together the walnuts and cinnamon to form a crumble."],[null,"Remove peaches from the oven and serve each peach half with 2 tablespoons mascarpone cream and 1 tablespoon nut crumble."]],"h":[]},"3014":{"s":[[null,"Spread the peanut butter and jelly on the bread, and place bread together. Butter the outside of the bread."],[null,"Heat a frying pan over medium heat. Grill the sandwich until lightly browned on both sides."]],"h":[[null,"If preferred use margarine instead of butter."],[null,"Any flavor jelly is acceptable.Serve with carrot sticks and apple slices."],[null,"Select low-sodium peanut butter to reduce sodium to 350 mg."],[null,"Peanut butter is a high potassium, high phosphorus ingredient but still works in a kidney diet as a substitute for meat. Portion control is important."],[null,"Additional phosphate binder may be required if eaten as a snack—check with your renal dietitian."]]},"6359828":{"s":[[null,"Remove steak from the fridge 30 minutes before grilling. Rub steak with salt and pepper."],[null,"Preheat an indoor grill pan, skillet, or outdoor grill over medium-high heat."],[null,"Once the grill pan is hot, coat with oil. Add steak and cook for 6-8 minutes per side, until steak reaches desired doneness. Remove from heat and set aside on a plate; let rest for 5 minutes before slicing into thin strips."],[null,"Wipe the grill pan with a paper towel and spray it lightly with cooking spray. Return to medium heat."],[null,"Place two tortillas on the grill pan and grill for 2 -3 minutes, just until toasted. Flip and toast for another 2-3 minutes. Remove and grill the remaining tortillas."],[null,"Top the tortillas with salsa verde, sliced steak, avocado slices, diced tomatoes and cilantro."]],"h":[]},"4882636":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the grill to medium-high."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine the melted butter with the coconut extract."],[null,"With a brush, baste each pineapple slice on both sides with the flavored butter."],[null,"Reduce the heat on the grill to medium. Place the slices directly on the grill and cook for 2 minutes per side."],[null,"Serve with the raspberries and enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"* Coconut is very high in potassium and phosphorus but to still get the flavor you can use extract in moderation as we did in this recipe."],[null,"Instead of the grill you can use a griddle pan and make the recipe on the stove."],["Discover grilling fruit","Summertime is a great time to try new ways to prepare fruits. Consider grilling fruit to create unique flavors and textures. The best part is that you can grill almost anything. Choose lower-potassium fruits such as pineapple, pears, apples, lemon, limes, plums, and watermelon. No matter which fruit you choose, there are some basic techniques needed to create the perfect complement to a grilled meal. • Choose fruit that is ripe, but not too ripe. Heat weakens the fruit’s structure so overripe fruit will likely fall apart while grilling. • Cut fruit in large pieces to prevent it from falling between the bars of the grill. • Before grilling, lightly brush fruit with an oil that can stand up to high temperatures. Good choices include canola and safflower oil. Olive oil and butter are also an option when using lower temperatures. • Once the fruit is placed on the grill, do not disturb. It needs to sit on the hot grill for a few minutes before checking for grill marks, approximately 2 to 3 minutes. The fruit’s surface needs time to sear so it won’t stick to the grill. Be creative with your meal planning. Grilled fruit is delicious with both savory and sweet dishes so enjoy experimenting with a variety of combinations."]]},"6313311":{"s":[[null,"Rub the chicken breasts with 1 tablespoon olive oil and season with paprika, salt, and black pepper."],[null,"Preheat a grill or grill pan over medium-high heat. Grill the chicken for 6–7 minutes per side, or until fully cooked (internal temperature of 165°F). Remove from the grill and let rest for 5 minutes before slicing."],[null,"While the chicken rests, grill the pineapple for 2–3 minutes per side, or until caramelized and marked with grill lines."],[null,"Arrange the mixed greens evenly across 4 plates or a large serving platter. Scatter the sliced red onion over the greens."],[null,"Slice the grilled chicken into thin strips and cut the pineapple into bite-sized chunks. Divide evenly over the salad."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together 2 tablespoons olive oil, lime juice, and monk fruit sweetener. Drizzle the dressing over the salad."],[null,"Sprinkle chopped cilantro over the salad and serve immediately."]],"h":[]},"1954":{"s":[[null,"Drain the pineapple slices. Wash the pear and cut into wedges. Wash the bell pepper and cut into strips. Heat a grill pan over medium heat."],[null,"Spray the grill pan with cooking spray and place fruit and vegetables in the pan. (You may have to cook in two batches.) Cook about 5 minutes per side, until slightly browned."],[null,"Place cooked pineapple, pear, pepper and onion in a food processor or blender. Pulse until coarsely chopped."],[null,"Let salsa sit in the refrigerator overnight."]],"h":[[null,"Serve with low-sodium crackers or tortilla chips. Look for brands with the lowest amount of sodium."],[null,"You may also serve with homemade pita chips. Split the pitas in half and cut each half into quarters. Spray with cooking spray and bake in a 350º F oven for about 8 minutes."],[null,"Drain salsa through a fine sieve to remove fluid if you are on a fluid restriction."],[null,"If desired use fresh instead of canned pineapple."]]},"6549854":{"s":[[null,"Combine all of the marinade ingredients in a medium bowl and put into a large tightly sealed plastic bag. Marinate mushroom caps at least 15-30 minutes at room temperature for best results."],[null,"Preheat grill to medium high and place mushroom caps on grill grate. Cook under direct heat for 5 minutes per side until completely through to tender. Baste occasionally with additional marinade while cooking. You can pour any leftover marinade over mushrooms before serving."]],"h":[]},"6644588":{"s":[[null,"Preheat an outdoor grill to medium. Coat the grill rack with cooking spray."],[null,"Slice each romaine heart in half lengthwise, keeping the root end intact."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk the vinegar, mustard, and garlic. In a thin stream, slowly add the olive oil, and whisk until the dressing is emulsified. Stir in the salt and black pepper."],[null,"Add the romaine hearts to the grill, cut side down. Brush some of the vinaigrette over the romaine hearts. Grill, uncovered, for about 2 minutes. Using tongs, carefully turn the romaine hearts and brush with the remaining dressing; grill for 1 minute. Remove the romaine hearts from the grill and place on a plate to serve."]],"h":[]},"1761":{"s":[[null,"Prepare fresh salmon by sprinkling with salt-free lemon pepper seasoning. Squeeze a small amount of lemon juice over the fish. Spray with 3-4 sprites of liquid margarine spray."],[null,"Place on preheated grill and cook over medium heat for 15 to 20 minutes or until fish reaches desired doneness. Serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"Cooking time varies with thickness of salmon fillets."]]},"2611":{"s":[[null,"Preheat grill to medium-high heat. Rub salmon fillets with 1 tablespoon of the olive oil. Place salmon fillets on the grill and cover. Cook until the flesh flakes easily, 10 to 15 minutes."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine remaining olive oil, lime juice and lemon-pepper seasoning.\"#4. While salmon is resting, brush the sourdough bread with olive oil and place on the grill grates and grill 1-2 minutes on each side, or until toasted."],[null,"Remove salmon from grill, and allow to rest, covered with foil on a plate for 5-10 minutes. Remove the skin."],[null,"While salmon is resting, place sourdough bread on grill grates and allow 1-2 minutes on each side, or until toasted."],[null,"To assemble the open faced sandwich, start with sourdough bread, and top with an even amount of chipotle mayo, then the arugula, salmon, and top with the roasted red peppers."]],"h":[[null,"For a lower protein meal plan divide salmon fillets in half. Protein content is 15 grams per sandwich."],[null,"Consider adding diced scallions or chives for garnish."],[null,"Be sure there is no added salt in the lemon-pepper seasoning by looking at the ingredient list."],[null,"If you don’t like salmon, try using a different fish, such as cod or trout."],[null,"Sourdough bread could be substituted with other types of breads."],[null,"Chipotle mayonnaise has a slightly spicy/smoky flavor. If you dislike these flavors, easily substitute pesto sauce, plain mayonnaise, or dijonnaise (Dijon mustard and mayonnaise mixed)."]]},"3747":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400° F or preheat grill."],[null,"Using aluminum foil, create 1 cooking pocket for each fillet (if using frozen salmon, make sure it’s fully thawed)."],[null,"Chop oregano, cilantro, green onions and garlic. Combine with lemon juice, olive oil, salt and pepper in a food processor. Process to chop and mix."],[null,"Coat the salmon fillets generously with herb mixture."],[null,"Place each fillet in foil pocket and seal."],[null,"Place foil pockets on a baking sheet or grill plate if cooking on a grill."],[null,"Bake for 30 minutes or until done, or grill for 6 to 8 minutes depending on thickness."]],"h":[[null,"Use either fresh or frozen salmon. When using frozen salmon, make sure it is fully thawed before cooking."],[null,"Salmon can be baked in the oven or cooked on the grill."],[null,"Adjust portion size to meet your protein goals."]]},"6615019":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the grill to medium high heat."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine chili powder, cumin, garlic powder, cinnamon, and salt. Sprinkle the spice mixture evenly over the salmon fillets."],[null,"Lightly oil the grill grates with the canola oil. Place the salmon on the grill, skin side down. Cook uncovered for 7 to 8 minutes, turning halfway through. The salmon is done when it flakes easily with a fork."],[null,"While salmon is cooking, combine mango, tomatoes, cilantro, and half of the lemon juice in a medium bowl."],[null,"Remove salmon from grill and spritz with remaining lemon juice. Serve each fillet with 1/2 cup salsa."]],"h":[]},"6914404":{"s":[[null,"Prepare an indoor or outdoor grill."],[null,"In a medium bowl, mix together the tomatillo, jalapeno, cilantro, zucchini, lime juice, Stevia and garlic. Mix together and set aside."],[null,"Pat the scallops dry with a paper towel. Toss them with the olive oil, salt and pepper in a medium bowl."],[null,"Place scallops on grill, flat side down. Turning occasionally, grill until lightly charred and just cooked through, about 2 minutes per side. Serve scallops topped with the chunky salsa verde."]],"h":[]},"6981196":{"s":[[null,"Combine orange juice, lime juice, honey, salt, and cayenne pepper in a small mixing bowl. Mix well and set aside."],[null,"Cook the quinoa according to directions in water. Fluff quinoa with a fork. If any liquid remains, continue simmering until it is absorbed. Let the quinoa cool completely."],[null,"Toss the shrimp and scallops with the olive oil in a bowl."],[null,"Heat a grill pan or sauté pan over medium-high heat. Add the shrimp and scallops and sear until pink and just cooked through, about 2 minutes per side. Remove from the pan and let cool."],[null,"Place the cooled quinoa in a large bowl and add the shrimp and scallops, beans, jalapeno, bell pepper, tomato, scallions, mango and avocado. Pour the dressing over the mixture and toss gently to combine."],[null,"Divide the salad among four plates or bowls and scatter cilantro leaves over each."]],"h":[]},"6736784":{"s":[[null,"Preheat an outdoor grill or grill pan."],[null,"Add the asparagus spears and oil into a 9 × 13-inch dish. Toss with tongs to coat."],[null,"Grill the asparagus (in batches, if necessary) over direct medium-high heat until just cooked through and lightly browned, about 6–8 minutes total, rotating only as needed."],[null,"Remove spears from the grill and place back into the dish, sprinkle with the salt and sesame seeds, and serve."]],"h":[]},"6638790":{"s":[[null,"Prepare an indoor or outdoor grill."],[null,"In a medium bowl, whisk together olive oil, garlic, lemon zest, lemon juice, crushed red pepper flakes, salt (optional), pepper and scallions."],[null,"Add shrimp to bowl and toss to coat evenly. Cover and refrigerate for 30 minutes."],[null,"Divide shrimp evenly among nine skewers. Discard remaining marinade."],[null,"Grill skewers 2-3 minutes on each side or until shrimp are pink and slightly firm to the touch."]],"h":[]},"6077237":{"s":[[null,"In a bowl, mix together ½ tablespoon olive oil, minced garlic, dried oregano, smoked paprika, ¼ teaspoon black pepper. Add the steak and stir well to coat the meat in the oil and spices."],[null,"In another bowl, toss the vegetables with ½ tablespoon olive oil, 1/8 teaspoon salt and ¼ teaspoon pepper."],[null,"Thread the marinated steak cubes, zucchini slices, red onion wedges, and cherry tomatoes onto the skewers, alternating for variety."],[null,"Preheat the grill to medium-high heat."],[null,"Place the kebabs on the preheated grill. Grill, turning occasionally, until the steak reaches your desired level of doneness and the vegetables are tender with a slight char, about 8 minutes, for medium."],[null,"Remove the kebabs from the grill and let them rest for a few minutes before serving."]],"h":[]},"6482949":{"s":[[null,"In a medium bowl, whisk together the yogurt, Neufchâtel, and honey until thick and creamy. Spread the crème onto a serving platter or board."],[null,"Prepare and preheat a grill or grill pan. Brush the cut side of the strawberry halves with the oil and grill over direct medium-high heat, cut-side down, until rich grill marks form, about 4 minutes."],[null,"Arrange the strawberries on the crème. Drizzle with the balsamic glaze, sprinkle with the almonds and fresh herbs, and serve."],[null,"*Make your own balsamic reduction sauce: Add 1/4 cup balsamic vinegar to a small saucepan, bring to a boil over high heat, then reduce heat to medium and cook, stirring a couple times, until it can just coat the back of a spoon (to yield about 1 1/2 tablespoons), about 5 minutes. (Note: The balsamic reduction thickens slightly as it cools.)"]],"h":[]},"2195":{"s":[[null,"Wash squash with mild soap and water; rinse well."],[null,"Cut each squash into four pieces; cut both vertically and horizontally."],[null,"Place on a cookie sheet or large platter and spray with non-stick cooking spray."],[null,"Sprinkle with garlic powder and black pepper, to taste (both optional)."],[null,"Cook on either a George Foreman™ grill or a gas grill. If using the Foreman™ grill, cook for approximately three to five minutes, flipping once. The squash should be tender but not mushy. If cooking on a gas grill, place flat surface down on a sheet of aluminum foil sprayed with non-stick cooking spray."],[null,"Cook approximately 5 to 7 minutes over a medium flame, watching carefully. Flip and cook approximately 2 more minutes on the “round” side."]],"h":[[null,"*Note: This is a “cook once, eat twice” recipe. It makes 4 servings for the first dish, and then 4 servings for the second. Alternatively, the full recipe serves 8. See recipe for Italian Chicken Salad to use this for a cook once, eat twice recipe."],[null,"Serve 2 pieces of zucchini and 2 pieces of yellow squash with the Chicken in Rosemary-Garlic Sauce. Use remaining squash for the Italian Chicken Salad; cut squash pieces into 1/4″ thick half-moons."]]},"6828323":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the grill to medium-high heat."],[null,"In a large bowl, toss sliced zucchinis, red and yellow bell peppers, red onion rings, and halved cherry tomatoes with olive oil. Season with salt and 1/2 tsp black pepper."],[null,"Grill the veggies for about 10 minutes or until they are tender and have grill marks, turning occasionally."],[null,"Remove the grilled veggies from the heat."],[null,"To make the dressing: In a small bowl, whisk together extra virgin olive oil, balsamic vinegar, minced garlic, chopped fresh basil, chopped fresh parsley, fresh thyme leaves, salt, and 1/4 tsp black pepper."],[null,"Arrange the grilled veggies on a serving platter. Serve the dressing on the side."]],"h":[]},"6671502":{"s":[[null,"In a small saucepan, whisk together the soy sauce, water, honey, ginger, sesame oil, and garlic. Bring to boiling, then reduce to a simmer. Simmer for 7 to 8 minutes or until the sauce is reduced and slightly syrupy. Set aside to cool."],[null,"Preheat an outdoor grill to medium heat and spray one side of each sheet of foil with cooking spray."],[null,"In a medium bowl, toss together vegetables, garlic and seasoning."],[null,"Evenly divide the vegetables among the pieces of foil. Top the vegetables with a piece of tuna steak and drizzle 1 Tbsp. of prepared Teriyaki sauce over the tuna."],[null,"Bring the ends of the foil together and fold over tightly, three times until sealed to make a packet."],[null,"Grill the packets for 20 minutes. Be careful when opening the packets; the steam may be hot."]],"h":[]},"6994119":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, combine corn, red bell pepper, red onion, jalapeño, rice vinegar, olive oil, and cilantro. Toss well and set aside."],[null,"Pat the tilapia fillets dry with a paper towel. Spray with cooking spray on both sides. Sprinkle evenly with cumin, smoked paprika, garlic powder, and black pepper."],[null,"Preheat a grill or grill pan over medium-high heat. Spray the pan with oil. Grill the tilapia for 3–4 minutes per side, or until the fish flakes easily with a fork. Remove from heat and let rest for a minute."],[null,"Divide the arugula among 4 plates. Place a grilled tilapia fillet on top of the arugula. Spoon the crunchy corn salsa over and around the fish."]],"h":[]},"9627687":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, combine the vinegar, lime juice and salt and set aside."],[null,"Halve your tomatoes or cut in thirds if your tomatoes are very large. You want roughly 1/2\" thick tomato slices. Add the tomatoes to your marinade bowl and mix to coat."],[null,"Heat your grill to high heat and place the tomatoes in a single layer, basting the tops with the chimichurri sauce. Cook for 3-5 minutes, or until grill marks form. Then flip and baste the other side with more chimichurri and cook for an additional 3-5 minutes. Do not overcook or the tomatoes will get too soft."]],"h":[[null,"Use tomatoes that are firm (but ripe). Softer, overly ripe tomatoes will not hold up well on the grill. Do not cut your tomato slices too thin , or they won’t hold up on the grill. Make sure not to overcook your tomatoes , or they will get too soft."]]},"6822428":{"s":[[null,"DO AHEAD OR DELEGATE: Zest and juice the lemons."],[null,"Preheat the grill to medium heat and oil the grates to prevent the fish from sticking. (Alternatively, bake the trout at 400°F for about 25 minutes.) In a small bowl, combine the chopped herbs, the zest of 1 ½ lemons, and the juice of 1 lemon. Cut the other lemon into thin slices."],[null,"Lay the trout on a cutting board, skin side up, and brush the skin with olive oil to coat. Flip the fish and rub the lemon-herb mixture over the flesh of the trout, season with the salt and pepper, and lay the lemon slices on top of one half of each trout. Close the trout around the herbs and lemon slices, and transfer the fish to the grill."],[null,"Grill the fish with the lid closed, without flipping, for 8 minutes or until the flesh is opaque and flaky. Using a spatula, carefully transfer the trout to a plate to serve. Garnish the plate with a few fresh mint leaves and sprigs of rosemary, if desired."],[null,"SLOW COOKER DIRECTIONS: Place each piece of fish on an individual piece of foil, stuff each with the spices and lemon. Close the trout around the herbs and lemon slices, and fold the foil into a packet to completely surround the fish. Place the packets in the slow cooker and cook on low for 8–10 hours or on high for 4–5 hours. (Slow cooker cooking times may vary—get to know your slow cooker and, if necessary, adjust cooking times accordingly.)"],[null,"FLAVOR BOOSTER Season the fish with freshly ground black pepper or lemon-pepper seasoning at the table."]],"h":[]},"6953713":{"s":[[null,"Season tenderloins with garlic powder and black pepper."],[null,"In a medium bowl, whisk together all marinade ingredients. Place the tenderloins in a large plastic storage bag. Pour marinade over tenderloins and coat well. Seal bag and refrigerate 1 hour or overnight."],[null,"Spray grill with cooking spray and preheat to medium-high."],[null,"Remove tenderloins from marinade, discarding any remaining marinade. Grill tenderloins turning frequently, about 25 minutes or until done and internal temperature reaches 165 degrees."],[null,"While turkey is grilling prepare mango salsa. In a small bowl, combine all mango salsa ingredients and mix well."],[null,"Slice the tenderloins into about 3/4-inch slices and spread mango salsa evenly over tenderloins."],[null,"TIME-SAVING TIP: Use frozen mangoes to make the salsa. You can defrost in your refrigerator in the morning and dice them up for dinner time."]],"h":[]},"6740803":{"s":[[null,"Prepare an indoor or outdoor grill."],[null,"Cook pasta according to package directions, omitting salt."],[null,"Coat all of the vegetables with cooking spray and grill for 7-10 minutes, turning frequently."],[null,"Remove vegetables from grill and dice."],[null,"Drain the cooked pasta and immediately add the diced grilled vegetables to the hot pasta. Add the olive oil, garlic, oregano, salt (optional), and ground black pepper and stir well to coat. Serve this dish warm or cold."]],"h":[]},"6421780":{"s":[[null,"Preheat an indoor or outdoor grill."],[null,"In a large bowl, whisk together olive oil, balsamic vinegar and ground black pepper."],[null,"Add sliced zucchini, squash and bell pepper to marinade and let sit for 5 minutes."],[null,"Grill the vegetables about 2-3 minutes on both sides."],[null,"Lay out the tortilla and spread with 2 Tbsp. hummus, then add two fresh basil leaves and top with 2 slices of zucchini, 2 slices of yellow squash and 1 slice bell pepper."],[null,"Fold in the two sides of the tortilla and roll like a burrito. You can serve these immediately or wrap tightly in plastic and refrigerate."]],"h":[]},"6921889":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the grill or a grill pan to 350 degrees."],[null,"In a large bowl, toss the zucchini rounds with olive oil, dried thyme, salt, and pepper."],[null,"Use tongs to place the rounds on the grill."],[null,"Grill for 3–4 minutes on each side, until tender and charred in places."]],"h":[]},"6664734":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, mix together the tomato, kalamata olives, pine nuts, parsley, and ¼ tsp coarse salt. Set aside."],[null,"Preheat a grill pan or grill over medium high heat."],[null,"In a bowl, toss zucchini slices with coconut oil, minced garlic, and ¼ tsp coarse salt. Place on grill and grill 3 minutes per side."],[null,"Serve each slice warm with a generous topping of the salsa."]],"h":[]},"6051334":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the grill to medium-high."],[null,"Drizzle the olive oil evenly over the zucchini halves. Grill the zucchini 4-5 minutes per side, until tender."],[null,"Remove the zucchini from the grill and sprinkle each with feta cheese."]],"h":[]},"2473":{"s":[[null,"Peel and cube potatoes and place in a large pot of water; bring to a boil. Remove from heat, drain water and add fresh room temperature water. Bring potatoes to a boil and cook for 10 minutes. Drain."],[null,"Chop onion. Simmer ground beef, onion and 1/2 cup of water in a 3-quart pan until meat is crumbled and brown."],[null,"Add potatoes, green peas and remaining 2 cups of water to ground beef mixture. Continue to simmer for 10 minutes, until peas are tender."],[null,"Mix 1/4 cup of beef broth with cornstarch and stir until cornstarch is dissolved."],[null,"Add cornstarch mixture to pan along with remaining broth, and simmer until casserole is thick."],[null,"Serve hot and enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"This is a favorite from the Idle-Not ranch in Colorado."],[null,"Step # 1 instructs on the double boiling method to reduce potassium in potatoes. Skip the double boiling and cook potatoes until tender if a low potassium diet is not required."],[null,"Any type of potato can be substituted for new potatoes."],[null,"Mix it up– substitute ground deer or chicken for beef."],[null,"Substitute frozen mixed vegetables, frozen green beans, or frozen carrots for peas if desired."]]},"3077":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375° F. Spray a piece of foil with nonstick cooking spray. Chop the onion."],[null,"Combine the ground beef, onion and Worcestershire sauce into a patty and place on the foil."],[null,"Top patty with frozen peas and carrots."],[null,"Sprinkle Italian dressing mix and black pepper over the top."],[null,"Fold and seal the foil and place on a baking sheet. Bake for 35 minutes."],[null,"Carefully open one end of the foil packet and allow steam to escape before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Spray the foil with cooking spray."],[null,"Place the foil packet on a baking sheet before placing in the oven."]]},"3368":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Chop onion and dice bell pepper."],[null,"Brown ground beef with onion and bell pepper in a skillet over medium heat. Drain fat."],[null,"Add salt, chili powder, cayenne, oregano and garlic powder. Stir to mix. Spray a 2-quart casserole dish with nonstick cooking spray. Pour beef mixture into dish."],[null,"In a medium bowl, combine nondairy creamer and egg substitute. Stir in crumbled cornbread and jalapeno peppers until ingredients are combined. Do not over mix. Spoon over beef mixture. Bake 30 minutes or until cornbread topping is browned."]],"h":[[null,"A great way to use leftover cornbread. Try our recipe for Southern-style Cornbread—it’s low in sodium and phosphorus, but full or flavor!"]]},"6844012":{"s":[],"h":[]},"3630":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375° F. Let pie crust stand at room temperature according to package directions."],[null,"Dice carrot and chop onion."],[null,"Brown ground sirloin in a large skillet over medium heat. Drain and set aside."],[null,"Place carrot in a microwave dish. Add 1 tablespoon water; cover and cook on high for 2 minutes. Add frozen corn, and peas; microwave for 2 minutes. Drain."],[null,"To make filling, combine meat, vegetables, onion, Worcestershire sauce, black pepper and thyme in a bowl."],[null,"On a lightly floured surface, unroll pie crusts. Cut each pie crust into four pieces."],[null,"Spoon 1/4 cup of the filling onto half of each piece of piecrust. Lightly moisten pie crust edges with a small amount of milk or egg white."],[null,"Fold other half of pie crust over filling. Seal edges by crimping with a fork. Cut slits in the top of the pastries. Brush top with egg white. Place on a large, ungreased baking sheet."],[null,"Bake for 15 to 20 minutes or until crust is golden brown. Cool slightly on wire racks."],[null,"Serve each pastie with 1 teaspoon ketchup."]],"h":[[null,"Wrap and freeze extra pasties for a quick meal later. Reheat in the oven or microwave."],[null,"For variety substitute ground turkey or chicken for beef."]]},"7364517":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 180°C / gas mark 4."],[null,"De-stone, peel, and mash a ripe avocado into a bowl."],[null,"Add the tomatoes, onions, a pinch of pepper, yogurt, lime juice and coriander, then mix well. Place in a bowl and sprinkle with chilli, if using."],[null,"Meanwhile, place the tortillas onto a baking tray and bake for 10- 12 minutes, turning a couple of times. While they’re cooking, chop your dipping vegetables."],[null,"Arrange veggies and tortilla chips on a serving platter with the guacamole to serve."]],"h":[[null,"If you prefer a spicy guacamole, add chilli flakes and/or 1 tsp of chilli powder along with the pepper."],[null,"You can use any vegetables you like for dipping. Choose a variety of different colours or textures to keep things interesting."],[null,"This recipe can be made gluten-free easily - all you need to do is use gluten-free tortillas."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6182435":{"s":[[null,"Cut out the stem of each cherry tomato, cutting deep enough to make a hole into the middle of the tomato without going through the other end."],[null,"Scoop the insides of the tomato out and finely chop the insides of tomato and reserve for the guacamole. Place each scooped out tomato upside down on paper towels to drain."],[null,"In a medium bowl, mash the avocado with a fork and mix in the scooped out tomato pieces, lime juice, garlic, 1 Tbsp. cilantro, salt (optional), and pepper."],[null,"Scoop or pipe the guacamole into the hollowed out tomatoes, dividing it equally among each tomato. Sprinkle the remaining cilantro on top of each tomato."]],"h":[]},"2905":{"s":[[null,"Finely chop garlic and dice the onion into small pieces. Heat oil in a skillet and add chopped garlic and onion and cook until translucent."],[null,"Add guava paste and water and stir until smooth and the paste dissolves."],[null,"Add the remaining ingredients and cook over low to medium heat until smooth, about 5 to 10 minutes. Be sure to not let the sauce boil."],[null,"Remove the skillet from heat and let cool."],[null,"Store sauce in a jar or covered container until ready to use."]],"h":[[null,"Baste meat with sauce at the end of cooking."],[null,"Try Guava Barbecue Sauce on Puerto Rican Style Chicken Skewers or grilled beef."]]},"6421611":{"s":[[null,"Combine all ingredients in a large bowl and mix well."],[null,"Divide mixture into 28 serving and shape mixture into 2-inch patties."],[null,"In a large skillet over medium-low heat, cook patties 3-5 minutes per side, or until no longer pink in center. Ensure patties reach an internal temperature of 165°F. Serve immediately."]],"h":[]},"1002726":{"s":[[null,"Dice beef, finely chop celery and strip rosemary leaves from the stem. Melt butter with 2 tablespoons vegetable oil in a saucepan. Add rosemary and celery and sauté for a few minutes. Add cubed beef and brown on all sides."],[null,"Add finely chopped peeled tomato and 1/4 cup hot water and simmer, covered, for about 1-1/4 hours."],[null,"Meanwhile, peel and dice potatoes. Place in a large pan and cover completely with water. Bring potatoes to a boil and drain. Repeat the boiling process. Drain."],[null,"Ten minutes before removing the stew from the heat, add potatoes and stir everything well. Serve piping hot."]],"h":[[null,"Boiling potatoes twice reduces potassium."]]},"1002733":{"s":[[null,"Place 1/2 liter of water in a skillet."],[null,"Remove skin from chicken leg quarters and add them to the skillet."],[null,"Crush garlic. Finely chop all remaining ingredients and add them to the chicken."],[null,"Cook over low heat for 30 minutes."],[null,"Serve chicken with the stew sauce that has formed."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute chicken breast for chicken thighs if desired."]]},"7816882":{"s":[[null,"Give the haddock a pump of spray oil and lay skin side up on a sheet of parchment paper. Preheat the grill to high and grill the fish for 3-4mins. Turn, spray with oil and grill for a further 3-4 mins. Meanwhile, bring a large pan of water to the boil, add the beans and broccoli and simmer for 5 mins."],[null,"Put the herbs, garlic, oil and gherkins in a blender. Wash the salt from the anchovy fillets and pat dry. Add to the blender and blend the sauce until finely chopped, adding 1tsp of water to thin the sauce if necessary. Drain the broccoli and beans, return to the pan, add the crème fraiche and coarsely mash. Divide the mash between 2 plates, top each with the fish and add the salsa verde. Serve with a lemon wedge."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"7895649":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 150°C/gas 2. Place the oil, molasses and milk in a pan, and heat gently for 2 minutes."],[null,"In a bowl, mix together the flour, oatmeal, baking powder, ginger, mixed spice and sweetener. Beat in the egg and mashed banana."],[null,"Line a 30cm x 20cm baking tray with baking parchment. Gently stir the oil mixture into the bowl and pour into the lined tin until about 1cm thick. Bake in the centre of the oven for one hour, or until the centre of the cake is just firm to the touch."],[null,"Remove from the oven and leave it to cool in the tin for 15-20 minutes. Transfer to a chopping board and cut into shapes or squares."]],"h":[[null,"We used Halloween shapes for the picture, but you could just cut into more traditional squares. Or you could make the cake in a deeper baking tray and cut into smaller cubes."],[null,"Blackstrap molasses is high in sugar but has a strong taste, so you only need a little to add a lot of flavour to your recipe."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"4744423":{"s":[[null,"In a bowl, shred the tofu with a fork. Add the ground beef, 1 tablespoon olive oil, garlic, onions, cayenne pepper, black pepper, and eggs. Mix all ingredients with a fork and set aside for 15 minutes."],[null,"Turn on the grill and heat to medium-high."],[null,"In a non-stick frying pan, heat 1 teaspoon olive oil over medium heat. Add the onions and red bell peppers and fry for 2 minutes."],[null,"Add the vinegar to the onion and pepper mixture, turn the heat down to medium-low, and cook for another 10 minutes, stirring occasionally until vegetables are tender."],[null,"Add the honey to the vegetables in the last minute of cooking. Turn off the heat and set aside."],[null,"Form four patties with the meat/tofu mixture and place the hamburgers on the grill. Reduce heat to medium and cook patties for 5 minutes on one side. Turn them and cook for another 5-7 minutes. To ensure doneness, use a meat thermometer. The internal temperature should reach 160°F and the meat should have lost its pink color."],[null,"During the last 2-3 minutes of cooking, place the hamburger buns on the grill to toast them."],[null,"Once the buns are toasted and burgers are done, assemble the hamburgers, placing a pattie on a bun and top with vegetable mixture and lettuce."]],"h":[[null,"PLEASE NOTE: This recipe is higher in potassium and portion size is important. Check with your registered dietitian to see how this recipe can be included in your diet. For CKD and Transplant: make six slider-sized burgers with slider-sized buns."],["How to transition to using more plant-based protein","Whether you are in the earlier stages of chronic kidney disease or needing dialysis, plant-based proteins can be a healthy option. Eating more plant-based proteins compared to animal proteins will produce less acid in your body which can slow the progression of kidney disease, and if you require dialysis, this will help to protect your bones and muscles. It can be hard to make big changes in your eating habits overnight, especially if meat has always been a part of your diet. One way to achieve the goal of eating more plant-based proteins is to transition your diet over time by eating less animal protein and building in more plant-based proteins. This can be accomplished by adjusting your daily menus or one recipe at a time. This recipe is a classic example of adding a plant-based protein such as tofu to beef to make a more healthful hamburger. The resulting hamburger is lower in fat, saturated fat, and cholesterol and more kidney-friendly as it is lower in protein, potassium, and phosphorus."]]},"4836884":{"s":[[null,"Drain the jar of roasted red peppers. Puree the peppers in a food processor or blender with the beef broth. Set aside."],[null,"In a large saucepan over medium-high heat, sauté ground beef until browned and cooked through, approximately 8–10 minutes. Drain fat and return ground beef to saucepan."],[null,"To the same pan, add garlic, onion and celery. Sauté 2–3 minutes until aromatic."],[null,"Add roasted red pepper puree from step 1. Bring to a boil."],[null,"Add orzo, oregano, basil, thyme, garlic powder and vinegar. Simmer approximately 10–15 minutes or until orzo is cooked."],[null,"Serve immediately."]],"h":[["What’s the skinny on ground meat?","Any meat that has been finely chopped by a meat grinder is called ground meat. Ground beef is probably the most common type of ground meat sold in your grocery store, but if you look carefully, you’ll likely find ground turkey, chicken and possibly lamb as well. All ground meats are an excellent source of protein and can be added to a wide variety of dishes to boost their protein content when needed. Ground meats can be added to soups and casseroles as well as rice or pasta dishes. By adding other ingredients such as herbs and chopped vegetables to ground meats, you can create tasty meatballs, meat patties, a meat loaf or a meat pie. When shopping, buy ground meat with the lowest fat content that is affordable. For example, ground beef that is 93% lean, 7% fat contains less fat and calories than ground beef that is 80% lean, 20% fat. The lower-fat option is considered the healthier option. It is important to note that there are special food safety concerns with ground meat. If undercooked, it can lead to food borne illness so be sure to cook it well before eating."]]},"2010":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 425° F."],[null,"Chop onion and mince garlic clove. Crush crackers and measure 1/2 cup."],[null,"Mix together all ingredients in a large bowl."],[null,"Shape meat mixture into 6 hamburger patties."],[null,"Place patties in a baking dish."],[null,"Bake uncovered for 20 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"For a complete meal, add a small hamburger bun, a slice of onion, lettuce and 1 teaspoon of ketchup."],[null,"This recipe can also be used to make meatloaf."],[null,"For a high protein diet, make 4 patties to increase patty size to 3 ounces cooked. Protein is increased to 27 grams per serving."],[null,"Instead of baking you can grill patties on the barbeque, turning once until thoroughly cooked."]]},"54949":{"s":[[null,"Mix mayonnaise, mustard, chopped pickles, vinegar, sugar, chopped onion and paprika and set aside."],[null,"Heat sauté pan on medium and add beef, breaking up clumps until cooked through. Add pepper and mix in pan."],[null,"While beef is cooking, chop lettuce and slice onion."],[null,"When ready to serve mix lettuce, cheese and onion. This can be divided into 4 bowls, or you can store any unused portions."],[null,"Add about a 1/4 of beef to each bowl and drizzle with dressing. Serve right away."]],"h":[[null,"You can store the ingredients separately and use them as leftovers. If on a lower protein diet use only 8 ounces of beef."],[null,"May use light mayonnaise but look for the lowest sodium version."]]},"1002939":{"s":[[null,"Soak lentils in water for 6 hours before making the burgers, changing the water every 2 hours."],[null,"Crush garlic and chop onion and bell pepper."],[null,"Grind or mash lentils into a dough, adding garlic, onion and bell pepper."],[null,"Knead well, add the three egg whites, ground beef and 2 tablespoons wheat flour and continue kneading."],[null,"Heat oil in a skillet while shaping the burgers by hand."],[null,"Fry burgers on both sides until golden brown, watching that they don’t burn."]],"h":[[null,"Instead of flour, you can add bread crumbs, and you can add cilantro or parsley (15 grams) to taste."],[null,"You can also use other legumes, such as green peas or beans, as you prefer. You can make meatballs with the same mixture."],[null,"You can also use other legumes, such as green peas or beans, as you prefer."]]},"4544743":{"s":[[null,"In a small, non-stick frying pan, heat oil over medium heat."],[null,"Fry the onion and the peppers until the onions are soft. Season with cayenne pepper."],[null,"Add the beaten eggs and stir from time to time until the eggs are cooked, but still soft. Set aside."],[null,"Fill each tortilla with two leaves of lettuce and half of the egg mixture. Garnish with green onions, roll them closed and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Make a breakfast sandwich by serving the egg mixture on a slice of toast."],["Breakfast — a very important meal for all","Have you ever wondered why our first meal of the day is called breakfast? This is the meal to break your overnight time of fasting since your evening meal from the previous day. It is essential to “break” that fast to provide much needed nutrition for your body. For those who receive dialysis, a protein-rich breakfast can be an excellent way to help you consume enough protein in your diet. Without three protein-rich meals per day, it can be very difficult to eat all the protein that you require to prevent protein malnutrition. There are countless breakfast options to consider that will add protein to your diet. A traditional hot breakfast may consist of eggs with sausage. With these breakfast meats, the sodium content of this type of meal can be quite high. One option to lower the sodium content would be to have eggs alone. Another option would be to make your own low-sodium sausage. This can be done by adding spices such as sage and ground black pepper to fresh ground turkey and shape into patties for cooking. Another high protein breakfast option would be to break tradition with the egg and have leftovers from the evening before. This may be the best option on dialysis days when time may be limited to prepare a protein-rich breakfast. Ask your dietitian for other breakfast ideas to help you meet your nutritional goals for the day."]]},"6459632":{"s":[[null,"Lay the eggs in a single layer on the bottom of a large sauce pan and cover with cold water so that there is about an inch of water over the eggs."],[null,"Place the pan on a stovetop burner but before turning on the heat, set a timer for 20 minutes."],[null,"Start the timer then turn the heat to high and bring to a boil. Once boiling, reduce to a gentle simmer and simmer until the timer goes off."],[null,"When the timer goes off, immediately drain the water from the pan then gently shake the eggs in the pan to crack the shells."],[null,"Cover in ice water and let sit in the ice water for 15 minutes."],[null,"Drain the ice water, then gently roll each egg on a paper towel to loosen the shell, and peel the shell off of the egg."],[null,"Store in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to one week."]],"h":[]},"6724295":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375°F."],[null,"Bring a pot of water to a boil. Add haricots verts. Reduce heat to medium and cook until just tender, 3–4 minutes. Drain, and plunge haricots verts into an ice-water bath to chill. Drain, and set aside. (This can be done up to a day in advance.)"],[null,"Heat 1 tablespoon. oil in a large, wide skillet over medium heat Add onion, salt, and pepper, and cook, stirring occasionally, until onions are light golden brown, 4–5 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, place hazelnuts in a baking pan and toast in the oven until they darken, 5–7 minutes. Chop roughly and set aside."],[null,"In a large skillet, heat the remaining 1 tablespoon. olive oil over medium-high heat. Add haricots verts and cook, stirring occasionally, until heated through, about 3 minutes. Add cooked onions and hazelnuts and cook 1 additional minute. Transfer to a serving dish, and serve."]],"h":[]},"7540419":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a large pan, add the onion and cook for 5 minutes until starting to brown."],[null,"Add the lamb and cook for a further 7 minutes, stirring regularly."],[null,"Now add the peppers, carrots and aubergine, mix well and cook for 5 minutes."],[null,"Next, add the garlic, paprika, cumin, turmeric and cinnamon. Mix well, then add the tomatoes, crumble in the stock cube and stir in the water."],[null,"Bring to the boil, stir and cover. Turn down the heat and simmer gently for 1 hour, then add the chickpeas and lentils, including their water. Mix well and cook for a further 30 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, mix the yogurt and coriander together."],[null,"Ladle the soup into bowls and top with a dollop of the coriander yogurt and a squeeze of lemon."]],"h":[[null,"For a veggie version, swap the lamb for a pack of marinated or smoked tofu and a can of mixed beans."],[null,"Harira also works well with chicken or beef."],[null,"Keeps in the fridge for 2-3 days – it tastes even better the day after you've made it."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"7314971":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200°C, fan 180°C, gas mark 6, and line 2 baking trays with baking paper."],[null,"Put the yogurt and the flour into a mixing bowl and season well. Mix until a soft dough forms."],[null,"Dust a work surface with the flour. Divide the pizza dough into 4 pieces and roll out each piece to a 15cm circle. Transfer to the prepared baking trays, scatter over the onion then top with the tomato slices."],[null,"In a small jug, combine the harissa paste, vinegar and oil, then season well. Drizzle or brush the harissa mixture over the tomato slices, then bake the tarts for 20 minutes until the dough is crisp and golden."],[null,"Spoon over the yogurt, scatter over the chopped parsley and serve with the rocket on the side."]],"h":[]},"3848":{"s":[[null,"Dice cooked chicken."],[null,"Drain pineapple; chop bell pepper and shred carrots."],[null,"Combine all ingredients in a bowl."],[null,"Refrigerate until chilled."],[null,"Serve chicken salad open-face on flatbread or wrapped in a 6-inch flour tortilla."]],"h":[[null,"Adjust portion for a lower or higher protein diet."],[null,"Serve on top of mixed salad greens, instead of bread, if desired."],[null,"This is a great way to use leftover chicken."]]},"2540":{"s":[[null,"Slice mushrooms, chop bell peppers and mince ginger root."],[null,"Spray a nonstick frying pan with cooking spray. Sauté mushrooms, bean sprouts, and bell pepper."],[null,"Add pineapple, soy sauce, ginger root and salt. Stir and heat thoroughly."],[null,"Mix into hot rice and serve."]],"h":[[null,"For a one-dish meal add shrimp or chicken."],[null,"1 cup uncooked rice yields 2 cups cooked rice."]]},"6454316":{"s":[[null,"Cut off the bottoms of the brussels sprouts’ cores, then cut the sprouts into very thin slices with a knife, or slice them in a food processor."],[null,"In a large skillet over medium heat, heat the oil until it’s hot. Sauté the brussels sprouts for 5 to 7 minutes, or until they begin to brown, stirring occasionally. For crispier brussels sprouts, sauté a couple minutes longer."],[null,"Stir in the brown sugar, salt, pepper, and pineapple. Cook for 3 to 5 minutes, or until heated through. Sprinkle with the macadamia nuts and serve."]],"h":[]},"3078":{"s":[[null,"Brew coffee in coffee maker. Pour into small cups."],[null,"Add 2 teaspoons of the Torani® Sugar Free Classic Hazelnut Syrup and 1 tablespoon of milk (or creamer) to each mug and garnish each with a cinnamon stick."]],"h":[[null,"Try different flavors of the Torani® Sugar Free syrups."],[null,"If you prefer your coffee darker, omit the milk."],[null,"Many nondairy creamers contain phosphate additives. Be aware if you substitute nondairy hazelnut creamer for the syrup."]]},"9238842":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 325°F/162°C and line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Add all the ingredients to a mixing bowl and use a silicone spatula to mix until combined. You will have a slightly crumbly mixture that holds together when squeezed between your fingers. If the dough feels too wet/sticky, add more flour."],[null,"Place a sheet of parchment paper on a cutting board, and the ball of dough on top. Then add another sheet of parchment paper on top of the dough. Use a rolling pin to evenly stretch the dough until 1/8 inch thick."],[null,"Use a pizza cutter to cut the dough into a grid shape, making rectangular, or square cookies. (Or use cookie cutters of your choice.) Then use a fork to poke a few holes into each cookie, if you'd like."],[null,"Transfer the cookies to your lined baking sheet and arrange them in a single layer with a little space in between each one. Bake for 10-12 minutes, until the edges are lightly golden, but do not overbake. These healthier shortbread cookies will feel soft fresh out of the oven and will harden once they cool to room temperature."]],"h":[[null,"If the dough feels too sticky/wet , add a little more flour. If you weigh the flour using a kitchen scale, you shouldn’t need to add more. If the dough feels too crumbly (it should be slightly crumbly) and not holding together, add another 1-2 teaspoons of maple syrup. (Again, if you weigh the flour, this should not happen.) Stretch the dough as evenly as possible . If some areas are thinner or thicker, the cookies won’t cook evenly. Do not overbake the cookies or they will have an unpleasant taste . Remove from the oven as soon as the edges appear lightly golden, approx. 10 minutes, depending on how thin or thick you rolled your dough. The cookies are baked at a lower temperature to prevent burning the edges . Don’t be tempted to increase the heat! The cookies will be SOFT when freshly baked , so let them rest at room temperature for AT LEAST 15-20 minutes before handling them . Then, you may transfer them to a cooling rack to continue cooling, as they will harden once cooled."]]},"9261320":{"s":[[null,"Prepare your pie crust of choice and blind bake according to the directions for the crust of choice. If you're using my oil free pie crust, bake for 15-20 minutes, until the edges are golden. Set aside to let cool before filling."],[null,"Shake your canned coconut milk very well before opening. Then measure the amount needed and place in a medium pot, along with the sugar, lemon juice, corn starch and turmeric. Whisk well and bring to a boil over high heat. Then reduce heat and simmer 2-3 minutes until thickened, whisking often."],[null,"Evenly pour the mixture onto your cooled pie crust and refrigerate overnight, or 6 or more hours until set."],[null,"Once set, garnish with lemon slices, berries and slivered almonds, if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Make sure to shake your cans of coconut milk very well before opening. Since you’re not using the entire cans, you want to make sure the contents are mixed well before measuring the amount you’ll need. Make sure to plan ahead , as this dessert tastes best when refrigerated overnight. Do not cut your pie until it’s cool . The filling needs time to chill and set before slicing. Nutritional information is for one slice (or ⅛th) of the lemon pie, including my oil free pie crust . If you’re using another crust, nutritional info will vary."]]},"9659242":{"s":[[null,"Prepare your pie crust of choice and set aside. I use my oil free pie crust (see post for detailed directions and step by step photos on making the crust) with the almond flour option, which I highly recommend. If using this crust, there's no need to prebake (blind bake) the crust."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 325 degrees F."],[null,"Add all the filling ingredients, except the pecans, to a mixing bowl and whisk well until combined. Then add the pecan halves and give it a quick stir to coat the pecans."],[null,"Pour the mixture into your prepared crust and bake for 15 minutes. Then place a pie shield over your pie or loosely cover it with aluminum foil and bake for an additional 25 minutes. (Total bake time 40 minutes.) This will prevent your crust from baking too quickly and getting too dark."],[null,"Remove from the oven and cool on a cooling rack for a minimum of two hours before slicing."]],"h":[[null,"Let your pecan pie cool at room temperature for a minimum of two hours after baking. This cool down time is essential for your pie to set, and make slicing easier. Make sure the pie is completely cooled to room temperature before refrigerating or freezing. You may make your pie in advance, but it tastes best on days 1-2. Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-5 days, or freeze for up to 2 months."]]},"9738619":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350°F/176°C and line a muffin pan with cupcake liners."],[null,"If using fresh beets, peel and chop them into cubes. Then bring them to a boil over medium/high heat and cook until very soft and a fork easily pierces them, approx. 20-25 minutes. (You may also use canned beets for faster prep.) Once cooked, mash the beets to get 1 cup of puree. Make sure not to use more than 1 cup of beet puree."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the soy milk and apple cider vinegar to a small bowl and set it aside for 5 minutes to let it thicken and curdle. This is your vegan buttermilk."],[null,"Add the beet puree, your vegan buttermilk, vanilla, and maple syrup to a large mixing bowl. Stir until combined. If the beets weren't cooked enough and your batter looks lumpy, place all the liquids into your blender and process until smooth. Then return it to the bowl."],[null,"Now add all the dry ingredients to the same bowl and mix until combined, without overmixing."],[null,"Then divide the batter between your 12 cupcake tins and bake until a toothpick inserted in the middle comes out clean, approx. 18-20 minutes."],[null,"Let the muffins rest on a cooling rack until completely cooled before frosting them!"],["For the frosting","Add all the ingredients to your blender and process until completely smooth, starting with 5 tablespoons of maple syrup. Taste and add another tablespoon of syrup if you prefer it sweeter. Keep in mind not to go overboard, or the frosting will get too thin to pipe."],["For the frosting","If the frosting gets warm as you're blending (this can happen in strong blenders), transfer it to a bowl and place it in the freezer for 30 minutes before piping your cupcakes."]],"h":[[null,"Weigh your flour for the most accurate results . I highly recommend that you do not rely on cup measurements when baking. If you don't have a kitchen scale, you may spoon the flour into your measuring cup and use a knife to scrape off the excess, with similar results. Do not scoop from the bag! If using canned beets , make sure they are not pickled! Use beets that are canned only in water, no vinegar or oil as that will alter the flavour. Use fresh and active baking powder. Baking powder that is open in your pantry for 6+ months can start to lose its effectiveness. If you do not have a powerful blender , soak your cashews in hot water for 30 minutes before blending your frosting. This will help them swell and soften, making them easier to blend into a smooth frosting. Make sure to press your tofu very well to remove excess liquid to prevent your frosting from getting too thin. If the frosting gets warm as you’re blending (this can happen in strong blenders), transfer it to a bowl and place it in the freezer for 30 minutes before piping the frosting onto your cupcakes. Let your cupcakes cool in the muffin pan for at least 10 minutes before handling them. Then transfer them to a cooling rack to completely cool BEFORE frosting them. These taste best on days 1-2, but you may store leftovers in the fridge for up to 4 days. Keep them in a sealed container to preserve moisture. Or freeze in a freezer-safe airtight container for up to 3 months."]]},"9924261":{"s":[[null,"Wash and dice your eggplant into half inch pieces. (See step by step photos above if needed.)"],[null,"Now place your cut up eggplant in a large colander and place the colander inside a bowl. Generously sprinkle with salt and let it sit for 30 minutes. Then transfer to a clean, dry dish towel and using another dish towel, or paper towels, press and pat them dry."],[null,"Now, wipe out the bowl that was sitting under your colander and place the dry eggplant inside. Add the broth and all the seasoning to the bowl and mix well to evenly coat the pieces."],[null,"Place in your air fryer basket, set to 380 degrees and cook for 15-20 minutes, tossing once at the halfway point. Cook until nicely golden, and fork tender, then serve warm with a sprinkle of fresh parsley or chives and sriracha mayo for dipping."]],"h":[[null,"Try and cut your eggplant into as similar sized pieces as possible , for even cooking. If you leave some pieces too big, they will be underdone, and too small, they’ll burn. Don’t skip the salting! This extra step does require you to start a little ahead of time, but it really does improve the flavour! Feel free to play with the seasoning, to your taste. Some great additions include cumin or chili flakes, or sub the sweet paprika for smoked. Leftovers keep in a sealed container in the fridge for up to 4 days."]]},"9992614":{"s":[[null,"Halve your clean and dry mushrooms (or quarter if they're large) and place them in a mixing bowl. Add all remaining ingredients to the bowl and mix well."],[null,"Place them in your air fryer basket and set to 390 degrees F, cooking for 8-10 minutes. Shake your basket or mix the mushrooms every few minutes. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Shake your basket or stir your mushrooms every few minutes during cooking to prevent sticking and evenly brown them. Don’t cut your mushrooms too small . Since they will reduce a fair bit during cooking, just cut them in half. If your mushrooms are very large, then you may cut them into quarters. Try not to overcrowd your mushrooms in your basket. Since they release a fair bit of water while cooking, you don’t want them to steam. So place in a single layer."]]},"9808977":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your fryer to 400 degrees F for 5 minutes."],[null,"Then place a sheet of aluminum foil with the sides folded up slightly, on the bottom of your basket. Dump the kernels on top, no need to spread and close the lid. (See process photos above for a visual.)"],[null,"Air fry for about 7-8 minutes, or until the popping slows down. It should start popping around 4-5 minutes in. Note that different models will operate at different speeds, so carefully check on the popcorn by lifting the lid just enough to peak through."],[null,"Transfer the popcorn to a bowl and top as desired, or enjoy plain."]],"h":[[null,"Don’t forget the aluminum foil . Although it may shift or move around from the fan, it will prevent many of the kernels from falling through the small holes at the bottom of your basket before they get a chance to pop. Like any method of making popcorn, you will be left with some un-popped kernels when the popping stops, just discard them. Your popcorn will keep in a zip top bag at room temperature for 3-4 days. Push out as much air as possible when sealing it, so your popcorn stays fresh."]]},"9448585":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F and grab a muffin pan, enough to fit 12 muffins."],[null,"Combine the soy milk and apple cider vinegar in a small bowl and set aside for 5 minutes to let it thicken and curdle."],[null,"Meanwhile, mash your banana in a large mixing bowl. Add the shredded carrots, maple syrup, lemon zest and vanilla. Then pour in your curdled soy milk. Mix well."],[null,"Now add all the dry ingredients to the same bowl and mix until combined, without over mixing."],[null,"Divide the mixture between your 12 muffin cups and bake for 15-16 minutes, or until a toothpick inserted in the middle comes out clean."],[null,"Remove from the oven and cool for 10 minutes before removing your muffins from the pan. Enjoy warm or at room temperature."]],"h":[[null,"Use overripe bananas. The riper your bananas, the greater flavour, sweetness, and moisture they will add to your banana carrot muffins. Bananas with brown skin work best."],[null,"Measure your mashed banana to ensure you’re using one cup. Bananas vary greatly in size. Two large bananas did it for me."],[null,"Grate your own carrots . Freshly grated carrots will add more moisture than the already shredded kind you can find at your grocery store. You want moist carrots to help in adding moisture to your muffins."],[null,"If you don’t have chickpea flour , you can make some in a high-speed blender. Grind dry/raw chickpeas into a flour consistency."],[null,"If you don’t have oat flour , you may grind rolled oats into a flour consistency using your blender."],[null,"To skip the chickpea flour , you may use more oat flour instead."],[null,"For soy-free, you may use almond milk or another non-dairy milk instead of soy milk. However, to make vegan buttermilk, soy milk works best."],[null,"You may use a box shredder or a food processor to grate your carrots. If you need to hide the carrots from picky eaters , use the fine grate side of your shredder."],[null,"Use a non-stick muffin pan. If you do not have a non-stick muffin pan, make sure to grease your tins or liners as these muffins have very little fat to prevent sticking."],[null,"Let your muffins slightly cool for 10 minutes before removing them from the muffin pan so they will come out easily, without breaking."],[null,"Store your muffins at room temperature for 2 days in an airtight container , or tightly wrapped in plastic wrap, to keep them moist. Refrigerate for up to 5 days or freeze for up to 3 months."]]},"9966537":{"s":[[null,"Add all the ingredients to your blender and process until smooth. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Don’t sub for fresh banana unless absolutely necessary. Frozen banana really works best. If you don’t have frozen bananas , you may peel and slice fresh ones and freeze for 30-60 minutes. Make sure to slice them first to help them freeze faster. To use fresh bananas , if you really don’t have the time to freeze them, add a handful of ice cubes to the smoothie as well to get similar results. Make sure your bananas are VERY ripe . The sweetness is all coming from your bananas here, so the riper the better. Choose bananas that have spotted brown skins before freezing. For a sweeter smoothie , you may add a teaspoon of pure maple syrup or 2-3 pitted dates. If you don’t have walnuts , you may sub for almonds, hazelnuts, or pecans. For best results, use a high speed blender , but if you don’t have one, soak your walnuts for about 10-15 minutes or so in fresh water and then drain. This will make it easier for your blender to process them, without leaving any grittiness behind. Makes approx 3.5 cups."]]},"9602754":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350℉/176℃ and line a muffin pan with parchment liners."],[null,"Add all the wet ingredients to a blender and process until completely smooth. Set aside."],[null,"Then whisk together the dry ingredients in a large bowl. Pour the pureed liquid ingredients into the same bowl as the flour and stir until combined."],[null,"Fold in the chocolate chips if using, and then divide the batter between your 12 muffin tins, filling almost to the top."],[null,"Bake the muffins for 28-30 minutes, or until a toothpick inserted in the center of a muffin comes out clean and dry."],[null,"Remove the pan from the oven and let the muffins rest at room temperature for at least 20-30 minutes before transferring them to a wire rack to completely set."]],"h":[[null,"Weigh your flour for the most accurate results . If you don't have a kitchen scale, spoon the flour into your measuring cup and use a knife to scrape off the excess, with similar results. Do not scoop from the bag!"],[null,"If using canned beets , make sure they are not pickled! Use beets canned only in water, no vinegar or oil as that will alter the flavour."],[null,"Use fresh and active baking powder. Baking powder that is open in your pantry for 6+ months can lose its effectiveness."],[null,"Gently tap the muffin tray on a hard surface to close up any gaps in the batter before baking."],[null,"Let your muffins cool in the pan for at least 20-30 minutes before handling them. They are delicate and need time to completely set before transferring them to a wire rack."],[null,"Leftovers keep at room temperature for up to 2 days, in the fridge for up to 5 days, or frozen for up to 3 months."]]},"9523761":{"s":[[null,"Add the blueberries, lemon juice, zest, and maple syrup, (if using) to a medium sauce pot. Simmer over medium heat for about 5 minutes. You'll notice the blueberries start to burst."],[null,"Then gently mash with a potato masher or large fork until roughly half the blueberries are mashed, leaving several chunks throughout."],[null,"Increase the heat and boil for 5 minutes to reduce some of the liquid. Then turn off the heat and stir in your chia seeds."],[null,"Transfer the blueberry chia jam to clean and dry jars and refrigerate or freeze."]],"h":[[null,"You need 1 large lemon for both the zest and juice. Make sure to zest your lemon before juicing it . Don’t overly mash the jam into a puree . Some blueberry pieces throughout will add nice texture. If the jam seems thin after boiling, not to worry . The chia seeds will absorb most of the excess liquid as it cools. For a smoother texture (if you don’t like the chia texture), grind the chia seeds before adding them to the jam. Try it with other berries like raspberries and/or blackberries. Or try our strawberry version here . Store the jam in a clean glass jar/s in the refrigerator for up to 2 weeks or freeze for up to 6 months. I like to store it in 2 separate jars, one for the fridge and one for the freezer."]]},"9910859":{"s":[[null,"Add the onion and carrots to a large pot with a tablespoon or two of water. Sauté until slightly softened, about 2 minutes."],[null,"Add the potatoes, beans, broth, nutritional yeast, thyme and garlic powder to the pot and bring to a boil over high heat. Reduce heat and simmer until the potatoes are easily pierced with a fork, about 8 minutes. Then add the broccoli and simmer 5 more minutes."],[null,"Turn off the heat and using a slotted spoon, remove and set aside about 4 cups of the veggies. Then puree the remaining soup in the pot, using an immersion blender. Or you may transfer to a stand blender in batches, using caution when pureeing hot liquids. Return the reserved 4 cups of veggies to the pot, stir in the plant milk and taste for salt. I added 1/2 a teaspoon at this point, but salt to your taste. Then serve and enjoy."],["Instant Pot Directions","Set your Instant Pot to the sauté function, then add the onion and carrots with a tablespoon or two of water. Sauté until slightly softened, about 2 minutes."],["Instant Pot Directions","Add all remaining ingredients EXCEPT the milk and close the lid, making sure the valve is in the sealing position. Cook at high pressure for 7 minutes and then quick release the steam valve. Remove the lid once safe to do so."],["Instant Pot Directions","Use a slotted spoon to remove 4 cups of the veggies and set aside. Then puree the remaining soup using an immersion blender. Or you may transfer to a stand blender in batches, using caution when pureeing hot liquids."],["Instant Pot Directions","Return the reserved veggies to the pot, stir in the milk and taste for salt. I added 1/2 a teaspoon at this point, but salt to your taste. Then serve and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"I like this soup fairly chunky, but if you're serving picky eaters, you may puree the entire soup instead of reserving some chunkier veggies. You may use the reserved veggies to stir back into the pot, or use them to garnish each bowl of soup. If you're avoiding nuts, use soy or coconut milk instead of cashew milk. You may also use the canned coconut milk if you want an even richer and creamier finish, however, this will add more fat. I've kept the seasoning simple here to please some picky eaters, but if you wish to amp up the flavour, you may add some cumin, paprika, or even some cayenne to add a little heat."]]},"9080453":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350℉/176℃ and line a muffin pan with parchment liners."],[null,"Mash your bananas to a very fine mash, place them in a large bowl, and add the almond butter and maple syrup to the same bowl. Mix well."],[null,"Then add all the dry ingredients and stir until combined."],[null,"Divide the mixture between your 12 muffin cups and bake for 20 minutes, or until a toothpick inserted in the middle of a muffin comes out clean. Remove the buckwheat muffins from your oven and let them rest for 5-10 minutes before transferring them to a wire rack."]],"h":[[null,"Use overly ripe bananas with lots of brown spots on the peel for extra sweetness. You may also use frozen bananas, just let them come to room temperature before mashing them."],[null,"Weigh your flour using a kitchen scale for the most accurate results ! Scooping flour from a bag will compact the flour, and could mean too much flour is being used which could result in a denser muffin."],[null,"Use FRESH + ACTIVE baking powder . Baking powder that has been open in the pantry for 6+ months may start to lose its effectiveness."],[null,"Let your muffins rest for 5-10 minutes after baking . This short cool-down time will allow your muffins to completely set, and prevent them from breaking when removing them from the pan."],[null,"Keep your buckwheat muffins at room temperature for 2-3 days, refrigerated for up to 4 days, or freeze them airtight for up to 3 months."]]},"9032359":{"s":[[null,"Add the walnuts and sundried tomatoes to the bowl of your food processor and pulse until broken down and crumbly, without pureeing. Transfer to a small bowl and set aside."],[null,"Now add the onion, garlic, and cauliflower florets to your food processor and gently pulse until chopped, but do not overprocess. Keep the pieces chunky for a hearty sauce and the best texture, working in batches as needed. Transfer each batch to a sauce pot or deep nonstick skillet."],[null,"Sauté the veggies over medium-high heat, stirring occasionally, until reduced, approx 5-7 minutes. You should not need water or oil, as the veggies will release moisture. But if anything is sticking, add 1-2 tablespoons of water."],[null,"Then add all the remaining sauce ingredients: walnut and sundried tomato mixture, tomato sauce, broth, lentils, and all the seasoning. Simmer for 20 minutes, until the lentils are cooked and the sauce is thick. Taste for seasoning and add more if needed. Discard the bay leaves."],[null,"Meanwhile, bring a large pot of generously salted water to a boil, and cook your pasta according to package directions for 'al dente' pasta. Then serve the pasta with a generous scoop of the cauliflower bolognese sauce on top."]],"h":[[null,"Do not overprocess the veggies . You want a chunky, hearty cauliflower bolognese sauce, so make sure to keep some texture."],[null,"Simmer the sauce for at least 20 minutes. Simmering allows the flavours to marry beautifully. If you have extra time, simmer even longer. The more it simmers, the more the flavours will amplify."],[null,"Add more broth if your sauce gets too thick . It should be thick and rich, but if you find it’s getting too thick, add an extra half cup of vegetable broth ."],[null,"Salt your pasta water! Be sure to add enough salt to your pot of water for the best results. Here's a handy guide to help if needed."],[null,"Do not overcook your pasta. Follow the directions for 'al dente' pasta. Al dente translates as ‘firm when bitten’. If your package does not include directions for 'al dente' undercook your pasta by 1-3 minutes. 'Al dente' pasta is still firm once cooked, and not mushy. This gives you optimal texture."],[null,"For nut-free , use sunflower seeds or pumpkin seeds to replace the walnuts with similar results."],[null,"For lower calories , enjoy a smaller portion of pasta with a larger portion of the cauliflower bolognese sauce. OR use zucchini noodles, carrot noodles, or spaghetti squash."],[null,"For a thinner sauce , add more broth and/or tomato sauce."],[null,"Leftover cauliflower bolognese sauce will keep refrigerated for up to 5 days in a sealed container, or freeze it airtight for up to 3 months."]]},"9518496":{"s":[[null,"Add the cauliflower florets and the garlic cloves to a medium saucepot. Cover it with water and add 1 tablespoon of salt. Bring to a boil and cook for 8-10 minutes, or until the florets are fork-tender."],[null,"Use a slotted spoon to transfer the cooked cauliflower and garlic to your food processor, and reserve the cooking water. Start processing the cauliflower and add 2-4 tablespoons of the cooking water, as needed, until your mash is pureed and creamy."],[null,"Once smooth to your liking, you may discard the additional cooking water. Taste the mash and add salt and pepper, to your taste."]],"h":[]},"9289404":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350℉/176℃ and line two baking sheets with parchment paper."],[null,"Add everything EXCEPT the optional ingredients to your food processor and process until smooth."],[null,"Use a small cookie scoop to scoop the batter onto your baking sheets. You'll get about 26 cookies. Then with slightly wet hands or the back of a spoon press the cookies down and shape them into circles. The batter won't spread much, so shape them before baking."],[null,"OPTIONAL: If using chocolate chips for eyes, add those to your cookies now. If using candy eyes, add them AFTER baking."],[null,"Bake for 16-18 minutes, then remove the cookies from the oven and gently press the candy eyes (if using) into your cookies while they are still warm. To make mouths, use a toothpick or the end of a spoon or fork to glide different mouth shapes into each of your spooky cookies. Then let them cool."]],"h":[[null,"Use VERY ripe bananas that are spotted brown, since there’s not much added sweetness."],[null,"If using the candy eyes , press them into your cookies, immediately after removing them from the oven, while they are still warm."],[null,"Create fun mouth shapes in your green cookies while they are still warm . Use a toothpick or the tip/end of a spoon or fork."]]},"6679815":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400 degrees. Spray a 1.5 quart baking dish with cooking spray."],[null,"Heat cheese wedges in microwave for 30 seconds, stir. Set aside."],[null,"In a large sauté pan heat oil over medium heat. Add onions and sauté 2-3 minutes."],[null,"Add margarine to pan and melt. Add mushrooms, salt and pepper and cook for 4-5 minutes. Pour chicken broth into pan and simmer for 1 minute."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix together corn starch and water; add to chicken broth and stir for 1 minute."],[null,"Add melted cheese wedges to pan and mix well. Add milk to pan; stir to incorporate. Cook additional 2-3 minutes until thick."],[null,"Remove from heat and stir in green beans. Pour green bean mixture into baking dish."],[null,"In a small bowl prepare corn flake topping by, mixing together corn flakes and margarine. Spread corn flake mixture on top of green beans. Bake 15-20 minutes."]],"h":[]},"7798440":{"s":[[null,"Place all the hummus ingredients into a food processor or blender and blend until almost smooth and well combined."],[null,"Spoon into a serving bowl and serve with the warmed pitta."]],"h":[[null,"This recipe is a great source of fibre, which is essential for good digestive health."],[null,"If you don't have any tinned chickpeas you could use dried ones, and follow the pack instructions to prepare and cook them."],[null,"To add extra flavour, add 1 tsp of tahini, or 1 tsp smoked paprika or cumin. To give it more zing, add the grated zest of lemon."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Freeze in portions then defrost in the fridge, or microwave, taking care to stir regularly."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"9610471":{"s":[[null,"Add all the ingredients to your blender and process until smooth and creamy."],[null,"Pour into a glass and garnish if you'd like. Enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Use a very ripe banana that’s been frozen for the best results. If you’ve been freezing your brown bananas to make banana bread one day, that’s exactly the kind of banana you want for this vegan iced coffee. If you have a sweet tooth , add a couple of extra dates. You can start with 2-3, then taste and add more, if needed, and re-blend Don’t have a powerful blender ? Pre-soak your dates in cool water for about 15-20 minutes and then drain and blend. This will help soften them and prevent crumbly bits in your vegan iced mocha. If you don’t have a frozen banana available, you may use fresh, but add an additional ⅓ cup of ice cubes."]]},"9563775":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F and line a baking sheet with parchment paper. Add the raw hazelnuts in a single layer and bake for 15 minutes."],[null,"Remove from the oven and place a clean, dry dish towel over top the hazelnuts and rub your hands over the nuts to remove the skins. The rubbing back and forth will force most of the skins loose. Do this for about 30 seconds and remove the towel and continue with your bare hands when cool enough to do so. Don't worry if there are few stubborn skins that wont come off, as long as you get most of them."],[null,"Place your skinned hazelnuts in a high-speed blender, like a Vitamix, or in a food processor and process until you get a smooth nut butter. Stop and scrape down the sides as needed."],[null,"Now remove the nut butter and set aside in a bowl. To the same food processor, add the dates and begin processing. Then pour in 1/4 cup of the plant milk while the machine is running and process until smooth. Scrape down the sides as needed."],[null,"Return hazelnut butter back to the processor, along with the remaining plant milk, cocoa powder, vanilla, and salt. Pulse several times until blended. You may add an additional 2-3 tablespoons of milk if a thinner consistency is desired."],[null,"Store your healthy Nutella in a clean glass jar at room temperature for up to 1 week."]],"h":[[null,"After roasting the hazelnuts, work quickly to remove the skins as they come off easiest when warm. Most of the skins will come off easily, but don’t worry if there are a few stubborn ones."],[null,"The hazelnuts will take some time to go from whole nuts to nut butter . You will see the nuts go through stages of chunkier pieces, to flour, to lumps, and eventually smooth nut butter. Have patience. 🙂"],[null,"If you’re using a food processor , be sure to give it small breaks to prevent overheating. Processing time takes me about 1 minute, but individual appliances will vary."],[null,"Adding the milk as the food processor runs will produce smoother results . But, if using a blender, add both at the same time and process. If your blender or processor is not a powerful one, pre-soak your dates for 15-30 minutes and then drain for a smoother date paste."],[null,"While both a food processor and blender work well , a high-speed blender, like a Vitamix will yield smoother results. But in exchange, it’s easier to transfer the Nutella from a food processor bowl."],[null,"I like the sweetness level of this Nutella as is. However, if you want a sweeter Nutella , you may add a liquid sweetener, to taste, such as maple syrup, date syrup, or agave at the end and pulse a few times to mix through."],[null,"Recipe yields approx. 2 cups of healthy Nutella. Store in a clean glass jar at room temperature for up to 1 week. Refrigerate for up to 3 weeks. The serving size is two tablespoons."]]},"9406949":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350 degrees F and line a large baking tray with parchment paper."],[null,"Add all the ingredients to your food processor and process until smooth."],[null,"Using a metal teaspoon, scoop the mixture onto your prepared baking sheet and form your cookies."],[null,"Bake for 18-22 minutes, or until lightly golden around the edges. Allow cookies to cool completely to help them firm up before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Use peanut butter that is made with only peanuts and no added fat or sugar . Some \"natural\" brands are not made using just peanuts, so always read the ingredients. Or of course, you may make your own. I use a 13.5 oz can. If your can is larger and you want to use it all, not to waste, you can. However, you will need a little extra liquid to compensate. Either add another 1-2 tablespoons of coconut oil or unsweetened apple sauce to the mix. For oil free , sub the coconut oil with unsweetened apple sauce. The original recipe calls for coconut oil, but I have since tested it (many times) with apple sauce and actually now prefer them this way. For nut free , sub the peanut butter for sun butter or tahini. If you don't have pure maple syrup but still want to add some extra sweetness, use agave syrup, or honey works too, if not vegan. If you'd like, you may add ¼-1/3 cup of chocolate chips, raisins, chopped nuts, or shredded coconut. Choose one, and don't go overboard or the batter won't hold as well. If you want uniform cookies , use a cookie scoop. I use a small cookie scoop, which is 2 teaspoons worth. The chickpea cookies keep covered at room temperature for 2-3 days, refrigerated for 5-6 days, or frozen for up to 2 months in an airtight container."]]},"6545769":{"s":[[null,"Preheat an oven to 300 degrees F."],[null,"Coat a baking sheet with nonstick cooking spray and set aside."],[null,"In a bowl, combine the brown sugar substitute, cayenne pepper, pumpkin seeds, sunflower seeds, almonds and sesame seeds. Toss to coat."],[null,"Spread mixture onto the baking sheet and then spray again with a light coating of cooking spray."],[null,"Bake for 15 minutes, stirring every 5 minutes to ensure even browning."],[null,"Remove from oven and set aside to cool. When cool, toss the nut mixture in a bowl with the freeze-dried blueberries."]],"h":[]},"6372211":{"s":[[null,"In a medium bowl mix together refried beans, chili powder, cumin and garlic powder."],[null,"Spread the refried beans evenly on a medium serving platter. Spread mashed avocados evenly over beans."],[null,"Spread the salsa evenly over top of avocados. Top with tomatoes, shredded lettuce and shredded cheese on top."],[null,"Serve the dip with your choice of baked tortilla chips, black bean chips or jicama slices. If you follow a gluten-free diet, make sure tortilla chips are unseasoned and gluten-free."]],"h":[]},"9889051":{"s":[[null,"Heat your non stick griddle over medium heat. Then add the soy milk and apple cider vinegar to a small bowl and set aside to let it curdle."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the oats, hemp hearts and chia seeds to a blender and process until it resembles a flour consistency. (Don't worry if there are a few chunkier pieces.) Transfer to a large mixing bowl and add the chickpea flour and baking powder and whisk to combine."],[null,"By now your milk should be curdled, so pour that into the bowl of flour and mix until combined without over mixing. Gently fold in the blueberries."],[null,"Ladle your batter on your preheated griddle, making pancakes roughly 4 inches in diameter. You may gently press the pancakes down to help it spread a little as the batter will not be very runny. However, do not spread too much as these taste best a little thick and fluffy."],[null,"Cook for 4-5 minutes until golden and flip and cook for another 3-4 more minutes, until cooked through."],[null,"Serve with more fresh blueberries, raspberries, coconut shreds, chocolate chips, nuts, or maple syrup."]],"h":[[null,"Make sure your baking powder is active . If it’s been sitting in your pantry, opened, for more than 6 months, it may start to lose its effectiveness."],[null,"The oats and seeds don’t need to be perfectly blended . If there are some flaky bits that won’t grind down, your pancakes will still come out perfectly."],[null,"No need to overmix your pancake batter. If there are a few lumps, that’s perfectly fine. Just mix until combined and no floury bits remain."],[null,"Use medium heat for even cooking. High heat will cook the outside too quickly, resulting in undercooked middles. But make sure it’s preheated so your pancakes don’t stick!"],[null,"Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-4 days or freeze in zip-top bags or a freezer-safe container for up to 3 months. Reheat in the toaster for quick and easy breakfasts."]]},"9028983":{"s":[["For the cupcakes","Add the soy milk and the lemon juice to a large mixing bowl and set aside for 5 minutes to thicken and curdle. (This is your vegan buttermilk.)"],["For the cupcakes","Preheat the oven to 350°F/176°C and grab a nonstick muffin tin. (Or grease your tin or liners if needed.)"],["For the cupcakes","Once curdled, add the remaining wet ingredients to your bowl and mix well. Then add the dry ingredients to the same bowl and stir until combined WITHOUT over-mixing. (If using an optional fill-in, fold those in as well.)"],["For the cupcakes","Divide the cupcake batter among your 12 muffin cups and bake until a toothpick inserted in the center of a cupcake comes out clean, approx 18 minutes. Remove from the oven and let rest for 10 minutes before transferring to a cooling rack."],["For the frosting","Add all the frosting ingredients to your blender and process until smooth. Start with 5 tablespoons of the maple syrup, then taste, and add more until desired sweetness is reached. Don't go overboard or the frosting will be too soft."],["For the frosting","Once the cupcakes are completely cooled, frost your cupcakes with a piping bag, and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Weigh your flour for the most accurate results . I highly recommend that you do not rely on cup measurements when baking. If you don't have a kitchen scale, you may spoon the flour into your measuring cup and use a knife to scrape off the excess, with similar results. Do not scoop from the bag!"],[null,"Use a box grater or food processor to shred your carrots , but either way, freshly grated is best as store-bought shredded carrots may be dry."],[null,"Don’t overmix the cupcake batter . Stir until there are no floury bits, but don’t worry about working through every lump. Over-mixing can result in a gummy or dense texture."],[null,"Use fresh and active baking powder. Baking powder that is open in your pantry for 6+ months can start to lose its effectiveness."],[null,"Since these cupcakes have no added fat, make sure to use a non-stick muffin tin OR grease your pan or cupcake liners to prevent sticking."],[null,"If you do not have a powerful blender , soak your cashews in hot water for 30 minutes before blending your frosting. This will help them swell and soften, making them easier to blend into a smooth frosting."],[null,"Drain and pat your tofu dry to remove some excess liquid and prevent your frosting from getting too thin."],[null,"If the frosting gets warm as you're blending (this can happen in strong blenders), transfer it to a bowl and place it in the freezer for 30 minutes before piping the frosting onto your cupcakes."],[null,"Let your cupcakes cool in the muffin pan for at least 10 minutes before handling them. Then transfer them to a cooling rack to completely cool BEFORE frosting them."]]},"9336436":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 400 degrees F convection bake and line a baking tray with parchment paper. Then, arrange your cauliflower florets, quartered onion, jalapeno and garlic in a single layer."],[null,"Bake for 15-20 minutes, until edges are golden brown and cauliflower is fork tender."],[null,"Then transfer your roasted veggies (remove the peel from the garlic first) along with all remaining ingredients to a blender. Process until smooth and then taste and add more salt if needed or more broth to thin as desired. Serve with veggies, crackers, chips or pitas."]],"h":[[null,"Adjust the amount of broth to a consistency of your liking . I found one cup to give the perfect consistency, but start with ¾ cup if you want a thicker dip and add more, if needed. If you have a powerful blender , like a Vitamix , run it a little longer to make sure your cauliflower cheese sauce is nice and hot before serving. Make it ahead to save time. You can easily reheat the dip before serving (or serve cold). It tastes great both ways, but I do prefer this one warm. Use your vegan cauliflower cheese in a variety of ways . Use it as a dip with veggies for a light snack, with chips or crackers for a treat, or pour it over your broccoli, asparagus or any of your favourite steamed veggies. Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-4 days in an airtight container, or freeze (but completely cool first) airtight for up to 3 months."]]},"9426064":{"s":[["Before you begin","To prepare the sweet potato: Preheat your oven to 425°F/218°C. Then scrub the potato clean and place it on a baking sheet and roast for approx. 35-45 minutes, or until easily pierced with a fork. OR, if you have an air fryer, you can air fry using this method to save time. Set aside."],["For the cupcakes","Preheat the oven to 350°F/176°C and line a muffin pan with parchment liners."],["For the cupcakes","Peel the sweet potato or scoop out the flesh and mash it on a plate. Then measure six tablespoons (not more) to be used for the batter and place it into a large bowl. Add the milk and maple syrup to the same bowl and whisk to combine."],["For the cupcakes","Next, add all of the dry ingredients to the same bowl and stir until combined."],["For the cupcakes","Divide the batter between your 12 muffin tins and bake for 20-22 minutes, or until a toothpick inserted in the middle comes out clean. Set aside to completely cool before frosting them."],["For the frosting","Add all the frosting ingredients to a high-speed blender or food processor and blend until smooth. Once the cupcakes have cooled, use a piping bag to frost them and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Weigh your flour for the most accurate results . I highly recommend that you do not rely on cup measurements when baking. If you don't have a kitchen scale, you may spoon the flour into your measuring cup and use a knife to scrape off the excess, with similar results. Do not scoop from the bag! Use fresh and active baking powder. Baking powder that is open in your pantry for 6+ months can start to lose its effectiveness. If possible, roast your sweet potato one day in advance , or several hours before you plan to bake the cupcakes. Let your cupcakes cool in the muffin pan for at least 10 minutes before handling them. Then transfer them to a cooling rack to completely cool BEFORE frosting them. These taste best on days 1-2, but you may store leftovers in the fridge for up to 4 days. Keep them in a sealed container to preserve moisture. Or freeze unfrosted cupcakes in a freezer-safe airtight container for up to 3 months. I recommend making the frosting fresh before serving."]]},"9849806":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350°F/177°C and prepare a nine-inch cake pan or spring-form pan. Use a nonstick pan, or if you don't have a nonstick pan, line it with parchment paper, or grease it if you're not avoiding oil."],[null,"Combine the soy milk, lemon juice and the zest in a small bowl and set it aside for at least 5 minutes until it starts to thicken and curdle."],[null,"Meanwhile, add all the dry ingredients to a large bowl and whisk to combine."],[null,"Then add the curdled milk, with the remaining wet ingredients to the same bowl with the dry ingredients. Mix until no floury bits remain. Then fold in ¾ cup of the blueberries."],[null,"Pour the batter into your cake tin and sprinkle the remaining blueberries on top and gently press them into your cake, just a little."],[null,"Bake for 25-30 minutes, or until a toothpick inserted in the middle comes out clean. Remove from the oven and let rest 30 minutes or longer before handling."]],"h":[[null,"Weigh your flour for the most accurate results . If you don't have a kitchen scale, you may spoon the flour into your measuring cup and use a knife to scrape off the excess. Do not scoop from the bag! Don’t skip making the vegan buttermilk . (Mixing the soy milk with lemon juice.) This enhances the dairy flavour, and makes the texture fluffier. Make sure your baking powder + soda are active . Open products that sit in your pantry for 6+ months begin to lose their effectiveness and rising power. Keep leftover cake at room temperature in a sealed container or tightly wrapped for 2 days. Refrigerate for up to 5 days or freeze airtight for up to 3 months."]]},"9772597":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 350℉/176℃ and line a 9-inch square baking pan with parchment paper."],[null,"Add your dates and water to a high-speed blender and process until smooth to make date syrup. Set it aside."],[null,"Whisk all the dry ingredients in a large bowl. Then add the applesauce, lemon zest, lemon juice, and 1.5 cups worth (NOT more) of the date syrup you just made. Stir until combined. (Reserve the remaining date syrup for the glaze.)"],[null,"Transfer the batter to your baking dish and bake for 25-30 minutes, until a toothpick inserted in the middle comes out clean. Remove it from the oven and let it cool for at least 10 minutes. Then transfer the loaf to a cutting board or cooling rack to completely cool."],[null,"Meanwhile, add 2 tablespoons of lemon juice to the remaining date syrup and mix. (Taste it and add more lemon juice, if preferred.) Then drizzle the glaze on your lemon loaf and let it rest for a few minutes to set before slicing into 16 squares."]],"h":[[null,"Use active baking powder . Oat and rice flour are denser than white flour and need a little extra to rise nicely. If your baking powder is very old or has been open in your pantry for 6+ months, it may start to lose its effectiveness. Test it before using it if you’re unsure."],[null,"If you don’t have a high-speed blender or your dates are very dry, soak them first for 15 minutes in hot water, and then drain them. This will soften the dates, making them easier to blend."],[null,"Don’t dump all the date syrup into the loaf. Make sure to follow the instructions carefully. Use only 1.5 cups of your syrup, and reserve the rest for the glaze."],[null,"To maximize the juice you get from a lemon , you may soak whole lemons in a bowl of hot water for 30 minutes, or microwave them for 10-20 seconds. You may also roll lemons on a countertop with your hands to get the juices flowing."],[null,"For the glaze. Mix 2 tablespoons of lemon juice into the date syrup and taste the mixture. Add more lemon juice until the desired lemony flavour is reached."],[null,"The spices are subtle in flavour, since the lemon is the star of this dessert. For stronger spice , double the cinnamon, ginger, and nutmeg called for in the recipe."],[null,"Cool your loaf to room temperature before glazing . Once glazed, let it rest for a few minutes so it slightly hardens before slicing."]]},"9231462":{"s":[[null,"Add the soy milk, lemon juice, and lemon zest to a small bowl and set aside for 5 minutes to let it thicken and curdle."],[null,"In a large mixing bowl add all the dry ingredients and whisk to combine. Then add the curdled/thickened milk and the vanilla and mix until combined. Set the pancake batter aside for 5 minutes while you preheat your nonstick griddle."],[null,"Ladle the batter on your griddle to make your pancakes approx. 4 inches in diameter, gently spreading them as you pour."],[null,"Cook the pancakes for 4-5 minutes, then flip them and cook another 3-4 minutes longer until the edges are golden. Serve with toppings of your choice and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Use fresh, active baking powder . Baking powder that has been opened and sitting in the pantry for several months can start to lose its effectiveness. No need to overmix your pancake batter . If there are a few lumps, that’s perfectly fine. Just mix until combined and no floury bits remain. Preheat your pan or griddle. It should be hot before pouring your pancake batter to prevent sticking and for even cooking. Use medium heat to cook your pancakes . Although your pan should be hot, that doesn’t mean you should use high heat. This may result in uneven cooking, with crisp outsides and mushy middles. Flip your pancakes ONCE . When the edges are golden brown and they’ve cooked for at least 3-4 minutes flip them. Flipping too often can cause them to deflate and result in a denser pancake texture. The batter will thicken as it sits , so if it gets too thick in between cooking batches of pancakes, add 1-2 tablespoons of plant milk to the bowl. Leftovers keep in the fridge for 2-3 days or freeze for up to 3 months."]]},"9632103":{"s":[[null,"Line a baking sheet with parchment paper and preheat your oven to 350 degrees F."],[null,"Add the oats to a food processor and gently process until the oats are finely chopped, with some floury bits, but do not over process into flour."],[null,"Transfer the oats to a mixing bowl and add all remaining ingredients, except for your optional fill in. Mix well to evenly distribute. Now add your fill in of choice, if using and mix well."],[null,"Divide your cookie batter into 10 cookies, roll out a ball in your hands (use wet hands to prevent sticking) and then place down on your baking sheet. Now, using the back of a spoon, gently press each cookie down and shape the sides into a rounded cookie, if needed."],[null,"Bake for 10-12 minutes and remove from the oven. (They will look under done.) Let them cool for at least 5 minutes and then transfer to a cooling rack to cool for an additional 5-10 minutes to get your cookies to completely set and firm up. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Don’t over process the oats. You don’t want to make flour or this will alter the texture of your oatmeal cookies. Use wet hands to shape your cookie dough into balls. This will help prevent them from sticking to your hands, and make them easy to roll. When you press your cookies down , do so gently to prevent breaking them. Use your other hand to help shape the edges into a round cookie if they are not holding well at the edges. Don’t use more than ¼ cup of fill ins , whether it’s chocolate chips, raisins or another fill in. Too much of any fill in will make them tougher to hold together. Do not over bake your cookies. For chewy oatmeal cookies, they should be slightly under baked. They may appear under done, but make sure not to over bake to prevent them from getting dry. Edges will be firmer and the center will be soft. Let them rest at room temperature for at least 5-10 minutes after baking. This brief cool down period will firm up your cookies and let them completely set. Cookies keep 2-3 days refrigerated, up to 1 week in the fridge, or freeze for up to 3 months."]]},"9310264":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350°F/176°C and line a muffin pan with cupcake liners. Set aside."],[null,"Combine the wet ingredients in a large mixing bowl and whisk to combine. Then add all the dry ingredients and mix until no floury bits remain, without overmixing. (Don't worry about a few lumps.)"],[null,"Divide your cupcake batter between the 12 muffin tins and bake for 22-24 minutes, or until a toothpick inserted in the middle comes out clean. Remove from the oven and let cool completely before frosting."],[null,"To make the frosting, add all the ingredients to your blender and process until completely smooth, starting with 5 tablespoons of maple syrup. Taste and add another tablespoon of syrup if you prefer it sweeter. Keep in mind not to go overboard, or the frosting will get too thin to pipe."],[null,"If the frosting gets warm as you're blending (this can happen in strong blenders), transfer it to a bowl and place it in the freezer for 30 minutes before piping your cupcakes."]],"h":[[null,"Weigh your flour for the most accurate results . I highly recommend that you do not rely on cup measurements when baking. If you don't have a kitchen scale, you may spoon the flour into your measuring cup and use a knife to scrape off the excess, with similar results. Do not scoop from the bag! I recommend using superfine almond flour and fine oat flour for the best texture. I did try these with homemade oat flour as well, and while that works well, a finer oat flour will result in a lighter, more delicate crumb. Use fresh and active baking powder. Baking powder that is open in your pantry for 6+ months can start to lose its effectiveness. If you do not have a powerful blender , soak your cashews in hot water for 30 minutes before blending your frosting. This will help them swell and soften, making them easier to blend into a smooth frosting. Make sure to press your tofu very well to remove excess liquid to prevent your frosting from getting too thin. If the frosting gets warm as you’re blending (this can happen in strong blenders), transfer it to a bowl and place it in the freezer for 30 minutes before piping the frosting onto your cupcakes. Let your cupcakes cool in the muffin pan for at least 20 minutes before handling them. Then transfer them to a cooling rack to completely cool BEFORE frosting them. These taste best on days 1-2, but you may store leftovers in the fridge for up to 4 days. Keep them in a sealed container to preserve moisture. Or freeze in a freezer-safe airtight container for up to 3 months."]]},"9633263":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 375℉/190℃, and line a large baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Peel and cube your sweet potatoes, place them in a pan or pot, and cover with water. Bring to a boil and cook until soft, approx 8-10 minutes. Drain and return to the pan. Then mash well using a potato masher."],[null,"Add all the remaining ingredients to the pan with your mashed sweet potato and mix well. The batter will be thick."],[null,"Use a cookie scoop to make your cookie balls and place them on your baking tray. Then, gently press each one down with a fork to flatten and shape them. Bake the sweet potato cookies for 15-18 minutes, until golden."],[null,"Remove from the oven, allow to cool for 5 minutes and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Use very ripe bananas with brown spotted skins . Since these cookies are naturally sweetened, you want to use very ripe and sweet bananas."],[null,"If possible, use a scale to weigh your ingredients for the best results. If you do not have a kitchen scale, spoon and level your flour into your measuring cup. Don’t scoop from the bag, or you may end up with too much."],[null,"If you don’t have oat or brown rice flour , you may use all-purpose whole wheat flour with similar results. Use 110g (approx ¾ cup) only if you’re not avoiding gluten."],[null,"You can make brown rice flour and oat flour if you don’t have any on hand. I grind the ingredients in my Vitamix ."],[null,"Leftovers will keep in a sealed container at room temperature for 1-2 days, refrigerated for 3-4 days, or freeze them airtight for up to 3 months."]]},"9762208":{"s":[[null,"Begin by preparing your quinoa and sweet potato if you do not already have that ready. If possible, cook the quinoa and roast the sweet potato one day in advance or several hours before you wish to make the muffins.To prepare the sweet potato: Preheat your oven to 425°F/218°C. Then scrub the potato clean and place it on a baking sheet and roast for approx. 35-45 minutes, or until easily pierced with a fork. OR, if you have an air fryer, you can air fry using this method to save time. Set aside.To prepare the quinoa: Add 1/4 cup of raw quinoa with 1/2 cup of water to a small sauce pot and bring to a boil. Then lower the heat and simmer until the water is absorbed, approx 8-10 minutes. Set aside."],[null,"When ready to make your muffins: Preheat your oven to 350°F/173°C and line a muffin tin with parchment liners."],[null,"Then peel and mash the sweet potato and measure no more than 1/3 cup, and place it in a large mixing bowl. Add the cooked quinoa, maple syrup, and plant milk to the same bowl. Mix well."],[null,"Next, add all the dry ingredients to the same bowl and stir until combined. Then fold in the chocolate chips, if using."],[null,"Evenly distribute the mixture among your 12 muffin cups and sprinkle a few extra chocolate chips on top if you'd like. Bake for 22-24 minutes, or until a toothpick inserted in the middle comes out clean."],[null,"Remove from the oven and let the muffins cool for AT LEAST 10 minutes before handling so they have some time to firm up and set. Then transfer them to a cooling rack to continue cooling."]],"h":[[null,"Weigh your flour for the most accurate results . If you don't have a kitchen scale, you may spoon the flour into your measuring cup and use a knife to scrape off the excess. Do not scoop from the bag! Use fresh and active baking powder. Baking powder that is open in your pantry for 6+ months can start to lose its effectiveness. If possible, roast your sweet potato and cook the quinoa one day in advance , or several hours before you plan to make the muffins. For a different variation , you may use pumpkin puree or butternut squash puree to substitute for the potato. These muffins taste best the same day they’re made but will keep, covered, at room temperature for 1-2 days. Refrigerate for 3-4 days, or freeze them airtight for up to 3 months."]]},"9373393":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350℉/176℃ and grease a muffin tray.**(see notes if avoiding oil)"],[null,"Squeeze out the excess moisture from your shredded zucchini over a bowl or your kitchen sink. Then place it in a bowl with the remaining wet ingredients and mix."],[null,"Whisk the dry ingredients in another bowl and add that to the wet bowl. Stir until no floury bits remain, without overmixing. Let the batter rest for 10 minutes, it will thicken slightly, and then give it a quick stir before dividing it between your 12 muffin cups."],[null,"Bake for 18-22 minutes, or until a toothpick inserted in the center comes out clean and dry. Let the muffins cool for at least 10 minutes in the pan, and then transfer them to a wire rack to continue cooling."]],"h":[[null,"Use active baking powder for maximum lift. Baking powder that has been open in your pantry for 6+ months may start to lose its effectiveness."],[null,"You may use whole or ground flax seed for these muffins. Whole seeds add extra crunch and texture, and ground will offer maximum health benefits."],[null,"You may grate the zucchini using a box grater or food processor, either is fine."],[null,"For soy-free , use almond or cashew milk ."],[null,"For nut-free , just omit the walnuts or use chocolate chips or dried fruit for added sweetness."],[null,"Let the batter rest for 10 minutes before spooning it into your muffin pan for fluffier muffins. Give it a quick stir after 10 minutes and then divide and bake."],[null,"These muffins are NOT very sweet, so if you have a sweet tooth , I recommend using chocolate chips in place of the chopped nuts."],[null,"**If you have a good quality and relatively new, nonstick muffin pan, you won’t need to grease it. I’ve tested both ways and my muffins did not stick to the pan. However, you MUST wait 10 minutes before attempting to transfer the muffins to your cooling rack. Muffins keep covered at room temperature for up to 3 days, refrigerated for up to 1 week, and frozen airtight for up to 3 months."]]},"4479133":{"s":[[null,"In a frying pan, heat 1 tablespoon olive oil over medium-high heat and sauté onion and peppers (5 minutes). Set aside."],[null,"In a small bowl, mash half of the black beans (1/2 cup)."],[null,"In a medium saucepan, prepare the sauce. Heat 1 tablespoon olive oil over medium heat. While stirring, add flour and Mexican chili seasoning. Add the chicken broth and continue stirring until the sauce is creamy. Reserve 1/2 cup of the sauce in another container."],[null,"Add the cooked onion, peppers, black beans (mashed and whole) and chicken to the remaining sauce in the saucepan. Add the lime juice. Stir and continue cooking for 4–5 minutes. Set aside."],[null,"Heat the oven to 350°F. Coat an oven-proof dish with 1/2 tablespoon olive oil."],[null,"Place the four tortillas on a clean surface. Add the filling and fold them. Place the rolls, with joints facing the bottom, in the oven-proof dish."],[null,"Pour the reserved 1/2 cup sauce from step 3 over the top and garnish with cheese."],[null,"Bake in the center of oven for 10 minutes or until the enchiladas are heated through and the cheese has melted. Garnish with yogurt and cilantro before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Note: As a garnish, also try sliced jalapenos or chopped green onions."],[null,"PLEASE NOTE: This recipe is higher in potassium and portion size is important. Check with your registered dietitian to see how this recipe can be included in your diet. * CKD Non-Dialysis: reduce protein by leaving out the chicken."],["Benefits of home-cooked meals","When following a kidney-friendly diet, home-cooked meals offer several benefits over options from restaurants. While eating out may seem simpler, larger portion sizes and unknown recipe ingredients may throw you off track from specific nutrition goals. Restaurant meals can also quickly add up in cost in comparison to home-cooked options. In addition, meals that are considered “fast-food” are often higher in food additives. More specifically, foods that contain the word “phos” as a preservative ingredient should be avoided on a low phosphorus diet. Phosphorus additives are absorbed up to 100% by the body. With chronic kidney disease, eating too much of these foods can raise phosphorus lab values and negatively impact skin, eye, heart and bone health. Eating meals at home allows you to be more mindful of your diet but does require planning ahead. PREPARE A LIST BEFORE GOING GROCERY SHOPPING. Be sure to include all needed ingredients to make meal prep and cooking a smoother process. Try to include more fresh than processed foods. TRY DIFFERENT KIDNEY-FRIENDLY RECIPES. Mixing up meal ideas should promote choices that are enticing and provide a variety of different flavors and options. Choose lean protein sources for main entrees and side dishes with vegetables and whole grains to encourage a balanced diet. DOUBLE THE RECIPE. If the meal is a home-cooked favorite, make extra to save on time and dishes. Leftovers should be fully cooled, appropriately portioned and placed in freezer-safe storage to help retain freshness until consumed. The best options to freeze include soup, casseroles, meat and grains."]]},"2548":{"s":[[null,"Prepare salsa first by mixing together pineapple, cilantro, jalapenos, lime juice and brown sugar in a non-reactive bowl (glass, plastic or ceramic). Set aside."],[null,"In a nonstick skillet, heat oil and sauté green peppers and mushrooms over medium heat for 2 to 4 minutes."],[null,"Drain off excess liquid."],[null,"Pour beaten eggs over mixture in skillet and sprinkle the green onion evenly over eggs. As the eggs begin to set pull them across the skillet with a spatula, forming large curds."],[null,"Continue cooking and folding eggs until no visible liquid egg remains."],[null,"Season with pepper."],[null,"Spoon egg mixture onto individual tortillas, divided evenly."],[null,"Spoon 1/3 cup pineapple salsa onto each tortilla, fold ends, and roll up burrito-style."]],"h":[[null,"For hotter jalapeno flavor, leave seeds in. For less heat cut down to 1 pepper."],[null,"Substitute fresh pineapple with canned pineapple tidbits or chunks."]]},"6927789":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F. Spray an 8- x 8-inch baking pan with cooking spray."],[null,"In a medium bowl, whisk the eggs and egg substitute until well combined. Add in cottage cheese and yogurt and whisk to combine. Set aside."],[null,"In a large skillet, heat olive oil over medium heat. Add onion and red pepper and sauté for 3 minutes, until vegetables begin to soften. Add garlic and sauté for another minute."],[null,"Stir in spinach, kale, and broccoli, and cook to wilt the greens, about 2 minutes. Add the artichokes, red pepper flakes, and dried basil. Remove from heat."],[null,"Spread the vegetables in the bottom of the prepared pan. Pour the egg and cheese mixture over the vegetables and make sure they are covered well."],[null,"Place the pan in the middle of the oven and bake for 40–45 minutes, or until the mixture is set and doesn’t jiggle when lightly shaken."],[null,"Allow to cool for 10 minutes, then cut into 6 pieces. Garnish with fresh basil if desired."]],"h":[]},"4840847":{"s":[[null,"In a large 4 quart heavy bottomed pot, heat oil over medium-high heat for 1 minute and add chicken breast to brown lightly."],[null,"Add all vegetables and spices and continue to cook for 8–10 minutes, stirring frequently."],[null,"Add broth, water and lemon juice to the vegetable-chicken mix."],[null,"Cover, turn to high heat and bring to a boil (2 minutes). Reduce heat to minimum and let simmer 20 minutes."],[null,"Add pasta and finish simmering for 5–10 minutes depending on the size of the pasta."],[null,"Before serving, sprinkle fresh parsley on top and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Freeze in portions, reheat in the microwave and you can have a hearty meal in minutes!"]]},"1711":{"s":[[null,"Cut chicken into bite-size pieces. Dice onion and celery. Peel and slice carrots.Cut green beans into 2-inch pieces."],[null,"In a large skillet over medium heat, lightly brown chicken for 5 to 6 minutes. Remove from heat."],[null,"In a separate skillet, heat olive oil over medium heat and sauté onion and celery for 5 minutes."],[null,"Add chicken pieces, carrots, green beans, flour, oregano, basil, nutmeg and thyme. Mix well and cook for 3 minutes."],[null,"Transfer ingredients to a 4-quart pan. Add broth and milk; bring to a boil."],[null,"Stir peas into soup and cook for 5 minutes."],[null,"Add pepper to taste before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Reduced-sodium broth usually contains between 480 mg to 600 mg sodium per cup."],[null,"One medium onion yields 1/2-cup diced."],[null,"Count one serving as 4 ounces liquid, if you are limiting fluids."],[null,"Rice milk or almond milk can be used instead of 1% low fat milk. Compare labels and look for the lowest potassium and phosphorus content."]]},"3235":{"s":[[null,"Carefully add 8 ounces of very hot water to a wide mouth 16 ounce mason jar."],[null,"Season the water by adding the first three ingredients: coconut amino, crushed ginger and apple cider vinegar."],[null,"Next layer in the noodles, cooked shredded chicken and frozen vegetables. Tighten lid and let stand ten minutes or until noodles are tender. If jar has cooled, remove the lid and microwave to preference for warmth, 30 seconds at a time. Add additional toppings of cilantro, green onion and lime, if desired."]],"h":[[null,"This recipe is designed to limit fluid to 8oz. It may help to invert the mason jar a few times during the process in order to cover all the ingredients."],[null,"If using additional toppings, this adds a small amount of potassium, approximately 22 mg of potassium."]]},"7220139":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a large pan, add the garlic, onion, carrot, celery and potatoes and fry for 3-4 minutes until beginning to soften but not brown."],[null,"Add the stock and tomatoes, bring to the boil and simmer for 10 minutes. Add the pasta, beans, peas and cabbage and continue to cook for a further 10 minutes, or until the pasta is cooked."],[null,"Stir through the parsley and pesto and season well. Serve topped with Parmesan cheese shavings."]],"h":[[null,"Minestrone is great for using up vegetables as you can add most veggies, for example parsnip, swede, potato, courgettes, peppers or aubergine."],[null,"Add more flavour with 1 tsp oregano and a few chilli flakes."],[null,"Make this veggie by using vegetarian pesto and vegetarian hard cheese, such as strong Cheddar cheese."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Can be frozen in small pots for individual portions. Defrost in a microwave and slowly until piping hot."],[null,"The image on this page is a stock image and not one taken of actual recipe."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"7926248":{"s":[[null,"Cook the potatoes in boiling water for 5-6 minutes until just tender. Drain."],[null,"Heat the oil in a small pan, add the onion and pepper and fry for 3-4 minutes until softened."],[null,"Add the potatoes and parsley and gently combine. Beat together the eggs and Parmesan cheese and season."],[null,"Preheat the grill. Pour the egg mixture into the pan and cook for 3 minutes. Place under the grill and cook until golden and set."],[null,"Serve with a crisp salad."]],"h":[[null,"You could add all sorts of ingredients for extra flavour – such as a finely chopped mushroom. Try adding crushed garlic or cooked, chopped spinach."],[null,"To make this vegetarian, use a Parmesan alternative or try it with goat’s cheese or mature Cheddar cheese."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"3186":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F."],[null,"Process whole wheat bread in food processor until crumbled."],[null,"Slice squash and then microwave with water for 16 minutes or until tender."],[null,"Drain squash well in colander."],[null,"Grate fresh carrots and chop sweet onion."],[null,"Combine squash, carrots, sweet onion, salt, 1 tablespoon flaxseed and eggs. Blend well."],[null,"Add 1/2 of the whole wheat bread crumbs. Mix in."],[null,"Spray 9″ square pan with nonstick cooking spray. Pour mixture into baking pan. Set aside."],[null,"Melt butter and then add remaining bread crumbs and remaining flaxseed to make topping. Mix well."],[null,"Spread topping over casserole."],[null,"Bake for 30 minutes or until topping starts to brown."],[null,"Cool and cut into 8 servings."]],"h":[[null,"Feel free to substitute zucchini for yellow squash."],[null,"Use Vidalia® or other sweet onion."],[null,"Flaxseed is a good source of dietary fiber and omega-3 fatty acids."]]},"2496":{"s":[[null,"Place the flour, yeast, sugar, water and oil in a large bowl and mix together. Knead the dough. When a ball is formed add the salt. Place the dough on a floured surface and continue kneading for 10 minutes, until dough is smooth and soft and not sticky."],[null,"Coat the bowl and dough with 1 to 2 teaspoons of oil. Cover the bowl and set it in a warm place until the dough doubles in volume (1 to 2 hours)."],[null,"Knead risen dough for a few minutes. Divide the dough into 12 pieces and roll each piece into a strand to be braided, approximately 10″ to 12″ in length."],[null,"Braid 3 of the rolled dough strips together to form the challah. Repeat with remaining dough strips to make 4 challahs."],[null,"Place challahs on a baking sheet or in a baking pan, cover and let the dough rise again, approximately 40 minutes."],[null,"Preheat oven to 350º F. Brush each challah with beaten egg. Bake for approximately 30 minutes, until the challahs turn golden brown. Remove challahs from the oven and from baking pan and cool on a wire rack."]],"h":[[null,"Divide each challah into 8 portions for a total of 32 portions for the 4 loaves."],[null,"Sprinkle poppy or sesame seeds on top before baking if desired."],[null,"Check YouTube for online videos with instructions on braiding and shaping the challahs."]]},"4779899":{"s":[[null,"Slice the cheese thinly or grate it. Place the cheese and the pear slices on two muffin halves. Season with cinnamon and drizzle with honey. Cover with the remaining muffin halves."],[null,"Heat oil over medium heat in a non-stick pan. Grill the sandwiches for two minutes on each side or until the muffins turn golden and the cheese is melted. With the help of a spatula, apply some pressure to the sandwiches during cooking."]],"h":[[null,"* If you have a cheese slicer, use it for both, cheese and pear. You can also use apple instead of a pear."],[null,"TIP: Including a few leaves of arugula salad, as seen in our image, will add color and a slight peppery taste."],["Cheeses for melting can fit into a kidney diet","Comfort foods can still be part of a healthy lifestyle with a few recipe adjustments to meet the needs of a kidney-friendly diet. A warm bowl of soup with a sandwich is one example. It’s important to consider the ingredients of these foods to maintain the goals of your diet. Dishes made with condensed soups or heavy sauces should be eaten with caution. Many may be higher not only in sodium but also in potassium. Understanding which foods may be higher in potassium can be helpful with meal planning and including some of your favorites. With many sandwiches, melted cheese is used for flavor and as a topping. Choosing the right type of cheese is important to not only get the desired taste but to also ensure your choice isn’t too high in sodium, potassium, or phosphorus. Portion size can also make a difference and should be considered when creating your dish. Examples of low phosphorus cheeses that can create the desired melted effect include sharp cheddar, mozzarella, and fontina. In general, most of these are also low in the amount of potassium per serving. Caution should use used with a low-sodium choice. Be sure to read labels to ensure potassium chloride isn’t replacing sodium chloride in these cheeses."]]},"4269980":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375°F (conventional oven)."],[null,"Prepare zucchini and pineapple and let stand until ready to use."],[null,"In a large mixing bowl, prepare egg mixture by whisking together eggs, oil, apple juice, sugar and vanilla."],[null,"Measure yogurt and add baking soda, stir to mix and let stand for 1 minute."],[null,"Squeeze excess water from shredded zucchini and pineapple, add to egg mixture along with yogurt and stir well."],[null,"Add flour to wet mix all at once and stir until just combined. (Too much stirring will make the loaf chewy!)"],[null,"Pour into a greased and floured 9 × 5\" loaf pan. Bake for 60 minutes."],[null,"Turn out and let cool on wire rack. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Lower in sugar and fat but not on taste!"]]},"6431387":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6566587":{"s":[[null,"Place potatoes in a large pot, and cover with water. Bring to a boil over high heat, reduce heat to medium, and cook, uncovered, for 10-15 minutes or until tender. Drain. Add lemon juice and olive oil, and begin mashing by hand or with an electric mixer. When mixture is smooth and creamy, stir in lemon zest, cilantro, dill, salt and pepper. Serve warm."]],"h":[]},"6815712":{"s":[[null,"Cut potatoes into 1-inch cubes. Place in medium saucepan and cover with water. Bring to a boil. Cover, reduce heat, and simmer 12 minutes or until potatoes are tender. Drain."],[null,"Mix dressing ingredients."],[null,"Combine hot potatoes, celery, green onions, and dressing. Serve hot or refrigerate and serve cold."]],"h":[]},"2942":{"s":[[null,"Mix all ingredients and store in an airtight container."],[null,"To prepare sauce for one portion of meat, melt 1 tablespoon unsalted butter or olive oil and add 1/2 tablespoon of herb sauce mix."],[null,"Pour over meat and bake in the oven or use as a sauce topping on beef, chicken or fish."]],"h":[[null,"Hungarian paprika is known for it’s sweet taste. Do not substitute smoked paprika."],[null,"For variety, try substituting other spices like chili powder, onion powder or poultry seasoning."],[null,"Save money by making your own herb sauce."],[null,"Make a sodium-free version by omitting the celery salt."]]},"6651941":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F. Line a large roasting pan with foil. Set a rack inside the roasting pan and coat it with cooking spray. Set aside."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine the butter with 2 tsp each of the sage, thyme, and rosemary, plus the salt and pepper. Reserve the remaining 1 tsp of each of the herbs."],[null,"In a small saucepan, add the white wine vinegar and chicken broth, bring to a gentle boil. Add the reserved herbs and lower to a simmer."],[null,"With your hands, separate the turkey breast skin from the breast meat, creating a pocket without removing the skin. Rub the butter herb mixture all over the breast meat. Place the skin back down on the breast."],[null,"Set the turkey on the prepared rack in the pan. Roast the turkey for about 1 hour, 20 minutes to 1 hour, 40 minutes until the internal temperature reaches 170 degrees F and the juices run clear. Baste every 15–20 minutes with the mixture of chicken broth and white wine vinegar."],[null,"Remove the turkey from the oven, cover loosely with foil, and let stand for 15 minutes before slicing. Discard the skin and serve."]],"h":[]},"6969063":{"s":[[null,"Place olive oil in large sauté pan. Add celery and onion and sauté until softened, approximately 3-5 minutes."],[null,"Add apple and poultry seasoning. Toss well. Add stock and simmer 2-3 minutes. Add bread cubes and fresh herbs and toss well. Set aside to cool before stuffing poultry."],[null,"Place in an ovenproof casserole. Bake for 30 minutes. If you want crispy stuffing, bake uncovered. For softer stuffing, cover with foil."]],"h":[]},"7065016":{"s":[[null,"First, make the pastry. Place the flour in a bowl and using a fork, mix in the herbs, egg, olive oil and water until it forms a dough. Shape the dough into a ball and refrigerate for at least 30 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, preheat the oven to 200ºC/gas 6 and make the filling. Heat the oil in a large frying pan, add the onion, garlic and pepper and fry for three minutes until beginning to soften."],[null,"Add the cauliflower, courgette, celery and carrot and continue to fry for three minutes."],[null,"Add the lentils, tomatoes, stock, Parmesan cheese, herbs and pepper. Bring to the boil and simmer for 10 minutes, until the vegetables are almost cooked."],[null,"Transfer to a pie dish. Roll out the pastry and cover the pie."],[null,"Cook for 25-30 minutes, until the pastry is golden and crisp."]],"h":[[null,"You could make this vegetarian by using a Parmesan alternative or use a little vegetarian goat's cheese."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"6466719":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Add the breadcrumbs and cook 1–2 minutes or until golden, stirring constantly. Set aside on separate plate."],[null,"Bring the water to a boil in the skillet over medium-high heat. Add the asparagus, return to a boil, reduce heat, cover, and simmer 3 minutes or until just tender. Drain well, discarding water. Place the asparagus on a serving plate."],[null,"Meanwhile, in a small bowl, whisk together the sour cream, mayonnaise, milk, mustard, tarragon, and salt. Place in the skillet over medium-low heat and cook 1 minute or until heated, stirring constantly. Spoon over the asparagus and sprinkle with the breadcrumbs."]],"h":[]},"9080740":{"s":[[null,"In a large pot add the sliced potatoes and salt, and then fill it with water, covering the potatoes by about one inch. Bring to a boil over high heat, then reduce the heat to medium-low and cook until the potatoes are fork-tender, approx. 10 minutes. Drain the potatoes, but RESERVE 1/4 cup of the starchy water."],[null,"Meanwhile, combine all the salad dressing ingredients plus the reserved cooking water in a small bowl and mix well. Then add salt and pepper to your taste."],[null,"Place the drained potatoes in a large bowl and add the herby dressing. Mix well and let the potatoes rest for a few minutes before gently tossing again. (The potatoes will absorb the sauce as they sit.)"],[null,"You may serve the potato salad warm or cold. Refrigerate it for a few hours, or overnight if planning to serve cold."]],"h":[]},"6967822":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, combine the low-fat ricotta cheese, parsley, basil, black pepper, and garlic powder. Mix well and set aside."],[null,"Lightly toast the slices of whole grain bread until golden and crisp."],[null,"In another small bowl, toss the halved cherry tomatoes with olive oil, balsamic vinegar and dried oregano."],[null,"Spread an even layer of the herbed ricotta mixture over each slice of toast. Top each with a portion of the marinated cherry tomatoes."]],"h":[]},"6960040":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400 degrees F. Line a sheet pan or baking sheet with aluminum foil or parchment paper."],[null,"Place the tomatoes, squash, zucchini, onion, garlic cloves, and walnuts in a large bowl."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix the olive oil, basil, oregano, parsley, red pepper, and black pepper."],[null,"Add 2 tsp of the olive oil and 2 tsp of the spice blend onto the vegetables and toss to coat."],[null,"Divide the last tsp of the olive oil and last tsp of the spice blend between the cod fillets and spread over the top."],[null,"Place the cod on one end of the baking sheet and spread the vegetables over the other end. Roast in the oven until the cod reaches an internal temperature of 145 degrees F or until the fish easily flakes apart with a fork and is no longer translucent, about 20 minutes."],[null,"While the cod and vegetables are roasting, prepare the quinoa according to package directions."]],"h":[]},"6744025":{"s":[[null,"Toast the bread in a toaster or toaster oven to desired doneness."],[null,"While the bread is toasting, prepare the eggs: fully heat the oil in a medium stick-resistant skillet over medium-low heat. Pour the eggs into the hot skillet and cook while gently stirring (or folding) the mixture until the eggs are no longer runny, yet are still moist, about 1 1/2–2 minutes. Remove the skillet from the heat, sprinkle with the salt, and gently stir (or fold) in the herbs."],[null,"Transfer the toasts to plates. Top each toast with half the herbed eggs. If desired, sprinkle with freshly ground black pepper to taste. Serve."]],"h":[]},"6081956":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 425°F."],[null,"Place the chicken in a baking pan. Brush the chicken skin with the oil. Sprinkle with the herbs de Provence and salt."],[null,"Roast until the chicken is well done (internal temperature of at least 165°F) and skin is crisped and browned, about 40–45 minutes."],[null,"Let stand for at least 5 minutes. If desired, drizzle the chicken with any pan juices. Serve."]],"h":[]},"6766444":{"s":[[null,"Add all ingredients to a bowl and mash with a fork or potato masher to combine."],[null,"Serve with cut up raw vegetables, whole grain tortilla chips or crackers, or use as a sandwich or wrap filling."]],"h":[]},"7953493":{"s":[[null,"Mix the sumac, pepper, lemon juice, olive oil, parsley and mint together to make the vinaigrette, then reserve."],[null,"Mix the lentils, tomato, green pepper, cucumber and onion together, then stir in the vinaigrette."],[null,"Place the chopped lettuce in the centre of a serving dish, and the whole lettuce leaves around the outside. Pile the lentil mixture on top, arrange the tomatoes around the outside, sprinkle with a good pinch of sumac and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Try adapting the recipe with your favourite vegetables - most will work with this salad."],[null,"The salad is extra delicious if sprinkled with a little crumbed goat’s cheese."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"7720686":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200ºC/gas 6."],[null,"Remove the heads from the mackerel, split along the belly and remove the guts. Wash thoroughly and pat dry with kitchen paper."],[null,"Open out each fish so that it lies skin-side up and press firmly along the length to loosen the back bone. Carefully, lift the bone from the flesh then cut off at the tail end leaving the tail intact. Rinse and dry."],[null,"In a food-processor, pulse the bread with the parsley, fresh coriander, zests, cumin, ground coriander, chilli flakes and olive oil until it forms fine crumbs."],[null,"Arrange the mackerel flesh side up in a large baking dish and sprinkle with the breadcrumbs. Pour the stock around the mackerel but not over."],[null,"Cook for 8-10 minutes until the fish is opaque. Meanwhile, combine all the salad ingredients."],[null,"Serve the mackerel with any juices from the baking dish, the salad and rocket leaves."]],"h":[[null,"Mackerel fillets work just as well if you don’t like dealing with the whole fish."],[null,"Other fish fillets such as river cobbler, cod, tilapia or trout are great with this herby crust."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"7320245":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200ºC/gas 6. Add the bulgur wheat to a large bowl, pour over 600ml boiling water and leave to soak for 30 minutes or until tender."],[null,"Place the aubergine halves, skin-side down, on a baking tray, and brush the cut surface with half the olive oil. Bake for 25–30 minutes or until golden."],[null,"Remove from the oven, scoop out the flesh and roughly chop."],[null,"Meanwhile, drain off any excess liquid from the bulgur wheat. In a pan, heat the remaining oil and fry the onion and garlic for 2–3 minutes until softened."],[null,"Stir in the ground cumin and coriander and continue to fry for 1 minute."],[null,"Add the remaining ingredients, including the soaked bulgur wheat and the aubergine flesh, but not the Parmesan."],[null,"Heat through then divide the mixture between the aubergine shells. Return to the oven and cook for 10–15 minutes until the topping is golden. Sprinkle with Parmesan shavings to serve."]],"h":[[null,"For a gluten-free version, use quinoa in place of bulgur wheat."],[null,"You could also top with a little dairy-free cheese instead of the Parmesan to make this a vegetarian and vegan dish."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"7731476":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 200°C/fan 180°C/gas 6. Lightly spray a non-stick ovenproof 18cm flan or pie dish with low-calorie cooking spray."],[null,"Spray a non-stick frying pan with a couple of pumps of low-calorie cooking spray and put it over a medium heat. Stir-fry the onion, garlic, courgette and tomatoes for 6-8 minutes, or until softened. Remove from the heat. Stir in the herbs and peppers, then mix together the cottage cheese and eggs and pour in. Season lightly with pepper and spoon into the flan or pie dish."],[null,"Bake for 30-35 minutes, or until lightly golden and cooked through. Scatter over the extra herbs and serve with a salad."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"6195793":{"s":[[null,"In a blender or food processor, combine the oats, protein powder, banana, eggs, Greek yogurt, baking powder, cinnamon, vanilla extract, and salt. Blend until smooth."],[null,"Let the batter sit for a few minutes to thicken slightly."],[null,"Heat a non-stick skillet or griddle over medium heat and lightly spray with cooking spray."],[null,"Pour 1/4 cup portions of batter onto the skillet to form small pancakes."],[null,"Cook for 2–3 minutes on one side or until bubbles form on the surface."],[null,"Flip the pancakes and cook for an additional 1–2 minutes until golden brown."],[null,"Repeat until all the batter is used."]],"h":[]},"2750":{"s":[[null,"Blend ingredients in a blender for 30 to 45 seconds."],[null,"Divide into two servings. Serve one now; freeze the second serving for later."]],"h":[[null,"Ask your dietitian to recommend an acceptable brand of protein powder."],[null,"For flavor variations try strawberries, raspberries or blackberries instead of blueberries."]]},"2616":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 325°F."],[null,"In a mixing bowl, beat margarine and brown sugar."],[null,"Blend in egg and vanilla."],[null,"Combine remaining ingredients. Mix will be very dry. (You can add 1 tablespoon of molasses or water to make it stick together.)"],[null,"Spray a cookie sheet with non-stick spray."],[null,"Roll batter into 1-inch balls, and place on sheet."],[null,"Bake for 10 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Use old fashioned or quick cooking oatmeal. Avoid instant oatmeal because sodium content is much higher."],[null,"Omit baking powder for a crunchy cookie. Phosphorus will decrease to 42 mg per serving and sodium decreases to 146 mg."],[null,"Soy protein powder may be used but nutrient content will change. Soy protein is usually higher in phosphorus compared to whey protein powder. Ask your dietitian for a list of recommended protein powders that are lowest in phosphorus and potassium."]]},"2876":{"s":[[null,"Combine all ingredients in a large bowl. Mix well."],[null,"Refrigerate until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Serve this dip with low potassium fruits such as apples, pineapple or grapes. May also serve with vanilla wafers or graham crackers, if desired."],[null,"Some whipped toppings have phosphorus additives. Look in the ingredients list to be sure phosphorus is not added."],[null,"Protein powder can vary in protein, potassium, phosphorus and sodium. You may talk to your dietitian to see which one would be appropriate for you."],[null,"One and a half cups of whipped topping equals about 4 ounces."]]},"2629":{"s":[[null,"Pour pineapple juice into the blender"],[null,"Add the protein powder and blend until smooth"],[null,"Add crushed ice and blend until smooth"],[null,"Pour into serving glass"],[null,"Add lemon lime soda or ginger ale"],[null,"Garnish with small pineapple slices."]],"h":[[null,"Syntrax Nectar Whey Protein Isolate® may be purchased online or at The Vitamin Shoppe. One scoop or individual package equals 1 ounce and provides 23 grams protein."],[null,"Freeze the extra serving until ready to drink later."],[null,"Use ginger ale (regular or diet) instead of lemon-lime soda if desired."]]},"3636":{"s":[[null,"Combine rice milk and protein powder in a blender and blend well."],[null,"Divide into 2 servings. Enjoy one now and one later."]],"h":[[null,"Refrigerate extra serving until ready to drink."],[null,"EAS 100% Whey Protein Powder® was used in this recipe analysis. Ask your dietitian about other protein powder options."],[null,"Stir in a glass or shake in a shaker instead of the blender if desired."]]},"1751":{"s":[[null,"Mix the thawed whipped topping, protein powder and vanilla extract. Freeze mixture until firm."],[null,"Divide frozen mixture into 2 scoops and place in two 8-ounce glasses. Pour 4 ounces chilled root beer over scoops of whipped topping mixture in each glass."],[null,"Serve and enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Check ingredients on root beer and only buy phosphate-free brands."],[null,"Protein powders vary in scoop size and protein content. Ask your dietitian for recommendations on whey protein powders that are kidney-friendly."],[null,"Substitute diet root beer for a low carbohydrate version. Carbs are reduced to 10 grams."]]},"3471":{"s":[[null,"Blend egg whites in a blender for 2 minutes."],[null,"Add strawberries, pineapple concentrate and protein powder. Blend at medium speed until smooth."],[null,"Pour 3/4 cup of the smoothie into a glass and top with whipped cream."],[null,"Store the remainder in the refrigerator (1 day) or freezer to enjoy later."]],"h":[[null,"Increase protein powder to 2 scoops for a higher protein smoothie."],[null,"Omit protein powder for a low protein smoothie (3 grams per serving)."],[null,"Pasteurized egg whites are recommended to avoid the risk of salmonella. Look for refrigerated egg whites in a carton in the dairy section, or dried egg whites in the baking section at your local grocery store."]]},"1804":{"s":[[null,"Freeze blueberries and yogurt for 30 minutes before making recipe."],[null,"Place all the ingredients in a blender and blend until smooth."],[null,"Divide into 2 servings. Enjoy one now and freeze the other serving for later."]],"h":[[null,"Use frozen blueberries if desired."],[null,"Substitute pineapple or strawberries for blueberries for a different tropical twist."],[null,"LiquaCel™ is a liquid protein supplement that is low in potassium and phosphorus. Ask your dietitian for information or go to GlobalHP.com"]]},"3378":{"s":[[null,"Slowly add protein powder to the yogurt, mixing after each addition. Do not mix all at once or it may be clumpy."],[null,"Wash the blueberries and pat dry. Place on top of the yogurt mixture."]],"h":[[null,"Greek yogurt has more protein per serving than regular yogurt. Look for at least 12 grams of protein or more per serving."],[null,"You may use a different lower potassium fruit, if desired. Try strawberries, raspberries, grapes, pineapple, pears, blackberries or a combination of these fruits."],[null,"There are many different brands of protein powder. They can vary on protein, potassium, phosphorus and sodium level. Your dietitian can help give a recommendation on what to look for in a protein powder."],[null,"Yogurt is a good source of calcium. Check with your dietitian or doctor to be sure your blood calcium level is in a healthy range."]]},"6989427":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F. Spray a 9 by 9-inch square baking pan with cooking spray."],[null,"In a blender, puree the beans with the oil and water. Add the eggs, cocoa, low- or no-calorie sweetener, coffee, and vanilla and blend well."],[null,"Add the baking mix to blender and pulse until just incorporated. Stir in mini chocolate chips. Pour into the prepared pan."],[null,"Bake for 18-20 minutes"],[null,"Let cool at least 15 minutes before cutting and removing from the pan. Cut into 12 equal-sized brownies."]],"h":[]},"1865":{"s":[[null,"Heat the olive oil in a large sauce pan over medium heat. Chop onion and add to the pan. Cook until tender, about 2-3 minutes."],[null,"Add rice and cook and stir for 30 seconds to 1 minute."],[null,"Add water to the rice and bring to a boil. Once boiling, turn heat down to low, cover and simmer for 20 minutes."],[null,"Remove the pan of rice from the heat. Stir in the butter. Zest the lime and stir the zest into the rice. The zest should be about 2 teaspoons."]],"h":[[null,"If you are looking for more of a lime flavor, the lime can be cut in half and squeezed over the rice."],[null,"Look for unenriched rice."]]},"6142717":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400 degrees F. Spray a baking sheet with cooking spray."],[null,"In a medium bowl, add remaining ingredients and mix well."],[null,"Pour Brussels sprouts on baking sheet."],[null,"Bake for 25-30 minutes; toss once during baking."]],"h":[]},"1714":{"s":[[null,"Soften the cream cheese."],[null,"In a medium bowl combine the cream cheese, salad dressing and onion powder."],[null,"Place in the refrigerator for 30 minutes to chill."],[null,"Form cheese mixture into a ball."],[null,"Place ground walnuts on a plate and roll the cheese ball to cover."],[null,"Wrap the cheese ball in plastic wrap and chill until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Serve cheese ball with low-sodium crackers and apple slices."]]},"2140":{"s":[[null,"Peel, core and thinly slice or chop apples."],[null,"In a 13” x 9” baking dish, combine brown sugar, melted butter and one teaspoon of the cinnamon. Add apples and cranberries; toss well to coat."],[null,"Spread apple mixture evenly over bottom of the baking dish."],[null,"Cut bread into 3/4” slices and arrange on top of apples."],[null,"Mix eggs, rice milk, vanilla and remaining 2 teaspoons cinnamon until well blended. Pour mixture over bread, soaking bread completely. Cover and refrigerate 4 to 24 hours."],[null,"Preheat oven to 375° F."],[null,"Bake covered with foil for 30 minutes. Uncover dish and bake 15 minutes or until top starts to brown."],[null,"Remove dish from oven and let stand for 5 minutes before cutting into 9 servings."],[null,"Serve warm. Dust top with powdered sugar before serving."]],"h":[[null,"3 large apples yields approximately 4-1/2 cups. Cut into chunks instead of slices if preferred."],[null,"Cut into smaller 1-1/2” x 2” portions for lower calories and carbohydrates."],[null,"Use French bread instead of Italian and trim crust from bread if desired."]]},"3009":{"s":[[null,"Set cream cheese out to soften for 30 minutes."],[null,"Drain canned tuna and flake with a fork."],[null,"In a mixing bowl combine cream cheese, tuna, cranberries, celery, onion and cumin. Mix with an electric mixer until well combined."],[null,"Combine the bread crumbs and parsley then place on a plate. Shape the cream cheese mixture into a ball and roll in bread crumbs to cover."],[null,"Wrap the ball in plastic wrap and refrigerate until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Serve with low-sodium crackers, apple slices or raw veggies."]]},"6631665":{"s":[[null,"Arrange vegetables on a large, round platter. Alternate red vegetables with green vegetables in a circle on platter."],[null,"Place hummus in a small bowl in center of platter."]],"h":[]},"2146":{"s":[[null,"Chop onion."],[null,"Place shredded cabbage, onion and water in a large pan and steam over medium-low heat for an hour until tender. Stir frequently so cabbage does not stick. Add more water if needed."],[null,"Cook noodles according to package directions, omitting salt. Drain well."],[null,"When all liquid is evaporated from cabbage, add margarine. Toss and continue to cook for 10 to 15 minutes."],[null,"Season cabbage with black pepper."],[null,"Add noodles to mixture and blend. Heat over low heat until hot."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute wide egg noodles if kluski noodles are unavailable."],[null,"8 ounces dry kluski noodles or wide egg noodles yields 3-1/2 cups cooked."],[null,"Holushki is a recipe of Ukrainian origin."],[null,"1/2 medium cabbage head yields approximately 8 cups."],[null,"Select a trans-fat free margarine."]]},"3181":{"s":[[null,"Using a 1-quart, microwavable bowl, beat egg product and sugar until well blended."],[null,"Stir in non-dairy creamer and microwave for 1 minute, or until mixture thickens."],[null,"Remove from heat. When cool, stir in vanilla."],[null,"Pour mixture into center container of the ice cream machine."],[null,"Layer ice and rock salt around container, alternating layers until bucket is full."],[null,"Process according to manufacturer’s instructions for your particular ice cream machine."]],"h":[[null,"If you have an ice cream machine, pour mixture in and follow manufacturer instructions."],[null,"This recipe may be doubled. Freeze extra for a later treat."],[null,"Variations can be made by adding 1-1/2 cups of low-potassium fruit of choice such as fresh strawberries or peaches. When adding fruit, increase sugar to 2/3 cup."],[null,"Coffee Rich® non-dairy creamer and Egg Beaters® low-cholesterol egg product were used in the development of this recipe. If these brand-name products are not available in your area, ask your renal dietitian about substitute products."],[null,"One serving counts as 4 ounces of liquid in a dialysis diet."]]},"2132":{"s":[[null,"Place raw almonds in a jar and cover with filtered water. Cover jar and soak at room temperature for 6 hours, or overnight in the refrigerator."],[null,"Drain the almonds and place in a blender."],[null,"Add 3 cups of fresh filtered water to the blender"],[null,"Blend on a low setting, gradually moving to high setting. Blend for 2 minutes, until liquid turns white and almonds are finely chopped."],[null,"Place a cheesecloth or nut bag over a bowl. Pour the liquid through in batches to strain liquid from almond meal. Squeeze the cheesecloth or nut bag to remove the liquid. Discard the almond meal."],[null,"Add vanilla extract and other flavorings as desired."],[null,"Pour almond milk into a jar, cover and refrigerate for up to 3 days. Shake before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Suggested flavorings include maple syrup or honey, ground cinnamon, sugar, stevia, Splenda or other desired sweetener."],[null,"Adjust water for thicker or thinner beverage."],[null,"The almond meal is discarded because it contains the majority of phosphorus and some potassium from the nuts. Generally nut milks are much lower in potassium and phosphorus compared to a serving of nuts."],[null,"Commercially prepared almond milk contains added salt, calcium, thickeners and emulsifiers. Some brands also contain phosphate additives. Homemade almond milk is salt-free and has no additives."]]},"3904":{"s":[[null,"Grate onion and mince garlic clove."],[null,"Heat all ingredients over low heat until butter is melted and onion and garlic are soft cooked."],[null,"Sauce is ready to use immediately, or store in a covered container in the refrigerator for up to one week."]],"h":[[null,"For thicker sauce add 1 tablespoon all-purpose flour or 1 teaspoon rice flour during cooking."],[null,"Commercially prepared BBQ sauce averages 350 mg sodium for a 2 tablespoon serving. This recipe contains only 51 mg sodium including 1/4 teaspoon of salt. If you omit the salt sodium content is only 18 mg per serving."]]},"9936271":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350 degrees F and line two baking sheets with parchment paper."],[null,"If you do not have black bean flour on hand, you can make some in a powerful blender, like a Vitamix. Measure half a cup of dry black beans and blend on high until a flour like consistency is reached. It will take about 15-20 seconds."],[null,"Combine the salt and bean flour in a medium bowl. Then add the oil and mix well. Use a fork to get the oil mixed in and incorporated. Then slowly pour the water, starting with 1/2 a cup, and adding more as needed to reach a slightly runny batter."],[null,"Pour teaspoons of batter onto your baking sheet, leaving plenty of space in between each one. The chips should spread slightly. Then, using a fork, press and stretch each chip GENTLY to spread the batter nice and thin for maximum crispiness."],[null,"Bake for 10 minutes, then using a fork, flip your chips and bake for an additional 8-10 minutes, watching closely so they don't burn. **see note 3"],[null,"Remove from the oven and let your chips cool completely before handling. These chips pair particularly well with homemade guacamole, or you may enjoy as is."]],"h":[[null,"Don't worry if your black bean flour has a few thicker specs. You will see some black specs throughout from the skin of the beans. When dropping the batter onto your baking sheet, don't worry about size and shape of your chips. They don't need to be uniform, as long as they are thin, they will crisp up. However, make sure not to leave holes when spreading the chips, or they may break when flipping. Use a large fork to flip the chips, and rather than lift them from the parchment paper, glide or push the fork under each chip to ensure it's not sticking to the paper, then flip. Pushing the fork under each chip will also give it the ripples as shown in the image. To make these oil free, skip the oil and use extra care when flipping your chips. They may get a little stuck to the parchment paper when baking, so carefully scrape/glide the bottom of each chip with a large fork to flip them. To make flavoured chips, you may also add a pinch of garlic powder, cumin, cayenne pepper, or paprika to your bowl of dry ingredients, before mixing in the oil or water. These chips taste best the same day they’re made, as they may lose their crispiness, so plan to enjoy immediately. Keep them in a single layer until ready to serve so they don’t get soggy from being piled on top of one another."]]},"6188015":{"s":[[null,"Bring water, ginger, cardamom, and cinnamon to a simmer."],[null,"Add the tea bag and steep for 3-5 minutes."],[null,"Stir in the milk and heat until warm."],[null,"Remove tea bag and strain out spices before serving."]],"h":[]},"3024":{"s":[[null,"Peel and slice potatoes. Soak in a lage pot of water for 3-4 hours to remove some of the potassium, or boil potatoes for 5 minutes, drain water, then add fresh water and cook until tender.Place chicken or turkey pieces in Dutch oven with 6 cups water. Add celery, salt, pepper and herb seasoning. Bring to boil. Reduce heat and simmer, covered for 60 minutes or until tender. Remove meat from bones and set aside."],[null,"Add leached or double-boiled potatoes and onion to broth. Bring broth to a boil and cook until potatoes are tender, approximately 15 minutes. Remove vegetables with slotted spoon and set aside."],[null,"In a large bowl, mix flour and butter together with a fork. Add egg and 2 tablespoons water; mix with fork until ingredients are moistened."],[null,"Roll out dough 1/3” thick. With a sharp knife, cut dough into strips."],[null,"Add noodle strips to broth and cook for 15 minutes (If using prepackaged dumpling noodles, simply add them to the broth at this time.)"],[null,"Add vegetables and meat to the broth and simmer for 5 minutes."],[null,"Sprinkle with fresh parsley and serve."]],"h":[[null,"For convenience, you can use a package of prepared dumpling noodles like Mary B’s® brand, which can be found in the frozen food section of your grocery store."],[null,"If you are on a protein-modified diet, select a smaller 2.5-pound chicken to reduce protein to 21 grams per serving."],[null,"Substitute 3 turkey legs, skinned, boned and chopped for chicken."]]},"9967440":{"s":[[null,"Add the jalapeno with a tablespoon or two of your broth to a small saucepan and sauté for 2 minutes."],[null,"Add all remaining ingredients, mix well and bring to a boil. Then reduce heat to medium low and simmer for 8 minutes until slightly reduced."],[null,"Use in your favourite Mexican dishes."]],"h":[[null,"Use anywhere from 1 to 3 jalapenos depending on your level of spice. If you want a more mild sauce, stick with 1 jalapeno and remove the seeds. For medium, 1-2 with the seeds kept in. For hot, use 3 jalapenos with their seeds. Store leftovers in a sealed container or jar in the refrigerator for up to 5 days. Or you may freeze for up to 1 month. You may blend the sauce once simmered, if preferred. But if you've chopped the jalapenos very finely, it's not necessary. The optional corn starch works well if you're using the sauce straight away, as is. If you're adding the sauce to my Veggie Enchilada Casserole , skip the corn starch. The nutritional information is for ⅛ of the sauce, approx 4 tablespoons or ¼ cup."]]},"6800231":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 300°F. Line a baking sheet with unbleached parchment paper."],[null,"In a medium bowl, stir together all ingredients. Spread in an even layer on the baking sheet."],[null,"Bake in the oven until toasted, about 35 minutes. No stirring required. Cool on the tray on a cooling rack. Serve or store in a sealed jar or container for up to a week."]],"h":[]},"9523666":{"s":[[null,"Add the peanuts and optional sea salt if using to your Vitamix. Blend on high, using your tamper to push the peanuts down while blending, until a smooth consistency is reached. The peanut will quickly go from whole peanuts, to ground up pieces to creamy peanut butter."],[null,"Store in a clean sealed jar or container."]],"h":[[null,"To make peanut butter in the Vitamix, don’t use less than 2 cups of peanuts. You’ll need some volume for it to blend nicely. If you want to make more than 4 cups at a time, I suggest multiple batches. If using salted peanuts, skip the additional sea salt. I’ve kept my peanut butter in a sealed jar at room temperature for up to 2 weeks. You may refrigerate for longer but it may harden slightly. Flavour will not be affected."]]},"3141":{"s":[[null,"Sift together cream of tartar and baking soda using a fine strainer."],[null,"Store in an airtight jar or baggie at room temperature until ready to use."]],"h":[[null,"Note the amount and nutrients are used throughout a recipe, so the nutrient values will be spread out. Most recipes call for less than a tablespoon of baking powder for an entire recipe."],[null,"This baking powder recipe uses a 2-to-1 ratio of cream of tartar to baking soda. To replace one tablespoon of commercial baking powder in a recipe, use 2 teaspoons cream of tartar and 1 teaspoon baking soda."],[null,"You can use this mixture in the same proportion as commercial baking powder when making cakes, quick breads, muffins, tortillas, pancakes and waffles."],[null,"Cream of tartar is the potassium acid salt of tartaric acid. One teaspoon contains 495 mg potassium. When using cream of tartar with baking soda to replace phosphorus-containing baking powder, be aware the potassium content of food will be higher but phosphorus is much lower."]]},"9847094":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 350℉/176℃ and arrange the pistachios on a baking sheet. Bake for 5-6 minutes to heat them up without browning them, and then remove them from the oven."],[null,"Transfer the pistachios to the bowl of your food processor or blender and start processing. They will go from pieces to flour, then they will start to lump together, and eventually, you'll have creamy, smooth pistachio butter. Make sure to pause and scrape down the sides, as needed, and give your appliance breaks in between processing so it doesn't overheat. The entire process (with breaks) can take up to 15 minutes, depending on your processor."]],"h":[]},"3530":{"s":[[null,"Place cooked rice and filtered water in a blender. Add sugar and vanilla."],[null,"Blend on high speed for 4 minutes or until liquid is milky and the rice is finely blended."],[null,"Strain mixture using cheesecloth or a nut bag. Discard rice solids."],[null,"Pour rice milk into a jar, cover and refrigerate for up to 3 days. Shake jar before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Rice milk can also be made with uncooked rice that is soaked in filtered water for 24 hours. Use 1 cup rice to 3 cups water. Adjust water for desired thickness."],[null,"Optional ingredients: 1-2 teaspoons canola oil added during blending; ground cinnamon; agave or maple syrup or honey instead of sugar or other sweetener of choice."],[null,"Homemade rice milk is free of additives and preservatives like calcium phosphate and salt, and costs less than commercially prepared rice milk."],[null,"Rice milk is low in protein. Add 1-2 scoops of protein powder to make high-protein rice milk."],[null,"Analysis includes white rice but you can substitute brown rice if desired."]]},"9725091":{"s":[[null,"Add the sesame seeds to a blender or food processor and process until smooth and creamy. This may take anywhere from 5-10 minutes depending on your equipment."],[null,"Once smooth, add the salt and garlic powder if using and process to combine. Serve with all your favourite dishes."]],"h":[[null,"If you want a deeper flavour, toast your sesame seeds first. You may do this on a lined baking sheet in the oven, or in a large skillet. Turn the seeds often to prevent burning, you just want to toast them until fragrant. For creamier tahini, you may use hulled sesame seeds, and/or add 1-2 tablespoon of a neutral oil. Tahini will keep refrigerated in an air tight container for up to 1 month, possibly longer."]]},"3654":{"s":[[null,"Chop the onion, tomato, cilantro and jalapeno into small pieces. Combine in a bowl."],[null,"Juice the lime. Add the lime juice, olive oil, salt and pepper to the vegetable mixture."],[null,"Let the salsa marinade for 15 minutes or more."],[null,"Serve with low-sodium tortilla chips or use as a topping on fish, chicken, meat or salad."]],"h":[[null,"Use red, white or yellow onion in this recipe."],[null,"The firmer the tomato, the better for this recipe."],[null,"The jalapeno is optional, or you may use another hot pepper of your choice."],[null,"A lime will produce about 2 tablespoons of juice."],[null,"coarse salt and fresh ground pepper give a better flavor, if they are available."],[null,"Use a food processor to chop the vegetables if desired."]]},"2509":{"s":[[null,"Crush the fennel seed."],[null,"In a small bowl combine turkey with crushed fennel seed, garlic powder, onion powder and salt. Cover the bowl and refrigerate overnight."],[null,"Divide the seasoned turkey into portions about the size of a ping-pong ball and flatten into patties to cook."],[null,"Cook over medium heat in a nonstick skillet until browned, about 1 to 2 minutes per side."]],"h":[[null,"Extra patties may be frozen for later use. Be sure to place a double layer of wrap or waxed paper between portions to make it easy to separate patties."]]},"7659367":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4. Slice the vegetables very thinly – a mandoline slicer is perfect."],[null,"Spray a little oil over a baking sheet and arrange the vegetable slices ensuring they don't overlap. You may need to make them in separate batches depending on the size of your oven."],[null,"Cook for 20 minutes, until lightly browned. It's vital to turn the vegetables frequently during cooking as they can easily burn. You may need to remove some crisps before the 20 minutes is up, as some will cook faster than others."],[null,"When all the crisps are ready, allow them to cool then mix together and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Take care not to burn your veggies. Root vegetables have a lot of natural sugar, so can scorch if you have the oven too high or don’t turn often enough during cooking."],[null,"You can cook the crisps in the microwave on 300W for 10 minutes, then 1 minute on full power, which works quite well but only for smaller batches."],[null,"These can also be cooked in an air fryer until crisp."]]},"2105":{"s":[[null,"Cook pasta according to package directions. Transfer to colander and rinse under cold water; drain and set aside."],[null,"Chop celery and red onion. Finely chop bell pepper and jalapeno pepper."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine remaining ingredients until well blended. Add cooled pasta and toss to coat."],[null,"Chill in refrigerator at least 1 hour before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Two ounces dry pasta makes 1 cup when cooked al dente."],[null,"Wear gloves when mincing raw hot peppers."],[null,"Low-fat mayonnaise may be substituted to reduce fat to 5 grams per serving. Sodium will be higher, so decrease or omit salt."]]},"6143641":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F and cover a sheet pan in parchment paper."],[null,"In a medium bowl, toss almonds with ground cinnamon, salt and honey."],[null,"Spread the almonds on a sheet pan and bake for 20 to 25 minutes, stirring occasionally until golden brown."],[null,"Allow the almonds to cool. Store in an airtight container at room temperature."]],"h":[]},"6969512":{"s":[[null,"Carefully cut a slit lengthwise in the pitted dates, gently open, and separate into halves."],[null,"Stuff each date half with a walnut half."],[null,"Drizzle honey over the stuffed dates before serving."]],"h":[]},"3393":{"s":[[null,"Slice apple into 4 to 6 wedges."],[null,"Spread each rice cake with one tablespoon of cream cheese"],[null,"Top rice cakes with apple wedges, drizzle with honey and sprinkle with pomegranate arils."]],"h":[[null,"Crisp apples such as Fuji, honey crisp, gala or golden delicious are great for this recipe."],[null,"Select unsalted or lightly salted rice cakes."],[null,"Apples with dribbles of honey, along with pomegranate, express hope for a sweet and fruitful new year."]]},"2734":{"s":[[null,"Slice green onions, keeping white and green parts separate."],[null,"Cut cherry tomatoes in half, cut green beans in half if desired."],[null,"Pat salmon filets dry with a paper towel and season all over with 1 teaspoon black pepper."],[null,"Heat air fryer at 390 degrees F for 3 minutes."],[null,"Brush salmon with 1/2 tablespoon of olive oil. Air fry the filets for 11-13 minutes at 390 degrees F."],[null,"Mix butter, honey, and crushed red pepper in a bowl."],[null,"Remove salmon from air fryer to a plate and cover."],[null,"Mix green beans with 1/2 tablespoon olive oil. Air fry green beans 8-10 minutes at 390 degrees F."],[null,"Sauté cherry tomatoes and white portions of green onion in small pan over medium heat for 3-4 minutes."],[null,"Place each salmon on a plate and spread honey butter over the top. Evenly distribute green beans, tomatoes and white green onion on the plates."],[null,"Sprinkle green tops of onion evenly on each plate."]],"h":[[null,"If you have diabetes, you may eliminate the honey butter and use only butter. Or you may eliminate the butter all together."]]},"4407596":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F."],[null,"In a small saucepan, melt butter and honey and stir together. Bring to a boil and remove from heat. Add vanilla."],[null,"In a mixing bowl, stir together puffed rice, Corn Flakes®, and cranberries. Add the melted butter and honey and mix thoroughly."],[null,"Press cereal mixture firmly into a 9\" non-stick pan."],[null,"Bake for 15 minutes."],[null,"Cut into 16 bars. Once they have cooled, cover with plastic wrap and store at room temperature."]],"h":[]},"3297":{"s":[[null,"Chop chives and grate ginger root."],[null,"In a small bowl whisk all ingredients together."],[null,"Serve dressing over salad greens or arugula."]],"h":[[null,"Look for soy sauce brand with the lowest sodium content."],[null,"Add an Asian flair to your entrée –drizzled Honey Chive Dressing over broiled or baked white fish such as flounder or tilapia."]]},"3011":{"s":[[null,"Wash and dry fresh fruit. Peel the peach and core the unpeeled apple and dice into bite-size pieces. Slice the strawberries. Chop the mint."],[null,"In a large bowl combine the fruit."],[null,"Drizzle honey over fruit and add the mint. Stir to combine."],[null,"Refrigerate until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"If fresh peach and blueberries are not in season use frozen. Thaw before making fruit salad."],[null,"This salad keeps for up to 1 week in the refrigerator."]]},"6595296":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375 degrees F. Spray baking dish with cooking spray."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine mustard, garlic and pepper."],[null,"Spread about 1 1/2 Tbsp. mustard mixture evenly on top of each chicken thigh."],[null,"Arrange chicken in a glass baking dish. Bake for 40 minutes or until mustard mixture has formed a crust and is slightly hardened."],[null,"Remove from oven and sprinkle thyme on top of chicken. Serve each chicken thigh with 1/2 cup wild rice and 1 cup steamed broccoli."]],"h":[]},"2937":{"s":[[null,"Stir mustard, mayonnaise, honey and Worcestershire sauce together in a small bowl."],[null,"Chill sauce in the refrigerator until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Use as a dipping sauce for chicken or fish nuggets, or use as a salad dressing."]]},"3975":{"s":[[null,"Stir mustard, mayonnaise, honey and Worcestershire sauce together in a small bowl."],[null,"Chill sauce in the refrigerator until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Use as a dipping sauce for chicken or fish nuggets, or use as a salad dressing."]]},"1916":{"s":[[null,"Place all ingredients in a jar; secure lid and shake until well mixed."],[null,"Store in the refrigerator until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Select the lowest sodium mustard and mayonnaise brands."],[null,"Look for unseasoned rice vinegar and add sweetener, if desired. Seasoned rice vinegar is very high in sodium and sugar."],[null,"Use regular mayonnaise if you need more calories in your diet. Calories are increased to 154, fat increased to 13 g and sodium is reduced to 143 mg."]]},"4724969":{"s":[[null,"Drain tofu, press a paper towel on it to remove liquid, and cut in cubes."],[null,"In a medium-sized bowl or sealable plastic bag, mix the ingredients for the marinade: olive oil, honey, mustard, turmeric, and cumin. Add the tofu and refrigerate for a minimum of 6 hours or overnight."],[null,"In a non-stick frying pan, heat 1 teaspoon of olive oil over medium heat. Take the tofu out of the marinade. Set the marinade aside. Fry the tofu for 2 minutes on each side."],[null,"Transfer the browned tofu to a plate, brush the remaining marinade on the tofu and keep warm."],[null,"Keeping the heat on, add the broccoli, peppers, water, and vinegar to the frying pan. Stir-fry the vegetables for three minutes or until the liquid has almost disappeared and the vegetables are cooked but still crunchy. Transfer to a plate and keep warm."],[null,"Prepare the noodles following the instructions on the package."],[null,"Toss the noodles and vegetable mixture and serve the tofu on the side or on top, enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Note: Marinades are the key to making tofu tasty. The longer you marinade the more flavor will be absorbed. You can marinade more than 6 hours without a problem but you can also marinade for just 15 minutes if in a rush. Unlike other marinades for meat, fish, or poultry that need to be discarded after use, there is no danger in using leftover marinade as a sauce when using tofu."],["Tofu — a great source of plant-based protein","For those with chronic kidney disease (CKD), it is important to follow a diet that is both kidney-friendly and heart-healthy. Eating more plant-based protein can help protect the kidneys while also promoting heart health. A lower-protein diet is typically recommended for earlier stage CKD to decrease the workload on the kidneys. Adding plant-based proteins, such as tofu, to your diet is a good way to lower protein intake. These foods can provide a satisfying amount of food at a much lower protein content than animal type proteins. Tofu is made from soybeans. At the market you will find several varieties sorted by firmness – silken, firm, extra-firm, and super-firm. Silken is the softest tofu with a custard like thickness. It can be used to make sauces and as an egg substitute. Firm tofu is pressed into a block and has the same consistency as feta cheese. It can be cubed and added to a stir-fry, rice bowl, soup, salad, or threaded on skewers with vegetables to make a kebab. Tofu has the ability to absorb the flavor of whatever it is prepared with, so it is very easy to use as a meat substitute in your current recipes. A four-ounce portion of firm tofu (approximately ¼ block) contains only 166 milligrams of potassium and thus can be used as a good source of protein on a lower-potassium diet. Ask your registered dietitian nutritionist how much plant-based protein is right for you."]]},"2837":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, combine mayonnaise, mustard, honey, vinegar and green onions to make a sauce. Reserve 1/4 cup to serve with cooked chicken."],[null,"Grill 1 pound boneless, skinless chicken breasts over medium heat. Brush with honey mustard sauce and turn several times until chicken is cooked through."],[null,"Remove from grill and serve with reserved honey mustard sauce."]],"h":[[null,"This recipe may also be prepared on the stove in a skillet over medium heat."]]},"3341":{"s":[[null,"Place honey, grated lemon peel, ground pepper, garlic powder and hot water in a small bowl and whisk until blended. With gloved hands, rub mixture over salmon fillets."],[null,"Heat olive oil in a skillet over medium heat. Add spice-rubbed salmon fillets and cook 4 minutes. Carefully turn fillets with a spatula."],[null,"Reduce heat to medium-low and cook an additional 4 to 6 minutes, until fish turns opaque throughout and flakes easily when tested with a fork."],[null,"Arrange 1/2-cup arugula on each plate. Place salmon fillet on top of arugula and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Purchase 4 salmon fillets, 4 ounces each."],[null,"Serve with Cucumber Dill Salsa."],[null,"Cook the salmon fillets on an outdoor grill if desired."],[null,"For a low-protein diet, adjust portion according to your meal plan or consult with your dietitian."]]},"6309151":{"s":[[null,"Combine all of the marinade ingredients in a medium bowl and put into a large, tightly sealed plastic bag. Marinate chicken breasts at least 30 minutes, or overnight in the refrigerator for best results."],[null,"Preheat grill to medium high and place chicken on grill grate. Cook under direct heat (close the grill cover) for 8-10 minutes per side, or until an internal temperature of 165 degrees F is reached."]],"h":[]},"6519498":{"s":[[null,"In a blender, puree yogurt and raspberries."],[null,"Once blended, drizzle the honey and vanilla into the mix. Blend thoroughly."],[null,"Pour the mixture into popsicle molds. Freeze for 8 hours or overnight."]],"h":[]},"4737568":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 325°F (conventional oven)."],[null,"Cream together wet ingredients in one bowl."],[null,"Prepare dry ingredients by sifting flour with soda and spices in a second bowl."],[null,"Blend dry ingredients into wet and mix thoroughly yet quickly."],[null,"Drop in heaping tablespoons into granulated sugar, roll into balls and place on greased cookie sheet or on parchment paper, 2 inches apart."],[null,"Bake 8–10 minutes in the middle of the oven, remove and cool on tray before transferring to rack."]],"h":[[null,"These cookies are very low in phosphorus and potassium: non-diabetic patients can have two."]]},"2060":{"s":[[null,"Place ingredients in a jar. Top with the lid and shake until well mixed."],[null,"Drizzle dressing over salad. Refrigerate leftover dressing for up to one week."]],"h":[[null,"Ginger paste is packaged in a tube and available in the produce section of some grocery stores. If unavailable, use minced fresh ginger root."]]},"3758":{"s":[[null,"Combine Golden Grahams, Rice Chex, Teddy Grahams and pretzels in a large bowl."],[null,"Melt butter in a small saucepan; add brown sugar, honey and maple syrup. Cook over low heat until sugar is melted."],[null,"Pour over cereal mixture and mix well until all pieces are coated."],[null,"Preheat oven to 325° F."],[null,"Prepare 3 jelly roll pans by lining with aluminum foil and spraying the foil with cooking spray. (Can be done in 3 batches). Spread cereal mixture evenly over pans. Bake at 325° F for 20 minutes; stirring once halfway though."],[null,"Mix cranberries and apple chips; divide evenly among pans and stir."],[null,"Bake 5 more minutes; cool completely and store in an airtight container."]],"h":[[null,"For an extra twist sprinkle trail mix with Mrs. Dash® Caribbean Citrus or Fiesta Lime seasoning blend."],[null,"If you have diabetes, reduce portion size to 1/2 cup for a lower carbohydrate snack."],[null,"Look in the produce section for apple chips if you do not find it in the snack section."],[null,"Share extra servings with family and friends or cut recipe in half to make less."]]},"7464478":{"s":[[null,"Cut each of the parsnips and carrots in half lengthways and then into quarters. Cook in boiling water for 5 minutes. Drain, rinse with cold water and leave to cool."],[null,"Mix together the honey, oil, tamari and herbs in a bowl. Add the parsnips and carrots. Leave to marinate in the fridge for at least 30 minutes."],[null,"Preheat oven to 200°C/fan 180°C/gas 6. Line a baking tray with greaseproof paper."],[null,"Tip the parsnips and carrots, with their marinade, on to the prepared tray and roast for 20–25 minutes until golden. Transfer the roasted vegetables to a platter. Sprinkle with the pistachios and lemon juice."]],"h":[[null,"Turnip or sweet potatoes would make a perfect substitute for the parsnips or carrots in this recipe."],[null,"Extract from Detox Kitchen Vegetables by Lily Simpson. Photographs © Issy Croker"]]},"1691":{"s":[[null,"Add water, rice and cinnamon sticks to the water, cover and soak 8 hours or overnight."],[null,"Pour water, rice and cinnamon mixture into a blender and blend until smooth."],[null,"Use a fine strainer to strain the rice mixture at least 4 times. The goal is to strain out all the solids."],[null,"After straining out the solids, add the almond milk and sugar and stir to mix. May pour over ice to serve or just into glasses. May sprinkle with ground cinnamon if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Horchata can be stored in the refrigerator for up to 5 days."],[null,"You may use a 1/2 cup of sugar if desired, but it will increase the carbohydrate."]]},"2980":{"s":[[null,"Pierce the flank steak with a fork so that the steak can soak up the flavors of the marinade. Lightly pepper both sides."],[null,"Crush and mince the garlic. Whisk the oil, garlic, horseradish and mustard together in a covered container or disposable bag. Coat the steak and massage in marinade. Let stand in the refrigerator for at least 2-4 hours or for best results overnight."],[null,"Grill steak for around 5 minutes per side to desired doneness and when internal temperature has reached 165 degrees. Remove the steak from the grill to a clean cutting board and allow to rest for 5-10 minutes before serving. Alternatively you may use a grill pan or skillet on the stove top."]],"h":[[null,"Look for steak that is pre-cut and thin. If it is not thin you may cover with plastic wrap and pound flat. This helps the steak cook quicker and more evenly."],[null,"Look for horseradish and coarse mustard with the lowest amount of sodium per serving."]]},"1928":{"s":[[null,"Combine all ingredients in a Crock-Pot®."],[null,"Let steep for an hour or longer. Remove tea bag."],[null,"Serve hot cider in a small mug."]],"h":[[null,"Add 1/4 cup brownsugar for a sweeter beverage."]]},"2935":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375º F. Set cream cheese out to soften. Finely mince the onion."],[null,"Place softened cream cheese in a bowl."],[null,"Add the onion, lemon juice, Worcestershire sauce, black pepper and cayenne pepper. Mix well. Stir in milk."],[null,"Add the crab meat and stir until blended."],[null,"Place mixture into an oven-safe dish. Bake uncovered for 15 minutes or until hot and bubbly."]],"h":[[null,"Serve warm with low-sodium crackers."],[null,"Try this recipe with fresh steamed crab meat instead of canned crab."],[null,"Decrease fat to 4 grams per serving by using reduced-fat cream cheese. Be aware, the sodium content is higher."]]},"5207914":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 190°C / 170°C Fan / Gas Mark 5."],[null,"In a large mixing bowl, add the flour, brown sugar, cinnamon, mixed spice, 30g of butter and yeast. Rub with your fingertips until a sandy texture is formed."],[null,"Mix the orange zest and cranberries into the flour mixture."],[null,"Warm the Renastep and remaining butter in a small saucepan (do not boil)"],[null,"Pour the Renastep into the flour mixture, add the eggs and combine until the mixture forms a soft, sticky dough."],[null,"Tip the dough out onto a lightly floured work surface and knead well for 5 minutes, or until the dough is smooth and elastic. Alternatively, this can be done in a freestanding mixer using a dough hook."],[null,"Place the dough in an bowl, cover with a damp tea towel and leave to rise for about 1 hour. This is best done in a warm room."],[null,"Divide the dough into 3 equal amounts and roll with your hands into a bun type shape."],[null,"Cover loosely with a clean tea towel and let the dough rise for 15 minutes."],[null,"Once the buns have risen, put them in the oven and bake for 20-25 minutes or until golden-brown."],[null,"Remove the buns from the oven and let them cool slightly before transferring them to a cooling rack."],[null,"Meanwhile, warm the apricot jam for a few seconds in the microwave and then, using a pastry brush, brush the top of the hot cross buns with the warm jam."],[null,"Mix the icing sugar and water, then transfer to a disposable piping bag and snip off a tiny snip at the end. Pipe a cross shape on top of the bun."]],"h":[["Renastep note","Renastep is a Food for Special Medical Purposes and must be used under medical supervision."],["Renastep note","Renastep is a ready to use feed for the dietary management of kidney disease from 3 years of age onwards. Renastep contains milk and fish. This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutrimen dietary analysis software."],["Renastep note","Refer to labels for allergen and other product information."]]},"3169":{"s":[[null,"Pour cider into a Crock-Pot® and add cinnamon, cloves and allspice."],[null,"Heat and let steep for one hour to blend the flavors."]],"h":[[null,"This tasty beverage also brings a wonderful holiday fragrance to your house."]]},"3128":{"s":[[null,"Combine ingredients in a large pot or crock pot."],[null,"Heat to a simmer and serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"Hot Mulled Punch can be simmered in a crock pot until ready to serve. It’s a great way to fill the house with fall fragrance."],[null,"For a lower carbohydrate version, diabetics can substitute low-calorie cranberry juice cocktail and Splenda® brown sugar blend. Carbohydrate = 24 grams per serving, 1-1/2 carbohydrate choices."]]},"7733869":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 190ºC/gas 5. Slice off the bottom end of the apples, then cut around the top edge of each and scoop out the flesh, leaving about a ½cm border. Brush the cut edges with the lemon juice."],[null,"Roughly chop the apple flesh and place in a pan with 1 tbsp water. Cover and simmer for 5-6 minutes or until soft, then push through a sieve."],[null,"Beat the butter, nutmeg, sugar and egg yolk through the apple. Meanwhile, whisk the egg white until it forms stiff peaks. Carefully fold through the apple mixture."],[null,"Spoon the soufflé mixture into the apples, place on a baking tray and bake for 20-25 minutes until golden and risen. Serve with crème fraiche and a sprinkling of extra nutmeg."]],"h":[[null,"You could use ground cinnamon or ginger in place of nutmeg."]]},"3174":{"s":[[null,"Mix all ingredients in a large Crock-Pot® and place on low heat until warm."],[null,"Serve and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Make this cider before holiday guests arrive to fill your home with a delicious aroma."]]},"9117377":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees and line a large baking tray with parchment paper. Arrange the almonds in a single layer and bake for 8-10 minutes. They're ready when they are golden brown, but NOT burned. Remove from the oven."],[null,"Add the almonds and salt (if using) to a food processor. Process on high speed until creamy, stopping to scrape down the sides often. The almonds will turn from whole, to flour, to clumps, to a large ball, and eventually, creamy, luscious butter. It will take several minutes of processing, anywhere between 3-10 minutes. Give your machine 30-60 second breaks, as needed, to prevent overheating."],[null,"Transfer to a clean and dry container or jar and use as you would any other nut butter."]],"h":[[null,"Give your machine small breaks in between processing to prevent overheating. Turn off your food processor for 30-60 seconds at a time, as needed, and then continue. Use that break to scrape down the sides . Your homemade almond butter will go through many stages , and it may feel like it’s never going to become butter, but it will. It goes from whole almonds, to broken down pieces, to flour, to small clumps, then large clumps, then one giant ball, and finally creamy nut butter. (See process shots above for a visual.) Store in a clean and dry container or jar at room temperature for up to 1 week, or refrigerate for up to 4 weeks. You may freeze air tight in a freezer safe container for up to 4 months."]]},"9689734":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees and line a large baking tray with parchment paper. Arrange the cashews in a single layer and bake for 5-6 minutes. They're ready when they are golden and warm, but NOT burned. Remove from the oven."],[null,"Add the cashews to a food processor. Process on high speed until creamy, stopping to scrape down the sides often. The cashews will turn from whole, to flour, to clumps, and eventually, creamy, nut butter. It will take several minutes of processing, anywhere between 5-12 minutes with breaks. Give your machine 30-60 second breaks, as needed, to prevent overheating."],[null,"OPTIONAL: Once completely smooth, add any optional fill ins, if using and pulse a couple of times to combine."],[null,"Transfer your cashew butter to a clean and dry jar and use as you would any other nut butter."]],"h":[[null,"Give your machine small breaks in between processing to prevent overheating. Turn off your food processor for 30-60 seconds at a time, as needed, and then continue. Use that break to scrape down the sides . Your homemade cashew butter will go through many stages , and it may feel like it’s never going to become butter, but it will. It goes from whole cashews, to broken down pieces, to flour, to small clumps, then large clumps and finally creamy nut butter. (See process shots above for a visual.) For sugar free , skip the optional maple syrup, or if you have a sweet tooth, increase to two tablespoons. (Try it with one first) You may use a high speed blender , such as a Vitamix for faster results, but I find it easier to remove the nut butter from a food processor. Store in a clean and dry container or jar at room temperature for up to 1 week, or refrigerate for up to 4 weeks. You may freeze air tight in a freezer safe container for up to 4 months."]]},"6551703":{"s":[[null,"To make the apple cider vinaigrette: Pour the apple cider vinegar into a bowl or a small jar with a lid. Add ¼ teaspoon of salt and shake or whisk to combine."],[null,"Add the Dijon mustard and olive oil and shake vigorously or whisk it well to combine."],[null,"Add the freshly chopped mint right before dressing the salad (otherwise it will turn brown)."],[null,"To make the salad: In a large bowl, toss together the greens, radishes, sugar snap peas, half of the pepitas, and half of the pomegranate seeds."],[null,"Add a few tablespoons of the dressing and toss. You want the greens to be just barely coated with the dressing."],[null,"Taste and season with freshly ground black pepper as needed. Garnish with the remaining pepitas and pomegranate seeds before serving."]],"h":[]},"9040812":{"s":[[null,"Using a food processor, process your onions and garlic until finely chopped, but not pureed. Set aside."],[null,"Slice each tomato in half, looking for any bad spots as you cut into them. (You do not want to use any rotten tomatoes, as this may ruin the batch of sauce.)"],[null,"Bring a large pot of water to a boil and add the cut tomatoes. The cold tomatoes will likely cause the water to stop boiling. Once it returns to a low boil, drain the tomatoes immediately. Do NOT overcook the tomatoes in this step. Drain them once the water starts boiling, and/or once you see that the water is foaming orange on top. (See pic for reference.)"],[null,"Use a food mill to crush your tomatoes which will separate the skins and seeds and leave you with only the tomato sauce."],[null,"Heat the oil with the onions, garlic and bay leaves and cook for about 5 minutes, until onions and garlic are slightly golden. Watch carefully not to burn. Add the sauce and salt to the pot and bring to a low boil. Cook for 1 hour, adding the basil in the last 20 minutes or so. Stir often! You do not want any sauce to burn at the bottom of the pot, or you may spoil the entire batch. Taste for salt, and adjust if desired."],[null,"Now depending on the size of jars you're using, add the citric acid to the bottom of each jar. *see notes"],[null,"Carefully fill your jars leaving 1/4\" space from rim of the jar. Then tightly seal your mason jars using Bernardin lids and rings."],[null,"Heat a couple inches of water in a large pot and place the sealed jars into your pot once heated. Do not add the jars to cold water! The jars are very hot, and adding them to a pot of cold water may cause them to crack. Once the jars have all been placed in the pot, slowly fill with enough water to cover all the jars and bring to a boil for at least 30 minutes, then turn off the heat and let them sit for 12 hours or overnight. (So call it a day.) Once the water and jars are cooled enough to handle, remove from the pot and store in a cold dark place for up to 12 months."]],"h":[[null,"*For the citric acid, add ½ teaspoon to quart (32oz) size jars or a ¼ teaspoon to pint (16oz) jars before filling with the tomato sauce. Although there are methods to use bottled lemon juice or vinegar instead of citric acid, I find these will affect the taste of your sauce. So our preferred choice is citric acid for preserving your tomato sauce. If you prefer to use lemon juice , make sure to use the already bottled kind to ensure the correct level of acidity and PH which can vary among fresh lemons and use 1 tablespoon for pint jars or 2 tablespoons for quart jars. If you prefer vinegar , use 5% or higher acidity, and add ¼ cup to quart jars or 2 tablespoons to pint jars. If you’re avoiding oil, you may sauté the veggies in water instead. Just watch carefully to ensure nothing gets stuck to the bottom of the pot. You do not want anything to burn, or you risk spoiling the batch."]]},"9572814":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees and line a large tray with parchment paper. Arrange the pecans in a single layer and bake for 5 minutes. Then remove from the oven."],[null,"Transfer the toasted pecans to your food processor and begin processing. Stop to scrape down the sides, as needed and give your machine a 30-60 second break to prevent overheating. The pecans will go from whole, to crumbly, to flour, to clumps and eventually creamy pecan butter. Depending on your appliance, this will take anywhere from 2-6 minutes."],[null,"Once smooth, add any or all of the optional fill ins (if using) and pulse until combined."],[null,"Store in a clean and dry glass jar or container, and use as desired."]],"h":[[null,"Give your machine small breaks in between processing to prevent overheating. Turn off your food processor for 30-60 seconds at a time, as needed, and then continue. Use that break to scrape down the sides . For sugar free , skip the optional coconut sugar, or if you have a sweet tooth, you may increase to two tablespoons, instead. (Try it with one first) Your homemade nut butter will go through many stages . It goes from whole pecans, to broken down pieces, to flour, to small clumps, then larger clumps, and finally creamy nut butter. (See process shots above for a visual.) You may use a high speed blender , such as a Vitamix for faster results, but I find it easier to remove the butter from a food processor. Keep at room temperature for up to 1 week, or store in the refrigerator for up to 4 weeks. You may also freeze, air tight in a freezer safe container for up to 3 months."]]},"9984117":{"s":[[null,"Wash your strawberries well and remove the stems."],[null,"Juice the strawberries and lemon, give it a quick stir and enjoy right away."]],"h":[[null,"Make the amount of juice you plan to consume , not extra. Freshly made juice without preservatives will not keep very long, and for optimum health benefits, should be enjoyed straight away."],[null,"To speed up juicing prep time , you may wash and dry your produce the night before and refrigerate it in a sealed container. Then in the morning, your fruit is ready to pass through your juicer."]]},"9344136":{"s":[[null,"Add everything to your blender and process, starting on low speed and increasing to high speed until smooth."],[null,"Pour the liquid into a small sauce pot or pan and cook over medium heat, stirring constantly. You will see the mixture go from liquid, to lumpy, to eventually a big ball of cheese. This process will take about 3-4 minutes. Make sure to keep stirring so it doesn't burn."],[null,"Serve hot with crackers, chips or veggies for dunking. Or scoop onto pizza, or into a grilled cheese."]],"h":[[null,"If you do not have a powerful blender , presoak your cashews. Soak them either overnight in cool water or for at least 30 minutes in boiling hot water. Soaking will help them soften and expand , making them easier to blend. If you have a Vitamix , NO need to soak first. Do NOT substitute the tapioca starch (or tapioca flour) for another ingredient. The tapioca is essential to getting stretchy mozzarella. Use a smaller blender if possible, to assist in a smoother consistency. This gives the cashew bits less space to float around in. Or, after blending your ingredients , strain through a nut milk bag for a perfectly smooth cheese. I like the bigger better nut bag that I use to make my homemade cashew milk . One last tip, if you don’t have a high speed blender. It helps to add only half of the water to begin blending your ingredients into a paste first. Once blended, add the remaining water and blend to stir it in. This helps prevent loose cashew bits in your cheese. Store leftovers in an air tight container in the fridge for up to 5 days, and reheat to return to dipping consistency. Or use the cheese cold and slice or scoop onto desired dishes. You may also freeze the fully cooked cheese in a freezer safe, air tight container . OR, you may freeze the liquid (before cooking) in an ice cube tray for individual portions to heat and use as needed. Recipe adapted from It Doesn’t Taste Like Chicken"]]},"9401943":{"s":[[null,"Add all the ingredients to a food processor and process until a fine meal is achieved."],[null,"Store in an airtight container or jar in your refrigerator and serve sprinkled over your favourite dishes."]],"h":[[null,"Make sure your jar or container is completely clean and DRY to prevent any spoilage from moisture when storing you vegan parm. Store in your refrigerator to preserve freshness. Do not use fresh herbs or spices . This will prevent your “cheese” from keeping fresh, and will spoil sooner. If you don’t have cashews , I’ve successfully made this with blanched almonds and pine nuts with similar results. For nut free , you may use raw sunflower seeds or pumpkin seeds/pepitas to replace the cashews with similar results. For no nutritional yeast , you may use a mix of mushroom powder, onion powder, basil powder and more garlic powder. Keep in mind this will reduce the cheesiness, but still provide umami deliciousness. For low sodium , simply halve the salt, or salt to your taste. I’ve keep mine refrigerated for up to 4 weeks, but I’m sure it would last even longer than that."]]},"9221793":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 325°F/163°C. Then arrange the walnuts on a baking sheet and bake for 6-8 minutes. You only want to heat them up until slightly fragrant so be careful not to burn them, or your walnut butter will be bitter."],[null,"Remove from the oven and transfer the toasted walnuts to the bowl of your food processor. The walnuts will go through a few stages, from crumbled pieces, then flour, then it will start to lump together, and eventually, you'll have creamy, smooth walnut butter. Make sure to pause and scrape down the sides, as needed, and give your appliance small breaks in between processing so it doesn't overheat. The entire process (with breaks) will take about 3-5 minutes, depending on your processor strength."]],"h":[[null,"Give your machine small breaks in between processing to prevent overheating. Turn off your food processor for 30-40 seconds at a time, as needed, and then continue. Use that break to scrape down the sides . Your homemade walnut butter will go through many stages , and it may feel like it’s never going to become butter, but it will. It goes from whole walnuts, to broken down pieces, to flour, to small clumps, then larger clumps, and finally creamy nut butter. (See process shots above for a visual.) For sugar free , skip the optional coconut sugar, or if you have a sweet tooth, increase to two tablespoons. (Try it with one first) You may use a high speed blender , such as a Vitamix for faster results, but I find it easier to scrape the nut butter out of a food processor bowl."]]},"2568":{"s":[[null,"Chop the onion and bell pepper."],[null,"Heat 2 tablespoons oil in a skillet and crisp the tortillas for about a minute on each side or until they start to brown. Set aside on paper towels to drain."],[null,"In the same skillet, sauté the onion and bell pepper until soft. (Add additional oil if needed.) Remove from skillet."],[null,"Heat remaining oil in the skillet and cook eggs over easy."],[null,"Place one crisp tortilla on each plate and top with egg and sautéed vegetables."],[null,"Serve with red chile sauce."]],"h":[[null,"Crisp tortillas are available at the grocery store."],[null,"To reduce fat in this recipe, crisp the tortillas in the oven and use a nonstick skillet sprayed with cooking spray to prepare eggs."],[null,"Make the Chile Colorado Sauce (Basic Red Chili Sauce) recipe on DaVita.com to serve with this recipe."]]},"6606672":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 425 degrees F."],[null,"Place the tortillas on the baking sheet and bake 3 minutes on each side."],[null,"Meanwhile, place the tomatoes, cumin, cayenne, and salt in a medium non-stick skillet and bring to a boil over medium-high heat. Reduce the heat to medium-low and cook, covered, for 3 minutes or until slightly thickened. Break one egg into a measuring cup. Carefully slide egg onto the tomato mixture. Repeat with the remaining eggs. Simmer gently over medium heat, covered, for 2 1/2 to 3 minutes or until the egg whites are completely set and the yolks just begin to thicken slightly."],[null,"Place a tortilla on each plate. Top with the tomato mixture and eggs and sprinkle with cheese and cilantro."]],"h":[]},"2554":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375° F."],[null,"Grate onion and dice bell peppers."],[null,"Combine ground beef, eggs, 1 tablespoon cornstarch, onion, black pepper, nutmeg and garlic powder. Mix well."],[null,"Form into 1” balls and place on a baking sheet."],[null,"Bake for 10 to 15 minutes, until meatballs are cooked through."],[null,"Drain juice from pineapple cans into a measuring cup. Add water to make 2 cups. Reserve pineapple chunks."],[null,"Combine remaining 6 tablespoons cornstarch, reduced sodium soy sauce, vinegar, water, unpacked brown sugar, white sugar and pineapple juice. Heat until thickened, stirring constantly. Remove from heat."],[null,"Place meatballs, sauce, pineapple chunks, green and red peppers in a covered warming dish or crock pot set on low setting until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Reduced sodium soy sauce contains 500 to 600 mg sodium per tablespoon compared to 950 to 1050 mg sodium in regular soy sauce. Limit to the amount specified in the recipe."],[null,"Make meatballs ahead and refrigerate. When ready to serve, heat ingredients together and transfer to a warming dish."]]},"6800112":{"s":[[null,"Fill each celery rib with 1 tablespoon of hummus, then cut each rib into 3 equal pieces. Place 2 pieces of red bell pepper on each piece of celery."]],"h":[]},"2044":{"s":[[null,"Trim the celery rib ends. Cut the red bell pepper into 1/4-inch square pieces."],[null,"Fill each celery rib with 1 tablespoon of hummus."],[null,"Cut each celery rib into 3 pieces"],[null,"Place 2 pieces of red bell pepper on each piece of hummus-filled celery."]],"h":[[null,"Mix it up with different flavored hummus blends."],[null,"Place hummus in a plastic bag, snip the corner and pipe onto the celery log."],[null,"Instead of roasted red peppers you can substitute a small jar of diced pimentos if preferred."]]},"6352737":{"s":[[null,"Slice hardboiled eggs in half lengthwise and discard the yolk."],[null,"Add garbanzo beans, garlic, lemon zest, lemon juice, olive oil, broth, salt, pepper, salsa and parsley to a blender or food processor. Process until hummus is smooth."],[null,"Fill each egg half with a heaping tablespoon of hummus."]],"h":[]},"2561":{"s":[[null,"Remove pits from cherries."],[null,"Add water to a medium sauce pan together with cherries, sugar and salt. Bring to a boil then simmer at a very low heat for 10 minutes."],[null,"Remove 2 tablespoons of liquid and set aside for garnish."],[null,"Remove another 1/4 cup of the liquid and allow to cool slightly."],[null,"Whisk together with the flour and sour cream then return to the sauce pan."],[null,"Simmer for another 5 minutes over low heat."],[null,"Remove from heat and allow to cool."],[null,"Serve in a soup bowl. Swirl in the reserved cherry juice as a garnish."]],"h":[[null,"Alter the sugar or Splenda to your taste."],[null,"If Splenda or other sugar replacement is substituted for sugar the carbohydrate is 16 grams per serving which equals one Carbohydrate Choice."],[null,"Look for canned cherries in juice or light syrup to make this an even easier recipe."],[null,"This is an excellent light lunch for those who have no taste for meat, fish, poultry, etc. To increase the protein content add protein powder as advised by your renal dietitian. Two scoops of ProSource® or ProCel® protein powder are excellent additions."]]},"5828545":{"s":[[null,"Place the aubergines under a hot grill and allow to char on all sides, remove from the grill and allow to cool."],[null,"Once cooled peel the aubergines charred skin and set aside."],[null,"Heat oil and flour in a pan and stir to form a paste."],[null,"Add the roasted aubergines to the pan, once heated mash the aubergines to form a smooth paste."],[null,"Reduce the heat and gradually add in the Renastep, black pepper and nutmeg to the mixture and stir well until combined."],[null,"Allow to cook for a further 2 minutes and then set aside."],[null,"In a separate pan, heat oil in a pan and add in the turkey chunks. Allow to cook until browned."],[null,"Add the onions and peppers to the meat and cook until softened."],[null,"Add in the grated tomato mixture and the additional water, allow to cook until the sauce has reduced and the meat is fully cooked."],[null,"Serve on top of the roasted aubergine puree and serve."]],"h":[["Renastep note","Always check with your dietitian or doctor that this recipe is suitable for you."]]},"9801698":{"s":[[null,"First, make the vegan mozzarella cheese, transfer to a container or bowl and refrigerate to let cool."],[null,"Preheat your oven to 425 degrees F convection bake and line a large baking tray with parchment paper."],[null,"Peel or scrub your potatoes and slice into fries using a french fry cutter or a sharp knife."],[null,"Toss the french fries with the oil, salt, rosemary and cornstarch until evenly coated. Then spread into a single layer on your prepared tray. Bake for 20-25 minutes, then flip your fries and bake an additional 15-20 minutes, or until desired crispiness level is reached."],[null,"While the fries are baking, make the gravy. Add the sliced mushrooms and tamari to a small pot and cook over medium heat until the mushrooms are reduced, approx. 5 minutes. Add the broth and bring to a boil, cooking for 1-2 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, mix the tablespoon of flour with a tablespoon of water in a separate small bowl to make your slurry. (This will thicken your gravy.) Then pour the slurry into the pot and whisk well to combine. Cook for 1 more minute and remove from the heat. The gravy will further thicken as it begins to cool."],[null,"Assemble your poutine by layering the fries first, and then scoop the vegan cheese using a melon baller (or teaspoon) to add the \"cheese curds\" on top. (As you scoop the curds listen for the SQUEAK! :)) Finally, pour the gravy on top and sprinkle with green onion, if desired. ENJOY!!!"]],"h":[[null,"Make sure to arrange your fries in a single layer with plenty of space in between for the crispiest baked french fries and to prevent sticking. For a non convection oven , the fries may need a little more cooking time. Keep baking until desired crispiness level is reached. For a smooth gravy without mushroom pieces , you may blend it once cooked. If you don’t like mushrooms , you can follow the same technique using thinly sliced onions, or try this onion gravy instead. Don’t skip making a slurry! You may be tempted to add the flour directly to your hot gravy, but doing so will result in lumps. If working ahead , you may fully prepare the cheese and refrigerate for a couple of days, until needed."]]},"3509":{"s":[[null,"Pat chicken dry. Lightly salt, being careful of portion size. Sauté chicken in oil, in batches, 5-7 minutes per side. Remove chicken and set aside. Chicken does not need to be cooked through yet."],[null,"Chop onion, Poblano and jalapeno peppers. Sauté in the same pan used for the chicken, scraping browned bits from pan. Cook until soft. Chop or mince the garlic, add to pan along with green chilis. Cook 1-2 minutes. Add frozen corn and garbanzo beans. Season with cumin and pepper."],[null,"Chop or shred chicken and return to pot. Cook for 3-5 minutes, stirring every few minutes."],[null,"Add broth and bring to boil. Add cornmeal and lower heat to simmer. Simmer for one hour. Remove from heat. After 10 minutes, add cream cheese."],[null,"Garnish with optional toppings: unsalted tortilla chips, small dollop of sour cream, lime, cabbage, radish, hot sauce, or other kidney-friendly toppings of your choice! The toppings are not included in the nutrient analysis."]],"h":[[null,"Marie Sharp’s Jabanero Hot Sauce® comes recommended by recipe’s author for a flavor profile and low-sodium content."],[null,"O Organics Garbanzo Beans® are an excellent low-sodium choice, also recommended by recipe’s author."],[null,"May also use up to 2 pounds of chicken, this would change the nutrient content of the recipe."],[null,"When looking for unsalted chicken broth, be sure to also look for one with a lower potassium content as well. Less than 100mg for sodium and potassium if possible."]]},"4363518":{"s":[[null,"Combine all ingredients in a blender and mix. Serve immediately. 2017-04-13 8:53 AM"]],"h":[[null,"* Ask your physician, dietitian or pharmacist about kidney-friendly oral nutritional supplements."],["Role of oral nutritional supplements (ONS)","With a diagnosis of chronic kidney disease (CKD), normal kidney function is impaired. Not only does this change how your kidneys filter certain nutrients, but this also influences the amount of calories and protein your body needs, putting you at a greater risk for malnutrition. Adequate snacks and meals, as well as a kidney-friendly ONS, are the first steps in improving your nutrition status with CKD. ONS are packed with nutrition. Certain drinks were created to meet the needs of kidney patients and are limited in sodium, potassium and phosphorus. ONS as snack or meal replacement If you are not eating enough calories and protein to meet your nutritional goals, your dietitian or doctor may recommend ONS as a snack or meal replacement. If your goal is healthy weight loss, it may replace an unhealthy meal. If your appetite is poor or you don’t regularly consume 3 meals per day, a kidney-friendly ONS can replace the missed meal. ONS in other recipes Add variety to your meals and snacks by including ONS as part of protein bars, muffins, smoothies or main courses."]]},"7568376":{"s":[[null,"Pour the boiling water over the teabags and leave to infuse, removing them when the tea is slightly stronger than you would normally think."],[null,"Remove the teabags or strain, then stir in the sweetener. Add a couple of slices of lemon then set aside to cool."],[null,"Meanwhile, add slices of lemon and a sprig of mint to glasses, along with some ice cubes."],[null,"Half fill a jug with ice cubes, add the rest of the lemon and a sprig of mint. Then, fill the jug with cooled tea and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Try using different tea such as green tea, mint, fruit tea or lapsang souchong."],[null,"Oranges or limes work as an alternative to lemons."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"5178196":{"s":[["For the sambhar","Heat oil in a pressure cooker and add onions, sauté well."],["For the sambhar","Add in the radish, carrot, brinjal and bottle gourd. Stir fry for 2 minutes."],["For the sambhar","Add soaked red gram with water, mix well and add the tamarind pulp."],["For the sambhar","Boil for 10-15 minutes."],["For the sambhar","Heat oil in a pan and add mustard seeds, chilli flakes, and a few curry leaves. This process is known as tempering."],["For the sambhar","Pour oil mixture over the sambar, serve immediately."],["For the idli","Rinse rice and black gram separately, 2–3 times and then soak both in water for 6 hours."],["For the idli","Drain black gram and rice, grind to a smooth, fluffy batter with little water."],["For the idli","Mix both batters in a large bowl. The consistency should be thick but pourable."],["For the idli","Cover and keep the batter in a warm place for 8–12 hours (overnight). The batter should rise and look airy with tiny bubbles."],["For the idli","Grease idli moulds with oil. Pour batter into each mould (¾ full), steam for 10–12 minutes on medium heat."],["For the idli","Allow idlis to cool for 2–3 minutes, then gently remove with a spoon. Serve hot with sambar."]],"h":[]},"1781":{"s":[[null,"Peel and chop tomato. Mince onion, garlic and ginger root. Remove skin from chicken and discard."],[null,"Heat oil in a large, wide pot over a medium-high flame. When hot, put in the cumin seeds, cinnamon, bay leaves and peppercorns. Stir once."],[null,"Add the onions, garlic and ginger. Stir this mixture until the onion picks up brown specks."],[null,"Add the tomatoes, chicken, salt and cayenne pepper. Stir to mix and bring to a boil."],[null,"Cover pot tightly, turn heat to low and simmer for 25 minutes or until chicken is tender. Stir a few times during this cooking period."],[null,"Remove cover and turn up the heat to medium. Sprinkle in the garam masala and cook, stirring gently for about 5 minutes to reduce the liquid."]],"h":[[null,"The whole spices in this dish should be eaten for optimal flavor."],[null,"Decrease the cayenne pepper to 1/2 teaspoon for a less spicy dish."]]},"6894160":{"s":[[null,"Heat 2 teaspoons of the oil in a wok or heavy skillet over medium-high heat. Add the cumin, mustard seeds, and turmeric and stir fry for 1 minute until seeds begin to pop. Add the salmon and stir fry quickly but gently for about 3-4 minutes. Remove the salmon from the pan and set aside."],[null,"Add the remaining oil to the pan. Lower the heat to medium. Add the onion and stir fry for about 6-7 minutes until onions are soft. Add in the garlic, ginger, and chili pepper and stir fry for 1 minute. Add in the cherry tomatoes and stir fry for 1-2 minutes until cherry tomatoes just begin to soften. Add back the salmon and stir fry very gently for 1 minute."]],"h":[]},"6189913":{"s":[[null,"Puree the onion, garlic, jalapeno, and water in a blender or food processor to make a paste."],[null,"Add the oil to a wok or large sauté pan over high heat. Add the onion paste and curry powder to oil and sauté for 3-4 minutes, stirring constantly."],[null,"Add the sweet potatoes and carrots to the paste and sauté for 4-5 minutes, stirring constantly."],[null,"Add the red bell pepper, green beans, and scallions. Sauté for 2 minutes."],[null,"In a separate cup or bowl, whisk together the coconut milk beverage, vegetable broth, and cornstarch. Pour over the vegetables and bring to a boil. Reduce to a simmer. Simmer, covered, for 10 minutes."],[null,"Stir in the cilantro, paprika, salt (optional), and black pepper."]],"h":[]},"3520":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Finely chop onion. Crush soda crackers."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine ground sirloin, nondairy creamer, egg whites, crushed crackers, onion, salt and garlic powder."],[null,"Divide meat into 8 portions and shape into individual loaves."],[null,"Spray a baking dish with nonstick cooking spray and place loaves in the dish."],[null,"In a small bowl combine tomato sauce, brown sugar and mustard."],[null,"Spoon ketchup mixture over each loaf."],[null,"Bake for 45 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Freeze extra loaves and microwave later for a quick meal."]]},"6702627":{"s":[[null,"Place the chicken, bay leaves, and enough cold water to cover in a medium saucepan; bring to a simmer. Cover and simmer until the chicken is cooked through, about 15 minutes; drain. Discard the bay leaves. Transfer the chicken to a cutting board. Let cool, then shred with two forks. Set aside."],[null,"Meanwhile, puree the tomatoes, 1/4 cup cilantro, chipotle chilies, adobo sauce, vinegar, garlic, thyme, marjoram, and salt in a food processor or blender."],[null,"Heat the oil in a large nonstick skillet over medium-high heat. Add the onion and cook, stirring occasionally, until the onion is softened, about 8 minutes. Add the tomato mixture and the shredded chicken. Cook, over medium heat, stirring occasionally, until the flavors are blended and the chicken is heated through, about 10 minutes. Sprinkle with the remaining 2 tbsp cilantro."]],"h":[]},"6683291":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a large nonstick skillet over medium-high heat. Add the onion and garlic and cook until the onion is tender, about 6 minutes."],[null,"Add the beans, broth, chipotle chilies, cumin, salt, and pepper. Cook until beans are heated through, about 5 minutes."],[null,"Mash the bean mixture with a fork or potato masher until coarsely mashed."]],"h":[]},"6825784":{"s":[[null,"Bring the water to a boil in a medium saucepan. Add the quinoa and boil until the liquid has almost evaporated. Reduce the heat to medium low and cook, loosely covered, until the quinoa is tender, about 20 minutes. Remove from the heat and fluff with a fork."],[null,"Meanwhile, heat the oil in a large nonstick skillet over medium heat. Add the onion, bell pepper, and garlic and cook, stirring occasionally, until the vegetables are tender, about 8 minutes. Add the beans, broth, tomato sauce, salt, and pepper, and cook 5 minutes."],[null,"Stir in the quinoa and heat through."]],"h":[]},"6325149":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the broiler. Line a broiler pan with foil. Lightly spray the foil with nonstick spray. Place the poblanos on the pan and broil, 4 inches from the heat, turning occasionally, until the poblanos are tender and slightly charred in spots, about 8 minutes."],[null,"Place the poblanos in a zip-close plastic bag; squeeze out the air and seal the bag. Let stand 15 minutes. Leave the broiler on."],[null,"Heat the oil in a large nonstick skillet over medium-high heat. Add the mushrooms, carrots, scallions, garlic, and salt and cook, stirring occasionally, until the vegetables are tender, about 8 minutes. Remove from the heat. Stir in the basil until well mixed."],[null,"Meanwhile, peal the poblanos. Make one slit to create a pocket and remove the seeds. Stuff each pepper with one-quarter of the mushroom mixture and top with 1 Tbsp of cheese."],[null,"Broil the stuffed peppers, 4 inches from the heat, until the filling is hot and the cheese begins to melt, about 4 minutes."]],"h":[]},"6176359":{"s":[[null,"Press the Sauté button on the multicooker. When the pot is hot, add the almonds and cook for 4 minutes, stirring occasionally. Set aside to cool, then coarsely chop."],[null,"In a small bowl, add the chopped almonds, crushed candies, and salt. Set aside."],[null,"Place the water, juice, and cinnamon stick in the multicooker pot. Place the steamer basket in the pot and arrange the pears on top of it."],[null,"Seal the lid, close the valve, and press the Cancel button. Select Manual and cook for 2 minutes. (If you prefer a very tender pear, cook an additional minute.) Use a quick pressure release."],[null,"When the valve drops, carefully remove the lid. Remove the steamer basket and pears. Place the pears, cut side up, in four dessert bowls. Remove and discard the cinnamon stick."],[null,"Press the Cancel button, then press the Sauté button. Bring the liquid in the pot to a boil. Boil for 3 minutes, or until the liquid is reduced to ¼ cup. Stir in the butter, vanilla extract, and almond-candy mixture. Cook for 30 seconds, or until the toffee has melted, stirring constantly."],[null,"Working quickly, spoon about 4 tsp of the toffee sauce into the center of each pear half."]],"h":[]},"9188036":{"s":[[null,"Add the apple cider vinegar, cinnamon, nutmeg, vanilla and salt to your Instant Pot and whisk together."],[null,"Remove any stickers from your apples, wash them well and cut into quarters. Remove the core and discard. No need to peel the apples. Place them inside your Instant Pot, close the lid and set the valve in the sealing position."],[null,"Set the pot to high pressure for 5 minutes. (It will take about 10-15 minutes to build pressure.) Once the timer completes, allow the pot to naturally release for 20 minutes and then quick release any remaining steam and remove the lid once safe to do so."],[null,"Use an immersion blender (or carefully transfer, in batches to a stand blender) to puree your apples. Once completely smooth, taste for sweetness and add some maple syrup and/or molasses, if needed, to your taste."],["Choose ONE Method: Slow Cook OR Saute","SLOW COOK: Set to slow cook on HIGH. Select slow cook, adjust and then HIGH. Place a glass lid on top with a vent (the IP lid, or another lid that fits) and cook for 2-3 hours until desired thickness is reached, stirring occasionally."],["Choose ONE Method: Slow Cook OR Saute","SAUTE: Set to the sauté function on LOW. Select sauté, adjust, and then then LOW. Cook your apple butter for 30 minutes, using a splatter guard, and whisk often. Use EXTREME CAUTION as it will bubble and may cause burns."],["Storage","Turn off the pot and let cool slightly. Then transfer to clean and dry jars to can, freeze, or give away. (See above for canning directions.)"]],"h":[[null,"The level of sweetness will depend on the apples you’re using. Use sweet apples for naturally sweet apple butter, and to avoid adding sugar. I like Fuji apples for this. If using tart apples , or a mixture of varieties, you may want to add some sweetener once cooked. Taste and adjust to your level of desired sweetness AFTER cooking so you don’t add any more than needed. If you have a good quality blender , there’s no need to peel the apples. They will puree smoothly and add additional fiber and flavour. See above for images and how to tell when your apple butter is ready/thick enough. The recipe makes approx. 6 cups of apple butter and the nutritional information serving size represents 2 tablespoons worth."]]},"6971311":{"s":[[null,"Pierce the squash over the entire surface with the tip of a sharp knife. Place in the microwave and set on high for 2 minutes. Using 2 dish towels or pot holders, carefully remove the squash from the microwave (it will be hot). Cut the squash in half crosswise, not lengthwise. Scrape out the seeds and connecting strands with a spoon."],[null,"Place the water and a trivet in the Instant Pot. Place the 2 squash halves on the trivet. Seal the lid, close the valve, and set the Manual/Pressure Cook button to 7 minutes."],[null,"Use a quick pressure release. Meanwhile, combine the soy sauce, juice of 1 of the limes, sugar, ginger, and crushed pepper flakes in a small bowl. Whisk until well blended and set aside."],[null,"When the valve drops, carefully remove the lid. Remove the squash halves and place on a cutting board. Remove the trivet."],[null,"Press the Cancel button and set to Sauté. Then press the Adjust button to “More” or “High.” Add the edamame to the water, bring to a boil, and boil for 2 minutes. Drain well."],[null,"To create long spaghetti squash strands, run a fork around the outer edges of the squash to release the strands, rather than “raking through” the strands."],[null,"Place the squash in a large serving bowl or divide among 6 individual bowls. Top the squash evenly with the edamame, carrots, and green onion, spoon the soy sauce mixture evenly over all, and sprinkle with the nuts and cilantro. Do not stir. Cut the remaining lime into 6 wedges and serve with the squash to squeeze over all."]],"h":[]},"9730903":{"s":[["Instant Pot Directions","Add all the ingredients to your Instant Pot and stir to combine. Then close the lid and set the valve to the sealing position. Set to high pressure and pressure cook for 3 minutes. (It will take about 20 minutes to build pressure before counting down.) Then quick-release the valve once the timer is complete, and remove the lid when safe to do so."],["Instant Pot Directions","Taste the soup for salt and pepper and add some if needed. Then transfer 2 cups of the cooked soup to a blender and process until smooth. Stir it back into the pot. (Or use an immersion blender to pure SOME of the soup to thicken it.)"],["Instant Pot Directions","Serve with toppings of your choice."],["Stove Top Directions","Add all the ingredients to a large pot, plus additional broth or water if needed to just barely cover the vegetables. Simmer over medium/low heat for 25-30 minutes, or until the carrots and celery are tender."],["Stove Top Directions","Taste the soup for salt and pepper and add some if needed. Then transfer 2 cups of the cooked soup to a blender and process until smooth. Return it to the pot and mix well. (Or use an immersion blender to pure SOME of the soup to thicken it.)"],["Stove Top Directions","Serve with toppings of your choice."]],"h":[[null,"Use canned beans unless you plan to precook beans from dry. Dried beans will not cook enough in the short cooking time called for in this quick recipe."],[null,"To use dried beans: Don’t increase the cooking time or the veggies will overcook. Instead, precook your beans on the stovetop OR pressure cook the beans separately first."],[null,"Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-4 days or freeze for up to 3 months."]]},"9779919":{"s":[[null,"Sort through your dried black beans, discarding any small rocks or debris. Then give them a good rinse and place them in your Instant Pot. Add 6 cups of water (or use broth for added flavour) to the pot and close the lid, ensuring the valve is in the sealing position."],[null,"Pressure cook on high for 30-35 minutes (see notes). It will take about 15 minutes to reach pressure and begin counting down. Once the timer is complete, naturally release for 10 minutes (not more) and then quick release the remaining steam."],[null,"Open the lid and drain immediately to prevent the beans from overcooking. Enjoy right away or store for future dishes."]],"h":[[null,"Use fresh beans that have not been sitting in your pantry for months for the best results. When beans get old, they take much longer to cook and do not get very tender. I like my beans tender but not mushy, especially for use in salads or wraps so I find a 30 minute pressure time to result in the best Instant Pot black beans. If using for soup and you prefer your beans softer, increase the pressure time to 35 minutes. Storage Allow your beans to cool slightly before storing, but don’t leave them at room temperature for more than 2 hours or bacteria can start to grow. HINT : Place them in shallow bowls to cool faster, and then refrigerate or freeze. Refrigerate for 3-4 days in zip-top bags or sealed containers. To freeze , pat your beans dry with a clean dishtowel. Then measure approx. 1.5 cups of cooked beans and store in zip-top bags or freezer-safe, air-tight containers. This is equivalent to about a 15 ounce can of beans, which makes for convenient portions for future meals. Make sure to push out the extra air from your zip-top bags , before freezing so they keep longer, and the bags will be less likely to break. Keep frozen for up to 3 months."]]},"9413497":{"s":[[null,"Add everything except the butter into your pressure cooker and give it a stir. Close the lid and make sure your valve is in the sealing position. Then set to high pressure for 22 minutes. It will take about 15-20 minutes for the pot to reach pressure."],[null,"When the timer is complete, allow your pressure cooker to naturally release for 10 minutes. After 10 minutes, quick release the remaining pressure by setting the valve to the venting position, and open the lid once safe to do so."],[null,"Stir in the butter if using it and taste and add salt and pepper if needed. Serve garnished with fresh parsley and/or Parmesan cheese."]],"h":[[null,"Give yourself enough time . Although the cooking time is set to 22 minutes, it will take an additional 15-20 minutes to reach pressure, and then 10 minutes of natural release time. Leftovers keep refrigerated in a sealed container for 3-4 days. Reheat on the stovetop, or use the sauté function on your Instant Pot."]]},"9957667":{"s":[["Instant Pot Directions","Select the sauté function on your Instant pot and add the onion, carrot, and celery with 2-3 tablespoons of water. Sauté until softened, about 5 minutes."],["Instant Pot Directions","Add all remaining ingredients, except the milk, and give it a stir. Close the lid and set the valve to the sealing position. Now set to pressure cook for 6 minutes (it will take about 15 minutes to reach pressure). When the timer is complete, quick-release the steam valve and open the lid once safe to do so."],["Instant Pot Directions","Use an immersion blender to puree the soup. (Or carefully transfer to a blender, working in batches.) Stir in the plant milk and add salt and pepper to taste. Then serve garnished with cashew cream if desired."],["Stove Top Directions","Add the onion, carrot, and celery with 2-3 tablespoons of water to a large pot and sauté until softened, approx 5 minutes."],["Stove Top Directions","Add all the remaining ingredients, except the milk, and mix well. Bring to a boil and then reduce heat to a simmer and cook until squash and potatoes are fork tender, approx 20-25 minutes."],["Stove Top Directions","Turn off the heat, and puree your soup using an immersion blender. (Or carefully transfer to a blender, working in batches.) Stir in the plant milk and add salt and pepper to taste. Then serve garnished with cashew cream if desired."]],"h":[[null,"For added depth of flavour (and if time allows) halve your butternut squash and roast it flesh side down until easily pierced with a fork. Then add the roasted squash to your pot of soup and puree together. To save time , you may purchase pre-cut butternut squash in your grocery store. You will need approx. 5 cups of cubed squash. For nut-free , use soy milk, oat milk, or coconut milk (the carton kind, not canned) instead of cashew. Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-5 days in a sealed container or freeze airtight in a freezer-safe container for up to 3 months."]]},"9272338":{"s":[["Instant Pot Directions","Add everything to your Instant Pot, close the lid, and set the valve to the sealing position. Pressure cook on high for 4 minutes (it will take about 10 minutes to reach pressure) and once the timer completes, quick release the steam vent."],["Instant Pot Directions","Open the lid once safe to do so, and use an immersion blender to puree it. Serve your vegan cauliflower soup with toppings of your choice."],["Stove Top Directions","Add all the ingredients to a large pot and bring to a boil over high heat. Reduce low/medium heat and simmer for approx. 8 minutes, until the cauliflower is fork tender."],["Stove Top Directions","Turn off the heat, and use an immersion blender to blend your soup until smooth. Serve your vegan cauliflower soup with toppings of your choice."]],"h":[[null,"If you don’t have an immersion blender , carefully transfer to a blender and puree in batches as needed."],[null,"Add more seasoning if desired . This soup is designed to be simple, using minimal ingredients, while still delivering great flavour. If preferred, add some cumin, coriander, celery seed, nutritional yeast, and/or smoked paprika to amp up the flavours."],[null,"Add protein with a can of white beans or a block of silken or soft tofu and puree into the soup."],[null,"For a thicker soup , add 2 roughly chopped potatoes to the soup and puree together with the cauliflower once cooked. Or, add ½ cup of raw cashews before blending."],[null,"Bulk it up and make this simple soup suitable for a main dish by adding a scoop of cooked brown rice, pasta, barley, farro, or quinoa to each bowl before serving."],[null,"Leftovers keep refrigerated for up to 5 days or frozen for up to 3 months."]]},"9630210":{"s":[[null,"Sort and rinse your dried chickpeas. Then transfer them to your Instant Pot and pour the water on top. Close the lid and make sure the valve is in the sealing position. Then set to high pressure for 40 minutes. (It will take approx. 15 minutes to reach pressure.)"],[null,"When the timer is complete, do NOT quick release. Allow for a manual release for 10 minutes before quick releasing the remaining steam. Once safe to do so, open the lid and transfer your cooked chickpeas using a small strainer or slotted spoon, in order to reserve the cooking liquid for use in other recipes."],[null,"You may use immediately, or let cool at room temperature before storing. (See storage instructions in the notes below.)"]],"h":[[null,"Don’t soak the chickpeas first . There’s no need, and they’ll be too soft. Use chickpeas that are fresh and haven’t been sitting in your pantry for years, for the best flavour and most desirable texture. (Super old beans and legumes can require hours of cooking and still not get soft.) Make sure to sort through and rinse your dry chickpeas before cooking. Don’t dump the cooking water . Use it for broth, or a variety of other dishes. Do not quick release. Let your pressure cooker naturally release for 10 minutes first , or the chickpea liquid will splatter all over the place. Storage Instructions Refrigerate or freeze your chickpeas ONCE COOLED . Keep refrigerated for 3-4 days in zip top bags or sealed containers."],[null,"To freeze, pat your chickpeas dry with a clean dish towel. Then measure approx. 1.5 cups of cooked chickpeas and store in zip top bags or freezer safe, air tight containers. This is equivalent to about a 15 ounce can of chickpeas, which makes for convenient portions for future meals."],[null,"Make sure to push out extra air from your zip top bags , before sealing and freezing so they keep longer, and the bags will be less likely to break. Keep frozen for up to 3 months."]]},"9367621":{"s":[["Stove Top Directions","Add a few tablespoons of water or broth to your pot with your onions, carrots and celery. Sauté until softened, approx. 5 minutes."],["Stove Top Directions","Add all remaining ingredients and bring to a boil. Then lower the heat and simmer with the lid on the pot, but slightly askew for 25-30 minutes. Taste and adjust for salt and pepper if preferred, and serve."],["Instant Pot Directions","Add a few tablespoons of water or broth to your pot with your onions, carrots and celery. Sauté until softened, approx. 5 minutes."],["Instant Pot Directions","Add all remaining ingredients, close the lid and place the valve in the sealing position. Set to high pressure for 8 minutes. (It will take about 15 minutes to build pressure before the timer counts down.) Then quick release, remove the lid once safe to do so, and serve with extra salt and pepper, if needed."]],"h":[[null,"Depending on your preferred thickness , use between 6-8 cups of vegetable broth. For a thicker soup, use six cups. For a thinner soup, use eight. Remember that the soup will absorb more liquid as it cools."],[null,"Use low-sodium vegetable broth. You can always add more salt if needed, but you cannot remove it."],[null,"If you don’t have low-sodium broth , use half broth and half water. Once cooked, taste and add more salt, if needed."],[null,"Or, if you don’t have any broth on hand, you can make some with this easy bouillon recipe . (I highly recommend this broth for its fantastic flavour."],[null,"Leftovers keep refrigerated for up to 4 days or freeze them airtight for up to 3 months."]]},"9759865":{"s":[["Instant Pot Directions","Select sauté on your Instant Pot, and add the onions and peppers with a tablespoon or two of water and sauté for 2-3 minutes until softened. Then add all remaining ingredients, close the lid and turn the valve to the sealing position. Set to high pressure for 6 minutes. (It will take 10-15 minutes to build pressure before counting down.) When the timer is complete, quick release the steam valve."],["Instant Pot Directions","Serve with buns and toppings or enjoy as a soup."],["Stove Top Directions","In a large sauce pan over medium heat, add the onions and peppers with a tablespoon or two of water and sauté for 2-3 minutes until softened"],["Stove Top Directions","Add all the remaining ingredients to the pot and bring to a boil over high heat. Once boiling, lower the heat to medium low and let simmer for 25-30 minutes, or until lentils are cooked and the liquids are mostly absorbed."],["Stove Top Directions","Serve with buns and toppings or enjoy as a soup."]],"h":[[null,"*Make it a soup : To make vegan sloppy joe soup, add an additional cup of tomato sauce and two additional cups of veggie broth to your pot. So, use 6 cups of broth and 2 cups of sauce. Do not add salt . Omitting salt in the recipe was not an oversight. If you’re using broth and Tamari or soy sauce, you likely won’t need extra salt. Once cooked, taste and add more salt if needed. Use SPLIT red lentils , not whole red lentils. Split lentils absorb more broth and sauce and make the dish thick so that a sandwich will hold nicely. If you don’t have split red lentils , split yellow or green peas also does a good job of this. If you don’t have any split lentils or peas, use more green or brown lentils with similar results. Adjust the seasoning : Don’t be afraid to spice these up to amp up the flavour. I keep these mildly spiced to keep them kid-friendly, but if you want heat, add some cayenne pepper or a dash or two of hot sauce. For soy-free : Omit the Tamari and use coconut aminos OR omit, and add a little salt, to taste. For added nutrients , add more chopped veggies like celery, diced potato, mushrooms, peas, and/or carrots. Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-4 days or freeze airtight in a freezer-safe container for up to 3 months."]]},"9479544":{"s":[[null,"Peel and cut your potatoes into one inch pieces. Place them in your pot with the broth and close the lid, setting the valve in the sealing position. Set to high pressure for 6 minutes. (It will take about 10 minutes to reach pressure, and then the timer will start counting down.) When the timer completes, quick release the pressure, and open the lid once safe to do so."],[null,"Add the milk, salt and any optional ingredients. Then mash with a potato masher until smooth and creamy. Taste and add more salt, if necessary, then serve warm."]],"h":[[null,"*This recipe as written is for a 6qt Instant Pot model. If you’re using an 8qt model, increase the broth to 1.5 cups. If doubling the potatoes, NO need to double the broth . Just double the potatoes and leave the broth at 1 cup or 1.5 cups, depending on your model size. For the best no drain mashed potatoes, weigh your potatoes ! This will give the best results since they can vary greatly in size. If you do not have a kitchen scale , and you need to eye ball it, use 10 average sized Yukon Gold potatoes to make approximately 3 lbs. Do your best to cut your pieces in similar sizes. For even cooking, you don’t want some pieces too big, or others too small. Don’t over-mash your taters! Once smooth, you’re good to go. Overly processing and mashing them can result in a gummy texture, and nobody wants that! Make them extra creamy . Add a dollop of cashew cream , or vegan cream cheese to your potato mash and stir it in for extra creaminess. Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-4 days or frozen, air tight, for up to 3 months."]]},"9816028":{"s":[["Instant Pot Directions","Dump all the ingredients into your Instant Pot and close the lid, ensuring the valve is in the sealing position. Set to high pressure for 2 minutes, (it will take about 15-20 minutes to reach pressure) then quick release the steam once the timer is complete."],["Instant Pot Directions","Serve garnished with desired toppings."],["Stove Top Directions","Add all the ingredients to a large pot with and bring to a boil. Once boiling, lower the heat and simmer for 12-15 minutes, until veggies are fork tender"],["Stove Top Directions","Serve garnished with desired toppings."]],"h":[[null,"Cut your zucchini and mushroom pieces larger since they cook faster and you don’t want them overly soft. The sweet potato can be a little smaller since it has a longer cook time. This will give you evenly cooked veggies . Quick release and remove the lid immediately (when safe to do so) once pressure cooking completes, to prevent the veggies from over cooking. Leftovers keep in a sealed container in your fridge for up to 4 days."]]},"9054548":{"s":[["Instant Pot Directions","Set your Instant Pot to sauté. Add 3-4 tablespoons of water, with the onion, carrots, and celery, and sauté until softened, approx. 5 minutes. (Add more water if needed to prevent sticking.)"],["Instant Pot Directions","Add all the remaining ingredients, except the spinach, and give it a stir. Lock your lid in place, ensuring the valve is set to the sealing position. Then set to high pressure for 2 minutes. (It will take approx. 15 minutes to reach pressure.) Once complete, quick release, remove the lid and stir in the spinach until wilted."],["Stove Top Directions","In a large soup pot, add 3-4 tablespoons of water, with the onion, carrots, and celery, and sauté over medium heat until softened, approx. 5 minutes. (Add more water as needed to prevent sticking.)"],["Stove Top Directions","Then add all the remaining ingredients, except the spinach, cover your pot with a lid, and bring to a low boil. Then simmer the soup for 12-15 minutes, until the quinoa is cooked and the soup has thickened. Turn off the heat, and stir in the spinach until wilted."]],"h":[[null,"Dice the onion, carrots, and celery into small pieces, but keep the zucchini pieces larger so they don’t overcook and get too soft."],[null,"If using the Instant Pot method , make sure the valve on your lid is in the sealing position, or it will not reach pressure. When the timer completes, quick release immediately to prevent overcooking."],[null,"If using the stovetop method , keep your pot or saucepan covered with a lid while cooking to prevent the liquids from evaporating too much and the soup from getting too thick."],[null,"As the soup cools, the quinoa will absorb more broth. Add a little extra broth , as needed, if the soup gets thicker than you’d like."],[null,"Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-4 days or freeze airtight for up to 3 months. Make sure to cool the soup before freezing and leave some room for expansion."]]},"9712628":{"s":[[null,"Add the drained beans and all remaining ingredients to your Instant Pot. Stir to combine, then close the lid, ensuring the valve is set to the sealing position. Set to high pressure for 30 minutes. (It will take about 10-15 minutes to build pressure before counting down.) Let it naturally release for 10 minutes, and then quick release any remaining pressure."],[null,"Serve with your favourite toppings."]],"h":[[null,"For firmer beans skip the soaking. For softer, melt-in-your-mouth beans , soak them overnight, or for 6-8 hours."],[null,"If you’ve forgotten to soak your beans use this quick soak method. Add the beans to a pot and cover with water leaving at least 2-3 inches of water above the beans. Place the lid on the pot, bring it to a boil on your stovetop, then remove it from the heat, and soak for 1 hour."],[null,"Nutritional information is for ¼ of the recipe and does not include optional toppings. Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3 days, reheat with a little water or broth on stovetop."]]},"9042335":{"s":[["Instant Pot Directions","In a small bowl, combine all your sauce ingredients and whisk together. Set aside."],["Instant Pot Directions","Turn your Instant Pot to sauté mode, add a tablespoon or two of water, the carrots and red pepper and sauté until lightly softened, about 5 minutes. Do not overcook, they will cook more with the noodles. Then add the sauce and the water, and give it a stir."],["Instant Pot Directions","Break your noodles in half and place inside your pot. Make sure they're covered with the water by gently pushing them down with a spatula if needed. Close the lid, turn the valve to the sealing position, and set to high pressure for 4 minutes. (It will take about 10 minutes to build pressure before the pot begins counting down.)"],["Instant Pot Directions","Once complete, quick release the steam valve, then add your green onions (reserving some to garnish if desired) and give it a stir. Serve garnished with chopped peanuts, green onion, lime wedges or more sriracha if desired."],["Stove Top Directions","In a small bowl, combine all your sauce ingredients and whisk together. Set aside."],["Stove Top Directions","Use a large skillet and add a tablespoon or two of water, the carrots and red pepper and sauté until lightly softened, about 5 minutes. Then add the peanut sauce, and 1 cup of water and simmer for about 5 minutes."],["Stove Top Directions","Meanwhile, bring a large pot of salted water a boil, and cook your pasta according to package directions. Drain and return to the pot. Then pour the sauce over your pasta, mix well and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Do not overcook your veggies when sautéing. They will continue to cook, while pressure cooking, so just a gentle sauté is plenty. Make sure to push your noodles down , into the water and sauce mixture before pressure cooking. Noodles that are sticking out, above the liquid will not cook as well. Use peanut butter that’s made from JUST peanuts , without added sugar, oil or salt. Your Instant Pot noodles will keep refrigerated for 2-3 days. The noodles will absorb the sauce, as they cool. So add some moisture to your pan when reheating. Use a little broth, soy sauce or Tamari, or a splash of water with a sprinkle of salt."]]},"9668816":{"s":[[null,"Prepare and chop all your veggies before you begin. Then set your Instant Pot to sauté and add the coconut oil (if using) and the chopped onion and sauté for 3-5 minutes, stirring often. Then add your minced/grated ginger and garlic to the pot, mix well and sauté another 30 seconds or so."],[null,"Turn the pot off and add all remaining ingredients EXCEPT the lime juice. Mix well, close the lid and set the valve to the sealing position. Set your pot to manual or pressure cook (depending on your model) for 3 minutes on high pressure. It will take about 10 minutes to reach pressure and then begin counting down."],[null,"Once complete, quick release the steam valve and open the lid once safe to do so. Squeeze the lime juice into your pot and mix well. Serve with rice, noodles, or naan bread and garnish with sriracha and fresh herbs, if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Give your Thai curry a protein boost by adding in a can of chickpeas or lentils, if desired. For extra spiciness , add half a teaspoon of cayenne pepper or chili flakes. I find this dish only mildly spicy as is. Use FRESH ginger and garlic for the best flavour results. If you’re following a low fat diet . you may omit the coconut oil and sauté in veggie broth or water instead. You may also sub the coconut milk for a light version, however, keep in mind, you’ll have a slightly less coconut flavour. For soy free, skip the Tamari or soy sauce and add a little extra salt instead. Or, sub for coconut aminos . Don’t have broccoli? Swap for snap peas, green beans, cauliflower or kale. Store leftover rice and Thai curry in separate containers in your refrigerator for up to 3 days. Reheat and enjoy."]]},"9376343":{"s":[[null,"Turn your Instant Pot to the sauté function and add a couple tablespoons of water or broth to the pot. Place the onion, garlic, peppers, mushrooms, walnuts and all the seasoning inside. Then sauté for 2-3 minutes, until slightly softened."],[null,"Add the remaining ingredients (broth, tomato sauce and rice), mix well and close the lid. Set the valve to the sealing position pressure cook for 22 minutes. (It will take about 8 minutes to build pressure before the pot begins counting down.) Once the timer is complete, let it naturally release for 10 minutes. Then quick release the remaining pressure and remove the lid when safe to do so. Enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Do not slice your veggies too thin . They will cook for a while in the pot, so they’ll withstand cooking best, if they are thick cuts. Alternatively, if you prefer your veggies crisp , remove from the pot once sautéed, pressure cook your rice in the broth and tomato sauce, then add the veggies back in and mix well. Make sure to push down any loose grains of rice on the sides of your pot before pressure cooking . Everything should be covered in the liquid for even cooking. If you already released pressure and forgot to do a 10 minute natural release , just hit sauté and stirring often, continue cooking for 3-5 minutes to absorb excess liquid. Or, set aside for about 10 minutes or so. The rice will continue absorbing the liquid as it rests and cools. Leftovers keep refrigerated for up to 3 days, and you may reheat on stove top or in your Instant Pot."]]},"9357101":{"s":[["Instant Pot Directions","Add all the ingredients (EXCEPT the pasta AND using ONLY 2 cups of the water) to a high speed blender and process until smooth and creamy. Transfer to your Instant Pot and add the remaining 3.5 cups of water and stir. Then place the pasta on top and gently push it down into the sauce."],["Instant Pot Directions","Close the lid and ensure the valve is set to the sealing position. Then cook on high pressure for 4 minutes (it will take about 10 minutes to reach pressure) and quick release immediately once the timer is complete. Open the lid once safe to do so, give everything a good stir, and serve."],["Stove Top Directions","Bring a large pot of water to boil and cook your pasta according to package directions. Then drain and return to the pot."],["Stove Top Directions","Meanwhile, add the cheese sauce ingredients (using ONLY 2 cups of the water) to your blender and process until smooth. Pour the sauce over your drained pasta, mix well, and serve."]],"h":[[null,"* If you do not have a high speed blender like a Vitamix or Blendtec, soak your cashews in boiling hot water for at least 30 minutes. Then drain and use as directed. This will help soften your cashews, making them easier to process into a smooth vegan cheese sauce. Note that your mac and cheese might appear a bit watery upon removing the lid. However, a few stirs and that extra sauce will quickly absorb . If you want to amp up the nutrients here, add 2 cups of frozen peas or mixed frozen veggies to the pot before pressure cooking. Leftovers keep refrigerated in a sealed container for 3-4 days. However, the pasta will continue to absorb the sauce as it cools so to reheat, add some plant milk or broth to the pan to loosen and return to a creamy state ."]]},"3840":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Peeled potatoes and cut into small pieces."],[null,"Leave stems on bell peppers and cut in half, from stem to bottom. With a spoon, remove seeds and membrane. Place on a baking sheet sprayed with nonstick cooking spray."],[null,"Mix cornstarch with cold water and stir until free of lumps."],[null,"In a sauce pan combine beef broth, Worcestershire sauce and coffee powder. Add dissolved cornstarch and stir over medium heat until thickened."],[null,"In a skillet crumble the ground beef; cook over medium heat until browned. Add mixed vegetables, stir and heat with beef until hot. Combine gravy with beef and vegetable mixture."],[null,"Stuff each bell pepper half with 1/2 cup beef mixture. Place in oven and bake uncovered for 40 minutes."],[null,"While peppers are baking, make reduced-potassium potatoes. Place cut-up potatoes in a pot and add 6 cups water; bring to a boil. Remove from heat and drain water. Add fresh water and boil until potatoes are tender."],[null,"With a hand mixer whip potatoes with butter or margarine and nondairy creamer or half and half."],[null,"Remove peppers from oven. Spread 1/4 cup whipped potatoes on top of each stuffed pepper half and serve."]],"h":[[null,"If desired, add a dash of Tabasco® sauce or reduced-sodium Worcestershire sauce before serving."],[null,"One teaspoon reduced-sodium Worcestershire sauce contains 45 mg sodium."],[null,"Substitute lamb or ground turkey for beef if desired."],[null,"Substitute margarine for butter or nondairy creamer for half and half if desired."]]},"7786545":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a large, flame-proof casserole dish, add the onions and lamb and fry for 3–4 minutes, until the meat is browned."],[null,"Add the remaining stew ingredients and enough water to cover the contents. Bring to the boil, cover and simmer very gently for 1½–2 hours, until the meat is tender."],[null,"Meanwhile, make the colcannon. Place the potatoes into a large pan of boiling water and cook for 10–12 minutes until tender. Drain, mash together with the milk and margarine, and season with plenty of black pepper."],[null,"Cook the cabbage in a pan of boiling water until tender, drain and stir a quarter of it through the mash with the spring onions."],[null,"Serve the remaining cabbage with the stew and colcannon."]],"h":[[null,"You could use beef or venison instead of lamb."],[null,"If using fatty meat, cook the dish the day before, refrigerate and when cooled then skim the fat from the top of the dish before reheating."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"3750":{"s":[[null,"Chop onion, bell peppers and cilantro."],[null,"Thaw shrimp and pat dry."],[null,"In a large bowl, mix shrimp, coleslaw mix, onion, pepper, cilantro and 1/8 teaspoon cayenne pepper."],[null,"In a small bowl combine mayonnaise, sour cream, lemon juice, Italian seasoning and remaining1/8 teaspoon cayenne pepper. Pour dressing over shrimp cabbage mixture and toss well."],[null,"Chill for 2 hours and serve."]],"h":[[null,"If all ingredients are chilled prior to preparation, the 2-hour chill time can be eliminated."],[null,"If you want to “kick it up a notch,” add more cayenne pepper to taste."],[null,"For variety and a touch of sweetness, add 1/2 cup pineapple tidbits."]]},"6517612":{"s":[[null,"In a large skillet, cook the turkey bacon until crispy and sausage until browned."],[null,"Place greens, cannellini beans, and onions in a large bowl."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk the olive oil, vinegar, garlic, and black pepper together. Drizzle over the salad and toss to coat the greens. Sprinkle with Parmesan cheese."]],"h":[]},"3533":{"s":[[null,"Place the beef roast, oregano, pepper, garlic powder and red pepper in a Crock-Pot®. Cook on high for 4 to 5 hours until tender."],[null,"Remove beef from Crock-Pot and let cool."],[null,"Shred beef and remove fat."],[null,"Place the shredded beef back into the Crock-Pot. Add the sliced peppers, onion and pepperoncini juice."],[null,"Cook on high for 45 to 60 minutes, until the vegetables are tender."]],"h":[[null,"Serve Italian beef on a hamburger bun or roll."],[null,"Pepperoncini juice is high in sodium and replaces other sodium sources in this recipe. Limit portion and avoid adding salt to keep total sodium intake low."],[null,"For a lower-protein diet, reduce meat portion according to your diet plan or consult with your dietitian."]]},"1802":{"s":[[null,"Snip 2 parsley sprigs into small pieces. Chop bell pepper; finely chop onion. Slice grilled squash into half moons."],[null,"Mix mayonnaise, lemon juice, snipped parsley and cayenne pepper (optional) in a mixing bowl."],[null,"Chop chicken into 1/2-inch cubes."],[null,"Add chopped chicken, pepper, onion and squash to the mayonnaise and toss to coat."],[null,"Chill at least one hour to allow flavors to blend."],[null,"Serve over 1/2 cup of baby arugula or baby romaine lettuce. Garnish with remaining 4 parsley sprigs."]],"h":[[null,"Feel free to experiment with different combinations of herbs such as basil, rosemary, thyme, savory, oregano, etc., depending upon your personal tastes and availability and costs."],[null,"If you are following a lower protein diet reduce chicken portion to half or to the amount recommended by your dietitian."],[null,"Please see Chicken in Rosemary-Garlic Sauce and Grilled Summer Squash recipes to use this for a cook once, eat twice recipe."],[null,"Substitute cooked, diced chicken breast for the Chicken in Rosemary-Garlic Sauce if you did not prepare the recipe."],[null,"Replace arugula with baby romaine lettuce if preferred."]]},"2813":{"s":[[null,"Mix seasonings together."],[null,"Add to vinegar and oil."],[null,"Shake well to mix."]],"h":[[null,"Homemade salad dressings keep well in the refrigerator for several weeks."],[null,"For variety try different oils, including flavored or spicy oils."]]},"2261":{"s":[[null,"Chop the bell pepper, onion and basil."],[null,"In a large skillet, cook and sauté onion and green pepper in oil until tender."],[null,"Beat eggs until blended; add black pepper and crushed chili flakes. Pour into skillet with onion and green peppers."],[null,"Cook over medium heat. As mixture begins to set at bottom and sides, gently lift cooked portion with spatula so the uncooked egg can flow to bottom. Avoid stirring constantly."],[null,"Cook until eggs are thickened throughout but still moist, 3 to 5 minutes. Serve hot with fresh basil on top."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute 2 cups liquid low cholesterol egg substitute for eggs if you are on a low cholesterol diet."]]},"6987636":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the broiler."],[null,"Heat the oil in a medium, ovenproof, nonstick skillet over medium-high heat. Add the potatoes and sauté 3 minutes. Add the ground turkey, Italian seasoning, and onion, sauté for 3-5 minutes, stirring several times."],[null,"Add the spinach, mushrooms, and garlic. Continue to cook 1 to 2 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, whish the whole eggs, egg whites, and milk together. Tear the basil into small pieces and add to the egg mixture along with the black pepper."],[null,"Pour egg mixture into the skillet and gently stir vegetables to make sure the egg mixture spreads throughout the pan. Press the turkey and vegetables into the egg mixture. Turn the heat to low and cook 10 minutes. Frittata will be mostly cooked through."],[null,"Place the frittata under the broiler for 1 to 2 minutes to brown. Watch to make sure the top doesn’t brown too much."],[null,"To serve, loosen frittata around edges, cut in half, and slip each half onto an individual plate."]],"h":[]},"2389":{"s":[[null,"Prepare Roasted Red Pepper Tomato Sauce. Set aside."],[null,"Preheat oven to 375° F. Chop onion."],[null,"Beat eggs in a large bowl, then add all ingredients and mix together."],[null,"Roll into 1” balls and place on a baking sheet."],[null,"Bake for 10 to 15 minutes, until meatballs are cooked through."],[null,"To serve, place meatballs in a warming dish or slow cooker on low heat setting. Serve with 2 teaspoons sauce on the side or add sauce to the meatballs."]],"h":[[null,"Find the recipe for Roasted Red Pepper Tomato Sauce on DaVita.com. It adds 37 mg potassium and 21 mg sodium for one tablespoon. This lower-potassium, low-sodium sauce can be used as a substitute for tomato sauce in a variety of dishes."],[null,"Make meatballs ahead and refrigerate. When ready to serve, heat ingredients together and transfer to a warming dish."]]},"9624396":{"s":[[null,"Bring a large pot of generously salted water to a boil and cook your pasta according to package directions for \"al dente\" pasta. Immediately drain and rinse the pasta to prevent overcooking. Then transfer it to a large bowl."],[null,"While the pasta is cooking, combine all the salad dressing ingredients in a small bowl or jar and mix well."],[null,"Then add all the remaining salad ingredients to the bowl with the cooked pasta and pour the dressing on top. Mix well and refrigerate for 1 hour (or longer) or enjoy immediately."]],"h":[]},"2214":{"s":[[null,"Boil eggs until hard boiled, about 10 minutes. Remove eggs to a bowl of cold water to cool."],[null,"While eggs are cooking, boil 1 pound of small shells or ditalini pasta until al dente. Drain."],[null,"Add pasta to a bowl and mix in mayonnaise."],[null,"Add 6 ounces canned tuna and mix with pasta."],[null,"Add chopped baby gherkin pickles and a tablespoon of pickle juice; mix with pasta."],[null,"Peel and slice hard boiled eggs and add to pasta."],[null,"Refrigerate until ready to serve. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Freda uses Pastene® brand Italian-style tuna (tonno) canned with olive oil."],[null,"Ditalini pasta is a type of pasta shaped like small tubes and described as very short macaroni."],[null,"Adjust portion for a lower carbohydrate diet."]]},"3069":{"s":[[null,"Chop bell pepper and onion. Dice chicken."],[null,"Place oil in a large nonstick frying pan and stir-fry the bell pepper, onion and broccoli. Sprinkle with the rosemary, basil, red pepper flakes, garlic powder and salt."],[null,"Stir in the cooked chicken."],[null,"Mix chicken broth with cornstarch and add to vegetable and chicken mixture. Cook until thickened slightly. Stir in the cup of hot cooked pasta."],[null,"Remove from heat and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Chicken may be increased to 6 ounces for those on dialysis. Protein content will be increased to 29 grams per serving."],[null,"For quick preparation, use 1-1/4 cups of a frozen vegetable mixture of similar composition to replace fresh vegetables."],[null,"Add more or less red pepper flakes to suit your own tolerance for spicy foods."],[null,"Squeeze on lemon juice or sprinkle with balsamic vinegar to add a tangy flavor."]]},"6146598":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a large saucepan over medium heat. Add the onion and cook while stirring occasionally until fully softened, about 8 minutes."],[null,"Add the tomato purée, broth, and salt, and bring to a boil over high heat. Reduce heat to medium low and simmer, uncovered, until flavors are combined, about 5 minutes. (Hint: For a thinner soup, drizzle in more broth.) Stir in the basil and vinegar."],[null,"Ladle into bowls. Serve hot or chilled."]],"h":[]},"2145":{"s":[[null,"Slice spinach leaves. Dice carrots and chicken. Mince onion."],[null,"Place the beef, beaten eggs, bread crumbs, cheese, basil and onion in a bowl. Combine thoroughly."],[null,"Roll seasoned meat into a 1/2” diameter log. Cut into 80 pieces. Roll into tiny meatballs and set aside."],[null,"In a large stockpot heat chicken broth to boiling. Stir in the spinach, pasta, carrots and meatballs. Return to boil; reduce heat to medium."],[null,"Cook (stirring frequently) at a slow boil for 10 minutes or until pasta is al dente and meatballs are no longer pink inside."],[null,"Add diced chicken. Allow chicken to heat thoroughly and serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"Look for low-sodium broth without potassium chloride. If unavailable, substitute with reduced-sodium broth and omit the salt or use your own homemade low-sodium broth."],[null,"Omit the salt if desired. Sodium difference equals 107 mg per serving."],[null,"Wedding Soup is an Italian-American soup that is popular in the United States, especially northeastern Ohio and western Pennsylvania. The translation of “minestra maritata” is married soup, a reference to the fact that the ingredients go well together. Try this blend of tiny meatballs, diced chicken, spinach, carrots and tiny pasta in a chicken broth – no wedding necessary!"]]},"6466239":{"s":[[null,"In a large skillet over high heat, heat the oil until it’s hot. Sauté the tomatoes for 4 to 5 minutes, or until their skins begin to brown and blister."],[null,"Stir in the garlic and cook for 1 minute. Add the balsamic vinegar and sugar substitute and continue to cook for 1 to 2 minutes, or until the mixture begins to thicken. Serve hot or at room temperature."]],"h":[]},"7523019":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4. Add 1 tsp of the oil to a pan over a low-medium heat, add the onions and gently brown for 3-4 minutes, turning regularly. Set aside."],[null,"Coat the lamb in flour and add the remaining oil to the pan. Cook for 2-3 mins on each side."],[null,"Return the onions to the pan, add the garlic, rosemary and oregano. Stir in the stock and bring to a gentle boil."],[null,"Add the tomatoes, balsamic vinegar and pepper."],[null,"Place in an ovenproof dish and cook for 45-50 minutes. Garnish with a little fresh rosemary and serve."]],"h":[[null,"You could cook the whole dish on the hob if you prefer – just simmer gently for 45-50 minutes. Take care not to boil dry so add a little water if required."],[null,"Works well with skinless chicken thighs."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"1946":{"s":[[null,"Cook rice (or pasta) according to package directions without added salt. Refrigerate to chill."],[null,"Slice celery and finely chop red onion and bell pepper. Peel and dice cucumber and slice radishes. Chop eggs."],[null,"Add mayonnaise, celery, onion and mustard to chilled rice or pasta. Mix well and refrigerate until ready to serve."],[null,"Stir in eggs, radish slices, cucumber and red peppers before serving chilled salad."]],"h":[[null,"Choose rice or salad pasta (elbow, mini shells, salad macaroni). Both work well in this amazing salad."],[null,"Reduce mayonnaise or use fat-free mayonnaise for a lower fat dish."],[null,"Two medium celery stalks will yield about 1 cup sliced celery, a medium onion is about 2-1/2″ in diameter, 1 small cucumber is 6-7″ long and a medium radish is about 1″ in diameter."],[null,"A large red bell pepper will yield 1 cup chopped. When preparing this recipes, the left over pepper can be sliced and used as a snack"]]},"2547":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400° F."],[null,"In a bowl, combine flour, cornmeal, sugar and baking powder."],[null,"In another bowl, combine egg substitute, rice milk and melted butter."],[null,"Stir dry ingredients into wet ingredients just until moistened."],[null,"Fill greased or paper-lined muffin cups 2/3 full."],[null,"Bake for 15 to 20 minutes or until a toothpick comes out clean."],[null,"Serve warm."]],"h":[[null,"By using egg substitute instead of egg and rice milk instead of milk, phosphorus is reduced from 130 mg to 100 mg. The baking powder contributes 76 mg phosphorus to each muffin. Limit portion to one muffin."],[null,"Do not substitute self-rising corn meal — it’s higher in phosphorus."],[null,"Freeze leftover muffins and reheat for a quick meal addition later."],[null,"To make skillet-baked cornbread instead of muffins use a medium-size iron skillet and decrease sugar to 2 tablespoons."]]},"9761419":{"s":[[null,"Drain and rinse the chickpeas, and remove the stems from the jalapenos."],[null,"Then put everything in a food processor or blender and blend until it's as smooth as you want. You can add more water if you want it thinner, or you can use oliver oil, but I like to keep it low in fat so we use water."],[null,"You may garnish the hummus with more chopped jalapenos, or skip that part."],[null,"Serve with raw veggies, bread, or whatever you like."]],"h":[]},"4002784":{"s":[[null,"ONE: Preheat an outdoor grill or a grill pan or in a large nonstick sauté pan over medium-high heat, heat half of the canola oil on medium-high (a George Foreman® grill may also be used). TWO:In a medium size bowl, combine the first 5 ingredients plus 2 tablespoons of olive oil. THREE:Form 6 equal-sized burger patties and lightly brush them with the remaining 2 tablespoons of olive oil.FOUR: Cook the burgers for 5-7 minutes per side, flipping once, or until an internal temperature of 165° F is reached on an instant-read thermometer. FIVE: Top each burger with about 2 tablespoons of cheese and melt in a toaster oven or an oven set to broil. SIX: Serve each burger on a toasted bun. (If using George Foreman® grill, once cooked, unplug the grill and add cheese to the burger. Leave the grill open and allow the cheese to slightly melt.) * When handling or cutting hot peppers, it is best to wear plastic or rubber gloves and do not touch your face. If you do not wear gloves, wash your hands thoroughly with soap and water before touching your face or eyes."]],"h":[[null,"** To zest, hold fruit still and move a grating tool (e.g., zester, peeler, box grater) slowly back and forth across the peel. Be careful to remove only the outermost, colorful layer of peel and not any of the bitter, white pith."]]},"6571015":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a large soup pot over medium heat. Add the onion, carrot, celery, jalapeño, garlic, and corn and sauté for 5 to 7 minutes."],[null,"Add the no-salt seasoning, black pepper, and chicken broth. Bring to boiling, then reduce the heat and simmer, covered, for 20 minutes."],[null,"Remove the pot from the heat and puree about half of the soup, using an immersion blender or an upright blender. If using an upright blender, puree in batches and be sure not to overfill the blender. Return the puree to the pot."],[null,"Add the chicken and heat through. Remove the pot from the heat."],[null,"Stir in the yogurt and serve. Do not boil the soup once the yogurt is added."]],"h":[]},"2633":{"s":[[null,"Coarsely chop the green and yellow onions. Peel and chop the ginger. Mince the garlic cloves. Seed and chop the hot peppers."],[null,"Place all ingredients, except chicken, in a food processor and process until smooth."],[null,"Place chicken and blended mixture in a dish or large zip-top bag. Seal and refrigerate to marinate for 3 to 24 hours."],[null,"Remove chicken from the container and discard remaining marinade."],[null,"Heat a grill on medium-high heat. Oil the grill rack, then add chicken and cook on each side for about 10 to 12 minutes. Chicken should reach 165° F before removing from the grill."]],"h":[[null,"Use a grill pan if grill is not available to get char marks on chicken."],[null,"If habanera and scotch bonnet peppers are unavailable substitute with your favorite hot chili."]]},"6659101":{"s":[[null,"Place all ingredients except chicken in a food processor and blend until smooth."],[null,"Place chicken and blended mixture in a dish or large zip-top bag. Seal and refrigerate to marinate for 3 to 24 hours."],[null,"Remove chicken from the container and discard remaining marinade."],[null,"Heat a grill on medium-high heat. Oil the grill rack, then add chicken and cook on each side for about 10 to 12 minutes. Chicken should reach 165° F before removing from the grill."]],"h":[]},"7534224":{"s":[[null,"Put the onion, garlic, ginger, chilli, curry powder and spices, sweetener, chopped tomatoes, coconut milk and a little pepper to season in your slow-cooker pot. Stir well, cover and cook on high for 1 hour."],[null,"Add the okra, cover again and cook for another 2 hours."],[null,"Stir in the spinach, cherry tomatoes and prawns. Season the fish chunks lightly with pepper and lay them on top of the curry. Cover again and cook for a further 1 hour until the prawns and fish change colour and are cooked through."],[null,"Stir in the lime juice and scatter over the extra spinach leaves to serve."]],"h":[[null,"If you don’t have a slow cooker, put all the ingredients up to the coconut milk in a large non-stick saucepan or casserole pan, cover and simmer over a low heat for 30 minutes. Add the okra, cover and simmer for 30 minutes more. Stir in the spinach, cherry tomatoes and prawns, then lay the fish on top. Cover and simmer for 5 minutes or until the prawns and fish are cooked through."],[null,"Watch out for spice/seasoning blends that have added sugar, salt, flour or oil. Choose spice blends made with herbs and spices only."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"6472756":{"s":[[null,"Score the skin of the fish with a sharp knife. Spray the scored surface of the fish with the cooking spray. Squeeze the lime over the skin and sprinkle with salt. Rub into the surface."],[null,"Make the stuffing by combining the crushed crackers, thyme, hot chili, scallions, and melted butter in a medium bowl. Fill the cavity of the fish with the stuffing, and using a toothpick or metal skewer, secure the opening by weaving skewer to close fish. You can also stick toothpicks into the bottom of the fish at 2-inch intervals to secure."],[null,"Preheat grill to medium-high heat and place on grill grate. Cook for 15–18 minutes, turning occasionally, until cooked through and crusted on the outside."]],"h":[]},"3730":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350º F."],[null,"Chop onion, bell pepper and garlic. Peel shrimp."],[null,"In a large bowl combine all ingredients except margarine."],[null,"Pour into a 9” x 13” baking dish and spread out evenly."],[null,"Slice margarine and place over top of ingredients."],[null,"Cover with a lid or foil."],[null,"Bake for 1 hour and 15 minutes. Serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"Uncle Ben’s® converted white rice is a popular brand. Converted rice, also know as parboiled rice, is steamed before it is husked. As a result the kernals absorb nutrients from the husk and the rice cooks more quickly."],[null,"1 stick of butter or margarine is equal to 1/2 cup."],[null,"For variation, try substituting cooked cubed chicken for shrimp."]]},"6366362":{"s":[[null,"Place the chicken in a medium slow cooker. Add the celery pieces, onion wedges, garlic, soy sauce, vinegar, and hot pepper flakes. Add the water and chicken stock. Cover and cook on low for 3 to 5 hours, or until the chicken is fully cooked and the chicken reaches a temperature of 165 F."],[null,"About an hour before serving, prepare the rice using the package directions, omitting the salt and margarine."],[null,"Using a slotted spoon, lift the chicken out of the slow cooker and place on a cutting board. Strain the broth through a fine mesh sieve into a deep bowl. Pour the hot broth back into the slow cooker. Turn the slow cooker to High."],[null,"Cut the chicken into bite-size pieces and stir back into the hot broth in the slow cooker. Stir in the spinach. Cover and cook on High for 15 minutes."],[null,"Spoon 1/2 cup cooked brown rice into each serving bowl. Ladle 1 1/2 cups chicken, spinach, and broth mixture over the rice. Top with sliced radishes and green onions. Sprinkle with sesame seeds."],[null,"Pressure Cooker Variation: Place the chicken, celery, onion, garlic, soy sauce, vinegar, and hot pepper flakes in the pressure cooker. Add the water and chicken stock. Secure the lid. Cook on High pressure for 6 minutes. Quickly release the pressure. Remove the chicken and set on a cutting board. Strain the broth and return it to the pressure cooker. Cut the chicken into bite-size pieces and stir it into the broth. Set the pressure cooker on the sauté setting. Stir in the spinach and cook, stirring frequently, for 3 to 5 minutes or until the spinach is cooked. Proceed as the recipe direct, ladling the chicken and spinach over the cooked brown rice and top with radishes, green onions, and sesame seeds."]],"h":[]},"6782992":{"s":[[null,"Peel the cucumbers to leave alternating green stripes. Slice the cucumbers in half lengthwise and scrape the seeds out with a spoon."],[null,"Using a mandolin, food processor, or knife, slice the cucumber into very thin slices."],[null,"In a medium bowl, whisk together the vinegar, canola oil, low- or no-calorie sweetener, and salt (optional)."],[null,"Toss the cucumbers and sesame seeds in the dressing and serve."]],"h":[]},"2707":{"s":[[null,"In a medium saucepan combine sugar and 1 cup water; bring to a boil."],[null,"Add cranberries to water and return to a boil. Reduce the heat to medium and boil for 10 minutes while stirring occasionally."],[null,"Pour cooked cranberries into a wire mesh strainer over a mixing bowl. Using the back of a spoon mash berries to force pulp into the bowl. Discard skins."],[null,"Stir sauce and pour into a serving bowl. Cool at room temperature, then chill in the refrigerator until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"For a low sugar version use Splenda or other sugar-free sweetener."],[null,"Use frozen cranberries if fresh are not available."]]},"7997094":{"s":[[null,"To make the jerk seasoning, add everything except the chicken to a blender and blend to a paste. Or use a stick blender or pestle and mortar."],[null,"Prick the chicken with a sharp knife and add to a food bag with the jerk seasoning. Leave for at least six hours or overnight, if possible."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 190°C/gas 5. Spread the marinated chicken out onto a baking tray and bake for 25 minutes, until crisp and golden and starting to char on the edges."],[null,"Alternatively, if barbecuing cover in foil and cook in the oven for 20 minutes. Then switch to the barbecue for another 10 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"*The recipe contains soy sauce which may contain gluten. If following a gluten-free diet please check the label for a gluten-free version."],[null,"Try serving with rice and peas and plenty of salad."],[null,"You could use this marinade on fish fillets, large prawns or cubes of tofu."],[null,"You can add the chicken and jerk seasoning to a food bag, mix well and freeze it ready for future use."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"7014881":{"s":[[null,"Using a sharp knife, slash the chicken flesh a few times and place in a non-metallic dish. Dry fry the allspice berries for 2–3 minutes until fragrant, then tip into a mortar and pound to a powder. Add the remaining jerk ingredients and pound to a thick paste. Stir into the chicken to coat evenly. Cover and leave to marinate overnight if you have time, or for at least 1 hour."],[null,"Meanwhile, cut out and discard the core of the pineapple and slice the flesh. Heat a chargrill pan until smoking. Spray the pineapple with low-calorie cooking spray and chargrill for 2 mins on each side until pleasantly charred with lines."],[null,"Preheat the grill to high. Place the chicken on a grill rack over a baking tray and grill for 20–25 minutes, turning occasionally until cooked through (check with a meat thermometer or by pushing a metal skewer into the thickest part of the chicken – if the juices run clear it is cooked. If not, pop back under the grill for 4–5 mins, then test again)."],[null,"While the chicken is cooking, toss together the carrots, apples and cider vinegar. Season with freshly ground black pepper and sprinkle over the seeds. Serve with the chicken and salsa. Scatter a little extra coriander and red chilli over the chicken if desired."]],"h":[[null,"This recipe is high in protein and vitamin C and is a source of iron."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"3256":{"s":[[null,"Peel jicama and carrot. Cut both into 1/4-inch match stick cuts and place in a medium bowl."],[null,"Finely dice red onion and add to jicama and carrots."],[null,"Cut grapes in half and add to vegetables."],[null,"Cut basil leaves into small pieces and add to bowl."],[null,"Drizzle apple cider vinegar, lemon juice and lime juice over other ingredients."],[null,"Mix and chill before serving."]],"h":[[null,"For variety, you can substitute other low potassium fruits for the seedless grapes. Try apples, pineapple or strawberries."],[null,"1/2 of a medium-sized red onion is about 1/2 cup."],[null,"1 medium jicama yields 3 cups."],[null,"1 large carrot yields 1 cup."]]},"7651076":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a large pan then add the onion and cook 3-4 minutes until starting to brown."],[null,"Add the chicken chunks and cook a further 3-4 minutes, stirring regularly to make sure the chicken cooks evenly."],[null,"Add the red and yellow peppers and stir another 2 minutes then add the garlic, ginger, chili and tomato purée and mix well."],[null,"Now add the rice and mix again, stirring for a minute to coat all the rice with the tomato purée mixture."],[null,"Add the stock and tomatoes and mix well, bring to the boil then reduce the heat, cover and simmer for 8 minutes."],[null,"Scatter the okra on top of the rice, replace the lid and simmer a further 5 minutes."],[null,"Now turn off the heat but don’t remove the lid and leave to stand for 5 minutes. Add the coriander, mix well and serve."]],"h":[[null,"You could make this dish with lamb, beef or turkey"],[null,"For a vegetarian/vegan version try adding chunks of courgette, aubergine and marinated tofu in place of chicken and use a vegetable stock cube."],[null,"For a seafood version use a fish stock cube and add cubes of salmon or some prawns along with the okra."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Chill quickly. Defrost in the fridge and reheat thoroughly until piping hot throughout. Eat immediately and discard any leftovers."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"2256":{"s":[[null,"Cut chicken into small cubes and season with Mrs. Dash® seasoning."],[null,"Chop carrots, green beans, bell peppers, and cauliflower. Finely chop garlic and jalapeno peppers."],[null,"Combine the chopped carrots, green beans, bell peppers and cauliflower in a bowl. Divide in half."],[null,"Heat oil in a frying pan over medium-high heat. Add chicken pieces and fry until golden brown."],[null,"Move chicken to a large saucepan. Add 3-cups chicken stock and bring to a boil. Reduce to a simmer and cook until chicken begins to soften."],[null,"Place onion, garlic and jalapeno peppers in the frying pan used to brown chicken. Sauté until tender. Add the tomatoes, tomato paste, half the chopped vegetables and 1-cup reserved chicken stock. Simmer for 5 to 7 minutes, stirring frequently."],[null,"Add cooked vegetable mixture to the saucepan with chicken and stock; simmer for 3 minutes. Stir in uncooked rice and continue simmering for 15 minutes."],[null,"Place remaining chopped vegetables on top of rice. Simmer until rice absorbs all the stock and is fully cooked (add additional water if needed)."],[null,"Garnish and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Jollof Rice is of West Africa origins and the name means \"one pot\"."],[null,"Homemade chicken stock is always best—it’s full of flavor and much lower in sodium compared to regular or reduced-sodium broth."],[null,"Use disposable gloves when chopping hot peppers. Remove the seeds and membrane inside for a milder heat."],[null,"Try substituting beef for chicken for a variation of this recipe."]]},"3664":{"s":[[null,"Crush raspberries and chop tarragon."],[null,"Whisk together first 7 ingredients."],[null,"Slowly whisk in oil until well blended. Serve."],[null,"Store remaining dressing in a tightly sealed jar and refrigerator until ready to serve. Keeps for up to one week."]],"h":[[null,"Two fresh limes yield approximately 1/4 cup lime juice."],[null,"Drizzle 2 tablespoons dressing over salad greens topped with fresh raspberries."],[null,"Substitute low sugar preserves or fruit spread to reduce carbohydrate to 5 grams."],[null,"Substitute 1/4 teaspoon dried terragon if fresh is unavailable."],[null,"Grape seed oil is a great tasting substitute for canola oil."]]},"6926611":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, stir together the yogurt, honey, and vanilla."],[null,"Spritz the cut side of peach halves with cooking spray and place the peaches cut-side-down on a hot grill. Grill until grill marks start to form, and the peaches are heated through, 2-3 minutes."],[null,"Place each peach half onto a small plate, cut-side up. Top each half with the yogurt mixture, almonds, and mint, and serve."]],"h":[]},"7176015":{"s":[[null,"Put the oil in a pan over a medium heat, add the onions and stir for 7–10 minutes until well browned."],[null,"Add the carrot and celery and cook for a further 2–3 minutes stirring regularly."],[null,"Now add the garlic, cumin, tomato purée, lentils and mix well."],[null,"Add the stock, bring to the boil, turn down the heat, cover and simmer gently for 12 minutes."],[null,"Add the kale, replace the lid and simmer a further 5 minutes, season with pepper and serve."]],"h":[[null,"You could use any stock, such as chicken or beef. Stock can be high in salt so choose reduced-salt options whenever possible."],[null,"Try adding a shredded chicken breast or pieces of marinated or smoked tofu."],[null,"You can also add other vegetables, such as peppers, courgettes, broccoli or tinned sweetcorn."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Freeze in portions then defrost in the fridge, or defrost in a microwave, taking care to stir regularly."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"6012711":{"s":[[null,"Rinse the dry quinoa in a strainer under cold running water. Combine the rinsed quinoa and water in a medium sauce pan and bring to a boil. Reduce to a simmer and cover. Cook the quinoa for 12-15 minutes until all the liquid is absorbed. Turn off the heat and leave the lid on for 10 minutes to steam. Spread the quinoa on a sheet pan to cool."],[null,"In a large salad bowl, whisk together the vinegar, garlic, mustard, honey, parsley, salt (optional), and pepper. Add the olive oil and whisk until emulsified."],[null,"In the same bowl, toss together the kale, cranberries, sunflower seeds, feta cheese and cooled quinoa until coated with dressing."]],"h":[]},"6488782":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, whisk together the yogurt, garlic, mustard, olive oil, lemon juice, water, salt, and black pepper."],[null,"Add the kale, cabbage, and apple to the bowl and toss to evenly coat. Cover and place in the refrigerator for 30 minutes before serving for the flavors to combine."]],"h":[]},"6689398":{"s":[[null,"Cook pasta according to package directions. Drain."],[null,"While the pasta is cooking, place kale, lemon juice, pepper, salt, parmesan cheese, garlic, and walnuts in a food processor. With the processor running, pour the olive oil through the feed tube in a steady stream. Use a spatula to push the pesto down the sides of the bowl and continue blending until the pesto is smooth."],[null,"Place the pasta in a large bowl and toss with the pesto and tomatoes. Garnish with parmesan cheese if desired."]],"h":[]},"6951554":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F. Coat a baking sheet with cooking spray and set aside."],[null,"In a blender or food processor, blend the kale, walnuts, garlic, olive oil, water, lemon juice, Parmesan cheese, and pepper until smooth."],[null,"Lay the salmon filets skin side down on the baking sheet. Spread the top of each salmon filet with 1/4 of the pesto."],[null,"Bake the salmon for 20 minutes."]],"h":[]},"6072658":{"s":[[null,"In a large salad bowl, combine the chopped kale and toasted almonds."],[null,"To make the dressing: In a small saucepan, combine pitted cherries, finely chopped shallot, balsamic vinegar, and Dijon mustard."],[null,"Heat the mixture over medium heat, stirring occasionally, until the cherries are warmed through and begin to break down, about 5 minutes."],[null,"Remove the saucepan from heat and let the cherry mixture cool slightly."],[null,"Transfer the cherry mixture to a blender or food processor. Add olive oil, salt, and black pepper."],[null,"Blend until the vinaigrette is smooth."],[null,"Pour the warm vinaigrette over the kale salad."],[null,"Toss the salad gently to ensure even coating."],[null,"Finish with the shaved parmesan."]],"h":[]},"2835":{"s":[[null,"Remove kale from stalks and finely chop. Measure 3 cups for slaw. Chop shallots."],[null,"Shred Brussels sprouts and measure 2 cups."],[null,"In a medium bowl, combine kale, Brussels sprouts, cranberries and shallots."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine olive oil, vinegar, honey, Mrs. Dash seasoning blend, mustard and pepper. Pour over vegetables and mix."],[null,"Refrigerate for 30 minutes before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Kale slaw keeps in the refrigerator for 5 days."],[null,"For a variation, heat the slaw and stir-fry for a hot dish."]]},"6955418":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a large soup pot over medium-high heat. Add the onion and green peppers, and sauté for 3 minutes or until clear. Add the garlic and sauté for 30 seconds."],[null,"Add the turkey and cook it about 8 minutes until brown. Add the remaining ingredients except for the Parmesan cheese."],[null,"Bring the soup to a boil; then reduce the heat and simmer for 15 minutes."],[null,"Remove the soup from the heat and stir in the Parmesan cheese."]],"h":[]},"7353647":{"s":[[null,"Rinse the basmati rice in water and add to a pan with 700ml boiling water (1 part rice to 2 parts water). Add 1 heaped tsp of the curry paste and all the smoked paprika, mix bring back to the boil, cover, reduce the heat and simmer for 10-12 minutes. Turn off the heat and leave to stand for 3 minutes with the lid on. All the water should then be absorbed."],[null,"Meanwhile, boil 4 eggs for 5 minutes, refresh in cold water, peel and cut into quarters."],[null,"Heat the sunflower oil in a frying pan and add the leeks and red pepper. Cook for 5–7 minutes, stirring regularly, until they’re soft."],[null,"Mix the remaining curry paste with the leeks and pepper abd add the salmon. Cook for 3–4 minutes and set aside."],[null,"Add the lemon juice, yogurt and coriander to the rice and mix well."],[null,"Fold the vegetable and salmon mixture into the hot rice and top with the egg quarters, lemon wedges and a sprig of coriander."]],"h":[[null,"Kedgeree can easily be made vegan if you omit the eggs and use mushrooms or smoked tofu instead of fish."],[null,"You could use any white fish, such as cod or haddock, or add some prawns, too. Parsley works well if you don’t have coriander."],[null,"For a quicker dish, you could use ready-cooked rice and add the paprika to the vegetables and salmon. Eggs can be hard boiled the day before and kept in the fridge."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"4386278":{"s":[[null,"Mix the eggs, sugar, non-dairy creamer and vanilla in a shallow dish or pie pan. Soak the bread in mixture until soft, turning once. In another large, shallow baking dish spread the cornflakes, then coat all the soaked bread slices with cornflakes on each side."],[null,"Add the margarine to a skillet or frying pan and cook the bread slices over medium high heat, turning to brown on each side. Mix cinnamon and sugar together in a separate bowl. Sprinkle over top of slices and serve."]],"h":[]},"1975":{"s":[[null,"Prepare spaghetti according to package directions, but omit the salt."],[null,"In a large skillet, brown ground beef with onion. Drain fat."],[null,"Add brown sugar, Italian seasonings and garlic powder. Cook for 2 minutes."],[null,"Add spaghetti sauce and simmer for 5 to 10 minutes."],[null,"Drain pasta and stir into the sauce."],[null,"Toss and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Brown sugar takes the harshness out of the tomato sauce. Kent’s children love the sauce prepared this way."],[null,"Check labels on spaghetti sauce and select a brand lower in sodium."],[null,"Spaghetti sauce, like other tomato products, is high in potassium. By limiting the portion to 1/4-cup per serving, this recipe is acceptable for a low-potassium diet."],[null,"Suggested sides include iceberg lettuce with low-sodium Italian dressing, Italian bread toasted with garlic spread and a small glass of lemon-lime soda."],[null,"Refrigerate or freeze leftovers for a quick meal later."],[null,"If you do not like whole wheat spaghetti, white spaghetti may be substituted."]]},"7392822":{"s":[[null,"Rinse the split peas and add to a pan with boiling water to fully cover them. Simmer for 40 minutes, then drain."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the oil to a pan with the onion and cook for 3-4 minutes."],[null,"Add the garlic, butternut squash and curry paste, then cook for 2 minutes, stirring regularly."],[null,"Add the tomatoes and water, mix well, then bring to the boil. Turn down the heat, cover, then leave to simmer for 10 minutes."],[null,"Add the aubergine, cover, and cook for 5 minutes."],[null,"Next, add the okra, mix well, cover and cook for a further 5 minutes, before add the spinach and mix again. Cover and cook for 2-3 more minutes."],[null,"Check the split peas are tender then drain and add to the pan along with the coriander and yogurt. Mix well and serve scattered with pomegranate, cucumber, spring onion and chilli."]],"h":[[null,"Try using other vegetables such as carrots, courgettes, mushrooms, peppers and any type of squash."],[null,"For a vegan version, use a non-dairy yogurt or oat-based cream alternative in place of yogurt."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked, without the toppings. Defrost in the fridge and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 6"]]},"1819":{"s":[[null,"In a medium pan, combine pudding mix, rice milk, lime juice, lime zest and food coloring. Cook and stir over medium heat until thickened. Refrigerate to chill."],[null,"Heat oven to 350° F (325° F for dark or nonstick pan). Spray bottom only of a 9″ x 13″ baking pan with baking flour."],[null,"In a large bowl, beat cake mix, water, egg whites and oil with an electric mixer on low speed 30 seconds, then on medium speed 2 minutes, scraping bowl occasionally. Pour into pan."],[null,"Bake for 25 to 35 minutes or until toothpick inserted in center comes out clean. Cool 5 minutes. With handle of wooden spoon (1/4″ to 1/2″ diameter), poke holes almost to bottom of cake every 1/2 inch, wiping spoon handle occasionally to reduce sticking."],[null,"Remove pudding mixture from refrigerator and set aside 1-1/2 cups to add to icing. Pour remaining filling mixture over cake. Spread over cake surface, working back and forth to fill holes. Some filling should remain on the top of the cake. Refrigerate for one hour."],[null,"Mix frosting and reserved filling in a bowl and whip together. Frost cake and garnish with lime zest."]],"h":[[null,"In addition to grated lime peel you can garnish with fresh strawberries, lemon leaves and key lime slices."],[null,"Store cake loosely covered in the refrigerator."],[null,"Instant pudding mix is very high in phosphorus. Do not substitute."],[null,"May use 4 packages of shelf stable Snack Pack Sugar Free Vanilla Pudding® cups to replace pudding mix and rice milk. Place in a bowl and stir in lime zest and food coloring. Mix half with frosting and spread the other half over cake."]]},"6788786":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F. Spray a baking sheet with cooking spray"],[null,"In a shallow dish, mix together the cornmeal, garlic powder, black pepper, and thyme."],[null,"In another shallow baking dish, whisk together the egg, egg whites, and hot sauce."],[null,"Dip a chicken breast strip in the egg mixture, and then drench in the cornmeal mixture. Coat well and place on baking sheet. Repeat procedure for the rest of the chicken strips."],[null,"Bake for 30 minutes or until done (internal temperature of 165 degrees F). Turn chicken pieces over half way through cooking time."]],"h":[]},"6912677":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350 degrees F."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the ketchup and vinegar for the sauce."],[null,"In a medium bowl, mix together remaining ingredients for the meatballs. Shape into 1-inch balls."],[null,"Place meatballs on a baking sheet and top evenly with sauce (11/2 Tsp. per meatball)."],[null,"Bake for 45 minutes or until done."]],"h":[]},"6466720":{"s":[[null,"In a blender mix together all ingredients until smooth."],[null,"Pour smoothie mixture evenly into 4 ice pop molds. Insert ice pop handle on top. Place upright and freeze until solid; about 3 hours."]],"h":[]},"6571661":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a large nonstick skillet over medium-high heat. Add the onion, bell pepper, and garlic, and cook, stirring occasionally, until the vegetables are tender, about 8 minutes."],[null,"Add the pumpkin, beans, broth, tomato sauce, salt, and pepper and bring to a boil. Reduce the heat to medium. Cover and cook until the pumpkin is tender, 10–12 minutes. Toss in the cilantro and stir."]],"h":[]},"3215":{"s":[[null,"Wash the outside of the kiwis and remove the skin. Dice."],[null,"Wash apples, strawberries and raspberries. Core the apples, then dice. Cut the tops off the strawberries; dice the strawberries and raspberries."],[null,"Place all the fruit in a bowl, and add brown sugar and preserves. Stir gently until well mixed."],[null,"Chill salsa in the refrigerator overnight."]],"h":[[null,"Serve with low-sodium crackers or tortilla chips. Look for brands with the lowest amounts of sodium"],[null,"You may also serve with homemade pita chips. Split the pitas in half and cut each half into quarters. Spray with cooking spray and bake at 350º F for about 8 minutes. If desired, sprinkle a mixture of cinnamon and sugar after you spray the pita with cooking spray."],[null,"Drain salsa in a fine sieve to remove extra fluid if you are on a fluid restriction."]]},"2514":{"s":[[null,"Place all ingredients in a blender."],[null,"Blend until smooth and serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"Kool-Aid® Liquid Drink Mix does not contain phosphate additives like the powdered Kool-Aid."]]},"6531377":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400° F. Line a large rimmed baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Place the salmon, skin side down, on the baking sheet."],[null,"In a small bowl, stir together the ketchup, jam, tamari, vinegar, and hot pepper sauce. Lightly spread the mixture onto the top of each fillet using the back of the spoon. Sprinkle with the sesame seeds."],[null,"Bake until the salmon is flaky and cooked through (with an internal temperature of at least 145°F), about 16 minutes. Serve."]],"h":[]},"6410409":{"s":[[null,"In the bowl of a food processor, pulse the garlic, pear, onion, and ginger until smooth. Transfer the mixture to a medium bowl."],[null,"Add the chicken, scallion, soy sauce, sesame oil, and pepper to the bowl. Stir to coat, then refrigerate for at least 30 minutes. While the chicken marinates, prepare the garnishes and keep the lettuce leaves fresh."],[null,"Preheat a large cast iron skillet or sauté pan over high heat."],[null,"Add the chicken and any remaining marinade to the hot pan. Cook, stirring frequently, until most of the liquid has evaporated and the chicken is browned, about 10 minutes. Sprinkle with sesame seeds."],[null,"To serve, place a lettuce leaf in your palm. Add brown rice, chicken, and any desired garnishes. Dab with gochujang, wrap, and enjoy."]],"h":[]},"2030":{"s":[[null,"Combine vinegar with soy sauce in a small bowl. Set aside until ready to serve fish."],[null,"Rinse fish and pat dry with a paper towel. Cut each fish fillet into 1-1/2″ pieces."],[null,"Place flour and pepper in a zip-top bag. Add fish, seal and shake to coat."],[null,"In a small bowl, beat eggs lightly."],[null,"Heat sesame oil in a large skillet."],[null,"Dip each piece of flour-coated fish into beaten eggs to coat. Place in hot oil and fry until golden brown, turning once."],[null,"Divide into 4 portions and serve hot. Sprinkle 1 teaspoon vinegar-soy sauce mixture on each portion."]],"h":[[null,"If white fish is unavailable, substitute catfish, cod, orange roughy or tilapia."],[null,"Drain cooked fish on paper towels to soak up extra oil."],[null,"Measure vinegar-soy sauce to help keep sodium content low."],[null,"For a low protein diet, reduce portion to match your meal plan or consult your dietitian."]]},"3637":{"s":[[null,"Peel and grate the potato, then soak in warm water for 2 hours to reduce potassium. Rinse, drain and squeeze excess water using a clean dish towel."],[null,"Grate the white onion; dice the red onion and shred the lettuce."],[null,"Mix ground beef, white onion, grated potato, egg, turmeric, garlic powder, black pepper and Mrs. Dash seasoning until well mixed."],[null,"Heat the oil in a medium-size skillet."],[null,"Make 5 patties (round, the size of your palm) and fry over medium heat until browned on both sides."],[null,"Serve each patty on a pita with lettuce, red onion and fresh basil."]],"h":[[null,"French bread, lavash, hamburger buns or tortillas are also good bread choices."],[null,"Use less oil and a non-stick pan to lower calorie and fat."],[null,"It’s easy to get very creative with Kotlets by adding or substituting various ingredients. Serve cold or hot for lunch, dinner or as an appetizer."],[null,"Shredded hash brown potatoes can be substituted for fresh potato. No need to soak potatoes if you are not on a potassium restriction."]]},"6952098":{"s":[[null,"Whisk together the rice vinegar, soy sauce, toasted sesame oil, honey, and cornstarch in a small bowl. Whisk until the cornstarch has dissolved and the sauce is smooth."],[null,"Heat the vegetable oil in a 12-inch skillet over medium-high heat. Once the pan is hot, add the ginger, garlic, and chili-garlic sauce and sauté until fragrant, about 15 seconds."],[null,"Add the chicken to the skillet and cook and stir until browned and no longer pink inside, 3–5 minutes."],[null,"Stir in the bell peppers and cook until slightly softened, about 2 minutes."],[null,"Pour in the sauce and stir to coat the stir fry. Simmer the sauce until it has thickened and is heated through, about 2 minutes."]],"h":[]},"2155822":{"s":[[null,"In a deep frying pan, place the onions in the vegetable oil over a low heat until golden."],[null,"Take it out from the heat, add the lamb and stir until it mixes."],[null,"When the mutton becomes brown, add spices, salt and crushed garlic."],[null,"Add potatoes, tomatoes, and mixed tomato paste; keep the pan on medium heat until the lamb is tender."],[null,"When serving, place the bread on a serving plate, then add potatoes and lamb with vegetables over the bread. Garnish with crushed parsley"]],"h":[[null,"The seven Arabic spices usually contain black pepper, cumin, cinnamon, cloves, garlic powder and ground black lemon, all crushed and mixed together."]]},"7268954":{"s":[[null,"Add the oil to a saucepan over a low to medium heat, add the lamb and heat for 5 minutes."],[null,"Add the onion and gently brown for 5-7 minutes, stirring regularly."],[null,"Add the leeks, carrots and cubed sweet potatoes, stir 2-3 minutes."],[null,"Sprinkle the vegetables with flour and mix well ensuring all pieces are coated."],[null,"Stir in the stock and add the split peas, bay leaf and white pepper."],[null,"Cover and simmer gently for 45 minutes, stirring occasionally, and adding water if more liquid is needed. After about 30 minutes preheat your oven to 180C/gas 4."],[null,"Remove from the heat and add to an ovenproof dish. Arrange the sweet potato slices on top. Bake for 15-20 minutes until the potato is golden brown and crisping at the edges."]],"h":[[null,"You could make this dish with beef, chicken pieces, turkey or lentils."],[null,"Any root vegetables work well – try a combination of carrots, swede and turnip."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Freeze in portions then defrost in the fridge, or defrost in a microwave, taking care to stir regularly."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"7454682":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a large pan, add the onion and fry for 3-4 minutes until lightly golden. Remove ¼ of the onion and set aside."],[null,"Add the lamb, garlic, ginger, cinnamon stick, cardamom, cloves and peppercorns to the pan and fry for 8-10 minutes until the lamb is lightly browned all over."],[null,"Stir the chilli powder and ground coriander into 2 bsps boiling water, then pour into the pan. Cover the pan and cook the meat over a low heat. Cook for 40-45 minutes until the meat is tender."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 150ºC/gas 2. Add the yogurt to the pan and stir. Meanwhile, place the reserved onion in a pan and continue to fry for 5-6 minutes until dark brown."],[null,"Place ⅓ of the rice into the base of a heavy casserole dish, drizzle over a little of the saffron mixture. Layer over half of the meat mixture and cover with another ⅓ of the rice and sprinkle with a little saffron mixture. Repeat, finishing with a layer of rice and drizzling with saffron. Press down lightly. Place the onion on top."],[null,"Cover the pan with a tight fitting lid and cook for 10 minutes. Remove from the oven, sprinkle with fresh coriander and serve."]],"h":[[null,"You could also use chicken for this dish."],[null,"For a vegetarian version, add a selection of chopped vegetables such as peppers, aubergines and mushrooms in place of lamb. They will only need 5 minutes to cook before adding to the rice."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Chill quickly. Defrost in the fridge and reheat thoroughly until piping hot throughout. Eat immediately and discard any leftovers."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6348205":{"s":[[null,"Combine 1 tbsp olive oil, garlic, salt, pepper, and rosemary. Fully coat lamb chops and marinate for 2 hours in the refrigerator. Remove from the refrigerator 30 minutes before grilling."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 450°F. Spray a sheet pan with cooking spray"],[null,"Place the potatoes in a bowl and toss with 1 tsp olive oil and 2 tbsp chopped rosemary. Place them on the sheet pan and place them in the middle of the preheated oven and roast for 10 minutes."],[null,"In the same bowl, place the carrots and toss with the remaining oil and rosemary. Add to the potatoes along with the asparagus and continue roasting for 10 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, preheat the grill and place the lamb chops directly on the grill. Grill for 5 minutes, then flip the chops and continue grilling for 3 – 5 minutes. They should reach an internal temperature of 135°F."]],"h":[]},"6454224":{"s":[[null,"Combine 1 tbsp olive oil, garlic, salt, pepper, and rosemary. Fully coat lamb chops and marinate for 2 hours in the refrigerator. Remove from the refrigerator 30 minutes before grilling."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 450°F. Spray a sheet pan with cooking spray"],[null,"Place the potatoes in a bowl and toss with 1 tsp olive oil and 2 tbsp chopped rosemary. Place them on the sheet pan and place them in the middle of the preheated oven and roast for 10 minutes."],[null,"In the same bowl, place the carrots and toss with the remaining oil and rosemary. Add to the potatoes along with the asparagus and continue roasting for 10 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, preheat the grill and place the lamb chops directly on the grill. Grill for 5 minutes, then flip the chops and continue grilling for 3 – 5 minutes. They should reach an internal temperature of 135°F."]],"h":[]},"7605212":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a pan and add the lamb and onions. Cook for 5 minutes stirring regularly until starting to brown."],[null,"Add all the other ingredients, except the coriander, stir and bring to the boil. Put the lid on, reduce the heat and simmer gently for 2–2.5 hours stirring regularly, until the lamb is tender. Add a little more water if needed."],[null,"Serve with a sprinkle of coriander."]],"h":[[null,"For a lower fat version, use chicken thighs – they will cook more quickly so reduce the cooking time by an hour."],[null,"Be warned, Scotch bonnet chillies may be very small – but they're also very hot!"],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"7161543":{"s":[[null,"Add the oil to a pan, then add the onion and cook for 3-4 minutes until starting to brown."],[null,"Add the lamb and cook for a further 4-5 minutes, until well browned. Add the carrots, garlic and ginger and cook for a further 2-3 minutes, stirring regularly."],[null,"Add the lentils, stock, tomatoes and curry paste and mix well. Bring to the boil, add a lid, reduce the heat, then simmer for 1 hour."],[null,"Add the sweet potato and aubergine, mix and cover again. Simmer for a further 20 minutes."],[null,"Check the lamb is tender. If not, simmer for another 10-15 minutes. Stir in the fresh coriander, saving a little for the top, and serve."]],"h":[[null,"You can make this dish with any lean meat, such as beef."],[null,"For a speedy version, use cubed chicken or turkey and simmer for 15 minutes instead of 1 hour, before adding the sweet potato and aubergine."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"7427026":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 190°C/gas mark 5. Add the lamb to a non-stick frying pan and cook for 4-5 minutes, turning regularly to seal the outside."],[null,"Make the pistou by blending all the ingredients together into a paste, then set aside."],[null,"Add the rapeseed oil to a saucepan with the red and yellow peppers and the courgette. Cook for 5-6 minutes, stirring regularly,"],[null,"Add the spring onions, lentils, beans and mustard, then mix well. Add the stock, put a lid on the pan, turn the heat low and simmer gently for 10 minutes, stirring occasionally."],[null,"Meanwhile, sprinkle the lamb with oregano and black pepper, put on a baking sheet and bake for 5-7 minutes for pink or 10-12 for well done. Remove from the oven and allow to rest for 5 minutes before slicing thinly."],[null,"Plate up the lentils, arrange the sliced lamb on top, then drizzle with the pistou."]],"h":[[null,"You can use chicken breast in place of lamb, but it will need an extra 10 minutes in the oven. Check the meat is cooked right through and no pink flesh is visible before serving."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. For best results, freeze the pilaf, pistou and lamb separately. Defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat the pilaf and lamb until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"3083":{"s":[[null,"Measure water and put in a stew pot."],[null,"Trim fat from meat and cut into bite-size pieces. Add meat and bones to water. Set on stove over medium heat."],[null,"Coarsely chop onion. Cut zucchini in half lengthwise and sliced into 1/2” slices"],[null,"Add onion, zucchini and chilies to stew."],[null,"Once the stew has come to a low boil, turn heat to low and let simmer for at least 1 hour."],[null,"While stew is cooking, mix flour, salt, baking powder and sugar in a bowl."],[null,"Knead in warm water to dry ingredients to form a soft ball of dough."],[null,"Cover dough and let it rest for 20 to 30 minutes."],[null,"After cooking stew for 1 hour, shape an approximately 2-1/2” dough ball into a flat round. (It does not need to be perfect or flat)."],[null,"Tear off penny-sized pieces of dough and drop them into the stew."],[null,"Continue to shape 2-1/2” dough ball into a flat round and tear off penny-sized pieces of dough and drop in stew until all dough is in stew."],[null,"Cook dumplings in the stew for an additional 20 minutes."],[null,"Serve and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Roast 2-3 Hatch chilies instead of canned chilies."]]},"7709454":{"s":[[null,"Add the oil to a large pan. Add the onions and stir for 2 minutes over a medium heat. Next, add the red, yellow and green peppers and stir for a further 2 minutes. Add the garlic and courgettes, and stir for 2-3 minutes."],[null,"Add the rosemary, thyme, oregano and parsley to the vegetables, and then stir in the tomatoes. Cover and simmer gently for 10 minutes, stirring occasionally."],[null,"Meanwhile, grill the lamb steaks and cook until well done."],[null,"Remove the meat from the heat, cover and leave to rest for 3 minutes. Serve with the Provençal sauce and a green salad."]],"h":[[null,"The Provençal sauce for this dish works well with any meat, such as turkey escalopes, or with grilled fish."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"7308963":{"s":[[null,"Add oil to a pan, then add the onion and cook for 3 minutes until starting to brown. Add the lamb and stir for another couple of minutes to brown the outside."],[null,"Add the carrots, yellow pepper, tomatoes, mint, cinnamon, cumin, chilli flakes, 200ml water and salt. Bring to a gentle boil, turn the heat down, add a lid and simmer gently for 30 minutes, stirring regularly."],[null,"Add the apricots and chickpeas, and simmer for another 15 minutes."],[null,"Serve with couscous, rice or flatbread, and salad."]],"h":[[null,"For best value, try using dried chickpeas. Soak and cook the whole packet of chickpeas, following the instructions on the pack, and then freeze them. You can defrost what you need and add them to all sorts of dishes, such as stews, soups, curries and salads."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"6203520":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375°F. Coat a 12-cup standard muffin pan with cooking spray."],[null,"Add one wonton wrapper to the bottom of each cup, pressing down into the center with the pointed ends set up."],[null,"Mix together the ricotta and mozzarella cheeses, egg, dried oregano, and black pepper. Add a scant tablespoon of the cheese mixture over the wonton wrapper. Lay a basil leaf on top of the cheese. Add a tablespoon of the marinara sauce over the basil leaf. Repeat all the layers one more time ending with sauce. Sprinkle the top of each muffin with Parmesan."],[null,"Bake the lasagna muffins for 18-20 minutes until bubbly and browned. Remove from the oven and let cool for 5 minutes. Run a knife around each cup to loosen. Remove from the pan and serve."]],"h":[]},"9277390":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400℉/204℃ and line a large baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Brush your mushrooms clean and scrape out the gills using a metal teaspoon. Use caution to avoid breaking the mushrooms. Then place them stem side down on your tray. Sprinkle the tops with salt and pepper and bake for 10 minutes. This step allows some moisture to escape the mushrooms so that they won't be watery later."],[null,"Meanwhile, sauté the spinach in a skillet or pan to wilt it over medium heat. Add a drop or two of water if needed to get it going. Stir often to prevent sticking. Once wilted, squeeze as much liquid out of the spinach as possible using a clean dish towel, nut milk bag, or paper towel. Set aside."],[null,"Add the ricotta cheese ingredients EXCEPT the spinach to a food processor. Process until smooth, scraping down the sides as needed. Once smooth, add the spinach and pulse 3-4 times to get it incorporated. Do NOT over-process or the cheese will turn green."],[null,"Next, combine all the bolognese sauce ingredients into a small bowl. Stir and set aside."],[null,"Remove the mushrooms from the oven and flip them stem side up. Absorb the excess moisture by blotting the mushrooms with a clean dish towel or paper towel."],[null,"Divide the ricotta between your six mushrooms. Then top each one with the bolognese sauce. Bake the stuffed mushrooms for 10-12 minutes, remove from the oven, and serve with fresh parsley, red pepper flakes, and/or vegan parmesan cheese."]],"h":[[null,"If you don’t have a powerful food processor , soak the cashews in boiling hot water for 15-30 minutes, and then drain, before making your ricotta cheese."],[null,"If using frozen spinach , measure out about 1 cup and thaw and squeeze out as much moisture as possible using a nut milk bag , dish cloth or paper towels."],[null,"Do not overprocess the spinach when making the ricotta . Just pulse a few times to get it mixed in. You want to see ribbons of spinach throughout your ricotta, and not green cheese."],[null,"To make these into appetizers , use about 2-3 times as many mushroom caps or cremini mushrooms, depending on their size."],[null,"If planning ahead , make the ricotta cheese and the bolognese sauce and refrigerate them separately for 2-3 days in advance. Then stuff and bake your mushrooms the day of serving."],[null,"Leftovers will keep refrigerated for 2-3 days in a sealed container."]]},"6169270":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425ºF. Lightly spray a small baking sheet with nonstick spray."],[null,"Place baking sheet in oven for 10 minutes to heat prior to putting the chicken cutlets on it."],[null,"Whisk together the lime juice, egg white, soy sauce, oregano, and garlic in a medium bowl."],[null,"Place the panko, adobo seasoning, and salt on a sheet of wax paper. Dip the chicken, one piece at a time, into the lime mixture then into the panko mixture, pressing lightly so the crumbs adhere."],[null,"Place the chicken on the baking sheet. Lightly spray with nonstick spray. Bake, without turning, until the crust is golden and the chicken is cooked through, about 20 minutes."]],"h":[]},"5174250":{"s":[[null,"Mix the Renastep, water, semolina and sugar well in a pan and gently warm on a low to medium heat stirring continuously and scraping the bottom to stop the semolina sticking to the pan."],[null,"Once the mixture starts to simmer, lower the heat to minimum, add the ground mastika and continue stirring."],[null,"When the mixture starts to thicken, remove from the heat, add the rose water and orange blossom water and stir well."],[null,"Pour the pudding into a bowl and leave to cool for about 40 minutes."],[null,"Once the pudding has rested and cooled, place in the fridge for 5-10 minutes to chill."],[null,"Whip the cream to form soft peaks."],[null,"Serve with whipped cream and finely chopped pistachios if permitted."]],"h":[[null,"Pour permitted syrup or honey over to serve."],["Renastep note","Renastep is a Food for Special Medical Purposes and must be used under medical supervision. Renastep is a ready to use feed for the dietary management of kidney disease from 3 years of age onwards. Renastep contains milk and fish. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information. This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutrimen dietary analysis software."]]},"6079494":{"s":[],"h":[]},"7585135":{"s":[[null,"Boil the potatoes whole for 15-20 minutes until just cooked. Refresh in cool water and set aside to cool for 15 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, place the leeks into a bowl with the yogurt, chives and parsley, mustard and pepper. Mix together well to ensure all the leeks are coated. Set aside in the fridge."],[null,"When the potatoes are cool, cut in half and toss in the yogurt dressing and sprinkle with more herbs."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"4788811":{"s":[[null,"CRUST: 1½ cups crushed graham crackers, 1 tablespoon sugar and 6 tablespoons unsalted butter, melted. FILLING: 2½ pounds cream cheese, 1½ cups sugar, 5 eggs, ¼ cup sour cream, 1 teaspoon almond extract, 1 teaspoon lemon zest. TOPPING: Mix ½ cup sour cream with ½ teaspoon vanilla extract and 1 teaspoon sugar."],[null,"Preheat oven to 350⁰ F."],[null,"Combine all ingredients for crust and press into round cake pan. Bake for 10 minutes and cool."],[null,"Mix all ingredients for filling with hand mixer at high speed until smooth and pour into crust."],[null,"Bake for 1 hour, then refrigerate for 4 hours."],[null,"Spread the sour cream topping mixture over top of chilled cheesecake and serve."]],"h":[]},"7536929":{"s":[[null,"Place the chicken in a non-metallic dish, add the lemon rind and juice and the garlic, combine and set aside for 30 minutes."],[null,"Heat the oil in a non-stick frying pan, add the mustard seeds and cumin seeds and fry for 1 minute until fragrant."],[null,"Add the chicken to the pan and fry for 2 minutes on each side. Then add the marinade to the pan along with 200ml boiling water, cover and simmer for 7–8 minutes, turning occasionally until cooked through."],[null,"Add the remaining ingredients, cook for a further 2 minutes, season well and serve."]],"h":[[null,"If you need to thicken the sauce slightly, mash a few of the chickpeas with a fork and stir them in."],[null,"Serve with different colourful vegetables to add interest and extra nutrition."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Then defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"3541":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F. Coat a 9 x 5-inch loaf pan with cooking spray and dust with flour."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine flour and baking powder."],[null,"In another bowl, mix oil, granulated sugar, milk, lemon extract and egg whites."],[null,"Add flour mixture to oil and sugar mixture. Stir just until blended; do not overmix."],[null,"Fold in blueberries and lemon peel."],[null,"Pour batter into loaf pan and bake for 40 to 50 minutes or until toothpick once inserted comes out clean."],[null,"Prepare glaze while bread is baking. In a small saucepan, combine powdered sugar and lemon juice. Heat until sugar is dissolved."],[null,"After removing bread from the oven, immediately poke holes at 1-inch intervals into the top and pour lemon glaze over bread."]],"h":[[null,"For people with diabetes reduce carbohydrates to 17 grams by substituting low calorie sweetener for sugar and omitting the lemon-sugar glaze."]]},"4835566":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375°F. Line a 12- cup muffin tin with paper muffin cups. In a large bowl, whisk together flour, baking powder and lemon zest. In another bowl, whisk together eggs, canola oil, soy milk and sugar substitute. Make well in center of dry ingredients; pour egg mixture and blueberries in center and stir just until evenly combined. Spoon batter evenly into prepared muffin pan. Bake 18-20 minutes until light golden brown, and toothpick inserted in center of muffin comes out clean. Cool on wire rack."]],"h":[[null,"Renal and Renal Diabetic Exchanges:"],[null,"1 Starch"],[null,"½ Fruit"],[null,"2 Fat"]]},"2380":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 450° F."],[null,"Beat sugar and butter until creamed. Add beaten egg yolks and stir."],[null,"Add flour, lemon peel, lemon juice and milk. Stir to mix."],[null,"Beat egg whites until stiff, but not dry, until peaks form. Fold egg whites into lemon mixture and mix gently—do not over mix."],[null,"Pour filling into pie shell and bake at 450° F for 10 minutes. Reduce heat to 325° F and continue baking for 20 minutes, or until filling sets and top is golden brown."]],"h":[[null,"Due to high carbohydrate content, people with diabetes are advised to reduced the portion to 1/2-piece of recommended serving size."]]},"2823":{"s":[[null,"Place bell peppers, green beans and carrots in an 8″ square baking dish."],[null,"Arrange chicken breasts over vegetables. Sprinkle evenly with lemon juice and olive oil."],[null,"In small bowl, combine black pepper and thyme. Mix well. Sprinkle evenly over chicken and vegetables."],[null,"Cover dish with plastic wrap. Microwave on high for 10 to12 minutes until chicken is no longer pink and juices are clear. (Rotate dish a half turn after 5 minutes if you do not have a rotating microwave.)"],[null,"Serve each chicken breast with 1/2 cup vegetables."]],"h":[[null,"Use frozen vegetables for an even faster meal."]]},"6460875":{"s":[[null,"Place lemon juice and sugar substitute in saucepan. Heat and stir until sugar dissolves. Remove from heat."],[null,"Crack eggs into the bowl and whisk well. Slowly pour the lemon sugar mix into the eggs while whisking. Whisk for 1 minute, then return the egg mixture to the saucepan."],[null,"Whisk and cook on low to medium for several minutes until the egg mixture thickens. (The more you whisk, the lighter the mixture will be.) This will take 2-5 minutes depending on your equipment. The mixture is ready to be removed from heat when it coats the back of a spoon."],[null,"Refrigerate for one hour or more. It will thicken more as it cools."],[null,"Place some of the lemon chiffon in a dessert glass or bowl and spoon berries over top. Alternate layers of lemon cream and berries. Top with berries."]],"h":[]},"3926":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F. Thaw frozen dessert topping."],[null,"Grease cookie sheets."],[null,"In a large bowl combine cake mix, dessert topping, egg and vanilla."],[null,"Drop one heaping teaspoon of dough into bowl of powdered sugar and coat. (It is not necessary to make dough into balls.) For larger cookies drop dough by tablespoon instead of teaspoon."],[null,"Drop powdered sugar coated dough onto a greased cookie sheet."],[null,"Bake for 10 minutes."],[null,"Let cookies cool for 2 minutes before removing from the baking sheet."]],"h":[[null,"Cookies may not appear fully cooked after 10 minutes, but they are ready to remove from oven."],[null,"Makes 64 small cookies (teaspoon) or 32 large cookies (tablespoon)."],[null,"Truwhip® is a frozen dessert topping that does not contain phosphate additives."]]},"2574":{"s":[[null,"Place all ingredients in a blender."],[null,"Set on ice/crush setting and blend for 30 seconds to one minute or until ice is well chopped and slush is at desired consistency."],[null,"Pour into a glass and garnish with lemon wedge, if desired."]],"h":[[null,"For people with diabetes substitute stevia, Splenda® or other preferred low calorie sweetener for sugar. Calories are reduced to 90 and carbohydrate is 6 grams."],[null,"May be used as a calorie booster for those who need extra calories in their diet."],[null,"Remember to count this toward your total daily fluid intake if you are on a fluid restriction."]]},"2820":{"s":[[null,"Thaw lemonade concentrate. Dice chicken. Cut grapes in half, and slice celery."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine oil, lemonade concentrate and spices."],[null,"Add remaining ingredients and toss lightly."],[null,"Chill before serving."]],"h":[[null,"For variation substitute turkey for chicken and use purple grapes."],[null,"Adjust chicken if you need a higher or lower protein meal."]]},"6056440":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven or air fryer to 400 degrees F. Line a sheet pan with parchment paper if cooking in the oven."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine the salmon, breadcrumbs, and cheese."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk the egg substitute, yogurt, lemon juice, lemon zest, and dill weed. Gently mix into the salmon mixture and combine well, being careful not to break up the salmon pieces too much."],[null,"Form into 8 patties, about 1/4 cup each, and place on the sheet pan or in the air fryer basket."],[null,"Bake in the oven for approximately 15 minutes, or air fryer for 8 minutes, or until lightly browned and crispy."],[null,"While the salmon cakes are cooking, whisk the ingredients for the dressing in a small bowl. Whisk 2 tablespoons olive oil; 2 tablespoons lemon juice; ½ teaspoon lemon zest; ½ teaspoon chopped fresh dill weed; and 1/8 teaspoon sugar free multi-use syrup."],[null,"Divide the salad plates between 4 plates and top with salad greens, the cucumbers and tomato."],[null,"Place 2 salmon cakes on top of each salad and drizzle with dressing. Garnish with extra chopped dill if desired."]],"h":[]},"2655":{"s":[[null,"Chop celery, onion and parsley. Quarter and slice zucchini."],[null,"In a sauce pan, combine the water and 1 tablespoon of the oil and bring to a boil. Stir in couscous and cover. Remove from heat; let stand 5 minutes."],[null,"Combine lemon juice with zest, cayenne pepper and cumin."],[null,"In a large skillet, heat remaining 1 tablespoon of canola oil over medium heat and sauté celery, onion and zucchini until softened."],[null,"Transfer into a large serving dish and mix together the cooked couscous, the vegetables, cranberries, parsley, lemon juice and seasonings. Fluff with fork before serving. Serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"Mix lemon juice and seasonings together before adding to couscous."],[null,"Crookneck squash or other varieties of summer squash can be substituted for zucchini."]]},"6632910":{"s":[[null,"If using wooden skewers, soak them in water for at least 15 minutes to prevent burning during grilling."],[null,"Zest and juice one of the lemons. Thinly slice the other."],[null,"In a bowl, combine the olive oil, minced garlic, lemon zest, lemon juice, dried oregano, rosemary, and black pepper."],[null,"Add the peeled and deveined shrimp to the marinade, making sure they are well coated. Let them marinate for at least 15 minutes"],[null,"Preheat your grill or grill pan to medium-high heat."],[null,"Thread the marinated shrimp onto the skewers, along with one or two lemon slices per skewer."],[null,"Place the shrimp skewers on the preheated grill and cook for about 2–3 minutes per side or until the shrimp are fully cooked and develop a light char."]],"h":[]},"6960253":{"s":[[null,"Place the steamed edamame in a small bowl."],[null,"Add a squeeze of lemon juice and sprinkle with your choice of fresh herbs."],[null,"Toss gently to combine."],[null,"Top with the cashews."],[null,"Serve right away."]],"h":[]},"6398349":{"s":[[null,"Prep the Marinade: In a small pot, warm the lemon zest, lemon juice, 2 tablespoons of olive oil, minced garlic, chopped thyme, coarse salt, and black pepper to create the sauce."],[null,"Heat the remaining tablespoon of oil in a skillet over medium-high heat. Add the chicken and lemon slices to the skillet. Cook the chicken until it’s golden brown and reaches an internal temperature of 165°F (74°C), about 5 minutes a side."],[null,"Serve the chicken and lemon slices with the warm sauce and garnish with additional fresh herbs."]],"h":[]},"4407629":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F (conventional oven)."],[null,"Sift together the dry ingredients: flour, baking soda and add the lemon zest."],[null,"In a separate bowl, prepare the egg mixture. Whisk together eggs, sugar, Splenda®, olive oil, lemon juice, and vanilla."],[null,"Add dry ingredients to egg mixture and fold them together with a spoon."],[null,"Pour batter into a non-stick loaf pan (4\" × 8\") and bake for approximately 1 hour or until the cake springs back when touched."]],"h":[[null,"This cake is excellent as a snack."],[null,"You can freeze individual slices in plastic wrap."],[null,"The loaf is also good for a plated dessert by topping a slice of cake with 1 tablespoon of Cool Whip® and a handful of summer berries."]]},"2133":{"s":[[null,"Combine lemon juice, chicken broth, olive oil, oregano and bay leaf in a glass dish or zip lock bag."],[null,"Add chicken breasts, turn to coat, and marinate 2 hours."],[null,"Broil or grill 4-5 inches from heat source for 5-6 minutes per side or until thoroughly cooked."]],"h":[[null,"Look for reduced sodium broth containing less than 500 milligrams sodium per 1 cup serving. Avoid low sodium broth that contains potassium chloride—it’s very high in potassium. Recommended brands include Health Valley No Salt, Fat Free Chicken Broth (800-423-4846), Kitchen Basics Natural Chicken Stock, and Swanson 50% Less Sodium Chicken Broth."],[null,"If you are on a lower protein diet adjust the portion to match your meal plan."]]},"3382":{"s":[[null,"Drain and rinse the chickpeas and place in a food processor or blender."],[null,"Reserve 1 tablespoon of olive oil. Add remaining olive oil, juice from the lemon, lemon pepper seasoning and garlic powder to the chickpeas."],[null,"Process or blend until smooth. Add 2 to 3 tablespoons of water to thin if needed."],[null,"Place in a bowl and top with reserved tablespoon of olive oil."]],"h":[[null,"Compare brands and select chickpeas with the lowest sodium content."],[null,"Serve hummus with a cut pita, low-salt pita chips or raw vegetables."],[null,"If using a lemon, use a small sieve to catch the seeds when pouring into other ingredients."]]},"3398":{"s":[[null,"Set the oven to the lowest temperature."],[null,"Wash and dry the lemons. Using a microplane zester or fine kitchen grater, remove the yellow part of the lemon peel."],[null,"Mix the zested lemon peel with the cracked peppercorns."],[null,"Line a baking sheet with parchment paper and spread out the mixture. Set baking sheet in the oven for 1 hour and 15 minutes, stirring the mixture every 15-20 minutes."],[null,"Add the coriander and place the mixture into a food processor or spice grinder. Process until ingredients are finely ground."],[null,"Store in an airtight container or tabletop shaker. Use as a salt replacement at the table or add to meat, chicken, fish, salad or vegetables."]],"h":[[null,"You will need 3/4 cup of fresh lemon zest."],[null,"Lemon Pepper Seasoning will keep for 3-4 months if stored in an airtight container."],[null,"Most commercial lemon pepper blends contain salt."],[null,"You can purchase dried lemon zest for a quick recipe but the fresh zest tastes better."]]},"6057267":{"s":[[null,"Pulse the oats in the bowl of a food processor until they are finely ground."],[null,"Add the almonds and continue pulsing until it is a finely ground mixture."],[null,"Pour in the syrup along with the sunflower butter, lemon zest and juice, vanilla, and salt and blend until it turns into a dough."],[null,"Transfer the dough to a mixing bowl and stir in the poppy seeds."],[null,"Using a 2-tablespoon portion scoop, scoop out 20 balls. Roll each between your hands to form a smooth ball."],[null,"Store in an airtight container in the fridge for up to 12 days or in the freezer for 1 month."]],"h":[]},"6284164":{"s":[[null,"In a bowl, whisk together the lemon juice, water, and stevia."],[null,"Pour into popsicle molds, using around 1/2 cup of liquid for each."],[null,"Freeze for 6 hours or overnight."]],"h":[]},"3438":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 325° F."],[null,"Grease and flour a tube pan."],[null,"Using a mixer, cream butter and sugar together."],[null,"Add eggs, one at a time, beating after each egg is added."],[null,"Fold in flour, lukewarm milk and extracts."],[null,"Pour batter into a greased tube pan and bake for 1 hour and 20 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Use a larger capacity tube or bundt pan."],[null,"This recipe is not recommended for people with diabetes due to the high carbohydrate content."]]},"6093298":{"s":[[null,"In a small mixing bowl, whisk together all ingredients except the raspberries. Put mixture in the refrigerator for at least one hour until chia seeds soak up the liquid and it becomes a pudding consistency."],[null,"To serve, put 1/3 cup pudding in a small bowl with 1/2 cup raspberries."]],"h":[]},"2232":{"s":[[null,"Combine all ingredients."],[null,"Mix until whipped cream melts completely."]],"h":[[null,"People with diabetes can substitute stevia, Equal®, Splenda® or other sugar substitute if desired. Carbohydrate is reduced to 6 grams per serving if sugar substitute is used instead of sugar."]]},"6452790":{"s":[[null,"In a bowl, whisk the lemon juice, water, and stevia."],[null,"Pour into an ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's instructions."],[null,"For a soft sorbet, eat this immediately. For a firmer texture, transfer to a freezer-safe container and freeze for 2 hrs."]],"h":[]},"2315":{"s":[[null,"To make crust mix together 1/4 cup confectioner’s sugar, 1/8 teaspoon salt, flour and 1/2 cup butter."],[null,"Pour into ungreased 8″ square pan and bake at 350º F for 15 minutes.Remove from oven."],[null,"To make filling mix together granulated sugar, baking powder, 1/8 teaspoon salt, beaten eggs, 2 tablespoons lemon juice and grated lemon rind."],[null,"Pour over crust and spread evenly."],[null,"Return to oven and bake 20 minutes longer at 350º F. Remove from oven and cool."],[null,"To make icing mix together remaining 2 tablespoons lemon juice, 3/4 cup confectioner’s sugar and 1 tablespoon softened butter."],[null,"When crust and filling layers are completely cool, spread icing over the top."],[null,"Refrigerate. Cut into 36 squares."]],"h":[[null,"Lemon squares freeze well. Place on a tray and freeze then store in a freezer bag or container."]]},"4492509":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F. Spray 8×8-inch square baking pan with non-stick cooking spray."],[null,"To make the shortbread crust, in a mixing bowl, add the first amount of flour, butter and powdered sugar. Mix to combine."],[null,"Press crust mixture firmly in the bottom of the baking pan. Bake 20 minutes. Remove from oven."],[null,"In a mixing bowl, immediately before baking, whisk together the eggs, sugar, and flour. Add the lemon juice and continue to whisk*."],[null,"Pour lemon mixture over warm baked shortbread crust."],[null,"Bake 20–25 minutes until lemon custard is set and reaches an internal temperature of 160°F. Remove from oven and cool."],[null,"Cover and refrigerate."],[null,"Cut into 16 pieces before serving."]],"h":[[null,"* Do not prepare the lemon mixture in advance."],[null,"PLEASE NOTE: Always watch for saturated fat content in desserts. Moderation is key!"],["Reducing Potassium Content In Recipes","Monitoring how much potassium you eat is an important part of your kidney diet. The daily amount will depend on your labs and stage of chronic kidney disease. Selecting low-potassium ingredients for recipes not only decreases the amount of potassium in your diet but also limits the potassium your kidneys need to filter. Plan ahead when grocery shopping and know which foods are best for you and which options are lower in potassium. This will make it easier to stick to your kidney-friendly diet. • For breakfast, choose cereals or egg dishes that are lower in potassium. • At lunch, top sandwiches with lower-potassium vegetables such as onions and bell peppers in place of tomatoes. • When making soups that are broth-based, select lower-sodium versions that do not use potassium chloride as a salt replacement. • Dinner can also include many lower-potassium choices of meats, salads and rice or noodle dishes. Avoid high-potassium sauces and when seasoning, select garlic, herbs and pepper. • For snacks, choose lower-potassium fruits and vegetables such as a small apple or a handful of carrots."]]},"2291":{"s":[[null,"Trim chicken breasts and pound until thin."],[null,"In a large skillet, brown chicken in oil."],[null,"Transfer chicken to a plate, and reserve."],[null,"Add onion to oil left in the skillet and sauté until onions are translucent."],[null,"Add broth, lemon juice, thyme and black pepper. Continue to cook for 10 minutes."],[null,"Return chicken to skillet and cook another 10 minutes, stirring occasionally."],[null,"Serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"Purchase thinly sliced chicken breast at the meat counter to eliminate pounding, if desired."],[null,"Serving ideas: over rice with green beans, or with noodles and carrots or as an open-faced sandwich on white bread and ladle broth mixture over it."],[null,"Low-sodium broth contains 140 mg or less sodium per serving. Reduced-sodium broth contains 220 to 600 mg sodium per serving."],[null,"Avoid low-sodium broth with potassium chloride — it’s very high in potassium."],[null,"If you are on a low protein diet adjust the portion to match your meal plan."]]},"6980895":{"s":[[null,"Prepare an ice cream maker if using. If not using, omit this step."],[null,"Combine sugar substitute, water, thyme, lemon zest and lemon juice in a small sauce pan. Heat to a boil and then remove from heat to cool. Remove thyme sprig."],[null,"Once the lemon mixture is cooled, whisk in to the Greek yogurt. Pour into the ice cream maker and churn until frozen and thick. Serve immediately and freeze leftovers in a plastic container."],[null,"If not using an ice cream maker, whip mixture with an electric mixer or by hand with a whisk for 3 minutes. Add to a plastic container and freeze."]],"h":[]},"6757804":{"s":[[null,"In a large skillet or wok, heat olive oil over medium heat. Add the mixed vegetables and sliced green onions to the skillet. Stir-fry for 3–4 minutes until the vegetables are crisp-tender."],[null,"Add the minced garlic and sauté for 1–2 minutes until fragrant."],[null,"Add the shrimp to the skillet and cook for about 3–4 minutes until they turn pink and opaque."],[null,"Add the cauliflower rice to the skillet. Cook for about 3–4 minutes, stirring occasionally, until the cauliflower rice is tender."],[null,"Stir in the soy sauce, fresh thyme leaves, lemon juice, salt, and black pepper. Stir everything together to combine well and heat through."],[null,"Garnish with fresh thyme sprigs and lemon wedges, if desired."]],"h":[]},"4002988":{"s":[[null,"In a small saucepan, bring lemon juice, water and sugar to a boil. Stir until the sugar has dissolved. Remove from heat and let cool."],[null,"In a bowl, whip the cream with an electric mixer until fluffy. Add the sugar, mascarpone cheese and lemon juice. Blend carefully and set aside."],[null,"Dip half of the cookies, one at a time, in the cooled syrup and arrange side by side in one layer in a rectangular dish (7\"×11\"). When dipping the cookies make sure to do it quickly. You don’t want the cookies to become soggy and fall apart."],[null,"Cover the layer of cookies with half of the cream mixture from step 2."],[null,"Dip the other half of the cookies in the syrup and start a new layer on top of the cream mixture. Finish with spreading the rest of the cream mixture on top."],[null,"Dust the top with cocoa powder using a sieve. Cover with plastic wrap and let rest in the fridge for 12 hours before serving."]],"h":[["Cheese please!","In moderation, dairy can be eaten as part of a kidney-friendly diet. Cheese, yogurt and milk naturally contain potassium and phosphorus, but these foods also provide beneficial vitamins, minerals and some protein so it’s important to work with a registered dietitian to determine which dairy sources and how much are right for you. Cheese is a versatile ingredient in many different dishes. The content of sodium, potassium and phosphorus varies depending on the type and quantity of cheese. Cheeses considered lower in phosphorous and potassium are generally softer such as Brie, cream cheese, mascarpone and natural sharp cheddar. Read labels, but most brands of these selections contain 200 milligrams or less of sodium per serving. Cottage cheese is often encouraged for a kidney-friendly snack. Limit your portion to a half-cup and keep in mind that this food can be higher in phosphorus and sodium when consumed in larger quantities. Processed cheeses and cheese spreads should be eaten very sparingly."]]},"2150":{"s":[[null,"Mix Greek yogurt, vanilla extract, lemon juice and lemon zest together until smooth. Fold in 1/2 cup of the whipped topping."],[null,"Divide half of the mixture into 4 portions in parfait glasses. Place 5 raspberries on top, then layer with the remaining yogurt mixture. Chill."],[null,"When ready to serve, top each parfait with 1 tablespoon whipped topping and remaining raspberries."]],"h":[[null,"Check with your dietitian to be sure this recipe is acceptable for your individual diet. Greek yogurt is a significant source of protein, potassium, phosphorus and calcium. This recipe provides an easy way to increase protein intake but portion must be limited to keep other nutrients of concern within an acceptable amount."],[null,"For variety substitute blueberries or strawberries for raspberries."]]},"3586":{"s":[[null,"Rinse chicken under cold water, pat dry with paper towel, and place chicken pieces skin-side-down in a 2-quart baking dish, Pyrex® bowl or other oven-safe cookware."],[null,"Pour oil and lemon juice into a 16-ounce container (with a tight-fitting lid) and shake to mix."],[null,"Mix black pepper, garlic powder and rosemary flakes together, reserving two teaspoons for later use. Add remaining spices to lemon/oil mixture, and shake until blended."],[null,"Sprinkle one teaspoon of the reserved spices over the chicken, cover and marinate overnight or at least 8 hours."],[null,"Pre-heat oven to 350° F. Uncover chicken and bake in oven for 25 minutes. (Leave chicken in the marinade.)"],[null,"Remove from oven and turn chicken so that skin side is up. Sprinkle with remaining teaspoon of the spice mixture."],[null,"Bake for an additional 25 to 30 minutes or until chicken pieces are no longer pink inside."],[null,"Pour some of the remaining liquid over chicken when serving."]],"h":[[null,"Use chicken breasts or a combination of breasts and thighs if desired."],[null,"Season with garlic powder and rosemary to your personal taste. Amounts are suggestions only."],[null,"Use 1 teaspoon fresh rosemary instead of dried if available."],[null,"The longer the dish marinates the more flavorful. Marinate at least 8 hours but for full flavor, overnight."],[null,"If you are on a protein-limited diet, decrease the portion to match your meal plan."]]},"6464139":{"s":[[null,"Heat olive oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat."],[null,"When olive oil begins to release its aroma, add shrimp, salt, black pepper, and crushed red chile flakes. Cook shrimp on one side just until the tail of the shrimp is bright pink, approximately 1–2 minutes."],[null,"Turn shrimp over and squeeze lemon juice over top. Cook shrimp until all gray color is gone and they are pink and cooked through, approximately 1–2 more minutes. At this point, shrimp should be coiled slightly tighter than when they were raw. Shrimp will continue to sizzle in the pan."],[null,"When they are cooked completely through, transfer shrimp to a serving platter, garnish with lemon zest, and serve immediately."]],"h":[]},"2613":{"s":[[null,"In a medium saucepan, stir water and sugar or sugar substitute over medium heat until sugar is dissolved. Remove from heat; cool 20 minutes. (If you are in a hurry skip the heat. Instead, dissolve the sugar in room temperature water then go to step #2.)"],[null,"Add citrus peel and juice to sugar mixture. Pour into a jar or pitcher; cover and chill. Keeps for up to 3 days."],[null,"For each glass of lemonade or limeade, combine 3 ounces base and 3 ounces water in ice-filled glasses. Stir and sip slowly to enjoy. Freeze leftover base in ice cube trays and add to beverages instead of ice."]],"h":[[null,"3 ounces liquid is 6 tablespoons."],[null,"Base made with Splenda® instead of sugar has 20 calories and 5 grams carbohydrate. Count as 1/2 carbohydrate choice."]]},"3050":{"s":[[null,"Mince onion."],[null,"Pour lemonade and water into rice cooker or saucepan. Add rice, onion, mixed vegetables and seasonings."],[null,"Start rice cooker or cook on stove, covered, over medium heat for 20 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Fresh, frozen, bottled or canned lemonade may be used in this recipe. Be aware, some lemonades contain phosphate additives which increases phosphorus content. Read labels and avoid brands with this additive."],[null,"Select a vegetable mix with carrots, corn, green beans, green peas or substitute your favorite low potassium frozen vegetable blend."],[null,"If you have diabetes, try sugar-free lemonade in this recipe to lower carbohydrates by 5 grams per serving."],[null,"For best results, do not remove cover or stir rice during cooking."]]},"2094":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400° F."],[null,"Chop the onion and rosemary."],[null,"Place the chicken wings in a baking dish."],[null,"Add all remaining ingredients to a saucepan and cook for 3 minutes."],[null,"Pour the mixture over the chicken and bake for 30 to 35 minutes. Test for doneness."],[null,"Serve the wings hot or place in a covered warming dish or crock pot until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Carbohydrate content is less than 1 gram if sugar-free lemonade is used. Check lemonade ingredients and avoid brands that contain phosphate additives."],[null,"Buy fresh wing drummettes at the grocery. A 1-1/4 pound package contains 12 drummettes. If unavailable, ask your butcher to cut whole chicken wings into drummette size."],[null,"Boneless chicken pieces may be used in this recipe. Check for doneness after 20 minutes."]]},"6224028":{"s":[[null,"This zesty low-carb salad made with fresh and delicious ingredients makes a delightful spring or summer lunch."],[null,"Alternatively, place all ingredients in a small mason jar, seal tightly, and shake."],[null,"Assemble the salad. Divide the arugula between 2 plates. Top each with 3 oz. of shrimp. Sprinkle the salads with 1/2 the Parmesan cheese and ½ the pine nuts."],[null,"Drizzle the salads with the dressing."]],"h":[]},"1919":{"s":[[null,"Add coconut flour and oats to a food processor. Process into a fine powder, about 1 minute."],[null,"Add remaining ingredients, and process until smooth, about 1 minute."],[null,"Using a small cookie scoop or approximately a tablespoon, form about 20-25 balls."],[null,"Place formed balls on parchment paper on a cookie sheet."],[null,"Refrigerate 2 hours to firm up. Store in an airtight container in the refrigerator."]],"h":[[null,"Play around with flavors. Almond extract or orange extract works nicely too."]]},"3492":{"s":[[null,"Chop celery, cucumber, onion and parsley."],[null,"In a sauce pan, combine 2 cups water with olive oil and bring to a boil. Stir in couscous and cover. Remove from heat; let stand 5 minutes. Transfer couscous to a large serving bowl and cool in refrigerator while preparing the other ingredients."],[null,"Combine lemon juice with cayenne pepper and cumin."],[null,"To the cooled couscous, stir in the lemon juice and seasonings, chopped vegetables, cranberries and parsley; mix well with a wooden spoon."],[null,"Return to the refrigerator for several hours. Fluff with a fork before serving. Garnish with lemon slices and parsley."]],"h":[[null,"A 10-ounce box of couscous is equal to 1-1/2 cups."],[null,"Serve cold as a salad."],[null,"Great for a picnic or for a buffet or a pot luck."]]},"6520204":{"s":[[null,"Add all ingredients to a food processor or blender and blend until smooth."]],"h":[]},"3332":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350º F. Chop the onion and mince the parsley and garlic."],[null,"In a Dutch oven melt butter over medium heat. Add the rice and stir to toast, about 4 minutes. Add the onion and garlic and sauté for 2 minutes."],[null,"Add the lemon juice, parsley and seasonings to the rice. Mix well."],[null,"Heat chicken broth to a boil and add to rice mixture. Stir well. Cover with a lid, and place in pre-heated oven. Bake for 20 minutes."],[null,"Remove rice from the oven and fluff with two forks and stir in Parmesan cheese. Garnish with parsley sprigs before serving."]],"h":[[null,"In step #5, if broth is not boiling, the end product will be heavy and will stick to the pan."]]},"3594":{"s":[[null,"Cook orzo and quinoa according to package directions and set aside."],[null,"Mince garlic; dice onion and bell pepper; slice mushrooms."],[null,"Cut chicken into 1″ pieces. Place chicken in a zippered plastic bag with juice from 1 lemon and 1 tablespoon of salt-free herb seasoning blend. Mix together and place in the refrigerator."],[null,"Heat 1/2 tablespoon olive oil in medium nonstick skillet over medium heat. Add garlic and onion. Sauté until onion is translucent (about 3 to 5 minutes). Add bell pepper and mushrooms. Cook, stirring occasionally, until peppers are just tender (about 5 to 7 minutes). Remove from heat and set aside."],[null,"Heat 1 tablespoon olive oil in a large nonstick skillet over medium heat. Add chicken and cook until no longer pink inside (about 7 minutes)."],[null,"Whisk together remaining 1 tablespoon olive oil, juice of 1 lemon and 1/2 tablespoon salt-free herb seasoning blend and add to chicken."],[null,"Stir in cooked orzo, quinoa and sautéed vegetables, and then cook another 3 to 5 minutes until chicken is fully cooked and all ingredients are heated through."],[null,"Divide evenly to make 4 portions."]],"h":[[null,"Two ounces dry orzo pasta and two ounces dry quinoa yield 1 cup each when cooked."]]},"6295599":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F."],[null,"In a medium saucepan, combine the lentils and vegetable broth. Bring to a boil, then reduce heat and simmer for about 20–25 minutes or until lentils are tender. Drain any excess liquid."],[null,"While lentils are cooking, place the halved bell peppers in a baking dish. Cover with foil and bake for 30 minutes until softened."],[null,"In a large skillet over medium heat, add the chopped onion and sauté for 5 minutes until softened. Add garlic to the skillet, then the ground turkey. Cook until browned and barely cooked through."],[null,"Stir in the ground cumin, smoked paprika, dried oregano, coarse salt, and black pepper."],[null,"Add the cooked lentils, diced tomatoes, and 1/2 cup of shredded mozzarella to the skillet. Stir until well combined."],[null,"Spoon the lentil and turkey mixture into each softened bell pepper half."],[null,"Top each stuffed pepper with the remaining shredded mozzarella."],[null,"Cover the baking dish with aluminum foil and bake for 20–25 minutes or until the peppers are fully cooked through."],[null,"Remove the foil and broil for an additional 3–5 minutes until the cheese is melted and bubbly. Garnish with fresh parsley if desired"]],"h":[]},"6438996":{"s":[[null,"In a medium saucepan, combine the lentils and vegetable broth. Bring to a boil, then reduce the heat, cover, and simmer for 15–20 minutes, or until lentils are tender but still hold their shape. Drain any excess liquid."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together soy sauce, sesame oil, rice vinegar, and maple syrup. Set aside."],[null,"Heat vegetable oil in a large skillet or wok over medium-high heat. Add minced garlic and grated ginger, and sauté for 30 seconds until fragrant."],[null,"Add broccoli, carrots, red bell pepper, yellow bell pepper, and snap peas to the skillet. Stir-fry for 5–7 minutes until the vegetables are tender-crisp."],[null,"Incorporate the cooked lentils into the vegetable mixture."],[null,"Pour the prepared sauce over the lentils and vegetables. Stir well to ensure everything is coated in the flavorful sauce."],[null,"Continue cooking for an additional 2–3 minutes until everything is heated through."],[null,"Garnish with sesame seeds and chopped scallions if desired."]],"h":[]},"6224700":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350 degrees F."],[null,"In a medium sauce pan, combine lentils and hot water. Bring to a boil over high heat, then reduce to a simmer, uncovered, for 20 minutes."],[null,"While the lentils are cooking, combine tomatoes, red bell pepper, red onion, cucumber, garlic, cilantro, red wine vinegar, olive oil, crushed red pepper flakes, feta cheese and ground black pepper. Stir to incorporate and set aside."],[null,"Arrange sliced baguette pieces on a large baking sheet. Spray the tops of the bread slices lightly with cooking spray. Bake on the top rack of the oven for 10 minutes. Set aside to cool. (See note in step 6)."],[null,"When the lentils are done cooking, drain and rinse them under cold water. Shake the colander to get rid of all of the water on the lentils, then add them to the bruschetta mixture and stir to incorporate."],[null,"To serve, either add the bruschetta mixture to a serving bowl and arrange the toasted baguette around the bowl for self-serve bruschetta, or top each toasted baguette slice with 2 heaping Tbsp of bruschetta mixture. Note: If you plan to serve the bruschetta on the baguette, you may want to toast the bread a little longer to avoid sogginess."]],"h":[]},"9671588":{"s":[[null,"Bring a large pot of generously salted water to a boil and cook your pasta according to the package directions for 'al dente' pasta. Drain, (BUT reserve 1/2 cup of pasta water) place in a large bowl, and set aside."],[null,"Meanwhile, add all the lentil pesto ingredients except the broth to your food processor and process until finely chopped, scraping down the sides as needed. Then add 2-3 tablespoons of the broth to thin your pesto to your liking. Taste for salt and pepper and add some if needed."],[null,"Now add the pesto, the other 1/2 cup of lentils, the cherry tomatoes, and slivered almonds (reserving some for garnish) to the bowl of cooked pasta. Mix well and add some of the reserved pasta water if needed. Serve warm or cold."]],"h":[[null,"Salt your pasta water. Make sure to add enough salt to your pot of water for the best texture and flavour. Here's a handy guide to help you salt your water perfectly each time."],[null,"Cook your pasta 'al dente' . Al dente pasta is typically 1-3 minutes \"underdone\". This is how Italians eat their pasta. 😉 We like a little bit of bite, and no mush."],[null,"Leftover lentil pasta salad will keep refrigerated for 3-4 days. I don’t recommend freezing."]]},"4500022":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, prepare the dressing by mixing olive oil, vinegar, honey, and cumin. Add pepper to taste."],[null,"In a larger bowl, combine lentils, cucumber, celery, parsley, and mint. Add the dressing and gently toss the salad. Garnish with pomegranate seeds before serving."]],"h":[[null,"* or English cucumber, seeds removed"],[null,"TIPS: You can prepare this salad in advance (up to 2 days). Add the dressing just before serving. For a portable version of this salad (like we used in the photo), use a mason jar: pour ¼ of the dressing into the jar, followed by ¼ of all other salad ingredients. Stir and enjoy!"],["The many health benefits of lentils","Protein is an important part of your diet as it is needed for many different functions in your body. Both the type and amount of protein must be considered in a kidney-friendly diet. Research shows that increasing the amount of plant-based protein in the diet is beneficial to those with chronic kidney disease. Lentils are a plant-based protein. In addition to being high in protein, lentils are a good source of fiber and rich in minerals such as iron, zinc, potassium, and phosphorus. While lentils contain a significant amount of potassium and phosphorus, they can still be part of a kidney-friendly diet. Talk with your registered dietitian nutritionist about how much you should add to your diet to enjoy the health benefits of lentils while following a kidney-friendly diet. Lentils are available in several varieties such as brown, green, and red, which are the varieties most commonly found at the grocery store. Dry lentils are easy to prepare, but when short on time, canned lentils are available for use. Lentils have a subtle, earthy taste and are easily flavored by different seasonings, making them easy to use in a variety of dishes and in most types of cuisine. You can serve lentils hot with rice, in tacos and soup, or cold on a salad."]]},"6022006":{"s":[[null,"Combine lentils, water and garlic in a pot over medium heat. Simmer for 15 minutes until the lentils are tender. Drain lentils and run under cold water. Discard the garlic."],[null,"While the lentils are cooking, whisk together the dressing ingredients."],[null,"In a salad bowl, add lentils, green onion, green pepper and tomatoes. Drizzle dressing over lentils and mix to combine. Refrigerate until serving."]],"h":[]},"9829268":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 425 degrees F."],[null,"Place potatoes in a large pot of water (just covering potatoes) and bring to a boil, cooking until fork tender, approx. 10 minutes. Drain and return to the pot, add the milk, salt and garlic powder if using, and mash with a potato masher. Add more milk if needed and set aside."],[null,"Meanwhile, add your cooked or canned lentils and all remaining filling ingredients to the bottom of a 9\"x13\" baking dish (or similar). Mix well."],[null,"Top with the mashed potatoes and spread them out evenly across the top. Then, use a fork to make crisscross pattern across the top. Cover the tray with parchment paper and then aluminum foil."],[null,"Bake for 20 minutes, then remove the foil and paper and bake another 10 minutes uncovered. Remove from the oven and let cool for a few minutes before slicing and serving."]],"h":[[null,"Weigh your potatoes for best results . Since potatoes vary greatly in size, weighing them will be the most accurate. If you don’t have a kitchen scale and you have to eye ball it, use approx 10 average sized Yukon Gold potatoes. Don’t overly mash your potatoes , just until smooth and then spread them over top your lentil and veggie mixture. Overly mashing potatoes can bring them from smooth and fluffy to gummy territory. Once your lentil and veggie mixture is prepared , taste and add more Tamari , salt, pepper or other seasoning, if needed. Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-4 days, although reheating may cause the potatoes to dry up a little. Add a splash of milk on top of the potatoes before reheating. Or, heat up as a deconstructed shepherd’s pie with some broth or milk and mix everything together to re-moisten it. You may freeze an entire uncooked tray and cook from frozen, adding 20 minutes of covered cooking time. Or thaw first and cook as usual."]]},"6131476":{"s":[[null,"Place a saucepan over medium heat. Add the oil, onion, and garlic. Cook, stirring occasionally, until onion begins to soften, 3–4 minutes."],[null,"Add the broth and lentils. Bring to a boil, then reduce heat to a simmer and cover for about 20 minutes, until lentils are tender."],[null,"Stir in the tomato sauce, brown sugar, Worcestershire sauce, and spices."],[null,"To serve, divide lentils between buns. Top with lettuce and onion rings."],[null,"Serve with a tossed salad on the side."]],"h":[]},"6140067":{"s":[[null,"In a large pot, heat the olive oil over medium heat. Add the onion, carrots, and celery. Sauté for 3–4 minutes until they begin to soften."],[null,"Add the garlic, cumin, coriander, and paprika. Cook for another 30 seconds until fragrant."],[null,"Stir in the lentils, tomatoes, vegetable broth, and water. Bring to a boil, then reduce heat and simmer for 25–30 minutes, with lid slightly open, until the lentils are tender. Stir in the salt and pepper."],[null,"Stir in the spinach and dates. Cook for 2–3 minutes until the spinach wilts."],[null,"Stir in the fresh lemon juice. Serve soup warm."]],"h":[]},"6579046":{"s":[[null,"Add oil to a soup pot over medium high heat. Add the onion, celery, carrots, and jalapeno pepper and sauté until the onions turn clear, about 5 minutes."],[null,"Add the garlic and sauté 1 additional minute."],[null,"Stir in the lentils and add the vegetable broth and water."],[null,"Add the bay leaf, salt (optional), and ground black pepper. Bring to a boil. Then, reduce to a simmer. Simmer, covered, for 40 minutes."],[null,"Remove the bay leaf and stir in the spinach until the spinach is wilted."]],"h":[]},"2718":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400° F. Cut peppers in half vertically and remove ribs and seeds. Dice the onion and squash. Drain and rinse lentils and set aside."],[null,"Place cut peppers on a baking sheet, face down. Brush with 2 tablespoons olive oil and roast in oven for 15 minutes."],[null,"Place large pan over medium-high heat and drizzle in 1 tablespoon olive oil."],[null,"Add onion, squash and dried herbs; sauté 5 to 7 minutes until soft."],[null,"While onion and squash soften, chop garlic and add to pan; sauté an additional 2 minutes."],[null,"Add tomato sauce, broth and half the fresh basil leaves. Stir until basil wilts and all ingredients incorporated."],[null,"Add lentils and cooked rice and stir to combine."],[null,"Remove peppers from the oven, flip them and fill 1/2 cup lentil mixture into each pepper. Top each pepper half with 1 tablespoon feta cheese. Return to oven to bake an additional 3 to 5 minutes."],[null,"Remove from oven and garnish with remaining basil leaves."]],"h":[[null,"Lentil filling works great in lettuce wraps for an easy lunch."]]},"9582665":{"s":[[null,"Drain and rinse the lentils. Then chop the walnuts in a food processor until finely chopped."],[null,"Add everything (except lettuce) to a bowl and mix well. Taste it and add more seasoning if you'd like."],[null,"Scoop the mixture into the lettuce wraps, and top them with tomato, avocado, cashew cream, or whatever you'd like."]],"h":[]},"6626248":{"s":[[null,"In a medium saucepan, combine dry lentils and vegetable broth. Bring to a boil, then reduce heat, cover, and simmer for 15–20 minutes or until lentils are tender. Drain any excess liquid."],[null,"In a large skillet, heat olive oil over medium heat. Add chopped onion and sauté until translucent."],[null,"Add minced garlic to the skillet and sauté for an additional 1–2 minutes until fragrant."],[null,"Stir in the chopped mixed greens and cook until wilted."],[null,"Add cooked lentils to the skillet, stirring to combine with the greens."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together apple cider vinegar, Dijon mustard, maple syrup, salt and pepper."],[null,"Pour the dressing over the lentil and greens mixture. Stir to coat evenly."],[null,"Gently fold in the thinly sliced apples. Sprinkle chopped walnuts over the top and finish with the avocado."]],"h":[]},"3860":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"In a large bowl, cream butter and confectioner’s sugar until light and fluffy."],[null,"Beat in peppermint extract. Gradually add flour and mix well."],[null,"Roll tablespoonfuls of dough into balls. Place one-inch apart on ungreased baking sheets; flatten with bottom of a drinking glass."],[null,"Sprinkle with green-colored sugar."],[null,"Bake for 12-14 minutes or until firm. Remove to wire racks to cool."]],"h":[[null,"Change the colored sugar to match different holidays."],[null,"Store in a covered container."],[null,"Limit portion as these cookies are very rich in fat."]]},"3740":{"s":[[null,"Chop onion and shred carrot."],[null,"Combine vegetables in a large bowl and toss."],[null,"Divide into 4 portions and serve in chilled salad bowls."]],"h":[[null,"Use exact measures to ensure potassium content is not too high."],[null,"Add your favorite low-sodium salad dressing."]]},"6556304":{"s":[],"h":[]},"7642926":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a saucepan, add the onion and potato and fry for 2-3 minutes. Add the stock to the pan, bring to the boil and simmer for 15- 20 minutes until the potato is tender."],[null,"Remove the pan from the heat, add the watercress and blend with a stick blender or food processor until smooth."],[null,"When fully blended add the yogurt, season well and heat through gently, without boiling, then blend for 1 more minute."],[null,"Serve topped with a swirl of yoghurt and a sprinkle of black pepper."]],"h":[[null,"A ladleful of this soup makes a great sauce served with grilled fish or vegetarian dishes such as tofu kebabs and rice."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Can be frozen in small pots for individual portions. Defrost in a microwave and slowly until piping hot."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6113306":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6494648":{"s":[],"h":[]},"1762":{"s":[[null,"Prepare rice according to instructions but omit the salt."],[null,"Chop the cilantro; gate the ginger and lime peel."],[null,"In a small bowl combine cilantro, ginger, lime peel, 1/4 teaspoon pepper, salt, and lime juice. Place chicken breasts in a zip-top bag and pour in half the marinade. Marinate chicken in the refrigerator 30 to 60 minutes. Place the remaining cilantro mixture in a screw-top jar and set aside to use as dressing."],[null,"Heat a large-ridged, cast-iron grill pan over medium heat. Drizzle chicken with 2 teaspoons oil. Place on heated pan and cook 4 to 5 minutes per side or until cooked through."],[null,"While chicken is cooking cut the zucchini in quarters, lengthwise and toss with remaining pepper and oil. Cook on grill pan, turning often, 10 minutes or until browned and tender crisp. Cover with foil until ready to serve."],[null,"Divide rice among 4 bowls. Slice chicken in thick strips and arrange on rice. Shake dressing well and drizzle over chicken. Serve with zucchini."]],"h":[[null,"Cook chicken and zucchini on a barbecue grill if preferred."],[null,"For a reduced protein diet, adjust chicken portion according to your diet meal plan or consult your dietitian."]]},"3185":{"s":[[null,"Zest one of the limes and set aside."],[null,"Juice both limes into a small bowl."],[null,"Add mayonnaise and pineapple preserves to lime juice and whisk together until well blended."],[null,"Fold in lime zest. Stir in a few drops of hot sauce if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Serve Lime Caribbean Dressing over iceberg lettuce or blend with shredded cabbage for a Caribbean twist on traditional coleslaw."],[null,"Try as a dip for grilled chicken fingers or shrimp on the Bar-B!"]]},"1780":{"s":[[null,"Mix all ingredients in a blender until smooth."],[null,"Serve chilled."]],"h":[[null,"For a snack-sized portion divide in half and freeze the extra serving for later."],[null,"Substitute lime sorbet for the sherbet if desired."],[null,"This is a high carbohydrate recipe. If you have diabetes and limit carbohydrate intake check with your dietitian before including in your eating plan."],[null,"NovaSource Renal Formula is an oral liquid nutrition supplement formulated to meet the needs of people on dialysis. Ask your dietitian for information or go to NestleNutritionStore.com."]]},"2040":{"s":[[null,"Soften frozen sherbet in microwave for 45 seconds to 1 minute. Scoop it into the large bowl."],[null,"Pour Sprite over sherbet and stir until evenly mixed."],[null,"Mix whey protein powder and pineapple juice in blender until smooth. Pour into sherbet mixture and stir until evenly mixed."],[null,"Serve immediately or refrigerate. After refrigeration, stir before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute Sprite Zero with ginger ale or any other phosphate-free light colored soda. Add food coloring for a more vibrant green."],[null,"Substitute with other sherbet flavors if desired."],[null,"For parties, add spoonfuls of completely frozen sherbet last and let it float on top."]]},"1903":{"s":[[null,"Peel and clean shrimp. Chop parsley."],[null,"Boil water in a large pot. Add pasta and cook for 10 minutes or until tender."],[null,"While pasta is cooking, separate garlic cloves, leaving skin on. Heat cloves in a frying pan over medium heat, stirring frequently. Garlic is ready when it darkens and becomes soft to touch. Skin will be easy to remove. Remove garlic from pan and peel off skin."],[null,"Heat olive oil in the frying pan and return peeled garlic to the pan. Cook garlic until golden. (Cloves can be cut in half or left whole.)"],[null,"Add parsley and shrimp and cook 1 to 2 minutes, until shrimp turns pink."],[null,"Drain pasta and reserve 1 cup of liquid. Add pasta to pan with shrimp and garlic. Mix all ingredients together and add the reserved cup of liquid."],[null,"Add lemon juice and black pepper. Mix and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Adjust shrimp portion for a higher or lower protein diet."]]},"2154":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the grill."],[null,"Finely chop the onion."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine ground beef, onion, egg and Mrs. Dash® seasoning until all ingredients are mixed throughout."],[null,"Divide ground beef mixture into 4 equal size patties"],[null,"Grill to desired temperature and doneness."],[null,"Serve on hamburger buns. Add red onion, thin tomato slice and lettuce if desired."]],"h":[[null,"These burgers need no ketchup or mustard. They are full of flavor!"],[null,"Use your favorite Mrs. Dash seasoning blend."]]},"2182":{"s":[[null,"Preheat grill according to manufacture’s direction."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine ground beef, onion, egg and Mrs. Dash® seasoning until all ingredients are mixed throughout."],[null,"Divide ground beef mixture into 6 equal size patties."],[null,"Grill to desired temperature and doneness."],[null,"Place on hamburger buns."]],"h":[[null,"These burgers need no ketchup or mustard. They are full of flavor!"],[null,"Use your favorite Mrs. Dash® seasoning blend."],[null,"One large onion yields 1 cup chopped."],[null,"This lower protein version of Lisa’s Awesome Burgers has a smaller burger portion compared to the original recipe on DaVita.com. The nutrients have been adjusted to reflect this change."]]},"2293":{"s":[[null,"Finely chop the red onion."],[null,"Mix all ingredients in a large bowl until well combined."],[null,"Cover and refrigerate for at least 30 minutes and up to 24 hours."],[null,"Split turkey mixture into 4 equal portions and form patties."],[null,"Cook in a heated nonstick skillet prepared with nonstick cooking spray or on a grill. Patties are done when the internal temperature reads 165° F on a meat thermometer."]],"h":[[null,"Serve burgers on a bun, roll, or over salad or coleslaw (not included in nutrient analysis)."],[null,"If you don’t like the spicy heat substitute black pepper for the crushed red pepper."],[null,"For a lower protein diet divide turkey mixture into 6 or 8 patties."]]},"1908":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 425° F."],[null,"Stir together flour, 3 tablespoons powdered sugar and salt. Add butter using a pastry blender or fork, until mixture appears crumbly."],[null,"Press mixture into bottom and sides of an 8” tart pan (or other 8” pan with removable bottom such as a spring form pan). Prick bottom of crust with a fork; cover and place in the freezer for 15 minutes."],[null,"Place tart pan on a larger pan and bake for 12 to 13 minutes. Remove from oven to let cool."],[null,"Reduce oven temperature to 350° F."],[null,"Beat cream cheese in mixing bowl until smooth. Add granulated sugar and continue to beat until smooth. Add eggs, one at a time and beat well. Add lemon juice and zest, and beat again until smooth."],[null,"Pour filling into prepared crust and bake 25 to 30 minutes."],[null,"Remove from oven and cool. Cover tart and refrigerate 1 hour until chilled."],[null,"Beat whipping cream and remaining 1 tablespoon powdered sugar together until soft peaks form. Spoon dollops of topping around edge of tart and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Whipping cream is also known as heavy cream. It doubles in volume when whipped."],[null,"Without the whipped cream fat is 19 grams per serving."],[null,"To make a diabetic-friendly version, substitute Splenda® granular sweetener for powdered and granulated sugar and replace whipped cream with a dollop of light whipped topping (carbohydrate 18 g, fat 20 g, calories 270)."]]},"2652":{"s":[[null,"Chop onion and cilantro. Mince chili, garlic and bell pepper. Thinly slice cucumber."],[null,"Peel and devein shrimp."],[null,"For dressing, stir together lime juice, green onion, cilantro, jalapeno, oil, garlic and salt in a medium bowl."],[null,"In a separate medium size bowl, toss shrimp with 2 tablespoons of the dressing to marinade. Reserve remaining dressing. Cover and refrigerate for 30 minutes."],[null,"Heat broiler. Remove shrimp from marinade and broil 3-inches from the heat source for 1-1/2 minutes per side or until opaque."],[null,"Remove from broiler and immediately toss hot shrimp with reserved dressing and red bell pepper. Cool to room temperature."],[null,"Arrange shrimp on cucumber slices and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Barbecue shrimp on a grill instead of broiling if desired."]]},"7208015":{"s":[[null,"Heat 1 tsp of the oil in a large saucepan, add the onions and cook for 20 minutes, stirring regularly, until soft and caramelised."],[null,"Season the flour with black pepper and coat the liver. Add the remaining oil to a frying pan, add the liver and brown for 3 minutes. Set aside."],[null,"Once the onions are cooked, add the garlic to the saucepan and stir in the 2 tsp of flour."],[null,"Slowly add the stock and more pepper, bring to the boil, stirring frequently, and add the liver. Cook a further 5 minutes until the liver is tender and the sauce thickens."],[null,"Meanwhile, cover the vegetables in water and boil for 15 minutes until tender and drain."],[null,"Mash the swede, potato and parsnip together and serve with the liver and green beans."]],"h":[[null,"Capture all the nutrients by using the cooking water from the vegetables for the sauce. You could cook the veggies first and reheat once the liver is ready."],[null,"This works well with calves' or chicken livers."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Freeze the vegetables and liver separately. Defrost in the fridge or microwave. Reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 5"]]},"2519461":{"s":[[null,"Place the flour in a deep dish with the baking powder, yeast and sugar; and stir well."],[null,"Mix the milk, oil and water together and add them to the previous mixture."],[null,"Mix well until blended paste is formed."],[null,"Cover the mixture and let it ferment for one hour."],[null,"In a large skillet let the oil boil and knead the dough by hand or by a dedicated machine, put dough in the oil on low heat."],[null,"Keep moving dough until it becomes golden."],[null,"Add a spoonful of honey as desired."]],"h":[[null,"Total Serving: Equal to 4 peices."]]},"1764":{"s":[[null,"Chop bell pepper, onion, garlic, celery, green onion tops and parsley."],[null,"To make a roux, heat oil and flour in a large skillet over medium heat. Stir constantly until flour is pecan colored."],[null,"Add bell pepper, onion, garlic, celery and 1 cup water to the roux. Cover and cook on very low heat until vegetables are tender."],[null,"Increase heat to high and add 2 cups water and 4 cups low-sodium chicken broth. Boil for 5 minutes."],[null,"Reduce to medium heat and add shrimp and crab meat. Boil 10 minutes."],[null,"Add green onion tops and parsley. Reduce to low heat and simmer for 5 minutes."],[null,"Season with pepper and hot sauce and serve over rice."]],"h":[[null,"Roux varies in flavor, depending on how long the flour is cooked. For a deeper flavor, cook the roux until it is the color of coffee with cream added."],[null,"Use fresh, frozen or canned lump crabmeat."]]},"3965":{"s":[[null,"Prepare rice according to package directions omitting salt."],[null,"Slice onion and bell peppers; mince garlic."],[null,"Rinse chicken parts in cold water. Pat dry with paper towels."],[null,"Heat oil in skillet or pot; add chicken parts browning chicken on all sides."],[null,"Add onion and green pepper."],[null,"Sprinkle flour over vegetables and chicken parts, stirring to coat all pieces."],[null,"Allow chicken and flour to brown for approximately 5 minutes."],[null,"Add garlic, black pepper and red pepper."],[null,"Stir in broth and water."],[null,"Cover pot and allow to simmer for approximately 30 minutes or until chicken is fully cooked. (Gravy will thicken as it simmers)."],[null,"Serve over white rice."]],"h":[[null,"May substitute other chicken parts or turkey necks for the meat."],[null,"Adjust portion if you are on a lower or higher protein diet."]]},"9590770":{"s":[[null,"Whisk all the ingredients in a small saucepot and heat over medium-high heat until the desired temperature is reached."],[null,"Enjoy immediately."]],"h":[[null,"Nutritional information reflects one teaspoon of maple syrup. For sugar free , just skip the maple syrup. For nut free , use soy milk or oat milk instead of almond. But stick to unsweetened varieties to avoid added sugar. For a richer version (not as low calorie of course) use canned coconut milk. Make it a peppermint hot chocolate by adding ⅛ teaspoon of peppermint extract."]]},"6030116":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 375 degrees F (190 degrees C)."],[null,"Grease a 9x13 baking dish with cooking spray or butter. Arrange a layer of sliced zucchinis at the bottom of the dish, slightly overlapping. Sprinkle a portion of the sliced onions over the zucchinis. Sprinkle a bit of the grated cheese over the onions. Repeat the layers until all zucchinis, onions, and half of the cheese are used."],[null,"Sprinkle the cooked chicken evenly over the layered zucchinis and cheese."],[null,"In a small saucepan, add olive oil over medium heat. Stir in the half and half, coriander, salt, and pepper. Heat the mixture until it's warmed through."],[null,"Pour the cream mixture evenly over the layered zucchinis, onions, cheese, and chicken. Sprinkle the remaining cheese on top."],[null,"Cover the baking dish with aluminum foil and bake in the preheated oven for 30 minutes."],[null,"Remove the foil and continue baking for an additional 15–20 minutes, or until the zucchinis are tender, the chicken is heated through, and the cheese is melted and golden. Let the casserole rest for a few minutes before serving."]],"h":[]},"6910935":{"s":[[null,"Cook the frozen cauliflower rice according to package instructions. Transfer to a bowl and mix in the vinegar, sesame oil, and salt. Let it cool to room temp."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the mayonnaise, sriracha, and lime juice. Set aside."],[null,"To assemble, divide the cauliflower rice among 4 bowls. Top each bowl with the diced shrimp, avocado, cucumber, radishes, and green onions."],[null,"Drizzle the spicy mayo over each bowl and top with sesame seeds."]],"h":[]},"2085":{"s":[[null,"Cut potatoes into 4″ x 1/2″ pieces and soak or double-boil to reduce potassium if you are on a low potassium diet. (See details in helpful hints)."],[null,"Heat oil over medium heat in a skillet. Add potatoes to hot oil and cook for 10 to 12 minutes until golden brown."],[null,"Remove fried potatoes to a paper towel to absorb extra oil."],[null,"Combine cumin, paprika and white pepper in a small dish or shaker. Sprinkle over hot potatoes and toss."],[null,"Serve 8 fries with 2 teaspoons ketchup."]],"h":[[null,"Potatoes are very high in potassium but you can remove part of the potassium by using one of these methods:"],[null,"Double cook method: Peel and dice or cut potatoes. Place in a large pot of water and bring to a boil. Drain the water and add fresh water to the pot. Bring to a boil, cook for 10 minutes then drain and set aside."],[null,"Leaching method: Peel and dice potatoes. Place in a large pot of warm tap water and soak for 2 to 4 hours. Drain and set aside."],[null,"Dry potatoes well before adding to hot oil."],[null,"If no salt added ketchup is substituted for regular ketchup sodium will be reduced to 7 milligrams per serving. (Avoid brands containing potassium chloride)."]]},"3359":{"s":[[null,"Dice potatoes into 1/2-inch cubes and soak or double-boil to reduce potassium if you are on a low potassium diet. (See details in helpful hints)."],[null,"Place potatoes in a saucepan with 4 cups water and boil over medium heat for 15 minutes or until cooked."],[null,"Drain potatoes, discard water and return to pan. Add 1/2 cup hot water, nondairy creamer, garlic or onion powder, pepper and margarine. Heat to a boil."],[null,"Combine 2 teaspoons flour in a tablespoon of cold tap water. Stir into potatoes and continue stirring until liquid thickens."]],"h":[[null,"Potatoes are very high in potassium but you can remove part of the potassium by using one of these methods:"],[null,"Double cook method: Peel and dice potatoes. Place in a large pot of water and bring to a boil. Drain the water and add fresh water to the pot. Bring to a boil, cook for 10 minutes then drain and set aside."],[null,"Leaching method: Peel and dice potatoes. Place in a large pot of warm tap water and soak for 2 to 4 hours. Drain and set aside."],[null,"Add a little water if sauce thickens too much."]]},"2684":{"s":[[null,"Dice chicken and set aside. Chop onion, celery and parsley; slice carrots 1/2-inch thick."],[null,"Sauté butter and onion in a 4-quart pot for 5 minutes, until tender."],[null,"Add water and chicken broth and bring to a boil."],[null,"Add chicken, celery, parsley and pepper, then cover and simmer for 30 minutes."],[null,"Add carrots, cover and simmer for 20 minutes."],[null,"Add frozen vegetables, cover and simmer 20 minutes longer."]],"h":[[null,"Look for reduced sodium broth containing 500 milligrams sodium or less per 1 cup serving. Avoid low sodium broths and bouillons containing potassium chloride—it’s very high in potassium. Recommended brands include Health Valley No Salt, Fat Free Chicken Broth (800-423-4846), Kitchen Basics Natural Chicken Stock and Swanson 50% Less Sodium Chicken Broth."],[null,"If you are on hemodialysis or restricted fluid, be sure to count liquid in the soup as part of your fluid allowance for the day."]]},"6234115":{"s":[],"h":[]},"2987":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350o F."],[null,"Grease and lightly flour a 9″ x 13″ pan."],[null,"Sift flour, salt, baking soda, baking powder and cinnamon together. Set aside."],[null,"Combine oil and Splenda® Sugar Blend for Baking. Add in one egg at a time, mixing after each egg is added."],[null,"Gradually add dry ingredients. Mix well."],[null,"Fold in shredded carrots. Pour into baking pan and bake for 55 to 60 minutes until a toothpick inserted in the middle comes out clean."],[null,"To make icing, combine butter and cream cheese in a mixing bowl. Beat with a mixer until light and fluffy."],[null,"Gradually add Splenda® granulated sweetener while beating. Add vanilla and mix well."],[null,"Spread icing on cake after it cools well."]],"h":[[null,"For a lower fat version, replace 1/2-cup canola oil with 1/2-cup unsweetened applesauce; replace eggs with 1-cup low-cholesterol egg product; use reduced-calorie cream cheese. (250 calories, 18 grams fat per serving)."],[null,"If desired, replace Splenda products with equal amounts of sugar."],[null,"Splenda is available in four forms: Splenda® Sugar Blend for Baking (half Splenda®, half sugar), Splenda® Brown sugar Blend (half Splenda, half brown sugar), Splenda® granulater sweetener and Splenda® tabletop sweetener. For best results use the two types specified in this recipe."]]},"5239891":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a pan and fry the onions, carrots and celery for 5 minutes. Add the garlic and fry for a further minute."],[null,"Add the mince to the pan and brown, breaking it up with a wooden spoon."],[null,"Add the stock, passata, basil and nutmeg and season to taste with salt and pepper."],[null,"Allow to simmer on a low heat for about an hour, using a lid that is slightly ajar to let out the steam. Serve with pasta and garlic bread. This recipe is taken from the Kidney Friendly Cookbook produced by Dietitians and Dietetic Support Workers at a Paediatric Renal Unit in the UK. Please check with your Dietitian or Doctor that this recipe is suitable for you."]],"h":[]},"5474634":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180ºC / 160ºC Fan / 350ºF / Gas mark 4."],[null,"Divide the 400g of minced beef into 16 evenly sized meatballs and roll them into shape. Then put the meatballs onto a baking tray."],[null,"Cook the meatballs in the oven for 20 minutes."],[null,"Heat the oil in a pan and fry the onions, carrots and celery for 5 minutes. Add the garlic and fry for a further minute."],[null,"Add the stock, passata, basil and nutmeg and season to taste with salt and pepper."],[null,"Simmer on a low heat for about an hour. Put the lid of the pan slightly ajar to let out the steam."],[null,"Add the sauce to the cooked meatballs. Serve with pasta and garlic bread. This recipe is taken from the Kidney Friendly Cookbook produced by Dietitians and Dietetic Support Workers at a Paediatric Renal Unit in the UK. Please check with your Dietitian or Doctor that this recipe is suitable for you."]],"h":[]},"6929227":{"s":[[null,"Whisk the egg, egg white, and milk until well combined and slightly frothy. Sift the coconut flour into the mixture and whisk again until well combined. Let the batter rest at room temperature for 15 minutes."],[null,"While the wrap batter is resting, toss together the chicken, artichoke hearts, red onion, baby spinach, and Italian dressing. Keep the filling refrigerated until needed."],[null,"Add the cooking spray to a 10-inch nonstick sauté pan over medium heat. Let the pan heat until a drop of water sizzles in the bottom of the pan."],[null,"Re-whisk the wrap batter and then pour 1/4 cup of the wrap batter to thinly coat the bottom of the pan (add a little more if needed to coat the bottom of the pan). Let the wrap cook until the edges begin to brown. Using a spatula, flip the wrap and continue to cook for another minute. Slide the wrap on to a plate and continue this process to make 6 “wraps” or crepes. Let the wraps cool."],[null,"Divide the chicken mixture evenly among each wrap (about 1/2 cup of filling per wrap) and roll."]],"h":[]},"6933134":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 375°F."],[null,"Line a rimmed baking sheet with parchment paper and spray with cooking spray. Pour on the riced cauliflower and spread into an even layer. Bake for 15 minutes. Remove cauliflower from the oven, and turn the temperature up to 450°F."],[null,"Line a large bowl with two layers of paper towels or a clean dish towel. Pour in the cooked cauliflower and let it cool."],[null,"Add another layer of towels on top of the cooled cauliflower and press down with your hands. Squeeze out as much liquid as you can."],[null,"In a large mixing bowl, mix the cauliflower, egg whites, 1/2 cup of cheese, garlic powder, herbs and pepper."],[null,"Line your baking sheet with a fresh layer of parchment paper. Spray with cooking spray. Place your cauliflower dough on the prepared baking sheet and press into an even rectangle about 1/4” thick and 7x9” in size. Bake for 20 minutes, then sprinkle the rest of the cheese on top. Broil a couple more minutes until the cheese melts and starts to brown."],[null,"Let cool, then cut into 12 breadsticks."]],"h":[]},"6288870":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 400°F. Line two baking sheets with parchment paper. Spray with avocado oil cooking spray."],[null,"In a large bowl, mix the ground flax, chia seeds, cheese and rosemary. Add the egg and water and mix well."],[null,"Take teaspoon sized amounts of the dough and roll into balls. Place the balls on the prepared baking sheet with enough room to spread into crackers. Cover with another layer of parchment paper. Press down using your hands to flatten into round crackers."],[null,"Bake for 6 minutes. Turn over and bake for another 2 minutes or until golden brown."],[null,"Let cool completely before eating. Store in an airtight container for up to 10 days."]],"h":[]},"3964":{"s":[[null,"In a medium sauce pan combine water, cranberry juice, cranberries and sweetener. Heat to a boil then reduce to medium heat."],[null,"Stir in orange zest and cinnamon."],[null,"Cook for 10 minutes. Remove from heat and cool."],[null,"Refrigerate until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Cranberry sauce keeps for 1 week in the refrigerator."],[null,"Sweetness of one cup of a granular sweetener is equal to 1 cup of sugar. Adjust to your taste."],[null,"Use frozen cranberries if fresh are not available."]]},"6028849":{"s":[],"h":[]},"4936056":{"s":[[null,"Brush the diced bell pepper and the tomatoes with olive oil."],[null,"Divide the cheese, bell pepper and tomato evenly among the 4 pitas."],[null,"Toast under oven broiler or in toaster oven for 5 minutes, or until cheese is melted."]],"h":[]},"6418319":{"s":[],"h":[]},"3677":{"s":[[null,"Finely chop the celery and onion."],[null,"In a small bowl mix all ingredients together."],[null,"Weigh the finished salad and divide by 2 to determine weight of serving size."]],"h":[[null,"Virgil prefers StarKist® Low Sodium Albacore White Tuna because the sodium content is low. Check at Target if you are unable to find it at your local grocery store."]]},"6194859":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the mayonnaise, Greek yogurt, buttermilk, garlic, bleu cheese and black pepper."]],"h":[]},"4047168":{"s":[[null,"Heat 1 tablespoon unsalted butter or canola oil in pan."],[null,"Add fish fillets (dry with paper towel first)."],[null,"Season both sides of fish with spice blend."],[null,"Fry in pan for 3 minutes each side."],[null,"Squeeze fresh lemon over fish fillets to taste."]],"h":[]},"6793421":{"s":[[null,"Combine vinegar, peppercorns, coriander seeds, dill, Stevia, salt, and red pepper flakes (optional) in a medium saucepan over high heat. Bring to a boil then turn off the heat and set aside to cool."],[null,"Tightly pack the cucumbers, onions, and garlic into a quart-sized glass jar, or other heat safe container, with a lid. Pour the liquid over the cucumbers and onions, and ensure all vegetables are completely submerged."],[null,"Close the lid tightly and refrigerate for at least 1 day before serving."]],"h":[]},"6942750":{"s":[],"h":[]},"7564027":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4. Add the cauliflower to a saucepan of boiling water and, after 3 minutes, add the broccoli. Cook a further 6 minutes until almost cooked but still firm. Drain and set aside."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the oil to a saucepan and cook the onion, soften for 3-4 minutes but don’t brown it. Sprinkle the flour over the onions, add the mustard and gently stir for 1 minute to coat all the onions."],[null,"Gradually pour in 100ml of the milk, mixing to ensure there are no lumps. As it starts to thicken, gradually stir in the rest of the milk until it becomes a sauce. Add the 25g of Cheddar and all the Parmesan, stirring until the cheeses have melted."],[null,"Arrange the broccoli and cauliflower in an ovenproof dish, pour the sauce over and top with the remaining Cheddar. Bake for 20-25 minutes, until the top has browned."]],"h":[[null,"If you have any left over, blend with some vegetable or chicken stock for a great soup."],[null,"This dish is delicious with 1 tsp curry paste added to the sauce with the mustard in step 2."],[null,"You can assemble this in advance and leave it in the fridge then just pop it in the oven when needed. If baking straight from the fridge, add an extra 5-10 minutes to the cooking time."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"3919":{"s":[[null,"Combine flour, phosphorus-free baking powder and salt."],[null,"Cut in shortening until mixture is crumbly."],[null,"Add 3/4 cup hot water, and stir until ingredients look moist."],[null,"Mix and knead to a soft dough. (You may need to sprinkle in another 1 to 2 tablespoons of flour)."],[null,"Cover dough with a towel and let rest 1 hour."],[null,"Cut into 12 pieces."],[null,"Lightly roll into a 6” to 7” tortilla, or put in a tortilla press, to 1/8” thickness."],[null,"Cook on a hot iron skillet for 30 to 60 seconds per side until no longer doughy and brown spots begin to appear."]],"h":[[null,"Cream of tartar is the potassium acid salt of tartaric acid. One teaspoon contains 495 mg potassium. When using cream of tartar with baking soda to replace phosphorus-containing baking powder, be aware the potassium content of food will be higher but phosphorus is much lower."],[null,"Since the potassium in a tortilla made with low phosphorus baking powder is higher than regular tortillas, be sure to limit portion and other potassium sources if you are on a low-potassium diet."]]},"2991":{"s":[[null,"Thaw whipped topping."],[null,"Drain the juice from crushed pineapple."],[null,"In a medium bowl mix the cottage cheese and crushed pineapple together."],[null,"Gently fold in the whipped topping and green food coloring until mixed well."],[null,"Refrigerate until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"To serve as a festive Saint Patrick’s Day dessert, garnish the top with a dash of green sprinkles or colored sugar."],[null,"For other holidays change the food coloring and garnish colors."],[null,"This is a tasty way to boost high quality protein intake."]]},"3900":{"s":[[null,"Heat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Grease a 9″ x 11″ baking pan."],[null,"In a large bowl combine flour, sugar, baking soda and cinnamon. Add oil, eggs, 1 teaspoon vanilla and skim milk; blend until smooth. Stir in grated carrot."],[null,"Pour batter into pan and bake for 45 to 60 minutes until done."],[null,"Cool cake completely."],[null,"To make icing, cream the butter, cream cheese, confectioner’s sugar and 1 teaspoon vanilla together until smooth. Spread over top of cooled carrot cake."],[null,"Cut and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Confectioner’s sugar is also known as powdered sugar."],[null,"To check for doneness, insert a knife into the cake. If it comes out dry, the cake is done."],[null,"1 pound of untrimmed carrots yields approximately 3 cups shredded carrots."]]},"6329487":{"s":[[null,"Combine avocado with lemon juice in a nonreactive large bowl. Add berries, oil, vinegar, honey, salt, and pepper and combine well. Serve over a bed of arugula or watercress on each of the four plates. Garnish with pine nuts."]],"h":[]},"9079053":{"s":[[null,"To make the sauce: In a skillet over medium heat, heat the vegetable oil."],[null,"Add the onion and cook until tender, about 5 minutes."],[null,"Stir in the curry paste, salt, and pepper. Cook, stirring constantly, for 1 minute."],[null,"Stir in 1 cup (240 ml) of water and remove the skillet from the heat."],[null,"In a high-speed blender, combine the cashews and remaining 1 cup (240 ml) of water. Blend until completely smooth. Add the curry mixture and blend again until smooth. Set aside."],[null,"To make the pasta: Bring a large pot of salted water to a boil over high heat. Add the pasta and cook according to the package directions until al dente. Drain well and return it to pot."],[null,"To finish: Stir in the curry sauce and coconut milk. Place the pot over low heat and cook, stirring occasionally, for a few minutes to heat through and thicken the sauce. Taste and adjust the seasoning, as needed. Transfer to a large serving dish and serve hot, sprinkled with peanuts, basil, and red pepper flakes (if using), with lime wedges on the side for squeezing."]],"h":[[null,"Vegan Mac & Cheese by Robin Robertson © 2019 Quarto Publishing Group USA Inc. This is a recipe review, and not my recipe, please note the recipe ingredients and directions are by Robin Robertson. To make this recipe under 400 calories, enjoy a smaller serving."]]},"3411":{"s":[[null,"Cook macaroni following package directions."],[null,"While pasta cooks, warm up creamer and cream cheese in a medium saucepan over low heat."],[null,"After cream cheese is melted, add parmesan cheese."],[null,"Add carrots and spices and mix together."],[null,"When ingredients are thoroughly incorporated, add cooked macaroni and stir. Serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"Many half & half brands contain phosphorus additives. Be sure to check the ingredient label. We found Horizon® Organic Half & Half does not. If you cannot find a brand without additives, you may substitute with 1/4 cup sour cream."],[null,"Suggested portion for a side dish is 1/2 cup."],[null,"Use baby food carrots for puree short cut."],[null,"For variety, use 4 ounces sautéed orange and yellow sweet peppers in place of carrots (sauté the peppers and puree when cooled.)"],[null,"Use your favorite salt-free herb seasoning blend."]]},"2971":{"s":[[null,"Cook pasta according to box instructions, omitting salt."],[null,"In a saucepan on low heat, melt butter. Add garlic and simmer for one minute. Add cream cheese and stir until melted. Add 1/2 cup milk and whisk to make a sauce. Add more milk to desired consistency. Simmer sauce on low-medium heat, being careful not to burn."],[null,"Stir in the parmesan cheese. Add a few sprinkles of the red pepper flakes and black pepper to taste."],[null,"Mix sauce with the cooked pasta and enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Vegetables and cooked chicken can also be added if desired to make a one-dish meal."]]},"5485658":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 190°C/375°F/Gas Mark 4"],[null,"Place the macaroni into a saucepan of boiling water. Boil for 9-10 minutes whilst stirring occasionally."],[null,"Meanwhile, place the vegetable margarine into a saucepan and heat on low until melted."],[null,"Add the flour to the pan and stir until the mixture forms a smooth paste. Cook on a low heat for approximately 2 minutes."],[null,"Pour half of the Renastep into the pan and allow to boil without stirring."],[null,"Stir until the mixture blends smoothly and then beat with a whisk. Add the remaining Renastep to the mixture and stir in until it is all combined."],[null,"Take off the heat and stir in the soft cream cheese, emmental cheese, wholegrain mustard and pepper."],[null,"When the pasta is cooked, drain and add the sauce. Stir well until it is all combined together."],[null,"Place the mixture into an oven proof dish, sprinkle with nutmeg and bake in the oven for 25 minutes."]],"h":[["Renastep note","Renastep is a Food for Special Medical Purposes and must be used under medical supervision."],["Renastep note","Renastep is a ready to use feed for the dietary management of kidney disease from 3 years of age onwards. Renastep contains milk and fish. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information."],["Renastep note","This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease."]]},"7485658":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4. Heat the oil in a saucepan and fry the onions for 4-5 minutes until soft, but not brown. Add the leek and cook for a further 3-4 minutes."],[null,"Sprinkle the flour over the onions and leek. Mix well. Add the mustard and mix again."],[null,"Gradually stir in the milk and keep stirring for 2-3 minutes until the sauce thickens."],[null,"Add three-quarters of the Cheddar and stir until it has dissolved, mix in the peas and remove from the heat."],[null,"Stir the macaroni into the sauce, pour into an ovenproof dish and sprinkle with the remaining Cheddar. Bake for 20 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"You could use wholemeal pasta for added fibre – if you can't find it in the supermarket it's available in health shops. But wholemeal penne or any pasta shape would work, too."],[null,"You could add sweet corn or cooked mushrooms, cauliflower or broccoli."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"1717":{"s":[[null,"Cook the macaroni according to package instructions, omitting salt. Rinse under cold water and drain well."],[null,"Chop the onion, green peppers, celery, pimentos and hard boiled eggs."],[null,"In a large bowl combine all ingredients. Mix well."],[null,"Sprinkle the paprika and black pepper over the top."],[null,"Chill the salad before serving."]],"h":[[null,"12 ounces uncooked macaroni equals 3 cups cooked."],[null,"For variety, use oil and vinegar instead of mayonnaise. Sodium will be lower."],[null,"For a twist, omit onions or celery and add green peas, cucumbers or parsley."],[null,"Leftover portions will keep in the refrigerator up to 5 days."]]},"7511563":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a large saucepan and fry the onion over a low heat for 4–5 minutes until softened but not coloured. Stir in the garlic, thyme, paprika and cumin and fry for 30–40 seconds stirring continuously until fragrant."],[null,"Add the coconut milk, 200ml water, tomatoes, peppers and butternut squash and stir well."],[null,"Stab the chilli a few times with a sharp knife and then push under the surface of the coconut milk. Bring to the boil, then simmer uncovered for 15 minutes."],[null,"Cut each mackerel fillet into four or five pieces and scatter over the top of the sauce. Cover and simmer for a further 10 minutes until the fish is thoroughly cooked through."],[null,"Discard the scotch bonnet – or if you are feeling brave, discard the stalk and seeds, mash the flesh and stir back into the stew. Scatter over the parsley if liked, and serve immediately."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"7419051":{"s":[[null,"Add the onion, lime juice, olive oil, cumin and chilli powder to a bowl, and mix well."],[null,"Mix in the plums, tomatoes and coriander. Cover and set aside for 5 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, make three slits across the skin of each mackerel fillet."],[null,"Grill or barbecue each mackerel fillet skin side up under a grill, or skin side down on a barbecue, for around 4 minutes. This should be enough to cook the fillet right through but if not, turn it over and cook it for 1 minute on the flesh side too."],[null,"After warming the tortilla, add some salad leaves and a mackerel fillet. Top it with a dessertspoon of salsa and roll up."],[null,"Serve the rest of the salsa on the side."]],"h":[[null,"Salsa works well with grilled tuna, salmon or prawns."],[null,"Mackerel are a great source of Omega 3s, as well as vitamin D."],[null,"If taking for a picnic, cover the wrap with greaseproof paper and twist each end."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"7294698":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C (160° fan)/ gas 4."],[null,"Arrange the mackerel fillets in an oval baking dish or ovenproof pan."],[null,"Whisk together the olive oil, lemon juice, chopped garlic, and diced tomatoes in a mixing bowl. Season with some freshly ground black pepper."],[null,"Spoon the mixture over the fish. Bake for 15-20 minutes until the mackerel is firm to the touch and opaque in appearance."],[null,"Remove from the oven and let stand briefly before sprinkling with some chopped parsley and serving with lemon wedges and the baguette slices on the side, if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Serve with a mixed salad instead of bread for a low-carb version."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"7269383":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 220°C/200°C fan/gas 7. Line a baking tray with baking paper."],[null,"Boil the potatoes for 20 minutes, or until tender. Drain and thickly slice. Return to the pan and cover."],[null,"Meanwhile, place the mackerel skin-side down on the prepared baking tray. Drizzle over half the lemon juice, season with pepper and sprinkle over the chilli flakes. Bake for 15 minutes, then leave to cool. Peel off the skin and flake the fish."],[null,"For the dressing, put the onion, yoghurt and horseradish in a small bowl together with the remaining lemon juice. Whisk lightly, then season with black pepper to taste."],[null,"Boil the peas for 1-2 minutes. Drain and put in a large bowl with the cabbage and tomatoes. Toss and add the potatoes and watercress and toss again. Spoon on to 4 plates and top with the mackerel. Serve the dressing on the side, sprinkled with black pepper."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"6156760":{"s":[[null,"In a small saucepan, combine honey, ketchup, apple cider vinegar, and soy sauce. Heat the mixture over low heat, stirring constantly until well combined and slightly thickened. Remove from heat and set aside."],[null,"Mix the chicken with coarse salt, pepper, and lemon juice. You can leave it for 30 minutes to 1 to 2 hours for flavors to develop, although it's not necessary."],[null,"Put the flour in a shallow bowl."],[null,"Lightly whisk eggs in a separate bowl."],[null,"Put crushed cornflakes in another shallow bowl."],[null,"Preheat your air fryer to 375 degrees F."],[null,"Dip each chicken nugget first into the flour, then into the egg, and finally into the cornflakes mix. Make sure to coat each nugget thoroughly by pressing the cornflakes onto them."],[null,"Place the coated chicken nuggets in the air fryer basket in a single layer. Spray oil on the nuggets liberally, covering all surfaces."],[null,"Cook at 375 degrees F for 10 to 12 minutes, or until the nuggets are golden and crispy with an internal temperature of 165 degrees F, flipping them over halfway through the cooking time."],[null,"Serve the air-fried chicken nuggets with the homemade sweet and sour sauce for dipping."]],"h":[]},"5172480":{"s":[[null,"Put ghee and refined flour in a broad non-stick pan, mix well and cook on a medium flame till light brown for 3 to 4 minutes, while stirring continuously. Add milk to bind the mixture together."],[null,"Transfer the mixture into a large plate, cool for at least 10 minutes."],[null,"Add the sugar and cardamom powder and mix gently with your hands. The mixture should bind like a dough."],[null,"Rest for 10 minutes."],[null,"Divide the mixture into 2 portions."],[null,"Roll each portion into a ball and then flatten it slightly in between your palms. Form a depression in the centre, put one strand of saffron (dipped in milk) on top of peda for better presentation."],[null,"Serve the peda or store in an air-tight container and refrigerate it till serving."]],"h":[["Renastep note","Always check with your dietitian or doctor that this recipe is suitable for you."]]},"3582":{"s":[[null,"Lightly spoon flour into measuring cup and level off."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine flour, sugar, salt and yeast."],[null,"In a medium saucepan, heat milk and butter until warmed to 120-140°F."],[null,"Add warm liquid and eggs to flour mixture and beat with a mixer at medium speed until smooth."],[null,"Cover and refrigerate at least 1 hour or up to 4 days, adding 2 tablespoons sugar after the second day."],[null,"For pancakes, lightly grease a griddle or skillet, heat and pour 1/4 cup batter for each pancake. Turn pancakes when edges look dry and bubbles begin to break on the surface."],[null,"For waffles, bake 1/2 cup batter in a hot waffle iron until steaming stops."]],"h":[[null,"The yeast in this recipe replaces baking powder, a high phosphorus, high sodium ingredient."]]},"2930":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Arrange chicken in a baking pan and bake until done, approximately 45 minutes. Remove cooked chicken from oven and let cool."],[null,"Chop chicken into fine pieces and place in a large bowl. Finely chop green onions and celery. Peel mandarin oranges."],[null,"Add green onions, celery and mayonnaise to chicken. Mix well. Chill until ready to serve."],[null,"Before serving, cut mandarin orange section in half and fold into the chicken salad."]],"h":[[null,"Serve over mixed salad greens, on bread or rolls as a sandwich, or as a spread on crackers for a high protein snack."],[null,"Substitute 1 cup drained, canned mandarin oranges if fresh fruit is unavailable."],[null,"To increase the protein content of this recipe for people on a high protein diet, 1/4 cup of protein powder may be added."],[null,"If you are on a lower protein diet you may need to decrease the portion size according to your meal plan. Consult with your dietitian for help."]]},"4654972":{"s":[[null,"Cover a baking sheet with parchment paper. Distribute the mandarin orange wedges on the sheet and put into the freezer for a minimum of 2 hours."],[null,"With a blender, mix the frozen wedges, the egg whites and lemon juice and pulse until you get an icy consistency."],[null,"Serve immediately or place in individual serving cups and freeze for later use."]],"h":[["Canned fruit choices for the kidney diet","A balanced low-potassium diet can provide you with the different nutrients your body needs. Fruit is a natural source for fiber, folic acid, and vitamins C and A. Aim for 3 servings per day from this food group. While fresh fruit is an excellent option, canned fruit can also be a low-potassium choice. Choose canned fruit items such as apricots in juice, fruit cocktail, peaches, pears, applesauce and mandarin oranges. Roughly a ½ cup portion of these fruits is considered a single serving. When browsing the grocery aisle, consider the following when selecting canned fruit. First, read labels and stay clear of choices with potassium-containing additives. Next, aim for the most natural fruit choice with limited added ingredients. Fruit canned in fruit juice is a healthier choice in place of those canned in heavy syrup to limit added sugars and unwanted calories. Lastly, select cans free of deep dents to ensure food safety and proper storage."]]},"6131682":{"s":[[null,"Determine how much jalapeno you want to use. If you prefer to remove the seeds, do so carefully. Avoid touching eyes and nose."],[null,"Mix all ingredients."],[null,"Serve with warm corn tortillas or grilled meats."]],"h":[]},"2556":{"s":[[null,"Finely chop onion. Mince ginger root and garlic.Cut mango into chunks."],[null,"In a medium skillet heat oil and sauté onion until soft. Add ginger and garlic; cook for 2 minutes."],[null,"Add mango, sugar, vinegar, raisins, cranberries, pepper flakes and allspice."],[null,"Bring mixture to a boil then reduce heat to medium. Continue cooking and stirring 10 to 15 minutes until fruit is soft and mixture is thickened."],[null,"Refrigerate to chill. Serve with fish, poultry or meat."]],"h":[[null,"Use frozen mango when fresh is not in season."],[null,"Adjust chili flakes to your preference."]]},"3266":{"s":[[null,"Mince ginger root and garlic."],[null,"Mix together first seven ingredients to make marinade."],[null,"Wash fish fillets and pat dry on paper towel."],[null,"In a shallow glass pan place fish fillets with skin side down. Pour the marinade over fish, covering all around the fillets. Refrigerate for 20 minutes."],[null,"In a large skillet heat the canola oil and place marinated fish fillets skin side down. Cook over medium heat for 4-6 minutes on each side, turning only once."],[null,"Transfer fish to a serving plate."],[null,"In a small saucepan cook the left over marinade to a glaze consistency. Pour over the cooked fish before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Purchase six mahi mahi fillets, 4 ounces each."],[null,"Try the DaVita.com low sodium Mango Chutney recipe or use commercially prepared chutney. Mango Chutney is located in preserves & jams section of the grocery store. Check labels for sodium content – some brands are high in sodium."],[null,"Adjust fish portion for a lower or higher protein diet."]]},"9412428":{"s":[[null,"If you have a small food processor, I highly recommend using that to finely chop your habanero pepper. This minimizes touching the pepper with your hands. Remove the stem and cut the pepper in half. Then process."],[null,"If you do not have a small processor, you may cut by hand. However, I recommend wearing gloves when handling hot peppers, if possible. Make sure to thoroughly wash your hands after chopping."],[null,"Add all the chopped ingredients, lime juice, and salt to a medium bowl and mix well to evenly distribute the flavours. Serve immediately, or refrigerate for 1 hour to chill."]],"h":[[null,"If using frozen mango , make sure to completely thaw first. For less heat , remove the seeds of your habanero pepper or use jalapeno pepper instead. Wear gloves when handling spicy peppers , if possible, and make sure to thoroughly wash your hands when you’re done. Avoid touching your face . If you don’t have gloves , try using a sheet of plastic wrap around your hands."]]},"4979488":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, prepare mango cream. With the help of an electric mixer or blender, combine all ingredients until creamy."],[null,"In another bowl, prepare vanilla cream. With the help of an electric mixer or blender, combine all ingredients. It takes about 1–2 minutes of mixing until sugar is dissolved and peaks form."],[null,"Distribute the crushed Graham crackers among 4 dessert glasses. Add the mango cream and top with the vanilla cream."],[null,"Cover with plastic wrap and refrigerate for 1 hour before serving. Garnish with lime zest."]],"h":[[null,"*You can freeze leftover condensed milk."],[null,"Tip: This dessert can be frozen. Defrost in the fridge two hours before serving."],[null,"* For Transplant: This recipe is higher in saturated fat. Check with your registered dietitian to see how this recipe can be included in your diet."],["Watch for additives in lower fat dairy products","When following a kidney-friendly diet, it is important to eat just the right amount of phosphorus. One must eat enough to maintain healthy teeth and bones and help nerves and muscles do their job, but not too much because it can lead to complications of kidney disease. Eating too much phosphorus increases the level of phosphorus in the blood. Over time, this will pull calcium from bones and make them weak. This then leads to calcium deposits in blood vessels, heart and lungs, increasing the risk for heart disease. Avoiding phosphate additives when possible is the best way to prevent high blood phosphorus levels. Read the ingredient list on foods to know whether it contains phosphate additives. Ingredients with the letters “phos” are phosphate additives. Check the ingredient list of all packaged foods. Some foods can be tricky as one form of the food contains additives while other forms do not. For example, regular cream cheese normally does not contain phosphate additives, but a fat free version likely contains sodium tripolyphosphate or a similar additive. Another example is fat free half and half which may contain disodium phosphate when the regular version has no additives. It may be better to buy the regular version and use a smaller portion to decrease overall calorie and fat content to avoid eating the additives. Ask your registered dietitian which option is best for you."]]},"6527594":{"s":[[null,"Combine the mayonnaise and green onions in a small bowl, cover, and chill. Combine the chicken, mango, and bell pepper in a large bowl."],[null,"Combine the vinegar, lemon juice, and sugar in a container with a tight lid. Shake well. Add lemon mixture to the mayonnaise and green onion mixture and stir well."],[null,"Pour the dressing over the chicken and mango, toss well, and chill for 30 minutes. To serve, spoon onto a plate lined with lettuce leaves."]],"h":[]},"9483756":{"s":[[null,"Add all the ingredients to your blender and process until smooth and creamy. Enjoy cold."]],"h":[[null,"You may sub the fresh banana for frozen if you don't have any fresh on hand. You'll get a little less banana flavour this way, but still the sweetness it provides. You may also need a touch more milk or some water to get it smooth when using more frozen ingredients. For the milk , you may sub with any milk you have and prefer. Make it kid friendly. Since we eat with our eyes first, kids may be opposed to drinking a green smoothie, so have some fun with it and call it a \"Hulk Smoothie\" or \"Ninja Turtle\" or whatever else they might be in to. 🙂 For peanut free , sub the peanut butter with almond butter or another nut butter of choice. To make it completely nut free, sub the peanut butter with sunflower butter or another seed butter of choice, and sub the cashew milk with oat, coconut or soy milk. Use what you have! If you don't have spinach, but you have kale, try that instead. Or if you have fresh mango and strawberries, but not frozen, use those! Make this mango spinach smoothie your own. Just remember to increase or decrease liquids accordingly when adjusting the fresh vs frozen ratio of ingredients."]]},"7973577":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 150°C/gas 2. Lightly spray a medium-sized ovenproof pudding dish with low-calorie cooking spray."],[null,"Place the pudding rice into a sieve and rinse under cold running water. Drain and tip into the ovenproof dish. Stir in the sweetener, almond milk, vanilla extract, lime juice and cardamom. Bake for 50 mins."],[null,"Stir well and bake for a further 1 hr. Arrange the mango slices over the top, sprinkle with the desiccated coconut and pop back into the oven for 10 mins. Scatter over the lime zest and serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"If you use fortified almond milk, this is a good source of calcium, which is important for maintaining healthy bones."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"1783":{"s":[[null,"Mix all ingredients in a blender until smooth."],[null,"Serve chilled."]],"h":[[null,"Turn a plain vanilla nutrition supplement into a tasty treat by adding extra flavorings."],[null,"This is a high carbohydrate recipe. If you have diabetes and limit carbohydrate intake check with your dietitian before including in your eating plan."],[null,"NovaSource Renal Formula is an oral liquid nutrition supplement formulated to meet the needs of people on dialysis. Ask your dietitian for information or go to NestleNutritionStore.com."]]},"6558356":{"s":[[null,"Toss the apple slices with the lemon juice."],[null,"In a large skillet, heat the oil over medium heat. Add the apples and sauté for 3 minutes. Reduce the heat to low, cover, and simmer for about 6 to 7 minutes, stirring occasionally. Remove the apples from the pan and set aside."],[null,"In the same skillet add all the remaining ingredients except the almonds. Bring to a boil and cook over medium-high heat until syrupy, scraping up any bits of apple remaining in the pan. Add back the apples and sprinkle with the sliced almonds."]],"h":[]},"9229801":{"s":[[null,"Add the carrots and remaining ingredients (except parsley) to a small mixing bowl. Mix until evenly coated."],[null,"Then use a slotted spoon to place your carrots in the basket of your air fryer. (Don't dump everything in.) Arrange in a single layer and air fry at 400 degrees F for 12-16 minutes. Shake or mix the carrots every 5 minutes or so."],[null,"Once cooked to your liking, remove the carrots from the basket and toss with the remaining glaze if you'd like. Then serve with fresh herbs and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"* For oil free , omit the oil or butter and use a tablespoon of broth in its place. Carrot size and fryer model will determine cook time . Make sure to check on your carrots often towards the end of cooking. Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-4 days but tastes best when freshly made."]]},"2065":{"s":[[null,"In a medium mixing bowl combine the flour, sugar, baking powder and salt. Make a well in the center of the dry mixture. Set aside."],[null,"In a large mixing bowl combine the egg whites, milk, oil and maple extract."],[null,"Add egg mixture all at once into to the dry mixture. Stir just until moistened (batter should be lumpy)."],[null,"To make 4” pancakes, pour about 1/4 cup batter onto a hot, lightly greased griddle or heavy skillet."],[null,"Cook over medium heat about 2 minutes on each side or until pancakes are golden. Flip the pancake when it has bubbly surface and edges are slightly dry. To keep pancakes light and fluffy, turn only once and avoid pressing with the spatula."]],"h":[[null,"Serve with syrup, fruit spread or berries."],[null,"To keep total breakfast sodium intake low, use unsalted butter on pancakes and avoid salty breakfast meats."],[null,"This recipe was revised after the video was made. The 1/4 cup liquid egg substitute was replaced with 2 egg whites, and the 1 cup nondairy creamer was replaced with 1 cup 1% low-fat milk. These changes were made to omit ingredients that contain phosphate additives."]]},"6177288":{"s":[[null,"In a saucepan, combine the chopped pears, 1/4 cup water, maple extract, ground cinnamon, and lemon juice."],[null,"Place the saucepan over medium heat and bring the mixture to a simmer."],[null,"Cover with lid."],[null,"Reduce the heat to low simmer, stirring occasionally, for about 40 minutes or until the pears are tender and easily mashed with a fork or stick blender."],[null,"Serve warm or chilled."]],"h":[]},"4773244":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F."],[null,"Bring water to boil, add rutabaga and boil for 5 minutes. Drain and discard water. Place rutabaga in a 2 quart ovenproof dish and add the peppers."],[null,"Dredge chicken cubes in flour and pepper them."],[null,"In a non-stick skillet heat oil over medium-high heat, brown the chicken gently. (5 minutes)"],[null,"Combine garlic with herbs, seeds, vinegar, syrup and water. Pour over cooked chicken and bring to a simmer. Transfer to the ovenproof dish with the rutabaga."],[null,"Place in oven and cook for 25 minutes."]],"h":[]},"2168":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a nonstick pan over medium heat. When hot, add the chicken and season with salt and pepper. Cook until chicken is browned and opaque throughout. Transfer to a warm platter."],[null,"Discard oil in pan and place over medium heat. Add the maple syrup, and heat until it bubbles; stir in the marmalade and add the juice of one lemon. Boil until the sauce thickens, about 1 minute."],[null,"Pour sauce over the chicken. Garnish with fresh parsley and scallions if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Cindy says “My husband and I love this dish. It is easy and quick, taking only about 10 minutes to prepare.”"],[null,"Use sugar-free maple syrup to lower carbohydrates if you have diabetes. Carbohydrate is reduced to 10 grams and carbohydrate count is 1/2."],[null,"Buy large chicken breasts if you are on a dialysis diet and need high protein. Recipe analyzed with four 5-ounce chicken breasts."],[null,"For CKD non-dialysis on a lower protein diet, reduce the serving size to 1/2 chicken breast or weigh the portion according to your meal plan."]]},"6501895":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 450 degrees F."],[null,"Trim and halve the Brussels sprouts. Add them to a medium bowl."],[null,"Remove the thyme leaves from the stems and add them to the bowl."],[null,"Add the garlic, olive oil, maple syrup, salt, and pepper to the bowl and toss to combine."],[null,"Spread the sprouts out in a single layer on a baking sheet. Roast in the oven until they are fork-tender and beginning to brown, 20–25 minutes."]],"h":[]},"6019263":{"s":[],"h":[]},"2277":{"s":[[null,"Set the ice cream out to soften; thaw limeade concentrate. Zest the peel of one lime and measure 2 teaspoons to add to the pie mixture. Juice the zested lime and measure 1 tablespoon."],[null,"Combine the softened ice cream, limeade, lime juice and lime zest in a large bowl. Stir until well blended."],[null,"Pour mixture into the graham cracker crust. Cover and freeze until firm."],[null,"Cut pie into 10 servings. Garnish each slice with a fresh lime slice."]],"h":[[null,"For variety substitute cranberry, lemon or pineapple frozen concentrate for lime concentrate."],[null,"This dessert is not recommended for people with diabetes due to the high carbohydrate content. However you can make the following changes to reduce carbs to 26 grams per serving: make the filling and freeze in dessert cups and divide into 10 servings; omit the graham cracker crust; and use sugar-free ice cream."]]},"6117798":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 450°F."],[null,"Place naan bread on a baking sheet and toast in the oven for 5 minutes, until lightly toasted."],[null,"Remove from oven and cover each bread with 2 tbsp tomato sauce and a few slices of cheese. Return to the oven for 2 minutes, or just until the cheese starts to melt."],[null,"Place each pizza on a plate and top with 3 olive halves and fresh basil."]],"h":[]},"4119454":{"s":[[null,"Mix flour with ½ cup cold water, 1/8 teaspoon salt and 1/2 teaspoon black pepper, knead flour and water to make soft dough and roll out flat with rolling pin. Cut into squares and brush with oil. Bake at 350⁰ F in oven until lightly toasted."],[null,"Sauté onion and garlic with 1 tablespoon of olive oil in a large pan until tender. Add chicken and cook until chicken has an internal temperature of 165⁰ F."],[null,"Add cumin seeds, turmeric, coriander, ginger and salt to the pan and stir for 2 minutes."],[null,"Pour hot water over mixture, then add the carrots, zucchini and eggplant and cook until soft."],[null,"Add the dough squares to the broth and serve."]],"h":[]},"2079":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl combine marinade ingredients."],[null,"Pour over your favorite chicken pieces and marinate in the refrigerator for 1 to 4 hours."]],"h":[[null,"*Nutrient analysis is for the ingredients in this recipe. The amount actually absorbed by the chicken is approximately 25%, but this may vary depending on how long you marinate it, the container size, and if you leave the skin on or remove it. Estimated calories absorbed by 3 to 4 ounces chicken is 32 and 3.5 grams of fat."],[null,"Always discard extra marinade unless you plan to cook it to boiling point."]]},"7878991":{"s":[[null,"Place the chicken, buttermilk, pesto and garlic into a bowl and stir well to combine. Soak the wooden skewers in water for 15 minutes to prevent them from burning."],[null,"Leave to marinate for 20 minutes. Thread the chicken onto skewers alternating with the pepper and mushrooms."],[null,"Place under a hot grill and grill for 6-7 minutes, turning occasionally."],[null,"Meanwhile, place the couscous into a bowl, pour over the stock and lemon zest and juice. Cover the bowl with clingfilm and stand for 5 minutes."],[null,"Stir through the rocket leaves and spring onions and serve with the chicken skewers."]],"h":[[null,"For an even healthier version, try serving with wholemeal couscous."],[null,"This is great served cold and makes an excellent packed lunch."],[null,"For a fishy version, use cubes of salmon or extra big prawns."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"2017":{"s":[[null,"Peel and cube cucumbers; chop onion."],[null,"In a medium bowl combine vegetables and black pepper."],[null,"In a separate bowl combine vinegar and water with sugar and let stand for 15 minutes."],[null,"Pour vinegar mixture over cucumber mixture and refrigerate for at least 3 hours before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Use sugar substitute to reduce carbohydrate to 5 grams."],[null,"Marinated Cucumber Salad goes great with chicken dishes or tuna or egg salad. It’s a refreshing accompaniment to any meal."]]},"2580":{"s":[[null,"Cut broccoli and cauliflower into bite-sized pieces. Slice bell peppers and celery. Finely chop onion."],[null,"Combine broccoli, cauliflower, mushrooms, bell pepper and celery."],[null,"In a separate bowl, combine remaining ingredients to make marinade. Mix well and pour over vegetables. Refrigerate at least 3 hours before serving."],[null,"Use a slotted spoon to remove vegetables from marinade before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Adjust portion size to 1/2 cup for a lower potassium serving (167 mg)."],[null,"Leftovers will keep well in the refrigerator for 5 days."]]},"6008935":{"s":[[null,"In a medium bowl, whisk together clementine juice, 1 tbsp olive oil, garlic, and black pepper. Place the chicken tenderloins in a large plastic storage bag. Pour marinade over tenderloins and coat well. Seal bag and refrigerate 1 hour or overnight."],[null,"Spray grill with cooking spray and preheat to medium-high. Place chicken tenderloins on grill and brush with any remaining marinade. Grill about 4-5 minutes per side or until done."],[null,"Brush zucchini with 2 tbsp olive oil. Grill 3-5 minutes per side. Serve chicken tenderloins with zucchini rounds."]],"h":[]},"6235196":{"s":[[null,"Prepare an indoor or outdoor grill."],[null,"Whisk together all ingredients, excluding the salmon, in a medium sized bowl."],[null,"Pour marinade over the salmon, making sure to coat both sides. Marinate in the refrigerator for 30 minutes."],[null,"Remove salmon from the marinade. Grill fillets 4-6 minutes on each side and discard any leftover marinade."]],"h":[]},"7833058":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the grill to 180ºC/gas 4."],[null,"Flake the mackerel fillets, discarding the skins and any bones."],[null,"Toss with the lemon juice, sugar and juniper berries and set aside for at least 1 hour."],[null,"To make the salad, split the pitta breads in half, grill until crisp and break into pieces. Toss the rocket with the cherry tomatoes, mackerel and any juices, pitta bread pieces and olive oil."],[null,"Divide between 8 plates and serve."]],"h":[[null,"For a gluten-free version, you could use thickly sliced boiled new potatoes rather than pitta bread."],[null,"Try smoked trout fillets in place of mackerel for a lighter more colourful dish."],[null,"For vegetarians, replace the mackerel with a quarter of an avocado – there’s no need to marinate."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"7806347":{"s":[[null,"Place the monkfish in a shallow dish. Mix together the lime, soy sauce and chilli flakes, pour over the fish and marinate for 20 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, cook the basmati rice in a pan of boiling water with a vegetable stock cube. Drain and place in a large bowl. Add the carrot, sultanas and chopped basil leaves, mix well and keep warm."],[null,"Preheat the grill to high. Place the monkfish on a baking tray and season with black pepper. Cook under the hot grill for 2-3 minutes on each side."],[null,"Pile on top of fragrant rice."]],"h":[[null,"You could also use tuna or salmon steaks in place of monkfish."],[null,"For a vegetarian alterative, marinate cubes of tofu and thread onto skewers with red onion before grilling for 10 minutes, turning a couple of times."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"7540200":{"s":[[null,"In a non-metallic bowl, mix together the oil, vinegar, garlic and thyme."],[null,"Add the tofu to the bowl, coat in the marinade and set aside for at least 10 minutes. Soak the wooden skewers in water to stop them burning."],[null,"Thread the marinated tofu and remaining ingredients alternately onto the skewers and cook over a medium grill for about 10 minutes until they begin to char, turning occasionally."]],"h":[[null,"For a Chinese twist, try adding a heaped tsp of Chinese 5-spice to the marinade."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"3376":{"s":[[null,"Put all ingredients into a blender, and blend into a smooth slush."],[null,"Pour into a tall glass and serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"For variety omit chocolate syrup and use flavored sugar-free syrups, like the ones made by Torani®."],[null,"If desired, top with 1 tablespoon Reddi-Wip® Dairy whipped topping."],[null,"If desired use a low-calorie sweetener instead of sugar. This will save approximately 4 grams of carbohydrate."]]},"2087":{"s":[[null,"In medium bowl, pick through crab meat and remove any shell pieces."],[null,"Cut bread slice into cubes. Chop the parsley."],[null,"Add bread, mayonnaise, mustard, Old Bay® seasoning, parsley, cayenne pepper and egg to the crab. Mix lightly until all ingredients are mixed together. Do not over mix."],[null,"Use a 1/3 cup measure to portion out 6 crab cakes, each 3/4-inch thick. Refrigerate for one hour."],[null,"In a heavy skillet (preferably a cast iron skillet) heat olive oil or cooking spray."],[null,"Fry crab cakes about 5 minutes on each side until browned. Serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"Paprika can be used instead of Old Bay® seasoning. Sodium is reduced to 360 mg per serving."],[null,"1/2-cup crushed saltines, unsalted tops, can replace the bread."],[null,"For an attractive presentation serve on a bed of chopped lettuce garnished with mandarin orange slices."]]},"6047974":{"s":[[null,"Melt butter in a large pot over moderate heat. Add onion and cook for a few minutes, until the onion become soft and transparent."],[null,"Add crab meat. Cook 2 to 3 minutes, stirring constantly."],[null,"Add chicken broth and bring mixture to a boil. Reduce heat to low."],[null,"Combine half & half creamer and cornstarch in a small bowl. Whisk until smooth. Add to soup and increase heat slightly, stirring constantly until mixture thickens and comes to a boil."],[null,"Add dill weed, Old Bay seasoning and pepper to soup. Cook for 5-10 minutes longer. Serve warm."]],"h":[]},"1844":{"s":[[null,"Melt butter in a large pot over moderate heat."],[null,"Chop onion and add to pot. Cook, stirring until onion becomes soft and transparent."],[null,"Add crab meat. Cook 2 to 3 minutes, stirring constantly."],[null,"Add chicken broth and bring mixture to a boil. Reduce heat to low."],[null,"Combine half & half creamer and cornstarch in a small bowl. Whisk until smooth. Add to soup and increase heat slightly, stirring constantly until mixture thickens and comes to a boil."],[null,"Add dill weed, Old Bay seasoning® and pepper to soup. Ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Fresh Maryland lump crabmeat is best, but other varieties or imitation crab can be used if unavailable."],[null,"Old Bay Seasoning® is a popular seasoning made from celery seed, salt, mustard, red pepper, black pepper, bay leaves, cloves, allspice ginger, mace, cardamom, cinnamon, and paprika. It contains 160 mg sodium for 1/4 teaspoon. If unavailable, substitute another low-sodium seasoning or spice mix."],[null,"Look for low-sodium broth containing less than 250 mg sodium per cup. Avoid low-sodium broth that contains potassium chloride—it’s very high in potassium. Reduced-sodium broth containing 500 milligrams sodium or less per 1 cup serving is also a good choice in limited amounts."]]},"2397":{"s":[[null,"Drain juice from cherries into a measuring cup. Add water to make one cup."],[null,"Stir sugar and cornstarch together in a medium saucepan. Gradually add the cherry juice."],[null,"Heat juice mixture over medium heat until it starts to thickened. Add reserved cherries and reheat until filling starts to bubbles. Set aside to cool. Prepare crust."],[null,"In a medium bowl, combine flour and salt. Cut tablespoons margarine into flour with a pastry blender or two knives until mixture forms pieces the size of peas."],[null,"Stir in ice cold water just until a ball forms. Let rest in refrigerator 30 minutes."],[null,"Preheat oven to 425 ºF."],[null,"Divide dough in half. On a floured surface, roll half the dough to fit an 8” or 9” round pie pan. Place pie crust in pan and add cherry filling. Roll out second half of dough and place over top of pie."],[null,"Crimp edges of pie to seal. Cut slits in crust. Brush crust with a small amount of milk or egg to help brown. Bake for 20 to 25 minutes, until crust is brown and cherries begin to bubble."]],"h":[[null,"Diabetics can substitute Splenda® granular sweetener for sugar. Carbohydrate is reduced to 31 grams and carbohydrate choices equal 2."],[null,"Adjust sugar depending on tartness of cherries."],[null,"Nutrient analysis includes 3/4-cup sugar added to cherries."]]},"6904987":{"s":[[null,"Heat oil in a cast iron frying pan over medium-high heat. Add red onion, chili, garlic, and turmeric and sauté until soft."],[null,"Reduce heat to medium and add cumin and tomato. Sauté for 2 minutes, stirring occasionally."],[null,"Add the beaten eggs, swirling the pan to help the eggs set on the bottom. Cook for about 2-3 minutes."],[null,"When eggs are cooked through, fold the omelet and sprinkle with salt and fresh cilantro. Serve hot."]],"h":[]},"6127449":{"s":[[null,"Steam or boil the butternut squash cubes until the cubes are fork-tender. If steamed, remove the cooked squash from the steamer basket and pour it into a large bowl. If boiled, strain the butternut squash and then add to a large bowl."],[null,"Add the minced garlic, olive oil, salt, and pepper and mash until smooth."]],"h":[]},"6774328":{"s":[[null,"Pour 1/4 cup of water into a medium pot fitted with a steamer basket and bring to a boil over high heat. Add the red potatoes, cover, and reduce the heat to medium. Cook until the potatoes are tender, 25–30 minutes. Set aside to cool."],[null,"In a small saucepan, heat the milk and butter over medium heat until the butter melts, 2 minutes. Remove the saucepan from the heat and set aside to slightly cool."],[null,"Add the potatoes to a large bowl and, using a potato masher, mash until almost smooth. Add the milk mixture, salt, and black pepper and mix until well combined."]],"h":[]},"6181063":{"s":[[null,"Add water to a large saucepan and bring it to a boil over high heat."],[null,"Add the cubed turnips and boil until tender, about 20 minutes."],[null,"Drain and then return the turnips to the pot."],[null,"Add butter, minced garlic, and milk. Mash until smooth. Season with salt and pepper."]],"h":[]},"6743973":{"s":[[null,"Use a large (24 to 32 oz-wide mouth) mason jar with a tight-sealing lid."],[null,"Layer the dry ingredients as follows in the jar: bouillon (if using), ginger root, rice noodles, cooked beef, mushrooms, peppers, cabbage, carrots, green onion, and cilantro. Seal tightly and place in the refrigerator until ready to use."],[null,"In a separate small container, mix the soy sauce and lime juice and place in the refrigerator."],[null,"When you are ready to prepare the soup, remove the jar from the fridge at least 15 minutes before preparing it. Heat a cup of warm water (or beef broth) in the microwave until boiling. Stir in the soy sauce and lime juice."],[null,"Pour the water and soy sauce mixture into the jar and seal it tightly again. Swish it around to make sure the noodles are covered in liquid. Allow it to sit for 2-3 minutes or until the noodles are softened. Alternatively, heat the water (or broth) in a medium saucepan until boiling. Pour the ingredients from the jar into the saucepan and stir until combined and the noodles soften. Pour into a bowl to enjoy."]],"h":[]},"6954503":{"s":[[null,"In a medium-sized bowl, combine the chicken with 1 tbsp of the soy sauce, rice vinegar, and 2 tsp of the cornstarch. Set aside to marinate at room temperature for 15 minutes."],[null,"In another bowl, combine the remaining 1/2 tbsp soy, the remaining 1 tbsp cornstarch, 3/4 cup of the chicken broth, hoisin sauce, and sriracha. Set aside."],[null,"Heat half the vegetable oil in a large wok over high heat. When hot, turn the heat to medium high and add the chicken. Stir fry for 5 minutes or until the chicken is cooked through. (You do not need to continuously stir the chicken as you want the chicken to develop a crust and sear.) Remove the chicken from the wok to a plate and set aside."],[null,"Add the remaining oil to the wok. Add in the garlic and ginger and stir fry for 30 seconds. Add the red pepper, celery, and broccoli and stir fry for 30 seconds. Add the remaining chicken broth, cover, and steam 3 minutes."],[null,"Add the chicken and stir fry for 1 minute. Add in the sauce and cook for 1 minute, coating the chicken and vegetables with the sauce. Serve immediately."]],"h":[]},"9491703":{"s":[[null,"Add everything except the water to your food processor and pulse until everything is broken down without being pureed. Then add 2 tablespoons of water and pulse until combined."],[null,"Touch the mixture, and if it is sticky enough to roll into balls, don't add more water. If it still feels too dry, add another teaspoon at a time until you're able to roll it into balls."],[null,"Roll the mixture into small bite-sized balls, approx. 1 tablespoon worth of batter per ball. You should get around 20 servings."],[null,"Optional: Roll some or all of the balls into the crushed pistachio mixture if you'd like."],[null,"Chill in the refrigerator for 1 hour or longer and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"If your dates are very dry , soak them in hot water for 10-15 minutes, and then drain them before adding them to your food processor. This will help soften them and make them easier to process."],[null,"Don't overprocess the mixture . These matcha energy balls taste best with a little texture."],[null,"Use slightly wet hands to shape the balls to prevent sticking. The batter will be sticky, which is normal."]]},"2977":{"s":[[null,"Drain tuna and finely chop apple, celery and onion."],[null,"Mix tuna, apple, celery, onion, mayonnaise, black pepper and salt in a medium bowl."],[null,"Serve on top of bed of lettuce, with unsalted crackers or make a sandwich."]],"h":[[null,"Adjust portion if you are on a lower protein diet. Ask your dietitian to recommend the correct portion for your individual needs."],[null,"The juices from the fruit and vegetables will maintain moisture in the tuna salad."],[null,"If you’d like to munch something crunchy, try Matilde’s Tuna Salad with celery sticks or lightly steamed green beans."],[null,"Sodium is 121 mg per serving if salt is omitted."]]},"3019":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, mix ground beef, egg and rice."],[null,"After thoroughly mixed, roll into 24 small balls."],[null,"Brown balls in skillet on all sides."],[null,"Mix the Mrs. Dash® herb seasoning with the water."],[null,"Carefully pour the water and Mrs. Dash mixture in the skillet with the meatballs."],[null,"Bring water to a boil."],[null,"Cover and simmer for 20 to 30 minutes, rotating balls on all sides."]],"h":[[null,"For a lower fat dish, replace ground beef with ground turkey."],[null,"If you are on a lower protein diet, adjust the portion to match your meal plan."]]},"6164365":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400°F. Coat a six-cup muffin tin with nonstick cooking spray. Evenly divide the hash browns among the muffin cups and press firmly into the bottom and up the sides of each cup."],[null,"In a large skillet, heat the oil over medium heat. Sauté the onion until tender. Add the garlic and sausage; cook for 1 minute more. Remove the skillet from the heat; stir in the sour cream."],[null,"In a medium bowl, beat the egg substitute with the salt and black pepper, then pour it evenly into the potato-lined muffin cups. Top each cup with some of the sausage mixture, turkey bacon, and cheese."],[null,"Bake 15 to 18 minutes, or until the eggs are set. Serve immediately, or freeze for later."]],"h":[]},"6978207":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F. Coat a baking sheet with cooking spray. Set aside."],[null,"Combine the egg whites, Parmesan cheese, garlic, ground turkey, salt (optional), and pepper. Mix well and make 12 meatballs. Refrigerate the meatballs for at least 30 minutes."],[null,"To prepare the onion, cut in half. Cut each half into quarters. Then cut each quarter into 3 sections, for a total of 12 onion pieces."],[null,"Skewer 2 meatballs, 2 tomatoes, 1 mushroom, and 1 piece of onion alternating on each skewer."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk the balsamic vinegar and olive oil together."],[null,"Place the kabobs on the baking sheet and brush the kabobs on all sides with the balsamic and olive oil mixture. Reserve the marinade."],[null,"Bake the kabobs for 10 minutes. Brush all sides with the marinade again and bake for an additional 10-15 minutes. The meatballs should be cooked to an internal temperature of at least 165 degrees F."]],"h":[]},"6567916":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375°F. Coat a baking sheet with cooking spray. Set aside."],[null,"Combine the egg whites, parmesan cheese, garlic, turkey, salt, and pepper. Mix well, and form 24 meatballs. Refrigerate the meatballs for at least 30 minutes."],[null,"Skewer 2 meatballs, 2 tomatoes, 1 piece of mushroom, and 1 piece of onion alternating on each skewer."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the vinegar and olive oil."],[null,"Place the kebabs on the baking sheet and brush the kebabs on alludes with the vinegar and olive oil mixture. Reserve the marinade."],[null,"Bake the kebabs 10 minutes. Brush all sides with the marinade again and bake an additional 10-15 minutes. The meatballs should be cooked to an internal temperature of at least 165°F."]],"h":[]},"6217028":{"s":[[null,"Mix fennel seeds, oregano and 1/2 tsp pepper into ground beef. Roll into meatballs about 1 inch diameter to make 8 meatballs."],[null,"Heat a nonstick saucepan over medium-high heat. Spray with nonstick cooking spray. Brown meatballs on all sides, about 5 minutes. Remove to a plate."],[null,"Add onion and celery to the saucepan. Sauté 3 minutes, without browning the vegetables, stirring once or twice. Add the garlic and sauté for an additional minute. Add the diced tomatoes, chicken broth and water. Bring to a boil."],[null,"Add pasta and meatballs and cook gently for 8-9 minutes, stirring once to make sure the pasta rolls freely in the liquid. Add spinach and beans."],[null,"Lower heat to medium and return meatballs to the soup and cook to heat through, about 2 minutes. Add 1/8 tsp each of salt and pepper."],[null,"Serve in 4 large soup bowls with parmesan cheese sprinkled on top."]],"h":[]},"6356142":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 425 degrees F. Line a muffin pan with muffin papers."],[null,"Clean the potatoes and prick them several times with a fork. Bake the potatoes in the oven for 20 minutes. Remove the potatoes from the oven and microwave them for an additional 5 minutes or until soft. Remove the skins from the potatoes and place the potatoes into a medium bowl. Mash with a potato masher and whisk in the margarine. Mix well."],[null,"In a medium bowl, mix together the meatloaf ingredients."],[null,"Scoop about 1/4 cup meatloaf mixture into each lined muffin cup. Bake for 25 minutes."],[null,"Top each cooked meatloaf muffin with a scoop of sweet potatoes."]],"h":[]},"6575594":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F."],[null,"Lay the eggplant rounds on a baking sheet."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the olive oil, minced garlic, dried oregano, dried thyme, smoked paprika, salt, and black pepper."],[null,"Brush both sides of each eggplant round with the olive oil mixture."],[null,"Bake in the preheated oven for 15 minutes, then flip the eggplant rounds and bake for an additional 15 minutes or until they are tender and golden brown."],[null,"Remove the eggplant from the oven."],[null,"Sprinkle halved cherry tomatoes and crumbled feta cheese over the baked eggplant."],[null,"Return the baking sheet to the oven and bake for an additional 5 minutes, or until the feta is softened and tomatoes are slightly roasted."]],"h":[]},"6927830":{"s":[[null,"Spray a nonstick pan with cooking spray and heat over medium heat. Whisk in the egg and egg substitute and cook until partially firm. Stir in the cottage cheese, tomatoes, basil, pepper, and garlic powder. Continue cooking until the eggs are cooked."],[null,"Place half the mozzarella cheese on the inside of half of the pita. Lay half the spinach leaves on top and fill the pita with half the egg mixture. Repeat with the second pita."],[null,"Heat a grill pan or skillet over medium heat. Spray lightly with cooking spray and place the stuffed pitas, cheese side down, on the pan once hot. Allow to cook until browned and cheese has melted. Turn the pita over and cook until the other side is browned."]],"h":[]},"6992159":{"s":[[null,"In a medium mixing bowl, mix together the chicken and tzatziki sauce. Stuff ½ cup of the chicken mixture into each pita pocket."],[null,"Top each filled pita pocket with ¼ cup cucumbers, ¼ cup tomatoes, and 2 Tbsp sliced almonds."]],"h":[]},"6685325":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F. Spray a baking sheet with cooking spray."],[null,"Place the chicken breasts in a plastic freezer bag or between plastic wrap. Use a mallet or rolling pin and pound the chicken breasts until it is 1/2 inch thick."],[null,"Squeeze the lemon juice over the chicken breasts and season with the garlic powder and black pepper. Bake the chicken 25 minutes."],[null,"While the chicken is baking; warm the olive oil in a skillet over medium-high heat. Add the garlic and cook for 1 minute. Add the artichoke hearts and cook about 3 minutes. Add the chicken broth and simmer for 5 minutes. Stir in the parmesan cheese."],[null,"Remove the chicken from the oven. Spread the artichoke mixture evenly over the chicken breasts. Bake for 10 more minutes or until the chicken is done."]],"h":[]},"6788134":{"s":[[null,"Set out 2 12–16 oz. mason jars and lids. In a small bowl, whisk the Tzatziki dressing ingredients together (¼ cup nonfat plain Greek yogurt; 2 T. diced cucumber; 1/8 teaspoon dried oregano; 1 ½ tablespoons lemon juice and 1/8 teaspoon coarse salt. The dressing will be divided between the two jars."],[null,"Assemble your jars. Divide the chicken between the jars and place it on top of with 2.5 Tablespoons Tzatziki dressing in each jar. Add half the red pepper, cucumber, onion, cauliflower, tomatoes, chickpeas, and feta cheese to each jar."],[null,"If there is room, add the torn lettuce on top, or pack it separately in a resealable bag. Seal both jars tightly until you are ready to use them."],[null,"Store the jars in the refrigerator. They will last for 3–4 days when sealed tightly."]],"h":[]},"6561654":{"s":[[null,"In a bowl, combine the cucumbers, red onion, dill, and pistachios."],[null,"In a separate small bowl, whisk together the Greek yogurt, olive oil, red wine vinegar, salt, and pepper."],[null,"Pour the dressing over the cucumber mixture and toss to coat."]],"h":[]},"6722950":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a large soup pot over medium-high heat. Add the onion and sauté for 3 minutes or until clear. Add the garlic and sauté for 30 seconds."],[null,"Add the turkey Italian sausage and cook about 8 minutes until brown. Add the remaining ingredients."],[null,"Bring the soup to a boil; reduce the heat and simmer for 15 minutes."]],"h":[]},"7974942":{"s":[[null,"Cook the pasta according to the pack instructions. Drain and refresh under cold water."],[null,"Toss the pasta together with the remaining ingredients and serve."]],"h":[[null,"To toast pine nuts, add them to a dry frying pan over a medium heat, mix regularly for a couple of minutes until starting to brown then remove from pan immediately to stop them cooking further."],[null,"For a gluten-free version, replace the pasta with a tin of chickpeas."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6337735":{"s":[[null,"Lay the flour tortilla flat on a cutting board or plate."],[null,"Spread the hummus and tabouli in a long row, side by side down the center of the tortilla."],[null,"Add romaine lettuce on top."],[null,"Add sprouts and chopped tomatoes on top"],[null,"Get ready to roll! Starting from the edge of a long side, roll it up."],[null,"Cut it in half and enjoy immediately or wrap it tightly in plastic wrap to enjoy later."],[null,"Optional additional step: To eat this as an appetizer, wrap it in plastic wrap and let it “set” in the refrigerator for 2–3 hours. Remove the plastic wrap and cut the rolls into 1-inch slices, using a sawing motion. Serve cut side up on a platter."]],"h":[]},"2475":{"s":[[null,"Slice the black olives. Rinse the chickpeas."],[null,"Layer all ingredients in the order listed in a 16-ounce glass jar."],[null,"Refrigerate until ready to prepare and serve."],[null,"Remove jar from refrigerator 15 minutes before ready to eat."],[null,"Pour 5 ounces boiling water into the jar, close the lid and shake to combine. Let ingredients set in unopened jar for 2 minutes."],[null,"Pour contents of jar into a deep, wide bowl. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Serve with low-salt crackers or your favorite roll or bread."],[null,"Reduced-sodium olives are available online if you do not find them in the grocery store."],[null,"Whole milk ricotta cheese adds creaminess to the soup and is lower in sodium than low fat or skim ricotta cheese."],[null,"For an extra flavor boost, add a dollop of pesto. See the DaVita Basil Pesto recipe."]]},"1915":{"s":[[null,"Heat oven to 400 degrees F."],[null,"Cut spaghetti squash in half, length-wise. Remove seeds with a spoon."],[null,"Drizzle 1 tablespoon olive oil on both halves of the squash, and place flesh side down in a 9×13” baking pan. Bake in the oven for 30-40 minutes, until tender."],[null,"When spaghetti squash is cooled, shred flesh with a fork, and set aside."],[null,"Add remaining olive oil to a pan over medium-high heat."],[null,"Dice onion and add to the pan. Sauté 3 minutes."],[null,"While onion is cooking, slice red bell pepper and mushroom. Mince the garlic, half the tomato and rinse and drain cannellini beans."],[null,"Add all vegetables (except tomatoes) and herbs to the pan with the onion. Stir together and cook an additional 5 minutes."],[null,"Add the broth, spaghetti squash flesh, beans, and tomatoes to the same pan. Cook for 10 more minutes."],[null,"When cooking is complete, add the feta and basil, and serve."]],"h":[[null,"An ice cream scooper works great for scooping out the spaghetti squash seeds."],[null,"A small spaghetti squash will yield about 4 cups of shredded squash."],[null,"A portobella mushroom cap is about 3 ounces, which yields about 1 cup."],[null,"A small onion will yield 1/2 cup coarsely chopped, 1/4 cup finely chopped."],[null,"This is a higher potassium dish, but can be considered a full meal. This meal can be incorporated into a kidney friendly meal plan, considering other meals throughout the day to balance potassium intake."]]},"6872161":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F. Coat a large baking sheet with cooking spray. Set aside."],[null,"Add the yeast and honey to warm water and let sit for 5 minutes. The yeast should be foamy. Whisk in the egg and salt, then stir in flours to form a ball. Dough will be sticky. Set aside, covered."],[null,"Toss yellow bell pepper, grape tomatoes, arugula, and feta cheese with olive oil, balsamic vinegar, and black pepper."],[null,"Dust your hands with additional spelt flour and spread the dough onto a baking sheet to form about a 9-inch x 13-inch rectangle or larger. The dough should be relatively thin."],[null,"Pour the vegetable mixture evenly over the dough, leaving about 1/2 inch around the edge."],[null,"Bake for 20 minutes, then cut into 8 pieces."]],"h":[]},"6282423":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). Lightly grease or line a 12-cup silicone muffin pan."],[null,"Heat olive oil in a skillet over medium heat. Add spinach and cook for 3–4 minutes until wilted and most of the liquid has evaporated. You should end up with ~1 cup (150 g) cooked spinach. Let cool slightly."],[null,"In a large bowl, whisk eggs, milk, black pepper, and oregano (if using) until smooth."],[null,"Divide the spinach evenly among muffin cups. Top each with diced tomato and a sprinkle of feta. Pour egg mixture over the spinach and tomato, filling each cup about ¾ full."],[null,"Bake for 22–25 minutes, or until the eggs are puffed and set in the center."],[null,"Let them rest for 5 minutes before removing from the pan. Serve warm or refrigerate up to 4 days and reheat gently in the microwave."]],"h":[]},"6151126":{"s":[[null,"Spray a medium-sized skillet with cooking spray. Place the tofu in the skillet and break it apart with a fork or potato masher. Mix in the turmeric, garlic powder, salt, and 2 Tbsp almond milk. Cook over medium-low heat until warmed through."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine the tahini, yogurt, lemon juice, and 1 Tbsp almond milk and mix until combined and the tahini has thinned to a dressing consistency. You can add a little more milk or lemon juice if needed."],[null,"Place half of the cauliflower rice and quinoa in a bowl and mix to combine. Add half of the carrots and radishes to the bowl. Repeat with the second bowl."],[null,"Spray the kale with the olive oil cooking spray. Rub it into the kale until it is softened and bright green in color. Add half the kale to each bowl."],[null,"Divide the scrambled tofu and add half alongside the kale and other vegetables. Drizzle with the dressing."]],"h":[]},"6266956":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, whisk lemon juice, syrup, chopped tarragon, and oil."],[null,"Arrange cantaloupe on a platter, drizzle generously with dressing, and finish with a sprinkling of salt."]],"h":[]},"2423":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 200° F."],[null,"In a mixing bowl combine ingredients and beat until stiff peaks form."],[null,"Spoon onto a foil covered cookie sheet (or pipe to make them look pretty)."],[null,"Bake for 2 hours. Turn oven off."],[null,"Leave meringues in oven for at least 2 additional hours (until completely cool) or overnight."],[null,"Carefully peel off foil and store in an airtight container."]],"h":[[null,"Vanilla sugar is granulated sugar flavored with a vanilla bean. You can substitute 1 teaspoon vanilla extract and granulated sugar."]]},"3546":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 220º F. Cover cookie sheet with foil."],[null,"Beat egg whites and cream of tartar in a large bowl with mixer at high speed until soft peaks form. Gradually add the sugar. Add vanilla extract and food coloring. Continue mixing well until stiff peaks form and all the sugar is dissolved."],[null,"Drop by heaping tablespoons onto foil-lined cookie sheet. Smooth tops of meringue with bottom of spoon to form a \"peak.\" Sprinkle cookies with decorative red sugar."],[null,"Bake in oven 50 minutes. Let cool in oven with door slightly ajar for about 1 hour."],[null,"Store covered at room temperature. Recipe makes approximately 30 cookies."]],"h":[[null,"Use different colors of decorative sugar and food coloring."]]},"6089659":{"s":[[null,"Spray a large soup pot with cooking spray. Add oil and onion and sauté over medium-high heat for 3 minutes or until clear."],[null,"Add chicken and season with 1/4 Tsp. Adobo seasoning and pepper. Cook chicken until slightly brown, about 6-7 minutes."],[null,"Add remaining ingredients (including the other 1/4 Tsp. Adobo seasoning). Reduce heat and simmer for 15 minutes."]],"h":[]},"2559":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Place flour tortillas on a baking sheet coated with nonstick cooking spray. Bake at 350° F for 10 minutes or until edges are light brown. Remove from oven; stack and press down to flatten. Set aside."],[null,"Drain corn; dice onion, red peppers and chicken. Chop garlic and cilantro."],[null,"Heat a large skillet over medium-high heat; coat pan with cooking spray."],[null,"Add corn to skillet and cook 1 minute or until lightly charred. Add onion, red peppers, chicken and garlic; cook 2 minutes or until thoroughly heated."],[null,"Remove from heat; stir in lime juice."],[null,"Place tortillas on baking sheet. Spoon 3/4-cup chicken mixture onto each tortilla; top each with 2 tablespoons of cheese. Bake at 350° F for 2 minutes or until the cheese melts."],[null,"Remove from oven and sprinkle each pizza with 1 teaspoon cilantro."]],"h":[[null,"Always select natural cheeses instead of processed cheese. Sodium and phosphorus contents are usually lower in natural cheeses."],[null,"Stick with the recommended cheese portion (2 tablespoons per pizza—or less) to keep phosphorus in a reasonable range."]]},"2919":{"s":[[null,"Chop green onions, bell pepper and cilantro. Seed and mince jalapeno pepper."],[null,"In a large bowl combine coleslaw mix with the onion, bell pepper, jalapeno, and cilantro."],[null,"In a medium bowl combine all remaining ingredients and mix well."],[null,"Pour over cabbage mixture and toss well to combine."],[null,"Cover and refrigerate at least 2 hours before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Look for a package of coleslaw mix with shredded cabbage and carrots."],[null,"Make enough for leftovers. Mexican Coleslaw is even better the second day."],[null,"Adjust hot peppers to your taste."],[null,"Use low-fat mayonnaise to reduce fat to 6 grams per serving."]]},"2959":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400° F. Finely chop 1/4th of the onion and set aside until ready to make the meatballs. Dice the remaining onion, carrot and zucchini into 3/4-inch dice pieces. Chop the cilantro."],[null,"Pour broth into a pot and heat over medium heat. Add the diced vegetables, 1 teaspoon cumin, green chiles, tomato sauce, 1/4 cup cilantro, lime juice, paprika salt and cayenne pepper. Cover the pot and reduce to low heat."],[null,"In a medium bowl, combine egg, 1 teaspoon cumin and garlic. Add in ground beef, cooked rice and reserved finely chopped onion. Mix until combined."],[null,"Form mixture into meatballs about 1-1/2-inch diameter to make 18 meatballs. Place on a parchment-lined baking sheet and bake for 20 minutes until browned and cooked through. Cool meatballs for 5 minutes."],[null,"Add meatballs and remaining 1/4 cup cilantro to the soup and simmer for 10 minutes before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Meatballs can be cooked in the broth instead of baked if desired, but will make the broth cloudy. Add uncooked meatballs to hot broth, cover and cook over medium heat for 30 minutes."]]},"6099939":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F. Spray a 9x14-inch baking dish with cooking spray."],[null,"Heat the olive oil in a pot over medium-high heat. Add the onions and green pepper, and sauté until the onions turn clear. Add the garlic and sauté for another 30 seconds."],[null,"Add all remaining ingredients except the cheddar cheese. Bring to a boil. Reduce the heat and simmer 20 minutes."],[null,"Pour quinoa mixture into the baking dish and spread evenly. Top with cheddar cheese and bake 10 minutes until the cheese is melted and slightly golden."]],"h":[]},"2836":{"s":[[null,"Chop onion and garlic."],[null,"In a skillet, heat oil over medium-high heat. Add rice and cook until browned, stirring frequently."],[null,"Add onion and garlic; sauté until tender."],[null,"Add tomato sauce, water and salt."],[null,"Cover and simmer about 20 minutes until water is absorbed."]],"h":[[null,"Omit salt if regular tomato sauce is used instead of low sodium. The sodium content is about the same."],[null,"For best results, resist lifting lid from skillet when cooking rice."]]},"3716":{"s":[[null,"Mix spices together in a small jar or bowl."],[null,"Store in a jar or covered container for up to 6 months."],[null,"Use to season meat or vegetables for tacos, fajitas or burritos."]],"h":[[null,"Use as a dry rub, add to sour cream or Greek yogurt to make dip or season your favorite homemade salad dressing."],[null,"Adjust cayenne pepper to suit your taste."]]},"6112652":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a medium nonstick skillet over medium heat. Add the eggs, cook 1 minute, and gently stir until just set (Note: eggs will still be very wet). Remove from heat."],[null,"Top with the remaining ingredient in the order given. Cover and cook over medium-low heat 2–3 minutes or until cheese melts."]],"h":[]},"3944":{"s":[[null,"Grill the shucked ears of corn until char marks are seen on all sides. If a grill is unavailable, boil the corn for 9 to 10 minutes."],[null,"Spread a teaspoon of butter over each ear of corn until melted."],[null,"Sprinkle each ear with chili powder, then drizzle with crema fresca or sour cream mixture. Sprinkle with the Cojita cheese."],[null,"Cut the lime into wedges and squeeze over corn. Garnish with cilantro leaves and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Crema fresca can be found in the dairy section near the sour cream in most grocery stores. If unavailable, substitute 1 tablespoons buttermilk or mayonnaise mixed with 3 tablespoons sour cream."],[null,"If queso cojito is unavailable, substitute 4 teaspoons parmesan cheese."],[null,"To make this recipe with the corn off the cob, slice corn kernels off the cob and mix with all the ingredients. Divide into 4 servings."]]},"7733710":{"s":[[null,"Put the tuna into a bowl, and add all the ingredients except the yogurt and mix well."],[null,"Stir in the yogurt and mix again."],[null,"Serve with tortilla and salad."]],"h":[[null,"Spread the pate onto a wholemeal tortilla, roll into a cigar shape and secure with cocktail sticks, then cut into rings – ideal for a simple party nibble."],[null,"Alternatively, place a teaspoon onto a tortilla chip for Mexican-style canapés. (Add to the chips just before serving so they stay crisp)."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"7627305":{"s":[[null,"Combine the mince, breadcrumbs and half the spices and dried herbs in a bowl. Roll the mixture into 20 balls."],[null,"Lightly mist a non-stick frying pan with cooking spray. Cook the meatballs over a medium heat, turning occasionally, for 5 minutes, or until browned all over."],[null,"Set the meatballs aside and mist the pan again. Add the onion, cook for 5 minutes, then add the remaining dried spices and herbs, along with the tomatoes, kidney beans, 125ml water and the meatballs. Stir, then bring to a boil. Reduce the heat and simmer, covered, for 10 minutes or until the meatballs are cooked."],[null,"Serve topped with the coriander and yogurt."]],"h":[[null,"Add a chopped red pepper to the onions to boost the veg content and flavour of the sauce"],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"9570781":{"s":[[null,"If you don't have cooked brown rice, start by cooking your rice according to package directions. Rice will roughly triple in size, so use 1/3 cup raw brown rice to get approx 1 cup needed for this recipe."],[null,"In a large skillet, add 2-3 tablespoons of water or broth along with the chopped onion and pepper and sauté until softened and reduced, approx 5 minutes. Turn off the heat and add the cooked rice, beans, corn, salsa, and all the seasoning and mix well. Taste and add more seasoning if desired, and then set aside."],[null,"Line a 9\"x13\" (or similar size) baking dish with parchment paper and preheat your oven to 425 degrees F (218 degrees C)."],[null,"Slice your zucchini in half lengthwise as evenly as possible. Then carefully scrape out the flesh using a metal teaspoon. Place your hollowed zucchini boats hollow side up in your baking dish."],[null,"Divide the stuffing between your 8 zucchini boats. Then cover the tray with parchment paper and then foil and bake for 25-30 minutes, until zucchini is easily pierced with a fork."],[null,"Serve with guacamole and any other desired toppings."]],"h":[[null,"Use caution, and gently scrape, to avoid breaking your zucchini . Hold the zucchini half firmly in one hand, and scrape from the top down with a metal teaspoon. You may sub the brown rice with cooked quinoa or cooked barley if preferred. Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-4 days. Reheat in the oven or toaster oven. The nutritional information is for 2 stuffed zucchini boats (2 zucchini halves) not including optional toppings."]]},"6716322":{"s":[[null,"In a skillet, heat oil over medium heat."],[null,"Add diced onions and cook until softened."],[null,"Stir in cauliflower rice and cook for 3–5 minutes until it begins to soften."],[null,"Add diced bell peppers, black beans, ground cumin, and chili powder to the skillet. Cook for an additional 3–5 minutes. Season the mixture with salt and pepper."],[null,"Push the mixture to the side of the skillet, creating wells for the eggs."],[null,"Crack one egg into each well and cook until the whites are set but the yolks are still runny. If desired, cover the skillet to help the eggs cook more evenly."],[null,"Once the eggs are cooked to your liking, remove the skillet from heat."],[null,"Divide the egg, cauliflower rice and veggie mixture into four bowls."],[null,"Top each bowl with salsa and fresh cilantro, if using. Serve with lime wedges on the side."]],"h":[]},"3330":{"s":[[null,"Set butter out to soften."],[null,"To make cherry filling, mix the cherries, granulated sugar, corn starch and lemon juice in a sauce pan and bring to a boil over medium heat. Boil for 10 minutes or until thickened, stirring frequently. Once thickened, remove from heat and let cool to room temperature. Put in a covered bowl and refrigerate until ready to use."],[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F and spray a 9 x 9-inch square baking dish with nonstick spray. You can then line the bottom of the dish with parchment paper to make it easier to remove the bars."],[null,"Combine flour, oats, brown sugar, baking powder and salt into a bowl and mix to combine."],[null,"Add softened butter and use a pastry blender or your hands to work the mixture into crumbs."],[null,"Add 2/3 of the crumb mixture to the prepared pan and press down firmly. Top with cooled cherry filling. Sprinkle remaining crumb mixture on top of the cherries. Place in oven and bake for 30 to 35 minutes or until just golden brown."],[null,"Remove from oven and let cool completely before cutting into bars. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"You can make the filling ahead and refrigerate up to 2 days before making bars."],[null,"Bars are delicious both at room temperature or chilled in the fridge. This recipe is not recommended for people with diabetes due to the high carbohydrate content. However, it can be made with low-calorie sweeteners to decrease carbohydrate to 25 grams."]]},"3442":{"s":[[null,"Spray a 12-ounce coffee cup with cooking spray. Combine the milk, egg and egg whites in the mug and beat until blended."],[null,"Place coffee cup in microwave and cook for 45 seconds; remove and stir. Microwave an addition 30-45 seconds, until eggs are almost set."],[null,"Sprinkle with pepper and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Microwaves vary in cooking time. Adjust as needed to avoid overcooked eggs."],[null,"Add 1/4 cup chopped onion, bell pepper or mushrooms for additional flavor."],[null,"Add a dash of hot sauce if desired."]]},"3363":{"s":[[null,"In a small skillet cook the turkey sausage until browned. Chop into crumbles while cooking."],[null,"Prepare the jars by spraying the insides with cooking spray."],[null,"Dice the bell pepper, onion, broccoli and mushrooms. In a small bowl combine the chopped vegetables. Slice the jalapeno pepper."],[null,"Add 1/4 cup sausage, 1 tablespoon cheese, 1/4 cup diced vegetables mixture and 2 to 3 jalapeno pepper slices to each jar."],[null,"Cover and store the jars for up to 4 days in the refrigerator."],[null,"When ready to eat, beat 2 eggs, add to the jar and stir well. Microwave for 30 seconds and stir. Repeat until eggs are set. (It may take 1-1/2 to 2 minutes depending on your microwave.)"],[null,"Carefully remove the jar from the microwave and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"• The jars can be frozen. Transfer from the freezer to the refrigerator the night before you plan to add eggs and cook. • Mix and match other lower potassium vegetables such as asparagus, green onion, kale or zucchini. • Select a natural low-sodium cheese like cheddar or Swiss. If using a higher sodium cheese like parmesan or feta reduce the amount to 1/2 tablespoon •Choose from chicken or turkey sausage without phosphorus additives. Be aware some reduced-sodium breakfast meats are quite high in potassium due to potassium additives. • For an additive-free, lower sodium sausage try Homemade Turkey Sausage or Homemade Pan Sausage from recipes on DaVita.com."]]},"2529":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, melt butter in microwave for 1 minute."],[null,"Add marshmallow crème and microwave for 30 seconds; stir. Microwave 30 seconds more and stir until well blended."],[null,"Quickly add protein powder and mix until smooth."],[null,"Quickly add pre-measured rice crispy cereal and mix until coated."],[null,"Pour into a greased 13” x 9” pan and press down evenly."],[null,"Cool, and then cut into 12 bars, 3” x 4” each."]],"h":[[null,"After protein powder is added mix quickly and add rice crispy cereal in as soon as possible because the protein powder will start to harden as it cools."],[null,"Nutrition facts based on use with EAS 100% Whey Protein powder. One half cup weighs 84 grams and contains 54 grams protein. Since protein powders vary in the amount of protein, phosphorus and calcium, ask your dietitian for a list of acceptable brands."],[null,"These treats are great for a snack, dessert, or breakfast on the go!"],[null,"Marshmallow crème is also known as marshmallow fluff."],[null,"Compared to the other High Protein Rice Treats recipe on DaVita.com, this version has less protein powder so it is less dense. Both are very tasty!"]]},"2016":{"s":[[null,"Spray a 12-ounce microwave-safe mug with cooking spray."],[null,"In a bowl, combine the milk (or milk substitute), ketchup, oats and onion powder."],[null,"Crumble beef over the mixture and mix well. Pat into the mug."],[null,"Cover and microwave, on HIGH, for 3 minutes or until meat is no longer pink."]],"h":[[null,"Compare brands and select the lowest sodium ketchup."],[null,"Look for ground beef with at least 7% fat for this recipe. Ground turkey makes a good substitute."],[null,"Use your favorite milk substitute instead of milk if desired."],[null,"If you are on a lower protein diet, adjust the amount of ground beef to match your meal plan."]]},"7046638":{"s":[[null,"Add the oats, optional sweetener, cinnamon and apple to a mug and mix."],[null,"Add 100ml water and cook at full power (800W) for two minutes."],[null,"Add the milk, mix and sprinkle over a little cinnamon."]],"h":[[null,"You could use pear or banana instead of apple or add a little dried fruit, such as prunes or raisins."],[null,"Try adding a few chopped nuts, or sunflower or pumpkin seeds."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"7284915":{"s":[[null,"In a bowl, beat the egg, yogurt, white pepper and cheeses together, mixing well. Stir in the spring onion and peas."],[null,"Stir in the flour and baking powder, mixing well. Lightly oil a mug, then add the ingredients. Heat for 2 minutes on full power (800W) then leave to stand for 1 minute."],[null,"Sprinkle with paprika and a few chives to serve."],[null,"Can either be eaten direct from the mug or turned out onto a plate and served with salad."]],"h":[[null,"Add more fresh herbs, such as parsley, mint or basil for extra flavour."],[null,"You could use other vegetables such as sweetcorn, finely chopped celery or peppers."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"7671544":{"s":[[null,"Slice the banana and divide between 4 small coffee cups, to three quarters of the way up to the top."],[null,"In a bowl, mix together the beaten egg, cocoa powder and sweetener."],[null,"Add the yogurt and almond extract. Beat until smooth."],[null,"Mix in the baking powder and divide the mixture evenly between the four cups."],[null,"Microwave on full power (800W) for two minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Use chunks of fresh pear instead of the banana."],[null,"Try adding vanilla extract in place of almond, or spice it up with a teaspoon of ginger powder."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"7951025":{"s":[[null,"Place the salmon in a bowl and add the sesame oil and five-spice, mixing well to coat the salmon."],[null,"Put some of the broccoli and spring onions into a mug, add some salmon and then more broccoli, distributing evenly. You can cram it in as it will shrink a little when cooked."],[null,"Add 2 tsp water then cover with cling film and pierce a hole in the top."],[null,"Heat for 2 minutes, leave to stand for 1 minute before removing the film and serving."]],"h":[[null,"Try adding other vegetables, such as mangetout or thin slices of pepper."],[null,"For a tandoori twist, try using curry powder in place of the Chinese five-spice powder."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"7163244":{"s":[[null,"Add the egg to a bowl and beat in the yogurt, cornflour and cheese. Stir in the spring onion and sweetcorn. Add a grind of pepper."],[null,"Lightly oil a mug and add the ingredients. Heat for two minutes on full power (800W). Leave to stand for 1 minute before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Can either be eaten directly from the mug or turned out onto a plate and served with salad or seasonal vegetables."],[null,"Frozen peas work well instead of corn, or try a mixture of both."],[null,"Add some fresh basil, chives, coriander or parsley for extra flavour."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"3029":{"s":[[null,"Place ingredients in a jar and shake to combine."],[null,"Store until ready to use."]],"h":[[null,"Use to season meat, poultry or rice."],[null,"Adjust the amount to suit your taste."]]},"3538":{"s":[[null,"Slice tortillas into 1 to 2-inch strips. Chop the green onions and bell pepper half."],[null,"Heat oil in a sauté pan on medium to medium-high heat."],[null,"Sauté tortilla strips in oil until lightly browned."],[null,"Add onions and bell pepper; sauté with tortillas until softened, around 2 minutes."],[null,"Scramble eggs in a bowl and pour over the tortilla mixture."],[null,"Cook eggs to desired consistency."],[null,"Add pepper to taste and top with salsa verde. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Try the DaVita.com low sodium Salsa Verde to serve with Migas. If using commercially prepared salsa verde look for the brand lowest in sodium."],[null,"For a higher protein breakfast add extra egg whites."]]},"6238095":{"s":[[null,"Add all ingredients to a blender and blend until smooth."]],"h":[]},"6106729":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375 degrees F. Coat a 9-inch x 13-inch baking dish with cooking spray. Set aside."],[null,"Add the olive oil to a nonstick sauté pan over medium heat. Add the onions and asparagus and sauté for 4-5 minutes, or until the onions turn clear."],[null,"Mix the sautéed vegetables with the cooked millet and set aside to cool."],[null,"Slice a pocket into one side of each chicken breast that runs the entire length of the chicken breast, without coming out the other side."],[null,"Once the millet and vegetables are cooled, stuff 1/2 cup of filling in the pocket of each chicken breast and lay them side by side in the baking dish."],[null,"Brush each breast with Dijon mustard."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix together the breadcrumbs, tarragon, salt (optional), and pepper. Divide the breadcrumb topping among each breast, coating the top completely. Spray each breast with cooking spray and bake for 35 minutes or until the internal temperature of chicken is 165 degrees F."],[null,"Let the chicken rest for at least 5 minutes before slicing."]],"h":[]},"7393623":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4. Make the pastry by mixing all the ingredients together, then kneading a few times. Roll into a ball, cover with cling film and place in the fridge for 20 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, mix the mincemeat with the grated apple, carrot, sunflower seeds and mixed spice."],[null,"Roll out the pastry, cut into rounds and line a 12-cup shallow bun tin."],[null,"Add the mincemeat mixture to the pastry cases so they are three-quarters full, then bake in the oven for 15-20 minutes. Once cooked, remove from the oven and allow to cool on a rack."],[null,"Prepare the toppings (see ingredient list), squeezing lemon juice over the apple and pear to stop browning."],[null,"Just before serving, garnish the pies with a variety of the topping ingredients: wedge of fresh fig and a walnut: 1 tsp apple or pear, plus a cherry: a few flaked toasted almonds with orange zest, or any combination you like – use your imagination!"]],"h":[[null,"For a citrus zing, try adding the grated zest of an orange or lemon to the mincemeat."],[null,"You can also add ground cinnamon, nutmeg or ginger in place of mixed spice."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Defrost for 2 hours to serve, or defrost in the microwave or a moderate oven."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"7683555":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4. Heat the oil in a saucepan, add the onions and stir until lightly browned."],[null,"Add the mushrooms and minced beef and stir for 4-5 minutes breaking up any clumps of meat with a wooden spoon."],[null,"Add the diced carrot and sweet potato, sprinkle with the flour and mix well. Stir in the tomato puree, pepper and thyme."],[null,"Stir in the stock, bring to the boil, cover with the pan lid, reduce the heat and simmer for 12-15 minutes until the carrots are tender. Add the peas, stir and place the mixture in an ovenproof dish."],[null,"Spray a little oil onto the filo sheets and put slightly ‘scrunched’ layers on top of the beef mixture."],[null,"Bake for 10 minutes until the pastry is lightly browned. Serve with steamed carrots, corn and broccoli."]],"h":[[null,"You could use any mince, such as turkey, or meat alternative (e.g. soya) for this dish."],[null,"For a gluten-free version, use gluten-free flour to thicken the sauce and top with very thinly sliced sweet potato rather than the filo. You'll need to increase the cooking time to 15 minutes."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"6618374":{"s":[[null,"Heat olive oil in a large sauté pan over medium heat. Add onions and carrots and sauté until they start to soften, about 4 minutes."],[null,"Add garlic and sauté an additional 1 minute, being careful not to burn it."],[null,"Stir in the dry spices and coat the vegetables. Add the tomatoes, chickpeas, white wine vinegar, and broth."],[null,"Add the pasta and stir it well. Cover the pan and allow it to cook for 6–7 minutes, until the pasta is just starting to soften."],[null,"Add the kale and continue cooking for another 2 minutes, just long enough to wilt the kale and finish cooking the pasta."]],"h":[]},"4485103":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F. Spray muffin tins with non-stick cooking spray."],[null,"In a mixing bowl, whisk egg whites until frothy."],[null,"Add rice milk, 1/3 cup of maple syrup, vanilla and cinnamon."],[null,"Fold in grated apples, cranberries and bread cubes. Allow bread to absorb the liquid, approximately 5 minutes."],[null,"Divide the bread pudding mixture between 8 muffin compartments and bake for 30 minutes or until the bread pudding is firm to the touch."],[null,"Glaze the tops with the remaining maple syrup and serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"You can let the bread puddings cool and refrigerate them until ready to serve. Apple sauce and powdered sugar also make a good garnish."],["Unenriched rice beverage: a kidney-friendly milk replacement","On a kidney diet, one of the first changes is to limit dairy because of its potassium and phosphorus content. One cup of reduced-fat cow’s milk contains 8 fluid ounces, 342 milligrams of potassium and 224 milligrams of phosphorus. In comparison, one cup of unenriched, unsweetened rice beverage has 8 fluid ounces, 65 milligrams of potassium and 134 milligrams of phosphorus. When substituting ingredients, consider the following ideas to ensure cooking success. Portion Size: While many recipe substitutions require adjusting the portion size, rice beverage and milk are interchangeable. If the recipe includes one cup of milk, simply replace with one cup of rice beverage. Flavor Preference: Depending on the recipe, choose flavored or unflavored rice beverage. For example, if you are preparing an egg casserole, keep plain rice beverage on hand versus vanilla rice beverage, which may alter the flavor of the final product. Composition: With similar consistency to milk, rice beverage can serve as an ingredient replacement. Desserts, breakfast dishes and other recipes will turn out fine and are a better choice for your kidney diet."]]},"7661931":{"s":[[null,"In a bowl, mix together the soft cheese, lemon zest and juice, capers, herbs and salmon. Season to taste, then chill in the fridge until ready to serve."],[null,"Split and toast the mini bagels, spread with the salmon mixture and serve."]],"h":[[null,"'At risk' groups such as infants, children, pregnant women, the elderly and those who are unwell should avoid eating ready-to-eat, cold-smoked or cured fish. Therefore, this recipe is not suitable if this applies to you."],[null,"Choose wholemeal bagels for a higher fibre option."]]},"4410134":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F. Prepare muffin tins with muffin liners."],[null,"In a mixing bowl, combine graham crumbs with melted butter. Place approximately 1 tablespoon of graham crumb mixture in the lined muffin tins, and press down. Bake for 5–10 minutes or until crumbs have set and are lightly browned."],[null,"In a mixing bowl, blend together cream cheese, sugar, flour, and lemon zest to a smooth consistency. Scrape down the sides of the mixing bowl to minimize lumps. Add the egg, egg whites, yogurt, and vanilla to combine. Do not overmix."],[null,"Divide the cheesecake mixture between 12 lined muffin tins. Bake for 15–20 minutes or until the cheesecake is firm to the touch. (Do not over bake or cheesecakes will crack!)"],[null,"In a saucepan, heat raspberry jam, frozen blueberries, and lemon juice. Simmer until the blueberries begin to break down and become saucy."],[null,"Allow both the cheesecakes and sauce to cool before applying the blueberry topping."],[null,"Divide the topping among the cakes. Refrigerate until ready to serve."]],"h":[["Blueberries","Fruits should be incorporated regularly into your kidney diet. Fruits rich in color give your body fiber, carbohydrates and a variety of vitamins and minerals. Blueberries are one “Power Food” that you should regularly eat. The color of blueberries comes from anthocyanidins, a powerful antioxidant that research has shown to be beneficial to reduce inflammation and support heart, bone, brain health. A one-cup portion of blueberries is low in sodium, potassium and phosphorus. These berries are also packed with vitamin C, vitamin K, manganese and fiber making this food an excellent choice to include at any meal. Try using blueberries as a topping for breakfast pancakes or waffles. Add as part of a low potassium fruit salad or a sandwich topper for lunch. Create a delicious dinner by using blueberries as a sauce on poultry or beef. If you are short on time, grab a handful to take with you for a quick and healthy snack."]]},"7197806":{"s":[[null,"Mix the flour and baking powder in a bowl."],[null,"In a separate bowl, beat together the egg, milk and vanilla extract."],[null,"Make a well in the middle of the flour, then gradually stir in the egg and milk mixture until you get a smooth batter. Ideally, leave the batter to stand for a few minutes before cooking."],[null,"Lightly crush half the blueberries with a fork and mix these into the batter, along with the remaining (whole) blueberries."],[null,"Add a little oil to a non-stick pan, then add the batter to the pan, 1 tbsp at a time, to create small pancakes, making sure the blueberries are evenly distributed."],[null,"Cook the pancakes on a medium heat for 2–3 minutes, then turn and cook for a further 2 minutes. The pancakes are ready to turn when you see bubbles appearing on the surface. Sprinkle with a little sugar before serving, if using. Serve with some unsweetened yogurt or unsweetened crème fraiche, if liked."]],"h":[[null,"You should be able to cook 3–4 pancakes at a time, depending on pan size, but it’s a good idea to just cook one pancake first to check the pan isn’t too hot or too cool."],[null,"Keep the first batch of pancakes warm by placing on a plate over a pan of gently simmering water."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Defrost for 2 hours, or defrost/warm in the microwave or a moderate oven."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"7034454":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 170°C/ gas 3. Put the mixed fruit, figs and spices into a bowl. Mix, then add the boiling water, cover and leave to stand for 15 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, mash the banana and mix in the grated apple, oatmeal, ground almonds, seeds and zest."],[null,"Next, combine everything together in one bowl, mixing well."],[null,"Lightly oil two 12-cup mini bun tins (or simply make 2 batches in the same tin) and place the mixture into the tins."],[null,"Bake in the oven for 15-25 minutes, depending on the size of the bun tins."],[null,"When cooked (they are firm and a knife comes out clean), turn out onto a wire rack and allow to cool."]],"h":[[null,"You can use any sized bun tin, just adjust the cooking time accordingly, as larger buns will take longer to cook."],[null,"These small puddings cook much more quickly and you don't need to steam them, making them ideal for pre-Christmas parties, too."],[null,"Try topping with nuts or orange slices for super-luxury puddings."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Defrost in the microwave then steam, microwave, or heat in a moderate oven."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"7512154":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4. Lightly oil a shallow muffin tray."],[null,"Cut the filo pastry into 8cm squares and spray a little oil on one side. Arrange a filo square into each of the muffin compartments. Spray more squares with oil and add them on top. Repeat so each muffin compartment has three layers of pastry."],[null,"Meanwhile, make the filling by mixing together the eggs, pumpkin, yoghurt and spices in a large bowl."],[null,"Place the filling into the pastry cases and bake for 10-12 minutes until the filo case is lightly browned and the pumpkin still feels a bit wobbly in the centre. Top with the pumpkin seeds and orange zest to serve."]],"h":[[null,"If you prefer, you could make one large pie - line a baking tin with the filo pastry and allow an extra 8-10 minutes cooking time."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"6827574":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350 degrees F."],[null,"Arrange thawed phyllo cups on to a baking sheet. Set aside."],[null,"In a medium bowl, mix together pears, goat cheese, egg whites and ground black pepper."],[null,"Fill each phyllo cup with a heaping Tbsp. of pear mixture."],[null,"Drizzle to top of each tart with a little balsamic vinegar."],[null,"Bake for 15 minutes. Serve hot or room temperature."]],"h":[]},"4214336":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F (conventional oven)."],[null,"Brush wontons with olive oil and press into mini muffin cups. Bake for approximately 5 minutes or until they turn golden brown."],[null,"Heat olive oil in a frying pan and sauté shrimp with the chili powder until they turn pink and opaque."],[null,"In a mixing bowl, combine corn, red pepper, garlic, jalapeno, onion, lime juice, and cilantro."],[null,"Fill wonton tacos with corn salsa and top with a shrimp."]],"h":[[null,"Baked Wonton cups can be made ahead of time. They can be the basis for many appetizers. Examples: Fill them with your favorite dips and garnish with a vegetable. When you brush them with olive oil and herbs before baking they make homemade chips, which can be enjoyed as a snack without any other ingredients."]]},"7573930":{"s":[[null,"Beat the egg, yogurt and almond extract into the milk, then place the flour, baking powder, sweetener and spices into a bowl and gradually stir in the milk mixture until you make a smooth batter."],[null,"Add the orange juice, zest and dried fruit and mix well."],[null,"Add the oil to a large non-stick pan. Add small dessertspoons of the mixture to the pan to fry for 1-2 minutes, then flip over with a spatula and cook for another minute or two on the other side."],[null,"The pancakes should be about 3-4cm in diameter and only 3–4mm thick."],[null,"To serve, add the pancakes to a serving platter and top with orange segments, scatter with zest and pomegranate seeds."]],"h":[[null,"To neatly segment an orange, remove the top and bottom of the orange and place the orange onto a cutting board. Cut downwards from the top to the bottom, removing all the skin plus white pith without cutting into the orange. Once you’ve removed all the pith carefully, slice into one segment, avoiding the membrane, then twist your knife to slice outwards. You’re then able to remove each segment without any of the bitter pith."],[null,"Try adding different spices such as ginger or nutmeg to the pancakes, or use lemon rather than orange zest."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"7100422":{"s":[[null,"Line 4 teacups, dariole or individual mini pudding basin moulds with clingfilm."],[null,"Cut 4 x 5cm circles out of the bread and press into the base of the moulds. Cut 4 larger circles of bread (big enough to cover as a lid). Cut the remaining bread into strips and use to line the sides of the moulds."],[null,"Place the summer fruits in a saucepan, and heat gently until defrosted. Sweeten to taste. Strain the fruit and reserve the juice."],[null,"Divide the fruit mixture between the bread lined cups, then top with the bread \"lids\". Spoon over the reserved juices, keeping a little juice for serving."],[null,"Cover the cups with cling film, top with a small plate and press down with a heavy weight. Refrigerate for a couple of hours."],[null,"Turn out onto plates and use the reserved juice to cover any remaining bread."],[null,"Serve with a spoonful of light crème fraiche or yogurt."]],"h":[[null,"Keep a few berries to serve with the puddings, or top with fresh raspberries or blackberries."],[null,"For best results, leave the puddings overnight in the fridge so the bread gets fully soaked with the fruit juices."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6175376":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F. Line a muffin pan with muffin papers."],[null,"Spray a sauté pan with cooking spray and heat the pan over medium-high heat. Add the onions and pepper and cook for 5 minutes. Set aside."],[null,"In a medium bowl, whisk together the remaining ingredients. Add the green pepper and onions to the egg mixture and mix well."],[null,"Pour the egg mixture into muffin cups, filling each about 2/3 full. Bake 20 minutes or until the centers of the frittatas are firm."]],"h":[]},"6975068":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350 degrees F. Line muffin tins with muffin papers and spray with cooking spray."],[null,"In a medium bowl mix together all ingredients."],[null,"Spoon artichoke mixture evenly into 10 muffin cups. Bake 20-23 minutes until lightly golden on top."]],"h":[]},"6283603":{"s":[[null,"In a medium bowl combine all ingredients, except cucumbers, and mix well."],[null,"Place cucumbers on serving platter and top with a spoonful of crab salad."]],"h":[]},"6820987":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F. Spray six, 4-ounce ramekin dishes with cooking spray."],[null,"In a medium pot heat peaches, water, and low- or no-calorie sweetener over medium-high heat. Bring to a boil; reduce heat and simmer for 10 minutes."],[null,"In a small bowl combine 1 Tsp. cornstarch and 1 tsp. cold water; stir until smooth. Pour into pot with peaches and stir 1 minute."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine Crisp Topping ingredients using hands."],[null,"Pour peach mixture evenly into six ramekin dishes. Evenly divide crisp topping and place on top of each peach ramekin dish."],[null,"Place ramekins on a baking sheet and bake in oven for 25–30 minutes."]],"h":[]},"6311574":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350 degrees F."],[null,"Line mini-muffin pan with paper baking cups and place one Nilla wafer in the bottom of each cup."],[null,"In medium bowl, add remaining ingredients and mix with an electric mixture until smooth."],[null,"Fill each muffin cup with pumpkin-cream cheese mixture."],[null,"Place muffin pan in oven and bake for 30 minutes or until done. Serve cool."]],"h":[]},"3615":{"s":[[null,"Open cream cheese and place entire bar onto a serving plate."],[null,"Spread jelly on the top of the cream cheese."],[null,"Serve with low-sodium crackers or flat bread."]],"h":[[null,"Prepare the night before or right before serving. It’s very easy and inexpensive!"],[null,"You can use any jelly flavor, but green is nice for St. Patty’s Day. Try jalapeño pepper jelly for an extra kick."]]},"7403442":{"s":[[null,"Bring a large pan of water to the boil, add the peas, cucumber, mint, basil and watercress and simmer for 5 mins. Drain. Set aside 2 tbsp peas then return the mixture to the pan. Add the juice and water, and heat until almost boiling."],[null,"Remove from the heat and stir in the crème fraiche. Blend until smooth."],[null,"Divide between two bowls, scatter over the remaining peas, drizzle with a little extra crème fraiche and some freshly ground black pepper."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"7494114":{"s":[[null,"Chargrill or grill the aubergine slices and courgettes for 3-4 minutes each side, then reserve and keep warm."],[null,"Mix the balsamic vinegar, mint, olive oil and pepper together and set aside."],[null,"Toss the aubergine and courgettes into the oil and vinegar mixture and reserve."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the pine nuts to a dry pan over a medium heat. Toast them until starting to brown, then remove from heat and set aside."],[null,"Place the rocket onto a serving plate and top with the aubergine and courgettes. Scatter with the beans, onion and pine nuts."]],"h":[[null,"Try serving in pitta breads with a little grated cheese."],[null,"You can use any beans you like, or try with frozen baby broad beans."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"2482":{"s":[[null,"In a 1-quart pitcher, mix lemon juice, sugar and mint leaves. Add 3-1/2 cups of cold water to fill the pitcher."],[null,"Chill until cold."],[null,"Serve in a 6-ounce glass with a sprig of mint to garnish."]],"h":[[null,"For a stronger mint flavor crush the mint leaves."],[null,"To reduce carbohydrate and calories substitute Splenda® sweetener for sugar (12 packets or 1/2 cup Splenda® granular. Calories are reduced to 16 and carbohydrate to 4 grams."]]},"6009687":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, whisk the soy sauce, white rice miso paste, rice wine vinegar, toasted sesame oil, olive oil, unsweetened multi-use syrup, fresh ginger, and lime juice in a small bowl."],[null,"Add in the cabbage, red onion, corn, carrot, scallions, and cilantro and toss to combine."],[null,"Allow to rest at least 15 minutes before serving so flavors can meld."]],"h":[]},"6182454":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to broil. Place a rack in the middle of the oven. Coat a baking sheet with cooking spray."],[null,"Cut the fish into 4, 4-oz portions and arrange on the prepared baking sheet."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix together 1 ½ Tsp. of sesame oil and the miso soup mix powder to form a paste. Brush the tops of each of the fish fillets with the glaze (coating will be very thin). Spray each fillet with cooking spray and place baking sheet on middle rack of the oven. Broil for 6 minutes."],[null,"While the fish is broiling, add the remaining 1 ½ Tsp. of sesame oil and more cooking spray to a wok or large sauté pan over high heat. Stir fry the cabbage, garlic, snow peas and hot sauce for 4 minutes, until just wilted but still slightly crunchy."],[null,"Remove fish from baking sheet and serve on top of 3/4 cup of the stir-fried vegetables."]],"h":[]},"6970983":{"s":[[null,"Whisk the maple syrup, miso, vinegar, red pepper flakes, and orange zest and juice in a small bowl to combine."],[null,"Spray a medium nonstick skillet with cooking spray and heat over medium heat. Place the salmon in the skillet—skin side down—and cook until the skin is very crisp and deep golden brown, 7–9 minutes. Continue to cook until it’s very lightly browned on the flesh side and registers 145 degrees F on an instant read thermometer, approximately 2 minutes."],[null,"Add the glaze. Cook, stirring occasionally, until the glaze begins to thicken, about 2 minutes."],[null,"Place salmon on plates and garnish with any remaining glaze from the pan."]],"h":[]},"9066125":{"s":[[null,"Whisk all the ingredients in a small pot and bring to a boil."],[null,"Then lower heat to medium to maintain a low boil and whisk often until thickened. Serve warm."]],"h":[[null,"Make sure to whisk the ingredients at room temperature (before starting to heat the gravy) so the flour doesn’t get lumpy. For thicker miso gravy , add an additional 2 tablespoons of flour. For gluten free , use brown rice flour. Leftovers keep refrigerated in a sealed container for up to 5 days, or freeze air tight for up to 3 months. It will thicken as it cools, so loosen with a splash of broth or water, as needed and reheat on stove top."]]},"9791180":{"s":[[null,"Bring a large pot of salted water to a boil and cook your pasta according to package directions for 'al dente' pasta. If there are no package directions for 'al dente' undercook the pasta by 1-2 minutes."],[null,"Reserve 1/2 cup of the pasta water, drain the pasta, return it to the pot and set it aside."],[null,"Meanwhile, add all the pesto ingredients to your food processor, blending until combined and adding 2-4 tablespoons of water, if needed."],[null,"Toss the cooked pasta with the miso pesto, adding as much of the reserved pasta water as you'd like to thin out the sauce to your taste. Then serve."]],"h":[[null,"Use UNSALTED sunflower seeds to prevent the dish from being too salty."],[null,"Salt your cooking water. Make sure to add enough salt to your pot of water for the best texture and flavour. Here's a handy guide to help you salt your water perfectly each time."],[null,"Cook to 'al dente' texture. Do not overcook! Al dente means that the pasta is still firm once cooked, giving optimal texture in every bite. To ensure it does not overcook, start taste testing a few minutes before the package says it will be ready. It should be tender, but still firm."],[null,"Reserve some starchy cooking water before draining your pasta to thin out the miso pesto sauce to your taste."]]},"7837338":{"s":[[null,"Heat the sunflower oil in a medium pan, add the onion, garlic, red and green peppers and chilli, fry for 3-4 minutes until beginning to soften."],[null,"Lightly crush half the pulses using the back of a fork. Add to the pan with the remaining pulses, chopped tomatoes, tomato puree, sweetcorn, cumin, oregano, salt and pepper."],[null,"Bring to the boil, turn down the heat and simmer for 10 minutes. Stir through the coriander and serve with the cooked rice."]],"h":[[null,"You can add more or less chilli, depending on how hot (or not) you like your food."],[null,"Why not try red or green lentils, red kidney beans or chickpeas."],[null,"Freezing instructions (not rice): Suitable for freezing once cooked. Then defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"4546780":{"s":[[null,"Drain and rinse the chickpeas and red beans."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine chickpeas, red beans, red onion, green onion, bell pepper, and celery."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the vinegar, garlic, sugar, and black pepper."],[null,"Pour the dressing over the salad and mix until all ingredients are well coated."],[null,"Cover with plastic wrap and refrigerate overnight or for at least 12 hours."],[null,"Drain the salad to remove excess dressing before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Note: This salad can be kept in the refrigerator for a couple of days. Drain the liquid from the portion you are serving and return the rest to the refrigerator."],["Cost effective plant-based eating","Plant-based protein is an important part of a diet for chronic kidney disease (CKD). In comparison to protein from meat, poultry, and fish, plant-based choices are often less expensive, lower in fat, and rich in fiber. While reading food labels is necessary to watch for sodium and additives, choosing healthy plant-based foods for people with CKD can add variety and be budget-friendly. Beans also naturally contain phosphorus, however, because beans come from plants, only about 20 to 40% of the phosphorus is absorbed by the body. For example, a one-half cup serving of black beans contains roughly 120 milligrams of phosphorus, but the body absorbs approximately 48 milligrams or less from that portion. In comparison, this is much lower than the amount of phosphorus absorbed from meat or phosphate additives. Knowing this, beans can easily be part of a healthy CKD diet. Many different recipes use beans as a high-protein, flavorful ingredient. Using the right portion can help support CKD diet goals for sodium, potassium, protein, and phosphorus. Try adding a small amount of black beans to a taco salad or a burrito. Dip fresh vegetables in hummus made from garbanzo beans. Replace sausage or ground meat with low-sodium kidney beans. Top a green salad with an ounce of edamame (soybeans)."]]},"1820":{"s":[[null,"In a medium bowl combine almond milk, vinegar and sugar."],[null,"Cut strawberries into quarters."],[null,"Add berries to liquids and and toss well."],[null,"Cover and refrigerate for 1 hour to chill."],[null,"When ready to serve chop the basil and stir into the salad."]],"h":[[null,"Try other berries in season."],[null,"Use your favorite milk or cream substitute, preferably one without phosphate additives."],[null,"Almond Breeze® almond coconut milk blend does not contain phosphate additives and is low in phosphorus and potassium compared to milk or cream. If you are limiting calcium due to high calcium levels choose another milk substitute as this product does contain calcium carbonate."]]},"6098453":{"s":[[null,"Just scoop, sprinkle, and stir all the ingredients — no cooking is needed."]],"h":[]},"2546":{"s":[[null,"In a blender add water, frozen berries, ice cubes and liquid flavor enhancer drops. Blend until slushy and mixed well."],[null,"Add whipped topping and blend well."],[null,"Add protein powder. Blend well."],[null,"Divide into 2 servings and enjoy one right away or freeze and defrost to enjoy later."]],"h":[[null,"Increase protein powder for a higher protein drink."],[null,"Select a combination of your favorite berries: raspberries, strawberries, blueberries or blackberries."]]},"7253865":{"s":[[null,"Melt the butter in a large pan, add the onion, bay leaf, celery and potatoes and fry for 3–4 minutes."],[null,"Add the coconut, milk and fish stock, bring to the boil, cover and simmer for 20–25 minutes, until the potatoes are cooked."],[null,"Using a fork, mash most of the potato and mix well to combine."],[null,"Add the fish, prawns, peas and the sweetcorn to the pan and continue to simmer for a further 5 minutes or until the fish is cooked."],[null,"Season well and serve topped with the parsley."]],"h":[[null,"To add extra vegetables, simply sautée a few mushrooms or chopped courgette and a chopped red pepper and mix in just before serving."],[null,"Spice it up with 1 tbsp mild curry paste added with the stock. Serve with a sprinkle of finely chopped coriander."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6178770":{"s":[[null,"Add the 1 cup of cranberries to a food processor and pulse a few times to coarsely chop, or chop by hand. In a bowl, toss the cranberries with the sugar-free sweetener."],[null,"Peel and section the oranges. Add the oranges and celery to the cranberries and gently toss; set aside."],[null,"For the dressing: In a small bowl, whisk together the lemon juice, ginger, honey, and mustard. Slowly add the oil in a thin stream, whisking to emulsify. Whisk in the salt and pepper."],[null,"Toss the mixed greens with 3/4 of the dressing. Add the greens to a shallow platter. Top the greens with the cranberry-orange mixture, red onions, and, if desired, whole cranberries as a garnish. Drizzle with the remaining dressing."]],"h":[]},"6204544":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6774988":{"s":[[null,"Heat olive oil in a large, wide skillet over medium heat. Add peppers, and cook until browned."],[null,"Stir in garlic and cook for 1 minute. Add green olives, then reduce heat to low and cover. Cook for 20 minutes, or until peppers are tender."],[null,"Stir in balsamic vinegar. Taste, and add salt if necessary."]],"h":[]},"7683747":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a medium pan. Add the onion and potato and fry for 3–4 minutes, until beginning to soften. Add the curry paste and continue to fry for 1 minute."],[null,"Pour over 300ml water, cover and simmer for 8–10 minutes until the potato is almost tender."],[null,"Add the cauliflower and peas and continue to boil for 5–6 minutes, stir through the baked beans, heat through and serve with pitta bread and raita."]],"h":[[null,"You could use a tin of mixed beans in chilli sauce in place of baked beans."],[null,"Try using a sweet potato in place of ordinary potato."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Then defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"3051":{"s":[[null,"Peel, seed and dice cucumber and red pepper."],[null,"Chop dill and scallions."],[null,"Combine all ingredients in a serving bowl and mix."],[null,"Chill for at least one hour before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Use low-fat sour cream if desired."]]},"9996156":{"s":[[null,"Line a tray with parchment paper and set it aside. Then, add all the ingredients to your food processor bowl. Pulse until well combined without completely pureéing the mixture."],[null,"Use a small cookie scoop or spoon to scoop the mixture and roll balls. Place each ball on your lined tray."],[null,"You may enjoy immediately, or refrigerate for 1 hour or longer to chill."]],"h":[[null,"Don't over-blend the mixture, as these snacks taste best with a little bit of texture."],[null,"The batter is a little sticky, so use wet hands to roll the mixture into balls to prevent it from sticking to your hands."],[null,"Store your mocha energy balls in the fridge for up to 5 days or keep them frozen for up to 3 months."]]},"5359320":{"s":[[null,"Break the Vitabite into a small bowl and add the Renastep."],[null,"Microwave at 10 seconds intervals until completely melted."],[null,"Mix until combined and then add in the coffee. Then mix again."],[null,"Pour into lolly moulds and freeze for 24 hours."]],"h":[["Renastep note","This recipe may not be suitable for children under the age of 12 years as it contains caffeine"],["Renastep note","Renastep and Vitabite are foods for special medical purposes and must be used under medical supervision. Renastep is for the dietary management of kidney disease and is suitable from 3 years of age onwards. Vitabite is for use in protein restricted diets and is suitable from 1 year of age onwards. Renastep contains Milk (milk protein) and Fish (Tuna Oils). Vitabite contains Milk (lactose) and Soya (soya lecithin)."],["Renastep note","This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutrimen dietary analysis software. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information."]]},"4052289":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400°F. Place oven rack in middle of oven. Line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Remove excess liquid from the tofu by placing the tofu block between paper towels and applying some pressure with your hands. Place chunks of the tofu into the food processor and chop until the texture resembles minced meat."],[null,"Prepare mock meat balls: Add all ingredients, except the olive oil, to the food processor. Chop until the mixture becomes a paste."],[null,"Heat oil in a non-stick frying pan over medium-high heat and fry the vegetable mixture for about 10 minutes."],[null,"Prepare sauce: in a bowl, combine the chicken stock, ketchup, and other sauce ingredients."],[null,"Combine sauce (step 8) and vegetables (step 7) and reduce heat to medium. Cover and simmer for another 15–20 minutes. {10 Cook the pasta according to package instructions. {11 Serve the mock meat balls with the sauce over pasta and enjoy!"]],"h":[["Low phosphorus pasta sauces","Different oils, milk-based creams, meat, seasonings, spices, and vegetables make pasta sauces rich in flavor, but certain ingredients can be high in phosphorus. With chronic kidney disease, limiting phosphorus is recommended. This may require changes to the recipe or a limit in portion size. Meals don’t have to be lacking in flavor though. Choosing and creating tasty, low phosphorus sauces allows you to consume some of your favorites as part of a kidney-friendly diet. When selecting a pasta meal, top noodles with a blend of simple and unprocessed ingredients to meet your nutrition goals. Sauces made with cow’s milk, nonfat evaporated milk, canned cream soups, or American cheese are naturally high in phosphorus. Read the ingredient list on food labels and make note of ingredients that contain the word “phos” to determine those that contain phosphorus additives. If choosing this type of food, limiting the total portion will be necessary as the phosphorus absorption from these foods is high. Ingredients for sauces that are lower in phosphorus include broth, oil, fresh vegetables and herbs. For many individuals with kidney disease, high-potassium tomato-based sauces need to be limited. Depending on your preference, sauces can be pureed by combining cooked ingredients with oil or broth with use of a blender or food processor. For more texture, add diced vegetables such as sautéed peppers, onions and mushrooms. The addition of small amounts of plant-based protein such as cubed or crumbled tofu can also add protein without too much added phosphorus."]]},"6769262":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F. Coat a 9x13-inch baking dish with cooking spray. Set aside."],[null,"Cook the pasta according to the package directions minus two minutes (the pasta should be slightly undercooked)."],[null,"While the pasta is cooking, add the olive oil to a large sauté pan over medium-high heat. Add the onion and mushrooms and sauté until the onions turn clear, about 5 minutes."],[null,"Add the spinach and no-salt seasoning and sauté until the spinach is wilted and soft, about 3 more minutes."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the flour, milk, salt and ground black pepper until all the flour lumps are mixed in. Pour over the vegetables and bring to a boil. Stir in the tuna and pasta and pour into the prepared baking pan."],[null,"Sprinkle the parmesan cheese on top of the casserole and bake for 15 minutes."]],"h":[]},"2731":{"s":[[null,"Wash and dice strawberries, cucumber and grapes. Dice watermelon. Shred mint leaves."],[null,"Combine fruit and cucumbers in a bowl. Zest the lime over the fruit. Cut the lime in half and juice into a small bowl. Add the honey and mix well."],[null,"Stir fruit with lime mixture, or if using a processor pulse until coarsely chopped. Mix in mint leaves."],[null,"Let salsa sit overnight in the refrigerator."]],"h":[[null,"Serve with low-sodium crackers or tortilla chips. Look for brands with the lowest amount of sodium."],[null,"You may also serve with homemade pita chips. Split the pitas in half and cut each half into quarters. Spray with cooking spray and bake at 350º F for about 8 minutes. You may also sprinkle with cinnamon and sugar after you spray with cooking spray."],[null,"Drain salsa through a fine sieve to remove fluid if you are on a fluid restriction."]]},"6876375":{"s":[[null,"Put the whole sweet potatoes in a large saucepan and add enough cold water to cover. Bring the potatoes to a boil over high heat. Reduce the heat to medium-low and simmer until tender, 30–35 minutes. Drain the potatoes and rinse under cold water until they're easy to handle."],[null,"Meanwhile, warm the oil in a small saucepan over high heat until warm, about 1 minute. (Or microwave the oil in a microwavable bowl on high until the oil is warm, about 30 seconds.) Add the mint leaves and crush with the handle of a wooden spoon or a pestle. Set aside."],[null,"Peel the sweet potatoes and return them to the saucepan. Add the mint mixture, lime juice, salt, and pepper. Mash the potatoes with a potato masher until smooth and creamy. Transfer the potatoes to a serving bowl, garnish with the mint sprigs, and serve hot."]],"h":[]},"2767":{"s":[[null,"Remove seeds from the jalapeno pepper."],[null,"Place ingredients in a blender or food processor and blend until smooth."],[null,"Store sauce in the refrigerator in a covered container for up to one week."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute parsley instead of cilantro if preferred. Replace jalapeno with your choice of chile pepper."],[null,"Adjust cumin and oregano to your taste."],[null,"Use Mojo Sauce as a marinade or dipping sauce. Try it with Sylvia’s Arroz a la Cubano recipe."]]},"4083992":{"s":[[null,"Finely chop onion, cabbage, garlic and ginger in a food processor."],[null,"Mix chicken or turkey with the chopped vegetables and spices to make the filling."],[null,"Moisten a wonton wrap with small amount of water."],[null,"Put about 1 tablespoon of the filling in the center of the wonton wrap and fold to seal."],[null,"Steam dumplings in a vegetable steamer for about 10 minutes, until chicken/turkey reaches 165⁰ F. Alternatively, dumplings can also be pan fried: In a sauté pan, brown the bottom of the dumplings in a small amount of cooking oil over medium heat. Add 1 cup of water to the sauté pan and cover, then cook until the water has evaporated."]],"h":[[null,"Nutrition info for steamed preparation only."]]},"9125690":{"s":[["Press the tofu","Cut your tofu into half-inch cubes. Then arrange some paper towels or a clean dish towel on a cutting board and place the tofu cubes in a single layer on top. Now add more paper towels on top of the cubes and place another cutting board, flat plate, or baking sheet on top. Finally, place something very heavy on top like a cast-iron skillet or a heavy book. Press like this for 15 minutes while you prepare the remaining ingredients."],["For the Mongolian tofu","Preheat your oven to 425°F/218°C convection bake and line a baking tray with parchment paper."],["For the Mongolian tofu","Place the pressed tofu cubes in a large mixing bowl and add the 2 tablespoons of soy sauce, and mix well. Then add the 2 tablespoons of tapioca flour and mix again."],["For the Mongolian tofu","Arrange the tofu in a single layer with space in between each piece on your baking tray. Bake for 15 minutes, then flip the cubes and bake for another 10 minutes or until desired crispiness is reached."],["For the Mongolian tofu","While the tofu is baking, prepare the Mongolian sauce. Add all the sauce ingredients to a large pan or wok and whisk to combine. Bring to a simmer over medium heat and whisk often until thickened, approx. 3 minutes."],["For the Mongolian tofu","When the tofu is baked, transfer the pieces to your pan with the sauce and give it a gentle stir."],["For the Mongolian tofu","Serve immediately with a sprinkle of sesame seeds and brown rice or side/s of your choice."]],"h":[[null,"Don’t forget to press your tofu for the best texture . Use my quick press method or you may use a tofu press if you have one."],[null,"Try and cut your cubes as uniformly as possible for even cooking."],[null,"Arrange the cubes in a single layer on your baking sheet with space in between each piece so they do not stick together and crisp up nicely."],[null,"Leftovers keep refrigerated in a sealed container for 3-4 days. The sauce will thicken as it cools, so add the Mongolian tofu to a pan with a few splashes of water to loosen it up while reheating."]]},"3412":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375° F."],[null,"While oven is still preheating, place butter in a 2-quart baking dish, and pop into oven until butter is completely melted. (Don’t forget to remove from oven once butter has finished melting.)"],[null,"As butter is melting, combine blackberries and 1 tablespoon of sugar in a small bowl."],[null,"Mix together flour, salt, baking powder and remaining 12 tablespoons (3/4 cup) sugar in another small bowl."],[null,"Add Rice Dream® to flour mixture and stir well."],[null,"Pour batter into the baking dish with the melted butter, and top with fruit mixture."],[null,"Bake for 45 minutes to an hour."]],"h":[[null,"You can substitute any other low-potassium fruit, such as blueberries, strawberries or mixed berries."],[null,"Be sure to purchase rice milk that does not contain phosphorus additives. Rice Dream Original Rice Drink®, unenriched is a great choice, as it is additive-free and tastes great."],[null,"For diabetics, use Splenda® granular sweetener instead of sugar to decrease calories to 245 and carbohydrate to 27 grams per serving."]]},"6383468":{"s":[[null,"Place the avocado, banana, milk, and ice into a blender. Blend until there are no pieces of avocado remaining and the mixture is smooth and frothy. Divide into chilled glasses and enjoy."]],"h":[]},"2078":{"s":[[null,"Place chicken legs and 6 cups water in a covered soup pot and simmer until chicken is cooked thoroughly (approximately 1 hour)."],[null,"While chicken is cooking, prepare spaghetti squash. Cut squash in half and remove seeds. Place cut side down in a baking dish with 2 tablespoons water and cover with plastic wrap. Microwave on high for 8 minutes until tender but still firm. Let squash cool 10 minutes; remove skin and cut squash into cubes. Measure 2 cups; reserve extra squash for use in other meals."],[null,"Add spaghetti squash and garbanzo beans to soup pot with chicken. Simmer for 15 minutes."],[null,"Chop zucchini and cilantro. Add zucchini, cilantro and spices to soup pot. Cook for another 15 minutes."],[null,"To prepare couscous, boil 1-1/2 cups water. Remove from heat, add dry couscous and stir well. Cover pan and let stand for 5 minutes. Fluff with a fork before serving. Makes 3 cups."],[null,"Serve soup over 1/2-cup prepared couscous."]],"h":[[null,"If desired, remove chicken from bones after step #1."],[null,"Garbanzo beans are also known as chickpeas. Measure carefully—portion must be limited due to higher potassium and phosphorus content in beans."],[null,"This recipe makes a complete meal when complemented with a beverage and dessert."]]},"7619989":{"s":[[null,"Crumble the bread and add to the beaten egg, set aside but mix occasionally until the bread has absorbed all the egg."],[null,"Meanwhile In a large bowl thoroughly mash half the chickpeas then roughly mash the other half and stir together."],[null,"Add the lamb, onion, mint, cumin and chili flakes and mix, then add the egg and bread mixture and mix well - the best way is by hand, squidging everything together."],[null,"Form into 8 burgers (approx 8 cm diameter and 2½ cm thick) and put on a plate or tray, cover with cling film and refrigerate for at least 20 minutes, an hour or two is better."],[null,"Carefully place burgers on a BBQ, griddle pan or under the grill and cook for 5-7 minutes on each side. Once you place them on a griddle or BBQ don't move or turn them until they've had chance to form a crust (4-5 minutes). Once cooked put on a plate and cover with foil."],[null,"Toast the buns if desired then build your burgers with the lettuce, tomato and onion."]],"h":[[null,"Works well with beef mince or for a lower-fat version use turkey mince."],[null,"Try with pitta bread rather than rolls and drizzle with tatziki."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Freeze in individually wrapped portions with greaseproof paper between each burger."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"6674090":{"s":[[null,"Place lentils in a medium saucepan, and add water to cover. Bring to a boil over high heat, reduce to low, and simmer, covered, for 30 minutes or until tender. Drain and set aside. (This step may be done a day ahead of time.)"],[null,"Combine lentils, tomatoes, onion, coriander, salt, and pepper in a large saucepan. Add 1 cup water, and bring to a boil over high heat. Reduce heat to low, and simmer, covered, for 10 minutes."],[null,"Add cilantro, and stir. Serve hot."]],"h":[]},"6646306":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 400 degrees F. Line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the pomegranate molasses (or balsamic vinegar), white miso paste, lemon juice, and pepper."],[null,"Place the salmon filets on the prepared baking sheet. Brush the pomegranate mixture over the salmon, making sure to coat each filet. Top each fillet with a fresh thyme sprig."],[null,"Bake the salmon in the preheated oven for about 12–15 minutes, or until the salmon is cooked through to 145 degrees F."],[null,"Remove the salmon from the oven and garnish with pomegranate arils."]],"h":[]},"4568797":{"s":[[null,"Heat oil in a skillet. Sprinkle paprika on chicken thighs. Brown chicken on both sides and transfer to a plate (10 minutes)."],[null,"In the same skillet, sauté onion, garlic, and ginger. When onions are soft, add spices and rice. Stir to coat rice."],[null,"Add cauliflower and chicken broth."],[null,"Place chicken on top of rice mixture, sprinkle with the lemon zest and bring to a boil. Cover skillet with lid and simmer until liquid is absorbed and chicken is cooked through (approximately 30 minutes)."],[null,"Before serving, add fresh cilantro."]],"h":[[null,"* Choose the broth with the lowest sodium content but be aware that low sodium products often contain more potassium. Look for potassium chloride under ingredients on the label. Potassium is a hidden ingredient normally not listed in the nutrient analysis."]]},"7902347":{"s":[[null,"Add the oil to a pan, followed by the onion, and stir for 3–4 minutes until just starting to brown."],[null,"Next, add the aubergine and butternut squash. Heat for 3–4 minutes, stirring regularly."],[null,"Add the garlic, ginger and chilli and cook for 1–2 minutes, again stirring regularly."],[null,"Add the cinnamon, turmeric and cumin. Mix well, pour in the water, stir, and then add in the tomatoes."],[null,"Mix well and bring to a gentle boil. Turn down the heat, cover and simmer for 15 minutes until the squash is soft."],[null,"Mix and serve with fresh coriander, plus some wedges of lemon."]],"h":[[null,"If you don’t have butternut squash, try sweet potatoes or a mix of other root vegetables, such as carrot, parsnip and swede."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 6"]]},"6317081":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F. Line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix the cumin, coriander, paprika, cinnamon, salt, and pepper."],[null,"Rub the spice mixture over the cod fillets. Set aside."],[null,"Toss the carrot ribbons with olive oil and a pinch of salt. Spread on the baking sheet and place cod fillets on top."],[null,"Bake for 15–18 minutes, or until the cod flakes easily with a fork and the carrots are tender-crisp."],[null,"Finish with a squeeze of lemon and sprinkle of fresh herbs before serving."]],"h":[]},"7014811":{"s":[[null,"Wrap each chicken thigh around a cinnamon stick."],[null,"Mix together the garlic, paprika, cumin and half the oil. Place the chicken into a non-metallic dish, spoon over the spice mixture and coat, then leave to marinate for at least 1 hour."],[null,"Heat the remaining oil in a pan, add the chicken pieces (still wrapped around the cinnamon stick) and brown all over. Remove from the pan using a slotted spoon and set aside."],[null,"Add the carrot and beans to the pan, cook over a low heat for about 5–6 minutes. Stir in the turmeric and add all the remaining ingredients to the pan, along with the chicken."],[null,"Pour over the stock, bring to the boil cover and simmer for 12–15 minutes, until the chicken is tender."],[null,"Season, garnish with mint and serve with plenty of steamed couscous."]],"h":[[null,"If you don’t have cinnamon sticks add 1 tsp ground cinnamon to the marinade."],[null,"For a gluten-free alternative, serve with basmati rice sprinkled with pomegranate seeds."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Then defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"7489290":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven 180°C/gas 4. Grill the aubergine slices for 3-4 minutes on each side and set aside."],[null,"Heat the oil in a pan and add the onions. When they start to brown, add the minced beef and stir for 5 minutes, breaking up any clumps with a wooden spoon."],[null,"Add the red pepper and carrot and cook for 5 minutes then stir in the garlic, tomatoes, purée, oregano and cinnamon."],[null,"Stir in the stock, bring to the boil then turn down the heat, cover and simmer for 10-15 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, make the topping mix the yogurt, Cheddar and nutmeg together."],[null,"In an ovenproof dish, place a layer of aubergine, add a spoonful of the beef mixture then layer alternately, ending with a layer of aubergine."],[null,"Spoon the yogurt mixture over the top and bake for 45 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Leave to cool for 15-20 minutes before serving."],[null,"Moussaka is often made with minced lamb. For a lower-fat version use minced turkey instead."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"6380518":{"s":[[null,"Combine mozzarella balls, tomatoes, and chickpeas in a medium bowl. Add olive oil. Stir, taste, and add salt and pepper to taste."],[null,"Wash spinach, and layer it in the bottom of a serving bowl. Arrange 1/2 cup of mozzarella-tomato-chickpea mixture on top of spinach. Serve at room temperature."]],"h":[]},"3226":{"s":[[null,"Heat a 2-quart heavy saucepan over medium heat."],[null,"Add butter and melt, then add garam masala (or spice substitute*)"],[null,"Cook for 1 or 2 minutes until spices become fragrant."],[null,"Add the diced onion and sauté until soft and golden."],[null,"Cut turkey breast into 1″ cubes. Add the turkey, raisins and apple to the pan and sauté for 5 minutes, stirring occasionally."],[null,"Add the rice and stir."],[null,"Add the chicken stock, bring to boil and cover."],[null,"Cook on medium-low heat until rice has absorbed all of the liquid, about 20 minutes."],[null,"Add the peas during the last few minutes to heat through, then toss and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Compliment this dish with a cucumber salad (sliced cucumbers, thin sliced onion, white vinegar, black pepper and sugar or sweetener)."],[null,"Spice substitute for garam masala: Combine 1/2 teaspoon cardamom, 1/2 teaspoon cinnamon, 1/4 teaspoon black pepper, 1/4 teaspoon nutmeg, 1/4 teaspoon coriander and 1/4 teaspoon cloves."],[null,"If you have diabetes you may need to reduce the rice portion if carbohydrate content is too high."]]},"1736":{"s":[[null,"To reduce potassium in potatoes use the Double Cook method. Peel and slice potatoes 1/8″ thick. Place in a large pot of room temperature water and heat to a boil. Remove from heat and drain the water. Add fresh room temperature water and boil potatoes for 10 minutes. Drain the water and add fresh water to the pot. Bring to a boil and cook until potatoes are soft enough to mash."],[null,"Mash potatoes together with the cheese and set aside."],[null,"Place flour in a medium bowl. Beat eggs and add to flour mixture. Add water 1 tablespoon at a time to make a dough that is easily rolled (more or less water may be required dending upon humidity)."],[null,"Allow dough to stand 10 minutes before rolling."],[null,"Divide dough into three balls. Roll one at a time into 1/8″ thickness. Cut into 12 squares or use a drinking glass to cut into 12 circles."],[null,"Place approximately 2 tablespoons of the potato-cheese mixture in the center of each square."],[null,"Fold edges to meet and press moderately firm to seal edges. You can use a little extra flour if necessary."],[null,"Set formed pierogies on waxed paper and allow to sit at least one hour before boiling."],[null,"Thinly slice the onions. Spray a medium skillet with non-stick cooking spray, add onions, and sauté over low heat for approximately 5 minutes. Add margarine, and continue to sauté on low heat until onions are soft and golden. Turn off heat and set aside."],[null,"Fill a large pot with water and bring to a boil. Divide pierogies into 3 batches and place first batch into the boiling water and reduce to a slow boil. When the pierogies float on top, they are ready, approximately 10 minutes. Drain and set aside. Repeat with next 2 batches."],[null,"Spray a large skillet with non-stick spray. Add the sautéed onions and boiled pierogies. Cook over low-medium heat until pierogis are just lightly golden."]],"h":[[null,"Potatoes are very high in potassium but you can remove part of the potassium by using the double cook method described in this recipe. This step is not necessary if you do not need to restrict potassium. Anne uses Idaho or white potatoes."],[null,"Look for Vidalia, Maui or Walla-Walla onions."],[null,"Choose a trans-fat free margarine such as SmartBalance®."],[null,"Pierogies are ubiquitous through Central and Eastern Europe and can be filled with meat, sauerkraut, and even prunes, although many fillings are not ideal for renal patients."],[null,"Always check with your renal dietitian regarding how often and how much you can include reduced potassium potatoes according to your potassium levels."],[null,"Remember to limit your dairy due to the cheese and take your binders."]]},"7108962":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4. Lightly oil a large baking sheet."],[null,"Add the oats to a bowl, stir in the water and set aside."],[null,"In another bowl, beat the mashed bananas a little so they become almost creamy, and then add the sweetener and cinnamon."],[null,"Next, add the carrot and courgette, and mix well. Add the soaked oats, apple, apricots, and seeds, and mix again."],[null,"Spread out the mixture to a thickness of 1½–2cm thick and gently press down onto the baking sheet."],[null,"Bake for 30–40 minutes. Check after 20 minutes and if it’s starting to get very brown around the edges cover with foil for the remainder of the cooking time."],[null,"Allow to cool, cut into 16 portions and serve."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"2117":{"s":[[null,"Mince the garlic. Peel and thinly slice the potatoes."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 400˚ F. Prepare 12 muffin cups with non-stick cooking spray."],[null,"Heat the butter in a small saucepan over medium heat. Add garlic and cook until fragrant, about 1 minute."],[null,"Add flour and cook for 1 minute. Slowly add milk, stirring constantly until sauce is smooth and thickened, about 5 to 6 minutes."],[null,"Remove the pan from heat and stir 1/2 cup Parmesan cheese into the sauce until melted. Add ground pepper and set the saucepan aside."],[null,"Stack the potato slices in prepared muffin cups, then spoon the sauce over the potatoes. Top each potato stack with 1 teaspoon of remaining Parmesan cheese."],[null,"Bake until potatoes are tender and browned, about 25 minutes. Let cool in cups for 5 to 7 minutes. Loosen with a knife and remove from cups to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Potatoes are a higher potassium vegetable. Be cautious with portions. To reduce potassium in potatoes soak the slices in a pot of room temperature water for 4 hours."],[null,"Serve the potatoes with eggs and fresh berries to make a balanced breakfast."]]},"1002729":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400° F."],[null,"In a bowl, combine flour, cornmeal, sugar and baking powder."],[null,"In another bowl, combine egg substitute, rice milk and melted butter."],[null,"Stir dry ingredients into wet ingredients just until moistened."],[null,"Fill greased or paper-lined muffin cups 2/3 full."],[null,"Bake for 15 to 20 minutes or until a toothpick inserted comes out clean."],[null,"Serve warm."]],"h":[[null,"Using egg substitute instead of egg and rice milk instead of milk reduces phosphorus from 130 mg to 100 mg. Baking powder adds 76 mg phosphorus to each muffin. Limit your portion to one muffin."],[null,"Do not substitute self-rising cornmeal, since it is higher in phosphorus."],[null,"Freeze leftover muffins and reheat them later for a quick addition to a meal."],[null,"To make skillet cornbread instead of muffins, use a medium-size cast-iron skillet and reduce the sugar to 2 tablespoons."]]},"5766147":{"s":[[null,"Pour the Renastep and water into a pan and warm on a low to medium heat."],[null,"Add the sugar, cornflour and rose water and whisk continuously for 3-4 minutes until the mixture starts to thicken."],[null,"Remove from the heat (it will continue to thicken when chilled)."],[null,"Line a bowl with cling film and pour the mixture in."],[null,"Let the mixture cool at room temperature for 30 minutes, then transfer to the fridge and chill for 2-3 hours or overnight if possible."],[null,"When chilled, loosen the cling film, and flip the pudding over on to plate."],[null,"Serve garnished with pistachios (if permitted) and rose petals."]],"h":[[null,"Water can be replaced with Renastep. Use a warm knife to smooth the top of the pudding before serving."],["Renastep note","Renastep is a food for special medical purposes and must be used under medical supervision. Renastep is for the dietary management of kidney disease and is suitable from 3 years of age onwards."],["Renastep note","Renastep contains Milk (milk protein) and Fish (Tuna Oils). This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutrimen dietary analysis software."],["Renastep note","Refer to labels for allergen and other product information"]]},"7276005":{"s":[[null,"Place 1 of the oranges with 1 of the cinnamon sticks, ginger, star anise and cloves in a saucepan with a litre of boiling water, and simmer gently for ten minutes."],[null,"Add the apple juice and gently heat for 3-4 minutes, taking care not to boil."],[null,"Strain, pour into a jug or individual glasses and garnish with cinnamon sticks, slices of orange, cloves and star anise."]],"h":[[null,"You could make this recipe with no added sugar cranberry juice for a ruby-red seasonal drink."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"7019856":{"s":[[null,"Add the oil to a large pan with the onion. Cook for 5 minutes, stirring regularly, until it starts to brown."],[null,"Add the carrot and sweet potato, and cook for a further 5 minutes, stirring regularly."],[null,"Now add the tomatoes, lentils, garlic, stock cube, curry paste and 1 litre of boiling water. Bring to the boil, turn down the heat, cover and simmer for 15 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, boil the rice for 10 minutes, rinse in a sieve under cold water and reserve."],[null,"Blend the vegetables with a stick blender or food processor until smooth."],[null,"Stir the rice into the soup and serve with a sprinkle of freshly chopped coriander."]],"h":[[null,"Add a finely diced chicken breast along with the tomatoes and use a chicken stock cube."],[null,"This recipe is high in Vitamin A, which helps to keep your immune system working properly."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Freeze in portions then defrost in the fridge, or defrost in a microwave stirring regularly."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"3193":{"s":[[null,"Boil water in a 1-1/2 quart covered pot."],[null,"Add grits; stir briefly."],[null,"Add bulgur, buckwheat, and oats; stir briefly."],[null,"Reduce heat to a vigorous simmer; liberally spray nonstick cooking spray on simmering surface."],[null,"Cover pot; simmer for 25 minutes."],[null,"Remove pot from burner; stir in couscous."],[null,"Let pot stand covered for 8 minutes, then serve."]],"h":[[null,"If desired, drizzle with honey or your favorite sweetener. Add unsalted margarine or butter, blueberries or dried cranberries before serving."],[null,"Makes a thick cereal. Thin by adding water or milk substitute in 1/2 ounce increments."],[null,"Refrigerate extra serving and reheat in the microwave for 30-60 seconds for a quick breakfast."],[null,"You can buy smaller amounts of grains if you shop at a market that offers grains in bulk containers. Find a variety of grain products at supermarkets, natural food stores and on the internet."]]},"7891662":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a pan, add the onion, garlic and ginger and fry until light brown."],[null,"Add the tomatoes, green chillies and chilli powder, mix well and continue to cook until the onion is softened. Add 2 tbsp water and stir"],[null,"Add the chicken pieces to the pan with the garam masala, yogurt and 200ml water, cover and simmer for 8–10 minutes, until the chicken is cooked."]],"h":[[null,"You could use turkey escalope or chicken breast in place of thighs."],[null,"For a veggie version, add 2 x 400g tins chickpeas and 250g button mushrooms instead of the chicken."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"3712":{"s":[[null,"Dice the mushrooms, onion and red peppers."],[null,"Melt 1 teaspoon of the butter in a skillet over medium heat. Add the mushrooms and onion; sauté 5 minutes until onion is tender. Stir in diced red pepper. Remove vegetables from skillet and set aside."],[null,"Melt the remaining teaspoon of butter in the skillet. Beat eggs with Worcestershire sauce and cook over medium heat. Cook the omelet evenly by shaking the pan and gently lifting edges to allow uncooked egg to run underneath cooked egg."],[null,"When eggs are partially cooked, top with vegetable mixture. Place dollops of whipped cream cheese over vegetables. Continue cooking until eggs are set."],[null,"Remove the skillet from heat and fold omelet in half. Sprinkle with pepper. Divide into two portions and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Sautéed onion will appear transparent but not brown when cooked."],[null,"Compare sodium content on bottled or canned red peppers."],[null,"Reduce fat and cholesterol by using nonstick cooking spray or a nonstick skillet, trans-fat free margarine instead of butter and liquid low cholesterol egg substitute instead of whole eggs."]]},"4446289":{"s":[[null,"Rinse rice under cold water to remove excess starch. In a small pot bring water to a boil and add the rice. Lower heat to medium and simmer for 6–7 minutes. Pour into strainer over the sink, drain and rinse with cold water."],[null,"While rice is cooking, chop mushrooms and garlic and set aside. Crack the eggs into a bowl and mix with the parmesan."],[null,"Heat a medium-sized non-stick pan over medium-high heat for 1 minute. Drop in the margarine and add the mushrooms. After 3 minutes, add the garlic. Fry for another 1–2 minutes until the mushrooms are brown."],[null,"Turning down the heat to medium-low, add the rice, soy sauce and green onions, warm through for 1–2 minutes."],[null,"Pour the eggs over the rice and stir gently on the surface until the omelet starts to set (1 minute). Cover, turn off the heat and let sit for a couple of minutes to finish."]],"h":[[null,"Stirring helps the egg to set because it distributes the heat. However, avoid too much stirring not to end up with scrambled eggs!"],[null,"If you have leftover rice in the fridge this recipe is a wonderful way to use it!"],[null,"Use the leftover half of the omelet in a sandwich the next day."]]},"6214232":{"s":[[null,"Heat the olive oil in a non-stick skillet over medium heat. Add the chopped onion and minced garlic to the skillet and sauté for 5–6 minutes or until the onion becomes translucent."],[null,"Add the sliced mushrooms to the skillet and cook for about 5–7 minutes until they become tender and any moisture evaporates. Season with salt and pepper. Remove the mushroom mixture from the skillet and set it aside."],[null,"Using the same skillet, lightly coat it with cooking spray and place it over medium-low heat. Pour half the egg substitute into the skillet, swirling to create an even layer."],[null,"Allow the eggs to cook undisturbed for a few minutes until they start to set. Then, using a spatula, lift the edges of the omelet and tilt the pan to let any uncooked eggs flow to the edges."],[null,"Once the omelet is mostly set but is still slightly runny on top, add half the sautéed mushroom mixture and half the chopped spinach on one side of the omelet. Sprinkle 1 tbsp low-fat grated cheese on top of the vegetables."],[null,"Carefully fold the other half of the omelet over the filling to create a half-moon shape. Cook for another 1–2 minutes until the omelet is cooked through, but not overcooked."],[null,"Gently slide the omelet onto a plate and repeat the process to make the second omelet."]],"h":[]},"6425583":{"s":[[null,"In a large skillet, heat the olive oil over medium heat. Add sliced mushrooms, onions, and minced garlic. Sauté until mushrooms are browned and onions are translucent, about 5–7 minutes. Season with coarse salt and black pepper."],[null,"Add the fresh spinach to the skillet and cook until wilted, about 2–3 minutes. Remove from heat."],[null,"Place a tortilla in a dry skillet over medium heat. Sprinkle a portion of both cheeses over half of the tortilla."],[null,"Spoon a generous portion of the mushroom and spinach mixture over the cheese."],[null,"Fold the tortilla in half, covering the filling, and press it down gently."],[null,"Cook the quesadilla on both sides until the tortilla is crispy, and the cheese is melted, about 2–3 minutes per side."],[null,"Repeat the process for the remaining tortillas and filling."],[null,"Once cooked, cut each quesadilla into wedges and serve."]],"h":[]},"7114004":{"s":[[null,"Break the eggs into a bowl, add the pepper, beat with a fork and set aside."],[null,"Heat the oil in a pan and cook the mushrooms and spring onion for 5 minutes over a medium heat, stirring regularly, until soft."],[null,"Stir the egg into the mushrooms/onion for 1 minute, then cook gently for 3 minutes, using a spatula to ease the omelette from the sides of the pan."],[null,"When the omelette is cooked, sprinkle the cheese on top and turn it out onto a plate, folding the omelette in half."]],"h":[[null,"Rather than making a plain omelette with a filling, it’s far tastier to use this method and mix ingredients into the omelette then add a couple of extras into the middle such as cheese or herbs."],[null,"Almost anything can go into an omelette. Use different cheeses such as goat’s cheese, or lower fat garlic and herb cream cheese."],[null,"Add freshly chopped herbs such as basil, chives, parsley or tarragon. You could also add a little curry paste or powder."],[null,"Most vegetables work, although root vegetables need to be pre-cooked. Cooked leftover vegetables such as broccoli, peas, courgettes and carrots are all excellent additions."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6468907":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350°F. Coat 4 (8-ounce) ramekins with cooking spray. Set the ramekins aside."],[null,"Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium heat. Sauté the onions and mushrooms for 10 minutes or until richly browned. Add in the red pepper and sun-dried tomatoes and sauté about 8 minutes. Add in the Italian seasoning, salt and pepper and sauté 1 minute."],[null,"Add the mushroom mixture to a large bowl, allow to cool for 2 minutes. Add in the egg, breadcrumbs, milk and walnuts. Mix gently. Divide the mixture among all the ramekins, pressing down on the mixture to fit all the ramekins."],[null,"Set the ramekins onto a baking sheet and bake in the oven for 30-35 minutes until the top is browned. Run a knife around each ramekin to loosen the loaf"]],"h":[]},"6428942":{"s":[[null,"In a skillet, sauté 2 cloves minced garlic, the onion, and mushrooms in olive oil for about 10 minutes or until mushrooms are golden brown."],[null,"In a food processor, combine arugula, ricotta, 2 whole cloves garlic, and white pepper and pulse until smooth."],[null,"Place 6 sandwich thin halves on a baking pan. Add 1 tbsp of the arugula mixture to each half of sandwich thin. Top with the mushroom mixture and shredded mozzarella, dividing them evenly among all six pizzas."],[null,"Broil for 5 minutes on low in the oven until cheese is melted."]],"h":[]},"9863545":{"s":[["Stove Top Instructions","Melt the butter, if using, in a medium pot. Then add the shallots, garlic, and sliced mushrooms. Sauté until reduced, approx. 5-6 minutes, and then sprinkle with salt and pepper."],["Stove Top Instructions","Add the broth and barley, and bring to a boil with the lid on your pot, but slightly askew. Cook over medium/high heat until the barley is tender, approx. 40-45 minutes, stirring occasionally."],["Stove Top Instructions","Once cooked, add a little more salt and pepper, if needed, and serve garnished with fresh parsley or red pepper flakes, if desired."],["Instant Pot Instructions","Set your Instant Pot to the sauté function and add the butter to melt, if using. Add the shallots, garlic and sliced mushrooms and sprinkle them with salt and pepper. Sauté until reduced, approx. 5-6 minutes."],["Instant Pot Instructions","Add the broth and the barley and close the lid. Make sure you set the valve to the sealing position and set to high pressure for 22 minutes. It will take about 10-15 minutes to build pressure and begin counting down."],["Instant Pot Instructions","Once the timer is complete, quick release the steam valve and open the lid once safe to do so. Season with more salt and pepper, if needed and serve garnished with fresh parsley or red pepper flakes."]],"h":[[null,"Cook your soup with the lid on but slightly askew . Cooking without the lid will cause too much of the broth to evaporate. Barley has a long cook time, so it will appear like a lot of liquid at first, but the barley will absorb more and more as it cooks. For no oil, use water or broth to sauté the veggies. If time permits , you may add more veggies to the sauté step. Chopped carrots and celery would make great additions. Or add some baby spinach to the very end of cooking, if desired. Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-4 days, or you may freeze in a freezer-safe, airtight container for up to 3 months."]]},"6047124":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F."],[null,"In a bowl, whisk the egg substitute with salt, pepper, and dried thyme."],[null,"Heat the olive oil in an oven-safe skillet over medium heat."],[null,"Add in the diced onions and cook until softened."],[null,"Add the sliced mushrooms to the skillet and cook until they release their moisture, about 6 minutes."],[null,"Pour in the whisked eggs over the mushroom mixture."],[null,"Allow the edges of the frittata to set, lifting them with a spatula to let the uncooked eggs flow underneath."],[null,"Once the edges are set, sprinkle the grated Parmesan cheese evenly over the top."],[null,"Transfer the skillet to the preheated oven and bake for about 10–12 minutes or until the frittata is cooked through and the top is golden brown."],[null,"Remove from the oven and let it cool for a few minutes before slicing."]],"h":[]},"7179097":{"s":[[null,"Spray a large, deep, non-stick frying pan with a couple of pumps of low-calorie cooking spray and place over a medium heat. Fry the onion for 5 minutes until softened. Add the garlic, ginger and green chilli with a splash of water, then fry for 3 minutes. Add the spices and a little water and fry for 2 minutes."],[null,"Add the tomatoes along with the almond drink to the pan, and bring everything up to a simmer. Bubble gently for 8-10 minutes, or until the tomatoes have collapsed, stirring frequently."],[null,"Put 200g dried basmati rice in a lidded, non-stick saucepan with 1 cinnamon stick, the cardamom pods, cloves and saffron. Pour in enough water to come a fingernail’s height above the rice and place over a medium-high heat. Bring to a simmer, bubble for 1 minute and cover. Reduce the heat to as low as it will go and, without removing the lid, cook for 20 minutes, or until all the liquid is absorbed."],[null,"Transfer the tomato mixture to a large measuring jug, then whizz into a smooth sauce using a stick blender. Transferring the sauce to a jug rather than keeping it in the pan helps the blender to whizz it more smoothly. (You could also use a jug blender.) Set aside."],[null,"Spray a large, non-stick frying pan with a couple of pumps of low-calorie cooking spray and place over a medium-high heat. Once hot, add half the mushrooms and fry for 5-6 minutes, stirring occasionally, until they turn to a deep golden brown. Transfer to a plate and repeat with the remaining mushrooms."],[null,"Return the sauce to the pan. Add the saffron, bay leaf and cinnamon, and bring to a simmer. Add the mushrooms and simmer for 8-10 minutes, stirring frequently. Season with pepper. Divide between 4 bowls, discarding the bay leaf and cinnamon. Top with the yoghurt and coriander."],[null,"Fluff up the rice with a fork for perfect results, discarding the cinnamon, cardamom pods and cloves to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Use brown basmati rice to increase the fibre."],[null,"Check spice/seasoning blends for added ingredients such as sugar, salt, flour or oil. Choose blends made from herbs and spices only if possible."],[null,"You can use a plain yoghurt of your choice. However, this will change the nutritional information and the texture of the dish."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"7524534":{"s":[[null,"Add the oil to a pan over a medium heat, then add the shallots, stirring regularly for 5 mintues until browned."],[null,"Add all the mushrooms and turn up the heat a little. Cook for 3-4 minutes until the mushrooms are soft and any liquid from them has evaporated."],[null,"Add the garlic and pepper, cook for another minute, then add the soy sauce and parsley, mix, then remove from the heat and allow to cool."],[null,"Put the mushrooms on a chopping board and chop finely, then add to a bowl with the cream cheese, mix and refrigerate. Serve with toast."]],"h":[[null,"This pâté also makes 15–20 great canapés. For wheat-free canapés, try using baked baby potatoes – cut cooked potatoes in half, scoop out a little of the potato flesh, then fill the centre with pâté."],[null,"For a gluten-free pâté, use reduced-salt, gluten- free tamari in place of the soy sauce in this recipe."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Defrost in the fridge to serve."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"7055081":{"s":[[null,"Put the oil in a pan and gently cook the leek for 3–4 minutes, stirring regularly."],[null,"Add the mushrooms, garlic, chilli and oregano. Continue cooking gently for 5 minutes, still stirring regularly. Meanwhile, toast the seeds and reserve."],[null,"Plunge the spiralised vegetables (homemade or ready prepared) into boiling water for 2 minutes."],[null,"Just before serving, stir the yoghurt into the mushrooms."],[null,"Divide the spiralised vegetables between 2 bowls. Top each with the mushroom sauce, and sprinkle with toasted seeds, black pepper, a few shavings of parmesan and a sprig of basil."]],"h":[[null,"Other spiralised vegetables work well with this dish, such as butternut squash or beetroot."],[null,"For a higher-carb option, serve with wholegrain pasta instead of spiralised veg."],[null,"For a vegetarian alternative to Parmesan, swap it out with vegetarian-style hard cheese."],[null,"You can use an unsweetened plain yoghurt of your choice, but this will change the nutrition information and texture of the dish."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"7757165":{"s":[[null,"Add the oil to a saucepan and fry the onions and chilli for 5 minutes, until starting to brown."],[null,"In a separate pan, heat the stock and leave it simmering very gently."],[null,"Add the garlic, a pinch of pepper and the mushrooms to the onion, stir for 1 minute and add the rice. Stir for 2 minutes, then add two ladles of stock, enough to just cover the rice and stir again."],[null,"Regularly stirring the rice, add the hot stock, a little at a time, so the rice is just covered. The risotto should be very gently bubbling."],[null,"After 15 minutes, add the basil, stir for another 2-5 minutes, testing the rice to make sure it’s cooked ‘al dente’ (slightly firm) and adding any remaining stock."],[null,"Finally, add the yogurt. Beat vigorously for 1 minute with a wooden spoon, cover and allow to stand 2 minutes. Sprinkle with basil and black pepper before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Beating the risotto with a wooden spoon helps plump up the rice and makes the risotto more creamy."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Chill quickly. Defrost in the fridge and reheat thoroughly until piping hot throughout. Eat immediately and discard any leftovers."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"9039315":{"s":[[null,"If you do not have cooked rice, start by cooking according to package directions while you prepare the remaining ingredients."],[null,"Preheat your oven to 425 degrees F and line a baking tray with parchment paper."],[null,"Add your mushrooms to a food processor and finely chop them, scraping down the sides as needed. If you have a smaller food processor, you may need to do this in batches."],[null,"Transfer the mushrooms to a large skillet and dry sauté over medium heat until the moisture and liquid evaporates, approx 6-8 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the onion, garlic, carrot and kale to your food processor and finely chop these as well. Scrape down the sides as needed, and make sure there are no large chunks remaining. Transfer to the skillet with the cooked mushrooms, along with the peas, nutritional yeast and seasoning and sauté another 2-3 minutes, then remove from heat. Add 1.5 cups worth of your cooked rice to the skillet, mix well and taste the mixture and add more salt or other seasoning if desired."],[null,"Add the remaining half a cup of your cooked brown rice to a small blender with a tablespoon or two of water, as needed to get it pureed. Once smooth, transfer to the skillet and mix well. Now add the tapioca starch, starting with 5 tablespoons and mix until combined. Form a ball in your hands to test the mixture and see how well it holds. You want the mixture to hold together, but not be overly sticky. If it's very sticky and difficult to form a ball or patty, add another tablespoon or two of the tapioca starch, mix well and test again."],[null,"Now divide the mixture into six patties. You'll use a scant 3/4 cup of the mixture per burger. Start by forming a ball in your hands and squeezing gently to ensure there are no gaps. Then flatten in your hands into a patty shape and place down on the baking tray. Do not press the patties into the tray or they may stick while cooking."],[null,"Bake for 20 minutes, then remove from the oven and carefully flip each one. Return to the oven for another 10-15 minutes, until the edges are golden brown. Remove from the oven and let them rest at room temperature for 5 minutes before serving."]],"h":[[null,"For added flavour, cook your brown rice in vegetable broth."],[null,"Make sure your veggies are very finely chopped, but not pureed. Large chunks of veggies will not hold well."],[null,"When testing the mixture, squeeze some into your hands to see how well it holds together. The pureed rice will make the batter a little sticky, which acts as a binding agent. However, it should not be so sticky that you can’t form a ball or patty without the batter completely sticking to your hands. Add more tapioca starch until you reach a slightly sticky consistency. You should need somewhere between five and eight tablespoons. (It will depend on how much water you used to blend your rice.)"],[null,"When forming your patties, do so in your hands and not on the tray. Since there’s no oil in this recipe, if you press them into the tray too much, they will stick to the parchment paper. Squeeze the mixture into a ball in your hands, and then flatten into a patty shape and place on the tray gently. If the patties are still sticking to your hands, use slightly damp hands to form them."],[null,"Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-4 days and you may reheat in the oven or in a skillet on stove top. To freeze, let the patties cool and then place in a freezable container with your patties layered between sheets of parchment paper to prevent sticking."]]},"7375715":{"s":[[null,"Slice the squash into 12 thick rounds (each about 1-2cm thick), scooping out and discarding any seeds and pulp. Using a cookie cutter or a small knife, cut a circle from the middle of any solid slices to make large rings. Grate the circles you cut from the middle and set aside."],[null,"Spray a large non-stick frying pan with a couple of pumps of low-calorie cooking spray and place over a low heat. Add the onion and cook for 5 minutes, then add the mushrooms, chopped sage and grated squash and cook for 5 minutes."],[null,"Preheat your oven to 200°C/fan 180°C/ gas 6."],[null,"Crumble the stock cube into the pan, stir well to make sure it fully dissolves and cook for 10 minutes. Stir in the oats and tip into a large bowl."],[null,"Arrange all the squash rings on a large non-stick baking tray (you might need 2 trays) and fill them with the mushroom mixture, levelling the tops as neatly as you can. Spray with a couple of pumps of low-calorie cooking spray and roast for 30-35 minutes or until cooked through and lightly golden."],[null,"When the squash rings are nearly done, fry the whole sage leaves in low-calorie cooking spray for a couple of minutes."],[null,"Divide the stuffed squash rings between plates, scatter over the sage leaves and serve with your favourite veg. We recommend steamed long green beans and peppers."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"7385601":{"s":[[null,"Boil the new potatoes and cut into bite-sized chunks. Meanwhile prepare the mussels (see Chef's tips, below)."],[null,"Thinly slice the stems of the purple sprouting broccoli, leaving the heads intact. Prepare the rest of the ingredients."],[null,"Add the oil to a large pan over a medium-low heat, add the purple sprouting broccoli and sliced leeks. Cook for 5–6 minutes."],[null,"Add the garlic and spring onion, stir for 2 minutes and turn the heat up high."],[null,"Now add the mussels, mix and put a lid on the pan then cook for 3–4 minutes shaking the pan a few times."],[null,"Add the broad beans, milk, new potatoes, pepper and parsley. Bring to boiling point (2–3 minutes), mixing regularly, then turn down the heat and simmer for 1 minute."],[null,"Divide into 4 bowls and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Wash under cold running water discarding any with broken shells."],[null,"Look for any open mussels, tap them, if they don't close discard them."],[null,"Pull out any 'beards' (the little tuft of brown fibres)."],[null,"Scrape off any barnacles with a small knife and scrub with a kitchen brush."],[null,"Give the mussels another rinse in a colander. Set aside."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"3800":{"s":[[null,"Put chicken pieces in a Crock-Pot® and sprinkle with the salt and garlic powder."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine lemonade concentrate, brown sugar, ketchup and vinegar. Pour over chicken. Cover and cook on low-heat setting for 4-1/2 hours."],[null,"Add bell pepper slices and diced onion. Cover and continue cooking on low for 1-1/2 to 2-1/2 hours longer. Remove chicken and vegetables to a serving dish; cover and keep warm. Pour juices from Crock-Pot into a saucepan. Combine cornstarch with cold water; stir into juices. Cook, stirring over medium heat, until thick and bubbly."],[null,"Serve sauce over chicken, along with white rice."]],"h":[[null,"Try this recipe with chicken drumbsticks and thighs if you are on a lower protein diet and require a smaller portion of chicken."],[null,"This is a high carbohdrate meal and is not recommended for people with diabetes who require a lower carbohydrate meal."]]},"7367825":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 190°C/gas 5."],[null,"Add the oil to a baking tray. Add the onions and peppers, and bake for 15–20 minutes until just starting to brown."],[null,"Remove the onions and peppers from the oven. Mix in the oregano and sundried tomatoes. Set aside and leave to cool."],[null,"Meanwhile, bake the naan breads according to pack instructions (3–4 minutes) and set aside."],[null,"Once the naan bread and vegetables are cool (about 30 minutes), spread each naan with the cream cheese and dot with the cottage cheese."],[null,"Scatter with half the basil leaves, followed by the roasted peppers and onions."],[null,"Top with the tomatoes and the remaining basil leaves, plus a good grind of black pepper to serve."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"7190087":{"s":[[null,"Mix all the ingredients for the pickles together, cover, then set aside, mixing occasionally."],[null,"Add a teaspoon of oil to a non-stick pan, then add the eggs and cook for 30-60 seconds to make a thin pancake omelette. Remove from the pan, roll up, then set aside."],[null,"Add another teaspoon of oil to the pan, add the sliced onions and cook for 4-5 minutes, stirring regularly. Add the turkey strips and red pepper, then cook for a further 4 minutes."],[null,"Add the garlic, chilli, cabbage and spring onions, then cook for 3 minutes. Stir in the nasi goreng paste and mix well, adding a dash of water if it starts to stick."],[null,"Mix in the cooked rice and stir regularly for 4-5 minutes, until piping hot. Put into a serving bowl, top with sliced omelette and serve with the pickled vegetables."]],"h":[[null,"Don’t store cooked rice for more than 24 hours in the refrigerator. Always chill fully as soon as possible."],[null,"You can use chicken in place of turkey."],[null,"Nasi goreng paste contains shrimp so it’s not vegetarian, so replace it with tofu for a vegetarian option."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"3894":{"s":[[null,"Shred cabbage and mix together in a large bowl. Finely chop onion and add to cabbage; set aside."],[null,"Combine milk, sour cream, celery seed, Tabasco® sauce, vinegar and minced garlic."],[null,"Pour dressing over cabbage mixture."],[null,"Refrigerate 2 hours, serve and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Sweet onion varieties include Maui, Vidalia and Wala Wala onions."],[null,"Serve as a side dish or as a topping on a beef or chicken sandwich."]]},"6002187":{"s":[[null,"Fill each celery stalk with the nut butter, and top with dried fruit. Serve immediately."]],"h":[]},"2006":{"s":[[null,"To prepare marinade blend together all ingredients except chicken to a smooth paste consistency."],[null,"Wash chicken and pat dry on paper towel. Place in a shallow glass pan. Pour marinade paste over chicken, coating each piece well. Place in refrigerator for 2 hours to marinate. Turn once or twice."],[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F. Place chicken in a baking pan and bake for 20-25 minutes."],[null,"Heat extra marinade to a boil then use for basting."]],"h":[[null,"Purchace 4 chicken breasts, 4 ounces each."],[null,"This is a great recipe for the grill."]]},"2483":{"s":[[null,"Steam lobster until meat is opaque, about 5 to 6 minutes. Let cool then cut lobster into bite-sized pieces. Finely chop celery while lobster is cooking."],[null,"Combine mayo, celery, lemon juice and hot sauce. Add lobster meat and toss to coat."],[null,"Split buns and spread with butter. Toast in a skillet."],[null,"Make lobster rolls by dividing the lobster mixture between the 4 buns. Serve with lemon wedges."]],"h":[[null,"Buy regular hotdog buns if split-top hotdog rolls are unavailable."],[null,"Look for fresh or frozen lobster meat or lobster tails, or cook a whole lobster. Two 6-ounce lobster tails work great."],[null,"Lobster meat is naturally high in sodium. Select lower sodium foods for your remaining meals to stay within your sodium limit."]]},"2247":{"s":[[null,"Place beef lengthwise on a cutting board. Cut the beef with the meat’s grain into 4 flat even slices. Place each slice between 2 sheets of plastic wrap and pound to 1/4” thickness with a meat mallet. Season with ground pepper and arrange in a 9” x 13” baking dish."],[null,"In a bowl, combine the 1/2 cup thinly sliced onion, parsley, garlic, bay leaves and vinegar. Whisk thoroughly and pour over the meat. Cover the meat and marinate for 8 minutes; turn meat over and marinate 8 minutes longer."],[null,"Preheat grill or broiler. Coat sweet onion slices with cooking spray and grill until nicely browned, about 4 minutes per side. Place onion slices onto a platter."],[null,"Place beef on grill or broiler and dispose of marinate. Grill marinated beef for 2 minutes per side for medium rare or to the internal temperature of 150º F for medium. Arrange beef slices on top of grilled onions."],[null,"Serve with 3 ounce portions cooked tenderloin with 2 tablespoons Chimichurri Sauce."]],"h":[[null,"Use a stronger white or yellow onion in the marinade and grill the sweet onion slices."],[null,"For a lower protein diet, adjust portion of beef according to your meal plan and protein prescription."]]},"6685157":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, add the lettuce and 3 Tbsp of the vinaigrette and toss well to combine. Arrange on a platter or individual plates."],[null,"Top the salad with the eggs, olives, tuna, and tomatoes. Drizzle with the remaining vinaigrette and serve."]],"h":[]},"9216639":{"s":[["For the cheesecake crust","Add the dates, hot water, and vanilla to the bowl of your food processor and process until mostly smooth, scraping down the sides, as needed. Then add the oats and pulse several times to break them down but don't puree them."],["For the cheesecake crust","Divide the crust between your individual cups and press it down using a spoon or shooter glass."],["For the cheesecake filling","Add all the filling ingredients to your food processor and blend until smooth, scraping down the sides as needed. Then pour and divide the filling over the crust."],["For the topping","Add all the ingredients to a medium bowl and gently mash with a potato masher or large fork, but leave some chunks for texture. Then top each mini cheesecake with a large spoonful of the fruit topping."],["For the topping","Optional: Garnish with fresh raspberries and mint leaves."],["For the topping","Place the layered cheesecakes in your fridge for at least 1 hour before serving, but these taste best when refrigerated overnight."]],"h":[[null,"Don’t overprocess the oats when making the crust. You want a nice texture, not a puree."],[null,"Wet your spoon or shooter glass when pushing the crust down into the individual cups to prevent sticking."],[null,"If possible, make your mini cheesecakes one day in advance as these taste best when refrigerated overnight."],[null,"You may use strawberries, blueberries, or a mix of berries for the topping. Or, to save time , you may use your favourite store-bought jam for the fruit topping."],[null,"The serving size pictured is 6-ounce glasses. Portion sizes will vary according to the size of the glass being used. Leftovers will keep refrigerated for 3-4 days."]]},"9986100":{"s":[["For the Crust","Add the pitted dates and half a cup of hot water to your food processor and process until smooth, scraping down the sides, as needed. Add another tablespoon or two of hot water, if needed to get a smooth consistency."],["For the Crust","Add the rolled oats to your date paste mixture and process until combined, and most of the oats are broken down, but no need to make it smooth."],["For the Crust","Transfer the mixture into your nonstick tart pan and use wet fingers to press down evenly on the base and sides. Set aside."],["For the Filling","Add all the filling ingredients to your food processor and process until completely smooth, scraping down the sides as needed."],["For the Filling","Then pour the filling over your prepared crust and use a silicone spatula to evenly spread it and smooth out the top."],["For the Filling","Freeze for 2 hours and then garnish with chocolate chips and a drizzle of extra peanut butter before serving, if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Use a nonstick tart pan with a removable bottom . This will make transferring your pie MUCH simpler. (This pie is photographed using an 11 inch nonstick tart pan, but this will also work using a 9 or 10 inch pan.) Use wet hands to press the crust into your tart pan, to prevent sticking. If you have a sweet tooth , taste the filling once processed (before pouring over your pie crust) and add an additional ¼ cup of maple syrup if needed. Storage If you won’t be consuming all the pie, return leftovers to the freezer immediately. Don’t let it fully thaw and then refreeze as it alters the flavour and texture."],[null,"If you don’t mind the pie being very soft, you may also store leftovers in the refrigerator for 3-4 days."]]},"9422406":{"s":[[null,"Add all the ingredients to your blender and process on high until smooth. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Blending frozen fruit works best with a high speed blender . If you don't have a high speed blender, you may need a little more liquid to get things moving. Start with the amount listed and add more as needed. If you're subbing any of the frozen fruit for fresh , decrease the liquid a little to start and add more, if needed. Add a handful of ice cubes if you're using mostly fresh fruit. A smoothie without banana won't be quite as thick if sticking with all fresh fruit options. Feel free to sub any of the frozen fruits to accommodate your freezer . Mango, raspberries, cherries, or mixed berries all work well. If you don't have pecans , you may use walnuts, cashews, almonds or macadamia nuts instead. You may also sub the raw nuts for nut butter . Try 2 tablespoons of peanut butter , almond butter , pecan butter , or any of your favourite nut butters. For extra sweetness , add 2-3 pitted dates or 1-2 teaspoons of maple syrup."]]},"9084623":{"s":[[null,"Add all the ingredients to a small mixing bowl and whisk well to thoroughly combine."],[null,"Transfer the BBQ sauce to a CLEAN jar or container."]],"h":[[null,"If you do not have or cannot find ketchup without added sugar , reduce the maple syrup. Adjust to your taste ! If you prefer spicier BBQ sauce, double up on the hot sauce. For no heat, omit it. For an extra smoky flavour , add a teaspoon of liquid smoke or double up on the smoked paprika. Keep the sauce in the refrigerator for up to 3 weeks in a sealed jar or container. Or freeze airtight for up to 3 months. This vegan BBQ sauce recipe makes approx. 1.5 cups in total, for 12 servings of 2 tablespoons each. The nutritional information represents 1 serving of approx. 2 tablespoons."]]},"2492":{"s":[[null,"Spread butter over bread or English muffin. Cut into cubes."],[null,"Place buttered bread cubes in a microwave-safe bowl."],[null,"Pour egg whites over bread to cover."],[null,"Sprinkle syrup on top."],[null,"Microwave for 1 minute; push up edges of egg white to let uncooked egg out to edges."],[null,"Microwave another minute or until egg is set."]],"h":[[null,"Serve warm as French toast or chill and eat as bread pudding."],[null,"Egg whites provide excellent quality protein with minimal phosphorus or fat."],[null,"If desired substitute 2 whole eggs, beaten for 1/2-cup egg white. This change will increase nutrients to 288 calories, 15 g fat, 434 mg cholesterol and 226 mg phosphorus; sodium is reduced to 353 mg."],[null,"If desired, substitute natural maple syrup or cinnamon sugar for lite or sugar-free syrup."],[null,"This recipe works well with an English muffin half instead of a slice of bread."]]},"6144228":{"s":[[null,"In a medium bowl, mash together egg whites, cheese wedges, mustard, horseradish, salt (optional) and ground black pepper using a potato masher or sturdy whisk. You can also use a food processor but take care not to over process the egg salad. Pulse until combined but still slightly chunky."],[null,"Serve 1/2 cup egg salad mixture on top of 1 cup arugula. You could also serve with arugula on toasted whole wheat bread for an open-face sandwich."],[null,"Crack and peel the hard-boiled eggs. Slice the eggs in half and discard the yolks."]],"h":[]},"1897":{"s":[[null,"Measure 3 cups water into a small container. Add crushed garlic, and heat on high in microwave for 3 minutes. Let this cool down while the rest of the ingredients are being measured."],[null,"Measure flour, salt and yeast into the large bowl/container and mix well to distribute evenly. When measuring flour, do not sift. Instead, use the “scoop and level” method: lightly scoop the flour into a one cup measuring cup, then use a knife to level off the top."],[null,"When the water has cooled to lukewarm (about 100 degrees), add to the dry ingredients and mix by hand with the wooden spoon. The dough will be very sticky. Add a little more water if the dough is too dry to mix in all the flour."],[null,"Cover the container very loosely with the lid or plastic wrap and let rise at room temperature for 2 hours or more. The dough may rise to the top of the container and then fall a bit. That is OK. Remember, kneading is not necessary."],[null,"At this point, you can refrigerate the dough for up to10 days and bake as needed. The longer it is refrigerated, the better the flavor. If you bake some of it the day it is mixed up, the dough will be sticky and harder to handle unless it has been refrigerated for at least 3 hours."],[null,"Prepare a cookie sheet/pizza peel for the dough to rise on by putting a piece of parchment paper on the cookie sheet or pizza peel and dusting it liberally with corn meal."],[null,"Sprinkle the top of your refrigerated dough with flour. Use scissors or a knife to cut the dough in the bowl into 4 pieces."],[null,"Flour your hands and pull out a piece of dough. Place it on one palm, and gently stretch up a side of the dough to the top of the loaf, rotating the ball a quarter turn as you go. Do this on all four sides of the circle. You will now have an upside-down round loaf in your hand. The loaf can be kept round, or you can stretch it a bit into a longer shape."],[null,"Flip the loaf smooth side up/ folded side down on the dusted cookie sheet/pizza peel. Let it rise for about 40 minutes."],[null,"Twenty minutes before the end of the rising time, put one oven rack in the middle of the oven with another cookie sheet (or a bread stone if you have one) on the rack. Put another rack toward the bottom of the oven, with the broiler pan, or another small metal (not glass) pan, on it. Preheat the oven to 450° F for 20 minutes."],[null,"Now you are ready to bake! Dust the top of the loaf with flour, and then use a serrated knife to slice a 1/4” deep “X “on top of the round loaf. You can slice crosswise across the top of a longer loaf in a few places."],[null,"You can transfer the loaf onto the hot baking surface in a number of ways, but be careful — the oven is very hot. Slide a metal pancake turner under the parchment paper and transfer the loaf to the hot cookie sheet/baking stone; or pick up the cookie sheet /pizza peel with the dough on it and hold it close to the hot cookie sheet/ bread stone. With a quick forward push/shake motion, slide the dough onto the hot surface."],[null,"Quickly pour the one cup of hot water into the broiler pan or metal pan on the bottom oven rack and close the oven door. The water will make steam for a crispier crust."],[null,"Bake for 30 minutes, or until the crust is well browned."],[null,"Cut cooled loaf into 10 slices."]],"h":[[null,"This is a very forgiving recipe. For example, if during the initial rise you forget it and it rises for 5 hours, that’s OK. More garlic can be added as well."],[null,"Remember to keep the container lid on loosely; gases made by the yeast can build up pressure in the container if the lid is put on too tight."],[null,"During the second rise, the bread may not seem to rise as much as you might expect. This is normal; it will also rise in the oven."],[null,"Using the parchment paper AND the cornmeal makes it easier to flip the loaf onto the hot baking surface in the oven. Otherwise, the dough can stick and make a mess."],[null,"If you can do this safely, about halfway during the baking time, gently scoot a metal pancake turner between the bread and the parchment paper. Just peel the parchment off the bottom of the loaf, and then let the bread continue to bake on the hot surface. This will make the crust crispier."],[null,"Using an oven thermometer can be helpful to make sure your oven is hot enough. Many ovens are actually up to 50 degrees off."],[null,"It may take a couple of loaves before you are comfortable with the process. That’s OK — it tastes great whether it looks good or not!"]]},"6007976":{"s":[[null,"Line two baking sheets with parchment paper and set aside."],[null,"Heat the olive oil and 5 cloves of minced garlic in a large skillet with a lid over low heat (do not use a deep pot, as you want the water to quickly evaporate and the sauce to become thick). Cook the garlic for about 6-7 minutes, stirring occasionally."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the drained tomatoes to a deep bowl. Crush the tomatoes with your hands, until coarse. Add the tomatoes and basil to the skillet and simmer, uncovered, for 20-25 minutes until thick. Add some of the reserved liquid from the can of tomatoes if the sauce is too thick."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 400°F. As the sauce simmers, slice the zucchini lengthwise into 1/8-inch thick slices with a knife or mandolin. Arrange the zucchini on the prepared baking sheet. Sprinkle the zucchini lightly with salt. Bake the zucchini for about 10-12 minutes until lightly browned. Remove the zucchini from the oven. Gently roll up the zucchini slices in a towel to get rid of the excess moisture, or just use paper toweling and blot very well. Be careful to keep the slices intact. Add in 1/4 tsp salt, 1/4 tsp pepper, and crushed red pepper (if using) to the tomato sauce."],[null,"In a food processor or blender, process the tofu, parsley, lemon juice, lemon zest, and remaining clove of garlic until smooth. Add to a large bowl and mix in the ricotta cheese, mozzarella cheese, egg, 1/4 tsp salt and pepper."],[null,"Pour about 1/3 cup of the marinara sauce over the bottom of a 9 × 12 baking pan. Add a layer of zucchini slices, overlapping them slightly. Add 1/3 of the filling mixture over the zucchini, spreading evenly with a spatula. Add about 1/3 of the remaining marinara sauce over the tofu cheese filling. Repeat the layering process until all ingredients are used up, finishing with marinara sauce. Sprinkle the top of the lasagna with the Parmesan or Romano cheese."],[null,"Cover loosely with foil and bake for 35 minutes. Remove the cover and bake for 15 minutes more. Remove the lasagna from the oven, let stand at room temperature for 10-15 minutes so lasagna can settle and it will be easier to cut. Cut into squares."]],"h":[]},"3311":{"s":[[null,"Finely chop cabbage and onion. Chop jalapeno and cilantro."],[null,"Mix all the ingredients in a small bowl."],[null,"Refrigerate until ready to serve.Enjoy as a condiment with your favorite foods."]],"h":[[null,"Save leftover No Tomato Salsa in the refrigerator. It keeps well for 2 to 3 days."],[null,"Use this salsa on tacos, enchiladas or with chips."],[null,"For more color, try making this renal-friendly salsa with red cabbage instead of green."]]},"2019":{"s":[[null,"Set cream cheese out to soften."],[null,"Using a mixer on low speed, combine cream cheese and mint extract."],[null,"Mix in 2 cups of the powdered sugar until smooth"],[null,"Add 1 additional cup of powdered sugar and 2 tablespoons of the sprinkles. Mix on low speed until blended"],[null,"Fold in remaining cup of powdered sugar until combined."],[null,"In a separate bowl, combine granulated sugar and remaining holiday sprinkles."],[null,"Shape dough into 3/4-inch balls and roll in sugar and sprinkles mixture."],[null,"Place balls on a baking sheet and refrigerate for 30 minutes."],[null,"Remove from fridge and gently flatten balls with a fork."],[null,"Store in an airtight container in fridge until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Use colored granulated sugar for even more color."],[null,"Increase mint extract to 1/4 teaspoon for a stronger mint flavor."],[null,"Try chocolate sprinkles for a mint-chocolate flavor."]]},"4203044":{"s":[[null,"In a microwave safe bowl, add peanut butter, honey and vanilla. Microwave for 30 seconds."],[null,"Add ground flax and rice crisp cereal to the melted peanut butter mixture."],[null,"Mix all ingredients well to combine."],[null,"Chill rice crisp mixture for 10 minutes in the freezer."],[null,"Roll into 16 balls."],[null,"Cover and place in a serving container. Refrigerate."]],"h":[[null,"*Choose low-sodium peanut butter to lower the overall sodium content of the recipe."],["Peanut butter and nut butters","Eating the right amount of protein is very important when you have chronic kidney disease (CKD). During the earlier stages of CKD, it is common to limit the amount of protein in your diet. However, for those who require dialysis, a higher protein diet is needed. Dialysis patients often find it challenging to eat all of the recommended protein. Peanut butter and other nut butters such as almond or cashew butter can add protein to your diet. These however can be higher in potassium, phosphorus and even sodium than other protein sources, so ask your registered dietitian how much is right for you. Once you know how much nut butter you can include in your diet, it can be added in a variety of ways. You can find peanut butter and other nut butters without added salt. Choose these lower-sodium options whenever they are available. Spread them on your toast in the morning. For snacking, nut butters can be a flavorful topping for low-sodium crackers or celery. Mix peanut butter with a little bit of yogurt and honey and add a pinch of cinnamon to create a delicious dip for sliced apples or pears."]]},"4834365":{"s":[[null,"In a small mixing bowl, add graham cracker crumbs and melted margarine. Mix to combine."],[null,"Divide graham crumb mixture between 6 ramekin dishes and press firmly in the bottom."],[null,"In a mixing bowl or stand mixer, cream together the cream cheese and powdered sugar. Add yogurt, lime juice, and lime zest. Continue to mix until mixture is smooth and creamy."],[null,"Divide the key lime mixture between the 6 ramekins."],[null,"Refrigerate until dessert sets, approximately two hours. Garnish each dessert with whipped topping."]],"h":[["Low-Potassium Desserts","Desserts are a welcome treat after meals or during the holidays. Depending on the type of dessert, sweets can contain high amounts of potassium. While it is unrealistic to never eat dessert as part of your kidney diet, planning ahead can allow you to curb your sweet tooth and stay within your nutritional goals. Consider the following tips when selecting a treat: • PIE: Depending on the ingredients, the amount of potassium in a slice of pie can add up quickly. Avoid high-potassium pecan and pumpkin pie. Instead, try a slice of fruit pie, like apple or cherry. • ICE CREAM: Milk naturally contains potassium and one 8-ounce portion of ice cream can contain over 300 milligrams depending on the ingredients. Replace milk-based desserts with fruit ice or popsicles for a cold, lower-potassium treat. • CHOCOLATE: Even a small portion of milk chocolate can contain over 200 milligrams of potassium. Eat chocolate only on special occasions. Instead, choose sugar-free hard or sour candies sparingly. • NUTS: While often found as a topping or mixed into a dessert, nuts are a high-potassium food. A one-ounce portion of almonds has about 200 milligrams of potassium. Choose desserts and candy without nuts to limit unnecessary potassium in your diet."]]},"6161139":{"s":[[null,"In a small saucepan, combine sugar blend and milk over medium heat. Stir well and bring to a boil for 1 1/2 minutes. Stir in peanut butter and vanilla."],[null,"Remove from heat and add oats. Stir until oats are evenly coated in the peanut mixture and everything has cooled. Fold in the chocolate chips."],[null,"Scoop oat mixture into 1 Tbsp. balls and place on waxed paper. Let cool and refrigerate."]],"h":[]},"3173":{"s":[[null,"Line a 5 x 7-inch or 8-inch square baking dish with wax or parchment paper."],[null,"In a medium bowl mix together oats, cinnamon and salt."],[null,"In a medium bowl mix protein powder, peanut butter and agave nectar; stir until smooth."],[null,"Mix the oats with peanut butter mixture until well blended."],[null,"Pat mixture evenly into lined baking pan. Sprinkle chocolate chips on top and pat down evenly. Refrigerate for at least one hour."],[null,"Cut into 5 sections then in half for 10 bars. If desired, wrap each bar in plastic wrap. Keep refrigerated until ready to eat or carry on the go."]],"h":[[null,"Honey may be substituted for agave syrup."],[null,"Substitute dried cranberries or cherries for chocolate chips."],[null,"Vanilla or unflavored protein powder can be used."]]},"4619274":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400°F."],[null,"Cut the leeks lengthwise and rinse under running water. After washing, cut them in small slices."],[null,"In a non-stick frying pan, heat the oil over medium heat. Sauté the leeks for 4-5 minutes while stirring often, until leeks are wilted and tender."],[null,"In a large bowl, whisk the eggs. Add the flour, rice beverage, and milk. Add the sautéed leeks from step 3, and season with pepper."],[null,"Pour the mixture directly into a pie pan. Place the basil leaves on top."],[null,"Bake the quiche in the oven for 30-35 minutes. Test for doneness by inserting a knife near the center of the quiche. When the knife comes out clean the quiche is ready."]],"h":[[null,"* Because of phosphate additives in fortified rice beverage we are recommending the unfortified product."],["Including lower-potassium vegetables in the kidney diet","As part of the kidney diet, lower-potassium foods are often encouraged. With this goal in mind, there are many different vegetables that can be selected to provide a variety of vitamins, minerals, and flavor. Watching the portion size of each vegetable is important as different foods contain varying amounts of potassium. Even some vegetables that are higher in potassium can be consumed in smaller portions, less frequently so you can enjoy this ‘taste’ in your diet. Discuss options with a registered dietitian nutritionist. Leeks are a strong-tasting vegetable that add a distinct sweet, onion flavor to meals. There are three parts to this vegetable with only the root end not able to be eaten. Once washed, leeks can be eaten raw or cooked, and make a great addition to a salad, main entrée, soup, or side dish. A half-cup of leeks contain approximately 80 milligrams (mg) of potassium. In comparison, the same portion of chopped white onion provides roughly 117 mg of potassium. Using this lower-potassium vegetable also has other benefits, as leeks are a good source of magnesium and vitamins A and C."]]},"6862739":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6424759":{"s":[],"h":[]},"3182":{"s":[[null,"Break graham crackers into squares (2-1/2″)."],[null,"Spread 2 tablespoons Reddi-Wip® topping on 10 of the graham cracker halves."],[null,"Top with the remaining 10 graham cracker halves to make sandwiches."],[null,"Place sandwiches on a cookie sheet and freeze for 2 hours before serving."]],"h":[[null,"This recipe can be made in batches and kept frozen for a yummy snack later."],[null,"Wrap each sandwich in plastic wrap and place in a freezer bag."],[null,"Check graham crackers for phosphate additives before purchasing."]]},"9822376":{"s":[[null,"Add all the ingredients except the water to a food processor or blender. Process until smooth and scrape down the sides as needed."],[null,"Add 1 tablespoon of water at a time, as needed to reach desired consistency."]],"h":[[null,"You may store your pesto in a jar in your fridge to use within a few days. Or keep frozen for up to 6 months. You may sub any herb for the basil, as desired. Just keep the same ratio. Use a food processor for pesto with a little texture, or a blender for smoother results. Feel free to double or triple the recipe to make freezer portions for future use. This is especially useful when harvesting herbs from your garden to ensure no waste."]]},"9265013":{"s":[[null,"Add all the ingredients to your blender and process until smooth."],[null,"Serve with tortilla chips, on nachos, with steamed or roasted broccoli or cauliflower, or over potato wedges or poutine."]],"h":[[null,"Use unsalted, raw pepitas or sunflower seeds . If you don’t have, or cannot find unsalted, make sure to reduce or omit the added salt. Once blended, taste and add more salt, only if needed. To ensure the cheese sauce has no oil , use roasted red peppers that have been jarred in water, and not marinated in oil. (Or roast your own .) Leftovers keep refrigerated in a sealed container for up to 5 days. Or freeze them in a freezer-safe, airtight container for up to 3 months."]]},"5308141":{"s":[[null,"Add the onions, carrots, peppers, rosemary, sage, thyme, garlic, and black pepper to a roasting tin. Drizzle with sesame oil and roast for 30 minutes or until soft."],[null,"Meanwhile, in a jug, add the boiling water, balsamic vinegar, stock cube, miso paste, and lemon juice, mix well, and set aside."],[null,"Once roasted, add all the vegetables, walnuts, chestnuts, and cornflour to a blender. Blend until a coarse consistency."],[null,"Once blended, remove from the blender and pour into a bowl, gradually adding the stock to loosen the mixture"],[null,"Pour the mixture into a pie dish and crinkle each sheet of filo into a ball and place on top of the mixture, drizzle generously with olive oil, continue this process until all sheets of filo are used."],[null,"Bake for 25 minutes or until golden brown."],[null,"Cut to portions and serve."]],"h":[["Renastep note","Always check with your dietitian or doctor that this recipe is suitable for you."],["Renastep note","This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutritics dietary analysis software. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information."]]},"7308141":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 175°C/ gas 3. Peel the butternut squash, remove the seeds and cut into chunks. Place in a pan of water and bring to the boil. Boil for 10–15 minutes until tender. When the flesh is soft, drain and mash, and set aside."],[null,"Meanwhile, add 1 dash of the oil to a pan over a medium heat, then add the onion, stirring regularly. When it's starting to brown, add the red pepper and cook for another 4–5 minutes. Add the garlic, mix and remove from the heat, and allow to cool."],[null,"Divide the nuts into 3 piles. Reserve a third of the nuts whole and set aside. Roughly chop another third and finely chop the final third."],[null,"Add the eggs to a bowl with the ground almonds, onion, red pepper, finely chopped and roughly chopped nuts, the chestnuts, pepper, water and nutmeg. Mix thoroughly."],[null,"Rub remaining oil around a 1lb loaf tin and line it with greaseproof paper."],[null,"Add two-thirds of the egg mixture and press it around the tin to line it, leaving room in the centre for the filling."],[null,"Add the butternut squash followed by a layer of spinach to the centre. Finally, sprinkle on the cranberries."],[null,"Next, carefully add the rest of the egg mixture to create a lid and sprinkle with the reserved whole nuts, pressing them gently into the topping."],[null,"Cover with a piece of foil and place the loaf in another, larger oven dish. Fill with water to half way up the loaf tin. (This technique is called a bain-marie.) Cook in the oven for 30 minutes, then remove the foil and cook for another 10 minutes."],[null,"Remove from the oven, turn out onto a plate and serve."]],"h":[[null,"The nuts in this recipe make this dish high in fat. But, the fats found in most nuts make them a good source of unsaturated fat, which is good for your heart health. Nuts are also high in protein and fibre."],[null,"If you're having nuts, they're better eaten unsalted."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Then defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"6536985":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6135574":{"s":[[null,"Split and toast English muffin."],[null,"Spread each half with almond butter."],[null,"Top with sliced strawberries."],[null,"Sprinkle with coconut."]],"h":[]},"7347873":{"s":[[null,"Place all the ingredients in a food processor and process for 2–3 minutes, or until a sticky dough ball forms."],[null,"Roll 2 teaspoons of the mixture into balls and roll in the extra cocoa powder to coat. Repeat until all the mixture is used."]],"h":[[null,"You could try coating your truffles with roasted sesame seeds, liquorice powder, desiccated coconut, chopped nuts, matcha green tea powder, or leave them plain. The flavouring is versatile, too – orange, coffee or peppermint make great alternatives."],[null,"These truffles are advised as an occasional treat, but are perfect for sharing or giving as gifts."]]},"6009716":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 425 degrees F."],[null,"Mix the first four ingredients in a large bowl. Set aside."],[null,"Combine milk, egg, and oil. Mix applesauce with mashed banana and blend with liquid ingredients. Add to dry ingredients and mix just until moistened."],[null,"Pour into muffin tins that have been sprayed with nonstick cooking spray. Do not use paper liners, as the muffins have a tendency to stick to the paper. Bake for 15-17 minutes."],[null,"TIP: The tops of these muffins don’t brown well due to the low sugar content, but they are still moist and full of flavor!"]],"h":[]},"4556233":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F (conventional)."],[null,"Using an electric mixer, cream together, margarine, sugar, honey and egg for 2 minutes. Then add applesauce, zest and extract. Continue mixing for 1 minute. Set aside cream mixture."],[null,"Prepare flour mixture by adding flour, baking soda, oatmeal, cinnamon and coconut to a bowl. Stir until well combined."],[null,"Pour flour mixture on top of the cream mixture and stir by hand until well combined (1 minute). Add cranberries and finish."],[null,"Line a baking sheet with parchment paper. Arrange 2 tablespoons of batter per cookie on the sheet, leaving enough room for the batter to spread."],[null,"Bake for 10 minutes on the middle rack. Remove from heat and wait one minute before transferring to a wire rack to cool completely."]],"h":[[null,"* Coconut is a higher potassium fruit and should be enjoyed in moderation."],[null,"These chewy-crisp cookies are a great on-the-go snack!"]]},"9985547":{"s":[[null,"Line a baking sheet with parchment paper and set it aside."],[null,"Add everything to a large mixing bowl and stir until combined and the oats are evenly coated."],[null,"Use a small cookie scoop to portion and roll the mixture into bite-sized balls, placing them on your parchment-lined tray."],[null,"Refrigerate the energy balls for 1 hour (or longer) to firm them up before enjoying."]],"h":[[null,"Use slightly wet hands to shape the balls to prevent sticking. The batter will be sticky, which is normal."],[null,"The rolled balls will be soft, so refrigerate them for at least 1 hour before enjoying them to help them harden and set."]]},"6553785":{"s":[[null,"Add the oats, broth, and soy sauce to a sauce pan over high heat. Bring to a boil, then reduce to a simmer until the oatmeal is tender, about 10 minutes."],[null,"Coat a small nonstick sauté pan with cooking spray. Add the mushrooms and sauté until tender and all liquid is evaporated, about 4 minutes. Add the lime juice and sauté until the liquid has evaporated. Stir the mushrooms into the oatmeal porridge."],[null,"Clean the sauté pan, then add cooking spray. Fry the eggs until the yolks are just set."],[null,"In a bowl, pour in ¾ cup oatmeal porridge, top with a fried egg, and 1 ½ Tsp. scallions and cilantro. Repeat for the remaining 3 bowls."]],"h":[]},"6123989":{"s":[[null,"Using a food processor, process the oats to a flour-like consistency. Mix oats and baking powder in a small bowl and set aside."],[null,"In a separate bowl, mix eggs, milk, mashed banana, and vanilla. Add to dry ingredients, and mix until just combined. Then fold in pecans."],[null,"Heat oil in nonstick skillet over medium heat. Drop 1/4 cup of batter onto the hot skillet to make each pancake. Cook until lightly brown on both sides."]],"h":[]},"7424102":{"s":[[null,"Place the bread into a small bowl and pour over the milk and egg. Leave to soak for 5 minutes, then mash with a fork."],[null,"Meanwhile, mix the mince, garlic, onion, red pepper, oregano, and pepper and combine well. Mix in the egg and bread mixture"],[null,"Wet your hands and form into 20 pieces and roll into small balls (it's best to use your hands for this)."],[null,"Place onto a lightly-oiled baking sheet and put under a hot grill for 10-12 minutes, turning occasionally until browned all over and cooked through. Allow to cool a little."],[null,"Insert a red pepper slice into each olive pit then carefully slice and place a disk of mozzarella on top."],[null,"Stack the mozzarella slice underneath the olive pit and secure with a cocktail stick."]],"h":[[null,"You could use beef or lamb mince for the meatballs. Or you can use minced fish such as cod."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"2463":{"s":[[null,"In measuring cup, whisk all ingredients."],[null,"Toss dressing with salad and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Homemade salad dressing is easy to make and is much lower in sodium compared to commercially prepared salad dressing."]]},"9560531":{"s":[[null,"Drain your chickpeas over a bowl, so you can reserve a tablespoon of the aquafaba, and do NOT rinse them."],[null,"Place the drained (but not rinsed) chickpeas in your fryer basket in a single layer. Air fry at 400 degrees F for 10 minutes, mixing at the halfway point."],[null,"Meanwhile, combine the tablespoon of aquafaba (and lime juice for the chili lime option) with HALF of your seasonings for your flavour of choice. Then open the fryer (once cooked for 10 mins) and evenly pour the mixture over the chickpeas and mix well to evenly coat. Continue air frying for another 5-7 minutes, until desired crispiness is reached. Make sure to mix them every few minutes, to prevent burning."],[null,"Immediately transfer your air fried chickpeas to a bowl and sprinkle with the remaining seasoning while they're still hot. Mix well and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Do not rinse the chickpeas . Rinsing them makes the skins come loose and then they burn if you don’t remove them all, which is tedious and completely unnecessary. Use no salt added chickpeas since we’re not rinsing them, to control the sodium level. No need to dry the chickpeas . Your fryer will dry them for you, making this recipe easier than ever! Mix your chickpeas every few minutes once seasoned, to prevent burning. Store leftovers in a paper bag at room temperature. Do not refrigerate or place in a sealed container or they will get moist and lose their crispiness. The nutritional information is for one third of a batch, but does not include the seasoning. Edited June 2021 to add two additional flavours, Italian + ranch."]]},"9114619":{"s":[[null,"Add all the ingredients, except the lime juice and the vinegar to your food processor. Process until finely chopped."],[null,"Then transfer the herbs to a bowl or jar and pour in the lime juice and vinegar. Mix well and let rest for 1 hour to blend the flavours. Serve with your favourite grilled foods."]],"h":[[null,"Do you hate cilantro? We love it, but I know some of you don’t. No problem. Just use all parsley instead, or a smaller ratio of cilantro. If you don’t have red wine vinegar , white wine vinegar or apple cider vinegar also work. Want some heat? Spice it up with a pinch of cayenne pepper or red chili flakes. Want smoky flavour? Use smoked paprika instead of sweet and/or add a splash of liquid smoke. Switch up the citrus if preferred. Use lemon over lime, or a combo of both, or add some freshly squeezed orange to the mix for a touch of sweetness. Do not add the liquids to your food processor with the herbs. The herbs should be finely chopped everything BEFORE adding liquids to prevent blending the mixture into a puree. If you don’t want to transfer the ingredients to a bowl to mix with the liquids, add them to the processor AFTER the other ingredients have been finely chopped and pulse once or twice (NOT MORE) to combine."]]},"9719129":{"s":[[null,"Add all the salad ingredients to a large bowl and set aside."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine all the dressing ingredients and mix well. Then pour over the salad and mix until well combined."],[null,"Serve as a salad, or dip with chips or crackers. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Serve chilled or at room temperature, both ways taste great. This dish is very adaptable, feel free to add more ingredients, like black olives, celery, avocado, garlic or green onion. For extra heat , use more jalapeno or leave in the seeds. Or add some cayenne pepper or a splash or two of hot sauce to your cowboy caviar dressing. You may prepare the ingredients ahead , but this dish tastes best when the dressing is added no more than 2-3 hours ahead, as the veggies will start to soften. Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-4 days."]]},"9834844":{"s":[[null,"Add the black beans, all your seasonings, plus 1/4 cup of water to a large skillet. Mix well and heat over medium heat for about 5-6 minutes to heat the beans and absorb the seasoning and most of the water."],[null,"Meanwhile, combine all the salad ingredients in a bowl and mix well. Set aside."],[null,"Divide the components between your two bowls and garnish with extra cilantro and lime wedges if you'd like."]],"h":[[null,"For no cilantro : Try it with fresh parsley, dill, or another herb you enjoy."],[null,"Switch up the brown rice for wild rice, quinoa, barley, farro, or another grain you have available."],[null,"For less calories , use cauliflower rice instead of brown rice."],[null,"For corn-free , just omit or add more tomato salad or another veggie."],[null,"Swap the black beans for brown lentils or chickpeas if you prefer."]]},"9970596":{"s":[[null,"Add the four tablespoons of broth to a large skillet with the diced onion. Sauté until soft, approx. 4-5 minutes, adding more broth or water, if needed to prevent sticking."],[null,"Then add the garlic and the spices, mix well and cook another 30 seconds."],[null,"Next, add the pinto beans and the remaining 3/4 cup of broth to the pan and simmer for 5 minutes, until the liquid is mostly reduced. Turn off the heat and use a potato masher to mash most of the beans."],[null,"Now add the cilantro, and lime juice, and mix well. Taste for salt and add if needed. (This will depend on the saltiness of your broth.)"],[null,"Use in dishes like burritos, tacos, fajitas, and more!"]],"h":[[null,"Use a good quality, flavourful/salty broth for the best flavour. I use this homemade bouillon mix . If using a low sodium broth , you may need to add a little salt to the final product. Taste and adjust as needed. For smoother refried beans , mash longer or use a food processor or blender if you don’t want any texture at all. Leftover refried beans will keep in an airtight container in your fridge for 3-4 days or freeze in a freezer-safe container for up to 6 months."]]},"9969020":{"s":[[null,"Add all the ingredients to your blender, starting with 2 tablespoons of water. Blend until smooth."],[null,"Taste and adjust for salt if needed and add another 2 tablespoons of water if a thinner consistency is preferred."],[null,"Serve with veggies, pita, tortilla chips, or anything else you'd like."]],"h":[[null,"Use roasted red peppers that are packed in water (not oil) to keep the fat content low. Or roast your own peppers if preferred. If roasting your own peppers , remove most of the charred/black skins, but don’t worry about removing every little piece as those bits will add a stronger depth of flavour. Keep leftovers in a sealed container in your fridge for up to 5 days. Or freeze airtight for up to 3 months."]]},"9480093":{"s":[[null,"Combine the chickpea flour and the seasoning (if using, skip for pancakes) in a mixing bowl. Then add the water and mix well. Let the batter rest for 5 minutes while you heat your nonstick griddle."],[null,"When your griddle is hot, pour half the batter for each flatbread. You will get two rounds of about 6-7 inches each. Cook for 4-5 minutes until the edges appear cooked through and there are several bubbles on top. Carefully flip, scraping around the edges first to ensure it's not stuck."],[null,"Cook the other side for another 3-4 minutes, until golden and cooked through. Transfer to a dish or cutting board and serve as desired, according to whichever method you're using."]],"h":[[null,"Let the batter rest for at least 10 minutes before cooking. Make sure your griddle is very hot before pouring the batter on top. Also ensure your griddle is non stick, otherwise, you may need to grease it. An older, heavily used griddle will eventually lose it's non sticking power, so use your own discretion, as you know your tools best. If in doubt, grease the plates or do a test with a small amount of batter first. When flipping the socca, scrape around the edges first, to ensure it is not stuck. Then flip. Feel free to add more seasoning, like cumin, chili powder, or cayenne pepper to amp up the flavour if using a savoury option. If making the socca pancakes , omit all the seasoning listed, and you may use a dash of cinnamon or nutmeg instead. Optional toppings and dips are not included in the nutritional information."]]},"9291733":{"s":[[null,"Shred the cabbage and the carrots and place them in a large bowl."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine the mayo, maple syrup, vinegar, mustard, and black pepper. Whisk until combined. Then pour it on the coleslaw and mix until evenly coated."]],"h":[[null,"For oil-free , use my pepita mayo for this recipe. Store-bought mayo usually has a LOT of oil."],[null,"For a no-mayo option , try our peanut-dressing coleslaw ."],[null,"Use store-bought shredded coleslaw for quicker prep . Use 6-8 cups of your favourite mixture."],[null,"Taste the dressing before pouring it on your salad and adjust the seasoning if needed. You want a very bold flavoured dressing since the veggies are not seasoned."],[null,"For the salad , I like purple cabbage for its vibrant colour, but you may use green or a mixture of both cabbage colours, if preferred. Other additions include parsley, cilantro, celery, green onion, or red onion."],[null,"For the dressing , you may add more seasoning if you’d like. Some options include celery seed, cumin, chili powder, garlic powder, smoked paprika, or cayenne pepper."],[null,"This vegan coleslaw tastes best the same day it’s made, however, leftovers keep in the refrigerator for up to 3 days."],[null,"The nutritional information includes my pepita mayo. If you sub for store-bought, it will add more calories and fat."]]},"9688344":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 400℉/204℃ and line a 9\"x9\" square baking pan with parchment paper."],[null,"Place the soy milk and the apple cider vinegar in a small bowl and set it aside for a few minutes until thickened and curdled."],[null,"Meanwhile, add all the dry ingredients to a mixing bowl and whisk to combine. Then add the curdled milk with the remaining wet ingredients to the same bowl and stir until combined without over mixing."],[null,"Pour your batter into your prepared baking pan, and bake for 15-18 minutes, or until a toothpick inserted in the center comes out clean."],[null,"Remove from the oven and let cool for 5-10 minutes before slicing."]],"h":[[null,"If using another size pan, bake time will vary. For example: an 8″x8″ pan will require a few additional minutes. Always check with a toothpick to ensure doneness."],[null,"Use cornmeal NOT cornstarch ! They are not the same. Corn starch is JUST the starch with everything else removed. You can find cornmeal in the flour section of your supermarket."],[null,"For optimal texture, use fine or medium ground corn meal , not course, unless you enjoy a gritty texture."],[null,"Use ACTIVE baking powder for best results. Baking powder that has been open in the pantry for 6+ months may start to lose its effectiveness."],[null,"Line the baking pan with parchment paper for easier transferring once baked . Grab both sides of the paper and lift the bread out and onto a cutting board or cooling rack, so it cools quicker."],[null,"Do not overmix the batter . It might feel tempting to keep mixing until your batter is perfectly smooth. But a few lumps are perfectly fine. Overmixing may result in a dry and/or gummy texture."],[null,"Tastes best when freshly made or within 1-2 days. Leftovers keep at room temperature for 3-4 days, covered with a clean dry towel, or in a sealed container. OR freeze airtight for up to 3 months."]]},"9250282":{"s":[[null,"Add the pumpkin seeds to your blender and process until they are broken down and a flour like consistency."],[null,"Now add all remaining ingredients and process until smooth and creamy."],[null,"Refrigerate until ready to use, as it tastes best when cold."]],"h":[[null,"Processing the seeds first, separately will help ensure there are no loose bits of seeds in your mayo, resulting in smoother mayo. Store in an airtight container in your refrigerator for up to 1 week. If you're not avoiding nuts, and want the mayo to be white, you may sub the pumpkin seeds for cashews. If you don't have a high speed blender, you will need to soak the cashews first in boiling hot water for at least 15 minutes. For spicy mayo add some hot sauce or cayenne, or check out my Sriracha Mayo"]]},"6341327":{"s":[[null,"Combine water, oats, and salt in a medium-size pan. Bring to a boil, reduce heat, and simmer 10 minutes uncovered. Remove from heat and let stand 2 minutes."],[null,"Place the fruit spread in a small microwave-safe bowl and cook on high setting for 15 seconds or until slightly melted. Remove from heat and stir in the extract."],[null,"Spoon equal amounts of the oatmeal in 4 bowls. Top with 1 Tbsp. fruit spread, 1/2 cup berries, and 1 Tbsp. almonds."]],"h":[]},"3790":{"s":[[null,"Heat milk and butter in small saucepan over medium-low heat until butter is melted, 3 to 5 minutes. Cool milk/butter mixture until warm to the touch."],[null,"Meanwhile, whisk flour, sugar, salt and yeast in a large bowl to combine."],[null,"Gradually whisk warm milk/butter mixture into flour mixture; continue to whisk until batter is smooth."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk eggs and vanilla until combined, then add egg mixture to batter and whisk until incorporated."],[null,"Scrape down sides of the bowl with a rubber spatula, cover with plastic wrap and refrigerate at least 12 hours and up to 24 hours."],[null,"When ready to make waffles, heat oven to 200° F to keep waffles warm after cooking. Heat the waffle iron."],[null,"Remove batter from refrigerator when waffle iron is ready (batter will be foamy and doubled in size). Whisk batter to recombine (batter will deflate)."],[null,"Use 1/2-cup batter for 7” waffle iron or 1-cup batter for 9” waffle iron."],[null,"Serve immediately or crisp and keep warm in the oven."]],"h":[[null,"Make batter the day before use."],[null,"This recipe has not been tested with nondairy creamer or other milk substitutes."],[null,"For flavor variety use pure vanilla extract or orange extract in place of almond extract."],[null,"Top with fresh berries or a bit of powdered sugar if desired."],[null,"Most waffle mixes or frozen waffles contain over 400 mg sodium and over 180 mg phosphorus for a serving comparable to this recipe. Replacing baking powder with baker’s yeast makes a difference."]]},"3420":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Blend all ingredients in order given, apples last and blended least."],[null,"Grease a 12” x 7-1/2” glass baking pan or 2 smaller pans."],[null,"Pour mixture into pan and bake at for approximately 1 hour. Cake will be golden."]],"h":[[null,"Do not over cook, the cake should be moist."]]},"2409":{"s":[[null,"Chop carrot, celery and onion."],[null,"Melt the butter in a 3-quart saucepan on stove top burner set to medium-high heat. Add the vegetables to the saucepan and cook until tender."],[null,"Add the pre-cooked salmon chunks to the pan."],[null,"Stir in the chicken broth, milk and black pepper. Bring mixture to a near-boil, but do not boil. Reduce heat to simmer."],[null,"Combine the cornstarch and water. Slowly pour into broth mixture, stirring, until the soup is thickened."],[null,"Simmer for another five minutes. Serve warm and enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"You can substitute boneless canned salmon for fresh, but replace reduced-sodium broth with low-sodium broth to keep sodium content lower."]]},"3237":{"s":[[null,"Cream margarine and beat in sugar until soft and fluffy."],[null,"Add flour and mix. Knead dough to incorporate the flour. Form into a ball."],[null,"Wrap dough in plastic wrap and chill for at least 1 hour."],[null,"Roll dough out about 1/4” thick on a lightly floured board."],[null,"Cut with cookie cutters, or with a knife into diamond shapes. Bake cookies on a lightly greased cookie sheet at 325° F for 10 minutes or until lightly browned."]],"h":[[null,"Decorate cookies with cinnamon, colored sugar or icing for a holiday touch."]]},"2373":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F. Set butter out to soften."],[null,"Cut each plum into 8 pieces."],[null,"In a mixing bowl, cream together the butter and 12 tablespoons (3/4 cup) sugar. Beat in the eggs, vanilla and lemon juice and mix well."],[null,"Stir together the flour and baking soda. Mix dry ingredients into the creamed mixture."],[null,"Spoon batter into a greased 8” or 9” baking pan. Place the plum slices on top, skin sides down."],[null,"Combine cinnamon with remaining 2 tablespoons sugar. Sprinkle mixture over the top of cake."],[null,"Bake for about 40 minutes, or until toothpick inserted into center comes out clean."],[null,"Remove cake from the oven and let cool for 10 to 15 minutes. Loosen around the edges and remove from pan, turning twice so the plum side faces up."],[null,"Top with whipped cream. Serve warm or cold."]],"h":[[null,"Recipe analysis includes salted butter. Substitute a trans-fat free margarine of desired."],[null,"Save some for later. This cake freezes well."],[null,"Four large plums will yield approximately 1-1/2 cups."]]},"1002590":{"s":[[null,"Chop onion and green pepper. Shred potato."],[null,"Heat oil in a nonstick skillet. Add onion and green pepper; sauté for 2 minutes. Add shredded potatoes and cook for 5 minutes until browned, turning once. Remove from skillet and set aside."],[null,"Spray skillet with oil and heat over medium heat. Beat eggs with non-dairy creamer and pour into skillet. Cook until eggs are set."],[null,"Place shredded potatoes in the center of the omelet. Fold both sides of the omelet over with a spatula, then slide onto a plate."],[null,"Garnish with parsley sprigs and season to taste."]],"h":[[null,"For a lower potassium omelet, soak fresh or frozen shredded potatoes in 2 cups of water for 2 hours. Place on a clean kitchen towel, cover and roll up to remove excess water before cooking. This reduces the potassium content by approximately 43 milligrams."]]},"3351":{"s":[[null,"Heat a small saucepan over medium-high heat. Coat pan with cooking spray. Add corn, zucchini and onions to pan; sauté 4 minutes or until vegetables are crisp-tender. Remove from heat."],[null,"Heat a 10” nonstick skillet over medium-high heat. Combine water, pepper (or Mrs. Dash®), egg whites and egg in a bowl, stirring well with a whisk."],[null,"Coat pan with cooking spray. Pour egg mixture into pan; cook until edges begin to set (about 2 minutes). Gently lift the edges of the omelet with a spatula, tilting the pan to allow uncooked egg mixture to come into contact with the pan."],[null,"Spoon vegetable mixture onto half of omelet, sprinkle cheese over vegetable mixture. Loosen omelet with a spatula and fold in half. Cook 2 minutes more or until cheese melts. Carefully slide omelet onto a plate."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute any variety of Mrs, Dash seasoning or black pepper if you do not like spicy seasonong."],[null,"For those following a CKD non-dialysis diet: This higher protein recipe may be appropriate for your diet if the portion size were adjusted to reduce protein content. Adjustments should be based on your individual protein prescription. Check with your dietitian if you are unsure."]]},"7833905":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200ºC/gas 6."],[null,"Flour the worktop and roll out the pastry to a round 25cm in diameter. Brush with a little of the milk and sprinkle over the semolina."],[null,"Mix together the apples, blackberries and half the sugar and place onto the pastry, leaving a 6cm gap around the edge."],[null,"Fold up the edges of the pastry and press together (the top of the pie should remain open) brush with the remaining milk and sprinkle over the remaining sugar."],[null,"Bake for 25–30 minutes until golden and the fruit is tender. Serve with a little crème fraiche, yogurt or ice-cream."]],"h":[[null,"If you like a juicer and softer pie, cook the apple and blackberries for 3–4 mins in a pan with 1 tbsp water and spread over the pastry."],[null,"You could also use pears, apricots, peaches, nectarines or cherries."]]},"4789611":{"s":[[null,"Pour the chicken broth and the cream into a large frying pan or pot. Add the garlic, parmesan cheese and peas. Season with half of the lemon zest and pepper."],[null,"Add the spaghetti and bring the liquid with the pasta to a boil. Stir, reduce the heat, cover and let cook for 10 to 12 minutes until the pasta is cooked. Lift the cover once or twice during the cooking period to make sure that there is enough liquid left until the pasta is cooked. Add additional chicken stock if necessary to get a creamy sauce."],[null,"Once the pasta is cooked, remove the pan from the heat and add the egg whites. Stir the pasta and the sauce. The egg whites will cook with the heat of the pasta and its sauce."],[null,"Garnish with the rest of the lemon zest and the basil and serve immediately."]],"h":[["Cow’s milk alternatives","Different beverages contain varying amounts of protein and potassium. Depending on your stage of kidney disease, your registered dietitian may recommend one type over another to limit these nutrients when cooking. Dairy (like cow's milk and cream) is an excellent source of protein and potassium, but with chronic kidney disease, should be used in limited amounts. Consider non-dairy alternatives such as soy, almond and rice products for recipes substitutions. Soy: This plant-based beverage comes from soybeans. Read labels on different brands to compare nutrient content. On average, a ½ cup of soy beverage contains 4 grams of protein and 143 milligrams of potassium. Almond: Almonds are ground and blended with water to make almond milk. ½ cup of almond beverage contains less than 1 gram of protein and 88 milligrams of potassium. Rice: Rice beverage is made from milled rice. It contains the least amount of these nutrients with less than 1 gram of protein and 32 milligrams of potassium per ½ cup."]]},"6311044":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F."],[null,"Season the chicken with the rosemary. Spray a Dutch oven or oven-safe pot with cooking spray and add the oil. Heat over medium-high heat. Place the chicken in the pot and sear for 3 minutes per side."],[null,"Cut the acorn squash in half lengthwise and scoop out the seeds. Cut each half into quarters; discard ends."],[null,"Place the acorn squash and apple slices around the chicken. Drizzle the honey evenly over the squash and apple slices and then sprinkle them with cinnamon. Pour the water over the chicken."],[null,"Bake for 45 minutes in the oven, uncovered. To serve, pour some of the juices over the chicken, squash, and apples."]],"h":[]},"4522325":{"s":[[null,"Pre-heat oven to 350°F (conventional)."],[null,"In a large frying pan, cook the onions with the margarine over medium heat until very soft and golden, stirring frequently (15–20 minutes)."],[null,"Bring water to a boil and cook noodles according to package directions."],[null,"Prepare noodle mixture: drain noodles and add them to the pan with the cooked onions. Toss with cream cheese to coat evenly. Season with black pepper to taste. Add parmesan cheese."],[null,"Prepare egg mixture: mix eggs and egg whites in a medium bowl. Add rice milk and parsley."],[null,"Grease a 2-inch deep, 10-inch wide quiche pan and dust with bread crumbs."],[null,"Put noodle mixture in the bottom of the pan, spreading evenly. Pour egg mixture over it and garnish with parsley."],[null,"Place pan in the middle of pre-heated oven and bake for 40 minutes or until golden and set."],[null,"Remove from oven and allow to cool 10 minutes before cutting."]],"h":[[null,"© (NoYolks are a good choice)"],[null,"Can be prepared ahead of time and heated up in portions."],[null,"Keeps 3–4 days in the fridge. Wrap in foil."]]},"2091":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl combine yogurt or sour cream, peach preserves and mustard. Refrigerate until ready to serve."],[null,"Preheat oven to 400 °F."],[null,"In a medium mixing bowl combine flour, Mrs. Dash seasoning and sugar."],[null,"Make a well in the middle of dry ingredients. Add water, oil and egg white. Mix together until dough forms."],[null,"Flour a dough board and knead dough for 3-4 minutes. Divide into 4 pieces and form each into a ball."],[null,"On lightly floured board roll dough ball out until very thin."],[null,"Cut into cracker rounds or strips and place on an ungreased baking sheet. Pierce with a fork to keep dough from bubbling."],[null,"Bake for 7 to 9 minutes until crackers start to brown and crisp. Be careful not to overcook."],[null,"Repeat with each dough ball to make 4 dozen crackers."],[null,"Serve crackers with Peachy Dip."]],"h":[[null,"Serve crackers with Peachy Dip or your favorite low-sodium cracker topping."],[null,"Store leftover crackers in a sealed zip top bag or container."],[null,"Making your own batch of crackers helps with sodium control and saves money. Be creative with herbs and spices and cracker shapes."],[null,"Choose Greek yogurt or substitute with sour cream based on your diet goals. Comparison of sour cream and Greek yogurt:"],[null,"Greek yogurt (non-fat) 1/2 cup = calories 68, protein 11.5 g, carbohydrate 2.7 g, fat 0 g, sodium 40 mg, potassium 160 mg, phosphorus 153 mg"],[null,"Sour cream (regular) 1/2 cup = calories 185, protein 2 g, carbohydrate 4 g, fat 19 g, sodium 77 g, potassium 135 g, phosphorus 110 g."]]},"2272":{"s":[[null,"Place ingredients in a jar and shake to combine."],[null,"Store until ready to use in cooking or place in a shaker to use at the table."]],"h":[[null,"Use a table top shaker with large holes."]]},"6923760":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F. Heat 1 tsp of the olive oil in a large nonstick ovenproof skillet over medium heat. Add the onion and shallot and sauté for about 7 to 8 minutes. Remove the onion mixture from the skillet and set aside."],[null,"Beat the eggs, egg whites, basil, and salt and pepper. Fold in the onion mixture."],[null,"In the remaining 1 tsp of oil, heat the egg mixture on medium low in the skillet. Cook without stirring for about 8 minutes."],[null,"Transfer the skillet to the oven, sprinkle with the cheese, and bake for about 10 minutes until top is no longer runny. Cook an additional 5 minutes if necessary. Cut into wedges to serve."]],"h":[]},"6448197":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F."],[null,"In a large skillet, heat olive oil over medium heat. Add onion and saute for 5 minutes, stirring frequently. Add artichokes and thyme and cook for an additional 3 minutes or until veggies begin to brown. Add spinach and cook for an additional 1-2 minutes until spinach is wilted. Remove skillet from heat."],[null,"In a microwave-safe bowl, combine light mayonnaise, cheese wedges, and 1 tbsp Parmesan cheese. Heat in microwave for 30 seconds to soften, then mix well. If needed, heat mixture in 15-second increments until cheeses are softened and easily mixed with mayonnaise."],[null,"Add cheese mixture and lemon juice to sauteed vegetables and mix well. Spread dip into a small baking dish, top with remaining 1 tbsp of Parmesan cheese, and bake in the oven for 5 minutes. Serve warm."]],"h":[]},"7025833":{"s":[[null,"Deseed and finely slice ½ small red chilli."],[null,"Drain a can of sardines, reserving some of the oil."],[null,"Put a handful of rocket on top of the slices of bread and arrange the sardines on top."],[null,"Scatter with the chilli slices and drizzle over a little of the reserved oil."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"6139190":{"s":[[null,"Drain and rinse the chickpeas. Transfer to a medium bowl."],[null,"Add fresh dill, mayo, Dijon, vinegar, and spices to the bowl."],[null,"Use a fork or potato masher to crush the chickpeas, making a semi-smooth spread."],[null,"Toast the bread slices. Divide between plates and top with spring mix, tomato slices, and chickpea spread. Serve with a side of veggie sticks."]],"h":[]},"6840128":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 450 degrees F. Coat a baking sheet with cooking spray and set it aside."],[null,"Slice one round edge of the sweet potato thinly lengthwise. Slice the other round edge of the sweet potato thinly lengthwise. Discard those slices."],[null,"Slice the sweet potato down the middle lengthwise and peel. Repeat for other sweet potato. You will end up with four 1-inch-thick lengthwise slices of sweet potato."],[null,"Place on the prepared baking sheet and spray the tops of the sweet potatoes with cooking spray. Bake the sweet potatoes for 10 minutes, then reduce the heat to 350 degrees F."],[null,"Flip the sweet potatoes and then lay equal amounts of thinly sliced zucchini and red bell pepper on each sweet potato. Season with the salt-free seasoning."],[null,"Cut each slice of swiss cheese in half and top each sweet potato with the swiss cheese. Return the potatoes to the oven for 15 more minutes."],[null,"Serve immediately."]],"h":[]},"1933":{"s":[[null,"Mix Kool-Aid® with 2 cups water. Fill ice tray to make orange ice cubes."],[null,"To serve, place 2 orange ice cubes in a small glass and add 4 ounces diet 7 UP®."]],"h":[[null,"One ice cube is approximately 1 ounce of liquid."],[null,"Try your favorite Kool-aid flavor."],[null,"Kool-Aid® liquid drink mix is very concentrated and it’s phosphate-free. Powdered Kool-aid® mix contains calcium phosphate, a phosphate additive."]]},"6868420":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350°F. Lightly spray an 8-inch square baking dish with cooking spray."],[null,"In a medium bowl, stir together the oatmeal, flour, sugar, cardamom, nutmeg, and baking soda."],[null,"In a small bowl, using a fork, lightly beat the egg whites. Stir in the oil and 2 tbsp fresh orange juice."],[null,"Add the egg white mixture to the oatmeal mixture, stirring until the combined mixture holds together. Press three-fourths of the mixture into the baking dish."],[null,"In a medium bowl, whisk together the fruit butter and 2 tsp of the orange zest. Using a rubber scraper, spread the fruit butter mixture over the oatmeal mixture. Sprinkle with the remaining oatmeal mixture."],[null,"Bake for 30–35 minutes, or until the top is golden brown. Transfer the dish to a cooling rack and let cool completely, then cut into 24 equal bars."]],"h":[]},"6895022":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together extra-virgin olive oil, lime juice, unsweetened multi-use syrup, salt, and black pepper."],[null,"Arrange oranges, avocados, red onion, and fresh mint on a platter."],[null,"Pour the dressing over the salad and top with toasted slivered almonds."]],"h":[]},"6916353":{"s":[[null,"Place the greens on a platter. Top with the carrots, onion, and oranges."],[null,"For the vinaigrette, whisk together the orange and lemon juices, honey, and mustard. Slowly add the oil in a thin stream, whisking constantly."],[null,"Drizzle the vinaigrette over the salad. Add pepper to taste, and top with the walnuts."]],"h":[]},"1748":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 F. Completely zest the orange. The zest will measure to approximately 2-1/2 to 3 tablespoons. Set the orange aside. Combine cake mix, water, oil, eggs, orange zest and 1 teaspoon of the orange extract. Mix with a hand mixer on low to medium speed for 2 minutes. Spray a bundt pan with non-stick cooking spray."],[null,"Pour the batter into the prepared pan and bake in the pre-heated oven for 35-40 minutes. Insert a toothpick in the cake to test for doneness. There should only be crumbs on the toothpick when ready, not uncooked batter."],[null,"Place hot pan on a wire rack to cool for about 10 minutes. Use a rubber spatula to loosen the cake around the edges and then invert the cake onto a large plate or serving dish. The cake should release out of the pan and onto the plate. Let cool completely."],[null,"For the glaze: Cut the orange in half and squeeze about 2 tablespoons of juice from the orange into a medium bowl. Add honey, powdered sugar and the remaining 1 teaspoon of orange extract. Whisk gently to incorporate. Slowly drizzle the glaze over the top of the entire cake."]],"h":[[null,"Oranges are generally very limited on a kidney diet due to the high potassium content. This recipe shows how oranges can still be incorporated into cooking and baking in small quantities. The flavor can still be enjoyed in this recipe without consuming the whole orange."],[null,"White cake mix can also be used in place of the yellow cake mix."],[null,"A tube pan may also be substituted for the bundt pan."]]},"6631366":{"s":[[null,"Add the orange, banana, orange juice, yogurt, and vanilla in a blender. Blend until smooth."],[null,"Pour into two glasses. Enjoy immediately."]],"h":[]},"3480":{"s":[[null,"Pour the almond milk, protein powder and vanilla syrup in a blender. Blend well."],[null,"Add orange extract and blend."],[null,"Pour mixture into 4 cups and slowly add 2 tablespoons of orange soda to each cup. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"When soda is added mixture will foam, so add slowly and stop until bubbles reduce if needed to prevent bubbling over."],[null,"If orange extract is unavailable, vanilla extract may be substituted."],[null,"Crush® and Sunkist® orange diet sodas are acceptable for a kidney diet because there are no phosphate additives. Fanta® orange soda does contain phosphate additives."],[null,"Look for almond milk marked ‘original’ and check ingredients to select a product free of phosphate additives."],[null,"If Syntrax Nectar® Whey Protein Isolate Powder is unavailable, ask your dietitian for an appropriate substitute. EAS® 100% Whey Protein Powder is an option and gives approximately 13 grams of protein per scoop."]]},"9661912":{"s":[[null,"Tear your kale into large bite sized pieces and remove the thick stems and discard them. Rinse thoroughly and then add to a large mixing bowl. Pour the lemon juice on top and massage the kale with your hands for 2-3 minutes. This will gently wilt and soften the kale."],[null,"Add the chickpeas and hemp hearts to the same bowl and set aside."],[null,"Combine the dressing ingredients in a small bowl and whisk thoroughly to combine. Then pour the dressing on your salad and mix well to evenly distribute."],[null,"Garnish with the orange segments and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Make sure to massage the kale. Don’t skip this step. It only takes 2-3 minutes of time and the results are well worth the effort. Use freshly squeezed orange juice for the absolute best flavour. If you don’t have apple cider vinegar , sub for white wine vinegar or white balsamic with similar results. Leftovers keep refrigerated for 1-2 days."]]},"4846825":{"s":[[null,"Spray inside of microwave safe mug with non-stick cooking spray."],[null,"Sift together the first four dry ingredients and place in mug."],[null,"To the dry ingredients, add oil, milk, orange juice and vanilla extract. Whisk until well mixed and free of lumps."],[null,"Place mug in a microwave and cook for approximately 1 minute. The cake should rise and be firm to the touch. Do not overcook."],[null,"Serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"* You can use lemon zest and lemon juice instead"],[null,"Note: Cooking times may vary based on microwave."],["Oranges and mandarin oranges","It is very common for those who follow a kidney-friendly diet to be cautious about their potassium intake. When this is the case, there are a number of fruits and vegetables that should be consumed in moderation due to their higher potassium content. An orange is one of those foods. Eating a fresh orange or drinking orange juice may not be possible, at least on a regular basis. A good lower-potassium alternative for a fresh orange would be a mandarin orange. One mandarin orange contains 146 milligrams of potassium compared to 238 milligrams of potassium in one medium-sized orange. A ripe mandarin is firm to slightly soft, heavy for its size and has pebbly looking skin. The peel is very thin, so they are usually easier to peel and split into segments than a traditional orange. You can enjoy them as a snack or healthy dessert. Peel and section to add to a tossed lettuce, fruit or chicken salad to add color and flavor. When fresh mandarins are out of season, you can purchase them in a can or individual serving cups. Choose those packed in water, not syrup."]]},"6397951":{"s":[[null,"Place asparagus in a pot of boiling water over high heat. Reduce heat to low and simmer until asparagus is tender, about 10 minutes. Drain asparagus and submerge immediately in a bowl of ice water."],[null,"Divide lettuce evenly among six salad bowls or plates."],[null,"Combine orange, tomato, and avocado in a medium bowl."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together olive oil, vinegar, salt, and pepper until combined."],[null,"Drain asparagus and add to orange mixture. Pour dressing over orange mixture and stir gently to combine. Spoon mixture on top of romaine lettuce on plates and serve."]],"h":[]},"6332960":{"s":[],"h":[]},"2292":{"s":[[null,"Combine juice and sherbet in a punch bowl."],[null,"Fill the rest of the bowl with the limon-lime soda."]],"h":[[null,"Use sweetened soda if preferred for extra calories."],[null,"Stir punch to keep it from becoming foamy as the sherbet melts."],[null,"Add an ice ring to keep punch chilled."]]},"6747790":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400°F. Line a baking sheet with parchment paper or foil"],[null,"Place broccolini on one side of the baking sheet and drizzle with olive oil."],[null,"Pat salmon dry with paper towels and place on the other side of the baking sheet."],[null,"Combine the orange zest, orange juice, broth, brown sugar substitute, garlic, rosemary, cornstarch, and flaxseed in a small saucepan over medium heat. Cook, whisking occasionally, until the sauce reduces by half and thickens, 8–10 minutes. It should cling to a spoon."],[null,"Brush sauce over the salmon. Place the baking sheet in the oven and bake until salmon reaches an internal temperature of 145°F and the broccolini is tender, 6–10 minutes. Season with salt and pepper."]],"h":[]},"7516891":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a non-stick frying pan or wok. Trim any fat from the steak, cut into thin strips and add to the pan."],[null,"Stir-fry for 1–2 minutes to seal, add the garlic, peppers, broccoli florets and spring onions, along with 2 tbsp water."],[null,"Stir fry for 3 minutes, add the pak choi, water chestnuts and oyster sauce. Allow to heat through thoroughly and serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"You could use chicken in place of beef."],[null,"For a veggie version, use firm tofu cut into strips. Fry for 3–4 mins each side then remove from the pan, cook the rest of the ingredients, add the tofu back, mix well and serve."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"4687871":{"s":[[null,"In a large saucepan, bring water to a boil. Add orzo and cook according to instructions on package (approximately 8 minutes). Drain and rinse with cold water. Set aside in a salad bowl."],[null,"Cook beans in boiling water for 3–5 minutes. Drain and rinse under cold water to stop the cooking process. The beans should still be crisp."],[null,"Heat the barbecue or grill pan on the stove on medium heat."],[null,"Rub chicken breasts with olive oil and sprinkle with spices. Grill the chicken until it reaches an internal temperature of 165°F (approximately 7–10 minutes per side). Cut chicken in slices."],[null,"To make the vinaigrette, whisk together the shallots, mustard, syrup, lemon juice and olive oil."],[null,"To assemble the salad, pour vinaigrette over the cooked orzo. Add the green beans, dill, and red pepper. Mix together. Fan sliced chicken on top of the salad and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Try adding another protein to the salad, such as sliced steak or a hard-boiled egg."],[null,"This salad is just as tasty as a vegetarian dish. It makes a great side dish for your grilled meats or fish."]]},"5745564":{"s":[[null,"Place the orzo into a pan, add 400ml of low salt vegetable stock and bring to the boil. Cook until the orzo is soft."],[null,"Turn off the heat and place the peas into the orzo. Allow to cook until warmed through."],[null,"Stir in the lemon juice and cheddar until the cheese melts."],[null,"Serve and enjoy."]],"h":[["Renastep note","Always check with your dietitian or doctor that this recipe is suitable for you."],["Renastep note","This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutritics dietary analysis software. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information."]]},"6468122":{"s":[[null,"Bring a large pot of water to a boil over high heat. Add 1/4 tsp salt and reduce heat to medium."],[null,"Add orzo and stir. Cook orzo until tender, but still al dente. Drain orzo when done and return to pot."],[null,"Meanwhile, bring a medium-size pot of water to a boil over high heat. Add asparagus and cook until tender (about 5 minutes), then drain."],[null,"Add asparagus, artichoke hearts, lemon juice, lemon zest, additional 1/4 tsp salt (if desired), freshly ground pepper, and olive oil into the pot with the orzo and stir."],[null,"Taste and adjust seasoning, if necessary. Garnish with cheese and serve hot."]],"h":[]},"6695161":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350 degrees F. Combine all sauce ingredients in a small saucepan and simmer for 15 minutes over medium-low heat, stirring occasionally."],[null,"Place chicken in a 9x13-inch baking dish coated with cooking spray. Cover chicken evenly with 1 cup barbecue sauce."],[null,"Back for 20-25 minutes, baste with remaining sauce, and cook another 5-10 minutes (or until chicken is tender and reaches internal temperature of 165 degrees F)."]],"h":[]},"6743498":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400ºF. Line a small baking pan with foil. Spray the foil with nonstick spray."],[null,"Place the plantains slices in one layer on the baking pan and spray the tops with nonstick spray. Bake until softened, about 12 minutes."],[null,"Turn the slices, spray with nonstick spray, and bake until the plantains are tender, about 6 minutes longer."]],"h":[]},"9360305":{"s":[[null,"Add all 3 base ingredients to an airtight container or mason jar and mix well or shake vigorously. Refrigerate overnight or 6 hours."],[null,"Enjoy topped with fresh fruit, chopped nuts, shredded coconut or granola."]],"h":[[null,"Feel free to double, triple, or quadruple the recipe , as needed. I like to make a large batch and divide into small containers or jars to have ready made breakfasts or snacks for a few days. For best results, re-stir or shake your pudding 10-15 minutes after refrigerating to break up any clumps of seeds, and get the best texture. If your pudding is not as thick as you’d like, add more chia seeds and let sit in the fridge a bit longer. If you don’t like the texture of chia pudding, you may blend the pudding in a high speed blender which will give you a more traditional pudding texture, as opposed to a tapioca type texture. The basic chia pudding recipe keeps refrigerated for 4-5 days. Check out all 10 flavour options in the post above!"]]},"4390197":{"s":[[null,"In a glass or plastic container, combine all ingredients. Cover with a lid or plastic wrap and place in the fridge for a minimum of 2 hours or overnight."]],"h":[[null,"Overnight oats should remain in the refrigerator. It should be consumed within 3-4 days. We recommend you make a few servings to keep on-hand for a quick snack or breakfast."],["Ready to eat breakfast cereals — what to buy?","On a busy morning, it can be difficult to squeeze in time for breakfast, but one must do what they can to avoid skipping this very important meal. There are many quick and healthy options to consider when following a kidney-friendly diet. Ready to eat cereals such as puffed wheat, puffed rice, shredded wheat, corn flakes, crispy rice, and Special K™are all great options. Hot cereals such as oatmeal, cream of wheat, and cream of rice can be prepared in advance, placed in the refrigerator, and quickly reheated in the microwave when needed. Oats can also be used in a chilled recipe such as these overnight oats so that they are prepared and ready to eat. Ready to eat cereals require milk, which is a rich source of potassium. If following a low-potassium diet, use limited amounts of milk to lower the amount of potassium added to your cereal or consider using a non-dairy option such as unenriched rice or almond beverage, which contains very little potassium. These non-dairy options are also lower in protein, which can be beneficial for those with chronic kidney disease not requiring dialysis."]]},"3043":{"s":[[null,"Dice the pear half."],[null,"Combine all ingredients in a mason jar and stir well. Refrigerate overnight."],[null,"Ready to eat the next day. You can take your breakfast on-the-go. Heating is not necessary. Add sweetener if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Prepare a few jars at a time for quick breakfasts all week."],[null,"If you desire a crunchy texture use fresh pears and add them in the morning. Instead of fresh pears you can substitute a fruit cup of diced pears (drained) or other low potassium fruits such as apple, berries, cherries or peach."],[null,"The soaking of the oats overnight acts as “cooking”. If warm oatmeal is preferred microwave the jar for 1-2 minutes before eating."]]},"1994":{"s":[[null,"Chop bell peppers and jalapeno pepper, Dice onion and finely chop celery. Peel potato and cut into small cubes."],[null,"In a large stock pot, under a medium heat, mix together olive oil, flour, and bouillon cubes. Fill pot 3/4 full of water. Add peppers and bring to a boil. Add oxtail and vinegar. Cover and cook until oxtails are tender and liquid reduces (about 1 to 1-1/2 hours)."],[null,"Add black pepper and a dash of Mrs. Dash herb seasoning blend."],[null,"Place potato cubes in a medium saucepan, cover with water and boil for 8 minutes; drain. (This process removes some potassium from the potato.)"],[null,"Add onion, celery, boiled potato and frozen vegetables. Cover and let cook until vegetables are tender."]],"h":[[null,"Small ends ox tails preferred with fat trimmed."],[null,"Enjoy Oxtail Soup as a main course for lunch or dinner by adding a piece of cornbread and peach cobbler for dessert."]]},"54947":{"s":[[null,"Soak the rice noodles by placing them in a shallow pan and cover with boiling water for 4-7 minutes, stirring occasionally until al dente; drain, rinse with cold water."],[null,"Finely chop onion and roughly chop garlic. Whisk the two eggs in a bowl with a fork and set aside. Make the Pad Thai Sauce: whisk fish sauce, rice vinegar, brown sugar and coconut aminos in a small bowl. Set aside."],[null,"Slice chicken into very thin strips. (If using tofu: Blot tofu with paper towels pressing down firmly. Cut tofu into ¾ inch cubes, and for extra crispy tofu, dredge in a little corn starch. If using shrimp: Pat dry with paper towel.)"],[null,"Heat 1 tablespoon oil in a large saucepan or wok, over medium-high heat. Sear the seasoned chicken (If using shrimp or tofu cook the same until cooked through.) Set aside."],[null,"Heat a little more oil in the wok or large skillet over medium heat, add onion & garlic and sauté for 2-3 minutes. Scoot the onion mixture to the side, add more oil, and pour in the eggs. Scramble and break them apart into little bits and move them to the side. Add more oil, and the noodles, sauté 2-3 minutes until the noodles are soft and pliable and even a little crispy."],[null,"Add Pad Thai Sauce and stir everything together and cook 1-2 minutes, then add the cooked chicken (shrimp or tofu) and sauté until warm. Squeeze with a little lime juice. Turn off heat."],[null,"Toss in 1/2 the bean sprouts. Give one more toss and serve immediately. Divide between two plates. May add chili flake and/or scallions as an optional topping."]],"h":[[null,"Coconut aminos vary in sodium, choose the lowest you can find. Cut back noodles and use a sugar substitute in place of brown sugar to make this more diabetes friendly."],[null,"This dish is a bit higher in sodium but is about ½ of a take-out Pad Thai meal, which can reach around 1300 mg of sodium."]]},"7700186":{"s":[[null,"Cook the noodles according to the packet instructions, around 3-5 minutes. Plunge them into cold water, drain and reserve."],[null,"Heat the oil in a large pan or wok. Add the spring onions and stir-fry for 3 minutes. Add the garlic, ginger and chilli and stir-fry for another 2 minutes."],[null,"Add the red pepper and courgette, stir-fry for another minute add the broad beans and pak choy. Stir-fry for 1 minute."],[null,"Add the noodles, stir-fry for 2 minutes and add the beansprouts, pineapple, soy sauce and lime juice. Stir-fry for a further 2 minutes and add the coriander."],[null,"Put into a bowl, top with the peanuts and lime wedges."]],"h":[[null,"For a side dish, cut half a cucumber into ribbons with a vegetable peeler and add fresh coriander leaves and a squeeze of lime."],[null,"To add more protein to this dish, use soya beans in place of broad beans or add some tofu."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"6094992":{"s":[[null,"Cut spaghetti squash in half lengthwise and remove seeds. Place squash in a microwave-safe baking dish, cut side down. Cover loosely with a lid and leave room to vent. Microwave for 10-15 minutes, rotating every 5 minutes. Squash is done when it’s soft to touch. Set aside."],[null,"Heat olive oil in a large sauté pan over medium-high heat. Add scallions, carrots, zucchini and mushrooms and sauté for 5-7 minutes. Add garlic and sauté for 30 seconds. Add ginger and Pad Thai sauce and heat for 2 minutes. Mix well."],[null,"Use a fork to scoop out spaghetti squash. Add the spaghetti squash “noodles” and shrimp to the pan with vegetables. Heat for another 2 minutes and mix well. Top with chopped cilantro."]],"h":[]},"3513":{"s":[[null,"Thaw the shrimp. Cut chicken breast into bite-sized cubes. Chop the green pepper."],[null,"Heat olive oil in a 12-inch skillet over medium heat. Add rice and cook for 30 seconds, stirring constantly."],[null,"Stir in the stock, salsa, green pepper and turmeric and heat to a boil. Reduce the heat to low. Cover the skillet and cook for 15 minutes."],[null,"Stir in the shrimp and chicken. Cover skillet and cook for 5 minutes or until the rice is tender and most of the liquid is absorbed."]],"h":[[null,"Buy frozen, precooked shrimp that has been peeled and deveined."],[null,"Compare salsa brands and select the lowest sodium product."]]},"6226195":{"s":[[null,"Mix chickpea flour, turmeric, chili powder, cumin, and salt in a bowl. Gradually whisk in water until the batter is smooth."],[null,"Fold in onion, carrot, and cilantro."],[null,"Heat a non-stick pan with 1/4 tsp oil over medium heat. Pour 1/4 cup of batter and spread into a thin pancake. Cook for 2–3 minutes on each side. Repeat with remaining batter."],[null,"Serve hot with a side of low-fat Greek yogurt."]],"h":[]},"3897":{"s":[[null,"Chop onion, chilies and curry leaves. Add salt and baking soda and mix well."],[null,"Mix chickpea flour, rice flour and melted margarine."],[null,"Combine all ingredients (except oil) and mix to the consistency of a loose dough by gradually adding small amounts of water as needed. (You may need up to 2 tablespoons water. Adjust as needed.)"],[null,"Heat the oil. Transfer small amounts of the dough into the oil. Cook until crisp and brown."]],"h":[[null,"Chickpea flour is also called gram flour."],[null,"Reduce salt to 1/4 teaspoon or omit completely for a lower sodium snack."]]},"1812":{"s":[[null,"To make filling place cottage cheese into a cheese cloth and twist into a ball. Place in a colander, place colander into a mixing bowl, and refrigerate for safety. Allow liquid to drain for at least two hours."],[null,"Mix flour, 1 tablespoon sugar and salt."],[null,"In a separate bowl beat eggs lightly and add the non-dairy creamer."],[null,"Combine flour mixture and egg mixture and whisk until it is a smooth, thin batter. Allow batter to rest for an hour."],[null,"Heat an 8″ omelet pan and spray with non-stick cooking spray."],[null,"Pour 1/4 cup batter onto hot pan and flip when bubbles appear in the center."],[null,"Stack the pancakes onto a dinner plate and keep in a warm oven until ready to assemble."],[null,"Mix drained cottage cheese with raisins, 5 tablespoons sugar and vanilla."],[null,"Fill each palacsinta with 1/4 cup filling and roll it up. Dust with powdered sugar and serve."]],"h":[[null,"This is Anne’s family recipe, modified to be more heart-healthy. Traditional Palacsinta are prepared with a filling of cottage or pot cheese, sugar, and raisins; however, this is not the most renal-friendly filling due to the sodium in cottage cheese. Other fillings such as apple, cheery, or blueberry pie filling are excellent alternatives. Look for no-sugar-added pie fillings if you have diabetes."],[null,"Compare brands and buy the lowest sodium cottage cheese without phosphate additives."],[null,"Alter the sugar to your taste. Splenda® or other sugar substitute may be used to replace the sugar to reduce carbohydrate to 16 grams."]]},"1002829":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F. Coat a 9” x 5” x 3” loaf pan with cooking spray and dust with flour."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine flour and baking powder."],[null,"In another bowl, mix oil, 2/3 cup sugar, extract and egg whites."],[null,"Add the oil mixture to the flour mixture, alternating with milk. Beat just until mixed; do not overbeat."],[null,"Fold in blueberries and lemon zest."],[null,"Pour batter into loaf pan and bake for 40-50 minutes or until a toothpick inserted comes out clean."],[null,"Prepare the glaze while the bread is baking. In a small saucepan, combine sugar and lemon juice. Heat until sugar dissolves."],[null,"Once you remove the bread from the oven, poke holes in the top at 1” intervals and pour the lemon glaze over the bread."]],"h":[[null,"People with diabetes can make one or more of the following changes:"],[null,"Omit the lemon glaze and reduce the portion to 1/2 slice."],[null,"Substitute Splenda® sugar substitute for the sugar. Nutrition content changes to 154 calories and 17 grams carbohydrate per slice; other nutrients stay the same."],[null,"Counts as 1/2 starch, 1/2 fruit, low potassium, 1 fat and 1 carbohydrate choice."]]},"3296":{"s":[[null,"Slice the tofu into 4 rectangle slices. Pat each piece dry with a paper towel."],[null,"Heat a frying pan with 2 tablespoons of vegetable oil on high heat."],[null,"Add the tofu and reduce to low-medium heat for 5 to 7 minutes or until golden brown."],[null,"Once the bottom of each piece is golden brown, turn it over and cook for another 5 to 7 minutes or until golden brown."],[null,"To make the dipping sauce mince the garlic and chop the green onion. Combine minced garlic, chopped green onion, sugar or honey, reduced-sodium soy sauce, sesame oil and hot pepper flakes (optional) in a small mixing bowl."]],"h":[[null,"Be cautious with reduced-sodium soy sauce, it does still contain high amounts of sodium."],[null,"You may substitute sugar for the honey."],[null,"If you prefer, leave out the hot pepper flakes."]]},"6959709":{"s":[[null,"Whisk together the soy sauce, vinegar, scallion, ginger, apple-apricot sauce, sesame oil, and hot pepper flakes in a small bowl. (Makes 1/2 cup.) Pour into a 9 × 13-inch pan or similar-size dish."],[null,"Cut the tofu lengthwise into 9 slices; then, cut each slice in half lengthwise or crosswise, creating 18 pieces. Place the tofu slices in a single layer in the soy sauce mixture and marinate about 10–15 minutes per side."],[null,"Preheat a grill pan over medium-high heat. Transfer each tofu slice to the pan using tongs, reserving the marinade. Grill (in batches) until deep grill marks form on both sides, about 3 1/2–4 minutes per side."],[null,"Insert reusable or bamboo skewers into the cooked tofu, sprinkle with the sesame seeds and cilantro leaves, and serve while warm with the remaining marinade on the side."]],"h":[]},"6621202":{"s":[[null,"Heat a large, heavy skillet or frying pan over medium-high heat. Add 1–2 tablespoons of olive oil, depending on your preference and the size of your skillet."],[null,"When the oil is hot and shimmering, add the Padron peppers to the skillet. You can leave them whole with the stems on. Let the peppers cook, undisturbed, for about 3–5 minutes or until they start to blister and char. Use tongs to turn them occasionally, so they cook evenly."],[null,"Once the Padron peppers are tender, blistered, and slightly charred, remove them from the skillet and transfer to a serving plate."],[null,"While the peppers are still hot, generously sprinkle them with coarse sea salt."]],"h":[]},"6562027":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the skillet over medium heat. Once the pan is hot, add 1 tsp oil and swirl to coat the bottom. Add veggies and 1/4 tsp black pepper; cook, stirring occasionally, until starting to soften, 3–4 minutes."],[null,"Add rice and spinach to the skillet and cook, stirring occasionally, until the rice is warmed through and spinach has wilted, 2–3 minutes. Cover and set aside."],[null,"Preheat another medium skillet over medium-high heat."],[null,"While the skillet heats up, pat fillets dry with paper towels and place skin-side down on a plate; season the top side with 1/4 tsp garlic powder and 1/4 tsp black pepper."],[null,"Once the skillet is hot, add 1 tsp oil and swirl to coat the bottom. Add salmon, skin-side down, and cook, flipping once, until skin is crispy and flesh is opaque, 3–4 minutes per side. Transfer to a clean plate and loosely cover with aluminum foil. (Reserve skillet for next step)."],[null,"Wipe the skillet clean with paper towels and return to medium-high heat; add remaining 1 tsp oil and swirl to coat the bottom. Add mushrooms and 2 garlic cloves; cook, stirring occasionally, until softened, 4–5 minutes."],[null,"Add soy sauce to the skillet and continue to cook until the liquid has evaporated, 1–2 minutes more; remove from heat."],[null,"To serve, divide rice, salmon, and mushrooms between plates."]],"h":[]},"3682":{"s":[[null,"Combined the spices to make a rub mix."],[null,"Rinse the chicken breasts, pat dry, and brush lightly with oil."],[null,"Rub the chicken breasts with spice rub mix."],[null,"Refrigerate the chicken breast for 3 to 4 hours."],[null,"Preheat oven to 400º F."],[null,"To set up a smoke-roasting pan, place hardwood chips in a disposable foil pan and set a rack on top. Heat the pan over stovetop burner on medium-high until the smoke appears. Place the marinated chicken breasts on the rack and cover the pan tightly with foil."],[null,"Reduce heat to medium and smoke the chicken breast for 10 minutes."],[null,"Transfer the chicken breasts to a baking pan and roast in the oven for 10 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Serve with white rice and Stir-Fry Vegetables."],[null,"Select chicken breasts that weigh approximately 4 ounces each uncooked."],[null,"Adjust the portion to match your meal plan if you are on a lower or higher protein diet."]]},"2738":{"s":[[null,"Make sour milk: add 1 tablespoon vinegar to 2 cups milk. Let sit for about 5 minutes until soured."],[null,"Sift flour; add baking soda, salt and sugar."],[null,"Beat eggs with mixer until fluffy. Combine with “sour” milk and oil."],[null,"Add dry ingredients and beat until smooth."],[null,"Cook on a hot griddle or heated frying pan, greased with nonstick cooking spray until bubbly. Turn only once for fluffy, light pancakes."]],"h":[[null,"Sour milk is used instead of buttermilk, which is higher in sodium."],[null,"The griddle must be hot. It is hot enough if a drop of batter sizzles."],[null,"Pour 1/4 cup batter for medium-sized pancake. Recipe makes 18 pancakes."],[null,"As soon as bubbles form, flip over."],[null,"This recipe is easy to cut in half. Leftover batter can be stored in sealed container for several days in refrigerator."]]},"5224415":{"s":[[null,"Place the Renastep, egg, plain flour and vanilla extract into a bowl and mix thoroughly."],[null,"Heat a frying pan or crepe pan on a medium heat and add 1 tsp of sunflower oil to the pan."],[null,"When heated, pour ₁⁄₃ of the batter into the pan and cook for 1-2 minutes on each side until golden."],[null,"Repeat this step until all of the batter is used."]],"h":[[null,"Serve with lemon and sugar or maple syrup."],["Renastep note","Renastep is a Food for Special Medical Purposes and must be used under medical supervision."],["Renastep note","Renastep is a ready to use feed for the dietary management of kidney disease from 3 years of age onwards. Renastep contains milk and fish. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information."],["Renastep note","This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease."]]},"7848709":{"s":[[null,"Beat together all the ingredients in a bowl."],[null,"Heat a medium non-stick pan and brush with a little oil."],[null,"Stir the batter mixture before adding a ladleful to the pan – tip the pan so the mixture covers the base. Cook for 1–2 minutes on each side until golden."],[null,"Repeat until the mixture has been used up (each time, stir the batter before adding it to the pan). Turn out onto a plate and serve with fruit."]],"h":[[null,"To keep pancakes warm, put a plate on top of a gently simmering saucepan of water and stack the pancakes on top as you make them."],[null,"These pancakes are also good with savoury fillings. Try leek and mushrooms with a cheesy sauce or ratatouille."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Freeze in individually wrapped portions with greaseproof paper between each crepe. Defrost for 1 hour, or in the microwave."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"1913":{"s":[[null,"Mince garlic and dice onion. Shred carrots and cabbage and diagonally cut celery. Rinely chop green onions."],[null,"In a wok or large skillet, over medium heat, sauté garlic and onion in olive oil until soft."],[null,"Stir in chicken, shrimp and soy sauce. Add 3 cups chicken broth and bring to boil."],[null,"Add noodles using 2 wooden spoons to stir in noodles. Cook for 15 minutes until noodles are translucent. Be careful that noodles don’t become gummy. May need to add more broth (or water) to prevent this from happening."],[null,"Add vegetables and cook until cabbage begins to soften."],[null,"Transfer pancit to a serving dish and garnish with sliced eggs, green onions and one lemon sliced into wedges."],[null,"Squeeze the juice of one lemon over top of noodles before serving. Serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"Use sesame oil instead of olive oil if desired."],[null,"You can use a mixture of chicken and shrimp."],[null,"Rice noodles, also known as rice sticks, may be purchased at any Asian grocery store. Excellent® brand is a good choice."],[null,"Shred the cabbage and carrots in a food processor or buy the pre-shredded slaw mix."],[null,"Use a large wok or very large Dutch oven."]]},"7972804":{"s":[[null,"Heat the almond milk until it just comes to the boil. Sprinkle over the agar agar and simmer for 2 minutes, stirring continuously."],[null,"Remove the vanilla pod and scrape out the seeds using a sharp knife. Whisk in the vanilla seeds, 2tbsp sweetener and buttermilk until smooth."],[null,"Divide equally between 4 glasses. Alternatively, use 4 x 175ml ramekins, lightly sprayed with low-calorie spray if you want to turn these desserts out. Chill for 2 hours until set or ready to serve."],[null,"Place the lemon rind and juice, 2tbsp water, strawberries, raspberries and blueberries into a small saucepan with the remaining sweetener and heat gently for 2–3 minutes to warm through. Allow to cool."],[null,"Once the panna cottas are set, either spoon the fruit compote into the glasses and scatter with the pistachio nuts. If using ramekins, dip the base of each dish into warm water for 20–30 seconds and turn over onto a plate to release the puddings. Serve with the compote and nuts."]],"h":[[null,"If you use fortified almond milk, this is high in calcium, which is important for maintaining healthy teeth and bones."],[null,"Berries a good source of vitamin C."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6949633":{"s":[[null,"In a bowl, mix the almond flour, coconut flour, baking powder and salt."],[null,"In a separate container, beat the eggs and add the almond milk, 1 tablespoon of olive oil, the maple syrup and the vanilla extract. Mix well."],[null,"Pour the wet ingredients into the dry ingredients and stir until combined. Let the batter rest for a couple of minutes to thicken."],[null,"Heat a skillet or griddle over medium heat and grease with 1 teaspoon of olive oil or cooking spray."],[null,"Pour ¼ cup of batter into the skillet for each pancake. Spread the batter slightly with the back of a spoon."],[null,"Cook until bubbles form on the surface, then flip and cook until the other side is golden."],[null,"Repeat with the remaining batter."]],"h":[]},"6860841":{"s":[[null,"Fill a soup pot with water and bring the water to a boil."],[null,"Using a vegetable peeler, peel thin strips of each vegetable (zucchini and carrot) to make wide “noodles.” You should end up with about 5 cups of vegetable ‘noodles’. Take care to avoid the seeds in the zucchini."],[null,"Boil the vegetable “noodles” for 2-4 minutes or until just softened. Drain and lay out in a single layer on a baking sheet to dry."],[null,"In a medium nonstick sauté pan, add the olive oil over medium-low heat."],[null,"Sauté the turkey bacon and onion until the onions begin to soften. Add the garlic and cook for an additional two minutes. Stir in the flour and let it cook for 2 minutes."],[null,"Stir in the milk and cheese and bring to a boil, scraping the bottom of the pan to incorporate all of the flour until thickened."],[null,"Once thickened, add the vegetable “noodles” and toss gently to coat."],[null,"Season with salt (optional) and ground black pepper, and stir in the parsley. Serve immediately."]],"h":[]},"6115515":{"s":[[null,"Combine first 7 ingredients in a food processor and blend until smooth."],[null,"Serve in 6 tall thin glasses and garnish with mint leaves and ground cardamom before serving."]],"h":[]},"7721061":{"s":[[null,"Place the beetroot, carrots and sweet potato in a bowl.&nbsp"],[null,"Add the lemon juice and smoked paprika and mix well, thoroughly coating all of the vegetables."],[null,"Oil a large baking tray with rapeseed oil before laying out the vegetables evenly. Bake at 180C/gas 5 for 30-35 minutes, mixing a couple of times to make sure the vegetables cook evenly."]],"h":[[null,"Try roasting other vegetables like swede, ordinary potatoes, butternut squash or large chunks of onion."],[null,"Just before serving, add a handful of freshly chopped herbs such as coriander, parsley, chives or mint."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"6247707":{"s":[[null,"Shuck corn, and wrap each ear in a damp paper towel."],[null,"Place in ears on a dinner plate, and microwave on high 2 minutes. Turn corn over and microwave on high 1 1/2 minutes."],[null,"Remove paper towel, and rub corn with oil. Sprinkle Parmesan cheese over corn, add salt and pepper to taste, and serve."]],"h":[]},"6992179":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 425 degrees F. Spray a baking sheet with cooking spray."],[null,"In a shallow dish, mix together cornmeal, Parmesan cheese, garlic powder and black pepper."],[null,"In another shallow baking dish, whisk together egg whites."],[null,"Dip chicken breast strip in egg mixture and then drench in cornmeal mixture. Coat well and place on baking sheet. Repeat procedure for all chicken strips."],[null,"Spray chicken strips with cooking spray. Bake 15-20 minutes or until done; turn chicken pieces over halfway through cooking time."]],"h":[]},"6510389":{"s":[[null,"Place the cauliflower florets in a microwave-safe dish and microwave for about 8 minutes, until the cauliflower is soft. Stir halfway through the cooking time."],[null,"Place the cauliflower, yogurt, cheese, garlic powder, and pepper in a food processor or blender and blend until smooth,"],[null,"Top with the onions and serve."]],"h":[]},"7573996":{"s":[[null,"Parboil the parsnips for 5 minutes in a pan of boiling water."],[null,"Drain, then return to the pan and toss in the spread."],[null,"Tip into a roasting tin, sprinkle with the Parmesan cheese and thyme and season well."],[null,"Roast for 25-30 minutes at 200ºC/gas 6 until golden and tender."]],"h":[[null,"You could use this method using sweet potato wedges or carrots instead of parsnips."],[null,"For a vegetarian dish, use a Parmesan alternative or another strong, hard cheese."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6223318":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F."],[null,"In a large bowl, toss cauliflower florets with olive oil, grated Parmesan cheese, garlic powder, dried thyme, salt, and black pepper until well coated."],[null,"Spread the cauliflower in a single layer on a baking sheet."],[null,"Roast in the preheated oven for 25 minutes or until the cauliflower is golden brown and crispy, tossing halfway through."],[null,"Remove the cauliflower from the oven."],[null,"Transfer the cauliflower to a serving dish."],[null,"Serve the cauliflower as a savory and diabetes-friendly side dish."]],"h":[]},"6360930":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F. Line a baking sheet with aluminum foil."],[null,"Slice each tofu block in half along the long side. Place on the baking sheet and drizzle with 1 tsp oil. Bake for 15 minutes, flip, then bake for another 15 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, peel the tough skin from the squash. Use a julienne peeler to cut noodles from the squash."],[null,"Preheat a large skillet over medium heat. Add 1 tsp oil, squash, and ¼ tsp Italian seasoning. Cook, stirring occasionally, until squash noodles are tender, 7–8 minutes. Remove from heat, cover, and set aside."],[null,"Combine the Parmesan, mayo, 1/4 tsp Italian seasoning, onion powder, and garlic powder in a small bowl."],[null,"After the tofu has baked for 30 minutes, remove from the oven. Set the oven to broil on high and move an oven rack to the top shelf, underneath the broiler."],[null,"Spread the cheese mixture over the tops of the tofu. Return to the oven and broil until the topping is bubbly and beginning to brown, 1–2 minutes."],[null,"Serve on a bed of squash noodles with a handful of fresh basil."]],"h":[]},"6489812":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400°F."],[null,"Place the cod filets on a parchment paper lined baking sheet. Lightly drizzle with 1 tbsp oil. Place the baking sheet in the oven and cook until the internal temperature of the fish is 145°F, 8–10 minutes."],[null,"Place the garlic, onion, parsley, cilantro, crushed red pepper, and black pepper in a food processor. Process until finely chopped."],[null,"Add vinegar, lime zest and juice, and 3 tbsp olive oil. Process until smooth and set aside."],[null,"To serve, divide fish between plates and top with chimichurri sauce."]],"h":[]},"6188990":{"s":[[null,"Combine the ricotta and lemon zest and juice in a medium bowl. Stir to combine."],[null,"Add the parsley, dill, green onions, olive oil, salt, and pepper. Stir to combine."],[null,"Chill for an hour before serving."]],"h":[]},"6629246":{"s":[[null,"Place the diced onion in a bowl of cold water for 10 minutes, then drain."],[null,"In a medium bowl, combine the chickpeas, olive oil, lemon zest and juice, parsley, and pepper. Stir to combine."],[null,"Add the drained onions and stir again to combine. Taste and adjust with more lemon, salt, or pepper, if necessary."]],"h":[]},"7426196":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a saucepan, add the onion and the cumin seeds and fry for 2–3 minutes."],[null,"Add the parsnips and apple and continue to fry for 3 minutes."],[null,"Add the stock, bring to the boil and simmer for 20–25 minutes, until the parsnips are tender."],[null,"Transfer to a blender or food processor and whiz until smooth. Season to taste."],[null,"To make the parsnip crisps, peel the parsnip then slice it into very thin crisps using a peeler. Heat the oil in a small frying pan and fry the parsnip strips until crisp and golden then drain on kitchen paper."],[null,"Top the soup with the parsnip crisps and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Spice up the soup with 1 tsp of curry paste."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Freeze in portions then defrost in the fridge, or defrost in a microwave stirring regularly."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"3338":{"s":[[null,"Place soda in a punch bowl or a large mixing bowl."],[null,"Add fruit punch concentrate and stir."],[null,"With an ice cream scoop add sherbet."],[null,"When sherbet starts to melt stir and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Look for frozen fruit punch concentrate, not fruit punch juice."],[null,"Fruit punch already made in jugs, boxes or cartons generally has added phosphorus. Which is why frozen fruit punch concentrate is recommended."]]},"1002846":{"s":[[null,"Peel cherry tomatoes and cut into slices."],[null,"Grate cheese."],[null,"Finely chop onion and cilantro."],[null,"Mix cold cooked pasta with tomato, cheese, onion and cilantro."],[null,"Combine vinegar, olive oil, water and pepper and pour over pasta."],[null,"Heat over low heat for 3 minutes and serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"Use whole wheat pasta for more fiber."]]},"9405296":{"s":[[null,"Bring a large pot of generously salted water to boil and add your pasta, cooking according to package directions for al dente pasta. Add the broccoli to the pot when there are 8 minutes left to cook your pasta so the broccoli does not overcook. *See notes* Drain pasta and broccoli once cooked, reserving 1/4 cup of the pasta water."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the olive oil, garlic and peppers to a large skillet and sauté over medium heat until peppers and garlic are slightly browned, approx. 5 minutes. Add the reserved pasta water, your pasta and broccoli to the pan. Sauté everything together, constantly mixing for 1-2 minutes."],[null,"Serve with extra chili flakes or Vegan Parmesan Cheese if desired."]],"h":[[null,"If your pasta requires 13 minutes to cook, add the pasta to the boiling water and cook for 5 minutes, then add the broccoli to cook for the remaining 8 minutes."]]},"7482026":{"s":[[null,"Cook the pasta according to the pack instructions, adding the peas and sweetcorn."],[null,"Two minutes before the end of the cooking time, drain. Meanwhile, place the spread, flour and milk in a saucepan and cook over a medium heat, whisking continuously, until the sauce has thickened."],[null,"Stir through the Cheddar cheese. Season to taste, add to the pasta and vegetables, toss and serve."],[null,"Or, if you prefer, pop under the grill for a few minutes to brown the top."]],"h":[[null,"Try adding some sautéed mushrooms or red pepper to boost the veggie content."],[null,"You could try using goat's cheese instead of Cheddar."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"7905259":{"s":[[null,"Place the onion, pepper, garlic and mince in a non-stick frying pan and fry for 5 minutes until the minced is browned and the onions are beginning to soften. Add the tomatoes, tomato purée, chilli powder and paprika to the pan, bring to the boil, cover and simmer for 10 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, cook the pasta according to pack instructions."],[null,"Stir the kidney beans and parsley into the pasta heat through. Transfer to an ovenproof dish. Mix together the breadcrumbs and Parmesan cheese and sprinkle over the pasta."],[null,"Place the dish under a preheated grill for 1-2 minutes until golden."]],"h":[[null,"To create a TexMex flavour, add 1 level tsp each of ground cumin and dried oregano."],[null,"You could also stuff this chilli mixture into halved peppers, top with crumbled Cheddar cheese and bake for 20 minutes."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"6847213":{"s":[[null,"Bring a large pot of water to a boil. Add the baby spinach to the pot and blanch for 1 minute. Use a slotted spoon to remove the spinach and place it in a bowl of ice water. Add the packed parsley and basil to the pot and blanch for 15 seconds. Remove and add to the bowl of ice water. Drain the water and squeeze as much liquid as possible from the greens."],[null,"Add the spinach, parsley and basil to a food processor. Add the half-and-half to the food processor and puree. Set aside."],[null,"Heat a saucepan over medium heat. Add 2 tablespoons of olive oil, garlic and onion powder. Add the flour and whisk for 1 minute. Add the milk and whisk until smooth."],[null,"Add the cheese, Italian seasoning, salt (optional) and pepper. Stir until the sauce thickens."],[null,"Add the vegetable puree and stir to combine."],[null,"Meanwhile, heat a large skillet over medium heat. Add the remaining olive oil. Cook the chicken for 3-4 minutes on each side, until browned and cooked through."],[null,"To serve, divide the chicken and pasta among plates. Top with sauce, parmesan cheese and fresh basil strips."]],"h":[]},"9564162":{"s":[[null,"Heat a deep sauté pan over medium heat on your stovetop. Then add 1/4 cup of the broth, the chopped onion, garlic, and red pepper flakes. Sauté until softened, approx. 5 minutes, stirring often."],[null,"Then add the remaining 3 cups of broth, the peas, pasta, and the vegan cheese to the same pan. Cover it with a lid, maintain a gentle simmer, and stir often, until the pasta is cooked al dente. Remove the lid in the last few minutes of cooking so that most of the liquid absorbs. (Unless you prefer it soupy, in which case, keep the lid on for the entire cooking process.)"],[null,"Serve garnished with fresh basil, black pepper, and/or more vegan parmesan cheese if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Cook your pasta al dente. Do not overcook! Al dente means that the pasta is still firm once cooked, giving optimal texture in every bite. To ensure it does not overcook, start taste testing a few minutes before the package says it will be ready. It should be tender, but still firm."],[null,"Taste the pasta once cooked and add salt and black pepper, if needed. This will vary according to the saltiness of the broth you use."],[null,"Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-4 days. Reheat on the stovetop with a splash of water or broth to loosen, as required."]]},"6632676":{"s":[[null,"Coat a large soup pot with cooking spray over high heat. Add bacon and sauté until crisp."],[null,"Reduce heat to medium and add onion, garlic, celery, and carrots. Sauté about 5-7 minutes or until vegetables begin to brown. Add broth and simmer for 5 minutes."],[null,"Stir in beans, tomatoes, parsley, basil, and pepper and simmer for 10 minutes. Add the pasta and continue to simmer for 10-15 minutes or until pasta is al dente."],[null,"Serve soup in a bowl sprinkled with Parmesan cheese."]],"h":[]},"6112072":{"s":[[null,"In a large pot, heat the olive oil over medium heat. Add the diced onion, carrots, and celery. Sauté until the vegetables are softened, about 5 minutes."],[null,"Add the minced garlic to the pot and sauté for an additional 1–2 minutes until fragrant."],[null,"Pour in the vegetable broth, diced tomatoes, cannellini beans, dried oregano, dried basil, dried thyme, coarse salt, and pepper. Bring the mixture to a boil, then reduce heat and let it simmer for 15 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, cook the shell pasta according to package instructions. Drain and set aside."],[null,"Add the chopped spinach to the pot and cook until wilted."],[null,"Stir in the cooked pasta. Simmer for an additional 5 minutes to let the flavors meld. Top with fresh grated parmesan if desired."]],"h":[]},"7520378":{"s":[[null,"Add the pasta to a pan of boiling water, cook for 8 minutes, then drain."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the olive oil to a pan and mix in the onion, yellow pepper and carrot. Stir regularly for 5 minutes, until starting to brown."],[null,"Add the stock and oregano, bring to the boil, then reduce the heat and add the endamame beans and cabbage. Bring back to a gentle boil, stirring regularly for 2 minutes."],[null,"Add the pasta, bring back again to a gentle boil, then remove from the heat."],[null,"Divide into two bowls and add a blob of pesto to each. To serve, sprinkle with plenty of black pepper and a little parmesan cheese."]],"h":[[null,"This is great for using up any dried, broken-up pasta and almost any vegetables."],[null,"Choose reduced-salt stock to lower the salt in this dish, or make your own."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Then defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"3030":{"s":[[null,"Cook pasta and vegetables in separate pots according to package directions, but omitting salt. Drain."],[null,"Pour low-sodium chicken broth in a medium-sized stockpot and heat on low heat."],[null,"Add flour to broth whisking vigorously to avoid clumps from forming."],[null,"Add half and half and garlic powder and stir."],[null,"Simmer on low heat for 5 to 10 minutes until mixture thickens slightly. Stir occasionally while simmering."],[null,"Add cooked vegetables and pasta. Cook until heated through."],[null,"Sprinkle with Parmesan cheese and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Frozen vegetable mixtures vary in potassium content. Choose a mixture with lower potassium vegetables or ask your dietitian to recommend the best choices for your diet if you are limiting potassium."],[null,"12 ounces uncooked pasta equals approximately 6 cups cooked pasta."]]},"6217481":{"s":[[null,"Heat olive oil in a large sauté pan over medium heat. Add onion and peppers and sauté for 3 minutes. Stir in garlic and cook for another minute."],[null,"Add broccoli, carrots, asparagus, zucchini, basil, oregano, and pepper and sauté for 1 minute, until the spices are fragrant."],[null,"Add the vegetable broth and tomatoes. Cook for 5–7 minutes, until the liquid is reduced by half. Stir in the cannellini beans and keep warm."],[null,"While the vegetables are cooking, boil the pasta following the package instructions, until al dente. Drain and mix into the vegetable mixture."],[null,"Serve with shaved parmesan cheese if desired."]],"h":[]},"3611":{"s":[[null,"Finely mince onion, shred carrots, cut broccoli florets into small pieces, dice cucumber and chop bell pepper."],[null,"Combine vinegar, oil, garlic powder, pepper, oregano, celery seed and onion to make dressing. Set aside."],[null,"Cook pasta al dente; do not overcook."],[null,"Drain and rinse pasta. Toss with enough dressing to coat."],[null,"Add parmesan cheese to pasta and refrigerate for at least 12 hours."],[null,"Two hours before serving, add the remaining vegetables, Mrs. Dash® and paprika, and toss. Add more dressing if needed or desired."],[null,"Refrigerate until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"It’s important to refrigerate the Pasta Salad for a minimum of 12 (but no more than 24) hours before serving to allow the seasonings time to infuse into the pasta."],[null,"The amount of dressing and paprika used in this recipe is a matter of personal preference. Analysis includes all the dressing."]]},"5445414":{"s":[[null,"Boil the pasta until fully cooked, rinse with cold water and set aside to cool."],[null,"In a large bowl mix together pasta, cucumber and feta."],[null,"Whisk together olive oil and lemon juice until emulsified."],[null,"Pour over the pasta mix and mix until thoroughly coated."],[null,"Serve and enjoy!"]],"h":[["Renastep note","Always check with your dietitian or doctor that this recipe is suitable for you."],["Renastep note","This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutritics dietary analysis software. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information."]]},"7982558":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200°C/gas 6."],[null,"Place the aubergine, courgettes, garlic and chilli (if using) into an ovenproof dish, drizzle over the oil and vinegar and cook for 30–40 minutes until the vegetables are tender and beginning to char."],[null,"Meanwhile, cook the pasta according to the pack instructions. Drain."],[null,"Toss through the pasta with the pine nuts and ricotta cheese, then sprinkle over the basil and serve."]],"h":[[null,"If you can’t get ricotta cheese, you could use reduced-fat cream cheese or goat's cheese."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"3714":{"s":[[null,"Wash cauliflower and cut into bite-sized pieces. Finely chop onion and mince garlic."],[null,"Heat olive oil in a large pot over medium heat. Add onion and garlic and sauté for about 5 minutes until onion is transparent."],[null,"Add cauliflower, black and red pepper and sauté for 5 minutes."],[null,"Add chicken broth and bring to a boil. Reduce heat to simmer and allow cauliflower to cook until tender."],[null,"Cook linguine according to package directions, omitting salt. Drain and return to the pot used to cook it. Add several spoonfuls of the broth from cauliflower mixture to linguine and toss to prevent sticking."],[null,"Divide linguine into 8 individual servings and top with cauliflower and broth."],[null,"Add 1 tablespoon grated Parmesan cheese and more black and red pepper to taste. Chop parsley and garnish each serving evenly."]],"h":[[null,"Limit Parmesan cheese to 1 tablespoon per portion to keep phosphorus low."]]},"7735462":{"s":[[null,"Heat half of the oil in a non-stick pan, add the onion and garlic and fry for 4-5 minutes until softened."],[null,"Add the paprika, tomatoes and stock, bring to the boil and simmer for 15 minutes. Season with plenty of black pepper, transfer to a blender or food processor and blend until smooth."],[null,"Meanwhile, cook the potatoes in boiling water for 7-8 minutes, until just tender."],[null,"Drain and toss in the remaining oil. Place on a baking sheet and cook under a hot grill for 5-6 minutes until golden brown all over."],[null,"Serve the potatoes with the tomato sauce."]],"h":[[null,"Smoked paprika adds a wonderful flavour to dishes, you can get mild (dulse) or hot (picante) depending on how bravas you are!"],[null,"Often served as tapas, these potatoes are a great side dish served with a grilled piece of salmon or tuna and salad."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"3663":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 300º F. Set egg whites out to bring to room temperature. Slice the strawberries and set aside."],[null,"Beat egg whites with salt at high speed until soft peaks form. Add 2 cups of the sugar, 1 tablespoon at a time, beating well after each addition. Gently fold in vinegar and 1-1/2 teaspoons vanilla."],[null,"Smooth mixture into an 8” round, ungreased cookie sheet or pizza pan. Smooth top."],[null,"Bake for 45 minutes. Turn off oven and let shell set for 1 hour with oven door shut. Remove from oven and let cool completely."],[null,"For the whipped cream, place bowl and whisk in the freezer for 10-15 minutes. Put sugar, heavy whipping cream, and remaining 1 teaspoon vanilla into bowl and whip until stiff. (Can be done with a hand mixer, stand mixer, or by hand.)"],[null,"Fill Pavlova shell with whipped topping and sliced berries on top."]],"h":[[null,"When beating egg whites, start on low to medium speed until half whipped. At this point add pinch of salt or cream of tartar and increase mixer to high speed. The result is whipped whites that are more stable and take less time to whip."],[null,"Not recommended for people with diabetes due to high carbohydrate content."]]},"5647740":{"s":[[null,"Cut the courgettes into small chunks."],[null,"Boil the courgette for 5 minutes."],[null,"Add frozen peas and boil for a further 3-4 minutes."],[null,"Drain vegetables and cool."],[null,"Add 100ml breast milk, standard infant formula or a specialised low potassium, low phosphate feed (as advised by your dietitian)."],[null,"Use a blender to whizz up to a purée consistency."],[null,"Add more breast milk, standard infant formula or the specialised low potassium, low phosphate feed if a thinner consistency is required."],[null,"Add into ice cube trays and freeze or use straight away."]],"h":[]},"6174921":{"s":[[null,"Add the lime juice, jalapeno, salt, and pepper to a medium bowl. Whisk in the oil until well combined. Stir in the peach, scallions and oregano until combined. Stir in the beans and adjust seasoning."],[null,"Arrange the tortilla chips on a platter around a bowl of the salsa, and serve at room temperature. Alternatively, serve individual portions of salsa with the chips."]],"h":[]},"6399914":{"s":[[null,"In a blender, combine the peaches, ginger, maple syrup, and fresh lemon juice."],[null,"Blend the mixture until it becomes a smooth purée."],[null,"Pour the peach and ginger purée in an even layer into a shallow freezer-safe pan."],[null,"Place the dish in the freezer and let it set for about 1 hour."],[null,"After 1 hour, use a fork to scrape the frozen edges into the center. Repeat this process every 30 minutes for the next 3–4 hours or until the entire mixture is granular and frozen."],[null,"Once the granita has reached the desired texture, scoop and serve in small bowls."]],"h":[]},"5439314":{"s":[[null,"Put the peaches and raspberries into a blender."],[null,"Pour the Renastep into the blender with the peaches and raspberries and blend until smooth."],[null,"Serve and enjoy!"]],"h":[["Renastep note","Renastep is a Food for Special Medical Purposes and must be used under medical supervision. Renastep is a ready to use feed for the dietary management of kidney disease from 3 years of age onwards. Renastep contains milk and fish. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information. This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutrimen dietary analysis software."]]},"7439314":{"s":[[null,"Blend together all the ingredients and serve."]],"h":[[null,"For a dairy-free version, use soya milk and a soy-based yogurt alternative."],[null,"On a really hot day, add 8-10 ice cubes before blending to create a fruity ‘slush’."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"3574":{"s":[[null,"Peel the peach and remove the pit. Dice the shallot."],[null,"Place all dressing ingredients into a small blender or food processor. Blend until smooth."],[null,"Store dressing in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 1 week."]],"h":[[null,"White vinegar or apple cider vinegar may be substituted for champagne vinegar."]]},"2221":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"In large bowl, mix almond milk, flour, baking powder and Splenda® (or sugar) until smooth. Set aside."],[null,"In a microwave-safe dish, melt butter and pour into 9” x 13” baking dish."],[null,"Add milk mixture directly on top of melted butter in baking dish."],[null,"Open pie filling and scoop heaping spoonfuls onto the mixture in the baking dish, placing filling randomly across the mixture."],[null,"Sprinkle ground cinnamon on top of cobbler."],[null,"Bake for approximately 40 to 45 minutes or until crust is brown and fluffy."]],"h":[[null,"For a different flavor, substitute your favorite renal-friendly, low-potassium fruit pie filling."],[null,"Along with the cinnamon, you can also sprinkle additional Splenda® or sugar on the top of the cobbler prior to baking."]]},"2637":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350º F. Spray a 9” x 9” baking dish with nonstick spray."],[null,"Mix peaches with lemon juice and granulated sugar or Splenda® granular sweetener. Pour into baking dish."],[null,"Combine flour, oats, brown sugar, nutmeg and cinnamon in a bowl. Cut in margarine with pastry blender or two knives until mixture is crumbly. Sprinkle over peaches."],[null,"Bake for 35 to 45 minutes, until fruit is soft and crumbs are brown. Serve warm or at room temperature. Garnish with two tablespoons nondairy whipped topping and a mint leaf."]],"h":[[null,"If fresh peaches are unavailable, use canned or frozen sliced peaches."],[null,"2 medium peaches yield approximately 1 cup when peeled and sliced."],[null,"If made with Splenda No Calorie Sweetener granular and Splenda brown sugar blend, calories decrease to 247 and 32 g carbohydrate. Count as 2 carbohydrate choices."]]},"3503":{"s":[[null,"Place peaches in blender and blend until smooth."],[null,"Add all remaining ingredients and continue blending until smooth."]],"h":[[null,"Just Whites® are a powdered egg white product available at your local grocery store in the baking section. The product is pasteurized so it is safe to consume without cooking."],[null,"If substituting frozen peaches add 1/4 cup water instead of the ice. The degree of “frozenness” will determine how much your blender will be able to take. It will also give a more “soft serve” consistency than a smoothie, which is great in the warmer season."],[null,"Adjust sugar or use low calorie sweetener to taste."]]},"2164":{"s":[[null,"Place fruit in blender and blend until smooth."],[null,"Add all remaining ingredients and continue blending until smooth."]],"h":[[null,"Just Whites® are a powdered egg white product available at your local grocery store in the baking section. The product is pasteurized so it is safe to consume without cooking."],[null,"If using frozen fruit, the degree of “frozenness” will determine how much your blender will be able to take. It will also give a more “soft serve” consistency than a smoothie, which is great in the warmer season."],[null,"Adjust sugar or artificial sweetener to taste."],[null,"Use artificial sweetener instead of sugar to reduce to 28 grams carbohydrate and 2 carbohydrate choices."]]},"6614887":{"s":[],"h":[]},"2455":{"s":[[null,"Cook the quinoa according to package instructions."],[null,"Slice the bell pepper and dice the shallot. Cut peaches in half and remove the pits. Chop the walnuts."],[null,"Lightly spray a medium skillet or grill pan with cooking oil and heat over medium-high heat."],[null,"Add walnuts to hot pan for 1-2 minutes, just until lightly toasted. Remove from pan and set aside."],[null,"Add bell pepper, shallot and peach halves to the pan. Cook until soft and lightly browned. Remove from heat."],[null,"To assemble salad, top 1 cup arugula with 1/2 cup cooked quinoa. Divide the remaining ingredients and top each salad."],[null,"Serve with 2 tablespoons Peach Basil Vinaigrette Dressing or your favorite vinaigrette dressing."]],"h":[[null,"Make Brittany’s Peach Basil Vinaigrette Dressing for this salad."],[null,"White vinegar or apple cider vinegar may be substituted for champagne vinegar."],[null,"If desired skip cooking the bell pepper, shallots and peaches for a faster raw salad."],[null,"For a lower potassium salad decrease the peach to 1/2 per salad. The potassium is 487 mg instead of 630 mg."]]},"1855":{"s":[[null,"Drain the peaches well and wash strawberries. Dice fruit and set aside."],[null,"Chop the and add to fruit. Add balsamic vinegar and honey and stir gently until well mixed."],[null,"Let salsa sit overnight in the refrigerator."]],"h":[[null,"Alternatively you may add all ingredients to a food processor or blender and pulse until coarsely chopped."],[null,"Substitute fresh peaches when in season."],[null,"Serve with low-sodium crackers or tortilla chips. Look for brands with the lowest amounts of sodium"],[null,"You may also serve with homemade pita chips. Split the pitas in half and cut each half into quarters. Spray with cooking spray and bake in a 350º F oven for about 8 minutes. You may also sprinkle a mixture of cinnamon and sugar after you spray with cooking spray."],[null,"Drain salsa through a fine sieve to remove fluid if you are on a fluid restriction."]]},"1708":{"s":[[null,"Thaw raspberries and peaches, if frozen. Do not drain."],[null,"Pre-heat oven to 375 ºF."],[null,"In a large mixing bowl combine sugar, flour and ginger. Add berries, peaches, and their juices; toss to coat. Add 2 cups of the bread cubes; toss gently until combined. Transfer filling to an ungreased 2-quart square baking dish."],[null,"To make topping place remaining bread cubes in a medium mixing bowl. Drizzle with melted butter; toss to coat. Sprinkle topping over fruit filling. Bake about 30 minutes or until fruit is tender and topping is golden."],[null,"Serve warm with whipped topping."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute 3 cups fresh raspberries and 2 cups freah peaches for frozen when in season."],[null,"Seven slices of bread yields approximately 5 cups cubed."]]},"6962321":{"s":[[null,"Add the peach slices, almond milk, yogurt, flaxseed, and honey to a blender. Blend until smooth."],[null,"Pour into two glasses and enjoy immediately."]],"h":[]},"2122":{"s":[[null,"Trim the celery rib ends."],[null,"Fill each celery rib with 1 tablespoon of peanut butter."],[null,"Spread jelly on top of the peanut butter."],[null,"Cut each celery rib into 3 pieces and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Use any flavor of jelly or fruit spread."],[null,"Place peanut butter and jelly in plastic bags, snip the corner and pipe onto the celery logs."],[null,"To reduce sodium to 38 mg per serving use unsalted peanut butter."],[null,"Cover and refrigerate leftover celery logs. They will keep for 2-3 days."]]},"6878911":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F. Line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"In a medium bowl whisk together peanut butter, banana, egg, vanilla, and brown sugar substitute."],[null,"In a small bowl mix together oats, baking soda and salt. Add milled flaxseed."],[null,"Add oat mixture to peanut butter mixture and mix well."],[null,"Scoop batter into 1 Tbsp. balls and place on baking sheet. Bake for 10-12 minutes. Cool on wire rack."]],"h":[]},"9740076":{"s":[[null,"Drain and rinse your can of beans and add them to your food processor, along with all remaining ingredients, starting with 3/4 cup of almond flour. Process until fully combined, scraping down the sides as needed."],[null,"Check the consistency of your mixture, if it feels too soft or too sticky to shape into balls, add the remaining 1/4 cup of almond flour, and pulse to combine."],[null,"Use a small cookie scoop or tablespoon to scoop the mixture and roll it into a half-inch ball. Place it on a sheet of parchment paper or plate and repeat with the remaining peanut butter mixture. You should get around 22 bliss balls."]],"h":[[null,"Use natural peanut butter where the only ingredient is peanuts, without added sugar or salt."],[null,"If your nut butter is very drippy , you may need extra almond flour to get the consistency firm enough to roll."],[null,"Roll your balls using damp hands to prevent the mixture from sticking to your hands and fingers."],[null,"Store the balls at room temperature for 2-3 days, in the fridge for up to 5 days, or airtight in the freezer for up to 3 months."]]},"3403":{"s":[[null,"Rinse and drain the garbanzo beans. Preheat oven to 350 degree F. Line a cookie sheet with parchment paper to reduce sticking."],[null,"Put all ingredients, except the chocolate chips, into a food processor and blend until smooth. Use a blender if you do not have a food processor."],[null,"Mix chocolate chips into the dough by hand."],[null,"Spoon out about a tablespoon of dough for each cookie onto the cookie sheet."],[null,"Bake for about 12 minutes or until cookies get a little brown on the edges."]],"h":[[null,"These cookies do not spread out much while baking and the dough is a little sticky. If you want a smoother, rounder cookie, try freezing the batter for about an hour so you can shape them into discs before placing them on the cookie sheet."],[null,"Natural, pure maple syrup should not contain phosphorus additives. Some more processed varieties do, be sure to look for pure maple syrup and read the ingredient list for phosphates."],[null,"Our bodies do not absorb all of the potassium and phosphorus in plant-based foods, such as the garbanzo beans in this recipe, which also gives you a bit more protein than a regular cookie."],[null,"Peanut butter can be enjoyed in small amounts in a kidney friendly diet. You may also substitute any other natural nut butter."],[null,"Semisweet chocolate chips can be substituted for the dark chocolate chips."]]},"9980070":{"s":[[null,"Add all the ingredients to a food processor and process until smooth and combined."],[null,"Optional: Serve sprinkled with an extra sprinkle of cayenne pepper or paprika if desired."]],"h":[]},"2413":{"s":[[null,"Spread peanut butter and honey on raisin bread to make the sandwich."],[null,"Trim celery and cut into sticks."],[null,"Assemble sandwich, celery sticks, raspberries and cheese on a plate or in a divided food container with a lid for a meal on-the-go."]],"h":[[null,"Peanut butter naturally contains potassium and phosphorus. Used in small amounts, such as in this recipes, it can fit into a kidney-friendly meal plan."]]},"6698238":{"s":[[null,"Toast one slice of wholegrain bread to your preferred level of crispness."],[null,"Spread 1.5 tablespoons peanut butter evenly over the warm toast."],[null,"Serve immediately while the toast is still warm."]],"h":[]},"6590213":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6123574":{"s":[[null,"Lay the 12 slices of apples on a flat surface. Spread each slice with 1 teaspoon of peanut butter."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix together the cranberries, walnuts, and coconut flakes."],[null,"Evenly sprinkle each apple with about 1 tablespoon of the cranberry mixture."]],"h":[]},"6661132":{"s":[[null,"Combine all ingredients in a bowl. Toss gently and serve immediately."]],"h":[]},"6311954":{"s":[[null,"Spray a large skillet with cooking spray and heat over medium heat. Add chicken and cook, stirring often, until golden brown. Transfer chicken to a plate and return the skillet to medium heat."],[null,"Add the sesame oil and stir in the onion, garlic, ginger, and chili-garlic sauce. Cook, stirring occasionally, until onion softens, 4–5 minutes."],[null,"Add soy sauce, peanut butter, coconut milk, almond milk, and tomatoes. Stir until the sauce is creamy and the peanut butter is fully distributed."],[null,"Bring to a simmer. Return chicken to the pan and add the chopped cilantro. Reduce heat to low and simmer until the sauce thickens, 3–4 minutes."],[null,"Serve chicken over cauliflower rice and garnish with peanuts and more cilantro, if desired."]],"h":[]},"4109231":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F."],[null,"In a saucepan, over medium-high heat, melt peanut butter, honey and oil for 5–7 minutes. Stir with a wooden spoon."],[null,"In a bowl, mix together the oatmeal, fiber cereal, flour, flaxseed and pecans."],[null,"Add the oatmeal mixture to the saucepan, stir to combine and pour into a 9\"×12\" pan."],[null,"Bake in the oven for 20–25 minutes."],[null,"Let cool and cut into 18 portions."]],"h":[["Breakfast cereals and the kidney diet","The basic ingredient of all breakfast cereals is grain. Sometimes a cereal consists of a single grain or in many cases it is a combination of grains. Whole grain products are a rich source of vitamins, minerals, fiber, carbohydrates, fat and protein. With all of these nutritional benefits, grains are usually considered to be a staple in one’s diet. Quite often, grains are refined which is a process where the hull, bran and germ are removed. The remaining part for the grain is mostly carbohydrate. In many cases, refined grains are recommended in a kidney-friendly diet. This is because when the hull, bran and germ are removed, the final grain product is significantly lower in potassium and phosphorus. Fortunately, rice and corn are naturally lower in potassium and phosphorus. Because of this, those who have kidney disease can eat them on a regular basis and take advantage of the entire grain and all the nutrition it has to offer. Other whole grains such as oats and wheat are higher in potassium and phosphorus. However, don’t avoid all other whole grain cereals entirely, just ask your dietitian how much whole grain cereal is right for you. One potential concern about eating cereal may be the milk that you add — as milk and soy beverage are high in potassium and phosphorus. A helpful tip is to either limit the amount of milk and soy beverage that you use or try almond or unfortified rice beverage instead. These milk alternatives are much lower in potassium and phosphorus making them more kidney-friendly. Ask your dietitian which milk alternative is right for your diet."]]},"6897570":{"s":[],"h":[]},"7809362":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4 and lightly grease a baking tray (approx 20cm x 25cm) with 1 tsp of the rapeseed oil."],[null,"In a bowl, beat the eggs, sugar, rapeseed oil and almond essence together."],[null,"Add the flour and baking powder, mix well and add to the baking tray."],[null,"Arrange the pears on top, sprinkle with the almonds and the reserved tsp of sugar. Bake for 20-22 minutes. The cake is cooked when a knife inserted into the centre comes out clean."]],"h":[[null,"Tinned pears also work well in this recipe."],[null,"You could use other fruit such as apples, peaches, nectarines, cherries or plums in this traybake."],[null,"Try using a different essences, such as vanilla or lemon or add some grated lemon or orange zest."],[null,"Freeze wrapped in foil or greaseproof in labelled freezer bags for up to three months."]]},"6859231":{"s":[[null,"Toast the whole wheat bread slices until golden and crisp. Set aside to cool slightly."],[null,"In a small bowl, stir the low-fat cottage cheese with ground cinnamon until evenly mixed."],[null,"Spread the cinnamon cottage cheese mixture evenly over each slice of toast. Top with sliced pear and a sprinkle of chopped walnuts."]],"h":[]},"3977":{"s":[[null,"Clean the watercress; core and slice pear then cut each slice into 3 pieces."],[null,"In a large bowl combine watercress, lettuce, pear, cranberries and pecan pieces."],[null,"In a jar combine vinegar, honey, olive oil, ginger and mustard. Cover with a lid and shake until well mixed."],[null,"Pour dressing over salad and toss before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Adjust the amount of salad dressing added according to your preference for more or less dressing."],[null,"Ginger paste is packaged in a tube and available in the produce section of some grocery stores. If unavailable, use minced fresh ginger root."]]},"4973268":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375 F."],[null,"In a microwave-safe deep bowl or measuring cup, prepare the syrup. Crush the ginger slices with a wooden spoon. This unleashes the flavor of the ginger. Add sugar, lemon juice, and water. Heat in the microwave for 2 minutes. Then stir to dissolve the sugar. Add more time in the microwave if the sugar is not completely dissolved. Pour the mixture into a 9-inch cake pan. Place the pear slices on top and set aside."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix the flour, cream of tartar, and baking soda. Set aside."],[null,"In a bigger bowl, with the help of an electric mixer, mix butter and sugar for about 2 minutes until smooth. Add the eggs and continue to mix for 2 minutes. Add vanilla, lemon zest and grated ginger."],[null,"With the help of a wooden spoon, slowly add the dry ingredients from step 3 and milk while alternating."],[null,"Pour the mixture into the cake pan over the pear slices. Use a spoon to gently distribute the mixture evenly. Bake in the oven for 40 minutes or until a toothpick inserted in the center comes out clean. Take out of the oven and let cool for 10 minutes."],[null,"Cut around the edge of the cake, place a large plate on top, and flip the cake upside down to release from the pan."]],"h":[[null,"Tip: Canned pears in place of fresh ones can lower the potassium in a recipe."],["Ginger and low-potassium desserts","Choosing a dessert that fits into a low-potassium diet for chronic kidney disease can be a challenge. It’s important however to find a sweet treat you can enjoy. Many desserts contain potassium-rich ingredients such as chocolate, nuts, or dairy. Preparing a recipe from scratch allows you to maintain low-potassium ingredients. Portion size also makes a difference to limit the potassium you are eating. Sweetness can be maintained in desserts with lower-potassium fruits and spices. Ginger is one spice that can enhance dessert taste. The rich flavor in ginger comes from compounds called ginerols. Ginger not only adds flavor to a low-potassium diet, but is also beneficial to blood pressure, blood cholesterol, and your body’s immune system. When selecting fresh ginger, pick a piece that has smooth rather than wrinkled skin, which points to less freshness. Avoid peeling until just before use to optimize flavor. Ginger can be stored short-term on a countertop or more long-term wrapped in the freezer."]]},"5235256":{"s":[[null,"Peel 2 pears and chop into small pieces."],[null,"Place the pear into a saucepan, add a dash of water and boil until soft (10-12 minutes)."],[null,"Add the raspberries and boil for a further 1-2 minutes."],[null,"Allow to cool and then use a blender to whizz up to a purée consistency."],[null,"Add into ice cube trays and freeze or use straight away."]],"h":[[null,"Top tip:"],[null,"Mix up any combination of the fruit and vegetables above to make your own unique combination!"]]},"4374776":{"s":[[null,"Heat vegetable oil over medium heat in a saucepan."],[null,"Add chopped onions and bell pepper and sauté for 5 minutes or until onions are transparent."],[null,"Add tomato paste and thyme and sauté for another 2-3 minutes."],[null,"Drain water from pigeon peas and add peas to saucepan. Set water from can aside to use for cooking the rice."],[null,"Take water from the can of peas and add enough water to make up to 3½ cups."],[null,"Add Season All and bring ingredients to a boil over high heat. Add the rice."],[null,"Turn heat down to low and cook until all the water is absorbed (approximately 20 minutes)."]],"h":[]},"6106833":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350 degrees F. Spray large rectangular baking dish with nonstick cooking spray."],[null,"In a medium shallow bowl, whisk together egg and egg whites."],[null,"In another medium shallow bowl, combine garlic powder, pepper and pecans."],[null,"Dip turkey breast tenderloin in egg mixture and coat well. Dredge turkey in pecan mixture and cover on both sides. Place in baking dish. Discard leftover egg mixture."],[null,"In a medium bowl, mix together the sweet potatoes, oil, cinnamon and brown sugar substitute."],[null,"Arrange the sweet potatoes around the turkey breast tenderloin in baking dish. Bake for 50 minutes or until done (turkey breast reaches 165 degrees)."]],"h":[]},"6140897":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425° F. Prep a large rimmed baking sheet. For easier cleanup and less sticking, line with parchment paper (optional)."],[null,"Place the pecans in a food processor. Pulse until they look like breadcrumbs. Transfer to a rimmed plate."],[null,"Place the chicken on the baking sheet. In a small bowl, stir together the applesauce and mustard. Spoon the applesauce-mustard mixture on top of each breast, spreading it evenly with the back of the spoon."],[null,"Firmly press the applesauce-mustard side of each chicken breast into the pecans. Place the chicken back on the baking sheet, pecan-crusted side up."],[null,"Sprinkle any remaining pecans on the chicken; press to adhere. Sprinkle with salt."],[null,"Bake for about 20 minutes, or until the chicken reaches an internal temperature of 165° F. Divide among four dinner plates and serve."]],"h":[]},"6344459":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6461923":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6192124":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425°F."],[null,"Loosen the skin of the turkey breast by gently pushing your fingers between the skin and the meat. Season under the skin with 1 tablespoon of olive oil, 1/2 teaspoon of salt and 1/2 teaspoon of pepper. Rub the spice blend under and over the loosened skin, then place the turkey breast in a roasting pan."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix the remaining oil, the remaining salt and pepper, the garlic, onion, celery, carrots, rutabaga, turnip, sweet potato, oregano, orange zest, orange, cumin and smoked paprika. Arrange the vegetable mixture in a single layer around the turkey breast."],[null,"Transfer the pan to the oven and roast the turkey and vegetables, uncovered, for 15 minutes. Loosely cover the pan with aluminum foil. Reduce the oven temperature to 325°F and roast for 30 to 45 minutes more, or until an instant-read thermometer inserted into the meatiest part of the turkey breast registers 165°F."],[null,"Remove the pan from the oven, transfer the turkey to a cutting board and loosely cover it with aluminum foil. Let the turkey rest for 20 minutes, then discard the skin and slice the meat."],[null,"Remove and discard the oranges from the roasted vegetables, stir the vegetables well and serve them with the sliced turkey."]],"h":[]},"6836343":{"s":[[null,"Preheat broiler. Using a sharp knife, slice eggplant into 1/4-inch slices, and place on a baking sheet. Brush the eggplant with 2 Tbsp olive oil, then broil for 5–7 minutes per side until they are dark gold and cooked through. Set aside to cool. (This step can be done a day in advance.)"],[null,"Heat remaining olive oil in a large saucepan over medium heat. Add garlic and cook until it begins to release its aroma, but do not allow garlic to turn color."],[null,"Pour in tomatoes, and stir. Add crushed red pepper, basil, salt, and freshly ground pepper. Cover, reduce heat to low, and simmer for 20 minutes."],[null,"When eggplant is cool enough to handle, stack three slices together, and chop into dime-size pieces. Repeat until all eggplant is chopped."],[null,"While sauce is still cooking, bring a gallon of water to a boil over high heat. Add pasta and cook until al dente."],[null,"After sauce has cooked for 20 minutes, turn off heat, remove lid, and add eggplant pieces and cheese. Stir well. Cover, and simmer sauce over medium heat until pasta is done cooking (10–12 minutes)."],[null,"Drain pasta. Toss in sauce to coat. Serve hot garnished with chopped basil (if desired)."]],"h":[]},"6445111":{"s":[[null,"The marinade liquid should be drained well and discarded from the cucumbers before serving. Serve in small salad bowls as a salad or snack."],[null,"Cover the container with plastic wrap and leave it in the refrigerator for the last 2 hours."],[null,"Pour over the cucumbers and onion. Add pepper and, if desired, ¼ teaspoon of salt."],[null,"Combine the sugar and vinegar. Stir until the sugar dissolves completely."],[null,"Cut the cucumbers and onions into slices about 1/8 inch thick. Place in a large bowl."]],"h":[]},"2768":{"s":[[null,"In a large skillet brown meat in oil over medium high heat."],[null,"Add all vegetables and 1/4 cup water. Cover skillet and cook, stirring occasionally, until soft."],[null,"Add brown gravy mix and 1 cup water."],[null,"Stir over medium heat until thick."]],"h":[[null,"Compare brands and buy the lowest sodium gravy mix."]]},"6354484":{"s":[[null,"Preheat a grill or grill pan. Brush the chicken with the oil and sprinkle with salt. Grill over direct medium heat until fully cooked and grill marks form. Set aside."],[null,"Add the hummus, tea, cheese, garlic, mustard, Worcestershire sauce, lemon juice, and 1 Tsp. peppercorns to a blender. Cover and puree."],[null,"When ready to serve toss the dressing with the greens in a large mixing bowl. Transfer to 4 separate bowls or plate, top with grilled chicken, sprinkle with pistachios and the remaining 1/4 Tsp. peppercorns, and serve."]],"h":[]},"4499972":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400°F."],[null,"To prepare the sauce, add peppers, garlic and basil to a food processor or blender and puree."],[null,"Spread 2 tablespoons of sauce on each pita. Sprinkle with ¼ cup of mozzarella cheese and ¼ cup of diced chicken."],[null,"Place the four pita pizza on a baking tray."],[null,"Bake for 10–15 minutes or until the crust is crispy."],[null,"Garnish each pizza with 1 teaspoon of thinly sliced basil. Serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"Note: As a pizza base you can also use Naan bread, which we used for the photo or flour tortillas."],["Using dried and fresh herbs","A kidney-friendly diet usually recommends reducing daily salt and potassium intake. While this may change how you prepare and cook your food items, this doesn’t mean your meals have to be lacking in flavor. Instead of adding salt or a potassium chloride salt substitute, use fresh or dried herbs to create a variety of different mouth-savoring tastes. Dried herbs are either ground, diced, flaked or whole. This type of herb can be cost-effective as it is easily stored and lasts longer than a fresh herb. Common dried herbs include basil, thyme and rosemary. Since most recipes require only a small amount of dried herbs, the added potassium content is low. Fresh herbs are typically purchased from the produce section of the grocery store. To extend the life of a fresh herb item, experts recommend washing and then using a salad spinner to remove excess water. Follow recipe directions for fresh herb prep before use. To add flavor to your meals and reduce sodium and potassium intake, try meat or poultry with dill, thyme with steamed vegetables, and cilantro with tacos or rice dishes. Substituting: Dried herbs are more concentrated and therefore stronger in flavor than fresh herbs. When using fresh herbs you need approximately three times the amount of dried herbs. For example, if a recipe calls for 1 tablespoon of fresh thyme, you need to add only 1 teaspoon of dried thyme."]]},"6170402":{"s":[[null,"Add the frozen banana coins, cocoa powder, and extracts to a food processor. Cover and pulse 10 times to chop the bananas."],[null,"Process the banana mixture on high speed until creamy, about 2½ minutes. Every 30 seconds, stop and scrape down the inside of the food processor."],[null,"Add the cacao nibs and pulse 3 times to combine."],[null,"Enjoy immediately, soft-serve style. Or freeze until solid; at serving time, set it out for 15 minutes, scoop, and serve."]],"h":[]},"3013":{"s":[[null,"Pour juices and water into a coffee percolator."],[null,"Place remaining ingredients in the percolator basket."],[null,"Perk just like regular coffee, until perking stops. Serve warm."]],"h":[[null,"No percolator? No problem. Use a saucepan to heat ingredients to a boil then simmer for 20 minutes."]]},"7285911":{"s":[[null,"Sift the plain flour into a bowl."],[null,"Add the beaten egg, then gradually beat in the skimmed milk to make a smooth batter."],[null,"Leave to stand for 30 minutes-1 hour."],[null,"Lightly oil a hot pan. Add 2-3 tbsp batter and swirl it gently to spread out thinly round the pan. Leave for 30-40 seconds, it should form a crust on the edges and the pancake will bubble in the middle"],[null,"Cook for 1-2 minutes then toss or flip and cook the other side for 1 minute or until golden."]],"h":[[null,"To keep pancakes warm, put a plate onto a saucepan of very gently simmering water, add the pancakes and cover with another plate."],[null,"Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"6585792":{"s":[[null,"In a large skillet, heat olive oil over medium heat."],[null,"Add the carrots to the skillet, spreading them out in a single layer."],[null,"Sauté the carrots for 8–10 minutes, stirring occasionally, until they are tender-crisp and slightly caramelized."],[null,"Season the carrots with the salt, thyme and black pepper."]],"h":[]},"3568":{"s":[[null,"Remove skin from chicken and place in a pot with finely chopped onion. Cover and cook for 1-1/2 hours over low heat. No water is needed, as chicken makes its own juice. When done, allow chicken to cool and save broth."],[null,"In a large bowl, whisk together chicken broth, mayonnaise, Dijon mustard, olive oil, vinegar, lime juice and black pepper. Set aside. This is the dressing for the chicken salad."],[null,"Chop the carrots, spring onion, celery, parsley and hard-boiled eggs. Rinse the pickle spear and olives to remove some of the sodium; chop."],[null,"Mix together the chicken, vegetables, eggs, peas, parsley, pickles and olives."],[null,"Cover chicken mixture with dressing mixture and toss to combine ingredients."],[null,"Transfer to flat plate, cover and chill for at least 2 hours before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Instead of using a pot, cook chicken and onion in a crock pot according to manufacturer’s recommended cooking time."],[null,"Use fresh or frozen green peas."],[null,"Choose green olives instead of black if preferred."],[null,"Look for Vlasic® brand reduced-sodium pickles or substitute low-sodium sweet pickles."],[null,"Serve with hot pita bread or French bread."],[null,"If you are on a lower protein diet, reduce the portion size to 1/2 cup (15 grams protein)."]]},"6346471":{"s":[[null,"Sprinkle the chicken with the salt and pepper. Heat 2 tsp oil in a large nonstick skillet over medium-high heat. Add the chicken and cook until browned, about 6 minutes. Transfer to a plate."],[null,"Add the onion and the remaining 1 tsp oil and cook, stirring occasionally, until softened, about 5 minutes. Add the tomatoes, garlic, soy sauce, and vinegar, and cook, stirring occasionally, until the tomatoes are softened, about 5 minutes."],[null,"Return the chicken to the skillet and heat through."]],"h":[]},"4151597":{"s":[[null,"Defreeze the corn at room temperature by placing the corn in a bowl of water."],[null,"Preheat the grill on high, reduce the temperature and cook the chicken breast 7–8 minutes on each side, until the meat reaches an internal temperature of 165°F."],[null,"Take the breasts off the grill and wrap in aluminum foil to keep them warm."],[null,"In a salad bowl, combine the peppers, mozarella cheese, red onion, oil and vinegar. Drain the corn and add to mixture. Season the salad with black pepper."],[null,"Cut the chicken breast into small cubes and add to the salad."],[null,"Prepare a bed of romaine lettuce on each of the four plates and top with a quarter of the salad."]],"h":[[null,"The warm chicken in combination with the other cold ingredients gives a special taste to this salad. But, of course, you can also use cold leftover chicken. Please note, the original recipe for Solterito calls for lima beans which we replaced with chicken."],[null,"PLEASE NOTE: The recipe is higher in potassium and portion size is important. Check with your registered dietitian to see how this recipe can be included in your diet."],["Corn and the kidney diet","Corn is a common vegetable, which deserves more attention given its healthful properties. Its soluble fiber feeds the good bacteria in your gut and is helpful in improving digestive health. Also, fiber helps you feel full longer so you are less likely to overeat. Corn is loaded with lutein and zeaxanthin, two phytochemicals that help promote healthy vision. It is also a good source of B vitamins. Finally, it provides a complex carbohydrate source in the diet making it a good source of energy. Corn is the hallmark of fall harvest. Enjoy fresh corn at that time. Sprinkle with various herbs to add some zest. Be adventuresome and try a sprinkle of cayenne pepper along with a dash of cinnamon. Other times of the year, it is easy to purchase frozen or canned corn. Be sure to purchase corn without added salt. Corn can add both color and texture to a variety of food items. Add it to soups, salads, tacos and casseroles. Fortunately, ½ cup of corn contains only 196 milligrams of potassium making it a lower-potassium vegetable. Ask your registered dietitian how much corn is right for you."]]},"6831029":{"s":[[null,"Place garlic and pignoli in food processor and process until minced. Add basil and Parmigiano-Reggiano cheese and process until smooth. Add olive oil and pulse until well blended."]],"h":[]},"6675170":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your grill or grill pan on medium-high heat. Brush with olive oil."],[null,"Place the chicken breasts in a shallow dish and coat them evenly with the pesto sauce."],[null,"Grill the marinated chicken breasts for about 6–8 minutes per side or until fully cooked, with an internal temperature of 165 degrees F."],[null,"Remove the chicken from the grill and let it rest for a few minutes before serving."]],"h":[]},"6070049":{"s":[[null,"Soak the bamboo skewers in warm water for at least 30 minutes."],[null,"Preheat an indoor or outdoor grill."],[null,"While the skewers are soaking, blend the olive oil, garlic, basil, pine nuts, black pepper, and parmesan cheese in a blender or food processor."],[null,"Thread alternating pieces of chicken, zucchini, and tomato onto the soaked skewers, using 3 pieces of chicken, 3 pieces of zucchini, and 3 tomatoes."],[null,"Brush the kabobs with the basil mixture, coating well."],[null,"Grill the kabobs about 7 minutes, brushing with the basil mixture until it is all used. Turn the kabobs frequently until the chicken is cooked through and reaches 165°F."]],"h":[]},"6074589":{"s":[[null,"Season chicken with salt and pepper."],[null,"Heat a large skillet over medium heat and spray with cooking spray. Add chicken and cook until golden brown on both sides and cooked through. Transfer to a plate and cover with foil."],[null,"Return the skillet to medium heat, spray with cooking spray and add garlic, onion, tomatoes, peppers, and mushrooms. Cook, stirring occasionally, until the vegetables soften, 6–7 minutes."],[null,"Stir in half and half and pesto. Add chicken back to the skillet, turning to coat in sauce."],[null,"Divide spaghetti between plates, top with chicken and vegetables. Garnish with parmesan cheese."]],"h":[]},"6563572":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, mix the shredded chicken with the pesto and set aside."],[null,"Lay the tortillas on a flat surface. Lay the lettuce leaves on the tortilla, leaving about 1 inch of the outside of the tortilla uncovered."],[null,"Divide the chicken between the tortillas and spread it over the lettuce."],[null,"Sprinkle the feta cheese on top of the chicken and add the red pepper strips and tomato slices."],[null,"Fold two opposite sides of the tortilla in about 1 inch. Take one of the other sides and roll it toward the other side making a tight roll. Be careful to keep the filling from spilling out. Cut the rolled wrap in half."],[null,"Serve with a side salad if desired."]],"h":[]},"6992930":{"s":[[null,"Place the eggs in a single layer in a saucepan and cover with water. Bring the water to a boil, then reduce the heat to low, cover, and simmer for 10–12 minutes."],[null,"Transfer the boiled eggs to an ice water bath to cool."],[null,"Once the eggs are cool, peel them and cut them in half lengthwise. Remove the yolks and place them in a bowl."],[null,"In the bowl with the egg yolks, add mayonnaise, prepared basil pesto, Dijon mustard, salt, and pepper. Mash and mix the ingredients together until smooth."],[null,"Spoon or pipe the pesto filling into the hollowed-out egg whites."],[null,"Chill the deviled eggs in the refrigerator for at least 30 minutes before serving."]],"h":[]},"6501487":{"s":[[null,"Cook the pasta according to the package directions to the al dente stage."],[null,"While the pasta is cooking, place the chopped kale in a large bowl and drizzle it with olive oil. Gently rub the oil into the pieces of kale until they soften slightly and turn dark green. Add the zucchini, pepper, and tomatoes to the bowl and toss."],[null,"Once the pasta is done, drain it and add it to the vegetables and toss well. Stir in the pesto until the pasta is coated. Cover it tightly and place it in the refrigerator to chill for at least an hour."],[null,"Just before serving, gently break apart the tuna and mix it into the pasta and vegetables, coating it with pesto."],[null,"Place 2 cups of mixed greens on a plate or a bowl. Top with 2 cups of the pesto pasta tuna."]],"h":[]},"9758847":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 425℉/218℃ convection roast and line a large baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Arrange the chopped vegetables on your tray and roast them for 15 minutes, or until the edges are golden brown."],[null,"Meanwhile, bring a large pot of generously salted water to a boil, and cook your pasta according to package directions for 'al dente' pasta. Drain it, (BUT RESERVE 1/4-1/2 cup of the water) return it to the pot, and set it aside."],[null,"Meanwhile, make the pesto. Add the basil, garlic, and lemon juice to your food processor and process until finely chopped. Then with the processor running, slowly add 1/4 cup (or more if needed) of the reserved starchy water to reach your desired consistency. Taste for salt and pepper and adjust as needed."],[null,"Add the pesto and the roasted veggies to the pot of drained pasta, mix well, and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Salt your cooking water. Make sure to add enough salt to your pot of water for the best texture and flavour. Here's a handy guide to help you salt your water perfectly each time."],[null,"Cook to ‘al dente’ texture. Do not overcook! Al dente means that the pasta is still firm once cooked, giving optimal texture in every bite. To ensure it does not overcook, start taste testing a few minutes before the package says it will be ready. It should be tender, but still firm."],[null,"Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-4 days."]]},"6886722":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375 degrees F. Coat a baking dish with cooking spray. Set aside."],[null,"In a small bowl, toss together tomatoes, red onion, oregano, red wine vinegar and olive oil."],[null,"Butterfly each chicken breast, and open each like a book. Season both sides of all chicken breasts with salt and pepper."],[null,"Toss basil and parmesan cheese together in a small bowl and then divide the mixture evenly between each open chicken breast. Fold the chicken breast back in half and place in the baking pan."],[null,"Pour the tomato mixture over the chicken breasts and bake for 35-45 minutes (depending on the size of the chicken breasts) or until the internal temperature is 165 degrees F."]],"h":[]},"9354957":{"s":[[null,"Spiralize your zucchini and place them in a large colander in your kitchen sink or a large bowl. Sprinkle with the salt to force excess moisture to release. Set aside for at least 20 minutes. You will notice the zucchini will reduce which will prevent watery noodles later."],[null,"Heat the pesto over medium high heat, in a large skillet, and then add the spiralized zucchini and red pepper flakes, if using. Sauté the noodles for 2-4 minutes until heated through, but do not overcook."],[null,"Turn off the heat and add the tomatoes, mix, and serve with extra red pepper flakes, fresh herbs, or parmesan cheese, if desired."]],"h":[[null,"For ease of spiralizing , use zucchini that are narrow, long, and straight. Or you may purchase pre-spiralized zucchini noodles from your grocery store to save time. Don’t skip the salting! This step is important to prevent watery noodles after cooking. You want to reduce the zucchini to remove excess moisture. Do NOT overcook the noodles. You want the noodles tender but crisp, and not overly soft, for the best texture and to mimic ‘al dente’ pasta. For less spice , reduce the red pepper flakes by half, or adjust to your taste. You may spiralize the noodles for up to 3 days before salting and cooking and store them in a sealed container or zip-top bag in your fridge. Once cooked, leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-4 days in a sealed container. Reheat on the stovetop, but be careful not to overcook."]]},"6121290":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400°F (200°C). Line a sheet pan with parchment paper."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix basil pesto, ½ tablespoon olive oil, ½ the lemon zest, ¼ teaspoon coarse salt, and ¼ teaspoon black pepper."],[null,"Place cod filets on the sheet pan. Spread a generous layer of the pesto mixture over each filet."],[null,"Toss cherry tomatoes and asparagus with the remaining ½ tablespoon of olive oil, the rest of the lemon zest, ¼ teaspoon coarse salt, and ¼ teaspoon pepper and arrange around the coated cod on the baking sheet."],[null,"Roast in the preheated oven for approximately 20 minutes or until the cod reaches an internal temperature of 145°F (63°C) and flakes easily with a fork."]],"h":[]},"6452003":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F. Arrange the bell pepper halves on a baking sheet with the cut sides facing up. Bake for about 30 minutes or until they are tender but still firm enough to hold their shape."],[null,"While the peppers are in the oven, warm the olive oil in a large skillet over medium heat. Add the sliced onions and cook for about 4–5 minutes, stirring occasionally, until they soften and start to brown."],[null,"Stir in the mushrooms and continue cooking for another 5 minutes, allowing them to release their moisture."],[null,"Add the steak slices to the pan, along with the Italian seasoning, black pepper, and salt. Cook for 3–5 minutes, stirring frequently, until the steak is browned and cooked through."],[null,"Pour in the Worcestershire sauce, stir to combine, and remove the skillet from the heat."],[null,"Switch the oven to broil."],[null,"Fill each bell pepper half with an equal portion of the steak mixture and sprinkle with cheese."],[null,"Return the peppers to the oven and broil for 2–3 minutes, or until the cheese is fully melted and slightly golden."],[null,"Top with the chopped green onion to serve."]],"h":[]},"1733":{"s":[[null,"Shred roasted chicken and measure two cups for recipe."],[null,"Sauté chicken in a skillet with ghee or butter and water."],[null,"Sprinkle Mrs. Dash, onion powder and garlic powder onto cooking chicken."],[null,"Stir occasionally and cook 5 to 8 minutes. Add more water if chicken appears dry."],[null,"Cut the rolls or pistolettes in half and spread mayonnaise on each side."],[null,"Divide cooked chicken into four portions and spoon onto each roll or pistolette. Top with the other roll half."]],"h":[[null,"Leftover chicken works great for this recipe."],[null,"Pistolettes are a type of submarine shaped bread about half the size of a baguette. It is popular in New Orleans for sandwiches."],[null,"Ghee is clarified butter that is prepared by simmering butter and removing the residue."]]},"7493655":{"s":[[null,"Add the oil to a pan with the onion and cook for 4-5 minutes. Stir regularly until well browned."],[null,"Add the ginger and garlic, and cook for a further 2-3 minutes."],[null,"Add the star anise, cinnamon, coriander seeds, chilli and the chicken breast. Mix well and cook for 3-4 minutes, ensuring the chicken breast is lightly browned and coated with the spices."],[null,"Add the stock and mix well again. Bring to the boil, then turn down the heat. Cover, then simmer gently for 15 minutes."],[null,"Remove the chilli, cinnamon stick and star anise and discard. Remove the chicken breast and set to one side."],[null,"Add the broccoli and cook for 5 minutes, then add the carrot and cook a further 2 minutes before adding the noodles and beansprouts. Bring to the boil, then divide between 4 bowls."],[null,"Slice the chicken and place some on top of each bowl, then scatter with spring onion, coriander, a chilli and a squeeze of fresh lime."]],"h":[[null,"You could add prawns with the broccoli."],[null,"For a vegan version, replace the chicken with tofu and use a vegetable stock cube."],[null,"For gluten-free version, use a gluten-free stock cube."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"7267024":{"s":[[null,"Place the split peas into a pan, cover with water and boil rapidly for 10 minutes then simmer for 25–30 minutes until tender. Drain."],[null,"Transfer to a food processor or blender, add the onion, garlic and flour, and blend until smooth."],[null,"Season well. Make into 16 patties."],[null,"Meanwhile, preheat the grill to high."],[null,"Brush the patties a little oil and grill for 4–5 minutes until golden, turning halfway through cooking."],[null,"To make the hot pepper sauce, place all the ingredients into a pan, bring to the boil and simmer for 20 minutes."],[null,"Transfer to a blender and blend until almost smooth. Serve with the fritters."]],"h":[[null,"As an alternative to the hot pepper sauce, make a herb dip by blending 2 tbsp each chopped fresh coriander, mint and parsley along with a crushed clove garlic and 4-5 tbsp low-fat yogurt."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Freeze the fritters and sauce separately. Defrost in the microwave. Take care when reheating the fritters as they may crumble."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"6284632":{"s":[[null,"In a large pot over high heat, heat 7 cups of the water and bring to a boil. Add 1 cup of water to a bowl filled with ice."],[null,"Add the Brussels sprouts to the boiling water and cook for 2 minutes. Use a slotted spoon to transfer the sprouts to the ice water to cool. Drain the cooled sprouts and pack into the jar."],[null,"Add the vinegar, 1/2 cup water, salt, and sugar to a saucepan over high heat. Bring to a boil and stir until the salt and sugar dissolve. Boil for 2 minutes. Remove the brine from the heat."],[null,"Add the bay leaf, dill, garlic, onion, and pickling spice to the brine."],[null,"Carefully fill the jar with the brine, covering the Brussels sprouts completely."],[null,"Place the lids on the jar and shake the jar gently to distribute the ingredients."],[null,"Refrigerate for at least 2 hours before serving. Store in the refrigerator for up to 3 months. Before serving, remove and discard the bay leaf."],[null,"Chef’s Tip: Only tough vegetables, such as Brussels sprouts and carrots, need to be blanched first. Softer vegetables, such as cucumbers and zucchini, can go in the jar raw before you add the brine."]],"h":[]},"2080":{"s":[[null,"Place the mustard seeds, vinegar and water in a bowl and soak overnight. The seeds will swell up and become more pungent and flavorful the longer they soak."],[null,"Place the soaked mustard seed mixture in a saucepan and add the salt, turmeric and honey. Cook on medium heat until the mixture starts to bubble. Turn heat down to medium low. Continue to stir often and cook for another 15 minutes. Add a little more vinegar if the mixture gets too thick."],[null,"Take off the heat and cool. Refrigerate until ready to use."]],"h":[[null,"Add more turmeric or honey to taste or red pepper flakes if you want it spicy."],[null,"If mustard seeds are too thick, mix in a little more vinegar."],[null,"Use a good quality mustard seed. Poor quality or old seeds taste very bitter."],[null,"You can experiment with different vinegars (white, champagne, rice wine, red wine) or different types of mustard seeds (black or brown)."],[null,"Try Pickled Mustard Seeds on boiled eggs, in salad dressings, with chicken, seafood, salmon, roasted vegetables, sandwiches, or anything that you like mustard on."]]},"1891":{"s":[[null,"Thaw and drain okra."],[null,"Sterilize two one-pint jars and lids."],[null,"Place 1-teaspoon dill seed into each jar. Pack okra into jars."],[null,"To each jar add 1 red pepper, 1 chili pepper and 2 cloves of garlic."],[null,"Combine vinegar and water and bring to a boil, simmer for 5 minutes."],[null,"Pour hot mixture over okra in each jar. Cap jar and cool."],[null,"Refrigerate and okra pickles will be ready to serve in 2 weeks."]],"h":[[null,"Fresh okra can be substituted for frozen okra when in season."]]},"3434":{"s":[[null,"Pour boiling water over thinly sliced onions and drain."],[null,"Place onion slices and 2 whole cloves (optional) into 1 large or 2 small glass jars."],[null,"In a saucepan mix the vinegar, lime juice and sugar and simmer until sugar is dissolved. Pour mixture over onions in the glass jars and seal."]],"h":[[null,"Try Pickled Red Onions on fish tacos or hamburgers."],[null,"Refrigerate pickled onions until ready to serve. Keeps for 3 weeks in the refrigerator."]]},"3690":{"s":[[null,"Boil eggs to hard-cooked stage."],[null,"To reduce potassium in potatoes, peel potatoes, cut into small pieces, cover with water and bring to a boil. Discard the water and add fresh water. (Skip this part if a low potassium diet is not required.) Boil potatoes until tender but still firm when punctured with a fork."],[null,"While potatoes are cooking, finely chop celery, onion and bell pepper. Peel and chop hard boiled eggs."],[null,"Drain potatoes and place in a bowl. Add vegetables and chopped eggs. Do not stir."],[null,"Mix salad dressing ingredients together; add to potatoes and toss gently."],[null,"Cover and chill until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Dialysis patients on a low potassium diet need to double boil potatoes to lower the potassium content. Skip step #2 if you are not on a low potassium diet."],[null,"If regular mayonnaise is substituted for reduced-fat mayonnaise fat increases to 24 grams per serving. Make this change if you need extra calories."],[null,"Use green or yellow bell peppers if desired, or try jalapeno peppers for a spicy flavor."]]},"5804641":{"s":[["To make the dough","Place the flour into a bowl and make a ‘well’ in the middle. Add the egg, melted butter and hot water."],["To make the dough","Mix together until a dough forms."],["To make the dough","Turn onto a board and knead dough until smooth. Roll into a ball, cover and set aside for 20 minutes."],["To make the filling","Heat 1 tbsp of the oil in a frying pan over medium heat and add the minced garlic and chopped onion. Fry until the onions become translucent."],["To make the filling","Add in the minced beef and fry until browned."],["To make the filling","Add in the grated carrot, black pepper and oregano and cook for a further 3 minutes."],["Assembly","Roll out dough into a 10” (25cm) to 11” (28cm) circle. Cut 12 circles in the dough with a 3” (8cm) round cookie cutter."],["Assembly","Place a heaped teaspoon of filling in the middle of each dough circle. Fold over, stretch and press sides together to form a crescent-shaped dumpling"],["Assembly","In a large saucepan of boiling water, carefully place two or three dumplings in the water. The pierogi will float to the top when done. Remove with a slotted spoon and place onto kitchen paper."],["Assembly","Once boiled, lightly fry the pierogi in the remaining 1 tbsp of olive oil over a medium heat. Fry for 3 minutes on each side until crispy and golden brown."],["Creamy Cheese Sauce","In a pan, on a low heat add the Renastep, cream cheese, mixed herbs and garlic powder and stir until combined."],["Creamy Cheese Sauce","Simmer for 3 minutes until thickened (do not boil)."],["Creamy Cheese Sauce","Divide the cheese sauce over the 4 portions of Pierogi."]],"h":[["Renastep note","Renastep is a Food for Special Medical Purposes and must be used under medical supervision. Renastep is a ready to use feed for the dietary management of kidney disease from 3 years of age onwards. Renastep contains milk (milk protein), fish (tuna oil)."]]},"3605":{"s":[[null,"Finely shred cabbage, finely chop onion and slice mushrooms."],[null,"Place flour in a bowl and make a well in the middle. Add egg, melted margarine and hot water."],[null,"Blend with a pastry knife until a dough forms. Turn onto a board and knead dough until smooth. Roll into a ball, cover and set aside for an hour."],[null,"Put cabbage in a medium saucepan, cover with water, and bring to a boil. Reduce heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes until tender. Drain cabbage and squeeze out extra liquid."],[null,"Sauté chopped onions and mushrooms in a tablespoon of oil until slightly caramelized."],[null,"Combine cabbage with onion and mushrooms. Set aside to cool."],[null,"After cooled, finely chop the vegetable mixture. Add pepper to taste and stir."],[null,"Roll out dough into a 10” to 11” circle. Cut 12 circles in the dough with a round cookie cutter."],[null,"Place a heaping teaspoon of filling in the middle of each dough circle. Fold over, stretch and press sides together to form a crescent-shaped dumpling."],[null,"Drop dumplings, two or three at a time, into a pot of boiling water. Pierogi will float to the top when done. Remove with a slotted spoon."],[null,"Once boiled, lightly fry dumplings in oil for a crispy treat, if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Adjust the hot water for proper consistency of dough. Dough should be smooth and pliable but not sticky."],[null,"To save time, you can use pre-shredded coleslaw cabbage."],[null,"The filling can be prepared ahead and refrigerated overnight, if needed."],[null,"This recipe yields 3 servings, but can easily be increased and extra uncooked pierogi frozen for later."],[null,"Garnish with a drizzle of melted margarine and a dollop of sour cream."]]},"3413":{"s":[[null,"Dice the pimento. In a small bowl combine the whipped cream cheese, pimento, sugar and pepper."],[null,"Spread 1/4-cup of the mixture on bread of choice to make sandwiches."]],"h":[[null,"For additional protein, add 1 scoop of whey protein powder when blending ingredients together."],[null,"The cream cheese is easier to work with when softened, making it easier to spread on the bread."],[null,"If you are making only one sandwich, store remaining pimento cream cheese in the refrigerator for up to 5 days."],[null,"For more variety try different types of bread such as sourdough, rye or whole wheat."]]},"5763741":{"s":[[null,"Finely dice or blend the pineapple."],[null,"Pour the coconut milk and Renastep into a jug."],[null,"Add the pineapple to the jug, mix the pineapple and pour into the lolly mould."],[null,"Allow to freeze for 24 hours."]],"h":[["Renastep note","Renastep is a food for special medical purposes and must be used under medical supervision. Renastep is for the dietary management of kidney disease and is suitable from 3 years of age onwards. Renastep contains Milk (milk protein) and Fish (Tuna Oils)."],["Renastep note","This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutrimen dietary analysis software. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information"]]},"1002963":{"s":[[null,"Cut chicken thighs into two-inch, bite-size pieces. If using bamboo skewers, soak them in water for 1/2 hour to keep them from burning."],[null,"Mix adobo seasoning, oregano, vinegar, olive oil and bay leaves and place in a zip-top bag."],[null,"Add chicken to the marinade. Refrigerate for at least half an hour or overnight."],[null,"Heat the grill and grease the grates once hot."],[null,"Thread chicken onto skewers and place on the hot grill. Brown for 5 minutes on each side."],[null,"Baste skewers with guava barbecue sauce or another low-sodium barbecue sauce and cook for about 4 minutes more."]],"h":[[null,"Keep chicken pieces the same size to ensure even cooking."],[null,"Find recipes for guava barbecue sauce and other low-sodium barbecue sauces on DaVita.com."]]},"2775":{"s":[[null,"Chop bell pepper, onion, and cilantro. Cut cherry tomatoes in half. Shred ginger root."],[null,"Heat oil and when hot add ginger and red onion. Cook until onion is transparent."],[null,"Microwave peppers on high for 6 minutes. Add the peppers to onion mixture. Close the lid of the pan and cook on low for 10 minutes, stirring to avoid burning peppers."],[null,"Add pineapple tidbits and simmer for 2 minutes. Add curry powder and cilantro. Turn the vegetables once and let simmer on low for 2 minutes."],[null,"Garnish with cherry tomatoes and lemon juice before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Serve curry with bread or rice."]]},"3041":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Blend dry cake mix and entire can of undrained pineapple with a mixer until well blended and fluffy."],[null,"Pour mixture into an ungreased 9″ x 13″ cake pan. Bake 25 to 30 minutes until lightly brown on top."],[null,"Cool completely."],[null,"Frost with non-dairy whipped topping. Store in the refrigerator."]],"h":[[null,"For higher calories use pineapple packed in heavy syrup."]]},"2907":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400° F."],[null,"Blend flour, shortening and milk or milk substitute."],[null,"Press onto a 17” X 11” ungreased jelly roll pan."],[null,"Mix pineapple, cornstarch and granulated sugar together."],[null,"Pour over crust and bake for 20 minutes. Let cool."],[null,"Cream together powdered sugar, margarine, cream cheese and vanilla."],[null,"Spread over cooled crust; chill, and then cut into squares."],[null,"Top with diced maraschino cherries if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Use pineapple canned in juice or syrup; both work well in this recipe."]]},"4115872":{"s":[[null,"Cook the rice following the instructions on the package."],[null,"While the rice is cooking, in a small bowl, combine the rice vinegar, water, cornstarch, sugar, garlic and ginger. Set aside."],[null,"In a non-stick frying pan, heat the oil over medium heat. Stir-fry the beef until it turns brown and is thoroughly cooked (4-5 minutes). You may want to sauté the beef in two batches so as not to overload the pan. Set the cooked beef aside."],[null,"In the same pan, stir-fry the red peppers and the celery for 2 minutes. When vegetables are tender, add the pineapple chunks, red pepper flakes, and the cooked beef."],[null,"Pour in the cornstarch mixture from step 2 and stir until the sauce has thickened. Season with extra black pepper, if desired."],[null,"Serve the pineapple beef with the cooked rice and enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"* fresh, frozen or canned (drained)"],[null,"For individuals with CKD not on dialysis, reduce the amount of protein by reducing the amount of beef."],["Adding low-potassium flavor and seasoning to meals","When following a kidney-friendly diet, some common seasonings should be limited. Avoid salt and salt substitutes that replace sodium chloride with potassium chloride when you are on a low-potassium diet. The good news is that you can use plenty of flavorful seasonings without adding unwanted potassium to meals. • Fresh herbs including basil, cilantro, sage, and parsley can be added to dishes to create a variety of flavors. Select fresh over more concentrated dried herbs for low-potassium seasonings. • Spices can enrich the taste and smell of food items. Cinnamon, paprika, turmeric, and ginger add different tastes to meats, vegetables, or other kidney-friendly foods. • Pepper is a low-potassium choice which comes in several different types. Red, black, and white pepper will each add a different kick of flavor to your meal. Looking for more heat and spice? Try cayenne pepper! • Garlic: Fresh, cooked, or roasted garlic can enhance the natural flavor of foods. Mix it with herbs or spices to create more flavors without adding too much potassium."]]},"2779":{"s":[[null,"Set butter out to soften. Drain the pineapple. Chop the cherries."],[null,"With a mixer, beat sugar and butter until light and fluffy. Add eggs and mix well."],[null,"Mix flour and baking powder together."],[null,"Combine sugar and flour mixtures and blend. Add pineapple and cherries and mix to combine. Pour into a greased 9 x 5-inch pan. Bake at 350° F for 1 hour."],[null,"Cool for 10 minutes, then remove loaf from pan and transfer to a wire rack to cool. Cut into 15 slices."]],"h":[[null,"Make extra loaves and freeze until ready to share or enjoy."],[null,"To reduce carbohydrates use a granular sugar substitute."]]},"3249":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F."],[null,"Combine flour, sugar, soda and eggs."],[null,"Drain juice or syrup from pineapple into above mixture, stirring to combine. Beat to mix; batter will be thick."],[null,"Fold in pineapple, mixing well."],[null,"Pour into a greased and floured 13” x 9” x 2” cake pan and bake for 35-40 minutes, or until cake springs back when touched."],[null,"To make frosting, beat together butter and cream cheese."],[null,"Gradually stir in powdered sugar and vanilla. Beat until smooth."],[null,"Spread frosting over cake as soon as it is removed from oven, while still hot."]],"h":[[null,"For a lighter dessert serve cake without the icing—it still tastes great."],[null,"This cake is a great source of calories if you need to gain weight."]]},"2436":{"s":[[null,"Drain pineapple, reserving juice."],[null,"Rub chicken with garlic and thyme, then sprinkle with black pepper to taste."],[null,"Heat oil over high heat in a non-stick skillet. Brown chicken on both sides then reduce heat to medium."],[null,"Combine 2 tablespoons of the reserved pineapple juice with cornstarch; set aside."],[null,"Combine honey and mustard; stir into skillet with remaining pineapple juice."],[null,"Spoon sauce over chicken. Cover and simmer 15 minutes."],[null,"Stir cornstarch mixture into skillet with chicken and sauce."],[null,"Add pineapple rings. Cook, stirring, until sauce boils and thickens."],[null,"Serve 3 ounces chicken per plate with 1/2 cup rice, 1/4 of the sauce and 1/4 of the pineapple for each serving."]],"h":[[null,"Pineapple chunks can be used instead of slices, if desired."],[null,"For a lower protein dish try boneless, skinless chicken thighs instead of chicken breast ."],[null,"For a lower carbohydrate dish omit the rice and serve with a non-starchy vegetable such as summer squash, carrots or green beans."]]},"6260150":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, mix the Greek yogurt, sugar substitute, and coconut extract. Adjust the sweetness to your taste."],[null,"In serving glasses or bowls, begin by adding a layer yogurt mixture."],[null,"Add a layer of pineapple on top of the yogurt."],[null,"Sprinkle the almonds over the pineapple."],[null,"Repeat the layers until your glass is filled. Serve cold."]],"h":[]},"4028523":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F. Spray loaf pan with non-stick cooking spray."],[null,"In a mixing bowl, add eggs, sugar, oil and vanilla. Whisk together to combine."],[null,"In a separate mixing bowl, sift together the flour, baking soda, ginger and cinnamon."],[null,"Add the dry ingredients to the egg mixture. Mix well."],[null,"Add crushed pineapple and frozen cranberries and mix to combine."],[null,"Pour pineapple mixture into loaf pan (4\"× 8\")."],[null,"Bake an hour and 15 minutes or until a tooth pick inserted in the center of the loaf comes out clean. Remove from oven and cool."],[null,"Cover and store at room temperature."]],"h":[["Incorporating pineapple into your kidney diet","Choosing foods with a variety of flavors and textures is important to keeping your kidney diet interesting. Fruit offers a choice of flavors, fiber, and vitamins and is a nutrient-dense food. Recent studies have shown that diets higher in fruits and vegetables may be good for the health of kidneys, but more research is needed for specific recommendations. Pineapple is an excellent lower-potassium food for your kidney diet. A one-cup portion of fresh pineapple chunks contains less than 200mg of potassium and minimal amounts of sodium and phosphorus. Pineapple can be incorporated in many different dishes. Use pineapple as a breakfast topping or as part of a low-potassium fruit cup. Top sandwiches with pineapple to create a different flavor and texture in place of high-potassium tomatoes. Or add pineapple to stir-fry dishes or meals in the slow cooker to make your meals more interesting. Desserts like muffins or smoothies are another great way to add fresh pineapple flavor."]]},"1950":{"s":[[null,"Sprinkle both sides of chicken thighs with pepper and garlic powder."],[null,"Heat oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Add chicken to skillet and cook 2-3 minutes on each side, until browned."],[null,"Transfer chicken to a 4-quart crock pot® coated with cooking spray."],[null,"Drain pineapple juice in a measuring cup. If less than 1 cup, add water to make 1 cup. Stir the juice into skillet drippings, and scrape to loosen browned chicken bits. Remove from heat, and stir in brown sugar, soy sauce and Tabasco sauce. Add 1 cup of the pineapple chunks. Pour mixture over chicken thighs in crock pot. Cover and cook on low heat setting for 3 hours."],[null,"Remove chicken from crock pot and turn heat to high setting. Combine cornstarch and 3 tablespoons water in a small bowl. Stir into sauce in the crock pot. Cook 2 minutes or until sauce thickens, stirring constantly with a whisk. Add green onions and stir to coat."],[null,"Serve each chicken thigh over 1/2 cup rice."]],"h":[[null,"Sauce may not thicken in the Crock-pot if the temperature is not high enough. If not thickened after 2-3 minutes pour sauce into a sauce pan and heat over medium heat, stirring until thickened. Add back to crock-pot with chicken and pineapple."],[null,"Chicken thighs vary in size and weight. We made this recipe using a 1-1/2 pound package of six boneless, skinless chicken thighs, about 4 ounces each uncooked. For a lower protein diet cut the chicken thighs in half ( 2 ounces) or use smaller thighs if available."],[null,"There will be approximately 1 cup of pineapple tidbits left. Eat as a snack or dessert the next day or try another pineapple recipe."]]},"6169011":{"s":[[null,"Lightly crush the mint leaves in your hand to help release their flavor. Add the mint, pineapple, and water to a pitcher. Refrigerate overnight before serving to fully infuse the flavors."]],"h":[]},"3061":{"s":[[null,"Mix drained pineapple and protein powder well, fold in the whipped topping."],[null,"Place a single layer of graham cracker squares on a cookie sheet and spread about 2 tablespoons topping mixture on each cracker."],[null,"Place another graham cracker square on top and place cookie sheet in the freezer."],[null,"When well frozen, wrap individually in plastic wrap and store them in an airtight container in the freezer."]],"h":[[null,"Some whipped toppings have phosphorus additives. Look at the ingredients list to be sure phosphorus is not added."],[null,"A 14.4 ounce box of graham crackers contains about 27 rectangle sheets."],[null,"Protein powder can vary in protein, potassium, phosphorus and sodium. You may talk to your dietitian to see which one would be appropriate for you."]]},"6018266":{"s":[[null,"Place all the ingredients in a blender and blend until smooth."],[null,"Place the sorbet in a container or into popsicle molds and freeze immediately."]],"h":[]},"9410019":{"s":[[null,"Dice and chop all the ingredients and add them to a mixing bowl. Then squeeze the fresh lime juice on top and mix well to evenly distribute."],[null,"Taste and add 1/8 teaspoon of salt, if needed, or salt to your taste. Mix well and refrigerate for 1 hour or serve right away."]],"h":[[null,"For less heat , remove the seeds and membranes of your pepper before chopping. Wear gloves when handling spicy peppers , and make sure to thoroughly wash your hands when you’re done. Avoid touching your eyes and face! Let your pico rest in the fridge for 1 hour before serving to give the flavours time to blend nicely."]]},"3528":{"s":[[null,"Mix all ingredients in a large punch bowl."],[null,"Serve in a punch cup, or any clear glass."],[null,"Add a piece of sliced pineapple on the rim of the glass, if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Chill ingredients before assembling. Adjust ice as needed."],[null,"Use diet lemon-lime soda for a diabetes-friendly lower carbohydrate punch. Count as 12 grams carbohydrate, one Carbohydrate Choice."],[null,"This is a quick punch to make, and it is very refreshing. It’s great for any last-minute preparation for a party or to serve unexpected guests since most of the ingredients have a long shelf life."],[null,"Pour the soda in the mixture slowly to prevent foam."]]},"3153":{"s":[[null,"Drain pineapple and reserve juice."],[null,"Mix together the pineapple, rice, reserved pineapple juice & water in a saucepan."],[null,"Bring to a boil, cover and reduce heat. Simmer for 20 to 25 minutes, until all of the water is absorbed and the rice is tender."]],"h":[[null,"Serve with any of the curry recipes."]]},"3208":{"s":[[null,"Mince onion, garlic and jalapeno. Chop cilantro."],[null,"Drain pineapple and place in non-reactive bowl. Add other ingredients and mix well."],[null,"Refrigerate several hours or overnight to blend flavors."]],"h":[[null,"Serve Pineapple Salsa on tacos or fish or chicken entrees."]]},"3734":{"s":[[null,"Shred cabbage and carrots and combine in a 2 quart bowl."],[null,"Add crushed pineapple with juice and dried cranberries to bowl."],[null,"Mix slaw ingredients together and chill in refrigerator at least 30 minutes before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Shred cabbage into coleslaw size pieces using a food processor or chop with a sharp knife."],[null,"2-1/2 cups shredded cabbage is approximately 3/4 of a small head of cabbage."]]},"5492935":{"s":[[null,"Place all the ingredients in a blender and blend until smooth."]],"h":[["Renastep note","Renastep is a Food for Special Medical Purposes and must be used under medical supervision. Renastep is a ready to use feed for the dietary management of kidney disease from 3 years of age onwards. Renastep contains milk and fish. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information."],["Renastep note","This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease."]]},"3669":{"s":[[null,"Cut squash and zucchini into 1 inch cubes, dice the green bell pepper. Place squash in a 3-1/2 or 4 quart slow cooker."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix the pineapple, green bell pepper, cinnamon, brown sugar and butter."],[null,"Spoon mixture over squash and mix well."],[null,"Cover and cook on low heat setting for 6-7 hours or until squash is tender. Stir gently to mix."],[null,"Serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"Diabetics may use Splenda® brown sugar substitute in equal amounts."]]},"3618":{"s":[[null,"Open the can of pineapple and drain."],[null,"Place pineapple chunks on a baking sheet in a single layer and freeze."],[null,"When chunks are frozen, place in food processor or blender."],[null,"Add limeade and lime juice. Process until well blended and fluffy in texture."],[null,"Serve immediately or freeze in 1/2-cup servings."]],"h":[[null,"Protein powder can be added for a more nutritious snack/dessert. Mix it into the lime juice before adding to the processed pineapple."],[null,"You can substitute 16 ounces frozen pineapple chunks for the canned pineapple and skip steps 1 and 2."]]},"3339":{"s":[[null,"Dice pineapple."],[null,"Chop mint leaves."],[null,"Add all ingredients to a pitcher."],[null,"Refrigerator overnight before serving."]],"h":[[null,"If you are on limited fluids, adjust the portion size to meet your needs."],[null,"After flavors develop you can pour into ice cube trays to make flavored ice."]]},"2405":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375° F."],[null,"Remove seeds from jalapeno pepper; coarsely chop cilantro and onion."],[null,"In a food processor, combine cilantro, jalapeno and onion. Pulse until blended, but not pureed."],[null,"Cut tomatoes into quarters and add to mixture. Pulse until tomatoes are in small pieces."],[null,"Add drained pineapple and pulse until mixture is thickened, but not pureed."],[null,"Add lemon zest. Mix until blended."],[null,"Brush flour tortillas with melted margarine."],[null,"Cut each tortilla into 8 pie-shaped pieces. Place on a lightly sprayed baking sheet."],[null,"Bake 10-12 minutes until tortillas are firm. Remove from oven and let cool."],[null,"Serve baked tortilla pieces as dipping scoops for salsa."]],"h":[[null,"Leftover salsa will keep up to 4 days in the refrigerator."],[null,"Serve salsa with kidney-friendly tacos or burritos."]]},"9847862":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 425℉/218℃ convection bake. Slice the top and bottom stems off your beet and then cut it in half. Place it cut-side down in a foil pocket on a baking tray. Fold the sides of your foil up to keep the juices in the pocket and avoid a mess. Then bake the beet until fork tender, approx. 30-45 minutes. (Bake time will vary according to the size of your beet, and how fresh it is.)"],[null,"Remove it from the oven and let it cool slightly. Then preheat your griddle to medium heat and peel the beet halves. The skin will peel easily after being roasted."],[null,"Add the beet with all remaining ingredients to your blender and process until smooth. Then pour the batter from your blender onto your hot griddle, making pancakes that are about 4 inches in diameter. Cook for 3-4 minutes, until bubbly on top and the edges appear set. Then flip and cook an additional 3-4 minutes until cooked through. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Leave the peel on to roast your beets. Removing the peel is tedious and messy when beets are raw and they peel very easily once roasted."],[null,"Roast, rather than boil , if time permits. The result is naturally sweeter beet pancakes. (That means less or no syrup needed!)"],[null,"If you’re cooking your pink pancakes in batches, the batter will thicken as it sits in the blender. If needed, add another 1-2 tablespoons of milk and re-blend for a few seconds before cooking the next batch."],[null,"Leftovers keep refrigerated for up to 3 days or freeze them airtight for up to 3 months."]]},"7178593":{"s":[[null,"Peel pears and core from the base using a small knife or vegetable peeler. Trim the base flat so the pears stand up."],[null,"Add the pears to a pan with cordial diluted 3:1, making sure they are fully immersed."],[null,"Add star anise and the cinnamon stick, then bring to the boil. Turn down the heat and simmer for 20-30 minutes until the pears are tender."],[null,"Remove from pan and set aside. Boil the liquid for 10-15 minutes until the liquid is reduced to about 200ml, then remove the star anise and cinnamon stick."],[null,"Place the pears on a serving dish and drizzle with the sauce. Serve with a dollop of low-fat yogurt or non-dairy alternative."]],"h":[[null,"Works very well with apples in place of pears."],[null,"Try using a different cordial or add a few slices of fresh ginger or 2 cloves."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6411039":{"s":[[null,"Make the Garlicky Cilantro Lime Dressing."],[null,"In a large salad bowl combine the yellow bell pepper, cucumber, pinto beans and rice. Gently mix in the queso fresco and the dressing."],[null,"Divide spinach between 4 bowls. Top with the pinto bean and rice mix and toss."],[null,"Bulk Cooking Dry Pinto Beans: Add 1 lb (16 oz.) dry pinto beans to a large pot of boiling water (at least 6 cups of water). Boil rapidly for 2 minutes. Remove from heat and cover. Let sit for 1 hour. Drain and rinse beans. Add 6 fresh cups of water. Bring to a boil, then reduce to a simmer for one hour or until the beans are soft but not split. Makes 5 cups cooked beans. These beans can be used in any recipe calling for cooked or canned beans. Store in an airtight container in the refrigerator for 7 days or package in freezer bags in one cup increments for up to 6 months."],[null,"Bulk Cooking Brown Rice: Add 1 lb (16 oz.) of long grain (not instant) brown rice to a large soup pot with 5 cups of water. Bring to a boil then reduce to a simmer. Cover and simmer for 45 minutes or until all liquid is absorbed. Makes 10 cups cooked brown rice. This rice can be used in any recipe calling for cooked brown rice. Store in an airtight container in the refrigerator for 7 days or package in freezer bags in one cup increments for up to 6 months."]],"h":[]},"2769":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Mix dry ingredients together in a large bowl. Add oil, water, eggs and pumpkin. Stir until well blended. Add nuts, if desired."],[null,"Pour batter into loaf pans, lightly sprayed with nonstick cooking spray."],[null,"To makes 3 regular-sized loaves, bake for 1 hour or until a toothpick inserted in the middle comes out clean. To make 6 mini loaves, bake 45 minutes."],[null,"Cool loaves on a rack for 10 minutes in pans; then invert, remove from pans and turn right side up and continue cooling. Wrap in aluminum foil when totally cool."]],"h":[[null,"One cup chopped pecans (optional) added to this recipe increases potassium to 70 milligrams and phosphorus to 40 milligrams."],[null,"One cup walnuts (optional) added to this recipe will increase potassium to 86 milligrams and phosphorus to 57 milligrams."],[null,"Make loaves ahead and freeze until ready to share or enjoy."]]},"7843879":{"s":[[null,"Slice the chicken breasts into 2-3 pieces, depending on size, to create 1cm thick slices."],[null,"Place the chicken slices in a food bag and add the olive oil, chillies, garlic, paprika and lime juice. Mix well so the chicken is coated. Set aside for 15 minutes or place in the fridge and leave overnight."],[null,"Heat your grill, barbecue or griddle pan and add the chicken. Turn over after 3 minutes and cook for another 3 minutes. Check it's cooked through, ensuring there is no pink meat in the middle. Place on a plate."],[null,"Finally, cut the lime in half and pop it, cut-side down, onto the griddle for a couple of minutes. Serve with the chicken."]],"h":[[null,"You could also use this piri piri marinade on turkey escalopes, too."],[null,"For a veggie version, cook and cool large chunks of vegetables such as carrots, beetroot, sweet potatoes, potatoes or butternut squash and marinate them in the piri piri mixture before grilling or barbecuing."],[null,"To freeze, wrap in foil/greaseproof inside freezer bags and label. They'll keep for up to 3 months."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"6697521":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400 degrees F."],[null,"In a shallow dish, combine pistachios and flour. In another shallow dish, add egg whites."],[null,"Dip one side of the salmon in egg whites and then press into pistachio mixture."],[null,"Place fillets nut side up on nonstick baking sheet."],[null,"Repeat for remaining three fillets. Spray top of fillets with cooking spray."],[null,"Bake for 25 minutes."]],"h":[]},"9349945":{"s":[[null,"Add the pistachios, basil, lime juice, and garlic to the bowl of your food processor and process until combined and mostly smooth. Then taste for salt and pepper, adjust as needed, and add water if needed to thin out the sauce."],[null,"Serve as a dip with veggies, crostini, crackers, and/or breadsticks. Or use it as a sauce with pasta or vegetable noodles."]],"h":[[null,"Use a food processor for a finely chopped texture."],[null,"For a smoother texture use a blender."],[null,"Choose any fresh herbs you prefer , but keep the same ratio."],[null,"This recipe is easily doubled, tripled, or more . Especially useful during harvest time when you have plenty of fresh herbs in the garden to use up."],[null,"If using your pesto for pasta, add a generous pinch of salt to your pasta water for the best texture and flavour. Here's a handy guide to help you salt your water perfectly each time"]]},"6262722":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6871291":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F. Coat a baking sheet with cooking spray. Set aside."],[null,"Brush each pita with some of the olive oil, using the whole tablespoon."],[null,"Drizzle each pita with 2 tsp balsamic vinegar."],[null,"Top each pita with 1/4 cup red onion, 1/2 tbsp olives, 1/2 cup spinach, 1/4 cup artichokes, 1/2 cup chicken, and half of the feta cheese."],[null,"Sprinkle the top of each pita with dried oregano. Place on the prepared baking sheet."],[null,"Bake for 15 minutes. Cut into quarters and serve."]],"h":[]},"6621196":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425°F (218°C)."],[null,"Remove your CAULIPOWER® pizza crust from the box and plastic wrapping, and place it on a clean surface."],[null,"Spread the pesto sauce evenly over the CAULIPOWER® pizza crust."],[null,"Top with peach, fennel, red onion and parmesan and bake for 13 to 16 minutes."],[null,"Remove it from the oven and add arugula and sliced almonds, and drizzle balsamic glaze over the pizza."]],"h":[]},"3416":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl combine the water, yeast and a pinch of sugar; stir gently. Let mixture sit for a few minutes to activate (it will bubble)."],[null,"In a mixing bowl combine the flour, remaining 1 tablespoon sugar, salt and 2 tablespoons olive oil; stir well. Add the yeast mixture to the flour mixture; stir well."],[null,"Knead the dough. Use a mixer with a dough attachment or knead on a floured surface until smooth and easily stretched. Oil the bottom and sides of a bowl and lay the dough inside. Loosely cover the bowl with a dish towel or paper towel."],[null,"Place the covered bowl on the stovetop and let the dough rise until double in size for 1-1/2 to 2 hours. Punch the dough down and divide it into 5 equal parts."],[null,"Roll out each piece of pizza dough into a 10-inch circle or rectangular shape to prepare for pizza toppings."]],"h":[[null,"If you are making only 1 pizza you can refrigerate the extra dough for up to 3 days or freeze for up to 2 months. Freeze each part in a separate freezer bag. Thaw in the refrigerator when ready to use."],[null,"Roll each pizza dough into 10-inch round or rectangular shape to make 3 to 4 servings of pizza with toppings."],[null,"Nutrient analysis is for 1 pizza dough divided into 5 servings. The actual amount may vary depending on how many servings are in your pizza."]]},"6893756":{"s":[[null,"Place all dry ingredients in the bowl of your food processor. Pulse a few times to blend well."],[null,"With the machine running, add 1 cup of water in a slow and steady stream. The dough should form a ball and clean the sides of the food processor. If it seems too dry, add more water, 1 tablespoon at a time. The dough is perfect when it is no longer sticky and feels smooth. If it is too sticky or wet, you can add more flour 1 tablespoon at a time."],[null,"Place dough in a large bowl with extra virgin olive oil. Turn dough to completely cover with oil and then cover tightly with plastic wrap and a cloth towel."],[null,"Let dough rise in a warm place for at least one hour. A good place to rise is in the oven with the oven off and the oven light on."],[null,"After the dough doubles in size, punch it down and let it rise again for as long as possible, at least one hour. I am a huge fan of the longer rise for lighter dough, especially when using whole-wheat flour."]],"h":[]},"7432104":{"s":[[null,"Put the onion, pepper and garlic in a small non-stick saucepan. Spray with a couple of pumps of low-calorie cooking spray and cook for a few minutes until softened. Stir in the fresh tomatoes, canned tomatoes, tomato purée and oregano and simmer for 5 minutes. Set aside."],[null,"Preheat your oven to 220°C/fan 200°C/gas 7."],[null,"Cut the chicken breast in half horizontally, being careful not to cut it all the way through. Fold it open to create a butterfly shape."],[null,"Spray a non-stick frying pan with a couple of pumps of low-calorie cooking spray and put it over a medium heat. Add the chicken and cook until browned on both sides. Put the chicken on a non-stick baking tray and bake for 15-20 minutes or until cooked through and no pink flesh is visible (the juices should run clear when you insert a skewer into the thickest part of the chicken)."],[null,"Remove the chicken from the oven and spread the tomato mixture on top. Sprinkle over the cheese and put the cherry tomato on top. Cook for a further 5 minutes, until the cheese melts."],[null,"Sprinkle with the basil and serve hot with homemade potato wedges baked in the oven with the skin on, and a big crispy green salad."]],"h":[]},"6163468":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F."],[null,"Top the pita bread with sauce, olives, peppers, artichokes, shallot and Italian cheese."],[null,"Bake in the oven until the cheese melts and the pita is crisp, 7-8 minutes."],[null,"Remove from the oven and top with feta cheese and fresh basil."]],"h":[]},"6270488":{"s":[[null,"Add the unsweetened coconut milk, pineapple, banana, yogurt, and flaxseed to a blender and blend until smooth."],[null,"Pour into two glasses and enjoy immediately."]],"h":[]},"3670":{"s":[[null,"Add pasteurized liquid egg whites to greased fry pan."],[null,"Cook on medium heat, cover or flip over."]],"h":[[null,"Season with your favorite low-sodium herb seasoning blend."],[null,"Use butter instead of oil for extra flavor."],[null,"Make a sandwich or wrap or eat as a meat replacement with vegetables and starch."]]},"6390581":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6274572":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6105928":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6409832":{"s":[],"h":[]},"7249160":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 190°C/170°C fan oven/gas 5. Line a large baking tray with non-stick baking paper."],[null,"Mash half of the tomatoes with a fork and spoon into a bowl. Roughly chop the remaining tomatoes and add to the bowl with the red onion, pineapple, chilli, coriander, lime juice to taste and Jerk seasoning. Stir well until combined. Chill for 20 minutes to allow the flavours to mature."],[null,"Peel the plantains and slice 1/8-inch thick. Toss in the oil, garlic granules and black pepper and spread in a single layer onto the prepared baking tray."],[null,"Bake for 15–18 minutes until completely baked and cooked. Allow to cool and sprinkle with the cayenne pepper, if liked."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6530550":{"s":[[null,"Mix the yogurt and chia seeds. Refrigerate overnight. Mix in 1/8 tsp cinnamon."],[null,"On a very large platter, place the strawberries in the top row to form the top of a rainbow pattern."],[null,"Place the cantaloupe cubes as the second row below the strawberries. Continue this process with the pineapple, going through the blackberries, to make the rainbow pattern."]],"h":[]},"6114948":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F. Grease a muffin tin or line with paper liners."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine flour, sugar substitute, baking powder, baking soda, cinnamon, and salt."],[null,"In another bowl, mix applesauce, milk, eggs, oil, and vanilla."],[null,"Add wet ingredients to dry ingredients and stir until just combined. Fold in chopped plums. Spoon batter into muffin cups, filling two-thirds full."],[null,"Bake for 15–20 minutes or until a toothpick comes out clean. Allow to cool for 5 minutes in the pan, then transfer to a wire rack to cool completely."]],"h":[]},"6115966":{"s":[[null,"Season with salt and pepper to taste."],[null,"Add walnuts and goat cheese. Drizzle with balsamic vinaigrette and toss gently to coat."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine salad greens, plums, and cucumber."]],"h":[]},"6991688":{"s":[[null,"Fill a wide, shallow pan with water and bring it to a gentle simmer. Add a splash of vinegar to the water."],[null,"Crack each egg into a small bowl."],[null,"Carefully slide each egg into the simmering water, one at a time. Poach for 3–4 minutes for a runny yolk, or longer for a firmer yolk."],[null,"While the eggs are poaching, heat oil in a separate skillet over medium heat."],[null,"Add chopped onions and cook until softened, about 5 minutes."],[null,"Stir in minced garlic and cook for an additional 30 seconds."],[null,"Add the chopped mixed greens to the skillet and sauté until wilted."],[null,"Season the greens with​ salt and ​pepper."],[null,"Remove the poached eggs from the water using a slotted spoon and place them on a plate lined with paper towels to drain excess water."],[null,"Serve the poached eggs on a bed of sautéed greens with whole-grain bread on the side."]],"h":[]},"7482887":{"s":[[null,"Put the apple juice, cinnamon stick and star anise in a saucepan and heat gently. Add the apples, pears, plums and figs. Simmer for around 20 minutes until the fruit is tender, adding the blackberries for the last 5 minutes. Remove the fruit with a slotted spoon and set aside. Continue cooking the liquid until it reduces to a sticky syrup. Remove the cinnamon and star anise, then pour the syrup over the fruit."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 200°C, fan 180°C, gas mark 6. Mix the oats, flour, sugar and ground cinnamon together in a bowl. Rub in the spread using your fingers, until the mix resembles coarse breadcrumbs."],[null,"Put the fruit into a 20cm x 22cm dish. Scatter over the crumble and bake for 20-25 minutes, until golden brown. Serve with 1tbsp Greek yogurt per serving."]],"h":[]},"3066":{"s":[[null,"Mix cinnamon and sugar in a small bowl."],[null,"Cut pears in half and using a spoon scoop out seeds and stem."],[null,"Make a thin slice across round part of pear, so that it lays flat in baking dish."],[null,"Place pears skin side down in a baking dish and sprinkle tops with cinnamon and sugar mix."],[null,"Place 1 teaspoon butter in the seed hole of each pear."],[null,"Pour juice in bottom of pan."],[null,"Cover with foil and bake at 350° F approximately 30 minutes or until pear is soft when poked with fork."]],"h":[[null,"If your baking dish is shallow you may need less juice. The juice should only come halfway up the side of the pears."],[null,"Pour juice over pears before serving if desired."],[null,"For people with diabetes use low calorie cranberry juice and subar substitute instead of sugar."]]},"7463414":{"s":[[null,"Add the salmon steaks to a small pan, cover with boiling water and simmer gently for 5 minutes with a lid on. Turn off the heat, leave to stand for 3 minutes, or until the salmon is thoroughly cooked through, then drain and set aside to cool."],[null,"Once the salmon has cooled down, remove the skin and any brown fat from the fish."],[null,"For the sauce, roughly chop the watercress and blend with the yogurt, lemon zest and half the lemon juice."],[null,"Warm the blinis in a dry frying pan for 1–2 minutes on each side."],[null,"Spread each blini with a little cream cheese and flake the salmon on top. Drizzle with the remaining lemon juice and top with blobs of the watercress sauce."]],"h":[[null,"To save time, you can cook the salmon the day before and refrigerate it overnight, ready for when you assemble your blinis the next day."],[null,"Try mixing it up a bit by serving a batch of blinis topped with prawn or herring and some low-fat cream cheese, as well."],[null,"Garnish with some lemon zest before serving."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"7660536":{"s":[[null,"Put the grape juice, cinnamon stick, cardamom pods and vanilla essence into a large pan with 300ml water."],[null,"Heat gently being careful not to boil. This will only take a few minutes. Add the pears. Cover and simmer gently for 10–12 minutes or until the pears are softened slightly."],[null,"Serve the pears hot with a little of the cooking liquid."]],"h":[[null,"Serve with 0% fat Greek yogurt to cut back on fat and calories."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"2471":{"s":[[null,"Cook rice according to package instructions."],[null,"Cut fish into bite sized pieces. Very lightly poach fish in a non-stick pan using a small amount of water. Do not overcook. Drain and let cool."],[null,"Thinly slice green onion; cube cucumber and avocado; and shred carrot."],[null,"Combine fish in a bowl with green onion, lime juice, low-sodium soy sauce and sesame oil. Marinate for 10 minutes."],[null,"Mix hot sauce into mayonnaise."],[null,"Cut nori sheet into small pieces. Mix nori pieces and rice vinegar into the cooked rice. Divide into two serving bowls. Let cool for 10 minutes."],[null,"Top each rice bowl evenly with cucumber, avocado, carrot, fish mixture and spicy mayo. Sprinkle with sesame seeds."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute a different type of fish per preference, like tuna or salmon."],[null,"Bluefin tuna and farm-raised salmon are lower in potassium than wild salmon or yellowfin tuna."]]},"4218425":{"s":[[null,"In a medium microwave-safe dish, combine couscous, chicken broth, and canola oil. Cook for 2 minutes in the microwave, or until water has been absorbed. Fluff the couscous with a fork and let cool."],[null,"Prepare the sauce: Add all sauce ingredients to a small bowl and whisk. Add a bit of water if you prefer the sauce to be more liquid."],[null,"Assemble two poke bowls: Divide couscous, vegetables, fruits, and shrimp among the two bowls. Top with sauce and garnish with green onion, cilantro, and sesame seeds."]],"h":[[null,"* Check the label and avoid shrimp with phosphate additives. Choose shrimp with lower than 20% DV for sodium."],[null,"PLEASE NOTE: This recipe is higher in potassium and portion size is important. Check with your registered dietitian to see how this recipe can be included in your diet. * For CKD Non-Dialysis: To lower protein, consider decreasing the amount of shrimp. Check with your registered dietitian how this recipe can be included in your diet."],["What to look for when choosing frozen fish and shellfish","Fish and shellfish are an excellent source of protein and thus a good substitute for red meat in your diet. They also provide several vitamins and minerals as well as healthy fats. These nutrients are important to maintain brain and eye health. Eating more fish and shellfish has also been linked to a lower risk of heart disease and certain cancers. Buying fresh fish and shellfish would be ideal but may not be realistic for most people. Buying them frozen is likely more practical and will provide more affordable options. Frozen fish and shellfish often have solutions added to them to keep them moist, tender and flavorful. These solutions may contain unwanted sodium and phosphorus. For example, a common additive to shrimp is sodium tripolyphosphate or STPP. Read labels to see if this has been added. When possible, choose shrimp without additives. If this is not possible, thaw shrimp in cold water, drain and rinse with cold water to help remove some of the STPP. Be sure to cook fish and shellfish in healthful ways. Season with herbs such as garlic powder, parsley, black pepper, dill or smoked paprika. Instead of deep frying or pan frying try baking, broiling, sauteing, searing or steaming. Pair it with vegetables, beans or whole grains or add it to a salad or pasta."]]},"5966316":{"s":[[null,"Bring the stock to a boil in a saucepan and add the polenta in a steady stream. Cook, stirring continuously, for 5 minutes (take care as polenta bubbles furiously)."],[null,"Take off the heat and stir in the parmesan (if using)."],[null,"Spoon the mixture onto the tray and flatten into a large rectangular shape, about 5-10 mm thick (depending on how thick you want your chips!) using the back of the wooden spoon. Leave to cool for 10-15 minutes."],[null,"Add the chips to a baking tray and brush with oil. Bake in the oven on a medium heat (180ºC) for 15 minutes until golden brown. Alternatively, shallow fry the chips in oil, frying lightly and evenly on all 4 sides. Serve hot and enjoy! This recipe is taken from the Kidney Friendly Cookbook produced by Dietitians and Dietetic Support Workers at a Paediatric Renal Unit in the UK. Please check with your Dietitian or Doctor that this recipe is suitable for you."]],"h":[]},"7459232":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200°C/ gas 6. Add 1.1⁄2 tbsp olive oil to a bowl with the onions, peppers and courgettes. Mix well, spread out on a baking tray and roast for 25-30 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the boiling water to a large pan and gradually mix in the polenta, stirring with a wooden spoon for around 5 minutes. Then, transfer into a lightly oiled 2lb loaf tin (approx 22cm x 11cm), and flatten the top with back of a spoon. Set aside for 5 minutes."],[null,"Add the tinned tomatoes, garlic, oregano and chilli flakes to a pan, stir together and simmer gently for 5 minutes."],[null,"Turn the polenta out onto a chopping board and cut into 1.1/2-cm thick slices, then cook on a hot griddle pan or under the grill for around 3-4 minutes on each side until lightly golden."],[null,"To serve, drizzle a slice of the polenta with a spoonful of the tomato and herb sauce, scatter some of the roasted vegetables on the top and finish with a few fresh basil leaves. Add a small handful of grated cheese, if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Use any vegetables of your choice to create a variation of this dish. Aubergines and mushrooms work well."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Freeze the polenta and vegetables separately. Then defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"1002918":{"s":[[null,"Rinse chicken, remove skin and cook for about 20 minutes."],[null,"Wash eggplant and zucchini and, without peeling, cut into pieces about 1 centimeter wide. Set aside."],[null,"Peel onion and cut into squares slightly smaller than the eggplant; set aside as well."],[null,"Wash bell pepper, cut in half, remove seeds and cut into small squares. Set aside."],[null,"Dip ripe tomato in boiling water for a few seconds, peel and finely chop. Set aside."],[null,"Peel and crush garlic cloves and set aside."],[null,"Heat 1 tablespoon oil in a pot. Add chopped onion. Let it soften without browning too much, stirring occasionally."],[null,"Add eggplant to the pot and fry for about 2 minutes over medium heat."],[null,"Add bell pepper and let it soften slightly. Stir occasionally with a wooden spoon."],[null,"Add the precooked chicken."],[null,"Add zucchini and crushed garlic and cook 1 or 2 minutes over low heat, then immediately add chopped tomato and stir again. Add pepper and let everything cook over low heat for about 15 minutes or until vegetables are cooked."]],"h":[[null,"Don’t add the eggplant and zucchini too soon, or they will lose their texture and flavor."],[null,"To reduce the potassium in this recipe, you can dice the eggplant and zucchini, then soak them in warm water for 2 to 4 hours. Discard the water and continue with the recipe."]]},"1002629":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 177° C. Coat baking sheet with cooking spray."],[null,"Place chicken breasts on the baking sheet."],[null,"Finely mince garlic."],[null,"In a small container, combine pepper, olive oil, lemon juice and garlic. Mix together well."],[null,"Spread lemon mixture over the chicken breasts."],[null,"Sprinkle paprika evenly over the chicken breasts and bake for 35 minutes or until chicken reaches an internal temperature of 165° F or 74° C."],[null,"Let chicken breasts rest, covered with aluminum foil, for 10-15 minutes before slicing or serving."]],"h":[[null,"Natural seasonings such as oregano or bay leaf can be added for even more flavor."]]},"4806925":{"s":[[null,"Cut the chicken breasts into 1-inch squares."],[null,"Smash the garlic and mix it with the cut chicken breasts to marinate."],[null,"Heat the oil in a large pan at medium heat and add the cut chicken breasts."],[null,"Sauté the chicken until it turns brown."],[null,"Add the chopped onion and sauté for one minute, then add the bell peppers, broccoli, squash and sliced carrots and sauté for an additional 6 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"*Salmon can be substituted for chicken in this dish if desired."],[null,"Nutrition info for chicken version only."]]},"6270743":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375°F convection or 400°F in a conventional oven. Place the bread crumbs, garlic and stress-free Italian seasoning mix in the food processor. Process until well combined."],[null,"Place the flour in a pie dish. Place the eggs and egg whites in a separate pie dish. Place the bread crumb mixture in a third pie dish."],[null,"Line a large baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Dip the chicken in flour and coat it on all sides, then in egg and then in bread crumbs. Coat evenly. Place it on a baking sheet lined with parchment paper. If you have time, refrigerate the chicken for a while before cooking it."],[null,"Bake the chicken for 45 minutes until crispy and well browned. Serve with picnic-style condiments or salads. It can be made ahead and frozen to reheat in a very hot oven. Thaw before reheating."]],"h":[]},"3888":{"s":[[null,"Peel and cut potato into a large dice. Boil potatoes until soft in a large pot of water. Drain water and set aside. Dry the chicken thighs thoroughly with paper towels. Cut into two-inch cubes and season with adobo."],[null,"Place a pot on medium high heat and add oil. Add chicken in one layer and brown, turning once."],[null,"Once brown, remove chicken from pot and set aside. Large dice the onion and finely chop garlic. Add onion and garlic and cook for 2 minutes on low heat."],[null,"Large dice the green pepper. Add the tomato sauce and bell pepper and bring to a boil."],[null,"Cut carrot into 1/4-inch rounds. Add the Sazon, bay leaves, oregano, olives, carrots, and chicken broth. Bring to a boil."],[null,"Add the chicken back to the pot along with potatoes. Lower the heat and allow to simmer for 45 minutes."],[null,"Remove from heat and enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"This recipe is higher in potassium, but it is a one-dish meal, which would be an acceptable amount of potassium. If you are on a lower potassium diet, omit the tomato sauce."],[null,"Homemade Sazon use equal parts garlic powder, ground cumin, ground coriander, ground annatto (or turmeric), and ground oregano. This recipe would be 1/4 teaspoon each. Keep a mixture on hand to use in other recipes. Store bought Sazon is higher in sodium."],[null,"Make a batch of DaVita’s Adobo seasoning to also keep on hand for other recipes. This recipe already contains salt in the ingredients, so omit for this recipe when making adobo seasoning."],[null,"Boiling potatoes reduces potassium content by 50-75%. You may also double boil them to reduce potassium a bit more."]]},"2098":{"s":[[null,"To make dressing, whisk together oil, vinegar, salt, pepper, minced garlic, basil, oregano and 1/4 cup of the chopped parsley. Set aside."],[null,"Chop bell peppers and onion. Mince dill weed; cook and quarter artichoke hearts."],[null,"In a large bowl combine rice, shrimp, bell peppers, onion, artichoke hearts, 1/2 cup minced parsley, dill, cranberries, pineapple and peas."],[null,"Stir dressing into salad and chill for several hours to marinate."],[null,"Serve over a bed of lettuce."]],"h":[[null,"Leftover salad can be frozen. Thaw before serving."]]},"6917203":{"s":[[null,"Place the tofu, pomegranate juice, raspberries, and syrup in a blender or food processor. Blend on high until creamy and pink in color."],[null,"Divide the mix between 2 bowls. Top each with half the pomegranate seeds and 2 tablespoons muesli."]],"h":[]},"3082":{"s":[[null,"Add pomegranate and lemon juice to a small glass."],[null,"Top with club soda."],[null,"Add in pomegranate arils and garnish with lemon."]],"h":[[null,"Pomegranate juice is limited to 1/4 cup in this recipe. One cup of pomegranate juice contains over 500 mg potassium."],[null,"Substitute cranberry juice for pomegranate juice if preferred. Potassium is decreased to 46 mg."],[null,"Add a small amount of your favorite sweetener for added sweetness."]]},"5600058":{"s":[[null,"Pour Renastep into a blender. Add the other ingredients and blend."],[null,"Pour into a glass. Serve cold."]],"h":[[null,"Swap frozen raspberries for blueberries if permitted. Serve over re-usable plastic ice cubes for a refreshing drink with less fluid."],["Renastep note","Renastep is a Food for Special Medical Purposes and must be used under medical supervision. Renastep is a ready to use feed for the dietary management of kidney disease from 3 years of age onwards. Renastep contains milk and fish. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information. This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutrimen dietary analysis software."]]},"3623":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F."],[null,"Mix the first 5 ingredients in an ungreased 9” x 13” baking pan."],[null,"Make 3 holes in the dry ingredients."],[null,"Pour 2 tablespoons vinegar in one hole."],[null,"Pour 3/4 cup oil in second hole."],[null,"Pour 2 teaspoons vanilla in the third hole."],[null,"Add 2 cups of cold water and mix."],[null,"Bake for 30 to 45 minutes until a toothpick inserted into the center comes out clean."]],"h":[[null,"Great for cupcakes too! Pour 1/3 cup batter into each regular size cupcake liner to make 24 cupcakes."],[null,"Cocoa processed with alkali, also known as Dutch chocolate, is much higher in potassium than natural cocoa powder."]]},"7746605":{"s":[[null,"Heat a large deep pan with a lid, add half (or a third, depending on the size of your pan) of the popping corn and cover. Shake regularly and after 2-3 minutes you’ll hear the corn start to pop – don’t be tempted to open the lid! Keep shaking until the popping stops."],[null,"Put the popped corn into a large bowl and discard any corn that hasn’t popped. Repeat until all your corn is done."],[null,"Meanwhile, in another saucepan warm the orange juice, ginger and sweetener and until dissolved. Mix until it reaches boiling point then heat for 2-3 minutes until it becomes sticky and the volume is reduced by three quarters."],[null,"Stir in the zest and add the popcorn, mixing well so it is all coated."],[null,"Spread onto a tray and leave to dry completely before bagging it up."]],"h":[[null,"Don’t put too much corn in at once – cook in batches as it expands a lot. Don’t open the lid while it’s popping as it will pop out all over the kitchen."],[null,"Take care not to let the pan dry completely as you need enough sauce to coat the popcorn, but if the sauce is too wet your popcorn will be soggy."],[null,"Make sure the popcorn is thoroughly cooled before you bag it."],[null,"Try adding a good pinch of spice, such as cinnamon or nutmeg."],[null,"If you put this sticky orange and ginger popcorn into bags and tie with a ribbon, it’s a healthy treat for Halloween."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"1868":{"s":[[null,"Pour canola oil in medium saucepan and place over medium-high heat."],[null,"Add three popcorn kernels and place lid, slightly cracked on the pan."],[null,"When all three kernels have popped, add the remaining kernels and gently shake pan to coat kernels in oil. Replace lid, slightly cracked on pan."],[null,"Popcorn kernels will begin popping rapidly. When popping slows, remove pan from heat and pour into 3 separate bowls."],[null,"Drizzle chili sauce over popcorn in first bowl and gently toss to coat."],[null,"Mix nutritional yeast with 2 teaspoons melted butter. Drizzle over popcorn in second bowl and gently toss to coat."],[null,"Combine the remaining melted butter with the cinnamon and sugar. Drizzle over popcorn in the third bowl and gently toss to coat."],[null,"Divide each bowl into 2 servings so each person gets 1 cup of each popcorn flavor."]],"h":[[null,"Use white or yellow popcorn."],[null,"CAUTION: Oil will be hot and can pop out of pan during popping. Be careful!"],[null,"Increase Sriracha sauce to 2 teaspoons if more heat is desired."],[null,"This spicy, sweet and cheesy popcorn keeps for 1 to 2 days if sealed in a container or zip-top bag."]]},"3005":{"s":[[null,"Line a baking sheet with foil; coat foil with cooking spray. Set aside."],[null,"Place popped popcorn in a large, zip-top plastic bag; seal. Crush popcorn using a meat mallet or rolling pin; set aside."],[null,"Combine sugar, syrup and 1/4 cup water in a medium saucepan over medium heat. Cook 1 minute or until sugar dissolves, stirring constantly. Cook, without stirring, until a candy thermometer registers 270° F (about 8 minutes)."],[null,"Stir in molasses and butter. Cook until thermometer registers 290° F (about 5 minutes)."],[null,"Stir in baking soda, vanilla and salt."],[null,"Stir crushed popcorn into boiling syrup mixture and remove from heat."],[null,"Working quickly, pour popcorn mixture onto prepared pan. Spread to 1/4″ thickness using a wooden spoon coated with cooking spray."],[null,"Cool completely; break into large pieces."]],"h":[[null,"Store brittle in an airtight container at room temperature for up to 4 days."],[null,"Not recommended for people with diabetes due to high sugar content."]]},"3092":{"s":[[null,"Spread popcorn in a shallow pan."],[null,"Combine sugar, corn syrup and butter in a 1/2-quart saucepan."],[null,"Cook over medium heat until a small amount dropped in cold water separates into thin threads which are hard but not brittle (280° F on the candy thermometer). Remove from heat."],[null,"Add vanilla."],[null,"Pour syrup over popcorn, stirring until well-coated. Spread on a greased baking sheet. Break into pieces."],[null,"Allow to cool. Store in an air tight container until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Portion into individual servings and store for a quick snack or dessert during the week."]]},"7748136":{"s":[[null,"Remove the stalks from the mushrooms and finely chop."],[null,"Add the oil to a frying pan and brown the onion and chopped mushroom stalks for 4-5 minutes then allow to cool."],[null,"Meanwhile, squeeze out any excess water from the spinach and place in a bowl."],[null,"Mix the onion and spinach with plenty of pepper and the nutmeg. Stir in the cream cheese mix together well and form into 4 even-sized balls."],[null,"Meanwhile, grill or griddle the gill-side (inside) of the mushrooms, then top each with the spinach mixture. Set aside until you are ready to grill or barbecue."],[null,"Put the mushrooms onto the barbecue or griddle pan, loosely placing a piece of kitchen foil over the top, to trap the heat, allowing the smoky flavour to be absorbed. Cook for 4-5 minutes."],[null,"Lightly toasted the bun and add the mushroom with lettuce, sliced tomato and red onion."]],"h":[[null,"You could cook the mushrooms in a medium oven for 10-15 minutes instead on the barbecue."],[null,"Try making mini versions using smaller mushrooms and buns, they're great for a party."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"9914907":{"s":[[null,"Slice the portobello mushrooms and set them aside. Then slice the peppers and onion and place them in a large cast-iron skillet or wok with 2-3 tablespoons of water. Sauté until slightly softened, without overcooking, approx. 2-4 minutes. You want the veggies tender-crisp."],[null,"Then add the mushrooms and fajita seasoning and continue to sauté until the mushrooms are slightly reduced. Stir often. This will take approx 2-3 minutes."],[null,"Turn off the heat and add the lime juice, then mix to combine. Taste and adjust the seasoning or lime juice if needed."],[null,"Serve with corn tortillas and all your favourite toppings."]],"h":[[null,"Do not overcook the vegetables . They taste best when tender-crisp and not too soft. Prepare additional toppings in advance so once your mushroom fajita filling is ready, you can enjoy them straight away. Keep leftover filling in the fridge, in an airtight container for 3-4 days, and reheat on the stovetop. Do not assemble the fajitas in advance or the wrap will get soggy. The nutritional information does not include optional toppings."]]},"6201927":{"s":[[null,"Heat a sauté pan and thinly film with olive oil. Add onion, garlic, and mushrooms. Cook until soft and onions are translucent. Add salt and pepper to taste and red pepper, if desired."],[null,"Heat balsamic vinegar in a small saucepan, bring to a boil, and reduce to low. Cook until syrupy, or the vinegar lightly coats the back of a spoon, about 20 minutes. Set aside."],[null,"Spread mushroom mixture on grilled bread and drizzle with balsamic vinegar."]],"h":[]},"1002857":{"s":[[null,"Remove pits and cut peaches into 3/4″ slices."],[null,"Spray a 12″ x 12″ baking pan with cooking spray. Place peaches and blueberries in the pan."],[null,"Sprinkle sugar and lemon juice over the fruit."],[null,"In a bowl, mix flour and brown sugar. Use two knives to cut the butter into the flour and sugar mixture until crumbly. Sprinkle the"],[null,"crumbs over the fruit."],[null,"Bake at 375° F for 45 minutes or longer, until fruit is tender and crumbs are golden brown."],[null,"Serve warm or at room temperature."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute 4 cups drained canned peach slices when fresh peaches are out of season."]]},"6181283":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375 degrees F. Coat a baking sheet with cooking spray."],[null,"Lay cauliflower and potatoes in a single layer on the baking sheet and coat the vegetables with cooking spray. Roast for 45 minutes until vegetables are golden brown and tender."],[null,"In a large bowl, whisk together the balsamic vinegar, olive oil, Dijon mustard, honey and parsley."],[null,"Add red onion, bell pepper and hot potatoes and cauliflower right out of the oven. Toss well to coat."],[null,"Refrigerate salad until cooled (at least 1 hour). Stir again before serving."]],"h":[]},"3942":{"s":[[null,"Reduce potassium in potatoes by one of the methods shown below in the Helpful hints. (Skip this step if you do not need a low potassium diet.)"],[null,"Heat the oil in a skillet and add the diced potatoes. Cook until potatoes are browned."],[null,"Beat the eggs and pour over the potatoes. Reduce heat to low and stir eggs with potatoes for 2-3 minutes until eggs are set."],[null,"Spoon the egg and potato mixture evenly onto sandwich thins. Top each sandwich with a teaspoon of salsa if desired. Add sandwich thin top to make sandwich and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute whole wheat toast or a soft warm flour tortilla (fajita size) for sandwich thins."],[null,"One medium baking potato weighs about 12 ounces."],[null,"Double-cook technique for reducing potassium in potatoes: Peel potatoes and cut into thin slices, diced small or shred for hash browns. Place potato pieces in a pot of water and bring to a boil. Drain water then add fresh water. Bring water to a boil and cook potatoes until tender. Drain water and prepare potatoes as desired. The double cook method reduces potassium below 200 mg for a 100 gram portion (2/3 cup)."],[null,"Another well-known technique for reducing potassium in potatoes is to cut up and soak potato pieces in water. To learn more about this technique read the article “Lowering Potassium in Potatoes” on DaVita.com."]]},"7975803":{"s":[[null,"Heat the sunflower oil in a medium saucepan. Add the onion and fry for 2-3 minutes. Add the mustard seeds, ginger, chilli powder, coriander, turmeric and fresh coriander and continue to fry for 1 minute."],[null,"Add the tomatoes, tomato puree and lentils to the pan and pour over the stock. Bring to the boil, reduce the heat, cover and simmer for 25 minutes or until the lentils are almost tender."],[null,"Stir in the potatoes and continue to cook for 10-15 minutes until tender. Stir through the coriander leaves and serve with a yogurt raita."]],"h":[[null,"You could use sweet potatoes rather than ordinary potatoes – they count towards your 5 a day."],[null,"For a quick red onion relish to serve with the curry, thinly slice 1 red onion and 1 finely chopped tomato, mix with the juice of 1 lemon and a small pinch salt. Allow to infuse for 10 mins before serving."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"9295060":{"s":[[null,"Bring a large pot of salted water to a boil."],[null,"Add the peas and asparagus, cooking for 2-3 minutes. Then remove using a slotted spoon and transfer to a large mixing bowl."],[null,"Next, add the baby potatoes and cook them until fork-tender, approx. 15-20 minutes. Drain and rinse the potatoes until they are cool enough to handle."],[null,"While the potatoes are cooking, add the dressing ingredients to a small bowl or jar and mix well. If needed, add a few drops of water to thin the dressing."],[null,"Slice the cooked potatoes in half (or quarters if they are larger) and add them as well as the red onion to the bowl of peas and asparagus. Then add the dressing and stir until evenly coated."]],"h":[[null,"Taste the dressing for salt and pepper before tossing with the salad. Adjust if needed."],[null,"You may prepare this potato asparagus salad in advance and keep it refrigerated for 1-2 days before serving."]]},"6946528":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375° F."],[null,"Coat a 13 x 9-inch pan with cooking spray. Spread hash browns on bottom of pan."],[null,"In a large nonstick skillet, melt margarine over medium-high heat. Add onion and sauté until clear. Add remaining ingredients and mix well. Cook about 5 minutes, stirring occasionally."],[null,"Pour soup mixture over hash browns. Bake for 50-60 minutes."]],"h":[]},"5072689":{"s":[[null,"Cut the potatoes into small pieces and boil them in hot water. When the potatoes are soft, drain the water. Please be careful when you do this as the water will be very hot."],[null,"If you have been advised to follow a low potassium diet, boil and drain the potatoes again to reduce the potassium content further."],[null,"Once drained, add the butter and yolk to the potatoes and, using a potato masher, mash until creamy. You can add pepper to taste."],[null,"Cover the mash and leave until firm and cool enough to handle."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 200°C/180 Fan/Gas 6."],[null,"Shape the mashed potato into 6 croquettes, weighing around 60g."],[null,"Put the flour, whole egg and breadcrumbs into three separate shallow bowls. Beat the egg."],[null,"Dip each croquette in the flour, pat off any excess, then coat in the egg before dipping in the breadcrumbs. Transfer to a baking tray."],[null,"Using spray oil, lightly spray the croquettes."],[null,"Bake for 20 minutes or until golden-brown. If preferred, the potato croquettes can be cooked in an air fryer for 12 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Finely chopped spring onions and herbs can be added to the mash for extra flavour."]]},"7759221":{"s":[[null,"Boil the potatoes for 10-12 minutes or until tender. Drain and mash well or pass through a potato ricer. Leave to cool completely, then stir through the beaten eggs, nutmeg and flour and season with pepper."],[null,"Whisk the egg whites, until they form soft peaks, then gently fold through the potato mixture. Heat a little oil in a non-stick frying pan, add the mixture in spoonfuls and cook for 2–3 minutes until golden."],[null,"Place on a piece of kitchen paper to absorb any excess oil, then serve."]],"h":[[null,"Spice up your pancakes by adding half tsp turmeric and 1 tsp curry powder to the mixture."],[null,"These pancakes make a great alternative to bread to serve with soup."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Freeze with greaseproof paper between each pancake. Defrost for 1 hour, or in the microwave then reheat in a pan or microwave."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"7224947":{"s":[[null,"Grate the potatoes, cover and set aside."],[null,"In a separate bowl, beat the eggs with the salt and herbs and spices. Mix into the grated potatoes."],[null,"Add 1 tsp of the oil to a non-stick frying pan over medium to low heat and spoon the potato mixture into the pan, shaping into small pancakes. Cook in batches, for 2–3 minutes on each side, and set aside until all the pancakes are cooked."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the remaining oil to a separate pan and add the onion, garlic and mushrooms. Heat gently for 10–15 minutes, stirring regularly."],[null,"Once you've cooked your final batch of pancakes, add the reserved pancakes back to the pan for 1–2 minutes to ensure they're warm. Serve with the mushroom sauce."]],"h":[[null,"You could use 2 tsp curry powder and add 50g peas to make Indian-style pancakes and serve with a raita and/or mango chutney."],[null,"To make a creamier sauce add 2 tbsp low-fat yogurt to the mushrooms."],[null,"Try using leeks instead of onions, or use 1 onion and 1 leek."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"7006166":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 220°C/gas 7."],[null,"Place the flours and yeast in a large bowl. Mix together the milk, oil and 125ml warm water, pour over the flour and bring together to form a soft dough."],[null,"Tip onto a lightly floured surface and knead for 5-6 minutes until smooth. Place in a lightly oiled bowl, cover with a damp cloth and set aside in a warm place for 30 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, simmer the potatoes in lightly salted water for 5 minutes. Drain."],[null,"Heat the oil in a non-stick frying pan and fry the onion for 3-4 minutes until softened."],[null,"Cut the dough in two and shape each piece into a 23cm circle, approximately ½-1cm thick, and place on a heavy baking sheet."],[null,"Prepare the topping, adding the rosemary, thyme, creme fraiche and pepper to the potatoes and divide between the bases. Set aside for 5 minutes, then bake for 15-20 minutes until crisp and golden."]],"h":[[null,"Scatter the cooked pizza with a handful of fresh rocket leaves and a dash of balsamic vinegar or a few chopped cherry tomatoes and a couple of chopped spring onions."],[null,"Try spreading 1 tsp curry paste over the pizza base before cooking."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"4062222":{"s":[[null,"Boil leached water potatoes (use 5 cups water for each cup of potatoes), until tender but not mushy."],[null,"In a bowl, mix together relish onions, celery, mayo and celery seed. Toss in potatoes."],[null,"Sprinkle with paparika. Refrigerate to blend flavors for at least one hour."]],"h":[[null,"Leaching instructions: Peel, cut into small pieces, exposing as much surface area as possible. Rinse in warm water for a few seconds. Place potatoes in a large container and add large amount of tap water (use 10 cups of water for each cup of potatoes). Soak for 2-4 hours at room temperatue. Drain and rinse the leached potatoes."]]},"7500982":{"s":[[null,"Place the potato, leek and stock into a pan."],[null,"Bring to the boil, cover and simmer for 15 minutes until the vegetables have softened."],[null,"Add the cream cheese, season to taste and blend until smooth. Top with the leek slices to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Try adding 2-3 cloves garlic with the leek. No need to crush them as you’re blending the dish."],[null,"To give this soup a rich green colour and an extra portion of vegetables, add a handful of defrosted frozen peas with the cream cheese."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost thoroughly and reheat until piping hot. The soup may separate while frozen, so stir vigorously when reheating to keep the consistency."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6052473":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl or mug, whisk together the Greek yogurt, egg, and vanilla extract."],[null,"Add the oat flour and baking powder. Mix until smooth."],[null,"Stir in the cinnamon and blueberries."],[null,"Microwave on high for 1 minute and 30 seconds to 2 minutes, or until the muffin is puffed and set. Cooking time may vary based on your microwave."]],"h":[]},"2251":{"s":[[null,"Prepare griddle or skillet with nonstick cooking spray and heat."],[null,"Combine all ingredients in a blender or food processor until smooth."],[null,"Pour batter onto prepared griddle or skillet making two 6″ pancakes. Cook on each side."],[null,"Served plain or topped with fruit, preserves or syrup."]],"h":[[null,"Analysis does not include the suggested toppings."],[null,"Make a savory sandwich pancake by adding 2 teaspoons dried Italian spice or other spices of your choice to the batter before cooking. After cooking, top with meat and sandwich fixings."]]},"7334595":{"s":[[null,"Place the oats, buckwheat and quinoa flakes in a small pan, cover with the water, add the sweetener (if using), and then place over a low heat. Cook for 3–4 minutes."],[null,"Divide the porridge between 2 bowls, and top with the berries and toasted seeds. Serve with milk, if desired."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"2732":{"s":[[null,"Blend cranberry-tangerine juice, whey powder, sweetener and ice in a blender till pink and frothy."],[null,"Pour into a glass and serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"Ask your dietitian for more information about acceptable protein powders for kidney patients."],[null,"Sweeten to taste."],[null,"Serve with a swizzle stick of peppermint or a sprig of mint, if desired."],[null,"Juice may be substituted with Sunkist® regular or diet orange soda, cranberry, cranberry-raspberry or cranberry-grape juices."]]},"6197232":{"s":[[null,"In a medium bowl, mix together all ingredients."],[null,"Portion into 1/3 cup servings."]],"h":[]},"7967885":{"s":[[null,"Lightly toast the sandwich thin halves. Mix the cottage cheese with some snipped dill, a few drops of Tabasco, if using, and some black pepper."],[null,"Pile the mixture on top of the sandwich thins, then add the cucumber slices, prawns, another sprinkling of dill and splash of Tabasco, then serve."]],"h":[]},"7137182":{"s":[[null,"Beat together the egg yolk and with 200ml ice-cold water. Tip in the flour and roughly combine."],[null,"You're not making a smooth batter, the mixture should remain fairly lumpy as this gives it its lightness when fried."],[null,"Heat the oil in a large pan until a piece of bread browns in 30 seconds."],[null,"Dip the prawns and vegetables into the batter and fry in batches. Turn regularly to ensure even cooking, until light golden in colour about 2-3 mins per batch."],[null,"Drain on kitchen paper and serve."]],"h":[[null,"You need to use quick-cooking veggies for tempura. Sugarsnap peas, mange tout, green beans, celery and spring onions are also ideal."],[null,"For a healthy dipping sauce, simply blend together 2 handfuls mixed fresh herbs (e.g. parsley, coriander, mint, basil) with a clove fresh garlic, juice and zest 1 lemon and 2 tbsp olive oil."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"7084429":{"s":[[null,"Add the broccoli to a microwave-proof dish with 1 teaspoon of water, cover with cling film, then pierce and heat on full for 1.5 minutes, then reserve."],[null,"Meanwhile, heat the oil in a non-stick pan or wok, then add the spring onions and pepper. Cook for 2-3 minutes over a high heat, stirring constantly."],[null,"Next, add the ginger, chilli and garlic to the pan and cook for 1 minute."],[null,"Add the king prawns, water, courgette spaghetti, noodles and reserved broccoli and mix well. Add a lid and cook for 2 minutes."],[null,"Add the spinach, lime juice, zest and soy sauce and mix again. &nbsp"],[null,"Cover and heat for another 2-3 minutes."],[null,"Make sure the dish is heated through and the prawns are pink, then serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"Try adding salmon or another fish instead of prawns."],[null,"For a vegetarian/vegan version, use mushrooms or tofu in place of prawns."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"7959955":{"s":[[null,"Use the browning function on your pressure cooker to soften the onions, garlic, then sprinkle with the ginger."],[null,"Add the mushrooms, peppers, soya mince and balsamic vinegar. When browned, add the carrots and cook for 20 minutes."],[null,"Add the tomatoes, beans, chickpeas, tomato purée and enough stock to reach the middle of your cooker."],[null,"Add the chilli flakes and set your pressure cooker for 30 minutes. Serve with rice."]],"h":[[null,"This recipe has been created by Balance cover star, Shivali, as part of her journey to remission."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 5"]]},"3527":{"s":[[null,"Chop green onions. Mince garlic. Julienne cut zucchini, yellow squash and bell pepper."],[null,"Warm olive oil in a large, uncovered frying pan on medium heat."],[null,"Add green onions and garlic and sauté until soft."],[null,"Add remainder of vegetables and stir-fry lightly."],[null,"When vegetables soften, cover pan and lower heat to medium-low."],[null,"Cook for 20-30 minutes, until sauce has thickened. Season with oregano and serve over pasta."],[null,"Sprinkle one teaspoon of parmesan cheese over each serving of sauce."]],"h":[[null,"This is nice served over linguine cooked al dente."],[null,"If sauce seems too dry, you can add a little water."],[null,"1 medium zucchini and 1 medium yellow summer squash each yield 3/4 cup julienne cut."],[null,"Crushed red or black pepper adds extra zest."]]},"3910":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"In a large bowl, mix oats with the yogurt. Add oil, water, sugar and egg; mix well."],[null,"In a separate bowl combine flour, protein powder, salt, baking soda and cream of tartar."],[null,"Mix dry ingredients into wet ingredients. Add blueberries and mix well."],[null,"Fill 12 muffin cups or grease muffin pans and fill 2/3 full with batter. Bake for 20 to 25 minutes or until firm to the touch."]],"h":[[null,"Use frozen blueberries when fresh are out of season."],[null,"Substitute cranberries for blueberries to make high protein cranberry muffins."]]},"2764":{"s":[[null,"Drain tuna from can, and place in small mixing bowl. Dice celery and red onion."],[null,"Add mayonnaise, diced celery, diced onion, and spices to tuna bowl. Mix to combine."],[null,"Slice and skin cucumbers into spears. Slice apple into thin slices. Use 5 slices of cucumber from a medium cucumber for each box, if you are unable to find mini cucumbers."],[null,"Use two bento boxes. Put half he tuna mix, half of the carrots and half the cucumber to the boxes. Slice eggs in half and add 1 egg and 1 rice cake to each box."]],"h":[[null,"To make perfect hard-boiled eggs: add eggs to pan, and cover with water. Let water boil for 5 minutes, turn water off and leave egg in water for 10 minutes. Rinse in cool water, and peel immediately."],[null,"Instead of rice cakes, you may also use multi-grain crackers or corn thins. Stick to the serving on the box and look for lower sodium varieties."],[null,"This bento lunch box is a full meal. The potassium is higher than a normal entree, but it is considered a full meal and acceptable for a kidney friendly diet. Most of the potassium comes from fresh, natural foods."]]},"6877039":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 425°F. Use 1 Tbsp olive oil to grease the bottom of a large roasting pan."],[null,"Pat the turkey breast dry with a paper towel and season with salt and pepper. Place turkey breast skin side up in the pan. Brush the turkey with the remaining olive oil. Sprinkle Herbes de Provence and poultry seasoning on turkey, and rub into skin with your hands. Place whole garlic head, 1 lemon half, rosemary, thyme, and sage in the pan. Squeeze lemon juice from remaining lemon half over the top of the turkey."],[null,"Place turkey in the oven, add a cup of water to the bottom of the pan, and roast for 1 hour, uncovered. Baste turkey after the first hour of cooking. If turkey looks very brown, cover it with foil. Continue to bake for another 30-45 minutes or until the internal temperature of the thickest part of the turkey breast reads 180°F on a meat thermometer. Remove from the oven, and place on a carving board. Let rest for 10 minutes before carving. Remove skin while carving."],[null,"Strain the liquid from the bottom of the pan into another saucepan. Juice the remaining 2 lemon halves, add to the saucepan, and stir. Bring to a boil over high heat, and cook for 10 minutes or until sauce has reduced. Taste, and adjust seasoning if necessary. Serve sauce in a gravy boat next to turkey."]],"h":[]},"2989":{"s":[[null,"Dice chicken thighs into 2-inch bite-sized pieces. If using bamboos skewers, soak in water for 1/2 hour to prevent burning."],[null,"Mix together the Adobo Seasoning, oregano, vinegar, olive oil and bay leaves and put in a zip top bag."],[null,"Add chicken to the marinade. Place in the refrigerator to for at least a half hour to overnight."],[null,"Heat the grill and oil the grates when hot."],[null,"Thread the chicken on skewers and place on the hot grill. Sear for about 5 minutes on each side."],[null,"Baste the pinchos with Guava Barbecue Sauce or other low sodium barbecue sauce and cook for about 4 more minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Keep the chicken pieces about the same size to ensure even cooking."],[null,"Check out our Guava Barbecue Sauce and additional low-sodium barbecue sauce recipes on DaVita.com."],[null,"Make your own lower sodium Adobe Seasoning."]]},"3806":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400º F."],[null,"Place butter in a 10-inch ovenproof skillet or glass pie plate. Place in oven for 3 to 5 minutes or until butter melts."],[null,"In a medium mixing bowl use a wire whisk or rotary beater to beat eggs until combined. Add rice flour, rice milk and salt. Beat until smooth."],[null,"Remove skillet or pie plate from oven. Immediately pour batter into the hot pan. Bake for 25 to 30 minutes until pancake is puffed and well browned."],[null,"Transfer to a serving plate and cut into 4 portions. Add toppings of choice. Serve warm."]],"h":[[null,"Ensure pancake is well browned in step #4. Otherwise pancake will not be done on the inside."],[null,"Suggested fruit toppings include blueberries, sliced strawberries, raspberries, sliced peaches or applesauce. For additional toppings sprinkle with powdered sugar or top with whipped cream or syrup."],[null,"This pancake is gluten-free."]]},"3937":{"s":[[null,"Thaw chicken. In a large Crock-Pot® combine the tomato puree and chicken."],[null,"Puree all other ingredients in food processor (this will have to be done in batches in most food processors)."],[null,"Add vegetables to Crock-Pot and cook on high for 4 hours or low for 6-8 hours."],[null,"Remove chicken to a plate. Using 2 forks, shred chicken then return to sauce in the Crock-Pot®."]],"h":[[null,"When done the chicken should pull apart with a pair of tongs or a fork."],[null,"Select the type of hot pepper based on heat desired."],[null,"Serve shredded chicken over rice or on buns."],[null,"For a lower protein diet decrease portion to 1/2 cup and count as 2 meat choices."]]},"6920949":{"s":[[null,"In a medium bowl, stir together the onion, lime juice, and salt. Cover with plastic wrap and set aside at room temperature for 3 to 5 hours, while the chicken cooks."],[null,"Place the chicken in a medium slow cooker. Sprinkle with the chili powder and cumin. Pour the chicken broth around the chicken. Cover and cook on low for 3 to 5 hours or until chicken reaches a temperature of 165°F."],[null,"Remove the chicken from the slow cooker and using the tines of two forks, shred the chicken. Place the chicken in a bowl and toss with the onion lime mixture. Serve with lime wedges and chopped cilantro sprinkled on top."],[null,"Electric pressure cooker variation: Prepare the onion lime mixture as above. Place the chicken in the pressure cooker. Sprinkle with chili powder and cumin. Pour the chicken broth around the chicken. Secure the lid. Cook on high pressure for 6 minutes. Allow the pressure to release naturally for 5 minutes, then quickly release the remaining pressure. Proceed as above."]],"h":[]},"9968027":{"s":[[null,"Combine all the bbq sauce ingredients in a medium bowl and mix well. Set aside."],[null,"Pull apart the chunks of jackfruit using your hands or two forks. It will shred quite easily, and place it in a large skillet. Then pour the sauce over top and mix well."],[null,"Over medium heat, cook the jackfruit in the sauce, it will be a little soupy at first but it will quickly absorb the sauce as it cooks. This will take about 5-8 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, layer your chips in a serving dish, and once ready, top it with the jackfruit and your choice of toppings. Serve your jackfruit nachos with guacamole, cashew cream, and/or salsa."]],"h":[[null,"Make sure to purchase jackfruit that is canned in water or brine, and not syrup. The syrupy kind is very sweet and you want it to absorb the BBQ sauce flavour, and not be overpowered by the syrupy taste. If you’re short on time, or don’t want to make your own BBQ sauce, you may sub for a store bought sauce instead. Use about ¾ cup of prepared sauce in replacement of the homemade version. If you prefer some crispy edges on your jackfruit, transfer it, once cooked, to a baking tray in a single layer and bake at 375 degrees for 15-20 minutes before adding to your nachos. For oil free chips, here’s a recipe by Sweet Simple Vegan to make your own healthy tortilla chips . Remember, the jackfruit is the star of the show, so add a generous layer to your chips before sprinkling additional toppings. If you have leftovers, store in a sealed container in the refrigerator for up to 5 days. Use your leftovers to make a vegan pulled BBQ-style sandwich topped with my creamy vegan coleslaw ."]]},"6792714":{"s":[[null,"In a blender, combine the canned pumpkin purée, sliced banana, almond milk, almond butter, ground cinnamon, ground nutmeg, and vanilla extract."],[null,"Blend the ingredients on high speed until smooth and creamy."],[null,"If you prefer a colder smoothie, you can add a handful of ice cubes and blend again until well incorporated. Serve immediately."]],"h":[]},"9105121":{"s":[[null,"Add the chopped onion and garlic to a large pot with two tablespoons of water and sauté until soft and golden, about 3 minutes."],[null,"Add all remaining ingredients and bring to a boil over high heat. Then lower to medium and cook for about 8 minutes, until veggies are fork tender."],[null,"Using an immersion blender, purée your soup until smooth and creamy. Serve garnished with pumpkin seeds, if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Don’t stress over uniform sized veggie pieces . Since you’ll be pureeing the soup, you won’t need similar sizes. Use an immersion blender to puree your soup for less mess, ease, and less dishes to wash! If you don’t have an immersion blender , use extreme caution when blending hot liquids. Don’t overfill your blender, and work in batches to prevent spills. Taste for salt or other seasoning once cooked , and add more, if needed. Depending on the broth you’re using, you may need more salt. This soup is thick in texture. If you prefer a thinner texture , use an additional cup of broth or stir in a cup of your favourite milk after pureeing. Cashew or soy milk also work well. If time permits, roast the veggies for added depth of flavour . Roasting the squash, sweet potatoes, onion and garlic will add even more incredible flavour to your soup. For a sweeter version , add up to ¼ of cup maple syrup or unrefined coconut sugar to your soup. Leftovers keep refrigerated in a sealed container for 3-4 days. Or freeze airtight for up to 3 months."]]},"6109291":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F. Coat an 8x8-inch baking pan with cooking spray."],[null,"In a medium bowl, whisk together the egg, egg whites, vanilla, brown sugar substitute, pumpkin, applesauce, and grated apple."],[null,"In another medium bowl, mix together the oats, almond flour, protein powder, cinnamon, and baking powder."],[null,"Add the wet ingredients to the dry ingredients and mix until blended."],[null,"Pour into a prepared baking dish and bake for 25 minutes."],[null,"Let cool before cutting and serving."]],"h":[]},"9159728":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350℉/176℃ and line a muffin pan with parchment liners OR grease the tins."],[null,"Mash the bananas into a large bowl, and add the pumpkin puree and milk. Mix well."],[null,"Then add all the dry ingredients, and stir until combined without overmixing. Lastly, fold in the chocolate chips, if using them."],[null,"Divide the mixture between your 12 muffin tins, filling them almost to the top. Gently tap the muffin tray down on a hard surface a few times to ensure there are no gaps and then bake them for 22-24 minutes or until a toothpick inserted in the middle comes out clean."],[null,"Remove the muffin pan from the oven and let them rest for at least 10 minutes before transferring them to a cooling rack. Enjoy warm or let them cool to room temperature."]],"h":[[null,"Use overly ripe bananas with lots of brown spots on the peel for extra sweetness. You may also use frozen bananas, just let them come to room temperature before mashing them."],[null,"Don’t overmix . The texture of the muffins comes out best when folded together until just combined."],[null,"Let your muffins rest for 10 minutes after baking . This short cool-down time will allow your muffins to completely set, and prevent them from breaking when removing them from the pan."],[null,"If you don’t have oat flour on hand , you can make some by grinding oats in a high-speed blender. Weigh the oats first and then blend them. You may also use whole wheat flour if a gluten-free option is not needed."],[null,"You may omit the optional chocolate chips OR use chopped nuts, raisins, dried cranberries, fresh blueberries, etc."],[null,"Pumpkin pie spice works if you don’t have the individual spices. Use three teaspoons of the mix to replace the cinnamon, nutmeg, and ginger."],[null,"For soy-free , use almond milk, cashew milk , or another non-dairy milk of your choice."],[null,"These banana pumpkin muffins will keep covered at room temperature for 2-3 days, or refrigerated for up to 4 days. Freeze the muffins airtight for up to 3 months."]]},"6099038":{"s":[[null,"In a large saucepan, heat the oil over medium heat. Add the onion and sauté for 5 to 7 minutes, until soft. Add the garlic, curry powder, coriander, cayenne, salt, and pepper and sauté for 1 minute."],[null,"Add the broth and bring to boiling. Lower the heat and simmer, uncovered, for 20 minutes."],[null,"Add the pumpkin and simmer for 10 minutes. Using an immersion blender, process the soup until smooth. Or carefully add the hot soup (in batches) to a blender and process until smooth; return the soup to the pot."],[null,"Add the half-and-half and sugar-stevia sweetener and simmer on low for 2 minutes. Ladle into individual serving bowls. Garnish each bowl with generous pinches of pumpkin seeds and chives."]],"h":[]},"9266414":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 375 degrees F and line a baking tray with parchment paper."],[null,"Add all the ingredients to a food processor and pulse until combined, stopping to scrape down the sides if needed. Do not over process, some chunkier pieces is ideal."],[null,"Divide your mixture into 5 patties and bake for 20-25 minutes. Do not overcook or they will get dry. The burgers are ready when they start to look cracked around the edges as shown in photo 4 above."],[null,"Remove from the oven and let cool for 5 minutes before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Do NOT over-process . These patties truly taste best when the ingredients are still quite chunky. Use the pulse button on your food processor to combine the ingredients, without blending them."],[null,"Do NOT overcook . Don’t overcook these burgers, or they will get dry and fall apart. The sweet spot is 20-25 minutes. That said, don’t undercook either, or they will be too soft. For the best texture, cook until the edges appear cracked and firm to the touch, as shown in photo 4 above, but the centers will be softer."],[null,"Let them rest . When you remove your pumpkin burgers from the oven, be sure to let them rest for 5 minutes before serving. These extra few minutes will help your burgers complete setting and firm up."],[null,"Adjust the seasoning . Feel free to adjust these pumpkin burgers to suit your taste. Remember, these are not pumpkin spice burgers; the pumpkin provides moisture and nutrients. If you want pumpkin spice flavours in your burger, add some cinnamon, nutmeg, ginger, and/or cloves if desired. Don’t go overboard. Alternatively, if you prefer a spicy flavour over a smoky one, substitute half or all of the smoked"]]},"1969":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350º F."],[null,"In a large mixing bowl beat together the sugar, pumpkin, water, eggs and oil."],[null,"Add the baking powder, cinnamon, ginger, salt, baking soda and flour. Stir until smooth."],[null,"Pour the batter into 3 loaf pans and bake for 45 minutes or until inserted toothpick comes out clean."],[null,"Cool loaves in the pans for 10 minutes, then remove and cool on wire racks. Cut each loaf into 10 slices when ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"To modify for a low-fat, low-cholesterol diabetic diet, substitute 1/2-cup low-cholesterol egg product for two of the eggs and substitute 1-cup Splenda® granular sweetener for 1-cup sugar. Carbohydrate is reduced to 18 grams, fat to 4 grams, cholesterol to 14 mg and calories to 120."],[null,"Add a cup of fresh cranberries to batter before baking for variety."]]},"3863":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Set out butter and cream cheese to soften."],[null,"In a medium bowl, combine flour and brown sugar. Cut-in butter to make a crumb mixture."],[null,"Set aside 3/4-cup mixture for topping. Press remaining mixture into bottom of a 8″ x 8″ x 1-1/2″ baking pan."],[null,"Bake in for 15 minutes and remove from oven. Cool slightly."],[null,"Lightly beat eggs. Combine cream cheese, sugar (or substitute), pumpkin, eggs, cinnamon, allspice and vanilla in large mixer bowl. Blend until smooth."],[null,"Pour mixture over baked crust. Sprinkle with reserved topping."],[null,"Bake an additional 30 to 35 minutes."],[null,"Cool before cutting into bars."]],"h":[[null,"Be sure to pack brown sugar when measuring 1/3 cup."],[null,"Substitute Splenda® granular sweetener for 3/4 cup sugar to reduce carbohydrate to 14 grams per serving."],[null,"Pumpkin is high in potassium but the small amount per serving keeps this recipe kidney-friendly."]]},"2854":{"s":[[null,"Chop onion and celery; thinly slice carrots and mince garlic cloves."],[null,"In a large pot heat 1 tablespoon olive oil over medium heat and sauté onion, celery, carrots and garlic until tender. Remove from pot and set aside."],[null,"Add turkey and remaining 1 tablespoon of olive oil to pot and cook until crumbles are no longer pink."],[null,"Add sautéed vegetables and remaining ingredients to the pot and stir."],[null,"Reduce heat to a simmer and cook for 1 hour. Stir occasionally to prevent ingredients from sticking to the pot."],[null,"Remove bay leaves before serving."],[null,"If desired, add red chili pepper flakes for added spice."]],"h":[[null,"Pumpkin replaces tomatoes and tomato sauce in this recipe. Follow the recommended portion size to keep potassium within an acceptable range for a low potassium kidney diet."],[null,"Beans are high in potassium and phosphorus. Limit recipe to 1 cup. Optionally, you can omit the beans to further reduce potassium and phosphorus."],[null,"Serve chili over rice or with low-sodium crackers. If desired top with chopped chives or cilantro and a spoonful of sour cream or Greek yogurt."],[null,"If you are on a lower protein diet make the recipe with 1 pound of ground turkey and reduce to 8 portions. Protein is 17 mg per cup."]]},"6862793":{"s":[[null,"Place squash, broth, tomatoes, onion, pepper, ginger root, scallions, and thyme sprigs or dried thyme in a nonreactive large saucepan. Bring to a boil, reduce heat, and simmer uncovered for 45 minutes, stirring occasionally, until all ingredients are tender."],[null,"Add cilantro, lime juice, and salt. Remove thyme stems before serving. Garnish each bowl of soup with pepitas before serving. Makes about 2 quarts."]],"h":[]},"3357":{"s":[[null,"Set the butter out to soften. Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Mix the flour, ginger, cinnamon, baking soda, cloves, allspice and salt in large bowl. Set aside."],[null,"Beat butter and brown sugar in a large bowl with an electric mixer on medium-speed until light and fluffy."],[null,"Add the pumpkin, egg and vanilla; beat well. Gradually beat in the flour mixture on low speed until well mixed."],[null,"Using about a tablespoon form dough into balls. Roll in granulated sugar. Place 2 inches apart on an ungreased baking sheets and press gently with a fork to flatten slightly."],[null,"Bake 8 to 10 minutes or until edges of cookies just begin to brown. If desired, after removing baking sheet from the oven, immediately press 3 to 4 white chocolate chips into the center of each cookie. Remove to wire racks and cool completely."],[null,"Store cookies in airtight container up to 5 days."]],"h":[[null,"Dark chocolate or semi-chocolate whips work well in this recipe."],[null,"Without the white chocolate chips carbohydrate content is 18 grams per serving."]]},"3814":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Combine flour, pumpkin pie spice and baking powder in a large bowl."],[null,"Combine eggs, sugar, pumpkin puree and oil in a small mixing bowl. Beat until blended."],[null,"Add pumpkin mixture to flour mixture. Stir until just moistened, and then fold in cranberries."],[null,"Spoon batter into 2 greased 9″ x 5″ loaf pans. Bake for 55 to 60 minutes."],[null,"Remove pans from the oven and let cool for 5 to 10 minutes. Remove loaves from pans and cool on a wire rack before slicing each loaf into 10 slices."]],"h":[[null,"Make extra bread and freeze the loaves. Thaw a few hours before serving."],[null,"If cranberries are unavailable, omit from recipe or substitute blueberries instead."]]},"6637373":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F. Line a 9 x 9” baking pan with parchment paper."],[null,"In a bowl, combine the pumpkin puree, eggs, zero-calorie maple syrup, almond milk, vanilla extract, 1 tsp ground cinnamon, ground nutmeg, ground ginger, and salt."],[null,"Pour the pumpkin mixture into the prepared pan and spread in an even layer."],[null,"In another bowl, combine the oats, almond flour, chopped pecans, 1 tsp cinnamon, and vegetable oil. Stir until the mixture is crumbly."],[null,"Sprinkle the oat mixture evenly over the top of the pumpkin."],[null,"Bake until the pumpkin filling is set and the oat topping is golden brown, about 35 minutes."],[null,"Let it cool for 10 minutes and then serve warm."]],"h":[]},"6681879":{"s":[[null,"Add all of the ingredients except the pumpkin seeds to a food processor or blender and blend until smooth."],[null,"Garnish with a sprinkling of pumpkin seeds, if desired. Serve with pita chips or fresh vegetables, such as celery, sugar snap peas, or carrots."]],"h":[]},"2332":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350º F. Set cream cheese out to soften and melt margarine."],[null,"In a medium bowl combine graham cracker crumbs, 1 tablespoon sugar and melted margarine. Press into bottom or a 9″ spring form pan and bake for 8 minutes. Set aside to cool."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine cream cheese, Splenda, remaining 4 tablespoons sugar and vanilla. With an electric mixer, beat on medium speed until smooth. Blend in eggs one at a time."],[null,"Set aside one cup of the cream cheese mixture and pour remaining mixture over pie crust in spring form pan."],[null,"Combine the cup of cream cheese mixture with pumpkin puree and pumpkin pie spice. Pour over top of the cream cheese filling in the spring form pan."],[null,"Bake for 30 minutes, or until center of pie is almost set."],[null,"Cool pie to room temperature. Cover and refrigerate until chilled."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute one 9″ prepared graham cracker pie crust instead of the spring form pan and homemade graham cracker crust."],[null,"To reduce fat and cholesterol content substitute 1/2 cup low cholesterol egg product for 2 whole eggs."],[null,"Be sure to use canned pumpkin, not pumpkin pie mix."],[null,"Portions are small due to calorie, fat and sodium content."],[null,"Top each piece of pie with whipped topping before serving if desired."]]},"9983478":{"s":[[null,"Add everything to a small bowl, and stir to combine."],[null,"Refrigerate overnight, or at least 4 hours. Then add your favourite toppings and enjoy."]],"h":[]},"6318845":{"s":[[null,"Combine Greek yogurt, 1 Tbsp. ground flax seed, pumpkin puree, almond milk, pumpkin pie spice and ice in a blender. Blend until smooth."],[null,"Pour smoothie into a glass, top with whipped topping and sprinkle with 1/4 Tsp. ground flax seed."]],"h":[]},"6956653":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F. Line a muffin tin with 8 paper liners or lightly coat with nonstick spray."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine dry ingredients: oats, flaxseed, cinnamon, baking powder, nutmeg, and salt."],[null,"In a separate bowl, whisk together the pumpkin, egg, yogurt, almond milk, and vanilla."],[null,"Add the wet mixture to the dry ingredients and stir until fully combined. Let it sit for 5 minutes to thicken slightly."],[null,"Spoon the mixture evenly into 8 muffin cups."],[null,"Bake for 25–28 minutes, or until set and lightly golden on top."],[null,"Let them cool for 5 minutes before removing from the tin. Serve warm or store in the fridge for up to 5 days."]],"h":[]},"2229":{"s":[[null,"In a medium sauce pan combine the pudding mix and almond milk."],[null,"Bring to boil over medium heat, stirring constantly. Stir until pudding thickens."],[null,"Remove from heat and mix in protein powder and pumpkin pie spice. Mix completely."],[null,"Place plastic wrap directly on surface of pudding and cool in fridge for at least 3 hours or overnight. Pudding will thicken as it cools."],[null,"Stir before serving chilled pudding."]],"h":[[null,"Change flavor of pudding mix for variety."],[null,"The addition of whey protein powder makes the protein content similar to pudding made with milk."],[null,"Protein powders vary in scoop size and amount of protein. Analysis uses EAS whey protein powder."],[null,"Do not substitute instant pudding mix. It is very high in sodium."]]},"6876203":{"s":[[null,"In a medium mixing bowl, whisk together the pudding mix and milk for 2 minutes. Let sit for 5 minutes."],[null,"Fold in the pumpkin, cinnamon, and nutmeg. Fold in 1/2 cup of the yogurt and refrigerate for 10 minutes."],[null,"Scoop 1/2 cup pudding mixture into each parfait glass. Top each with 1 heaping tablespoon of the remaining yogurt and 1 crumbled gingersnap cookie. Repeat procedure for the remaining 6 parfaits."]],"h":[]},"6080447":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F. Coat an 8-inch baking pie pan with cooking spray. Set aside."],[null,"To prepare the crust, mix together the cooked quinoa, cream cheese, and egg white in a medium bowl until thoroughly combined. Cover and refrigerate for 1 hour."],[null,"Press the quinoa crust mixture into the bottom and up the sides of the pie pan. Bake the crust for 10 minutes, remove from oven and set aside. Reduce the oven temperature to 350 degrees F."],[null,"In a large bowl, whisk together the milk, whole eggs, thyme, salt, pepper, nutmeg, and pumpkin puree until well blended and frothy."],[null,"Gently pour the pumpkin mixture into the partially cooked quinoa crust. Bake for 45-50 minutes or until the filling is set."]],"h":[]},"9109371":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425℉/218℃ convection roast and line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Peel and cube your pumpkin into small half-inch pieces. Arrange them in a single layer on your baking tray and sprinkle them with salt and pepper. Roast the cubes for 15 minutes, then flip and roast an additional 15 minutes, or until fork tender and the edges are golden."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the quinoa and broth to a small sauce pot, cover it with a lid, bring to a low boil, and let it simmer for 10-12 minutes, or until the liquid has all been absorbed. Then fluff up the cooked quinoa with a fork, transfer it to a large bowl, and set it aside."],[null,"Add all the dressing ingredients to a small bowl and stir until combined."],[null,"Then add the roasted pumpkin cubes, baby spinach, pecans, and dried cranberries to the bowl with the quinoa. Pour the dressing on top, mix well, and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Cut the pumpkin cubes as uniformly as possible for even cooking."],[null,"To save time , you may purchase cubed pumpkin pieces from the store."],[null,"If you don’t have a convection oven , roast the pumpkin a little longer until fork-tender and the edges are golden brown."],[null,"Keep leftovers in an airtight container stored in the fridge for 3-4 days."]]},"6045990":{"s":[[null,"Place a large nonstick skillet over medium-high heat until hot. Cook the pumpkin seeds and peanuts 2 to 3 minutes or until beginning to lightly brown, stirring frequently. Set aside on paper towel in a thin layer to cool quickly, about 5 minutes."],[null,"Combine the pumpkin seed mixture with the remaining ingredients."]],"h":[]},"6923905":{"s":[],"h":[]},"2555513":{"s":[[null,"In a preheated pot add olive oil then add the finely chopped onion."],[null,"Sauté for about 2 minutes, stirring often, until slightly softened but still vibrant."],[null,"Now, add the whole chicken breast and stir for 5 minutes on medium low heat, then add the spices."],[null,"Add the pumpkin, carrots, and zucchini (better to boil all beforehand to eliminate some K+)"],[null,"Cook for about 30 minutes on medium heat."],[null,"Grind the soup with hand blinder until smoothing. (Add water for more smother texture)"],[null,"Serve in a bowl and garnish with coriander."],[null,"Enjoy it with a squeeze of limon."]],"h":[]},"9767450":{"s":[[null,"Add everything (except the toppings) to a food processor or blender and process until smooth."],[null,"Transfer to a shallow dish, and add some chocolate chips and/or chopped nuts, if using and place in the freezer for one hour."],[null,"Remove from the freezer and give your ice cream a good mix, especially around the edges as that will freeze first. Return to the freezer for one more hour. Then serve topped with more chocolate chips and nuts, if you'd like, and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"If your dates are very dry (happens if they’ve been sitting in your pantry a while), soak them in cool water for 15-20 minutes and then drain, before adding to your blender or food processor. For smoothest results , use a high speed food processor or blender. Tastes best when consumed within 2-3 hours of freezing . However, you may keep frozen in an airtight, freezer safe container for up to 3 months. Place a sheet of plastic wrap on top of your nice cream, before sealing the lid to prevent freezer burn. Once frozen overnight, the nice cream will freeze solid. Remove from the freezer 15-20 minutes before you plan to enjoy, to make scooping easier."]]},"9727858":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your waffle iron over medium heat."],[null,"Combine all the wet ingredients in a mixing bowl. Then add the dry ingredients and stir until combined without overmixing."],[null,"Ladle the waffle batter onto your preheated waffle iron and cook them for approx. 7-8 minutes. NOTE: These waffles take a little longer to cook than classic waffles."],[null,"Serve the waffles warm with chocolate chips, fresh fruit, nuts, maple syrup or any of your favourite toppings."]],"h":[]},"6556849":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F and line a muffin tin with liners."],[null,"Mix flour, sugar, baking soda, salt, pumpkin pie spice in a large bowl."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix together the eggs, pumpkin puree, oil, banana, and vanilla."],[null,"Pour the wet ingredients into the dry ingredients and stir to combine. Gently fold in the walnuts."],[null,"Scoop the batter into muffin tins and bake for 18-20 minutes, until a toothpick comes out clean."]],"h":[]},"6551725":{"s":[[null,"In a 3-quart saucepan, whisk together the sweetener and the corn starch."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the milk and egg yolks. Over medium heat, slowly whisk the egg mixture into the sweetener mixture. Bring to boiling, continuing to whisk the mixture until it thickens, about 3 to 5 minutes."],[null,"Add the pumpkin, cinnamon, cloves, ginger, and nutmeg. Mix well and cook on low heat for 3 minutes. Add the vanilla bean seeds and cook 1 minute more."],[null,"Remove the saucepan from the stove. Place the pudding in a bowl and cover with plastic wrap. Refrigerate for 1 hour before serving. To serve, spoon the pudding into individual dishes, top each dish with 1/2 Tbsp pecans, and dust with cinnamon. If desired, dollop with whipped topping."]],"h":[]},"2619":{"s":[[null,"Combine ginger ale and grape juice concentrate in a large punch bowl."],[null,"Scoop sherbet into punch and stir to mix."]],"h":[[null,"Not recommended for persons with diabetes due to high carbohydrate content."]]},"7923594":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200°C/fan 180°C/gas 6. Line a couple of baking sheets with baking parchment and spray 10–12 evenly spaced spots with oil."],[null,"Sift the gram and rice flours into a mixing bowl. Add the turmeric, carom seeds, ground coriander and chilli powder."],[null,"Add 6 tablespoons of cold water and mix well, turning the spiced flours into a thick paste and squashing any lumps that may form."],[null,"Add the onions to the batter and stir them through for a couple of minutes to completely coat them with the batter. They will soften slightly, too, as they release moisture when stirred."],[null,"Using a couple of tablespoons, load even amounts of batter-covered onions onto the spots of oil on the baking sheets. Bring any stray bits of onion close to the mound so you don’t get too many burnt edges."],[null,"When the onions are all used up, spray each mound with more oil and place in the oven for 20 minutes. Remove from the oven, flip the pakoras over and cook for another 10 minutes. Allow to rest for 5 minutes before you tuck in."]],"h":[[null,"Make sure the onions are very finely sliced to ensure they come out of the oven well-cooked through."],[null,"Extract from Masala by Mallika Basu, Photographs © Issy Croker"]]},"7778417":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 190°C/gas mark 5."],[null,"Add the oil to a baking sheet, place the red peppers and onions on top, then roast for 20 - 25 minutes, turning occasionally. Allow to cool, then chop finely."],[null,"While these are cooling, prepare your vegetables for dipping."],[null,"Mix the Ras El Hanout and pepper into the quark, then mix in the roast onions and peppers."],[null,"Place the dip in a serving dish or bowl, sprinkle with chives, then serve with the vegetable sticks."]],"h":[[null,"For a vegan version, use a non-dairy alternative."],[null,"This dip is also great in a wholemeal tortilla or pitta bread stuffed with salad."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"9864024":{"s":[[null,"Drain and rinse your jackfruit very well and use your hands to pull apart the chunks to resemble shredded chicken. Use all the pieces, even the slightly harder core bits, no need to toss any of that out."],[null,"Add the oil (if using) to a pan and over medium high heat, sauté the jackfruit until lightly browned, approx. 8-10 minutes."],[null,"Then add the veggie slices and ALL the seasoning and sauté an additional 2-3 minutes until the peppers are tender crisp. Do not over cook. Remove from the heat and serve with tortillas and toppings of choice."]],"h":[[null,"Make sure to use young green jackfruit canned in water or brine . Do not sub for fresh jackfruit, dried jackfruit that comes packaged and seasoned, or canned jackfruit in syrup. Do not overcook the veggies , you want them tender crisp for the best texture. Serve the jackfruit fajitas unassembled and let everyone make their own. The tortillas will get soggy if assembled too far in advance. Store leftovers in separate containers (don’t store assembled fajitas or they’ll get soggy) in your fridge for 3-4 days."]]},"9354381":{"s":[[null,"Bring a large pot of generously salted water to a boil and cook your pasta according to package directions for 'al dente' pasta. Drain and set it aside."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the tofu, broth, nutritional yeast, lemon juice, garlic, thyme, salt, and pepper to a blender and process until smooth."],[null,"Transfer the sauce to a large skillet and add the spinach and tomatoes. Heat over medium heat until the spinach is wilted. Then stir in the cooked pasta, mix well, and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Salt your pasta water. Make sure to add enough salt to your pot of water for the best texture and flavour. Here's a handy guide to help you salt your water perfectly each time."],[null,"Cook your pasta 'al dente' . Al dente pasta is typically 1-3 minutes \"underdone\". This is how Italians eat their pasta. 😉 We like a little bit of bite, and no mush."],[null,"Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-4 days. The sauce will thicken as it cools, so reheat on the stovetop with a splash of broth to loosen until heated through."]]},"9733821":{"s":[[null,"Place the drained chickpeas in a mixing bowl and use a fork or potato masher to gently mash them. Leave some whole, don't over mash, you want some texture."],[null,"Add all remaining salad ingredients and mix well."],[null,"Serve on sliced bread of choice (soft or toasted), with lettuce, tomato and pickles, if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Do not overly mash your chickpeas . You want texture, so keep some pieces whole. Prepare the salad in advance , but hold off on assembling your sandwich until the day you plan to eat it to prevent soggy bread. Try this chickpea salad without the bread , if preferred. Top it over a bed of romaine, iceberg or baby spinach. You may also make it a wrap. Or spread it on crackers or celery. Nutritional information includes one third of the chickpea salad, without any bread or toppings. Individual brands of sliced bread will vary widely, so always check the nutritional label. Leftover chickpea salad keeps refrigerated for up to 4 days."]]},"1935":{"s":[[null,"Core and finely chop apple half."],[null,"Combine oats, egg and almond milk in a large mug. Stir well with a fork. Add cinnamon and apple. Stir again until fully mixed."],[null,"Cook in microwave on high for 2 minutes. Fluff with a fork. Cook an additional 30 to 60 seconds if needed."],[null,"Stir in a little more milk or water if thinner cereal is desired."]],"h":[[null,"For additional flavor replace ground cinnamon with finely grated stick cinnamon."],[null,"Cooking time may vary for different microwaves."],[null,"Drizzle oatmeal with 2 teaspoons of honey if desired. Count as an additional 12 grams of carbohydrate and 1 carbohydrate choice if you follow a carbohydrate counting meal plan for diabetes."],[null,"Substitute 1/4 cup 1% low fat milk and 1/4 cup water for almond milk if preferred. This changes the protein to 12 grams, phosphorus to 278 mg and potassium to 358 mg."],[null,"Oatmeal is higher in potassium and phosphorus compared to refined grains, but can be included in most kidney diets. Discuss with your dietitian if you are unsure."]]},"1758":{"s":[[null,"Shred cooked chicken breast meat."],[null,"In a large wok, heat 1 tablespoon of the oil and add the broccoli slaw; cook for 5 minutes."],[null,"Add hoisin sauce, water and remaining 2 tablespoons oil to wok. Stir together."],[null,"Add shredded chicken to wok. Stir chicken and broccoli slaw together"],[null,"Serve over rice or rice noodles if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Serve over rice or rice noodles if desired."],[null,"Two cooked chicken breasts yield approximately 8 ounces."],[null,"To reduce potassium to 290 mg substitute 4 cups of shredded green cabbage for the broccoli slaw."],[null,"Hoisin sauce is usually found in the Chinese or Asian food section of most grocery stores. It is high in sodium—limit the amount used."]]},"3003":{"s":[[null,"Chop onion. In a large saucepan, brown ground beef with onion. Drain fat."],[null,"Add seasoning and browning sauce, broth, water, rice and mixed vegetables."],[null,"Bring to a boil on high heat. Reduce to medium-low heat, cover and cook 30 minutes."],[null,"Remove from heat, stir in sour cream and serve."],[null,"Optional preparation method:"],[null,"Mix uncooked ground beef, chopped onion, Mrs. Dash and Kitchen Bouquet together in a bowl. Roll into walnut-size meat balls."],[null,"In a large saucepan combine broth, water, rice and mixed vegetables. Bring to a boil on high heat."],[null,"Drop meatballs into the boiling broth, reduce to medium-low heat and cook for 30 minutes or until meatballs are cooked through."]],"h":[[null,"Look for reduced-sodium broth containing 500 milligrams sodium or less per 1 cup serving. Avoid low-sodium broth that contains potassium chloride—it is very high in potassium."],[null,"Optional vegetable mixture includes cauliflower, carrots and snow peas (reduces phosphorus to 190 milligrams per serving.)"]]},"6226659":{"s":[[null,"Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium heat."],[null,"Add the garlic and red pepper flakes, if using, to the skillet. Sauté for 1–2 minutes until the garlic becomes fragrant."],[null,"Add the collard greens to the skillet. Toss to coat in the garlic and oil."],[null,"Sauté the collard greens for 5–7 minutes, or until they are wilted and tender."],[null,"Season with the salt and black pepper."],[null,"Drizzle apple cider vinegar over the collard greens. Toss to combine."],[null,"Continue cooking for an additional 2–3 minutes, allowing the flavors to meld."]],"h":[]},"6921067":{"s":[[null,"In a salad bowl, mix together the broccoli slaw, raisins, and turkey bacon."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the mayonnaise, yogurt, and vinegar. Pour the dressing over the salad and toss to coat."]],"h":[]},"6064318":{"s":[[null,"Microwave the frozen squash for 5 minutes."],[null,"In a large soup pot, heat the oil over medium-high heat. Add the onion and carrot and sauté for 5 minutes, or until clear. Add the garlic and sauté for 30 seconds. Add the squash and sauté for 3 minutes."],[null,"Add the remaining ingredients. Bring to a boil, reduce heat, and simmer for 15 minutes."],[null,"After the soup has cooled slightly, transfer it to a blender and blend until smooth or use an immersion blender in the pot to blend until smooth. If desired, return the pureed soup to the pot to reheat before serving."]],"h":[]},"7563745":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a non-stick frying pan."],[null,"Add the onion and fry for 4-5 minutes until softened. Add the curry paste and continue to fry for 2 minutes."],[null,"Add the tomatoes, bring to the boil and simmer for 2 minutes."],[null,"Transfer to a food processor and blend until almost smooth."],[null,"Return to the pan, add the chicken and heat for 5-7 minutes or until the chicken is cooked."],[null,"Stir in the ground almonds and yogurt, heat through gently - without boiling. Top with a few toasted almonds and serve with plenty of steamed basmati rice."]],"h":[[null,"This is also great served cold with plenty of salad in a rolled-up roti or tortilla."],[null,"For a veggie version, just make the sauce then toss in chunks of cooked sweet potatoes and sautéed whole mushrooms in place of the chicken."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Then defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat thoroughly until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"3298":{"s":[[null,"Chop onion and garlic. Drain and rinse hominy."],[null,"Brown beef in a Dutch oven."],[null,"Add to beef and sauté until onion is transparent."],[null,"Add remaining ingredients and simmer for 30 to 45 minutes."],[null,"Serve with warm bread or crackers."]],"h":[[null,"To thicken, sprinkle in a little corn meal."],[null,"Portion and freeze leftover chili for a quick meal later."]]},"7396460":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4. Use the sunflower oil to lightly grease a 1lb loaf tin (approx 19cm x 10cm)."],[null,"Place the raisins in a bowl with the cinnamon and 100ml boiling water. Set aside."],[null,"In another bowl, mash the banana and mix with the yoghurt."],[null,"In a large bowl, mix the flour and bicarbonate of soda together."],[null,"Add the banana and yoghurt mix to the flour mixture. Add the raisins and water and mix thoroughly. Pour the mixture into the loaf tin."],[null,"Bake for 25 minutes until firm and golden. The bread is cooked when a knife inserted into the centre comes out clean."]],"h":[[null,"Once the wet ingredients are added to the dry ones, you activate the bicarbonate of soda, so pop it into the oven quickly for maximum lightness."],[null,"You could use any dried fruit instead of raisins, such as chopped apricots, sultanas, prunes or mixed fruit."],[null,"Try adding a teaspoon of mixed spice or a pinch of ground cloves."],[null,"You can freeze this bread, whole or cut into slices, for up to three months. Simply wrap in foil, put into freezer bags and label. This fruity bread can be toasted from frozen."]]},"3189":{"s":[[null,"Thaw pineapple just enough to get out of can."],[null,"Place all fruit in food processor and process until pureed."],[null,"Serve immediately or spread into an 8” x 8” pan and freeze."]],"h":[[null,"You can freeze unopened can of pineapple."]]},"6282037":{"s":[[null,"In a small saucepan, stir together all the ingredients except the parsley. Bring to a simmer over medium-low heat. Reduce the heat and simmer for 5 minutes. Carefully pour into a blender and process until smooth (or remove from the heat and use an immersion, or handheld, blender."],[null,"Return to the pan. Heat over medium-low heat for 2 to 3 minutes, or until just simmering. Ladle into bowls. Garnish with the parsley."]],"h":[]},"6081174":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400 degrees F."],[null,"Coat a large loaf pan generously with cooking spray. In a small bowl, whisk together ketchup and balsamic vinegar."],[null,"In a medium bowl, combine all ingredients and half of the ketchup-balsamic mixture. Set aside the other half. Mix the turkey meatloaf ingredients well."],[null,"Spread the mixture evenly into the loaf pan. Top with the remaining ketchup-balsamic mixture."],[null,"Bake for 60 minutes or until it reaches 165 degrees F when checked with a thermometer."]],"h":[]},"3703":{"s":[[null,"Wash and core apples. Trim 1-2 inches of the peel from the top of the apples."],[null,"Place apples in a high-sided microwave-safe bowl."],[null,"Pour honey into center of cored apples."],[null,"Add nutmeg and cinnamon."],[null,"Cover bowl with a microwave-safe lid. Microwave on high for about 6 minutes."],[null,"Serve immediately, topped with whipped topping."]],"h":[[null,"Small microwave ovens require 6 minutes to cook a medium apple. Cooking times vary depending on the size of the apples and the microwave. Apple is done when it is easy to cut."],[null,"Avoid covering food with plastic wrap during microwaving due to possible contamination of food with toxins from the plastic."],[null,"Reduce portion to 1/2 apple for a lower carbohydrate dessert."]]},"2567":{"s":[[null,"Heat olive oil in a pan over medium heat. Add chicken and sprinkle with pepper."],[null,"Sauté chicken for 5 minutes on each side, until brown."],[null,"Add balsamic vinegar and sauté for one minute, flipping chicken over to coat."],[null,"Add honey and basil. Stir and flip chicken to coat. Cook for one minute longer."],[null,"Remove to a plate and spoon pan sauce over chicken."]],"h":[[null,"Be creative and season chicken with herbs or low sodium seasoning blends of your own choice. Garlic and onion powder go well with the black pepper."],[null,"If you are on a lower protein diet, decrease the portion to 1/2 chicken breast or substitute smaller boneless chicken thighs for the breast meat."]]},"2881":{"s":[[null,"Chop bell pepper and parsley."],[null,"Prepare frozen vegetables according to package instructions."],[null,"Mix oil, vinegar and Mrs. Dash® herb seasoning. Toss with vegetables and hot pasta."],[null,"Sprinkle with chopped parsley. Serve with lemon wedge."]],"h":[[null,"Left over portion is good as a cold pasta salad. Add 1 tablespoon Italian salad dressing–choose a lower sodium brand."]]},"2043":{"s":[[null,"Blend cottage cheese, sour cream, green onions, hot sauce and spices in food processor until smooth."],[null,"Add blue cheese and process for a few seconds."],[null,"Garnish with chopped green onion, if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Dip stores well, which enhances cheese and garlic flavors. If storing for more than three days, reduce blue cheese and garlic."],[null,"Natural, unprocessed sharp cheddar can substitute for blue cheese. Recipe limits the blue cheese to 1-1/3 teaspoon per serving."],[null,"Other spices can be added to taste. Experiment!"],[null,"This dip is lower in phosphorus and higher in protein than many comparable recipes."],[null,"Pair with low-sodium crackers, raw veggies, sliced apples or low-salt tortilla."]]},"6195958":{"s":[[null,"Cook dried quinoa in water according to package directions."],[null,"Puree 1 can black beans, 1/4 cup salsa and egg in a blender or food processor until smooth."],[null,"Pour cooked quinoa in a medium bowl; add pureed beans, remaining 1 can black beans, cornmeal, chili powder, cumin and cayenne pepper and mix together until well blended."],[null,"Form bean mixture into nine, 1/2-inch thick patties."],[null,"Coat a large skillet or grill pan with cooking spray and heat over medium heat. Add black bean patties and grill about 2-3 minutes per side, until slightly brown."],[null,"Serve each black bean burger in lettuce wrap topped with 1 Tbsp. salsa and an avocado slice."]],"h":[]},"6178626":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400°F. Coat a large baking sheet with Cooking Spray."],[null,"Cook quinoa according to package directions. Fluff with a fork and set aside to cool."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine cooked quinoa with onion, garlic, black beans, 1 Tbsp cilantro, carrot, flour, baking powder, egg, salt (optional) and pepper."],[null,"Form mixture into eight patties (press firmly to form patty) and place onto prepared baking sheet. Spray the top of the cakes with Cooking Spray."],[null,"Bake the cakes for 15 minutes, then flip. Respray them with the cooking spray. Continue cooking for 15 more minutes or until lightly golden brown."],[null,"While the cakes are baking, combine the remaining cilantro, yogurt and lime juice in small bowl. Serve the sauce with the warm quinoa cakes."]],"h":[]},"6259247":{"s":[[null,"Rinse quinoa under cold water for 2 minutes."],[null,"Whisk together milk, fat-free half-and-half, brown sugar blend, vanilla, cinnamon, and nutmeg in a medium saucepan over medium heat. Bring to a simmer."],[null,"Once the milk mixture is simmering, stir in quinoa and reduce heat to a low simmer. Partially cover the pan and cook 40 minutes, stirring every 10 minutes."],[null,"When quinoa is done cooking, stir in toasted pumpkin seeds and serve."]],"h":[]},"3808":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350º F."],[null,"Chop onion and dice celery. Set aside."],[null,"Add stock and water to medium saucepan and bring to a boil over high heat. Stir in the quinoa and bring back to a boil. Reduce the heat to low, cover, and simmer for 12 minutes, or until the quinoa has absorbed all the liquid."],[null,"Meanwhile, melt the butter in a large skillet over medium heat. Stir in the onion and celery, stirring occasionally, until translucent, about 10 minutes."],[null,"Remove the onion mixture from the heat. Add quinoa to the onion mixture. Stir in the parsley, sage, garlic and pepper. Mix thoroughly."],[null,"Add cranberries to dressing and mix."],[null,"Transfer the dressing to an 8″ square pan and bake for 30 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Quinoa is higher in potassium and phosphorus compared to other whole grains, but is a good source of protein and fiber. In general, only half of the phosphorus in whole grains is absorbed during digestion. By limiting the portion you may still enjoy quinoa in your kidney diet. Check with your dietitian."],[null,"Each stalk of celery yields about 1 cup after trimmed and diced."],[null,"This recipe works well as a stuffing."]]},"6893480":{"s":[[null,"Combine the milk and water in a large saucepan and bring to a simmer over medium heat."],[null,"Add the oats, quinoa, honey, cinnamon, vanilla, and salt. Reduce the heat to low."],[null,"Cover and cook, stirring occasionally, until the oats and quinoa are tender, about 15 minutes. Serve topped with the raspberries and almonds."]],"h":[]},"9463454":{"s":[[null,"Add the quinoa and vegetable broth to a small pot. Bring to a boil, then reduce heat and simmer until the broth is completely absorbed, approx. 12-15 minutes. Stir often towards the end of cooking. Set aside to cool slightly."],[null,"While the quinoa is cooking, add all the dressing ingredients in a small bowl and mix well. Set aside, Then chop up your veggies, if you haven't already."],[null,"Transfer your cooked quinoa to a large bowl and add all the veggies and mix. Then pour the dressing on top and mix well to evenly coat. Chill for 1 hour or longer, or enjoy immediately."]],"h":[[null,"Feel free to sub or omit any veggies you’re not fond of . Some other options that would be great in this quinoa pasta salad include: Corn (thawed frozen, or canned)"],[null,"Halved cherry or grape tomatoes"],[null,"Bite sized broccoli florets"],[null,"Chopped pickles"],[null,"Green onion or chives"],[null,"Diced zucchini"],[null,"If you can’t have sesame seeds , you may sub the tahini for almond butter , with similar results. Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-4 days."]]},"6614257":{"s":[[null,"Add the olive oil to a medium saucepan. Sauté onion and celery over medium-high heat and cook about 3 minutes or until the onions are clear."],[null,"Add mushrooms and cook until brown. Add the quinoa to the pan and stir for 1-2 minutes."],[null,"Slowly add the chicken broth, salt, pepper and thyme and bring to a boil. Reduce heat to low, cover and simmer. Cook 15 minutes and fluff with a fork when done."]],"h":[]},"6843906":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a large nonstick skillet or paella pan over medium-high heat. Add the onion, bell peppers, and garlic, and cook, stirring occasionally, until the vegetables are tender, about 8 minutes."],[null,"Add the tomato paste and saffron to the skillet, stirring until well mixed. Add the quinoa, broth, tomatoes, and salt; bring to a boil. Reduce the heat to medium low. Cover and simmer until the liquid is absorbed and the quinoa is tender, about 20 minutes."],[null,"Tuck the shrimp and calamari into the quinoa mixture. Cover and cook until the shrimp and calamari are cooked through, about 5 minutes. Remove from the heat; sprinkle with parsley and garnish with lemon wedges."]],"h":[]},"7157800":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4. Cut the squash in half lengthways, scoop out the seeds and bake 35-40 minutes until tender."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the quinoa to a pan of boiling water, bring to the boil and turn down the heat. Cover and simmer gently for 10-15 minutes."],[null,"Add the oil to another pan and cook the onions and pepper for 5 minutes. Add the cumin, garlic and chilli flakes and cook for another 2 minutes."],[null,"Drain off any excess water from the quinoa and stir it into the onion mixture. Add the pumpkin seeds and mix well."],[null,"Mound the quinoa onto the squash, top with the tomatoes and bake a further 10 minutes. Serve with sprigs of rosemary."]],"h":[[null,"You could use couscous or bulgar wheat for the stuffing, instead of the quinoa."],[null,"Try using different spices, such as curry paste, or fresh herbs, such as coriander or tarragon."],[null,"Top with a little low-fat cheese if desired."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat in the oven or microwave until piping hot."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"6567846":{"s":[[null,"Rinse quinoa and then combine with 1 ½ cups water. Bring to a boil then reduce to simmer. Cover and cook for 15 minutes or until all liquid is absorbed. Fluff with a fork and then cool completely."],[null,"Combine cooled quinoa with olive oil, lemon zest, lemon juice, tomato, cucumber, parsley, mint, salt (optional), and ground black pepper. Refrigerate or serve."]],"h":[]},"6830683":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6245289":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, toss together the quinoa, apricots, onion, pine nuts, feta cheese, and lemon juice."],[null,"Place 1 cup of the arugula in a small salad bowl and drizzle with ½ tsp of the olive oil. Toss lightly to coat, then top with ¼ of the quinoa mixture (about 1/3 cup) and season with pepper to taste."],[null,"Repeat for the remaining three salads."]],"h":[]},"6086214":{"s":[[null,"Place 1/4 cup raw quinoa in a fine-mesh strainer and rinse thoroughly under cold water for about 30 seconds."],[null,"Add the rinsed quinoa and 1/2 cup of water to a small saucepan."],[null,"Bring the mixture to a boil over medium-high heat."],[null,"Turn the heat to low, cover the pot with a lid, and simmer for 15 minutes, or until the water is fully absorbed."],[null,"Remove the pan from the heat and let it sit (covered) for 5 minutes to steam."],[null,"Remove the lid and fluff with a fork."]],"h":[]},"6749490":{"s":[[null,"Rinse the quinoa under cold water."],[null,"In a medium saucepan, bring 1 cup of water to a boil. Add the quinoa, reduce heat to low, cover, and simmer for about 15 minutes, or until the water is absorbed. Remove from the heat and let it sit, covered, for 5 minutes. Fluff with a fork.​"],[null,"In a bowl, whisk together the egg whites, salt, and chopped chives.​"],[null,"Heat a 10-inch nonstick skillet over medium-low heat and lightly coat with nonstick cooking spray.​"],[null,"Pour half the egg mixture into the skillet, swirling to evenly coat the bottom. Cook until the bottom is just set and the top is slightly moist, approximately 3–4 minutes. Carefully flip the wrap and cook for an additional 10 seconds. Transfer to a plate and repeat with the remaining egg mixture."],[null,"In a food processor, combine the baby spinach and parsley leaves. Pulse until finely chopped. Fold into the cooked quinoa."],[null,"To assemble, lay each egg wrap flat on a clean surface.​ Spread a generous tablespoon of lemon hummus over half of each wrap. Spoon half the quinoa mixture over the hummus, pressing gently to adhere. Top with slices of tomato. Fold the wraps in half over the filling, then fold once more to create a quarter-fold."]],"h":[]},"2341":{"s":[[null,"Peel and cube potatoes. Place in a pan and cover with water. Bring to a boil, remove from heat and drain water. Add fresh water and boil for 5 minutes. Drain and set aside."],[null,"Clean chicken, remove and discard skin."],[null,"In a large pot heat oil over medium-high heat. Add chicken pieces and brown on both sides."],[null,"Sprinkle salt, pepper, garlic powder and half the dill weed over chicken pieces."],[null,"Stir cornstarch into 1/4 cup of water. Add remaining water and stir into pot with chicken and seasonings."],[null,"Place green beans on top of chicken, cover pot and cook for 15 minutes or until beans are fork tender."],[null,"Add remaining dill weed and potatoes to pot. Add additional water if needed. Cover and cook for 5 to 8 minutes until potatoes are tender."],[null,"Garnish with a sprig of dill and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Double boiling potatoes reduces potassium content. A second method is to peel and soak potatoes in water for 2-4 hours before cooking. Skip this step if yu do not require a low potassium diet."],[null,"Dried dill weed can be substituted for fresh dill weed. As a general rule, use half the amount because dried herbs are more potent."],[null,"Frozen green beans may be used instead of fresh."]]},"6513384":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the vinegar, salt, pepper, olive oil, and mint."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine the watermelon, onion, radishes, and feta cheese."],[null,"Add dressing and stir gently to combine. Serve on a bed of baby arugula."]],"h":[]},"6499683":{"s":[[null,"Toast the bread under the broiler or in a toaster."],[null,"Place the ricotta cheese and chives (reserve some chives for garnishing) in a blender or food processor and purée until smooth. Set aside."],[null,"Carefully slice (using a mandolin if you have one) the radishes into ⅛ thick rounds."],[null,"Divide the cheese and chive mixture between the 4 slices of bread and smooth into an even layer."],[null,"Top the cheese with slices of radishes and any extra chopped chives. Sprinkle with pepper if desired."]],"h":[]},"7639641":{"s":[[null,"Add the sweet potatoes and carrots to a pan of boiling water and boil for 10 minutes."],[null,"Add the asparagus and carry on boiling for 5 minutes."],[null,"Check that the asparagus is cooked and remove from the pan, check the carrots and sweet potatoes too and either remove or carry on cooking for a couple of minutes if they're not yet tender."],[null,"Once the sweet potatoes and carrots are cooked turn off heat and add the broad beans and peas to the pan. This will defrost them and stop the other vegetables from over cooking."],[null,"Drain the vegetables, allow to cool then dice the sweet potato and carrot and cut the asparagus into ½ cm rings."],[null,"Make the dressing by mixing all the ingredients together."],[null,"Fold the sweet potato, carrot, asparagus, broad beans and peas into the dressing and serve."]],"h":[[null,"You can add almost any cooked vegetables to this salad including green beans, celery and apple."],[null,"If you want a warm rainbow salad then just dice and mix the vegetables together as soon as they're cooked and serve immediately."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"2346":{"s":[[null,"In a large mixing bowl, place the water and yeast and stir to dissolve. Let stand 5 minutes."],[null,"Add the Rice Dream®, oil, salt and sugar."],[null,"Beat in the flour, cornmeal and eggs to mix, but do not over beat."],[null,"Set the mixture in a warm place until mixture just begins to rise, about 15 minutes."],[null,"Cook in a pre-heated waffle iron."],[null,"Divide cooked waffle into 2-square portions (1/2 large waffle) and top with your favorite syrup, fruit spread or fresh fruit."]],"h":[[null,"For those with diabetes, top with a sugar free syrup or fruit spread."],[null,"1/2 cup whole wheat flour may be substituted for 1/2 cup white flour. Waffles are higher in fiber (2.3 g for 2 small squares), potassium 130 mg, phosphorus 119 mg."]]},"6760120":{"s":[],"h":[]},"2073":{"s":[[null,"Cook pasta as directed on package, omitting salt; drain and set aside."],[null,"In a large saucepan or Dutch oven, melt butter. Whisk in flour until smooth."],[null,"Gradually add rice milk and seasonings."],[null,"Bring to a boil. Cook and stir for 2 minutes or until thickened."],[null,"Reduce heat and fold in sour cream until well mixed."],[null,"Add chicken and pasta. Cook and stir until heated through."],[null,"Remove from heat. Stir in Mexican cheese blend until melted. Sprinkle with parmesan cheese and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Freeze leftovers in individual portions for a quick meal later."],[null,"Chicken may be increased to make a higher protein dish."],[null,"Add 2 cups cooked broccoli or carrots in step 6 to make a one dish meal."],[null,"The cheese in this recipe contributes 1-1/2 tablespoons per serving and 56 mg phosphorus which is acceptable for a kidney diet. For a lower phosphorus version you can omit the cheeses."],[null,"Ask your dietitian to recommend the rice milk or nondairy creamer brand lowest in phosphorus and potassium."]]},"6413436":{"s":[[null,"Place the eggs in a single layer in a saucepan and cover them with water. Bring the water to a boil, then reduce the heat and simmer for about 10 minutes."],[null,"Transfer the eggs to a bowl of ice water to cool. Peel the eggs when they are cool enough to handle."],[null,"Cut the peeled hard-boiled eggs in half lengthwise and carefully remove the yolks."],[null,"Place the yolks in a bowl and mash them with a fork. To the mashed yolks, add ¼ cup low-fat mayonnaise, 1 teaspoon of Dijon mustard, 1 tablespoon ranch dressing mix. Mix everything together until well combined and season with salt and pepper to taste."],[null,"Once the filling is ready, spoon or pipe it back into the egg white halves. Consider using a plastic bag with the corner snipped off for a neater look."],[null,"Refrigerate for at least 30 minutes before serving to allow the flavors to meld. Sprinkle lightly with paprika. Serve chilled and enjoy these delicious, diabetes-friendly appetizers or snacks."]],"h":[]},"3725":{"s":[[null,"Place all the ingredients in a jar with a lid. Shake well until ingredients are blended."],[null,"Refrigerate for 30 minutes before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute with low-fat mayonnaise and sour cream to reduce fat and calories."]]},"6514260":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6111989":{"s":[],"h":[]},"9553231":{"s":[[null,"Line a tray with parchment paper and set it aside."],[null,"Add all the ingredients to your food processor bowl. Pulse until well combined without completely pureéing the mixture."],[null,"Use a small cookie scoop or spoon to scoop the mixture and roll balls. Place each ball on your lined tray. OPTIONAL: Roll some of the balls in cocoa powder or shredded coconut."],[null,"Refrigerate for 1 hour or longer to chill and set. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Don’t over-blend the mixture, as these snacks taste best with a little bit of texture."],[null,"The batter is a little sticky, so use wet hands to roll the mixture into balls to prevent it from sticking to your hands."],[null,"The rolled balls will be soft, so refrigerate them for at least 1 hour before enjoying them to help them harden and set."],[null,"Keep your raspberry bliss balls refrigerated for up to 5 days. Or freeze them for up to 3 months."]]},"3467":{"s":[[null,"In a medium saucepan, cook berries on medium heat for about 10 minutes, until fruit begins to break down. Mash with a spoon or potato masher to help break the fruit into smaller pieces."],[null,"Stir in chia seeds and the lemon juice."],[null,"Remove from heat and let cool until it starts to thicken."],[null,"Store in an airtight container in the refrigerator."]],"h":[[null,"You may substitute various other fruit for the raspberries, such as blueberries, strawberries, peaches or pineapple."],[null,"Use as you would any jam on bread, crackers or in oatmeal."],[null,"If you do prefer more sweetness, add 1 tablespoon honey, natural maple syrup or agave syrup. This is option and will add more sugar to the recipe."],[null,"This jam can be refrigerated for up to 3 weeks or freeze for up to 3 months."],[null,"Less potassium and phosphorus is absorbed in the body in plant based foods, like seeds and fruit."]]},"7320020":{"s":[[null,"Place half of the raspberries into a blender or food processor and purée."],[null,"Mix together the yoghurt and sugar and transfer to a freezer-proof container, freeze for 1 hour, stir well then gently fold through the remaining raspberries and the raspberry purée."],[null,"Return to the freezer for 30 minutes, then mix again with a fork and and return to the freezer. Freeze a further 30 minutes until solid."],[null,"Remove from freezer for 5 minutes before serving"]],"h":[[null,"You could use most fruits with this method, try mango, blueberry, strawberry or nectarine."],[null,"If using an ice-cream scoop to serve, dip it into hot water between scoops for easy serving."]]},"7967911":{"s":[[null,"In a bowl, gently crush half the raspberries with a fork and mix with the sweetener."],[null,"In another bowl, crumble up the shortbread biscuits."],[null,"Reserve a couple of whole raspberries and a little crushed shortbread, to garnish."],[null,"Fold the remaining whole and crushed raspberries, plus the shortbread, into the yogurt."],[null,"Arrange in glasses or bowls, sprinkle with crushed shortbread and top with a raspberry."]],"h":[[null,"This recipe works well with strawberries or blackberries, too. Or try chopped peaches or nectarines."],[null,"Try using a different biscuits, such as digestives or ginger biscuits."],[null,"For a vegan version, use a soy or coconut-based dairy free alternative to the yogurt."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Remove from freezer a few minutes before serving."]]},"6281813":{"s":[[null,"In a blender or food processor, puree all of the ingredients until smooth."],[null,"Pour the dressing through a fine mesh strainer to remove the seeds."],[null,"Store in the fridge in an airtight container for up to 1 week."]],"h":[]},"2861":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400° F."],[null,"Heat the jam, soy sauce and vinegar in a saucepan, stirring until smooth."],[null,"Place the wings in a large bowl. Pour the jam sauce over wings and toss to coat heavily."],[null,"Place the chicken wings in a large baking dish sprayed with nonstick cooking spray."],[null,"Bake for 30 to 35 minutes. Check for doneness."],[null,"Serve the wings hot or place in a covered warming dish or crock pot on low setting until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Buy fresh wing drummettes. A 1-1/4 pound package contains 12 drummettes. If unavailable, ask your butcher to cut whole chicken wings into drummette size."],[null,"Boneless chicken pieces may be used in this recipe. Check for doneness after 20 minutes."]]},"3028":{"s":[[null,"Thinly slice lime."],[null,"Finely chop mint leaves."],[null,"Add all ingredients to a pitcher."],[null,"Refrigerator overnight before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Add a few berries to each cup of flavored water."],[null,"For variety try strawberries instead of raspberries."],[null,"If you are on limited fluids, adjust the portion size to meet your needs."],[null,"After flavors develop you can pour into ice cube trays to make flavored ice."]]},"3002":{"s":[[null,"Dice onion, squash, eggplant, carrots and peppers. Mince garlic cloves. Add canola or olive oil to large skillet, with garlic, herbs, black pepper and carrots."],[null,"Cook 2 minutes, then add the rest of the vegetables, except tomatoes."],[null,"Sauté well and stir frequently, 10–15 minutes or until vegetables are semi-tender."],[null,"Add tomatoes and parmesan cheese and mix well."],[null,"Simmer covered for approximately 1/2 hour."]],"h":[[null,"If using dried herbs instead of fresh, decrease to 1 teaspoon each instead of 1 tablespoon."],[null,"Substitute an Italian herb blend for separate herbs, if desired."],[null,"If you are on a low potassium diet count as 1-1/2 vegetable servings."],[null,"Prepare Ratatouille as a side dish or add pasta (small shells, bow ties or elbows) or make it a complete meal by adding cooked ground turkey, chicken or beef."],[null,"Freeze extra portions for a quick dish later."]]},"6119094":{"s":[[null,"Heat oil in a large nonstick skillet over medium-high heat. Add garlic and sauté 30 seconds."],[null,"Add remaining ingredients and cook 10-15 minutes, stirring occasionally, until vegetables are tender."]],"h":[]},"2961":{"s":[[null,"Julienne cut zuchinni and slice green onion; coarsely chop bell pepper."],[null,"Cook ravioli as directed on the package."],[null,"Spray a large, nonstick skillet with cooking spray, and heat over medium-high heat."],[null,"Add zucchini, green onions, bell pepper, garlic powder, basil and black pepper. Cook for 3 to 5 minutes until veggies are crisp-tender."],[null,"Drain ravioli, add broth, and stir into the vegetable mixture."],[null,"Cover skillet and cook over medium-low heat for another 5 minutes, or until thoroughly heated. Stir occasionally, being careful not to break the ravioli."]],"h":[[null,"If vegetables are prepared earlier, this is a quick and easy meal that anyone can put together."],[null,"Goes well with tossed salad and French bread."],[null,"Try other types of ravioli–frozen or fresh, beef or chicken."]]},"1893":{"s":[[null,"Combine Mrs. Dash® herb seasoning with sour cream and refrigerate at least one hour to blend flavors."],[null,"Cut each celery stalk in half lengthwise, then cut each into 4 pieces."],[null,"Cut carrot in half lengthwise, then cut into 4 pieces."],[null,"Cut bell pepper in half and remove seeds. Slice into 8 pieces."],[null,"Slice cucumber half into 8 slices."],[null,"Prepare radishes."],[null,"Place dip in dish and arrange with veggies on a serving platter."]],"h":[[null,"Try different salt-free seasoning blends for a variety of flavors."]]},"4280791":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350°F. If using store-bought dough, let the pie shell thaw at room temperature for a couple of minutes. Use a nonstick spray to coat the bottom of a pie dish, place dough into pie dish."],[null,"In a bowl, fold together the berries, sugar, cinnamon and lemon juice. Pour into the pie shell."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix together flour, sugar, melted butter and egg. Spread this mixture over the berries in the pie shell."],[null,"Bake for 45–60 minutes until the pie shell is golden brown and the fruits become bubbly."]],"h":[["Store-bought pastry shells","While moderation is recommended to limit unwanted fat and calories, an occasional dessert like fruit pie, can be part of your low-potassium kidney diet. If time allows, and you make your own crust, it can be easier to control the amount of sodium and phosphorus additives you are eating. If not, keep in mind the following tips when using a store-bought pastry shell. Label reading: Review labels when using a pre-made crust. Read the Nutrition Facts label and the Ingredients list for the best selection. Depending on the type of preservatives used, the crust may be high in salt and phosphorus additives. Portion size: The portion that you eat is also important. You can cut the pie into more than the recommended 8 slices to reduce salt intake. Pie fillings: Choosing certain fruit fillings can reduce the amount of potassium in your dessert. Select lower-potassium foods such as apple, blueberry, cherry, blackberry or strawberry in place of higher-potassium banana or pumpkin."]]},"3519":{"s":[[null,"Thinly slice or shred cabbage."],[null,"Place red kidney beans and corn in a strainer and rinse under running water for 1 minute; drain."],[null,"Place cabbage, beans and corn in a bowl."],[null,"Mince garlic. In a small jar with a lid, combine garlic, balsamic vinegar and sesame oil. Shake to mix ingredients, then toss with vegetable mixture. Garnish with cilantro."]],"h":[[null,"Leftover salad keeps for several days in the refrigerator."],[null,"Beans may be limited in your meal plan due to higher potassium content. Check with your dietitian to see if this recipe fits into your plan if you are on a low potassium diet."]]},"6142402":{"s":[[null,"In a large pot, heat avocado oil over medium heat. Add onion, garlic, and ginger. Sauté until the onion becomes translucent."],[null,"Add turmeric, cumin, coriander, garam masala, and coarse salt to the pot. Stir well to coat the onions with the spices."],[null,"Pour in the diced tomatoes with their juices, coconut milk, and water. Stir to combine."],[null,"Add the red lentils to the pot. Bring the mixture to a gentle boil, then reduce the heat to low, cover, and simmer for about 20 minutes or until the lentils are tender."],[null,"Add spinach leaves to the pot and stir until wilted."]],"h":[]},"6181016":{"s":[[null,"Add olive oil to a saucepan over medium heat. Sauté onion, garlic and ginger until onions turn clear (about 4 minutes)."],[null,"Add lentils and stir to coat with oil. Add the broth and soy sauce. Bring to a boil and reduce to a simmer. Simmer, covered, for 20 minutes."],[null,"Pureé the lentils using an immersion blender or food processor and stir in scallions."],[null,"Peel the jicama and slice into nine rounds. Cut each round into quarters. Use the raw jicama to dip into the dal."]],"h":[]},"6436642":{"s":[[null,"In a small saucepan combine water and dried red lentils and bring to a boil over medium-high heat."],[null,"Reduce the heat to low and simmer, covered, stirring occasionally, about 30 minutes or until the lentils have split and become soft. Cool and transfer to a food processor."],[null,"Add the olive oil, tahini, lemon juice, minced garlic, cumin, salt and black pepper and process for 30-60 seconds or until smooth, stopping to scrape down sides as needed."],[null,"Transfer to an air-tight container and store in the refrigerator for up to 5 days until serving time."]],"h":[]},"9920004":{"s":[[null,"Line a 12\" round pizza tray with parchment paper and preheat your oven to 450 degrees F convection bake."],[null,"Add all the ingredients to a high speed blender and process on high for about 30-60 seconds, or until completely pureed."],[null,"Pour the mixture on your prepared pizza tray and spread it out as thinly and evenly as possible, using a silicone spatula."],[null,"Bake for 12 minutes. Then carefully flip the dough, using the parchment to help flip it over. Then peel off the parchment paper and return the crust to the oven for 5 more minutes until golden."],[null,"Top your pizza as desired and bake for a 3-5 minutes to heat your toppings. Then remove from the oven and let rest for 1-2 minutes before slicing."]],"h":[[null,"Make sure it’s evenly spread! For the best tasting, crispiest lentil pizza crust possible, do your best not to leave thicker spots in your crust. Be extra mindful of the center when spreading your crust to the edges. Thicker spots won’t crisp up as well. Don’t spread TOO thin. Try not to fuss too much when spreading your dough and do so gently. Gently spread the batter across your tray without moving the parchment paper around too much or you may make create gaps in your dough. The wet parchment will crease easily, so don’t use much force to spread the batter around. Use convection bake. Convection bake uses a fan to blow the hot air around your oven. By circulating the air, you’ll get a steady, dry temperature resulting in even cooking and a crispier crust. If you don’t have a convection bake oven, you may need to cook your crust for a couple of extra minutes. Just keep an eye on it until desired crispiness is reached. Use the bottom rack. Cook your lentil pizza crust on the bottom rack for best results. Again, this will help increase the crispiness of your dough. Since individual ovens vary greatly, just make sure to keep an eye on your crust to prevent it from being overdone. Parchment paper is your friend. Use the parchment paper to help flip the dough with ease after the first step of baking. Then gently remove the paper and discard to bake the other side. Topping Ideas: Vegan mozzarella w/ sautéed onions, peppers, and mushrooms with steamed broccoli."],[null,"Vegan mozzarella w/ jalapeno or hot banana peppers with red onion and pineapple."],[null,"Grilled zucchini, roasted red pepper and caramelized onion."],[null,"Very thinly sliced potato, sautéed onion and rosemary."],[null,"Caramelized onion, roasted red peppers and black or green olives."],[null,"The nutritional information is for half of the pizza crust. Toppings are not included in the calculation."]]},"7044698":{"s":[[null,"Place the lentils, onion, carrot, garlic and stock into a pan, bring to the boil and simmer for 20-25 minutes until the lentils are tender."],[null,"Transfer to a blender with the crème fraîche and parsley and blend until smooth. Season and serve with a chunk of bread"]],"h":[[null,"For a vegan version, simply omit the crème fraîche or add 4 tbsp soya milk instead."],[null,"Spice it up with 1 tsp curry paste or powder or a pinch of chilli flakes."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Freeze in portions then defrost in the fridge, or defrost in a microwave, taking care to stir regularly."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"6487300":{"s":[[null,"Bring a 6-quart pot of water, filled 2/3 full, to boiling. Add the salt. Add the green beans and turn off the heat. Let the green beans stand in the water for 3 to 4 minutes. Drain. Plunge the green beans into a bowl of ice water. Drain the beans; set aside."],[null,"In a large skillet, heat the butter and oil over medium heat. Add the onions and cook, stirring occasionally, for 20 to 25 minutes, until very soft. Lower the heat if the onions begin to brown too quickly."],[null,"Add the thyme and green beans to the onions and heat through, using tongs to gently turn the vegetables. To serve, place the onion–green bean mixture on a platter and top with the almonds and lemon zest."]],"h":[]},"4957725":{"s":[[null,"Cook the couscous according to the instructions on the package, leaving out the salt. Transfer the cooked couscous (warm or cold) to a plate and place in the refrigerator to cool."],[null,"In a bowl, combine couscous, peppers, parsley, red onions, garlic, lemon zest, lemon juice, and the olive oil. Season with pepper to taste."]],"h":[[null,"* Choose product with lowest sodium content"],[null,"This side dish can become a meal by adding a protein, such as sliced chicken, fish, or meat."],["Types and uses of couscous","Choosing a wide variety of carbohydrate sources should be part of a kidney-friendly diet. On average, these foods provide about half of your daily calories and are necessary to create the energy your body needs. Many dishes include grains such as rice, pasta or other noodles to provide these carbohydrates. These foods may contain different amounts of potassium depending on the ingredients used and seasonings added. Reading the labels and determining the correct portion size can help you pick different grains and maintain your lower-potassium diet goals. Couscous, eaten warm or cool, can be used in recipes as a grain or carbohydrate source. While the shape may look like rice or a seed, couscous is actually a small pasta. Often yellow in color, it can mix nicely with other flavors from the dish or offer a light, nuttier taste. Couscous is made from semolina and is a good source of fiber and protein. In addition, ¼ cup portion of dry couscous also fits within a kidney-friendly diet as it offers only 150 mg of potassium and 10 mg of sodium. When trying different couscous recipes, serve it prepared with a source of protein, mixed with grilled vegetables or as an addition to salad greens."]]},"6145617":{"s":[[null,"Cook quinoa in water according to package instructions, omitting any added salt."],[null,"While the quinoa is cooking, saute onion, garlic, and red pepper over medium-high heat in olive oil for about 10 minutes. Add kale and beans and continue to saute until kale is wilted, about 5 more minutes."],[null,"Stir pepper mixture, walnuts, lemon juice, and balsamic vinegar into the quinoa. Serve warm or cold."]],"h":[]},"3049":{"s":[[null,"Mince the garlic; cut the asparagus into 2″ pieces."],[null,"Heat the oil in a skillet, add the garlic and sauté for 1 minute."],[null,"Add the asparagus pieces; stir to mix."],[null,"Add the red wine vinaigrette dressing and pepper."],[null,"Stir and heat an additional minute."],[null,"Remove from the heat and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Make your own red wine vinaigrette dressing by combining equal parts of red wine vinegar and olive oil with low sodium herb blend."]]},"2242":{"s":[[null,"To make filling, beat whipped cream cheese and preserves until smooth with an electric mixer on medium speed."],[null,"Fold whipped topping into cream cheese mixture."],[null,"Spread filling evenly over the bottom of the graham cracker crust."],[null,"Chill at least 30 minutes in the refrigerator or freezer."],[null,"Before serving arrange blueberries around outer ring of pie. Layer raspberries around inner ring of pie."],[null,"Finish decorating with a dollop of whipped topping in the center and a raspberry or strawberry on top."]],"h":[[null,"Portion leftover pie into single servings, wrap and freeze for a quick dessert later."],[null,"For variety make pie with different fresh fruits and preserves. Try strawberries, peaches, pineapple or mandarin oranges."]]},"6077307":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, prepare pudding according to package directions. Cool in refrigerator for 5 minutes."],[null,"Fold whipped topping into pudding and incorporate well."],[null,"In a trifle bowl, spread 1/3 pudding mixture in bottom of bowl. Top with 2 cups raspberries; spread evenly. Layer another 1/3 of pudding mixture and top with 2 cups blueberries; spread evenly. Spread remaining pudding mixture on top of blueberries. Top pudding with 1/2 cup blueberries, 1/2 cup raspberries and all of strawberries."]],"h":[]},"2994":{"s":[[null,"Combine ingredients in a small bowl."],[null,"Use as desired."]],"h":[[null,"Mix with salad ingredients or as a sandwich spread."],[null,"Heat and use as a cream sauce on vegetables."],[null,"Substitute low fat mayonnaise for even lower fat content."]]},"1002610":{"s":[[null,"Place all ingredients except the garnish slices in a blender and blend for 30 seconds."],[null,"Pour into 2 small glasses, garnish with watermelon slices and enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Watermelons vary in sweetness. Adjust by adding sweetener if needed."],[null,"For fluid-restricted diets, enjoy a Watermelon Summer Cooler now and freeze a serving for later. Remove from freezer 10 to 15 minutes before serving."],[null,"If you use a sugar substitute instead of sugar, carbohydrates are reduced by 6 grams and calories to 26 per 6-ounce serving."]]},"2167":{"s":[[null,"In a large punch bowl, mix together juice, lemonade, sherbet or sorbet and diet ginger ale."],[null,"Stir in un-drained, thawed raspberries."]],"h":[[null,"Punch will foam as sherbet starts melting. Be sure to use a large enough punch bowl. Stir to combine as sherbet melts."],[null,"Recipe analysis includes sherbet."]]},"5192533":{"s":[["For the cake","Preheat the oven 180°C/ fan 160°C/ gas mark 6. Grease and line a Swiss roll tin with baking paper."],["For the cake","Whisk the caster sugar and eggs in a large bowl (for around 5 minutes) until pale and light."],["For the cake","Sift the self-raising flour and cocoa powder together into the mixture."],["For the cake","Gently combine with a spatula (it is important not to over-mix to keep the cake light and fluffy)."],["For the cake","Pour the mixture into the lined Swiss roll tin. Spread the mixture gently across the baking tray ensuring it is level."],["For the cake","Bake for 10-12 minutes until firm but springy to touch and the edges of the cake are starting to shrink away from the sides of the tin."],["For the cake","Meanwhile put a clean tea towel on your work surface."],["For the cake","Remove the sponge from the oven and turn it out onto the tea towel whilst it is still warm. Carefully peel away the baking paper from the bottom of the sponge."],["For the cake","Roll the sponge up from the short end, using the tea towel underneath to help. Leave the sponge to cool."],["For the buttercream","Add the softened butter and icing sugar to a large mixing bowl and whisk until smooth, light and fluffy"],["For the buttercream","Add in the melted Vitabite and semi-skimmed milk. Whisk until smooth."],["Assembly","Unroll the sponge, spread a thin layer of buttercream and carefully roll up tightly again"],["Assembly","Cover the sponge with the remaining buttercream."],["For the decoration","Melt the Vitabite and pour ¾ onto baking paper, smooth to create a disc that will fit the end of the Yule log. With the remaining Vitabite, pour onto the parchment in the shape of 2 antlers (connecting the face and antlers together)."],["For the decoration","While the Vitabite is still soft add on 2 edible eyes and 1/2 glace cherry for the reindeer's shiny nose! Leave to set."],["For the decoration","Once set, add the reindeer's face onto the end of your Yule log and decorate the body with permitted sprinkles"]],"h":[["Renastep note","Nutritional analysis excludes sprinkles, edible eyes and 1/2 glace cherry"],["Renastep note","Always check with your dietitian or doctor that this recipe is suitable for you."],["Renastep note","Vitabite is a Food for Special Medical Purposes and must be used under medical supervision. Vitabite is for use in the dietary management of children from 1 year of age and adults on protein restricted diets. Vitabite contains milk and soya."],["Renastep note","This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutrimen dietary analysis software. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information."]]},"7468432":{"s":[[null,"Place newspaper sheets on a tray. Place a clean towel on top."],[null,"Empty the yogurt onto the tea towel, drain all water from the yogurt for 3–4 minutes. Once drained, put the yogurt into the large bowl, add sweetener and whisk thoroughly for 2–3 minutes. It should be thick and creamy."],[null,"Boil ½ the quantity of saffron strands and ½ the quantity of ground cardamoms in a small pan with the milk. Allow it to cool completely. Once cold, add to the yogurt mixture."],[null,"Again whisk well. Slice the pistachios and almonds very finely. Add ½ the quantity into the yogurt mixture. Transfer to the serving bowl. Decorate by sprinkling the remaining saffron strands, finely sliced nuts and cardamoms. Refrigerate for 2–24 hours for best results."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"3701":{"s":[[null,"Rinse and drain green chilies."],[null,"Cook noodles in boiling water without salt or butter until the noodles are al dente."],[null,"Drain noodles. While noodles are hot, add the pimento cheese spread and chilies."],[null,"Stir until the cheese spread is melted into the noodles."],[null,"Serve hot. Add pepper at the table for taste, if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Elbow, shell or bowtie pasta are great choices for this recipe."],[null,"For a higher protein variation, add browned and drained ground beef."],[null,"Most cheese spreads are very high in sodium and phosphorus. The pimento spread in this recipe is made with cream cheese instead of processed cheese. (Look for the Philadelphia® brand cream cheese logo on the label). This is what keeps the sodium and phosphorus content low enough for a renal diet. Avoid bottled or canned spreads made with processed cheese."]]},"7668562":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 180°C / gas mark 4."],[null,"Add rhubarb to a microwave/oven-proof dish with the water. Cover with cling film, pierce, then microwave for 2-3 minutes until tender."],[null,"Mix in 1 tbsp of sweetener. Add more if needed according to taste."],[null,"Add the eggs to a bowl with the yogurt and oil, then beat well."],[null,"Stir in the flour, ginger, baking powder and remaining sweetener."],[null,"Beat in the milk to create a batter, then pour it over the rhubarb. Bake for 25-30 minutes until lightly golden on top."]],"h":[[null,"Experiment with other fruits such as apples, pears, apricots or frozen berries."],[null,"Try adding other spices such as cinnamon or mixed spice - especially good with apple."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge and reheat until piping hot."]]},"7176104":{"s":[[null,"Add the rhubarb to a pan with 3 tbsp water. Bring to the boil, turn down the heat, add a lid and simmer for 6 minutes, stirring regularly, adding another tablespoon of water if it starts to stick. The rhubarb should be soft, but still hold its shape."],[null,"Transfer the rhubarb to a bowl and add the artificial sweetener, if using. Mix well and taste adding a little more artificial sweetener if needed, then leave to cool. Remember the fruit contains natural sugars so don't over sweeten."],[null,"In a bowl, mix the yoghurt and crème fraiche together and fold in the rhubarb. Place in glasses and chill before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Can be made in advance and kept in the fridge for a few hours. Or if you want to make it a day before serving, just chill the rhubarb separately and mix with the yoghurt and crème fraiche when needed."],[null,"This recipe works well with other tart fruits, such as gooseberries or redcurrants."],[null,"You can use most fruit, although you won't need to sweeten it quite as much if the fruit is sweet. Try apricots, peaches, nectarines, raspberries or cherries."],[null,"This recipe uses 0% fat yoghurt and reduced-fat crème fraiche, but you can use a plain version of your choice. However, this will change the nutritional information and texture of the dish."],[null,"For a vegan version, use unsweetened soy or coconut-based yoghurt."]]},"4145299":{"s":[[null,"Simmer rhubarb, 1 cup sugar and water in a medium sauce pan until tender (about 20 minutes)."],[null,"Cool and place in freezer. Freeze to a mush. It takes about 1 1/2 hours depending on freezer. Whisk to fluff."],[null,"Beat egg whites and 1/4 cup sugar until soft peaks form."],[null,"Fold into fluffed rhubarb mixture, add Cool Whip and mix thoroughly with a spoon."],[null,"Put into a plastic container with cover and freeze for a minimum of 2 1/2 hours."],[null,"Serve half a cup of rhubarb ice cream with half a cup of strawberries per person."]],"h":[[null,"* Instead of using raw eggs the FDA recommends to use either shell eggs that have been treated to destroy Salmonella, by pasteurization or another approved method, or pasteurized egg products."],[null,"The ice cream can be kept in the freezer for 1 month."]]},"7557682":{"s":[[null,"Drain and rinse the beans, place in a large pan and add the stock."],[null,"Bring to the boil and simmer for 5 minutes."],[null,"Add the remaining ingredients, cover and simmer for 15-20 minutes or until the liquid has absorbed and the rice is cooked."],[null,"Season well and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Try using other beans such as black eye beans, borlotti beans or a tin of mixed beans."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Chill quickly. Defrost in the fridge and reheat thoroughly until piping hot throughout. Eat immediately and discard any leftovers."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"3053":{"s":[[null,"To cook rice, bring 1-3/4 cups water to a boil in a 2-quart saucepan and add rice and salt. Bring water to a boil again, stir once, cover and reduce heat to simmer for 15 minutes or until water has evaporated. Remove from heat and set, covered for at least 10 minutes."],[null,"To roast chile, place under broiler, turning often until uniformly charred. When the pepper is blackened on all sides, transfer to a plastic bag or bowl, cover and seal and let cool. Remove charred skin from chiles, rinse and pat dry. Dice the chilies."],[null,"Thaw peas; peel and seed cucumber; chop cucumber,green onions and cilantro; dice bell peppers and mince garlic."],[null,"To assemble salad, combine rice and diced chiles. Add thawed peas, bell peppers, onion, cucumber and cilantro. Toss well to combine."],[null,"To prepare dressing, combine all dressing ingredients and mix well."],[null,"Toss dressing with rice and vegetable mixture. Chill until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Poblano chiles are also known as ancho chiles."],[null,"Roast chiles ahead of time to allow time to cool."],[null,"Wear rubber gloves when removing seeds and vein from hot chiles."],[null,"For a nice presentation, serve on a platter lined with lettuce leaves."]]},"5619043":{"s":[[null,"Preheat an oven to 180°C/356°F/Gas mark 4."],[null,"Onto a baking tray add the carrots and red pepper, drizzle with a little oil, and roast for 20-30 minutes or until soft."],[null,"Heat 1/2 the oil in a pan and add cloves and cardamom pods, allow to toast slightly."],[null,"Add onions, garlic, and allow to soften slightly."],[null,"Once softened, add in the chicken pieces and allow to brown slightly on all sides."],[null,"Once browned, add in the cinnamon, allspice, white pepper, dried lime powder, nutmeg, coriander, and cumin. Stir until the chicken is fully coated with the spices."],[null,"Remove the red pepper and carrots from the oven and add to a blender with enough stock to cover the vegetables and form a thin puree."],[null,"Blend until smooth and then add into the pan with the rest of the vegetable stock, stir well, and bring to boil."],[null,"Once boiling, reduce the heat to low and allow to simmer for 15 minutes."],[null,"Remove the chicken from the pan and set aside."],[null,"Add in the rice and cook for 10 minutes or until the liquid is fully absorbed."],[null,"Once cooked, place the rice on a plate and add the chicken on top and set aside."],[null,"Add the butter to a pan and melt, add in the macadamia nuts and pumpkin seeds and cook until slightly brown."],[null,"Pour the butter and nuts over the rice, serve and enjoy."]],"h":[]},"3203":{"s":[[null,"Soak rice and lentils in water. Grind the lentils in a food processor or liquidizer to a smooth paste."],[null,"Grind rice not too fine, a little coarse. Mix the two pastes and add salt. Let the batter ferment for 12-14 hours at a warm place (avoid the inside of the oven or on top of a gas stove)."],[null,"Just before cooking, add the baking soda. Steam idlis on idli moulds. Serve with sambar."]],"h":[[null,"Lentils contribute extra potassium and phosphorus, so portion must be limited to 2 rice idles."],[null,"Sambar is a vegetable stew containing pigeon peas, tamarind, vegetables and ground spices. It is very popular in southern India."],[null,"Serve with cilantro chutney or with a dollop of butter topped with a spoon of sugar."]]},"5743791":{"s":[[null,"Heat a pan on a medium heat and add the rice, milk, cream, water and sugar. Mix well until combined."],[null,"Allow to gently simmer for 1 hour, stirring regulatory to ensure it does not stick or burn."],[null,"Once the rice is cooked, stir in the vanilla essence and cinnamon."],[null,"Allow to cook for a further 10 minutes."],[null,"Serve and enjoy!"]],"h":[]},"3711":{"s":[[null,"Chop onion, celery and parsley. Break vermicelli into small pieces."],[null,"Melt margarine in a skillet that has a cover."],[null,"Sauté onion and celery for 1 minute."],[null,"Add the rice and vermicelli and stir for 30 seconds."],[null,"Add the chicken broth, water and parsley. Bring to boil."],[null,"Cover and reduce to simmer about 15 minutes until all the liquid is absorbed."]],"h":[[null,"Angel hair pasta can be substituted for the vermicelli in this recipe."]]},"3265":{"s":[[null,"In a medium saucepan combine almond milk, rice and sugar. Bring mixture to a boil over medium high heat. Stir constantly. Reduce heat to low and simmer for 6 minutes. Remove from heat."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk eggs and vanilla together. Stir a small amount of the hot almond milk and rice mixture into the eggs, to temper them and keep them from curdling."],[null,"Slowly add egg mixture into hot almond milk mixture, stirring constantly."],[null,"Place saucepan back on low heat. Stir and cook until thickened, about 1 minute. Do not boil."],[null,"Remove saucepan from heat and let stand for 30 minutes."],[null,"To serve, place 1 almond in in the bottom of each bowl. Spoon rice pudding into 6 single serving bowls."],[null,"Divide the cranberry sauce between the 6 bowls. Dust the top of the pudding with cinnamon. Serve and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"In Scandinavian countries, rice pudding is served as a holiday treat. A single almond is hidden in the pudding, and whoever gets the almond has good luck for the next year. In this recipe we included an almond in each serving–good luck for all!"]]},"4872310":{"s":[[null,"In a large pot on medium heat, combine the oil, cumin seeds and butter. Add the onion and sauté for 5 minutes."],[null,"Add the carrots and peas to the pot, sauté for another 5-10 minutes, until tender."],[null,"Add 2½ cups of water and 2 cups Basmati rice to the pot. Cover the pot and simmer on medium heat until all the water evaporates and rice is cooked. Remove from heat and let sit for 5 minutes before serving."]],"h":[]},"7649613":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 170°C/gas 3. Add the sultanas, raisins and peel to a bowl, cover with the boiling water and set aside."],[null,"Mix together the mashed banana, eggs and oil in a large bowl, and beat well."],[null,"Mix in the courgette, apple and carrot, then stir in the flour, baking powder and mixed spice. Next, add the dried fruit, plus soaking water."],[null,"Mix well and put into a 20cm cake tin lined with baking parchment, top with the cherries and almonds. Cover with foil and bake in the oven for 1½ hours. Remove the foil 15–20 minutes before the end of the cooking time, then bake for the remainder of the time."],[null,"Test with a skewer or knife, which should come out clean when cooked, and remove from the oven."]],"h":[[null,"You could easily make this cake with gluten-free flour, but you may need to add an extra 50ml liquid, depending on the type of flour you choose."],[null,"Any dried fruits work well – prunes, apricots, currants or mixed fruit."],[null,"Once cooked, you can drizzle with 1 tsp runny honey, if preferred."]]},"4679807":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F. You can skip this step if using the microwave."],[null,"In a small saucepan, bring water to a boil and cook the rice according to package instructions."],[null,"In a large frying pan, sauté the ground turkey, garlic, and onions in olive oil. Add the four spices and continue to cook until the meat has browned."],[null,"Add corn and zucchini and sauté until vegetables are soft. Stir in the cooked rice (1 cup) and cilantro."],[null,"Cut the tops off the peppers and remove stems and seeds. Trim the bottoms if necessary so that the peppers can stand upright in a roasting pan or dish. Stuff peppers with turkey and rice filling. Cover the peppers with their tops."],[null,"Microwave: Add 1 cup of water to bottom of microwave-safe dish and cover with a microwave safe lid. Cook on HIGH for 30 minutes or until peppers begin to soften on the outside."],[null,"If using the oven: Add 1/3 cup of water to the bottom of the roasting pan and cover with aluminum wrap. Bake for 1 1/2 hours or until the peppers are soft and juices are well developed in the pan."]],"h":[[null,"Leftover stuffed peppers can be frozen or reheated the next day."],[null,"PLEASE NOTE: This recipe is higher in potassium and portion size is important. Check with your registered dietitian to see how this recipe can be included in your diet."],["Ground turkey as a lower-potassium meat choice","Eating the right amount of protein is very important when you have chronic kidney disease (CKD). During the earlier stages of CKD, it is common to limit meat portions to the size of a deck of cards. If CKD progresses and dialysis is needed, a much higher protein diet is commonly recommended to prevent protein malnutrition. While all meats are a healthful source of protein, their nutrient content can vary, particularly when it comes to the amount of potassium in various meats. For example, the amount of potassium in ground turkey is much less than that of ground beef. One ounce of cooked lean ground beef contains 133 milligrams of potassium while one ounce of cooked lean ground turkey contains only 86 milligrams of potassium.1 With 35% less potassium per ounce, a recipe prepared with ground turkey instead of ground beef can help lower your potassium intake. To benefit from this tip, try to substitute ground turkey for ground beef when preparing your meals."]]},"6466152":{"s":[[null,"Using a bread knife, trim off the rounded ends of the roll. Cut the roll into 12 slices, about 1/2 inch thick each. Toast the bread slices in a toaster until golden brown."],[null,"Top each slice with 1 Tbsp of the ricotta cheese, then 1 tsp of the jam. Evenly top with the blackberries, then sprinkle with the salt. Arrange on a platter and serve."]],"h":[]},"3966":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350˚ F. Set butter out to soften."],[null,"In a large bowl using a hand-mixer on low speed, beat together sugar and butter. Blend well. Increase the speed to high; beat until light and fluffy, about 5 minutes."],[null,"With the mixer on medium speed mix in the ricotta cheese, vanilla, eggs and lemon juice. Set mixer to low speed and add flour, baking soda and salt. Beat until a dough forms."],[null,"Drop by tablespoons onto an ungreased cookie sheet, spaced about 2-inches apart. Bake for 15 minutes, or until slightly golden brown."],[null,"Remove from the oven and cool cookies completely on a wire rack."],[null,"Make icing by whisking together powdered sugar and milk until smooth and free of lumps. Ice each cookie, then set aside for icing to dry."]],"h":[[null,"Whole milk ricotta cheese has less phosphorus and potassium than part-skim ricotta cheese."],[null,"Replace the vanilla extract with almond extract, if desired."],[null,"For Christmas, use red and green sugar sprinkles to decorate the cookies while the icing is still wet."]]},"4320200":{"s":[[null,"In a large pot, bring water to boil and cook pasta, according to instructions on package. After draining the cooked pasta keep 3/4 cup of the water and set aside."],[null,"Transfer the cooked pasta back into the pot. Add the ricotta cheese and the sage and stir to combine and set aside."],[null,"In a large frying pan over medium-heat, heat the olive oil. Add the beans, garlic and pepper and fry for 3–4 minutes, paying attention to not burn the garlic."],[null,"Add the pasta water and bring to a boil. Reduce the heat and continue to simmer until the beans are cooked (approximately 4 minutes)."],[null,"Add the bean mixture to the cooked pasta and cheese mixture."],[null,"Add the tomatoes and gently stir."],[null,"Sprinkle with lemon zest and serve."]],"h":[["Ricotta cheese is lower in sodium and phosphorus","Cheese is a common food in many people’s diets, however, individuals with kidney disease need to talk to their dietitian on how much cheese they can safely eat as most cheeses are high in both sodium and phosphorus. Processed cheeses such as American cheese slices and cheese spreads have the highest sodium and phosphorus content and should not be a part of a CKD diet. Hard, natural cheeses such as cheddar, mozzarella and Swiss are lower in both sodium and phosphorus, but still contain enough of these nutrients that they should be limited. Fortunately, soft cheeses such as ricotta and cream cheese can add flavor to recipes without adding a significant amount of sodium or phosphorus. Use in dips, on scrambled eggs, spread on toast or add to salads and pasta dishes. Potassium content is generally low in most cheeses. A cheese that is labeled “low-sodium” may contain added potassium. Always check the ingredients list and avoid cheese with added potassium if you are on a low-potassium diet."]]},"4210635":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 425°F (conventional oven)."],[null,"Place all pesto ingredients in a food processor or blender and puree."],[null,"Heat olive oil in a frying pan over medium heat and sauté the leeks until they soften. Add chicken, mushrooms and season with black pepper. Continue to sauté until the chicken is cooked and the mushrooms take on a reddish brown color (10 minutes)."],[null,"Place tortillas on a cookie sheet. Divide the pesto between the 2 tortillas and spread to cover the surface. Add the chicken, mushroom and leek mixture. Sprinkle with parmesan cheese."],[null,"Bake for approximately 10 minutes or until tortillas are crisp."]],"h":[[null,"* You can use already cooked leftover poultry or meat. In that case, there is no need for frying. Just put the slices on the tortillas as described in step 4."]]},"6672801":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F. Combine the black pepper, salt, and garlic, and rub all over the roast. Place the meat in a large roasting pan. Roast the meat for about 20 minutes."],[null,"Reduce the heat to 325 degrees F and bake for about 50 additional minutes or until a meat thermometer inserted in the roast registers 140 degrees F for medium rare. Cook longer if desired."],[null,"Remove the roast from the oven. Cover loosely with foil and let stand for 15-20 minutes. Cut the meat across the grain into thin slices."],[null,"To make the horseradish sauce, combine the horseradish, sour cream, and mustard. Serve with sliced beef."]],"h":[]},"7041630":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200°C/gas 7. Cut the butternut squash into quarters lengthways, scoop out the seeds, brush with a little of the oil and bake in the oven for 25 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the onion and carrot to the pan with 1 tsp of the oil, cook gently for a few minutes, until the onion starts to brown."],[null,"Now, pour the stock into the pan and add the lentils, stir together and simmer for around 15 minutes."],[null,"Remove the butternut squash from the oven, scoop out the flesh and add to the soup."],[null,"Simmer for a further 5 minutes, add a good pinch of pepper, then whizz with a stick blender or in a food processor until smooth."],[null,"Serve with a swirl of half-fat crème fraiche and a few chopped chives."]],"h":[[null,"This recipe is high in vitamin A, which helps your immune system function at its best."],[null,"Stock cubes contain salt, so don't add any extra salt during cooking. When simmering the soup, you'll be reducing the water content and concentrating the salt content, so taste it once cooked and add salt only if needed."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Freeze in portions then defrost in the fridge, or defrost in a microwave and reheat thoroughly until piping-hot."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"7476296":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas mark 4."],[null,"Place the chicken onto a rack and place over a roasting tin. Squeeze the lemon over the bird and place the lemon shells in the cavity of the bird."],[null,"Place some of the herbs on top of the bird and place the remaining herbs into the cavity. Season with black pepper."],[null,"Pour the water into the roasting tin, then place in the oven and cook for 45 minutes per kilo, plus 20 minutes (1 hour and 50 minutes for a 2kg bird), topping up the water if necessary."],[null,"Take out of the oven, cover with foil and allow to stand for 15 minutes."],[null,"Remove the skin, carve, and serve with plenty of vegetables and potatoes."]],"h":[[null,"To check if the chicken is cooked, pierce the skin between the thigh and breast – the juices should be clear."],[null,"If using the pan juices to make gravy, pour into a jug and allow to stand for a few minutes. The fat will float to the top and can be removed with a spoon before making the gravy."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. For convinience, you can freeze this dish in portions, then defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat thoroughly until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"4859949":{"s":[[null,"Position the oven rack in the middle and preheat the oven to 350°F."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix the olive oil with paprika and fennel seeds."],[null,"Spread the onion slices on the bottom of a roasting dish. Pat the chicken dry with paper towels and place it breast-side up on top of the onions."],[null,"Rub the chicken with the lemon halves on all sides (remove lemon seeds if possible). Stuff the cavity with the lemon halves and garlic cloves."],[null,"Brush the chicken generously with the oil and spice mixture. Season with ground black pepper."],[null,"Roast for about 2 hours, or until a thermometer inserted in the thigh reads 180°F."]],"h":[[null,"• Skim the fat off the cooking juices and serve the remaining cooking juice with the chicken as a sauce. • You can make chicken broth with the crushed bones: add bones to water, boil, then simmer for 3–4 hours. • Use whole fennel seeds and grind some of them to get a mix of ground and whole seeds. • For a different flavor: replace the spices with 1 tablespoon curry powder, 1 tablespoon coriander seed, or 2 tablespoons Italian seasoning."],[null,"* For CKD Non-Dialysis: lower the amount of protein by reducing the chicken portion."],["Advantages of roasting your own chicken","Cooking meals at home can be especially helpful when following a kidney-friendly diet. While fast food may seem convenient, choices are often more expensive and higher in sodium, fat, and harmful potassium and phosphate additives. Planning and preparing meals, like roasted chicken, lets you enjoy a budget-friendly dish at home without worrying about diet restrictions. Depending on how many people you are serving, a whole roasted chicken may give you leftovers. A whole chicken provides multiple portions of meat that can be used in other recipes (such as soups, salads, and sandwiches), saving time and money. When roasting your own chicken, a few small steps can make a big difference in ensuring moist and flavorful poultry. Start by drying the outside of the chicken before cooking. This helps the poultry cook and brown evenly. Removing the skin prior to eating the chicken is also recommended to help lower fat. Temperature also matters. Whether using high or low heat, cook chicken until the internal temperature of at least 165°F has been reached. Experiment with different kidney-friendly seasonings from your pantry as you prepare the roasted chicken. A blend of rosemary, thyme, marjoram, and oregano can offer a mild herb option. For taste with a kick, try a mix of paprika, garlic powder, cayenne pepper, and onion powder. As another option, create a sweeter poultry flavor by combining green herbs with honey or sugar-free fruit preserves to make a glaze."]]},"7393112":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 200°C/fan 180°C/ gas 6."],[null,"Put the chicken on a non-stick baking tray and insert the lemon into the cavity. Roast for 1 hour, or until cooked through (the juices should run clear when you insert a skewer into the thickest part of the chicken)."],[null,"Meanwhile, spread the celeriac chips out on a large, non-stick baking tray in a single layer. Spray with a couple of pumps of low-calorie cooking spray and add to the oven below the chicken when it has 30 minutes left to cook."],[null,"Remove the chicken from the oven, cover with foil and leave to rest. Turn the chips and cook for a further 15-20 minutes or until golden and tender. Meanwhile, mix together the dressing ingredients with 1-2 tbsp of water and season with black pepper. Set aside half, then cover and chill for the next day."],[null,"Spray a non-stick frying pan with a couple of pumps of low-calorie cooking spray and place over a medium-high heat. Fry the garlic until golden, then add the cavolo nero, season with black pepper, add a splash of water and stir-fry for 5 minutes, until tender."],[null,"Discard the skin and remove any visible fat from the chicken, then slice. Divide the chicken, chips and garlicky greens between plates, spoon over the dressing and add a twist of black pepper."]],"h":[[null,"If you have two portions of this left over, cool, cover and chill until the next day. To make a chicken and bulgur wheat salad, cook 70g dried bulgur wheat according to the pack instructions. Shred the chicken and chop the chips and greens. Toss everything together with the remaining dressing and ½ small bag chopped fresh parsley. Divide between 2 plates to serve."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"7232073":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4. Add the oil to a saucepan then add the onions and mushrooms and cook for 3 minutes."],[null,"Sprinkle with the flour, covering evenly."],[null,"Gradually stir in the stock. Add the lentils and yoghurt."],[null,"Place the vegetable and lentil mix into a shallow ovenproof dish, and place the cod on top."],[null,"Bake for 15 minutes and serve with parsley and freshly ground black pepper."]],"h":[[null,"Most firm fish is ideal for this dish – try coley, salmon or haddock."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"2599":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 325° F. Set butter out to bring to room temperature."],[null,"Wash and lightly trim the fat from the lamb and set aside in a roasting pan."],[null,"Chop rosemary and mince the garlic."],[null,"Blend the oregano, rosemary, garlic, salt and pepper and half the soft butter or margarine together in a small bowl."],[null,"Make slits into the leg of lamb with a sharp knife and stuff the herb and butter mixture into the slits."],[null,"Spread the remaining herb and butter mixture over the lamb."],[null,"Mix lemon juice with remaining butter and pour over lamb."],[null,"Cover and bake 30 minutes for each pound."],[null,"After an hour, remove the lid, add the water to the drippings in the pan and baste often until the meat is well browned and tender."],[null,"Uncover during the last half hour of cooking for a crisp skin."]],"h":[[null,"For a lower protein diet reduce portion to match your meal plan or check with the dietitian to determine portion size."],[null,"Use this guide for cooking times: medium rare, 145° F internal temperature, 20 to 30 minutes per pound; medium, 160° F internal temperature, 30 to 35 minutes per pound; well done, 170° F internal temperature, 35 to 40 minutes per pound."]]},"7912812":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas mark 4. Lightly spray an oven tray with oil."],[null,"Place the onions and peppers onto the tray and bake for 10 minutes, mixing around a couple of times to ensure even cooking."],[null,"Meanwhile, drizzle the fish with lime juice and spread the curry paste carefully over each fillet."],[null,"Mix together the coriander and lime zest and press onto the mackerel fillets, on top of the curry paste."],[null,"Place the fish on top of the peppers and bake for a further 12-15 minutes, until the fish is cooked through. Serve with wedges of lime."]],"h":[[null,"Experiment with other fish for this dish such as tilapia, cod, bream, haddock or salmon."],[null,"Try with other herbs such as parsley or dill. Or use mustard in place of curry paste."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"7276558":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200°C/gas 6. Slice the bread into 1cm-thick discs – you need around 20."],[null,"Add 1 tsp of the oil to a baking sheet and spread evenly (using kitchen paper). Arrange the slices of bread over the baking sheet and bake in the oven for 7–8 minutes. Then, turn the slices of bread over, moving them around if they are cooking unevenly, and bake for a further 5 minutes. They should be golden brown and crisp."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the pepper, red onion and carrot to a bowl with the second tsp of olive oil, and mix well. Spread the mixture out on a baking sheet and roast for 15–20 minutes."],[null,"Once the vegetables have cooled, chop them finely and then add to a bowl with the oregano, balsamic vinegar and sundried tomatoes."],[null,"To serve, place a spoonful of the mixture onto each slice of bread and garnish with fresh basil. (We used Greek basil, but parsley, chives or coriander work just as well). Once served, the crostini will last for 2–3 hours, but the toast will then start to soften."]],"h":[[null,"For a more intense garlic flavour, rub each crostini with a clove of garlic before topping."],[null,"Make the crostini toasts a day in advance and store in an airtight container."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"7358851":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 190°C/375°F/gas mark 5. Cut the squash into 8 wedges, discarding the seeds."],[null,"Place in a roasting tin, spray with oil, sprinkle the cumin and roast for 10 mins. Add chickpeas and onions and roast for 20 mins, tossing occasionally. Add seeds and cook for 5 mins, then leave to cool."],[null,"Arrange the rocket, coriander, chicken, onion, squash and chickpeas on a plate."],[null,"Blitz remaining ingredients together, except the mint. Stir in the mint, drizzle the dressing and serve."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6628712":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400 degrees F. Spray a baking sheet with cooking spray."],[null,"In a medium bowl mix together garbanzo beans, 1 Tbsp. olive oil, cinnamon, cumin, chili powder and salt."],[null,"Spread garbanzo bean mixture evenly on baking sheet. Bake for 40–45 minutes, stirring every 10 minutes, until beans are crispy and dry."],[null,"Remove from oven and place hot beans in a medium bowl. Add 1 Tbsp. olive oil and brown sugar substitute. Mix well."],[null,"Pour beans on parchment paper and allow to cool for 20 minutes."]],"h":[]},"6330258":{"s":[[null,"Heat oven to 375 degrees F. Line a sheet pan with parchment paper."],[null,"In a bowl, toss the chopped apples with olive oil, sugar-free baking sugar substitute, ground cinnamon, ground nutmeg, ground cloves, and lemon juice until the apples are evenly coated."],[null,"Spread the seasoned apples on the sheet pan in a single layer."],[null,"Roast the apples for about 30 minutes or until they are tender and slightly caramelized."],[null,"Remove the roasted apples from the oven and let them cool for a few minutes."],[null,"Add the apples and 2/3 cup water to a food processor. Pulse to the desired texture."],[null,"Serve warm or chilled."]],"h":[]},"6055640":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 400 degrees F and cover a sheet pan in parchment paper."],[null,"Toss asparagus and cherry tomatoes with olive oil, balsamic vinegar, salt, and pepper."],[null,"Spread evenly on the sheet pan and roast for 15–20 minutes until asparagus is tender and tomatoes are slightly caramelized."],[null,"Platter and garnish with fresh basil."]],"h":[]},"6824792":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 425 degrees F. Line a baking sheet with aluminum foil. Lightly spray with cooking spray."],[null,"Arrange the asparagus in a single layer on the baking sheet. Sprinkle the walnuts around the asparagus. Lightly spray the asparagus with cooking spray. Roll back and forth to coat."],[null,"Roast for 5 minutes. Using tongs, turn the asparagus over gently. Roast for 4 minutes, or until the walnuts begin to brown. Transfer to a plate."],[null,"Spoon the vinaigrette over the asparagus and walnuts. Roll back and forth to coat. Sprinkle with the pepper. Let stand for 10 minutes so the flavors blend."],[null,"Cook’s Tip: Be sure to dry the asparagus thoroughly before cooking or it will not brown properly."]],"h":[]},"6499860":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 425°F. Line a baking sheet with parchment paper. Snap the tough ends off of the asparagus and discard."],[null,"In a large bowl, toss the asparagus with the olive oil, pepper and lemon zest."],[null,"Place the asparagus on the prepared baking sheet in a single layer. Bake for 15 minutes or until tender. Remove from the oven, then sprinkle with cheese and lemon juice."]],"h":[]},"6494336":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F. Spray a baking sheet with cooking spray."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix together the carrots and olive oil. Pour the mixture onto the baking sheet."],[null,"Bake for 15-20 minutes, until the carrots are tender."],[null,"Place the carrots into a bowl and mix with the honey or artificial sweetener. Sprinkle the carrots with parsley or other herbs."]],"h":[]},"6979207":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6149233":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F. Coat a baking sheet with cooking spray. Set aside."],[null,"Wrap the beets in aluminum foil and place them on the baking sheet. Lay the chicken breasts on the baking sheet next to the beets. Coat the chicken with cooking spray and season it with the salt (optional) and black pepper. Roast the chicken and beets for 25-30 minutes or until internal temperature of the chicken is 165 degrees F. Remove the chicken breasts from the oven and set aside. Once slightly cool, slice the chicken into thin slices."],[null,"Continue to roast the beets until tender, another 15-20 minutes. Remove the beets from the oven and set aside."],[null,"Once the beets are cool, peel the skin off and cut each beet into 1/2-inch chunks."],[null,"In a medium bowl, whisk together the balsamic vinegar, olive oil, vegetable broth, honey, Dijon mustard, and garlic."],[null,"Add the arugula and beet chunks to a large bowl. Pour the dressing over the salad and toss to coat."],[null,"Divide the salad among 4 plates. Top each salad with 1/4 of the chicken breast slices, 1 Tbsp. goat cheese and 1 Tbsp. slivered almonds."]],"h":[]},"9506425":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425℉/218℃ convection roast and line a baking sheet with parchment paper. (If you do not have a convection oven, allow more time for roasting.)"],[null,"Peel and cube the beets into small half-inch pieces and arrange them in a single layer on your tray with the quartered onion and garlic cloves. Roast the veggies for 25-30 minutes, until golden brown and the beets are fork-tender."],[null,"Meanwhile, bring a large pot of generously salted water to boil and cook the pasta according to package directions for 'al dente' pasta. Drain it BUT reserve 1/2 cup or so of the pasta water, and set it aside. Return the drained pasta to the pot."],[null,"By now, your veggies should be ready, so add them to your blender with all the remaining sauce ingredients and process until smooth and creamy. If needed. add some of the reserved pasta water to thin out the sauce. Then pour the sauce into the pot with the pasta and stir until evenly coated."],[null,"Serve with garnishes of your choice."]],"h":[[null,"Salt your pasta water. Make sure to add enough salt to your pot of water for the best texture and flavour. Here's a handy guide to help you salt your water perfectly each time."],[null,"Cook your pasta al dente. Do not overcook! Al dente means that the pasta is still firm once cooked, giving optimal texture in every bite. To ensure your pasta does not overcook, start taste testing a few minutes before the package says it will be ready. It should be tender, but still firm."],[null,"Reserve some pasta water when draining the cooked pasta to thin your sauce if needed."],[null,"If you do not have a high-speed powerful blender , soak the cashews in hot water for 20 minutes first, then drain them and use as directed."],[null,"Leftovers will keep in the fridge for 3-4 days. I do not recommend putting pasta in the freezer as it alters its texture. However, if you’re making extra sauce, the sauce can be frozen in an airtight container for up to 3 months."]]},"9389046":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425℉/218℃ convection roast. If you don't have a convection oven or a roast function, just use the bake setting, allowing a little more time for tender beets."],[null,"Scrub/wash your beets and slice off the ends. If your beets are large, cut them in half for faster cooking, otherwise, leave them whole. Using aluminum foil, make pockets to hold your beets inside, and place the pockets on a baking tray. Fold up the sides of the foil to prevent the red beet dye from spreading and making a mess. (Refer to process photos above, if needed.) Sprinkle the beets with salt and pepper and roast until fork tender. This will take anywhere from 30-60 minutes depending on how fresh (fresher beets cook faster) and how large your beets are."],[null,"While the beets are roasting, melt the butter (if using) in a pan and add the chopped onion, carrot, and celery. Sauté until softened, about 5-7 minutes. Then set aside."],[null,"Remove the beets from the oven and let cool slightly, just enough to handle. Then peel the beets (the skin will remove easily once roasted) and place them in your blender. Add the sautéed veggies, and ALL remaining ingredients to your blender and process until smooth. Work in batches, if needed."],[null,"Serve with cashew cream and more fresh dill if desired. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"To save time , roast and peel your beets 1-2 days in advance. Then when you want to make your soup, sauté the other veggies and blend."],[null,"Leave the peel on your beets when roasting. They’re easier to peel after being roasted. (Wear gloves when peeling to prevent red fingers.)"],[null,"For oil-free , simply omit the butter and sauté in water or broth instead."],[null,"Leftovers keep in the fridge for up to 4 days or freeze airtight for up to 3 months."]]},"6516194":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400°F."],[null,"Rub canola oil on beets, making sure to cover the whole surface. Pierce a few holes in beets so heat can circulate and speed up the cooking process. Place beets in a small baking dish and cover tightly with foil. Roast beets for 1 hour 10 minutes, until you can easily pierce the flesh of the beet with a fork. Remove from oven and place beets directly into a bowl with ice water. This will cool down the beets rapidly, stop the cooking process, and make removing the skins that much easier. When beets are cooled, peel off skins with a paper towel. Put beets into 1/2-inch cubes and set aside."],[null,"Add avocado oil, lime juice, salt, and black pepper to a bowl and whisk briskly for 30 seconds to create your dressing. Set aside."],[null,"In a separate bowl, add apples, 2 cups beet cubes, cilantro, queso fresco, and onions, and toss gently. Add dressing and toss once more. Now it’s ready to serve. Enjoy!"]],"h":[]},"6206148":{"s":[[null,"Place the beets in a food processor. Add the tahini, olive oil, salt, and yogurt to the food processor. Pulse until the mixture is smooth."],[null,"Add water, tablespoon by tablespoon, to get an extra-creamy consistency (you should need less than 1/4 cup)."],[null,"Scrape down the sides of the food processor, then puree for 1 to 2 minutes, or until the dip is extremely creamy."],[null,"Spoon onto a small, round dish, and serve immediately. (If desired, use the back of the spoon to create a smooth top on the dip and make dents in the top, filling them with olive oil.) Store in a lidded container in the refrigerator for up to a week."]],"h":[]},"9762136":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425℉/218℃ and line a large baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Chop your broccoli into small florets and peel and cube the beets into small half-inch pieces. Arrange the chopped veggies and chickpeas in a single layer on a baking sheet and sprinkle with salt and black pepper. Bake for 25-30 minutes, until the beets are fork tender. Remove the tray from the oven and allow the veggies to cool slightly."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the dressing ingredients to a small bowl, whisking to combine well."],[null,"Add the roasted beets, broccoli, chickpeas, dried cranberries and the dressing to a medium/large bowl and stir until everything is evenly coated. Enjoy your beet broccoli salad when freshly made for the best textures."]],"h":[[null,"Chop the beets small for quicker cooking. Or if you're having trouble cutting them small enough, give them a 15 minute baking headstart, and then add the broccoli and chickpeas to the tray."],[null,"Taste and adjust the salad dressing to your taste before tossing."]]},"9193390":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425℉/218℃ convection roast. (If you don't have a convection oven, allow extra time to roast vegetables.) Line a large baking tray (or two smaller ones) with parchment paper and set aside."],[null,"Peel and cube your beets and pumpkin into half-inch pieces for quick cooking. Then arrange them in a single layer on your baking tray and sprinkle them with salt and pepper. Roast for 25 minutes. Then remove the tray from the oven, add the chickpeas and continue roasting for another 15-20 minutes until the veggies are fork tender and the chickpeas are crispy."],[null,"Meanwhile, combine the dressing ingredients in a small bowl and mix well."],[null,"Add the roasted vegetables, chickpeas, almonds, cranberries, and salad dressing to a large bowl. Stir until evenly coated, and serve warm or refrigerate for 1 hour before serving the salad."]],"h":[[null,"Chop the beets and pumpkin into small cubes for quicker cooking ."],[null,"To save time , you may purchase cubed pumpkin pieces and beets from the store."],[null,"Taste and adjust the salad dressing, adding sea salt and black pepper to your taste before you toss it with the salad."],[null,"Leftovers will keep in the fridge for 2-3 days in an airtight container."]]},"6155441":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F. Prepare a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"In a bowl, toss the diced beets with olive oil, salt, and black pepper until well coated."],[null,"Spread the beets in a single layer on a baking sheet."],[null,"Roast in the preheated oven for 45 minutes or until the beets are tender, stirring halfway through."],[null,"Remove the beets from the oven and transfer them to a serving dish."],[null,"Sprinkle crumbled blue cheese and toasted hazelnuts over the roasted beets."],[null,"Garnish with chopped fresh parsley if desired."]],"h":[]},"6013330":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 450° F. Coat a baking dish with nonstick cooking spray."],[null,"Wash the beets, then pierce each beet several times with a fork and place in the prepared baking dish. Cover with aluminum foil and bake until a fork can pierce the beets with ease, about 1 hour. Remove the baking dish from the oven and allow the beets to cool for 15 minutes. Remove the skin and cut the beets into ¼-inch slices."],[null,"Zest the lemon half (set the zest aside), then use a paring knife to remove the remaining skin and pith (white part) of the halved lemon. Cut in between the membranes to release the lemon segments, and then chop."],[null,"In a medium bowl, combine the canola oil and cumin. Add the beets, lemon zest, chopped lemon, onion, dill, salt, and pepper and gently toss together. Transfer to a serving dish and serve warm."]],"h":[]},"6392793":{"s":[],"h":[]},"9388632":{"s":[[null,"Add the sliced peppers, chickpeas, onion and halved cherry tomatoes to a mixing bowl."],[null,"Then, in a small bowl or jar, combine all of the salad dressing ingredients."],[null,"Toss the salad with the dressing until evenly coated, and serve."]],"h":[[null,"If you don’t have roasted red peppers on hand , bake or broil red bell peppers in your oven until soft and the skins have blackened. Then peel the skins once cool enough to do so and cut the peppers into very thin slices."],[null,"Leftovers keep in the refrigerator for 2-3 days in an airtight container."]]},"6262997":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F. Line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Zest and juice one lemon."],[null,"In a large bowl, toss broccolini with olive oil, lemon zest, lemon juice, grated Parmesan cheese, minced garlic, salt, black pepper, and red pepper flakes if using. Ensure the broccolini is evenly coated."],[null,"Spread the broccolini in a single layer on a baking sheet."],[null,"Roast in the preheated oven for 15 minutes or until the broccolini is tender-crisp and the edges are slightly charred."],[null,"Serve with additional grated Parmesan on top. Slice the remaining lemon into wedges to serve on the side if desired."]],"h":[]},"6947052":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6052689":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 450°F."],[null,"Slice Brussels sprouts in half. Cut larger pieces of squash into 1-inch cubes."],[null,"Place sprouts and squash in a large bowl and drizzle with olive oil. Stir in thyme, and toss to coat."],[null,"Spread the sprouts and squash in a single layer in a baking pan and bake for 25 minutes, until the veggies are tender and beginning to brown."]],"h":[]},"6934057":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400 degrees F. Spray a baking sheet with cooking spray."],[null,"Place Brussels sprouts in a bowl and add oil; toss to coat."],[null,"Add remaining ingredients and mix well."],[null,"Place Brussels sprouts on a baking sheet and bake for 35-40 minutes or crisp on the outside."]],"h":[]},"6930473":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F."],[null,"Toss the halved Brussels sprouts with the olive oil, salt, and black pepper."],[null,"Spread the Brussels sprouts in a single layer on a baking sheet."],[null,"Roast in the preheated oven for 25 minutes or until the Brussels sprouts are golden brown and crispy on the edges."],[null,"While the Brussels sprouts are roasting, prepare the aioli."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine the mayo, minced chipotle peppers, minced garlic, lime juice, and salt. Mix well."],[null,"Once the Brussels sprouts are roasted, transfer them to a serving dish. Serve chipotle aioli on the side."]],"h":[]},"6552861":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425°F. Line a flat baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Toss the trimmed sprouts with the olive oil, salt, and pepper in a large bowl. Put the sprouts on the parchment-lined baking sheet in one single layer."],[null,"Roast the brussels sprouts for about 45 minutes or until crispy, shaking the sheet about every 15 minutes."],[null,"Mix together the mustard and honey in a small bowl. When the sprouts are done, add them to a serving bowl. Add in the honey mustard mixture, and toss well. Serve immediately."]],"h":[]},"3085":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375° F. Spray a baking sheet with nonstick cooking spray."],[null,"Trim the Brussels sprouts and cut each one in half. Peel the carrots and cut into 1-inch pieces. Core the apple and cut into 1/2-inch cubes."],[null,"Place Brussels sprouts, carrots and apple pieces in a large bowl."],[null,"In a small bowl combine the olive oil, maple syrup and spices. Stir to combine."],[null,"Pour sauce into the large bowl and stir to coat vegetables and apples. Place ingredients on the baking sheet. Sprinkle with the 1/4 teaspoon salt."],[null,"Bake for 30 to 40 minutes until carrots are fork tender and Brussels sprouts begin to darken."]],"h":[[null,"Replace carrots with 2 medium turnips if desired."],[null,"Add leftovers to mixed salad greens for a hearty roasted veggie salad the next day."]]},"6673467":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400°F and line a baking sheet with parchment paper. Arrange the cabbage slices on the sheet and brush lightly with olive oil. Sprinkle with garlic powder, onion powder, salt, and black pepper. Roast for 20 minutes, flipping halfway through, until the edges turn golden and slightly crisp."],[null,"While the cabbage roasts, heat a small saucepan over medium heat. Add crushed tomatoes, oregano, and red pepper flakes (if using). Simmer for 5 minutes, stirring occasionally, until slightly thickened. In a bowl, toss the shredded chicken with 2 tablespoons of the tomato sauce to keep it moist."],[null,"Remove cabbage from the oven and evenly distribute the shredded chicken over each slice. Spoon the remaining tomato sauce over the chicken layer. Sprinkle with mozzarella and Parmesan."],[null,"Return to the oven and bake for 10 more minutes, or until the cheese melts and turns lightly golden."]],"h":[]},"6886675":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F. Cut cabbage head into six 1\" thick slices."],[null,"Arrange cabbage slices on a baking sheet and drizzle with olive oil. Sprinkle seasoning blend and dill weed over cabbage. Cover with aluminum foil."],[null,"Bake for 45 minutes. Remove foil and let cabbage steaks brown in oven for 15 minutes longer."]],"h":[]},"2048":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 425° F. Cut cauliflower into florets. Peel carrots, cut in half vertically, then cut into 2-inch pieces. Peel turnip and dice into bite-size pieces. Dice onion into bite-size pieces."],[null,"In a large bowl toss cauliflower, carrots, turnips and onions with 3 tablespoons of the olive oil and Italian seasoning blend. Place onto a baking sheet and roast for 20 minutes. Remove baking sheet from oven and stir vegetables. Continue baking for 15 minutes or until vegetables are tender."],[null,"While vegetables are roasting, make the salad dressing. In a small bowl combine remaining 3 tablespoons of olive oil, rice vinegar, maple syrup, mustard, salt and black pepper."],[null,"To assemble the salad combine the lettuce and roasted vegetables, then toss with the dressing. Top with pomegranate seeds and serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"Do not assemble the salad until ready to serve."],[null,"Buy cauliflower florets and baby carrots for faster preparation."]]},"9942188":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400℉/204℃ and line a large baking tray with parchment paper. (Or use two if you don't have a very big one.)"],[null,"Trim the ends of your asparagus, and remove the peels from your carrots. Then quarter the carrots lengthwise if they are medium thickness. If your carrots are very thick, slice them to be approx. the same thinness as your asparagus for even cooking."],[null,"Arrange the vegetables on your baking sheet in a single layer. Then drizzle them with lemon juice and sprinkle with the seasoning."],[null,"Bake for 20 minutes, and then flip. Then continue baking for another 5-10 minutes or until the desired doneness is reached. (Bake time will vary according to the thickness of your veggies.)"]],"h":[[null,"Slice your carrots very thin (approx. the same thickness as your asparagus) for even cooking."],[null,"If your carrots are much thicker than your asparagus, and you’re having a hard time cutting them thin enough, give the carrots a 10-15 minute baking head start before adding the asparagus."]]},"6149915":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F. Spray a baking sheet with cooking spray."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix together the cauliflower, olive oil, black pepper and salt. Pour the mixture onto baking sheet."],[null,"Bake for 15-20 minutes, until the cauliflower tips are slightly brown and tender."]],"h":[]},"7149915":{"s":[[null,"Cut your cauliflower into big florets."],[null,"Mix the other ingredients together."],[null,"Place your cauliflower florets into the mixture to marinate."],[null,"Leave your cauliflower to marinate for at least 3 or 4 hours, although doing so overnight would be best."],[null,"Preheat your oven to 200 degrees (fan assisted), put marinated cauliflower into roasting dish and cook for 30 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"The amount of time you leave the cauliflower in the oven depends on how well-done you like it. For a slightly more charred taste, leave the roasting dish in the oven a little bit longer."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6274164":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 400 degrees F."],[null,"Toss the cauliflower florets with olive oil and spread them on a baking sheet in a single layer."],[null,"Roast in the preheated oven for about 25 minutes or until the cauliflower is tender and golden brown, stirring halfway through. Allow the roasted cauliflower to cool for a few minutes."],[null,"In a food processor, combine the roasted cauliflower, minced garlic, tahini, lemon juice, ground cumin, smoked paprika, salt, and pepper. Pulse the mixture until it starts to break down, then scrape down the sides of the food processor."],[null,"With the food processor running, add water gradually until you achieve a smooth and creamy consistency. You may need to stop and scrape down the sides of the processor a couple of times."],[null,"Serve topped with chopped, fresh parsley and a sprinkle of smoke paprika for garnish."]],"h":[]},"9296884":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425℉ convection roast and line a large baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Cut your cauliflower into small florets for quick cooking. Quarter the onion and leave the skins on the garlic. Arrange them in a single layer on your baking sheet and roast for 20 minutes, or until golden brown."],[null,"Once roasted, transfer the veggies and all remaining ingredients to your blender, working in batches if needed. Puree the soup until smooth, but reserve a few cauliflower pieces to garnish your bowls if you'd like."]],"h":[]},"3068":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 450° F."],[null,"Cut cauliflower florets into bite-size pieces. Chop rosemary."],[null,"In a large bowl, toss cauliflower with remaining ingredients."],[null,"Spread seasoned cauliflower on an ungreased baking sheet."],[null,"Roast for 15 minutes; remove from oven and stir."],[null,"Continue roasting for 10 minutes or until cauliflower is tender and lightly browned."]],"h":[[null,"Use caution when removing baking sheet from oven to stir cauliflower."]]},"6909702":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 425°F."],[null,"Place the cauliflower, potatoes, and onion on large foil-lined baking sheet. Drizzle with the oil and toss gently until well coated. Arrange vegetables in a single layer and bake 10 minutes. Stir and bake 10–11 minutes or until potatoes are tender. Remove from oven."],[null,"Sprinkle evenly with the salt and nutmeg. Wrap the vegetables in the foil and seal the edges. Let stand 10 minutes to absorb flavors and allow the natural juices to be released slightly."]],"h":[]},"7014156":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven 180°C/gas mark 4 and lightly oil a baking sheet with 1 tsp of oil."],[null,"Rinse the cauliflower in cold water, shake off any excess, then add to a bowl. Sprinkle with turmeric and mix well. Place on the baking sheet and roast for 20 minutes, until the edges are starting to char, then set aside."],[null,"Meanwhile, add 1 tsp oil to a pan and add the onion. Cook for 3-4 minutes until softened, but not browned."],[null,"Add the sweet potato, red pepper, garlic, cumin and curry paste, then cook for a further 2-3 minutes, stirring regularly."],[null,"Pour over the stock, mix well, cover, then simmer for 8-10 minutes until the potato is almost tender."],[null,"Add the paneer, chickpeas and peas, then continue to boil without the lid for 5-6 minutes. Stir in the yogurt and serve topped with the roasted cauliflower."]],"h":[[null,"Experiment with mixed beans or cannellini beans rather than chickpeas."],[null,"Try adding different vegetables such as 150g fresh spinach or mushrooms."],[null,"You can use a plain yoghurt of your choice, but this will change the nutritional information."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge or microwave, then reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"6679034":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F."],[null,"Place tomatoes, rosemary, salt, and garlic in a round baking dish."],[null,"Add the oil and stir to combine. Place in the oven and cook for 45–60 minutes, until garlic is golden brown and softened and the tomatoes burst."],[null,"Squeeze garlic cloves out of bulb and mix with tomatoes. Garlic cloves will be soft and creamy."],[null,"Top each quarter of toast with tomato mixture. One serving is 3 quarter slices of toast with ¼ cup tomatoes."]],"h":[]},"2330":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375° F."],[null,"Add olive oil to skillet and begin heating."],[null,"Rinse chicken inside and out and pat dry."],[null,"Sprinkle chicken with salt and pepper, inside and out."],[null,"Place 1 whole garlic head and 2 sprigs of rosemary inside chicken."],[null,"Add chicken to skillet and brown on all sides."],[null,"After browning, squeeze the juice of the lime over chicken and place uncovered skillet with chicken into oven."],[null,"During cooking, periodically spoon juices over chicken."],[null,"Check after 1 hour and 30 minutes. To test for doneness, pierce chicken at thickest part of thigh; juices should be clear."]],"h":[[null,"Divide extras into single portions and refrigerate or freeze for a quick heat and eat serving later."],[null,"Make Chicken Noodle Soup or Cool ‘n’ Crunchy Chicken Salad from leftovers."],[null,"Adjust chicken portion if you are on a low protein diet."]]},"6114026":{"s":[[null,"Make the dressing by placing the pomegranate juice, oil, mustard, vinegar, syrup, salt, and pepper in a small bowl or mason jar. Whisk the ingredients in the bowl or shake them in the jar to combine. Set aside."],[null,"Assemble the salad by placing 2 cups of spinach on each plate or bowl. Top with sliced chicken breast."],[null,"Sprinkle each salad with 1 tablespoon walnuts, onions, pomegranate seeds, and feta cheese. Add 1/4 of the sliced apple to each salad."],[null,"Drizzle each with 1 tbsp of dressing and toss."]],"h":[]},"6024800":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F."],[null,"Season chicken breasts with salt."],[null,"Heat a large Dutch oven or large ovenproof skillet over medium-high heat. Add ½ Tbsp of olive oil, then add the chicken. Sear until golden brown on both sides (but not cooked through). Remove chicken to a plate."],[null,"Return the skillet to medium heat and add other ½ Tbsp of oil. Add onion, garlic, rosemary, and carrots and cook until onion is translucent, about 4–5 minutes."],[null,"Add syrup and white wine vinegar and cook until reduced by half, about 3–4 minutes. Stir in the cranberries."],[null,"Add the chicken back to the skillet and nestle it between the vegetables and cranberries."],[null,"Cover with a lid and bake for 10–15 minutes until the chicken is cooked through to an internal temperature of 165 degrees F and the vegetables are tender."],[null,"Serve with a sprinkle of parsley."]],"h":[]},"6254354":{"s":[],"h":[]},"7483758":{"s":[[null,"Halve the chicory and place in a non-metallic roasting dish."],[null,"Sprinkle over the chopped garlic cloves and drizzle with the olive oil."],[null,"Add the lemon zest and juice."],[null,"Roast for 25–30 minutes at 200ºC/gas 6 until tender and beginning to char, then scatter over the toasted pine nuts and chopped parsley."]],"h":[[null,"Toast the pine nuts by adding them to a dry frying pan and cooking for 2-3 mins turning regularly. As soon as they start to brown, remove from the pan as they burn quickly."],[null,"You can also make this recipe with halved fennel bulbs, which are less bitter."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"7328009":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200ºC/gas 6. Place the chicory in an ovenproof dish. Mix together the orange rind and juice, oil and thyme. Drizzle over the chicory then season with plenty of black pepper."],[null,"Cook for 25-30 minutes until tender and beginning to char. Toss together with the orange segments and serve drizzled with any cooking liquid and the orange zest. Cool a little or chill before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Chicory has a slightly bitter flavour which complements the sweetness of the orange."],[null,"Look out for red chicory which has a similar flavour with a great colour."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"2273":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425° F."],[null,"Cut the ends off the pineapple. Peel and core, and cut into six one-inch wedges."],[null,"Cover a rimmed baking sheet with foil and coat with non-stick spray."],[null,"Melt the butter and stir together with honey, lime juice and cinnamon in a small bowl."],[null,"Place the pineapple wedges flat side down on the baking sheet. Brush half the sauce over wedges evenly. Flip wedges over and repeat with the remaining sauce."],[null,"Place baking sheet in the oven and roast pineapple for 10 minutes. Turn wedges over and roast for another 15 minutes until pineapple is lightly browned and caramelized."],[null,"Let cool slightly, top with lime zest and serve warm."]],"h":[[null,"External color does not tell you how ripe pineapples are. Pineapples are picked at the peak of ripeness and do not ripen more after that point. Instead, look for pineapples with full green leaves, firm skin, and a sweet smell."],[null,"Brown sugar can be substituted for the honey."],[null,"Roasted pineapples are a treat on their own but for a more decadent kidney-friendly dessert, serve with non-dairy ice cream or a dollop of homemade whipped cream on top."]]},"6581480":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 425°F."],[null,"Place tomatoes, zucchini, and onion in a large baking dish, and season with salt and pepper. Drizzle with olive oil, and roast for about 20 minutes or until vegetables are tender."],[null,"Remove from oven, and stir in garlic, olives, and basil. Place cod fillets on top of vegetables, and sprinkle with salt and pepper. Drizzle with lime juice. Return to oven. Bake for about 15 minutes, until fish is cooked through."]],"h":[]},"6090675":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F."],[null,"In a bowl, toss the delicata squash slices with olive oil, balsamic vinegar, pomegranate molasses, chopped rosemary, salt, and pepper until evenly coated."],[null,"Spread the squash slices in a single layer on a baking sheet lined with parchment paper."],[null,"Roast in the preheated oven for about 20–25 minutes or until the squash is tender and caramelized, flipping the slices halfway through."],[null,"Remove from the oven and transfer to a serving dish."],[null,"Drizzle any remaining glaze from the baking sheet over the squash."],[null,"Garnish with pomegranate seeds for a burst of freshness and color."],[null,"Serve as a flavorful and visually appealing side dish."]],"h":[]},"6240828":{"s":[],"h":[]},"4982271":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400°F."],[null,"Cut the eggplant in half lengthwise and place the skin side facing up on a lined or non-stick baking sheet."],[null,"Cut the tops off the garlic bulb. Wrap the garlic bulb in aluminum foil and place on the same baking sheet as the eggplant. Bake for 40 minutes or until eggplant and garlic both soften and become aromatic."],[null,"Once the eggplant and garlic have been roasted and cooled, the dip can be made. Scoop out the softened eggplant from its skin and squeeze the garlic from the bulb into a mixing bowl or food processor. Add all other ingredients for the dip. Puree in a food processor or with a handheld blender."],[null,"To make the tortilla crisps, preheat oven to 400°F."],[null,"Cut each tortilla into eight wedges and spread them on a lined or non-stick baking tray. Brush the tortillas with olive oil (or spray with oil). Sprinkle them with a blend of chili powder and cumin if desired. Bake for approximately 8 minutes or until crispy."]],"h":[]},"6982210":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F. Spray a baking sheet with the cooking spray."],[null,"In a large bowl, mix together all ingredients. Pour the vegetables onto the prepared baking sheet."],[null,"Bake on the lower oven rack for 25 minutes."]],"h":[]},"7333382":{"s":[[null,"Place the garlic on a square of kitchen foil and rub with a teaspoon of the oil. Fold into a package and bake in the oven 190°C/gas mark 5 for 30-35 minutes."],[null,"Add the rest of the oil to a pan, then add the onion and cook for 5-6 minutes, stirring regularly until browned."],[null,"Next, add the sliced cup and Portobello mushrooms, then continue cooking for a further 5 minutes until softened. Add the stock, pepper and dried thyme, mix well, bring to the boil, then turn down the heat. Add a lid and simmer gently for 5 minutes."],[null,"Squeeze the garlic out of the skin and add to the saucepan along with the cannellini beans and bring back to the boil. Add the milk, blend, and reserve."],[null,"Meanwhile, sauté the wild mushrooms in a non-stick pan for 3-4 minutes and reserve."],[null,"Add the yogurt to the soup, blend well, then divide into 4 bowls. Top with the sautéed wild mushrooms, a good grind of black pepper and fresh thyme leaves."]],"h":[[null,"You can use any combination of mushrooms for this soup. Also works well with other beans, such as butter beans."],[null,"Try with basil or oregano in place of thyme."],[null,"Roasting the garlic makes it much milder and sweeter, so don’t be put off by the amount you’re using."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Stir in the sautéed mushrooms before freezing. Defrost in a microwave or over a very low heat until piping hot."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6788995":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F. Line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Place the cauliflower florets and unpeeled garlic cloves on a baking sheet."],[null,"Drizzle the olive oil over the cauliflower and garlic. Toss to coat evenly."],[null,"Sprinkle with the salt and black pepper."],[null,"Roast in the preheated oven for 25–30 minutes or until the cauliflower is tender and golden brown."],[null,"Remove from the oven and let it cool slightly."],[null,"Squeeze the roasted garlic cloves out of their skins."],[null,"In a food processor, combine the roasted cauliflower, roasted garlic, almond milk, and nutritional yeast."],[null,"Blend until smooth and creamy. If needed, add more almond milk for desired consistency."],[null,"Garnish with fresh chopped herbs if desired."]],"h":[]},"1885":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Remove the outer papery skin from garlic head. Slice off the bottom of garlic head (largest end) and separate the cloves, leaving the outer skins in place."],[null,"Put the cloves in a shallow baking dish, and drizzle with olive oil."],[null,"Bake for about 20 minutes until the garlic is soft."],[null,"Cool and remove the skins."],[null,"In a food processor or blender, add garlic, pepper and vinegar. Process 30 seconds or until almost smooth, scraping sides occasionally. You can also mash by hand."]],"h":[[null,"Suggested uses for roasted garlic: use roasted garlic alone as a spread; add to recipes to add a mellow garlic taste; add it to mayonnaise, salad dressing or bread dough; mix a little olive oil to the puree and add it to hot pasta with chopped basil; mash garlic with cream cheese and serve on crackers or bread (add fresh dill to this for a nice spread)."],[null,"An alternative way to roast garlic is to slice 1/4-inch from the top of the garlic head and leave the cloves intact. Bake until garlic is soft enough to easily squeeze out from the head."],[null,"Vinegar acidifies the garlic to help preserve it. For safety, throw out homemade garlic products after 10 days."]]},"3355":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400° F."],[null,"Remove the outer papery skin of garlic heads, leaving the cloves intact."],[null,"Cut the top 1/4-inch off garlic heads to expose the cloves."],[null,"In a small baking dish place heads with cut side up. Pour oil over garlic heads. Cover with foil and bake for 45 to 60 minutes or until cloves are soft. Let cool, then pull or squeeze garlic cloves from the skins."]],"h":[[null,"Add roasted garlic to recipes, spread on toasted bread, or stir into sour cream or Greek yogurt to make a dip."],[null,"Store unused garlic in the refrigerator or freezer."]]},"6664964":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400°F. In a small bowl, whisk together the marinara sauce, lemon juice, oil, garlic, salt, and cinnamon. Arrange the eggplant wedges, skin side down, on an unbleached parchment paper–lined baking sheet. Generously brush the cut surfaces of the eggplant wedges with the marinara mixture."],[null,"Roast the eggplant wedges until fully cooked, about 30 minutes."],[null,"Transfer to a platter, sprinkle with the parsley, mint, feta, and lemon zest, and serve."]],"h":[]},"6669746":{"s":[[null,"Preheat an oven to 400 degrees F. Coat a baking sheet with cooking spray. Set aside."],[null,"In a large bowl, toss the green beans with 1 Tsp. olive oil, salt, pepper and garlic. Pour onto prepared baking sheet and roast for 25 minutes or until cooked through and starting to brown."],[null,"While green beans are cooking, whisk together 1 Tbsp. olive oil, champagne vinegar, Dijon mustard, sugar substitute and crushed red pepper flakes. Set aside."],[null,"When green beans are done roasting drizzle with champagne vinaigrette and toss to coat."]],"h":[]},"6223265":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F."],[null,"Toss the trimmed green beans with 1 Tbsp olive oil, salt, and black pepper."],[null,"Spread the green beans in a single layer on a baking sheet."],[null,"Roast in the preheated oven for 20 minutes or until the green beans are tender-crisp and slightly caramelized, tossing halfway through."],[null,"While the green beans are roasting, prepare the mushroom sauce."],[null,"For the creamy mushroom sauce: In a skillet, heat 2 Tbsp olive oil over medium heat."],[null,"Add sliced cremini mushrooms to the skillet and sauté until they release their moisture and become golden brown."],[null,"Sprinkle flour over the mushrooms and stir continuously for 1–2 minutes to form a roux."],[null,"Gradually whisk in vegetable broth and milk to the skillet, ensuring no lumps form."],[null,"Add minced garlic, salt, and black pepper. Stir continuously until the sauce thickens."],[null,"Reduce the heat and let the sauce simmer for an additional 2–3 minutes."],[null,"Remove the sauce from the heat."],[null,"To finish, once the green beans are roasted, transfer them to a serving dish and spoon the creamy mushroom sauce over the top."]],"h":[]},"6977081":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F. Line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"In a large bowl, toss the green beans with olive oil, salt, and pepper until they are well-coated."],[null,"Spread the green beans in a single layer on the prepared baking sheet."],[null,"Sprinkle lemon zest, sesame seeds, and minced garlic over the green beans."],[null,"Roast for 15 minutes, or until the green beans are tender-crisp and slightly caramelized."]],"h":[]},"6225448":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 375 degrees F and cover a sheet pan with parchment paper."],[null,"Drizzle the eggplant with olive oil and sprinkle with Italian seasoning, salt, and pepper."],[null,"Roast for 20–25 minutes until the eggplant is slightly brown and creamy on the inside."]],"h":[]},"2531":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400° F. Line a small baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Cut pears in half and scoop out the core."],[null,"Place pears on baking sheet, then drizzle with maple syrup and sprinkle with cinnamon."],[null,"Bake for 20 minutes. Serve warm."]],"h":[[null,"Use 100% pure maple syrup for best flavor. Honey or non-nutritive sweetener such as stevia, sweet leaf sweet drops or Splenda may be used instead of maple syrup or omit sweetener. Roasting brings out the natural sweetness and the cinnamon adds extra flavor."],[null,"Experiment with additional spices such as nutmeg, clove or cardamom."],[null,"Serve as a breakfast dish with 1/2 cup vanilla Greek yogurt and 1/2 cup Apple Cinnamon Maple Granola, another recipe from Brittany."]]},"6675530":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F. Line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"In a bowl, whisk together olive oil, maple syrup, Dijon mustard, minced garlic, dried thyme, salt, and black pepper."],[null,"Add the carrot sticks to the bowl and toss until evenly coated with the marinade. Allow the carrots to marinate for at least 30 minutes."],[null,"Spread the marinated carrot sticks in a single layer on the prepared baking sheet."],[null,"Roast in the preheated oven for 25 minutes or until the carrots are tender and slightly caramelized, stirring halfway through."]],"h":[]},"6866329":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F."],[null,"In a large bowl, toss the pears with melted butter. Pour the pears into a baking dish and roast, uncovered, for 20 to 25 minutes or until pears are tender, stirring once or twice. Set the cooked pears aside to cool."],[null,"Add the pears back to the large bowl; add the honey and lemon juice. Using an immersion blender or stand up blender, blend the pear mixture until almost smooth. Stir in the walnuts."]],"h":[]},"6274363":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oven to 350 degrees F. Line a sheet pan with parchment paper."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix together the maple syrup, ground cinnamon, and ground nutmeg."],[null,"In another small bowl, combine the oats, almond flour, vegetable oil, and chopped pecans. Mix until the crumbled topping is well combined."],[null,"Place the pear halves on a baking sheet, cut side up. Brush the cut sides of the pears with the maple syrup mixture."],[null,"Sprinkle the oat crumble mixture evenly over each pear half."],[null,"Roast the pears until the pears are tender and the crumble is golden brown, about 30 minutes. Serve warm."]],"h":[]},"6599227":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven broiler. Place the whole bell peppers on a baking sheet and broil, turning occasionally, until the skin is charred and blistered. Remove from the oven and let them cool. Once cool, peel off the skin, remove seeds, and slice into strips."],[null,"In a bowl, combine the roasted pepper strips, drained capers, sliced Kalamata olives, and chopped fresh parsley."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together extra-virgin olive oil, red wine vinegar, minced garlic, salt, and black pepper."],[null,"Pour the dressing over the roasted pepper mixture. Toss gently to combine, ensuring even coating."],[null,"Let the salad marinate for at least 15 minutes to allow the flavors to meld."]],"h":[]},"6887659":{"s":[[null,"In a food processor, combine the white beans, roasted and chopped red bell peppers, olive oil, minced garlic, fresh lemon juice, ground cumin, smoked paprika, salt, and pepper."],[null,"Pulse the mixture until it starts to break down. With the food processor running, add juice from the roasted red peppers gradually until you achieve a smooth and creamy consistency. You may need to stop and scrape down the sides of the processor a couple of times."]],"h":[]},"6101698":{"s":[[null,"Mix pizza crust according to package directions, using apple cider vinegar, 1 tbsp olive oil and water."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 450 degrees F. Spray a 12-inch pizza pan with nonstick cooking spray. Using your fingertips or the heel of your hand, spread the dough so that it covers the bottom of the pan."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine 1/2 tbsp olive oil, garlic powder, onion powder, and black pepper. Add the bell peppers and toss to coat, then place in a 9’x13’ baking dish. Bake for 20 to 25 minutes, or until the peppers are fork-tender."],[null,"Spread the sauce over the dough and sprinkle with the mozzarella cheese."],[null,"Place the roasted peppers over the cheese and bake for 13 to 15 minutes, or until the crust is crisp and brown. Cut and serve."]],"h":[]},"6157754":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400°F. Brush the peppers with 1 tablespoon of the olive oil and arrange them in a shallow roasting pan. Roast for about 35 minutes or until the pepper skins are evenly darkened, turning them 3 or 4 times. Place the peppers in a bowl, cover with plastic wrap, and leave until they are cool enough to handle."],[null,"Working over a bowl to catch the juice, peel the peppers. Cut them in half and discard the cores and seeds (strain out any seeds that fall into the juice), then cut into thick slices."],[null,"Measure 1 ½ tbsp. of the pepper juice into a small bowl (discard the remainder). Add the vinegar and garlic and whisk in the remaining 1 tablespoon of olive oil."],[null,"Arrange the peppers on a serving platter or on individual salad plates. Drizzle with dressing and garnish with the olives and basil."]],"h":[]},"7235332":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200°C/gas 6. Place the peppers on a baking tray, cut side up."],[null,"Toss together the remaining ingredients and use to fill the peppers."],[null,"Cook for 30 minutes until the peppers are tender."]],"h":[[null,"You could use other cheeses such as goat’s cheese, mature cheddar or mozzarella."],[null,"Try using baby peppers to create mini versions of this dish (cooking time will reduce to 20 minutes)."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"6035386":{"s":[[null,"In a skillet over high heat, cook pineapple chunks until slightly charred, about 2 minutes. Remove from skillet and cool to room temperature."],[null,"Refrigerate in an airtight container, stirring occasionally, for 1 hour or up to 24 hours."],[null,"Place pineapple chunks in a large bowl. Add onion, bell pepper, jalapeno, and green onions. Mix well."]],"h":[]},"6754918":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400°F."],[null,"Cut the tips off the plantains. Insert the tip of a paring knife about 1/2 inch into each plantain and run it from top to bottom. Wrap each plantain in a foil sheet. Roast in oven for 30 minutes, then remove from oven and set aside. Leave oven on."],[null,"Wash and dry poblano pepper. Rub avocado oil on the outside of pepper and (carefully) place over a flame or in oven until the outside is charred. Once pepper is charred, place in a bowl and cover until steam loosens the skin. Run pepper under cold water to remove the char, then dice pepper."],[null,"In small saucepan add stock, shallots, garlic, poblano pepper, guava, and bring up to a rolling simmer. Cook until a smooth paste forms, about 5 minutes. Add rice vinegar, salt, and pepper, and whisk well to make sure you don’t have any lumps in the sauce. Reduce heat to low and continue cooking for 2 minutes. Pour sauce in blender and purée until sauce is smooth."],[null,"Remove foil from plantains and cut each into 4 equal quarters. Carefully split open the plantain along the cut. Add 1 tablespoon guava sauce, top with queso fresco, and garnish with cilantro. Enjoy!"]],"h":[]},"6011738":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oven to 450 degrees F. In a large bowl, combine the vegetables with the oil, salt, and herbs. Toss to coat."],[null,"Arrange vegetables on two parchment paper-lined baking sheets. Roast until soft on the inside and browned on the outside, about 20-30 minutes. Flip the vegetables halfway through the cooking."],[null,"Serve warm or at room temperature."]],"h":[]},"6058861":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F."],[null,"Wash the radishes and trim off the stems. Reserve a few leaves from the radishes and slice into thin strips for garnish. Halve the radishes and toss with the garlic, oil, and salt."],[null,"Line a baking sheet with foil and place radishes cut-side down. Place in the oven and roast for 20–25 minutes until tender when pierced with a fork."],[null,"Remove from the oven and toss with lemon juice and radish leaves."]],"h":[]},"6636614":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 400 degrees F and cover a sheet pan in parchment paper."],[null,"Toss the radish halves with olive oil, dried rosemary, salt, and pepper."],[null,"Roast for 15–20 minutes until tender."],[null,"Serve warm. Garnish with fresh chopped parsley if desired."]],"h":[]},"6821943":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425° F. Spray a baking sheet with cooking spray."],[null,"Peel and cut the carrots into equal-size rounds and wedges, each about 1/2 inch in size."],[null,"Place the carrots on the baking sheet. Drizzle the olive oil over the carrots and mix well. Sprinkle with pepper."],[null,"Bake for 30 minutes, until soft and crinkly. Remove to a bowl or platter and serve."]],"h":[]},"9477520":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F convection bake, and line a large baking sheet with parchment paper. Arrange your veggies in a single layer and drizzle with the oil (if using) and sprinkle with the parsley and basil."],[null,"Roast the veggies for 30-40 minutes, or until the pepper skins have somewhat blackened, then remove from the oven. Peel your peppers once cool enough to touch. (The skins will come off easily, but if there's any stubborn pieces, just leave them on.)"],[null,"Peel the garlic, they will pop out very easily once roasted and place in your blender, along with ALL remaining ingredients, except any garnishes. Blend until smooth, taste for salt and pepper and adjust if necessary."],[null,"Serve garnished with fresh basil, croutons, crackers or black pepper."]],"h":[[null,"For oil free , drizzle the veggies with broth instead but make sure to check on them often and add more water or broth if needed. Don’t peel your garlic before roasting or your garlic may burn. The peel will remove very easily once roasted. Use fresh, ripe tomatoes, for the best results. Canned or jarred will not work well here. Make sure the pepper skins are nicely blackened so the skins peel off easily. You may place them in a bowl with a dish towel on top to steam them after roasting, if you’re having trouble peeling. Blend your soup for a couple extra minutes if you have a high speed blender to heat it up more, if your veggies have cooled. If you do not have a high speed blender , soak your cashews in boiling hot water for 20-30 minutes and then drain, before adding to your blender. (You can do this while the veggies are roasting.) Leftovers keep refrigerated for up to 4 days, or freeze in a freezer safe, air tight container for up to 3 months."]]},"1846":{"s":[[null,"Rinse the red peppers and dry. Light the two burners on the back of the stove on medium. Using tongs, place each pepper on one of the burners. When the side starts to blacken turn the peppers using tongs. Keep cooking and turning until all of the sides of the pepper are blackened. It should take 5-7 minutes."],[null,"Using tongs, place the peppers in a paper bag and close, leave for 5-8 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile cut each of the rolls in half."],[null,"Place the olive oil in a small bowl. Using a pastry brush, brush inside of each sandwich roll with the oil."],[null,"Place one slice of the Daiya cheese on each of the roll halves and put in a toaster oven. Toast until the cheese starts to melt. Remove rolls from the oven and set aside."],[null,"Take the red peppers out of the bag. Remove the outer charred skin of the pepper with your hands and discard."],[null,"Cut off the stem of the pepper and cut peppers open to remove the seeds and any excess water with a paper towel. Cut each pepper in half."],[null,"Place two pepper halves on one side of each roll, place 4 fresh basil leaves on top, cover with the remaining roll half to make the sandwich."]],"h":[[null,"If you are on a lower carbohydrate meal plan select bread or roll with lower carbohydrate count or change the portion to 1/2 sandwich."],[null,"Italian, Portuguese and ciabatta rolls tend to be longer and more rectangular in shape and will hold the roasted red pepper shape nicely. Any rectangular sandwich roll is fine to use. Compare and choose the lower sodium brand."],[null,"The peppers can be roasted a day in advance, stem & seeds removed. This makes for an even easier and quicker assembly of the sandwiches the next day."],[null,"Daiya® nondairy cheeses are relatively low in phosphorus and potassium. There are other flavors of this vegan cheese available. Check your local grocery store."],[null,"If desired, fresh mozzarella cheese can be used for those who include dairy."],[null,"This recipe can be made on a gas stove or an outdoor grill, DO NOT attempt this on an electric or induction stovetop. These types of stovetops will not roast the peppers."]]},"6494663":{"s":[[null,"Place whole peppers directly on a grill or gas burner or under your broiler. Roast until they are completely blackened on the outside. Place in a bowl and cover tightly with plastic wrap for at least 15 minutes. Once cooled, you can peel away the blackened skin."],[null,"Place the roasted pepper in the food processor and purée until fine."]],"h":[]},"3289":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425° F. Spray an 8 x 11-inch baking dish with cooking spray."],[null,"Dice the onion, red peppers and pimentos. Mince garlic cloves. Cut cream cheese into cubes."],[null,"Bring a pot of water to a boil and add macaroni (do not add salt). Cook macaroni until about halfway done, about 5 minutes. Drain and return to the pot."],[null,"Heat olive oil in a small skillet and sauté the onion and garlic until fragrant and tender."],[null,"Combine all ingredients with the partially cooked macaroni. Pour into the baking dish."],[null,"Bake, uncovered, for 15 minutes. After 15 minutes remove baking dish from oven and mix until the cream cheese has thoroughly coated all the ingredients."],[null,"Place baking dish, uncovered, back into the oven and bake for another 10 minutes."],[null,"Serve hot immediately or refrigerate to enjoy later"]],"h":[[null,"Add diced chicken, ground beef, tofu or shrimp if a higher protein dish is desired."],[null,"Add fresh basil as a garnish for some extra color and flavor, or play around with other herbs and spices to change it up!"],[null,"If you are in a rush skip sautéing the onions and garlic. Baking will bring out the flavors."],[null,"To save time prep all the ingredients while waiting for the pasta to cook."],[null,"Roasted red peppers are available prepared and jarred or you can make your own using fresh red peppers."]]},"4571160":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 450°F or medium broil (conventional oven)."],[null,"Place red peppers on baking sheet and broil on top shelf, turning if necessary, until the entire skin has turned black and blistery (20 minutes)."],[null,"For removal of the skin: place roasted red peppers in a bowl and cover with plastic wrap."],[null,"Once the peppers have cooled, proceed with skin removal: remove stems, cut pepper lengthwise in 4 slices, remove the seeds and peel off the skin."],[null,"Heat oil in saucepan over medium-high heat."],[null,"Sauté garlic and onions until onions soften (5 minutes). Add roasted red peppers, cayenne pepper, and chicken broth to pan."],[null,"Bring to a boil, close lid and simmer for 10 minutes."],[null,"Add lemon juice, marjoram, oregano and mix with a blender."]],"h":[[null,"* Choose the broth with the lowest sodium content but be aware that low sodium products often contain more potassium. Look for potassium chloride under ingredients on the label. Potassium is a hidden ingredient normally not listed in the nutrient analysis."],[null,"Soup may be served hot or cold."]]},"5886497":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200°C."],[null,"Place the red pepper, onions and sweet potatoes into a baking tray with the garlic."],[null,"Drizzle over the olive oil, then add the paprika, chilli flakes and black pepper, mix thoroughly until the vegetables are evenly coated ."],[null,"Roast in the oven for 35 minutes or until soft."],[null,"Once cooked add to pan with the low salt stock and Renastep and cook on a medium heat until warmed through."],[null,"When warm, blend until smooth, serve and enjoy!"]],"h":[["Renastep note","Renastep is a food for special medical purposes for the dietary management of kidney disease. Suitable from 3 years of age. Must be used under medical supervision. Renastep contains Milk (milk protein) and Fish (Tuna oil). This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutritics dietary analysis software. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information."]]},"3506":{"s":[[null,"Drain red peppers and measure 1/2 cup, (approximately 2 whole peppers)."],[null,"Place peppers and garlic in food processor or blender and process until smooth."],[null,"Add tomato sauce, olive oil and Italian seasonings. Process until well blended. Ready to use on pizza, pasta or as a replacement for tomato sauce in recipes."],[null,"May be refrigerated 2 to 3 days or frozen until ready to use."]],"h":[[null,"Red peppers are available bottled, canned or fresh. Compare roasted red peppers and select the brand lowest in sodium or make from fresh peppers."],[null,"Adjust red pepper chili flakes according to desire for hot and spicy flavor."],[null,"This lower potassium, low sodium sauce can be used as a substitute for tomato sauce in a variety of dishes. Try it on pizza, pasta, rice or as a topping for chicken."]]},"6807069":{"s":[[null,"Place peppers and garlic in food processor or blender and process until smooth. Add tomato sauce, olive oil and Italian seasonings. Process until well blended. Ready to use on pizza, pasta or as a replacement for tomato sauce in recipes. May be refrigerated up to 3 days or frozen until ready to use."]],"h":[]},"7378019":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200ºC/gas 6."],[null,"Add half the oil to a large, shallow ovenproof dish and pack in the tomatoes, peppers and onions into a single close layer."],[null,"Sprinkle with ginger and tuck garlic cloves and sprigs of thyme among them."],[null,"Drizzle over the remaining oil and season with pepper."],[null,"Turn so that everything is evenly coated then slide into the oven, uncovered."],[null,"Roast for about 40–45 minutes, turning occasionally, until tender and patched with brown. Serve hot or warm."]],"h":[[null,"Once cooked, you can easily squeeze the garlic out of its skin by pressing between your thumb and forefinger."],[null,"Turn this into a pasta sauce by roughly chopping the finished dish and stirring through cooked pasta."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Freeze in a bag. Defrost in a microwave and use as a sauce for pasta."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"6002802":{"s":[[null,"Preheat an oven to 400 degrees F. Coat a large baking sheet (or two medium sized) with cooking spray. Set aside."],[null,"In a large bowl, toss all of the vegetables, including the garlic, with the olive oil, and Herbs de Provence. Pour onto prepared baking sheet(s) and roast for 45 minutes or until cooked through and starting to brown."],[null,"After vegetables are done roasting, pour them into a large soup pot. Mix with the Vegetable broth and bring to a boil. Reduce to a simmer for 10 minutes."],[null,"Puree the soup with an immersion blender or in batches in an upright blender."],[null,"Season the soup with Sherry vinegar, salt and pepper."]],"h":[]},"2007":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375° F."],[null,"Slice the zucchini 1/2″ thick; slice the carrot and bell pepper 1/4″ thick; cut onion into 1/2″ wedges; crush garlic cloves."],[null,"Combine the zucchini, carrot, bell pepper, onion, garlic and oil in a 13″ x 9″ roasting pan. Season the mixture with 1/2 teaspoon black pepper and toss to coat. Roast until vegetables are heated through, about 10 minutes."],[null,"While vegetables are roasting, lift up the skin from the chicken breasts and rub the flesh with black pepper and crumbled rosemary. Replace the skin, and then season the chicken all over with additional pepper and rosemary, as desired."],[null,"Remove the roasting pan from the oven, and place the chicken, skin sides up, on top of the vegetables. Return to the oven and continue roasting until the chicken is cooked through and vegetables are tender (about 35 minutes)."]],"h":[[null,"If additional flavor is desired, you may also use Mrs. Dash® herb seasoning blend or herbed poultry seasoning for the chicken rub."],[null,"Goes well with a side of rice or bread."],[null,"Chicken should be cooked through until juices run clear when cut into or a temperature of 165° F is reached."],[null,"If you are on a lower protein diet, reduce the chicken portion to match your meal plan."]]},"3247":{"s":[[null,"Cover toaster oven tray with aluminum foil and place salmon fillets on foil."],[null,"Season salmon with black pepper, olive oil, fresh lemon juice and lemon zest"],[null,"Top with chopped fresh cilantro."],[null,"Place salmon in toaster oven on dark roast (full circle) for 6-1/2 minutes"],[null,"Remove tray from toaster oven, squeeze lemon over salmon and serve."]],"h":[[null,"If recipe prepared in a conventional oven set temperature to 425º F and cook for 8-12 minutes."],[null,"Adjust portion size to match your meal plan."],[null,"This recipe is featured in the DaVita Eats: Chef Tips video series."]]},"6209976":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F."],[null,"Add water and lemon juice to a large pot and bring to a boil."],[null,"Peel off the first layer of the outer leaves of the artichoke and cut in half lengthwise. Scoop out the hairs in the center (the choke), leaving the flesh of the artichoke intact. Drop into the boiling water for 5 minutes."],[null,"Remove the artichokes from the boiling water and place cut side up in a baking dish."],[null,"Add the whole wheat bread, garlic, parmesan cheese, parsley, and ground black pepper to a food processor and blend until crumbs. Drizzle in the olive oil while blending to make the stuffing."],[null,"Divide the stuffing evenly among each artichoke half, pressing it in to the artichoke."],[null,"Place on the middle rack of the oven and bake for 30 minutes or until topping is golden brown."]],"h":[]},"3045":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375° F."],[null,"Rinse and dry vegetables. Cut turnips and carrot into 2-inch pieces; mince garlic."],[null,"Place turnips, carrots and half of the minced garlic in a bowl and drizzle with 2 teaspoons of olive oil. Add marjoram and toss to coat vegetables with oil."],[null,"Spray two baking sheets with nonstick cooking spray; divide and layer vegetables evenly on sheets. Place baking sheets in oven for 30 minutes."],[null,"While turnips and carrots are cooking, cut onion, red bell pepper and zucchini into 2-inch pieces and slice mushrooms in half. Remove ends from green beans but keep them whole. Place vegetables in a bowl and drizzle with 2 teaspoons of olive oil. Add remaining garlic and black pepper; toss gently until vegetables are coated with oil."],[null,"After turnips and carrots have cooked for 30 minutes remove baking sheets from oven. Divide the green bean vegetable mixture between the two baking sheets. Mix vegetables with partially cooked turnips and carrots, forming a single layer on the baking sheets. Return to oven for another 15–20 minutes, cooking until vegetables are tender."]],"h":[[null,"Roasted vegetables have extra flavor compared to steamed or boiled vegetables. No salt is needed."],[null,"Experiment with different vegetable combinations."]]},"6104868":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F."],[null,"In a large bowl, toss the diced sweet potatoes with olive oil, smoked paprika, salt, and black pepper until evenly coated."],[null,"Spread the sweet potatoes in a single layer on a baking sheet."],[null,"Roast in the preheated oven for 20–25 minutes or until the sweet potatoes are tender and golden brown, stirring halfway through."],[null,"Remove the sweet potatoes from the oven and let them cool slightly."],[null,"In a large salad bowl, combine arugula, roasted sweet potatoes, toasted and chopped pecans, and dried cranberries."],[null,"Drizzle the balsamic vinaigrette dressing over the salad."]],"h":[]},"6685472":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F. Line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Toss the sweet potato wedges with olive oil. Bake for 20–25 minutes, until tender, tossing halfway."],[null,"Meanwhile, zest and juice the lemon into a small bowl. Add garlic, yogurt, dill, salt, and pepper."],[null,"Drizzle yogurt sauce over the wedges and serve."]],"h":[]},"7813247":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 220°C/gas 7."],[null,"Place the lentils in a medium pan with the garlic and stock, bring to the boil and simmer for 15–20 minutes until tender. Drain off any excess liquid then add the tomatoes and spring onions and stir well to combine. Season."],[null,"Meanwhile, place the swordfish on a baking sheet, drizzle over the oil and season. Place in the oven and cook for about 10 minutes until crisp and cooked through."],[null,"To make the salsa, place all the ingredients for the salsa into a blender or food processor and blend until combined, but still retaining some texture."],[null,"To serve, spoon the lentils onto serving plates top with a piece of swordfish and then spoon over the salsa."]],"h":[[null,"Children, pregnant women and women who are trying to get pregnant should not eat swordfish as it contains more mercury than other fish. Other adults are advised to eat no more than one portion of swordfish per week."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"7696438":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 220ºC/gas 7."],[null,"Place the bulgur wheat into a bowl and pour over enough boiling water to cover by about 1cm. Leave to soak for 30 minutes, then drain off any excess liquid."],[null,"Meanwhile, place the tomatoes onto a baking sheet with the peppers and roast for 10-15 minutes until softened."],[null,"Gently toss through the bulgur wheat with the remaining ingredients and season well."]],"h":[[null,"For a gluten-free version, use quinoa in place of bulgur wheat."],[null,"This is also great served warm with chickpea, chicken or lamb tagine."],[null,"Freezing instructions: suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge or microwave to serve, or reheat in the oven or microwave."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"9440103":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400℉/204℃ and line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Arrange the tomatoes, strawberries, onion and garlic on your tray in a single layer. Sprinkle with salt and pepper and then bake for about 20-22 minutes, or until lightly caramelized. Remove from the oven."],[null,"Transfer the cooked veggies and strawberries to your blender and add the broth, vinegar, and maple syrup. Blend until smooth, then taste for salt and pepper and adjust as needed."],[null,"Serve garnished with freshly chopped basil."]],"h":[]},"9532392":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 425℉/218℃ convection roast and line a large baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Arrange the quartered tomatoes, onion, and garlic cloves (don't peel the garlic) on the tray and roast for 25 minutes, or until the veggies are golden brown. Remove from the oven."],[null,"Once roasted, peel the garlic (they will pop out of their skins easily now) and add the roasted veggies, broth, miso paste, and beans to a blender and process until completely smooth. Taste for salt and pepper, and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Use a low-sodium vegetable broth since the miso paste also adds a salty flavour. Once blended, taste and add salt and pepper, if needed."],[null,"If you do not have a convection oven , use the same temperature, but note that you may need an additional 5 minutes or so to roast the veggies."],[null,"Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-4 days, or freeze them airtight for up to 3 months."]]},"2741":{"s":[[null,"Check plastic wrap on turkey to determine cooking time."],[null,"Preheat oven to 425º F. Remove neck and giblet bag from cavity of turkey. Rinse turkey with cold water, then pat dry with clean paper towels."],[null,"Using several fingers, loosen skin from turkey breast and drumsticks. Rub poultry seasoning onto turkey flesh under skin. Place parsley, sage, rosemary, and thyme sprigs between turkey skin and flesh."],[null,"Place a meat thermometer in the fleshy part of the thigh, without touching the bone."],[null,"Coat turkey with melted butter (or oil) and place breast side up in a roasting pan on a rack. Cover loosely with aluminum foil. Cook 30 minutes then reduce heat to 325º F."],[null,"Begin basting the turkey every 15 to 20 minutes with the giblet stock and pan juices. During last 30 minutes remove foil from roasting pan. Cook for 3 to 4 hours until meat thermometer registers 165º F."],[null,"Let turkey rest 30 minutes before carving."]],"h":[[null,"Three days before serving: if frozen, thaw turkey in refrigerator for 3 days. One day before serving: remove giblets from turkey and make giblet stock (see recipe)."],[null,"Make the Fresh Herb Cranberry Stuffing if you wish to stuff the turkey. After step 3 above loosely place stuffing in the body cavity and neck. Use skewers and string to fasten neck skin under the body and tie legs together."],[null,"For CKD non-dialysis diet, please reduce serving size to match your meal plan."]]},"6952872":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375° F. Coat a baking dish with nonstick cooking spray."],[null,"Toss the celery, carrots, onion, cabbage, and thyme together and place in the pan. Pour the chicken broth over the vegetables."],[null,"Remove the skin from the turkey breast. Place the turkey bone side down on top of the vegetables. Drizzle the turkey and vegetables with the olive oil. Sprinkle them with the all-purpose seasoning and black pepper."],[null,"Roast the turkey and vegetables in the oven for 1 hour, or until the internal temperature of the turkey is 165° F."],[null,"When the dish comes out of the oven, set the turkey on a cutting board to rest. Remove the thyme stems and stir the vegetables."],[null,"Slice the turkey into 4-oz portions and serve each with ¼ of the vegetable mixture."]],"h":[]},"3945":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350º F."],[null,"Finely mince the onion. Melt the butter, and then add the onion and herb seasoning blend. Divide the mixture in half."],[null,"In a large roasting pan or skillet, place the turkey breast skin side down. Coat with 1 tablespoon of the seasoning mixture."],[null,"Turn the breast over and loosen the skin with your fingers. Spread 3 tablespoons of the seasoning mixture between the flesh and skin. Use toothpicks to attach the edges of the skin to the breast meat."],[null,"Place the pan in the oven and bake for 1 hour."],[null,"Remove the pan from the oven and spread remaining seasoning mixture over turkey skin."],[null,"Return the pan to the oven and cook for 15 to 20 minutes or until meat thermometer reads 160º F."],[null,"Remove the pan from the oven and let turkey breast rest for 10-15 minutes before slicing."]],"h":[[null,"Use an herb seasoning blend with garlic and onion for optimal flavor."],[null,"Adjust portion size to match your meal plan if you need a lower or higher protein intake."]]},"6752392":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F."],[null,"Heat the oil in a large, deep, nonstick skillet over medium-high heat. Add the onion and sauté until the onion is softened, about 3 minutes then add the peppers and continue sauteing for another 5 minutes, until softened. Remove to a heatproof bowl."],[null,"Add the mushrooms to the pan and sauté until softened, about another 5 minutes. Stir in the spinach, and toss until just wilted, about 1 minute. Add the beans, cilantro, oregano, cumin, and salt, and sauté until fully combined and heated through, about 1 minute. Stir in the peppers and onions. Adjust seasoning."],[null,"Spread 1/2 cup salsa into a 9x13-inch baking dish. Arrange 6 tortillas to cover the bottom of the dish. Evenly top with half of the vegetable mixture. Arrange the remaining 6 tortillas on top. Cover with remaining ½ cup of salsa. Evenly top with remaining vegetable mixture. Sprinkle with the cheese. Bake until fully cooked through and the cheese is melted, about 20 minutes."],[null,"Cut the casserole into 6 portions and serve."]],"h":[]},"7817889":{"s":[[null,"Add the potatoes to a pan of boiling water and cook 15 mins until soft, then mash."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 220ºC/gas 7. In a large bowl, mix together the gram flour, ground rice, cornflour, bicarbonate of soda and cream of tartar."],[null,"Rub in the potato and spread, until the mixture resembles breadcrumbs."],[null,"Add enough milk to make a soft dough and form into a ball, then roll out to a 30cm round and place on a lightly oiled baking sheet."],[null,"Top with slices of tomato, peppers and onion, and mushroom halves."],[null,"Crumble over the feta and bake for 15–20 minutes until the vegetables are tender and the pizza base is golden and crisp."],[null,"Scatter over the basil and serve."]],"h":[[null,"To make a garlic crust, simply add 2-3 cloves crushed garlic to the potato."],[null,"For extra flavour, sprinkle 1 tsp dried organo and pinch of chilli flakes over the tomato slices before adding the peppers and onion."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"3299":{"s":[[null,"Cut potatoes into 1″ cubes. Place in a large pot of water and boil for 10 minutes. Drain water, add fresh water and cook until tender."],[null,"Cut bell peppers into bite-sized pieces, cut mushrooms in half, slice zucchini and mince garlic."],[null,"Add the bell peppers, mushrooms, zucchini, garlic, olive oil and rosemary to potatoes. Mix well."],[null,"Spread vegetables on a broiler pan, sprinkle with black pepper, and broil for 12 to 15 minutes, until vegetables are slightly browned at the edges. Stir a few times during cooking."],[null,"Add vegetables back to the large bowl and toss with the balsamic vinegar. Serve hot or at room temperature."]],"h":[[null,"Line your broiler pan with aluminum foil to keep in the juices and speed up cleaning."],[null,"One medium bell pepper yields approximately 3/4 cup cut-up, raw pepper pieces."]]},"6325867":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 425°F."],[null,"Place eggplant in a large bowl. Lightly salt eggplant and let sit for 10 minutes. (This will prevent it from absorbing too much oil.) Add remaining vegetables and toss with olive oil."],[null,"Line baking sheet with parchment. Place vegetables on baking sheet. Sprinkle with salt and pepper to taste. Roast to desired doneness, approximately 20–30 minutes. Adjust seasonings to taste."],[null,"Place on serving platter and sprinkle with balsamic vinegar. Garnish with fresh herbs."]],"h":[]},"6857343":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 400 degrees F and cover a sheet pan in parchment paper."],[null,"Toss the mixed vegetables with olive oil, dried oregano, salt, and pepper."],[null,"Roast for 20-25 minutes until tender and slightly charred."],[null,"Serve on top of feta."]],"h":[]},"6769296":{"s":[[null,"Rinse and cook the quinoa according to the package instructions. Set aside and keep warm."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F. Toss the sweet potatoes, zucchini, bell pepper, and onion with olive oil and salt. Spread on a baking sheet and roast for 25–30 minutes, stirring halfway, until tender and slightly caramelized."],[null,"Pat trout fillets dry and season with garlic powder, paprika, and black pepper. Heat a nonstick or cast iron skillet over medium heat. Sear tilapia skin-side down for 3–4 minutes, then flip and cook another 2–3 minutes, or until the flesh flakes easily."],[null,"In a small bowl, add the Greek yogurt, lemon juice, Dijon mustard, dill, and grated garlic. Whisk until smooth and well combined."],[null,"In each of the 4 bowls, layer the quinoa, arugula, and roasted vegetables. Top with the seared trout and drizzle with the yogurt sauce just before serving."]],"h":[]},"6927328":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F."],[null,"In a saucepan, combine the dry quinoa with 2 cups of water. Bring to a boil, then reduce heat. Cover, and simmer for 15 minutes or until quinoa is cooked and water is absorbed."],[null,"While the quinoa is cooking, spread the cubed chicken and chopped vegetables on a baking sheet."],[null,"Drizzle olive oil over the chicken and vegetables, sprinkle with the dried oregano, garlic powder, salt, and pepper. Toss to coat evenly."],[null,"Roast the chicken and vegetables in the preheated oven for about 20–25 minutes or until they are tender and slightly browned and the chicken reaches an internal temperature of 165 degrees F."],[null,"Assemble by dividing the cooked quinoa and roasted vegetable mix among bowls."],[null,"Top with crumbled feta cheese and serve with fresh lemon wedges."]],"h":[]},"6480190":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375°F. Coat a large baking sheet with cooking spray."],[null,"Toss all of the vegetables together and spread evenly on the baking sheet. Spray the vegetables with 5-6 sprays of cooking spray and season with salt-free Spike seasoning."],[null,"Roast the vegetables for 30 minutes, then set aside to cool slightly."],[null,"Whisk together the eggs, egg whites, dried mustard, sage, and black pepper."],[null,"Coat a 9x13-inch casserole dish with cooking spray. Tear four pieces of the whole wheat bread into pieces and layer them on the bottom of the casserole dish. Top with 1/2 the roasted vegetables and 1/4 cup Parmesan cheese. Pour half the egg mixture over the bread, vegetables, and cheese."],[null,"Repeat the layering process with the remaining torn bread, vegetables, cheese, and egg mixture. Press down on the casserole with a spatula to ensure all of the bread soaks in the egg mixture. Let the strata sit at room temperature for 15 minutes."],[null,"Bake the strata for 30 minutes."],[null,"To serve, cut the strata down the middle lengthwise, then cut down the middle width-wise. Cut each half down the middle width-wise again to make 8 equal servings."]],"h":[]},"6183832":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400°F. In a large bowl, combine all the ingredients except the parsley and thyme."],[null,"Divide the vegetables between 2 large baking sheets, and spread them in a single layer on each sheet. Roast the vegetables for 45 to 60 minutes, turning and stirring them halfway through, until they are tender and lightly browned."],[null,"Add the vegetables to a serving bowl, and mix in the parsley and thyme."]],"h":[]},"6565884":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F."],[null,"In a large bowl, toss squash with olive oil, dried oregano, salt, and pepper."],[null,"Place on baking sheet and roast for 15–20 minutes until tender."]],"h":[]},"6952937":{"s":[[null,"Heat your oven to 425°F."],[null,"Wash the zucchini and cut it into halfmoons or small pieces."],[null,"Place the zucchini on a small baking sheet."],[null,"Drizzle with olive oil and sprinkle with salt, pepper, garlic powder and Italian seasoning."],[null,"Toss to coat the pieces evenly."],[null,"Spread the zucchini in a single layer."],[null,"Roast for 12–15 minutes, or until tender and lightly browned."],[null,"Serve warm."]],"h":[]},"6070144":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F."],[null,"Place rice and chicken stock in a saucepan. Bring to boil over a high heat. Cook, stirring constantly, for 20 minutes, or until rice is tender but firm (al dente). Add more water, 1/4 cup at a time, if rice begins to stick to the bottom of the pan. When rice is finished cooking, set aside."],[null,"Meanwhile, wipe off the tomatoes, discard the stem without damaging the skin, and lay the tomatoes stem side down. Cut a round slice from the side opposite to the stem; you will be using it as a lid. With a melon scoop, scrape out the flesh of the tomato, being careful not to break the skin. Reserve the pulp and the juice."],[null,"Chop the pulp and mix it with the juice (you can use a food processor). In a bowl, combine the pulp and juice with the rice, 3 tbsp olive oil, basil, mint, salt, and pepper."],[null,"Stuff hollow tomatoes with the rice mixture. Cover with the tomato lids and arrange in a greased baking dish, standing the stuffed tomatoes with the lid side up. Drizzle with the remaining 1 tbsp olive oil and bake for 20–30 minutes, or until the tomatoes are cooked through. Serve hot or at room temperature."]],"h":[]},"6655334":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F."],[null,"Core the apples, making sure to leave the bottoms intact. Cut off the top of each apple, about 1/4 inch from the top."],[null,"In a medium bowl, combine 2 tablespoons lime juice and 2 cups water. Soak the apples in the water for about 5 minutes to prevent browning."],[null,"In another bowl, add almond butter, cinnamon, nutmeg, vanilla extract, remaining lime juice, and pumpkin spice. Mix together."],[null,"Remove apples from water and pat dry. Stuff each apple with 1 tablespoon almond butter mixture. Once all apples are stuffed, place them in a deep baking dish. Add about 1/2 inch water to the baking dish, and make sure apples are upright in the water. (The water keeps the apples from drying out.) Bake for 1 hour. While the apples bake, keep an eye on the water level; add more water if needed."],[null,"Once apples are fork tender, remove from baking dish and serve."]],"h":[]},"6579178":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375 degrees F. Line a large baking sheet with parchment paper or a silicon mat."],[null,"Combine all ingredients in a large mixing bowl and mix well."],[null,"Pack the root vegetable mixture into a 1/2 cup measure and turn out onto the baking sheet. Press lightly to form a cake. Repeat this process for remaining 9 cakes (depending on the size of your baking sheet, you may need to make these in batches or use two baking sheets)."],[null,"Spray the tops of the cakes with cooking spray and bake for 35 minutes."],[null,"Let the cakes slightly cool before removing from pan."]],"h":[]},"5020726":{"s":[[null,"Place the rose tea bag into a cup with the boiling water and allow to brew for 3-4 minutes or as per guidance the packaging. Then carefully remove the tea bag."],[null,"Warm Renastep gently in a pan on a low heat."],[null,"In a cup, mix the beetroot powder with a small amount of Renastep to make a paste, then stir in the remaining Renastep."],[null,"Pour in the rose tea and mix well."],[null,"Serve warm."]],"h":[[null,"Serve as an iced latte – use chilled Renastep and serve over re-useable ice plastic cubes. Red or pink food colouring can be used instead of beetroot powder. Sprinkle with cinnamon to serve."],["Renastep note","Renastep is a Food for Special Medical Purposes and must be used under medical supervision. Renastep is a ready to use feed for the dietary management of kidney disease from 3 years of age onwards. Renastep contains milk and fish. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information. This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutrimen dietary analysis software."]]},"7400058":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 5. Remove the papery outer layer of the onions, leaving their skins intact, then trim off their tops and bottoms."],[null,"Cut a cross in the top of each onion, slicing down to cut into four, but only three quarters of the way through, making sure the onions stay whole."],[null,"Place each onion on a square of foil and create a loose parcel that's open at the top. Cut 4 cloves garlic into 5 slices each, then push one slice into each of the cross cuts and one in the centre, pushing down to the core."],[null,"Do the same with the rosemary spigs, using one for each onion, breakingthe sprigs into smaller pieces."],[null,"Add balsamic vinegar, olive oil and a grind of pepper to each parcel. Then, bring up the corners of the foil and twist it at the top to seal. Bake for 45 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Open up the foil parcel at the table to enjoy the aromas that are sealed in."],[null,"Use smaller onions, but reduce the cooking time by 10 minutes."],[null,"Use fresh sprigs of thyme or sage as an alternative to rosemary."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"6135376":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F. Coat a large glass or metal baking dish with cooking spray."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the olive oil, lemon zest, lemon juice, Dijon mustard, garlic, salt (optional), black pepper, and minced rosemary."],[null,"Cut each game hen in half lengthwise and remove the skin. Pat dry with a paper towel. Lay 4 rosemary sprigs on the bottom of the baking dish."],[null,"Arrange the hens breast side up in the baking dish (one half on top of each of the rosemary sprigs). Brush each hen generously with marinade (using all of the marinade)."],[null,"Bake for 30–35 minutes or until the internal temperature reaches 165 degrees F."]],"h":[]},"6383220":{"s":[[null,"Heat 1 tsp olive oil in a skillet over medium heat. Add the bread cubes, then sprinkle with dried oregano and garlic powder. Toast the cubes, stirring frequently, until they are golden brown and crisp, about 4-5 minutes. Remove from the skillet and let them cool."],[null,"In a small mixing bowl, whisk together the Greek yogurt, lemon juice, minced garlic, Dijon mustard, Worcestershire sauce, 2 tsp olive oil, and black pepper until smooth and well combined."],[null,"In a large bowl, toss the chopped romaine lettuce and peppers with the dressing, ensuring everything is evenly coated."],[null,"Gently mix the cooked pasta into the salad. Add the toasted croutons and toss lightly to combine."],[null,"Divide into 4 servings and top with shaved Parmesan cheese."]],"h":[]},"2584":{"s":[[null,"Place beaten eggs, 1/2 teaspoon black pepper, dry mustard, salt, prepared mustard, sugar and flour in a saucepan and mix well."],[null,"Add water, vinegar and butter. Stir to mix well."],[null,"Cook over medium heat; bring to a boil and continue boiling until mixture thickens, stirring constantly."],[null,"Cool dressing before adding to rotini mixture."],[null,"Cook rotini according to directions on package, omitting the salt."],[null,"Drain and rinse with cold water."],[null,"Chop onion and eggs; dice cucumber."],[null,"In a large bowl, mix rotini, onion, eggs, cucumber and pepper."],[null,"Add homemade salad dressing and mix well."],[null,"Refrigerate several hours before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Rotini is pasta shaped like little corkscrews."],[null,"4 ounces dry rotini yields 2-1/2 cups cooked."],[null,"To reduce cholesterol, omit 4 egg yolks from the hard boiled eggs."]]},"2178":{"s":[[null,"Cook rotini according to directions on package omitting salt. Drain and rinse with cold water."],[null,"Hard boil eggs, cool and peel."],[null,"Chop onion and eggs; dice cucumber."],[null,"In a large bowl, mix rotini, onion, eggs, cucumber and pepper."],[null,"Combine remaining ingredients to make dressing."],[null,"Add homemade dressing to pasta and mix well."],[null,"Refrigerate to chill before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Rotini is pasta shaped like little corkscrews."],[null,"4 ounces dry rotini yields 2-1/2 cups cooked."]]},"3870":{"s":[[null,"Remove chicken from bones and chop into bite-sized pieces. Measure 4 cups for the soup."],[null,"Pour chicken broth in a large stock pot; bring to a boil."],[null,"Chop onion; slice celery and carrots."],[null,"Add chicken, vegetables and noodles to stock pot."],[null,"Bring to a boil and cook approximately 15 minutes until noodles are done."],[null,"Garnish with chopped parsley."]],"h":[[null,"Make a batch and eat soup all week, or cut recipe in half to make a smaller batch."],[null,"Low-sodium broth contains 140 mg sodium or less per cup. Look for Campbell’s® low-sodium broth, Health Valley® low-sodium broth or Nature’s Choice® low-sodium broth. Avoid low-sodium broth with potassium chloride — it is very high in potassium."]]},"3004":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 275° F."],[null,"Lightly butter and flour two large cookie sheets."],[null,"In a large bowl, let the egg whites warm to room temperature, about 15 minutes."],[null,"With electric mixer at high speed, beat egg whites with cream of tartar, salt and vanilla until soft peaks form when beater is slowly raised."],[null,"Gradually beat in granulated sugar two teaspoons at a time, until very stiff peaks form. Mixture should be moist and shiny."],[null,"Drop meringue by tablespoonfuls, using rubber spatula to push meringue from spoon to form mounds, 1” apart. There should be approximately 40 mounds."],[null,"Sprinkle each mound with sprinkles if desired."],[null,"Bake about 1 hour or until crisp and very light golden color."],[null,"Open oven door and let meringues cool for 1 hour before removing from cookie sheet. Store in a covered container until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Add an extract such as lemon or almond for extra flavoring."]]},"4049324":{"s":[[null,"Make spice rub by blending coffee and all spices together. You will need 2–4 tablespoons of rub for 1.3 lbs of steak. Keep any extra spice rub (must not have touched the meat) in a jar with a lid for up to 3 months."],[null,"Remove flank steak from the refrigerator at least 30 minutes before grilling to allow it to reach room temperature. This will allow for a more accurate cooking doneness. Apply the spice rub."],[null,"Toss vegetables with the olive oil, garlic, rosemary and pepper on a large piece of aluminum foil. Seal the vegetables in the foil by making a pouch."],[null,"Using the grill Preheat grill to medium-high heat. Grill the vegetables in the pouch for 15–20 minutes. Flank steak is a lean cut of meat and is best served medium rare.* Grill steak for approximately 4 minutes per side."],["Using the stove","Preheat the oven to 400°F. Bake the vegetables in the pouch for 15–20 minutes. You can also roast the vegetables uncovered on a baking sheet. For the steak, heat grill pan to medium-high and add 1 tablespoon of oil. Fry approximately 4 minutes per side."],["Using the stove","When the steak is ready, allow the meat to rest for at least 5 minutes before slicing. By resting the meat, you ensure that the juices don't run out of the steak when sliced. Cut the steak in slices against the grain and serve with the vegetables."]],"h":[[null,"* Mechanically tenderized meat, such as flank steak, must be cooked until an internal temperature of 160°F is reached."]]},"6042443":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400 degrees F. Spray a baking sheet with cooking spray."],[null,"In a medium bowl mix together potatoes, 1 Tbsp. olive oil, 1/4 Tsp. garlic salt, 1/8 Tsp. pepper and 1/4 Tsp. parsley."],[null,"Place potatoes on half of baking sheet and bake for 15 minutes."],[null,"In a medium bowl mix together green beans, 1 Tbsp. olive oil, 1/4 Tsp. garlic salt and 1/8 Tsp. pepper."],[null,"After potatoes have baked for 15 minutes; add green beans to other half of baking sheet. Bake potatoes and green beans for additional 20 minutes."]],"h":[]},"6262343":{"s":[[null,"In a large saucepan combine the rutabaga, potatoes, carrots, garlic, bay leaf, salt and pepper to taste, broth and water. Bring to a boil over medium heat, reduce to a simmer, cover, and cook for 30 minutes until tender. Drain the vegetables, reserving 1/2 cup liquid. Remove and discard the bay leaf."],[null,"With a potato masher, mas the vegetables with the reserved cooking liquid and the olive oil. Readjust seasonings if necessary and serve."]],"h":[]},"1002990":{"s":[[null,"Heat olive oil in a skillet over medium heat. Add chicken and sprinkle with pepper."],[null,"Sauté chicken for 5 minutes on each side, until browned."],[null,"Add balsamic vinegar and sauté for one minute, turning chicken to coat."],[null,"Wash and finely chop basil."],[null,"Add honey and basil. Stir and turn chicken to coat."],[null,"Cook for one minute more."]],"h":[[null,"You can season the chicken with aromatic herbs or your favorite low-sodium seasonings. Garlic and onion go well with black pepper."],[null,"If you are on a low-protein diet, reduce the portion to half a chicken breast, or use boneless chicken thighs instead of breasts."]]},"7145749":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a non-stick frying pan, add the onion, garlic, chilli and ginger and cook for 2-3 minutes until softened."],[null,"Stir in the turmeric and cook for 5 minutes. Add the potatoes and red chilli powder, stir, cover and cook for 15-20 minutes over a medium heat, stirring regularly."],[null,"Stir through the spinach, cover and cook for 25 to 30 minutes, until the potatoes are tender and the mixture quite dry."]],"h":[[null,"This dish works well with frozen spinach. Just defrost and add when the potatoes are almost cooked."],[null,"If you don’t have fresh chillies, ginger or the spices you could add 1 tbsp curry paste – mild or hot, whichever you prefer."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost thoroughly and reheat until piping hot."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"3366":{"s":[[null,"Chop parsley, onion, cilantro and garlic. Slightly beat eggs."],[null,"Place all ingredients, except the oil, in a bowl. Stir until well mixed."],[null,"Heat oil in a skillet over medium heat."],[null,"Pour the mixture into the skillet to make one large patty."],[null,"Cover and cook until the mix is golden brown and crispy."],[null,"Turn over gently and brown the other side (like a pancake) without the cover."],[null,"Divide patty into 4 equal portions. Serve with pita bread and a lemon wedge."]],"h":[[null,"Koko sandwich can be baked instead of fried. Heat oven to 350° F, place mixture in an oiled baking dish and bake for 50 to 60 minutes, until top is golden brown. Cut into 4 portions."],[null,"If desired, lavash bread, flour tortilla or white bread may be used in place of the pita bread."],[null,"Use 1-1/4 cup low cholesterol egg product instead of eggs for a low cholesterol dish."]]},"7682200":{"s":[[null,"Add the oil to a large pan, fry the onion and pepper for 3–4 minutes, stirring regularly, until softened."],[null,"Add the carrots and ginger then cook for five minutes, stirring regularly. Remove everything from the pan and set to one side."],[null,"Add the potatoes to the same pan and cook for 5 minutes, stirring regularly. Return the onion, pepper, ginger and carrots to the pan."],[null,"Add the spices and green chilli (the amount will vary according to how hot you like it!) and cook for 3 minutes until the spices start to stick."],[null,"Add the stock and simmer for 20 minutes until thickened."],[null,"Stir in the fresh coriander and half the spinach and cook for 3 minutes. Once the spinach has wilted, stir in the remaining spinach. Keep in the pan for a further for 1–2 minutes then serve with rice."]],"h":[[null,"Try replacing the potato with sweet potato, which gives you an extra portion of veg towards your five a day."],[null,"This is great stuffed into halved peppers (any colour) topped with a small amount of cheese and baked for 15-20 minutes at 180°C/gas 4 until golden brown on top."],[null,"Try rolled up in a roti or chapatti with salad and a cucumber raita for a healthy wrap."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"6630493":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375° F. Add the bread to a large bowl."],[null,"Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium heat. Add the onions and celery, and sauté for 3 minutes. Add the walnuts and sauté for 2 minutes. Add in the sage and cook for 1 minute."],[null,"Add the onion-sage mixture to the bread. Pour the hot chicken broth and egg over the onion-sage, and mix well (until moist). Add in the cranberries or cherries. Season well with salt and pepper. Add the mixture to a large casserole dish, and sprinkle with paprika. Bake for about 40-45 minutes, or until the top is browned and crusty."]],"h":[]},"7201713":{"s":[[null,"Add the onions to a pan with the rapeseed oil and cook gently for 6–7 minutes until softened and starting to brown."],[null,"Add the pepper and sage. Then add the breadcrumbs, sweet potato and 200ml water from the boiled potato."],[null,"Mix well, place the mixture in a lightly oiled ovenproof dish and bake for 20 minutes until the top has browned."]],"h":[[null,"If you don’t like sage, try adding a tablespoon of freshly chopped parsley and a teaspoon of dried thyme or use oregano or tarragon instead."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Freeze in portions then defrost in the fridge,or defrost in a microwave and reheat until piping hot."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"6526998":{"s":[[null,"Combine the beans, tomato, corn, cucumber, red onion, and cilantro."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the tomato juice, lime juice, olive oil, chili powder, salt, and pepper. Pour over the salad and mix gently. Serve over the mixed greens."]],"h":[]},"6294641":{"s":[],"h":[]},"7714393":{"s":[[null,"Boil the potatoes 15-20 minutes until just tender, then refresh in cold water to cool."],[null,"In a bowl, toss together the potatoes, beans, egg, tomatoes, olives and anchovies. Drizzle over the lemon rind and juice, stir and set aside for 10 minutes."],[null,"Heat a frying or griddle pan until hot, rub the oil over the tuna and sear for 2-3 minutes on each side. Allow to cool for a few minutes then cut into thick slices."],[null,"Arrange the salad on a platter, season and top with the tuna."]],"h":[[null,"'At risk' groups such as infants, children, pregnant women, the elderly and those who are unwell should avoid eating ready-to-eat, cold-smoked or cured fish. Therefore, this recipe is not suitable if this applies to you."],[null,"This recipe also works well with flaked poached salmon in place of tuna."],[null,"If you don't like anchovies, add a few finely sliced sundried tomatoes instead."],[null,"You could make this with hard boiled quail's eggs, which are available ready cooked."],[null,"Seared tuna isn’t to everyone’s taste and may not be suitable, so you might want to leave it on the griddle for longer, until it's cooked through."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"6087905":{"s":[[null,"Combine the cream cheese and lemon zest in a small bowl."],[null,"Add the arugula to a medium bowl. Drizzle 1 Tbsp. lemon juice and the olive oil over the arugula. Sprinkle the black pepper over the arugula and toss gently to coat."],[null,"Lay out one flat bread. Spread 1 ounce of the cream cheese mixture down the center of the flatbread. Top with 1 portion of salmon and 1 cup of dressed arugula. Wrap tightly and cut in half. Then, slice each half into four equal rounds."],[null,"Repeat for the remaining three wraps."]],"h":[]},"6443719":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 425°F."],[null,"Cut off a 15 x 10-inch sheet of cooking parchment and fold in half to for a 7.5 x 10-inch rectangle. Starting at the bottom of the fold, cut into a half-heart shape. Open and spray with cooking spray. Repeat with a second sheet. Place one filet of salmon skin side down centered on half of each parchment heart. Top each filet with half of the shallots, pepper, and asparagus."],[null,"Fold the other heart halves over the fish and asparagus. Seal each packet by forming a small fold at the top of the heart and continuing to fold the edge until reaching the bottom. Twist the point to shut tightly. Place the sealed packets on a baking sheet, and bake for 10 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, make the gremolata: finely chop the parsley and garlic together. Add the lemon zest, and continue chopping until well blended."],[null,"Remove the parchment packets from the oven. Let stand for 3 minutes. Being careful to prevent steam burns, cut an X in the center of each packet. Test to be sure the salmon flakes easily when tested with a fork. If necessary, return the packets to the oven for 1 to 2 minutes to finish cooking."],[null,"Transfer packets to a plate and open the rest of the way. Sprinkle each with 2 teaspoons of gremolata."]],"h":[]},"7084875":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 200°C/fan 180°C/gas 6."],[null,"Put the new potatoes in a saucepan of boiling water over a high heat and cook for 18-20 minutes or until tender."],[null,"Meanwhile, put the salmon fillets in a non-stick baking tray and dust with the sumac. Spray with a couple of pumps of low-calorie cooking spray and cook in the oven for 15 minutes or until cooked through."],[null,"To make the sauce, put the watercress, yoghurt and most of the basil in your food processor, blitz until smooth and season with a little pepper (or use a stick blender and a jug)."],[null,"Spray a non-stick frying pan or griddle pan with a couple of pumps of low-calorie cooking spray and place over a high heat. Add the asparagus and mangetout and cook for about 2 minutes or until they're charred but still have a little bite."],[null,"Drain the potatoes and lightly crush with a fork, then toss with the mangetout, asparagus, lemon juice and most of the lemon zest. Divide between plates, top with the salmon (you can keep it whole or flake it into chunks) and drizzle over the watercress sauce. Scatter over the rest of the basil leaves and lemon zest to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Sumac is a Middle Eastern spice available from most large supermarkets. If you can't find any, replace it with a little extra lemon zest."],[null,"Check spice/seasoning blends for added ingredients such as sugar, salt, flour or oil. Choose blends made from herbs and spices only if possible."],[null,"Use a plain yoghurt of your choice. However, this will change the nutritional information and texture of the dish."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6371783":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together soy sauce, honey, sesame oil, minced ginger, and minced garlic to create the sauce."],[null,"Brush salmon with some of the sauce."],[null,"Heat a large skillet over medium high heat and sear the salmon till cooked through, about 4 minutes per side."],[null,"Brush the top of the salmon with more marinade."],[null,"Build the bowls with brown rice, steamed broccoli, salmon, and avocado. Drizzle with sauce. Finish with green onions."]],"h":[]},"6658275":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F. Line a large baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix the olive oil, chili sauce, ginger, and lower sodium soy sauce."],[null,"Place salmon filets in the center of the sheet pan and brush liberally with the sauce."],[null,"Stir the vegetables into the remaining sauce and place on the sheet pan around the salmon."],[null,"Roast in the preheated oven for approximately 20 minutes, or until the salmon is cooked through to 145 degrees F and the vegetables are tender."],[null,"Garnish with a squeeze of fresh lime juice if desired."]],"h":[]},"7583393":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4. For the filo pastry, Lightly spray oil onto a large baking sheet, place on it 4 oven proof dishes (approx. 10cm across and 2 cm deep) upside down and spray with a little oil."],[null,"Divide the mixture between the pastry cases and add the salmon to each case and pour over the milk and egg mixture."],[null,"Arrange 3 filo squares, oiled side down, over each of the dishes to create a flower shape."],[null,"Carefully cover with a damp tea towel and set aside."],[null,"Lightly spray a little oil into a pan and add the yellow pepper. Cook for 3-4 minutes until softened, and add the spring onions. Cook for a further minute, stir in the spinach, pepper and chopped dill."],[null,"Divide the mixture between the pastry cases and add the salmon to each case and pour over the milk and egg mixture."],[null,"Top with the tomato halves and use a scrunched offcut of pastry to make a shape in the centre."],[null,"Cook for 15 minutes. Serve topped with a sprig of dill and a wedge of lemon on the side."]],"h":[[null,"Make sure you keep the filo pastry damp throughout. Cover it with a damp tea towel until you use it. Only make the filo cases just before you plan to fill them."],[null,"If you don’t have small oven proof dishes you could make one large tart."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6420755":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F. Spray a 9x13-inch casserole dish with cooking spray."],[null,"Place the asparagus, peas, and broccoli in a medium saucepan with about 1 inch of water. Cover and bring to a boil and cook for about 2 minutes, or until the vegetables are bright green and just slightly tender. Drain and place the vegetables in a bowl of ice water to cool quickly. Once cold, drain well, mix in the red bell pepper, and spread the vegetables out in the prepared casserole. Distribute the salmon pieces over the vegetables."],[null,"In a medium bowl, beat the egg whites and eggs on medium speed for about 1 minute. The mixture should be slightly bubbly. Add the cottage cheese, dill, black pepper, and lemon juice and beat on medium speed for another minute to break up the cheese and combine."],[null,"Pour the egg mixture over the vegetables and salmon. Top with mozzarella cheese."],[null,"Bake for 50-60 minutes, until the egg mixture is firm and no liquid remains. An inserted knife or toothpick should come out clean."],[null,"Cut into 6 pieces, garnish with fresh microgreens if desired, and serve with a slice of toast."]],"h":[]},"2831":{"s":[[null,"Chop shallot and dill weed. Cut squash into thin sticks 1/4″ x 2-1/2″."],[null,"In a salad dressing bottle, combine shallot, dill weed, vinegar, 2 tablespoons olive oil and 1/4 teaspoon pepper. Set aside."],[null,"Rub salmon fillet with oil and season with pepper. Spray a nonstick skillet with cooking spray and heat over medium heat. Add salmon fillet, skin side down, and cook for 3-5 minutes; turn and cook 3-5 minutes or until cooked through and opaque."],[null,"In a separate skillet heat 1 tablespoon olive oil over medium-high heat. Add crookneck squash, salt and 1/4 teaspoon pepper. Stir-fry for 3-4 minutes until squash is tender-crisp."],[null,"Remove skin from salmon filet and cut fillet into 4 portions. Arrange salmon and squash on a serving plate. Drizzle with vinaigrette and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Use any variety of summer squash."],[null,"Serve with steamed rice to complete the meal."],[null,"Salmon is a great source of omega-3 fatty acids."],[null,"Adjust the fish portion to match your meal plan if you are on a lower protein diet."]]},"6360759":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F. Line a sheet pan with aluminum foil and spray lightly with cooking spray."],[null,"Cook the wheat berries according to their package directions."],[null,"Brush each of the salmon fillets with half a teaspoon of pesto. Place on the prepared sheet pan and place in the oven. Cook until the salmon reaches 145 degrees F, about 15–20 minutes depending on the thickness of the salmon fillet."],[null,"When the wheat berries are cooked, drain them and toss them with 4 1/2 teaspoons of pesto."],[null,"Divide the spinach and arugula between 2 large plates or bowls. Toss in the wheat berries to coat the greens with pesto."],[null,"Place 1 salmon fillet on top of each plate of greens. Add half the green beans and tomatoes and sprinkle each bowl with pine nuts and microgreens."]],"h":[]},"3244":{"s":[[null,"Mix together Greek yogurt, vinegar, onion powder and Mrs. Dash seasoning. Add coleslaw mix and stir until yogurt has coated the coleslaw mix. Refrigerate until burgers are ready to eat."],[null,"Empty salmon pouches into a large bowl and break apart with a fork. Add egg, egg white, panko, dried dill and pepper. Mix well."],[null,"Heat a large skillet over medium heat; spray with cooking spray. Cook salmon burger for 4 to 5 minutes per side, until golden brown."],[null,"Serve the salmon burger on top of about 1 cup of coleslaw."]],"h":[[null,"Look for the lowest sodium salmon pouch."],[null,"Some panko bread crumbs are seasoned, which makes them higher in sodium. Plain panko bread crumbs have a lower sodium content."],[null,"Make the coleslaw overnight to allow the flavors to blend."],[null,"May also serve with 1-2 teaspoons of mustard."],[null,"The burger can be served on a bun, bread or flatbread. Sodium can vary widely so look for the lowest sodium bread products."]]},"7349349":{"s":[[null,"Boil the potatoes 10-15 minutes until tender, then mash."],[null,"Roughly mash together the salmon, potato, spring onion, anchovies, herbs and mayonnaise and season well"],[null,"Form into 4 patties and chill for about 30 minutes."],[null,"Dust each fishcake in flour, then dip in the egg and coat in breadcrumbs."],[null,"Place the fishcakes on an oiled baking sheet and drizzle with a little oil."],[null,"Cook under a medium grill for 2–3 minutes on each side. Serve with lemon wedges."]],"h":[[null,"Try using a mixture of fish such as salmon, crab and prawns."],[null,"You could use wholemeal bread to make a higher fibre, slightly denser fishcake."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Freeze in individually wrapped portions with greaseproof paper between each fishcake. Defrost in the fridge, or in the microwave and heat thoroughly until piping-hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"7364467":{"s":[[null,"Add the fish stock to a large pan."],[null,"Add the broccoli and the leeks. Simmer gently for 7–8 minutes, then stir the semi-skimmed milk and bring to a simmer."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the cornflour mixture to the pan, stirring until it starts to thicken."],[null,"Next, stir in the Dijon mustard, white pepper and Parmesan cheese. Add the salmon, cover and cook for 3–4 minutes, or until the fish is just cooked through."],[null,"Carefully stir in the cream cheese and chopped parsley. Finish the dish with a sprinkle of chopped parsley and serve."]],"h":[[null,"This recipe would work well with most types of fish."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6068003":{"s":[[null,"Heat a large skillet over medium heat. Spray with a little bit of cooking spray. Season salmon with salt and pepper. Place salmon skin-side down in the skillet and cook for about 3 minutes, until the skin is crispy. Flip the salmon over and cook for another 3 minutes, until it easily lifts from the skillet and the top is lightly browned. Remove from the pan and place on a plate."],[null,"Add the onions, garlic, and tomatoes to the pan and sauté for 3 minutes. Slowly pour in the vegetable broth and stir, scraping up any brown bits from the bottom of the pan."],[null,"Dissolve the cornstarch in the half-and-half and mix into the vegetable broth, cooking for a minute or two until the sauce begins to thicken. Stir in the greens and cook until wilted. Add the salmon back to the pan and simmer, covered until the salmon reaches an internal temperature of 145 degrees F."],[null,"Roll the zucchini noodles in a clean towel and squeeze lightly to get as much moisture out as possible. Heat olive oil in a large nonstick skillet. Add the zucchini noodles and sauté for 1–2 minutes, until hot."],[null,"Divide the noodles between 4 plates. Place 1 salmon fillet on each. Top with sauce and sprinkle with feta cheese."]],"h":[]},"7277182":{"s":[[null,"Put the oil in a large pan on medium heat. Add the onion and stir for 2–3 minutes until it softens."],[null,"Now add the yellow pepper and stir regularly for 3–4 minutes."],[null,"Add the garlic, oregano, seasoning, tomatoes and fennel. Stir for 2 more minutes and bring to a simmer."],[null,"Place the salmon on top of the ratatouille, add the water and cover with a lid or with foil. Simmer gently for 4–5 minutes or until the salmon is cooked through."],[null,"Remove the salmon, stir a few torn fresh basil leaves into the ratatouille and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Use sea bass or cod instead of salmon."],[null,"Add an aubergine to the ratatouille."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 6"]]},"7496258":{"s":[[null,"Remove the skin from the salmon but retain the bones. Add to a bowl, then mix in all the ingredients, except the cream cheese, and mix well."],[null,"Stir in the cream cheese, mix again and serve topped with a sprig of dill."],[null,"Serve with small squares of wholegrain toast."]],"h":[[null,"Ideal for spreading on toast, rolling into wraps or as a super sandwich."],[null,"Add a little Greek yoghurt to use as a dip."],[null,"Spice it up with 1 tsp smoked paprika or chilli seasoning."]]},"6682626":{"s":[[null,"To poach salmon—Fill a 4-quart saucepan with water and put salmon filet into the water. Place saucepan over high heat until water boils. Once water boils, remove pan from heat and let sit for 10 minutes. Remove fish from water and flake. Set aside."],[null,"In a 4-quart saucepan, heat 1 tablespoon of olive oil over medium-high heat. When oil is shimmering, add diced onion. Sauté onion until transparent. Add quinoa to onion mixture and stir—to toast—for 2 minutes."],[null,"Add 1 cup of vegetable stock to quinoa and onion. Stir until stock is absorbed. Once stock is absorbed, add another 1 cup of stock. Continue stirring until stock is absorbed. Add remaining stock in 1/2-cup intervals, stirring until all stock is absorbed. Remove from heat."],[null,"While preparing the onion quinoa mixture, heat 1/2 tablespoon of oil over medium-high heat in a sauté pan with chopped garlic. Once garlic is sizzling, add chopped kale to the pan. Turn kale to coat with oil and garlic. Turn kale mixture until fragrant, approximately 2 minutes. Remove kale mixture from heat."],[null,"Once quinoa is complete, add kale and salmon. Stir to combine and add salt and pepper to taste."]],"h":[]},"2314":{"s":[[null,"Finely chop celery."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix together salmon along with the other ingredients."],[null,"Make a sandwich or eat with low-sodium crackers."]],"h":[[null,"Look for boneless salmon to keep phosphorus and calcium lower. Compare sodium content on cans and foil pouches and choose the lower sodium container. Better yet, cook extra fresh salmon for dinner and save leftover for this recipe."],[null,"This recipe can be prepared ahead of time. Just cover and refrigerate until ready to serve."],[null,"Low-calorie mayonnaise can be substituted for regular mayonnaise, or reduce amount to 1-1/2 tablespoons (unless you need the extra calories)."],[null,"Additional bread options include cracked wheat, French, Italian, light rye, pita or sourdough, or choose a wrap."]]},"4170096":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F."],[null,"Cut the salmon into four or eight portions. Sprinkle with black pepper and refrigerate until ready to cook."],[null,"To make the onions, heat a skillet over medium heat. Add oil, vinegar and onions and sauté until the liquid is absorbed and the onions soften (approximately 10 minutes). Add the maple syrup and remove from heat."],[null,"To make the herb mayo, combine all ingredients and refrigerate until ready to use."],[null,"To cook the salmon, heat the oil in a skillet over medium-high heat. Place the salmon skin side up in the pan and sear. Once the salmon has a golden sear, flip the salmon skin side down in the pan. Transfer skillet to the preheated oven and cook for 10 minutes."],[null,"To assemble, spread the herb mayo on the top and bottom of the buns. Top with onions, arugula and salmon (skin removed)."]],"h":[]},"3912":{"s":[[null,"Cut one lemon into 6 wedges and set aside. Zest 1/2 teaspoon from peel of the other lemon. Juice lemon for 5 tablespoons. Slice onion and chop parsley and dill weed."],[null,"For dressing, in a small mixing bowl combine mayonnaise or salad dressing, buttermilk, 2 tablespoons dill weed, chives, lemon zest, and 1 tablespoon lemon juice. Cover and chill at least one hour."],[null,"In a 12″ skillet combine 1-1/2 cups water, remaining 4 tablespoons lemon juice, onion, peppercorns, parsley, bay leaves, and salt. Bring to a boil; add salmon steaks. Cover; simmer 8 to 12 minutes (12 to 18 minutes for frozen) or until fish just flakes easily when tested with a fork."],[null,"Serve salmon steaks topped with dressing. Garnish with remaining dill weed and lemon wedges."]],"h":[[null,"You will need 6 salmon steaks , cut 1 to 1-1/4″ thick (about 2 pounds)."],[null,"For a lower protein diet, reduce the serving size to 1/2 salmon fillet, about 1-3/4 to 2 ounces cooked."],[null,"Use fat-free mayonnaise to reduce fat to 8 grams per serving."]]},"6396740":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350 degrees F. Heat 1 Tbsp olive oil in skillet over medium heat. Add the spinach and stir to coat. Add the feta, salt, pepper, and mint. Stir to combine, remove from heat and set to the side."],[null,"Spray the bottom of an oven-safe baking dish with nonstick cooking spray."],[null,"Place the salmon fillets on a work surface and top each with 1/2 cup of the spinach mixture. Roll the fillets up and stand on one end. Place in baking dish and turn to coat with the cooking spray. Pour the stock into the bottom of the baking dish. Pour the lemon juice on the top of the fillets. Cover the rolls with foil. Bake for 20 minutes or until salmon is cooked through to 145 degrees F."]],"h":[]},"6814777":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425°F. In a small bowl combine the cumin, turmeric, allspice and coriander and set aside."],[null,"Combine the peas, the juice of 1 lemon, the vegetable stock, salt, and pepper in a blender. Puree until smooth."],[null,"Grease a baking dish with the olive oil. Place the salmon in the dish and turn to coat with the oil. Sprinkle each piece with the seasoning mix and the remaining juice of 1 lemon. Bake for 15 to 20 minutes, or until the salmon is cooked through."],[null,"Pour the puree on a serving platter. Place the salmon on top. Garnish with lemon wedges."]],"h":[]},"6070270":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 450 F."],[null,"In a small bowl, toss grapes with 1 tablespoon olive oil, garlic, thyme, 1/8 teaspoon salt, and 1/8 teaspoon pepper. Arrange the grapes in a rimmed baking dish and roast for 20 minutes, or until slightly brown and bursting."],[null,"While the grapes are roasting, arrange the salmon fillets on a rimmed baking sheet. Drizzle with remaining olive oil and season with remaining salt and pepper."],[null,"Once the grapes are roasted, remove from the oven. Decrease oven temperature to 400°F and roast the salmon for 10–12 minutes, or until salmon reached your desired doneness."],[null,"Remove salmon from the oven, top with the roasted grapes, and serve."]],"h":[]},"6244202":{"s":[[null,"In a bowl, toss the mixed salad greens with olive oil, lemon juice, and pepper."],[null,"Divide the dressed salad greens into 4 bowls."],[null,"Arrange smoked salmon slices, ​​avocado slices​, and chickpeas​ on top of the salad greens.​ ​"],[null,"Garnish with capers and fresh dill​.​​"]],"h":[]},"7414318":{"s":[[null,"Drain the salmon and remove the skin, but keep the bones as they are packed with calcium. Add to a bowl and mash roughly with a fork."],[null,"Add the onion, red pepper, cucumber, yogurt, lemon juice and black pepper to the salmon and mix well."],[null,"Warm the tortillas in a dry frying pan or griddle pan for 1-2 minutes. Place on a clean work surface, divide the salad and the salmon between the two tortillas, placing the mixture in the middle and leaving a 3-4cm gap around the edges."],[null,"Roll up, tucking in the edges, then cut in half at an angle to serve."]],"h":[[null,"For packed lunches or picnics, roll the packed tortilla tightly in greaseproof paper or foil, twisting the ends to secure. When eating just unwrap one end and peel the paper off as you eat it, tearing in a spiral as you munch your way down."],[null,"Try using tinned mackerel, sardines or tuna in place of salmon and spice it up with a little chilli powder, or add herbs such as fresh coriander or dill."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6398040":{"s":[[null,"Place the canola oil in a large pot. Heat and add the onion, garlic and celery. Cook over medium heat, covered, until the onion becomes translucent. Add the carrots and barley and cook uncovered until the barley begins to look toasted. Add broth. Cover and cook 30 minutes."],[null,"Cut the tomatoes in half and place them in a large bowl with balsamic vinegar, basil, salt, pepper and salmon. Let it rest while the barley cooks for the first 30 minutes. After 30 minutes, remove the salmon from the tomato mixture. Add the tomato mixture to the barley and place the salmon on top of the barley. Cover and cook 10 more minutes to steam the salmon."],[null,"Place some barley pilaf in a pasta bowl and top with a piece of salmon to serve."]],"h":[]},"3464":{"s":[[null,"Mix ingredients together."],[null,"Pour into a squeeze bottle for drizzling."],[null,"Refrigerate leftover salsa for up to 5 days."]],"h":[[null,"Use your favorite salt-free seasoning blend."]]},"1002887":{"s":[[null,"Remove seeds from jalapeño pepper."],[null,"Place ingredients in a blender or food processor and blend until smooth."],[null,"Store sauce in a covered container in the refrigerator for up to one week."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute parsley for cilantro if you prefer. Replace the jalapeño with the chile pepper of your choice."],[null,"Adjust cumin and oregano to taste."],[null,"Use Mojo Sauce as a marinade or sauce. Try it with Sylvia’s Cuban-Style Rice recipe."]]},"3763":{"s":[[null,"Soak tomatillos in a medium bowl of water for 5 minutes. Place a small plate over the tomatillos to keep them submerged under water. While tomatillos are soaking, line a rimmed baking sheet with aluminum foil and preheat the broiler with rack 4 inches below the heat source."],[null,"Remove husks and any stems from soaked tomatillos. Rinse off any sticky residue remaining on the skin. Dry tomatillos and cut in half."],[null,"Remove stem from jalapeno and cut into quarters. Cut onion into quarters."],[null,"Place tomatillos and jalapeno cut side down on prepared baking sheet. Place garlic clove, and quartered onion on baking sheet. Broil 5 to 7 minutes until slightly brown or small charred spots appear. Adjust time as needed and watch carefully as they can burn fast. Remove from oven."],[null,"Carefully transfer the broiled items and their juices into a food processor or blender. Add cilantro, lime juice, salt and black pepper."],[null,"Pulse mixture until it is smooth with no big chunks of tomatillo remaining. Be careful not to puree it. Salsa will be thin, however, it will thicken after being refrigerated for a few hours."]],"h":[[null,"Remove the jalapeno seeds and veins to produce a mild salsa or add another jalapeno to increase the spiciness."],[null,"Look for firm tomatillos. Soaking the tomatillos helps remove the sticky residue from the skin."],[null,"Salsa Verde can be stored in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to a week, or in the freezer for future use."],[null,"Serve warm or cold over eggs, tacos or your favorite Mexican dish."]]},"1002819":{"s":[[null,"Soak tomatillos in a medium bowl of water for 5 minutes. Place a small plate on top of the tomatillos to keep them submerged. While tomatillos soak, line a rimmed baking sheet with aluminum foil and preheat the broiler with a rack 4 inches below the heat source."],[null,"Remove husks and stems from soaked tomatillos. Rinse off any sticky residue left on the skin. Pat tomatillos dry and cut in half."],[null,"Remove stem from jalapeño and cut into quarters. Cut onion into quarters."],[null,"Place tomatillos and jalapeño cut-side down on the prepared baking sheet. Place garlic clove and onion quarters on the baking sheet. Broil for 5 to 7 minutes until small charred or lightly browned spots appear. Adjust the time as needed and watch carefully, since they can burn quickly. Remove from oven."],[null,"Carefully transfer the broiled vegetables and their juices to a food processor or blender. Add cilantro, lime juice, salt and black pepper."],[null,"Pulse until smooth with no large chunks of tomatillo. Be careful not to turn it into a purée. The salsa will be thin, but it will thicken after it has been refrigerated for a few hours."]],"h":[[null,"Remove the seeds and ribs from the jalapeño for a mild salsa, or add another jalapeño for more heat."],[null,"Look for firm tomatillos."],[null,"Salsa Verde can be stored in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to one week, or in the freezer for future use."],[null,"Soaking tomatillos helps remove the sticky residue from the skin."],[null,"Serve warm or cold over eggs, tacos or your favorite Mexican dish."]]},"1002982":{"s":[[null,"Wash and drain all vegetables that need it."],[null,"Combine all ingredients in a salad bowl. Blend all ingredients."],[null,"Add dressing to salad to taste."]],"h":[[null,"Herbs such as mint, marjoram or oregano can be used to vary the flavor."]]},"6092225":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 400 degrees F. Line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"In a bowl, toss the thawed edamame with olive oil until they are evenly coated."],[null,"Spread the edamame in a single layer on the prepared baking sheet. Sprinkle sea salt and black pepper evenly over the edamame. Toss to ensure the seasoning is well distributed."],[null,"Roast in the preheated oven for about 15 minutes or until the edamame is slightly crispy, stirring once or twice during the cooking time for even roasting. If you like a bit of heat, sprinkle red pepper flakes over the roasted edamame before serving."],[null,"Remove from the oven and let the edamame cool slightly before serving."]],"h":[]},"3328":{"s":[[null,"Mix all ingredients together."],[null,"Store in an airtight container."],[null,"Add to any savory dish that needs more heat and spice."]],"h":[[null,"Regular Cajun seasoning with salt contains over 1000 mg sodium per teaspoon."],[null,"Use Salt-free Cajun Seasoning for the DaVita.com Shrimp Brouillette recipe."]]},"6137953":{"s":[[null,"Combine all ingredients together. Store in an airtight container."]],"h":[]},"6612695":{"s":[],"h":[]},"9566547":{"s":[[null,"Add all 4 ingredients to your food processor and process until combined and you have an even consistency, without overprocessing. (Some texture is nice.)"],[null,"Scoop the batter and roll it into bite-sized balls, placing each one on a flat plate or baking sheet. You should get around 18 balls depending their size."],[null,"Optional: Roll some or all of the balls into dessicated coconut."]],"h":[[null,"If your dates are very dry , soak them in hot water for 10-15 minutes, and then drain them before adding them to your food processor. This will help soften them and make them easier to process."],[null,"Use raw macadamia nuts OR dry roasted, with or without salt. However, if the nuts are salted , halve the added salt."],[null,"Don't overprocess the mixture . These taste best with a little texture; process until combined without overdoing it."],[null,"These energy bites keep at room temperature for 2-3 days, in the fridge for up to 1 week or in the freezer for up to 3 months."]]},"2774":{"s":[[null,"Chop onion; finely chop ginger root and cilantro. Set green peas out to thaw."],[null,"Heat 3 tablespoons oil in a large skillet, over medium heat. Add onion, ginger root, coriander, pepper and Garam Masala."],[null,"Add the ground beef and cook until it is no longer pink. Drain fat."],[null,"Add green peas and cook until the mixture is dry. Add cilantro and stir."],[null,"Mix 1 tablespoon of flour with enough water to make a thin paste."],[null,"Roll out pastry on a floured board. Put 2 tablespoons of the beef mixture in the center of the pastry and fold over. Seal edges with a paste of flour and water."],[null,"Heat oil for deep frying and fry pastries until golden brown."]],"h":[[null,"Egg roll wrappers or filo dough can be used instead of spring roll pastry if desired."],[null,"For a lower fat version you can bake the Samosa on a greased baking sheet instead of frying."],[null,"Instead of beef try ground turkey for variety."]]},"1002750":{"s":[[null,"Chop beef and onions and fry with the tablespoon of oil and thyme until browned."],[null,"Remove from heat and add curry powder and pepper."],[null,"Take a sheet of pastry and form a triangular cone by folding the edges around itself, sealing with beaten egg and leaving one side open for filling."],[null,"Fill with beef mixture and seal."],[null,"Heat oil and fry samosas until golden brown."],[null,"To make the cilantro sauce, finely chop cilantro and walnuts. Mix with chili powder, garlic powder and lemon juice in a small bowl."],[null,"Serve hot with cilantro sauce."]],"h":[[null,"Samosas are triangle-shaped turnovers, a traditional food of India."]]},"3555":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400º F."],[null,"Trim crust and cut bread in half diagonally."],[null,"Beat egg slightly and add to almond milk."],[null,"Pour oil into a skillet and heat."],[null,"Dip bread into egg mixture. Fry in oil until brown on both sides."],[null,"Place browned toast pieces on a hot, baking sheet. Cook for 4 minutes in the oven to puff the toast."],[null,"Remove from oven and drain on paper towel if needed. Serve immediately with powdered sugar, syrup or jelly."]],"h":[[null,"Try one of these toppings with Santa Fe French Toast:"]]},"2627":{"s":[[null,"Place all ingredients into a jar with a tight lid and shake."],[null,"Ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Leftover dressing keeps well in the refrigerator for about 2 weeks."],[null,"Use dressing as a marinade for meat or vegetables."]]},"2123":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375° F."],[null,"To make sausage, mix together ground beef, sage, black pepper, basil and garlic powder, and set aside"],[null,"Cut bread into 1″ cubes and toss on a baking sheet with olive oil and Mrs. Dash seasoning. Bake until golden brown, about 8 minutes. Set aside."],[null,"Crumble sausage into a large saucepan and fry until done. Remove from pan and drain on paper towels"],[null,"Keep 2 tablespoons of drippings in the pan. Mince garlic and sauté 1 to 2 minutes. Add the broth, water and chopped parsley. Cover and bring to a boil, then reduce heat and simmer for 10 minutes."],[null,"Adjust heat so broth is barely boiling. One at a time, crack each egg into a small bowl and gently slip into the broth. Poach until just set, about 3 minutes."],[null,"Divide sausage into four individual soup bowls. Transfer the eggs with a slotted spoon onto the sausage. Ladle 1 cup of broth into each bowl."],[null,"Top each bowl with one-quarter of the homemade croutons and 1/2 tablespoon of parmesan cheese."]],"h":[[null,"Be careful not to poach the eggs too long or they will be hard."],[null,"Enjoy Sausage Egg Soup for breakfast, lunch or dinner."]]},"6468501":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400°F. Remove stems from mushrooms and finely chop stems. Mix 2 Tbsp. breadcrumbs and Parmesan in small bowl."],[null,"Lightly coat large nonstick skillet with nonstick cooking spray and set over medium heat. Cook sausages until they begin to brown, about 5 minutes, breaking up with side of spoon. Stir in onion, red pepper, mushroom stems and parsley and cook until vegetables are soft, about 5 minutes. Stir in remaining bread crumbs and black pepper. Remove from heat. Add 1 Tsp. of water at a time until you have s tuffing that is moist enough to mound."],[null,"Mound stuffing in mushrooms and arrange, stuffing-side up, in 13 x 9-inch baking dish. Sprinkly with Parmesan mixture. Bake until heated through, about 9 minutes."]],"h":[]},"6122165":{"s":[[null,"Add oil to a large soup pot or Dutch oven and heat over medium-high. Add onion and green pepper and sauté over medium-high heat for 5 minutes. Add garlic and sauté for 30 seconds."],[null,"Remove onion and pepper mixture from pot and set aside. Spray pot with cooking spray. Add sausage and sauté for 3-5 minutes until brown."],[null,"Add onion and peppers back to pot. Add tomatoes, kidney beans, chicken broth, black pepper, cayenne pepper if desired and thyme. Bring to a boil. Add quinoa, reduce heat to low and cover. Simmer for 15 minutes."],[null,"Remove lid and add water. Simmer for 5 more minutes."]],"h":[]},"55012":{"s":[[null,"In a small skillet sprayed with nonstick cooking spray, pour egg and cook and scramble over medium low heat. When egg appears almost cooked through, turn over with a spatula and cook an additional 30 seconds."],[null,"Toast bagel thins."],[null,"Place turkey sausage patty on a plate, cover with a paper towel and cook in the microwave for 1 minute or the time recommended on package."],[null,"Assemble cooked egg on bagel thin (fold to fit bagel thins). Top with sausage patty, then sharp cheddar cheese and remaining bagel thin half."]],"h":[[null,"Sandwiches can be prepared ahead of time and reheated in the morning. They can last in the refrigerator for up to 3-4 days."],[null,"This recipe is lower in sodium than similar fast foods sandwiches. They can range from ~900-1490 mg of sodium."]]},"6761249":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in an extra-large skillet over medium heat. Add the garlic and sauté until it begins to lightly brown, about 2 minutes. Transfer the garlic to a small dish and set aside."],[null,"Add the spinach to the skillet, one large handful at a time. Cook and toss with tongs until all of the spinach is just wilted, about 4 minutes. Add the lemon juice and currants, and toss to combine, about 30 seconds. Remove from the heat and sprinkle with the salt and, if using, pepper."],[null,"Using tongs, transfer the spinach to a serving bowl or platter. Top with the reserved garlic slices and the pine nuts, and serve with the lemon wedges."]],"h":[]},"4471551":{"s":[[null,"Thinly slice meat and toss in flour."],[null,"Slice shallots thin and set aside."],[null,"If you do not have pre-sliced mushrooms, slice to medium thickness."],[null,"In medium- or large-sized non-stick pan, heat 2 tablespoonsof oil on medium-high heat."],[null,"Loosely but carefully drop sliced meat into pan of heated oil and brown meat lightly, about 5-8 minutes."],[null,"Remove meat from pan and set aside."],[null,"Add remaining 2 tablespoons of oil and sauté mushrooms and shallots for 3-5 minutes until translucent and lightly browned."],[null,"Return meat to pan, sauté meat with mushroom and shallot mixture."],[null,"Add garlic and onion powder, and stir together for 2-3 minutes."],[null,"Add ¼ cup of water and stir."],[null,"Turn off heat and add pepper and sour cream."],[null,"Stir gently."],[null,"Pile noodles on a serving platter and top with beef mixture."],[null,"Top with scallions or chives, and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Nutrient values are the sum of the separate analyses given for each component."]]},"6550239":{"s":[[null,"Add enough water to fill a large skillet 2/3 full. Over medium heat, bring the water to simmering. Add the fish and simmer for 5 to 7 minutes, or until the fish is cooked through. Remove the fish chunks with a slotted spoon. Add the fish to a mixing bowl and let cool for 5 minutes."],[null,"Drain any excess liquid from the bowl. Add the yogurt, mustard, lemon juice, salt, lemon zest, and egg and mix well. Add ½ cup of the bread crumbs plus the scallions and hot sauce and mix well. Shape the fish mixture into 6 cakes. Coat each side of the cakes lightly with the remaining bread crumbs. Add the cakes to a plate and refrigerate, covered, for 30 minutes."],[null,"Remove the cakes from the refrigerator and let stand 5 minutes. In a large skillet, heat the oil over medium heat. Add the cakes to the skillet and sauté for about 5 minutes on each side, until golden brown."]],"h":[]},"6368221":{"s":[[null,"Heat olive oil in a large sauté pan or wok over medium-high heat. Add asparagus, onion, mushrooms and red pepper and cook for 15-18 minutes, stirring frequently."],[null,"Add garlic to pan and cook for 1 minute. Stir vegetables and garlic to incorporate."]],"h":[]},"6004272":{"s":[[null,"In a large skillet, heat the olive oil over medium heat."],[null,"Add the thinly sliced cabbage to the skillet, tossing to coat in the oil."],[null,"Sauté the cabbage for 10–12 minutes or until it is tender but still has a bit of crunch."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the apple cider vinegar, Dijon mustard, maple syrup, and caraway seeds."],[null,"Pour the cider vinegar dressing over the sautéed cabbage. Toss to coat evenly."],[null,"Season with the salt and black pepper."],[null,"Continue sautéing for an additional 2–3 minutes to allow the flavors to meld."]],"h":[]},"6980737":{"s":[[null,"Add the olive oil to a large skillet and heat on medium-high."],[null,"Sauté the shredded cabbage until tender but still crisp, about 3–5 minutes."],[null,"Zest and juice the lemon."],[null,"In a small saucepan, melt the butter and stir in the water, lemon zest, lemon juice, and poppy seeds."],[null,"Pour the lemon butter over the sautéed cabbage and season with salt and pepper. Serve warm."]],"h":[]},"2515":{"s":[[null,"Make mustard sauce by combining vinegar, mustard, olive oil, apple cider and caraway seeds."],[null,"Chop cabbage into bite-size chunks."],[null,"Spray nonstick skillet with cooking spray and heat over medium heat. Add cabbage and sauté 8 to 10 minutes, stirring several times."],[null,"Pour mustard sauce over cabbage and stir. Reduce to low heat, cover pan and simmer for 5 minutes to combine flavors."]],"h":[[null,"Serve as a side vegetable dish or use as a topping on a hot beef sandwich."],[null,"Do not substitute Chinese (napa) cabbage—potassium content is much higher."]]},"6286531":{"s":[[null,"Bring water to a boil in a medium saucepan. Add cubed potato and cook for 7 minutes. Drain."],[null,"In a large skillet, heat olive oil over medium-high heat."],[null,"Add the sliced chicken sausage to the skillet and sauté until browned on all sides, approximately 5-7 minutes."],[null,"Remove the sausage from the skillet and set aside. Add the sliced onions and peppers to the skillet. Sauté until softened, about 10 minutes."],[null,"Season the mixture with minced garlic, dried oregano, dried basil, fresh thyme, coarse salt, and pepper. Stir well to combine."],[null,"Add the potatoes and sausage back to the skillet and sauté 2-3 minutes more. Serve warm."]],"h":[]},"6673934":{"s":[[null,"Heat margarine in a sauté pan over medium-high heat. Add apples and sauté for 3 minutes, stirring frequently."],[null,"Add remaining ingredients. Reduce heat to low and simmer for 12 minutes, stirring occasionally."]],"h":[]},"6103875":{"s":[[null,"Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium heat. Add the garlic and mushrooms and sauté until mushrooms are browned, about 8 minutes."],[null,"Season with the salt and pepper."],[null,"Add kale and cook until darkened and tender, about 5 minutes."]],"h":[]},"6434931":{"s":[[null,"Heat a large pot over medium-high heat. Add the turkey bacon and cook for 4-5 minutes until done."],[null,"Add the kale and chicken broth to the pan; mix well. Cover and cook for 5 minutes."],[null,"Remove the lid from the pot and stir in the black pepper and red wine vinegar."]],"h":[]},"6001200":{"s":[[null,"In a large skillet, heat the olive oil over medium heat."],[null,"Add the garlic to the skillet and sauté for 1–2 minutes until fragrant."],[null,"Add the fresh spinach to the skillet in batches, allowing each batch to wilt before adding more."],[null,"Toss the spinach gently to coat it with the olive oil and garlic."],[null,"Continue sautéing for 2–3 minutes or until the spinach is wilted and tender."],[null,"Season with salt and black pepper to taste. Toss to combine."],[null,"Serve with lemon wedges on the side if desired."]],"h":[]},"6562343":{"s":[[null,"Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat."],[null,"Add the sliced mushrooms to the skillet and cook for about 6–8 minutes, stirring occasionally, until the mushrooms release their moisture and become golden brown."],[null,"Add the minced garlic and fresh thyme leaves to the skillet. Sauté for another 1–2 minutes until the garlic is fragrant."],[null,"Season the mushrooms with salt (optional) and black pepper, adjusting the amount to taste. If desired, drizzle the mushrooms with lemon juice for a tangy flavor."],[null,"Continue cooking the mushrooms for an additional minute, stirring to evenly distribute the flavors."],[null,"Remove from heat and transfer the sautéed thyme mushrooms to a serving dish."]],"h":[]},"6110430":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F. Use either 6 ramekins that are 4 oz. each or a muffin tin. Coat the ramekins or muffin tin with cooking spray and set aside."],[null,"Add the olive oil to a medium non-stick sauté pan. Heat over medium heat and sauté the asparagus and sundried tomatoes for 8–10 minutes or until the asparagus begins to soften. If the asparagus is thick, add a few tablespoons of water to the sauté pan and cover for 5 minutes to steam, then continue sautéing until all the liquid is absorbed. Set aside to cool."],[null,"In a medium bowl, whisk together the basil, egg substitute, milk, flour, salt, and pepper until smooth with no lumps."],[null,"Divide the asparagus mixture evenly between the ramekins or muffin tins. Cups should be full."],[null,"Carefully pour the egg mixture over the asparagus just to the top—do not overfill."],[null,"Bake for 30 minutes or until the custards are puffed and just starting to brown."],[null,"Remove from the oven and cool slightly. Turn the custards out of the ramekins or muffin tins and serve."]],"h":[]},"6387433":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F. Line a muffin tin with paper liners."],[null,"Place the cauliflower florets in a food processor and pulse until you get a fine texture similar to rice."],[null,"In a medium bowl, mix together the cauliflower and remaining ingredients."],[null,"Scoop about 1/4 cup cauliflower mixture into each muffin cup. Bake for 30-35 minutes until the cakes are lightly golden on top."]],"h":[]},"6756951":{"s":[[null,"In a non-stick skillet, cook egg substitute over medium heat, stirring to scramble. Mix in the paprika and garlic powder."],[null,"Spray a medium skillet with cooking spray and heat over medium heat. Add the sausage links and cook until browned. Remove from the pan and add the onions and mushrooms. Cook until they are browned, about 5 minutes. Add the spinach and cook just until wilted. Remove from heat."],[null,"Divide the eggs between two bowls. Slice the sausage and place one link in each bowl. Add half of the rest to each bowl: the cottage cheese, the spinach and mushroom mix, the cherry tomatoes, and avocado. Sprinkle with chives. Drizzle with lime juice if desired."]],"h":[]},"3046":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400° F."],[null,"Chop onion and mince garlic."],[null,"Cook green beans in microwave according to package directions."],[null,"In a medium skillet, heat oil and sauté onion with garlic, until onion is translucent."],[null,"Add dill weed, lemon juice and Worcestershire sauce and stir to mix."],[null,"Add green beans and toss. Place in a casserole dish."],[null,"Melt butter and mix with bread crumbs. Sprinkle over green bean mixture and bake for 5 to 10 minutes to brown."]],"h":[]},"3302":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350˚ F. Chop the onion and pecans."],[null,"In a skillet over medium heat sauté the onion, nuts and seasoning blend in olive oil. Add remaining ingredients, mixing well."],[null,"Divide the mixture into 12 muffin cups (approximately 1/3 cup each) and bake for 30 to 40 minutes until an inserted toothpick comes out clean. Rest for 5 minutes; remove from muffin tin to cool."],[null,"Eat warm or chilled."]],"h":[[null,"Place entire recipe into a greased casserole dish and bake for 45 to 60 minutes. Serve plain or with low-sodium gravy as a meatless meatloaf."],[null,"Add green or red pepper, jalapenos or other vegetables of choice, if desired."],[null,"Try as a high protein dessert muffin with cinnamon and sugar or maple syrup and even chopped apples instead of onion and seasoning mix."],[null,"Substitute the Greek yogurt for cottage cheese or tofu. Cottage cheese is higher in sodium. Check the label for the brand lowest in sodium."],[null,"Bake, covered with foil if you prefer a softer texture, or bake longer until rich golden or dark crust if you like a little crunch."]]},"6548283":{"s":[[null,"Add 1 cup nonfat Greek yogurt to a small bowl."],[null,"Stir in 1/2 cup shelled edamame until evenly distributed."],[null,"Crumble the pack of roasted seaweed over the top or fold it in for a softer texture."],[null,"Serve immediately so the seaweed stays crisp."]],"h":[]},"6402897":{"s":[[null,"Preheat a cast-iron skillet over medium-high heat. In a small bowl, combine all of the spices. Sprinkle and rub the mixture over both sides of the steak."],[null,"Toss apples with ground cinnamon."],[null,"When the skillet is hot, cook the steak for 3 to 5 minutes per side, or longer if desired. Slice the steak into thin strips and serve with the cinnamon apples."]],"h":[]},"6976675":{"s":[[null,"Slice the 3-inch-long piece of cucumber into quarters lengthwise. Then slice the four (3-inch-long) pieces into thin slices crosswise."],[null,"Scatter half the cucumber pieces onto a plate or shallow bowl. Dollop the yogurt onto the cucumbers. Spread it with the back of a spoon. Attractively arrange the remaining cucumber on the yogurt."],[null,"Drizzle with the oil. Sprinkle with the salt and mint leaves. Serve."]],"h":[]},"6453245":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375°F (190°C) and line a muffin tin with 8 paper liners or lightly grease the cups with cooking spray."],[null,"Shred the zucchini and carrot, then squeeze out excess moisture using a clean towel. Dice the red bell pepper and red onion and combine all the vegetables in a bowl."],[null,"In a medium bowl, whisk together the eggs, egg whites, and low-fat milk until well combined."],[null,"In another bowl, mix the whole wheat flour, baking powder, black pepper, and smoked paprika."],[null,"Gradually fold the dry ingredients into the wet ingredients, stirring gently until just combined. Add the shredded vegetables and cheddar cheese to the batter, folding until evenly distributed."],[null,"Divide the batter evenly among the 8 prepared muffin cups. Fill each about 3/4 full."],[null,"Bake for 18–22 minutes, or until a toothpick inserted into the center of a muffin comes out clean."],[null,"Allow the muffins to cool in the tin for 5 minutes, then transfer to a wire rack. Serve warm or at room temperature."]],"h":[]},"2319":{"s":[[null,"Thinly slice celery, green onion and mushrooms."],[null,"Pour rice into saucepan. Add chicken broth and heat over medium-high heat until boiling."],[null,"Add celery, green onion, mushrooms to boiling broth. Lightly press vegetables into broth. Reduce heat to low and cover."],[null,"Cook for 20 minutes or until broth has evaporated and rice is tender."],[null,"Add margarine and pepper. Mix until rice is coated."]],"h":[[null,"Refrigerate leftover rice and reheat for a quick side dish the next day."],[null,"Add cooked diced chicken, tofu or shrimp to change this dish from a side to an entree."]]},"7478749":{"s":[[null,"Heat a large deep pan with a lid and place in the popping corn and cover. Shake the pan regularly and after 2-3 minutes you’ll hear the corn start to pop – don’t be tempted to open the lid. Keep shaking until the popping stops."],[null,"Put the popped-corn into a large bowl and discard any corn that hasn’t popped. Repeat until all your corn is done, then divide into two."],[null,"Meanwhile, make your flavourings. To make the cheesy garlic popcorn, add the oil to a pan with the garlic, oregano and pepper. Cook gently for 1 minute without browning the garlic. Add half the popped corn and the finely grated Parmesan. Mix well and serve."],[null,"To make the chilli lemon popcorn, add 1 tsp rapeseed oil to a pan with the red chilli. Cook gently for 1 minute."],[null,"Add the lemon juice and zest and heat a further minute until the lemon juice has halved in volume. Add the remaining half of popped corn, mix well and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Don't put too much corn in at once – cook in batches as it expands a lot."],[null,"There's no end to the range of flavours you can make – try different spices such as cumin or smoked paprika. Just make sure you don't make the mix too wet or you'll get soggy popcorn."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"7299915":{"s":[[null,"Remove any really thick stems, then finely shred the cabbage using a mandolin or food processor."],[null,"Finely shred the leek and grate the carrots."],[null,"Add the olive oil, lemon juice, mustard and pepper. Mix well and refrigerate for at least and hour before serving."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"3770":{"s":[[null,"Finely chop the scallions and set aside."],[null,"Thoroughly mix flour and cornstarch in a bowl. Using a fork, mix in the boiling water. Add the cold water and mix with your hands until all the flour is incorporated."],[null,"Cover the dough and let it rest for 20 minutes."],[null,"Coat hands with flour to prevent dough from sticking and shape the dough into a long rope. Cut into 8 pieces."],[null,"On a floured surface, roll one piece of dough as thin as possible. Brush with sesame oil and sprinkle with 2 tablespoons of the scallions."],[null,"Roll up jellyroll style. Coil the roll like a cinnamon bun. Roll out the bun until 1/4-in thick."],[null,"Repeat with the other pieces of dough."],[null,"Heat the canola oil on medium-high heat in a nonstick pan (or use cooking spray). Fry each pancake, about 1 to 2 minutes per side, until the dough puffs up a little and becomes crispy. Serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"One scallion yields approximately 2 tablespoons when trimmed and chopped."],[null,"Top with siracha chili sauce or dip in a low-sodium sweet chili sauce."]]},"6495824":{"s":[[null,"Add the wooden skewers to a pan of hot water. Set aside for 1–2 hours."],[null,"Cover a broiler pan with aluminum foil. Coat the foil with cooking spray. Preheat the oven broiler to high with the rack set about 5 inches from the heat source."],[null,"Combine the breadcrumbs, Parmesan cheese, garlic, and Italian seasoning together on a plate. Roll each scallop in the breadcrumb mixture."],[null,"Remove the wooden skewers from the hot water. Using two skewers per kebab, thread the scallops onto the skewers so the scallops are lying flat through the skewer."],[null,"Place the skewers on the prepared broiler pan. Coat each skewer with olive oil cooking spray. Broil the scallops for about 4 minutes per side until cooked through."]],"h":[]},"6561298":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400 degrees F. Peel potatoes and slice into thin rounds."],[null,"Coat a large nonstick skillet with cooking spray and sauté onions over medium-high heat until the onions turn clear."],[null,"Spray a pie pan or 8-inch round cake pan with cooking spray."],[null,"Place a thick layer (about half) of the potatoes and onions in the bottom of pan."],[null,"Add salt and pepper to half-and-half. Pour 1/2 cup of the half-and-half over the potatoes. Sprinkle 1/4 cup of the cheese on top."],[null,"Add remaining potatoes and pour 1/2 cup half-and-half over the potatoes and top with remaining cheese."],[null,"Bake for 40 minutes or until potatoes are soft."]],"h":[]},"7624456":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, beat together the butter, oil, chilli and rind and juice of the lime. Season well."],[null,"Heat a non-stick frying pan, add the butter mixture and heat until bubbling. Add the scallops and fry for about 1 minute on each side."],[null,"Remove from the pan, serve with a little rocket and drizzle with the pan juices."]],"h":[[null,"You could also add 2cm finely chopped fresh ginger and 2 cloves crushed garlic to the butter."],[null,"This recipe also works with prawns or cubes of fresh salmon."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"7239635":{"s":[[null,"Mix the cucumber, red onion and lemon juice together and set aside."],[null,"Mix the horseradish, mayonnaise and yoghurt in a small bowl or cup."],[null,"Spread each slice of rye bread with 1 tsp of the horseradish dressing."],[null,"Scatter the salad leaves over the bread, then scatter half the cucumber and onion over the salad and drizzle the rest of the sauce on top."],[null,"Now garnish with a little smoked salmon and scatter with the remaining onion and cucumber."],[null,"Add a few small capers, a good grind of fresh black pepper and lemon wedges to serve."]],"h":[[null,"There are a lot of different types of rye bread available, but always look for wholegrain."],[null,"If you find the flavour a little strong, try a loaf made with sunflower or pumpkin seeds, instead."],[null,"'At risk' groups such as infants, children, pregnant women, the elderly and those who are unwell should avoid eating ready-to-eat, cold-smoked or cured fish. Therefore, this recipe is not suitable if this applies to you."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"7995017":{"s":[[null,"Add the onion to the pan with 1 teaspoon of oil. Cook gently until the onion starts to brown."],[null,"Now add the squash, stock, lentils, tomatoes and puree, and simmer for 15-20 minutes."],[null,"Add a good pinch of pepper, then whizz with a stick blender or in a food processor until smooth."],[null,"Meanwhile, cut the bread into the shape of a tombstone, put the stencil into position, and spray onto the toasted bread."],[null,"Put the soup into bowls. Add the yoghurt to a piping bag with a really small nozzle, and pipe a thin spiral onto the soup. Take a skewer or chopstick and draw through the spiral from the centre outwards to create a spider’s web. Add the toast and serve."]],"h":[[null,"You could use an oat or soya-based, non-dairy alternative to yogurt for a lactose-free version."],[null,"The serving suggestion above includes wholemeal bread, but does not include the yogurt. For a lower-carb option, serve without bread."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"6001166":{"s":[[null,"Crack 3 eggs and separate the whites into a small bowl."],[null,"Whisk the egg whites until they look a little foamy."],[null,"Heat a nonstick pan over medium heat and lightly coat it with cooking spray."],[null,"Pour the egg whites into the pan."],[null,"Let them cook for a few seconds, then gently stir with a spatula."],[null,"Continue cooking and stirring until the egg whites are firm and no liquid remains."],[null,"Remove from heat and serve warm."]],"h":[]},"6887150":{"s":[[null,"Sprinkle the fillets with salt and pepper. In a large nonstick skillet, heat the olive oil over medium-high heat. Add the fillets and sear each side for about 4 minutes, or until cooked through. Remove the fish from the skillet and place on a plate. Cover loosely to keep warm."],[null,"Add the onion and red pepper to the skillet and sauté for 5 minutes, until softened. Add the garlic and sauté for 1 minute. Add the undrained tomatoes, tomato paste, and red pepper flakes and bring to boiling. Lower the heat to simmer and cook for 5 to 8 minutes, until the sauce is thickened. Add the olives and capers and cook for 1 minute."],[null,"Serve the sea bass with the sauce, finishing with a sprinkle of basil."]],"h":[]},"7212462":{"s":[[null,"Add the carrots to a pan, cover with boiling water, then add a lid and bring to the boil. Turn down the heat and simmer for 12-15 minutes, until the carrots are tender."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the spring onions and a quarter of the dill to a large frying pan, placing the fish fillets on top. Pour in the stock and bring to a gentle boil. Cver the pan - with foil if you don’t have a big enough lid - then simmer gently for 5-6 minutes, checking the fish is cooked through."],[null,"Carefully remove the fish from the pan, place on a warm plate, and cover."],[null,"Add the samphire to the spring onions and stock, then cook for 2 minutes to blanch the samphire. Pour off the stock and add to another saucepan over a medium heat. Put the samphire and spring onions to one side."],[null,"Drain the carrots and discard the water, then add the carrots, samphire and spring onions to serving bowls or plates. Finally, place the fish on top."],[null,"Stir the cornflour into the boiling stock, stirring until thickened, then add the rest of the dill and the yogurt. Mix well, then pour over the fish. Sprinkle with pepper and serve with a wedge of lemon and a sprig of dill."]],"h":[[null,"Use any carrots if you prefer, simply trim and cut into batons."],[null,"Also works well with salmon, haddock, cod or tilapia."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"3426":{"s":[[null,"Chop onion, celery and peppers."],[null,"In a saucepan melt butter over medium heat. Cook onion, celery, green and red peppers for 5 minutes until soft."],[null,"Add flour and cook and stir constantly for 2 minutes."],[null,"Gradually add chicken broth, stirring to blend. Bring to a boil."],[null,"Add nondairy creamer, evaporated milk, surimi, corn, black pepper and paprika."],[null,"Heat, stirring occasionally, for 5 minutes or until chowder is hot. Serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"Freeze extra chowder for a quick meal later."]]},"3197":{"s":[[null,"Remove cream cheese from the refrigerator to soften. Do not soften in the microwave."],[null,"Thaw shrimp per package directions. Remove the shells and any visible veins on the shrimp and cut into small pieces."],[null,"Chop the imitation crabmeat into small pieces."],[null,"Stir the shrimp and crabmeat together and place in the refrigerator."],[null,"In a small bowl combine ketchup, horseradish, lemon juice and Worcestershire sauce to make a low-sodium cocktail sauce."],[null,"In a medium bowl, stir the softened cream cheese until it becomes creamy."],[null,"Slowly add cocktail sauce to the cream cheese. Stir thoroughly."],[null,"Add a small amount of Tabasco® sauce to the cream cheese. Stir thoroughly. Sample the cream cheese mix. Add more Tabasco® sauce as needed."],[null,"Add shrimp and crabmeat to the cream cheese. Stir thoroughly. Sample the cream cheese mix. Add more Tabasco® sauce as needed."],[null,"Cover and chill in refrigerator overnight."],[null,"Serve with low-sodium crackers."]],"h":[[null,"Expecting a crowd? Make a large batch by doubling the ingredients."],[null,"This recipe can be made the same day, but does taste best if prepared the night before."],[null,"Low-salt Ritz® crackers pair excellently with the dip."],[null,"Low-fat cream cheese may be substituted but sodium and phosphorus is higher."],[null,"Definitely do not use fat-free cream cheese, as this will compromise the taste."],[null,"Some low-sodium ketchup brands contain potassium chloride instead of salt. Avoid these brands because the potassium is much higher."]]},"7833036":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 5. Blanch the broccoli for 3–4 minutes in boiling water and drain."],[null,"Divide the fish, seafood and vegetables equally between 2 large squares of foil measuring 25cm x 25cm."],[null,"Sprinkle with the parsley and a good grind of pepper. Squeeze lemon over each, and then add the water and olive oil."],[null,"Fold the foil into the centre to make a parcel, then place on a baking sheet and bake for 15 minutes."],[null,"Serve each parcel with a lemon wedge."]],"h":[[null,"This dish works with any white fish. Alternatively, you could just add salmon, or omit prawns."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"7247191":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a pan and cook the onion for 5 minutes."],[null,"In a separate pan, heat the stock, simmering gently and leave on a very low heat."],[null,"Add the yellow pepper, garlic, white pepper and half the parsley to the onion, stir for 1 minute and add the rice. Stir for 2 minutes, then add two ladles of stock, enough to just cover the rice, and stir."],[null,"Stirring the rice regularly, add the hot stock a little at a time, so the rice is just covered. The risotto should be very gently bubbling."],[null,"After 20 minutes, add any remaining stock and the salmon. Stir for another 3 minutes, add the prawns and squid, cook for 2 minutes then test the rice to make sure its cooked ‘al dente’ (slightly firm) and ensuring the salmon is thoroughly cooked through."],[null,"Finally, vigorously stir in the remaining parsley and the yogurt, cover and allow to stand 2 minutes. Sprinkle with black pepper and parsley before serving."]],"h":[[null,"You can use frozen, defrosted prawns and squid."],[null,"Keep stock simmering in a separate saucepan, so it’s hot when you add to the rice and doesn’t reduce the temperature and stop the rice cooking. Add a little at a time; if you run out just add a little boiling water."],[null,"Stirring regularly, with a wooden spoon, means rice releases its starch and ensures a creamy texture."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6425972":{"s":[[null,"Slice tempeh crosswise into thin strips and place in a medium bowl. Add bell peppers and barbecue sauce to the bowl with the tempeh and gently stir to coat."],[null,"Preheat a large skillet over medium-high heat."],[null,"Once the skillet is hot, add oil and swirl to coat the bottom. Add tempeh and bell peppers in a single layer and cook, flipping once, until tempeh is browned and warmed through, 4–5 minutes. Remove from heat."],[null,"To assemble the salads, divide romaine, cucumber, and tomatoes between plates or bowls. Top with barbecue tempeh and peppers, and drizzle with dressing."]],"h":[]},"6146081":{"s":[[null,"Remove tab from each scallop, if needed.The “tab” is a side muscle, which may or may not still be attached to the scallop. It feels and looks like a little tab and is tougher than the scallop itself. If the tab is still attached, gently pull to remove it."],[null,"Pat scallops dry with a paper towel. Season on both sides pepper."],[null,"Add 1 1/2 Tsp. olive oil to a nonstick sauté pan over high heat."],[null,"Sear scallops on both sides until just barely cooked through, about two minutes on each side. Remove from pan and set aside."],[null,"Add remaining olive oil to the pan and reduce heat to medium. Add onion and sauté until caramelized, about five minutes."],[null,"Add garlic and carrots and sauté three minutes. Add the vinegar and cook until all of the liquid is reduced."],[null,"Add the scallops and any accumulated juices to the vegetables and sauté three minutes to finish cooking the scallops through."],[null,"Stir in the chives. Serve 1 cup of the scallop mixture over 1/3 cup of the whole wheat pasta."]],"h":[]},"6999413":{"s":[[null,"Heat the olive oil in a skillet over medium-high heat."],[null,"Lay the tuna fillets in the hot oil and sear for 3-4 minutes on one side. Flip the tuna and apply 1 Tbsp. pesto sauce to each filet. Cook for additional 3-4 minutes."]],"h":[]},"6012687":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425° F. Cut a sheet of parchment paper or aluminum foil into 4 (12-inch) square pieces."],[null,"Top the right half of each square with, in order: 1 cup vegetables, 1½ tsp oil, a dash (about 1/ 16 tsp) of salt, 1 fish fillet, 1 Tbsp shallot, 1 tsp lemon juice, ¼ tsp herbs, and a dash of salt."],[null,"Fold the left side of each square over the ingredients. Seal the edges well. Place on a baking sheet. Bake for 18 minutes, until the vegetables are tender and the fish is flaky, with an internal temperature of at least 145° F."],[null,"Let the fish stand for about 5 minutes, then carefully open the pouches and serve, in or out of the pouch."]],"h":[]},"6792667":{"s":[[null,"Arrange the tomatoes on a platter in an overlapping style. Scatter the onion on top of the tomatoes."],[null,"In a small bowl or liquid measuring cup, whisk the vinegar and oil. Drizzle the vinaigrette over the tomatoes. Sprinkle with the salt, pepper, and basil, and serve."]],"h":[]},"2617":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Cut cabbage head into six 1″ thick slices."],[null,"Arrange cabbage slices on a baking sheet and drizzle with olive oil. Sprinkle seasoning blend and dill weed over cabbage. Cover with aluminum foil."],[null,"Bake for 45 minutes. Remove foil and let cabbage steaks brown in oven for 15 minutes longer."]],"h":[[null,"Make a sauce with 1/2 cup Greek yogurt and additional chopped fresh dill weed to serve with the cabbage steaks if desired."]]},"9077170":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 350℉/176℃ and line a square 8 inch baking pan with parchment paper."],[null,"Add the dates and water to your food processor and process until you have a smooth paste. Then add the chickpeas, aquafaba, peanut butter, cocoa, and process until well combined."],[null,"Next, add the optional fill-ins, if using, and pulse a few times to mix them through without overprocessing."],[null,"Scoop the brownie batter into your dish and smooth out the top with a silicone spatula. The batter will be very thick, so press it down to ensure there are no gaps. Sprinkle more chocolate chips and walnuts on top if you'd like and bake for 25-30 minutes."],[null,"Let it cool in the pan for 5 minutes, and then lift the brownies out, using the parchment paper, and transfer to a cutting board. Let cool for AT LEAST 20 minutes before slicing."]],"h":[[null,"For nut-free, use wow butter or sun butter instead of peanut butter and omit the optional walnuts. Feel free to sub for dried fruit, like raisins or cranberries, if desired. For sweeter brownies , add 1-2 tablespoons of maple syrup to the mix after processing the dates, and/or use up to ½ cup of chocolate chips. Use parchment paper to line your pan to make it easier to remove the brownies once baked. Do not overbake! Overbaking will result in drier, less fudgy-tasting brownies. They will look underdone when you take them out of the oven, but they will set as they cool. Wet your knife in between cuts when slicing your brownies for smoother edges and to prevent sticking. Leftovers keep in an airtight container at room temperature for up to 4 days."]]},"6686840":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6852942":{"s":[[null,"Mix all ingredients together and form 4 patties."],[null,"Grill 3–4 minutes on each side and serve with guacamole."]],"h":[]},"9558150":{"s":[["Cashew Ricotta Instructions","Wilt your spinach in a skillet with a few drops of water to get it going. Once wilted, lay the spinach on a clean dish towel, and press down with paper towels to squeeze the liquids out. You want to strain as much liquid as possible from the spinach."],["Cashew Ricotta Instructions","Add the cashews to your food processor along with all remaining ingredients, EXCEPT the spinach. Process until smooth. This will take about 1-2 minutes, scraping down the sides every 30 seconds or so. Then add the spinach and pulse once or twice to get it incorporated. Do NOT over process the spinach. You do not want to puree the spinach or turn the cheese green. Instead you should see pieces of spinach throughout. See process pics above."],["Cashew Ricotta Instructions","Transfer your ricotta into a small bowl and refrigerate until needed. It will thicken up a little more in the fridge."],["Mushroom Walnut Bolognese Sauce Instructions","Add the mushrooms to your food processor and process until finely chopped. Then add the oil and the mushrooms to a large sauce pan or pot. Cook the mushrooms for approx. 3 minutes, until slightly reduced."],["Mushroom Walnut Bolognese Sauce Instructions","Meanwhile, process the walnuts and sundried tomatoes in your food processor until a crumbly texture is achieved. Then add to the pot with the mushrooms. Give it a stir and then add your tomato sauce and seasonings and mix well."],["Mushroom Walnut Bolognese Sauce Instructions","Simmer your sauce for 20 minutes and then set aside until ready to use."],["Grilled Veggie Instructions","Line a large baking sheet with parchment paper and set your oven to broil on high."],["Grilled Veggie Instructions","Arrange your sliced veggies in a single layer and drizzle with the olive oil and sprinkle with salt and pepper. Broil for 4 minutes until lightly golden and reduced, watching carefully not to burn."],["Grilled Veggie Instructions","Remove from the oven and set aside."],["Lasagna Noodles Instructions","Bring a large pot of salted water to a boil and fill a large bowl with cold water. Place the bowl of cold water on your counter as close as possible to your boiling pot of water."],["Lasagna Noodles Instructions","Add about half the package of lasagna sheets to your boiling pot of water. Do not overcrowd the pot. Cook for 2-3 minutes until softened, or according to package directions. Using tongs, carefully transfer your softened lasagna sheets into your water bath."],["Lasagna Noodles Instructions","Repeat with remaining sheets."],["Assembly & Bake Instructions","Preheat your oven to 400 degrees F.I used a glass tray that measures 11\"x15\" and assembled my lasagna in the following order:Sauce | Noodles | Sauce | Ricotta Cheese | Zucchini | Sauce | Noodles | Sauce | Ricotta Cheese | Mushrooms | Noodles | Sauce | Parmesan Cheese (optional)"],["Assembly & Bake Instructions","Scoop a thin layer of sauce onto your glass baking dish. Then add a layer of lasagna sheets over top in a single layer. Add more sauce over the lasagna sheets and spread using a silicone brush."],["Assembly & Bake Instructions","Now add half of the ricotta cheese mixture on top of the sauce, using a fork to help spread it evenly across. Then top your cheese with the zucchini slices and add another thin layer of sauce over the zucchini."],["Assembly & Bake Instructions","Now add your second layer of lasagna sheets, followed by another thin layer of sauce. Then spread the remaining ricotta cheese on top."],["Assembly & Bake Instructions","Next, add the mushrooms in a single layer, followed by your third layer of noodles. Scoop more sauce over your noodles, making sure to get it in all the corners to prevent sticking while baking."],["Assembly & Bake Instructions","Optional: Generously sprinkle vegan parmesan cheese on top, if using. (Recommended!)"],["Assembly & Bake Instructions","Cover your tray with parchment paper and then aluminum foil and bake in your preheated oven for 45 minutes. Remove from the oven, uncover and let sit for 10-15 minutes before slicing into 12 slices and serving. Garnish each slice of lasagna with more parmesan cheese or hot peppers."]],"h":[[null,"Prepare ALL your layers in the order listed , saving the lasagna sheets for LAST. Do not cook your lasagna sheets until you’re ready to assemble. You don’t want them to stick together or get too soggy and break. (Ignore, if using oven ready sheets.) If you don’t have a powerful food processor , presoak your cashews in hot water for 30-60 minutes to soften them and help them blend smooth. Then drain and make the cashew ricotta as directed. Squeeze as much moisture as possible from your spinach to prevent a watery cashew ricotta. Do not puree the spinach. You don’t want green ricotta, just pulse to gently chop and distribute. Make sure not to over process the mushrooms, walnuts or sun dried tomatoes. You want nice, hearty texture for the best vegan lasagna. For the lasagna noodles , do not overcrowd them in your pot of boiling water when precooking. Also make sure to transfer the sheets to a water bath, immediately once tender. Or, use ready to bake sheets. Cut your lasagna sheets , as needed, to fit nicely into your baking dish. Alternate the direction of your three lasagna sheet layers , to make slicing easier once baked. To keep this recipe vegan , check the lasagna package label to ensure there are no eggs as some dried lasagna sheets may contain egg. Leftovers keep refrigerated for up to 4 days."]]},"6422262":{"s":[[null,"In a large pot, bring water to a boil. Add the broccoli florets and blanch for 2 minutes. Drain and transfer the broccoli to a bowl of ice water to stop the cooking process. Drain again."],[null,"In a large skillet or wok, heat the sesame oil over medium-high heat."],[null,"Add the blanched broccoli to the skillet. Stir-fry for 2–3 minutes until the broccoli is tender-crisp."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the soy sauce and rice vinegar."],[null,"Pour the soy sauce mixture over the broccoli. Toss to coat evenly."],[null,"Continue cooking for an additional 2 minutes, allowing the flavors to meld."],[null,"Remove the broccoli from the heat."],[null,"Sprinkle toasted sesame seeds and sliced scallions over the broccoli. Toss gently."]],"h":[]},"7891265":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4. Combine the lemon juice, sesame oil and Chinese five-spice in a bowl, mixing well, then thoroughly coat the salmon steaks."],[null,"Put the salmon steaks on a plate and sprinkle with the sesame seeds. Once well coated, place the salmon on a baking sheet, lightly oiled with 1 tsp sunflower oil. Sprinkle any remaining seeds on top of the fish and bake in the oven for 12–15 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, boil the beans for 3–4 minutes, then plunge into cold water to cool."],[null,"Mix the beans, tomatoes, onion and lettuce together, and divide between two plates. Flake the salmon on top and drizzle with the balsamic vinegar."]],"h":[[null,"This recipe works well with mackerel fillets or fresh tuna steaks, too."],[null,"When in season, asparagus can be used instead of green beans."],[null,"Plunging the fine green beans into cool water stops the cooking process."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"2917":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400° F."],[null,"Add all ingredients in the order listed, except salt, to a large mixing bowl."],[null,"Using clean hands or gloves, mix ingredients and form a ball of dough."],[null,"Lay a sheet of parchment paper on a flat surface. Place dough ball in center."],[null,"Cover with another sheet of parchment paper and roll dough out as thin as possible using a rolling pin. Remove top parchment paper and set aside for later use."],[null,"Transfer bottom parchment paper with flattened dough to a large sheet pan."],[null,"Bake 10 to 12 minutes. Remove from oven, lay second piece of parchment paper flat, and carefully flip dough onto parchment paper. Place on sheet pan. Sprinkle with the 1/8 teaspoon of salt and bake another 10 to 12 minutes until lightly toasted and crisp."],[null,"Allow to cool completely. Cut or simply break into smaller crackers."]],"h":[[null,"For more uniform crackers, score the dough with a knife into desired shape and size before baking. Cut through and flip after 10 to 12 minutes. Edges may become brown more quickly, check after 9 to 10 minutes."],[null,"Adjust sesame seeds to 1 tablespoon if desired."]]},"6698156":{"s":[[null,"Add all ingredients to a jar with a tight fitting lid. Shake vigorously until everything is well combined. Store dressing in the jar in the fridge for up to 2 weeks. If it separates, shake again just before using."]],"h":[]},"4064711":{"s":[[null,"In a sealable container, mix all marinade ingredients. Season with black pepper to taste."],[null,"Cut the tofu into 12 strips and add them to the marinade. Turn them so they are covered with the marinade. Close the container and keep in the fridge for a minimum of 1 hour or overnight."],[null,"In a bowl, prepare the sesame dressing. With the help of an electric mixer, beat pasteurized eggs, vinegar and mustard. Add the sesame and canola oil gradually while mixing. Place the dressing in the fridge."],[null,"In a shallow bowl, beat the egg. In another bowl, combine the breadcrumbs, sesame seeds, and basil."],[null,"In a non-stick frying pan, heat oil over medium heat. Dip each tofu strip first into the beaten egg and then into the breadcrumb mixture. Fry the breaded tofu strips for 1–2 minutes on each side."],[null,"Fill each tortilla with 2 strips of fried tofu, lettuce and sesame dressing."]],"h":[[null,"* For Transplant: This recipe is higher in saturated fat. Check with your registered dietitian to see how this recipe can be included in your diet."],["Adding flavor to tofu is easy","Focusing on the amount and type of protein is very important if you have or are at risk for kidney disease. The protein in your diet comes from an animal or plant source. Research shows that protein from plant sources is the healthiest option for those with kidney concerns. When you choose most of your protein from plant sources it is called a plant-based diet. Plant-based proteins include beans, legumes, nuts, nut butters, seeds, whole grains and soy sources such as tofu and tempeh. Tofu comes in many different textures from very soft to super firm. Firm tofu is an excellent substitute for meat. It comes packaged as a block in liquid. Drain, rinse, wrap in a towel and press between two plates with a weight such as a skillet on top, to remove excess moisture before cooking. This will help the tofu absorb marinades and decrease spatter when cooking. Cut tofu into slices or cubes. Tofu has a very mild flavor but is like a sponge and easily takes on other flavors. Create a marinade with olive oil, vinegar, honey and a combination of herbs that complement your dish. Marinate the tofu for at least 30 minutes (longer is better). Toss in cornstarch to make a light coating and then pan fry, stir fry or air fry. The outside becomes crispy while the inside stays tender. The prepared tofu can be added to grain or rice bowls, soups, stews or rolled up in a tortilla."]]},"2438":{"s":[[null,"Cook pasta according to package directions, omitting salt. Drain."],[null,"Separate scallion bulbs and green tops. Chop garlic and scallion bulbs and greens; set aside."],[null,"Mix together sesame oil, lemon juice and honey. Set aside."],[null,"Sauté garlic and scallion bulbs in vegetable oil until slightly browned."],[null,"In a large bowl, mix together peas, raw scallion green tops and vermicelli. Add sautéed scallion bulbs and sesame oil mixture."],[null,"Toss ingredients and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Vermicelli is a pasta thinner than spaghetti. Two ounces uncooked yields 1 cup cooked."]]},"5748807":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a pan and add in the almonds, cashews and cardamom pods, fry until golden and remove from pan."],[null,"Add in the ginger, garlic, green chilli and onions and cook until soft."],[null,"Add everything into a blender and blend to a smooth paste, some water may be added to achieve a smoother consistency."],[null,"In the same pan heat oil and add in the cumin seeds, cinnamon stick and cloves and allow to sizzle for 30 seconds."],[null,"Then add in the garam masala, turmeric and nut paste and cook for 3-4 minutes."],[null,"Add in the water and bubble for around 10 minutes."],[null,"Add in the Renastep and allow to warm through."],[null,"Once warmed add in paneer, cook for 1 minute and turn off the heat."],[null,"Serve with rice and enjoy."]],"h":[["Renastep note","Renastep is a food for special medical purposes for the dietary management of kidney disease. Suitable from 3 years of age. Must be used under medical supervision. Renastep contains Milk (milk protein) and Fish (Tuna oil). This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutritics dietary analysis software. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information."]]},"3084":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375° F."],[null,"Grease baking sheet with vegetable oil (can use parchment paper or silpat sheet) and set aside."],[null,"Combine bread crumbs, flour, parsley, paprika, onion powder, garlic powder, black pepper, marjoram and thyme. Stir to mix evenly."],[null,"Add oil to bread crumb mixture and stir with a fork to blend completely."],[null,"Store in airtight container in cool, dry place or store in freezer."],[null,"To prepare chicken: Rinse chicken with water and leave chicken pieces moist with water while shaking off excess liquid."],[null,"Pour 1 cup of bread crumb mixture into a clean plastic food storage bag. Add 1 to 2 pieces of chicken at a time to bag and shake to coat evenly."],[null,"Place on greased baking sheet and bake for 40 to 45 minutes. Turn once, after 20 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"This recipe makes enough coating mix for 3 meals. Store the remaining mixture in a sealed container or freezer bag and freeze until ready to use again."],[null,"To homemade dry breadcrumbs, toast day old bread until crisp but not burned. Crush in a blender or food processor."]]},"3320":{"s":[[null,"Combine bread crumbs, flour, parsley, paprika, onion powder, garlic powder, black pepper, marjoram and thyme. Stir to mix evenly."],[null,"Add oil to bread crumb mixture and stir with a fork to blend completely."],[null,"Store in airtight container in cool, dry place or store in freezer."],[null,"To use, place 1 cup coating mixture in a plastic bag. Add several pieces of chicken or other meat and shake to coat."],[null,"Bake meat on a greased baking sheet at 375° F for turning once after baking for 20 minutes. Continue cooking until meat is done according to meat thermometer. (Time varies with meat type and thickness)."]],"h":[[null,"This recipe makes enough coating mix for 3 meals. Store the remaining mixture in a sealed container or freezer bag and freeze until ready to use again."],[null,"To make homemade dry breadcrumbs, toast day old bread until crisp but not burned. Crush in a blender or food processor."],[null,"Makes a great coating for chicken or in place of breadcrumbs in any recipe."]]},"7962332":{"s":[[null,"Put the onion, peppers and garlic in a glass bowl with 1tbsp water. Cover with cling film and microwave at 800W for 2 mins. Stir and cook for a further 2 mins."],[null,"Stir the paste and spices into the onion mixture and microwave for a further 1 min. Tip into a medium frying pan."],[null,"Stir in the tomatoes and simmer gently for 15 mins or until thickened, stirring occasionally."],[null,"Make a dip in the middle, crack the egg into the dip. Cover the pan with a lid and cook until the egg is done to your taste."],[null,"Scatter with red pepper flakes (optional), a little chopped parsley and mint, and serve."]],"h":[[null,"You could use any colour peppers for this dish."],[null,"Try adding mushrooms or artichoke hearts."],[null,"Freezing instructions: the sauce can be frozen."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 5"]]},"6219418":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375°F. Arrange bell pepper halves cut-side up in a baking dish."],[null,"Heat olive oil in a skillet over medium heat. Add onion and cook until softened, about 3 minutes. Stir in garlic, cumin, paprika, coriander, and red pepper flakes, cooking for 30 seconds until fragrant."],[null,"Pour in crushed tomatoes, season with salt and black pepper, and simmer for 5 minutes until slightly thickened."],[null,"Spoon the tomato mixture evenly into each pepper half. Create a small well in the center of each and carefully crack an egg into each well."],[null,"Cover the dish loosely with foil and bake for 20-25 minutes, or until the egg whites are set but yolks remain slightly runny."],[null,"Remove from the oven, sprinkle with feta cheese and fresh parsley. Serve warm."]],"h":[]},"6178564":{"s":[[null,"In a large salad bowl, whisk together lemon zest, lemon juice, Dijon mustard, garlic, ground black pepper, Parmesan cheese and olive oil."],[null,"Trim woody ends off of asparagus and discard. Trim heads off asparagus and toss in the bowl with the salad dressing."],[null,"Using a vegetable peeler, shave asparagus stalks lengthwise and toss with the dressing in the bowl (or slice the asparagus using a slicing blade on a food processor)."],[null,"Shave radishes with the peeler, mandolin or slicing blade on the food processor. Toss with rest of salad ingredients."]],"h":[]},"6933181":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F. Line a large baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together balsamic vinegar, olive oil, honey, minced garlic, dried thyme, coarse salt, and black pepper to create the marinade."],[null,"Place chicken breasts in a large bowl and pour the marinade over the chicken, ensuring it's well coated."],[null,"Arrange the chicken breasts on the sheet pan and Brussels sprouts on the other."],[null,"Add the Brussels sprouts to the same bowl and coat well with the remaining marinade. Arrange the Brussel sprouts around the chicken on the sheet pan."],[null,"Bake in the preheated oven until the chicken is cooked to an internal temperature of 165 degrees F, about 25–30 minutes."],[null,"Remove from the oven, let it rest for a few minutes, and then garnish with fresh parsley and lemon zest and juice, if using."]],"h":[]},"2701":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400° F."],[null,"Remove the outside leaves of the Brussels sprouts. Cut in half. Cut the pears into 1/2-inch cubes."],[null,"Place 1 teaspoon olive oil in a mixing bowl. Add Brussels sprouts and toss to coat with the oil."],[null,"Transfer Brussels sprouts to a 9” x 13” pan and spread into a single layer on half of the pan. Bake for 12 minutes."],[null,"Place the remaining teaspoon olive oil in the mixing bowl. Add pears and toss to coat with oil."],[null,"Remove Brussels sprouts from the oven and add the pears to the other half of the pan. Roast for an additional 12 minutes, or until pears are tender."],[null,"Drizzle pears with 1 teaspoon balsamic vinegar glaze. Mix sprouts and pears together in a serving bowl."]],"h":[[null,"Balsamic vinegar glaze, also called balsamic vinegar reduction, may be purchased or made at home. For homemade, using a small saucepan bring 1 cup of vinegar to a boil then reduce to medium heat. Cook for 10 to 15 minutes until vinegar is reduced by half or until it reaches your desired consistency. Store extra in a covered container in the refrigerator."]]},"6619453":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 450 degrees F. Line a large baking sheet pan with aluminum foil."],[null,"Place turkey, egg, breadcrumbs, half of the Italian seasoning, and black pepper in a medium bowl. Mix with your hands until the meatloaf mixture is well combined."],[null,"Form the beef mixture into 12 short logs, approximately 3-inches long. Transfer to one half of the baking sheet."],[null,"Spread the bell peppers and onion on the unused side of the baking sheet. Drizzle the vegetables with oil, sprinkle with the remaining seasoning, and toss to coat evenly. Arrange them in a single layer."],[null,"Place the baking sheet in the oven and roast, stirring the vegetables midway, until the meatloaves are nearly cooked and the vegetables are tender when pierced with a fork, about 15–20 minutes."],[null,"Take the baking sheet out of the oven when the meatloaves are almost done. Lay slices of cheese on top of each meatloaf. Return the sheet to the oven and bake until the meatloaves are fully cooked and the cheese has melted, about 2–3 more minutes."]],"h":[]},"4245582":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400°F."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine mustard, olive oil, lemon juice, garlic, and basil. Set aside."],[null,"Place the chicken legs on a baking sheet lined with parchment paper or on a silicone sheet. Carefully detach and lift the skin off each chicken leg and distribute half of the mustard mixture under the skins."],[null,"Transfer the frozen vegetables and onion slices to a bowl. Add the remaining mustard mixture and toss the vegetables. Spread the vegetables on the baking sheet, filling the spaces between the chicken legs."],[null,"Bake in the oven for 45 minutes or until the chicken has lost its pink color and the internal temperature has reached 165°F."],[null,"In the meantime, cook orzo pasta according to the package instructions without the salt. Drain the orzo and transfer to a bowl. Mix with olive oil and lemon zest and serve with the chicken and vegetables. Add pepper to taste."]],"h":[[null,"* Chicken legs are available in various weights. Look for those which weigh 4 ounces each. You can also use skin-on chicken thighs or drumsticks for this recipe."],[null,"PLEASE NOTE: This recipe is higher in potassium and portion size is important. Check with your registered dietitian to see how this recipe can be included in your diet."],["Roasting vegetables","A healthy eating pattern is one that includes ample vegetables to help maintain a healthy body weight and prevent or manage chronic illness such as cancer, diabetes, heart disease, and kidney disease. Roasting vegetables is a healthy and delicious way to prepare vegetables. Experiment to create your favorite combinations. Chop a variety of vegetables, toss in olive oil, and add desired seasonings such as garlic, black pepper, or a mixture of herbs and roast on baking sheets in the preheated oven. Roast until vegetables are tender and beginning to brown, 15–20 minutes, tossing them half way through. Oven times vary. For example, cauliflower can be roasted in 20 minutes at 425°F. Use shallow pans and do not over crowd the vegetables. This will allow them to brown rather than steam. Roasted vegetables can be added to a sandwich, tossed with pasta, mixed into cooked rice, bulgur wheat or couscous, or served with a lean protein source. Prepare extra for leftovers. Place them in an airtight container and refrigerate up to 3 days. Pour off any accumulated liquid before using. When potassium is a concern, choose lower-potassium vegetables such as asparagus, broccoli, cabbage, carrots, cauliflower, corn, eggplant, green beans, mushrooms, onions, bell peppers, turnips, and yellow summer squash. Ask your registered dietitian nutritionist which vegetables and how much of them are right for you."]]},"6779793":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oven to 425 degrees F and line a sheet pan with parchment paper."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine chili powder, cumin, coarse salt, garlic powder, paprika, and ground pepper. Whisk in 1 tablespoon of oil. Add the chicken, onion, and red and green bell peppers and toss to coat."],[null,"Spread the chicken and vegetables in a single layer on the sheet pan. Bake for 15 minutes."],[null,"Combine black beans and the remaining 1 tablespoon of olive oil in a large bowl."],[null,"Remove the pan from the oven and stir the chicken and vegetables. Spread beans evenly over the top. Roast until the chicken is 165 degrees F and the vegetables are tender, 5–7 minutes more."],[null,"In a small bowl, stir yogurt, lime juice, and hot sauce."],[null,"Divide the lettuce, chicken, beans, and vegetables among the four bowls. Drizzle with the yogurt sauce and serve with additional hot sauce or salsa."]],"h":[]},"6248441":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400°F. Line a large baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the olive oil, Dijon mustard, apple cider vinegar, thyme, garlic powder, salt, and pepper."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine the chicken, Brussels sprouts, apple slices, and red onion. Drizzle with the marinade and toss to coat."],[null,"Spread everything evenly on the baking sheet. Roast for 25–30 minutes, stirring halfway through, until the chicken is cooked through (165°F internal temperature) and Brussels sprouts are tender and golden."],[null,"Serve warm, garnished with a squeeze of lemon."]],"h":[]},"3658":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400˚ F. Chop the potatoes into bite sized pieces. See helpful hints for instructions on potassium reduction if needed. Toss potatoes in 1 teaspoon olive oil."],[null,"Spray a 9 x13-inch sheet pan with cooking spray. Place the raw chicken strips down 1/3 of the pan. Place the potatoes down another 1/3 of the pan. Finally, lay the frozen green beans down the last 1/3 of the pan."],[null,"Melt the butter and drizzle over the entire pan of chicken, potatoes and green beans. Sprinkle Italian dressing dry mix over the entire pan."],[null,"Bake for 20 to 30 minutes. Check chicken for doneness after 20 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Nutrient analysis based on leached potatoes. If not leached the potassium content is 766 mg per serving."],[null,"To reduce potassium in potatoes: Chop potatoes. Place in a large pan and cover completely with water. Bring to a boil, then drain. Refill water over the potatoes, to cover by 1-inch. Bring to a boil again and boil for 10 minutes. Drain and toss with 1 teaspoon olive oil before adding to the sheet pan."],[null,"Packages of raw chicken breast strips will vary in weight. Generally they will weigh between 14-16 ounces. There are 16 ounces in 1 pound."],[null,"There are about 2 tablespoons of dry Italian dressing mix in a 19 gram packet. Look for a dry mix with the lowest amount of sodium possible. Be cautious, using too much dry mix will increase the sodium content of the meal."],[null,"Save the remaining Italian dressing mix and use for a different recipe or mix with sour cream for a vegetable dip."]]},"6189432":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400˚ F. Chop the potatoes into bite sized pieces. See helpful hints for instructions on potassium reduction if needed. Toss potatoes in 1 teaspoon olive oil."],[null,"Spray a 9 x13-inch sheet pan with cooking spray. Place the raw chicken strips down 1/3 of the pan. Place the potatoes down another 1/3 of the pan. Finally, lay the frozen green beans down the last 1/3 of the pan."],[null,"Drizzle 2 tablespoons of olive oil over the entire pan of chicken, potatoes and green beans. Sprinkle Italian dressing dry mix over the entire pan."],[null,"Bake for 20 to 30 minutes. Check chicken for doneness after 20 minutes."]],"h":[]},"6626676":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F. Line a large baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"In a large mixing bowl, combine the shrimp and asparagus. Add olive oil, minced garlic, red pepper flakes (if using), coarse salt, and black pepper. Toss everything together until the shrimp and asparagus are evenly coated."],[null,"Spread the shrimp and asparagus in a single layer on the prepared baking sheet."],[null,"Roast in the preheated oven for approximately 8–10 minutes or until the shrimp are opaque and the asparagus is tender but still crisp."]],"h":[]},"6633572":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oven to 375°F and cover a sheet pan with parchment paper."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine the olive oil, chopped dill, lemon zest, lemon juice, coarse salt, and pepper."],[null,"Place the salmon filets and asparagus on a sheet pan and spoon the herb mixture on top of each filet."],[null,"Bake until the salmon is cooked to an internal temperature of 145°F, about 20 minutes and the asparagus is tender."]],"h":[]},"6293155":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F. Line a large sheet pan with parchment paper or aluminum foil for easy cleanup."],[null,"Prepare the marinade by mixing the olive oil, lemon juice, oregano, thyme, garlic powder, salt, and pepper in a small bowl."],[null,"Arrange the chicken breasts on one side of the sheet pan. Brush them generously with the lemon herb marinade."],[null,"Toss the vegetables (broccoli, bell peppers, cherry tomatoes, and zucchini) in the remaining marinade. Arrange them on the other side of the sheet pan around the chicken."],[null,"Bake for 25–30 minutes or until the chicken reaches an internal temperature of 165 degrees F and the vegetables are tender."],[null,"To serve, divide chicken and veggies and add ½ cup cooked brown rice between each plate or bowl. Top with freshly chopped parsley."]],"h":[]},"6435330":{"s":[[null,"In a medium bowl or large resealable plastic bag, mix the miso paste, rice vinegar, ½ tbsp of sesame oil and garlic. Add the salmon and gently coat with the marinade. Cover the bowl or seal the bag and marinate in the fridge for 15 minutes (if you’re short on time you can skip the marinating step)."],[null,"Preheat your oven to 450°F. Line a rimmed baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Cut the root ends off the bok choy and cut each one in half horizontally."],[null,"Remove salmon fillets from the marinade and place on one end of the prepared baking sheet, skin side down. (Discard any remaining marinade.)"],[null,"At the other end of the baking sheet, arrange the bok choy cut side down. Drizzle with the remaining ½ tbsp of sesame oil and tamari."],[null,"Roast for 8 minutes or until the salmon is cooked through and the bok choy is tender."],[null,"Plate the salmon filets and bok choy and sprinkle the bok choy with sesame seeds."]],"h":[]},"6837569":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400 degrees F."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine oil, juice from 1/2 lemon, rosemary, garlic powder, paprika, salt, and black pepper; mix well. Add turkey and toss until evenly coated. Place on a baking sheet. Add bell peppers, zucchini, mushrooms, and onion to oil mixture and toss until evenly coated. Place vegetables and lemon halves on baking sheet."],[null,"Roast 25 to 30 minutes or until no pink remains in turkey and vegetables are tender. With a pair of tongs, squeeze roasted lemon halves over turkey and vegetables and serve immediately."]],"h":[]},"6946112":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400°F."],[null,"Coat a baking sheet with cooking spray. Place the sliced onion in the middle of the baking sheet. Place the salmon fillets on top of the onion slices, and place the asparagus around the salmon."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the mustard, olive oil, honey, and pepper. Spread the mustard mixture on top of the salmon fillets and drizzle any extra on the asparagus."],[null,"Bake 20 minutes. Serve each salmon fillet with the asparagus on the side and the onions on top of the salmon."]],"h":[]},"3522":{"s":[[null,"Rinse and pat salmon fillets dry, leaving skin on. Wash and trim the green beans."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 425° F. For easy clean up line a sheet pan with parchment paper or coat sheet with cooking spray. Place the fillets, skin-side down on the sheet pan."],[null,"Chop the dill and stir into the mayonnaise."],[null,"Spread the mayo-dill mixture evenly on top of both filets."],[null,"Toss the green beans with olive oil and then arrange around the salmon fillets."],[null,"Place the baking sheet on the middle rack and roast salmon for 14 to 16 minutes. Fish will be done when the flesh begins to flake easily with a fork."],[null,"Garnish with lemon slices and fresh dill."]],"h":[[null,"For additional seasoning add black pepper to the salmon and green beans."],[null,"If fresh green beans are out of season substitute frozen green beans."],[null,"Adjust the fish portion according to your dietary protein goal."],[null,"Instead of using prepared mayonnaise you can easily make your own. In a blender (an emersion blender works well starting at the bottom and working upwards until thick and fluffy) combine 1 cold egg, 1/4 cup olive oil, 2 tablespoons lemon juice and 1/4 teaspoon salt. Blend for 30 seconds or until the mixture begins to emulsify and look like mayo. After reaching the desired consistency, stir in the dill."]]},"6790312":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425° F. For easy clean up line a sheet pan with parchment paper or coat sheet with cooking spray."],[null,"Pat salmon fillets dry, leaving skin on. Place the fillets, skin-side down on the sheet pan."],[null,"Combine the dill and mayonnaise in a small bowl. Spread the mixture evenly over both fillets."],[null,"Toss the green beans with olive oil and then arrange around the salmon fillets."],[null,"Place the baking sheet on the middle rack and roast salmon for 14 to 16 minutes. Fish will be done when the flesh begins to flake easily with a fork. Garnish with lemon slices and more fresh dill."]],"h":[]},"1760":{"s":[[null,"Drain the pineapple and reserve the juice. Mince the garlic and ginger."],[null,"Combine pineapple juice, garlic, ginger, 1 teaspoon olive oil and salt in a zip top bag. Place sirloin tips in the marinade and seal the bag. Refrigerate overnight."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 450° F. Line 2 rimmed sheet pans with foil or parchment paper."],[null,"Cut the squash into 1/2-inch rounds. Toss with 1 teaspoon olive oil. Cut the red onion half into wedges. Toss with the remaining teaspoon of olive oil."],[null,"Arrange pineapple rings and squash in a single layer on one of the sheet pans. Roast for 5 to 7 minutes. Remove pan from the oven and turn the pineapple and squash pieces over. Add the onion and roast until lightly charred, about 4 to 5 minutes. Cover with foil to keep warm and set aside."],[null,"Remove the sirloin tips from the marinade and place in an even layer on the other sheet pan. Roast for 4 minutes then turn the pieces over. Cook for 4 minutes or until sirloin pieces are cooked through."],[null,"Arrange sirloin tips on a platter with squash and pineapple and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Thicker or larger pieces of meat require longer cooking time."]]},"6526217":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 400 degrees F. Line a sheet pan with parchment paper."],[null,"Press the tofu to remove excess water, then cut it into cubes."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine tofu cubes, sliced bell peppers, and sliced red onion."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together olive oil, taco seasoning, ground cumin, smoked paprika, chili powder, and black pepper to create the marinade."],[null,"Pour the marinade over the tofu and vegetables. Toss until everything is evenly coated. Let it marinate for at least 30 minutes."],[null,"Spread the marinated tofu and vegetables evenly on the sheet."],[null,"Roast in the preheated oven for 25 minutes or until the tofu is golden and the vegetables are tender, stirring halfway through."],[null,"Divide the fajita filling among the wraps."],[null,"Serve the sheet pan tofu fajitas and garnish with chopped cilantro and lime wedges."]],"h":[]},"6483274":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 450°F. Line a large rimmed baking sheet with unbleached parchment paper."],[null,"Pat or squeeze the tofu of excess liquid, if necessary. Cut the tofu into (3/4-inch) cubes."],[null,"In a large bowl, whisk together the ginger, tamari, vinegar, and oil. Add the zucchini and bell pepper pieces to the sauce mixture; toss by hand to coat."],[null,"Arrange the zucchinis and peppers in a single layer on the baking sheet (fill 2/3 of the sheet), letting excess sauce drip back into the bowl."],[null,"Add the tofu to the bowl with the remaining sauce mixture; toss to coat. Arrange the tofu in a single layer on the baking sheet (fill the rest of the sheet). Drizzle tofu with any remaining sauce."],[null,"Roast until the tofu and vegetables are browned, about 30 minutes; no stirring needed. Serve."]],"h":[]},"6569048":{"s":[[null,"In a medium bowl, hand-crush the tomatoes or pulse lightly in a blender until mostly smooth. Stir in the minced garlic, ½ teaspoon of the oregano, and ¼ teaspoon of the black pepper. Set aside."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 425°F. Line two large sheet pans with parchment paper. Arrange cabbage rounds in a single layer and lightly coat both sides with cooking spray. Scatter the bell peppers and onions around the cabbage. Roast for 20–25 minutes, flipping the cabbage halfway, until tender and lightly browned."],[null,"While the cabbage roasts, heat a dry skillet over medium heat. Add the crumbled tofu and cook for 2–3 minutes to drive off moisture. Add the soy sauce, fennel seed, garlic powder, remaining ½ tsp oregano, remaining ¼ tsp black pepper, and crushed red pepper flakes. Cook, stirring frequently, until lightly browned and aromatic, about 8–10 minutes."],[null,"Whisk together the non-fat Greek yogurt, lemon juice, dill, remaining 1/2 teaspoon garlic powder, and onion powder. Add water 1 tablespoon at a time until the drizzle reaches a pourable consistency. Set aside."],[null,"Remove cabbage rounds from the oven. Spoon 3 tablespoons of tomato sauce onto each round. Dollop 2 tablespoons of fat-free cottage cheese evenly over the sauce on each round, then sprinkle the pizzas evenly with the reduced fat mozzarella. Top with tofu crumbles, peppers, and onions. Return to the oven and bake for 10–15 minutes, until the cheese is melted and everything is heated through."],[null,"Let the pizzas cool for 5 minutes then scatter basil leaves over the top. Drizzle the yogurt ranch over each pizza just before serving. Serve 2 cabbage pizza rounds per person."]],"h":[]},"7138695":{"s":[[null,"Add oil to a pan and cook the onion for 5 minutes. In a separate pan, heat the stock and simmering gently."],[null,"Add the red pepper, courgette, garlic, white pepper and half the parsley to the onion. Stir for 1 minute before adding the rice. Stir for 2 minutes, then add 2 ladles of stock, enough to just cover the rice, and stir."],[null,"Add hot stock a little at a time, so the rice is just covered, whilst stirring regularly. The risotto should be bubbling very gently."],[null,"After 20 minutes, add any remaining stock and the seafood, then stir for another 3-4 minutes. Test the rice to make sure its cooked ‘al dente’ (slightly firm) and ensure all the seafood is fully cooked through."],[null,"Finally, vigorously stir in the remaining parsley, saving a little to serve. Add the yoghurt, stir, then cover and allow to stand for 2 minutes, before serving with a sprinkle of parsley and good grind of black pepper."]],"h":[[null,"Keep the stock simmering in a separate saucepan so it’s piping hot when added to the rice to ensure the rice cooks consistently. Add a little at a time - if you run out, just add some boiling water."],[null,"Stirring regularly with a wooden spoon ensures the rice releases its starch to ensure a creamy texture."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Then defrost in the fridge and reheat until piping hot throughout. Discard any leftovers and do not reheat/refreeze."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"4558148":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375°F."],[null,"In a large saucepan, cover the cauliflower florets with water. Bring to a boil and simmer until the cauliflower is tender. Drain and put cooked cauliflower in a mixing bowl or food processor. Puree with butter, garlic powder and black pepper."],[null,"Heat a skillet over medium heat and brown the beef. Add the onions, celery, garlic, thyme and black pepper, and continue to cook until the vegetables soften. Add peas and corn and bring to a simmer."],[null,"In a cup, mix together the beef stock and corn starch. Add the stock slurry to the ground beef and vegetables. Continue to heat and stir until it thickens into a gravy."],[null,"To assemble the shepherd’s pie, pour the beef and vegetable mixture into a baking dish (for example, 9-inch square). Smooth the cauliflower puree over the top."],[null,"Bake uncovered for approximately 30 minutes until gravy bubbles and cauliflower puree becomes slightly brown."]],"h":[[null,"* Look for low or reduced-sodium broth containing 200mg sodium or less per 1 cup serving. Avoid low-sodium broth that contains potassium chloride—it’s very high in potassium."],[null,"PLEASE NOTE: This recipe is higher in potassium and portion size is important. Check with your registered dietitian to see how this recipe can be included in your diet."],["Fresh, frozen or canned?","Choosing low-potassium fruits and vegetables are important to maintain a normal blood potassium level. Include fresh, frozen or canned foods in your grocery list with careful planning. Fresh items such as apples, grapes, peppers and green beans can be found in the produce section. They are low-calorie foods and rich in fiber, vitamins and minerals. Stick with the recommended portion size of each to stay within your potassium limits. Frozen fruits and vegetables can be a cost-efective way of adding these foods to your diet. Limit heavily seasoned foods or foods covered in a salty sauce. Skip blends that include high-potassium fruits or vegetables. Read the Nutrition Facts label to ensure there are no hidden sources of potassium. Canned items are a second option, but careful label reading is essential before purchasing. Avoid heavily salted items, foods preserved with potassium chloride and fruits and vegetables that are naturally high in potassium."]]},"1805":{"s":[[null,"Place ingredients in a blender and blend for 30 seconds."],[null,"Serve immediately or freeze for later."]],"h":[[null,"Low-cholesterol egg product is pasteurized. It is safe to consume without cooking."],[null,"Look for almond milk or other milk substitutes without phosphate additives."]]},"2817":{"s":[[null,"Combine the vinegar, oil, pepper, garlic powder and oregano to make a marinade."],[null,"Cut the beef into 1-1/2″ cubes. Cut the onions into quarters; cut the bell peppers into 1-1/2″ squares."],[null,"Place the meat and vegetables in a covered container and marinade for at least 30 minutes."],[null,"Load the skewers, alternating with meat and vegetables."],[null,"Grill kebabs over medium heat for 10 to 30 minutes, depending on desired degree of doneness."]],"h":[[null,"Dawn uses sirloin steak for her Shish Kebabs, but you can use whatever meat you prefer."],[null,"If using wooden skewers, soak them in water for at least 30 minutes prior to grilling to avoid burning them during the cooking process."]]},"2756":{"s":[[null,"Combine the vinegar, oil, black pepper, garlic powder and oregano to make a marinade."],[null,"Cut the beef into 1-1/2″ cubes; Cut the onions into quarters; cut the bell peppers into 1-1/2″ squares."],[null,"Place the meat and vegetables in a covered container and marinade for at least 30 minutes."],[null,"Load the skewers, alternating meat and vegetables."],[null,"Grill the kebabs over medium heat for 10 to 30 minutes, depending on desired degree of doneness."]],"h":[[null,"Dawn uses sirloin steak for her Shish Kebabs, but you can use whatever meat you prefer."],[null,"If using wooden skewers, soak them in water for at least 30 minutes prior to grilling to avoid burning them during the cooking process."]]},"9439579":{"s":[[null,"Soak your almonds or cashews in hot water for 15 minutes and then drain."],[null,"Meanwhile, place additional water on the stove top or in a kettle to bring to a boil. You will need 1.5 cups of boiled water, so add a little extra to make up for any loss in evaporation."],[null,"Find a heatproof dish, bowl, or container (glass, not plastic) that will hold approx. 3 cups of liquid and place beside your blender."],[null,"Add everything EXCEPT the water to your blender and once the water is boiling, add 1.5 cups of the boiling water to your blender, on top of all the other ingredients and blend immediately until smooth."],[null,"Pour the mixture into your heatproof dish and refrigerate for 3 hours or longer, until solid."],[null,"Use a butter knife, or silicone spatula to run around the edges of your vegan cheese and separate from the dish. (See process shots above for a visual.) Then flip it over on a clean surface, such as a cutting board to pop it out of the dish."],[null,"Now slice or shred your cheese for use in a variety of dishes."]],"h":[[null,"Even if you have a high-speed blender, like a Vitamix, for this recipe, I recommend soaking your almonds or cashews. Doing so will help them blend up much faster so you can quickly pour the mixture out before the cheese begins to set. Move quickly!! Once you add the boiling water to your blender, the mixture will start to thicken. Immediately pour the mixture into your heatproof dish once smooth. Make sure to use blanched almonds. If you don’t have blanched almonds you can blanch whole almonds yourself, quite easily. For the coconut oil: Make sure to use REFINED only as unrefined has a strong coconut flavour that you don’t want in your cheese. For oil free meltable vegan cheese : Skip the coconut oil and replace with ¼ cup of water to make up the liquid portion of the recipe. I’ve tested this vegan cheese with and without the oil (check out the oil free vegan cheese test above) and you absolutely CAN skip it. If you prefer to avoid kappa carrageenan , I’ve read that you may use double the amount (in this case 3 tablespoons) of agar agar instead. Now I haven’t tested it this way and cannot speak to the way it shreds or melts, but several sources state it works, albeit, not as well as kappa. Your meltable vegan cheese will keep refrigerated for 5-7 days. Or freeze (whole or shredded) in a freezer-safe airtight container or zip top bag for up to 3 months. How to Blanch Almonds Bring a small pot of water (enough to cover the almonds) to boil. Once boiling, add the almonds and boil for 1 minute. Then drain and rinse with cold water to cool them down, enough to handle. Then pinch the almonds and the skin will come off easily. Recipe inspired by my stretchy vegan mozzarella and method adapted from Vegan Blueberry ."]]},"6642831":{"s":[],"h":[]},"4536590":{"s":[[null,"In a large saucepan, bring water to a boil. Cook pasta for approximately 10 minutes until tender, but firm. Drain and set aside."],[null,"Heat oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Add the shrimp and sauté until they become pink. Remove them from the skillet."],[null,"In the same skillet, sauté the asparagus with the shallot and garlic over medium heat. Add the chicken stock, lemon zest, tarragon, and black pepper and bring the mixture to a simmer (approximately 5 minutes, uncovered)."],[null,"Once the liquid in the skillet has reduced by half, add the shrimp and rotini to the skillet. Toss together and serve immediately. Enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"* Choose frozen shrimp without phosphate additives."],[null,"** Look for low or reduced-sodium broth containing 200mg sodium or less per 1 cup serving. Avoid low-sodium broth that contains potassium chloride—it’s very high in potassium."],[null,"You can enjoy this recipe hot or cold. Brighten up your salads It makes a great salad “on the go.” with this tri-color pasta."],[null,"PLEASE NOTE: This recipe is higher in potassium and portion size is important. Check with your registered dietitian to see how this recipe can be included in your diet."],["Managing potassium in seafood","General dietary guidelines recommend at least two meals with seafood as part of a weekly healthy diet. Seafood is an excellent low-fat source of protein, vitamins and minerals. Certain types also contain omega-3 fatty acids, which support heart health and have been shown to reduce inflammation. Fish and seafood are also a source of protein low in total and saturated fat, which is important in maintaining or reaching a healthy weight. Experts recommend fish and seafood for people with chronic kidney disease. Make sure portions meet your dietary goals. Lower-potassium choices include low-sodium canned tuna and 3-ounce portions of perch, salmon, pickled herring and haddock. Shellfish can be had in moderation. For variety, add 3-ounce portions of cooked lobster and blue, king or imitation crab to your diet."]]},"6479129":{"s":[[null,"Combine the shrimp, avocado, tomato, scallions, and pineapple (and jalapeño, if desired). Remove a few of the central leaves from each lettuce head to make a bowl. Divide the shrimp mixture between the lettuce heads."],[null,"Stir the chili powder into the Greek yogurt."],[null,"Top each “taco” bowl with the Greek yogurt mixture and salsa. Sprinkle chopped fresh cilantro on top, if desired."]],"h":[]},"6129077":{"s":[[null,"Cook the grits according to the package instructions until creamy and smooth."],[null,"Fold in ½ cup cheddar cheese, 1/8 tsp salt and 1/8 tsp black pepper."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F."],[null,"Place the halved bell peppers in a baking dish, cut side up. Cover and bake for 40 minutes."],[null,"In a large skillet, heat the olive oil over medium heat. Add chopped onion and garlic, sauté until softened."],[null,"Stir in the cherry tomatoes, Old Bay seasoning, remaining coarse salt, and pepper. Cook for an additional 2 minutes."],[null,"Turn off the heat and add the shrimp to the skillet. Stir to combine."],[null,"Spoon the cooked grits into each pepper half, pressing down with the back of the spoon. Top the grits with the shrimp and tomato mixture."],[null,"Sprinkle the remaining shredded cheddar cheese over each stuffed pepper."],[null,"Cover with foil and bake until the cheese is melted, the peppers have softened, and the filling is cooked through, about 20 minutes."],[null,"Broil for 2-3 minutes until the cheese is bubbly."],[null,"Remove from the oven and let it cool for a few minutes. Garnish with fresh chopped parsley if desired."]],"h":[]},"3090":{"s":[[null,"Finely chop shrimp, onion, bell pepper and parsley. Beat eggs."],[null,"Mix all of the ingredients except flour together in a mixing bowl."],[null,"After mixing, gradually add flour. Continue adding flour a little at a time until mix gets thick and hangs on to the spoon."],[null,"To deep fry, heat oil in a large skillet or deep-fryer. Drop medium-sized spoonfuls of shrimp batter into hot oil and cook until browned and crisp on both sides."],[null,"Remove from oil and drain on paper towels. Serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"Suggested Cajun seasonings include homemade Salt-free Cajun Seasoning on DaVita.com, Mrs. Dash Cajun seasoning blend or Benoit’s Best Salt-Free Cajun seasoning. Avoid products with potassium chloride."],[null,"Instead of frying you can form batter into patties and bake on a greased baking sheet at 350° F until golden brown."],[null,"Try crab or crawfish instead of shrimp. Both are equally great!"]]},"6488181":{"s":[[null,"Place mixture in a serving bowl and add the chopped shrimp and olive oil. Chill for 30 minutes or more before serving"],[null,"In a food processor, add green onions, tomato, peppers, pineapple, and cilantro; pulse on-off button to chop to a very coarse consistency. Chunky texture is desired. Add lime juice, vinegar and garlic powder to the mixture."]],"h":[]},"6436140":{"s":[[null,"For the grits: Heat vegetable oil in a medium pot over medium-high heat. Add the cauliflower and cook until softened and lightly browned, about 10 minutes. Add 1 clove of minced garlic and heat until fragrant, about 1 minute."],[null,"Add the beans, broth, and water. Cook for 5 minutes. Turn off the heat. Add the Parmesan and onion powder. Using a masher or blender, mix until just creamy with a little texture remaining. Add more water as needed. Season with pepper. Cover to keep warm until serving."],[null,"For the shrimp: Pat the shrimp dry with a paper towel. Heat 1½ tsp oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat and add the shrimp in a single layer. Lightly sear on one side until curled and lightly charred. Remove shrimp to a plate and add the remaining oil to the pan."],[null,"Add the celery, onion, and bell pepper to the pan. Reduce heat to medium and cook, stirring occasionally until tender but not overly browned, about 7 minutes. If the pan gets too dry while the vegetables cook, add water as needed."],[null,"Add the remaining 3 cloves of minced garlic and seasoning and heat until fragrant, about 1 minute. Add the tomatoes, broth, and bay leaf. Use a spoon to scrape any bits stuck to the bottom of the pan. Bring to a boil and then reduce heat to a simmer. Cook for 10 minutes until thickened, stir frequently to prevent the bottom from burning."],[null,"Serve on top of cauliflower “grits” and garnish with green onions and hot sauce."]],"h":[]},"6450804":{"s":[[null,"Coat a large non-stick skillet with cooking spray. Cook the shrimp over medium heat for about 2 minutes. Remove the shrimp from the pan and set aside."],[null,"Add the oil to the pan and heat. Add the bell peppers and onions and cook for about 7 minutes or until they begin to brown. Add the shrimp and any juices back to pan."],[null,"Add the water and spices, including salt and pepper. Bring the mixture to a boil; reduce heat and simmer until the water evaporates. Serve the shrimp and peppers in the corn tortillas."]],"h":[]},"2753":{"s":[[null,"Dice onion and chop scallions. Mince garlic and ginger root."],[null,"Preheat 1 tablespoon of oil in a large non-stick skillet over medium-high heat."],[null,"Add onion and 1/2 teaspoon black pepper and cook until onion is tender, about 2 minutes."],[null,"Add the garlic, ginger and scallions and stir for about 1 minute."],[null,"Add shrimp and stir frequently until heated."],[null,"Add peas and carrots and stir until heated. Place shrimp and vegetable mixture into a large covered bowl."],[null,"Return skillet to the heat and add 2 tablespoons oil. Pour eggs into the skillet and scramble until done. Remove eggs to the bowl with shrimp and vegetables."],[null,"Return skillet to heat and add 1 tablespoon oil. Add 4 cups cooked rice and stir to heat and coat with oil."],[null,"Season rice with salt and pepper and let rice sit in skillet without stirring for about 2 minutes."],[null,"Stir rice and add the shrimp, vegetables and eggs. Serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"leftover chicken or 1/2-cup diced tofu for the shrimp"],[null,"1/4 teaspoon garlic powder or 1 teaspoon minced garlic for garlic clove"],[null,"1/2 teaspoon ground ginger for fresh ginger"],[null,"1 tablespoon reduced-sodium soy sauce for 1/4 teaspoon salt"],[null,"2 scallions yield approximately 3 tablespoons chopped."],[null,"Jasmine rice adds extra flavor."],[null,"For a higher protein diet, increase shrimp."]]},"6055159":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat and sauté the shrimp, onion, and bell pepper for about 5 minutes, until the shrimp is pink."],[null,"Stir in the remaining ingredients and cook for about 5 minutes, until heated through."],[null,"Meanwhile, cook rice according to package directions. Place in a large bowl and top with shrimp and vegetable mixture."]],"h":[]},"6838915":{"s":[[null,"Add cooking spray and sesame oil to a medium sauté pan over medium-high heat."],[null,"Add bell pepper and onion and sauté until vegetables are softened and onions are clear."],[null,"Add shrimp and sauté for 2-3 minutes, or until shrimp is partially cooked through."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together soy sauce, brown sugar substitute, chili garlic paste, ginger, garlic, lime zest, lime juice, chicken broth and peanut butter. Pour over shrimp and simmer until sauce begins to thicken and shrimp is cooked through."],[null,"Add chopped chives and stir."],[null,"Portion 1/4 cup of shrimp mixture in a lettuce leaf cup and top with diced avocado. Repeat for remaining 6 wrap, dividing avocado evenly among the 7 wraps."]],"h":[]},"6922278":{"s":[[null,"Add cooking spray to a large skillet over medium-high heat. Add sausage, onion, bell pepper and garlic. Sauté until onions are starting to caramelize, about 8 minutes."],[null,"Stir in turmeric and paprika. Add the broth, cauliflower rice, salt and pepper. Bring to boil then reduce heat to low, cover and simmer about 5 minutes."],[null,"Add the shrimp to the pan, then cover and cook until shrimp are just opaque in center, about 6 minutes."]],"h":[]},"1696":{"s":[[null,"Shell and devein shrimp. Rinse and cut into bite-size pieces. Chop cilantro."],[null,"Combine cilantro, lemon juice, cumin and cayenne pepper in a zip-lock bag to make marinade. Add shrimp pieces and set aside to marinate for 5 minutes."],[null,"Heat a skillet to medium heat and add shrimp with marinade. Stir-fry 1 to 2 minutes until shrimp turns orange. Remove skillet from heat and spoon shrimp out, leaving marinade."],[null,"Add sour cream to marinade in skillet and stir to mix."],[null,"Heat tortillas in a large skillet or microwave. Spread 2 teaspoons salsa onto each tortilla. Top with 1/2 shrimp mixture and sprinkle with 1 tablespoon cheese."],[null,"Spoon 1 tablespoon sour cream marinade mixture on top of shrimp. Fold tortilla in half, turn over in skillet to heat, then remove from pan. Repeat with second tortilla and remaining shrimp, cheese and marinade."],[null,"Cut each tortilla into 4 pieces. Garnish with cilantro and lemon wedge when ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Make with crab meat or chicken instead of shrimp for variety."]]},"6536371":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F. Halve or quarter the baby red potatoes, depending on their size. Toss them with 2 tsp olive oil, Italian seasoning, salt, and pepper on a baking sheet."],[null,"Roast in the oven for 20–25 minutes, flipping halfway through, until golden and tender."],[null,"Heat a skillet over medium heat. Add the remaining olive oil and grape tomatoes to the skillet. Cook, stirring occasionally, for 3–4 minutes, or until the tomatoes soften and release some of their juices"],[null,"Add the garlic, shrimp, and crushed red pepper to the skillet. Sauté the shrimp for 1–2 minutes per side, or until opaque and cooked through."],[null,"Add the spinach to the skillet in handfuls, stirring after each addition to allow it to wilt."],[null,"Reduce the heat to low and sprinkle half the grated Parmesan cheese over the skillet contents. Stir to combine, allowing the cheese to melt slightly."],[null,"Divide the shrimp, sautéed veggies, and spinach between plates. Garnish with the reserved Parmesan cheese and basil ribbons. Serve alongside the roasted red potatoes."]],"h":[]},"6052216":{"s":[[null,"Boil spaghetti according to package instructions. Drain and set aside in a large bowl."],[null,"Use a spiralizer or Julienne peeler to create zucchini noodles, set aside."],[null,"Heat olive oil in a large skillet over medium heat. Add onion, garlic, and red pepper flakes. When the onion is translucent, add shrimp and cook until pink."],[null,"Remove from heat, stir in the parsley, and toss to combine. Juice lemon over the shrimp and season with salt and pepper. Pour the shrimp and liquid over the spaghetti."],[null,"Add the zucchini noodles and tomatoes and toss until the zucchini wilts slightly."],[null,"Garnish with parmesan cheese."]],"h":[]},"1923":{"s":[[null,"Set cream cheese out to soften."],[null,"Mince shrimp and stir into cream cheese."],[null,"Stir in ketchup, Tabasco sauce, Worcestershire sauce and Mrs. Dash® herb seasoning."],[null,"Place 1 teaspoon of spread on each cracker. Garnish with minced parsley."]],"h":[[null,"Serve with celery sticks instead of crackers if desired."]]},"4091479":{"s":[[null,"To prepare the sauce, drain crushed pineapple. Reserve pineapple juice."],[null,"In a small saucepan over high heat, add the pineapple juice, crushed pineapple and chili flakes. Bring to a simmer."],[null,"In a small mixing bowl, whisk together cornstarch and rice wine vinegar until well combined."],[null,"Add the cornstarch mixture to the hot pineapple mixture. Cook 1 minute, until sauce is thickened."],[null,"Remove from heat. Refrigerate."],[null,"Bring a medium saucepan of water to a boil. Cook rice vermicelli for 1–2 minutes, or until al dente. Drain. Rinse with cold water. Toss with the canola oil."],[null,"Place a 1/4 cup vermicelli in the center of each lettuce leaf. Roll tight like a burrito."],[null,"Fill a large bowl with hot water. Place one spring roll wrapper into hot water until soft and pliable (10 to 15 seconds)."],[null,"Remove wrapper and blot on a clean paper towel to remove excess water. Lay wrapper flat."],[null,"Build the shrimp spring rolls by placing the lettuce-vermicelli package in the center of the wrapper, leaving about 2\" uncovered on each side. Behind the lettuce-vermicelli package, layer the shrimp, shredded cabbage and mint leaves."],[null,"Fold wrapper sides inward, and then tightly roll the wrapper over the lettuce-vermicelli package. Continue to roll over the shrimp and shredded cabbage until tightly rolled and sealed."],[null,"Serve shrimp spring rolls with pineapple-chili sauce."]],"h":[[null,"Note: The ingredients were layered in this manner to showcase the shrimp but you can layer them in any order."],[null,"* 1/2 serving if not main meal"],["Rice-based ingredients","Asian foods can be a regular part of your kidney diet; it just takes a little planning to stay within your salt, potassium or phosphorus limits. Read labels to identify added sodium or potassium in packaged or canned items. Limit added sauces or seasonings- particularly if you suspect these items may have added salt. With fresh items, such as fruits and vegetables, know the correct portion size and choose many colors to benefit from different vitamins and minerals. Rice-based spring rolls are a healthy alternative to a flour-based tortilla shell. For example, one medium spring roll contains approximately 50 milligrams of sodium and 20 milligrams of potassium. In comparison, a medium flour tortilla has 530 milligrams of sodium and 90 milligrams of potassium. Fill each spring roll with low-potassium meat and vegetables for a delicious meal or snack. Choose shrimp or chicken as a lean protein source. Add small amounts of carrots, cucumber, purple cabbage, green onion and bean sprouts for added crunch and flavor. Season with fresh lime juice, red pepper flakes, ginger or garlic for your at-home version of Asian take-out!"]]},"3436":{"s":[[null,"Shred the cabbage; chop the onion and cilantro; mince the garlic. Set aside."],[null,"Shell and devein the shrimp then place in a dish and squeeze lime juice from half a lime over shrimp. Sprinkle with minced garlic, cumin, chili powder and 1 tablespoon of the olive oil. Turn shrimp to coat with marinade and refrigerate for 15 to 30 minutes."],[null,"Make the salsa blanca by combining mayonnaise, sour cream, milk and juice of half a lime. Stir to combine and place in the refrigerator to chill."],[null,"In a large skillet heat the remaining 1 tablespoon of olive oil over medium-high heat. Add shrimp and cook and stir 2 to 4 minutes until shrimp turns pink. Remove shrimp from skillet. Do not overcook."],[null,"Heat the corn tortillas, one by one, in a pan, until soft and warm. Wrap them in a clean dish towel to keep them warm until ready to serve tacos."],[null,"To assemble tacos place 4 shrimp on each tortilla and top with salsa blanca, cabbage, red onion, cilantro and lime wedges. Add hot sauce if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Use frozen, thawed shrimp instead of fresh if desired."],[null,"Compare hot sauce brands and select the one lowest in sodium."]]},"6445063":{"s":[[null,"Bring water and salt-free seasoning to a boil in a medium saucepan. Reduce heat to just barely a simmer and add shrimp. Cook 6 minutes or until shrimp are pink and just cooked through."],[null,"While shrimp is cooking, add the arugula, yogurt, garlic, olive oil, cashews, Parmesan cheese and black pepper to a blender or food processor. Blend until smooth."],[null,"Drain shrimp and toss with the pesto while shrimp are still hot."]],"h":[]},"1860":{"s":[[null,"Cut cooked eggs in half lenght-wise. Carefully remove yolks and place in a bowl."],[null,"Finely chop shrimp and add to mustard, mayonnaise, lemon juice and pepper to egg yolks. Mix until ingredients are combined."],[null,"Fill egg white halves with shrimp and yolk mixture."]],"h":[[null,"Choose from fresh, frozen or unsalted canned shrimp."],[null,"Chill eggs before serving. Sprinkle with paprika if desired."]]},"6475348":{"s":[[null,"Place olives on a cutting board. Cover with a clean kitchen towel and smash them lightly with a meat hammer or the back of a skillet. (The objective is to slightly crush the olives.)"],[null,"Place olives in a bowl and stir together with remaining ingredients."],[null,"Marinate salad for an hour at room temperature, or cover and chill in refrigerator for at least 1 day and up to 3 days. Bring salad to room temperature before serving."]],"h":[]},"6027027":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the broiler. Place the eggplant slices on a baking sheet. Spray lightly with cooking spray and bake for a few minutes until tender and cooked through. Remove from the oven and set aside."],[null,"Heat olive oil in a large skillet over medium heat. Add the garlic and cook until it releases its aroma. Do not let the garlic turn brown. Stir in the chopped and strained tomatoes, basil, pine nuts, 1/4 tsp of salt, pepper, and pepper flakes. Stir and cover. Reduce heat to low. Simmer for 5 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, place a large piece of wax paper on a work surface. Place the fish fillets on wax paper and cover with another piece. Use a flat-edged meat hammer to pound the fish until they are very thin, about 1/4 inch. Check under the wax paper from time to time to make sure that the fish is not tearing. Cut each piece in half to make 4 pieces."],[null,"Top each piece of fish with thin layers of the eggplant slices. (If you have extra eggplant slices, reserve them as a garnish.) Starting at the wide end, roll up the fish, completely covering the eggplant with the fish. Use toothpicks or skewers to secure the rolls. Slowly remove the lid from the tomato sauce and add rolls to simmering sauce. Cover, and cook for 10-15 minutes, turning once, or until the fish is cooked through."],[null,"Transfer the fish to a serving platter, remove skewers, and top with remaining sauce. Season with the remaining 1/4 tsp salt, if desired. Serve the remaining eggplant slices along the sides of the dish."]],"h":[]},"6739070":{"s":[[null,"Add the lettuce, onion, cucumber, tomato, and olives to a large bowl. Toss to combine. Drizzle with the Red Wine Vinaigrette and toss again to evenly coat the vegetables."]],"h":[]},"6990247":{"s":[[null,"Place olive oil in large sauté pan or skillet. Add beef, onions, and garlic and cook until beef is browned."],[null,"Add vegetables and the seasoning, and mix well. Add the noodles and mix well. Add the broth and enough water to cover everything."],[null,"Bring to a boil. Reduce heat to medium and cook until noodles are tender, approximately 15 minutes."]],"h":[]},"1699":{"s":[[null,"Wash cucumber, cut in half vertically and remove seeds with a spoon. Cut into pieces."],[null,"Place all ingredients in a food processor or high powered blender. Blend until smooth."],[null,"Chill soup covered in the refrigerator at least 2 hours or overnight."]],"h":[[null,"Silken tofu is softer than regular soft tofu. It works well in soups and smoothies. Tofu is a high biological value vegetarian protein source."],[null,"This soup is a great choice for those with chewing or swallowing difficulty."],[null,"Adjust fresh dill and black pepper according to your taste."]]},"9571235":{"s":[[null,"Use a well-seasoned cast iron pan or nonstick skillet. Grease first, if necessary. Heat your pan on your stovetop over medium heat and once hot, place the tofu block inside."],[null,"Use a fork or spatula to break it into very large chunks and let it cook undisturbed for 4-5 minutes until golden. Then flip and cook the other side for 2-3 minutes longer, until most of the water from the tofu has evaporated. (Use care when flipping soft or silken tofu as it may break apart as you mix it. That's why we're starting off with large chunks first.)"],[null,"Add all the seasoning, except the black salt, and mix to evenly coat. At this point, you may break up the tofu pieces a bit more, if needed."],[null,"Turn off the heat, sprinkle with the black salt and serve."]],"h":[[null,"For oil free , use a newer nonstick pan or well-seasoned cast iron skillet. If your iron pan is not well seasoned, the tofu scramble may stick. Start with large (approx. 1.5-2 inch chunks) of your silken tofu. The tofu will shrink considerably as it cooks out the water. Don’t flip the tofu too often or you may break it down more than you’d like and it could turn a little mushy. At the end of cooking , you may break down the tofu more IF NEEDED ."]]},"5741556":{"s":[[null,"Warm the Renastep gently in a pan to no more than 30˚C. Meanwhile, mix the flour and sugar in a bowl."],[null,"Add the dried yeast and Renastep and mix well until a soft dough is formed."],[null,"Place the dough onto a clean work surface dusted with flour. Knead the dough for for 5 minutes until the dough feels stretchy."],[null,"Place the dough in a clean bowl, cover and leave to prove for an hour, until doubled in size."],[null,"Heat oven to 200˚C/180˚C fan/gas mark 6."],[null,"Toast the sesame seeds in a dry frying pan for 2-3 minutes until golden and set aside."],[null,"Mix the pomegranate molasses or molasses syrup with 50ml water in a shallow bowl."],[null,"When the dough has risen, roll out onto a clean, dusted work surface into a sausage shape about 45cm long and cut in half."],[null,"Place the two pieces lengthways together continuously twist them over each other for the full length of dough. Cut the twist into 2 equal pieces. Brush both sides with the molasses water."],[null,"Pour the toasted sesame seeds onto a piece of parchment paper and roll each twist of dough through the seeds until well covered. On a baking tray, join the ends of each twist to form two circles, cover and leave to prove for another 10 minutes."],[null,"When the bread has risen, uncover and bake for 15-18 mins until golden. Allow to cool before serving."]],"h":[["Renastep note","Renastep is a Food for Special Medical Purposes and must be used under medical supervision. Renastep is a ready to use feed for the dietary management of kidney disease from 3 years of age onwards. Renastep contains milk and fish. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information. This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutrimen dietary analysis software."]]},"6942761":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the soy sauce, olive oil, rice vinegar, and ginger. Drizzle the soy sauce mixture onto the rice and toss to evenly coat. Add the scallions and toss to incorporate."],[null,"In a saucepan over high heat, bring the rice and broth to a boil. Reduce the heat to medium low and simmer until the rice is tender, about 40 minutes. (Alternatively, you can use a rice cooker to cook the rice.) Fluff the rice with a fork and place in a large bowl."]],"h":[]},"6055302":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 450° F."],[null,"In a large bowl, toss cauliflower with rosemary, olive oil, salt, and pepper. Spread seasoned cauliflower on a large baking sheet (use two sheets if they are crowded on one)."],[null,"Roast for 15 minutes; remove from oven and stir."],[null,"Continue roasting for 10 minutes or until cauliflower is tender and lightly browned."]],"h":[]},"6386005":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425°F. Toss peppers together in a large bowl. Add oil, salt, and pepper. Toss to combine and spread out onto a large baking sheet."],[null,"Roast until tender, 20–25 minutes."],[null,"Transfer veggies to a serving dish. Squeeze lemon juice over peppers and garnish with parsley."]],"h":[]},"6672724":{"s":[[null,"Add the mixed greens, cucumbers, and tomatoes to a large bowl. Toss to combine."],[null,"Drizzle with the Light Balsamic Vinaigrette and toss again to evenly coat the vegetables."]],"h":[]},"6720715":{"s":[[null,"Cut each cucumber half in half and slice into large chunks. Cut cherry tomatoes in half."],[null,"Place the cucumber in a salad bowl with the cherry tomatoes and diced red onion."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the red wine vinegar, black pepper, olive oil, and salt. Pour the dressing over the salad and serve."]],"h":[]},"6926231":{"s":[[null,"Drain the 1/2 cup canned tuna and place it in a small bowl."],[null,"Add 1 tablespoon mayonnaise and mix until the tuna is evenly coated."],[null,"Arrange the 2 tomato slices on a plate."],[null,"Spoon the tuna mixture on top of the tomato slices or serve alongside them."],[null,"Enjoy immediately."]],"h":[]},"6510629":{"s":[[null,"In a bowl, mix together the shrimp, garlic, paprika, and chili powder, tossing to coat. Add 1 tsp. of the olive oil and the lemon juice. Let stand 3 minutes."],[null,"In a large skillet, heat the remaining 2 tsp. oil over medium-high heat. Add the shrimp and sauté on both sides for a total of 3 minutes, or until the shrimp is just opaque and cooked through."]],"h":[]},"1898":{"s":[[null,"Prepare the rice noodles according to the package directions and drain. Set aside in a bowl."],[null,"Slice snow peas thin on the bias. Slice carrots into thin matchsticks. Thinly slice the white bulb of scallions. Finely chop cilantro."],[null,"In another bowl mix together the chicken broth, soy sauce, curry powder, garlic powder and oil and set aside."],[null,"Heat broth mixture in a non-stick frying pan. Cover and cook on high until boiling then lower to medium heat. Add the snow peas and carrots, and cook until snow peas turn bright green and carrots have softened. Turn off the heat. Add half the cilantro and cooked rice noodles and mix together. Cover."],[null,"Spray another frying pan with non-stick cooking spray and place over medium heat. In a small bowl mix the eggs with a fork vigorously until well combined. When the pan is hot, add eggs, stirring as it cooks. When completely cooked through, chop into small pieces with a fork."],[null,"Add eggs to the rice noodle and vegetable mixture and mix together. Serve in individual bowls. Add the chopped scallions and remaining cilantro on top as a garnish."]],"h":[[null,"Compare and select the lowest sodium brand of rice noodles."],[null,"Adjust curry powder to taste."],[null,"For a higher protein, one-dish meal add cooked chicken or shrimp."],[null,"Use low-sodium vegetable broth for a vegetarian dish."]]},"1767":{"s":[[null,"Soak rice vermicelli noodles in a bowl of hot water from the tap (~10-15 mins)."],[null,"Mince garlic. Chop bell pepper and onion. Peel and thinly slice carrot."],[null,"Scramble the eggs in a bowl. Add 1 teaspoon of water, 1 teaspoon of low sodium soy, and black or white pepper."],[null,"Heat a skillet or wok on high heat with 1 tablespoon of oil until shiny on surface."],[null,"Quickly cook scrambled eggs until solid, remove from pan."],[null,"Place same skillet or wok back on high heat with another 1 tablespoon of oil."],[null,"Add minced garlic, sliced carrot, onion, and bell pepper, stir fry for 3-4 mins until crisp and tender, remove from skillet."],[null,"Drain the vermicelli noodles well in a colander. Drizzle remaining tablespoon of oil in the pan, add curry powder, stir in oil for 30 seconds until fragrant, remaining teaspoon of low sodium soy sauce."],[null,"Add noodles to the curry and oil mixture, toss well to coat, about 5 minutes. Add the vegetables and egg back to the pan for another 3-4 minutes. Remove from heat and top with (optional) scallions and another dash of pepper if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Prep vegetables and scrambled eggs in 2 separate bowls. When stir-frying it is best to work in steps with each batch of ingredients, until all combined."],[null,"If you are following a diabetic diet, you may use half of the rice noodles called for in the recipe. This will bring the carbohydrate down to 33 grams per serving."],[null,"Optional garnish: Two thinly sliced scallions can be used as garnish and distributed among the portions."]]},"7812028":{"s":[[null,"Simply thread the fruit onto cocktail sticks or skewers."],[null,"If you are making the sauce, place the strawberries and sweetener in a blender and blend until smooth, adding a little water if the sauce is too thick."],[null,"Spoon the berry sauce and the fromage frais into separate bowls and use as dips for the kebabs."]],"h":[[null,"Use an unsweetened soya-based yoghurt instead of fromage frais if you are lactose-intolerant or vegan."],[null,"The fruit sauce is optional, as blending fruit releases its natural sugars and turns them into free sugars. Whole fruit is a healthier choice, so you may prefer to enjoy the recipe without the sauce or just use a small amount."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"6568402":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400°F. In a small, dry skillet, toast the caraway seeds over medium heat for 2 to 3 minutes, just until lightly browned and fragrant; set aside. When the oven is hot, add 2 tsp. of the vegetable oil to a 9-inch cast-iron skillet. Heat the pan in the oven for 5 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, in a large bowl, mix the cornmeal, flour, baking powder, baking soda, salt, and caraway seeds."],[null,"In a separate bowl, beat the eggs with a wire whisk. Add the buttermilk, honey, and the 1/4 cup vegetable oil."],[null,"Add the wet ingredients to the dry ingredients and mix until just combined."],[null,"Carefully add the batter to the hot skillet and bake for 20 to 22 minutes, or until the cornbread is cooked through and a cake tester or toothpick inserted in the middle comes out clean. Let the cornbread cool for 5 minutes. Cut into 16 same-sized wedges and serve warm."]],"h":[]},"6288136":{"s":[[null,"Heat 1 teaspoon oil in a large nonstick skillet over medium-high heat. Cook fish 5 minutes on each side or until it flakes with a fork. Set aside on separate plate."],[null,"Add the remaining ingredients to the skillet, reduce the heat to medium, cover, and cook 5 minutes or until thickened slightly. Spoon over fish. Serve in shallow bowls, if desired."]],"h":[]},"6250256":{"s":[],"h":[]},"3766":{"s":[[null,"Chop the onion. Slice the rolls in half and set aside."],[null,"Divide the ground beef into 12 patties, making them slightly larger in diameter than the rolls."],[null,"In a large skillet over medium heat, sauté the onion in oil until translucent."],[null,"Place ground beef patties on top of the onions and fry until done, pressing down so that the onions will press into the patties."],[null,"Place a beef patty in each roll, top with 1/2 teaspoon mustard and 1 pickle chip before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Serve as an appetizer or double up for a main entrée."],[null,"Look for the lowest sodium sweet pickle chips brand."]]},"6474350":{"s":[],"h":[]},"2400":{"s":[[null,"Slice the carrots, green onions and celery. Crush the garlic. Rinse and slice the bamboo shoots and water chestnuts."],[null,"Heat the oil in a skillet and brown chicken on all sides."],[null,"Transfer chicken to a slow cooker."],[null,"Add all ingredients except the cornstarch and water. Stir, then cover and cook on low heat setting for 6 to 8 hours."],[null,"Turn slow cooker to high. Combine cornstarch and cold water, stirring until smooth, then stir into the slow cooker liquid. Position slow cooker lid ajar to allow steam to escape. Cook on high until thickened, about 15 minutes."],[null,"Serve chicken and vegetables over rice."]],"h":[[null,"Adjust portion size to 1/2 chicken breast for a lower protein eating plan."],[null,"Serve over white or brown rice."]]},"6259731":{"s":[[null,"Place the chicken breasts in a slow cooker. Sprinkle with the garlic powder and pepper. Place the sliced onion on top of the chicken. Pour in 1 cup water. Cover and cook on low for 6 hours, or until done."],[null,"Drain the cooking water from the slow cooker. Shred the chicken with two forks. Mix in the barbeque sauce and stir to coat the chicken. Heat through for an additional 15 minutes."],[null,"Assemble the sandwiches, using 1/3 cup BBQ chicken for each bun."]],"h":[]},"6914294":{"s":[[null,"In a large skillet over medium-high heat, heat 1 tablespoon of olive oil. Brown the beef chunks on all sides. Transfer the browned beef to the slow cooker."],[null,"In the same skillet, add the remaining tablespoon of oil if needed. Sauté the onions and garlic until softened."],[null,"Deglaze the skillet with water, scraping up any browned bits. Add tomato paste and stir to combine."],[null,"Transfer the onion and tomato mixture to the slow cooker."],[null,"Add carrots, turnips, dried thyme, bay leaves, salt and pepper to the slow cooker."],[null,"Pour the low sodium tomato sauce and the beef broth over the ingredients in the slow cooker."],[null,"Cover and cook on low for 6–8 hours or until the beef is tender."],[null,"Before serving, discard bay leaves and adjust the seasoning if necessary."]],"h":[]},"6679003":{"s":[[null,"In a large skillet, heat olive oil over medium heat. Add onion and sauté for 3–4 minutes until softened. Stir in garlic, ginger, garam masala, cumin, coriander, turmeric, and cayenne pepper. Cook for 1 minute until fragrant."],[null,"Transfer the onion mixture to the slow cooker. Add chicken, carrots, zucchini, crushed tomatoes, coconut milk, and salt. Stir to combine."],[null,"Cover and cook on low for 6–8 hours or high for 3–4 hours until the chicken is tender and fully cooked."],[null,"Once the chicken is cooked, stir in Greek yogurt to create a creamy sauce."],[null,"Divide the cooked brown rice among 4 bowls or plates. Spoon the butter chicken and vegetables over the rice. Garnish with fresh cilantro."]],"h":[]},"1932":{"s":[[null,"Remove chicken from the bones and skin. Shred then place in a slow cooker."],[null,"Pour the dressing and cranberry sauce over the chicken and stir to combine."],[null,"Cook on low setting for 4 hours."]],"h":[[null,"An average rotisserie chicken has approximately 3 cups of meat."],[null,"Look for minimally seasoned rotisserie chicken for a lower sodium content."],[null,"To reduce sodium replace rotisserie chicken with uncooked chicken pieces. Add ingredients and cook in the crockpot for 6 to 8 hours on low or 4 to 6 hours on high."],[null,"Compare dressing brands and select the one lowest in sodium."],[null,"Serve chicken over rice if desired."]]},"1971":{"s":[[null,"Combine carrots, green beans and onion. Place in a 4 or 6 quart slow cooker."],[null,"Arrange chicken breasts on top of vegetables."],[null,"Pour broth over chicken. Top with Worcestershire sauce and herb seasoning."],[null,"Cover and cook on high heat for 3 hours or low heat for 6 hours."],[null,"Serve chicken breast with 3/4 cup vegetables and 2 tablespoons broth."]],"h":[[null,"Look for reduced-sodium broth containing 500 milligrams sodium or less per 1 cup serving. Avoid low sodium broth that contains potassium chloride—it’s very high in potassium."],[null,"If desired, make gravy with pan broth. In a small saucepan mix 1 tablespoon flour with small amount cold water to dissolve. Turn heat to medium high and stir in broth from slow cooker. Continue stirring 3 to 4 minutes until gravy thickens."]]},"3824":{"s":[[null,"Pour the milk and rice milk into a 3 quart crock pot. Add the cinnamon."],[null,"Cover and turn to low heat setting. Cook for 1-1/2 to 2 hours to infuse the milk with the cinnamon flavor."],[null,"Add the white chocolate syrup, brown sugar blend, vanilla and additional cinnamon if desired. Let cook for 30-45 minutes covered."],[null,"For each serving pour 6 ounces into a small coffee cup and garnish with a tablespoon of marshmallow fluff and a drizzle of sugar-free caramel syrup."]],"h":[[null,"If you are looking for a way to increase protein intake add 1/2 cup whey protein powder or other protein supplement suggested by your dietitian to the milk mixture."],[null,"If you need higher calories you can use the regular syrups instead of sugar-free."]]},"1988":{"s":[[null,"Cut chicken thighs into 1″ size pieces, Coat chicken with flour and add to slow cooker.,"],[null,"Add onion, carrots, celery and chicken broth."],[null,"Cover with lid and cook on high setting for 4 hours."],[null,"Stir in cream cheese and peas."],[null,"Cover and cook for additional 30 minutes."],[null,"Garnish with chives and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Serve with warmed bread or over steamed white rice."],[null,"For a lower protein diet reduce portion to 1/2 cup (14 grams protein)."]]},"6473360":{"s":[[null,"Spray a slow cooker with cooking spray."],[null,"In a medium bowl, mix together ricotta cheese, Parmesan cheese, 1/4 cup mozzarella cheese, and spinach."],[null,"Spread 1 cup pasta sauce on bottom of slow cooker. Arrange 3 noodles side by side on top of sauce, break noodles apart to fit, if needed."],[null,"Spread about 1/3 cup of ricotta-spinach mixture on top of noodles. Repeat layering with pasta sauce, noodles and ricotta spinach mixture 2 more times. Top with remaining pasta sauce and canned tomato sauce. Sprinkle top with 1 cup mozzarella cheese."],[null,"Place cover on slow cooker. Cook on low setting for 2–3 hours or until done (cooking times vary based on slow cooker)."],[null,"* This recipe was tested with gluten-free lasagna noodles, but whole-wheat lasagna noodles could be used."]],"h":[]},"3095":{"s":[[null,"Core and cut each apple into 8 pieces and place in a slow cooker."],[null,"Sprinkle cinnamon over apple pieces and toss to coat."],[null,"Drizzle with honey, add butter and stir."],[null,"Set slow cooker to low temperature, cover with a lid and cook for 2 hours."]],"h":[[null,"This recipe can also be prepared in the oven. Cook at 325° F for 45 to 60 minutes."]]},"3681":{"s":[[null,"To prepare the carrots, peel, slice in half long ways, and cut each half into 4 pieces. Place in the slow cooker."],[null,"Add vinaigrette dressing, jelly, black pepper and herb seasoning. Stir to coat carrots."],[null,"Set slow cooker on low heat, cover with a lid and cook 3 to 4 hours until carrots are tender."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute frozen carrots or whole baby carrots instead of regular size raw carrots. No cutting required."]]},"2744":{"s":[[null,"Trim excess fat off of the boneless leg of lamb and then place in the slow cooker."],[null,"Roughly chop the carrots, celery and onion. Finely chop the fresh rosemary and thyme."],[null,"Place all ingredients on top of lamb in the slow cooker and cover with lid."],[null,"Set slow cooker to high setting for 5 to 6 hours or until lamb is cooked through and can easily be pulled apart with a fork."]],"h":[[null,"Serve with rice or pasta for a complete meal."],[null,"Makes great leftovers, and freezes well."],[null,"If using low heat setting cook for 8 to 10 hours."],[null,"For a lower protein diet reduce lamb portion to 2 ounces."]]},"3862":{"s":[[null,"Cut bread into cubes and place in slow cooker. Sprinkle with cinnamon."],[null,"Drain juice from fruit, reserving in a separate bowl. Add fruit to slow cooker."],[null,"In a mixing bowl whisk melted butter, rice milk, drained juice, eggs and brown sugar until combined. Pour mixture over bread and fruit."],[null,"Cover with lid and cook on high setting for 2 hours."]],"h":[[null,"Use day old bread for best results."]]},"4469334":{"s":[[null,"Turn the slow cooker** setting to LOW."],[null,"Add the shallots and mushrooms to the bottom of the slow cooker. Make a mixture with the beef broth and cornstarch. Pour over the vegetables."],[null,"Mix the rosemary, thyme, garlic powder, and pepper and rub the roast with it. Place the roast on top of the vegetables and close the lid."],[null,"After 7 1/2 hours, check for doneness. The roast should be fork tender."],[null,"Add the green beans to the slow cooker and continue cooking for 30 more minutes."],[null,"Serve pot roast with noodles or rice."]],"h":[[null,"* Choose the broth with the lowest sodium content but be aware that low sodium products often contain more potassium. Look for potassium chloride under ingredients on the label. You can replace the beef stock with water."],[null,"** If using the oven: Choose 350°F and roast in a Dutch oven or heavy pot for 3 hours (covered)."]]},"3579":{"s":[[null,"Dice the onion. Slice the celery and carrots."],[null,"Place the turkey breast in a slow cooker and sprinkle with poultry seasoning and bouillon granules."],[null,"Spoon cranberry sauce on top; add the vegetables."],[null,"Cover slow cooker with a lid, turn heat to high and cook for 4 hours."],[null,"Remove turkey breast and slice. Serve with vegetables and cranberry gravy."]],"h":[[null,"Whole turkey breast may be substituted for boneless turkey."],[null,"Spray slow cooker pot with nonstick cooking spray or use a slow cooker liner for easier cleanup."],[null,"Frozen onion and carrots may be used instead of fresh vegetables."],[null,"A very small portion of regular bouillon adds flavor. Portion control helps keep sodium content within the limits of a low-sodium diet."],[null,"Serve with noodles, rolls, margarine and fruit salad."]]},"9389346":{"s":[["Slow Cooker Instructions","Add all the ingredients except the water, corn starch and milk to your slow cooker. Cook on low for 8 hours."],["Slow Cooker Instructions","Switch the slow cooker to high. Then in a small bowl or jar, combine your water and corn starch and mix well. Add this mixture to your slow cooker and cook on high for 30 minutes. This will thicken your stew."],["Slow Cooker Instructions","Turn off your slow cooker, stir in the milk and serve."],["Instant Pot Instructions","Add all the ingredients except the water, corn starch and milk to your pot, and pressure cook on high pressure for 6 minutes."],["Instant Pot Instructions","Meanwhile, whisk the water and cornstarch in a small bowl and set aside."],["Instant Pot Instructions","When the timer completes, quick release the steam valve and open the lid once safe to do so. Switch the pot to the sauté function and pour the cornstarch slurry into the pot and sauté for 5 minutes, stirring often. Then turn off the pot, stir in the milk and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"The corn starch is needed to thicken your broth . If you cannot have corn starch, you may sub for all-purpose flour or brown rice flour at twice the amount. (So 8 tablespoons of flour and water for your slurry.) Slow cookers vary greatly, so if you find your veggies are not getting soft enough after cooking several hours on low, switch your appliance to high for the remaining cook time. For added protein , add canned white kidney beans or lentils towards the end of cooking. Or you may use blended silken tofu to replace the milk. To make this dish even richer (although this will up the fat content), use canned coconut milk (light for less fat) to replace the cashew milk at the end of cooking. Leftovers keep refrigerated for up to 4 days, or freeze for up to 3 months. You may sub the potatoes for sweet potatoes, or do a half and half mix, if preferred."]]},"1921":{"s":[[null,"Remove giblets from cavity and wash chicken; trim extra skin and visible fat."],[null,"Sprinkle part of the pepper inside the cavity. Place onion and celery pieces inside cavity. Sprinkle remaining pepper over chicken."],[null,"Place whole chicken in slow cooker, breast side down. Cook on high setting for 4 hours, until thigh and leg easily pull away and meat easily comes of f the bones."],[null,"Remove skin and discard. Remove meat from bones and separate into 3 portions to use in suggested recipes listed below."],[null,"If desired, use stock from cooked chicken to make soup or freeze for later use in recipes."]],"h":[[null,"A four-pound chicken yields 27 ounces of meat when skinned and deboned (approximately 4 cups)."],[null,"If desired, use stock from cooked chicken to make soup or freeze for later use in recipes."],[null,"For CKD non-dialysis, adjust the portion size according to your meal plan or consult your dietitian for guidance if you are on a low-protein diet."],[null,"Tortilla Rollups (use chicken instead of turkey)"],[null,"Chicken Fruit Salad"],[null,"Cool ‘n’ Crunchy Chicken Salad"],[null,"Lemon Curry Chicken Salad"],[null,"Chicken Fajitas"],[null,"Chicken Lettuce Wraps"],[null,"Crunchy Chicken Wraps"],[null,"Easy Chicken Enchiladas"],[null,"Moroccan Chicken Soup"],[null,"Myrna’s Scalloped Chicken"],[null,"Tasty Chicken Salad for Sandwiches"]]},"3501":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 325° F."],[null,"Shake flour into roasting bag."],[null,"Slice the onion. Put half the onion slices in the chicken cavity."],[null,"Place the bag in a roasting pan and add remaining onion slices. Place the chicken on top of the onion."],[null,"Sprinkle the chicken with salt, pepper and poultry seasoning. Close the bag according to package directions and slit the bag in 6 places."],[null,"Bake for 2 hours or until thermometer reads 165° F."],[null,"Remove from oven and let stand for 10 to 15 minutes; carefully open bag. Remove contents to a serving dish and pour sauce from bag into a gravy bowl."]],"h":[[null,"Instead of poultry season try a tablespoon of combined fresh thyme, oregano, marjoram, or several sprigs rosemary. If using fresh herbs place some in the cavity and some between the skin of the chicken and the breast meat."],[null,"Add peeled carrots and celery to bag, if desired."],[null,"The whole fresh or frozen chicken does not have phosphate additives frequently found in store-roasted chicken."],[null,"For a lower or higher protein diet adjust the portion to match your meal plan."]]},"6702969":{"s":[[null,"Combine eggs, milk, bread crumbs, onion, salt, sage, fennel, and mushrooms in a large bowl. Break up ground turkey over mixture and stir well to combine."],[null,"Shape into a round loaf; place in a 5-quart slow cooker. Cover and cook on low until a meat thermometer reads 165°F, 5–6 hours. (Or, if desired bake in 350°F oven [325°F for a convection oven] for 35–45 minutes until meat reaches an internal temperature of 165°F.)"],[null,"Whisk ketchup, brown sugar, mustard, and Worcestershire sauce in a small bowl; spoon sauce over meat loaf. Return to slow cooker and cook on low until heated through, about 15 minutes. Let stand 10 minutes before cutting."]],"h":[]},"6338529":{"s":[[null,"Remove inside giblets from the chicken if they are included (save them for making chicken broth). Pat the chicken dry with paper towels."],[null,"In a small bowl combine seasoning blend, pepper and garlic powder. Sprinkle half the seasonings inside the chicken. Rub the remaining seasoning on the outside of the chicken."],[null,"Place the chicken breast-side-up in an oval slow cooker or neck-up in a round slow cooker. Cover and cook on low setting for 8 hours."],[null,"Remove chicken from bones and discard the skin. Serve now, or store cooked chicken in the fridge for 3-5 days."]],"h":[]},"6504859":{"s":[[null,"Place the flour in a large resealable plastic bag. Add beef and toss to coat."],[null,"Add oil to a pan over high heat. Add beef and sauté for 6-8 minutes, turning frequently until evenly browned."],[null,"Transfer beef and all remaining ingredients to a large slow cooker."],[null,"Cover and cook in slow cooker on low for 8 hours."]],"h":[]},"6105903":{"s":[[null,"Place the flank steak in a slow-cooker. Sprinkle the meat with chili powder, cumin, and garlic powder. Pour the lime juice over the steak. Pour in the water."],[null,"Cover and cook on low for 6 hours or until done. Shred the steak with a fork."],[null,"Scoop about 1 1/2 ounces steak into each tortilla. Top each taco with 1 Tbsp. pico de gallo."]],"h":[]},"6837664":{"s":[[null,"Brush the inside of the slow cooker with the olive oil. Add the remaining ingredients to the slow cooker; stir to combine."],[null,"Cover and cook on low for 6 hours, until the vegetables and beans soften. Remove and discard the bay leaves before serving."]],"h":[]},"6914849":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 300°F. Toss together the fennel, orange and lemon slices, and jalapeño pepper in a 9-by-13-inch baking pan."],[null,"Lay the cod pieces next to the citrus mixture. Scatter the thyme sprigs over the fish. Drizzle with the olive oil and sprinkle with the salt and pepper."],[null,"Roast the fish for 25 to 30 minutes, or until it is opaque and cooked through. Serve the fish with the roasted fennel and citrus."]],"h":[]},"7273074":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 150°C/ gas 2. Mix the garlic, oregano, pepper and olive oil, crushing it all together with the back of a spoon."],[null,"Cut the tomatoes in half through the middle (equator). Then - with the tomatoes cut side up - make a few cuts into the centre of each half, being careful not to pierce through to the skin."],[null,"Divide the garlic mixture between the tomatoes, gently pushing it into the flesh."],[null,"Place on a lightly oiled baking sheet and bake in the over for 1 hour."]],"h":[[null,"These tomatoes will keep in the fridge for up to two days and can be reheated when needed."],[null,"This dish is fantastic served on toasted ciabatta, or with grilled meat or fish."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6309831":{"s":[],"h":[]},"9193815":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 450°F (232°C)."],[null,"Put the potatoes in a saucepan. Pour 1 cup (240 mof the vinegar over them, and add the salt. Top up with enough cold water to just cover the potatoes. Bring to a boil and cook for about 7 minutes, or until you can just insert a fork into them but they aren’t yet cooked through. Drain immediately and let sit in the colander for a few minutes to steam dry."],[null,"Return the potatoes to the saucepan you boiled them in and toss with the olive oil; then spread out on a large baking sheet in a single layer with room between each potato. Bake for 30 minutes, and then remove from the oven. Smash each potato with a potato masher or the bottom of a mug so it flattens and splits. Drizzle with the remaining ¼ cup (60 ml) of vinegar, making sure to do it as evenly as you can. Then return the pan to the oven and bake again for about another 30 minutes, or until really golden and crispy."],[null,"Sprinkle with a generous scattering of flaky sea salt and serve immediately"]],"h":[]},"6211497":{"s":[[null,"Steam the broccoli florets until they are just tender, about 5 minutes. Alternatively, blanch them in boiling water for 3–4 minutes. Drain and set aside."],[null,"Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium heat."],[null,"Add the red pepper flakes and minced garlic to the skillet. Sauté for 1–2 minutes until the garlic is fragrant."],[null,"Add the steamed broccoli to the skillet."],[null,"Using a fork or potato masher, gently smash the broccoli, allowing it to absorb the flavors of the garlic and red pepper flakes."],[null,"Continue cooking for an additional 5–7 minutes, stirring occasionally, until the broccoli edges are crispy and golden brown."],[null,"Zest the lemon over the smashed broccoli and squeeze the lemon juice on top."],[null,"Season with the salt and black pepper. Toss to combine."]],"h":[]},"6120286":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F."],[null,"Combine the beans, olives, garlic, shallot, rosemary, paprika, and salt in a baking dish."],[null,"Pour the oil over the mixture and stir to combine. Place in the oven and bake for 30 minutes, stirring halfway through. Serve warm."]],"h":[]},"6751867":{"s":[[null,"Cut the ends off of the cucumber. Slice into 24 rounds, about ¼-inch thick"],[null,"Chop 2 tbsp of the dill and add to a medium bowl. Remove the stems from the rest of the dill and separate into small sprigs. Set the sprigs aside."],[null,"In the medium bowl with the chopped dill, add the cream cheese, lemon zest and juice and pepper to the bowl."],[null,"Spread about 1 tsp of the cream cheese mixture onto each cucumber slice. Top each one with a piece of salmon and garnish with a dill sprig. Arrange on a platter and enjoy!"]],"h":[]},"6016224":{"s":[[null,"Toast the slices of whole grain or whole wheat bread until golden brown."],[null,"While the bread is toasting, cut the avocado in half, remove the pit, and scoop the flesh into a bowl. Mash the avocado with a fork until smooth and spreadable."],[null,"Spread the mashed avocado evenly over the toasted bread."],[null,"Drape smoked salmon slices over the avocado."],[null,"Serve with lemon wedges and fresh parsley for garnish."]],"h":[]},"7026697":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200ºC/gas 6."],[null,"Roll out the pastry thinly. Stamp out about 36 x 5cm rounds with a pastry cutter and use to line mini tartlet tins. Bake blind for 10 minutes."],[null,"Beat together the egg and crème fraiche, season well then stir through the chives and salmon."],[null,"Spoon a little mixture into each of the pastry cases and cook for about 10 minutes, until golden and set."],[null,"Allow to cool a little and serve."]],"h":[[null,"For a veggie version, use sliced sundried tomatoes to replace the smoked salmon."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"6357497":{"s":[[null,"In a bowl, whisk the eggs, egg whites, milk, salt, and pepper until smooth."],[null,"Heat the olive oil in a nonstick skillet over medium-low heat. Pour ¼ of the egg mixture into the skillet, swirling to coat the bottom. Cook until the edges start to set, about 2 minutes."],[null,"Add ¼ of the smoked salmon, a dollop of Greek yogurt, fresh dill, and red onion to one side of the omelet."],[null,"Carefully fold the omelet over the filling and cook for 30 seconds to warm through."],[null,"Transfer to a plate and repeat with remaining ingredients."]],"h":[]},"9790342":{"s":[[null,"Slice your block of tofu into rectangles that are approx. 1/4 inch thick."],[null,"Then place a clean dish towel (or paper towels) on a cutting board and arrange the slices in a single layer on top. Add another clean towel on top of the slices, followed by another cutting board (or flat baking pan). Then finally, place something heavy like a cast iron pan, or heavy books on top. Keep it like this for 15 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, add all the marinade ingredients to a small bowl and stir to combine."],[null,"Arrange the pressed tofu in a wide but shallow dish in a single layer and pour the marinade on top. Refrigerate for 60 minutes, and carefully flip the slices at the halfway point."],[null,"When your tofu has about 10 minutes of soak time left, preheat the oven to 400°F/204°C and line a baking sheet with parchment paper. Arrange the slices in a single layer and bake for 15 minutes. Then flip them and bake another 15-18 minutes.NOTE: Reserve the marinating liquid!"],["Optional: For grilling the smoked tofu","Heat a nonstick grill, or lightly grease your grill if needed."],["Optional: For grilling the smoked tofu","Pour the leftover marinade into a small saucepot and add 1/3 cup of water and a tablespoon of tapioca flour. Whisk well and simmer over medium heat for 2-3 minutes to thicken and make your BBQ sauce."],["Optional: For grilling the smoked tofu","Brush both sides of the smoked tofu slices with your sauce and place them on the grill on a diagonal to make grill lines, approx. 1-2 minutes on each side."]],"h":[[null,"Plan ahead ! You can marinate the tofu one day in advance to save time on the day you’re serving it."],[null,"Although the total time required is a little over 2 hours, note that this is not all active time and the tofu marinates in the fridge for 1 hour."],[null,"Leftovers will keep in the fridge for 3-4 days in a sealed container."]]},"4337918":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven on low broil."],[null,"Heat oil in a pan over medium-high heat. Combine ingredients for patties in a bowl, mix gently, and form 2 patties."],[null,"Cook patties for approximately 3–5 minutes* on each side."],[null,"Place bread on a baking sheet in the middle of the oven and toast lightly, turning once. Remove from oven and rub the bread with the garlic clove."],[null,"Place the bread on a baking sheet and garnish each bread slice with 2 slices of fire-roasted red peppers and 2 slices of fresh mozzarella. Broil the bread for 2 minutes or until cheese is well melted."],[null,"Transfer bread to a plate and assemble each with 2 leaves of Bibb lettuce and a hot burger."]],"h":[[null,"* Use a thermometer to be sure that the meat reaches an internal temperature of 165°F."],["Enjoy your burger","In the warmer months of the year, nothing tastes better than a burger cooked fresh from the grill. From the smell and the first delicious bite, burgers are known as a favorite summer food. You can enjoy burgers as part of your kidney diet, just consider a few key tips to lower potassium and sodium in your meal. Make at home: You can limit the fat content of your burger as well as unwanted sodium and potassium by making burger patties at home. Choose unseasoned, lean ground beef or turkey. Make 3-ounce patties, which are roughly the size of a deck of cards. When seasoning, use salt-free choices such as pepper, garlic, and fresh herbs. Select the right bread: Remember portion sizes when choosing the bun. Bigger is not necessarily better. Selecting a whole wheat bun can add fiber to your meal, but read labels to ensure your choice does not have extra salt or potassium preservatives. Choose good toppings: Burgers can be topped with lettuce, onion, and other low-potassium vegetables. Limit cheese and tomatoes. If you like mayonnaise, ketchup, or mustard, use a small amount or read labels to select lower-sodium condiments."]]},"4872286":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven on low broil."],[null,"Heat oil in a pan over medium-high heat."],[null,"Combine first 6 ingredients in a bowl, mix gently and form 2 patties."],[null,"Brown patties and cook on each side for 3 minutes.*"],[null,"Place bread on a baking sheet in the middle of the oven and roast lightly turning once."],[null,"Remove from oven and rub the bread with the garlic clove. Set bread aside."],[null,"Place the bread on a baking sheet and garnish each bread slice with 2 slices of fire-roasted red pepper and 2 slices of bocconcini. Broil the bread for 2 minutes or until cheese is well melted."],[null,"Transfer bread to a plate and garnish each with 2 leafs of bib lettuce and the hot burger."]],"h":[[null,"* We encourage you to use a meat thermometer to be sure that the burger is cooked. The internal temperature should be 170°F."]]},"6435485":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, combine the ground beef, smoked paprika, grated zucchini, and 1 tablespoon of the barbecue sauce. Mix thoroughly using clean hands, then shape the mixture into four patties, each about ¾-inch thick."],[null,"Preheat a large grill pan over medium-high heat. Lightly brush the patties and portobello mushrooms with olive oil. Place the mushrooms on the grill and cook for 4-5 minutes on each side until they are tender and have light char marks."],[null,"Cook the beef patties for about 4 minutes on the first side until lightly charred. Flip the patties, cook for an additional 2 minutes, then top each with a slice of cheddar cheese. Continue cooking for another 2 minutes until the cheese melts and the patties are cooked through."],[null,"Grill the red onion rings for about 2 minutes on each side until they are lightly charred."],[null,"To serve, place each grilled mushroom cap on a plate, gill side up. Top with arugula, a slice of tomato, a beef patty with melted cheese, and some grilled onion rings. Drizzle with the remaining barbecue sauce."]],"h":[]},"6549802":{"s":[[null,"Use a food processor to combine the drained and rinsed black beans, minced garlic, chopped fresh cilantro, lime juice, ground cumin, smoked paprika, salt, and pepper. Blend until you achieve a smooth and creamy consistency. You can gradually drizzle in 1 tablespoon of olive oil while blending to create your desired texture. Feel free to adjust the amount of oil according to your preference."],[null,"After blending, taste the dip and make any necessary adjustments to the seasonings. You can add more salt, pepper, or lime juice to suit your taste."],[null,"Transfer the black bean dip to a serving bowl and gently swirl in 2 tablespoons of plain Greek yogurt. This addition provides a creamy element and a touch of tanginess to the dip."],[null,"Serve with sliced cucumbers and bell peppers."]],"h":[]},"7950673":{"s":[[null,"To make the marinade, grind the coriander and cumin seeds to a powder."],[null,"Pound the garlic, ginger and chillies with a pinch of pepper, to a rough paste in a mortar."],[null,"Work in the coriander and cumin, tomato purée, vinegar, and olive oil. Mix in 2 tbsp water. Pour over the chicken pieces, and turn to coat each one."],[null,"Leave for at least half an hour (or up to 24 hours, covered, in the fridge)."],[null,"Preheat the grill or bbq thoroughly. Thread the chicken pieces onto 8 long skewers or 16 small ones, alternating with courgette rings. Grill or barbecue for around 10 minutes, turning several times until browned and cooked through. Serve with lemon or lime wedges, and rice or salad."]],"h":[[null,"If you don’t have a pestle and mortar, simply blend the marinade ingredients with a stick blender or food processor."],[null,"You could use cubes of salmon instead of chicken or tofu cubes for a vegan version."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"9690413":{"s":[[null,"Rinse and sort your lentils to discard any rocks or debris. Then place them in a small saucepot with the vegetable broth. Bring it to a boil, then reduce heat and simmer until cooked through, approx. 8 minutes."],[null,"Drain the lentils but reserve the cooking water in case needed to thin out the lentil dip."],[null,"Transfer the cooked lentils to your food processor and add all the remaining ingredients. Blend until completely combined, adding 1-2 tablespoons of the lentil water if needed for a thinner dip. (Keep in mind that the lentils will continue to absorb liquid and the dip will thicken as it sits.)"],[null,"Taste for salt and pepper and add if needed. Then serve your dip warm or refrigerate it for 1 hour or longer before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Cook the lentils in vegetable broth , not water, for the best flavour. If you don’t have broth on hand, try making our delicious bouillon mix ."],[null,"If you must use water, be sure to add extra seasoning, to taste."],[null,"If using canned lentils , increase the seasoning to make up for the loss of vegetable broth."],[null,"Store leftovers in the fridge in a sealed container for 3-4 days. Or freeze the dip in an airtight container for up to 3 months."]]},"6486814":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350°F. Line two baking sheets with parchment paper; set aside."],[null,"Trim the stems of the white mushrooms. Slice the mushrooms into 3/8-inch-thick pieces. Add the mushrooms to a bowl. Add the remaining ingredients and toss well. The mixture will look dry."],[null,"Spread the mushrooms in a single layer on each sheet. Roast for 10 minutes. Flip the mushroom slices and roast for 10 minutes more."],[null,"Increase the heat to 375°F and roast for 15 minutes. Flip the mushroom slices again and continue to roast for 10 minutes more. Serve as a side dish, or add to sandwiches, omelets, and soups."]],"h":[]},"7447100":{"s":[[null,"Add the carrot, artichokes, sweet potato, onions and peppers to a large bowl with the oil and mix well."],[null,"Add the paprika and mix again, so all vegetables are coated."],[null,"Spread out onto a lightly oiled baking sheet and bake in a preheated oven at 180°C/gas 4 for 35–45 minutes, turning occasionally."],[null,"Meanwhile, mix the tahini with the yoghurt and reserve until the vegetables are ready."]],"h":[[null,"Use a plant-based yogurt alternative to make this dish vegan."],[null,"Serve with chickpeas and wholemeal pitta bread or rice to turn this into a meal."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"4094416":{"s":[[null,"Poach the salmon in 2 cups water and 1 teaspoon smoked paprika for 4-6 minutes on medium-high heat, covered (do not boil). Remove and chill for at least 30 minutes. Mix all other ingredients together until smooth. Break salmon into bite size pieces and fold into cream cheese mixture. Chill for 20-30 minutes then serve with celery sticks, corn chips, and carrots or rolled in a leaf of iceberg lettuce."]],"h":[]},"6072254":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a large pot over medium heat. Add the onion, celery, bell pepper, salt, and black pepper, and cook, stirring occasionally, until vegetables have softened, 6–8 minutes. Add the garlic, red pepper flakes, paprika, and tomato paste. Continue to cook, stirring, for 1–2 minutes."],[null,"Pour in the broth and tomatoes with their juices. Bring mixture to a boil, then add the potatoes. Reduce heat to low and cover the pot. Simmer for 15–20 minutes, or until the potatoes are tender."],[null,"When potatoes are tender, increase heat to medium and add the lemon zest, lemon juice, and clams. Cover the pot and cook for 3 minutes. Stir in the shrimp and fish, cover again, and simmer for about 5 more minutes, until the clams open and the fish and shrimp are firm and opaque. Stir in the parsley and oregano, and serve immediately."]],"h":[]},"9200252":{"s":[[null,"Drain and rinse your beans. Then add them, along with all remaining ingredients to your crock pot. Mix very well to get everything combined."],[null,"Cook on low setting for 8 hours, or on high for 4-5 hours. **see notes"]],"h":[[null,"Soak the beans before cooking for 10-12 hours up to 24 hours. The water should be at least 2 inches above the bean line to allow for expansion. Add ¼ teaspoon of baking soda to your soaking water to help soften the beans even further . Plus this has also been said to help rid beans of their gassy causing effects. Very finely chop your onion and garlic. The smaller the pieces, the more the flavours will spread around to every single bean. Don't open the lid of your slow cooker for at least 2 hours . You want to keep the heat in there. So make sure you give everything a very good stir before you start cooking them. Towards the end of cooking, stir very well and taste and adjust for seasoning if needed. Leftovers keep refrigerated for up to 5 days and frozen for up to 2 months. *If you forgot the soak the beans, add them to a pot filled with water and cover with a lid. Bring to a boil and turn off the heat and let them soak for 1 hour. **Slow cookers vary greatly . If your beans start drying up before they're soft, add more broth or water, mix well and continue cooking. Don't go overboard. Just add ¼-1/2 cup at a time as needed. The beans are done when they are soft and creamy and the sauce is very thick."]]},"7557099":{"s":[[null,"Drain the tofu well and cut into 12 large cubes."],[null,"To make the marinade, begin by grinding the coriander and cumin seeds to a powder."],[null,"Next, pound the garlic, ginger and chillies with a couple of big pinches of pepper, to a rough paste in a mortar. Now work in the coriander and cumin, tomato purée, vinegar, and olive oil, then mix in 2 tbsp water."],[null,"Add the tofu to the marinade and mix gently, cover and set aside for a minimum of an hour, preferably 3–4 hours or longer. Microwave the courgette slices in two batches, covered in clingfilm, for about 60–80 seconds, until just tender enough to wrap around a piece of tofu but not so soft that they collapse. Alternatively, blanch in boiling water for 30 seconds or so and drain well."],[null,"Shortly before cooking, wrap strips of courgette around the cubes of tofu and slide onto skewers, so that the courgette stays in place."],[null,"Brush the courgette with any marinade left in the bowl, and grill or barbecue for 10-15 minutes, turning regularly."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"6050339":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a large saucepan over medium heat. Add the onion and sauté for 5 to 6 minutes. Add the garlic and smoked paprika and sauté for 1 minute."],[null,"Add the tomatoes and cook for 5 to 6 minutes. Add the beans and cook for 5 minutes. Add the spinach and cook until it is wilted. Stir in the balsamic vinegar and pepper and serve."]],"h":[]},"1002787":{"s":[[null,"Place strawberries in the blender and blend until smooth."],[null,"Beat egg whites until stiff peaks form."],[null,"Add all ingredients and continue blending until smooth."]],"h":[[null,"If using frozen fruit, add 1/4 cup water instead of the 1/2 cup ice. How “frozen” the fruit is determines how full you can fill the blender. It will also give you a “softer” consistency than a smoothie, which is very refreshing on hot days."],[null,"Adjust the amount of sugar or low-calorie sweetener to your taste."]]},"2570":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Mix cereals, pretzels and popcorn in large bowl."],[null,"Combine melted margarine, garlic powder and onion powder. Pour over cereal mixture and toss to coat. Add Parmesan cheese."],[null,"Bake for 7 to 10 minutes."],[null,"Cool before serving."],[null,"Store in sealed container."]],"h":[[null,"To reduce sodium further, use unsalted margarine or unsalted butter. Select the rice and corn cereal brand lowest in sodium."],[null,"For an added holiday twist, add 1 cup dried cranberries to the snack mix after it has cooled."]]},"9107096":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 400℉/204℃ and line a baking tray with parchment paper."],[null,"Add all the ingredients to a food processor and process until combined, but do not over process. Some chunkier pieces is totally fine."],[null,"Divide the mixture into 12 balls and place on your prepared baking tray. Bake for 30-35 minutes until edges are golden brown and meatballs are firm to the touch. Then remove from the oven and let rest for 5 minutes before serving with your favourite pasta and marinara sauce."]],"h":[[null,"For nut free: you may sub the walnuts for pumpkin seeds with similar results. Do not over process the mixture , you want the ingredients to combine, but leave some chunkier pieces for great texture. Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-4 days or frozen for up to 2 months. The serving size is for approx 3 balls, or ¼ of the recipe."]]},"1830":{"s":[[null,"Heat oven to 400° F."],[null,"Combine all cookie ingredients in large bowl and mix well."],[null,"Stir together remaining 1/4 cup sugar (or Splenda®) and cinnamon in a small bowl."],[null,"Form 1” balls and roll in the sugar mixture."],[null,"Place dough balls 2” apart on an ungreased cookie sheet."],[null,"Bake for 8 to 10 minutes until browned."]],"h":[[null,"Recipe analyzed with regular sugar. Use 3/4 cup Splenda® Sugar Blend instead of 1-1/2 cups sugar in step #2 to decrease calories to 160 and carbohydrate to 18 grams for 2 cookies."]]},"3316":{"s":[[null,"Combine all ingredients in a beverage shaker."],[null,"Shake vigorously until whipped topping melts completely."],[null,"Add ice if desired. Serve and enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Substitute any flavor Kool-Aid liquid flavor enhancing drops."]]},"6921975":{"s":[[null,"Place a 10-inch cast-iron skillet about 12 inches from your oven’s heating element and set the oven to “Broil.”"],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together chickpea flour, cumin, and salt. Slowly stream in water, whisking quickly to eliminate lumps, then stir in 1 tablespoon of the olive oil. Cover the bowl and set aside for at least 15 minutes. (Or store it in the refrigerator for up to 12 hours.) The batter should be a thin, pancake batter–like consistency."],[null,"After the batter has rested, carefully remove the hot skillet from the oven. Add the remaining 1 tablespoon of olive oil to the skillet and pour in the socca batter. Broil for 8–10 minutes, or until the edges of the socca are browned and the center is set."],[null,"Meanwhile, set a metal strainer in the bottom of a large pot, fill the pot 2/3 full with water, and add the vinegar. Crack each egg into a small prep bowl. Place the pot over medium-high heat and bring the vinegar and water to a simmer. Using a long-handled spoon, stir the water in a wide, circular motion to create a whirlpool. Quickly, while the whirlpool is still going, slide in the eggs, one by one. Once all the eggs are in the water, poach them without stirring until the whites are set and the yolks are no longer runny, about 4–6 minutes. Using tongs, carefully lift the strainer out of the water with the eggs."],[null,"Remove socca from the oven and cut it into 8 wedges. To serve, place a socca wedge on each of 8 plates and top each serving with 1 poached egg, 2 tablespoons roasted tomatoes, and 2 tablespoons chopped basil. Season servings with pepper."]],"h":[]},"7372432":{"s":[[null,"Sift together the flours, bicarbonate of soda and cream of tartar into a bowl and rub in the butter until the mixture resembles fine breadcrumbs. Quickly stir in the buttermilk and combine until a dough is formed."],[null,"Turn the dough onto a lightly floured surface and knead until smooth. Mould into a round shape, place onto a lightly floured baking sheet, cut a cross in the top, and sprinkle with a little flour."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 5 and bake for 25–30 minutes, until it sounds hollow when tapped."]],"h":[[null,"When sieving wholemeal flour, add back any bran that stays in the sieve after sifting."],[null,"You could add 75g mixed dried fruit and 1 tsp of mixed spice for a great fruit bread."],[null,"This soda bread is ideal for slicing and freezing – pop the slices straight into the toaster."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Slice, then wrap in foil to freeze. You can then use slices as required."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"7692699":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 190°C/gas 5. Prepare all the vegetables and slice the cheese for the toppings."],[null,"Add the flour and bicarbonate of soda to a mixing bowl."],[null,"Thoroughly mix in the yogurt and 75ml water. Shape into eight small balls and roll into rounds, using a little flour to stop them sticking."],[null,"Place on a lightly oiled baking sheet and spread with tomato puree then add a slice of tomato, sprinkle with oregano. Scatter with onion and sweetcorn and top each with a slice of mozzarella."],[null,"Bake for 10 minutes and serve."]],"h":[[null,"You could use any toppings you like – try spinach, red pepper and onion, or use reduced-fat Cheddar instead of mozzarella."],[null,"Make each pizzetta half the size for perfect party nibbles."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Freeze with greaseproof paper between each pizetta. Defrost 1 hour then bake as normal."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"2498":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350˚ F."],[null,"In a medium bowl combine flour, sugar, baking powder and salt. Mix well."],[null,"Add the eggs and garlic and mix. Add the root beer and cayenne. Mix all ingredients together well."],[null,"Pour the mixture into a greased 9 x 5-inch bread loaf pan."],[null,"Bake for 55 to 65 minutes. Let the loaf cool before removing from the pan."]],"h":[[null,"Use less cayenne pepper if you don’t like the heat."],[null,"Instead of using root beer and cayenne, try one of these substitutions: 12 ounces ginger ale and 1/3 cup fresh chopped rosemary leaves; or 12 ounces Orange Crush® or Orange Sunkist® soda with 1 tablespoon ground basil; or 12 ounces lemon lime soda with 1/2 cup chopped fresh cilantro."],[null,"Root beer, ginger ale, orange soda and lemon lime soda generally do not have phosphorus additives. However, always check the ingredient list for phosphate additives."]]},"3526":{"s":[[null,"Seed bell pepper. Cut bell pepper and onion into pieces."],[null,"Place green pepper, onion and garlic in a blender or food processor to chop."],[null,"Rinse roasted peppers then add roasted red pepper, cilantro, recao leaf, water and olive oil to food processor."],[null,"Blend into a sauce-like consistency. Add more water for desired consistency."]],"h":[[null,"Add 2 tablespoons Sofrito to meat and rice dishes for added flavor and seasoning."],[null,"One bell pepper is equal to 3/4 cup when chopped."],[null,"Look for recao leaf in Spanish stores. Bay leaf may be substituted if the recao leaf is unavailable."],[null,"3/4 cup canned red pepper is approximately 4 ounces. It is sold in different sized cans or bottles. Rinse to remove some of the sodium. Check nutrition label and choose brand lowest in sodium"],[null,"Refrigerate for up to 1 week."]]},"1002711":{"s":[[null,"Remove seeds from bell pepper. Cut bell pepper and onion into chunks."],[null,"Place green pepper, onion and garlic in a blender or food processor."],[null,"Rinse roasted peppers, then add roasted red pepper, cilantro, recao leaf, water and olive oil to the food processor."],[null,"Blend to a sauce-like consistency. Add more water to reach the desired consistency."]],"h":[[null,"Add 2 tablespoons Sofrito to meat and rice dishes for flavor and seasoning."],[null,"One green bell pepper equals 3/4 cup when chopped."],[null,"Look for recao leaves in Hispanic markets. Bay leaves can be used in place of recao if it is not available."],[null,"3/4 cup canned red pepper is about 4 ounces. It is sold in cans or jars of different sizes. Rinse to remove some of the sodium. Check the Nutrition Facts label and choose the brand with the least sodium."],[null,"Can be refrigerated for about 1 week."]]},"2715":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"In a medium bowl combine the flour, ginger, baking soda, cinnamon and cloves. Set aside."],[null,"In a large mixing bowl beat butter with an electric mixer on medium speed for 30 seconds. Beat in 1 cup sugar."],[null,"Add liquid egg substitute and molasses; beat well."],[null,"Stir flour mixture into egg mixture."],[null,"Shape dough into 1-1/2″ balls, using about 1 heaping tablespoon of dough for each."],[null,"Roll balls in the remaining sugar to coat."],[null,"Place balls about 2-1/2″ apart on an ungreased cookie sheet."],[null,"Bake for 10 minutes or until light brown and still puffed. (Do not over bake.)"],[null,"Cool cookies on cookie sheet for 2 minutes then transfer cookies to a wire rack and let cool."]],"h":[[null,"If dough is too soft to handle refrigerate for 1/2 hour for easier handling."],[null,"Store cookies in a sealed container to keep soft."]]},"2172":{"s":[[null,"Dissolve yeast in warm water and let stand for 10 minutes."],[null,"Add canola oil and half of the flour. Stir until thoroughly mixed. Add remaining flour and knead for 5 minutes."],[null,"Cover and let dough rest for 1 hour."],[null,"Divide dough into 24 pieces. Roll into 18” lengths and twist into pretzel shape. Let rise for 30 minutes."],[null,"Preheat oven to 475° F."],[null,"Add baking soda to 6 cups of water in a large pot and bring to a boil."],[null,"Add pretzels to boiling water for 1 minute then transfer to a baking sheet sprayed with nonstick cooking spray."],[null,"Bake for 12 minutes."],[null,"Serve each pretzel with 1/2 teaspoon mustard."]],"h":[[null,"Choose the mustard brand lowest in sodium."],[null,"You may need to add additional water to keep water level up in pot. Add pretzels in small batches."]]},"3726":{"s":[[null,"Make the Mexican Seasoning recipe (under Sauces and Seasoning in the Recipe section of DaVita.com)."],[null,"Chop the onion and lettuce."],[null,"Brown and drain the ground beef. Add the seasoning mixture and the low-sodium tomato sauce. Heat over medium heat. Warm the tortillas."],[null,"To assemble soft tacos, take 1 flour tortilla, add 1/4 cup seasoned ground beef, 1 teaspoon cheese, 1 teaspoon onion, 1 teaspoon sour cream and lettuce as desired."]],"h":[[null,"Ground turkey or vegetarian ground meat substitute can be used instead of ground beef."]]},"3847":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"To prepare using parchment paper (in papillote), fold parchment paper in half and cut into a large “half heart” shape. (Remember making Valentine’s cards in grade school?)"],[null,"Unfold paper and place one flounder filet, skin side down on one side of the heart-shaped parchment paper, leaving enough room around the edges to completely seal. Season each filet with 1/2 teaspoon ground black pepper and 1/2 teaspoon basil leaves. Place one teaspoon of unsalted butter on top of each filet. Set fish aside."],[null,"Trim snap beans. Parboil snap beans; set aside."],[null,"Remove seeds from bell peppers. Finely dice peppers and onions. Mince garlic cloves."],[null,"Combine yellow and green peppers, onion and garlic in a bowl. Squeeze juice from lemons into the bowl. Mix well. Spoon about 1/4 of the mixture on the top of each filet. Place 10 snap beans aroundeach fillets."],[null,"To close parchment paper, fold the other side of the heart shape over to cover ingredients and crimp together to seal. Be sure to leave some room inside the bundle for heat expansion, which will happen as the fish bakes. Make sure it is airtight"],[null,"Bake for 12 minutes or until fish flakes easily with a fork. After cooking, cut a U-shape in the top or the paper and fold open to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Use foil if parchment paper is unavailable."],[null,"Forty fresh snap beans is equal to 2 cups, if cut into 2” pieces."],[null,"Parboil means to cook partially by boiling for a brief period."],[null,"Any vegetable can be used in place of snap beans, such as: julienne yellow squash, zucchini, carrots, snow peas, etc. Thicker, tougher vegetables such as snap beans and snow peas need to be parboiled before steaming with fish to ensure doneness. Softer vegetables, including squash, can be substituted without parboiling."],[null,"Sole is also known as flounder. Substitutes include halibut and cod; both are just as delicious."],[null,"If available, substitute 1/2 tablespoon fresh basil for dried basil. For optimal flavor add it immediately after opening parchment instead of before baking the fish."]]},"7690806":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200ºC/gas 6. Place the potato, sweet potato and parsnip into a pan of boiling water and cook for 5 minutes."],[null,"Drain and place in a roasting dish and drizzle over half the oil."],[null,"Place in the oven and cook for 25–30 minutes until golden and tender. Mix together the parsley, polenta, garlic and lime zest in a reasonably flat bowl, and season with the black pepper."],[null,"Dip the sole pieces into the beaten egg and then dip into the polenta mixture to coat."],[null,"Heat the remaining oil in a non-stick frying pan, add the coated fish pieces and fry for 2 minutes on each side until golden and crisp."],[null,"Serve with the vegetable chips and a fresh green salad."]],"h":[[null,"You could use this coating on strips of cod, haddock, river cobbler or tilapia."],[null,"You can also make the recipe with strips of chicken or turkey."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Cook, then cool immediately and freeze on a baking sheet. Once frozen carefully bag in portions for use. Reheat thorughly until piping hot."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"1002783":{"s":[[null,"Wash potatoes well, peel and cut. Place in a pan, cover completely with water and bring to a boil. Drain and repeat the process."],[null,"Peel and cut carrots. Chop garlic and onion."],[null,"Remove bones and skin from chicken and rinse well."],[null,"Place all ingredients except rice and cilantro in a pot with the water."],[null,"Bring to a boil, then simmer for 45 minutes more."],[null,"Add rice and continue cooking for 25 minutes more."],[null,"Remove chicken from the pot. Cut into small pieces and return to the pot."],[null,"Add pepper to taste."],[null,"Serve garnished with finely chopped cilantro."]],"h":[[null,"To reduce potassium, soak the peeled, chopped potatoes in a bowl of water, changing the soaking water several times. Then add to the soup without the soaking water."]]},"1002597":{"s":[[null,"Peel carrot and bell pepper."],[null,"Wash all vegetables and chop into small pieces."],[null,"Peel potato and cut into pieces. Place in a pan and cover completely with water. Bring to a boil and drain. Repeat the process and set aside."],[null,"Trim lean beef and cut into small pieces."],[null,"Crush garlic cloves."],[null,"Place a pot with enough water to cook the ingredients over high heat and add the ingredients."],[null,"Stir constantly for 30 minutes until the ingredients are cooked."],[null,"Serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"Boiling potatoes twice reduces their potassium content."]]},"6373822":{"s":[[null,"Add the oil to a pot over medium-high heat. Add the barley and sauté until toasted, about 2 minutes. Add the sausage and sauté 2 more minutes."],[null,"Add the onion, celery, carrots, and bell peppers, and sauté for 3 minutes or until the onions begin to turn translucent."],[null,"Add the garlic and sauté 1 more minute."],[null,"Stir in the chicken broth and the tomatoes."],[null,"Add the bay leaf, salt (optional), and ground black pepper. Bring to a boil, then reduce to a simmer. Simmer, covered, for 15 minutes."],[null,"Remove the bay leaf and serve."]],"h":[]},"6165411":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350°F."],[null,"Wrap each beet in a piece of aluminum foil and roast until tender when pierced with a fork, about 1 hour. Remove the beets from the oven, unwrap them and let them cool for 5 minutes. Then peel the beets and cut them into 1/2-inch cubes."],[null,"Heat the oil in a medium heavy-bottomed saucepan over medium-high heat. Add the leek and garlic and cook for 5 to 8 minutes or until tender. Add the apples, the chopped beets and the ginger. Cook for 1 to 2 minutes, stirring constantly, then add the orange juice, the orange zest and the broth."],[null,"Bring the liquid to a boil, then reduce the heat to low, cover the saucepan and simmer until the vegetables are very tender, about 25 minutes."],[null,"Remove the pan from the heat, add the lemon juice and let the soup cool slightly. Carefully transfer the soup to a blender or food processor, in batches if necessary, and puree until smooth. Season with salt and pepper and serve immediately."]],"h":[]},"1002816":{"s":[[null,"Wash pumpkin well, peel and cut into small pieces."],[null,"Bring water to a boil."],[null,"When water is boiling, add pumpkin and cook until slightly softened."],[null,"Remove from heat and let cool."],[null,"Blend pumpkin, milk and sugar until thick and smooth."],[null,"Refrigerate for 30 minutes and serve well chilled."]],"h":[[null,"The milk can be skim or lactose-free."]]},"9939692":{"s":[[null,"Add all your ingredients to a blender and process until smooth. Enjoy immediately."]],"h":[]},"3876":{"s":[[null,"Dice the onion and chives."],[null,"Combine the onion, turkey, egg, Worcestershire sauce, garlic and pepper. Mix well and refrigerate for 1 hour."],[null,"Form turkey mixture into 4 patties and refrigerate until ready to cook."],[null,"Grill the turkey patties over medium heat, until well cooked, about 5 to 6 minutes per side. Burgers are done when a meat thermometer registers 165˚ F."],[null,"Place each burger on the bottom part of the bun, top with 1 tablespoon sour cream and 1/2 tablespoon chives. Place the other half of bun on top and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Top burgers with grilled onions for more onion flavor."],[null,"Look for hamburger buns that do not have phosphorus additives."],[null,"Add 1 tablespoon olive oil to ground turkey mixture to make burgers juicier if fat content is not a concern."],[null,"If you are on a lower protein diet make 8 patties instead of 4. Wrap and freeze extra burgers for a quick meal later. Protein is reduced to 18 grams per serving with the bun."]]},"3375":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Coat 8-1/2″ x 4-3/4″ loaf pan with cooking spray."],[null,"Peel Granny Smith apple and cut into 1/4″ pieces."],[null,"Combine flour, baking powder, baking soda, ground cinnamon and salt. Set aside for later use."],[null,"At medium speed, beat granulated sugar and oil until combined."],[null,"Beat in egg whites, applesauce and flour mixture until combined."],[null,"Stir in sour cream and apples until combined."],[null,"Spread mixture evenly in loaf pan. Bake 50 to 55 minutes or until toothpick inserted into the center comes out clean."],[null,"Cool on rack 20 minutes. Remove from pan and let cool."],[null,"Mix confectioners’ sugar and water. Drizzle over loaf. Slice into 10 portions."]],"h":[[null,"One medium apple yeilds approximately 1 cup."],[null,"Make several loaves and freeze one for later."],[null,"Use pasteurized, liquid egg whites instead of fresh egg whites if desired. 1/3 cup of All Whites® brand 100% liquid egg whites replaces 2 egg whites."]]},"2219":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375° F."],[null,"Chop onion, green peppers and jalapeno peppers. Beat eggs."],[null,"Combine ground beef, onion, green pepper, jalapenos, cooked rice, beaten eggs, garlic powder in a large bowl and mix together."],[null,"Roll into 1” balls and place on a baking sheet."],[null,"Bake for 10 to 15 minutes, until meatballs are cooked through."],[null,"Combine taco sauce and water in a saucepan and bring to boil."],[null,"Add meatballs to taco sauce and lower temperature to warm."],[null,"Serve hot or place in a covered warming dish or slow cooker on low heat setting."]],"h":[[null,"Make meatballs ahead and refrigerate. When ready to serve, heat ingredients together and transfer to a warming dish."],[null,"Choose lowest sodium brand of taco sauce."]]},"2411":{"s":[[null,"Mince garlic and chili pepper. Thinly slice onion and chop cilantro. Peel, seed and dice cucumber. Peel and devein shrimp."],[null,"Combine lime and lemon juice, garlic, ketchup, hot sauce and oregano in a medium saucepan and bring to a boil. Reduce to low heat, add shrimp and cook 1 to 2 minutes until shrimp turns orange. Remove from heat, place in a bowl and cool in the refrigerator."],[null,"Prepare onion, cilantro, cucumber and chili pepper. Add vegetables and olive oil to cooled shrimp mixture and stir to mix. Refrigerate until chilled."],[null,"Divide shrimp into six cocktail dishes or martini glasses. Pour 2 tablespoons liquid over each cocktail. Garnish with lemon or lime slice and cilantro before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Frozen shrimp can be substituted for fresh shrimp."],[null,"Wear rubber gloves when mincing hot chili pepper to prevent irritation to hands and eyes."]]},"6796988":{"s":[[null,"In a medium bowl, combine broccoli, onion, celery, and cheese; set aside."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine remaining ingredients. Add mayonnaise mixture to vegetable mixture and toss."],[null,"Cover and refrigerate at least 2 hours to “marry” the flavors."]],"h":[]},"3170":{"s":[[null,"Mince the green onions and pickle spear."],[null,"In a food processor, shred on high speed the carrots, cabbage and red cabbage and set aside."],[null,"In a separate large bowl, mix green onions, pickle spear and remaining ingredients."],[null,"Add the cabbages and carrots to the ingredients and mix until all colors are blended."],[null,"Chill in refrigerator for one hour."]],"h":[[null,"This is good on its own, on BBQ, and on tortilla chips as a snack."]]},"6944046":{"s":[[null,"Place beans, onion, and bay leaf in a large saucepan. Cover with water and bring to a boil over high heat. Reduce heat to medium-low, cover, and cook until tender, approximately 1 hour."],[null,"Drain beans and place in a food processor with cheese, 1 tablespoon. olive oil, and fennel seeds. Purée until smooth. Taste and season with crushed red chile flakes, salt, and pepper."],[null,"Spoon onto a serving platter and smooth out the top with a spatula. Drizzle with remaining 1 tablespoon. olive oil, and sprinkle crushed red chile flakes and fennel seed on top, if desired."]],"h":[]},"3960":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F. Spray a casserole dish with nonstick spray."],[null,"Dice onion and slice squash. Set cream cheese out to soften."],[null,"In a large skillet heat olive oil and sauté onions and squash until tender."],[null,"In a separate bowl, whisk together eggs and rice milk. Add cheese, cream cheese, black pepper to egg mixture."],[null,"Add squash to mixture then pour into the casserole dish and bake for 30 minutes."],[null,"Crush crackers and melt the butter. Mix together. Remove casserole from oven and add cracker topping. Bake for an additional 15 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Keep phosphorus lower by limiting the cheese and using unenriched rice milk instead of cow’s milk."],[null,"Crookneck squash can be replaced with other types of summer squash."]]},"7095342":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4. Mix all the spices and herbs together with the breadcrumbs, making sure they are well combined."],[null,"Beat the egg in a bowl and set aside."],[null,"Dredge the chicken with the flour, shaking off any excess and dip each chicken thigh into the beaten egg."],[null,"Toss the chicken pieces in the spicy breadcrumb mixture ensuring each thigh is thoroughly coated."],[null,"Lay the chicken on a lightly oiled baking sheet and sprinkle any leftover spice mixture on top."],[null,"Roast for 10 minutes, turn the pieces over and roast for another 10 minutes. Check the chicken is cooked through and serve."]],"h":[[null,"You could use chicken breasts or turkey escalopes with this coating."],[null,"When coating the chicken use just one hand and keep the other clean, otherwise you can get into a sticky mess!"],[null,"You could add other spices. For a spicy kick try cayenne pepper, or give it a Chinese flavour with a pinch of Chinese five-spice."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"3364":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375° F."],[null,"Core and de-seed bell peppers."],[null,"Brown ground beef and drain liquid."],[null,"Add onion, rice, garlic powder, black pepper, parsley and tomato sauce to cooked beef; simmer for 10 minutes."],[null,"Fill each bell pepper with mixture."],[null,"Bake for 1 hour."]],"h":[[null,"Freeze extra servings for a quick meal later."]]},"6703167":{"s":[[null,"Heat olive oil in a large skillet or pot over medium heat. Add the diced onion and sauté for 3–4 minutes until softened. Add garlic and cook for 1 minute until fragrant."],[null,"Stir in the chopped turnip greens, ¼ tsp smoked paprika, red pepper flakes, and ¼ tsp black pepper. Add 1 cup vegetable broth and bring to a simmer."],[null,"Cover and cook for 15–20 minutes, stirring occasionally, until the greens are tender. Stir in the apple cider vinegar just before serving."],[null,"In another skillet, heat 1 Tbsp olive oil over medium heat. Add remaining diced onion and sauté for 3–4 minutes until softened."],[null,"Stir in black-eyed peas, diced tomato, ½ tsp smoked paprika, cayenne pepper, and 1/4 black pepper. Add 1 cup vegetable broth and simmer for 10–15 minutes, stirring occasionally, until the flavors meld and the liquid slightly reduces."],[null,"Divide the turnip greens and black-eyed peas among 4 plates or bowls. Garnish with fresh parsley and a dash of hot sauce if desired."]],"h":[]},"3781":{"s":[[null,"In a large pot, bring 2 quarts of water to a boil. Add turkey wing. Reduce heat and cook for about 1 hour. Set aside."],[null,"Chop onion, garlic and collard greens."],[null,"In another large pot, heat oil and butter on medium heat. Add onion and sauté for 2 minutes or until tender."],[null,"Add garlic and red pepper flakes, and cook 1 minute."],[null,"Add collard greens and cook 1 minute."],[null,"Add enough turkey stock to cover greens (about 4 cups). Add salt and bring to a simmer."],[null,"Cook until greens are tender, about 40 to 50 minutes."],[null,"Debone the turkey wing and add meat to the cooked greens before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Most greens get a bad rap for being high in potassium when actually it is the portion consumed that makes the difference. Many people eat more than 1/2 cup. Stay within the suggested portion to keep potassium down."],[null,"To include turkey meat as an entrée, cook several turkey wings or legs. Remove and discard skin from the cooked turkey and add the meat to the collard greens if desired."]]},"3922":{"s":[[null,"Grease a 12″ skillet with oil and set on a warm stove."],[null,"Combine corn meal, 1 cup flour, sugar, yeast and salt in a large bowl."],[null,"Heat butter in microwave for 10-15 seconds to melt. In a seperate container, heat nondairy creamer and water to 120°-130° F. Add melted butter."],[null,"Stir liquid mixture into dry mixture and beat with an electric mixer on high speed for 2 minutes. Add eggs and beat an additional 1-2 minutes at high speed."],[null,"Gradually add remaining flour and keep stirring to form a stiff batter."],[null,"Move batter to greased skillet and form to fit. Pat top with oil, cover with a towel and let rise in a warm place for 45 minutes."],[null,"Bake for 30 minutes at 375° F or until top is golden brown."]],"h":[[null,"Making yeast bread was once a time consuming project. Fleishmann’s® Rapid Rise yeast reduces preparation steps and rising time. The batter in this recipe can be prepared in 15 to 20 minutes. Total time from start to table is only 1-1/2 hours!"],[null,"Temperature is very important in making yeast bread. Use a food thermometer to check liquid temperature 120°-130° F. When rising, keep dough covered in a warm, draft-free place."],[null,"Why make yeast cornbread? All breads require a leavening agent to rise properly. Baking soda is high in sodium, baking powder is high in sodium and phosphorus, and cream of tartar is high in potassium. In comparison, yeast is very low in all these elements. Compare on the chart below:"]]},"6895607":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F. Place the corn tortillas on a baking sheet lined with parchment paper. Lightly spray both sides with cooking spray. Bake for 6–7 minutes on each side or until they become crispy and golden brown. Remove from the oven and set aside."],[null,"In a small saucepan over medium heat, combine the black beans, garlic clove, water, chili powder, ground cumin, and salt."],[null,"Cook for 2–3 minutes until heated through. Using a fork or potato masher, mash the beans to create a spreadable consistency. Remove from the heat and set aside.​"],[null,"In a large nonstick skillet, heat 1 teaspoon of olive oil over medium heat. Add the spinach and salt. Cook, stirring frequently, until wilted, about 2–3 minutes. Transfer to a bowl and set aside."],[null,"In the same skillet, heat the remaining 1 teaspoon of olive oil over medium heat.​ Crack the eggs into the skillet, spacing them evenly. Cook the eggs to your desired doneness (e.g., sunny side up or over easy)."],[null,"To assemble, spread an even layer of the black bean mixture over each baked tortilla.​ Top with sautéed spinach, followed by a cooked egg and tomatoes.​ Add slices of avocado and sprinkle with fresh cilantro leaves."]],"h":[]},"1845":{"s":[[null,"Cook the pasta until tender but still firm, about 8 minutes or according to package instructions. Drain."],[null,"Drain and rinse the corn and black beans. Dice the bell peppers and onion. Chop the basil."],[null,"In a large bowl combine all ingredients and stir to combine. Refrigerate for at least 2 hours before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Make it a meal by adding chopped chicken."],[null,"Whole grain pasta instead of refined pasta can be used to boost the fiber content even more."],[null,"Try the davita.com Italian Dressing recipe instead of bottled Italian dressing if low sodium is unavailable."]]},"2951":{"s":[[null,"Seed and finely chop jalapeño peppers. Seed and chop cucumber; chop green onions and cilantro."],[null,"In medium bowl, combine mayonnaise, jalapeño pepper and lime juice."],[null,"Stir in drained tuna. Mix well."],[null,"Add cucumber and green onions. Chill until ready to eat."],[null,"Serve a scoop of Southwest Tuna Salad on lettuce or on a bagel or bread of choice. Garnish with chopped cilantro if desired."]],"h":[]},"6557494":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350°F. Coat a 9 × 5-inch loaf pan with nonstick cooking spray."],[null,"Add all of the remaining ingredients to a large bowl. Gently mix the ingredients until well combined."],[null,"Spoon the mixture into the prepared loaf pan, using the back of the spoon or a spatula to even out the top. Place the loaf pan in the oven and bake until a thermometer inserted into the center of the meatloaf reads 165°F, 1 hour."]],"h":[]},"6928135":{"s":[[null,"In a large salad bowl, combine the cabbage, carrots, red pepper, scallions, and jalapeño pepper and toss well."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the vinegar, lime juice, honey, and chipotle seasoning. Add the olive oil in a thin stream, whisking to emulsify. Pour the dressing on the cabbage mixture and mix well. Garnish the coleslaw with the toasted pecans."]],"h":[]},"1943":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F."],[null,"Cut tops off each red pepper. Remove seeds and stems."],[null,"Parboil peppers for about 4 minutes."],[null,"In a large skillet heat canola oil and sauté onions until translucent."],[null,"Add ground beef and stir meat around to separate."],[null,"Add ground garlic powder, cumin and dried oregano to meat mixture."],[null,"Add corn and canned tomatoes with chilies. Mix into meat mixture."],[null,"Stand bell peppers in a 2-quart baking pan. Fill with meat mixture, adding any left over to pan."],[null,"Cover and bake for 40 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"If you want less heat add the mild version of canned tomatoes with chilies."],[null,"Be sure to count as 2 vegetable servings if you are on a low potassium diet. To reduce the potassium to 534 mg add 1-1/2 cups of cooked rice, omit the corn and reduce canned tomatoes and chilies to 1/2 cup."],[null,"Patients who do peritoneal dialysis or daily home hemodialysis often require a higher potassium intake. This recipe can help provide more potassium."],[null,"For lower protein CKD-nondialysis diets reduce the ground beef to 1/2 pound of the amount recommended by your dietitian."]]},"2355":{"s":[[null,"Heat vinegar until hot but not boiling."],[null,"Peel and slice garlic cloves and add to hot vinegar."],[null,"Cover and let stand overnight in the refrigerator."],[null,"Strain and discard garlic."],[null,"In a glass jar, combine garlic vinegar with molasses and onion powder."],[null,"Refrigerate and use as needed."],[null,"Warm and shake well before using."],[null,"Lasts about 1 month refrigerated."]],"h":[[null,"Soy-Less Sodium Sauce keeps for up to 1 month refrigerated."],[null,"Erin prefers Spice Islands® onion powder. Avoid onion salt."],[null,"Molasses varies in potassium content. The lowest is light molasses (180 mg per tablespoon); then dark molasses (210 mg/tablespoon); blackstrap molasses is very high in potassium (450 mg /tablespoon—not recommended.) Molasses is made from extracted and boiled sugarcane or beet sugar juice."],[null,"Use vinegar of choice. Look for unseasoned rice vinegar as one option."]]},"6739333":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6406213":{"s":[],"h":[]},"7263439":{"s":[[null,"Bring a large saucepan of water to the boil."],[null,"In a large bowl, stir together the flour, egg and nutmeg. Gradually stir in approx 100ml cold water to make a smooth dough that doesn’t stick to the spoon."],[null,"Flour a cutting board, place the dough on it and roll out thinly. Cut the dough into small noodles about 5cm long. Cook the noodles in batches by adding to the boiling water. They cook quickly and are ready when they float to the surface. As the noodles finish cooking, remove them with a slotted spoon."],[null,"Transfer the noodles to a plate and toss with the olive oil and some parsley."]],"h":[[null,"Try making spaetzle with half wholemeal flour for more fibre."],[null,"For a simple sauce for 2, sauté a large chopped leek with 150g mushrooms. Stir in 2 tbsp reduced fat garlic and herb cream cheese."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"7183658":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a saucepan and gently cook the onions until starting to brown, stirring regularly."],[null,"Add the beef and cook for 8-10 minutes, breaking up any clumps of beef with a wooden spoon."],[null,"Add the carrot, yellow pepper and courgette and continue cooking gently for 5 minutes more, still stirring regularly."],[null,"Add the garlic, herbs and chilli flakes and stir for a minute. Add the stock cube, followed by the tomatoes and tomato puree."],[null,"Bring to a gentle simmer, cover and cook for 15 minutes, stirring occasionally and adding a little water if too much liquid evaporates and it starts to stick."],[null,"Meanwhile, cook the spaghetti according to pack instructions."],[null,"Stir the lentils and chopped parsley into the sauce then cook for 5 minutes."],[null,"Add a grind of black pepper, sprinkle with basil and serve with the wholemeal spaghetti."],[null,"Sprinkle with Parmesan shavings, if liked, to serve."]],"h":[[null,"You could use minced turkey for this sauce."],[null,"Ideal for cooking in a large batch then freezing in portions."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"6558830":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400° F. Fill a 9x13-inch glass or metal baking dish with 2 inches of water. Cut the ends off the spaghetti squash then cut in half lengthwise. Place the squash cut side down in the pan and bake for 40 minutes. Remove from oven and remove the squash immediately from the pan. Scoop out the seeds and discard. Using a fork, scrape the squash out of the skin and set aside. Makes 4 cups cooked squash."],[null,"While the squash is cooking, in a medium saucepan, heat the broth over medium heat until simmering. Add the soy sauce, sesame oil, fish sauce and hot sauce. Simmer for 2 minutes. Add the chicken and heat through, 2 minutes."],[null,"Place 1 cup of squash in a soup bowl. Pour 1 cup of broth over the squash and add 1/2 cup of chicken. Top with 2 Tbsp. scallions and 2 Tbsp. bell pepper strips."],[null,"Repeat process for remaining three bowls. Add 1 lime wedge to each bowl for serving."]],"h":[]},"6316003":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375°F. Coat a baking pan with cooking spray."],[null,"Fill baking pan with 1 inch of water. Cut squash in half lengthwise. Lay squash cut side down in the pan and roast for 1 hour."],[null,"Remove the roasted squash from the skin. Discard skin and any seeds and place into a large bowl. Set aside."],[null,"Coat another baking pan (9x9) with cooking spray. Set aside."],[null,"While squash is roasting, add olive oil to a medium sauce pan over medium high heat. Sauté chicken sausage until beginning to brown."],[null,"Add garlic and mushrooms and sauté until mushrooms are softened and all liquid is evaporated."],[null,"Sprinkle flour over the mushroom and sausage mixture and cook for 2-3 minutes, stirring constantly."],[null,"Add milk and whisk vigorously, scraping the bits off the bottom of the pan. Bring to a boil."],[null,"Reduce to a simmer and let simmer for 3-4 minutes. Add 1/4 cup of mozzarella cheese and stir to melt. Stir in salt, pepper and basil."],[null,"Pour sauce over the cooked spaghetti squash and mix to incorporate."],[null,"Pour into prepared baking dish, top with remaining mozzarella cheese and parmesan cheese. Bake for 45 minutes or until cheese is golden brown and casserole is bubbly and brown around the edges."],[null,"Cut into 9 even squares."]],"h":[]},"3587":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375º F."],[null,"Pierce spaghetti squash with a fork. Microwave for 5 minutes to soften. Cut the spaghetti squash in half and remove seeds and membranes."],[null,"Rub squash with olive oil. Place squash cut side down on a lightly greased baking sheet and bake for 50 minutes. Remove squash from oven and set aside to cool enough to be easily handled."],[null,"Finely chop garlic and shallot. Finely grate Parmigiano-Reggiano cheese."],[null,"Heat 2 tablespoons olive oil in a skillet over medium heat. Add garlic and shallot; cook and stir until fragrant, 2-3 minutes. Turn off heat."],[null,"Use a large spoon to scoop the stringy pulp from the squash into the skillet. Add Parmesan cheese, black pepper and red pepper chili flakes; stir to combine."],[null,"Remove to a serving dish and serve warm."]],"h":[[null,"Spaghetti squash is the only lower potassium winter squash, and is a tasty low carbohydrate substitute for pasta. It weighs from 4 to 8 pounds."],[null,"4 pound squash yields 5 cups"],[null,"5 pound squash yields 6-1/4 cups"],[null,"6 pound squash yields 7-1/2 cups"],[null,"7 pound squash yields 8-3/4 cups"],[null,"8 pound squash yields 10 cups"],[null,"Heat winter squash for 4-5 minutes in the microwave for easier cutting before baking. Cool for 10 to 15 minutes before cutting."],[null,"For a lower phosphorus and sodium version, reduce the cheese to 1/2 cup. Instead of adding to the squash during preparation, sprinkle 1 tablespoon on top of each serving. Sodium is reduced to 142 mg and phosphorus is 79 mg."],[null,"Serving suggestion: Top with with Roasted Red Pepper Tomato Sauce or your favorite kidney-friendly sauce."]]},"2692":{"s":[[null,"Slice celery diagonally and dice onion. Set aside."],[null,"Wash spaghetti squash and pierce with a fork several times around the squash. Microwave on high for 2 minutes to soften. Cut the stem end off, cut in half lengthwise and scoop out seeds with membrane."],[null,"Place squash halves cut side down in a microwave safe dish. Put plastic wrap over the top with one corner vented. Microwave on high for 12 minutes. Cool and scoop out with a fork. Set aside."],[null,"Whisk together soy sauce, water, garlic, brown sugar, ginger paste, pepper. Set aside."],[null,"Heat oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Add celery and onion, and cook until tender, approximately 3-4 minutes."],[null,"Add cabbage mix and stir until heated through, approximately 2-3 minutes."],[null,"Stir in spaghetti squash and soy sauce mixture until well combined, approximately 2 minute."],[null,"Serve immediately!"]],"h":[[null,"If desired use 2 teaspoons fresh grated ginger instead of ginger paste."],[null,"Adjust portion to 1/2 cup for a lower potassium meal."]]},"6416393":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F. Cut the squash in half lengthwise and scoop out the seeds. Place cut-side down on a baking sheet and roast until tender, 30–40 min. Let it cool slightly, then shred into strands with a fork."],[null,"While the squash roasts, heat 1 tsp olive oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Add the chicken, season lightly with black pepper, and cook until golden and cooked through. Transfer to a plate."],[null,"Add the remaining teaspoon of olive oil to the skillet. Stir in the garlic, cabbage, bell pepper, and carrots. Cook for 3–5 minutes, until just tender but still crisp."],[null,"Return the chicken to the skillet along with the spaghetti squash strands and green onions. Drizzle in soy sauce, rice vinegar, and sesame oil. Toss to combine and heat through."],[null,"Divide among bowls and garnish with chopped cilantro and a lime wedge."]],"h":[]},"6944484":{"s":[[null,"Pierce spaghetti squash with a fork in several places and place in microwave on high until skin is soft, approximately 10-15 minutes. Let cool."],[null,"While squash is cooking, combine marinara ingredients (1 tbsp olive oil, tomatoes, garlic, shallots, black pepper, and salt) in a medium-sized bowl."],[null,"Tear basil leaves and add to tomato mixture."],[null,"Cut squash in half and make “spaghetti.” Using a fork, pull out individual strands of “spaghetti.” Toss spaghetti squash with 1 tbsp olive oil and 1 tbsp Parmigiano-Reggiano cheese."],[null,"Place squash in a pie plate. Top with light marinara and a sprinkling of remaining Parmigiano-Reggiano cheese (optional)."],[null,"Serve over cooked spaghetti squash."]],"h":[]},"6075596":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400°F. Place the squash halves cut-side down on a parchment paper–lined baking sheet and roast for about 50 minutes, or until tender."],[null,"Meanwhile, heat the olive oil in a skillet over medium heat. Add the onion, shallot, and garlic and sauté for 4 minutes. Add in the pine nuts and cook for 2 minutes until the pine nuts are lightly browned. Set aside."],[null,"When the squash is cooked, turn over squash to cut side up. With a pasta rake or large spoon, scoop the flesh from the squash shell. The flesh will come out like strands of spaghetti."],[null,"Add the squash to a large serving bowl and rake through the strands to keep them separated. Add in the pine nut mixture, cheese, sage, crushed red pepper flakes, salt, and pepper. Toss well and serve."]],"h":[]},"6021807":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F."],[null,"Cut the spaghetti squash in half lengthwise. Scoop out the seeds with a spoon."],[null,"Place the squash halves, cut side up, on a baking sheet. Drizzle each half with 1/2 tbsp olive oil and season with 1/2 tsp coarse salt and black pepper."],[null,"Roast the spaghetti squash until the flesh is tender and easily shreds into spaghetti-like strands, about 40 minutes."],[null,"While the squash is roasting, prepare the tomato basil sauce. In a saucepan, heat 1 tbsp olive oil over medium heat. Add minced garlic and sauté until fragrant."],[null,"Pour in the crushed tomatoes, dried oregano, basil, coarse salt, and black pepper."],[null,"Simmer the sauce for about 15–20 minutes, allowing the flavors to meld."],[null,"Once the spaghetti squash is done, use a fork to scrape the flesh into spaghetti-like strands."],[null,"Serve the spaghetti squash with a generous ladle of tomato basil sauce. Garnish with fresh basil if desired."]],"h":[]},"7335144":{"s":[[null,"Cook the pasta according to the pack instructions. Drain and return to the pan."],[null,"Meanwhile, heat the oil in a non-stick pan, add the courgette, garlic and chilli and fry for 3–4 minutes. Add the passata, bring to the boil and simmer for 5 minutes."],[null,"Stir the sauce and the parsley through the pasta and serve."]],"h":[[null,"If you don't have passata, then blend tinned tomatoes to a pulp with a tablespoon of tomato purée."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"3374":{"s":[[null,"Chop green onion and basil; set aside."],[null,"Coat a medium non-stick skillet with 2 teaspoons olive oil. Spread cooked spaghetti noodles evenly in skillet and cook over medium heat for 2 minutes."],[null,"Whisk milk, eggs, egg whites and black pepper together in a bowl. Gently pour over pasta. Sprinkle the top of the frittata with cheese, green onions and basil. Cover and cook for approximately 8 minutes until set."],[null,"Cut the frittata into 4 wedges and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Top with 1/4 cup delicious Roasted Red Pepper Tomato Sauce from the DaVita.com recipe collection."],[null,"Substitute refined spaghetti for whole wheat if preferred."],[null,"Note to dietitians: This is a great recipe idea to serve at food sampling events. Double the recipe and cook in an electric skillet. Pre-cook/prep the pasta and sauce. Place a basil plant on the table for aroma and to demonstrate use of fresh herbs."]]},"6085816":{"s":[[null,"Cook the potatoes in a large pot of boiling water until just tender, about 10 minutes. Drain and let cool."],[null,"In a medium skillet, heat 2 teaspoons of olive oil over medium heat. Add onions and sauté for 3 minutes until just translucent. Add 2 cloves of minced garlic and sauté for an additional minute."],[null,"In a large bowl, whisk the eggs, egg substitute, salt, and pepper. Add the potatoes, onions, and garlic and stir gently to combine, being careful not to break up the potatoes."],[null,"Heat the remaining teaspoon of olive oil in the skillet used to cook the onions over medium heat. Gently pour the potato, onion, and egg mixture into the skillet and spread the potatoes out. Cover it and cook for 5–7 minutes, until the top sets and the bottom is browned."],[null,"Flip the potato tortilla and cook on the other side for an additional 5–7 minutes. (To flip this, remove the cover and put a plate over the skillet. Carefully turn it over onto the plate. Then slide the “tortilla” back into the pan from the plate.)"],[null,"Once the other side is brown and it is firm to touch, slide the “tortilla” out of the skillet."],[null,"Spray a large skillet with cooking spray. Add the spinach and kale and last clove of garlic and cook until the spinach and kale are mostly wilted."],[null,"Cut the “tortilla” in 6 pieces and serve with half a cup of the spinach and kale blend."]],"h":[]},"7987020":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200°C/gas 6. In a large bowl, sift together the flour and salt. Stir through the yeast. Mix together half of the oil, the milk and 50ml hand hot water, pour into the flour and combine to form a dough."],[null,"Tip the dough out onto a lightly floured surface and knead for 5 minutes until smooth."],[null,"Place in a lightly oiled bowl, cover with a damp cloth and set aside in a warm place for 1 hour until doubled in size. Re-knead, then shape into a square approximately 40cm x 40cm."],[null,"Meanwhile, heat the remaining oil in a frying pan, add the onions and fry gently for 8–10 minutes until softened and beginning to turn golden."],[null,"Scatter over the pizza base along with the remaining ingredients except chives, then bake for 20–25 minutes until the pizza base is golden and crisp. Scatter with the chives and serve."]],"h":[[null,"For a vegetarian version, use 75g shredded sundried tomatoes in place of the anchovies."],[null,"Make the pizza with red onions for more colour."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"2925":{"s":[[null,"Chop onion and green pepper."],[null,"In skillet, sauté onions and green pepper in olive oil until softened."],[null,"Add rice to skillet, stirring constantly until rice is lightly browned."],[null,"Add garlic powder, chili powder, tomato puree and water to skillet. Cover and simmer on low heat until rice is tender and water is absorbed, about 15 to 20 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Serve with fajitas, enchiladas or tacos recipes."]]},"6896958":{"s":[[null,"Puree the strawberries, mint leaves, lemon juice, and 1/2 cup of the sparkling water in a blender on low speed until smooth, at least 30 seconds."],[null,"Pour the puree into a serving pitcher. Very slowly pour in the remaining sparkling water."],[null,"Serve chilled over ice in tall beverage glasses. Garnish each with a sprig of fresh mint."]],"h":[]},"2462":{"s":[[null,"Cut chicken into 1-inch pieces; set aside."],[null,"To make sauce, stir together honey, vinegar, pineapple juice, soy sauce, and cornstarch; set aside."],[null,"Pour canola oil into a large skillet or wok. (Add more oil as necessary during cooking.) Preheat over medium high heat."],[null,"Stir-fry frozen vegetables for 3 minutes or until vegetables are crisp-tender."],[null,"Remove vegetables from skillet."],[null,"Add chicken to hot skillet. Stir-fry for 3-4 minutes or until chicken is no longer pink. Push chicken away from the center of the skillet. Stir sauce; add to center of the skillet. Cook and stir until thickened and bubbly."],[null,"Return cooked vegetables to skillet. Stir all ingredients together to coat. Cook and stir about 1 minute more or until heated through."],[null,"Serve immediately over rice."]],"h":[[null,"Select a frozen vegetable mixture of broccoli, red peppers, bamboo and mushroom or try green beans, red peppers and water chestnuts."]]},"7805746":{"s":[[null,"Mix together the herbs and lime rind and juice in a non-metallic bowl. Add the salmon and set aside to marinate for at least 10 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, cook the pasta according to the pack instructions, adding the sugarsnap peas 2 minutes before the end of cooking. Drain."],[null,"Meanwhile, heat a heavy pan or griddle until hot. Add the salmon and cook for 3 minutes on each side until thoroughly cooked through."],[null,"Toss together the pasta, sugarsnap peas, tomatoes and any remaining marinade."],[null,"Gently flake the salmon and fold into the pasta."]],"h":[[null,"You could use cod, haddock or tiger prawns in place of salmon."],[null,"Try 2 tbsp chopped fresh dill rather than parsley and use lemon in place of lime."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6291531":{"s":[[null,"In a large skillet, heat the oil over medium heat. Add the onion and red pepper and sauté for 6 to 7 minutes, until soft. Add the garlic and sauté for 1 minute."],[null,"Add the marinara sauce, cayenne, and black pepper. Turn the heat to low and simmer for 10 minutes."],[null,"Using the back of a spoon, make 4 wells, spaced apart from each other, in the sauce. Gently crack an egg into each indentation. Cover the pan and let the eggs cook until set but still soft, about 10 to 12 minutes. Sprinkle the basil leaves over the mixture in the skillet, cover, and cook for 1 minute. The eggs should be set, not runny."],[null,"Spoon 1 egg and 1/2 cup of sauce over each slice of the toasted bread to serve."]],"h":[]},"6077589":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400°F. Add the fennel seeds, coriander seeds, and peppercorns to a small skillet and toast over medium-high heat for 1 to 2 minutes, until fragrant. Allow the spices to cool, then grind them to a fine powder in a spice or coffee grinder. Add the spice mixture to a small bowl. Mix in the chili powder, cinnamon, and salt; set aside."],[null,"Rub the chicken thighs with the spice mixture. Add the thighs to a large baking dish. Drizzle the olive oil over the chicken. Roast the chicken for 30 minutes. Add the lemons and roast for 10 minutes, until the chicken is cooked through and the lemons are lightly browned. With tongs, squeeze the lemons over the chicken and serve."]],"h":[]},"7291211":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/ gas 4. With a fork, thoroughly mash the bananas, then beat them a little."],[null,"Add the apples, oats, apple juice, raisins, seeds and cinnamon. Mix well."],[null,"Oil a baking sheet and spread out the mixture to a depth of 2cm."],[null,"Bake in the oven for 15–20 minutes."],[null,"Allow to cool, cut into 16 portions and serve."]],"h":[[null,"You can add sesame, hemp or poppy seeds, and linseeds to this recipe. Or, you could buy a bag of ready-mixed seeds."],[null,"Store at room temperature in an airtight container for a couple of days, or in the fridge for up to one week."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"1769":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F. Line 2 baking sheets with parchment paper. Set butter out to soften."],[null,"Core and dice the apple. Toss with lemon juice to prevent browning."],[null,"Sift the flour. In a mixing bowl combine flour, oats, spices, baking soda and salt and then set aside."],[null,"In another bowl, add the softened butter and sugars and beat with an electric mixer until creamy in texture. Add in pumpkin and vanilla and stir. Add apples and stir until combined."],[null,"Add flour mixture to apple mixture and stir."],[null,"Drop cookie dough by rounded tablespoonful onto the baking sheet and gently flatten with the back of a spoon."],[null,"Bake for 12 to 15 minutes. Let cool on a wire rack. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Recipe can easily be made gluten-free with gluten-free all-purpose flour and gluten-free oats."],[null,"For glazed cookies whisk together 1/2 cup powdered sugar, 2 tablespoons heavy cream, 1 teaspoon vanilla and a pinch of cinnamon and drizzle on top of cooled cookies."]]},"7892992":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4."],[null,"Add the water to a pan, along with the sugar, stevia, ginger, cinnamon, cloves, raisins and candied peel. Stir and bring to boiling point, stirring until the sugar has dissolved."],[null,"Gradually stir in the polenta and keep stirring for 4–5 minutes until it has thickened, then remove from the heat."],[null,"In a bowl, mix the apple, egg, oil and baking powder together, then vigorously stir into the polenta."],[null,"Spoon into 25 cases and arrange on a baking sheet. Top each with either half a glacé cherry, an almond or a few pine nuts."],[null,"Place in the oven and bake for 16–20 minutes until lightly browned on top."]],"h":[]},"7404450":{"s":[[null,"Heat a splash of oil and add the onions. Cook until softening"],[null,"Add the chickpeas, lentils, tomatoes and celery"],[null,"Add the tomato puree and spices, cook for 5 minutes"],[null,"Next add the stock"],[null,"When the stock is hot through add 2 cupfuls to the sourdough starter"],[null,"When combined slowly add back into the soup"],[null,"When the vegetables and lentils are softened whizz the soup, add water to reach the desired consistency"],[null,"Add the chopped herbs and season to taste."]],"h":[]},"3638":{"s":[[null,"Combine the half & half creamer, egg product, sugar, rum extract and pumpkin pie spice in a chilled blender and blend for 1 to 2 minutes."],[null,"Pour into 6 small glasses. Top each serving with a tablespoon of whipped topping and a sprinkle of nutmeg."]],"h":[[null,"Replace sugar with low-calorie sweetener to decrease carbohydrate to 4 grams and calories to 125 per serving."],[null,"Check half & half ingredients and avoid brands with phosphate additives."]]},"6815565":{"s":[[null,"In a large pot, heat the olive oil over medium heat. Add the chopped onion and sauté until translucent, 4–5 minutes."],[null,"Add the minced garlic and freshly grated ginger. Sauté for about 1–2 minutes until fragrant. Stir in the coriander and turmeric. Cook for another minute to toast the spices."],[null,"Add the chopped carrots to the pot and sauté for a few minutes, coating them with the aromatic spices."],[null,"Pour in the vegetable broth and bring the mixture to a gentle simmer. Cover the pot and let the carrots cook until they are tender."],[null,"Once the carrots are cooked, use an immersion blender to pureé the soup until smooth. Alternatively, carefully transfer the soup to a blender and blend until smooth, then return it to the pot."],[null,"Stir in the coconut milk and season the soup with salt and pepper to taste."],[null,"Let the soup simmer for a few more minutes to heat through."],[null,"Serve the spiced ginger carrot soup hot, garnished with chopped fresh cilantro."]],"h":[]},"6363916":{"s":[[null,"Peel the oranges and slice them into rounds. Remove any seeds."],[null,"In a small saucepan over low heat, combine honey, 1 tablespoons water, ground cinnamon, ground nutmeg, ground ginger, and a pinch of sea salt. Stir until the mixture is well combined and heated through."],[null,"Arrange the orange slices on a serving platter or individual plates."],[null,"Drizzle the spiced honey glaze over the orange slices, ensuring each slice gets a flavorful coating."],[null,"Serve the oranges immediately."]],"h":[]},"7844829":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 200°C/fan 180°C/gas 6."],[null,"Mix the cumin, paprika, oregano, lemon zest and juice in a shallow dish. Add the lamb, toss to coat evenly then cover and chill for at least 1 hour, or overnight if possible."],[null,"Put the chips in a saucepan of boiling water over a high heat and cook for 5 minutes. Drain well, return to the pan and cover. Leave to cool slightly, then shake the pan to roughen the edges."],[null,"Line a baking tray with non-stick baking paper and arrange the chips over it in a single layer. Sprinkle with freshly ground black pepper and a little smoked paprika, spray with a couple of pumps of low-calorie cooking spray and bake for 25 minutes or until golden."],[null,"Preheat your grill to medium-high. Thread the lamb, onions and peppers onto 4 metal skewers and grill for 10-12 minutes, turning occasionally, until fully cooked. (You can also cook them in a non-stick griddle pan or on the barbecue for about the same amount of time.)"],[null,"Serve hot, with the lemon wedges, salad and chips and with the mint scattered over."]],"h":[[null,"Make sure lamb is cooked all the way through and you're following food safety practices."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"6459025":{"s":[[null,"Combine all ingredients, except the lemon quarters, in a gallon resealable plastic bag. Seal tightly and toss back and forth until well coated. Refrigerate 8 hours."],[null,"Heat a grill pan liberally coated with cooking spray over medium-high heat. Remove chicken from marinade, discarding marinade, and grill 3 minutes on each side or until no longer pink in center. Serve with the quartered lemon, if desired."]],"h":[]},"7212449":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200ºC/gas 6. Place the onion and mince in a medium frying pan and fry for 5-6 minutes until the mince has browned."],[null,"Add all the remaining ingredients, except the red peppers and cheese, bring to the boil and simmer for 10 minutes."],[null,"Place the pepper halves in an ovenproof dish, divide the mixture between them and sprinkle over the cheese."],[null,"Cover with foil and cook for 45 minutes until the peppers are tender."],[null,"Remove the foil and cook for a further 10 minutes until the cheese is golden."]],"h":[[null,"You could use this mince to stuff hollowed out rings of marrow or large flat mushrooms."],[null,"Minced lamb, turkey or vegetarian meat alternative also work well with this recipe."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"4965971":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F."],[null,"Sift together dry ingredients: flour, spices, baking soda, baking powder, and lemon zest."],[null,"In a separate bowl, prepare egg mixture: whisk together eggs, sugar, oil, and vanilla."],[null,"Add dry ingredients to egg mixture."],[null,"Fold in the fruits."],[null,"Pour into a non-stick loaf pan and bake for approximately 45 minutes or until loaf springs back when touched."]],"h":[[null,"* To lower the carbohydrate content you can use a sugar substitute which is suitable for baking."],[null,"After cooling you can cut the loaf in slices. Place them in freezer bags and freeze for later use."],["Raspberries: Lower-Potassium Fruit","Raspberries are a delicious fruit with many health benefits and a diet staple during the summer months. Fortunately for those with chronic kidney disease (CKD) and potassium concerns, they are also lower in potassium than many other fruits. With only 186 milligrams of potassium per 1-cup serving, they can usually be enjoyed every day if desired. Ask your dietitian how much fruit is right for you. Raspberries are also an excellent source of dietary fiber and disease fighting antioxidants. While other fruits typically contain 2–4 grams of fiber per serving, 1 cup of fresh raspberries contains 8 grams of fiber. To fully enjoy the health benefits of raspberries, add them to your cereal or muffins, toss in a salad or enjoy them as a healthy snack or dessert. When it is no longer berry season, purchase unsweetened frozen raspberries so you may enjoy them year-round."]]},"4095984":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F. Line muffin tin with liners."],[null,"In a large mixing bowl, add egg, sugar, oil, vanilla, lemon juice and milk. Whisk together to combine."],[null,"In a separate mixing bowl, sift together the dry ingredients: flour, baking soda and pumpkin pie spice."],[null,"Add the dry ingredients to the egg mixture. Mix well."],[null,"Fold-in diced pears into batter to combine."],[null,"Divide the batter evenly among the lined muffin cups."],[null,"Bake 20–25 minutes or until a tooth pick inserted in the center of the muffins comes out clean. Remove from oven and cool."],[null,"Place in a serving container. Cover and store at room temperature."]],"h":[["Adding pears to your kidney-friendly diet","Pears are a lower-potassium fruit that, in limited amounts, can typically be enjoyed every day. One small pear contains 172 milligrams of potassium and thus is considered to be a lower-potassium fruit. Enjoy pears as a snack or healthy dessert. They can also add color, flavor and texture to foods without adding sodium or a large amount of potassium. Add sliced or chopped pears to salads for extra flavor and crunch. Pears ripen best at room temperature as refrigeration will slow down the ripening process. It can be tough to judge how ripe a pear might be. Bartlett pears change from green to yellow as they ripen, but most varieties show very little color change. Pears ripen from the inside out, so the best way to judge how ripe it might be is to apply gentle pressure with your thumb to the stem end of the pear. If it yields to gentle pressure, then the pear is ripe. If it is firm, leave the pear at room temperature and check daily for ripeness."]]},"7544325":{"s":[[null,"Place all the ingredients into a large pan with a tight fitting lid."],[null,"Cover and cook over a low heat for 45 minutes, stirring occasionally, until the cabbage is tender. Serve."]],"h":[[null,"Adding vinegar to red cabbage while it is cooking, helps it keep its colour."],[null,"You could add raisins and/or walnuts to the cabbage when almost ready."],[null,"You can also use raw red cabbage to make a really colourful coleslaw."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"4000258":{"s":[[null,"Prepare the marinade: add olive oil, lemon juice, vinegar, honey and spices in a mixing bowl and whisk to combine."],[null,"Slice each salmon fillet lengthwise to make 4 separate 3-ounce pieces of salmon. Add the salmon to the bowl, making sure that all the salmon is covered with the marinade."],[null,"Cover the bowl and refrigerate for 30-60 minutes, then remove from refrigerator and let sit at room temperature for 10 minutes."],[null,"Heat oil in a large skillet pan over medium-high heat. Place the salmon fillets in the pan and cook them for about 4 minutes on each side, or until salmon reaches 145⁰ F."]],"h":[]},"6416905":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F and cover a sheet pan with parchment paper. In a small saucepan over medium high heat, whisk together maple syrup, salt, cinnamon, and cayenne."],[null,"Bring to a boil and remove from heat immediately."],[null,"Fold the peanuts and sesame seeds into the maple syrup mixture and spread evenly on the sheet pan."],[null,"Bake for 15 to 18 minutes until golden brown."],[null,"Remove the sheet pan from the oven and allow the peanuts to cool."],[null,"Store in an airtight container at room temperature."]],"h":[]},"6438385":{"s":[[null,"Coat a grill rack with cooking spray. Preheat the grill to medium-high. If you think your shrimp will fall through the grilling rack, prepare a fish basket to grill the shrimp in and coat the inside of the basket with cooking spray."],[null,"Drizzle the shrimp with the olive oil. Combine the cumin, chili powder, coriander, salt, and black pepper and rub onto the shrimp."],[null,"Six inches away from the heat source, add the shrimp directly to the grill rack or place in a single layer in the fish basket. Grill the shrimp for about 2 to 3 minutes per side or until cooked through. Meanwhile, add the lemon halves, cut side down, and grill for 3 to 4 minutes, just until the lemon is slightly charred."],[null,"Add the grilled shrimp to a platter. Garnish with the grilled lemon halves and minced parsley."]],"h":[]},"6201524":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350°F. Coat a 1 1/2- to 2-quart casserole dish with nonstick cooking spray; set aside. Add water to a large saucepot until it’s 2/3 full. Add the sweet potato to the pot and bring to boiling over medium heat. Cook the sweet potato for 20 minutes. Add the carrots to the pot and continue to cook for 15 to 20 minutes, until vegetables are tender. Drain, reserving 1/4 cup of the cooking water, and add the vegetables to a bowl."],[null,"Mash the sweet potato and carrots and the 1/4 cup reserved cooking water with a potato masher. Add 2 Tbsp. of the buttery spread, the brown sugar, cinnamon, cloves, and nutmeg, and mix well. Add the mixture to the prepared casserole dish. Top with the pecans and the remaining melted buttery spread."],[null,"Bake the casserole, covered, for 15 minutes. Uncover and bake 10 minutes more, until the top is lightly browned."]],"h":[]},"6252417":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 425°F."],[null,"Spray baking sheet with nonstick cooking spray."],[null,"Cut sweet potatoes into thick strips or wedges and put in a gallon-size Ziploc bag."],[null,"Add the olive oil and shake until the sweet potato pieces are coated. Place the uncooked “fries” on the prepared baking sheet in a single layer."],[null,"Mix the spices in a small bowl. Sprinkle the spice mix over the sweet potatoes."],[null,"Bake for 45 minutes to an hour."]],"h":[]},"9498029":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 450 degrees F convection bake."],[null,"Arrange your prepared veggies on a large baking tray lined with parchment paper. Sprinkle generously with salt and pepper. Then bake for 20-25 minutes, until fork tender and golden."],[null,"Slice the stem off your jalapeno and transfer the cooked veggies to a pot along with the broth and all the seasoning. Puree using an immersion blender. OR, use a stand blender, working in batches to puree your soup."],[null,"Serve garnished with cashew cream and fresh herbs, if desired."]],"h":[[null,"For less spice , remove the seeds from your jalapeno before blending into your soup. Weigh your potatoes and squash for best results . Since potatoes and squash vary greatly in size, weight will give the most accurate consistency. If you have an immersion blender , you may transfer the roasted veggies and remaining ingredients to a pot and puree the soup in one batch. To blend with a stand blender , work in as many batches as needed. (I was able to do mine in two batches.) Just be sure to reserve some broth for each batch, as your blender will need some liquid in order to puree the soup. Once each batch is pureed , transfer to a pot or large enough dish to fit all your soup and mix well to evenly distribute the seasoning. To save time on prep , you may purchase pre-cubed squash and sweet potato from your grocery store. Or you may prep ahead by peeling and cutting your vegetables up to 2 days in advance. Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3 days or you may freeze for up to 3 months."]]},"6733514":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F. Pat the turkey breast dry and place on a rack set in a shallow roasting pan. Loosen the skin by inserting your fingers, gently pushing between the skin and the meat."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine the orange juice, 2 tsp of the ginger, 1 tsp of the cinnamon, 1 tsp of the cloves, allspice, salt, and black pepper. Rub this mixture on the breast meat, under the skin. Roast the breast uncovered for about 1 hour 15 minutes, or until a meat thermometer registers 170 degrees F, making sure it doesn’t touch the breastbone. Check the turkey every 15 minutes or so as it roasts to avoid any overbrowning. Cover with foil if the breast meat starts to get too brown. After 30 minutes of roasting, you may also lower the oven to 350 degrees if the turkey is cooking too quickly."],[null,"Meanwhile, prepare the chutney. In a saucepan, combine the red onion, brown sugar, rice vinegar, raisins, remaining 1/2 tsp ginger, remaining 1/4 tsp cinnamon, remaining 1/4 tsp cloves, and crushed red pepper, and bring to boiling. Cover, reduce the heat, and simmer for 5 minutes. Remove the pan from the heat and cool for 10 minutes. Fold in the apples."],[null,"Remove the turkey breast to a platter and let it stand, loosely covered with foil, for about 10 minutes before serving."],[null,"To serve, slice the turkey, discard the skin, and serve with the chutney. Store the remaining 1 cup chutney, covered, in the refrigerator for up to three days."]],"h":[]},"2352":{"s":[[null,"Slice beef into bite-size pieces."],[null,"Wash and dry the basil leaves and chop coarsely. Dice onion into 1/2-inch pieces and dice bell pepper into 1/4-inch pieces. Mince the garlic."],[null,"If time permits, mix the beef, basil and 1/2 tablespoon peanut oil in a bowl. Cover and refrigerate for 1 hour or longer. Otherwise, mix together beef and basil."],[null,"Preheat a wok or large skillet over medium heat for 3 minutes. Add the remaining peanut oil and swirl it around the pan."],[null,"Add the garlic and onion, stirring a few times. Cook until the onion is soft, about 5 minutes."],[null,"Turn the heat up to high and add the beef-basil mixture. Stir quickly and add the red pepper flakes. Cook just until meat loses its redness, about 3 to 5 minutes depending on the size of the beef pieces."],[null,"Stir in the red bell pepper."],[null,"Stir soy sauce into cornstarch, beef broth and lime juice. Add to beef and cook until bubbling. Turn off heat and serve immediately, over rice."]],"h":[[null,"Try adding orange zest for extra flavor."],[null,"Change portion to 1/2 cup for a lower protein diet and increase the amount of rice for extra calories if needed."],[null,"If brown rice is preferred this will add 44mg phosphorus and 53mg of potassium per serving."]]},"2751":{"s":[[null,"Stir oil and flour together to make a paste."],[null,"Chop onion."],[null,"Add all remaining ingredients."],[null,"Cook the mixture on low heat until it thickens."],[null,"Brush sauce on baked or grilled meat."]],"h":[[null,"Kitchen Bouquet® is a browning and seasoning sauce composed of caramel with vegetable flavorings."]]},"7900398":{"s":[[null,"Spread the tortillas lightly with nut butter."],[null,"Mix everything else apart from the red onion together, and spread over one tortilla, laying the other tortilla on top."],[null,"Cook in a non-stick pan over a low heat (no need for oil) until the tortilla is turning browned and crisp."],[null,"Turn the tortilla over and cook the other side (3-5 minutes each side)."],[null,"Place on a board and slice, then scatter with red onion and coriander. Serve with salad."]],"h":[[null,"You can make up the tortillas in advance and fry when ready to eat."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"2990":{"s":[[null,"Dice the onion and tomato. Peel and chop the carrots. Cut stew meat into cubes."],[null,"In a large pan, heat oil until hot. Add the beef and cook and stir over medium heat until browned."],[null,"Add the onion to the meat and sauté until clear, about 5 to 7 minutes."],[null,"Add the water, tomato paste, red and black peppers and curry powder. Cover pan and cook over medium-low heat until vegetables are tender, 20 to 25 minutes."],[null,"Add the peanut butter and stir to combine. Cover and cook over low heat for an additional 20 minutes."],[null,"Serve over hot rice."]],"h":[[null,"Adjust the red pepper to taste."],[null,"Refrigerate or freeze leftover stew."]]},"2018":{"s":[[null,"Thinly slice red onion. Dice bell peppers."],[null,"Heat oil in a medium-sized pan, add the red onion and cook for 5 minutes."],[null,"Season onion with black pepper and curry powder and cook for 5 more minutes."],[null,"Stir in the bell peppers and cook for 15 minutes, stirring several times."],[null,"Season with salt and turn off heat. Let stand for about 5 minutes."],[null,"Serve hot with flour tortillas or over rice."]],"h":[[null,"Bolst’s® curry powder is Sindu’s favorite brand for this recipe."],[null,"One medium bell pepper yields approximately 1 cup. One medium red onion yields approximately 1 cup."],[null,"Do you need more protein in your diet? Before serving, mix-in 3 scoops of protein powder or add your favorite protein food to make this a protein-fortified dish."]]},"7505781":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a saucepan. Add the onion, chilli and garlic, and fry for 4-5 minutes until softened."],[null,"Add the squash and continue to fry for 5 minutes. Stir in the curry paste and fry for a further minute."],[null,"Pour 500ml boiling water over the squash, crumble in the stock cube and bring to the boil. Cover and simmer for 15-20 minutes, until the squash is tender. Transfer to a food processor or blender and blend until smooth."],[null,"Return to the pan, add the coconut milk and coriander. Heat through and serve sprinkled with black pepper. Garnish with a slice of chilli and torn coriander leaves."]],"h":[[null,"If you don't like things too spicy, omit the chilli and use a mild curry paste or powder instead."],[null,"You could make this soup with sweet potato instead of butternut squash."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Freeze in portions then defrost in the fridge, or defrost in a microwave taking care to stir regularly."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"4414020":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350⁰ F."],[null,"Let cream cheese soften at room temperature, or microwave for 20 seconds to soften."],[null,"Puree the red bell pepper in a blender."],[null,"Mix cream cheese and sour cream in a bowl. Add the red bell pepper puree, Tabasco sauce, onion powder, green onions and stir mixture."],[null,"Add cooked shredded chicken and stir until combined."],[null,"Bake in the oven for 20 minutes."],[null,"Serve warm with fresh vegetables (carrots, celery, bell peppers, etc.)."]],"h":[[null,"Nutrition info for dip only."]]},"3273":{"s":[[null,"Chop the onion and cilantro; mince the garlic and ginger. Drain and rinse the chickpeas."],[null,"Heat the oil in a large skillet and sauté onion, garlic and ginger for 3 minutes."],[null,"Add the tomatoes and cook for 3 to 4 minutes."],[null,"Add the chili powder, coriander powder, garam masala and turmeric; mix well and cook for 1 minute."],[null,"Add the chickpeas and 1/2 cup of water. Simmer for 10 to 15 minutes."],[null,"Serve with cilantro and lemon wedge. If desired, serve with naan bread, pita or rice."]],"h":[[null,"Chickpeas are also called garbanzo beans."],[null,"Rinsing the chickpeas reduces sodium. For even lower sodium look for low-sodium canned chickpeas or boil dried chickpeas."],[null,"Garam masala is a blend of ground spices commonly used in dishes from India."],[null,"Bean dishes that replace meat can be worked into most kidney diets. Ask your dietitian for guidance."]]},"3362":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400° F."],[null,"In large mixing bow, combine flour, cornmeal, sugar, baking powder, chili powder and pepper. Stir to combine."],[null,"Add rice milk, egg, egg white and oil to dry ingredients and stir just until moistened."],[null,"Gently stir scallions, carrots and garlic into cornbread mixture."],[null,"Pour batter into an 8”-square baking pan which been coated with nonstick cooking spray."],[null,"Bake for 25 to 30 minutes, until top starts to turn golden brown. Cut into eight 2” x 4” pieces."]],"h":[[null,"For variation, try onion instead of scallions and red bell pepper instead of carrots."]]},"7585916":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in non-stick frying pan. Add the onion, ginger, garlic, chilli flakes and cumin and fry for 2–3 minutes."],[null,"Remove the pan from the heat and stir in the crab meat and coriander."],[null,"Warm the tortilla according to the pack insructions."],[null,"Add some salad leaves and tomato slices to each tortilla. Top with the crab mixture and a squeeze of lime."]],"h":[[null,"To warm tortillas, add them all in a stack to a dry frying pan over a medium heat, take the bottom one and move to the top and keep doing this until they have all had a minute in contact with the hot pan. You can repeat on the other side for 30 seconds to get them really hot but still keep them soft and pliable."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"9317037":{"s":[["Press the tofu","Cut your tofu into half-inch cubes. Then arrange some paper towels or a clean dish towel on a cutting board and place the tofu cubes in a single layer on top. Now add more paper towels on top of the cubes and place another cutting board, flat plate, or baking sheet on top. Finally, place something very heavy on top like a cast-iron skillet or a heavy book. Press like this for 15 minutes while you prepare the remaining ingredients."],["For the tofu","Preheat the oven to 425°F/218°C convection bake and line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],["For the tofu","Add the pressed tofu cubes to a mixing bowl and gently toss with the soy sauce and hot sauce. Then add the onion powder and cornstarch and gently mix."],["For the tofu","Arrange the coated tofu cubes in a single layer on your baking sheet, leaving space between each piece. Bake for 20-25 minutes, flipping once after 10 minutes.NOTE: If you do not have a convection oven, it may take a little longer to reach desired crispiness."],["For the sauce","While the tofu is baking, combine all the sauce ingredients in a shallow pan, whisk until combined and simmer over medium-high heat until thickened, approximately 2-3 minutes."],["For the sauce","Add the baked crispy tofu to the pan with the marinade and stir to coat."],["For the sauce","Serve with grains, veggies, and garnishes of your choice."]],"h":[[null,"Arrange the cubes of tofu in a single layer with space between each piece . They shouldn't touch each other on the baking tray in order to get the maximum crisp level."],[null,"If you don't have a convection oven , it may take a few extra minutes for the tofu to get crispy. Bake until the desired crispiness level is reached."],[null,"For best texture , plan to enjoy this dish immediately. The longer it sits in the sauce, it will lose some of its crispy exterior."]]},"1746":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 250°F."],[null,"Melt margarine in a 10” x 15” pan. Stir in spices, Worcestershire sauce and lemon juice."],[null,"Add cereals, crackers and pretzels. Toss to coat evenly."],[null,"Bake for 45 minutes; gently mix every 15 minutes."],[null,"Spread on paper towels to cool."],[null,"Store in airtight container."]],"h":[[null,"Compare brands—cereals, crackers and pretzels vary greatly in sodium content. Always get the brand with the least amount of sodium."]]},"7002183":{"s":[[null,"Place the duck breasts in a non-metallic dish and rub all over with the Chinese 5 spice powder. Leave to marinate for at least 10 minutes. Slice the duck into small pieces."],[null,"Heat the oil in a non-stick frying pan. Add the duck and fry for 2-3 minutes until crisp and golden."],[null,"Mix together the cucumber, coriander and spring onions and place a little onto each poppadom."],[null,"Spoon on a little mango chutney and top each poppadom with a piece of duck."]],"h":[[null,"You could use chicken breast or lean steak in place of duck."],[null,"For a vegan version, replace the duck with small cubes of tofu."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"6342617":{"s":[[null,"Place canola oil in wok or large sauté pan. Add ginger and cook until fragrant. Add garlic and chicken and stir-fry until chicken is no longer translucent."],[null,"Add bok choy, bell pepper, and scallion and cook until bok choy begins to wilt."],[null,"Add stock, soy sauce, chili sauce and cilantro. Stir-fry until hot and well blended. Serve over brown rice."]],"h":[]},"1753":{"s":[[null,"Remove tips from green beans and cut into pieces. Finely chop onion. Seed and slice chili pepper and chop cilantro."],[null,"Steam the green beans to desired doneness (5 to 10 minutes). Rinse with water to cool."],[null,"Toss green beans with all remaining ingredients except egg whites."],[null,"Chop egg whites and sprinkle on top shortly before serving. Serve chilled or at room temperature."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute frozen green beans when fresh beans are out of season."],[null,"Use fresh-squeezed lime juice."]]},"6504360":{"s":[[null,"In a large (10-inch) cast iron skillet, sauté onions over medium heat until softened, about 3 minutes. Stir in the garlic and cook for an additional minute."],[null,"Increase the heat slightly and add the eggplant. Cook for about 5 minutes, stirring occasionally. Allow the eggplant to brown slightly."],[null,"Stir in the tomatoes, water, red pepper, and spices. Bring to a low boil. Stir in the kale and spinach and allow the greens to wilt."],[null,"Make 4 wells in the vegetable mixture. Crack the eggs one at a time and place them each in a separate cup or small bowl. Gently place each egg in a well in the vegetable mixture."],[null,"Cover the shakshuka and allow the eggs to poach until the yolks are firm, about 10–12 minutes."],[null,"Serve with chopped parsley if desired."]],"h":[]},"6666824":{"s":[[null,"In a blender or food processor, combine three roughly chopped green onions, garlic, soy sauce, gochujang, brown sugar alternative, sesame oil, and rice wine vinegar. Blend until smooth."],[null,"Place the chicken tenderloins in a large resealable plastic bag or shallow dish. Pour the marinade over the chicken, reserving 2 tablespoons for serving. Seal the bag or cover the dish and refrigerate for at least 20 minutes to marinate."],[null,"In a medium bowl, combine the sliced cucumbers, chopped red chili, sliced green onion, and cilantro."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the rice wine vinegar and ½ tsp brown sugar alternative until the sugar dissolves. Drizzle this dressing over the cucumber mixture and toss to coat. Set aside."],[null,"Preheat a lightly oiled grill pan or skillet over medium heat."],[null,"Remove the chicken from the marinade, allowing any excess to drip off. Place the chicken on the grill pan and cook for 6- 8 minutes, turning occasionally, until the chicken is cooked through and has a slight char."],[null,"Drizzle with the reserved marinade and sprinkle with 1 Tbsp toasted sesame seeds and two sliced green onions."]],"h":[]},"2783":{"s":[[null,"Chop onion, celery and bell pepper."],[null,"Melt butter in a nonstick frying pan and sauté onion, celery, and green bell pepper. Stir into hot pasta."],[null,"Mix lemon juice, lemon zest, and Mrs. Dash® herb seasoning. Add to hot pasta and stir. Serve."]],"h":[[null,"Use pasta of choice. Cook according to package directions omitting salt."]]},"6806074":{"s":[[null,"Coat a large soup pot with cooking spray. Over medium-high heat, sauté the sausage until lightly brown."],[null,"Add the celery, onions, carrots, and red bell pepper to the pot and sauté over medium-high heat for approximately 4 minutes or until the onions begin to turn clear."],[null,"Add the water, broth, lentils, salt, pepper, and bay leaf. Bring to a boil and reduce the heat. Simmer on low heat for 1 hour."],[null,"Remove the bay leaf. Sprinkle with parsley and serve."]],"h":[]},"3472":{"s":[[null,"Drain peaches; reserve the juice and set aside."],[null,"Combine cornstarch, whole cloves, cinnamon, nutmeg, ground cloves and orange rind in a medium saucepan."],[null,"Add reserved peach juice to the spice mixture. Stir mixture well and add peaches."],[null,"Bring mixture to a boil, stirring constantly. When mixture begins to boil, reduce heat and simmer for 2 minutes."],[null,"Divide peaches into dessert dishes; serve warm."]],"h":[[null,"Use sliced peaches instead of halves if desired."],[null,"For higher calories use peaches canned in heavy syrup."]]},"4892893":{"s":[[null,"Rehydrate the porcini mushrooms with 1/2 cup boiling water."],[null,"Bring 3 quarts of water to boil for the pasta."],[null,"Meanwhile prepare the sauce by heating the oil over medium heat in a large pan. The pan needs to be large enough to hold the noodles once cooked."],[null,"Add the garlic and hot pepper flakes, cooking them until garlic turns golden."],[null,"Add the white mushrooms, raise the temperature to medium-high and continue to cook."],[null,"Cook pasta in boiling water according to package directions."],[null,"Squeeze the liquid from the porcini, reserving it for the sauce. Chop the porcini and add to the pan."],[null,"Pour the soaking liquid through a fine sieve into the pan."],[null,"Add sage and cook for 5 minutes. [10 Drain the pasta (DO NOT RINSE) and toss into the pan with the mushroom sauce while hot. Add boconcini cheese, parsley and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Make ahead of time or freeze in portions. Recipe can easily be doubled. Leftovers freeze well. Defrost in fridge overnight, heat adding 2 tablespoons of water and serve."]]},"7034894":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200ºC/gas 6."],[null,"Place the potato wedges in a large pan of boiling water and simmer for 5 minutes. Drain and place in a large roasting tin."],[null,"Mix together the oil and the paprika and toss through the potato wedges. Place on a baking tray and cook for 20-25 minutes until golden and crisp."],[null,"For the garlic and herb dip, simply combine all the ingredients and spoon into a serving dish."],[null,"Drain any excess liquid from the tomatoes then blend with the chilli, garlic and coriander for 30 seconds. Spoon into a serving dish."],[null,"Serve the potatoes with the dips."]],"h":[[null,"If you’re passing these around as finger food, omit the paprika from the potatoes as it stains the fingers!"],[null,"You could use Chinese 5 Spice powder in place of paprika, or try dried thyme."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Wedges are suitable for freezing. Defrost in the microwave and reheat in the oven until piping hot."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"7741982":{"s":[[null,"Prepare the onion, red pepper, chestnut mushrooms, garlic and red chilli, and set aside."],[null,"Heat a wok or large frying pan over a high heat, add the rapeseed oil and when hot add the onion. Stir-fry for 2 minutes, then add the red pepper, mushrooms, garlic and chilli, and stir-fry for 1 minute."],[null,"Add the prawns, soy sauce, Chinese five-spice and pak choi stems, and keep stirring for a further 3–4 minutes until the prawns are cooked. The flesh of the prawns should turn pink or orange when cooked and loose their translucent appearance."],[null,"Add the pak choi leaves and water, cover with a lid and cook for a further minute. Mix well and serve immediately."],[null,"Serve with noodles or a few thin slices of red chilli and a wedge of lime."]],"h":[[null,"Assemble the ingredients first, ready to throw into the pan. And, always make sure the pan is really hot before you start adding them."],[null,"Stir-frying is a quick way to cook and more nutrients are retained in your food. You don't need much oil and as long as you keep stirring it around the pan, the food is steamed rather than fried."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"7256542":{"s":[[null,"Drain and rinse the chickpeas, and pat dry with kitchen paper."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 190°C/gas 5. Oil a large baking tray with 1 tsp rapeseed oil and place the tray in the oven for 3 minutes."],[null,"Spread the chickpeas onto the hot baking tray and cook for 15 minutes, mixing a couple of times to make sure they cook evenly."],[null,"Remove from the oven, place the chickpeas in a bowl and drizzle with the remaining oil. Mix well. Add the cumin and chilli powder. Mix again and tip back onto the baking tray."],[null,"Roast for another 10-15 minutes until brown and crunchy."],[null,"Serve immediately or enjoy cool."]],"h":[[null,"These can be made the day before and stored in an airtight container. If you’d like to serve them warm just reheat in a hot oven for two minutes."],[null,"This snack counts as half a portion of fruit and veg."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"3484":{"s":[[null,"Steam-cook rice according to package to make 6 cups cooked rice."],[null,"Thinly chop yellow onion, bell pepper, celery and green onions. Mince garlic cloves. Chop parsley. Set green onions and parsley aside for later use."],[null,"Peel and devein shrimp. Set aside."],[null,"In a medium saucepan, melt butter over medium heat."],[null,"Sauté yellow onion, bell pepper, celery and garlic. Stir often for about 10 minutes."],[null,"Add seasonings (cayenne, lemon pepper, white pepper, paprika, oregano, thyme and basil), stirring well for about 2 minutes."],[null,"Add the tomato paste and flour and continue stirring well for 3 minutes."],[null,"Add water, stir, and simmer for 10 minutes, stirring occasionally."],[null,"Add seafood, green onion and parsley to simmering water. Mix well and bring to a boil."],[null,"Cover, reduce heat to low and simmer for 10 minutes."],[null,"Remove from heat and leave covered for 5 minutes."],[null,"Serve over steamed rice and enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Decrease the cayenne pepper to 1/4 teaspoon or less if you prefer less heat."],[null,"Remember to limit fluids, even though this dish is lower in salt, spicy food may lead to excessive fluid intake. Use ice in drinks to minimize fluid intake or reduce cayenne pepper in the recipe as needed."],[null,"Measuring out all of the ingredients first before starting is recommended, so not to be frantically preparing ingredients while cooking."],[null,"This dish can be a little expensive, especially if seafood is not readily accessible. Ingredients can generally be found at a local grocery store."],[null,"For a healthy twist with full flavor, Daniel recommends Land o’ Lakes® Butter with Olive Oil and Sea Salt instead of regular butter."],[null,"If fresh crab is unavailable try Blue Star® pouch lump meat. It tastes fresher that canned crab."],[null,"2 cups regular long grain white rice yields 6 cups cooked. If you use converted (parboiled) rice or medium or short grain rice refer to package instructions for correct portion to make 6 cups cooked rice."],[null,"For people with diabetes you can decrease rice to 1/2 cup. This lowers the carbohydrate to 32 grams. Count as 2 carbohydrate choices."]]},"2398":{"s":[[null,"Dice onion, cut bell pepper julienne style and slice zucchini."],[null,"Heat oil, onion and corn in a skillet over medium-high heat. Cook 8 to 10 minutes, stirring frequently until onion turns translucent and corn begins to brown."],[null,"Add bell pepper, zucchini, mushrooms, black pepper, chili flakes and water. Stir and cover. Cook 3 to 5 minutes until zucchini is tender and water has evaporated."],[null,"Remove from heat and stir in barbeque sauce. Divide into 4 portions and serve."]],"h":[[null,"1 medium ear of fresh corn yields 3/4 to 1 cup of corn kernels. You can also use frozen or low-sodium canned corn."],[null,"1 medium-sized zucchini yields 1 cup sliced."],[null,"Julienne means to cut in thin, long strips."],[null,"Compare labels to select commercial barbeque sauce with the lowest sodium content."]]},"7737810":{"s":[[null,"Put all the spices in a bowl and mix well."],[null,"Spray a large non-stick frying pan with a couple of pumps of low-calorie cooking spray and put it over a medium-high heat. Add the mushrooms, peppers, spring onions, ginger, garlic and chilli and fry for about 8 minutes, or until everything just starts to brown."],[null,"Using your fingers, crumble in the tofu to get a nice ‘scrambled egg’ texture. Stir in the spice mix and stir-fry for another 6-8 minutes."],[null,"Season with pepper to taste and scatter over the dill to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Check spice/seasoning blends for added ingredients such as sugar, salt, flour or oil. Choose blends made from herbs and spices only if possible."],[null,"Find out more about our partnership with Slimming World."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"9717936":{"s":[[null,"Add all your ingredients to a high-speed blender, starting with just 1/3 cup of the water, and blend until smooth. Start on low and gradually increase the speed so you don't have loose cashew bits flying to the top of the blender. Once smooth, add the remaining water (if desired) and blend to combine."],[null,"Refrigerate for at least one hour, as it tastes best cold. Then serve with veggies, fries, pizza, sandwiches, wraps, or burgers. Enjoy"]],"h":[[null,"Nutritional info is for one tenth of the recipe, approx 2 tablespoons, using the cashew method. If subbing for pumpkin seeds, the calories and fat will be much lower. If you don’t have a Vitamix or a high speed blender, soak your cashews in boiling hot water for 30 minutes and then drain. Scrape down the sides if needed for a smooth and creamy consistency. Start blending with only ⅓ cup of the called for water at first. This helps with a smoother consistency since the cashew pieces have less room to float around. Then add the extra 2 tablespoons and blend to combine."]]},"9807591":{"s":[["Oven Instructions","Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F."],["Oven Instructions","Combine all the dry ingredients in a bowl and mix well. Then combine the wet ingredients in a separate bowl and whisk to combine."],["Oven Instructions","Pour the wet into the dry and start mixing until mostly combined and you have what resembles dough. Then transfer to a clean surface or cutting board and use your hands to knead and press the dough for 1-2 minutes. It should feel soft and look well combined."],["Oven Instructions","Now cut your dough into two equally sized pieces and roll them out into salami shapes that will be about 6 inches long. It doesn't have to be perfect, it will get smooth as it cooks. Then wrap each salami with parchment paper and then aluminum foil, making sure the foil is long enough to overlap and then twist the ends. (See process shots above for a visual.)"],["Oven Instructions","Place the wrapped salami on a baking sheet and bake for 45-55 minutes, flipping them over at the halfway point."],["Oven Instructions","Remove from the oven and gently peel the foil to see if the salami appear smooth and poke with your finger to test its firmness. They should feel firm, but still give a little to pressure. They will firm up more as they cool."],["Oven Instructions","Let cool completely, then slice and enjoy with pizza, in sandwiches, on a charcuterie board, or as a snack."],["Steaming Instructions","Follow steps 2-4 above to prepare your salami. Then add 1-2\" of water to a large pot that will fit your steamer basket, WITHOUT the water touching your basket. Bring to a boil and then reduce heat to maintain a low boil and place the salami inside your basket."],["Steaming Instructions","Cover and steam for 45-60 minutes, keeping an eye on your water to make sure it doesn't completely evaporate. Start checking on them around the 45 minute mark. Gently remove the foil, the salami should appear smooth. You may give it a poke with your finger or tongs to test firmness. They should feel firm but still give a little to pressure. They'll firm up more as they cool."],["Steaming Instructions","Let cool completely, then slice and enjoy with pizza, in sandwiches, on a charcuterie board, or as a snack."]],"h":[[null,"Make sure to knead and mix your dough very well for even flavour and best texture. Don’t spend too much time fussing over perfectly shaped salami . It will appear bumpy before baking, but gets nice and smooth while it cooks. If you don’t like having foil touch your food , use parchment paper between your salami and aluminum foil layer. For mild vegan salami , simply omit the chili flakes, but keep in the black pepper for best flavour. Keep refrigerated in a sealed container or zip top bag for up to 1 week. Or you may freeze for up to 3 months."]]},"7416466":{"s":[[null,"Cut wraps into halves ready to make into pockets for the healthy samosa."],[null,"Spray a couple of pumps of oil into the pan on medium heat and roast cumin seeds."],[null,"Add and sauté the onions, garlic and ginger until soft."],[null,"Add cubed sweet potatoes (cut to the size of a pea) and mixed vegetables. Season with garam masala, turmeric, sesame seeds and chilli flakes. Cover and cook on medium heat (add a splash of water so the mixture doesn’t dry and helps soften the vegetables) for about 20 minutes or until soft."],[null,"Add the lemon juice, sprinkle with the fresh coriander and allow the mix to cool."],[null,"Use a flour and water paste to seal the straight cut side of your wrap “pockets.” It should be a glue-like consistency."],[null,"Fill with the cooled vegetable mixture and seal the curved side of the pocket."],[null,"Refrigerate for 30 minutes to allow the pockets to seal."],[null,"Bake in the oven until golden."]],"h":[[null,"This recipe has been created by Balance cover star, Shivali, as part of her journey to diabetes remission."],[null,"These samosas can also be cooked in an air fryer until crisp and golden."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"6683124":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F. Line a sheet pan with foil and spray it with cooking spray."],[null,"Clean mushrooms, remove the stems, and gently remove the gills with a spoon. Brush the surface of the mushrooms with olive oil. Place the mushrooms on the prepared sheet pan, stem side up."],[null,"Bake for 10–15 minutes, until just soft. If there is liquid in the mushroom cap, drain it and place it back down on the sheet pan."],[null,"While they are baking, spray a large non-stick skillet with cooking spray and heat over medium heat. Add the egg substitute and cook, stirring until light and fluffy. Stir in the spinach and continue cooking until it wilts. Stir in the pepper, red pepper flakes, and cottage cheese. Remove from the heat."],[null,"Place 1/4 to 1/2 cup of the egg and spinach mixture into the mushroom caps. Sprinkle each with 1 to 1 1/2 tsp of Parmesan cheese."],[null,"Place the mushrooms under the broiler until the cheese begins to brown. Remove from the oven. Garnish with chopped fresh basil and serve."]],"h":[]},"6586894":{"s":[[null,"Place eggs and egg whites in a medium bowl. Whisk together with black pepper, garlic powder, and smoked paprika."],[null,"Heat olive oil in a nonstick skillet over medium heat. Add red onion and bell pepper. Sauté for 2–3 minutes until softened. Stir in the spinach and cook for an additional 1–2 minutes until wilted. Remove vegetables from the skillet and set aside."],[null,"Wipe the skillet clean and spray the skillet with cooking spray. Return to medium-low heat. Pour 1/4 of the egg mixture into the skillet, tilting to spread it evenly. Cook for 2–3 minutes until the edges are set. Sprinkle 1/4 of the cooked vegetables and 1 teaspoon of feta cheese on one side of the omelette."],[null,"Gently fold the omelet in half and cook for an additional 1–2 minutes until fully set. Transfer to a plate and repeat for the remaining omelets. Lightly toast the bread slices."]],"h":[]},"6129816":{"s":[[null,"In a bowl, season the egg substitute with salt and pepper and mix together."],[null,"Heat olive oil in a non-stick skillet over medium heat."],[null,"Add diced red onions and sauté until softened."],[null,"Add chopped spinach to the skillet and cook until wilted."],[null,"Pour the whisked eggs over the spinach and onions."],[null,"As the eggs begin to set, sprinkle diced tomatoes and crumbled feta cheese over half the omelet."],[null,"Once the eggs are fully set, carefully fold the omelet in half with a spatula."],[null,"Slide the omelet onto a plate, garnish with fresh herbs if desired, and serve."]],"h":[]},"6457517":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 375 degrees F and line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"In a skillet, heat 1 tablespoon of olive oil over medium heat. Add the minced garlic and chopped spinach, and sauté for 2–3 minutes until the spinach wilts and any excess moisture evaporates. Remove the skillet from the heat."],[null,"In a mixing bowl, combine the sautéed spinach and garlic with crumbled feta cheese, grated Parmesan cheese, plain Greek yogurt, salt, and pepper. Ensure all the ingredients are thoroughly mixed."],[null,"Take the cleaned mushrooms and fill each cap with the spinach and cheese mixture, gently pressing it down."],[null,"Arrange the stuffed mushrooms on the prepared baking sheet. If desired, you can lightly spray them with cooking spray to aid in browning."],[null,"Bake the stuffed mushrooms in the preheated oven for approximately 15–20 minutes or until they become tender, and the filling is heated through and slightly browned."]],"h":[]},"6067326":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F."],[null,"In a skillet, heat olive oil over medium heat."],[null,"Add diced red onions and cook until softened."],[null,"Add chopped spinach to the skillet and cook until wilted."],[null,"In a bowl, whisk the egg whites and season with oregano, salt, and pepper."],[null,"Grease a muffin tin with cooking spray."],[null,"Distribute the sautéed spinach and onions evenly among the muffin tin cups."],[null,"Pour the whisked egg whites over the spinach and onions in each cup. Sprinkle diced tomatoes and mozzarella cheese on top."],[null,"Bake in the preheated oven for 15 minutes or until the egg whites are set."],[null,"Allow the egg white bites to cool for a few minutes before removing them from the muffin tin."]],"h":[]},"7920525":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4. Blend together the tomatoes, tomato puree, garlic and oregano to make a tomato sauce, then set aside."],[null,"Heat the oil in a pan and add the onion. Cook for 2–3 minutes, add the red pepper and cook a further 2–3 minutes. Add the mushrooms, cook for 2 minutes then gradually stir in the flour to coat the vegetables."],[null,"Gradually, stir in the milk until it starts to thicken, add the spinach and stir for 1 minute then stir in the cream cheese, mustard and black pepper."],[null,"To an ovenproof dish add a little of the tomato sauce then top with a layer of lasagne sheets. Now add a layer of the mushroom, spinach and cream cheese mix and repeat until you end with a layer of tomato sauce then top with the thinly sliced tomatoes."],[null,"Sprinkle with Cheddar and bake for 30–35 minutes. Scatter with fresh basil to serve."]],"h":[[null,"For a gluten-free version or if you’re watching your carb intake, use 3-4 sliced aubergines in place of the lasagne sheets and use gluten-free flour in the sauce."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat until piping-hot throughout."],[null,"Serve alongside a large leafy green salad for extra vitamins, minerals and to add freshness to the dish."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"6149928":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F. Spray a baking dish with cooking spray."],[null,"Add the oil to a medium sauté pan over medium-high heat. Add the spinach and sauté for 3 minutes. Add the mushroom and cook an additional 4-5 minutes. Add the garlic and sauté for 30 seconds."],[null,"Place one chicken breast on a cutting board and cover it with plastic wrap. Pound the chicken with a meat tenderizer or rolling pin until it is about 1/4-inch thick. Repeat this process for the other 3 chicken breasts."],[null,"Spread 1 Laughing Cow cheese wedge on one side of one chicken breast. Spread 1/4 cup of the spinach mushroom mixture on top of the cheese. Roll the chicken breast and secure the seam with a toothpick. Repeat this procedure for the 3 remaining chicken breasts."],[null,"Sprinkle the chicken breasts with pepper and paprika. Place the rolled chicken breasts on a baking dish and bake for 30-40 minutes or until done."],[null,"To serve, remove the toothpicks and slice each breast into 5 rounds."]],"h":[]},"6942698":{"s":[[null,"In a medium salad bowl, toss together the spinach, celery, mushrroms, onion, and orange sections."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the remaining ingredients except the pumpkin seeds. Drizzle over the salad. Toss to combine. Garnish with the pumpkin seeds."]],"h":[]},"6356826":{"s":[[null,"Cook quinoa according to package directions with chicken broth."],[null,"Heat olive oil in a sauté pan over medium-high heat. Add garlic and sauté for 30 seconds. Add spinach and sauté for about 5 minutes."],[null,"Pour cooked quinoa in a medium bowl; add spinach and remaining ingredients and mix well."]],"h":[]},"6710331":{"s":[[null,"In a large salad bowl, combine fresh baby spinach, thinly sliced red onion, halved cherry tomatoes, toasted sliced almonds, and dried cranberries."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together olive oil, fresh lemon juice, Dijon mustard, honey, poppy seeds, salt, and black pepper."],[null,"Pour the dressing over the salad. Toss gently to ensure even coating."],[null,"Allow the salad to sit for 10 minutes to let the flavors meld."]],"h":[]},"7607126":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a medium frying pan."],[null,"Add the onion, garlic and carrot and fry for 3–4 minutes until beginning to soften."],[null,"Stir in the rice, spinach and stock, bring to the boil and simmer gently for 35 minutes until the rice is tender. Transfer to a blender or food processor with the cream and plenty of black pepper, blitz until smooth then return to the pan to reheat."]],"h":[[null,"If using frozen spinach in place of fresh, you’ll only need 100g."],[null,"If you don't use the soup straight away, you may need to add extra stock or water when you reheat as it will thicken after a while."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Freeze in portions then defrost in the microwave. Heat until piping-hot, stirring regularly. Eat immediately and discard any leftovers."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"7954392":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4. Add the oil to a saucepan and cook the onion and leeks for 5-8 minutes. Mix in the garlic, cook together for 1 minute and remove from the heat."],[null,"Add the spinach, ricotta cheese and nutmeg and mix well."],[null,"Meanwhile, put the tomatoes in a bowl and add the oregano, tomato puree and pepper. Mix together to make the sauce."],[null,"Stuff the spinach and ricotta mixture into the cannelloni."],[null,"Put half the tomato sauce into an ovenproof dish. Place the stuffed cannelloni on top and add the remaining sauce. Top with Mozzarella and bake for 15 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Cooking pasta, draining and placing it immediately in cold water, stops it from continuing to cook and makes sure it doesn’t go soggy."],[null,"For a dairy-free/vegan alternative, use soft tofu in place of the ricotta and top with a little dairy-free or vegan alternative to cheese."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"6385044":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 400 degrees F."],[null,"In a skillet, heat olive oil over medium heat. Add minced garlic and sauté for about 1 minute until fragrant."],[null,"Add chopped baby spinach to the skillet and cook until wilted. Season with coarse salt, black pepper, and dried oregano. Remove from heat and stir in ricotta cheese."],[null,"Butterfly each chicken breast by cutting a slit horizontally through the center, leaving the edges intact."],[null,"Season the inside of each chicken breast with a pinch of coarse salt and black pepper."],[null,"Stuff each chicken breast with the spinach and ricotta cheese mixture."],[null,"Secure the edges of the chicken breasts with toothpicks to keep the stuffing in place."],[null,"Place the stuffed chicken breasts in a baking dish and bake in the preheated oven until the chicken has an internal temperature of 165 degrees F, about 25 minutes."]],"h":[]},"6112105":{"s":[[null,"Add sweet potatoes and 1/2 cup water to a microwave-safe container or steamer with a lid. Microwave for 7-8 minutes or until sweet potatoes are just fork tender. Don’t overcook them."],[null,"While the sweet potatoes are steaming, add olive oil to a large sauté pan over medium heat. Add the onions and sauté for 3-4 minutes or until onions turn clear. Add the garlic and sauté 2 more minutes."],[null,"Add the salt, pepper, cumin, turmeric, ginger, chili powder and water or broth. Bring to a simmer."],[null,"Add in the spinach and cook until wilted, about 5 minutes."],[null,"Stir in the sweet potatoes to heat through."]],"h":[]},"7722208":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4."],[null,"Add the onion to a pan with the oil and cook until well browned."],[null,"Remove the stalk from the mushroom, chop it up and add it to the onion, along with the spinach, thyme and garlic."],[null,"Once the spinach has wilted, add the mustard, bread and pepper, and mix well. Cover and leave for a couple of minutes so the bread absorbs all the flavours."],[null,"Mix the stuffing again and then pile it onto the mushroom cap."],[null,"Sprinkle the cheese evenly on top, pressing it into the stuffing, and bake for 10 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Frozen spinach is a useful ingredient to keep in your freezer. Look out for leaf spinach, rather than chopped, and always defrost it before using so that you can squeeze out the excess water."],[null,"Fresh spinach leaves are a great alternative to lettuce."],[null,"If you don't like Wensleydale, try adding the same amount of Cheddar, feta or goat's cheese."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Freeze with greaseproof paper between each mushroom. Defrost for 1 hour, then heat in the microwave or a moderate oven."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"6665438":{"s":[[null,"In a small pot, boil spinach and artichokes in 1 cup water until tender. Discard liquid, drain well and set artichokes and spinach aside in a bowl."],[null,"In the same pot, melt Laughing Cow cheese wedges over low heat. Add remaining ingredients; mix well and continue to cook for additional 1-2 minutes."],[null,"Add drained spinach and artichokes to pot and stir. Cook additional 2 minutes."],[null,"Serve warm with your choice of vegetables or whole-wheat crackers."]],"h":[]},"6641474":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F and line a baking sheet with foil. Place mushrooms stem side down and spray with cooking spray."],[null,"Place mushrooms in the oven and bake for 10 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, heat a large skillet over medium heat. Spray with cooking spray. Add garlic, and onion. Cook, stirring occasionally, until onion softens, 3–4 minutes."],[null,"Stir in spinach, artichokes, salt, cream cheese, and broth or water until the spinach is creamy and smooth."],[null,"Once the mushrooms are soft, remove from the oven and spoon the filling into the mushrooms. Top with shredded cheese. Bake for another 10 minutes, until the cheese is melted."]],"h":[]},"6458377":{"s":[[null,"Squeeze excess water from the thawed spinach."],[null,"In a large bowl, mix together the drained spinach, ground turkey, red onion, garlic, beaten egg, breadcrumbs, feta, and pepper."],[null,"Form into 4 equal patties."],[null,"Heat olive oil in a large skillet over medium heat. Cook patties 4-5 minutes per side until cooked through and deep golden brown."]],"h":[]},"6858549":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F. Spray a baking sheet with cooking spray."],[null,"Season the chicken breasts with 1/4 Tsp. black pepper and dried basil. Bake for 35 minutes or until done. Put the chicken breasts in the refrigerator to cool."],[null,"In a food processor, combine the spinach, pine nuts, lemon juice, and mayonnaise. Lightly pulse. With the machine running, add the olive oil, blending until the mixture is creamy. Stir in the Parmesan cheese, garlic powder, and 1/4 Tsp. black pepper."],[null,"Cut the cooked chicken into 1/2-inch pieces and shred. In a medium bowl, combine the chicken and pesto sauce; mix well."],[null,"Serve 1/2 cup chicken salad in each tortilla. Fold in the two sides of the tortilla and roll like a burrito. You can serve these immediately or wrap tightly in plastic wrap and refrigerate."]],"h":[]},"6364389":{"s":[[null,"In a large salad bowl, combine the spinach, avocado, tomatoes, chicken, and sunflower seeds. Add the dressing and toss to coat evenly. Or, if preparing ahead of time, divide the salad between four containers. Add 1 ½ tbsp of dressing just before eating."]],"h":[]},"6625029":{"s":[[null,"Scrub the beets and trim and discard the tops. Place in a saucepan or pot and cover with water. Bring to a boil, then reduce heat and simmer until fork-tender, 30–45 minutes."],[null,"Remove from water and let cool, then peel and slice into wedges."],[null,"In a large bowl, whisk together the canola oil, water, honey, and Dijon mustard. Add spinach and toss to coat."],[null,"Add beets, goat cheese, and pine nuts. Toss again gently."]],"h":[]},"6591894":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil over high heat in a very large skillet until very hot. Add the spinach (you may need to work in batches) and cook, stirring, for about 1-2 minutes; the spinach should turn bright green and wilt slightly. Add the garlic and red chile flakes and continue to cook, stirring constantly, until the garlic begins to release its aroma, approximately 30 seconds."],[null,"Remove the spinach from the heat, and season with salt and pepper. Toss well to combine, and serve with lemon on the side (for squeezing juice over the spinach)."]],"h":[]},"6410077":{"s":[[null,"In a food processor or blender, puree the cottage cheese. Add to a medium bowl."],[null,"Add the yogurt, spinach and ranch dressing powder and whisk together. Refrigerate for at least 30 minutes, up to overnight."],[null,"Serve with assorted vegetables for dipping."]],"h":[]},"6520840":{"s":[[null,"Place the spinach, strawberries, blueberries, avocado, and onion in a large salad bowl."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the olive oil, vinegar, honey, lime juice, garlic, and black pepper."],[null,"Pour the dressing over the salad and toss to evenly coat."]],"h":[]},"7441520":{"s":[[null,"Add 1 tsp of oil to a saucepan, then add the onion. Cook for 2-3 minutes, then add the red pepper and fry a further 4-5 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the egg, spinach, cumin, chilli and sweetcorn to a bowl and mix well."],[null,"Stir in the onion and red pepper, then add the chickpeas, gram flour and coriander, and mix thoroughly.With wet hands, shape the mixture into 8 patties."],[null,"Add the remaining oil to a large non-stick frying pan over a medium heat. Place fritters in the pan and flatten slightly with a spatula to about ½-1cm thick, to ensure even cooking."],[null,"Cook the fritters until lightly browned for 3-4 minutes, then carefully flip over and cook the other side again for 3-4 minutes. You may wish to give each side a further 1-2 minutes to get a nice crust on them. Serve with salad."]],"h":[[null,"The nutritional information above does not include salad or pitta as a serving suggestion."],[null,"If you don’t have a big enough pan, you can cook the fritters in two batches. Place on a warm plate and set aside until they’re all ready."],[null,"You can serve the fritters either warm or cold."],[null,"If you don’t have gram flour you could use plain or wholemeal wheat flour instead."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Freeze in individually wrapped portions with greaseproof paper between each fritter. Defrost thoroughly and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"7944719":{"s":[[null,"Wash the spinach and add to a pan with a lid, cook for 2-3 minutes stirring a couple of times (there is no need to add oil or extra water, there will be enough water clinging to the spinach after washing). Strain off excess water and allow to cool."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the pine nuts to a dry pan and stir regularly for 1-2 minutes until they are just starting to brown, remove from pan and reserve."],[null,"Gently squeeze out any remaining water from the spinach and distribute over a platter."],[null,"Crumble the feta cheese over the top, then scatter with the roasted pine nuts."],[null,"Sprinkle lemon zest over the dish, then drizzle with the lemon juice and olive oil. Season with pepper and serve."]],"h":[[null,"You could try scattering this salad with a little goat's cheese or shavings of Parmesan cheese instead of feta. Or use lightly toasted flaked almonds or sunflower seeds rather than pine nuts."],[null,"This can be made in advance but only add the lemon juice and oil just before serving."],[null,"Also works with frozen spinach, just defrost and squeeze out the excess water, there is no need to cook it."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"7982930":{"s":[[null,"Boil the potatoes in their skins for 15–20 minutes (depending on size) until almost cooked, but still firm. Drain and run them under a cold tap to make them easier to handle, before cutting each potato into 1⁄2cm-thick slices."],[null,"Meanwhile, defrost the spinach, squeeze out the excess water and chop it slightly."],[null,"Add the oil to a large non-stick frying pan and put onto a medium heat. Add the onion and cook for 2–3 minutes until soft."],[null,"Beat the eggs with the pepper, mix in the spinach and then add the potatoes."],[null,"Pour the egg mixture into the frying pan. Use a spatula to press the tortilla down, and to press in the sides to create an even shape."],[null,"Once the tortilla has almost set (approx 5 minutes) invert onto a plate, then slide it back into the pan to cook the other side for 5 minutes. Reduce the heat and turn the tortilla twice more, cooking for 2–3 minutes on each side to make sure the centre is cooked."],[null,"Slide the tortilla onto a plate and leave to cool for 10-15 minutes. Ideally, serve warm, as it tastes much better. For a packed lunch, allow to cool completely before slicing and packing."]],"h":[[null,"For this tortilla recipe (also known as Spanish omelette), you can use other vegetables instead of spinach, such as peas and red pepper. Or, try adding some herbs or garlic."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"7665488":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a large saucepan and fry the onion, red pepper and carrots over a medium heat for 4–5 minutes stirring occasionally until softened. Add the garlic, allspice and chilli and fry for 1–2 minutes stirring constantly."],[null,"Stir in the sweet potato, thyme, vegetable stock and chopped tomatoes. Bring to the boil, cover and simmer over a low heat for 15 minutes until the sweet potatoes are tender."],[null,"Stir in the chickpeas and baby spinach leaves and cook for 1–2 minutes until the spinach has just wilted and the chickpeas are warmed through. Season to taste with freshly ground black pepper."]],"h":[[null,"Scotch bonnet chillies are readily available in supermarkets and packed full of flavour and heat! If you like spicy food, use a whole one – if not, use half. Wash your hands after preparing them. If you like a milder heat, replace with a red jalapeno chilli instead."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6509299":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375°F."],[null,"Spray 4 ramekins with cooking spray. Combine the spinach, tomato, feta cheese, and oregano; evenly distribute into ramekins.."],[null,"Place egg over spinach mixture and bake until egg whites are set but the yolks are still soft, about 10-12 minutes"]],"h":[]},"2406":{"s":[[null,"Drain water chestnuts and oranges; cut apple into wedges."],[null,"Place washed, drained spinach leaves into a 1-quart serving bowl. Sprinkle dried cranberries over top."],[null,"Add water chestnuts, chow mein noodles, apple wedges and mandarin oranges."],[null,"Sprinkle pepper over top. Cover and refrigerate to chill."],[null,"Toss lightly with 1/4-cup vinaigrette salad dressing and serve."]],"h":[[null,"One-half cup raw spinach contains 156 mg potassium. One-half cup cooked spinach (measured after cooking) contains 419 mg potassium."],[null,"You may substitute leaf lettuce, or use spinach and lettuce."],[null,"For a variation, add salad dressing to salad and chill 3 to 4 hours before serving. Portion size is 3/4 cup (smaller because the spinach wilts after the vinaigrette dressing is added)."],[null,"This salad is delicious using Wishbone® Light Raspberry-Walnut Vinaigrette® salad dressing."]]},"1735":{"s":[[null,"Let sherbet unthaw in refrigerator for 1 to 2 hours before preparation."],[null,"In a punch bowl, mix all ingredients."],[null,"Serve 4-ounces of punch in small 6-ounce cups."]],"h":[[null,"Kool-Aid® liquid drink mix is sugar-free and does not contain phosphate additives like powdered Kool-aid drink mix."],[null,"Change the Kool-Aid® and sherbet flavors so the color matches your event. Try red for Valentine’s Day and Fourth of July celebrations and green for St. Patrick’s Day."]]},"9552882":{"s":[[null,"Add the quinoa and broth to a small pot and bring it to a boil. Then reduce the heat and simmer for 12-15 minutes until the liquid is absorbed. Fluff with a fork and set it aside."],[null,"Meanwhile, grill or sauté the asparagus pieces, and sprinkle them with salt and pepper. (Alternatively, you may keep the asparagus raw for added crunch.)"],[null,"Combine the salad dressing ingredients in a small bowl and mix well, tasting for salt and pepper and adjusting to your taste."],[null,"In a large mixing bowl, add the cooked quinoa, cooked or raw asparagus (your choice), peas, cucumber, basil, and the salad dressing. Mix well and then serve immediately, or you may refrigerate for 1 hour or longer before serving."]],"h":[]},"6026861":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 500°F."],[null,"Place the green beans, asparagus, peas, and snap peas in a medium saucepan. Cover with water. Bring to a boil over high heat, then reduce the heat to low. Simmer for 5 to 10 minutes, until tender. Drain the vegetables and immediately submerge them in a bowl of ice water."],[null,"Pour the balsamic vinegar into a small bowl. Whisk in the mustard until well incorporated, then whisk in the olive oil until smooth. Season with the salt and pepper, to taste."],[null,"Place the cherry tomatoes in a single layer on a baking sheet. Roast for 5 minutes or until charred and soft."],[null,"Stir the tomatoes and olives into the vinaigrette."],[null,"Drain the vegetables well, then place them in the serving bowl with the lettuce. Toss with the vinaigrette and serve."]],"h":[]},"2882":{"s":[[null,"Remove tips and strings from the green beans and cut into 2-inch pieces. Dice the celery, onion, carrots, mushrooms and tomato."],[null,"In a large pot heat the olive oil and sauté the celery and onion until tender."],[null,"Add the remaining ingredients and bring to a boil. Reduce heat to a simmer and cook for 45 to 60 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"If desired add 1/4 to 1/2 cup of couscous or other small pasta to soup during the last 20 minutes of cooking."],[null,"1/4 teaspoon salt is included in the nutrient analysis, but is optional."],[null,"Adjust the oregano and garlic powder to taste."]]},"7742200":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 200°C/ fan 180°C/gas 6. Spread the squash on 1 or 2 non-stick baking trays in a single layer with a couple of pumps of low-calorie cooking spray. Roast for 40-45 minutes, or until golden and caramelised, turning halfway."],[null,"Meanwhile, spray a non-stick saucepan with a couple of pumps of low-calorie cooking spray and place over a medium heat. Fry the onion for 5-6 minutes. Add the garam masala, chilli powder, garlic and ginger with a splash of water, and cook for 2-3 minutes. Add the tomatoes and a can of water and bring to a simmer."],[null,"Add the chicken to the pan and simmer for 15-20 minutes until cooked through and no pink flesh is visible (the juices should run clear when you cut into the thickest part of the chicken)."],[null,"Stir the squash into the curry and season with pepper. Scatter over the coriander and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Check spice/seasoning blends for added ingredients such as sugar, salt, flour or oil. Choose blends made from herbs and spices only if possible."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"7419400":{"s":[[null,"Mix the squid and prawns with the garlic, chilli, lemon juice and zest, saving a little zest to garnish. Leave to marinate for 5 mins."],[null,"Thread a squid ring, a prawn and another squid ring onto each skewer."],[null,"Heat the oil in a large, non-stick frying pan and cook the skewers, turning once, to ensure the prawns are fully cooked and their flesh turns opaque and pink or white."]],"h":[[null,"If using wooden skewers, soak them in water for 10 minutes before threading on the seafood."],[null,"The skewers can also be cooked under a hot grill for 4-5 minutes turning once, to ensure the prawn is fully cooked through and opaque in colour. Put a little foil over the exposed wood on the skewers to prevent them from burning under the grill."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"6266360":{"s":[[null,"Place the eggs in a single layer in a saucepan and cover with water. Bring the water to a boil, then reduce the heat to low, cover, and simmer for 10–12 minutes."],[null,"Transfer the boiled eggs to an ice water bath to cool."],[null,"Once the eggs are cool, peel them and cut them in half lengthwise. Remove the yolks and place them in a bowl."],[null,"In the bowl with the egg yolks, add mayonnaise, Sriracha sauce, Dijon mustard, rice vinegar, salt, and pepper. Mash and mix the ingredients together until smooth. Spoon or pipe the Sriracha filling into the hollowed-out egg whites."],[null,"Chill in the refrigerator for at least 30 minutes before serving. Top with sliced scallions and sesame seeds."]],"h":[]},"2607":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"In a bowl, mix 1 cup flour and 1/4 cup sugar."],[null,"Using a pastry blender, cut in 1/4 cup butter until mixture looks like fine crumbs and starts to cling together."],[null,"Pat into the bottom of an ungreased 9 x 9 x 2″ baking pan."],[null,"In a large mixing bowl, beat 1-1/4 cups sugar and 3/4 cup butter with electric mixer until combined. Beat in corn syrup and eggs."],[null,"Alternately add remaining 1 cup flour and non-dairy creamer, beating on low speed after each addition just until combined. (Batter may look slightly curdled.)"],[null,"Pour batter over crust, spreading evenly to edges of pan."],[null,"Bake for 35 minutes or until nearly firm when shaken."],[null,"Cool in pan on wire rack. Sprinkle with powdered sugar when cool."],[null,"Cut into 12 squares and serve."]],"h":[[null,"For a special topping, add some berries or other low potassium sliced fruit and a dollop of whipped topping."]]},"3387":{"s":[[null,"Rinse carrots and peas in colander."],[null,"Cook carrots and peas in pineapple juice until carrots are tender. Substitute pineapple juice instead of water and follow package directions for cooking time. Drain."],[null,"Sprinkle with fresh or dry dill. Serve warm."]],"h":[[null,"Try this recipe with fresh baby carrots and green peas."]]},"7504418":{"s":[[null,"Mist a frying pan with the spray and put over a medium heat. Cook the steak for at least 2 minutes on each side."],[null,"Mist the pan again, cooking the peppers and onion for 6-8 minutes. Add the garlic and chilli and cook for 1 minute. Cut the steak into strips and mix in the peppers and onion."],[null,"Scatter half the cheese over 2 wraps. Top with the steak and veg, then the remaining cheese and coriander. Gently press 2 more wraps down. Mist the pan again and put over a medium heat. Cook one at a time for 3-4 minutes on each side, misting the pan each time. Quarter and serve."]],"h":[[null,"*You can use any wrap of your choice, but remember the carb content may vary from product to product."]]},"7194911":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 160°C/fan 140°C/gas 3. Put all the ingredients, except the pastry, egg yolk and spring greens, in a large, flameproof casserole dish and season with pepper. Bring to a simmer on the hob, then cover and cook in the oven for 2 hours."],[null,"Remove the lid. Stir well and return to the oven, uncovered, for a further 1 hour 30 minutes, adding the beans for the last 20 minutes. Meanwhile, stamp out 12 mushroom shapes from the pastry, weighing no more than 12.5g each, or slice the pastry into 6 x 25g squares. Line a large baking tray with baking paper and lay the pastry shapes on top. Brush with the egg yolk and chill until needed."],[null,"Remove the casserole dish from the oven, cover and place over your lowest heat on the hob to keep warm. Increase the oven to 220°C/fan 200°C/gas 7 and bake the pastry for 20-25 minutes until puffed and golden. When the pastry is almost ready, steam the spring greens for 2-3 minutes."],[null,"Divide the beef mixture between 6 bowls, discarding the thyme sprigs, then divide over the pastry shapes. Serve with the spring greens."]],"h":[[null,"Nutritional information includes serving suggestion."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"4913710":{"s":[[null,"Rub the steak with the oil, garlic and chili powder. Marinate in the refrigerator for a minimum of two hours or overnight."],[null,"In a skillet over medium-high heat, cook the steak to your desired doneness. Reserve at room temperature. Slice into thin strips. (You can also use the grill.)"],[null,"In a saucepan, cook rice according to instructions. Once cooked, combine with the corn and keep at room temperature."],[null,"In a skillet over medium-high heat, sauté the peppers and onions in olive oil. Remove from heat and reserve."],[null,"To prepare the dressing, combine all dressing ingredients in a food processor."],[null,"To assemble the salad, toss the lettuce with the cilantro dressing and divide into four bowls. Top with rice, beans, peppers, onions and steak."]],"h":[["Enjoy low-potassium vegetables","Eating vegetables every day is a very important part of a healthy diet. Vegetables add fiber and vitamins as well as antioxidants that can help protect your body’s cells and possibly prevent certain diseases. They are also rich in many minerals. One such mineral is potassium. Potassium is a mineral that can be harmful if you eat more than your kidneys can handle. When this occurs, the potassium level in your blood can increase to a very high level and become dangerous. Fortunately, there are a number of vegetables that are lower in potassium. If you have chronic kidney disease and your doctor has told you to limit your potassium intake, these are vegetables that you can eat on a daily basis. Lower-potassium vegetables include asparagus, cabbage, carrots, corn, cucumber, lighter-colored lettuces, onions and radishes. Typically, vegetables are considered to be a “free food,” meaning you can eat as many vegetables as you want every day. Even though many vegetables are lower in potassium, it is important to be mindful of the portion size. Ask your dietitian how much of these foods you should eat every day to improve your health while avoiding too much potassium in your diet."]]},"4880625":{"s":[[null,"To prepare the Chimichurri, combine all ingredients in a blender or food processor and purée. Reserve half of the mixture for the steak marinade and the other half to drizzle on the sandwiches."],[null,"Marinate the steaks for at least one hour in refrigerator. Steaks may marinate for up to 24 hours."],[null,"In a skillet over medium-high heat, sauté the peppers and onions in olive oil until the onions become translucent and the peppers begin to soften. Set aside."],[null,"Preheat your grill. Cook steaks until they reach an internal temperature of 145°F. Allow to rest at room temperature for 10 minutes before slicing."],[null,"Toast ciabatta buns."],[null,"Slice steak into thin strips."],[null,"To assemble the sandwiches, evenly place the thinly sliced steak over the toasted ciabatta buns. Drizzle with chimichurri and top with the peppers and onions."]],"h":[[null,"The Chimichurri marinade can be used with any cut of meat."],[null,"This colorful sauce from the Argentinian cuisine doubles as a marinade and as a sauce to accompany all cuts of beef. It can be prepared in advance and frozen in ice cube trays. Once the cubes are frozen, put cubes in a freezer bag and keep in freezer for later use."],[null,"PLEASE NOTE: This recipe is higher in potassium and portion size is important. Check with your registered dietitian to see how this recipe can be included in your diet."],["Use of marinades to add flavor without salt","Lowering sodium intake is a key element of the chronic kidney disease diet. To do so, one is often advised to reduce or eliminate salt in your daily diet. This can cause foods to taste a lot different than you are normally used to. Without salt, food may taste bland, but don't despair! Using herbs, spices and citrus to make homemade marinades is an easy way to add flavor without the salt or other high-sodium seasonings. Marinades typically contain three basic ingredients—oil to maintain the moisture of the food and to hold together the spices; an acid such as vinegar, lemon juice or other citrus to tenderize and herbs and spices to add flavor. Making your own marinade is a good idea because store-bought marinades are often high in sodium and potassium. Add meats and/or vegetables to a marinade and put them in the refrigerator until the food is ready to be cooked. The longer the food soaks in the marinade, the more flavor the food will absorb. Marinate food in a glass or plastic container, not metal as the acid in the marinade can interact with the metal. Remove food from the container and toss the leftover marinade to avoid cross contamination that can lead to food poisoning. If you would like to add a marinade to the cooked food, plan ahead and set aside some marinade that has not had any fresh meat added to it for this purpose."]]},"6497012":{"s":[[null,"Place frozen broccoli florets in a microwave-safe bowl."],[null,"Add 2–4 tablespoons of water."],[null,"Cover the bowl with a microwave-safe plate or lid."],[null,"Microwave on high for 2–4 minutes until tender."],[null,"Remove carefully, as steam will be hot."]],"h":[]},"6931873":{"s":[[null,"Place the broccoli florets in a steamer basket over a pot of boiling water."],[null,"Steam the broccoli for 5–7 minutes or until it is tender-crisp. Remove from heat."],[null,"While the broccoli is steaming, heat 1 Tbsp olive oil in a small skillet over medium heat."],[null,"Add the thinly sliced garlic to the skillet and sauté for 1–2 minutes until it becomes golden brown and crispy. Be careful not to burn the garlic."],[null,"Remove the crispy garlic from the skillet and place it on a paper towel-lined plate to drain excess oil."],[null,"Place the steamed broccoli in a serving dish."],[null,"Drizzle 1 Tbsp of the olive oil over the broccoli and toss to coat."],[null,"Season with salt and black pepper."],[null,"Sprinkle the crispy garlic and sesame seeds over the steamed broccoli."]],"h":[]},"6715874":{"s":[[null,"Wash and peel the carrots."],[null,"Cut them into slices, sticks, or small pieces so they cook evenly."],[null,"Place a steamer basket in a pot and add about an inch of water."],[null,"Bring the water to a boil over medium heat."],[null,"Add the carrots to the steamer basket and cover the pot with a lid."],[null,"Steam the carrots for about 5–10 minutes, or until they are tender when you poke them with a fork."],[null,"Remove from the heat and serve warm."]],"h":[]},"6208072":{"s":[[null,"Bring a medium pot with water and set a steaming basket on top."],[null,"Add the cauliflower florets and steam until tender, about 5–7 minutes."],[null,"Transfer to a medium bowl and toss with fresh dill, olive oil, salt, and pepper."]],"h":[]},"6062797":{"s":[],"h":[]},"3234":{"s":[[null,"Chop chili pepper, cabbage, and carrots. Mince ginger root."],[null,"Heat oil in a pan and add the mustard seeds. When seeds splutter add semolina and brown until it becomes light gold. Remove from heat and cool."],[null,"Mix yogurt, water, salt, baking soda, green chili and ginger into a smooth batter."],[null,"Grease idli molds lightly with a small amount of ghee."],[null,"Sprinkle some of the cabbage, carrot and peas into each mold. Top with the batter and steam for 15 minutes."],[null,"Serve hot. Make 12 idlis."]],"h":[[null,"Use batter immediately for best results."],[null,"Curious about unfamiliar ingredients? Semolina is the starch component of wheat kernels. It is known as farina or Cream of Wheat in the US. Ghee is clarified butter."]]},"2095":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven 375° F."],[null,"Set cream cheese out to soften. Dice tomato. Slice mushroom and zucchini. Remove kale from stems and chop coarsely."],[null,"Brown ground beef in a skillet. Set aside."],[null,"In a medium bowl, combine softened cream cheese, Parmesan cheese, 1 egg and 1/2-cup water. Mix well."],[null,"In another bowl, combine cooked ground beef, 1 egg, 1/4 cup water, garlic, basil and oregano. Mix with 3 tablespoons olive oil."],[null,"Sauté mushrooms and kale in remaining tablespoon olive oil."],[null,"In an 11″ x 7″ pan, spread 1/4 of the ground beef mixture on bottom of pan. Top with 4 uncooked lasagna noodles. Spread half the cream cheese mixture, about 1/4-inch thick, over noodles."],[null,"Layer zucchini, sautéed mushrooms, kale and remaining ground beef mixture evenly over noodles."],[null,"Repeat noodle and cream cheese layer. Top with diced tomato. Cover with foil and bake for 30 minutes. Remove foil and bake for additional 10-15 minutes."],[null,"Let stand for 10 minutes, cut into 8 portions and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Lasagna is a great food to make and freeze for a later date. Consider doubling the recipe to make two batches at a time."],[null,"To cook pre-made lasagna, preheat oven to 375° F and bake for 45 minutes. Let stand 10 minutes before serving."],[null,"Increase the amount of tomato, kale and zucchini if you do not need a low potassium diet."],[null,"Adjust herbs to taste."]]},"5706437":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a large pan and allow the meat to brown. Once the meat has started to go brown, add in the parsnips and carrots, cook for 5 minutes."],[null,"Pour over 1000ml low salt beef stock and allow to come to the boil."],[null,"Once boiling, reduce to a simmer and allow to cook for 2 hours or until the meat is tender and falling apart."],[null,"Add in the Worcestershire sauce, stir well and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Serve with bread of your choice to soak up the sauce!"],["Renastep note","Always check with your dietitian or doctor that this recipe is suitable for you."],["Renastep note","This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutritics dietary analysis software. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information."]]},"7090941":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°/gas 4."],[null,"Oil the loaf tin and set aside ready to use."],[null,"In a bowl, add the lemon extract, juice and zest of 1 lemon, sweetener, eggs and oil then beat together well."],[null,"Stir in the water and beat again until frothy, gently stir in the polenta and bicarbonate of soda then immediately place in the baking tin and bake for 20-25 minutes."],[null,"Remove the cake from the oven and allow to cool for 20 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, place the remaining lemon juice and zest into a small pan with the sweetener and warm gently for 1 minute, add the honey and warm 1-2 more minutes until it becomes syrupy."],[null,"Drizzle the hot honey and lemon over the cooled cake and leave to soak for a few minutes before serving."]],"h":[[null,"This cake is wonderful with limes or oranges instead of lemon (reduce the sweetener if using sweet oranges)."],[null,"Great served with fresh berries and a blob of unsweetened Greek-style yoghurt."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Slice, then wrap in foil to freeze (you can then use slices as required). May be a little crumbly when defrosted, but it will still taste delicious."]]},"7252558":{"s":[[null,"Add the oil to a pan over a low-medium heat and add the ginger and garlic, mixing well for 1–2 mins."],[null,"Now add the chilli flakes and stir for another minute."],[null,"Add the kale and mix well for 2–3 mins."],[null,"Turn the heat up, add the water, mix, put a lid on the pan and cook for a further 5–6 mins, stirring occasionally."],[null,"Drizzle with the lemon juice and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Kale stalks are edible but will take longer to cook than the leaves – if you remove and finely chop them first, you can cook them together with the leaves."],[null,"Try cooking 200g kale with a chopped leek and a chopped, unpeeled apple in a very small amount of water."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"2013":{"s":[[null,"Slice green and red peppers and celery. Chop onion. Crush garlic clove. Cut tomato half into 4 pieces."],[null,"In large skillet, heat oil. Add green pepper, red pepper, mushrooms, celery, onion, garlic, sugar, oregano, salt and pepper."],[null,"Stir-fry over medium-high heat until peppers are crisp tender."],[null,"Add vinegar, tomato and drained water chestnuts. Cook until heated thoroughly."]],"h":[[null,"One tablespoon of reduced-sodium soy sauce can be used instead of the salt."],[null,"Choose a firm tomato. Can substitute 4 to 6 cherry or grape tomatoes, sliced in half."]]},"3122":{"s":[[null,"Chop the strawberries, then coat with sugar or granular sweetener. Set aside."],[null,"Combine the water, soy milk and half & half in a small pot. Bring to a simmer over medium-high heat."],[null,"Add the strawberries and bring to a boil."],[null,"Add the oats and cook 4 to 5 minutes to desired thickness."]],"h":[[null,"For extra sweetness drizzle with honey, agave or sweetener of choice."],[null,"Try raspberries or blueberries instead of strawberries when in season."],[null,"A single serving is considered as a one dish meal. If serving as a side dish, decrease portion to 1/2 cup"],[null,"For a gluten-free diet check oatmeal for \"gluten-free\" on the label."]]},"6172613":{"s":[[null,"In a large serving bowl, combine the strawberries and balsamic glaze. Grind the black pepper on top and gently mix. Garnish with sprigs of tarragon."],[null,"* Balsamic glaze (sometimes called balsamic syrup) can be found where vinegars are sold. To make your own, heat 3 Tbsp. of balsamic vinegar in a saucepan. Bring to lightly boiling and cook, stirring occasionally, until the vinegar is thickened and reduced to half its volume."]],"h":[]},"6593652":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6512511":{"s":[],"h":[]},"2444":{"s":[[null,"Wash and dry the lettuce; remove the stems of the strawberries and slice vertically; cut the goat cheese into 8 even pieces."],[null,"In a small bowl mix the balsamic vinegar and olive oil together with a whisk."],[null,"Mash half the strawberries together with a potato masher or fork, and add them to the bowl. The mixture will be chunky. Set the dressing mixture aside."],[null,"Place the lettuce into a large bowl. Add the dressing and mix to coat."],[null,"Divide the lettuce onto four plates. Slice the remaining strawberries and add them to each plate of salad. Top with 2 of the goat cheese slices on each plate."],[null,"Add ground black pepper to taste."]],"h":[[null,"This salad tastes best when fresh local strawberries are available in season."],[null,"Soft goat cheese can be difficult to cut with a knife because of its soft texture. The easiest way is to use non-flavored dental floss. Take about a 6inch piece and hold in both hands. Use it to cut down into the goat cheese from top to bottom. This way you can cut smooth rounds that are not squished."]]},"4017183":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F and line the muffin tins with paper cups."],[null,"In a clean mixing bowl, whip the egg whites until frothy. Slowly add the white sugar and continue to whip until peaks form. Mix in the lemon zest and vanilla extract."],[null,"Carefully fold in the sifted powdered sugar and cake flour. Do not overmix."],[null,"Pour the angel food cake mixture into the lined muffin tins and bake for approximately 25 minutes or until cupcakes become firm and golden."],[null,"Once the cupcakes have cooled, place them in the refrigerator. Garnish each cupcake with a sliced strawberry and whipped cream before serving."]],"h":[[null,"* To lower the carbohydrate content you can use a sugar substitute"],[null,"Cupcakes can be stored in the freezer. Place them in freezer bags. Garnish after defrosting. 2017-04-11 2:06 PM"],["Strawberries","With so many limitations in the kidney diet, eating a variety of brightly colored fruit is important to ensure you are consuming a wealth of nutrients. The bright red color of the berry comes from an antioxidant it naturally contains. Eating strawberries helps your kidneys do their work by reducing inflammation in your body. A half-cup serving of strawberries, or roughly 5 medium berries, contains approximately 120mg of potassium and very low amounts of sodium and phosphorus. This fruit is also full of vitamin C, manganese, folate and fiber. Ofering a rich taste, strawberries can be added to any meal. Choose at breakfast to top hot or cold cereal. Treat your taste buds at lunch by adding strawberries to a low potassium fruit or chicken salad. Enjoy at dinner as a main entrée salad addition or a meat marinade. Select strawberries as a snack or mix as part of a smoothie for a low-calorie dessert."]]},"6409574":{"s":[[null,"Peel bananas and slice into 1/4-inch rounds. Place in a bowl and freeze for at least 2 hours."],[null,"Once bananas are frozen, add them to a blender or food processor along with the strawberries and coconut milk. Blend on high speed 30 seconds."],[null,"Scrape down the sides of the blender and blend on high 30 more seconds. Repeat this process until mixture is smooth and the texture of soft-serve ice cream."],[null,"You can serve immediately or freeze for 30 minutes for a firmer texture."]],"h":[]},"9273315":{"s":[[null,"Add all the ingredients to a food processor or blender and process to your desired consistency. I made these ones smooth, but you can leave a few fruit chunks if preferred."],[null,"Then fill your six popsicle molds, but leave a touch of space for expansion. Then tap the mold down on your counter to release air bubbles. Place the mold lids on top and freeze for 4-6 hours, or overnight. Keep frozen until serving.NOTE: If using popsicle sticks, freeze the mold for 1-2 hours, just enough for the sticks to hold straight, and then add the sticks and continue freezing until solid."],["To remove from the mold","Fill a bowl with warm water, as tall as your mold and place it inside, without overflowing the top where the sticks are. Wait 15-20 seconds before removing, and then use a side-to-side motion to remove the popsicles from the mold."],["To remove from the mold","You may also run the popsicles under warm water using your kitchen sink faucet for 15-20 seconds, or until they remove easily."],["To remove from the mold","If the popsicles are still soft, place them on a plate and return them to the freezer."]],"h":[[null,"Use a very ripe banana that is spotted brown for natural sweetness. When strawberries are in season and extra sweet, you may skip the optional maple syrup for a no sugar added dessert. For chunkier pieces of fruit in your strawberry banana popsicles, use a food processor and do not overprocess. For evenly smooth pink popsicles, use a blender until pureed. If using popsicle sticks (instead of the lids that come with your mold), freeze the mold for 1-2 hours, just enough for the sticks to hold straight, and then add the sticks and continue freezing until solid. Freeze time will vary according to the thickness of your mold . Most popsicles will freeze in 4-6 hours."]]},"9763958":{"s":[[null,"Wash and dry your strawberries, and remove the stems. Then line a baking sheet with parchment paper and set it aside."],[null,"Then add everything except the coconut to a food processor. Process until combined, scraping down the sides as needed. If the mixture feels too wet to roll into balls, add another 1-3 tablespoons of oats and re-process."],[null,"Use a one-tablespoon cookie scoop to scoop the strawberry mixture and roll it into a ball. Place it on your baking sheet and repeat with the remaining mixture. You should get approx. 26 balls."],[null,"OPTIONAL: Roll some or all of the balls in shredded coconut and return to the tray."],[null,"Refrigerate the balls for 1 hour (or longer) and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Wash and DRY the strawberries before processing to prevent excess moisture in the mixture. If your batter is too wet, it will be harder to roll into balls. If this happens, add another 1-3 tablespoons of oats as needed."],[null,"The juiciness of your strawberries will determine if more oats are required . Start with 1 cup, and you may always add if needed."],[null,"The batter will be sticky so use damp hands to roll the mixture into balls to prevent it from sticking to your hands."],[null,"The bliss balls will be soft, so refrigerate them for at least 1 hour before enjoying them to help them harden and set."],[null,"Store your strawberry bliss balls in the fridge for 3-4 days or the freezer for up to 3 months."]]},"3733":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F degrees."],[null,"Finely chop the strawberries."],[null,"In a medium mixing bowl, beat the eggs. Add the canola oil and strawberries and stir well."],[null,"Mix the dry ingredients together in a separate large mixing bowl."],[null,"Make a well in the center of the dry ingredients and pour in the egg mixture."],[null,"Use a large spoon and mix until well blended; do not over mix."],[null,"Pour the batter into two ungreased 9″ x 5″ loaf pans. Bake 50 to 60 minutes."],[null,"Cool for 15 minutes, then use a knife to loosen the sides of the bread from the loaf pans and remove gently. Finish cooling on a rack."],[null,"Serve or wrap the bread in plastic wrap or foil to keep it fresh. Loaves can be refrigerated or frozen."]],"h":[[null,"Check if loaves are cooked through by inserting a toothpick down into the center. If it comes out clean, the loaf is done."],[null,"Refrigeration keeps the berries fresher-tasting in the bread."],[null,"For people with diabetes, substitute Splenda® Sugar Blend for Baking for sugar and low cholesterol egg product for eggs. 1 slice equals 206 calories, 23 grams carbohydrate, 11 grams fat and 0 mg cholesterol."],[null,"2-1/2 cups chopped strawberries is approximately 14 ounces."]]},"1707":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl mix the oats, protein powder, chia seeds and almond milk together until well combined."],[null,"Pour oat mixture into a 12 ounce mason jar (or other portable container). Cover with a lid and refrigerate overnight."],[null,"Slice the strawberries and add to oats before eating. Add sweetener of choice as desired."]],"h":[[null,"Use different low potassium fruits such as apple, blueberries or peaches for variety."],[null,"If you have CKD and are not yet on dialysis, do not use the optional protein powder and see next helpful hint."],[null,"Try this recipe with coconut, rice, soy or other milk substitutes. Look brands that do not contain phosphate additives."],[null,"Look for oats marked gluten-free."]]},"9602755":{"s":[[null,"Blend the strawberries and the milk in a small blender to make strawberry milk."],[null,"Once smooth, transfer the strawberry milk to a jar or glass container and add the chia seeds. Stir well and refrigerate for 6 hours, or overnight."],[null,"Enjoy topped with additional fresh strawberries, other fruit, nuts, granola, oats, and/or shredded coconut."]],"h":[]},"6246200":{"s":[[null,"Mix mayonnaise, lemon juice, honey, and poppy seeds together in a medium bowl."],[null,"Add chicken, strawberries, celery, green onions. Toss to combine."],[null,"Line pita halves with the greens and add ¼ of the chicken salad to each pita half."]],"h":[]},"1734":{"s":[[null,"Generously coat a 9 x 13-inch baking dish with non-stick cooking spray."],[null,"Cube the bread and cream cheese. Slice the strawberries and separate into two 1-cup portions, setting one portion aside. Place half of the bread cubes in the prepared dish. Layer the cream cheese cubes over the top of the bread. Layer 1 cup of sliced strawberries over the cream cheese and top with remaining bread cubes."],[null,"In a large bowl, whisk together eggs, half & half and maple syrup until well combined. Pour mixture evenly over the bread cubes."],[null,"Press bread gently with the back of a spoon to moisten bread completely. Cover and chill at least 8 hours or overnight."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 350˚ F."],[null,"Bake the casserole uncovered until puffed, golden brown, and a knife inserted in the center comes out clean, about 45 to 50 minutes."],[null,"Prepare the sauce while the casserole is cooking. In a small bowl, toss the remaining 1 cup of strawberries and sugar. Let stand for 20 minutes, stirring occasionally. Then pour the mixture into a blender or food processor and blend until smooth."],[null,"Transfer the strawberry sauce to a small saucepan. Add butter and simmer over medium heat for about 5 minutes, stirring occasionally. Add food coloring (optional)."],[null,"Remove the casserole from the oven and cool for 5 minutes. Cut into 12 servings and serve with warm strawberry sauce."]],"h":[[null,"Look for Texas toast bread that is sliced thick, about 40 grams per serving. Choose the brand lowest in sodium and without phosphate additives if available."],[null,"If you would like to replace the strawberries with a different berries, raspberries or blueberries are a good alternative. Or you can used mixed berries."],[null,"For a lower carbohydrate serving cut the casserole into 15 servings (35 grams carbohydrate)."]]},"2127":{"s":[[null,"Set butter, eggs and rice milk out to warm to room temperature. Preheat oven to 350°F. Place cupcake liners in a 12-cup muffin tin; set aside."],[null,"Process strawberries in a small food processor until pureed to make approximately 1/3 cup of puree."],[null,"In a medium bowl, combine white and brown rice flours, baking powder, and salt; set aside."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine rice milk, vanilla, and strawberry puree; set aside."],[null,"Cream butter on medium-high speed with an electric mixer, until light and fluffy. Gradually add sugar and continue to beat until well combined and fluffy. Reduce the mixer speed to medium and slowly add egg and egg whites until just blended."],[null,"With the mixer on low, slowly add half the rice flour mixture; mix until just blended. Add the milk mixture; mix until just blended. Slowly add remaining rice flour mixture, scraping down sides of the bowl with a spatula, as necessary, until just blended."],[null,"Pour batter into muffin cups. Bake until tops are just dry to the touch, 22 to 25 minutes. Place muffin tin on a wire rack and let cupcakes cool before removing from tin."]],"h":[[null,"Use frozen strawberries if fresh are not in season. Thaw before pureeing."],[null,"Top cupcakes with your favorite icing (gluten-free if required)."],[null,"You can also make this recipe into a cake instead of cupcakes."]]},"1874":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 325° F. Thaw strawberries and chop pecans."],[null,"Mix the flour, butter, brown sugar and pecans. Press into a 9” spring-form pan. Bake 20 minutes. Let cool completely."],[null,"In a food processor, mix lemon juice, marshmallow crème and strawberries until well-blended."],[null,"Pour into a large mixing bowl. Fold in Reddi-Wip® lightly to maintain fluff."],[null,"Pour mixture onto cooled crust. Cover with plastic wrap and aluminum foil and freeze until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"This dessert will keep for several weeks in the freezer if covered well with plastic wrap and foil."],[null,"Nuts are high in potassium and phosphorus, but can still be used in very small amounts if your labs are controlled. The 1/3-cup pecans in this recipe provides 40 mg potassium and 28 mg phosphorus per serving."]]},"3972":{"s":[[null,"Pour the almond milk and protein powder in a blender. Blend well."],[null,"Add the strawberry extract and blend."],[null,"Pour mixture into 4 cups and slowly add 2 tablespoons of strawberry soda into each cup. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"If strawberry extract is unavailable, substitute vanilla extract."],[null,"Compare almond milk labels and ingredients and select one without phosphate additives."],[null,"Look for strawberry soda without phosphate additives. If strawberry soda is not available look for Big Red® diet soda."],[null,"If Syntrax Nectar® Whey Protein Isolate Powder is unavailable, ask your dietitian for an appropriate substitute. EAS® 100% Whey Protein Powder is an option and gives approximately 13 grams of protein per scoop."],[null,"When soda is added mixture will foam, so add slowly and stop until bubbles reduce if needed to prevent bubbling over."]]},"4244642":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 200°F and line a baking tray with parchment paper."],[null,"In a bowl, whip the egg whites until frothy. Slowly add the ¼ cup of sugar and whisk until soft peaks form. Mix in the vanilla."],[null,"Drop teaspoons of the meringue on the parchment-lined baking tray to form cookies. Bake for 1½ hours. Turn of oven and leave the cookies in the oven to continue to crisp."],[null,"In a mixing bowl, add the sliced strawberries and mash slightly to release their juices."],[null,"For the cookies to stay nice and crisp, assemble the Eton Mess just before serving: Crumble the meringue cookies into the bowl. Add the Cool Whip® and fold all the ingredients together. Serve in a trifle bowl or 4 individual bowls."]],"h":[[null,"Eton Mess comes from Great Britain and is traditionally made with strawberries, but feel free to substitute with your favo rite berries."],[null,"To save time, buy meringue cookies instead of making your own."],["The hidden potassium in beverages","Today there are so many beverages available. In general, fruit juices, vegetable juices and milk or dairy type drinks are rich in potassium. Fortunately, there are some fruit juices that are lower in potassium for you to enjoy. Examples include apple juice or cider, cranberry, grape or pineapple juice and various nectars. These juices are considered to be lower in potassium when they are consumed in ½ cup, or 4-ounce portions. Be aware that a small glass of juice is equal to a fruit serving and should be counted as such when adding up the number of fruit servings per day to avoid consuming more than the recommended allowance. Vegetable juices tend to be higher in potassium as they typically contain tomato juice. It is unusual for beverages to contain potassium additives, but it is important to read the ingredient list to make sure that this is indeed the case. In general, beverages that contain either no or very little potassium include water, sparkling water and tea."]]},"2500":{"s":[[null,"Wash strawberries with hulls (otherwise, water will seep into middle part causing strawberries to become soggy)."],[null,"Take off hulls with paring knife."],[null,"Cut strawberries into halves."],[null,"Place strawberries in a bowl and drizzle with vinegar, and sprinkle with Splenda®."],[null,"Stir gently to combine."],[null,"Cover and refrigerate for a few hours, preferably over night."],[null,"Just before serving grind pepper over strawberries."]],"h":[[null,"Take strawberries out of refrigerator 10 minutes before serving to take away the chill."],[null,"Can be served as a topping on angel food cake."],[null,"If desired, use sugar or other tabletop sweeteners instead of Splenda®."]]},"2460":{"s":[[null,"Place strawberries in blender and blend until smooth."],[null,"Add all remaining ingredients and continue blending until smooth."]],"h":[[null,"Pasteurized liquid egg white is safe to consume without cooking."],[null,"If substituting frozen fruit add 1/4 cup water instead of the 1/2 cup ice. The degree of “frozenness” will determine how much your blender will be able to take. It will also give a more “soft serve” consistency than a smoothie, which is great in the warmer season."],[null,"Adjust sugar or low calorie sweetener to taste."]]},"5703286":{"s":[[null,"Mix the Renastep with the strawberry jam until completely combined."],[null,"Pour into lolly moulds and allow to freeze for 24 hours."]],"h":[["Renastep note","Renastep is a food for special medical purposes and must be used under medical supervision. Renastep is for the dietary management of kidney disease and is suitable from 3 years of age onwards."],["Renastep note","Renastep contains Milk (milk protein) and Fish (Tuna Oils). This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutrimen dietary analysis software."],["Renastep note","Refer to labels for allergen and other product information"]]},"3601":{"s":[[null,"Hull and slice the strawberries. Slice the lemon into rounds and stripe the leaves off the rosemary sprig."],[null,"Add all ingredients to a pitcher. Let sit in the refrigerator for 2 hours. Remove lemon slices and let sit for 2 more hours."],[null,"Strain out strawberries and rosemary with a fine strainer and store in the refrigerator for about 3 days."]],"h":[[null,"You may add extra strawberries and the lemon to each serving as garnish if desired."],[null,"You may leave out the stevia packet if desired."],[null,"If needed, adjust the serving size based on your personal fluid limitations or goals."]]},"6403376":{"s":[[null,"Place 1 cup strawberries, mascarpone, sugar, flaxseed, and cinnamon in a blender, and whip until light."],[null,"Stir in yogurt. Pour 1/3 cup of mixture into each of 6 clear parfait glasses. Top with 1 layer of remaining strawberry slices (reserving 6 for garnish)."],[null,"Scatter 1 Tbsp granola on top of the strawberry slices in each glass, then top each glass with another layer of remaining strawberry mixture. Add another layer of 1 Tbsp granola on top of the strawberry mixture in each glass."],[null,"Garnish each glass with 1 remaining strawberry slice. Cover with plastic wrap, and refrigerate for at least 2 hours to a maximum of overnight before serving."]],"h":[]},"54955":{"s":[[null,"Place all ingredients in a blender."],[null,"Blend until smooth."],[null,"Pour into fun glass, garnish with a strawberry, and enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"The heavy cream can be replaced with coconut cream for a dairy free option."],[null,"Refrigerated coconut milk is located near the milk alternatives in the store cooler."]]},"2281":{"s":[[null,"Bake pie shell as directed on package. Set aside to cool."],[null,"Mash 2 cups of the strawberries and combine with sugar, cornstarch and lemon juice."],[null,"Place ingredients in a medium saucepan. Cook over medium heat, stirring until mixture is thick and clear. Let cool."],[null,"Slice remaining strawberries and add to cooled mixture."],[null,"Pour into cooled pie shell. Cover and place in refrigerator until chilled."],[null,"Serve with whipped topping if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Due to the high carbohydrate content, a half portion is recommended if you have diabetes. Sugar substitutes can be used to replace sugar in many recipes. Check with your dietitian for adjustments to recipes or serving size based on your individual carbohydrate requirements."],[null,"If sugar substitute is used instead of sugar, carbohydrate is reduced to 20 grams, carbohydrate choices are reduced to one."]]},"3301":{"s":[[null,"Place fruit in blender and blend until smooth."],[null,"Add all remaining ingredients and continue blending until smooth."]],"h":[[null,"Just Whites® are a powdered egg white product available at your local grocery store in the baking section. The product is pasteurized so it is safe to consume without cooking."],[null,"If using frozen fruit, the degree of “frozenness” will determine how much your blender will be able to take. It will also give a more “soft serve” consistency than a smoothie, which is great in the warmer season."],[null,"Adjust sugar or sugar substitute to taste."]]},"9171157":{"s":[[null,"Add all the ingredients to your blender and process until smooth. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Depending on the ratio of fresh or frozen fruit, you may need to adjust the liquid quantity . Fresh fruit is easier to blend and naturally has more liquid, so use only half a cup of plant milk with all fresh fruit. Add more milk as needed when using frozen fruit. Frozen fruit will give thicker, creamier results , but fresh fruit also works well, as the banana will slightly thicken your strawberry pineapple smoothie. For extra slush and to thicken your drink when using fresh fruit, add a handful of ice cubes. Skip when using frozen fruit. If you do not have hemp hearts, you may sub for a tablespoon of flax seeds, ground flax, chia seeds, or even a nut butter such as almond or peanut butter . For extra sweetness , add 1-2 pitted dates or a teaspoon of maple or date syrup. I find this smoothie to be plenty sweet as is, but if you like it extra sweet, make it to your liking. If you don't have pineapple , mango also works well as a replacement. Raspberries or cherries also work well to sub the strawberries if you don't have any on hand. The recipe makes approx 2 cups, enough for one large glass or two smaller servings."]]},"1884":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350º F."],[null,"In a medium bowl, mix flour, 1/2 cup granulated sugar and butter together to form a dough. Press dough into a round pizza pan and bake for 15 minutes. Cool to room temperature."],[null,"Beat cream cheese, vanilla and sugar until fluffy. Spread over cooled crust. Slice 2 cups strawberries and layer over cream cheese filling."],[null,"Mash the remaining cup strawberries. In a medium sauce pan, cook the mashed strawberries, remaining 1/4 cup granu.lated sugar and cornstarch until the sauce is clear. Spread over the sliced berries. Chill for at least 1 hour."],[null,"Cut into 12 portions and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute prepared cookie dough for homemade dough. Choose the brand lowest in sodium."],[null,"Splenda® instead of sugar will reduce calories to 207 and carbohydrate to 15 grams. Count as one carbohydrate choice."]]},"1879":{"s":[[null,"Crush strawberries."],[null,"Bring water to a boil. Stir in sugar. Drop crushed strawberries into boiling sugar water and bring to a gentle simmer. Add lemon juice and lemon zest. Stir as the mixture simmers for 3 minutes."],[null,"Mix cornstarch in a small amount of cold water and stir into strawberries. Stir and cook until mixture thickens, about 1 to 2 minutes. Remove from heat."],[null,"Divide mixture into 6 dessert dishes and cool in refrigerator."],[null,"Top each serving with 1 tablespoon whipped topping and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Fresh of frozen strawberries work well in this recipe."],[null,"Replace sugar with Splenda® No Calorie Sweetener or other sugar substitute to reduce carbohydrate."]]},"3531":{"s":[[null,"In a medium saucepan combine all ingredients and cook over medium heat until rhubarb is soft."],[null,"Add more honey if sauce is too tart."],[null,"Serve with chunky fruit pieces or process in a food processor or blender for a smooth sauce. Serve hot or chilled."]],"h":[[null,"Serve as a sauce for meat or poultry or increase to 1/2 cup and serve as a dessert."],[null,"Keep sauce in the refrigerator for one week or freeze part of it for later."]]},"9327887":{"s":[[null,"Add the baby spinach, sliced strawberries and almonds to a bowl or platter."],[null,"Then, in a small blender, blend all the salad dressing ingredients. Taste it for salt and pepper and adjust as needed."],[null,"Drizzle the dressing over the salad, or serve it on the side."]],"h":[]},"5356647":{"s":[[null,"Place all the ingredients in a blender and blend until smooth. Sieve to remove seeds, if desired."]],"h":[["Renastep note","Renastep is a Food for Special Medical Purposes and must be used under medical supervision."],["Renastep note","Renastep is a ready to use feed for the dietary management of kidney disease from 3 years of age onwards. Renastep contains milk and fish. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information."],["Renastep note","This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease."]]},"2973":{"s":[[null,"Place ice in blender"],[null,"Add all ingredients"],[null,"Turn speed to crush or liquefy"]],"h":[[null,"May be prepared in ice tray or Popsicle® holders."],[null,"Add sugar or sugar substitute for extra sweetness."]]},"2024":{"s":[[null,"Wash and dry the spinach leaves. Tear into bite-sized pieces and place in a bowl. Thinly slice strawberries."],[null,"Top spinach with sliced strawberries."],[null,"Mix together the vinegar, lemon juice, honey, dry mustard and oil."],[null,"Pour dressing over spinach and strawberries. Toss well and serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"A serving of raw spinach is lower in potassium than a serving of cooked spinach. This is because the raw spinach loses its structure and \"shrinks\" during cooking. Many more cooked spinach leaves are required to make a serving. For comparison: 1/2 -cup cooked, fresh spinach weighs 3 ounces and has 419 mg potassium, while 1/2 -cup raw, fresh spinach weighs 1 ounce and has 156 mg potassium."],[null,"A 6-ounce package of pre-washed spinach contains 3 cups."]]},"7965730":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200ºC/gas 6. Set a sheet of filo pastry on a non-stick baking tray. Brush with a little melted butter and sprinkle with a little icing sugar."],[null,"Repeat three more times, reserving about 1 tsp of the icing sugar."],[null,"Bake for 10 minutes until golden. Leave to cool. Mix the fromage frais with the lemon curd and spread over the pastry."],[null,"Top with the strawberries and sprinkle with the reserved icing sugar. Serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"This also works well with raspberries."],[null,"If you don’t have lemon curd, use 1 tbsp jam instead."]]},"3473":{"s":[[null,"Place strawberries, apple, mint and lemon in a juicer and process to extract juice. Add the green tea."],[null,"Pour into 2 small glasses to make 2 servings. Drink right away or place in the refrigerator to chill."]],"h":[[null,"Juicing sounds healthy, but for kidney patients on a low potassium diet a small amount of juice can provide a large amount of potassium."],[null,"To stay within your potassium goal for the day be sure to count as 1-1/2 serving of fruit from your daily plan."],[null,"Consult with your dietitian when incorporating juicing into your kidney diet. Juice blends are high in potassium and may not be recommended if potassium control is an issue."]]},"6699793":{"s":[[null,"Preheat a grill pan over medium-high heat. Season the chicken with salt and pepper and spray lightly with cooking spray. Grill the chicken until cooked through, 6–7 minutes per side."],[null,"Meanwhile, make the salsa by combining the strawberries, tomatoes, shallot, jalapeño, lime juice, garlic, olive oil and cilantro. Stir to combine."],[null,"Divide the chicken between plates and top with the salsa."]],"h":[]},"6929265":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, mix together the ricotta cheese, honey, lemon zest, and cinnamon."],[null,"Divide the mixture among four individual dessert dishes. Top each dish with a portion of strawberries and sprinkle with some of the graham cracker crumbs."]],"h":[]},"2260":{"s":[[null,"In a blender combine strawberries, lemon juice, and 1 tablespoon sugar or Splenda®. Blend until smooth."],[null,"With blender running, add 1/2 cup ice cubes, one at a time, through opening in lid until beverage is slushy."],[null,"Sip slowly to enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"If desired, add 1/3 cup lemonade base or sugar free lemon base from the DaVita recipe instead of the fresh lemon juice. The low sugar version made with sugar free lemonade base and sugar free sweetener has 50 calories and 13 g carbohydrate. Count as 1 low potassium fruit and one carbohydrate choice."]]},"2198":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375° F. Set butter out to soften."],[null,"Wash and dry apples. Using an apple corer or sharp knife, remove the core, leaving bottom of apple intact."],[null,"To make streusel, mix flour, sugar and spices together in a small bowl. Add butter and blend with a fork. Add chopped walnuts and cranberries."],[null,"Stuff mixture inside apples. Dot each apple with a small amount of butter."],[null,"Place apples into a baking dish. Add 1/2 cup boiling water to the dish."],[null,"Bake for 25 to 30 minutes until apples are tender."]],"h":[[null,"Serve warm apples with a dollop of whipped cream if desired."],[null,"Grace prefers Honeycrisp apples. Other baking apples include Jonagold, Braeburn, Winesap and Granny Smith."],[null,"The recommended portion for a low carbohydrate diet is 1/2 apple. Replace the brown sugar with 1 tablespoon brown sugar blend and omit the cranberries to reduce carbs to 19 grams and calories to 174 per 1/2 apple with strudel."]]},"6165250":{"s":[[null,"Sprinkle the steak with the salt and pepper."],[null,"Heat 1/2 Tbsp of the oil in a large cast-iron skillet over high heat. Add the steak and sear for about 3 minutes."],[null,"Turn the steak over, reduce the heat to medium, and cook for 4 to 6 minutes, or longer as desired for doneness. Remove the steak from the pan and keep it warm."],[null,"Add the remaining oil to the pan. Add the onions and sauté over medium heat for 5 minutes."],[null,"Add the water, thyme, and brown sugar, cover the pan, and simmer over medium-low heat for 10 minutes, until the onions are very soft."],[null,"Slice the steak. Serve the slices covered with the onions."]],"h":[]},"6248486":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F."],[null,"Place the acorn squash halves, cut side up, on a baking sheet. Drizzle with 2 tsp olive oil and season with 1/4 tsp coarse salt and black pepper."],[null,"Roast the acorn squash in the preheated oven for about 45 minutes to 1 hour or until fork-tender."],[null,"While the squash is roasting, prepare the stuffing. In a large skillet, heat the remaining 1 tsp olive oil over medium heat."],[null,"Add the chopped onion and sauté until softened, about 3–4 minutes. Add minced garlic and cook for an additional 1–2 minutes until fragrant."],[null,"Stir in the chopped celery and cook for another 3–4 minutes until it begins to soften."],[null,"Add the cauliflower rice, baby spinach, chopped walnuts, dried thyme, dried sage, and remaining 1/4 tsp coarse salt. Mix well and cook for an additional 5 minutes, allowing the flavors to meld."],[null,"Once the acorn squash is done roasting, fill each half with the stuffing."]],"h":[]},"7887932":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4."],[null,"Rinse the quinoa in a sieve, then add to a pan with 150ml water. Bring to the boil, turn down the heat and simmer gently for 15 minutes. Drain off any unabsorbed water and fluff with a fork."],[null,"Place the quinoa in a bowl with the garlic, raisins, cumin, spring onion, tomato puree and lemon juice. Mix well and set aside."],[null,"Meanwhile, lightly oil a baking tray and halve the peppers lengthways, leaving the stems in place and removing the seeds."],[null,"Divide the quinoa evenly between the peppers and top each with a tomato quarter and a small piece of mozzarella."],[null,"Place the peppers onto a baking tray and bake for 10-12 minutes until the peppers have softened and the cheese has melted. Sprinkle with chives and a grind of black pepper."]],"h":[[null,"You can assemble these the day before and leave in the fridge overnight and then bake them just before they are needed."],[null,"You could add other spices, such as curry powder, or use couscous instead of quinoa."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Freeze in portions then defrost in the microwave. Heat until piping-hot, stirring regularly. Eat immediately and discard any leftovers."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"7972818":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C / gas 4"],[null,"Mix together the walnuts, apricots and sultanas, then place on a board. Finely chop together to create a paste, then mix in the pumpkin seeds, cinnamon and orange zest."],[null,"Stuff the centre of each apple with the mixture, pressing it firmly into the fruit."],[null,"Place the apples into an ovenproof dish with the water, then drizzle the orange juice over them."],[null,"Cover with foil and bake for 20 minutes. Remove the foil and continue to bake for 10-15 minutes."],[null,"Serve with a dollop of unsweetened plain yoghurt or non-dairy alternative."]],"h":[[null,"Experiment with different combinations of fruits and nuts for the filling."],[null,"Try with cranberries and mixed spice for a Christmas flavour."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"7641472":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 200°C/fan 180°C/gas 6."],[null,"Halve the aubergines lengthways and, using a small knife, cut a 1cm-thick border inside each half. Scoop out and reserve the flesh inside the borders, so you’re left with 8 x 1cm-thick aubergine shells. Put them on a non-stick baking tray, cut-sides up, then spray with a couple pumps of low-calorie cooking spray and season lightly with pepper and dried mixed herbs, if you like. Cover with foil and bake for 15-20 minutes."],[null,"While they’re cooking, finely chop the aubergine flesh. Spray a non-stick frying pan with a few pumps of low-calorie cooking spray and stir-fry the aubergine and onion for 10-15 minutes, or until softened. Stir in the garlic, tomatoes, chopped basil, chilli and Italian seasoning and stir-fry for a further 2-3 minutes. Remove from the heat and stir in half the mozarella."],[null,"Divide the mixture between the cooked aubergine shells, then scatter over the remaining mozzarella. Return to the oven for 20 minutes, or until lightly browned, then scatter over the torn basil. Serve 2 aubergine halves per person with the salad."]],"h":[[null,"Find out more about our partnership with Slimming World."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"6702069":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400 degrees F."],[null,"Trim the ends of the Brussels sprouts and cut them in half, lengthwise. Bring a large pot of water to a boil and blanch the sprouts for 2 minutes, drain and set aside."],[null,"Using a melon baller or Tsp. measure, core the sprouts, set aside the shells and roughly chop the scooped cores."],[null,"Add olive oil to a medium sauté pan over medium heat. Add bacon and sauté until almost crisp. Add the chopped sprouts and garlic and sauté for a 3-4 more minutes until the sprouts have softened."],[null,"In a bowl, mix together the goat cheese, milk, salt (optional), black pepper and parmesan cheese. Add the sautéed bacon and sprouts and mix thoroughly."],[null,"Divide the filling mixture evenly among each sprout core (about a rounded Tsp.). Lay sprouts on a baking sheet and bake for 20 minutes or until the filled sprouts are a golden brown. Serve warm."]],"h":[]},"2499":{"s":[[null,"Cut bread loaf into 16 slices."],[null,"Spread 1 tablespoon cream cheese on each slice of bread. Top with 1 tablespoon jelly and add bread slice to make a sandwich. Repeat until 8 sandwiches are made."],[null,"Spray a 9” x 13” baking dish with nonstick cooking spray and place the 8 sandwiches in the dish."],[null,"Beat eggs and then mix with milk and vanilla extract. Pour over the bread slices, turning to coat the slices evenly. Cover and refrigerate overnight."],[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F. Cover pan with foil and bake for 1 hour. The last 5 minutes of baking, remove the foil to brown the top."]],"h":[[null,"Bring cream cheese to room temperature so it is easier to spread."],[null,"Serving suggestions: drizzle with syrup, garnish with fresh fruit and whipped cream or dust with powdered sugar."],[null,"This recipe is a good source of protein and calories, a great choice for a high-energy breakfast. Try this different spin on French Toast. It is a good use for leftover bread. Also, preparing this recipe the night before leaves you with nothing left to do in the morning except bake and serve. It’s perfect for brunch."],[null,"Compare breads and select the lower sodium brand."]]},"2136":{"s":[[null,"Cut peppers in half from stem to bottom. Remove seeds. Parboil 4 minutes."],[null,"In a large frying pan cook ground turkey. Remove meat and reserve. Discard pan drippings."],[null,"Sauté onion in 1 teaspoon butter until translucent. Add salsa, Mrs. Dash® herb seasoning, cooked rice and meat. Stir to combine."],[null,"Stuff green pepper halves with the meat and rice mixture, and place into a shallow baking dish. Add 1/2 cup water to the pan."],[null,"Combine bread crumbs, poultry seasoning and melted butter. Sprinkle over stuffed peppers."],[null,"Cover and bake at 350 F for 30 minutes. Uncover and bake 5 minutes until browned."]],"h":[[null,"Ground beef can be substituted for the turkey. It will increase the fat content a bit."],[null,"For variety use red or orange bell peppers instead of green peppers."]]},"6726437":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 325 degrees F. Coat a square baking dish with cooking spray."],[null,"Remove the stems from the mushrooms and chop them finely. Set aside the stems."],[null,"Place the mushroom caps in a bowl and toss them with 1 Tsp. olive oil and balsamic vinegar. Set aside the caps."],[null,"Heat the remaining Tsp. olive oil in a medium skillet over medium heat. Add the onion, green pepper, and mushroom stems and sauté for 3 minutes. Add the sausage and cook for another 8 to 10 minutes, stirring frequently, until the sausage is completely browned."],[null,"Add the bread crumbs, stirring to combine evenly with all the other ingredients. Stir in the mozzarella cheese and melt."],[null,"Remove the pan from the heat and stir in the Parmesan cheese."],[null,"Fill each mushroom generously with the sausage mixture (about 1 heaping Tbsp. per mushroom cap). Arrange the mushrooms in the baking dish and bake 40 minutes or until the stuffing is crispy on the top."]],"h":[]},"7677354":{"s":[[null,"Boil the sweet potato for 10–15 minutes until soft, then drain and mash."],[null,"Add the spring onions, turmeric, cumin, ground coriander, garlic and chilli, fresh coriander and peas to the sweet potato. Mix well and reserve."],[null,"Add the flour to a bowl with the baking powder, yogurt and water. Mix well into a dough."],[null,"Divide the dough into 8 balls. On a lightly floured surface, roll each ball out into thin circles, creating 8 pancakes."],[null,"Divide the filling into four and spread it out over four of the dough circles, leaving a 1cm border around the edge."],[null,"Brush the edges with a little water, then place another dough circle on top, pressing the edges firmly together."],[null,"Brush a non-stick frying pan with ½ tsp oil, then place a paratha in the pan and cook over a low to medium heat for 2 minutes, turn over with a spatula and cook the other side for 2 minutes. Flip again and give each side one more minute. (When ready, the surface of the paratha should have a few brown spots). Repeat with the remaining parathas."],[null,"Cut into quarters to serve."]],"h":[[null,"These parathas can be spiced up by adding some chopped fresh chilli and grated ginger when mixing the filling."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"2722":{"s":[[null,"Set cream cheese out to soften. Rinse and remove stems from strawberries."],[null,"Place point down side up on a cutting board and cut a deep “x” in the top of each strawberry. Carefully spread berries apart."],[null,"In a small bowl, beat cream cheese and sour cream until smooth."],[null,"Pipe or spoon filling into each berry."],[null,"Refrigerate until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Try stuffed strawberries at your next party or potluck. Your guests are sure to love this one."],[null,"Strawberries are a very low carbohydrate fruit. That’s why 4 large strawberries are counted as only 1/2 carbohydrate choice and only 1/2 serving of fruit."],[null,"One large strawberry is 1-3/8” diameter, not to be confused with extra large strawberries, 1-5/8” diameter. Twenty-four large strawberries is approximately one pound."]]},"3220":{"s":[[null,"Pre-heat oven to 375° F."],[null,"Cut zucchini in half lengthwise. Using a spoon, scoop out seeds, forming a trench in each zucchini half."],[null,"Place zucchini in a pot of boiling water, and boil for 3 to 5 minutes."],[null,"While zucchini is cooking, toast 2 slices of bread."],[null,"Place toast and 2 uncooked pieces of bread in food processor to make bread crumbs."],[null,"Add seasonings to bread crumbs and mix well."],[null,"Add 1/2 cup of the zucchini cooking water and blend with a fork to get the consistency of stuffing."],[null,"Remove zucchini from water and place in 8 x 8” baking dish, peel side down."],[null,"Spoon stuffing into trench in each zucchini half."],[null,"Bake for 20 minutes and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute one large zucchini and serve 1/4 instead of 1/2 medium squash pieces."]]},"6340387":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350° F. Heat the olive oil in a large, heavy ovenproof skillet over medium heat, and add the onions. Cook for 8 to 10 minutes, stirring occasionally, until they are golden."],[null,"Meanwhile, in a small bowl, combine the ginger, dill, salt, and pepper; set aside. Top the onions with the lemon slices and then the salmon, and top the salmon evenly with the spices. Transfer the skillet to the oven and cook the salmon for about 20 minutes, until it is cooked through. Remove from the oven and serve immediately. Green Beans With Lemon and Garlic make a great side dish for the salmon."],[null,"Slow Cooker Directions: Cut the salmon fillet into pieces that will fit into the slow cooker. Combine the onions in the bottom of the slow cooker. Place each piece of salmon onto a separate piece of aluminum foil large enough to fold into a packet. Sprinkle the spices evenly over the salmon pieces and top with lemon slices. Fold the foil into a packet, and place the packets into the slow cooker on top of the onions, stacking as needed. Cook on low for 6 to 8 hours or on high for 3 to 4 hours (for thinner fillets check for doneness sooner). Remove the salmon from the packets, then top with the onions before serving."]],"h":[]},"3827":{"s":[[null,"Heat the butter, sugar, cinnamon and nutmeg on the stove in a saucepan until butter melts and sugar dissolves. If preferred, microwave the ingredients in a microwave-safe bowl. Be careful not to burn the butter."],[null,"Drizzle spiced butter mixture over popped popcorn; mix well."],[null,"Serve immediately for best results."]],"h":[[null,"If you don’t have an air-popper, use 1 bag no-salt microwave popcorn, popped. Fat content will be higher."]]},"9330923":{"s":[[null,"Quarter the strawberries and add to a large pan. Cook over medium heat for 6-8 minutes, until soft and bubbling."],[null,"Then remove from the heat and use a potato masher to gently mash the strawberries, but still leaving some chunky fruit pieces. Add the chia seeds and maple syrup, if using, and mix well."],[null,"Set aside to let cool slightly, and then divide the jam into clean, air tight jars. Jam will completely set once refrigerated overnight or at least 4 hours. Refrigerate to use within 1 week or freeze for up to 4 months."]],"h":[[null,"Use CLEAN jars to store your strawberry jam. If the jam appears a little watery once cooked, not to worry. As it cools, the chia seeds will continue to absorb the liquid and leave behind a perfectly textured, thick jelly. I use black chia seeds, as those are easiest to find where I live. They do darken the jam colour slightly, but you may use white chia seeds for a brighter coloured jam , if available. For a slightly thinner consistency , reduce the chia seeds to ¼ cup. Makes approximately 3.5 cups of strawberry jam. Separate into small jars and keep one refrigerated and freeze the rest for future use. Your strawberry jam will keep refrigerated for 1 week, or freeze for up to 4 months."]]},"6711224":{"s":[[null,"In a bowl, mix Greek yogurt and SweetLeaf Sweet Drops Clear with a spoon until the mixture is a creamy consistency."],[null,"Take a tall glass or small bowl for your parfait and add a layer of yogurt to the bottom. Add berries and nuts (optional) between layers of yogurt until you reach the top. Enjoy!"],[null,"Tip: A finished parfait stores great in the fridge for easy meal prep on the go!"]],"h":[]},"6161118":{"s":[],"h":[]},"7942789":{"s":[[null,"Gently fold together all the ingredients and spoon into serving glasses. Sprinkle over the crushed biscuits if you like."]],"h":[[null,"If you don’t have amaretti biscuits, you could use shortbread or ginger biscuits."],[null,"The nutrition information provided includes the biscuit but they are optional."],[null,"For a vegan version, use a soya-based yogurt in place of the fromage frais."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"7156026":{"s":[[null,"Put the water, granulated sweetener and lemon juice in a small pan over a low heat until the liquid has reduced and begins to look sticky."],[null,"Meanwhile, put the egg whites and cream of tartar in a bowl, and slowly whisk together until they form soft peaks."],[null,"Slowly pour the sweetener mixture into the beaten egg whites."],[null,"Gently add the cornflour and continue to mix until the egg whites are stiff."],[null,"On a parchment-lined baking tray, spread or pipe the meringue to form a bowl, about 20-25cm (10 ins) across."],[null,"Bake in a cool oven, 100°C/gas ¼ for about 1 hour 20 minutes, until it is firm and just beginning to colour. Open the oven door and leave the meringue in the oven until it is cool."],[null,"When cool, carefully place the meringue on your serving plate."],[null,"Combine a third of the fruit with the yogurt, adding sweetener if needed. Pile into the meringue and top with the remaining berries and a few sprigs of mint."]],"h":[[null,"If your meringue starts to brown before it is cooked, open the oven door for a few minutes to reduce the heat."],[null,"Don’t fill your meringue until just before serving – it will go soggy if it’s left too long with the berry filling. However, you can make the yogurt/fruit mixture in advance and refrigerate until needed."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"7705270":{"s":[[null,"Add the raspberries and blueberries to the jam, mash with a fork and mix well."],[null,"Add half the berry mixture to the yogurt and crème fraiche, and mix well."],[null,"Divide the rest of the berry mixture between four glasses, placing a blob in the bottom of each and drizzling a little around the inside."],[null,"Divide the yogurt mixture between the glasses, topping each with a blueberry."]],"h":[[null,"For a variation, try using fresh apricots and apricot jam, or add crunch with a sprinkle of toasted almonds or chopped hazelnuts."],[null,"Half-fat crème fraîche has less than a third of the fat of double cream and also contains more protein."],[null,"Berries contain antioxidants and vitamins – especially vitamin C. The pigments that give them their different colours contain phytonutrients and flavonoids. They are a good source of fibre."]]},"4978734":{"s":[[null,"Combine the berries and water with the sugar in a saucepan and bring to a boil. Simmer until the berries soften (5–10 minutes)."],[null,"Allow berry mixture to cool and blend thoroughly. Pass berries through a fine strainer to remove the seeds."],[null,"In a separate bowl, whip egg whites until frothy. Slowly add the sugar and whisk until soft peaks form."],[null,"Add lemon juice and vanilla to the berry mixture. Fold in the Cool Whip® and beaten egg whites with a spoon."],[null,"Transfer into dessert dishes of your choice. Cover with plastic wrap and freeze for at least 4 hours."],[null,"Garnish with fresh berries and serve."]],"h":[[null,"* To lower the carbohydrate contents you can use a sugar substitute such as Splenda®"],[null,"You can also freeze the semifreddo in a single container, such as a square pan or a muffin pan. To make removal easy after freezing, line the pan or muffin compartments with plastic wrap. Always cover with plastic wrap before freezing."],[null,"This dessert can be made a day or two ahead of serving."],[null,"Try it with other types of fresh berries!"],["Enjoy low-potassium fruits","Eating fruit every day is part of a healthy diet. Fruits provide fiber and vitamins, as well as antioxidants and phytochemicals, which are nutrients that help protect you from a variety of diseases. However, they can also be a rich source of minerals such as potassium. Potassium is a mineral that can be harmful if you eat more than your kidneys can handle. When this occurs, the potassium level in your blood can increase to a dangerously high level. Fortunately, there are a number of fruits that are lower in potassium, so if you have chronic kidney disease and must monitor the amount of potassium in your diet, these are the fruits that you should choose on a daily basis. When limited to ½-cup portions, lower-potassium fruits include apples, berries, cherries, clementines, fruit cocktail, grapes, kiwi, lemon or lime, mandarin oranges, pears, pineapple, plums, tangerines and watermelon. Juices from these fruits are also considered to be a good choice for you. Ask your dietitian how much of these foods you should eat each day to maintain good health and avoid high potassium levels."]]},"4372522":{"s":[[null,"Combine the ingredients for the marinade in a sealable plastic bag or a container with a cover. Add the chicken breasts to the marinade mixture, making sure they are well covered with the marinade. Place in the fridge for 12 hours or overnight."],[null,"When ready to cook the marinated chicken breasts, heat the grill on high."],[null,"Take the chicken breasts out of the marinade and brush off the herbs (herbs remaining on the chicken breast during the grilling process may burn). Discard the marinade."],[null,"Reduce grill temperature to medium, brush the grill with oil and place the chicken breasts on the grill. Cover and grill for 7-8 minutes. Flip the chicken breasts, cover and grill another 7-8 minutes or until the internal temperature reads 165°F."],[null,"Transfer the grilled chicken breasts to a plate, cover with aluminum foil and let rest for 10 minutes to lock in the natural juices."],[null,"While the chicken is resting, mix the ingredients for the dressing in a small bowl."],[null,"Slice the chicken breasts, place them on a serving plate, and pour the dressing over the sliced chicken. Oven/stove method: Don’t have a grill, no worries! Preheat oven to 350°F. Place the chicken breasts on a baking sheet that is lined with parchment paper or aluminum foil. Bake for 10 minutes, turn the chicken then bake for an additional 10 minutes or until an internal temperature of 165°F has been reached. You can also use a grill pan on the stove."]],"h":[[null,"For individuals with CKD not on dialysis, reduce the amount of protein by reducing the chicken portion"],["Understanding potassium on food labels","The Nutrition Facts on a food label inform us about the nutrients in packaged foods. As an example, sodium, protein and potassium are important nutrients for people with kidney disease to keep track of, and are now listed on every label. To understand the potassium content of the food you like to eat: 1. Try to avoid foods with potassium additives. These are foods that have the word “potassium” in combination with another word listed under ingredients (e.g potassium chloride). 2. Determine the serving size. Many times, consuming only a single serving can allow certain lower- to moderate-potassium foods to fit within your diet. 3. Next, find potassium with minerals and vitamins mentioned on the bottom of Nutrition Facts. The amount of potassium is listed by serving size in milligrams and with a percent (%) Daily Value (DV). • Note that the % DV is based off a total of 4,700 milligrams of potassium. This is the amount of potassium the average adult should consume in a day. However, it is much higher than the amount many people with chronic kidney disease should consume. Therefore, if you are on a low-potassium diet, the % DV does not apply to you and may be much higher. Work with your healthcare team or a registered dietitian nutritionist that specializes in kidney disease to find out what amount is safe for you. • As a general rule, aim to select foods with less than 5% DV of potassium. Use the % DV for potassium to compare similar products side by side."]]},"3291":{"s":[[null,"Cook pasta according to package instructions, omitting salt. Drain and rinse with cold water."],[null,"Chop jalapeno and bell peppers after removing seeds and membrane."],[null,"Chop red onion and basil. Shred carrots."],[null,"Dice cooked chicken breasts. Drain and rinse olives."],[null,"In a large bowl toss all ingredients together."],[null,"Chill in the refrigerator until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Any type of pasta would work for this recipe."],[null,"To add extra flavor use grilled chicken breasts."],[null,"For a higher or lower protein dish you can adjust the amount of chicken."],[null,"The feta cheese and olives are limited, providing less than 1 tablespoon per serving. You can reduce the amount or omit to further reduce sodium and phosphorus."]]},"6956622":{"s":[[null,"In a medium bowl combine cabbage, chicken, carrots, cucumbers, cilantro, mushrooms and green onion."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the soy sauce, vinegar, hot water, olive oil, and ginger."],[null,"Before using, soak spring roll skin in water for 10-15 seconds and shake off excess water. Place about 1/3 cup of chicken-vegetable mixture in the bottom of spring roll. Take the spring roll edge nearest to you and fold to cover the filling. Take the side edges and fold in tightly. Roll outward to seal. Repeat procedure for remaining spring rolls."],[null,"Serve spring rolls with dipping sauce."]],"h":[]},"6781776":{"s":[[null,"In a medium bowl mix together all salad ingredients, except lettuce leaves."],[null,"Serve 1/2 cup crab salad on each lettuce leaf. You could also serve on whole-wheat bread or crackers."]],"h":[]},"4893996":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400°F (conventional oven)."],[null,"Over medium heat, warm oil and add garlic, onion, pepper, tomato and chilies, cooking until soft."],[null,"Add 1/2 cup of water, the basil and the lemon zest, cover and cook for 20 minutes."],[null,"Let the mixture cool a bit and blend it in the blender."],[null,"Place the pita on cookie sheet. Spread pepper sauce on pita and top with vegetables and cheese. Drizzle with olive oil."],[null,"Bake in oven for 10–12 minutes. Enjoy with salad."]],"h":[[null,"The left-over sauce may be frozen in ice cube trays. Be sure to transfer cubes to sealable plastic bags once frozen to ensure freshness."],[null,"This red pepper sauce replaces tomato paste and gives a lovely taste when mixed into soups and stews."]]},"6719399":{"s":[[null,"Combine all ingredients in a blender and puree until smooth."]],"h":[]},"3858":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350º F."],[null,"Cut eggplant into 1/2″ pieces. Measure 3 cups for recipe. Chop onion, celery, parsley and bell peppers."],[null,"Mix vegetables together."],[null,"Spray a 1-1/2 quart baking dish with cooking spray. Add vegetable mixture and cover. Bake for 40 minutes."],[null,"While the vegetables are baking mix melted margarine and Mrs. Dash® herb seasoning with the soft bread crumbs."],[null,"Uncover baking dish and sprinkle with crumb mixture. Return the uncovered dish to oven. Bake 10 minutes longer or until the topping is lightly browned."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute your favorite low potassium vegetables like green beans, asparagus or cauliflower."]]},"6460699":{"s":[[null,"Cook corn according to package directions."],[null,"In a small saucepan, heat oil; add garlic and saute until brown."],[null,"Remove from heat and cool; strain and reserve oil; discard garlic."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine reserved oil, vinegar, mustard, pepper, and sugar. Add 1/2 teaspoon salt, if desired."],[null,"Combine oil mixture with corn, sirloin, potatoes, green onions, carrots, and both kinds of peppers. Mix well, cover, and chill."],[null,"Serve in a bowl lined with salad greens."]],"h":[]},"3496":{"s":[[null,"Chop the tomato and slice the cucumber; shred the lettuce and carrot."],[null,"Place vegetables in a salad bowl and toss together."],[null,"Divide into 4 portions and serve in chilled salad bowls with low-sodium dressing."]],"h":[[null,"Use exact measures ensure the potassium content is not too high."]]},"3184":{"s":[[null,"Cut squash into 1-inch cubes. Dice bell pepper into small pieces."],[null,"Placed cubed squash in a slow cooker."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix the green bell pepper, pineapple with juice, cinnamon, brown sugar and melted butter."],[null,"Spoon over squash and mix well."],[null,"Cover squash and cook on low heat setting for 6-7 hours or until squash is tender."],[null,"Stir gently to mix before serving."]],"h":[[null,"People with diabetes may use Splenda® Brown Sugar Blend. Reduce the portion to 2-1/2 tablespoons to reduce carbohydrate to 8 grams per serving."],[null,"Cook on high heat setting for 4 to 5 hours if quicker cooking time desired."]]},"6422216":{"s":[[null,"Bring a large pot of water to boil."],[null,"Meanwhile, set a large sauté pan on medium high and add olive oil. When heated, add tomatoes."],[null,"Cook until tomatoes start to blister and lose their shape (about 5 minutes). shaking the pan every so often, until the tomatoes are just starting to blister and lose their shape (about 5 minutes)."],[null,"Turn heat down to low and add garlic. Cook until fragrant (about 1 minute). Remove tomatoes and garlic from heat and place in large bowl. Set pan aside for later use, you do not need to clean it yet."],[null,"Once water is boiled, add asparagus and cook for 1 minute. Remove with a strainer and add to veggie bowl. Repeat with broccoli and peas. Set veggie bowl aside."],[null,"Cook the package of zucchini spirals according to cooking instructions and set aside."],[null,"In a separate bowl, mix the cottage cheese, lemon zest, basil, and parsley."],[null,"Re-heat large sauté pan to medium high. Add the vegetables, zucchini spirals, cottage cheese mixture, and lemon juice. Stir to combine and cook until hot and everything is coated with the cheese sauce (about 5 minutes)."]],"h":[]},"7670689":{"s":[[null,"Place the fine beans into a pan of boiling water and cook for 2 minutes."],[null,"Add the courgettes, broad beans and peas and continue to cook for 1 minute. Drain and refresh under cold water, then transfer to a serving dish."],[null,"Mix together the remaining ingredients and toss through the vegetables. Serve."]],"h":[[null,"To toast pumpkin seeds, add to a dry pan and fry over a medium heat for 2-3 minutes stirring regularly until they start to brown."],[null,"You could use lemon or orange in place of lime."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"7096513":{"s":[[null,"Place the berries and the milk in a food processor or blender and blend until smooth and frothy, sweeten to taste and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Add 1 tbsp low-fat live yogurt to introduce some probiotics to your diet."],[null,"You could use other fruits such as mango, banana, peaches, nectarines or just one type of berry. If using very ripe fruits, you shouldn’t need to add sweetener."],[null,"Summerberries are naturally lower in carbohydrate than tropical fruits such as banana or mango."],[null,"For a dairy alternative, swap to unsweetened, fortified plant-based milk."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6320079":{"s":[[null,"Make the citrus dressing: In a blender or food processor, blend olive oil, lemon juice, orange juice, 1/4 of the avocado, parsley, salt, and garlic until smooth. Set aside."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine lettuce, tomato, quinoa, edamame, the rest of the avocado, and pepitas. Pour dressing over salad and toss gently. Serve immediately or chill until ready to serve."]],"h":[]},"6767827":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6793700":{"s":[[null,"In a large glass trifle or serving bowl, layer the broccoli, onion, raisins (or dried tart cherries), and cheese."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the yogurt, vinegar, honey, and mayonnaise. Pour the dressing evenly over the salad."],[null,"Cover and refrigerate until ready to serve. Sprinkle with the sunflower seeds just before serving."]],"h":[]},"4035983":{"s":[[null,"Heat oil in a small skillet over medium heat. Sauté the leeks until soft, approximately 5 minutes. Add the baby spinach and continue to sauté until wilted. Season with black pepper."],[null,"Place the 4 shells on a baking sheet. To the base of each shell, spread 1 teaspoon of garlic & herb cream cheese. Divide the spinach and leek mixture between the four shells, creating a well for the egg. Crack a whole egg into the well."],[null,"Bake for 15–20 minutes or until the egg whites set. Serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"* you can also use regular cream cheese and season with 1 teaspoon minced garlic and ¼ teaspoon dill"],[null,"PLEASE NOTE: For this photo the chef used frozen puff pastry dough to form larger shells. The dough is usually higher in fat than the store-bought shells."],["Cream cheese can be a low potassium cheese option","Lowering intake of high potassium foods is key when following your kidney diet. Cheese is found in many recipes and adds to the flavor, appearance and texture of your dish. Cheese provides calcium, protein and Vitamin D. However, moderation is necessary for the kidney patient as too much results in high sodium, phosphorus and potassium intake. Cream cheese is a lower potassium selection that can be used with your meals. A one-tablespoon portion contains approximately 20mg of potassium. Monitoring your portion size allows you to enjoy this food while following your kidney diet. Try cream cheese as a filling for appetizer dips, a sweet treat in desserts and breakfast dishes, a dressing in fruit salads as well as a spread for sandwiches and main dishes making this a very versatile food item for your kidney diet."]]},"6262970":{"s":[[null,"Brush a small nonstick skillet with 1 tsp. of the oil and heat over medium heat. Add the eggs one at a time and cook sunny side up for about 2 minutes. Using a spatula, transfer to a plate."],[null,"While the eggs are cooking, warm the tortillas in a separate skillet (no need to add any oil)."],[null,"For each serving, spread a tortilla with half of the mashed avocado, tomatoes, pine nuts, cilantro, and jalapeños, if using. Top with an egg, drizzle with the remaining extra-virgin olive oil, and season with the salt and pepper. Fold over and serve."]],"h":[]},"3947":{"s":[[null,"Place ground beef into a large mixing bowl."],[null,"Add ground red pepper, garlic powder, cumin, chili powder, black pepper, water, egg white, chopped green chile and onion. Mix well."],[null,"Divide mixture into 5 portions and make into patties."],[null,"Cook on stove top in frying pan over medium heat, turning patties only once."],[null,"Place each patty on a hamburger bun and top with 1/4-cup shredded lettuce, 1/2-tablespoon salsa and 1/2-tablespoon sour cream."]],"h":[[null,"Patties are done when internal temperature reaches 160° F for medium or 170° F for well done."],[null,"Compare labels to limit hidden sodium in buns, salsa and sour cream."]]},"6886220":{"s":[[null,"Rinse and cook the quinoa in 1 cup water for about 10 minutes or until the water is just absorbed. Fluff it and remove it from the heat."],[null,"Meanwhile, cook the edamame for 5 minutes in about 4 cups of boiling water."],[null,"In a small food processor or blender, puree the oil, lemon and orange juices, avocado, cilantro, salt and garlic."],[null,"In a large salad bowl, combine the lettuce, bell pepper, quinoa, edamame, and sunflower seeds. Pour the dressing over everything and toss gently. Serve immediately."],[null,"Do Ahead Or Delegate: Cook the quinoa and the edamame, juice the orange, chop the cilantro, peel the garlic, prepare the dressing and dice the bell pepper."]],"h":[]},"3099":{"s":[[null,"Add frozen fruit to blender."],[null,"Add chilled Nepro®, whey protein and crushed ice (if desired)."],[null,"Blend until smooth."],[null,"Pour into glass and serve with straw."]],"h":[[null,"Freeze or refrigerate the leftover portion for later."],[null,"Recipe analysis used values for Beneprotein® whey protein powder, 7 gram size scoops. Nutrient values may vary slightly with similar products."]]},"2815":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 450° F."],[null,"Beat eggs and milk in a medium bowl with a wire whisk or electric mixer."],[null,"Beat in flour, salt and nutmeg until blended (tiny lumps of flour left in the batter are okay)."],[null,"Pour oil into a 9″ ovenproof skillet or pie pan and place in preheated oven 5 minutes to heat oil."],[null,"Carefully pour batter in skillet and bake uncovered 18 to 20 minutes. (Avoid opening oven door until pancake is puffed up and crisp around the edges. Middle will be golden brown when cooked.)"],[null,"Cut into 4 wedges and serve with pancake syrup or fruit spread."]],"h":[[null,"Replace milk with a nondairy substitute such as unenriched rice milk or nondairy creamer. Phosphorus and potassium will be slightly lower."],[null,"For additional protein, add an extra egg white."]]},"7211263":{"s":[[null,"Prepare the noodles according to pack instructions and set aside."],[null,"Cut the tofu into cubes and toast in the frying pan. It won't take too long to brown so keep an eye on it."],[null,"Spray your frying pan with oil, if using. Place on a high heat and toss all of the vegetables to flash cook, along with the ginger and garlic."],[null,"Add the Chinese five spice mix, soy sauce, ketchup and chilli, if using. Toss as you cook until the vegetables are al dente."],[null,"Add the cooked noodles, garnish with the coriander and serve."]],"h":[[null,"This recipe has been created by Balance cover star, Shivali, as part of her journey to diabetes remission."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"3929":{"s":[[null,"Mince garlic and thinly slice onion and apples (skin on)."],[null,"Mix flour and all of the spices in a gallon size zip lock bag. Coat chicken breast with the mixture by shaking all ingredients in the locked bag."],[null,"Heat oil in a large skillet over medium heat. Add chicken and brown on both sides."],[null,"Remove the chicken from the skillet. Add onions and garlic. Cook and stir 3 minutes or until tender."],[null,"Add apples. Cook and stir 2 minutes."],[null,"Stir in apple juice, brown sugar and the cooked chicken, bringing to a boil. Reduce heat to low, cover and simmer 10 to 15 minutes or until desired tenderness."]],"h":[[null,"Another name Janis created for this recipe is “You don’t need teeth to eat this chicken.”"],[null,"If desired, cut chicken breast into pieces before browning in step #3."],[null,"Use any variety of apple desired."],[null,"Divide into 4 servings to increase protein to 27 grams if you need more protein in your diet."]]},"2191":{"s":[[null,"Cook pasta according to package instructions, omitting salt. Drain and set aside."],[null,"Mince onion and garlic. Shell and devein shrimp."],[null,"Sauté onion and garlic in oil until lightly brown."],[null,"Add sun dried tomatoes, shrimp and pea pods."],[null,"Cook until shrimp change color (but pea pods remain crunchy)."],[null,"Mix shrimp and pasta."],[null,"Sprinkle feta cheese on top and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Four ounces of dry pasta yields 2 cups cooked."],[null,"Frozen shrimp can be substituted for fresh shrimp."]]},"6414849":{"s":[[null,"Combine all ingredients in a blender and puree until smooth and thick."]],"h":[]},"2986":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375° F."],[null,"Chop onion. Beat eggs."],[null,"Combine first 11 ingredients in a large bowl and mix well."],[null,"Roll into 1” balls and place on a baking sheet."],[null,"Bake for 10 to 15 minutes, until meatballs are cooked through."],[null,"To make sauce, melt butter in a large saucepan."],[null,"Add flour, reduced-sodium broth, remaining tablespoon dried thyme and water.Cook over medium heat, stirring until thickened."],[null,"Add meatballs to sauce and lower temperature to keep warm or place in a covered warming dish or slow cooker on low heat setting."]],"h":[[null,"Reduced-sodium broth contains 450 to 500 mg sodium per cup. Low-sodium broth contains 140 mg sodium or less per cup."],[null,"Make meatballs ahead and refrigerate. When ready to serve, heat ingredients together and transfer to a warming dish."]]},"2308":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl mix all ingredients until a stiff dough forms. Cover and refrigerate for at least 4 hours."],[null,"Preheat oven to 325° F."],[null,"Spray jelly roll pan with nonstick cooking spray. Press dough into the pan."],[null,"Place in oven and bake for 45 minutes."],[null,"Remove from oven and cool for 5 minutes."],[null,"Make 1” slices across the jelly roll pan (the short way). Cut each length into 3 pieces for a total of 36 rusks. Flip each slice on its side on the baking sheet."],[null,"Bake an additional 45 minutes at 275° F."],[null,"Turn off oven and leave rusks in oven overnight (or for at least 8 hours). The cooked rusks will resemble biscotti."],[null,"Serve with morning coffee or as a snack anytime."]],"h":[[null,"Alternatively, dough can be shaped into 2 rectangular loaves instead of pressing it into the jelly roll pan. Slice into 1” pieces, lay cut side down and continue baking."]]},"4642661":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil over medium heat in a heavy skillet."],[null,"Pepper the chicken drumsticks and brown them on all slides."],[null,"Meanwhile prepare the peppers, onion, garlic and ginger."],[null,"Remove the chicken, leaving oil in the pan."],[null,"Reduce the temperature to medium-low, add curry paste, garlic and ginger directly to the pan. Add the peppers and onion and coat well."],[null,"Return chicken to pan, add peaches with their juice and increase heat to bring everything to a simmer."],[null,"Cover and cook in the oven for 40 minutes at 350° F."],[null,"Remove from oven and place on the stove over low heat. Add yogurt, coconut milk and lime juice. Stir gently till heated through. Do not boil."],[null,"Garnish with chopped coriander and serve over white rice."]],"h":[]},"4715278":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil over medium heat in a heavy skillet."],[null,"Pepper the chicken drumsticks and brown them on all sides."],[null,"Meanwhile, prepare the peppers, onion, garlic and ginger."],[null,"Remove the chicken, leaving oil in the pan."],[null,"Reduce the temperature to medium-low, add the curry paste, garlic and ginger directly to the pan. Add the peppers and onion and coat well."],[null,"Return chicken to pan, add peaches with their juice and increase heat to bring everything to a simmer."],[null,"Cover and cook in the oven for 40 minutes at 350°F (conventional oven)."],[null,"Remove from oven and place on the stove over low heat. Add yogurt, coconut milk and lime juice. Stir gently until heated through. Do not boil."],[null,"Garnish with chopped coriander and serve over white rice."]],"h":[[null,"This recipe can be easily halved."],[null,"May be made ahead up to step 7 and refrigerated or frozen in portions. To finish: cook over low heat until heated through and add yogurt, coconut milk and lime juice. Cook rice while heating chicken."]]},"9753801":{"s":[["To Air Fry","Preheat your fryer to 370 degrees F and spray the bottom of your basket with cooking spray. Then combine all the marinade ingredients in a small bowl and mix well."],["To Air Fry","Peel and slice your plantains (about 1/4\" thick) and place them in the bowl with the marinade. Gently mix to evenly coat each slice."],["To Air Fry","Arrange the plantains in a single layer with plenty of space in between and air fry for 4-5 minutes, then flip and cook another 4-5 minutes until edges are golden brown and crispy."],["To Bake","Preheat your oven to 425 degrees F convection bake and line a large baking tray with parchment paper. Then combine all the marinade ingredients in a small bowl and mix well."],["To Bake","Peel and slice your plantains (about 1/4\" thick) and place them in the bowl with the marinade. Gently mix to evenly coat each slice."],["To Bake","Arrange your plantains in a single layer on your tray and bake for 15 minutes. Then flip and bake for 5-10 more minutes longer, until edges are golden brown and crispy."]],"h":[[null,"Choose ripe plantains with dull yellow skins and plenty of black spots on them. Make sure to arrange your plantain slices in a single layer with plenty of space in between, no matter which cooking method you choose. This will result in the best texture and crispy edges, and prevent the pieces from sticking together. Handle the slices with care when flipping them, so you don’t squish them. These plantains taste best when freshly made but you may keep leftovers in a sealed container in your fridge for 3-4 days."]]},"6036759":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350 degrees F."],[null,"Place Ramekins on a baking sheet and coat each with cooking spray."],[null,"In a mixing bowl, combine the apples, melted Smart Balance, brown sugar substitute, ground nutmeg, and salt. Combine well."],[null,"Fill each ramekin about half full of apples. Place one cheese wedge on top of apples and press to spread over the apples. Fill the ramekins with the remaining apples, mounding them over the rim of the ramekin."],[null,"Bake in oven for 30 minutes. Remove from oven and top each ramekin with 1 Tbsp. of slivered almonds. Return to the oven to finish baking."],[null,"Bake for 15 more minutes or until apples are bubbling and almonds are toasted. Remove from oven and let cool to just warmer than room temperature and serve. Can also be eaten cold or heated up in the microwave the next day."]],"h":[]},"6112598":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F."],[null,"Wash tomatoes and cut in half. Scoop out the pulp and seeds, leaving about a 1/2-inch rim of tomato."],[null,"Place cut-side up in a greased glass baking dish."],[null,"Sprinkle each tomato half with pepper and cumin. Break an egg into each tomato “shell.” Sprinkle each egg with 1/2 tsp of the cheese."],[null,"Bake until the eggs are set, roughly 25 minutes."]],"h":[]},"3920":{"s":[[null,"Dice celery and onion. Slice bell pepper and carrots. Peel and de-vein shrimp."],[null,"Place carrots in a microwave safe dish. Add 2 tablespoons water, cover and cook for 3 minutes. Drain."],[null,"Heat both oils in a large nonstick frying pan or wok. Add celery, onion, green bell pepper and drained water chestnuts. Stir-fry for 3 minutes. Add the cooked carrots and heat. Add shrimp and continue to stir and simmer until the shrimp just turns pink, about 2 minutes. Remove frying pan from heat."],[null,"In a small bowl mix together lemon juice, water, brown sugar, soy sauce, grated ginger root and cornstarch."],[null,"Stir mixture and add to the vegetables and shrimp. Bring to a boil, then reduce to medium heat. Cook until sauce is thickened."],[null,"Divide into 4 portions and serve each over 1/2 cup hot rice."]],"h":[[null,"Use a frozen oriental vegetable blend with similar composition to replace the fresh vegetables and frozen shrimp when you are in a hurry."]]},"6675756":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F. Season the chicken thighs with black pepper."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the pineapple juice, ketchup, soy sauce, rice vinegar, brown sugar, and cornstarch until well combined. Set aside."],[null,"In an oven-safe skillet or baking dish, heat the canola oil over medium-high heat. Add the chicken thighs and sear until golden brown, about 3–4 minutes per side."],[null,"Pour the prepared sweet and sour sauce over the chicken, ensuring each piece is well coated."],[null,"Scatter sliced red and green bell peppers, as well as pineapple chunks, around the chicken in the skillet."],[null,"Transfer the skillet to the preheated oven and bake for approximately 25 minutes or until the chicken reaches an internal temperature of 165 degrees F and the sauce is bubbly and thickened."],[null,"Remove from the oven and let it rest for a few minutes."],[null,"Garnish with the sliced green onions and toasted sesame seeds"]],"h":[]},"3490":{"s":[[null,"Drain pineapple, reserving the juice."],[null,"Cut chicken into bite size pieces and place in a saucepan."],[null,"Add reserved pineapple juice, broth, vinegar, brown sugar, soy sauce and garlic. Cover and simmer over low heat for 15 minutes."],[null,"Add vegetables and pineapple. Cook 10 minutes, stirring occasionally."],[null,"Combine cornstarch and water. Gradually stir into hot mixture. Continue to cook until thickened, stirring constantly."],[null,"Serve over white rice."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute Splenda® brown sugar blend if desired to reduce carbohydrate content. Add after mixture is thickened with cornstarch."],[null,"Substitute 1/4 teaspoon garlic powder for fresh garlic if desired."],[null,"Replace chicken with shrimp for more variety."]]},"4665844":{"s":[[null,"Place vinegar, sugar and oil in a small saucepan and bring to a boil. Stir well to ensure sugar is dissolved, remove from heat."],[null,"Let cool and whisk in celery seed. Pour over coleslaw, mix and refrigerate."]],"h":[["The power of vegetables","Eating a variety of vegetables is key to a healthy diet for all, but is especially important for those who have diabetes, kidney or heart concerns. Vegetables are rich in antioxidants and phytochemicals that can decrease inflammation and strengthen the immune system. They are also a good source of fiber that promotes a healthy gut which is especially helpful for those with kidney concerns. “Eat from the rainbow” to ensure that you eat a wide variety of vegetables. This expression reminds us to eat vegetables of all colors as each provides a different type of healthy nutrient. Find ways to add color to your diet. Consider the following: • Change up recipe ingredients—swap yellow peppers for green peppers, purple cabbage for green cabbage and red onions for white onions. • Add sliced radishes to soup or salad for added crunch. • Nibble on baby carrots, radishes, celery or pea pods for a snack. • Add chopped red onions, peppers and mushrooms to eggs. • Drizzle a mixture of carrots, onions, mushrooms, broccoli and colored peppers with olive oil, season with herbs and roast in the oven. • Top your sandwich with spinach, onions, cucumbers, peppers, and grated carrots. • Put a stir fry or grilled vegetable kebabs on the weekly menu. Vegetables are low in sodium and phosphorus but can contain a fair amount of potassium. If you have been advised to limit the amount of potassium in your diet, ask your registered dietitian which vegetables are the best for you."]]},"2357":{"s":[[null,"Slice cucumbers and onions about 1/8-inch thick. Place in a large bowl."],[null,"Combine sugar and vinegar. Mix until sugar is dissolved completely. Add additional sugar or vinegar to desired taste."],[null,"Pour over cucumbers and onion. Add salt and pepper."],[null,"Cover bowl with plastic wrap and set in refrigerator at least 2 hours."],[null,"Serve in small salad bowls as a salad or snack."]],"h":[]},"7267124":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200ºC/ gas 6. Mix together the mince, onion, apricots, parsley and breadcrumbs in a bowl. Add enough egg to bind, and roll the mixture into 6–8 balls. (Let the kids help make the meatballs.) Place on a baking sheet and cook for 10–12 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, cook the basmati rice according to its pack instructions, adding the sweetcorn, peas and pepper 5 minutes before the end of its cooking time."],[null,"To make the sauce, heat the oil in a small pan and add the onion and pepper. Fry for 3 minutes."],[null,"Add the tomatoes and wine vinegar. Simmer for 1 minute."],[null,"Remove the mixture from the pan and pour into a blender and blend until smooth."],[null,"Return the mixture to the pan and add the cooked meatballs."],[null,"Heat through for 1 minute. Serve the meatballs and sauce on the rice."]],"h":[[null,"Meatballs freeze well, so it’s a good idea to make a batch to freeze. You could also make extra sauce and freeze individual portions of meatballs and sauce in plastic cups."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Freeze the sauce and meatballs separately. Defrost in the fridge or microwave and thoroughly reheat until piping-hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"4426683":{"s":[[null,"In a bowl, combine pineapple juice, water, vinegar, sugar, and corn starch. Set aside."],[null,"Cook the rice according to instructions on the package."],[null,"In a non-stick frying pan, heat olive oil over medium-high heat. Add the shrimp, carrots, garlic, and ginger. Stir fry until the shrimp are cooked and turn pink in color."],[null,"Whisk the liquid from step 1 again and add it to the shrimp and vegetables. Stir constantly until the sauce thickens. Season with pepper."],[null,"Sprinkle with parsley and serve over white rice."]],"h":[["Shrimp in the kidney diet","Protein is an important part of your diet and is essential for many different functions in your body. In early stages of chronic kidney disease, you’ll likely be asked to limit the amount of protein you eat. As kidney disease progresses, you will need to increase the amount of protein. Meeting with a registered dietitian can help you determine the amount of animal and plant-based types of protein you should be eating. Shrimp, a low-fat protein source and the most popular type of seafood in the United States, can be part of your low-potassium diet. A 3-ounce portion of fresh shrimp provides 17 grams of protein, 224 milligrams of potassium, and 101 milligrams of sodium. Shrimp can be served as an appetizer, as part of a main entrée, in a soup, and even as a side dish. When eating shrimp as part of your kidney diet, consider the portion size and read Nutrition Facts labels to find out if there are any additives. Shrimp with seasonings or preservatives may contain added sodium and phosphate."]]},"5122504":{"s":[[null,"Pour cornflour into a bowl and mix in the paprika, add tofu to the bowl and toss until evenly covered."],[null,"Heat half the sesame oil in a frying pan and add the tofu, cook until golden brown and crispy then remove from pan and place onto kitchen paper."],[null,"Heat the remaining oil into the pan and add in the onions and red pepper. Cook until soft."],[null,"Add in the garlic, ginger, pineapple chunks, soy sauce, honey, rice vinegar, tomato puree and cook until fragrant."],[null,"Add in water (you don’t have to use all of it) and mix until a sauce forms, add the tofu back into the mixture and coat with sauce."],[null,"Remove from heat and sprinkle with coriander, serve with rice."]],"h":[]},"2740":{"s":[[null,"Place sliced onion in slow cooker."],[null,"In large deep skillet, heat oil and brown beef on all sides."],[null,"Remove beef from skillet and place in slow cooker."],[null,"Add apple juice and spices to pan. Loosen browned bits from bottom of pan with spatula. Allow juice to simmer until reduced by approximately half."],[null,"Pour juice over beef in the slow cooker. Set slow cooker on low and cook for approximately 7 hours."],[null,"Remove beef from slow cooker to a deep platter or serving bowl. Shred using two forks."],[null,"Pour juice into a medium saucepan. Bring to simmer."],[null,"Wisk cornstarch into two tablespoons of water. Add to juice and cook until slightly thickened. If you would like a thicker sauce, simmer and reduce juice prior to adding cornstarch."],[null,"Pour sauce over meat and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Number of servings may vary depending on yield of meat."],[null,"This beef is delicious served in flour tortillas (think carne asada burrito) or on crusty rolls."],[null,"Serve with coleslaw or cucumber and onion salad."],[null,"Divide extra into portions and freeze for a quick meal later."],[null,"For a lower protein diet reduce portion size to match your meal plan"]]},"6586871":{"s":[[null,"To make, combine 1/2 cup reduced sugar apricot preserves with 1 Tsp. Thai style chili garlic sauce (or other hot sauce) and 1 Tsp. reduced sodium soy sauce in a bowl and"],[null,"Heat in the microwave for 30 seconds."]],"h":[]},"2362":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 425° F."],[null,"Spray a baking sheet with cooking spray."],[null,"Melt butter and mix with brown sugar and spices in a small bowl."],[null,"Cut each tortilla into 8 wedges. Arrange wedges in a single layer on the baking sheet."],[null,"With a pastry brush, coat tortillas with seasoning mixture."],[null,"Bake for about 8 minutes until golden brown. Serve warm or cool."],[null,"Store extra chips in an airtight container."]],"h":[[null,"Use kitchen shears to easily cut tortillas into wedges."],[null,"Corn tortilla may be substituted for flour tortilla for a lower sodium snack (48 mg). Be aware the phosphorus is higher (63 mg)."]]},"1904":{"s":[[null,"Heat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Lightly coat a 13” x 9” x 2” baking dish with nonstick cooking spray."],[null,"Whisk together low sugar apricot preserves, Dijon mustard, Worcestershire sauce and garlic powder in a small bowl."],[null,"Mix cornflakes, thyme and pepper in a large plastic bag (such as a bread bag or zipped-locked style bag)."],[null,"Brush chicken breasts with apricot mixture, then coat in crumb mixture."],[null,"Place chicken in prepared baking dish."],[null,"Bake for 35 minutes or until internal temperature registers 170° F on instant-read thermometer."],[null,"Serve immediately, or chill and take to a picnic."]],"h":[[null,"CKD non-dialysis: This higher protein recipe may be appropriate for your diet if the portion size were adjusted to reduce protein content. Adjustments should be based on your individual protein prescription. Check with your dietitian if you are unsure."]]},"2594":{"s":[[null,"Soften cream cheese. In a large bowl, mix cream cheese, sugar and vanilla with a mixer."],[null,"For the whipped cream, place bowl and beaters of a hand-mixer in freezer for 10-15 minutes. Remove bowl from freezer, put heavy cream in the bowl and beat until soft peaks form."],[null,"Fold whipped cream into cream cheese mixture."],[null,"Pour mixture into graham cracker pie crust."],[null,"Top with cherry pie filling."],[null,"Refrigerate until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute Splenda® No Calorie Sweetener and low-sugar pie filling to reduce calories to 299 and carbohydrate to 29 grams. Count as 2 carbohydrate choices."],[null,"For variation, use apple- or peach-pie filling instead of cherry."]]},"6905433":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F. Line a large baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Toss the sweet potatoes with 1 tablespoon of olive oil and salt. Add to the baking sheet in a single layer. Place in the oven and bake for 10 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, preheat a large skillet over medium-high heat."],[null,"Once the skillet is hot, add 1 tablespoon of oil and chicken. Sear until golden brown on both sides (but not cooked through). Remove from heat."],[null,"Once the sweet potatoes have been baking for 10 minutes, remove the baking sheet and add the chicken and broccoli. Drizzle the broccoli with the remaining 1 teaspoon of olive oil."],[null,"Place the baking sheet in the oven and continue to cook until the chicken is cooked through and the veggies tender."],[null,"Remove from oven and divide between plates. Drizzle with sweet chili sauce and serve."]],"h":[]},"4897121":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400°F. Bake frozen pie shell for approximately 15 minutes or until lightly browned."],[null,"Remove the pie shell from the oven and reduce oven temperature to 350°F."],[null,"Heat the olive oil in a skillet over medium-high heat. Sauté onion, corn, and zucchini until cooked. Remove from heat."],[null,"In a mixing bowl, whisk together eggs and milk."],[null,"Spread the cooked vegetable evenly in the cooked pie shell. Sprinkle with goat cheese and basil."],[null,"Pour the egg and milk mixture on top."],[null,"Place quiche on a baking sheet and bake for approximately 35–40 minutes or until the quiche is firm to the touch (internal temperature of 160°F). Serve warm."]],"h":[[null,"* A chopping technique in which herbs or leafy green vegetables (such as spinach and basil) are cut into long, thin strips."],["What type of squash to choose","Vegetables are part of a healthy diet for all. However, for those with chronic kidney disease, certain vegetables can contain too much potassium to be enjoyed on a daily basis. When it comes to squash, the potassium content can vary tremendously. Squash with the deepest colored flesh such as acorn, butternut and hubbard are very high in potassium and should be used in very limited quantities. In general, squash with lighter colored flesh such as crookneck or straightneck, scallop and spaghetti are lower in potassium and can be part of a potassium-controlled diet. Zucchini however is an exception to this rule as it is actually higher in potassium. Ask your dietitian how much squash in right for you. Crookneck or straightneck, scallop and zucchini squashes are harvested in the summer and are best when picked while small and tender. They can be grilled, steamed, boiled, sautéed, fried or used in stir-fry recipes. Spaghetti squash is harvested in the late summer or early autumn. It can be baked, boiled, steamed and microwaved. You can even use it as a substitute for pasta."]]},"2784":{"s":[[null,"Wash turkey breast and prepare for roasting."],[null,"Place in a roasting pan, breast side up; cover and bake at 350° F for 1-1/2 hours (170° internal temperature using a meat thermometer)."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine remaining ingredients and stir to blend."],[null,"Remove turkey breast from oven and brush glaze over top."],[null,"Return turkey to oven and cook uncovered for 30 minutes."],[null,"Remove from oven. Let turkey rest 15 minutes before slicing."]],"h":[[null,"Extra glaze can be served on the side as a dipping sauce."],[null,"Glaze can also be used on chicken."],[null,"CKD non-dialysis: This higher protein recipe may be appropriate for your diet if the portion size is adjusted to reduce protein content. Adjustments should be based on your individual protein prescription. Check with your dietitian if you are unsure."]]},"6710152":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a skillet over medium-high heat. Add the onion, sugar, and garlic and sauté for 5 minutes."],[null,"Add the mixture to a blender or food processor. Add the remaining ingredients and puree until smooth, but thick."]],"h":[]},"7432936":{"s":[[null,"Add 1 tsp oil to a pan over a medium heat, add the peppers and onion and cook for 10 minutes, stirring regularly."],[null,"Meanwhile, mix together the egg, water, yogurt and cheese. Stir in the flour to make a batter."],[null,"Stir the peppers and onion into the batter."],[null,"Add the remaining oil to a large non-stick pan. Add scant dessertspoons of the mixture to the pan to fry for 1-2 minutes, flipping once with a spatula to cook the other side for a further minute."],[null,"Meanwhile, make the sauce by blending together the parsley, lime juice, zest and fresh tomato together then mix in the chilli."]],"h":[[null,"When cooking the pancakes, make sure you distribute the peppers and onion evenly throughout the mixture. You can make them up to 1 day in advance and warm in the oven for a few minutes to serve."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"6825413":{"s":[[null,"Combine all ingredients except pepper, onion and tomato and mix well."],[null,"Pour dressing over vegetables and stir. Cover and refrigerate for several hours or overnight, stirring occasionally."]],"h":[]},"3743":{"s":[[null,"Pop popcorn and put in a large bowl. Set aside for use later."],[null,"Mix syrup, brown sugar, water and vinegar in a saucepan. Cook over medium heat, stirring constantly until mixture boils. Continue cooking and stirring almost constantly about 15-20 minutes on medium heat. Cook to hard ball stage (until a small amount of mixture forms a hard ball when tested in very cold water.)"],[null,"Remove from heat, quickly add butter, and stir."],[null,"Slowly pour mixture over popped popcorn in a large bowl, while mixing well. Form into balls, using as little pressure as possible."],[null,"Wrap each popcorn ball in plastic wrap and store in an airtight container."]],"h":[[null,"Butter hands, or better yet, wear rubber gloves with butter on them. The popcorn won’t stick as bad and is not as hot!"]]},"6738149":{"s":[[null,"Preheat a large pot over medium heat."],[null,"Add olive oil, onion, garlic, and ginger to the pot. Cook, stirring occasionally, until onion softens, 4–5 minutes."],[null,"Add black beans, sweet potatoes, broth, coconut milk, tomatoes, and chili powder. Bring to a simmer and cook, covered, for 15–20 minutes, until the potatoes are tender."],[null,"Stir in the baby spinach until wilted."]],"h":[]},"6020482":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F."],[null,"In a large mixing bowl, toss the diced sweet potatoes with 1 tablespoon olive oil, ground cumin, chili powder, smoked paprika, and minced garlic until evenly coated."],[null,"Spread the seasoned sweet potatoes on a baking sheet in a single layer. Roast until the potatoes are tender and slightly crispy, about 20–25 minutes. Stir halfway through the roasting time."],[null,"While the sweet potatoes are roasting, heat a skillet over medium heat. Add 1 tablespoon olive oil, then sauté the chopped red onion until translucent."],[null,"Add the black beans to the skillet, stirring to combine with the onions. Cook for an additional 3–5 minutes until the beans are heated through. Season with coarse salt and pepper."],[null,"Warm the corn tortillas in a dry skillet or microwave."],[null,"Assemble the tacos by spooning the roasted sweet potatoes and black bean mixture onto each tortilla."],[null,"Top each taco with yogurt, cheese, and cilantro."]],"h":[]},"7571970":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 200°C/fan 180°C/gas 6."],[null,"Spray a large non-stick saucepan with a couple of pumps of low-calorie cooking spray and put it over a medium heat. Add the onion, celery, leeks, garlic, thyme, chilli flakes and sweet potatoes. Fry for 6-8 minutes, until softened. Add the stock, bring to boil and simmer for 10-15 minutes, until all the vegetables are really tender."],[null,"Add half the sweetcorn, bring back to a simmer, then blitz with a stick blender until completely smooth. Add the lemon juice and season with pepper"],[null,"Divide the chowder between 4 bowls. Drizzle over the yoghurt, scatter with the remaining sweetcorn and sprinkle over the paprika and chives. Serve steaming hot."]],"h":[[null,"You can use a plain yoghurt of your choice. However, this will change the nutritional information and the texture of the dish."],[null,"Nutritional information includes serving suggestion."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"6325741":{"s":[[null,"In a medium pot over medium heat, add the sweet potatoes, water, ginger juice, and salt. Cook until sweet potatoes are tender."],[null,"Working in batches, transfer potatoes and cooking water to a blender or food processor and process to a smooth consistency."]],"h":[]},"6604257":{"s":[[null,"In a large nonstick pan, heat the oil over medium heat. Add the garlic and sauté for 30 seconds. Add the spinach and sauté for 3 to 4 minutes."],[null,"Add the sweet potato, cumin, black pepper, and water to the pan. Sauté for 2 minutes. Cover, reduce the heat to low, and cook for 8 minutes."],[null,"Add the chicken to the pan and mix to incorporate. Heat for 2 minutes."],[null,"Fill each tortilla with 1/4 of the chicken and sweet potato mixture. Top with 1 Tsp. of sour cream and 2 Tbsp. of pico de gallo."]],"h":[]},"7559129":{"s":[[null,"Pour the stock into a large saucepan and add the sweet potatoes and onion. Bring to the boil, then reduce the heat, cover and simmer gently for 4-5 minutes."],[null,"Add the spinach, garlic, red chilli, curry powder and passata to the pan. Stir well and cook over a medium heat for 10 minutes or until the sweet potatoes are tender. Season chilli slices scattered over"]],"h":[[null,"This recipe would work well with butternut squash or pumpkin instead of the sweet potato, if you prefer."],[null,"Check spice/seasoning blends for added ingredients such as sugar, salt, flour or oil. Choose blends made from herbs and spices only if possible."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"6487257":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F. Place the sweet potato on a baking sheet and bake for 40 minutes, or until soft when poked with a fork. Remove the sweet potato from the oven and set it aside to cool."],[null,"Meanwhile, in a large bowl, whisk the egg, egg whites, and cottage cheese until smooth. Fold in the Parmesan cheese, pepper, nutmeg, and spinach."],[null,"Remove the skin from the sweet potato and mash well. Fold in the mashed sweet potato and the flour to the egg-cheese mixture. The mixture will be wet and sticky. Let it rest for 10 minutes."],[null,"While the dough rests, coat a large sauté pan or Dutch oven with cooking spray and heat it over medium-high heat. Add the turkey and sauté until barely cooked through, about 8 minutes."],[null,"Pour the marinara sauce and broth over the turkey and stir to incorporate. Reduce the heat to low."],[null,"Scoop 2-inch balls of the dumpling batter and gently drop them into the sauce to make 24 dumplings. Cover and simmer for 20 minutes."]],"h":[]},"2082":{"s":[[null,"Peel and cube sweet potato. Double boil potatoes if you are on a low potassium diet. (See helpful hints)"],[null,"Once potatoes are drained, toss with paprika and garlic powder. Dice onion and seed and dice jalapeno. Mince the clove of garlic."],[null,"In a large saucepan heat olive oil over medium heat for one minute. Add the onion and cook until translucent, about 5 minutes."],[null,"Add jalapeno, garlic, chili powder, cumin to onion. Stir and cook for 2 minutes."],[null,"Add corn and beans, cook for 8 minutes."],[null,"Scoop sweet potato mix into flour tortilla and top with 1/3 cup of shredded lettuce. Fold in the sides of the tortilla and roll up to form the burrito."]],"h":[[null,"Double boil method: Peel and small dice potatoes. Place in a large pot of water and bring to a boil. Drain the water and add fresh water to the pot. Bring to a boil, cook for 10 minutes then drain and prepare as desired."],[null,"To cut back on carbohydrates, you may eat in a bowl or on top of salad greens, without the tortilla."],[null,"Potassium from whole foods such as beans and sweet potatoes are not 100% absorbed by the body. Whole foods can be part of a healthy kidney friend diet and contribute other nutrients and vitamins."],[null,"This recipe can be doubled and the second half can be frozen in an airtight container in the freezer for 3 months. Take out and reheat on stove or microwave before putting in tortilla."]]},"7313231":{"s":[[null,"Prepare the potatoes and allow to cool."],[null,"Add the flour, egg, pepper and dill to the mashed potato and mix well."],[null,"Stir in the spring onion and crab, combine together then form into small patties approx. 1 cm deep, then dust with flour."],[null,"Add 1 tsp oil to a non-stick pan, fry for 1-2 minutes turning carefully a couple of times to ensure even cooking (about 6 minutes altogether) until lightly golden and firm, making sure the patties are cooked through."],[null,"Meanwhile, for the salsa, blend the tomatoes with the tomato puree and stir in the green chilli."]],"h":[[null,"For flavour, the mixture of white and dark crab is ideal. Try making with salmon and/ or chopped prawns."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"4699538":{"s":[[null,"Bring a large pot of water to a boil. Add the cut sweet potatoes and cook them for 5 minutes. Drain the water."],[null,"Bring fresh water to a boil and cook the potatoes for 5 minutes for a second time. Drain the water and place the fries on a clean, lint-free kitchen towel to dry."],[null,"Line a baking tray with parchment paper. Mix the fries with canola oil and season with paprika and black pepper. Distribute the fries on the tray so that there is space between them."],[null,"Set the oven to broil and broil the potatoes for 1–2 minutes with tray on the upper rack. Turn fries and broil for another 1–2 minutes until the potatoes are golden brown."],[null,"Garnish with parsley and orange zest. Serve fresh from the oven."]],"h":[[null,"Replace the parsley with chopped coriander to add another flavor."],[null,"PLEASE NOTE: This recipe is higher in potassium and portion size is important. Check with your registered dietitian to see how this recipe can be included in your diet."],["Sweet potatoes and the kidney diet","Those with chronic kidney disease often need to be mindful of their potassium intake and are advised to eat lower-potassium foods or monitor the portion size of higher-potassium foods in their diet. Fruits, vegetables, and dairy products tend to be higher in potassium. Within each of these food groups, however, you can still find lower-potassium items to enjoy. Ask your registered dietitian for a list of these foods and advice about the amount right for you. Most foods in the starchy vegetable group are considered to be very high in potassium. The highest potassium foods in this group are sweet potatoes, yams, potatoes, pumpkin and squash. When following a lower-potassium diet, you likely will not be able to safely eat these foods on a regular basis; however, there is a way to remove some of the potassium from a few of these foods so you don’t have to give them up completely. Lower the potassium content in these foods by peeling, boiling, and draining them before use. For example, a sweet potato that has been peeled and then boiled has 32% less potassium than a raw sweet potato. Even though the potassium content is less per serving, the portion size is still important. Ask your registered dietitian how much sweet potato prepared this way is right for you."]]},"6018812":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425°F. Line a sheet tray with parchment paper or a silicone mat."],[null,"Rinse the sweet potatoes under cold running water until the water runs clear. Drain on paper towels and pat dry. Do your best to thoroughly dry all of the sweet potatoes then transfer to a large mixing bowl."],[null,"In a separate small bowl, whisk together the cornstarch, garlic powder, smoked paprika, black pepper, and salt. Drizzle the olive oil over the potatoes and toss to combine. Sprinkle the cornstarch mixture over the potatoes and toss until evenly coated. Transfer to the sheet tray and arrange the potatoes into a single layer, spacing them out as best as possible. If needed, use a second tray (this will give you crispier fries)."],[null,"Bake for 12 minutes. Use a spatula to flip the potatoes"],[null,"Taste and adjust seasoning as needed. Serve hot."]],"h":[]},"6554653":{"s":[[null,"In a large skillet, heat the olive oil over medium heat."],[null,"Add the diced sweet potatoes to the skillet, spreading them out in a single layer."],[null,"Sauté the sweet potatoes for 15–20 minutes, stirring occasionally, until they are tender on the inside and crispy on the outside."],[null,"Sprinkle the smoked paprika, garlic powder, onion powder, salt, and black pepper over the sweet potatoes. Toss to coat evenly."],[null,"Cook for an additional 5 minutes, allowing the spices to meld with the sweet potatoes."],[null,"Remove the skillet from the heat."],[null,"Garnish with chopped fresh parsley if desired."]],"h":[]},"6144347":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium heat."],[null,"Add sweet potatoes, onion, chili powder, cumin, garlic powder, and pepper to the skillet. Cook, stirring occasionally, until sweet potatoes are fork tender, 10–15 minutes."],[null,"Add kale to the skillet and stir until wilted, 3–4 minutes."],[null,"Remove from heat and fold in the cherry tomatoes. Divide between serving plates and garnish with cheese."]],"h":[]},"7370336":{"s":[[null,"Grate the sweet potato. Add to a bowl with the onion, egg and pepper, and mix well."],[null,"Add the flour, mix thoroughly and set aside for 5 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the chopped apples and water to a pan with a lid, and cook over a medium to low heat, stirring occasionally and mashing with the back of a spoon. Cook for 12–15 minutes until the apples are soft, then set aside."],[null,"Heat a non-stick frying pan over a medium heat, add a teaspoon of the oil and spread to coat the base of the pan. When the pan is hot, add a spoonful of the sweet potato mixture and flatten it out into a pancake shape. Cook for 3 minutes, then carefully flip with a spatula and cook on the other side for 2-3 minutes."],[null,"Serve with the apple sauce."]],"h":[[null,"For a lower-sugar accompaniment, these latkes would also taste great served with 0% fat Greek yogurt."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"6081227":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F."],[null,"Add the sweet potatoes to a bowl. In a separate small bowl, mix together the garam masala, cayenne pepper, salt, and black pepper. Sprinkle the spice mixture over the sweet potatoes."],[null,"Add the olive oil to the bowl and toss to coat. Line a baking sheet with parchment paper. Spread the sweet potatoes in a single layer on the baking sheet. Roast the sweet potatoes for 35 minutes, until golden brown."]],"h":[]},"3245":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 425° F. Set eggs out to bring to room temperature. Set butter out to soften."],[null,"In a medium pan peel and cube 2 medium sweet potatoes. Add water to cover and bring to a boil. Drain, add fresh water and return to a boil. Reduce heat; cook uncovered until tender 20 to 25 minutes."],[null,"Drain potatoes, return to pan and mash until smooth. Cool to room temperature."],[null,"In a large bowl, cream butter and sugar. Add eggs and mix well."],[null,"Add milk, 2 cups mashed sweet potatoes, vanilla, cinnamon, and nutmeg, mix well."],[null,"Pour into an unbaked deep-dish pie shell. Add pie shield or cover top of crust with aluminum foil to prevent crust from over browning. Remove shield the last 5 minutes of baking."],[null,"Bake at 425° F for 15 minutes. Reduce heat to 350° F and bake 35 to 40 minutes or until set or a knife inserted in the center comes out clean."],[null,"Cool, cover and store in refrigerator until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Double-boiling removes about half the potassium from sweet potatoes. If potassium is not restricted you can boil only once until potato pieces are tender."],[null,"Substitute a granular sugar substitute for sugar to reduce carbs to 26 grams per slice."]]},"7644993":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180ºC/gas 4. Place the sweet potatoes in a large pan, cover with water and cook for 20–25 minutes, until tender. Drain and mash well, cool a little then stir through the butter, sugar and lime zest and juice."],[null,"In a separate dish, beat together the remaining ingredients, and stir into the sweet potato mixture."],[null,"Grease and line a 900g (18cm x 8cm deep) loaf tin. Turn mixture into the tin and bake for approx 1½–1¾ hours until firm."],[null,"Check the firmness by inserting a skewer – it should come out clean when the dish is cooked."]],"h":[[null,"You could also put the mixture into individual ramekins/dishes and bake for around 45 mins."],[null,"Keeps in the fridge for up to 5 days. Warm up a slice and serve with reduced-fat crème fraiche or yogurt."]]},"6527440":{"s":[[null,"Peel sweet potatoes and cube. Place sweet potatoes in a large pot. Cover with water and bring to a boil. Boil until tender about 5-7 minutes. Drain potatoes and rinse with cold water; let cool."],[null,"While potatoes are cooking, cook turkey bacon until crisp, then chop or crumble into small pieces."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together, olive oil, apple cider vinegar, pepper and garlic powder."],[null,"Place sweet potatoes in serving bowl and add celery, green onions and turkey bacon. Pour dressing over salad and toss until potatoes are coated. Serve cold."]],"h":[]},"6538918":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F."],[null,"In a large bowl, toss the diced sweet potatoes with olive oil, cumin, smoked paprika, salt, and black pepper until evenly coated."],[null,"Spread the seasoned sweet potatoes in a single layer on a baking sheet."],[null,"Roast in the preheated oven for 30 minutes or until the sweet potatoes are tender and slightly caramelized, stirring halfway through."],[null,"While the sweet potatoes are roasting, prepare the dressing. Zest and juice the lime. In a small bowl, combine chopped fresh cilantro, lime zest, and lime juice."],[null,"Once the sweet potatoes are done, transfer them to a serving bowl."],[null,"Pour the cilantro and lime dressing over the roasted sweet potatoes."],[null,"Add finely chopped red onion, avocado, and black beans to the bowl."],[null,"Toss the salad gently to ensure even coating."]],"h":[]},"6028474":{"s":[[null,"Place sweet potatoes in steam basket in a medium pot with 2 cups water. Bring to a boil, reduce heat, and simmer. Cover and steam until tender, about 15 minutes."],[null,"While potatoes are cooking, spray a large sauté pan with cooking spray. Add onions and sauté over medium-high heat for 3 minutes or until onions look clear. Add garlic and sauté for 30 seconds. Remove from pan and set aside."],[null,"Add turkey and cook until brown, about 6-7 minutes. Add onions back to pan and stir to mix."],[null,"Add diced tomatoes, mixed vegetables, yellow mustard, Worcestershire, and black pepper. Bring to a simmer."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix together corn starch and water. Add to turkey mixture and stir. Let simmer for 5 more minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, drain the sweet potatoes. Place sweet potatoes in a medium bowl and mash with a potato masher. Add margarine and whisk until smooth."],[null,"Preheat broiler. Pour cooked turkey mixture evenly into a medium-sized casserole dish or individual casserole dishes. Spread sweet potatoes evenly on top of turkey mixture."],[null,"Broil for 5 minutes."]],"h":[]},"6168694":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400 degrees Fahrenheit. Coat a deep 8-inch round or square casserole dish with cooking spray. Set aside."],[null,"Coat a baking sheet with cooking spray. Arrange the washed and dried, whole sweet potatoes (with the skins on) on the sheet and coat generously with cooking spray. Bake for 50-60 minutes or until tender (check if they are tender by spearing the largest one with a paring knife or fork)."],[null,"Remove sweet potatoes from the oven and peel the skin. In a large bowl, whisk (or blend with a mixer) the roasted sweet potatoes with 1/4 cup Splenda Brown Sugar Blend, orange juice and salt (optional). Set aside to cool."],[null,"Using a food processor or chopper, grind the walnuts, flax seed and 2 Tbsps. brown sugar substitute together until it is the consistency of wet sand. Add the Smart Balance Buttery Spread to the mixture in the food processor and pulse to incorporate (do not overmix this or it will turn into a paste). Set aside."],[null,"Combine egg whites and cream of tartar in a large glass or metal bowl, and beat with an electric mixer on medium speed or with stand mixer using the whisk attachment until egg whites form soft peaks with tips that curl over when the beaters are lifted."],[null,"Working in batches, incorporate one third of the egg whites into the sweet potato mixture using a large flat rubber spatula and gently folding them in until combined. Repeat that process two more times until all of the egg whites are incorporated into the sweet potatoes."],[null,"Pour sweet potato soufflé mixture into the prepared casserole dish and top with the walnut mixture."],[null,"Place the soufflé into the oven and bake at 400 degrees Fahrenheit for 20 minutes, then turn the oven down to 350 degrees Fahrenheit and continue to bake for 15 more minutes. Serve hot. (Note: the soufflé may deflate a little bit after baking so it’s best served immediately but is still okay to hold in a warming oven for service)."]],"h":[]},"7792690":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a medium pan, add the onion and the garlic and fry for 3-4 minutes, until softened."],[null,"Add the carrot and the sweet potato and continue to fry for 2-3 minutes."],[null,"Pour over the stock, bring to the boil and simmer for 12-15 minutes until the vegetables are tender."],[null,"Transfer to a blender or food processor and blend until smooth."],[null,"Return to the pan, stir through the parsley, season well and serve with crusty bread."]],"h":[[null,"Spice this up with 1 tsp curry paste or a pinch of chilli flakes."],[null,"Try adding chopped coriander in place of the parsley."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Freeze in portions then defrost in the fridge; or defrost in a microwave stirring regularly."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"9328013":{"s":[[null,"Peel and spiralize your sweet potatoes into spaghetti. Set aside."],[null,"Use a large skillet and add the aquafaba (or broth), along with the garlic, parsley, pepper flakes and salt. Sauté over medium heat for 2-3 minutes, watching carefully to prevent burning."],[null,"Add the sweet potato spaghetti to the pan and mix to evenly coat with the spices and cook over medium-high heat for 5-7 minutes, until slightly softened, but do not overcook. Add a few splashes of water or broth as needed, to prevent the noodles from sticking to the pan."],[null,"Turn off the heat and add the spinach. Stir until wilted and then serve."]],"h":[[null,"For ease of spiralizing , use sweet potatoes that are narrow, long, and straight. Or you may purchase pre-spiralized sweet potato noodles from your grocery store to save time. If using canned aquafaba with salt , you may want to reduce the salt in the recipe, and then taste and add more, if needed. Do NOT overcook the noodles . You want the noodles tender but crisp, and not overly soft, for the best texture and to mimic ‘al dente’ pasta. If you don’t have spinach , you may sub for another green veggie. Precook your greens if necessary. For less spice , reduce the red pepper flakes by half. This dish is traditionally spicy, but be sure to spice to your taste and tolerance. Leftovers keep refrigerated in a sealed container for 3-4 days."]]},"7325527":{"s":[[null,"For the tagine: Heat the olive oil in a large casserole dish or tagine set over a moderate heat until hot."],[null,"Add the onion and garlic, sweating for about 5 minutes until softened and then add the ground spices."],[null,"Cook for a further 2 minutes before stirring in the sweet potatoes, carrots, water, and chopped tomatoes."],[null,"Bring to the boil and then reduce to a gentle, steady simmer until the vegetables are very soft and the sauce has thickened, about 25-30 minutes. Stir from time to time."],[null,"Stir in the ground almonds and chickpeas and season to taste with some freshly ground black pepper. Cover and keep warm off the heat."],[null,"To serve: Bring 375 ml water to the boil in a saucepan. Once boiling, remove from the heat and stir in the couscous."],[null,"Cover tightly with a lid and let stand. After 10 minutes, fluff the couscous to separate the grains."],[null,"Divide between plates and top with the tagine. Sprinkle on the chopped parsley."]],"h":[[null,"Butternut squash or pumpkin would make a good lower-carb substitute for the sweet potato in this dish."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"1906":{"s":[[null,"In a small saucepan, heat ingredients over low heat for 5 minutes. Stir frequently."],[null,"Serve hot sauce over meat or poultry."]],"h":[[null,"Add Tabasco® sauce for a spicy version."],[null,"Substitute apricot jam for peach jam."]]},"7238981":{"s":[[null,"Bring a pan of water to the boil, cut the potatoes, swede and parsnips into 2cm chunks and simmer for 15–20mins until tender."],[null,"Meanwhile, lightly spray a frying pan with the 1 cal spray and put on a high heat. Add the chicken, peppers and onion and stir fry for 5 mins."],[null,"Stir together the remaining ingredients except the sugar snap peas and milk. Add to the frying pan, bring to the boil and simmer for 10 mins."],[null,"Add the sugar snap peas. Cook for a further 5 mins."],[null,"Drain the potatoes. Mash until smooth, stir in the milk, divide between plates and serve with the chicken."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"3859":{"s":[[null,"Combine the ground turkey, egg, bread crumbs, finely chopped onion, garlic powder and pepper until well blended."],[null,"Shape turkey mixture into 3/4-inch meatballs to make approximately 48 balls."],[null,"In a large skillet, heat the oil and cook meatballs over medium heat. Turn several times to brown evenly. Continue cooking until meatballs are cooked all the way through."],[null,"Combine the jelly and chili sauce in a microwave safe bowl and heat in the microwave for 1 to 2 minutes, until jelly is liquefied. Stir well and pour over the meatballs in a chafing dish or slow cooker set on low heat."]],"h":[[null,"This recipe works best with ground turkey containing 7% fat. Meatballs made with ground turkey breast meat are not as moist."],[null,"Ground beef may be substituted for ground turkey."]]},"7585778":{"s":[[null,"Beat the eggs in a large mixing bowl. Stir through the sweetcorn, half the spring onions and the green pepper, then season with pepper."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix together the red pepper, tomatoes, chilli (if using) and remaining spring onions. Combine the tomato purée and lime juice, then stir it into the salsa and season to taste."],[null,"Preheat your grill to high. Spray a large non-stick frying pan with a couple of pumps of low-calorie cooking spray and put it over a medium-low heat. Pour in the egg mixture and cook for 5-6 minutes or until the top starts to set. Finish under the grill, until the egg is cooked through."],[null,"Remove the fritter from the pan, leave to cool, then slice it into 8 wedges and serve with the rocket. Or you can pack the wedges and the salsa into airtight containers and chill for up to 2 days. For a take-to-work lunch, put a handful of rocket in a lunch box, top with 2 fritter wedges and a dollop of salsa, then seal and chill until ready to eat."]],"h":[]},"7473723":{"s":[[null,"Add the pepper to a cup with the lemon juice and set aside."],[null,"Heat the oil in a wok or frying pan and add the chicken, stir constantly, for 3-4 minutes lightly browning the outside."],[null,"Add the chili, ginger and garlic and mix well for 2 minutes"],[null,"Add the spring onion, five-spice powder, sesame seeds and tomato puree. Mix well and cook for a further 2 minutes. Add 1-2tbsp water, remove from the heat and mix so the chicken gets coated."],[null,"Place in a serving dish and sprinkle with the pepper and lemon juice mixture."]],"h":[[null,"Works well with strips of turkey or beef or use prawns or chunks of salmon."],[null,"For a vegan version, use tofu in place of chicken."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat thoroughly until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"7857625":{"s":[[null,"Place the bulgur wheat in a bowl and cover with boiling water. Leave to soak for 15-20 minutes or until the grains are tender, drain off any remaining liquid."],[null,"Mix together all the remaining ingredients and toss through the bulgur wheat, season and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Use quinoa for a gluten-free alternative."],[null,"You can add lots of different things to tabbouleh. Try finely chopped sweet peppers, red onion, carrot, fennel or celery. Use chives or coriander and roasted vegetables such as butternut squash, courgettes and aubergines. Or add raisins nuts, seeds or pomegranate."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge or microwave to serve or heat in the microwave."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"3600":{"s":[[null,"Wash bulgur. Drain and place in a large bowl. Pour 1/2 cup boiling water over bulgur, cover bowl and let sit for 30 minutes. Drain excess liquid (if any)."],[null,"Dice tomato; chop peeled cucumber, green onions, parsley and mint."],[null,"Add vegetables to bulgur and mix well."],[null,"Juice the 3 lemons. Add olive oil, lemon juice, salt and pepper to bulgur mixture."],[null,"Let salad set at room temperature for about an hour to absorb the lemon juice and olive oil before serving. Refrigerate leftovers and serve during the week."]],"h":[[null,"Eat Tabbouleh Salad with lettuce leaves, tender grape leaves, or with a fork."],[null,"Bulgur is wheat berries that have been cracked (also known as cracked wheat). It is available in grinds from fine to extra course. Use fine or medium grind bulgur for this recipe."],[null,"One bunch of parsley, green onions or mint yields approximately 1 cup chopped."]]},"3820":{"s":[[null,"Cook the pasta according to package directions, omitting salt. Drain and rinse until cooled."],[null,"Mince garlic; slice green onions; chop bell pepper; shred lettuce."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine sour cream and salsa. Mix into the pasta."],[null,"Add hot taco sauce, garlic, chilies and olives to pasta and stir."],[null,"Sprinkle green onions and bell pepper over top of pasta mixture. Cover and refrigerate to chill."],[null,"Before serving, sprinkle cheese on top of pasta salad (optional). For each serving, place 1-cup shredded lettuce on a salad plate. Top lettuce bed with 1-cup Taco Pasta Salad."]],"h":[[null,"Look for canned or bottled hot taco sauce."],[null,"Compare labels and choose the brands of salsa, green chilies, olives and taco sauce lowest in sodium."],[null,"Look for queso anejo, a Mexican cheese that easily crumbles. If unavailable, buy the shredded cheese labeled \"Mexican.\" Cheese and olives are optional."],[null,"Make a wrap with flat bread or flour tortilla and Taco Pasta Salad with lettuce inside."]]},"6683608":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375°F. Coat a 9x13-inch sheet pan with cooking spray. Layer the tortilla chips in the bottom of the pan and set aside."],[null,"Add the oil to a sauté pan and heat over medium heat. Add the onions and garlic and sauté for 5 minutes, until the onions start to turn clear."],[null,"Add the onions and garlic, black beans, pepper, and chicken broth to a blender or food processor and purée until smooth. Pour the bean mixture over the chips."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix peppers, cilantro, lime juice, red onion, and 1 cup of the tomatoes. Add the chicken breast and spoon the mixture evenly over the top of the bean mixture."],[null,"Top with the cheese and bake for 20 minutes. Remove the pan from the oven and top the nachos with shredded lettuce and the remaining diced tomato."],[null,"Divide the nachos among 6 serving plates and top each with 4 teaspoons of yogurt."]],"h":[]},"7772137":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 190°C/gas 5. In a large bowl, stir together 150ml of the yogurt and paste. Cut each chicken breast into four pieces and add to the sauce with the cauliflower. Toss to combine."],[null,"Oil a baking sheet and spread out the cauliflower. Cook in the oven for 10 mins. Add the chicken and cook for a further 15 mins until tender and browning."],[null,"For the herby raita, grate the cucumber, then cup in your hands and squeeze to remove as much liquid as possible. Put in a bowl with the remaining yogurt. Finely chop the mint and coriander and stir into the yogurt."],[null,"Lightly toast the pitta. Serve the chicken and cauliflower with the warm bread topped with raita."]],"h":[]},"7533762":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200°C/ gas 6. Cube the chicken and add to a bowl with the yogurt, paprika, cumin and turmeric, then mix well to coat the chicken."],[null,"Sprinkle the tomatoes with garam masala."],[null,"Lightly oil a baking tray and arrange the onion and pepper evenly over it, then place the chicken pieces on the onion and pepper, and arrange the tomatoes on top."],[null,"Roast for 15 minutes, or until the chicken is thoroughly cooked, and serve with basmati rice or salad."]],"h":[[null,"Use curry paste if you don't have all the spices, or add grated fresh ginger and crushed garlic for extra flavour."],[null,"You can mix the chicken, spices and yogurt together in a food bag and keep in the fridge for a few hours before you start cooking, which helps the flavours to infuse."],[null,"Spicy dishes do not usually need any added salt, which means they're better for your heart."],[null,"Skinless chicken is rich in protein and has almost half the fat and saturated fat of skin-on chicken."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat thoroughly until piping-hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 5"]]},"7080625":{"s":[[null,"Add the sliced red pepper, red onion, coriander and lime juice to a bowl. Mix well and reserve."],[null,"Meanwhile, in another bowl, mix the yogurt with the tandoori paste and then stir in the chopped chicken."],[null,"Place the chapattis in a preheated dry frying pan over a medium heat for 45 seconds on each side to warm them through."],[null,"Lay the chapattis out and spread the chicken over half of each chapatti. Add the salad leaves, then top with the red pepper and onion mixture."],[null,"Roll them up, tucking in the sides and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"The mix of yogurt and tandoori paste in this recipe gives you the moisture of mayonnaise without the fat. Try it mixed into cooked potatoes for a spicy potato salad."],[null,"Choose chapattis without fat and don't add extra fat when serving, if you're watching your weight."],[null,"Chapattis are made with wholemeal flour so are higher in fibre and great for making a quick meal. You could fill them with salad and avocado, or use leftover lamb instead of chicken."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"4405567":{"s":[[null,"In a bowl, combine all ingredients for the marinade. Rub the chicken thighs with the marinade. The marinade will be quite thick. Cover the bowl and let the chicken marinate in the refrigerator for a minimum of one hour and for up to 24 hours."],[null,"Preheat oven to 400°F. Line a baking tray with parchment paper."],[null,"Heat a large non-stick skillet over high heat Leave some marinade on the meat and discard the rest. Sear both sides of the chicken thighs. Place them on the baking tray."],[null,"In a mixing bowl, toss the cauliflower florets with the olive oil and curry powder. Place them on the baking tray with the chicken thighs."],[null,"Roast the chicken thighs and cauliflower for approximately 30 minutes. The internal temperature of the chicken should be 165°F and the cauliflower should start to brown."],[null,"Cook the basmati rice according to package instructions."],[null,"Remove the baking tray from the oven. Combine the cauliflower, the cooked rice, frozen peas, and chopped fresh mint in the skillet and sauté until warmed."],[null,"Serve the chicken with the pilaf."]],"h":[["Using Marinade For Poultry Flavor","Poultry is one animal protein source that can be part of your diet. Chicken is likely the most common poultry available in your local grocery store; it’s easy to use in almost any dish and can be cooked in a number of ways. A variety of seasonings—including marinades—can be used to create savory meals that are lower in potassium. When using a marinade to flavor your poultry dish consider the following: • Avoid marinade ingredients that may be high in sodium or potassium. • Use marinade recipes lower in sodium to stay within your kidney diet goals. • Consider the time needed for the poultry to sit in the marinade, which can vary from a few hours to overnight. Too much or too little time in the marinade can alter the final flavor making it too powerful or lacking in taste. • Finally, consider the piece of poultry you are marinating. Thinner cuts absorb the marinade more easily than thicker cuts."]]},"4690157":{"s":[[null,"Cut English muffins in half and toast the four halves in toaster oven until golden brown. Place on a serving plate."],[null,"In a bowl, mix together mayonnaise, chopped cucumber, lemon juice and Tandoori spice. Add the tuna and combine with the mayonnaise mixture."],[null,"In a medium saucepan over medium heat, sauté onions in vegetable oil until cooked (3–5 minutes)."],[null,"Add the garlic and cabbage to the onions and stir occasionally until cooked (5–8 minutes)."],[null,"Spread the cabbage mixture on the four toasted muffin halves and top with the mayonnaise mixture. Sprinkle dill on top."]],"h":[["Using canned fish in your kidney diet","Protein is a necessary part of the kidney-friendly diet and can come from plant or animal sources. Canned fish is an excellent protein choice. Readily available in your grocery store aisles, this type of fish can be lower in cost and rich in heart healthy fats, vitamins and minerals. While a portion is considered to be 2 to 3 ounces, meeting with a registered dietitian can help determine the right amount for you. Consider the following tips when choosing canned fish as part of an entrée, salad, soup or side dish. 1. Canning Liquid: Canned fish is commonly packed in oil, brine or water. To reduce calories, select fish packed in water. Also, read the ingredient list and Nutrition Facts Label to avoid any high-sodium, potassium- or phosphorus-based additives. 2. Drain Canned Liquids: After opening, the fish will have some type of liquid within the can to help maintain freshness and moisture. Most instructions suggest draining this liquid to improve the texture of your fish with use in recipes. If the canned fish is in oil, draining the oil and then rinsing the fish with water may also be recommended. 3. Choice of Fish: There are certain types of fish ideal for a kidney diet that are low in salt and potassium. Tuna and salmon are the most popular and can be part of your diet if you read labels carefully, eat the correct portion, and pair with lower-potassium vegetables or grains for a healthy meal."]]},"1949":{"s":[[null,"Core and chop the apple. Finely chop the celery and onion. Place onion and olive oil in a small microwave- safe bowl and microwave for 2 minutes. Let cool for several minutes."],[null,"Drain tuna well and place in a mixing bowl. Pat with a paper towel to remove excess water."],[null,"Stir in the celery, onion mixture, mayonnaise, tarragon, lemon juice and sugar. Mix until well blended."],[null,"Add the chopped apples and walnuts and stir to combine."],[null,"Refrigerate to chill before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Serve on lettuce leaves, in a wrap or with bread sticks or low-sodium crackers."],[null,"If fresh tarragon is unavailable substitute fresh basil or parsley."],[null,"Use low-fat mayonnaise to reduce fat to 17 grams. Note sodium content will be higher."]]},"6156586":{"s":[[null,"Coarsely chop the tarragon, parsley, and mushrooms together in a food processor or by hand. Set aside."],[null,"Coat a large nonstick skillets with olive oil spray, and heat over medium-high heat."],[null,"Brown the chicken breasts for 4 minutes on each side, or until a meat thermometer inserted into the chicken reads 165° F. Remove the chicken from the pan. (if doubling the chicken, cook in two pans; set aside half of the chicken to cool, then store in a tightly sealed container in the fridge for up to 3 days.)"],[null,"Divide the chicken between 4 dinner plates and sprinkle with the salt and pepper."],[null,"Add the olive oil to the pan along with the garlic and chopped herbs and mushrooms. Toss to warm through, about 1 minute. Spoon over the plated chicken. Serve with an additional vegetable or whole grain side dish."]],"h":[]},"2846":{"s":[[null,"Chop shallot and tarragon."],[null,"Mix all ingredients except the oil in a blender and blend until smooth for approximately one minute."],[null,"Transfer to a mixing bowl and whisk in the oil. Do not emulsify."],[null,"Pour into a salad dressing cruet and store in the refrigerator until ready to use."]],"h":[[null,"See DaVita.com recipe Roasted Garlic to make pureed garlic or buy prepared garlic puree in the store."],[null,"Use olive oil or canola oil if desired."],[null,"Serve with Lettuce and Mushroom Salad or Summer Salad."]]},"6714664":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 450°F."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix together the mustard, tarragon, butter, 1 Tbsp of the olive oil, water, lemon juice, and garlic; set aside."],[null,"Sprinkle the cod with the salt and pepper. In a shallow ovenproof skillet, heat the remaining ½ Tbsp of olive oil over medium-high heat. Add the cod and sear on one side for 4 minutes. Turn the cod over and sear for 2 minutes on the other side."],[null,"Pour the mustard sauce over the cod and place the skillet in the oven; roast for 2 to 3 minutes. Serve the cod with the lemon wedges."]],"h":[]},"7628199":{"s":[[null,"Boil the potatoes whole in their skins for 15–25 minutes, depending on their size. Drain, then cut into a mixture of halves and quarters."],[null,"Heat the rapeseed oil in a large frying pan and add the potatoes. Cook, turning regularly, for 3 minutes."],[null,"Add the mushrooms to the pan with the potatoes and cook, stirring, for another 3 minutes, then add the spring onions and cook, stirring, for a further 2 minutes."],[null,"Sprinkle the flour over everything and stir to mix well. Next, gradually pour in the milk, stirring constantly, for 2–3 minutes."],[null,"Stir in the cheese, season with pepper and serve."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"3427":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Flatten fish fillets and turn several times in olive oil to coat completely."],[null,"Sprinkle fish with spices."],[null,"Place in baking dish."],[null,"Bake for approximately 20 to 25 minutes until fish flakes with a fork."]],"h":[[null,"Experiment with different fish flavors. Mild fish include orange roughy, perch, cod and catfish."],[null,"To flatten fish, place wax paper over and under fish then apply pressure with a heavy, flat object such as a large cast iron skillet."],[null,"Adjust portions for a lower or higher protein diet."]]},"2639":{"s":[[null,"Set cream cheese out to soften."],[null,"Using a fork, mash chicken with juices in a medium bowl."],[null,"Add the cream cheese, egg, sage, garlic powder, black pepper, onion powder, Italian seasoning and bread crumbs; mix well."],[null,"Form six patties."],[null,"In a medium skillet heat olive oil over medium heat."],[null,"Fry patties for 5- to 6 minutes on each side or until crispy on the outside and heated through."]],"h":[[null,"Choose the canned chicken lowest in sodium.Melanie uses Keystone Chicken (available at Walmart)."],[null,"Chicken Patties are very similar to salmon or tuna patties, but might be better liked by someone who doesn’t care for fish."],[null,"Look for Kikkoman brand panko bread crumbs– the sodium content is lower compared to commercial and generic unseasoned bread crumbs. Unsalted or low-sodium crushed saltines are an acceptable alternative to the bread crumbs."],[null,"Variations: instead of patties, form into 24 chicken meatballs. Meatballs could be eaten as a high-protein snack or used with theDaVita.com Roasted Red Pepper Sauce recipe over pasta."]]},"1749":{"s":[[null,"Dice chicken into small pieces. Chop onion, celery, apple and pickles."],[null,"In a medium bowl, combine chicken, onion, celery, apple and pickles. Stir to mix."],[null,"Add mayonnaise, lemon juice and black pepper. Mix well."],[null,"Refrigerate at least 30 minutes to chill. Serve 1/2-cup chicken salad on 2 slices of whole wheat bread."]],"h":[[null,"This is a great recipe for using up leftover baked or grilled chicken."]]},"6364308":{"s":[[null,"Remove stems and any yellowed leaves from greens, then rinse greens well and drain."],[null,"Heat oil in a large pot over medium heat. Add onion and sauté until onion is tender."],[null,"Add greens, water, and bouillon to the pot. Cover and bring to a boil. Reduce heat to low and simmer for 30 minutes or until greens are tender, stirring occasionally."],[null,"Add salt, sugar, and Tabasco sauce. Toss well and simmer an additional 5 minutes. May be served with cider vinegar to bring out the best in the greens."]],"h":[]},"2166":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Chop onion and bell pepper. Slice garlic and cut eggplant into cubes."],[null,"In a large skillet, heat oil and butter over medium heat. Sauté onion, green pepper and garlic with cayenne and black pepper."],[null,"Add thyme and eggplant to ingredients and cook until eggplant softens, stirring often."],[null,"Reserve 2 tablespoons bread crumbs for topping. Add the remaining breadcrumbs to eggplant and cook 15 minutes."],[null,"Beat egg and add to mixture, stirring quickly so egg does not solidify."],[null,"Place in casserole dish. Sprinkle remaining bread crumbs over mixture, and bake for 25 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Two medium eggplants yield approximately 8 cups."],[null,"Adjust cayenne pepper to your taste preference."],[null,"Refrigerate or freeze leftover casserole for a quick dish later."]]},"7209689":{"s":[[null,"In a large lightly greased ovenproof dish, layer the sliced potatoes, sliced garlic and fresh thyme."],[null,"Mix together the olive oil and 200ml water, season and pour over the potatoes."],[null,"Cover with foil and bake at 170ºC/gas 3, for 1 hour, removing the foil halfway through cooking time."]],"h":[[null,"You could also layer with thinly sliced onions."],[null,"For extra flavour, use stock instead of water or top with a little grated Cheddar cheese when you remove the foil."],[null,"You can do this with other root veg like swede or sweet potatoes."],[null,"Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"3151":{"s":[[null,"Cut tempeh into 12 slices. Thinly slice onion, bell pepper and mushrooms."],[null,"In a large skillet heat 1 tablespoon of the sesame oil over medium heat. Add sliced tempeh and cook each side for 3 to 4 minutes until browned. Add balsamic vinegar and cook one minute; flip and cook an additional minute. Remove tempeh from skillet."],[null,"Add remaining sesame oil to skillet and heat over medium heat. Add the onion, bell pepper and mushrooms and cook until tender."],[null,"Cut pita in half and open to form a pocket. Spread each half with 1 teaspoon mayonnaise. Add 3 pieces tempeh and 1/4 the vegetable mixture to each pita half. Serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"For a flavor change replace sesame oil with your favorite flavored oil."],[null,"Tempeh made from whole soybeans mixed with rice or millet., then fermented. It has a nutty-flavor and absorbs flavors from marinades or seasonings added during cooking."]]},"3552":{"s":[[null,"Tenderize meat by piercing well with a fork (on both sides), or pound with a tenderizing mallet."],[null,"Place steak in large shallow dish and carefully sprinkle with a minimal amount of meat tenderizer."],[null,"Combine remaining ingredients and spread over both sides of steak."],[null,"Marinate 1 to 4 hours."],[null,"Grill or broil for 3 to 5 minutes per side or to desired doneness. Remove from heat and let steak rest about 10 to 15 minutes"],[null,"Cut steak into thin slices at a slant against the grain."]],"h":[[null,"Most chemical meat tenderizers contain papain, an enzyme derived from papaya that helps breakdown the tough fibers in the meat. One well known brand of tenderizer is Adolph’s®. *Measure and limit the amount used because of the high-sodium content. Adolph’s original tenderizer contains 380 mg of sodium per 1/4 teaspoon; Adolph’s seasoned tenderizer contains 450 mg of sodium per 1/4 teaspoon. Reduce amount used if a smaller steak is prepared."],[null,"You can use top round steak if flank is not available."],[null,"Leftover portions can be used to top a salad, or wrapped into tortillas for an interesting wrap or fajita."],[null,"If you are on a protein-restricted diet, adjust portion to your meal plan or consult your renal dietitian."]]},"6293286":{"s":[[null,"In a small sauce pan, whisk together soy sauce, water, honey and garlic. Bring to a boil then reduce to a simmer. Simmer for 7-8 minutes or until the sauce is reduced to 1/4 cup. Set aside to cool."],[null,"Once cool, add the teriyaki sauce to a large bowl. Add in the mayonnaise and Greek yogurt and whisk well to combine."],[null,"Add the chicken, celery, carrots and almonds and stir well to combine."],[null,"Divide the chicken salad among 6 Bibb lettuce leaves (3/4 cup of chicken salad per lettuce cup)."]],"h":[]},"3027":{"s":[[null,"Slice tempeh into 12 crosswise short strips. Heat olive oil in a pan and add tempeh. Cook and flip for 8-10 minutes until it starts to turn brown."],[null,"Cook rice according to package directions, see Helpful Hints."],[null,"In a small saucepan whisk together coconut amino, 1/4 cup water, honey and rice vinegar, bring to a boil. Meanwhile combine cornstarch and 4 teaspoons water. Add to the boiling sauce and whisk until is starts to thicken."],[null,"Pour the sauce over the tempeh in the saucepan and heat through for 5-8 minutes."],[null,"Steam/cook the broccoli in the microwave. Drain if needed and set aside."],[null,"Divide rice into 4 bowls, about 1/3 cup per bowl. Add broccoli (1/2 cup) to each bowl and place 3 slices of tempeh on top. Drizzle each bowl with 2 tablespoons of crema. Slice scallion and sprinkle over each of the bowls, if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Used instant brown rice. Used 1-1/3 cups water to cook, bring to a boil and then simmer covered for 10 minutes."],[null,"The steamer vegetable bag at 12.6 ounces yields about 2 cups of vegetables."],[null,"Tempeh is naturally low in sodium. However, when comparing brands, be sure to choose the lowest sodium brand. If it is not marinated the sodium content should be very low."],[null,"A crema dressing can be added as an option. Stir together 4 tablespoons of sour cream with 3 tablespoons of water. This will add 15 mg potassium and 9mg of phosphorus per serving."]]},"2513":{"s":[[null,"Place chicken wings in a large zip-lock bag."],[null,"Add all ingredients and shake to mix and coat.Refrigerate overnight to marinate."],[null,"Preheat oven to 400° F."],[null,"Place wing drummettes in a baking dish and bake for 30 to 35 minutes. Check for doneness."],[null,"Serve hot or place in a covered warming dish or crock pot on low setting until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Regular soy sauce and teriyaki sauce are extremely high in sodium. Reduced-sodium soy sauce and teriyaki sauce contain less sodium, but are still considered high in sodium content. Be cautious to use only the amount required in the recipe."],[null,"Buy fresh wing drummettes at the grocery. A 1-1/4 pound package contains 12 drummettes. If unavailable, ask your butcher to cut whole chicken wings into drummette size."],[null,"Boneless chicken pieces may be used in this recipe. Check for doneness after 20 minutes."]]},"3831":{"s":[[null,"In a large frying pan, brown ground beef over medium heat. Drain well, remove from pan and set aside."],[null,"Heat oil in pan. Add 1/2 cup chopped onion and cook until clear. Add garlic, cook and stir for one minute."],[null,"Add cooked beef back into pan. Stir in chili powder, pepper, cumin and Tabasco® sauce. Remove from heat and prepare tacos."],[null,"Add 1/4 cup meat mixture inside each taco shell. Top with 2 tablespoons lettuce, 1 tablespoon each tomato, cheese and remaining onion."]],"h":[[null,"Select cheese that has the word \"natural\" on the package. Avoid processed cheese due to higher sodium and phosphorus contents."]]},"2481":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400° F."],[null,"Combine all ingredients except the chicken wings in a large bowl."],[null,"Add the chicken and toss to coat."],[null,"Place the chicken wings in a baking dish and bake for 30 to 35 minutes. Check for doneness."],[null,"Serve the wings hot or place in a covered warming dish or crock pot on low setting until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Buy fresh wing drummettes. A 1-1/4 pound package contains approximately 12 drummettes. If unavailable, ask your butcher to cut whole chicken wings into drummette size."],[null,"Boneless chicken pieces may be used in this recipe. Check for doneness after 20 minutes."],[null,"Choose lowest sodium brand barbecue sauce or instead of using commercial barbecue sauce, serve with DaVita.com’s recipe for Zesty Barbecue Sauce. Sodium content is much lower."],[null,"Look for the lowest sodium brand of green chili peppers. Sodium varies greatly between brands."]]},"3404":{"s":[[null,"Finely chop green pepper, red pepper, and onion. Remove the seeds from the jalapeno and finely chop the pepper. Combine oil, vinegar, sugar, salt, and pepper in a medium saucepan over medium-low heat. Stir together and simmer for 3 minutes until sugar is dissolved. Remove from the heat and set aside to cool."],[null,"Meanwhile, rinse and drain the black beans and black-eyed peas and then combine with corn in a large bowl. Add the onion, bell peppers and jalapeno, then pour in the vinegar mixture and stir until well combined."],[null,"Serve the Texas caviar immediately with low-sodium tortilla chips for a snack or with rice or noodles for an entrée. Cover and store remaining caviar in the refrigerator."]],"h":[[null,"You may leave out the jalapeno and substitute sriracha. This recipe was tested using Fix® Sriracha Hot Sauce. Look for a brand that is lowest in sodium."],[null,"The recipe is higher in potassium. However, with a whole food like beans your body may not absorb all the potassium. Consider the potassium when you are planning your meals for the day and what your blood potassium level is."],[null,"Can corned that is drained and rinsed can be used in place of frozen corn. However, it may add more sodium to the recipe."]]},"4049602":{"s":[[null,"In a non-stick frying pan, heat oil over medium heat. Fry the chicken with onion until the chicken is lightly browned."],[null,"Add the curry paste, garlic, ginger, lime juice and diced peppers and stir to combine."],[null,"Add the chicken broth and the basil. Simmer for 5 minutes."],[null,"Dilute the cornstarch in 1 tablespoon of water and add to the pan while stirring. Let simmer until the sauce has thickened."],[null,"Remove pan from heat and add the yogurt."],[null,"Serve with basmati rice and enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"PLEASE NOTE: This recipe is higher in potassium and portion size is important. Check with your registered dietitian to see how this recipe can be included in your diet."],["Kidney-friendly curry sauce","A kidney-friendly diet is low in sodium. Sodium is generally added in the form of salt and many people may feel that food has no flavor when prepared without salt. This is simply not true! Salt is more of an acquired taste and you can retrain your taste buds to not crave salt by adding flavor in other ways — such as with herbs and spices. Creating a curry sauce is an excellent way to add lots of flavor to a dish, because it contains a delicious mix of herbs and spices. Curry sauces Typically, curry sauces contain coriander, cumin, ginger, garlic and turmeric, but a wide variety of herbs and spices can be used depending upon taste preferences and the type of foods included in the dish. Other herbs and spices to consider are allspice, white pepper, ground mustard, cinnamon, cloves, nutmeg, mace, cardamom and bay leaves. For a spicier version, some heat can be added with fresh or dried chilis. The color and flavor of a curry sauce will vary depending upon the mix of herbs and spices and the base to which they are added. Don’t be afraid to experiment with different spice and herb combinations as you seek the best blend for you. Curry dishes Dishes called 'curry' may contain meat, poultry, fish or shellfish along with a variety of vegetables. Dry curries are cooked with very little liquid which is allowed to evaporate during cooking, leaving the other ingredients coated with the spice mixture. Wet curries contain larger amounts of liquid to create a sauce or gravy. To make the curry sauce, herbs and spices are added to a base of yogurt, cream, coconut milk, tomato purée, sautéed crushed onion or stock. Curry sauce made with coconut milk and tomato purée are higher in potassium than other liquid choices such as sautéed crushed onion or unsalted stock. Ask your dietitian what type of curry is right for you."]]},"7572993":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a frying pan or wok, until it begins to smoke. Add the chicken and fry for 2–3 minutes until golden, remove from the pan with a slotted spoon and set aside."],[null,"Add the garlic, ginger and chilli and fry for 1 minute, add the spring onions and pepper and continue to fry for 2 minutes."],[null,"Return the chicken to the pan with the remaining ingredients and heat through, until piping hot. Serve."]],"h":[[null,"This recipe also works well with thinly sliced lean beef, prawns, salmon, turkey or tofu instead of chicken."],[null,"Great wrapped up in a tortilla or roti with salad."],[null,"If you don’t have all the veggies to hand, you could use packets of stir fry veg, tinned bamboo shoots in water or sliced carrots."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"7767561":{"s":[[null,"Place the cod, curry paste and egg yolk into a food processor or blender and blend until combined."],[null,"Stir through the French beans, coriander and lime zest."],[null,"Form the mixture into 12 patties and season well."],[null,"Brush the patties with a little oil."],[null,"Prehat the grill. Place on a baking sheet and grill for 3-4 minutes on each side, until golden."],[null,"Mix together the ingredients for the dipping sauce and serve with the fish cakes."]],"h":[[null,"Serve with a little wilted pak choi and some finely chopped red chilli, spring onion and coriander leaves to garnish."],[null,"You could use salmon, prawns or crab in place of cod."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Freeze cod cakes and sauce separately. Freeze cod cakes in individually wrapped portions with greaseproof paper between each one. Defrost in the fridge or in the microwave and heat thoroughly until piping-hot."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"6424125":{"s":[[null,"Soak bamboo skewers in warm water for at least 30 minutes."],[null,"In a medium bowl, whisk the low- or no-calorie sweetener, soy sauce, pepper, garlic, and lemon grass. Add the beef to the marinade and marinate in the refrigerator for at least 1 hour (up to four hours)."],[null,"Prepare an indoor or outdoor grill."],[null,"Remove beef from marinade and divide meat evenly onto each of the 12 skewers. Discard marinade."],[null,"Grill the skewers for about 5 minutes per side."],[null,"Garnish the skewers with basil, cilantro and a lime wedge."]],"h":[]},"9038412":{"s":[[null,"Shred your veggies and add all the salad ingredients to a large mixing bowl. Set aside."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine all the dressing ingredients, using a fork until smooth."],[null,"When ready to serve, pour the dressing on your salad and mix well until evenly coated."]],"h":[[null,"If you’re working in advance , store the salad and the dressing separately until ready to serve. For convenience, you may purchase pre-shredded slaw to cut down on preparation time . Add 1-2 tablespoons of water to the peanut dressing, if needed, to thin. This Thai peanut salad tastes best when freshly dressed , but leftovers keep refrigerated for 1-2 days."]]},"3903":{"s":[[null,"Use towels to press tofu and remove/absorb water. Repeat as needed with new towels."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 F. Cube tofu into 1-inch sections. In a medium bowl and toss tofu with oil 1 tablespoon coconut aminos, and corn starch. Bake on baking sheet for 20-25 minutes or until edges are golden brown."],[null,"Meanwhile, use a spiral tool or hand spiralizer to make the zucchini noodles. You may also cut into thin strips with a vegetable peeler or cube if desired."],[null,"In a medium pot mix red curry, coconut cream, peanut butter, remaining coconut aminos, brown sugar, apple cider vinegar, and water. Simmer on low for about 10 minutes while stirring occasionally."],[null,"Peel and devein shrimp, add juice from the half lime and pepper. In a medium non-stick pan sauté shrimp with remaining olive oil for 2-3 minutes per side until shrimp is bright pink. Set aside."],[null,"Mince garlic and slice bell pepper into strips. Place back in the pan on medium-high heat along with zucchini and cook for 3-4 minutes. Don’t over cook or zoodles will become watery."],[null,"Place zucchini noodles on four plates and evenly divide tofu, shrimp and curry sauce over each. Top with cilantro leaves."]],"h":[[null,"Look for the lowest sodium variety of coconut aminos. Some can be as high as regular soy sauce."],[null,"Soba noodles can be substitute for the zucchini noodles. It will add about 6 grams of carbohydrate, 15 mg more sodium, and 70mg less potassium."],[null,"This dish provides a complete meal. With new research we have learned not all of the potassium and phosphorus are absorbed from whole foods sources such as tofu, peanut butter and vegetables."]]},"2448":{"s":[[null,"Cook rice according to package directions, omiting salt."],[null,"Place shrimp in a bowl. Squeeze the juice of 2 limes over shrimp and set aside for 5 to 10 minutes."],[null,"Drain pineapple, reserving juice; place in a large bowl; set aside."],[null,"Dice onion into 1/2″ pieces. Mince garlic. Chop mint and basil. Grate ginger."],[null,"In a sauté pan heat 1 tablespoon olive oil over medium-low heat and add mushrooms, onion and 3/4 of the garlic; sauté for 3 minutes. Add shrimp and chili sauce. Cook and stir until shrimp is pink. Remove from heat and stir in 1/2 cup of the mint, plus the basil and ginger."],[null,"Add shrimp mixture to the pineapple. Squeeze remaining two limes over mixture; stir and set aside."],[null,"To make the sauce, sauté remaining 1/4 cup mint and garlic in 1 tablespoon olive oil. Add coconut milk, chicken broth and cayenne pepper."],[null,"Dissolve cornstarch in 1/2 cup reserved pineapple juice and add to sauce, stirring constantly over medium heat, until thickened."],[null,"While sauce is thickening, heat peas in microwave for 3 minutes."],[null,"Combine sauce with shrimp and pineapple mixture and peas."],[null,"Serve 3/4 cup shrimp-pineapple mixture over 2/3 cup jasmine rice. Sprinkle with paprika."]],"h":[[null,"For a lower protein meal decrease shrimp to 1 pound; increase to 2 pounds for higher protein."],[null,"Sriracha sauce is a hot chili sauce from Thailand. Add extra at the table if you like the dish spicy hot. Dried, crushed red chili peppers may be substitiued for Sriracha sauce."],[null,"Cayenne pepper can be substituted for paprika if you like more heat."]]},"1870":{"s":[[null,"Mince the shallot. Cut cauliflower and green beans into 1″ pieces. Cut carrots into 1/2″ circles. Cut lime into wedges for garnish. Set aside."],[null,"In a pot with a lid, add oil and shallots, and sauté on low heat until shallots are translucent."],[null,"Add the red curry paste and cook for one minute until fragrant."],[null,"Add coconut milk, vegetable broth and kaffir lime leaf, cover and bring to a simmer."],[null,"Add cauliflower, green beans and carrots, cover, and cook for 8-12 minutes or until soft enough to easily cut with a fork. Turn off the heat when a fork can go through the vegetables."],[null,"Remove the lime leaf from the pot and throw it out."],[null,"Spoon 1/2-cup cooked rice into a bowl and then top with 1-1/2 cups vegetables and sauce."],[null,"Garnish with a wedge of lime to squeeze over the dish."]],"h":[[null,"This is a higher potassium recipe due to the 2 servings of vegetables. You may want to limit vegetables or fruit at other meals or eat a smaller portion if you are on a lower potassium diet."],[null,"Serving size is for a main dish vegetarian meal. You can serve as a side dish instead. Reduce portion to 3/4 cup vegetable mixture, eight servings per recipe instead of four."],[null,"Fresh kaffir lime leaf can be found in Thai, Asian or Indian specialty grocery stores. Dried kaffir lime leaf can be found in specialty spice shops and some large grocery stores. The lime leaf is used for flavor; it is not edible. Throw it out at the end of cooking."],[null,"Adding a squeeze of lime juice at the end provides brightness and more flavors to the dish."],[null,"Use full fat, unsweetened coconut milk, not light or sweetened. One can contains about 14 ounces; measure out 8 ounces for the recipe."],[null,"Use jasmine, basmati or long grain rice."]]},"2259":{"s":[[null,"Peel garlic cloves and de-seed peppers."],[null,"In the blender, purée together all the ingredients, except cornstarch and 2 tablespoons of the water."],[null,"Transfer the mixture to a saucepan and bring to a boil over medium-high heat."],[null,"Lower the heat to medium and simmer until the mixture thickens, and the garlic and pepper begin to soften, about 3 minutes."],[null,"Combine the cornstarch and 2 tablespoons water to make a slurry."],[null,"Whisk in the cornstarch mixture and continue to simmer one more minute."],[null,"Let cool completely before storing in a glass jar in the refrigerator."]],"h":[[null,"Most comparable bottled sauces contain 400 mg sodium for a 2 tablespoon serving."],[null,"Use Serrano or other chili pepper variety of choice. Skip de-seeding for more heat."],[null,"The cornstarch will help the sauce to thicken slightly, causing nice suspension of the garlic-pepper bits; otherwise, you get a thin sauce with all the little pieces floating on the surface."]]},"6662295":{"s":[[null,"Heat 1/2 tablespoon of the oil in a medium nonstick skillet over medium heat. Add the white part of the scallions and the chile pepper and sauté until the scallions begin to caramelize, about 3 1/2 minutes. Add the mango and soy sauce and cook, while stirring, until the mango is softened, about 7 minutes. Stir in the lime juice and green part of the scallions, transfer to a bowl, and set aside."],[null,"Season the fish with the salt and pepper. Heat the remaining 1 tablespoon oil in a large nonstick skillet over medium-high heat. Add the fillets and sauté until cooked through and lightly browned, about 3 minutes per side. (Note: Prepare in batches, if necessary.)"],[null,"Top the fillets with the mango relish, sprinkle with the cilantro, and serve."]],"h":[]},"6265858":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, combine the oil, nuts, cranberries, salt and pepper. Top the green beans with the cranberry-nut mixture. Garnish with the lemon zest."],[null,"Fill a large pot 2/3 full of water and bring to boiling. Add the green beans, turn off the heat, and let the green beans stand in the water for 3 minutes. Drain the beans and add them to a serving bowl or platter."]],"h":[]},"6023791":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the champagne vinegar, lemon juice, honey, salt, pepper, chives, and oil until well combine. Or, add ingredients to a jar with a tight fitting lid and shake until combined."],[null,"In a large serving bowl, combine the salad greens, blue cheese, pomegranate seeds, and hazelnuts. Toss with the dressing just before serving, or serve with dressing on the side."]],"h":[]},"9318277":{"s":[[null,"Add the flour, sugar and baking powder to a large bowl and whisk to combine. Then add the milk and vanilla and mix until combined, without over mixing."],[null,"Heat your non stick griddle over medium heat and once hot, ladle your batter to make pancakes that are approx. 4 inches in diameter. Cook for about 3-5 minutes until several bubbles form on top. Then flip and cook the other side for another 3-5 minutes until cooked through."],[null,"Serve with maple syrup or fresh fruit and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Do not over mix your pancake batter. If there are a few lumps, that’s perfectly okay. Don’t be tempted to mix until perfectly smooth as this may alter the texture of your pancakes. Preheat your pan or griddle. It should be hot before pouring your pancake batter to prevent sticking and for even cooking. Use medium heat to cook your pancakes . Although your pan should be hot, that doesn’t mean you should use high heat. This may result in uneven cooking, with crisp outsides and mushy middles. Flip your pancakes ONCE . Bubbles will appear on the surface of your pancakes soon after cooking, but wait until there are several bubbles and your pancake has cooked for at least 3-4 minutes before flipping. Flipping too often can cause them to deflate and lose their wonderful fluffiness. These pancakes also work well with whole wheat flour . They will be slightly less fluffy, but still delicious. Pancakes taste best when freshly made, but you may refrigerate leftovers and reheat in the toaster to enjoy within 1-2 days. You may also freeze these and reheat in the toaster from frozen."]]},"3566":{"s":[[null,"Thinly slice the zucchini. Finely chop the onion and garlic. Chop the tomatoes and cilantro."],[null,"Beat together eggs, egg whites, turmeric, salt and pepper to taste. Set aside."],[null,"Heat 1 tablespoon broth in a 10” or 12” stainless steel or non-stick skillet.."],[null,"Add onion, garlic, zucchini and green chilies. Sauté for about three minutes, stirring frequently."],[null,"Add tomato and cilantro."],[null,"Pour egg mixture over vegetables. Turn heat to low, cover and cook for about 10 minutes, checking periodically to see if eggs are firm."],[null,"When done, run a rubber spatula around edge of frittata, cut into four wedges and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Use a pan no more than 12”-inch in diameter, otherwise vegetables get too spread out and will overcook."],[null,"Have ingredients ready before cooking, otherwise, the zucchini will overcook, release water and dilute the flavor."],[null,"Check the firmness of eggs after 5 to 6 minutes to make sure they cook to perfection. Eggs won’t be very fluffy because of using more egg whites than yolks, but it helps to beat them well right before pouring over vegetables."]]},"6121396":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375 degrees."],[null,"In an oven safe sauté pan, add sesame oil and a generous amount of cooking spray over medium heat. Add onions and sauté until they turn clear but not brown, about 5 minutes."],[null,"Stir in curry paste, garlic, coconut milk and peanut butter and simmer until slightly reduced."],[null,"Season each tilapia filet with ground black pepper. Add filets to curry, coating both sides."],[null,"Place pan in the oven for 15-20 minutes or until tilapia is just cooked through."],[null,"Serve curry over 1/3 cup brown rice. Garnish with fresh cilantro if desired."]],"h":[]},"6419173":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375° F. Coat an 8x11-inch baking dish with cooking spray."],[null,"Place the four tilapia fillets side by side in the dish."],[null,"Top the fillets with the sliced onion and bell pepper."],[null,"In a medium bowl, mix all remaining ingredients and pour over the fish and vegetables."],[null,"Bake for 30 minutes. Let the fish rest for 15 minutes before serving. The vegetables should be slightly crisp and the fish should be fully cooked but tender."]],"h":[]},"4015375":{"s":[[null,"In a saucepan, bring 1 quart of water to a boil. Add the fish fillet and the cracked egg to the water. Reduce the heat and simmer for 6 minutes until the fish is cooked and the egg poached."],[null,"Remove both from the water and let cool."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix the fish and the egg together with a fork. Add the coriander, onion, lemon juice, ginger and mustard. Season with pepper, cover, and place in the refrigerator for 1 hour."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 300°F."],[null,"Spread the oil on the pita breads. Cut each pita into 8 wedges."],[null,"Place wedges, oiled side up, on a baking sheet and bake for 7 minutes."],[null,"Serve the cooled chips with the fish rillettes."]],"h":[["Rillettes: another way to enjoy fish","A fish rillette is a unique way to serve seafood in place of a standard baked or grilled recipe. Fish is poached and once tender, mixed with other mouth-watering ingredients to form a spread. Rillettes can be used as part of an appetizer, added to a sandwich, spread on a cracker or slice of bread, or blended into a pasta filling. When making rillette, choose ingredients lower in sodium and potassium. Added fats: Choose unsalted butter or margarine. Also, avoid fats with the first ingredient listed as partially hydrogenated oil to lower saturated fat. Lower salt: Replace salt with herbs and spices. Choose black pepper, bay leaf, black peppercorn, parsley, garlic and chili pepper depending on your desired flavor. Vegetable additions: Incorporate strong flavored vegetables to contribute to taste. Select small amounts of chives, leeks, shallots and red onion to add to your rillette. Serving suggestions: Consider how the rillette will be served to avoid unwanted salt and potassium. Toasted slices of a French baguette or unsalted crackers with a thin layer of rillette are just a few suggestions."]]},"6925458":{"s":[[null,"Place a large saucepan over medium heat until hot. Coat the pan with nonstick cooking spray, add the bell pepper, and cook 5 minutes or until beginning to lightly brown, stirring frequently."],[null,"Add the tomatoes and water, increase to high heat, and bring to a boil. Reduce the heat, cover tightly, and simmer until the tomatoes are tender. Using the back of a spoon, break up the larger pieces of tomato."],[null,"Add the fish and seasonings and stir very gently. Increase the heat to high and bring just to a boil. Reduce the heat, cover tightly, and simmer 3 minutes or until the fish is opaque in the center. Remove from the heat and let stand, covered, 10 minutes to develop flavors."]],"h":[]},"6288534":{"s":[[null,"Mash the capers with a fork or the back of a spoon. Stir the capers and 1/8 Tsp. salt into the sour cream."],[null,"Place a large nonstick skillet over medium heat until hot. Coat the skillet with nonstick cooking spray. Sprinkle one side of each filet evenly with the black pepper and 1/8 Tsp. salt. Cook 3 minutes, then turn and cook 2-3 minutes longer or until the fish is opaque in the center."],[null,"Place the filets on a serving platter, squeeze lemon juice evenly over all, and top each filet with 1 Tbsp. sour cream."]],"h":[]},"54932":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400 degrees F. Prepare DaVita’s Grilled Pineapple Salsa. Set aside."],[null,"Cover a baking sheet with foil and spray with non-stick cooking spray. Brush each fillet evenly with olive oil and sprinkle with pepper."],[null,"Bake for 15-20 minutes, until fish is fork tender and flakes. Place each fillet on a plate and top with 1/4 cup of the Grilled Pineapple Salsa."]],"h":[[null,"Naturally occurring potassium is only partially absorbed by our bodies. Approximately 40-60%, each food and/or person is different in what they absorb."],[null,"You may substitute tilapia with other white fish that you prefer."]]},"7446273":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200ºC/gas 6."],[null,"Place the pastry cases onto a baking sheet. Beat together all the remaining ingredients and use to fill the pastry cases."],[null,"Bake for about 15 minutes, until the filling is just set and turning golden. Cool a little and serve."]],"h":[[null,"These are best eaten (or frozen) the same day to stop the pastry going soggy."],[null,"For a vegetarian option, replace the crab with the equivalent weight of thinly sliced sautéed onions or mushrooms."],[null,"If you can't find bite-sized pastry cases, then line mini tart tins with very thinly rolled shortcrust or filo pastry (200g)."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"3534":{"s":[[null,"Using a serrated knife, cut pound cake into 10 equal slices and set aside."],[null,"Mix cream cheese, vanilla and sugar with electric mixer until smooth."],[null,"Combine cocoa and grated chocolate in a separate bowl and set aside."],[null,"Pour espresso into a shallow dish."],[null,"Dip both sides of 4 pieces of pound cake into the espresso, then place in bottom of 8″ loaf pan. Break up pieces, if necessary, in order to coat bottom of pan."],[null,"Gently spread 1/3 of cream cheese mixture over cake layer. Sprinkle with 1/3 cocoa mixture. Repeat procedure with remaining slices, cream cheese mixture and cocoa mixture to make 3 layers."],[null,"Refrigerate 2 hours, then cut into 10 pieces and serve."]],"h":[[null,"A 10-ounce prepared pound cake is the smaller size."],[null,"This is a low phosphorus version of traditional tiramisu."],[null,"To reduce carbohydrates and fat, use sugar substitute instead of sugar and replace regular cream cheese with low-fat cream cheese. You can also adjust to a smaller portion size."]]},"6162408":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 350°F. Line two rimmed baking sheets with parchment paper and spray with cooking spray. Spread the cashews, almonds, pecans and pistachios evenly on the baking sheets and bake for 6 minutes. Remove the nuts from the oven and let them cool. Lower the heat to 225°F."],[null,"In a large bowl, mix the cooled roasted nuts, cranberries, egg white, cinnamon, vanilla and salt until coated."],[null,"Spread the trail mix onto the same baking sheets. Bake for 45 minutes, stirring every 15 minutes."],[null,"Let cool, then store in an airtight container."]],"h":[]},"6212754":{"s":[[null,"Thoroughly rinse the quinoa in a fine mesh sieve under cold running water."],[null,"Add the quinoa to a medium sauce pan over medium-high heat. Sauté until all water evaporates (about 5 minutes) and the quinoa begins to pop. Add the chicken or vegetable broth and bring to a boil. Reduce to a simmer and cover. Cook for 15 minutes or until all water is absorbed. Set the quinoa aside to cool."],[null,"In a large bowl, whisk together the yogurt, olive oil, rice wine vinegar, dry dill, garlic powder, salt (optional), and pepper."],[null,"Add quinoa and remaining ingredients. Toss to coat."]],"h":[]},"6369435":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, combine the cubed tofu, shelled edamame, thinly sliced red cabbage, julienned carrot, sliced green onions, and sesame seeds."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the low-sodium soy sauce, rice vinegar, sesame oil, peanut butter, maple syrup, grated fresh ginger, minced garlic, salt, and black pepper."],[null,"Pour the dressing over the salad and gently toss to ensure even coating."]],"h":[]},"6451442":{"s":[[null,"In a bowl, whisk together soy sauce, rice vinegar, sesame oil, maple syrup or agave nectar, minced garlic, and grated ginger to create the marinade."],[null,"Cut the pressed tofu into cubes and place them in a shallow dish. Pour half of the marinade over the tofu, ensuring each piece is coated. Let it marinate for at least 30 minutes."],[null,"While the tofu is marinating, prepare the vegetables. Thread the marinated tofu, red onion chunks, bell pepper chunks, and yellow squash rounds onto skewers, alternating between the ingredients."],[null,"Preheat the grill or grill pan over medium-high heat."],[null,"Grill the skewers for about 10–15 minutes, turning occasionally, until the tofu is golden and the vegetables are charred and tender. Baste the skewers with the remaining marinade during grilling for extra flavor."],[null,"Once cooked, remove the skewers from the grill and let them rest for a few minutes before serving."],[null,"Serve alongside cooked brown rice, 1/3 cup per serving."]],"h":[]},"9798062":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425℉/218℃ and line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Place the tofu cubes in a medium bowl and add the soy sauce. Gently mix to coat the pieces. Then add the arrowroot and spices and stir until evenly coated."],[null,"Arrange the seasoned cubes in a single layer on your parchment-lined tray. Then bake for 15 minutes, flip the cubes, and bake for an additional 8-10 minutes, or until desired crispiness is reached."],[null,"While the tofu is baking, add all the peanut sauce ingredients to a small bowl and mix until combined, adding 1-2 tablespoons of water to thin to your preferred consistency."],[null,"Serve with fresh veggies of your choice, grain of choice, and drizzle each bowl with the peanut sauce, or serve it on the side for dipping."]],"h":[[null,"No need to press the tofu if you’re using extra firm for this one. I’ve tried it both ways, and the difference was very minimal. That said, you may press it first if you’d like."],[null,"Do your best to cut the tofu cubes the same size for even cooking."],[null,"Make sure to arrange the cubes in a single layer with plenty of space in between so they crisp up nicely."],[null,"Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-4 days."]]},"3516":{"s":[[null,"Soak nuts in hot water for an hour; drain off the water."],[null,"Lightly squeeze excess water from the tofu in a paper towel."],[null,"Blend all ingredients except the chives/green onions in a food processor until smooth."],[null,"Chop the chives or green onions and mix into tofu mixture with a spoon."],[null,"Use as a spread on bagels, toast, or crackers. Or use as a dip for fresh veggies."]],"h":[[null,"Nuts can be part of a kidney friendly diet. New research shows our bodies do not absorb all of the phosphorus in plant-based foods."],[null,"May substitute raw cashews for almonds."],[null,"Try various herbs in place of chives, such as dill, basil or parsley."],[null,"Store in a container in the refrigerator for up to 2 weeks."],[null,"Analysis is for the spread only, does not include any crackers, bread or vegetables used with the spread."]]},"2049":{"s":[[null,"Open package of tofu and squeeze out extra liquid in a towel. Chop the red onion, celery and fresh dill."],[null,"In a large bowl, mash tofu with a fork, potato masher or dough cutter."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix mayo, mustard, and seasonings together."],[null,"Place all ingredients over the mashed tofu in the large bowl and mix together. Enjoy as you would any egg salad."]],"h":[[null,"Get the plain unseasoned super firm tofu that is not packed in water for a firmer texture. Other tofus will also work though. But NOT silken tofu."],[null,"Black salt (kala namak) is an option to add to this recipe. It may be hard to find in the store, but can be ordered online. It is recommended for that sulfur flavor to make it taste like eggs."],[null,"May add other chopped veggies such as bell pepper or pickle relish (watch the sodium). If you do not like turmeric or the lemon juice, they can be left out of the recipe."],[null,"You may also used vegan mayonnaise to replace the regular mayonnaise in the recipe."]]},"6536401":{"s":[[null,"Cook the quinoa: Fill a medium pot 3/4 full with salted water; cover and heat to a boil over high heat. Once it boils, add the quinoa and cook, uncovered, for 18 to 20 minutes or until tender. Turn off the heat. Drain well and return to the pot."],[null,"Press the tofu: Meanwhile, drain the tofu and then place it on a plate lined with paper towels. Place several layers of paper towels on top and then place a heavy-bottomed pot (or skillet) on top of the paper towels. Set aside to release excess liquid for at least 10 minutes."],[null,"Prep the ingredients and make the glaze: Meanwhile, wash and dry the fresh produce. Peel the carrots; thinly slice them on an angle. Cut the mushrooms into small pieces. Cut out and discard the core of the cabbage; thinly slice the leaves. Peel and finely chop the ginger. Peel and coarsely chop 2 cloves of garlic. Thinly slice the scallions, separating the white bottoms from the hollow green tops. In a bowl, combine the sliced cabbage, chopped ginger, chopped garlic and sliced white parts of the scallions. In a separate bowl, whisk together the coconut aminos, maple syrup, half of the sesame oil and 1 tablespoon of water."],[null,"Cook the veggies and finish the quinoa: In a medium skillet (nonstick, if you have one), heat the remaining sesame oil over medium-high heat until hot. Add the sliced carrots and mushroom pieces in an even layer. Cook, without stirring, for 2 to 3 minutes or until lightly browned. Add the prepared cabbage mixture; season with salt (optional) and pepper. Cook, stirring occasionally, for 2 to 3 minutes, or until softened. Add the vinegar. Cook, stirring frequently, for 30 seconds to 1 minute, or until the liquid has evaporated. Transfer to the pot of cooked quinoa; stir to combine. Cover to keep warm. Rinse and wipe out the skillet."],[null,"Cook the tofu and serve your dish: Transfer the pressed tofu to a cutting board; cut it lengthwise into 4 equal-size pieces. Season with salt (optional) and pepper on both sides. In the same skillet, heat 2 teaspoons of olive oil over medium-high heat until hot. Add the seasoned tofu pieces in an even layer and cook for 5 to 6 minutes, or until browned. Flip and cook for 2 to 3 minutes, or until lightly browned. Add half of the glaze (carefully, as the liquid may splatter) and cook, frequently spooning the glaze over the tofu, for 1 to 2 minutes, or until the tofu is coated. Transfer to a cutting board. Cut crosswise into 1-inch pieces. Serve the finished quinoa topped with the cooked tofu and the remaining glaze. Garnish with the sliced green tips of the scallions and the furikake. Enjoy!"]],"h":[]},"7075143":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 190°/gas 5. Lightly oil a baking sheet and put the coconut milk into a shallow bowl. Mix the flour with the five-spice, then put the flour onto a dinner plate and the breadcrumbs on another dinner plate."],[null,"Put the tofu onto the plate of flour and mix so each piece is coated, separating the strips so they’re not touching each other."],[null,"Wash and dry your hands then pick up a strip of tofu, shake off any excess flour, dip into the coconut milk then place on the breadcrumbs and sprinkle more crumbs on top to fully coat the tofu, then place on the baking sheet. Repeat until all the tofu goujons are coated."],[null,"Bake for 15 minutes until the outside is crispy and lightly browned."]],"h":[[null,"It's a good idea to use one hand for dipping the goujons into the coconut milk and the other for bread-crumbing the nuggets, otherwise it can get messy."],[null,"To make breadcrumbs, dry out a couple slices of bread in the oven for a few minutes, break into smaller pieces, then use a blender or stick blender to crumb the bread. If it still feels moist and clumpy, spread onto a baking sheet and give it a couple more minutes before blending again."],[null,"Add spices such as smoked paprika, cumin or curry to your flour or breadcrumbs to add extra flavour."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"2039":{"s":[[null,"Chop bell pepper and onion."],[null,"Sauté bell pepper, onion and kale with olive oil on medium heat for about 5 minutes."],[null,"Blend tofu, chickpea flour, cornstarch, almond milk, and seasoning in blender until smooth."],[null,"Pour tofu mixture over vegetables in the pan and cover for 5-10 minutes."],[null,"Uncover, flip over and cook for about 10 minutes. If you have trouble flipping it over, simply stir it and cook like scrambled eggs."]],"h":[[null,"Make sure to use silken tofu, not regular tofu for this recipe. Silken tofu should be low in sodium, but always double check the nutrition label."],[null,"Use a good non-stick pan. If you divide the ingredients in half and use a smaller pan, it will be easier to flip over."],[null,"Use a tiny sprinkling of Indian black salt (Kala Namak) as an option for a sulfur egg-like flavor."]]},"6001726":{"s":[[null,"Prepare the potatoes, eggs, and green beans: Place the halved potatoes in a pot of cold water. Bring to a boil and cook for 10–12 minutes, or until tender. In the final 8 minutes of boiling, gently lower in the eggs. In the final 2 minutes, add the green beans. Drain everything, transfer green beans to an ice bath, and cool the eggs in cold water. Peel and quarter the eggs once cooled."],[null,"Prepare and cook the tofu: In a shallow dish, whisk together the soy sauce, Dijon mustard, olive oil, garlic powder, and black pepper. Add tofu slices and let marinate for 5–10 minutes. Heat a nonstick skillet over medium-high heat. Sear the tofu for 3–4 minutes per side until golden and lightly crisped. Set aside."],[null,"Assemble the salad: On a large platter or individual plates, arrange lettuce, potatoes, green beans, tomatoes, cucumbers, olives, and eggs. Add slices of seared tofu on top. Drizzle with dressing just before serving."]],"h":[]},"7594884":{"s":[[null,"Drain the tofu and pat dry with kitchen paper. Cut into bite-sized pieces and season with freshly ground black pepper."],[null,"Heat a non-stick wok. Lightly spray with oil and add the tofu. Stir-fry quickly over a high heat, stirring until lightly browned. Transfer to a plate."],[null,"Add the shallots and peppers to the wok and stir-fry over a high heat. Add the ginger, baby corn, carrots and mangetout, stir-fry for 2-3 minutes. Add the beansprouts and stir-fry for 2 minutes."],[null,"Fold in the noodles and soy sauce until heated through. Return the tofu to the work and stir well. Serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"For extra flavour, add one or two crushed garlic cloves or 1 tsp Chinese 5 Spice powder."],[null,"You could use 200g chicken, turkey or fish in place of tofu."],[null,"Use rice to make this recipe gluten-free."],[null,"For a higher fibre option, choose wholewheat noodles."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"1798":{"s":[[null,"Squeeze out excess liquid from block of tofu in a clean towel, paper towels or a tofu press."],[null,"Warm up olive oil in a frying pan."],[null,"Crumble up tofu directly into pan in bite-sized pieces."],[null,"Sprinkle turmeric and salt on top and stir ingredients until thoroughly mixed and heated."]],"h":[[null,"Add a light sprinkle of Indian black salt (Kala Namak) as an option. it gives a sulfur taste to the dish, similar to eggs. A tiny bit goes a long way."],[null,"Other seasoning such as cayenne pepper or Mrs. Dash can be added. As well as vegetables of choices such as onions, peppers, and/or mushrooms."],[null,"Serve with toast or as a side dish."]]},"6003360":{"s":[[null,"Heat a large skillet over medium heat and add the olive oil."],[null,"Add the onion, zucchini, garlic, and spices to the skillet. Crumble the tofu with your fingers into the skillet and stir to combine. Sauté until the veggies are softened, 5-7 minutes."],[null,"Remove from the heat and stir in the cherry tomatoes."]],"h":[]},"6935912":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 475 degrees F. Coat a baking sheet with cooking spray and set aside."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together soy sauce and brown sugar substitute."],[null,"Slice tofu into 6 slices. Place on the baking sheet and lightly brush each slice with the soy sauce mixture. Bake for 20 minutes. Cool completely."],[null,"Once the tofu is cool, cut each slice into three smaller slices."],[null,"Divide the mango and cucumber each into 6 equal portions."],[null,"Soak one rice paper wrapper in warm water until softened, about 30 seconds. Lay the rice paper on a clean, flat surface. Place one lettuce leaf on top of the rice paper."],[null,"Place one portion of the mango and cucumber each in the center of the rice paper. Top the vegetables with 3 small slices of tofu and two slices of avocado."],[null,"Fold the left and right sides of the wrapper and lettuces into the middle until almost touching. Roll paper from the bottom to form the roll tightly. Repeat for remaining rice papers. Set aside."],[null,"Combine the sauce ingredients in a small saucepan over high heat. Bring to a boil, stirring constantly. Simmer for 2 minutes. Serve warm with cold spring rolls for dipping."]],"h":[]},"6921480":{"s":[[null,"Mix the tofu and sesame ginger salad dressing in a bowl and marinate for 30 minutes."],[null,"Once the tofu is done marinating, remove the tofu from the marinade and reserve the marinade."],[null,"Add the sesame oil and cooking spray to a wok or large sauté pan over high heat. Add the tofu and stir fry for 7-8 minutes, or until the tofu is golden brown."],[null,"Add the broccoli and mushrooms, and stir fry for 3-4 minutes. Add in the scallions and almonds, and stir fry for an additional 2 minutes."],[null,"In a bowl or cup, whisk together the vegetable broth, cornstarch, soy sauce, hot sauce, brown sugar substitute, and garlic. Whisk in the reserved sesame ginger dressing marinade. Pour the mixture over the tofu and bring to a boil."],[null,"Reduce to a simmer and simmer for 5 minutes."],[null,"Serve Suggestion: Serve over brown rice or in lettuce cups"]],"h":[]},"7153228":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 180°C / gas mark 4. Place the mushroom caps (top-side down) onto a lightly-oiled baking sheet."],[null,"Heat oil in a large pan over a medium heat, then finely chop the mushroom stems and add to the pan with the spring onions and tofu.&nbsp"],[null,"Cook for 3-4 minutes, then add the spinach and pepper and cook for 2-3 minutes, mixing regularly."],[null,"Remove from the heat and mix in the tahini, mustard and basil."],[null,"Mound each mushroom with the tofu mixture and bake for 15- 20 minutes. Top with chopped tomatoes and serve."]],"h":[[null,"You can use leeks in place of spring onions and parsley rather than basil."],[null,"Spice it up with a pinch of chilli flakes or a teaspoon of smoked paprika."],[null,"You could also stuff halved peppers in place of mushrooms"],[null,"Freezing instructions: The mushrooms are suitable for freezing once cooked. Wrap individually in greaseproof paper and without the chopped tomatoes. Defrost for 2 hours, then warm in the microwave or a moderate oven."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"5481420":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a pan and add red peppers and onions, cook for 1-2 minutes."],[null,"Add in the paprika, cumin, coriander and chilli flakes, cook until peppers and onions are soft. Then remove from heat and place into a bowl."],[null,"Heat the oil in the same pan, fry the tofu until golden brown on both sides."],[null,"Once golden, remove from pan and set aside."],[null,"In another bowl place the mashed peas, olive oil, garlic, coriander and lime juice and mix together well."],[null,"Place wraps onto a plate and place the peppers, onions, tofu, and pea guacamole onto the wraps."],[null,"Fold up the bottom of the wraps and then fold the sides over."],[null,"Serve and enjoy!"]],"h":[]},"6461989":{"s":[[null,"Juice lime into a small bowl."],[null,"Add ginger, peanut butter powder, water, soy sauce, and brown sugar to a bowl. Whisk to combine the sauce."],[null,"Preheat a large skillet over medium heat."],[null,"While the skillet heats up, medium dice tofu. Place in a medium bowl, sprinkle with cornstarch, then gently toss to coat."],[null,"Once the skillet is hot, add 2 tsp oil and swirl to coat the bottom. Add tofu and pan-fry, turning occasionally, until browned and crispy, 5–7 minutes. Transfer tofu to a bowl."],[null,"Return the skillet to medium heat. Add remaining oil and broccolini to the skillet. Cook, stirring frequently, until tender-crisp, 4–5 minutes."],[null,"To serve, divide quinoa, tofu, and broccolini between bowls. Drizzle tofu with peanut sauce."]],"h":[]},"6628488":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375°F."],[null,"Lightly grease a nonstick muffin pan or use silicone muffin cups."],[null,"In a food processor or blender, combine tofu, plant-based milk, chickpea flour, olive oil, turmeric, garlic powder, onion powder, salt, and pepper. Blend until smooth and creamy."],[null,"Transfer the tofu mixture to a large bowl. Fold in the sun-dried tomatoes, basil, and chopped bell pepper."],[null,"Spoon the mixture evenly into 8 muffin cups, smoothing the tops."],[null,"Bake for 25–30 minutes, or until the tops are firm and lightly golden. Let cool for 5 minutes in the pan before removing."],[null,"Serve warm, or cool completely and refrigerate for up to 4 days."]],"h":[]},"6471870":{"s":[[null,"Cook the ramen noodles according to package instructions. Drain and set aside."],[null,"In a large pot, heat sesame oil over medium heat. Add sliced onion, minced garlic, and grated ginger. Sauté until the onion is translucent."],[null,"Pour in the vegetable broth and water and bring to a simmer."],[null,"Add sliced mushrooms, broccoli florets, chopped bok choy, shredded carrots, and cubed tofu to the pot. Simmer for about 5–7 minutes until the vegetables are tender."],[null,"Stir in coconut aminos and rice vinegar."],[null,"Divide the cooked ramen noodles among serving bowls. Ladle the vegetable-rich broth over the noodles and garnish with green onion."]],"h":[]},"6102737":{"s":[[null,"Set oven broiler to high. Place tomatillos, chiles, onion, and unpeeled garlic on a foil-lined baking sheet. Broil about 5-7 minutes, flipping once, until charred in spots and tomatillos have softened and turned olive-green."],[null,"Cool slightly, then peel the garlic cloves."],[null,"Add roasted vegetables, cilantro, lime juice, salt, and cumin to a blender or food processor. Pulse until you reach your desired texture—chunky or smooth."],[null,"Taste and adjust the salt and/or lime. Thin the salsa with a little bit of water if it’s too thick."],[null,"Chill for 30 minutes before serving for the best flavor."]],"h":[]},"6328863":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a large saucepan over medium-high heat. Add the onion and cook while stirring until lightly golden, about 5 minutes. Add the garlic and cook while stirring until fragrant, about 1 minute."],[null,"Stir in thawed okra, canned tomatoes (with liquid), and thyme, and cook uncovered until liquids are reduced to desired consistency, about 5 minutes, stirring occasionally. Serve."]],"h":[]},"6866643":{"s":[[null,"Whisk the eggs in a bowl and season with salt and pepper."],[null,"Heat the oil in a small non-stick pan over medium heat."],[null,"Pour the beaten eggs into the pan."],[null,"Sprinkle diced tomato and chopped basil on half the omelet."],[null,"Once the eggs are set, fold the omelet in half and cook until the tomato softens, about 30 seconds."]],"h":[]},"6926509":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, combine the peaches, tomatoes, cherry tomatoes, and red onion, and gently toss."],[null,"In a small bowl or measuring cup, whisk together the vinegar, lemon juice, and honey. Slowly add the oil in a thin stream, whisking to emulsify. Add the salt and black pepper."],[null,"Add the dressing to the peaches and tomatoes, and gently toss. Fold in the mint leaves. To serve, turn out the salad onto a large platter."]],"h":[]},"7859144":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a non-stick pan. Add the onion and fry for 2-3 minutes until softened."],[null,"Stir in the rice and coat in the oil. Pour in the tomatoes and stock, bring to the boil and simmer gently for 15-20 minutes, stirring continuously, until the rice is just tender."],[null,"Stir through the remaining ingredients, season well, heat through and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Keep a kettle of boiling water handy. If the risotto starts to stick you can add a dash of water. As long as you use boiling water, it won’t stop the rice from cooking as you add it."],[null,"Stirring a risotto constantly during cooking helps make it more creamy."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Chill quickly. Defrost in the fridge and reheat thoroughly until piping-hot throughout. Eat immediately and discard any leftovers."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"7108939":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a medium frying pan, add the onion and garlic and fry for 2–3 minutes until the onion begins to soften."],[null,"Add the chilli flakes (if using) and the tomatoes and gently squash with a wooden spoon. Bring to the boil and simmer over a low heat for about 10 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, cook the pasta according to the pack instructions and drain."],[null,"Stir the pasta through the sauce with the flaked tuna and serve topped with Parmesan cheese and basil (if using).."]],"h":[[null,"This is great served with salad if you have any. If not, add 1 cup of peas to the pasta 2 minutes before the end of cooking time to add colour and extra goodness – remember, this will increase your vegetable portion intake."],[null,"You could use a tin of salmon in place of tuna."],[null,"If your children are fussy eaters, look out for unusual pasta shapes to make food more appealing."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"6518949":{"s":[[null,"In a mixing bowl, combine the diced tomatoes, diced zucchini, finely chopped red onion, chopped cilantro, and minced jalapeño pepper. Add the minced garlic to the mixture. Drizzle the fresh lime juice over the ingredients. Season the salsa with salt and pepper."],[null,"Gently toss all the ingredients together until they are well mixed and coated with the lime juice and seasonings."],[null,"Let the salsa sit for about 10–15 minutes to allow the flavors to meld together. Adjust the seasoning to suit your preference"]],"h":[]},"7136807":{"s":[[null,"Heat the grill, and place the tomatoes onto a baking sheet, cut-side down. Grill for 3-4 minutes, then turn over and grill for a further 3-4 minutes until slightly browned."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the leeks to a microwave proof dish with a teaspoon of water, cover with film and cook on full power for 2-3 minutes until soft, allow to cool a little and drain off any excess liquid."],[null,"Cut the bagels in half, toast, then spread with cream cheese and scatter with leek. Place 3 tomato halves on one bagel half, sprinkle with chives and black pepper, then top with another bagel half. Repeat with the other bagel."],[null,"Top each with a little cream cheese, another tomato half and a little leek then garnish with the remaining chives and black pepper."]],"h":[[null,"Try adding cottage cheese or, for a vegan bagel, use a non-dairy alternative."],[null,"Experiment with different herbs such as basil, or try rubbing the toasted bagel with a clove of garlic."],[null,"Also delicious with grilled mushrooms in place of tomatoes."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"2965":{"s":[[null,"Cut tomatoes in half and discard the flesh to make “boats.”"],[null,"Lightly drizzle inside of the tomato boats with 1/2 tablespoon olive oil, 1/2 teaspoon pepper,1/2 teaspoon garlic powder and 1/2 teaspoon salt-free seasoning."],[null,"Rinse and drain chickpeas. In a bowl, add chickpeas, remaining olive oil, spices, juice of 1/2 lemon and vinegar. Mix together."],[null,"Spoon chickpea mixture into the tomato cups. Garnish with a mint leaf."],[null,"Refrigerate and serve chilled."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute 1/4 medium red bell pepper for each tomato half if desired. Potassium is 12 mg lower."],[null,"Chickpeas, also known as garbanzo beans, and other legumes are high in potassium and phosphorus. Small amounts can be included in a healthy kidney diet to increase fiber. Each boat contains approximately 1/6 cup of chickpeas."],[null,"Removing the pulp from tomatoes reduces the potassium content."]]},"6248410":{"s":[[null,"Thinly slice tomatoes."],[null,"On four small plates, layer the salad by placing tomato, basil, and fresh mozzarella in an alternating pattern."],[null,"Drizzle with olive oil and season with salt and pepper."],[null,"Drizzle 1 tsp premade balsamic glaze on the tomatoes."]],"h":[]},"6226156":{"s":[],"h":[]},"7460222":{"s":[[null,"Place all ingredients in a small saucepan."],[null,"Simmer for 5-6 minutes until reduced slightly."],[null,"Puree and set aside to cool."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"7832382":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a saucepan, add the onion and cook for 2 minutes until it starts to brown then add the garlic and cook a further 1-2 minutes."],[null,"Add all the other ingredients and simmer gently for 5 minutes."],[null,"Blend to a smooth consistency and serve."]],"h":[[null,"To make the sauce thicker for a pizza, just simmer gently for an extra 5-10 minutes stirring regularly to cook off more of the liquid."],[null,"To get more veggies into fussy kids, add a finely chopped red pepper with the onions."],[null,"Turn into a Putanesca sauce by adding a good pinch of chilli flakes, black olives and a few capers."],[null,"Freeze in plastic cups then wrap in freezer bags once frozen."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"7367467":{"s":[[null,"Spray a large saucepan with low-calorie cooking spray and place over a medium-high heat. Add the onion and 4tbsp water and cook for 3–4 minutes until the water has evaporated and the onion is softened."],[null,"Add the garlic and smoked paprika and cook for 1–2 minutes."],[null,"Add the chopped tomatoes, tomato purée and peppers. Bring to the boil, cover and simmer over a low heat for 15 minutes."],[null,"Add the butterbeans and kale. Stir well, push the kale beneath the sauce and cook uncovered for 6–8 minutes until wilted."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"7958217":{"s":[[null,"Preheat a grill or barbecue to a high heat. Cook the asparagus stems for 1–2 minutes on each side or until tender."],[null,"Place the asparagus, haricot beans, tomatoes, green olives, fresh basil and lemon zest in a large bowl."],[null,"Whisk the olive oil, balsamic vinegar and lemon juice in a small jug."],[null,"Drizzle the dressing over the salad, toss to combine and serve."]],"h":[[null,"If you don’t like olives, use thinly sliced sundried tomatoes instead."],[null,"This is ideal as part of a summer buffet and/or to accompany fresh tuna or salmon."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"1002863":{"s":[[null,"Cook macaroni in three cups of hot water with one teaspoon oil for 20 minutes. Once cooked, drain, rinse with room-temperature water and set aside."],[null,"Cook chicken breast in a cup of water with the two chopped garlic cloves, the red onion cut into large pieces and the cumin. Once the chicken is cooked, let it cool and shred it."],[null,"Finely dice the white onion (brunoise) and sauté in a skillet with the 3 tablespoons margarine and one teaspoon sunflower oil. Then add to the macaroni along with the chicken."],[null,"Beat eggs with the cup of milk and add to the mixture. Stir ingredients very well and pour into a greased and floured pan to keep it from sticking."],[null,"Bake in an oven preheated to 180° C for 25 minutes or until golden."]],"h":[[null,"Turkey can be substituted for chicken in this recipe."]]},"1730":{"s":[[null,"Heat a large skillet over medium heat. Pan fry steaks, turning once to desired doneness. Drain, rinse, and mash beans."],[null,"Slice rolls and spread 1 tablespoon sour cream on each side. Top with 2 tablespoons mashed pinto beans per sandwich, on the bottom bun. Place 1 cooked steak on each sandwich on top of pinto beans"],[null,"Slice tomato; peel, pit and slice avocado; and slice jalapeno peppers into quarters lengthwise. Layer each sandwich with a portion of tomato slices, avocado, pickled jalapeno slices, 2 tablespoons cilantro, 1/4 cup lettuce and 2 tablespoons queso fresco cheese."],[null,"Quarter lime and squeeze juice of 1 wedge over each sandwich, close and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Steak can be substituted for chicken, or removed completely for a vegetarian option."],[null,"This sandwich is a little higher in potassium. Consider the rest of your meals for the days, serve with a lower potassium side. Potassium from whole foods like beans are not 100% absorbed by our body, which should also be considered."],[null,"If you are on a lower potassium diet, you may leave off the avocado and tomato."],[null,"If you are on a lower protein diet, you may leave off the beef stead and just make it a vegetarian sandwich."]]},"3018":{"s":[[null,"Slice the roast beef and cucumber; chop the onion and bell pepper. Remove rib from romaine lettuce leaf."],[null,"To prepare the beef rollup, spread cream cheese on the tortilla. Layer roast beef slices and vegetables on top. Sprinkle with herb seasoning."],[null,"Roll tortilla up like a jelly roll and cut into 4 pieces."],[null,"Place rollup, grapes and almonds on a plate or in divided lunch container."]],"h":[[null,"Beverage suggestions: lemonade, flavored sparkling water, lemon-lime soda, fresh brewed tea or coffee."],[null,"For an on-the-go meal pack a lunch box with an ice pack to keep food cool until ready to eat."]]},"1747":{"s":[[null,"Spread cream cheese over tortillas."],[null,"Divide ingredients in half to make two torillas. Layer each tortilla with roast beef, red onion, pepper strips, cucumbers and lettuce."],[null,"Sprinkle with Mrs. Dash® herb seasoning blend."],[null,"Roll up like a jellyroll."],[null,"Slice each tortilla into 4 pieces, or serve whole."]],"h":[[null,"Rollups keep well in the refrigerator up to 2 days. Make ahead and eat as a high-protein snack or quick meal."],[null,"Whipped cream cheese spreads easier than regular cream cheese."],[null,"Check tortilla labels to compare sodium content and choose the lowest sodium brand."]]},"2474":{"s":[[null,"Spread cream cheese over tortillas."],[null,"Layer half the amount of roast beef, red onion, pepper strips, cucumber and lettuce on each tortilla."],[null,"Sprinkle with Mrs. Dash® herb seasoning."],[null,"Roll up like a jellyroll."],[null,"Slice each tortilla into 4 pieces, or serve whole."]],"h":[[null,"Whipped cream cheese spreads easier than regular cream cheese."],[null,"Check tortilla labels to compare sodium content and choose the lowest sodium brand."]]},"6040267":{"s":[[null,"In a bowl, season the egg substitute with salt and pepper and mix everything together."],[null,"Heat the olive oil in a nonstick skillet over medium heat."],[null,"Add the diced red onions and sauté until softened."],[null,"Add the chopped spinach to the skillet and cook until wilted."],[null,"Pour the eggs over the spinach and onions."],[null,"As the eggs begin to set, sprinkle diced tomatoes and crumbled feta cheese over half of the omelet."],[null,"Once the eggs are completely cooked, carefully fold the omelet in half with a spatula."],[null,"Slide the omelet onto a plate, garnish with fresh herbs if desired, and serve."]],"h":[]},"2565":{"s":[[null,"Chop spinach. Dice onion, pimento and turkey breast. Drain pineapple."],[null,"Spread cream cheese over each tortilla to cover. Sprinkle with Mrs. Dash® herb seasoning."],[null,"Place remaining ingredients in a bowl and mix."],[null,"Divide mixed ingredients into 2 portions. Place half on each tortillas and roll up like a jelly roll."],[null,"Trim ends and slice each roll into 6 pieces."]],"h":[[null,"Wrap un-cut roll in plastic wrap and refrigerate until ready to cut and serve."],[null,"Compare tortilla brands and select the lowest in sodium."]]},"2310":{"s":[[null,"Grate carrots. Chop green pepper and cucumber. Shred chicken."],[null,"Mix garlic and onion powder into cream cheese."],[null,"Spread half of the mixture over each tortilla."],[null,"Add vegetables and meat."],[null,"Roll up wrap and refrigerate or serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"Make ahead and refrigerate for up to 2 days."],[null,"Works with any flatbread wrap."],[null,"Looks delicious cut in half and arranged on a plate with fresh blueberries and strawberries. Add a cold glass of fresh-squeezed lemonade."],[null,"Coleslaw mix can be substituted for broccoli slaw and grated carrots, or try other low potassium vegetable as substitutes."],[null,"For variety try turkey or roast beef instead of chicken."]]},"7822207":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a non-stick frying pan. Add the onion and red pepper and fry for 2-3 minutes, until softened. Add the chicken and fry for 3-4 minutes until browned and cooked through."],[null,"Meanwhile, in a bowl, mash together the kidney beans and crème fraiche. Warm the tortillas."],[null,"Divide the bean mixture between the tortillas and spoon over the chicken mixture. Add the carrot and salad leaves, season well, roll up and serve."]],"h":[[null,"You could use sliced turkey escalopes in place of chicken."],[null,"For a veggie version, replace the chicken with 200g sliced mushrooms."],[null,"Tortillas freeze well so you can freeze the pack and use as needed."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"6032610":{"s":[[null,"Place 1 cup of air popped popcorn in a small bowl."],[null,"Add 1 ounce of mixed nuts over the top."],[null,"Sprinkle in 2 tablespoons of raisins."],[null,"Toss gently to combine and enjoy immediately."]],"h":[]},"6244327":{"s":[[null,"In a large dry skillet over medium heat, toast the raw pepitas, almonds, and walnuts for about 3–5 minutes, or until they become fragrant and lightly browned. Stir frequently to prevent burning."],[null,"Remove the toasted pepitas and nuts from the skillet and let them cool completely."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine the toasted pepitas, almonds, and walnuts with the sunflower seeds, unsweetened dried cranberries, ground cinnamon, and sea salt. Toss all the ingredients together until they are well combined."],[null,"Portion the trail mix into ⅓-cup individual servings or store it in an airtight container for later use."]],"h":[]},"1934":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Pour cherry pie filling into an ungreased 8” x 8” x 2” baking pan. Stir in almond extract."],[null,"In a medium mixing bowl, combine flour, brown sugar (or Splenda® brown sugar blend) and cinnamon; mix well. Add butter; stir with a fork until mixture is crumbly. Sprinkle mixture over pie filling."],[null,"Bake for 25 minutes, or until golden brown on top and filling is bubbly."],[null,"Serve warm or at room temperature. If desired, top with whipped topping."]],"h":[[null,"If you have diabetes, you can reduce carbohydrate to 34 grams by substituting lite pie filling and 1/4 cup Splenda brown sugar blend instead of 1/2 cup brown sugar. Count as 2 carb choices. Alternatively you could cut the portion to 1/4 cup."],[null,"Comstock® brand pie filling is available in regular and lite, reduced calorie."]]},"7356133":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4."],[null,"Blanch the green beans for 4 minutes in boiling water, and drain."],[null,"Spread the green beans, spring onions, peas, red pepper and cherry tomatoes out on an ovenproof dish."],[null,"Place the salmon on top, skin side up, and drizzle with the lemon juice and water. Cover with foil."],[null,"Bake for 20 minutes then check the fish is cooked through and if necessary bake for a further 5 minutes (depending on the thickness of your steaks)."],[null,"Serve with wedges of lemon."]],"h":[[null,"Works with other fish steaks such as cod, haddock or coley."],[null,"You could prepare in advance and leave refrigerated for a few hours until you’re ready to bake it."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Chill quickly. Defrost in the fridge and reheat thoroughly until piping-hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"6215386":{"s":[[null,"Heat oil over medium heat in a large saucepan. Sauté onion, garlic, and ginger for 2 minutes, stirring well."],[null,"Add zucchini, jalapeño pepper, and potato and sauté for 2 minutes longer. Add curry powder, chickpeas, tomato, water or vegetable stock, and scallions. Simmer for 20 minutes until potato is cooked through and a light sauce is formed."],[null,"Season with lemon juice and serve."]],"h":[]},"6101957":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F. Spray an 8x8 baking pan with cooking spray."],[null,"In a large bowl combine the oats, baking powder, cinnamon, nutmeg, and brown sugar substitute. Add the walnuts and berries in and toss to combine."],[null,"In a medium bowl, blend the egg substitute, milk, salt, butter, and vanilla extract. Stir to dissolve the salt."],[null,"Pour the liquid ingredients into the oats mixture and mix."],[null,"Pour the mixture into the prepared baking pan and spread into an even layer."],[null,"Place the pan in the middle of the preheated oven and bake for 45 minutes, or until the center is firm to touch."],[null,"Remove from the oven and allow to cool on a wire rack for 10–15 minutes."],[null,"Serve with 1/4 cup skim milk and a drizzle of sugar-free syrup if desired."]],"h":[]},"2061":{"s":[[null,"Cut strawberries into quarters. Combine all berries in mixing bowl and drizzle with honey (or desired sweetener) to taste."],[null,"Let stand 10 minutes."],[null,"Place whipped topping in a bowl and add protein powder. Whisk gently to incorporate protein powder into whipped topping."],[null,"Layer berries and whipped topping in alternating layers into parfait glass or bowl. Serve and enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"You can use either fresh or frozen fruit."],[null,"Jamie uses ProSource® protein powder and Stevia sweetener when she makes the parfait, but you can substitute your preferred brands."],[null,"You may substitute a packet of no-calorie sweetener in place of the honey. This will cut the added sugar to 0 g."]]},"2781":{"s":[[null,"Wash all berries well."],[null,"Slice strawberries and combine with remaining berries in a bowl."],[null,"Add lemon juice."],[null,"Place cottage cheese on a serving plate or bowl, then top with berries."],[null,"Sprinkle with ground cinnamon (optional)."]],"h":[[null,"Berries are a great source of antioxidants. Lemons are high in Vitamin C, and also a good source of antioxidants. Antioxidants help neutralize free radicals inside the body and keep cells healthy."]]},"6174318":{"s":[[null,"Combine all ingredients in a blender and process until smooth. Pour into a bowl, cover, and chill."],[null,"Store in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to one week."]],"h":[]},"6955115":{"s":[[null,"Combine all three ingredients and serve."]],"h":[]},"6764912":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350° F."],[null,"Cook the quinoa according to the package instructions, omitting any added salt."],[null,"Place the coconut and almonds on a baking sheet and toast in the oven for about 6 minutes. Stir every 2 minutes to prevent burning."],[null,"Heat the oil in a nonstick pan over medium-high heat. Sauté the kale and pineapple chunks for about 4 minutes."],[null,"Combine the quinoa, kale mixture, coconut and almonds, and the rest of the ingredients. Stir well. Scoop equal amounts into bowls and serve warm or cold, according to your preference."]],"h":[]},"4910262":{"s":[[null,"Combine pineapple, mango, lime juice, vanilla extract and 1/2 cup crushed ice in a blender."],[null,"Puree until smooth."],[null,"Fill each glass with 1 tablespoon crushed ice, half of the fruit mix and add 1/4 cup sparkling water. Stir and garnish with a slice of lime!"]],"h":[["How to incorporate citrus in a low-potassium diet","A variety of fruit adds valuable vitamins, minerals, and fiber to any kidney diet. In earlier stages of chronic kidney disease, fruit plays an important part in a healthy diet, with research suggesting that these foods are beneficial to overall kidney health. As kidney disease progresses, the amount and type of fruit you choose may need to be adjusted as part of a low-potassium diet. Depending on the kind, citrus fruit can contain different amounts of potassium. Working with a registered dietitian nutritionist is a great way to find out which citrus fruits can be safely included in your diet. Higher-potassium citrus fruit (1 whole fruit): grapefruit, oranges, orange juice, pomelo Moderate- and lower-potassium citrus fruit: clementine orange, kumquat, lemon, lime, canned mandarin oranges, pineapple, tangerine, ugli fruit"]]},"6987547":{"s":[[null,"Place the drained tuna in a medium bowl and gently stir in the avocado and mango."],[null,"Mix the mayonnaise, lime juice, and lime zest together in a small bowl then gently combine with the tuna mixture."],[null,"Place the lettuce cups on a platter. Divide the tuna mixture between the lettuce leaves and top each with the chopped pistachios."]],"h":[]},"7619702":{"s":[[null,"Place the trout fillets into a non-stick frying pan."],[null,"Pour over the orange zest and juice, cover and simmer gently for 5–6 minutes until the trout is cooked."],[null,"Gently stir in the basil and crème fraîche and heat through. Season to taste."]],"h":[[null,"Many supermarkets also sell thick-cut steaks from large trout rather than fillets from the traditional smaller fish. These need a little longer to cook through (2–3 minutes longer depending on size)."],[null,"You could use dill or parsley in place of basil."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"6783809":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, combine the drained tuna, diced avocados, cucumber, and red onion."],[null,"In a smaller bowl, whisk together the extra virgin olive oil, red wine vinegar, Dijon mustard, minced garlic, salt, and black pepper."],[null,"Pour the dressing over the salad and gently toss to ensure even coating."],[null,"Serve on top of the mixed salad greens and fresh herbs."]],"h":[]},"6419902":{"s":[[null,"In a mixing bowl, combine the drained tuna, mashed ripe avocado, plain Greek yogurt, fresh lemon juice, finely chopped green onions, finely diced celery, garlic powder, salt, and pepper. Stir the ingredients until well combined, ensuring the tuna and avocado are evenly distributed and the mixture has a creamy consistency."],[null,"Taste the spread and adjust the seasonings, adding more salt, pepper, or lemon juice as needed to suit your taste."]],"h":[]},"7863056":{"s":[[null,"Chop the herbs finely, then mix all the ingredients together and form into 12 walnut- sized balls."],[null,"Add the oil from the tin of tuna to a frying pan and brown the tuna balls for 10-12 minutes turning regularly."],[null,"Meanwhile, heat the passata, add the tuna balls and serve with a lemon wedge."]],"h":[[null,"If you don't have fresh herbs, use 2 tsps of dried, mixed herbs."],[null,"You could add a pinch of chilli flakes or a crushed clove of garlic to spice them up a little."],[null,"Portion sizes for children will vary depending on their age and nutritional needs. The nutrition information is based on an adults serving size."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"3239":{"s":[[null,"Drain tuna and pour into a small mixing bowl. Flake with a fork."],[null,"Chop cilantro and onion."],[null,"Mix the cilantro, onion, black pepper and Mrs. Dash seasoning and blend with the tuna."],[null,"Pour fresh lemon juice over the tuna mixture and mix ingredients well."],[null,"Cover and place in refrigerator to marinate for at least 2 hours."],[null,"Serve 1/4 cup ceviche with 6 saltine crackers, unsalted tops or 4 low-sodium whole wheat crackers."]],"h":[[null,"If low-sodium, canned tuna is unavailable, look for the brand of tuna lowest in sodium and rinse under running water for 1 to 2 minutes to further reduce sodium content."],[null,"Traditional ceviche is made from raw fish or seafood marinated in lemon or lime juice. Acid from the lemon “cooks” the fish. This is a safer version of ceviche for kidney patients."],[null,"Substitute parsley for cilantro if desired."],[null,"Water crackers and low sodium triskets are great replacements for the unsalted saltines or whole wheat crackers."]]},"6576870":{"s":[[null,"Combine the tuna, onion, cilantro, black pepper, and seasoning blend in a small bowl. Add the lemon juice and mix everything together well. Cover and refrigerate for at least 2 hours to marinate before serving."]],"h":[]},"4653203":{"s":[[null,"In a large pot, bring water to boil and cook pasta according to instructions on package."],[null,"Heat oil in a large skillet over medium heat. Sauté garlic with chili flakes and black pepper (2 minutes). Be careful not to burn the garlic."],[null,"Add artichokes, tuna, arugula, parsley and lemon juice to skillet and cook until arugula wilts."],[null,"Add the pasta to the sauce and toss it."],[null,"Sprinkle the pasta with parmesan cheese and serve."]],"h":[[null,"* Artichoke is a high potassium vegetable and should be enjoyed in moderation."]]},"6410737":{"s":[[null,"In a large glass baking dish, stir together the marinade ingredients. Remove and set aside 2 tablespoons of the marinade."],[null,"Add the fish to the marinade remaining in the dish, turning to coat. Cover and refrigerate for 15 minutes-1 hour, turning occasionally."],[null,"Drain the fish, discarding the marinade. Pat the fish dry with paper towels."],[null,"Lightly spray the grill rack with cooking spray. Preheat the grill on medium high. Or lightly spray a large indoor grill pan with cooking spray. Heat over medium-high heat."],[null,"Meanwhile, soak six 12-inch wooden skewers for at least 10 minutes in cold water to keep them from charring, or use metal skewers. Lightly spray the skewers with cooking spray. For each kebab, thread each skewer with 2 tuna cubes, 2 bell pepper squares, 2 slices of squash, 2 onion wedges, 2 pineapple cubes, and 2 tomatoes. Baste with the reserved marinade."],[null,"Grill the kebabs for 4 minutes. Turn over. Grill for 3-5 minutes, or until the fish is cooked to the desired doneness."]],"h":[]},"2869":{"s":[[null,"Chop onion, cilantro and garlic."],[null,"Place all ingredients, except the oil, in a bowl. Stir until well mixed."],[null,"Heat oil in a skillet over medium heat."],[null,"Spoon the tuna mixture into the skillet to make one large patty. Fry until golden brown and crispy, turning once."],[null,"Divide tuna patty into 4 equal portions. Serve with pita bread and a lemon wedge."]],"h":[[null,"Koko sandwich can be baked instead of fried. Heat oven to 350° F, place mixture in an oiled baking dish and bake for 50 to 60 minutes, until top is golden brown. Cut into 4 portions."],[null,"For a twist, try making koko sandwich with chicken instead of tuna."],[null,"Lavash bread, flour tortilla or white bread may be used in place of the pita bread, if desired."],[null,"Use 1-1/4 cups low-cholesterol egg product for a lower cholesterol dish."]]},"54953":{"s":[[null,"Drain tuna. Mix mayonnaise, black pepper and tuna in a bowl. Evenly divide mixture between hamburger bun bottoms."],[null,"Place cheese on top of tuna mixture, preheat oven to 350F. Place tuna half and top of the bun (face up) on a baking sheet. Bake for 15 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile slice cucumber, green pepper and red onion. Shred or chop lettuce. Remove sandwiches from oven and layer vegetables evenly on top. Plate and serve. May save the second sandwich for another day or share with family or friends."]],"h":[[null,"This recipe is higher in potassium, but it is naturally occurring from vegetables and tuna. From vegetables sources our bodies only absorb about 40-60% of the natural potassium."],[null,"If you are on a lower protein diet, you may cut back on the amount of tuna by half or a third."]]},"7434527":{"s":[[null,"Put the potatoes in a large pan, cover with cold water and bring to the boil. Reduce the heat to medium and cook for 5 minutes. Add the beans and cook for 4 minutes until the potatoes are tender and the beans are cooked but still firm. Drain and transfer to a large bowl."],[null,"Meanwhile, put all the dressing ingredients in a clean jar. Seal with a tight-fitting lid and shake until combined. Drizzle half the dressing over the potatoes and beans and toss to combine. Add the lettuce to the bowl and toss again to coat."],[null,"Arrange the dressed salad on a serving platter or in a large salad bowl, then top with the tuna, capers and olives. Drizzle over the remaining dressing and serve."]],"h":[[null,"If you don't have tuna, you can swap it out for any kind of tinned fish."],[null,"You could swap the herbes de Provence for any dried herbs."],[null,"You could also use sweet potatoes instead of new potatoes."]]},"1710":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F. Boil the egg noodles according to the package instructions, omitting the salt. Drain and flake the tuna."],[null,"In a medium bowl combine the sour cream, cottage cheese, tuna, mushrooms and peas."],[null,"Drain the cooked noodles and stir into the tuna mixture. Place into a small casserole dish sprayed with nonstick cooking spray."],[null,"Melt the butter and stir into the bread crumbs. Sprinkle over the noodle mixture."],[null,"Bake for 20 to 25 minutes until bread crumbs begin to brown. Divide into 2 servings and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Extra serving can be refrigerated for 2 to 3 days."],[null,"Add your favorite hot sauce if you like the heat and spice."]]},"2747":{"s":[[null,"Chop celery, bell pepper and green onion."],[null,"Combine cooked pasta, celery, bell pepper, onion and lemon zest in a mixing bowl."],[null,"In a separate bowl, whisk together mayonnaise and salad dressing."],[null,"Pour dressing over pasta mixture."],[null,"Add tuna to pasta mixture."],[null,"Mix gently until all ingredients are moist and well blended."],[null,"Refrigerate one hour to let flavors blend."]],"h":[[null,"Macaroni can be substituted for bow-tie pasta."],[null,"Make low-sodium dressing using the Italian Dressing recipe on DaVita.com or shop for Italian dressing with lowest sodium content. Powdered dressing mix is a good choice because the sodium can be adjusted by using less of the mix."],[null,"If low-sodium tuna is unavailable, reduce sodium in regular tuna by rinsing for one minute."]]},"4061703":{"s":[[null,"Drain the tuna and flake it with a fork."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine tuna, apple, onion, and the mayonnaise. Add hot sauce, lemon juice, and pepper to taste."],[null,"Fold the lettuce and carrots into the tuna mixture."],[null,"Cut the pita bread into two halves. Carefully open each half to make a pocket. Fill each pocket with half of the salad."]],"h":[["Foods with omega-3 fatty acids","Omega-3 fatty acids should be included as part of a kidney-friendly diet. This type of healthy fat comes from the food that you eat and unlike other fat, cannot be made in the body. With chronic kidney disease, foods with omega-3 fatty acids are important to consume because this type of fat helps to lower blood pressure, control blood sugar, decrease unhealthy blood fat levels, and protect how well your kidneys work. Different types of foods offer the health benefits of omega-3 fatty acids and can come from plant or animal sources. Depending on the type and amount of these foods that you consume, many can easily be consumed as part of a lower-potassium diet. Plant sources higher in this fatty acid include canola or olive oil, walnuts, flax seed, and leafy green vegetables. Certain types of fish also naturally have omega-3 fatty acids such as salmon, cod, and canned light tuna. In fact, in one 3-ounce portion of farm-raised salmon there is over 2,000 mg of omega-3 fatty acids while a 3-ounce serving of light tuna offers 228 mg. On a lower-potassium diet, choosing foods that have healthy fats such as omega-3 fatty acids is recommended."]]},"2208":{"s":[[null,"Drain tuna from can, and place in small mixing bowl. Dice celery and red onion."],[null,"Add mayonnaise, diced celery, diced onion, and spices to tuna bowl. Mix to combine."],[null,"Slice and skin cucumbers into spears. Slice apple into thin slices. Use 5 slices of cucumber from a medium cucumber for each box, if you are unable to find mini cucumbers."],[null,"Use two bento boxes. Put half he tuna mix, half of the carrots and half the cucumber to the boxes. Slice eggs in half and add 1 egg and 1 rice cake to each box."]],"h":[[null,"StarKist® Select brand (approximately 65mg Sodium per can)."],[null,"To make perfect hard-boiled eggs: add eggs to pan, and cover with water. Let water boil for 5 minutes, turn water off and leave egg in water for 10 minutes. Rinse in cool water, and peel immediately."],[null,"Instead of rice cakes, you may also use multi-grain crackers or corn thins. Stick to the serving on the box and look for lower sodium varieties."],[null,"The potassium is within a good range since this is considered a whole meal."]]},"1937":{"s":[[null,"Break tuna into fine pieces."],[null,"Finely chop onion and celery."],[null,"Combine tuna, celery, onion and mayonnaise."],[null,"Mix well."],[null,"Spread mixture on bagel with lettuce leaf."]],"h":[[null,"Check tuna ingredients and avoid brands with phosphate additives."]]},"6972957":{"s":[[null,"In a medium bowl, combine drained tuna, Greek yogurt, Dijon mustard, celery, diced carrots, garlic powder, and black pepper. Mix well until evenly combined."],[null,"Preheat a non-stick skillet or griddle over medium heat."],[null,"Spread the tuna salad evenly over each muffin half and top each with ½ tablespoon of cheese."],[null,"Spray the skillet with cooking spray. Place the assembled muffins onto the skillet, cover, and cook on low heat until the cheese melts, about 3–4 minutes. Remove from heat."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine mixed greens, cherry tomatoes, cucumber, and shredded carrots. Drizzle with balsamic vinegar and olive oil, then toss to coat."],[null,"Plate 2 muffin halves per serving alongside the salad."]],"h":[]},"6502606":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to broil (500°F). Line a baking sheet with parchment paper or aluminum foil (spritz with baking spray) and set aside"],[null,"Slice the tops off the tomatoes and carefully cut around the inner edge to release the core. Use a spoon to remove the seeds and membrane of the tomatoes to create hollow tomatoes."],[null,"In a medium bowl, combine tuna, mayonnaise, celery, shallot, and celery salt."],[null,"Stuff tomatoes with the tuna mixture and top with a slice of cheese."],[null,"Place tomatoes on the baking sheet and broil for 3–5 minutes, until the cheese melts and begins to brown."]],"h":[]},"6768885":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together yogurt, mayonnaise and lemon juice."],[null,"In a medium bowl, combine remaining ingredients. Pour mayonnaise mixture over tuna and mix well."],[null,"Serve tuna salad on your choice of lettuce, whole-wheat bread or crackers."]],"h":[]},"2581":{"s":[[null,"Dice bell peppers and thinly slice zucchini; Chop green onions and basil; mince garlic."],[null,"Pour 3/4 cup of water into a medium saucepan."],[null,"Place diced bell peppers and sliced zucchini into a steamer basket and place over the saucepan. Heat water to a boil and steam vegetables for 10 minutes."],[null,"Remove vegetables from heat, drain off any excess water and transfer to a serving bowl."],[null,"Add tuna, green onions and basil. Toss to combine ingredients."],[null,"To make dressing, combine vinegar, oil, garlic and black pepper in a jar with a tight-fitting lid and shake well."],[null,"Pour dressing over tuna and vegetable mixture and mix well."]],"h":[[null,"Recipe analysis includes low-sodium, canned tuna. If regular canned tuna is used, sodium is 160 mg per serving. Rinse tuna to further reduce sodium."]]},"6977174":{"s":[[null,"Add the olive oil to a soup pot over medium-high heat."],[null,"Add the onion, carrots, celery, and mushrooms to the pot. Sauté for 8 to 10 minutes, or until the onions start to turn clear."],[null,"Add the barley, broth, and water. Bring to a boil, then reduce the heat and simmer for 15 minutes."],[null,"Add the turkey. Season with the salt and pepper. Cook until the turkey is heated, then serve."]],"h":[]},"6277295":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, mix together avocado and Greek yogurt."],[null,"Spread avocado mixture evenly onto 4 tortillas."],[null,"Top each tortilla with 3 ounces turkey, 1 Tsp. sunflower seeds, 2 slices tomato and 1/4 cup lettuce."]],"h":[]},"6588001":{"s":[[null,"In a large skillet, heat the olive oil over medium heat and cook the ground turkey until browned, breaking it apart with a spoon as it cooks."],[null,"Add the chili powder, cumin, paprika, coarse salt, and black pepper to the skillet and cook for 3 minutes to toast spices."],[null,"Add the bell pepper and onions and cooked until softened. Add in the diced tomatoes and stir well to combine."],[null,"Simmer the mixture for about 10 minutes, allowing the flavors to meld and the ingredients to heat through."],[null,"In a separate skillet, warm the rice and black beans together."],[null,"To assemble each bowl, layer ¼ cup brown rice, ¼ cup black beans, ½ cup lettuce, and about ½ cup of the ground turkey mixture."],[null,"Top each bowl with about 1 Tbsp of the shredded Mexican blend cheese and chopped cilantro. Serve with lime wedges on the side."]],"h":[]},"1784":{"s":[[null,"In a large skillet add turkey and beef. Sauté until brown."],[null,"Chop onion, green pepper and garlic. Add to meat; stir."],[null,"Add cumin, oregano, salt, pepper and paprika; stir."],[null,"Sprinkle flour over mixture."],[null,"Mix together the boiling water and chili powder. Stir into skillet."],[null,"Cook slowly for 1 hour."],[null,"Add tomato paste and stir well."],[null,"Skim off any excess grease. Cook 30 minutes longer."],[null,"Serve over hot white rice."]],"h":[[null,"May be served over noodles instead of rice."],[null,"Freeze leftover portions in single serving containers for a quick heat and eat meal."]]},"3331":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F. Line 2 baking sheets with foil or parchment paper."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine the ground beef and turkey with dry ingredients; set aside."],[null,"In a separate bowl, combine the broth, egg and Worcestershire sauce."],[null,"Add the wet ingredients to the meat mixture and mix well."],[null,"Roll into 1″ meatballs and place on baking sheets."],[null,"Bake at 30 minutes turning once halfway through baking."],[null,"Eat meatballs plain or top with your favorite kidney-friendly sauce."]],"h":[[null,"Make ahead and freeze for a quick meal later."],[null,"Compare sodium on broth and buy the lower sodium brand. Avoid broth that contains potassium chloride."]]},"7260729":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a non-stick pan. Add the onion and fry for 2–3 minutes until softened."],[null,"Add the curry paste and continue to cook for 1 minute."],[null,"Add the stock, turkey, chickpeas and tomatoes, and simmer uncovered for 15 minutes."],[null,"Stir through the yogurt."],[null,"Serve with steamed rice and garnish with coriander."]],"h":[[null,"Try wrapping the curry in chapattis or roti with salad."],[null,"For extra vegetables, add a chopped red pepper along with the onions."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"7958623":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a large pan and add the potatoes with the onion, celery and carrot and stir-fry for 5 minutes, stirring occasionally. Sprinkle the flour over and cook for 2 minutes, stirring continuously."],[null,"Remove from heat and stir in the milk and stock. Return to the heat and slowly bring to the boil, stirring continuously. Add the turkey, sweetcorn and red pepper and simmer for 5-6 minutes until the potatoes are cooked through. Sprinkle with parsley and serve."]],"h":[[null,"If you're cooking for one, this meal can be portioned and frozen."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"7802312":{"s":[[null,"Stack the tortillas on top of each other and trim the rounded edges off to create square tortillas."],[null,"Warm the trimmed tortillas in a dry frying pan, shuffling them so each gets exposed to the hot pan for 1 minute."],[null,"Lay the tortillas out on a work surface."],[null,"Leaving a 2cm border at the top of each tortilla, first arrange turkey slices over each square, then spread with the low-fat quark and sprinkle with the thyme, black pepper and cranberries. Keeping the top margin, get the filling right to the edges and bottom of each tortilla square. It doesn’t matter if filling sticks out at the sides, you can trim it once rolled."],[null,"Lay the lettuce from left to right along the bottom edge of each tortilla. Above the lettuce lay a line of red pepper slices, and then – above that – place a spring onion."],[null,"Roll up tightly from the bottom, then with the seam on top secure each tortilla with 8 cocktail sticks."],[null,"With a sharp knife cut between the cocktail sticks to create 8 pinwheels, then arrange on a platter."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"7860482":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a pan. Add the onions and carrots and cook 4-5 minutes until the onions start to brown."],[null,"Add the turkey mince, mushrooms and celery. Cook for 4-5 minutes, breaking up any clumps of mince with a wooden spoon."],[null,"Sprinkle over the flour and mix well so that everything is coated. Gradually pour in the stock stirring continuously until it starts to thicken."],[null,"Add the pepper and soy sauce, stir and reduce the heat to low. Cover and simmer gently for 3-4 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Ideal served with leafy green vegetables and baked sweet potatoes."],[null,"This works well with beef or lamb mince."],[null,"For a vegan version use a vegan alternative in place of mince and a vegetable stock cube."],[null,"To make this into a low-fat pie, put the mince in a pie dish and top with 4 sheets of filo pastry lightly brushed with 2 tsp rapeseed oil and bake for 7-10 minutes."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat thoroughly until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"7673690":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C /gas mark 4. Add oil to pan, then add the onions and cook for 5 minutes, stirring occasionally until starting to brown."],[null,"Add the turkey and cook for a further 4-5 minutes, stirring regularly."],[null,"Next add the garlic and mushrooms and cook for a further 4-5 minutes again stirring regularly."],[null,"Mix in the thyme, mustard and flour, ensuring that everything is coated and there are no lumps of flour."],[null,"Gradually stir in the stock, bring to a boil, then turn the heat down. Cover and simmer for 10 minutes, stirring occasionally."],[null,"Place the turkey mixture in an oven proof dish, then spray the filo sheets with oil and place one on top of the turkey, folding it roughly. Add another sheet and spray with oil, then add the final sheet, creating folds across the top. Spray lightly with oil and bake for 12-15 minutes until golden brown."]],"h":[[null,"You could also use chicken for this dish."],[null,"Try other herbs such as basil, oregano or parsley in place of thyme."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Then defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat until piping-hot throughout. Although it will still taste great, the pastry won’t be as crisp once frozen and reheated."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6520930":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 375 degrees F and prepare a baking sheet by lining it with parchment paper or lightly greasing it with cooking spray."],[null,"In a skillet over medium heat, cook the lean ground turkey, breaking it into small pieces, until it's browned and fully cooked. Drain any excess fat."],[null,"In the same skillet, add finely diced onion and minced garlic, and sauté for 2–3 minutes until they become fragrant and slightly softened."],[null,"Add the chopped fresh spinach to the skillet and cook for another 2–3 minutes until it wilts and any excess moisture evaporates."],[null,"Stir in the grated Parmesan cheese, dried oregano and rosemary. Season the mixture with salt and pepper. Mix well and let it cool slightly."],[null,"Take the cleaned mushrooms and lightly brush or spray them with cooking spray or olive oil. Arrange them on the prepared baking sheet with the gill side up."],[null,"Fill each mushroom cap with the turkey and spinach mixture, pressing it down slightly to pack it in."],[null,"Bake the stuffed mushrooms in the preheated oven for about 15–20 minutes or until the mushrooms are tender, and the filling is heated through and slightly browned."],[null,"Remove the stuffed mushrooms from the oven and allow them to cool for a few minutes before serving."]],"h":[]},"6247739":{"s":[[null,"Heat the canola oil in a skillet over medium heat."],[null,"Add the diced onions and cook until softened."],[null,"Add the ground turkey to the skillet, breaking it apart with a spatula. Cook until browned."],[null,"Stir in the diced bell peppers and tomatoes, cooking for an additional 2–3 minutes."],[null,"Add the chopped spinach to the skillet and cook until wilted."],[null,"Push the turkey and vegetable mixture to the side of the skillet, creating a well."],[null,"Pour egg substitute into the well, season with salt and pepper, and scramble until cooked through."],[null,"Once the eggs are almost set, mix them with the turkey and vegetables."],[null,"Sprinkle shredded cheese over the scramble and cover the skillet until the cheese melts."]],"h":[]},"6362411":{"s":[[null,"Spray a large soup pot with cooking spray. Add the onions, carrots, and zucchini, and sauté over medium-high heat for 3-4 minutes or until the onions turn clear. Add the garlic and sauté 30 more seconds."],[null,"Add the ground turkey and cook until brown. Add the remaining ingredients; mix well and bring the chili to a boil. Reduce the heat and simmer for 15-20 minutes."]],"h":[]},"6384961":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, mix 2 Tbsp coconut aminos, 1 Tbsp avocado oil, 1 Tbsp sugar-free maple syrup, 1 Tbsp lime juice, and 1 pinch chili flakes until combined. Set aside."],[null,"Heat a large skillet over medium heat and add 2 Tbsp avocado oil. Once hot, stir in the ground turkey and chopped garlic. Cook while stirring occasionally until the turkey is browned and cooked through, about 8–10 minutes."],[null,"Add zucchini and carrots to the turkey mixture. Cook for 2–3 minutes, stirring to combine. Add kale and cook for an additional 1–2 minutes until it begins to soften."],[null,"Pour the prepared stir-fry sauce over the mixture and stir well. Cook for another 2 minutes to ensure everything is evenly coated and the kale is fully wilted."],[null,"Serve the stir-fry over rice and sprinkle peanuts on top for a crunchy garnish."]],"h":[]},"6426164":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F. Coat a baking sheet with cooking spray and set aside."],[null,"Add the peppers to a large sauté pan filled with one inch of water and cook over high heat. Bring to boiling, turn off the heat, and cover. Let the peppers steam for 10 minutes."],[null,"Remove the peppers from the pan and let them cool to the touch. Cut each pepper in half, lengthwise, and remove the ribs and seeds (if you like it spicy, leave these in or only remove some of them). NOTE: Wear gloves or use a sandwich baggie to protect your hands while handling the peppers. Wash your hands immediately after."],[null,"Lay the peppers cut side up on a sheet pan."],[null,"In a small bowl, mix together the cream cheese and diced sausage. Fill each pepper half with 1 Tbsp. of the cream cheese mixture."],[null,"Cut each piece of turkey bacon in half, lengthwise. Wrap each pepper with a strip of turkey bacon and place seam side down on the baking sheet or secure the bacon with a toothpick."],[null,"Bake the poppers for 20 minutes. Let them cool to room temperature before serving."]],"h":[]},"7882956":{"s":[[null,"In a bowl, crumble the bread and add to the beaten egg. Set aside, but mix occasionally, until the bread has absorbed all the egg."],[null,"Add the turkey mince, onion, carrot, garlic and pepper to the egg and bread then mix well."],[null,"Form into 8 burgers (approx 8cm diameter and 2½cm thick) and put on a plate or tray, cover with cling film and place in the fridge for at least 20 minutes, but an hour or two is better."],[null,"Grill the burgers for 6-8 minutes on each side, ensuring they are fully cooked."],[null,"Toast the buns, if desired, and build your burgers with the lettuce, tomato and onion."]],"h":[[null,"Spice up your burgers with a pinch of chilli flakes or 1 tsp ground cumin. Or add herbs such as thyme or rosemary."],[null,"For a festive zest, add 1 tbsp dried cranberries to the burger mix."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Can be frozen raw or cooked. Freeze in individually wrapped portions with greaseproof paper between each burger. Defrost fully in the fridge or microwave and heat thoroughly until piping-hot and cooked right through."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6139937":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F. Prick the skins of the potatoes and place on a baking sheet. Bake for 60 minutes or until soft all the way through."],[null,"Heat a large pot over medium heat. Add garlic, carrots, celery, onion, bell pepper, spices, and 1 Tbsp of olive oil. Cook, stirring occasionally, until softened, 4–5 minutes."],[null,"Add lentils, tomato sauce, and broth. Bring to a boil then reduce heat to low and simmer for 30 minutes until lentils are soft."],[null,"When the chili is almost done, heat a skillet over medium heat. Add the remaining olive oil and turkey. Cook, breaking apart with a spoon, until crumbly and browned. Add to the soup for the last 10 minutes."],[null,"Carefully slice each sweet potato open and mash the insides. Spoon 1 cup chili over each potato, then top with 2 Tbsp cheese."]],"h":[]},"3536":{"s":[[null,"Dice celery and carrots. Quarter onion and chop parsley."],[null,"Rinse giblets and place in a medium pot. Add 5 cups water, celery, carrot, onion, bay leaves and parsley."],[null,"Simmer for 1 hour until giblets are tender and broth is flavored."],[null,"Strain stock. Use giblet stock to baste turkey and for gravy."]],"h":[[null,"Makes 5 cups of stock."]]},"3563":{"s":[[null,"Heat fat from pan juices of cooked turkey in a medium saucepan."],[null,"Stir in flour, bring to a boil and whisk for one minute."],[null,"Gradually add pan juices, giblet stock and salt. Continue stirring until gravy boils. Reduce heat and simmer for 10 minutes to thicken."]],"h":[[null,"Sodium is 0 mg per serving if salt omitted."],[null,"Boil turkey giblets in water to make giblet stock."]]},"6966658":{"s":[[null,"In a large pot or Dutch oven, brown the ground turkey over medium-high heat until cooked through. Transfer the cooked turkey to a separate bowl and set aside."],[null,"In the same pot, heat olive oil over medium heat. Add the diced onion, green bell pepper, celery, okra, and garlic, then cook until vegetables are softened, about 5 minutes."],[null,"Add the Cajun seasoning, thyme, oregano, cayenne pepper, salt, pepper, and flour over the vegetables. Stir well to coat."],[null,"Gradually pour in the chicken broth, whisking constantly to avoid lumps."],[null,"Add the cooked turkey back to the pot, along with diced tomatoes. Stir to combine."],[null,"Bring the mixture to a simmer, then reduce the heat to low and let it cook for 20–30 minutes, until the flavors meld together."],[null,"Serve the Turkey Gumbo over cooked brown rice and garnish with green onions."]],"h":[]},"7212684":{"s":[[null,"Heat 1 tsp of the oil to a frying pan and add the turkey. Fry for 2 minutes on each side to brown the outside. Then put them on a plate, cover with foil and set aside, reserving any juices."],[null,"Add the other tsp oil to the same pan and add the leeks. Fry gently, stirring regularly, for 5 minutes until they start to soften, but don't allow them to brown."],[null,"Add the garlic, white pepper, flour and mustard and mix well so the leeks are coated, then gradually stir in 200ml water until it starts to thicken."],[null,"Gradually stir in the milk and carry on cooking and stirring, until the leeks are soft. If the sauce gets too thick, just stir in a little more milk."],[null,"Add the turkey escalopes back to the pan along with any juices that have come from them and cook for 2-3 minutes."],[null,"Remove the turkey and add the cream cheese and parsley to the sauce, mix well. Pour over the escalopes and serve with seasonal vegetables."]],"h":[[null,"You could use this recipe with chicken breast. It's also good with cod or salmon."],[null,"Try adding different herbs instead of parsley, such as tarragon, coriander or dill."],[null,"For a vegetarian version, use 400g whole mushrooms in place of the turkey"],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"2115":{"s":[[null,"Cook turkey breasts at 350° F for 1 hour or until meat thermometer reaches 180° F. Let cool."],[null,"Cut turkey into bite size cubes."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine reduced-sodium teriyaki sauce, sugar, oil, ginger and nutmeg."],[null,"Place turkey cubes in mixture. Cover and let sit in refrigerate for 30 minutes."],[null,"Cut onions and peppers into kabob-sized pieces. Drain pineapple chunks and mandarin oranges."],[null,"Using skewers, alternate turkey, onion, peppers, and pineapple chunks to make 24 kabobs."],[null,"Place kabobs in a large microwave safe dish and cover with wax paper. Microwave kabobs for 8 minutes."],[null,"Place kabobs on a serving platter. Pour dressing over kabobs and garnish with grapes and mandarin oranges before serving."]],"h":[]},"6418383":{"s":[[null,"Mix together the lime juice, salt, pepper, olive oil, and garlic. Place this mixture and the turkey in a plastic bag and marinate in the fridge for at least 20 minutes."],[null,"Cut tomatoes in half vertically. Cut the avocado into 18 chunks."],[null,"Grill or broil the turkey. Set aside to cool."],[null,"Thread the kebabs as follows: 1 piece of turkey, 1 piece of tomato, 1 piece of turkey, and 1 piece of avocado"],[null,"Squeeze lime over kebabs and serve with a drizzle of Mango Dipping Sauce, page 29 (optional)."]],"h":[]},"7091568":{"s":[[null,"Soak the wooden skewers in water while preparing the koftas."],[null,"Mix all the kofta ingredients together, divide the mixture into 6, and roll into sausage shapes. Thread on skewers and refrigerate for 15 minutes."],[null,"Grill for 10-12 minutes turning regularly, check they are cooked through."],[null,"Mix all the salad ingredients together, divide between 6 plates, then top each with a kofta."]],"h":[[null,"As well as soaking before use, cover the bamboo skewers with foil to stop them burning under the grill."],[null,"Any lean mince could be used for the koftas - beef or lamb both work well."],[null,"Great wrapped in a roti with salad and some mango chutney."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Freeze koftas individually, wrapped in greaseproof paper. Defrost in the fridge or microwave and grill until piping hot."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"3448":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425˚ F."],[null,"Dice the cucumber. Mix it together with the Greek yogurt, garlic powder, dill, 1/4 teaspoon black pepper and lemon juice to make tzatziki sauce. Cover and place in the refrigerator until ready to serve."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine the ground turkey, breadcrumbs, egg, garlic, cumin and remaining 1/4 teaspoon black pepper. Mix well. Using a tablespoon to measure, roll into 32 meatballs."],[null,"Place the meatballs on a greased cookie sheet. Bake for 10 to 15 minutes, or until browned and temperature reaches 165˚ F with a meat thermometer."],[null,"Remove meatballs from the oven and let rest 5 to 10 minutes."],[null,"Cut each pita in half. Spread about 2-1/2 tablespoons of the tzatziki in a pita half, add 4 of the meatballs, 2 tablespoons lettuce and 1/2 tablespoon of feta cheese. Repeat with remaining ingredients."]],"h":[[null,"Flatbread may be substituted for the pita bread. Compare brands and look for the lowest sodium option. To keep the balance in carbohydrates limit to 15 g-18 g of carbohydrate per serving in the flatbread, may need to cut in half."],[null,"One tablespoons of diced tomatoes may be added to the pita. This will add about 30 mg of potassium to the serving."]]},"6062299":{"s":[[null,"Heat a large pot over medium-high heat. Add broth, sesame oil, soy sauce, chili-garlic sauce, and fish sauce."],[null,"Add half of the garlic, ginger, cilantro, and green onions to the pot. Transfer remaining garlic, ginger, cilantro, and green onions to a medium bowl."],[null,"Add turkey, breadcrumbs, eggs, and 5 spice powder to the bowl. Mix with your hands until well combined."],[null,"Form rounded meatballs with a tablespoon measure and drop into the pot. Simmer for 5–6 minutes, until the meatballs are cooked through."],[null,"Add bok choy and carrots to the pot and cook for another 4–5 minutes."]],"h":[]},"6881554":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F. Line two sheet pans with parchment paper."],[null,"In a mixing bowl, combine ground turkey, breadcrumbs, Parmesan cheese, egg, minced garlic, dried oregano, and ¼ teaspoon black pepper. Mix until well combined."],[null,"With wet hands, form the mixture into meatballs, approximately 1 inch in diameter, and place them on the sheet pan. Bake for 20 minutes, or until the internal temperature reaches 165 degrees F."],[null,"While the meatballs bake, toss the zucchini noodles with olive oil, and ¼ teaspoon black pepper and spread them on the second sheet pan."],[null,"Bake until tender, about 10-15 minutes."],[null,"Warm marinara sauce on the stove and toss the warm meatballs in the sauce."],[null,"Serve meatballs over the zucchini noodles and garnish with the olives and fresh parsley."]],"h":[]},"3080":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Combine all ingredients in a large bowl and mix well."],[null,"Transfer to a greased 9″ x 5″ loaf pan and bake for 1 hour."],[null,"Slice into 6 equal pieces and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Select the brand of sausage lowest in sodium."],[null,"Use the hot and spicy turkey sausage for more flavor."]]},"2177":{"s":[[null,"Preheat grill pan or Panini machine to medium heat."],[null,"Spread each piece of bread with one teaspoon of butter."],[null,"On the unbuttered side of one piece of bread, layer one slice of cheese, leftover sliced turkey, cranberry sauce and remaining slice of cheese. Place remaining slice of bread on top, buttered side up."],[null,"Put sandwich in pan or onto Panini machine. Grill sandwich 5 minutes on Panini machine or until it is golden and toasted."],[null,"If using a pan, press sandwich down with a pan lid. Flip sandwich after about 3 minutes or when bottom is fully toasted. Cook other side about 3 minutes or until toasted."]],"h":[[null,"For a lower protein meal plan, reduce the turkey to 1 ounce and use 1 slice of cheese. Add more cranberry sauce for extra calories."],[null,"Each slice of cheese is .32 ounces so two slices equals about 2/3 ounce total."],[null,"Dietitian Erica says \"Love my Panini maker! I found it at a yard sale for about $3 and have gotten so much use out of it. I’ve heard a George Foreman grill or similar kitchen appliance works just as well. It just makes your typical grilled sandwich a little more special.\""]]},"2878":{"s":[[null,"Cut red pepper into thin 1/4″ strips (about 10 strips)."],[null,"Spread cream cheese evenly on tortilla wrap."],[null,"Layer with spring mix salad greens and turkey slices."],[null,"Space out roasted red pepper strips on top."],[null,"Grab the end tightly and start rolling."],[null,"Use toothpicks to hold the end in place (space out 4 to 6 toothpicks evenly along the edge)."],[null,"Cut into 6 pieces. For neat appearance, cut small slices at both ends and discard."],[null,"Serve with cross section facing up."]],"h":[[null,"Shredded lettuce can be used instead of spring mix. Spring mix gives a more intense color and flavor."],[null,"Use low sodium peppers in a jar or can or roast a fresh pepper over a stovetop burner, place in a paper bag 5 minutes then remove charred skin before slicing."],[null,"For summer flare, you can also add fresh mint, basil or cilantro for a more refreshing taste."],[null,"Be careful not to overfill the wrap as it will make rolling more difficult."],[null,"Serve on a dark or bright color serving plate to contrast the colors of the pinwheel ."]]},"3599":{"s":[[null,"Peel and dice potatoes. Chop onionand celery. Cut cooked turkey into cubes."],[null,"Double boil potatoes to reduce potassium (see instructions in helpful hints below)."],[null,"Preheat oven to 425° F."],[null,"Melt 1 tablespoon butter in large saucepan and sauté onions until tender."],[null,"Add celery and cook for an additional minute."],[null,"Blend in 2 tablespoons of flour, pepper, sage and thyme and cook over low heat for 1 minute."],[null,"Remove from heat. Stir in chicken broth and milk until blended. Bring to a boil and simmer for 1 minute, stirring constantly."],[null,"Stir in turkey, double boiled potatoes and peas and carrots. Set aside to cool."],[null,"In a separate bowl, cut 1 cup of butter into remaining flour using a pastry blender. Mixture should form pea-size particles."],[null,"Begin adding ice water, one tablespoon at a time, mixing well each time, until dough forms into a ball."],[null,"Divide dough in half and roll out one piece, using a rolling pin and additional flour until dough is pliable and no longer sticky. Be sure that dough is larger than the diameter of the 9-inch pie pan."],[null,"Place dough in pie pan, smoothing with fingers to fill pan, and then pour turkey mixture on top."],[null,"Roll second piece of dough to similar size and place on top of the turkey pie filling. Seal edges of pie."],[null,"Using a sharp knife, make four to five one-inch cuts across the top of the pie crust to vent the pie."],[null,"Place pie on sheet pan and bake for 35-40 minutes or until golden brown."]],"h":[[null,"To reduce potassium in potatoes use the Double Cook method. Peel and dice potatoes into 1” pieces. Boil in a large pot of water for 10 minutes. Drain the water and add fresh water to the pot. Bring to a boil and cook until potatoes are tender."],[null,"Use a refrigerated, prepared pie crust if desired. Look for the lowest sodium brand."],[null,"For a lower fat and calorie version make half the pastry and use to top pie ingredients instead of the double pastry version."]]},"4980045":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F."],[null,"In a mixing bowl, whisk together the eggs, rice milk and spices."],[null,"In a separate mixing bowl, toss the crusty bread with the cheese, green onions, turkey and red pepper. Transfer to a non-stick 9-inch square pan or your favo rite greased casserole dish."],[null,"Pour the egg mixture over the bread mixture. Press down on the bread to ensure that all the bread gets coated with the liquid."],[null,"Place the strata uncovered in the oven and bake for 50 to 60 minutes. The strata is ready when it is pufed up and firm to the touch."],[null,"Serve warm. Excellent for breakfast or lunch."]],"h":[[null,"The strata can be assembled the night before, covered with plastic wrap and refrigerated. Bake it in the preheated oven the next morning for an easy brunch treat!"],["The dangers of salt substitutes","When you need to limit salt in your diet, look for other ways to season foods. In your search for new flavors, you may come across products called salt substitutes. These products typically look like table salt, but claim to be low in sodium. Unfortunately, when sodium is removed from salt, potassium is typically added in its place. When sodium is removed and replaced with potassium, it is now potassium chloride, or KCL. It is important to read the ingredient lists on all salt substitutes to make sure you do not select one containing potassium chloride. The amount of potassium in a salt substitute varies from product to product, but generally is very high when it contains potassium chloride. A single teaspoon can contain 2,400 to 3,000 milligrams of potassium, which is equal to an entire day’s allowance of potassium on a low-potassium diet. Salt substitutes can also be found in foods that are labeled “low in sodium” or “sodium free.” Carefully read the ingredients for these foods to see if potassium chloride has been added. The best way to add flavor to foods is to use herbs and spices without adding unwanted sodium or potassium. If you are not sure how to use herbs and spices, ask your dietitian for suggestions."]]},"6281267":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F. Coat a 9x13 baking dish with cooking spray."],[null,"In a medium bowl, whisk together nonfat milk, green onions, dry mustard, salt (optional), pepper, and egg substitute."],[null,"Place bread cubes and sausage on the bottom of the baking dish, pour egg mixture evenly over bread and sausage. Top with cheddar cheese."],[null,"Cover pan with aluminum foil and bake for 20 minutes. Remove foil and bake for an additional 40 minutes."],[null,"Remove from oven and let cool for 20 minutes, then cut into 10 equal slices."]],"h":[]},"6321052":{"s":[[null,"Spray a large nonstick skillet lightly with cooking spray. Set to medium heat. Add the sausage and cook for 3 minutes or until beginning to brown, stirring occasionally."],[null,"Pour the egg substitute evenly over the sausage and cook for 1 minute. Do not stir. Then, gently lift to allow the uncooked egg to flow under. Remove from heat and allow to finish cooking."],[null,"Sprinkle the cheese, green onions, tomatoes, and basil evenly over top."]],"h":[]},"4595971":{"s":[[null,"Bring a large pot of water to a boil. Cook pasta according to directions. Drain and return pasta to the same pot. Add the frozen green beans to the cooked pasta. Remove from heat."],[null,"In a plate, combine flour with poultry seasoning and black pepper. Dredge each piece of turkey scaloppine in the seasoned flour."],[null,"In a skillet over medium-high heat, heat the olive oil. Cook the turkey slices for 3 to 4 minutes per side. Remove from heat."],[null,"In the same skillet the turkey scaloppine was cooked in, heat butter over medium heat. Add shallots, garlic and sage and sauté until softened and fragrant."],[null,"Deglaze the pan with the lemon juice and chicken stock. Bring to a boil. Add cooked pasta, green bean mixture and parmesan cheese. Cook until sauce reduces."],[null,"Sprinkle with red pepper flakes and serve immediately with turkey scaloppine."]],"h":[[null,"* Scaloppine is a thinly sliced cut of meat. Chicken can be substituted for turkey."],["Extra phosphorus in seasoned and breaded pieces of meat and poultry","Grocery stores are offering quick, time-saving meals of seasoned and breaded packages of chicken, beef and main entrée meats. With your kidney diet, it is important to pay attention to your selections and stay away from certain prepared meals. Reducing consumption of inorganic phosphorus preservatives reduces the waste load on your kidneys and improves the quality of your diet. Read the list of ingredients. Common phosphorus additives include phosphoric acid, sodium polyphosphate, pyrophosphate, sodium tripolyphosphate, polyphosphate, tricalcium phosphate, hexametaphosphate, trisodium phosphate, dicalcium phosphate, sodium phosphate, monocalcium phosphate, tetrasodium phosphate and aluminum phosphate. If possible, limit any food items with these additives or other ingredients that contain “phos”. Plan ahead to prevent impulse purchases. If you are hungry and feeling short on time, you are more prone to purchasing an already prepared item from the shelf. Planning ahead is key to sticking with your kidney diet, choosing foods that are healthy for your body, and having ingredients at home to prepare meals low in phosphorus, potassium and sodium, but still with plenty of flavor."]]},"6938670":{"s":[[null,"Cook noodles according to package directions. Toss noodles with poppy seeds and return to empty cooking pot to keep warm. Sprinkle turkey strips with salt and pepper; toss to coat. Remove and discard stems from mushrooms. Cut mushroom caps into quarters and thinly slice."],[null,"Meanwhile, lightly coat large nonstick skillet with nonstick cooking spray and set over medium-high heat. Sauté onion 2 minutes. Add mushrooms and sauté until mushrooms are tender, about 5-6 minutes. Transfer to large bowl."],[null,"Melt butter in skillet over medium heat. Add flour and cook for 1 minute, continuously stirring. Gradually whisk in broth. Cook, stirring with wooden spoon, until sauce thickens and boils, about 4 minutes."],[null,"Reduce heat to low. Whisk in Greek yogurt and mustard. Return turkey and reserved vegetables with accumulated juices to skillet. Cook until heated through (do not boil). Divide noodles among plates and spoon stroganoff on top."]],"h":[]},"3784":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Remove core from cabbage and cut out 3 cups of cabbage from the inside to make a cavity for stuffing."],[null,"Combine turkey, sausage, onion, bell pepper, Worcestershire sauce and herb seasoning in a bowl. Mix well then stuff into cabbage."],[null,"Insert 4 to 5 toothpicks around outside of cabbage to anchor it. Place with stuffed end up into a deep, ovenproof pot."],[null,"Pour 1/2-cup water into bottom of pot, cover with a lid and bake 45 minutes or until ground turkey temperature reaches 175° F."],[null,"Remove from oven and let rest 10 minutes before cutting into 6 equal servings."]],"h":[[null,"Make coleslaw out of the leftover cabbage that was removed to make the cavity for the turkey stuffing."],[null,"Select spicy hot turkey sausage for more flavor."],[null,"Sausage is higher in sodium and phosphorus that many other meats. When used in small amounts, it may be included in recipes that meet the goals of a kidney diet."],[null,"Divide leftover sausage into 1-1/2-ounce portions and freeze for later use."]]},"3054":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F."],[null,"Remove stems from peppers and clean seeds and membranes from inside."],[null,"Mix turkey, rice, egg, onion, garlic and seasonings well."],[null,"Stuff peppers with meat mixture."],[null,"Place peppers in a large roaster."],[null,"Pour crushed tomatoes and broth over peppers"],[null,"Bake for 1 hour 15 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Use ground turkey breast for the leanest possible filling, but lean ground beef is also a heart-healthy filling."],[null,"If you are not on a potassium restricted diet, use a 16-oz. can of crushed tomatoes."],[null,"Make a double batch and freeze individual peppers for an easy meal when you don’t feel like cooking."],[null,"Stuffed peppers are ubiquitous throughout Central and Eastern Europe. Seasoning and what type of meat with which they are stuffed vary not only from region to region, but within regions. Some use 100% ground beef, and others use a mixture of meats."],[null,"For a lower protein diet you can use one pound of turkey and increase the rice to 3 cups."]]},"6938246":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F. Line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Remove the stems and scrape out the gills from the portobello mushroom caps. Lightly spray the caps with olive oil and place them on the baking sheet, open side up."],[null,"Heat a non-stick skillet over medium heat. Add the ground turkey and diced onion. Cook, breaking up the turkey, until no longer pink (about 5–6 minutes). Add the minced garlic and cook for 1 additional minute."],[null,"Stir in the diced tomatoes, oregano, smoked paprika, salt, and pepper. Mix well and cook for another 3–4 minutes."],[null,"Divide the turkey mixture evenly among the mushroom caps. Bake for 15–20 minutes, or until the mushrooms are tender and the filling is heated through."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine the baby spinach, crumbled feta, toasted pecans, cucumber, and cherry tomatoes."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the balsamic vinegar, olive oil, and Dijon mustard. Drizzle the dressing over the salad and toss to coat evenly."],[null,"Serve one stuffed mushroom cap with salad on the side."]],"h":[]},"3277":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375° F."],[null,"Chop the onion and mushrooms. Mince the garlic. Cut ends from zucchini; slice in half lengthwise."],[null,"Use a spoon tip to scrape inside flesh from zucchini to make the zucchini boats. Chop the flesh and set aside."],[null,"Place zucchini boats in a 13 x 9-inch pan, cover with aluminum foil and bake for 20 minutes until fork tender."],[null,"Remove zucchini from oven and cool slightly."],[null,"While zucchini is cooking, place olive oil in a pan over medium heat. Add ground turkey, onion and garlic to skillet. Stir to break up the ground turkey until thoroughly cooked. Drain excess grease."],[null,"Add zucchini flesh, mushrooms, marinara sauce and Italian seasoning to skillet. Stir well to combine. Simmer for 15 minutes."],[null,"Scoop turkey mixture into partially cooked zucchini boats. Cover with foil and bake for 20 minutes."],[null,"Remove foil and top zucchini with mozzarella cheese and panko bread crumbs. Place in top rack of oven and bake for additional 3 to 5 minutes or until cheese just begins to brown. Remove from oven and enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"If flesh is difficult to remove from zucchini, very gently score with a knife, being careful not to slice through."],[null,"One average size garlic clove is about 1 teaspoon."],[null,"Compare marinara sauce brands and select the one lowest in sodium."]]},"6860194":{"s":[[null,"In a large skillet, heat the olive oil over medium-high heat."],[null,"Add the onion and jalapeño to the skillet and cook for 2 minutes. Add the turkey and cook until the meat is browned and the vegetables are cooked through, about 5 to 7 minutes. Add the garlic and cumin and cook for 30 seconds."],[null,"Lower the heat and add the chili powder, paprika, and water, and mix thoroughly."],[null,"Fill each tortilla with ½ cup of the turkey mixture, plus about 2 Tbsp diced avocado, 1 Tbsp yogurt, and 1 Tbsp pico de gallo."]],"h":[]},"1726":{"s":[[null,"Chop onion and zucchini. Mince garlic cloves."],[null,"Spray pan with cooking spray and add oil."],[null,"Sauté ground turkey, onion, garlic and zucchini until squash is tender."],[null,"Drain excess liquid well."],[null,"Add stewed tomatoes and spices. Crush and break up tomatoes with spoon or fork."],[null,"Simmer covered for approximately 1/2 hour."]],"h":[[null,"Two medium zucchini yields approximately 2 cups."],[null,"Substitute lean ground beef for turkey if desired."],[null,"Serve over cooked rice or pasta for a filling meal."],[null,"Be sure to count as 2 servings of vegetables in your daily meal plan to allow for the potassium in this recipe. If you are on a low-potassium diet, stick closely to the recommended portion."]]},"1899":{"s":[[null,"Cut turkey into cubes. Dice celery and apples; finely chop onion."],[null,"In a medium bowl, combine turkey, apple, celery and onion."],[null,"Add mayonnaise and apple juice. Stir together until well mixed."],[null,"Chill until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Some grocery stores sell diced, cooked turkey. Check the label to be sure it is not salted. You could also purchase fresh, uncooked turkey breast and cook in the oven or grill without adding salt."],[null,"Wondering how much produce to buy? One medium apple yields 1 cup; three celery ribs yield 1 cup; 1 medium onion or 1/2 large onion yields 1/2 cup."],[null,"Adjust mayonnaise portion to taste. Reduced-fat mayonnaise may be substituted for regular mayonnaise."]]},"3306":{"s":[[null,"Chop onion, bell pepper and carrots. Mince garlic. Shred turkey."],[null,"Bring 1-3/4 cups broth to boil in a sauce pan over medium heat; add quick-cooking wild rice to pan and bring to a boil. Reduce to medium-low heat. Cover and simmer for 5 minutes or until liquid is absorbed. Set aside."],[null,"Heat oil in a Dutch oven over medium-high heat. Add onion, bell pepper, carrots and garlic. Sauté, stirring occasionally."],[null,"Drain and rinse mushrooms, then add to vegetables."],[null,"Add remaining 3-1/4 cups broth, bay leaves, turkey, Mrs. Dash seasoning, thyme, salt and pepper to pan. Cook until thoroughly heated, stirring occasionally."],[null,"Remove bay leaves and add cooked wilds rice to soup. Serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"If quick-cooking wild rice is unavailable, use regular wild rice. Add rice to 2 cups boiling broth, return to a boil and simmer covered for 50 minutes or until rice kernels puff open."],[null,"Substitute 1 cup fresh mushroom pieces for canned mushrooms if desired."],[null,"For a lower protein diet reduce turkey to 1 cup instead of 2 cups. Protein is reduced to 17 grams per serving."]]},"6696604":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, combine all ingredients and cover. Refrigerate for 1/2 hour before serving. Bring the salad to room temperature and serve."]],"h":[]},"7053704":{"s":[[null,"For the base: Preheat the oven to 200°C (180° fan)/400F/gas mark 6. Grease and line a large round baking tray with greaseproof paper."],[null,"Place the cauliflower florets in a food processor and pulse until rice-like in texture. Bring a large saucepan of water to the boil and cook the cauliflower, covered, for 4-5 minutes until tender."],[null,"Drain well and gather the cauliflower in a large square of muslin or cheesecloth. You can also use a clean tea towel. Wrap the muslin around the cauliflower in a ball-shape and twist well to wring out as much excess water as possible."],[null,"Tip the dried cauliflower into a bowl and add the egg, cream cheese, flour, and freshly ground black pepper. Mix well until a rough dough comes together."],[null,"Transfer the cauliflower dough onto the lined tray and roll out into a large round. Brush the top with olive oil."],[null,"Bake for 25-35 minutes until dry to the touch and golden-brown all over."],[null,"For the toppings: In the meantime, heat the olive oil in a sauté pan set over a medium heat until hot."],[null,"Add the onion and sweat until softened, about 5 minutes. Stir in the Quorn and cook over a slightly increased heat until browned all over, breaking it up with a wooden spoon."],[null,"Stir in the spices and oregano, cooking for a further 2 minutes. Remove from the heat and cover to keep warm."],[null,"Remove the cauliflower base from the oven when ready. Top with the Quorn, diced cucumber, cherry tomatoes, and chopped parsley."],[null,"Stir the grated cucumber into the yoghurt in a small mixing bowl. Spoon dollops on top of the pizza and serve the remainder on the side."]],"h":[[null,"Replace the Quorn mince in this recipe with slices of grilled pepper or aubergine to increase your veg intake."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"6730582":{"s":[[null,"In a medium bowl, mix the Greek yogurt, garlic, fresh herbs, and lemon zest. Season with ¼ tsp salt and ¼ tsp pepper. Set aside at room temperature."],[null,"Make the spiced oil. In a small pan over low heat, warm olive oil with paprika, cumin, and red pepper flakes. Stir for 30 seconds until fragrant. Remove from heat and set aside."],[null,"Fill a medium saucepan with 2-3 inches of water and bring to a gentle simmer. Add vinegar. Crack eggs into small bowls. Swirl the water, then gently slide in the eggs. Cook for 3-4 minutes until whites are set but yolks remain runny. Use a slotted spoon to transfer eggs to a paper towel-lined plate."],[null,"Divide the Greek yogurt mixture between bowls. Top with poached eggs and drizzle with spiced olive oil. Garnish with extra fresh herbs and remaining ¼ tsp salt and ¼ tsp black pepper."],[null,"Pair each serving with 1/2 slice of sprouted whole grain bread."]],"h":[]},"2283":{"s":[[null,"Cut up garlic. Place all ingredients in a blender or food processor and blend until smooth."],[null,"Refrigerate leftovers in an airtight container."]],"h":[[null,"Turmeric is said to contain anti-inflammatory properties."],[null,"You can also use an immersion blender to blend ingredients."],[null,"To save time mince garlic first, add ingredients and shake well in container."]]},"1877":{"s":[[null,"Peel and cut each bananas into 3 pieces to fit lumpia wrappers. (There will be one extra piece. Save for later or discard.)"],[null,"Roll banana pieces in sugar to coat."],[null,"Roll up sugared bananas in lumpia wrappers. Fold over the corners of wrapper and press down firmly to seal."],[null,"Brush with beaten egg to seal edges of wrappers."],[null,"Heat oil in a wok or fryer to 350 to 375° F."],[null,"Place 4 rolls in the hot oil, frying until crisp and golden (approx. 5 to 7 minutes)."],[null,"Remove rolls with a spatula or tongs and place on paper towels to drain. Fry remaining banana rolls."],[null,"Sprinkle with powdered sugar or caramel sauce if desired. Serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"Lumpia wrappers are a thin pastry made from flour or cornstarch, eggs and water. Look for them at any Asian grocery store. If unavailable, substitute egg roll wrappers."],[null,"Plantains can be substituted for the bananas if a potassium-restricted diet is not required."],[null,"Limit to only one portion to keep potassium in control if you are restricting potassium. Each turon contains 1/3 of a medium-sized banana which has 140 mg potassium."]]},"6177299":{"s":[[null,"In a saucepot over medium heat, heat the olive oil. Add the onions, celery, and carrots and sauté for 5 minutes."],[null,"Add the garlic and rosemary and sauté 1 minute."],[null,"Add the remaining ingredients, except the fresh basil and vinegar. Bring to a boil."],[null,"Reduce heat and simmer, partially covered for 20 minutes."],[null,"Add the vinegar and basil and cook for 2 minutes. Serve immediately and enjoy!"]],"h":[]},"7177299":{"s":[[null,"Add the oil to a pan and mix in the onion, pepper and carrot. Stir regularly for 5 minutes until starting to brown."],[null,"Add the stock, tomatoes, cabbage, oregano, thyme, beans and garlic. Bring to the boil, then reduce the heat, add a lid and simmer for 10 minutes."],[null,"Put into bowls, add a blob of pesto to each and sprinkle with plenty of black pepper. To serve, add a shaving of cheese, if liked, and a sprig of fresh basil, to garnish."]],"h":[[null,"Like many traditional recipes, this soup tends to be made with whatever is available. You can add all sorts of vegetables, such as pumpkin, courgettes or celery, or add different beans, pasta, or even meat, such as chicken."],[null,"Borlotti beans are low in fat, packed with dietary fibre and a good source of protein and folate."],[null,"Using strong flavoured cheese, such as Parmesan, Gran Padano or Cheddar, means that you can use less of it in your cooking, but still enjoy great taste."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Freeze in portions then defrost in the fridge, or defrost in a microwave stirring regularly."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"6195934":{"s":[[null,"Combine oil, lemon juice, garlic, fennel seeds, red chili flakes, oregano, and vinegar in a medium bowl and put into a large tightly sealed plastic bag. Marinate at least 15 minutes room temperature or overnight in the refrigerator for best results."],[null,"Thread the chicken cubes on skewers, either alone or with chunks of your favorite vegetables such as red onion, bell pepper, or zucchini."],[null,"Preheat grill to medium-high heat and place on grill grate. Cook as per directions for direct heat method (page 3) for 10–12 minutes, turning occasionally, until cooked through and crusted on the outside."]],"h":[]},"7056258":{"s":[[null,"Line a 20 x 30cm swiss roll tin with baking paper. In a large bowl, beat together the Greek yoghurt and sweetener and spread into the tin to cover the base."],[null,"Crush the raspberries with a fork and drizzle randomly over the yoghurt. Pull a skewer through the raspberries to create a swirled pattern. Scatter over the remaining fruit and flaked almonds and freeze for 3–4 hrs, until set."],[null,"Remove from the freezer and allow to stand for 10 minutes before serving. Snap into pieces and serve immediately."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6425743":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F. Coat a sheet pan with cooking spray. Cut the squash in half lengthwise and place face down on the sheet pan. Bake for 45 minutes."],[null,"Remove the seeds from the squash and scrape the flesh away from the skin with a fork to make strands, keeping the squash shell intact. Place each squash shell cut side up on the sheet pan."],[null,"Add the squash strands to a large bowl. Add the sausage, marinara sauce, black pepper, and oregano and toss until combined. Divide the mixture evenly among the squash shells."],[null,"Top each squash half with 2 Tbsp shredded Parmesan cheese. Bake for 25 minutes, until golden brown. Cut each squash shell in half to serve."]],"h":[]},"2485":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F. Grease a 9-inch spring form pan."],[null,"Cut 4 tablespoons of the margarine into pieces. With the food processor metal blade in place, add 2/3 cup sugar, flour, 4 tablespoons margarine, baking soda, vanilla and one egg to food processor bowl. Process until mixture resembles cornmeal. Spread mixture in the bottom of well-greased pan."],[null,"Peel, quarter and seed apples. Insert slicing disk in food processor and stand apple quarters upright in feed tube. Slice using moderate pressure on the pusher."],[null,"Arrange apple slices in layers on top of the crumb mixture. Bake for 45 minutes."],[null,"While cake is baking, add remaining 3 tablespoons sugar, remaining 3 tablespoons margarine (melted), cinnamon and one egg to the bowl of the food processor fitted with the metal blade. Process until the mixture is smooth and sugar dissolves. Spoon mixture over apples and bake 30 minutes more or until top is firm."]],"h":[[null,"Recommended apple varieties include Cortland, Pippin, Rome or your personal favorite."],[null,"If you do not have a food processor, use a blender to mix the cake and topping."]]},"6677227":{"s":[[null,"In a large saucepan, heat the oil over medium heat. Add the onion and celery and sauté for 4 minutes. Add the carrot and leek and sauté for 6 to 7 minutes, until the vegetables are soft. Add the garlic and sauté for 1 minute."],[null,"Add the tomatoes and lemon zest and cook for 1 minute. Pour in the broth and bring it to a boil. Lower the heat, cover, and simmer for 20 minutes, until the mixture has thickened."],[null,"Add the beans and chopped kale and simmer, uncovered, for 5 minutes. Stir in the lemon juice, oregano, salt, and pepper and simmer for 1 minute."]],"h":[]},"7989211":{"s":[[null,"Place the cucumber in a clean tea towel and squeeze until most of the liquid has been removed."],[null,"Combine with the remaining ingredients and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Tzatziki makes an excellent sauce to serve with grilled fish, meat or vegetarian main courses."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"6715369":{"s":[[null,"12-24 hours before serving, line a strainer with a paper coffee filter or cheesecake cloth. Place over a bowl. Spoon yogurt into coffee filter, cover, and refrigerate for 12-14 hours."],[null,"Yogurt will now be thick. Discard the collected liquid beneath or use it in soups or breads. Remove yogurt from the filter and place in a small bowl."],[null,"Mix cucumber, garlic, dill weed, salt, lemon juice, and olive oil into yogurt. Refrigerate for one hour before serving."],[null,"Serve with a variety of vegetables like: fresh green beans (lightly steamed), green, red, or yellow bell peppers, carrots, celery, zucchini, yellow squash, tomatoes, cucumbers, radishes, broccoli, and cauliflower."]],"h":[]},"3631":{"s":[[null,"Peel the cucumber then grate using the large holes of a box grater."],[null,"Remove some of the liquid from grated cucumber by lightly squeezing while holding over the sink."],[null,"In a small bowl mix cucumber with the Greek yogurt, garlic powder, dill, pepper and lemon juice to make tzatziki sauce."],[null,"Cover and place in the refrigerator until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Serve Tzatziki Sauce with Turkey Meatball Gyros and Chickpea Burgers."]]},"9741235":{"s":[[null,"Boil some water in a kettle or on your stovetop and soak the cashews in the hot water for 20 minutes. Then drain them."],[null,"Then toast your bread in a toaster, and spread the butter on each slice, if using. Or you may grease a cast iron pan or skillet with butter and toast the bread on your stovetop. Set aside."],[null,"Add ALL the cheese ingredients, including the now drained cashews to your blender and process until smooth."],[null,"Then pour the liquid mixture into a pan on your stovetop and simmer the mixture until thick and stretchy, stirring often. It will go from a liquid to a melty, cheesy texture in approx. 2-4 minutes."],[null,"Divide the cheese between 3 sandwiches and add sliced tomato and avocado, if using. Serve immediately while the cheese is warm. If it cools down quicker than you can prepare it, return the assembled sandwiches to the pan to reheat on both sides."]],"h":[]},"5133605":{"s":[[null,"Pre-heat the oven to 200˚C/ 180˚C fan /Gas Mark 6."],[null,"If using pastry, unroll and place flat on baking sheet. Bake for 15 minutes in the preheated oven, or until puffed and golden. Once cooked, allow to cool and then break into small pieces."],[null,"Place ¾ of the broken pastry/palmier biscuits in the oven proof ramekin in layers. Sprinkle the coconut over the pastry."],[null,". Pour the Renastep into a pan and stir in the cinnamon and vanilla. Heat gently but don’t boil."],[null,"Pour the heated mixture over the pastry/palmier biscuits in the oven proof dish."],[null,"Use the final ¼ palmier biscuits or pastry to top the surface of the dish."],[null,"Place dish in the oven and bake for 10 minutes, until the liquid bubbles at the edges."],[null,"Serve warm, topped with a small portion of almonds, pistachios and raisins if permitted."]],"h":[[null,"Add a spoon of whipped cream on top to serve."],["Renastep note","Renastep is a Food for Special Medical Purposes and must be used under medical supervision. Renastep is a ready to use feed for the dietary management of kidney disease from 3 years of age onwards. Renastep contains milk and fish. This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease and has been analysed using Nutrimen dietary analysis software. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information."]]},"6510397":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6390967":{"s":[[null,"Heat the olive oil in a large soup pot over medium-high heat. Add the onion and sauté 2-3 minutes or until the onions turn clear. Add the ground turkey and cook for 5-7 minutes until the turkey browns. Add the cabbage and cook for an additional 4 minutes."],[null,"Add all remaining ingredients, except for the brown rice. Simmer the soup for 7 minutes. Bring the soup to a boil; add the brown rice. Reduce the heat to a simmer and cover the pot for 5 minutes."]],"h":[]},"6965875":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F."],[null,"Heat a large non-stick skillet over medium heat. Add turkey and cook, stirring often, until crumbed and browned, 8–10 minutes. Transfer to a bowl with a slotted spoon."],[null,"Return the skillet to medium heat and add olive oil and peppers. Cook, stirring often, until peppers have softened, 7–8 minutes."],[null,"Return turkey to the skillet along with the marinara and rice. Stir to combine and transfer to a 9x13 baking dish. Sprinkle with cheese."],[null,"Bake for about 20 minutes, until the cheese is bubbly."]],"h":[]},"6500937":{"s":[],"h":[]},"2791":{"s":[[null,"Place corn tortilla in the microwave for 1-1/2 to 2 minutes."],[null,"Crush tortilla into pieces, the size of chips."],[null,"Combine eggs and egg whites; scramble soft and set aside."],[null,"Put oil in a pan on medium heat and when hot, add onions and sauté 1 minute."],[null,"Add tortilla, tomato and eggs."],[null,"Stir until eggs are done. Serve hot and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Each microwave gives different cooking times, but you will know the corn tortilla is done when it smells like popcorn cooking."],[null,"Use 6 unsalted corn tortilla chips as a short cut."],[null,"Corn tortillas are high in phosphorus compared to flour tortillas or white bread. Limit corn tortillas to help reduce phosphorus, especially if your lab values have been higher than the normal range."]]},"6504760":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl or jar, combine 2 tablespoons chia seeds, 1/2 cup almond milk, and 1/2 teaspoon vanilla."],[null,"Stir well to make sure the chia seeds are evenly distributed."],[null,"Let the mixture sit for 2–3 minutes, then stir again to prevent clumping."],[null,"Enjoy immediately for a looser texture or refrigerate for a thicker pudding."]],"h":[]},"4662787":{"s":[[null,"In a saucepan, mix the egg yolks, milk, sugar, corn starch, vanilla extract, and cinnamon."],[null,"Bring to a boil over medium heat while stirring constantly until thickened."],[null,"Remove from heat and add butter. Stir to combine."],[null,"Transfer the cream into four dessert bowls or glasses and cover top of dessert with plastic wrap to avoid thickening of each top layer. Refrigerate for at least two hours."],[null,"Serve with ginger cookies."]],"h":[["Kidney-friendly and heart-healthy","For those with chronic kidney disease, it is important to follow a diet that is both kidney-friendly and heart-healthy. The key to a heart-healthy diet is eating less fat, especially saturated fat. Saturated fats can be naturally occurring, such as butter, meat fat, and coconut oil, or artificially made, called trans fats, commonly found in stick margarine and shortening. Saturated fats are easy to spot, as they are solid at room temperature. Many baking recipes include saturated fat. Margarine has less saturated fat than butter or shortening and is thus a better choice when baking. It is also possible to substitute oil for butter or shortening in many recipes. A good rule of thumb is to decrease the amount of oil by one-fourth compared to the amount of butter or shortening in the recipe. For example, if a recipe calls for 1 cup of butter or shortening, substitute three-fourths cup of oil. Experiment with your recipes to see if this substitution can work for you. To start, substitute half of the butter or shortening with oil. If that works well, then try substituting the entire amount. Packaged foods can have high levels of both saturated and trans saturated fats. Limit saturated fat as much as you can and avoid trans fat whenever possible. Fats that are liquid at room temperature such as olive and canola oils are unsaturated fats. These fats are the best to use. Careful reading of Nutrition Facts labels will help you accomplish this goal."]]},"3799":{"s":[[null,"Empty the vanilla pudding packs into a mixing bowl."],[null,"Gently cut 3 cups of the Reddi Wip® into bowl of pudding."],[null,"Layer the bottom of a 9” x 13” pan with graham crackers."],[null,"Spread half of pudding mixture on top of graham crackers."],[null,"Put another layer of graham crackers on top of the pudding mixture."],[null,"Spread the other half of pudding mixture on top of graham crackers."],[null,"Put last layer of graham crackers on top of pudding mixture."],[null,"Place in refrigerator overnight."],[null,"Upon removing from refrigerator and prior to serving, spray top of dessert with remaining whipped topping then sprinkle 1 cup of mini chocolate chip morsels over top of dessert."]],"h":[[null,"This recipe is best if prepared the night before you are going to serve it."],[null,"Reduce portion to 1/2 the size recommended if you have diabetes and count as 1-1/2 carbohydrate choices."]]},"3672":{"s":[[null,"Mix 1/4 to 1/2 of recipe at a time in a blender (depending on size of blender) for 20 seconds to blend the protein powder in well."],[null,"Serve cold and enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Recipe makes about 1/2 gallon. Store remaining beverage in a covered pitcher."],[null,"EAS whey protein powder used in the nutrition analysis contains 26 grams protein for 2 scoops. If you use a different brand of whey protein adjust the amount to provide approximately 156 grams protein for the recipe. Ask your dietitian about other protein powder options."],[null,"Substitute strawberry or chocolate whey protein powder for a different flavor beverage."]]},"3810":{"s":[[null,"Add popcorn kernels to brown bag. Microwave for 2-3 minutes until you only hear a few pops coming from the bag. You do not want to overcook and burn the popcorn."],[null,"Roll up the mint leaves and finely chop or crush. In a small saucepan combine olive oil, vanilla, sugar and mint. Bring to a slight boil, be sure all the sugar is dissolved. Add popcorn to a bowl and drizzle the mixture over the popcorn and stir or toss."]],"h":[[null,"You may also pop the popcorn in a large pot on the stove top if you don’t have a microwave. Add an additional 1 tablespoon of olive oil to the pot. Cover and place on medium to high heat until popcorn has stopped popping."],[null,"If mint leaves aren’t available, substitute 1/2 teaspoon of mint extract."]]},"3294":{"s":[[null,"Pour almond milk and protein powder in a blender. Blend well."],[null,"Add root beer extract and blend."],[null,"Pour mixture into 4 cups and slowly add 2 tablespoons root beer soda. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Select almond milk or other milk substitute without phosphate additives. Check labels and ingredient list or ask your dietitian about recommended products."],[null,"When soda is added mixture will foam, so add slowly and stop until bubbles reduce if needed to prevent bubbling over."],[null,"A & W® diet root beer and Barq’s® diet root beer are acceptable brands of root beer for a kidney diet because there are no phosphate additives."],[null,"If Syntrax Nectar® whey protein powder is unavailable, ask your dietitian for an appropriate substitute. EAS® 100% whey protein powder is an option and provides approximately 13 grams of protein per scoop."]]},"2042":{"s":[[null,"Combine all ingredients."],[null,"Mix until whipped topping melts completely"]],"h":[[null,"People with diabetes can substitute stevia, Equal®, Splenda® or other sugar substitute if desired. Carbohydrate is reduced to 5 grams per serving if sugar substitute is used instead of sugar."]]},"1843":{"s":[[null,"Using a handheld mixer, mix the cream cheese with the protein powder, cinnamon and vanilla extract."],[null,"Spread 1 teaspoon of cream cheese mixture on each of 4 vanilla wafers."],[null,"Top each cookie with 1 berry."]],"h":[[null,"Substitute blackberries or raspberries for blueberries if desired."],[null,"Lemon, almond or other extract can be used in place of the vanilla extract, if desired."],[null,"One box of vanilla wafer cookies contains 70-80 cookies."],[null,"Compare whey protein brands and look for a brand without added phosphate additives. Ask your dietitian for recommendations on the lower phosphorus brands."]]},"7772849":{"s":[[null,"Put the plums in a large, shallow non-stick pan. Add enough water so that the fruit is half covered and stick the pan over a medium heat. Sprinkle over the sweetener, if using, and add the cloves."],[null,"Split the vanilla pods in half lengthways and scrape out the seeds using a knife. Add the pods, seeds and bay leaf to the pan. Bring to a simmer, cover and reduce the heat to low. Cook for 6-7 minutes, until the plums have collapsed slightly and the juices have mixed together."],[null,"Add the redcurrants and raspberries and cook for a further 1-2 minutes."],[null,"Remove the vanilla pods, bay leaf and the cloves. Divide the fruit and the juice between 4 dessert bowls and serve decorated with the vanilla pods."]],"h":[[null,"When buying vanilla beans, look out for slightly wrinkled and very dark brown or black pods, which give the best flavour."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"9167347":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 350°F/176°C and line a baking tray with parchment paper."],[null,"Add everything except the milk to a medium bowl and mix well, adding the milk only if the batter appears too dry. (This will vary depending on how drippy your almond butter is.)"],[null,"Scoop the batter using a small cookie scoop onto your baking sheet, leaving plenty of space in between each one. You should get 14-15 cookies. Then, use a fork to gently press each cookie down and make a crisscross pattern."],[null,"Bake for 8-9 minutes, remove from the oven and let cool for 10 minutes at room temperature before handling."]],"h":[[null,"If the batter appears too dry (it should be thick), add 1-2 tablespoons of plant-based milk. Depending on how drippy your almond butter is, you may or may not need the milk."],[null,"Wet your fork after crisscrossing every few cookies or so to prevent it from sticking to the batter."],[null,"The cookies will appear underdone at the 8-9 minute mark, but they will firm up as they cool down, so do not overbake ."]]},"9762840":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350°F/176°C and line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Combine the almond flour, sugar, baking powder, and salt in a medium bowl. Then add 2 tablespoons of maple syrup and mix well. Use a fork to help get the syrup combined and keep mixing until you have a slightly sticky batter. If needed, add another tablespoon of maple syrup. (If you weigh the flour, 2 tablespoons should do it.)"],[null,"Roll the batter into one-inch balls (or use a small cookie scoop) and place them onto your baking sheet, spacing them at least 2 inches apart. You should get 9-10 cookies."],[null,"Bake until the edges are lightly golden, approx. 13-15 minutes and remove them from the oven. Let the cookies cool for at least 10 minutes before transferring them to a wire rack to cool completely."]],"h":[[null,"Weigh your flour for the best results . Scooping into a measuring cup can compact the flour and you may end up with more than needed. Use slightly wet hands to roll your cookie dough if the batter is sticking to your hands. Make sure to use active baking powder in order for these cookies to spread. If you have baking powder that’s been open in the pantry for several months, it may lose its effectiveness. If the cookies are not spreading in the oven after 8-10 minutes, press them down gently with the back of a spoon. Cookies keep covered at room temperature for 2-3 days, refrigerated for up to 1 week, or freeze airtight for up to 6 months. Blanched almond flour will produce cookies that are slightly fluffier and lighter in colour. Unblanched almond flour cookies will be slightly darker in colour, but still delicious. You may grind your own almonds in a powerful blender to make flour if you don’t have any on hand. However, if your flour is coarse , you will need extra liquid to make up for it. Add 1-2 tablespoons of water or milk until the batter is sticky and holds when rolling into balls. I like these cookies salty/sweet but if you’re watching your sodium intake, you may reduce from ¼ teaspoon to ⅛ teaspoon of salt, if preferred."]]},"9596194":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350℉/176℃ and line a loaf pan with parchment paper."],[null,"Add all the dry ingredients to a large mixing bowl and whisk. Then add the applesauce and soy milk and stir until no dry bits remain, without overmixing. Then, fold in the diced apples, reserving a small handful for sprinkling on top."],[null,"OPTIONAL: If using the cinnamon swirl, mix the sugar and cinnamon in a small bowl. Then pour half of the apple bread batter into your loaf pan and sprinkle the sweet cinnamon mixture on top in an even layer. (You may reserve a small amount of the mixture to sprinkle on top of the second half of the batter if you'd like.) Then pour the remaining half of the batter on top of the swirl, doing your best to evenly spread it across, without mixing the swirl into the batter. If you've reserved some apple pieces, sprinkle those on top, gently press them down and sprinkle any remaining sugar/cinnamon mixture on top of the apples."],[null,"If skipping the cinnamon swirl, pour the entire batter into your prepared loaf pan and sprinkle the reserved apple pieces on top."],[null,"Bake for 45-55 minutes, or until a toothpick inserted in the middle of your loaf comes out mostly clean, or with a few crumbs. Then remove it from the oven and let it cool for 10 minutes on a cooling rack before transferring the loaf to a cutting board. Continue cooling for another 5-10 minutes if you can wait (it makes slicing easier). Then slice your loaf and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Weigh your flour for the best results . If you don’t have a kitchen scale, spoon the flour into your measuring cup and level with a flat knife. Never scoop the flour from the bag."],[null,"Like most baked goods, do not over-mix your batter . When adding the wet ingredients to the dry, stir until no floury bits remain and gently fold in the apple pieces."],[null,"Dice the apples very small. Small pieces are distributed more evenly."],[null,"Prepare and cut your apples AFTER preparing the rest of your ingredients so they don’t brown. Or sprinkle them with lemon juice if you’re working ahead."],[null,"This bread is very moist and individual ovens will vary. Bake your vegan apple bread until a toothpick inserted in the middle comes out mostly dry . That may take a little less or a little more time, depending on your oven. Start checking around doneness around the 45-minute mark."],[null,"Leftovers will keep covered at room temperature for 2 days, refrigerated for up to 5 days, or in the freezer for up to 3 months. Make sure the loaf is completely cooled before freezing."]]},"9652525":{"s":[[null,"Bring a large pot of salted water to boil, and cook pasta according to package directions for al dente pasta. Drain and return to the pot."],[null,"Meanwhile, add all your ingredients (except the pasta) to a high speed blender and process until smooth. Pour the sauce over your pasta and mix well."],[null,"Serve with your choice of garnish and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"If you do not have a high speed blender , make sure to soak your cashews first. Soak in boiling hot water for 30 minutes, then drain and use as directed. Salt your pasta cooking water for best results. Do not overcook your pasta . Cook according to the package directions for al dente. Pasta tastes best with a little bite, and not overly soft. Leftovers keep refrigerated for 2-3 days. To reheat, add some plant milk, water or broth to a skillet with the pasta, to remoisten and heat through."]]},"9274349":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 425℉/218℃ and grab a casserole dish that is 9\"x 13\" or similar to set aside. Then, fill a large pot with generously salted water and bring it to a boil."],[null,"While waiting for your water to boil, make your dairy-free ricotta. Add all the ricotta ingredients to your food processor and process until smooth. Stop to scrape down the sides as needed and set it aside."],[null,"By now, your water should be boiling, so add your pasta to the pot and UNDERCOOK it by 2-3 minutes compared to the package directions. Then drain immediately."],[null,"While the pasta is cooking, prepare your sauce by stirring the Bolognese ingredients in a bowl. Set it aside."],[null,"When the pasta is cooked, begin assembling your vegan baked pasta dish."],["Assembly","Add a thin layer of sauce to the bottom of your dish to prevent sticking. Then add half of your cooked pasta on top, another thin layer of sauce, and half of the ricotta cheese. Spread the cheese as best as you can, but it doesn't need to be perfect."],["Assembly","Now add the remaining half of the pasta, another layer of sauce, and the remaining ricotta cheese. Spread the cheese, add one more layer of sauce, and then sprinkle with the vegan Parmesan cheese, if using."],["Assembly","Bake uncovered for 20 minutes, and then remove the tray from the oven. Garnish with fresh herbs, and sprinkle with red pepper flakes, black pepper, or more vegan parmesan cheese."]],"h":[[null,"Do not overcook your pasta . Remember that it will continue cooking in the oven, so it’s best to UNDERCOOK it by 2-3 minutes."],[null,"If you don’t have a strong food processor or blender, soak your cashews in hot water before blending. Boil some water in a pot or kettle and soak the cashews for 15-20 minutes. This will soften them, making them easier to process. Drain and make the cheese as directed."],[null,"For nut-free : use sunflower seeds instead of cashews for the ricotta with similar results. Omit the walnuts, or use pepitas with similar results. Or make my tofu ricotta instead."],[null,"Don’t be overwhelmed by the number of ingredients and steps. Most are pantry ingredients and spices and many of the steps are done simultaneously, so it won’t take long. See the process shots above, in the post, if needed, to assist with assembling."],[null,"Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-4 days or you may freeze for up to 3 months. Unlike most of the recipes on the blog, this one does exceed 400 calories per serving, so consider this for an occasional cheat day. 😉"]]},"9152488":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375℉/190℃ and grab a casserole dish or another oven-safe dish that is long enough to hold spaghetti."],[null,"Add half a cup of the tomato sauce to the bottom of your baking dish. Then place the pasta on top. Next, pour the broth on top and gently mix to get the liquid in between your noodles to prevent sticking."],[null,"Top with all the remaining ingredients: onion, garlic, spinach, sundried tomatoes, oregano, salt, pepper, and the remaining sauce."],[null,"Bake uncovered for 30 minutes. Then gently stir/mix and continue baking for another 15 minutes, or until desired doneness is reached."]],"h":[[null,"Bake your dish until the pasta is ‘al dente’ for the best texture . Do not overbake. Al dente means that the pasta is still firm once cooked, giving optimal texture in every bite."]]},"9340676":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350℉/176℃ and line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Mash the bananas in a mixing bowl and add the applesauce and sugar. Mix well."],[null,"Next, add all the dry ingredients: flour, baking soda, salt and stir until combined without overmixing. Then fold in the chocolate chips."],[null,"Scoop the mixture using a medium cookie scoop onto your prepared tray, leaving plenty of space between each cookie. You should get approx. 9 cookies. (Or use a small cookie scoop to get approx. 18 smaller cookies.)"],[null,"Bake for 12-15 minutes or until the edges and bottoms are golden brown. Remove the cookies from the oven and let them cool at room temperature for at least 15 minutes before handling them and transferring to a cooling rack."]],"h":[[null,"Use very ripe bananas for the best flavour and natural sweetness. The skins should be spotted brown."],[null,"I recommend using a kitchen scale to weigh the flour for the best results. Scooping flour from a bag can often lead to too much flour being used, resulting in denser cookies."],[null,"Leave plenty of space between your cookie dough balls to allow the cookies to spread in the oven."],[null,"Leftover cookies will keep at room temperature for 2 days, in the fridge for 3-4 days, or frozen for up to 3 months."]]},"9122292":{"s":[[null,"Add everything to your blender or food processor, starting with just 1 tablespoon of milk. Blend until smooth, and add more milk if needed. This will vary according to how dry your dates are, and how powerful your appliance is. Keep processing until the mixture is smooth and creamy, scraping down the sides, as needed."],[null,"Chill the pudding in the fridge for 1 hour or longer. Then divide the mixture between two cups and top them as desired."]],"h":[]},"9184828":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 350℉/176℃ and line a loaf pan with parchment paper."],[null,"Mash the bananas and combine all the wet ingredients in a large bowl. Then add the dry ingredients and still until combined without overmixing. Fold in the chocolate chips if using."],[null,"Pour the batter into your lined loaf pan, smoothing out the top and adding more chocolate chips to the top if you'd like. Gently press them down."],[null,"Bake the pumpkin banana bread for 45-55 minutes or until a toothpick inserted in the middle comes out clean. Then remove it from the oven and let rest for 15-20 minutes before transferring the loaf to a cooling rack or cutting board to continue cooling."]],"h":[[null,"Weigh the flour using a kitchen scale for the most accurate results . Scooping flour from a bag often results in too much flour being used and can alter the texture."],[null,"Use overly ripe bananas. The more brown spots, the better, as the sweeter they will be. Since the recipe uses very little sweetener, you want to make sure your bananas will provide ample sweetness."],[null,"Measure your mashed bananas. Bananas vary in size. So make sure to use enough for sweetness and moisture. Measure 1 full cup of mashed banana."],[null,"Use fresh + active baking powder ! Baking powder that has been open in the pantry for 6+ months may start to lose its effectiveness."],[null,"Use parchment paper to line your loaf pan. Although a nonstick loaf pan will do the trick, I find it easier to remove the loaf from the pan when using parchment paper. You can easily lift the bread out and place it on a wire rack without breaking it."],[null,"Individual ovens will vary. So test the doneness of your pumpkin banana bread using a toothpick inserted in the middle. When it comes out mostly dry and clean, it’s ready."],[null,"Let it cool. Allow extra time for the loaf cool down. A minimum of 20-30 mins on a cooling rack is recommended to completely set and make it easier to slice."],[null,"Leftovers keep at room temperature for 2-3 days, in the refrigerator for up to 5 days, or freeze it for up to 3 months."]]},"9440117":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your waffle maker over medium-high heat, or according to its manufacturer directions."],[null,"Mash your bananas and add them to a large mixing bowl along with the milk and vanilla. Mix well."],[null,"Then stir in the flour and baking powder until combined, without overmixing."],[null,"Cook the waffles according to the manufacturer's directions, approx. 4-6 minutes, or until the desired doneness is reached."]],"h":[[null,"Weigh your flour for the best results . If scooping from a bag, you may have too much and need more liquid to get the batter to the right consistency."],[null,"If you don't have a kitchen scale , spoon the flour into your measuring cup and use a knife to scrape off the excess."],[null,"Use very ripe bananas that are spotted brown for natural sweetness and the best flavour."],[null,"Make sure your waffle iron is HOT before adding the waffle batter to it, to prevent sticking."],[null,"Do not lift the lid too soon or your waffles will break and lift the lid slowly and carefully to check for sticking."],[null,"Subsequent batches of waffles cook a little faster than the first batch so watch closely."],[null,"Keep leftovers in the fridge for 3-4 days or frozen for up to 3 months."]]},"9966381":{"s":[[null,"Drain and rinse the beans, chop all the veggies, and add them to a large bowl."],[null,"In another small bowl, combine the salad dressing ingredients. Then pour the dressing over the salad and mix well to evenly coat. Enjoy immediately or refrigerate for 1 hour before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Plan to make the dish approx. 1 hour before serving as it tastes best when chilled."],[null,"This salad tastes best the same day its made, but leftovers keep in the fridge for 2-3 days,"]]},"9430487":{"s":[[null,"Place the soy curls in a large bowl and cover with the broth. Let that soak for about 7-8 minutes, mixing at the halfway point to ensure they all get soaked."],[null,"Meanwhile, steam your broccoli in a pot or pan of water for 4-5 minutes, until fork tender but still a little crisp (or your desired doneness). Then drain and set it aside."],[null,"Preheat a cast iron pan or another large skillet over medium high heat and then fish out the soy curls from the broth (reserving the broth) and dry sauté the curls for 3-4 minutes, stirring often, to slightly brown them."],[null,"Meanwhile, add all the sauce ingredients to the bowl with the remaining broth and whisk to combine. Then add the sauce and broccoli to the pan of soy curls and simmer for 2-3 minutes to slightly thicken the sauce. Serve with rice, noodles, green onion, and/or sesame seeds."]],"h":[[null,"Stir the curls often when sautéing to prevent sticking since we’re not using oil in this recipe. If you’re not avoiding oil, you may use a tablespoon of sesame oil for added flavour."],[null,"Leftovers keep refrigerated for 2-3 days in a sealed container."]]},"9551453":{"s":[[null,"Add the onion, carrots, and garlic to a pot with 3 tablespoons of broth or water and sauté until softened, approx. 5-6 minutes. Add a little more water or broth as needed to prevent sticking."],[null,"Then add all the remaining ingredients and bring to a boil over high heat. Once boiling, reduce heat to maintain a low boil/simmer and cook for 12-15 minutes until the carrots are tender."],[null,"Turn off the heat and use an immersion blender to puree SOME of the soup, while leaving some texture. OR, transfer half of the soup to a stand blender, puree it, and return it to the pot with the remaining soup."],[null,"Serve the black bean soup with garnishes of your choice."]],"h":[]},"9113470":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350℉/176℃ and line a loaf pan with parchment paper. Set it aside."],[null,"Add everything except the chocolate chips to a food processor and blend until smooth and combined."],[null,"Transfer the blondie mixture to your loaf pan and smooth the top with a wooden spoon or silicone spatula. Then top with the chocolate chips if you're using them. Gently press them down."],[null,"Bake the vegan blondies in your preheated oven for 30 minutes, or until a toothpick inserted in the middle comes out clean and dry. Then remove from the oven and let cool for 10-15 minutes in the pan before transferring to a wire rack to continue cooling. The blondies will be easier to slice once cooled."]],"h":[[null,"Use parchment paper to line your pan. Although greasing will do the trick for nonstick, it will be a lot easier to remove the brownies using the paper to lift them out. (And they'll cool faster this way!)"],[null,"Wet your knife in between cuts when slicing your blondies, for smoother, nicer-looking edges and to prevent sticking."],[null,"The optional chocolate chips are INCLUDED in the nutritional information below."],[null,"Leftovers keep at room temperature for 2-3 days, up to 1 week in the fridge, or keep them frozen for up to 3 months."]]},"9655561":{"s":[[null,"Prepare your pie crust of choice and blind bake according to its directions. If you're using my oil free pie crust, bake 1 crust for 15 minutes, until the edges are golden. Then remove from the oven and set aside. For the second pie crust roll it out and set aside to place on top of your pie, once filled."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F."],[null,"In a mixing bowl, combine the blueberries, sugar, corn starch, lemon juice and cinnamon. Mix well. Then pour the mixture into your prepared pie crust."],[null,"Now use the second pie crust to cover the filling. You may place the entire crust on top and crimp the edges, making vent holes in the middle of your crust. Alternatively, you may make a basket weave pattern or star shaped (or any shape) cut outs to cover the pie. Your choice."],[null,"Brush some plant milk of choice on your top crust and you may optionally sprinkle with sugar."],[null,"Bake your pie for 45-55 minutes, until the juices from the blueberries are bubbling and the crust is golden. If your pie is cooking too quickly, cover the top with a pie shield or use aluminum foil to prevent it from getting too dark."],[null,"Remove from the oven and let cool completely before slicing and serving. The pie must cool to completely set."]],"h":[[null,"If your crust is cooking too quickly , cover it with a pie shield or aluminum foil to prevent the crust from being over done. Make sure to cut vent holes if using a full pie crust for the top! If making a basket weave pattern or using the star cut outs, vents are not necessary. Let your blueberry pie cool completely before slicing ! The cool down time is crucial to getting your pie nicely set. Although you CAN cut while warm, it will be runny until cooled. Leftovers can be refrigerated for 3-4 days, or sealed air tight and frozen for up to 2 months. Nutritional information includes 2 full oil free pie crusts. If using another crust, skipping the top crust, or using star cutouts, nutritional info will vary."]]},"9608562":{"s":[[null,"Add the onion, celery and carrots to a large pot with a tablespoon or two of water. Sauté over medium heat until softened, approx 5 minutes. Add more water if needed to prevent sticking."],[null,"Then add the cauliflower, both potatoes, broth, and all the seasoning to the pot. Bring to a boil over high heat, then reduce to medium low. Cook until the vegetables are soft, approx 8-10 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, in a separate pot or skillet, cover your broccoli with water and bring to a boil, then lower heat to simmer and cook until fork tender, approx 4-6 minutes. Drain and set aside."],[null,"While the soup and broccoli are cooking, add all the cheddar sauce ingredients to your blender. Blend until smooth and set aside."],[null,"Use an immersion blender to puree your pot of soup until smooth. Then stir in the cooked broccoli and the cheddar sauce and mix well. Enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"If you do not have a highspeed blender , soak your cashews in boiling hot water for 15-20 minutes and then drain. This will soften them, making them easier to blend."],[null,"Make sure there are no loose bits of cashews in the cheese sauce for the best texture. Process a little longer if needed to make it smooth."],[null,"Cook the broccoli separately . You may use a steamer, another pot, or a skillet, but separately is best. Once the soup is pureed, add the cooked broccoli florets to the pot."],[null,"Cut your broccoli into SMALL bite-size florets since these will remain whole, and not be pureed with the remaining ingredients."],[null,"Use a deep pot to avoid splashes when hand-blending your soup with an immersion blender."],[null,"Leftovers will keep refrigerated for 3-4 days, or frozen airtight for 3-4 months."]]},"9775065":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your waffle iron on medium heat, or according to its manufacturer directions."],[null,"Combine the soy milk and apple cider vinegar in a large bowl and set aside for a few minutes. The milk will thicken and curdle, resulting in vegan buttermilk."],[null,"Once curdled, add all the remaining ingredients to the same bowl and stir until combined. Then cook the waffles according to the manufacturer's directions, approx. 3-5 minutes, or until desired doneness is reached."],[null,"Serve with your favourite toppings and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Weigh your flour and powder for the best results . If scooping from a bag, you may have too much and need more liquid to get the batter the right consistency."],[null,"If you don't have a kitchen scale , spoon the flour into your measuring cup and use a knife to scrape off the excess."],[null,"Make sure your waffle maker is HOT before adding the waffle batter to it, to prevent sticking."],[null,"Do not lift the lid too soon or your waffles will break and lift the lid slowly and carefully to check for sticking."],[null,"Subsequent batches of waffles cook a little faster than the first batch so watch closely."]]},"9264119":{"s":[[null,"Add everything to a high-speed blender and process until smooth and creamy."],[null,"Transfer the sauce to a clean glass jar or lidded container and store it in the refrigerator for up to 10 days."]],"h":[[null,"If you don’t have a high-speed blender, soak your cashews in cool water overnight, or soak them in boiling hot water for 30 minutes. Then drain the cashews and use them as directed. Soaking the cashews will soften them, making them easier to blend."],[null,"If you’re still having trouble getting your sauce smooth, you may strain any loose cashew bits using a fine mesh strainer or a nut milk bag ."],[null,"Make it nut-free and swap the cashews with shelled raw pepitas or sunflower seeds with similar results. Make sure they do not have added salt."],[null,"For lower sodium , use water instead of vegetable broth."],[null,"For less spice replace ¼ to ½ of the called-for hot sauce with broth or water."],[null,"For less tang , use only 2 tablespoons of the vinegar or sub for apple cider vinegar instead."],[null,"For a creamier/thicker sauce , use up to ⅔ cup of cashews or seeds."],[null,"Make it a smoky hot sauce and add 1 teaspoon of smoked paprika."],[null,"Store in a clean, glass jar or container in the refrigerator for up to 10 days, or freeze for up to 6 months. Use an ice cube tray to freeze it in individual portion sizes."]]},"9515780":{"s":[[null,"Bring a large pot of salted water to boil and cook your pasta according to package directions for al dente pasta. Drain, return to the pot, and set aside."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the squash to a small sauce pot, cover with water and boil for 8 minutes, or until easily pierced with a fork. Then drain it and add to your blender, along with all remaining sauce ingredients, starting with 3/4 cup of the milk. Blend until smooth, and add more milk if needed for a thinner consistency."],[null,"Then pour the sauce over the pasta, mix well, and serve with any garnish you like. (Reserve 1-2 cups of the sauce if you want to add more on top of each bowl for serving.)"]],"h":[[null,"Salt your pasta water. Make sure to add enough salt to your pot of water for the best texture and flavour. Here's a handy guide to help you salt your water perfectly each time. If you do not have a powerful blender , add the cashews to the same pot with the squash and boil until the squash is cooked. This will soften the cashews and help them blend more smoothly. You may need more or less milk, depending on the size of your squash. As the pasta sits with the sauce, it will continue to absorb it. So, if you plan to have leftovers , reserve a cup of the sauce in a separate container before mixing it into the pasta. Add the reserved sauce to a pan with the leftover pasta when reheating to return it to a creamy state. Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-4 days. You may freeze the sauce for up to 3 months in an airtight, freezer-safe container. I don’t recommend freezing pasta as it alters the texture."]]},"9373142":{"s":[[null,"Bring a pot of generously salted water to a boil and cook your pasta according to the package directions for 'al dente' pasta. When cooked, reserve half a cup of the pasta water, drain the rest and return to the pot."],[null,"Meanwhile, add all the sauce ingredients to your blender and process until smooth."],[null,"Pour the sauce over the pasta and then add the reserved pasta water to your empty (but NOT washed) blender. Give it a good swirl to collect any remaining sauce stuck on the sides of your blender. Then pour that over the pasta as well. Give everything a good stir and serve with extra freshly cracked pepper, and enjoy!"]],"h":[]},"9357019":{"s":[[null,"Make sure to prep all your ingredients and chop your vegetables before you begin, since this dish moves along rather quickly."],[null,"Cook your penne in a pot of generously salted water, according to the package directions for 'al dente' pasta. Drain and set it aside."],[null,"Meanwhile, combine the sauce ingredients in a small bowl or measuring cup, and set it aside."],[null,"Then, add the chopped onion, mushrooms, and peppers to a sauté pan with 1/4 cup of water. Sauté over medium heat for 4-5 minutes, stirring often, until the veggies are tender, but do not overcook them. Then add the chickpeas and the sauce you just mixed in the previous step to the same pan. Mix well and let that simmer for 3-4 minutes to slightly thicken the sauce. (Taste the sauce and add more Cajun seasoning if needed, or some salt + pepper.)"],[null,"Now turn off the heat, and add the cooked penne to the same pan, and mix to evenly coat each piece. Serve with fresh parsley or cilantro and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Salt your pasta water. Make sure to add enough salt to your pot of water for the best texture and flavour. Here's a handy guide to help you salt your water perfectly each time."],[null,"Cook your pasta al dente. Do not overcook! Al dente means that the pasta is still firm once cooked, giving optimal texture in every bite. To ensure your pasta does not overcook, start taste testing a few minutes before the package says it will be ready. It should be tender, but still firm."],[null,"Taste the sauce once cooked and add more Cajun seasoning if a spicier sauce is preferred, or add some salt and black pepper, if needed. (This will vary according to the broth you’ve used.)"],[null,"I made this CAJUN SEASONING BLEND for this dish. Results and spice levels will vary according to the recipe or store-bought brand being used. Taste your blend to ensure the spice level is to your liking."],[null,"Keep leftovers in the fridge for 3-4 days."]]},"9623848":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 350°F/176°C and grab a baking dish or another oven-safe dish that measures approximately 9x13 inches."],[null,"Add the spinach to a pan or skillet and wilt over medium-high heat. If needed, added a couple of drops of water to prevent sticking. Once wilted, set it aside."],[null,"Now, add all the vegan ricotta ingredients (EXCEPT the spinach) to your food processor and process until mostly smooth. Then add the wilted spinach and pulse several times to chop and distribute it throughout your ricotta. Do not over-process the spinach, or the cheese may turn green."],[null,"Combine the sauce ingredients in a medium bowl and mix well. Then ladle a thin layer of the sauce into your baking dish."],[null,"Use a pastry bag to fill your cannelloni shells with the vegan ricotta filling. Fill one side, then rotate and fill the other side. Place the stuffed cannelloni in your baking dish. Repeat with the remaining shells, arranging them in a single layer, with a little space in between each one."],[null,"Cover the cannelloni with the rest of the sauce and sprinkle with vegan parmesan cheese (if using). Then cover with parchment paper, followed by aluminum foil, and bake in your preheated oven for 40 minutes. Then remove the paper and bake 10 minutes longer, until the sauce is bubbling."],[null,"Remove from the oven, garnish with more basil if you'd like, and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Before adding the spinach to your ricotta , taste the cheese mixture and adjust for salt, pepper, or any other flavours you’d like to add. You may also add an additional tablespoon of water, vinegar, or lemon juice at this point if you feel it’s needed. Do NOT overprocess the spinach , as you don’t want the cheese to turn green. Instead, you want ribbons of spinach throughout, so pulse until chopped and distributed only. Use a piping bag/pastry bag to fill your vegan cannelloni without the tip. OR cut one triangular corner of a ziptop bag to make your own piping bag if you don’t have one. Stuff one side of the cannelloni shell, then rotate and stuff the other side. Leave a little space in between each stuffed cannelloni shell as they will grow as they cook. The serving size is for 3 stuffed cannelloni or ¼ of the recipe."]]},"9255743":{"s":[[null,"If making the ranch dipping sauce, start by putting your cashews to soak before you begin prepping your cauliflower. Once soaked, prepare the ranch according to its directions and refrigerate until needed."],[null,"Line a baking tray with parchment paper and preheat your oven to 450 degrees F."],[null,"Place your cut up cauliflower in a large bowl. Then in a separate bowl, combine your flour and all the seasonings and mix to combine. Then add the milk and mix well to make your batter. Now pour the batter into your bowl with the cauliflower and mix well to evenly coat each piece."],[null,"Place your coated cauliflower on your prepared baking tray, one at a time, in a single layer and bake for 20 minutes. Flip once at the halfway point."],[null,"Meanwhile, prepare your buffalo wing sauce by adding all its ingredients to a small sauce pan. Whisk to combine and simmer over medium heat 3-5 minutes, allowing the flavours to combine."],[null,"Remove the cauliflower from the oven, and coat the bites in your buffalo sauce. I use a silicone brush to brush each piece of cauliflower with a generous amount of the sauce. Then return to the oven for 10-15 minutes, flipping once halfway through."],[null,"Serve with ranch and dunk away."],["Air Fryer Instructions","Place your cut up cauliflower in a large bowl. Then in a separate bowl, combine your flour and all the seasonings and mix to combine. Then add the milk and mix well to make your batter. Now pour the batter into your bowl with the cauliflower and mix well to evenly coat each piece."],["Air Fryer Instructions","Place your coated cauliflower into your crisp basket, inside the Ninja Foodi appliance. Then set it to 390 degrees F and air fry for 20 minutes, shaking your basket every 5 minutes or so."],["Air Fryer Instructions","Meanwhile, prepare your buffalo wing sauce by adding all its ingredients to a small sauce pan. Whisk to combine and simmer over medium heat 3-5 minutes, allowing the flavours to combine."],["Air Fryer Instructions","Then use a silicone brush to evenly coat your florets in the buffalo sauce. Continue air frying for another 10-15 minutes, shaking or flipping your florets at the halfway point. Cook time will vary according to the air fryer model you're using and floret size."],["Air Fryer Instructions","Serve with ranch and dunk away."]],"h":[[null,"If using the ranch dressing , prepare first and refrigerate until needed. For nut free , use soy or oat milk instead of cashew. Leftovers can be stored in the refrigerator for 2-3 days and reheat in your air fryer, oven or toaster oven. Expert Tips for the BEST results, every time! After coating your Buffalo cauliflower wings in the batter, do not dump them onto your baking tray . Excess batter at the bottom of the bowl will pool on your tray, causing the bites to stick together, and stick to the parchment paper. This will make them less crispy."],[null,"I know it’s tedious, but for best results, place your vegan buffalo wings on your baking tray, one piece at a time."],[null,"Make sure your vegan buffalo wings are in a single layer , with space in between each one. This will help crisp them up more."],[null,"Flip your cauliflower at the halfway point of the first AND second round (after coating in the Buffalo sauce) of baking. This helps get the most crispiness out of these delicious buffalo bites."]]},"9064307":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 450℉/232℃ convection bake and prepare a 12-inch pizza pan. (If you do not have convection, use the same temp at regular bake.)"],[null,"Stretch out your dough on a floured countertop or cutting board and carefully transfer it to your pan."],[null,"Evenly spread the tomato sauce and sprinkle the seasoning on top. Then generously distribute the mozzarella to cover the sauce."],[null,"Bake for 10-12 minutes, or until the desired doneness is reached."]],"h":[[null,"Flour your counter and rolling pin to prevent sticking when stretching your pizza dough."],[null,"If you don’t have a convection oven , use the same bake temperature, and increase the cooking time as needed."],[null,"Leftovers keep refrigerated for 2-3 days in a sealed container or freeze airtight for up to 3 months."]]},"9005368":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 425 degrees F and line a baking tray with parchment paper."],[null,"Cover your cubed potatoes with salted water in a small pot and bring to a boil. Cook for 10 minutes, or until easily pierced with a fork. Drain and place in a large mixing bowl. Then gently mash with a potato mashed until broken down, without over mashing. You want to keep some texture. Set aside."],[null,"Add the rice, chickpeas, oats, water and all the seasoning to your food processor. Pulse until combined and broken down, without over processing. You do not want to puree the mixture."],[null,"Transfer the processed ingredients into the bowl of mashed potatoes and mix well using a spatula."],[null,"Using wet hands, squeeze the mixture into a ball and then press down into a disc shape. Keep the patties on the thinner side and place on your prepared baking tray. Repeat with remaining mixture. You should get 8 large patties."],[null,"Bake for 20 minutes, then carefully flip and bake for another 10 minutes, or until lightly golden brown."],[null,"Serve your vegan chicken patties with or without a bun, and with all your favourite toppings."]],"h":[[null,"For added depth of flavour , cook your potatoes (and rice if you don’t have leftover) in broth or with some bouillon powder . Do not overly mash your potatoes . Remember, you’re not making mashed potatoes, and they should be lumpy for the best textured patties. So just mash a few times to ensure there are no overly large pieces. Do not over process your rice and chickpea mixture . Again, for the best textured vegan chicken patties, you want to keep some chunkiness, and not puree the ingredients. Use wet hands to shape your patties. Keep a small bowl of water near by, or work near your sink and slightly wet your hands before shaping each ball and then again before flattening each patty. This will help you shape the patties without the mixture sticking to your hands. It will also help prevent the patties from cracking as you’re shaping them. Keep your vegan chicken patties on the thinner side for best texture and crispiness. Serving little ones? Make a few smaller patties to serve as vegan chicken nuggets. Refrigerate leftovers for 3-4 days or freeze for up to 3 months. To freeze , cook as directed and freeze in an airtight container. Separate each patty with parchment paper to prevent sticking and reheat in the oven. Nutritional information is for 1 vegan chicken burger. Bun and toppings are not included in the calculation."]]},"9897433":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 400℉/204℃ and line a large baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Rinse your jackfruit very well to remove the brine and pull apart all the pieces to shred it. Add the shredded jackfruit to your tray along with the chickpeas and walnut pieces. Bake for 15 minutes and remove from the oven."],[null,"Meanwhile, add all the dressing ingredients, starting with 3/4 cup of water to a high-speed blender and process until smooth and creamy. Add the remaining two tablespoons of water if needed, to thin out your dressing and reblend."],[null,"Place your jackfruit, chickpeas, walnuts, celery, grapes, and green onion in a serving bowl and pour the dressing on top. Mix well and refrigerate for 1 hour before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Use young green jackfruit canned in brine or water , only. Do not use fresh jackfruit, and do not use jackfruit that is canned in syrup."],[null,"If you do not have a high-speed blender, soak your cashews in cool water overnight, or in boiling hot water for 15-30 minutes, and then drain. The soaking time will swell and soften the cashews, making them easier to blend."],[null,"This salad tastes great when freshly made, but tastes best when chilled for 1 hour or longer."],[null,"For nut-free: Omit the walnuts or sub with pepitas for the salad. For the dressing use raw sunflower seeds instead of cashews with similar results."],[null,"For a mayo-style dressing , use store-bought vegan mayo or my homemade oil-free pepita mayo ."],[null,"Leftovers will keep refrigerated in a sealed container for 2-3 days."]]},"9772614":{"s":[[null,"To a large pot, add the chopped onion, carrots, celery, peppers, and mushrooms with a tablespoon or two of water. Sauté over medium heat until softened, approx 5-8 minutes."],[null,"Add all remaining ingredients, EXCEPT the tofu to your pot and bring to a boil. Once boiling, reduce heat to simmer until the rice is cooked, approx. 30 minutes. Remove the bay leaves once cooked."],[null,"Meanwhile, puree the tofu in your blender, and add a drop or two of water if needed to get it moving. Once the soup is cooked, turn off the heat, and stir in the tofu until combined."],[null,"Taste and add salt and pepper, if needed."]],"h":[[null,"You may sub the potatoes for sweet potatoes, if preferred. Note that this will make the soup sweeter in flavour. I like medium firm tofu , as it thickens the soup nicely. But use what you have on hand. Soft or silken tofu works too. For soy free , sub the tofu for a can of blended white kidney or canellini beans. Or, use a cup or so of your favourite plant based milk. Note that the milk option won’t thicken your broth, but it will add extra creaminess. If you want to amp up the protein content, the tofu or beans are recommended. Use a food processor for finely chopped veggies if you’re feeding picky eaters. If you prefer a stew-like texture, hand chop the veggies a little larger. If you’re not a tofu fan , DON’T WORRY! I promise, you won’t taste it in the soup. The tofu adds lovely creaminess and silkiness without altering the flavour. (But if you can’t have soy for health reasons, see above for substitution suggestions.) You may prep ahead of time by chopping all your veggies a day in advance. Just keep your potatoes in water once peeled and chopped to prevent them from turning brown. Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-4 days or freeze them for up to 2 months in an airtight container."]]},"9097779":{"s":[[null,"Add all the dressing ingredients to a small blender and process until smooth. Taste for salt and pepper, add some if needed, and then set aside. NOTE: A small blender works best since the quantities are small. A large blender will not blend as smoothly."],[null,"Place the chickpeas in a medium mixing bowl and use a potato masher or large fork to smash most of the chickpeas. (Don't worry about getting every single one.) Then add the remaining salad ingredients and the dressing you just made and mix well."],[null,"Lay out the six tortilla wraps, and divide the baby spinach and salad between them. Start with the spinach in the center of your wrap, followed by 1/6 of your salad on top. Fold the top and bottom, and then fold the remaining opposite sides to create a neat pocket so the filling won't fall out."],[null,"Optional: Use a panini press to grill your wraps, folded side down to seal them. This adds a little crunch and beautiful grill lines. Plus, it keeps the wraps neatly sealed. You may then cut each wrap in half and serve."],[null,"Alternatively, you may cut your wraps into pinwheels. For this method, add the spinach and salad to the bottom side of the tortilla. Then tightly roll it from the bottom up. Grill it seal side down to secure. Then slice it in approximately 2-inch intervals."]],"h":[[null,"A small blender works best to make this salad dressing since the quantities are small. A large blender will not blend as smoothly because there won’t be enough ingredients for the blades to catch. If you don’t have a small blender , double up the dressing ingredients and freeze half for later use. If you don’t have a powerful blender (I used a Ninja single serve), soak the cashews in hot water for 20-30 minutes first to soften them. Then drain and blend with the remaining dressing ingredients. Cut the apples last to prevent them from browning. Once mixed with the dressing, they will not brown. You may prepare the salad and dressing in advance . Mix the salad with the dressing and refrigerate in a sealed container for up to 3 days. For fewer calories , use lettuce wraps or swiss chard instead of tortilla wraps. Or skip the wrap and enjoy it as a salad. The nutritional information below is for ONE vegan chicken wrap which represents one-sixth of the salad and dressing with one ten-inch whole grain tortilla wrap. NOTE that different brands of tortilla wraps vary greatly in calories, fat, and ingredients. Choose wraps that fit your dietary needs ."]]},"9375021":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350 degrees F and line a 5\"x 9\" loaf pan with parchment paper."],[null,"In a large bowl, mash the bananas and combine all the wet ingredients. Mix well."],[null,"To the same bowl, add the dry ingredients and mix until just combined, without over mixing. (A few lumps are a-ok!)"],[null,"Pour the mixture into your loaf pan and gently smooth the top with a silicone spatula. Then sprinkle the chocolate chips on top (if using) and very gently press them down."],[null,"Bake for 45-55 minutes until lightly golden and a toothpick inserted in the center comes out clean. Then remove from the oven and let cool for 10 minutes before removing the loaf from the pan, using the parchment paper to help lift it out. Continue cooling on cooling rack for at least 20-30 minutes before slicing."]],"h":[[null,"After pouring the batter into the loaf pan, tap it down gently, a few times on a flat surface to fill any gaps in the bread. Cooking time will vary according to your loaf pan size , so always check “doneness” by inserting a toothpick in the center to see if it comes out clean. Make sure to let your banana bread rest for at least 30 minutes to make slicing easier. The resting time allows your bread to completely set. If you can’t find dairy free chocolate chips , you may use chocolate chunks, or grab any vegan chocolate bar and bread it up yourself into chunks. For gluten free , use certified gluten free oat flour and if you don’t have any on hand, you may grind up gluten free oats in a blender or food processor until a flour like consistency is reached. To make it soy free , use almond, cashew milk or your choice. If you’re not a chocolate lover , skip the chocolate chips. Or top the loaf with banana slices, walnuts or pecans. Store leftovers at room temperature for up to 3 days, tightly wrapped. In the refrigerator for up to 1 week or freeze for up to 3 months."]]},"9305421":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350℉/176℃ and line a large baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Whisk together the 3 dry ingredients in a small bowl and set aside. In a separate, medium bowl, combine the wet ingredients and mix well. Then, add the dry ingredients and chocolate chips to the bowl of wet ingredients, and stir to combine."],[null,"Use a cookie scoop or tablespoon to scoop the mixture onto your prepared baking tray to make approx. 20 cookies, leaving space in between each one."],[null,"Bake for 10 minutes, then remove the cookies from the oven and let them cool for 10 minutes before transferring them to a cooling rack. Enjoy warm, or continue cooling to room temperature and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Weigh your flour for the most accurate results . Scooping flour from a bag often results in too much flour, producing dry results. If you do not have a kitchen scale, spoon your flour into your measuring cups, and level it off with the back of a knife."],[null,"Use ACTIVE baking powder . Once opened for 6+ months in the pantry, baking powder will start to lose its effectiveness."],[null,"Your batter will look similar to pancake batter , and that’s to be expected. Remember, these are low fat plant based cookies and not your ordinary butter filled variety."],[null,"Let your cookies cool for 10 minutes once removed from the oven, before handling. This cool down period will help them firm up and set."],[null,"Best served within 1-2 days, but will keep 2-3 days at room temperature, up to 5 days refrigerated, or frozen for up to 3 months."]]},"9693255":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your waffle maker over medium-high heat, or according to its manufacturer's directions."],[null,"Add the flour, cacao powder and baking powder to a large mixing bowl and whisk until combined. Then add the milk and vanilla and stir until no floury bits remain, without overmixing."],[null,"Ladle the batter onto your preheated waffle iron and cook according to the manufacturer's directions, approx. 4-6 minutes, or until the desired doneness is reached."]],"h":[[null,"Weigh your flour for the best results . If scooping from a bag, you may have too much and need more liquid to get the batter to the right consistency."],[null,"Weigh your flour and powder for the best results . If scooping from a bag, you may have too much and need more liquid to get the batter to the right consistency."],[null,"If you don't have a kitchen scale , spoon the flour into your measuring cup and use a knife to scrape off the excess."],[null,"Make sure your waffle maker is HOT before adding the waffle batter to it, to prevent sticking."],[null,"Do not lift the lid too soon or your waffles may break . Instead, lift the lid slowly and carefully to check for sticking."],[null,"Subsequent batches of waffles cook a little faster than the first batch so watch closely."],[null,"Leftover waffles will keep in the fridge for 3-4 days or frozen for up to 3 months."]]},"9708016":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350℉/176℃ and line a 5\"x9\" loaf pan with parchment paper."],[null,"Whisk all the dry ingredients in a large bowl and set aside."],[null,"Add the dates and water to a food processor and pulse until a paste is formed, scraping down the sides as needed. Transfer the date paste to the bowl of dry ingredients, along with all remaining ingredients including the chocolate chips if using. Mix until no floury bits remain."],[null,"Pour the batter into your prepared loaf pan. Sprinkle with additional chocolate chips if you'd like, and gently press them down."],[null,"Bake for 50-55 minutes, or until a toothpick comes out mostly clean. Then remove from the oven and let cool for at least 10 minutes before carefully transferring to a cooling rack to completely cool before slicing. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Measure and prep your ingredients before you begin. This will ensure you don’t miss anything, and don’t feel rushed in prepping ingredients in between steps."],[null,"Weigh the flour for the most accurate results . Scooping flour from a bag often results in too much flour being used, and will alter the texture of the loaf. If you must use measuring cups, spoon the flour into the cup, and scrape off the excess with the back of a knife."],[null,"Squeeze the shredded zucchini of its excess moisture into a bowl, or over your kitchen sink, before mixing it into the cake batter."],[null,"Use parchment paper in your loaf pan . This not only makes transferring the loaf easier once baked but also means you can avoid greasing your pan."],[null,"Completely cool your vegan chocolate zucchini bread to room temperature before slicing. The cooldown time helps the loaf set and makes slicing easier."],[null,"Wet your knife in between cuts when slicing to help with smooth, clean pieces."],[null,"Leftovers keep covered in plastic wrap, or in a sealed container at room temperature for 2-3 days. Refrigerate for 4-5 days, or freeze airtight in a freezer-safe container for up to 3 months. You may freeze sliced for quick and easy breakfasts or snacks, or freeze the loaf whole."]]},"9214087":{"s":[["For the Dressing","Add all the dressing ingredients to your blender and process until smooth. Transfer to a bowl or jar and set aside."],["For the Mushrooms","In a large skillet, add the sliced mushrooms, tamari, maple syrup, and smoked paprika. Sauté until reduced and liquids are absorbed, approx. 6-8 minutes. Set aside."],["For the Salad","Add the lettuce to a large serving dish and arrange the mushrooms and remaining toppings in rows, or evenly sprinkled. Serve with the dressing on top or on the side."]],"h":[[null,"Make it soy-free by using coconut aminos to replace the tamari/soy sauce. Or if you don’t have that on hand, use a little water and salt, or salty broth with similar results. Sub or omit any ingredients you don’t like. Other topping options include: Black or green olives"],[null,"Chives or scallions"],[null,"Cucumber"],[null,"Shredded carrots or cabbage"],[null,"Red kidney beans or crispy chickpeas"],[null,"Chopped pickles"],[null,"Keep leftover salad and dressing stored separately in the refrigerator for 3-4 days."]]},"9074637":{"s":[[null,"Wash and slice your peaches, and remove the pits. Add them to a blender or food processor along with the coconut milk and any optional ingredients you're using. Pulse until mostly combined, leaving some small chunks of peaches for texture."],[null,"Evenly distribute the mixture between six popsicle molds and then tap the mold down on your counter to release air bubbles. Place the lids on top and freeze for 6 hours or overnight. Keep frozen until serving.NOTE: If using popsicle sticks, freeze the popsicles for 1-2 hours, just enough for the sticks to hold straight, and then add the sticks and continue freezing until solid."],["To remove from the mold","Fill a bowl with warm water, as tall as your mold, and place it inside, without overflowing the top where the sticks are. Wait 15-20 seconds before removing, and then use a side-to-side motion to remove the popsicles from the mold."],["To remove from the mold","You may also run the popsicles under warm water using your kitchen sink faucet for 15-20 seconds, or until they remove easily."],["To remove from the mold","If the popsicles are still soft, place them on a plate and return them to the freezer."]],"h":[[null,"When peaches are in season and extra sweet, you may skip the optional maple syrup for a no sugar added dessert. For chunkier pieces of fruit in your peach popsicles, use a food processor and do not overprocess. For perfectly smooth peach popsicles, use a blender until pureed. (If you have picky eaters, this is the way to go.) If using popsicle sticks (instead of the lids that come with your mold), freeze the popsicles for 1-2 hours, just enough for the sticks to hold straight, and then add the sticks and continue freezing until solid. Freeze time will vary according to the thickness of your mold . Most popsicles will freeze in 4-6 hours. For less fat , use LIGHT canned coconut milk. For low fat , use another plant based milk such as almond milk, or cashew milk instead of coconut milk. Note, that the peach popsicles will be less rich this way."]]},"9747909":{"s":[[null,"Set your oven to broil on high, with the top rack about 6 inches down from the top burner."],[null,"Melt butter in a cast iron pan or another ovenproof skillet over medium heat. Then add the onions and garlic and sauté until translucent and lightly caramelized, approx. 5 minutes."],[null,"Turn off the heat and add the quartered pears, lemon juice, cinnamon, and maple syrup, and toss to coat. Then place the skillet in your oven and broil for about 7-10 minutes until the pears are lightly browned."],[null,"Remove from the oven and carefully transfer your soup to a blender. Add the milk and puree until smooth and creamy. Taste and add some salt and pepper if needed."],[null,"Pour your pear soup into bowls and enjoy warm, OR let stand at room temperature for about 20-30 minutes before enjoying."]],"h":[[null,"Enjoy this pear soup warm OR cold . It tastes fantastic both ways, but the flavours seem to really mingle nicely together once slightly cooled to room temperature. Leftovers will keep refrigerated in a sealed container for 3-4 days, or freeze airtight in a freezer-safe container for up to 3 months."]]},"9462370":{"s":[[null,"Bring 2.5 cups of broth to a boil in a medium pot. Then add the couscous, cover with the lid, and turn off the heat. Let stand for 5 minutes, then fluff with a fork. Transfer to a large mixing bowl and set it aside to cool. (OR follow the package directions according to the variety of couscous you're using.)"],[null,"Meanwhile, add all the salad dressing ingredients to a small bowl and stir until combined."],[null,"Add all the remaining salad ingredients and the dressing to the bowl of couscous, and mix well to evenly distribute the dressing. Serve immediately or refrigerate for 1 hour or longer to chill."]],"h":[[null,"I highly recommend cooking the couscous in broth instead of water to amplify the flavour of this dish. Feel free to sub or omit any veggies you’re not fond of . Some other great options include: Corn (thawed frozen, or canned)"],[null,"Halved cherry or grape tomatoes"],[null,"Any colour bell peppers"],[null,"Diced celery"],[null,"Bite-sized broccoli florets"],[null,"Chopped pickles"],[null,"Green onion or chives"],[null,"Diced zucchini"],[null,"Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-4 days."]]},"9211594":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350℉/176℃ and line a muffin pan with parchment liners."],[null,"Stir all the wet ingredients (except the cranberries) into a large bowl and let it rest for 5 minutes to curdle the soy milk. (See process shots above for a reference.)"],[null,"Once curdled, add all the dry ingredients and mix until combined without overmixing. Then fold in the cranberries."],[null,"Divide the mixture between your 12 muffin tins and bake for 24-25 minutes, or until a toothpick inserted into the center of a muffin comes out dry. Remove from the oven and let the muffin tray rest for 10 minutes before transferring them to a wire rack."]],"h":[[null,"Use active/fresh baking powder . Baking powder that has been open for 6+ months may start to lose its effectiveness."],[null,"Do not overmix your batter. With most muffin recipes, it’s best not to over-mix for optimal texture and fluffiness. When combining wet and dry ingredients, just mix until there are no more floury bits, but don’t worry about working out every lump."],[null,"Let your muffins cool . They need at least 10 minutes to rest once removed from the oven. Then, transfer them to a cooling rack to continue cooling."],[null,"Store leftovers at room temperature for 3-4 days in a sealed container or covered in plastic wrap. Make sure you cover the muffins once cool or they will get dry. Refrigerate for up to 6 days or freeze them airtight for up to 3 months."]]},"9368185":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 350 degrees and line a large baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Mash the banana in a large mixing bowl, then add the applesauce and maple syrup. Mix well. Then add all the dry ingredients and mix until evenly coated."],[null,"Use a medium cookie scoop and press the mixture into the scoop before releasing onto your tray. You want to press them into the scoop to ensure there are no gaps and prevent them from breaking apart. Repeat with remaining batter, you should get about 14 cookies."],[null,"Bake for 13-18 minutes. Remove from the oven and let cool for 5-10 minutes to completely set. For softer, chewier cookies bake for 13-14 minutes, but for crispier cookies, bake for 17-18 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Use VERY ripe bananas . Bananas with brown skins work best here for added natural sweetness since we’re not using much sugar to sweeten. Use a medium cookie scoop for evenly sized cookies, or an ice cream scoop if you don’t have one. Firmly push down the batter into your scoop before releasing onto your tray. This will help prevent gaps in your cookies so they hold together well. For chewier, moister cookies , bake for 13-14 minutes and remove from the oven but let them set at room temperature for at least 5 minutes before enjoying. For crispier texture , bake for 17-18 minutes. Make sure to use certified gluten free oats if needed. Cookies keep 3-4 days at room temperature, 1 week in the fridge or 3 months in the freezer."]]},"9644787":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F and line a 9\" x 5\" (or similar) loaf pan with parchment paper."],[null,"In a large mixing bowl, combine all your dry ingredients and whisk together. Set aside."],[null,"Add the pitted dates and water to a blender and process until completely smooth. This will make about 2 cups of date syrup. Measure 1.5 cups worth that will be used in your loaf and the remaining 1/2 cup will be used later to make the glaze. Do not use more than 1.5 cups in the loaf."],[null,"Now add your wet ingredients (except the cranberries), to the bowl of dry ingredients: 1.5 cups of the date syrup you made, 1/2 cup of orange juice, the orange zest, and the applesauce. Mix until combined and then fold in the cranberries."],[null,"Pour the batter into your prepared loaf pan and gently tap the loaf pan down 2-3 times on a hard surface to ensure there are no gaps in the bread. Don't press down with a spatula."],[null,"Bake in your preheated oven for 45-55 minutes, until a toothpick inserted in the middle, comes out dry. Depending on your oven and loaf pan size, cooking time will vary. Once baked, remove from the oven and let cool for 10 minutes before removing the bread from the pan. Transfer to a cooling rack to cool completely before glazing."],[null,"To make your glaze: Add 2 tablespoons of freshly squeezed orange juice to your remaining 1/2 cup of date syrup and mix well. Then drizzle the glaze over your cooled loaf. Slice and enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"If you do not have a powerful blender , soak your dates in warm water for about 15 minutes first. Then drain and make the date syrup as directed. This will help soften the dates, making them easier to blend. Use fresh and active baking powder. Baking powder that is open in your pantry for 6+ months can start to lose its effectiveness. Make sure your cranberry orange bread is completely cooled before glazing . If you don’t have fresh cranberries available where you live, fresh blueberries also work beautifully in this sweet bread. The bread will keep covered, at room temperature for 2-3 days, or freeze in an airtight container for 3-4 weeks."]]},"9545277":{"s":[["To make in Vitamix","Add all the ingredients, except the dairy-free milk to your Vitamix, or other powerful blender and blend until smooth, creamy, and hot. The soup took about 4 minutes to get hot in my Vitamix. Then pour in the milk, run for a few seconds to stir it in, and serve."],["To make on the stovetop","If you're using the cashew butter option, you do not need a blender. Just add everything, except the milk to a medium saucepan and whisk to combine. Bring to a low boil over medium heat and boil for 1-2 minutes. Then turn off the heat and stir in the dairy-free milk and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Run your blender long enough to make the soup hot enough to consume. This works well with high-quality blenders, such as a Vitamix . (affiliate link) If you don’t have a powerful blender , you may soak your cashews in hot water for 20-30 minutes and then drain them, before blending. This will help them break down more easily. OR use cashew butter and whisk into a small pot to avoid using a blender, altogether. For low-fat options , see above under our variations section. Keep leftovers in the fridge for up to 4 days or freeze airtight for up to 6 months."]]},"9892214":{"s":[[null,"Add all the ingredients to a pan or skillet and mix well. Bring to a low boil over medium heat, stirring occasionally. Continue simmering for 8-10 minutes until reduced by about half."],[null,"Then transfer 1 cup of your corn mixture to a blender and process until smooth. Return the pureed corn to your pan and stir to combine. Serve warm."]],"h":[[null,"For lower calories and fat , use light canned coconut milk instead of full fat, but note this will make the dish a little less rich."],[null,"To sweeten , I prefer maple syrup, but you may use other liquid sweeteners if preferred."],[null,"For coconut-free , use another plant-based milk, like cashew or soy milk. Again, note that this will make the dish less rich."],[null,"For soy-free , use another unsweetened non-dairy milk of your choice."],[null,"Leftovers will keep refrigerated for up to 3 days. Reheat them on the stovetop with a splash of milk or water to loosen them."]]},"9964694":{"s":[[null,"Add all the ingredients to a high speed blender, like a Vitamix and process until smooth and creamy. Start with half a cup of water and add more 1-2 tablespoons at a time until desired consistency is reached. (I find half a cup plus two tablespoons to be perfect.)"],[null,"Serve with corn on the cob, nachos, tacos, soups or chilis or over a salad."]],"h":[[null,"If you don’t have a high speed blender , soak your cashews in boiling hot water for 30 minutes, and then drain, before blending. The soaking time will soften them, making them easier to break down. Refrigerate your crema before using as it tastes best chilled. If time doesn’t allow it, it still tastes great freshly made. For nut free , you may sub the cashews for raw sunflower seeds or pepitas with similar results. Make sure to use unsalted or omit the salt. Leftovers keep refrigerated for up to 5 days, or freeze for up to 3 months."]]},"9066355":{"s":[[null,"Add all the ingredients for the custard base to your food processor and blend until completely combined and smooth, scraping down the sides as needed."],[null,"Transfer the mixture to your ramekins. (I used three 6-ounce ramekins, or you may use six 3-4 ounce ramekins for additional servings.) Then refrigerate for at least one hour (or overnight.)"],[null,"Next, sprinkle one teaspoon of coconut sugar on top of each base. Then use a blow torch to burn the sugar until it's dark and crispy. Wait 2-3 minutes to let the sugar topping cool and then garnish as desired."]],"h":[[null,"Propane gas torches are highly flammable and must be kept away from heat, open flame, and prolonged sunlight exposure. Use them only in well-ventilated areas and follow the torch manufacturer’s instructions."],[null,"Using unrefined coconut sugar for the topping means that your topping will be darker than traditional creme brulee which uses white sugar."],[null,"Leftovers will keep refrigerated for 3-4 days, but tastes best when the sugar is freshly “burned”."]]},"9873294":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375℉/190℃ bake. Then slice your baguette into quarter-inch slices, and arrange them in a single layer on a large baking sheet (or two if needed). Bake the bread for 5-8 minutes, or until golden and crunchy."],[null,"Meanwhile, dry sauté the mushrooms with a sprinkle of salt + pepper (they will release a lot of moisture and should not stick to your pan) until reduced, approx. 3-4 minutes. Set aside."],[null,"Next, add all the ricotta ingredients to your food processor and process until mostly smooth and combined. It should be thick, but spreadable."],[null,"Assemble your vegan crostini by spreading the ricotta on each slice of toasted bread, then top them with a few slices of mushrooms, and finally drizzle them with balsamic glaze and sprinkle with chopped basil."]],"h":[[null,"Prep in advance by making the ricotta cheese mixture and refrigerate it until ready to use."],[null,"Plan to enjoy these crostini immediately , as they taste best when freshly made."],[null,"This vegan crostini recipe makes approx. 4 servings as a meal, or 6-8 servings as an appetizer. The nutritional information above represents 6 servings of approx. 2-3 slices of crostini with its toppings. (This will vary according to the size of your loaf and the thickness of your slices.)"]]},"9108556":{"s":[[null,"Place the sliced cucumber and red onion in a large bowl. Then combine the vinegar, maple syrup, and dill in a small bowl and mix well. Pour the dressing over the salad and stir to evenly coat the slices."],[null,"Refrigerate for 1 hour or longer to chill and then serve."]],"h":[[null,"For the best flavour and texture , plan to make this salad not more than 1-2 hours before serving, as it softens more and more as it sits in the vinegar. For a creamy dressing , add 2 tablespoons of dairy-free yogurt or cashew cream."]]},"9316983":{"s":[[null,"Add the cream cheese with the dill, green onion, and all the seasoning to a small mixing bowl. Mix to combine. Taste for salt and pepper and add more, if needed."],[null,"Optional: Use a sharp knife to slice the crusts off your bread for classic cucumber sandwiches. Or leave them on for added texture and fiber."],[null,"Generously spread the herbed cream cheese on 3 slices of your sandwich bread, then arrange the sliced cucumbers on top and sprinkle a little salt and pepper on your cucumber slices if desired. Place the remaining 3 slices of bread on top of the cucumbers."],[null,"Cut each sandwich into halves or quarters and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Use English cucumbers , not field. The former has fewer seeds and thinner skin, so there’s no need to peel or deseed them. The latter has thicker skin and bitter seeds. For oil free : The recipe is oil free as written, however, many store-bought sliced breads have oil, so be sure to read the ingredients. Alternatively, you may make your own whole wheat oil free bread . Just be sure to skip the added fig and walnut in this bread recipe for the purpose of these sandwiches. You may use store-bought or my homemade vegan cream cheese . If using the homemade version, you’ll need about half of the cheese recipe to make these sandwiches. Leftover sandwiches keep refrigerated for 2-3 days in a sealed container or zip-top bag. However, these taste best the same day they are made."]]},"9021515":{"s":[[null,"Add all the ingredients to your food processor and pulse until combined. It will be crumbly, but you can press everything together with your hands, so don't worry if it's not a perfect ball."],[null,"Remove the mixture from your processor and shape it into a log or disc shape. Then wrap it snugly in cheesecloth and secure the two ends like a candy wrapper. (See process images above for reference.)"],[null,"Use a steamer pot to place your turkey seitan inside OR make a DIY steamer if you don't have one. Do this by placing a heatproof bowl over a pot with water inside, but make sure the bowl does not touch the water. Maintain a low boil and cover the seitan with a lid."],[null,"Steam for 45 minutes, then flip it, and steam for another 35-45 minutes, or until the internal temperature reaches 160℉/71℃. Keep an eye on your water level to make sure it doesn't evaporate and add HOT/boiling water as needed."],[null,"For best results and easy slicing, let your turkey seitan log rest at room temperature for 30 minutes, and then refrigerate overnight or several hours until cold."]],"h":[[null,"Use a kitchen scale to weigh the vital wheat gluten for the most accurate results and the best texture."],[null,"Keep an eye on the water level during steaming to make sure it doesn’t run out. Add more boiling hot water to the pot as needed to maintain a low boil."],[null,"Steam time will vary according to the shape of your turkey seitan log or disc, so checking the internal temperature is the easiest way to get the best results."],[null,"If you don’t have cheesecloth , you may wrap the seitan in aluminum foil. However, to prevent aluminum from touching your food, you may use parchment paper first, and then wrap that in aluminum foil."],[null,"Leftovers will keep refrigerated for up to 5 days in a sealed container. Or freeze the vegan deli in slices or as a full log to use later."]]},"9340739":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350℉/176℃ and grease your mini muffin tray if needed. (Enough to make 20 donut holes.)"],[null,"In a medium bowl, whisk together the dry ingredients. Then add the applesauce and plant-based milk to the same bowl. Mix until combined."],[null,"Use a small cookie scoop to divide the mixture among 20 muffin tins. Do not fill to the top, remember we're making donut holes, not muffins, so you don't want them to overflow."],[null,"Bake for 7-8 minutes until a toothpick inserted into the center comes out mostly clean. Do not overbake them, or they will be dry. (They bake quickly because they're small.) Remove from the oven and let cool for 5-10 minutes before transferring them to a wire rack."],["For the glaze","Meanwhile, add the milk to a small bowl, and then combine the sugar and cinnamon in a wide and shallow dish."],["For the glaze","When the donuts are cool enough to handle, swirl them one at a time into the milk, shake off the excess, and then swirl them around into the cinnamon sugar mixture until coated on all sides. Repeat with the remaining donuts and enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Weigh your flour for the most accurate results . If you do not have a kitchen scale, spoon the flour into your measuring cup and scrape off the excess with the back of a knife. Never pack flour into your measuring cups or scoop from the bag."],[null,"Use active baking powder . Once open and sitting in the pantry for 6+ months, baking powder may start to use its effectiveness."],[null,"Wait for the donuts to cool before glazing them in the cinnamon sugar. If the donuts are too warm, the glaze will melt."],[null,"Do not stack the donuts when freshly glazed to prevent the glaze from melting. Arranging them in a single layer is best."],[null,"Leftovers keep at room temperate OR in the fridge for 2-3 days. (Refrigerate if you’re in a warmer climate.) Or freeze a batch (preferably without the glaze) for up to 3 months and glaze them before serving."]]},"9244792":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350℉/176℃ and line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Add all the dry ingredients to a medium mixing bowl and whisk to combine. Then add the wet ingredients and stir until no dry bits remain. Lastly, fold in the chocolate chips, reserving some to add to the tops of each cookie later if you'd like."],[null,"Scoop the batter onto your tray. You should get about 15 cookies. Then gently press each cookie down to give them a spreading headstart and press the reserved chocolate chips into each cookie."],[null,"Bake the cookies for 10-12 minutes until the bottoms are lightly golden and remove them from the oven. The cookies will feel soft and underdone but they will firm up as they cool. Let them cool for 10 minutes before handling and transferring them to a wire rack."]],"h":[]},"9675054":{"s":[[null,"Add all the dressing ingredients to your blender and process until smooth and creamy. Start on low speed and then increase slowly to prevent cashew bits from splashing around. Scrape down the sides, as needed. Set aside."],[null,"Combine all the salad ingredients in a mixing bowl and pour the dressing on top and mix well."],[null,"Chill for 1 hour or serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"If you don’t have a powerful blender , presoak your cashews. You may soak overnight in cool water, or soak in boiling hot water for 30 minutes. The soak time will expand and soften the cashews, making them easier to blend. Although you may enjoy straight away, this vegan elote tastes best when chilled for 1 hour , so plan ahead if possible. For less spice, halve the chili flakes, or sub for chili powder instead. If you don’t have lemon , you may sub with lime juice or use more vinegar. Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-4 days."]]},"9122275":{"s":[["For the Enchilada Sauce","Add the jalapeno with a tablespoon or two of your broth to a small saucepan and sauté for 2 minutes."],["For the Enchilada Sauce","Add all remaining ingredients, mix well, and bring to a boil. Then reduce heat to medium-low and simmer for 8 minutes until slightly reduced. Set aside."],["For the Enchilada Casserole","Preheat your oven to 400℉/204℃ and grab a baking dish that measures 11x15 inches or similar."],["For the Enchilada Casserole","Meanwhile, chop all your veggies and add them to the baking dish along with the uncooked quinoa. Pour the 2 cups of broth and the 2 cups of enchilada sauce you just made on top. Mix well."],["For the Enchilada Casserole","Cover the tray with foil and bake for 30 minutes. Then remove the foil, give everything a quick stir, and bake for another 15-20 minutes, until the liquid is mostly absorbed and the potatoes are fork tender."],["For the Enchilada Casserole","Serve with toppings of your choice."]],"h":[[null,"Cut the sweet potato cubes on the smaller side (no bigger than half-inch pieces) so they get soft enough during baking."],[null,"If using store-bought enchilada sauce add extra seasonings like cumin, chilli powder, and/or paprika to add extra flavour."],[null,"The dish will appear watery at first . Don’t worry! As the quinoa cooks, it will absorb all the liquid. If there’s liquid leftover at the end of baking, leave the dish to rest at room temperature for 5-7 minutes to absorb any excess."],[null,"The nutritional information is for one sixth of the casserole including the homemade enchilada sauce, but without the optional toppings."]]},"9396581":{"s":[[null,"Slice your bread into approx one inch thick strips and set aside."],[null,"Add all remaining ingredients (everything except the bread) to your blender and process until smooth."],[null,"Pour the mixture into a wide and shallow bowl, working in batches if needed. Then dip several of your sticks of bread on all sides, letting it soak up the batter for 30-60 seconds."],[null,"Heat a nonstick griddle, large skillet, or well-seasoned cast iron pan over medium heat. Grease first if necessary. Then cook your french toast sticks for 2-3 minutes on each side, working in as many batches as necessary, depending on the size of your griddle or pan."],[null,"Serve with a sprinkle of powdered sugar, fresh berries, maple syrup, or enjoy as they are."]],"h":[[null,"Use bread that is sturdy and denser than regular sliced sandwich bread and cut your sticks into one-inch-thick pieces. You don’t want them too thin or they may break after soaking in the batter. Do your best to cut your french toast sticks into similar sized pieces for even cooking. Make sure to preheat your pan or griddle before cooking your french toast. If you don’t preheat, the batter may fall and get stuck to the pan. For low fat , you may use any non-dairy milk like almond milk or soy milk in place of the coconut. The recipe will work just fine, but won’t be as rich. For gluten-free , use your favourite gluten-free bread instead."]]},"9660382":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400℉/204℃ and grab a nonstick muffin pan or grease if needed."],[null,"Place all the chopped veggies in a pan and sprinkle them with a little salt and pepper, if desired. Dry sauté, stirring often, until reduced and softened, approx. 5 minutes. Set aside."],[null,"Meanwhile, in a large bowl, add the chickpea flour, nutritional yeast, seasonings, and baking powder, and whisk to combine. Then pour in the water and mix well."],[null,"Divide the sautéed veggies between your 12 muffin tins, about 1 heaping tablespoon per muffin. Then pour the chickpea batter on top to evenly distribute it between your 12 muffins. Use a spoon to gently stir each muffin, to evenly distribute the veggies and the batter. (DON'T SKIP MIXING.)"],[null,"Bake for 30 minutes or until a toothpick inserted in the middle comes out clean. Remove from the oven and let cool for at least 10 minutes. Then carefully remove them from the pan."]],"h":[[null,"Stir the muffins BEFORE baking . This will ensure even distribution of the veggies. Also, make sure that some batter gets to the bottom of the tins so the muffins will be evenly shaped and prevent sticking."],[null,"Alternatively , you may pour a tablespoon of chickpea batter into the bottom of each muffin tin, followed by the veggies, and then pour the remaining batter on top."],[null,"Let the muffins rest at room temperature for at least 10 minutes before removing them from the pan. This cool-down period helps muffins set so that they don’t break when removing them."],[null,"If you’re avoiding oil and don’t want to grease your muffin pan, let your muffins cool a little longer before attempting to remove them. Then use a butter knife to gently glide around each muffin if they are a little stuck, and scoop them out."],[null,"Leftovers keep in a sealed container in your fridge for up to 5 days. Or freeze them for up to 3 months. Make sure to completely cool the vegan egg muffins before refrigerating or freezing. You may reheat the egg cups in the microwave or toaster oven, or enjoy them cold."]]},"9660403":{"s":[[null,"Add all the ham ingredients EXCEPT the vital wheat gluten to a food processor and process until mostly blended. Then add HALF the vital wheat gluten and continue processing until mixed through. Now add the remaining half and process until mostly combined."],[null,"Transfer the mixture to a clean surface and knead by hand for 1-2 minutes, twisting and knotting your mixture as you go. Then shape into an oval, as evenly as you can, but it doesn't have to be perfect. (See process shots above for a visual.)"],[null,"Wrap your roast tightly using a cheesecloth (or parchment and aluminum foil) and secure the ends."],[null,"Add 1.5 cups of water to the bottom of your Instant Pot and place its trivet inside. Then place your wrapped ham on top of the trivet. Close the lid and make sure the valve is in the sealing position. Set to the steam function for 40 minutes and let the pressure naturally release until the pin drops. It will take about 10 minutes for the pin to drop."],[null,"While the ham is steaming in your Instant Pot, preheat your oven to 375 degrees F. Then add ALL the glaze ingredients in a small mixing bowl and whisk to combine. Set aside."],[null,"Transfer the roast to a cutting board and use a sharp knife to score your ham. Start on one end and make cuts that are approx. 1/4-1/3 inch deep and approx. 1 inch apart. Then rotate the ham and repeat diagonally from one side to the other. (See process shots above for a visual.)"],[null,"Place the scored ham in an oven safe dish and pour your maple glaze on top, using a silicone brush to ensure the surface of your ham is completely covered in the glaze."],[null,"Bake uncovered for 15-20 minutes, basting every few minutes. Then you may optionally broil the ham for 2-3 minutes to slightly brown the top, but you can skip this step if preferred."],[null,"Remove from the oven and let rest for 5-10 minutes. Then use a serrated knife or electric knife to slice. Serve and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Don’t be intimidated ! It’s a LOT easier to make than it looks. 🙂 Make sure to use a good quality and very flavourful broth for the best results. I use and love this homemade broth , but store bought works too. Cheesecloth is easier than parchment and aluminum foil to wrap your vegan ham. Plus, it’s safe for food if you prefer to avoid foil. Give your ham a little time to rest before slicing . As it begins to cool, it further sets and makes slicing easier and allows for thinner slices. Leftovers keep refrigerated in a sealed container for up to 5 days. You may freeze leftovers, whole or sliced in a zip top bag or freezer safe container for up to 3 months."]]},"9708853":{"s":[[null,"Combine all the \"meat\" ingredients in a bowl and mix well. If the soy curls are not completely covered, add a little water to cover them. Let that soak for 15 minutes, and then drain in a colander."],[null,"Meanwhile, add all the cheese sauce ingredients to a blender and process until smooth. Set aside."],[null,"Heat a deep nonstick pan over medium heat and once hot, squeeze the excess moisture from your soy curls over your kitchen sink and place them in the pan. Sauté for 3-5 minutes until browned, adding a splash of water or oil if needed to prevent sticking. Then transfer the soy curls to your food processor to pulse into a uniform ground and set aside."],[null,"Wipe out the same pan and add 3.5 cups of broth and bring to a low boil. Then add the pasta and simmer until al dente, stirring often. Approx. 10 minutes."],[null,"If you have a little extra broth once your pasta is cooked, no need to drain. Add the ground soy curls to the pan and give it a mix to absorb some of the excess broth. Then pour the cheese sauce on top, mix well and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Since the soy curls are being ground up, feel free to use the bottom half of your bag that tends to be broken up. Make sure the soy curls are completely covered by liquid in order to rehydrate them. If needed, add some extra water to the bowl to cover them. Emphasis on low sodium broth for this one, to prevent the dish from being too salty. If you do not have low salt broth, use a 50/50 mix of broth and water. Make sure not to overcook your pasta . In fact, a little undercooked (or al dente) is best since it will continue to soften as it absorbs the excess broth. If your vegan hamburger helper is a little liquidy once everything is mixed in, don’t worry. Any excess liquid will quickly absorb as it starts to cool. This dish is best enjoyed straight away, but leftovers will keep refrigerated in a sealed container for up to 3 days. Reheat on stove top with a little extra broth or plant milk to loosen and rehydrate."]]},"9577836":{"s":[[null,"Shred the potatoes with a box grater or another shredding tool. Then place them in a large bowl and cover them with cold water. Let that soak for at least 20 minutes. Then drain the shredded potatoes and rinse well with cold water to remove excess starch. Then transfer to a clean and dry dish towel and pat them dry."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 425℉/218℃ and grab an oven-safe baking dish or casserole dish."],[null,"Shred the cauliflower and towel dry those too, to get out any excess moisture. Add them to a bowl with the dry potato shreds and the finely chopped onion and pepper."],[null,"Blend all the cheese sauce ingredients in a high-speed blender until smooth. Then pour the mixture in the bowl of shredded veggies and mix well."],[null,"Transfer the mixture to your oven-safe dish and bake for 30 minutes. Then broil the dish for 2-3 minutes (watching carefully) to brown the top. Remove from the oven and serve warm."]],"h":[[null,"For the best texture , don’t skip the extra step to soak the potatoes."],[null,"If you don’t have a high-speed blender , soak your cashews in hot water for 15-30 minutes and then drain them, before making the vegan cheese sauce."],[null,"Do not overbake the casserole as this can result in an overly soft texture."],[null,"Watch CAREFULLY when broiling to prevent burning your dish."],[null,"You may use 3 lbs of potatoes and skip the cauliflower if preferred."],[null,"For nut-free use sunflower seeds or pepitas instead of cashews with similar results."],[null,"Although you MAY substitute the tapioca starch for corn starch or flour, I don’t recommend it unless necessary. The tapioca starch is a unique ingredient that gives the vegan cheese sauce its stretchy texture."]]},"9766698":{"s":[[null,"Add everything to your blender and process until smooth and creamy."],[null,"Serve as a dipping sauce for fries or pizza, as a spread in sandwiches and burgers, or use it to dress a green salad."]],"h":[[null,"Make sure to run the blender a little extra to get a smooth texture, without graininess. Adjust the consistency to your liking . I prefer my honey mustard a tad thicker, but if you want it thinner, add 1-2 tablespoons of water or vinegar. Keep leftovers in the fridge for up to 4 days or freeze them in small airtight containers for up to 3 months. This vegan honey mustard recipe makes approx. 1.5 cups of sauce. The nutritional information represents a serving of approx. 2 tablespoons."]]},"9882145":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (if using the oven method) and tear 8 pieces of aluminum foil (and parchment paper if you prefer your foil doesn't touch your food) and set aside."],[null,"Add the white beans to a mixing bowl and gently mash with a large fork or potato masher. (They don't need to be completely mashed, some chunkier pieces are fine.) Then add all remaining WET ingredients to the same bowl and mix well."],[null,"Now add ALL the dry ingredients and begin mixing until mostly combined into a ball of dough. Then transfer to a cutting board or clean work surface to knead for approx. 1 minute, until you have a well combined mixture, but don't over knead."],[null,"Divide into 8 pieces and roll each piece into a cylinder shape to make your vegan hot dogs. (Don't worry if it's lumpy, it will get smooth when you cook it.) Then wrap each of your seitan dogs with the parchment paper (if using) and the aluminum foil and twist the ends to secure them inside. (See process shots above for a visual.) Choose a cooking method below."],["Steaming Instructions","Bring a large pot with a couple inches of water to boil and place your steamer basket inside. Make sure the basket is not touching the water. Once boiling, reduce heat to maintain a low boil/simmer and place your seitan dogs inside. Cover with a lid and steam for 45-55 minutes, flipping them at the halfway point. Check on your water every so often and add hot water IF needed. Remove the hot dogs from the basket and let cool for 5 minutes before removing the foil."],["Baking Instructions","Place your wrapped seitan dogs on a tray and bake for 45 minutes, flipping at the halfway point. Remove from the oven and let cool for 5 minutes or so, before removing the foil."],["Instant Pot Instructions","Add 1.5 cups of water to the bottom of your Instant Pot. Then place the trivet inside the pot. Arrange your wrapped seitan dogs on the trivet, stacking them as needed. Then close the lid and make sure the valve is in the sealing position. Steam for 45 minutes and let your pot naturally release pressure until the pin drops. Remove once safe to do so."],["Optional Grilling","You may enjoy straight away once baked or steamed. OR, you may grill your seitan dogs for those beautiful grill lines. Brush your vegan hot dogs with oil (if you'd like) and sprinkle a little extra salt and pepper. Then grill for 1-2 minutes to enhance the flavours."],["Optional Grilling","Serve with hot dog buns and all your favourite toppings. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"For best accuracy , weigh your vital wheat gluten. If you do not have a kitchen scale, use 2 cups worth. Make sure to mix your dough well for even flavour and best texture, but do not over knead. Kneading for 1-2 minutes is perfect. Don’t spend too much time fussing over perfectly shaped hot dogs . They’ll be lumpy before cooking, but get nice and smooth while they cook. If you don’t like having foil touch your food , use parchment paper in between the seitan dogs and aluminum foil layer. For spicy vegan sausages , add 1 teaspoon of chili flakes to the mix. To make ahead: Fully prep + cook your dogs 1-2 days in advance using the method of choice (steam or bake) and then grill just before serving. Leftovers keep refrigerated for up to 5 days or freeze for up to 3 months. How do I know they’re cooked? Gently peel back the foil, the hot dogs should appear smooth. You may give it a poke with your finger or tongs to test firmness. They should feel firm but still give a little to pressure. They’ll firm up more as they cool."]]},"9350784":{"s":[[null,"Add the onion, garlic, red pepper and jalapenos to your food processor and pulse until very finely chopped."],[null,"In a large sauce pot, add the butter or margarine if using, and melt over medium heat. (Or use water or broth if avoiding oil.) Then add the finely chopped veggies you just processed to the pot and sauté for 5-7 minutes, until softened and reduced."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the cauliflower to the same processor and pulse until broken down, without over processing or pureeing. You want some chunkier pieces. Work in batches if needed."],[null,"Add the processed cauliflower, along with the broth and corn to the pot and mix well. Bring to a boil over high heat, then reduce to medium low and simmer for 15 minutes."],[null,"While the soup is simmering, prepare your vegan cheese sauce. Add all the ingredients to a high speed blender and process until smooth."],[null,"Turn off the heat, pour in the cheese sauce and mix well. Taste for salt and pepper and add more if necessary. Then serve garnished with jalapeno slices, if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Adjust the spice level to your preference. We like ours very spicy, but if you want a more subtle spice, use less jalapenos, and remove the seeds for an even milder level of spiciness. Adjust the seasoning. Always season to your taste. Just because a recipe calls for half a teaspoon of salt, feel free to adjust. If you want added smoky flavour, up the smoked paprika as well. Make it oil free. Omit the butter or margarine and sauté using water or broth instead. For nut free. You may sub the cashews with sunflower seeds, with similar results. Cashews provide a little more richness, but if you can’t have cashews, sunflower seeds make a good substitution. For corn free. You may simply omit the corn or replace it with some diced carrots to add some colour and a touch of sweetness. Soak the cashews. If you don’t have a high speed blender like a Vitamix or Blendtec, soak your cashews first. Soak them in boiling hot water from a kettle or on stove top and soak them for 30 minutes. Then drain and use. Soaking the cashews makes them soften up and allows a less powerful blender to process them. Do not over process the cauliflower . Work in batches if needed to prevent the cauliflower from turning to mush. You want some nice hearty texture here. Want a smooth soup instead? Don’t bother with your food processor, just roughly chop everything. Cook as directed, and then use an immersion or stick blender to puree your soup before adding in the vegan cheese sauce. Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-4 days, just store in an airtight container, then reheat and enjoy."]]},"9361657":{"s":[[null,"Prepare your pie crust of choice and blind bake according to its directions. If you're using my oil-free pie crust, bake for 15-20 minutes, until the edges are golden. Set aside to let cool before filling."],[null,"Add all the filling ingredients to your blender and process until smooth. Then pour the mixture into your crust and spread as evenly as possible."],[null,"Freeze overnight, or for a minimum of 4-6 hours. Once frozen, rest at room temperature for 5-10 minutes, to make it easier to slice, then garnish and serve."]],"h":[[null,"If you don’t have a high-speed blender , soak your cashews in hot water for 30 minutes and then drain, before blending with the remaining ingredients. This will help them soften, making them easier to blend. Make sure to plan ahead , as this pie tastes best when frozen for at least 4-6 hours. This pie is more tart than sweet . If you prefer a sweeter pie, increase the sugar to half a cup, noting that this will increase the calorie content, too. If you prefer extra tart , use up to ¾ cup of fresh lime juice. You may also add 1-2 teaspoons of lime zest for extra zing. Nutritional information is for one slice (or ⅛th) of the lime pie, including my oil free pie crust . If you’re using another crust, nutritional info will vary."]]},"9928413":{"s":[[null,"Add the soy milk and 1 teaspoon of lemon juice to a small bowl and set aside for 5 minutes to let it curdle."],[null,"Meanwhile, add all the dry ingredients to a large mixing bowl, and whisk to combine. Then add the curdled soy milk, applesauce, vanilla, lemon juice, and lemon zest and mix to combine. Let the batter rest for 10 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, preheat the oven to 375 degrees F (190 degrees C) and prepare a muffin pan with muffin liners, or use a nonstick pan."],[null,"Add approx. 1 tablespoon of the plain batter to the bottom of each muffin cup. Then use a spatula to gently fold the blueberries into the remaining batter. Divide the remaining batter among the 12 muffin cups and bake for 18-22 minutes, or until a toothpick inserted in the center of a muffin comes out clean."],[null,"Remove from the oven and let cool at least 10 minutes before removing the muffins from the tray and transferring them to a cooling rack to completely cool."],["Optional Glaze","While the muffins are cooling, combine the icing sugar and lemon juice in a small bowl. Start with 1 teaspoon of lemon juice and increase as needed. Once the muffins are cooled, drizzle them with the icing."]],"h":[[null,"Weigh your flour for the most accurate results . If you don’t have a kitchen scale, you may spoon the flour into your measuring cup and use a knife to scrape off the excess. Do not scoop from the bag! Don’t skip making the vegan buttermilk . (Mixing the soy milk with lemon juice.) This enhances the dairy flavour, and makes for a fluffier muffin. Use fresh and active baking powder. Baking powder that is open in your pantry for 6+ months can start to lose its effectiveness. The reason for adding some plain mixture to the bottom of the muffin tins before folding the blueberries into the batter is to prevent most of the blueberries from sinking. If there are too many blueberries at the bottom of the pan, it will be too wet and heavy, resulting in uneven baking. If using the glaze, glaze before serving and not in advance. Do not cover the muffins once glazed . Storing glazed muffins in a sealed container will cause the glaze to melt. Make sure your muffins are completely cooled before glazing . Adding glaze to hot or warm muffins will melt the glaze. Leftover muffins will keep at room temperature, covered or in an airtight container for 2-3 days. Refrigerate to keep up to 5 days. Or freeze for up to 4 months."]]},"9717533":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 400°F/204°C and line a large tray with parchment paper."],[null,"Add the onion, carrot, and garlic to a skillet with a tablespoon or two of water and sauté for approx 5 minutes, until softened. Add more water if needed to prevent sticking."],[null,"Add the cooked veggies, cooked lentils, tomato paste, and all the seasoning to your food processor and process until combined, but not pureed, scraping down the sides if needed. Then add the pumpkin seeds and pulse a few times to break them down and mix them in but do not over-process. Taste the mixture and add more seasoning if desired."],[null,"Roll the mixture into small balls (approx 1-1.5\" diameter) and place them on the prepared tray. You should get 20 vegan lentil meatballs."],[null,"Bake for 25-30 minutes, then remove them from the oven and let cool for 3-5 minutes before handling."],[null,"Enjoy them plain, with pasta and marinara sauce, rice, or sweet potato noodles."]],"h":[[null,"Use dried GREEN lentils that have been cooked for the best texture. Do not sub for red as they get too mushy for these balls. For added depth of flavour, cook the lentils in veggie broth."],[null,"Make sure not to overcook your lentils or they will get too soft. Cook according to package directions, but undercook by 1-2 minutes for best results. (They’ll cook more in the oven later.)"],[null,"Do not over-process your ingredients . This will make the mixture too soft, difficult to roll, and result in a softer/mushier texture. (If this happens, you can refrigerate for a bit to help them firm up enough to roll, or add some oats or breadcrumbs to help firm up the texture."],[null,"Use wet hands to shape the balls . This will prevent them from sticking to your hands and fingers, making them easier to roll."],[null,"Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-4 days or freeze airtight for up to 3 months frozen. Serving size is approx. 4 vegan lentil meatballs."]]},"9279842":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425℉/218℃ convection roast and line a large baking tray with parchment paper."],[null,"Peel or scrub your potatoes and slice them into fries using a French fry cutter or a sharp knife. Toss them with broth or oil and salt. Then arrange them in a single layer on your tray. Roast for 20 minutes, then flip them, and continue roasting another 10-15 minutes, or until desired crispiness is reached."],[null,"Meanwhile, make the cheese sauce and prepare the remaining toppings while the fries are cooking."],[null,"Assembly: Use a large platter or the same tray you used to bake. Start with the fries, followed by approx. half of the cheese sauce, and then sprinkle all the remaining toppings in any order you'd like. Finally, finish it off by drizzling the remaining cheese sauce on top and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Arrange the fries in a single layer with some space in between for the crispiest baked french fries and to prevent sticking. For a non-convection oven , expect a little longer cooking time. Keep baking until the desired crispiness is reached."]]},"9237195":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425°F/218°C and line a baking sheet with parchment paper. Pierce your sweet potatoes using a fork or knife 5-6 times around the potato. (This will prevent them from exploding in the oven.) Then bake for 45-60 minutes, or until easily pierced with a fork."],[null,"Meanwhile, dump all the baked bean ingredients into your Instant Pot, give it a stir, and close the lid. Make sure the valve is in the sealing position and set to high pressure for 40 minutes. (It will take about 10 minutes to build pressure before counting down.) Once the timer is complete, you may quick release the steam valve."],[null,"While the beans and potatoes are cooking, prepare your guacamole or any other toppings you are using."],[null,"When the sweet potatoes are cooked, remove them from the oven and slice them open lengthwise, without cutting all the way through. Then gently mash the inside to create a pocket and serve with a generous scoop of baked beans and top as desired."]],"h":[[null,"If you forgot to soak your beans , use this quick soak method. Add the beans to a medium pot and enough water to cover them about 2 inches above the beans. Place the lid on the pot and bring it to a boil on the stovetop. Once boiling, turn off the heat and let them sit for 45-60 minutes. Then drain and cook as directed."],[null,"The baked beans may appear watery upon first removing your Instant Pot lid. Just give them a stir, keep the lid off, and let the beans sit for a few minutes while you slice your potatoes. They will quickly absorb the sauce and flavour."],[null,"If your sweet potatoes are large , they may need closer to 55-60 minutes of baking time. When they are soft enough to pierce with a fork, they’re ready."],[null,"If you don’t have an Instant Pot , try this slow cooker method OR visit the post above under “equipment” for a stovetop method."],[null,"Store leftovers separately in the fridge for 3-4 days and assemble your loaded sweet potatoes just before enjoying."]]},"9439640":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350℉/176℃ and line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Add all the dry ingredients to a large mixing bowl and whisk until combined. Then add the wet ingredients and stir until no floury bits remain."],[null,"Scoop the cookie batter onto your baking sheet to make 12 cookies. Then bake in your preheated oven for 8-9 minutes. They will be very soft when fresh out of the oven but will firm up as they cool down."]],"h":[[null,"Weigh your flour for the best results . Scooping into a measuring cup can compact the flour and you may end up with more than needed."],[null,"Use active baking powder . Baking powder that's been open in the pantry for several months may lose its effectiveness."],[null,"These cookies keep for 1-2 days at room temperature, up to 4 days in the fridge or up to 3 months in the freezer."]]},"9007563":{"s":[[null,"Add the quinoa and broth to a medium sauce pot and bring to a boil. Then reduce heat and simmer until the water is absorbed, approx 15 minutes. Stir often towards the end of cooking time to prevent sticking. Remove from the heat and add the black beans, corn, salsa, and all the seasoning to the cooked quinoa. Mix well and then taste and adjust the seasoning as desired."],[null,"Meanwhile, preheat your oven to 425°F/218°C and line a 9\"x13\" baking dish with parchment paper. Arrange the halved peppers, cut side up in the dish, and sprinkle them with salt and pepper."],[null,"Divide the mixture among your 8 pepper halves, then cover the dish with parchment paper followed by aluminum foil. Bake for 30-35 minutes, until the peppers are tender."],[null,"While the peppers are baking, prepare any optional toppings. Then serve."]],"h":[[null,"For the best results , cook the quinoa (or rice) in a salty and flavourful vegetable broth . You may use salted water to cook the quinoa (instead of broth), but it won’t be as flavourful. If you don’t care for quinoa , use rice instead, and follow the same cooking directions or use a rice cooker. The nutritional information is for one pepper (or two pepper halves) and one-quarter of the prepared stuffing. It does not include optional toppings."]]},"9023396":{"s":[[null,"In a medium pot, or deep skillet, add the mushrooms, garlic, thyme and a couple drops of water to prevent sticking. Sauté until the mushrooms are reduced, approx. 4 minutes."],[null,"Add the broth, miso paste and lemon juice and bring to a low boil, cooking for about 5 minutes. Turn off the heat, add the milk, and then use an immersion blender to puree your soup OR transfer to a blender. Taste and add salt and pepper, only if needed, and serve with crusty bread."]],"h":[[null,"Do not salt your soup before tasting, once pureed . The miso paste and vegetable broth add a fair bit of saltiness. Once blended, taste the soup and add some, only if needed. Use low sodium vegetable broth , or use a mix of regular broth and water if you don’t have low sodium on hand. You can always add more salt if needed, but you cannot remove. If you don’t have an immersion blender , carefully transfer the soup to a blender and process until smooth. Use extreme caution when blending hot liquids, don’t overfill your blender and work in batches , as needed! Leftovers keep refrigerated for up 4 days or freeze for up to 3 months."]]},"9344030":{"s":[["Strawberry Banana Nice Cream Directions","Add all the ingredients to a food processor or high speed blender and process until smooth and creamy, stopping to scrape down the sides as needed. Enjoy immediately for a soft serve texture. Or freeze for 30-60 minutes for a firmer \"scoopable\" texture."],["Vegan Coffee Ice Cream Directions","Add all the ingredients to a food processor or high speed blender and process until smooth and creamy, stopping to scrape down the sides as needed. Enjoy immediately for a soft serve texture. Or freeze for 30-60 minutes for a firmer \"scoopable\" texture."],["Mint Chocolate Chip Nice Cream Directions","Add the frozen bananas, milk and peppermint extract to a food processor or high speed blender and process until smooth and creamy, stopping to scrape down the sides as needed. Then add the spinach (if using) and process to combine."],["Mint Chocolate Chip Nice Cream Directions","Add the chocolate chips and pulse once or twice to fold in. Enjoy immediately for a soft serve texture. Or freeze for 30-60 minutes for a firmer \"scoopable\" texture."]],"h":[[null,"Use very ripe frozen bananas to maximize the natural sweetness of your vegan ice cream. If you don’t have bananas in your freezer , make sure your bananas are very spotted and soft. Then peel them, cut them into chunks and freeze until solid. Break your frozen bananas into chunks (if not already) to give your processor a head start, and make blending easier. * Start with the lower amount of plant milk and increase only if needed . The size of your bananas will determine how much milk is needed to process them. Use the least amount of milk possible to blend them into a thick and creamy texture. Too much milk will make your nice cream too thin and more smoothie like. The optional spinach in the mint chocolate chip nice cream is for the green colour, not flavour. You will not taste the spinach , but you may skip it, if preferred. Your nice cream will be white without it. If using a food processor , you will have tiny bits of spinach that don’t fully purée, but again, you won’t taste it. Use a blender for smoother consistency if you need to hide the spinach from picky eaters. 🙂 The nutritional info in the chart below is for the base recipe including the bananas and plant milk only . Additional flavours and optional ingredients are not included. The calories INCLUDING optional ingredients for each of the three flavours is as follows: Strawberry Banana Nice Cream – 149 calories for one third of the recipe. Vegan Coffee Ice Cream – 111 calories for one third of the recipe. Mint Chocolate Chip Nice Cream – 166 calories for one third of the recipe."]]},"6201760":{"s":[[null,"Preheat a large skillet over medium heat. Add oil, onion, garlic, carrot, and bell pepper. Cook, stirring occasionally, until softened, 4–5 minutes."],[null,"Add the plant-based ground and continue to cook, breaking it apart with a spatula, until crumbly and browned, 6–7 minutes."],[null,"Add broth, tomato sauce, coconut aminos, chili powder, and smoked paprika to the skillet. Stir to combine until heated through and the sauce thickens, 2–3 minutes."],[null,"Split the buns apart and divide between plates. Top with 1 cup of filling per half bun."]],"h":[]},"9784924":{"s":[[null,"In a medium bowl, combine all the marinade ingredients, EXCEPT the cornstarch or flour and whisk well. Then stir the soy curls into the bowl and let them soak for 10-15 minutes. Make sure they all get covered with the marinade."],[null,"Meanwhile, add your sliced mushrooms and peppers to a large skillet. Dry sauté to soften and reduce them for 4-5 minutes. You shouldn't need any oil or water since the mushrooms will release their own liquid. If anything is sticking, add a splash of water."],[null,"With a slotted spoon or tongs, transfer the soaked soy curls to your skillet with the veggies and RESERVE the sauce. Make sure to fish out the curls from the bowl, and do not dump them in. Sauté for 5 minutes to brown the edges of the soy curls."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the cornstarch to the bowl of sauce and stir to combine. Then pour the sauce into the pan with the curls and veggies. Cook over medium heat for 3-5 minutes to thicken the sauce, and serve."]],"h":[[null,"For a saucier stir fry, double the marinade recipe."],[null,"Make sure to use low-sodium vegetable broth for the marinade, since the Tamari/soy sauce has a lot of salt. If you don’t have low-sodium broth, use half a cup of the broth with half a cup of water."],[null,"For lower sodium , use low-sodium Tamari or low-sodium soy sauce."],[null,"Soy curls are not the same as soy chunks. Most natural food aisles or health food stores will have soy curls. Or you can buy them on Amazon."],[null,"The nutritional information is for one-fourth of the vegan orange chicken recipe and does not include noodles or rice."]]},"9685307":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350℉/176℃ and line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Combine the peanut butter, maple syrup, and milk in a medium bowl and mix well. Then add the oats, almond flour, and baking soda and mix until combined. If using the chocolate chips, fold those in next."],[null,"For large cookies (as photographed) use a two tablespoon cookie scoop. Scoop the mixture into 10 balls and place them on your baking sheet with plenty of space in between each one. Gently press each one down with the back of a spoon to give them a spreading head start. (They will keep spreading in the oven.)"],[null,"Then bake the cookies for 11-12 minutes and remove the tray from the oven. The cookies may appear underdone, but they will firm up as they cool. Let them rest for 10 minutes, then enjoy warm, or transfer to a wire rack to continue cooling them."]],"h":[[null,"I made the cookies very large for a breakfast cookie. However, you may easily get 20 cookies if using a smaller (1 tablespoon) cookie scoop . This will halve the nutritional information per cookie."],[null,"Weigh the almond flour for the most accurate results, as opposed to relying on cup measurements."],[null,"Leave plenty of space in between each cookie as these will spread a fair bit."],[null,"The cookies will appear underdone , but they will firm up at room temperature, so do not overbake them ."]]},"9717126":{"s":[[null,"Add the soy milk and apple cider vinegar to a medium bowl and set it aside for 5 minutes to let it thicken and curdle."],[null,"Preheat your nonstick griddle over medium heat."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the oats and chia seeds to your blender and process until it resembles a flour consistency. (Don't worry if there are a few chunkier pieces.) Transfer the mixture to a large mixing bowl along with the baking powder and whisk to combine."],[null,"Add the peanut butter and applesauce to the bowl of your curdled milk and mix well. Then pour the wet ingredients into the bowl of dry ingredients and mix until combined, without overmixing. Some lumps are perfectly okay."],[null,"Ladle the batter onto your hot griddle, making the pancakes roughly 3-4 inches in diameter. You may gently press the pancake down to help it spread a little if needed. (The batter should not be very runny.) Don't spread too much as these pancakes taste best thick and fluffy."],[null,"Cook for 4-5 minutes until golden and then flip them, and cook for another 3-4 more minutes until cooked through."],[null,"While the pancakes are cooking, add all the caramel ingredients, starting with 4 tablespoons of water to a blender, and process until smooth. Add more water to reach desired consistency and set aside."],[null,"Serve your pancakes with sliced bananas, chopped walnuts, chocolate chips, and/or the homemade caramel sauce."]],"h":[[null,"Make sure your griddle is hot before cooking your pancakes to prevent sticking and to avoid greasing your pan. You can test this by splashing the griddle with a sprinkle of water to see if it sizzles."],[null,"If you don’t have a strong blender , soak your dates for 15-30 minutes in boiling hot water and then drain them, before making your peanut butter caramel."],[null,"Make sure to use ACTIVE baking powder . Once your baking powder is open and sitting in the pantry for 6+ months, it may start to lose its rising power."],[null,"Leftover pancakes keep refrigerated for 3-4 days or frozen for up to 3 months. Reheat in the toaster for quick make-ahead breakfasts."],[null,"Leftover caramel keeps in a sealed container in the fridge for up to 1 week."],[null,"The nutritional information does not include the optional caramel sauce. There are 65 calories for one-tenth of the sauce, which is approximately 2-3 tablespoons, depending on the amount of water added to thin the sauce."]]},"9529996":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F and line a large baking tray with parchment paper."],[null,"In a medium bowl, add all the ingredients, starting with just 1 tablespoon of the milk and mix well. Your batter should be thick and sticky. If it feels too dry to hold together, add the second tablespoon of milk."],[null,"Use a SMALL cookie scoop, or tablespoon to scoop the cookie batter onto your tray, leaving plenty of space in between each one. You should get between 12-14 cookies. Use a fork to gently press down each cookie to give them a spreading head start. They will continue to spread in the oven."],[null,"Bake for 10-11 minutes and remove from the oven. They will feel soft and underdone, this is normal, so don't try to eat them straight out of the oven. Let them rest for at least 10 minutes before handling. Then transfer to a cooling rack to continue cooling and completely set."]],"h":[[null,"Make sure to only use 1 tablespoon of milk to start mixing your batter . Depending on the consistency of your nut butter, you may or may not need the second tablespoon. It will be tempting, but do not touch your cookies once you remove them from the oven . Let them rest for 10 minutes before handling, as they will be very soft and feel under done before cooling. For less sugar , you may reduce to ¼ cup with similar results. Keep your cookies at room temperature in a container for 2-3 days, or refrigerate up to 1 week. You may freeze air tight for up to 3 months."]]},"9349443":{"s":[[null,"OPTIONAL: Preheat your oven or toaster oven to 350 degrees F (177 degrees C) and line a small baking sheet with parchment paper. Arrange the slivered almonds in a single layer and bake them for 5-8 minutes, checking often towards the end of baking to prevent them from getting too dark. Remove from the oven and set aside."],[null,"Bring a large pot of generously salted water to a boil and cook your pasta according to package directions for \"al dente\" pasta. Immediately drain and transfer to a large bowl. Then add the remaining pasta salad ingredients to the same bowl and set aside. (NOTE: You may reserve some of the tomatoes, peas, and toasted almonds to garnish later.)"],[null,"Meanwhile, combine all your pesto ingredients in your blender and process until smooth. Then pour the pesto over the pasta salad and mix well."],[null,"Refrigerate for 1 hour or longer and then garnish with reserved tomatoes, peas, and toasted almonds, and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Salt your pasta water. Make sure to add enough salt to your pot of water for best texture and flavour. Here's a handy guide to help you salt your water perfectly each time. Cook your pasta al dente. Do not overcook! Al dente means that the pasta is still firm once cooked, giving optimal texture in every bite. To ensure your pasta does not overcook, start taste testing a few minutes before the package says it will be ready. It should be tender, but still firm. This pesto pasta salad tastes great warm or chilled, so you may serve it right away, or refrigerate it for 1 hour or longer. Leftovers keep in the fridge for 3-4 days in a sealed container or tightly wrapped bowl."]]},"9666805":{"s":[[null,"Melt the butter (if using) and sauté the garlic for 30-60 seconds until fragrant."],[null,"Add the broth and bring it to a boil. Then lower the heat and slowly pour in the corn meal. Cook on low heat, stirring often for 15-20 minutes until very thick and tender."],[null,"Turn off the heat, add the milk and vegan parmesan cheese, and mix well. Serve immediately."]],"h":[]},"9465261":{"s":[[null,"Line a 12\" round pizza tray with parchment paper and set aside. Have another sheet of parchment paper ready to place on top of your dough for rolling. This one doesn't need to be round."],[null,"In a medium sauce pan, add the stock and seasonings and bring to a low boil over medium/high heat. Once boiling, add the corn meal and whisk continuously until thick. This will happen quickly, about 20-30 seconds, so make sure you're ready."],[null,"Transfer the dough to the center of your round sheet of parchment paper and place the other sheet on top. You may want to work on a cutting board as the mixture will be hot. Use a rolling pin to evenly roll and stretch the dough to the edges of the sheet. Work quickly, as the dough will be harder to stretch as it cools. It doesn't need to be perfect. Slide it onto the pizza tray and set it aside."],[null,"Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F convection bake. Then prepare your toppings. For toppings like onion, peppers or mushrooms precook them to release their water and prevent your crust from getting soggy."],[null,"When the oven is hot, bake your polenta pizza crust for 20 minutes, then remove from the oven and use the parchment paper to very carefully flip the crust over. Discard the paper and return the crust to the oven for 10 more minutes."],[null,"Remove from the oven and add all your toppings. I like tomato sauce, shredded cheese and sautéed veggies. Switch the oven to broil and return the topped pizza to the oven for 1-2 minutes to brown your toppings and melt your cheese. Watch carefully to prevent burning! If using fresh basil, add this at the end as a garnish, do not cook it with the basil."]],"h":[[null,"Use parchment paper on your pizza pan to assist in flipping the crust after the first bake time. Top your pizza with any toppings you’d like but make sure to precook your veggies to release the water and lighten the load, so that your crust won’t get soggy. Nutritional information is for one fourth of the pizza crust and does not include optional toppings."]]},"9368018":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F and line a large baking tray with parchment paper. (Use 2 trays if they are smaller.)"],[null,"Add the wet ingredients to a large bowl and mix well. Then add the dry ingredients to the same bowl and mix until combined. Lastly, fold in the chocolate chips."],[null,"Use a cookie scoop to divide the batter into approx. 26 cookies on your baking sheet/s. Then use a spoon or damp fingers to gently press each cookie down and shape them into rounds, as they won't spread much during baking. Make them about 1/4 inch thick. Then, if you'd like, press a few more chocolate chips into the tops of each cookie."],[null,"Bake for 10-11 minutes and remove from the oven. They may seem a little underdone, but they'll firm up more as they cool. Let them cool for 5-10 minutes before transferring and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Weigh the flour using a kitchen scale , if possible. This will yield the most desirable results. Using too little or too much flour will alter the texture of your cookies. If you do not have a kitchen scale , measure 2 cups of flour, but do not scoop from the bag. Spoon it into the measuring cup and level off with a knife. These pumpkin cookies don’t spread much, so use slightly damp hands/fingers (to prevent sticking) to press them down and shape into rounds before baking. Gently press down a few extra chocolate chips on top of each cookie, before baking for the ultimate gooey goodness. The cookies may appear slightly underdone at the 10-11 minute mark, but remove them from the oven anyway as they’ll firm up more as they cool. Do not overbake , or they’ll get dry. Let your cookies cool for 5-10 minutes before transferring them from your baking sheet. Hot cookies can easily break, so walk away if you need to. 😉 Leftovers keep in a sealed container at room temperature for 3-4 days. You may refrigerate for up to 1 week or freeze air tight in a freezer safe container for up to 3 months. Make sure they’re fully cooled to room temperature before freezing."]]},"9433642":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F."],[null,"Add the wet ingredients to a large bowl and mix well. Then add the dry ingredients to the same bowl and mix to combine."],[null,"Divide the mixture among your nonstick donut pans, enough to make 12 donuts. Bake for 18-20 minutes, or until firm to touch, but gives a little when gently pressed with your finger. Then remove from the oven and let cool for at least 10 minutes before transferring to a cooling rack."],["Optional Glaze","While the donuts are cooling, prepare the glaze. Add the dates, water and cinnamon to a blender and process until completely smooth. Then, transfer to a shallow dish."],["Optional Glaze","When the donuts have cooled, dip them into the glaze and place them glaze side up on your cooling rack. Let them dry and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Weigh your flour if possible, for the most desirable results. Use a nonstick silicone donut pan to avoid greasing your pan, if you’re avoiding oil. Mine popped out easily once cooled. Allow your donuts to cool for 10-15 minutes before attempting to remove them from the pan. If the donuts are hot, you risk breaking them. Let your pumpkin donuts cool on a cooling rack for 10 minutes before glazing them. If you don’t have a powerful blender or your dates are very dry, soak them in cool water for 15-20 minutes, before blending. This will soften them and help them break down more smoothly. Leftover donuts will stay moist and fresh in a sealed container at room temperature for 2-3 days, although they taste best on the day they’re made. The nutritional information does not include the optional glaze."]]},"9228604":{"s":[["For the pumpkin puree","Preheat your oven to 400 degrees convection roast and line a baking tray with parchment paper."],["For the pumpkin puree","Cut your pumpkin in half or thirds, and scoop out the seeds. Place the pumpkin skin side down on your tray. Sprinkle with salt and pepper and roast until a fork easily pierces the pumpkin flesh, approx. 40 minutes, and then remove from the oven."],["For the pumpkin puree","Scoop the pumpkin from the skin and transfer it to a food processor or blender and process until very smooth. Work in batches, as needed. Measure 2 cups of puree and set it aside to make the gnocchi."],["For the vegan pumpkin gnocchi","In a large bowl, add 2 cups of pumpkin puree, 3 cups of flour, and the seasoning. Mix to combine and transfer to a large floured work surface."],["For the vegan pumpkin gnocchi","Knead the dough using your hands, adding a light sprinkle of flour to your surface and hands as needed to prevent sticking. Use the least amount of flour possible to prevent sticking, without adding too much. The dough should be a little sticky, this is normal. Be mindful not to add too much flour, or the gnocchi won't be soft."],["For the vegan pumpkin gnocchi","Use a rolling pin to roll your dough so that it's approx. half an inch thick."],["For the vegan pumpkin gnocchi","Then sprinkle a sharp knife or pizza cutter with flour and cut the dough into 1-inch strips. Then, cut each strip into approx. half-inch pieces to make a grid pattern. Sprinkle the pieces with a touch more flour if needed."],["For the vegan pumpkin gnocchi","Optional: Use a floured gnocchi board or a large fork to gently press and roll each gnocchi to make ridges. Re-flour your board or fork to prevent sticking."],["For the vegan pumpkin gnocchi","Place the prepared gnocchi in a single layer on a tray lined with parchment paper. If you'll be cooking your gnocchi within 2 hours, you may leave them at room temperature. Otherwise, follow the storage directions in the notes below."],["To cook the gnocchi","This makes a large batch, so you may freeze some and cook some straight away."],["To cook the gnocchi","To cook, bring a large pot of generously salted water to a boil. Then drop the gnocchi into the boiling water, working in batches to avoid overcrowding. Boil until tender and floating at the top of the water, approx. 5-10 minutes. NOTE: Cook time will vary according to how crowded the pot is, which flour you're using, and if using homemade pumpkin puree or canned."],["To cook the gnocchi","Remove the gnocchi using a slotted spoon and place them in a serving bowl. Repeat with remaining gnocchi until you've cooked the desired amount. Serve with your favourite sauce and garnishes."],["For the vegan sage butter sauce","Add all the ingredients to a high-speed blender and process until smooth. Serve over the gnocchi and garnish with fresh sage."]],"h":[[null,"Don’t overwork the dough . You don’t want to overly knead your dough or this will result in firmer gnocchi, and they taste best when soft. Work it for about 1-2 minutes and not longer. Don’t go overboard with the flour . Use enough so that the dough is not sticking to your hands and work surface, but don’t add too much or the gnocchi will be hard. A little stickiness is a-okay. A 3 lb pie pumpkin will produce approx. 2 cups of pumpkin puree which is what is needed for this recipe. If you have extra, refrigerate or freeze it to use in another recipe. Use only 2 cups for this recipe , or increase the flour to compensate for the difference if you want to use more. Keep extra flour handy while you work . You’ll need it to sprinkle your work surface, your hands, rolling pin, knife, gnocchi board, etc. Make sure to keep your gnocchi in a single layer once prepared to prevent them from sticking to one another. To save time , you may use 2 cups of canned pumpkin puree and skip roasting the pumpkin with similar results. If you don’t have a gnocchi board or don’t want to make the ridges, you may skip this step entirely. The ridges are cosmetic and will not affect the outcome or flavour of the dish. Once your gnocchi is prepared, (but not cooked) you may leave them at room temperature for up to 2 hours in a single layer. Or, refrigerate for 1-2 days if you’re working ahead. Freeze uncooked gnocchi in a single layer for a few hours, until solid. Then, transfer to a sealed container or zip-top bag and keep frozen for up to 3 months. Cook from frozen, DO NOT THAW . Pumpkin gnocchi takes a little longer to cook than potato versions . They are not necessarily ready as soon as they float to the top. Check tenderness level around the 5-minute mark, and continue cooking until soft. ***The nutritional information represents ⅛ of the pumpkin gnocchi with ⅛ of the quick vegan sage butter sauce. If you use another sauce the nutritional info will vary. Leftover cooked gnocchi keep refrigerated for 2-3 days."]]},"9559352":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 350 degrees F and line a large baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"In a medium mixing bowl, combine your wet ingredients. Then add all the dry ingredients and mix until incorporated. The batter will be thick, so a silicone spatula works best."],[null,"Use a small cookie scoop to make approx. 22-24 cookies and place them on your prepared baking sheet. Use a wet fork or spoon to flatten slightly."],[null,"Optional: Press any optional toppings gently into the center of some or all of your cookies."],[null,"Then bake for 12-14 minutes, until edges are lightly golden and remove from the oven. Let cool for 10 minutes before enjoying."]],"h":[[null,"If you have a premixed pumpkin spice blend (and don't have the individual seasonings) you may use 3 teaspoons of the mix instead. The cookie batter will be thick, and won’t spread in the oven , so make sure to shape them to your liking , before baking. It helps to wet the fork or spoon when pressing your cookies down so it doesn’t stick to the cookies. Let your cookies rest for 10 minutes before enjoying. This brief cool down period will allow your cookies to completely set. For nut free , skip the pecan garnish. Leftovers will keep at room temperature for 2-3 days, refrigerated for 1 week or freeze air tight in a freezer safe container for up to 3 months."]]},"9249680":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your griddle and then in a small bowl, combine the soy milk and apple cider vinegar. Set aside to let it curdle."],[null,"In a large bowl, whisk together the flour, baking powder, cinnamon, ginger, nutmeg and cloves. Once mixed, add the pumpkin puree, maple syrup, apple sauce, vanilla, and now curdled milk. Mix until combined, without over mixing."],[null,"Drop about 1/4 cup worth of your batter onto your hot griddle, leaving plenty of space between each pancake."],[null,"Cook until small bubbles have formed on the surface of your pancakes and the edges are golden brown, approx 5-6 minutes. Then flip and cook for another 3-5 minutes until golden brown."],[null,"Serve with chopped pecans, sliced banana, maple syrup, blueberry chia jam, or berries."]],"h":[[null,"If you don’t have all the spices called for , but you have pumpkin pie spice, you may use 2 teaspoons of the pie spice to replace all four seasonings. Do not over mix your pumpkin pancake batter . Like most pancake recipes, a few lumps is perfectly fine, so mix until just combined. Make sure your griddle is HOT before cooking your pancakes . Since we’re not using oil, you need a hot surface to prevent sticking. Test the heat by adding a drop of water to see if it sizzles. If you don’t have or don’t like pumpkin , you may use sweet potato or butternut squash puree in its place. Once cooled, you may refrigerate leftovers for 2-3 days, or freeze for up to 1 month. Make sure to let the pancakes cool before freezing."]]},"9908880":{"s":[[null,"Combine the vegetable broth, pumpkin puree, all the seasoning, and the arrowroot powder in a medium saucepan. Simmer over medium-low heat for 5-6 minutes, stirring often. Then turn off the heat and stir in the milk. Set aside and keep it covered."],[null,"Meanwhile, bring a large pot of generously salted water to boil, and cook your pasta according to package directions. Drain and return to the pot. Then pour the sauce over the pasta and mix immediately so the pasta doesn't stick together. You may reserve some of the sauce to garnish each plate or mix it all in."],[null,"Serve garnished with chili flakes and vegan Parmesan cheese if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Salt your water. Add enough salt to the boiling water for the best texture and flavour. Here's a handy guide to help you salt your water perfectly each time. The sauce is great with wheat pasta, zoodles, brown rice, chickpea or lentil pasta. Cook wheat pasta 'al dente' for best texture . (Al dente means the pasta is still firm once cooked, giving optimal texture in every bite.) To make this gluten-free , use your favourite gluten-free pasta and cook according to package directions for ' al dente ' pasta. Store leftover pasta and sauce separately or the pasta will absorb all the extra sauce. If you're cooking for picky eaters skip the cayenne pepper. If you can't have soy (but can have nuts) use unsweetened cashew or almond milk. Or try canned coconut milk for a richer sauce. Use light for less fat."]]},"9237341":{"s":[[null,"In a small sauce pot, combine all the ingredients, except the coffee and heat over medium heat, watching carefully not to boil. Stir often and heat until desired temperature is reached."],[null,"Meanwhile divide your hot coffee or espresso between your two mugs. Then pour the heated pumpkin spiced milk on top. Stir and enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"To save time, and if you don't have the individual spices listed, you may sub with ¾ teaspoon of pumpkin pie spice instead. Use espresso coffee for the best flavour. Sprinkle your latte with a dash of cinnamon or a dash of pumpkin pie spice mix for extra flavour, if desired. If you want it sweet , add 1-2 teaspoons of unrefined coconut sugar, or sweetener of choice to each mug. For soy free , sub the soy milk with unsweetened cashew milk , almond milk, oat milk , or your choice."]]},"9682858":{"s":[[null,"Add all the ingredients to a high-speed blender and process until smooth."],[null,"Transfer to a bowl or container and refrigerate for 1 hour before serving."]],"h":[[null,"If you do not have a powerful blender , soak your cashews in boiling hot water for 20-30 minutes. Then drain them before blending. For ranch dressing , add an additional 1-3 tablespoons of water to thin it out to your liking. OR add 1-3 tablespoons of apple cider vinegar. Once blended , taste and add more salt or other seasonings, if preferred. Keep refrigerated in a sealed container for up to 7 days, or freeze airtight for up to 6 months. Nutritional information is for approx. 2 tablespoons or ⅛ of the dip."]]},"9388968":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375℉/190℃ and grab a muffin tray to fit 12 muffins. If you don't have a nonstick pan use paper liners or grease the tins."],[null,"Combine the soy milk and lemon juice in a large bowl and set it aside for 5 minutes to thicken and curdle. (This makes vegan buttermilk.)"],[null,"Then add the lemon zest and applesauce to the bowl of curdled milk and mix."],[null,"Next, add the flour, sugar, baking powder and soda. Mix until combined without overmixing. Then gently fold in the raspberries."],[null,"Divide the batter between your 12 muffin cups and bake for 20-22 minutes, until a toothpick inserted in the middle comes out clean. Remove from the oven and let cool for at least 20 minutes before carefully transferring to a cooling rack. The muffins are delicate, so let them cool before transferring."],[null,"If using the optional glaze, mix the sugar and lemon juice in a small bowl Once the muffins are completely cooled, drizzle them with the glaze and let them sit for a few minutes so the sugar hardens, and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Weigh your flour using a kitchen scale for the most accurate results ! Scooping flour from a bag will compact the flour, and could mean too much flour is being used which could result in a denser muffin."],[null,"Use FRESH + ACTIVE baking powder . Baking powder that has been open in the pantry for 6+ months may lose its effectiveness."],[null,"Let your muffins cool in their pan for at least 20 minutes before transferring to a cooling rack. These muffins are delicate when warm so give them time to cool to prevent breaking them."],[null,"If using the optional glaze, ensure the muffins are completely cooled first and glaze them just before serving. Storing glazed muffins in a sealed container will cause the glaze to melt."],[null,"The muffins will keep in a sealed container at room temperature for 2-3 days, refrigerated for up to 1 week or frozen for up to 3 months. Inspired by my Lemon Blueberry Muffins ."]]},"9774483":{"s":[[null,"Bring a large pot of water to a boil and cook your pasta according to package directions for 'al dente' pasta. Once cooked, drain and set it aside."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the 1/4 cup of broth, onion, and sliced peppers to a large pan and sauté until slightly softened, approx. 5-7 minutes. Then add the garlic and sauté another 30-60 seconds, stirring often, until fragrant."],[null,"Add the remaining cup of broth, tomato sauce, chickpeas, and coconut milk to your pan and simmer over medium heat for 5-10 minutes, and turn off the heat."],[null,"Then add the cooked penne to your sauce and mix well to evenly coat the pasta. Let stand for a few minutes so the pasta absorbs some sauce, and then serve."]],"h":[[null,"Store-bought jerk spice blends normally have a lot of sugar. Make your own blend to control the amount of brown sugar or omit it entirely if preferred."],[null,"Keep your portions small since pasta and coconut milk are on the heavier side."],[null,"For lower fat , use light coconut milk instead of full fat. Or you may use another dairy-free milk, but note the sauce won’t be as rich."],[null,"Salt your pasta water. Make sure to add enough salt to your pot of water for best texture and flavour. Here's a handy guide to help you salt your water perfectly each time."],[null,"Cook your pasta al dente. Do not overcook! Al dente means that the pasta is still firm once cooked, giving optimal texture in every bite. To ensure it does not overcook, start taste testing a few minutes before the package says it will be ready. It should be tender, but still firm."],[null,"Leftovers will keep refrigerated for 3-4 days."]]},"9492507":{"s":[[null,"Add ALL the ingredients EXCEPT the vital wheat gluten to a food processor and process until mostly smooth. Then add the vital wheat gluten, half at a time and pulse until mostly combined. (It doesn't have to be perfect.)"],[null,"Transfer the mixture to a clean cutting board or other clean surface. Then knead the dough with your hands for 2-3 minutes. Shape it into a log that measures approx. 4 inches wide and 8 inches long."],[null,"Snugly wrap it with parchment paper and then aluminum foil and twist the ends to secure it. (See process shots above for reference.) Then choose ONE cooking method below."],["Instant Pot Instructions","Add a cup of water to the bottom of your Instant Pot and place the trivet on top. Then place your wrapped vegan roast on the trivet. Close the lid, ensure the valve is in the sealing position, and set it to \"steam\" for 60 minutes. Let the pot naturally release and then open it once safe to do so. (It will take approx. 10-12 minutes to naturally release.) Transfer your roast to a cutting board and LET IT REST for 10 minutes before slicing."],["Baking Instructions","Preheat the oven to 375℉/190℃ and place the wrapped seitan roast on a baking sheet. Bake it on the center rack for 45 minutes. Then flip it over and bake it for an additional 45 minutes. Remove it from the oven and LET IT REST for 10 minutes before slicing."],["Steaming Instructions","Bring a large pot with a couple of inches of water to boil and place your steamer basket inside. Make sure the basket is not touching the water. Once boiling, reduce the heat to maintain a low boil/simmer, place the wrapped vegan roast inside, and put the lid on top. Steam for 35 minutes, then flip it and steam an additional 35-45 minutes. Check your water level every so often and add hot water as needed. Once cooked, transfer your vegan roast to a cutting board and LET IT REST for 10 minutes before slicing."]],"h":[[null,"Weigh the vital wheat gluten for the most accurate results . If you must measure using cups, make sure to spoon and level the flour. DO NOT scoop from the bag or you’ll end up with more than needed."],[null,"Make sure to use a very flavourful and salty broth since there’s no other salt added. If you only have low-sodium broth on hand, add ½-1 teaspoon of salt."],[null,"To test for doneness: Gently peel back the foil, the seitan roast should appear smooth. Give it a poke with your finger or tongs to test firmness. (Careful it will be HOT !) It should feel firm but still give a little to pressure. It will continue to firm up as it cools."],[null,"Leftovers will keep refrigerated for up to 5 days. Or freeze the vegan roast in an airtight freezer-safe container for up to 3 months. You may freeze it whole, or in slices."]]},"9214034":{"s":[[null,"Bring a large pot of generously salted water to a boil. Cook your pasta according to package directions for 'al dente'. (This means to slightly undercook your pasta a couple of minutes.) Drain the pasta but RESERVE a cup of the cooking water and set it aside."],[null,"Meanwhile, add all the sauce ingredients to a strong blender and process until smooth. Then taste for salt and pepper, adding more if needed. Transfer the sauce to a deep skillet and heat it on the stovetop."],[null,"Transfer the cooked pasta and the chickpeas to the skillet with sauce and mix well. Add the reserved pasta water to the sauce if a thinner/saucier consistency is desired."],[null,"Serve your roasted red pepper pasta garnished with fresh herbs, red pepper flakes, or vegan parmesan cheese if you'd like."]],"h":[]},"9921915":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350°F/176°C and prepare a 9-inch pie plate or similar oven-safe dish. (Grease if needed.)"],[null,"Add all the cheese sauce ingredients to your blender, process until smooth, and set aside."],[null,"Peel and thinly slice your potatoes to approx. 1/8\" thick, using a sharp knife, a mandolin, or another slicing tool."],[null,"Layer half the slices in your dish, sprinkle with salt and pepper, and pour half of the cheese sauce on top. Repeat with the remaining slices and cheese sauce for the second layer. Then sprinkle with the vegan parmesan cheese, if using."],[null,"Cover the dish with parchment paper, followed by aluminum foil, and bake for 40 minutes. Then remove the paper and continue baking for another 20-25 minutes until golden brown. You may optionally broil the dish for another 1-2 minutes to get the top layer extra crispy."],[null,"Once baked, garnish with fresh parsley and serve."]],"h":[]},"9917964":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425℉/218℃ and line your baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Add the flour and baking powder to a large bowl and stir to combine. Then add the milk and vanilla and mix until combined, without overmixing."],[null,"Pour the pancake batter onto your baking sheet and spread it into an even layer. You may use a silicone spatula, or pick up the tray and rotate from side to side."],[null,"Top with any toppings you'd like, but don't press them down. Then bake for 10-12 minutes, until the pancakes are lightly golden, firm to the touch, and roughly doubled in thickness."],[null,"Remove the tray from the oven and let cool for a few minutes before transferring to a cutting board to slice and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Weigh your flour for the most accurate results . Scooping from a bag often results in too much flour being used due to compacting the flour into the measuring cup."],[null,"If you do not have a kitchen scale , spoon the flour into your measuring cup and scrape off the top with a knife, but do not scoop from the bag."],[null,"Use fresh, active baking powder . Baking powder that has been opened and sitting in the pantry for several months can start to lose its effectiveness."],[null,"Do not over-mix your pancake batter. If there are a few lumps, that's perfectly okay. Don't be tempted to mix until perfectly smooth as this may alter the texture of your pancakes."],[null,"Leftovers will keep refrigerated for 3-4 days, or freeze them airtight for up to 3 months."]]},"9226480":{"s":[[null,"Add the diced onion with 1/4 cup worth of the broth to a cast iron pan or nonstick skillet and sauté over medium/high heat. Stir occasionally and continue adding broth approx. 1/4 cup at a time, once the previous broth has completely evaporated, to prevent sticking. Continue until the onions are brown and caramelized and the broth is consumed. This will take approx. 15-20 minutes. Set aside when done."],[null,"Meanwhile, add all the sour cream ingredients, starting with 2 tablespoons of water to a high-speed blender. Process until completely smooth and add more water if a thinner consistency is desired. Taste for salt and add some if needed. (The soy sauce will add some saltiness, so taste before adding salt.)"],[null,"Transfer the vegan sour cream to a bowl and then stir in the caramelized onions. Refrigerate for at least 1 hour, but a little longer is even better. The dip tastes best when cold and the flavours have had a chance to marry."]],"h":[]},"9839357":{"s":[[null,"Add your soy curls to a large bowl and cover with water. Set that aside and let it soak for 10 minutes to rehydrate them. Then preheat the oven to 300℉/149℃ and line a large baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Meanwhile, combine all the marinade ingredients (everything except the soy curls) in another large bowl and stir until combined."],[null,"Drain your soy curls, and grab them one handful at a time, squeeze out the excess moisture in your kitchen sink, and transfer to the bowl with the marinade. Once all the curls are in your bowl of sauce, stir to evenly coat each piece. Let the curls absorb all the sauce, letting it rest for a couple of minutes if needed, then stir again."],[null,"Arrange the marinated soy curls in a single layer on your tray and bake for 30 minutes. Then flip the pieces and continue baking in 10-minute increments until the desired doneness is reached. Mine were perfect after 60 minutes in total. (Smaller pieces may be ready sooner.)"],[null,"Remove from the oven and let rest for a few minutes before enjoying."]],"h":[[null,"Squeeze out the excess moisture after soaking the soy curls . If you don’t, they will absorb less of the delicious marinade resulting in less flavourful soy curl jerky."],[null,"Don’t overcook the jerky or it will get too crispy and dry. The sweet spot is chewy insides with a firm exterior, so check on it often towards the end of baking."],[null,"Smaller pieces may be ready sooner so remove pieces from the tray as needed, so you don’t let any get overcooked."],[null,"Store leftovers in a container or jar at room temperature for up to 5 days."]]},"9279723":{"s":[[null,"Drain and rinse your artichokes, thinly slice them, and set them aside."],[null,"Add all the ingredients EXCEPT the artichoke and spinach to a high-speed blender. Process until smooth, it will be very liquidy but it will thicken when it cooks."],[null,"Pour the mixture into a nonstick skillet or use an oven-safe skillet like a cast iron pan if you want to broil the dip later. Add the sliced artichoke and spinach to the pan. Cook over medium heat, stirring often, for about 5 minutes until thick and bubbly."],[null,"OPTIONAL: Set the oven to broil on high. Then transfer the dip to an oven-safe dish (if not in one already). Broil for 2-5 minutes until golden brown and bubbly on top. Watch carefully to prevent burning. Remove from the oven."],[null,"Sprinkle with vegan parmesan cheese, if using. Then serve warm with tortilla chips, crackers, raw veggies, bread, or any of your favourite dippers."]],"h":[[null,"* If you’re using frozen spinach , make sure to squeeze and drain as much water as possible before adding it to your skillet. If you don’t have a high-speed blender , soak the cashews in boiling hot water for 15-30 minutes first, and then drain and use as directed. This will help soften them, making them easier to blend. If the dip gets too thick , add more milk or water to the pan to thin it out. Note that it will harden as it cools and reheating the dip will return it to a silkier texture. For added depth of flavour , use vegetable broth instead of water. To make it spicy, add ½ teaspoon of cayenne pepper or 1-2 teaspoons of your favourite hot sauce. For a smoky dip , add 1 teaspoon of smoked paprika. To make it ahead, blend and cook on the stovetop as directed and refrigerate until needed. Then pop in the oven at 350°F/176°C to heat through for about 10-15 minutes. Then broil for an additional 2-5 minutes to brown the top, if you’d like. Keep leftovers refrigerated in a sealed container for 3-4 days or freeze them airtight in a freezer-safe container for up to 3 months. Recipe inspired by my vegan mozzarella ."]]},"7293684":{"s":[[null,"Mix the burger ingredients together (apart from the oil), form into 4 patties and refrigerate for 20 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, chargrill or grill the aubergine, mushrooms, courgette &amp"],[null,"peppers and keep warm."],[null,"While the vegetables are grilling, prepare your salad garnish and tahini sauce."],[null,"Add the oil to a non-stick pan over a low-to-medium heat and cook the burgers for 4-6 minutes each side until golden brown and warm all the way through."],[null,"Toast the buns then add the salad, burger and chargrilled vegetables, drizzle with tahini and secure with a skewer."]],"h":[[null,"Most beans or chickpeas work for these burgers so use any you have to hand."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"9000851":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F and line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Arrange the cubed bread and chopped pecans on the tray and bake for 8 minutes, or until nicely toasted. Remove from the oven and set aside."],[null,"Meanwhile, melt the butter (if using) in a large skillet and add all the chopped veggies and seasoning to the pan. Sauté for 7-8 minutes, until the veggies are soft and golden."],[null,"Add the toasted bread and pecans to the pan of veggies and pour 2 cups of broth on top. Mix well. Taste and adjust for salt and pepper, and add more broth if you prefer a softer stuffing. Serve and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"I used half a loaf of this Dempster’s Ancient Grains w/ Quinoa bread. You may use any of your favourite sliced breads, or homemade. Start with only 2 cups of the broth , at first. Mix well and add more, if you prefer your stuffing softer."]]},"9249096":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375℉/190℃ and line a loaf pan with parchment paper. (Or grease it if you're not avoiding oil.)"],[null,"In a large bowl mash the bananas. Then add the applesauce, maple syrup and vanilla and mix well."],[null,"To the same bowl, add all the dry ingredients and mix until combined. Then gently fold in the strawberries. The batter will be thick."],[null,"Pour the batter into your prepared loaf pan and add some sliced strawberries and banana slices on top, if desired."],[null,"Bake for 50-60 minutes, or until a toothpick inserted in the middle of your loaf comes out clean. Remove it from the oven and let it cool for 10 minutes before transferring the sweet bread to a wire rack for at least 20 minutes before slicing."]],"h":[[null,"Use overly ripe bananas. The more brown spots, the better and sweeter the results. Since this recipe uses very little sweetener, you want to make sure your bananas will provide ample sweetness."],[null,"Measure your mashed bananas. Bananas vary in size. So use enough banana puree for optimal sweetness and moisture. Measure to ensure you're using a heaping cup of mashed banana."],[null,"Use parchment paper to line your loaf pan. While a non-stick loaf does the trick, it’s easier to transfer the loaf from the pan when using parchment paper without breaking it."],[null,"Individual ovens will vary. So test the doneness of your strawberry banana bread using a toothpick or knife inserted in the middle. When it comes out dry, it’s ready."],[null,"Let it cool. Give yourself extra time to let the loaf cool. At least 10 minutes before transferring it, and another 20 minutes on the cooling rack to help it set. This makes slicing a lot easier."],[null,"Leftovers keep tightly wrapped at room temperature for 2-3 days, refrigerated for 3-5 days or freeze (once cooled) in an airtight container for up to 3 months."]]},"9406639":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350℉/176℃ and line two cookie sheets with parchment paper."],[null,"Mash the bananas into a large mixing bowl. Then add the oats, tahini, sugar, vanilla, and mix well."],[null,"Fold in the strawberries and chocolate chips if using them."],[null,"Scoop the mixture onto your lined baking sheet to make approximately 30 cookies. Then press down each of the cookie dough balls to shape them, since they won't spread much in the oven."],[null,"Bake the cookies for 8-10 minutes and then remove from the oven and let them rest for 5-10 minutes before transferring to a cooling rack."]],"h":[[null,"Use overripe bananas. The riper your bananas, the greater flavour, sweetness, and moisture they will add to your banana chickpea muffins. Bananas with brown skin work best."],[null,"Measure your mashed banana to ensure you're using one cup. Bananas vary greatly in size. Two large bananas or three medium bananas work for me."],[null,"Don’t overbake the cookies , or they will be dry. They will appear underdone, but remember they firm up more as they cool down."],[null,"Let your cookies cool for 5-10 minutes before transferring them to a wire rack."],[null,"Store the cookies at room temperature for 1-2 days, refrigerated for 4-5 days, or keep frozen for up to 3 months."]]},"9228970":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 350℉/176℃ and grease or line a muffin pan with parchment liners, enough to make 12 muffins."],[null,"Combine the soy milk and apple cider vinegar in a large mixing bowl and set it aside for 5 minutes to curdle, thicken, and make your vegan buttermilk."],[null,"Once curdled, add the applesauce and vanilla to the same bowl and stir to combine. Then add all the dry ingredients: flour, sugar, baking powder, and stir until combined. Lastly, fold in your diced strawberries."],[null,"Divide the muffin batter between your 12 muffin cups and bake in your preheated oven for 18-22 minutes, or until a toothpick inserted in the middle comes out clean."],[null,"Let the muffins rest for 10 minutes before transferring them to a wire rack to continue cooling."]],"h":[]},"9769795":{"s":[[null,"Prepare your pie crust of choice and blind bake according to its directions. If you're using my oil free pie crust, bake for 15-20 minutes, until the edges are golden. Set aside to let cool slightly before filling."],[null,"Wash, hull and slice your strawberries and set aside."],[null,"Use 2 cups of your sliced strawberries to arrange on your baked pie crust. You may start around the edges and work your way towards the middle, or work in rows. You should have 2 layers of strawberries."],[null,"Shake your canned coconut milk very well before opening. Then add 1 cup worth to your blender, along with 1 cup of the sliced strawberries, the sugar, lemon juice, vanilla and tapioca. Blend until smooth."],[null,"Now pour the mixture into a small pot and bring to a boil, whisking constantly. Boil for about 1 minute, until thick and then pour over the strawberry layer immediately. Spread as evenly as possible and then refrigerate overnight or for a minimum of 4-6 hours, until set."],[null,"Once set, garnish with strawberry slices, if desired. It helps to use a wet knife for slicing as the top filling can get sticky. Enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Use fresh strawberries for the best results. If you have a sweet tooth , or if your strawberries are not very sweet, increase the sugar to ⅓-1/2 cup. Make sure to shake your can of coconut milk very well before opening. Since you’re not using the entire can, you want to make sure the contents are mixed well before measuring your cup full. If you’re having trouble, pour the contents into a bowl and whisk to combine. For low fat , sub the canned coconut milk for a light version. Or, you may also use water. The filling will be less rich, but still delicious. Make sure to plan ahead , as this dessert tastes best when refrigerated overnight. Do not cut your pie until it’s cool . The filling needs time to chill and set before slicing. It will hold and slice easily once chilled. Use a sharp, wet knife as it can get sticky. Nutritional information is for one slice (or ⅛th) of the strawberry pie, including my oil free pie crust . If you’re using another crust, nutritional info will vary."]]},"9124659":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350℉/176℃ and line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Use a paring knife to carefully remove the mushroom stems, finely chop them, and set aside. Then use a small spoon to gently scrape out the gills and discard."],[null,"Place the mushrooms hollow side down on your tray and bake for 10 minutes. Remove them from the oven and use a clean dish towel or paper towel to absorb the excess moisture that the mushrooms release during baking. (Dry the parchment paper too.) Then flip them hollow side up and set them aside."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the onion, garlic and chopped mushroom stems to a large pan and sprinkle with salt and pepper. Dry sauté for about 5 minutes (the mushrooms will release moisture so you won't need oil) until softened and reduced. Then add the rice and mix well, cooking/toasting for about 30 seconds."],[null,"Add approx. 1/2 cup of broth to your pan, stirring often until absorbed. Continue adding broth about 1/2 cup at a time, stirring your risotto often. Wait until the liquids are absorbed before adding the next portion of broth. Repeat until all 3 cups of broth are used. This will take around 20 minutes. Then remove the pan from the heat, and stir in the cranberries."],[null,"Increase the oven temperature to 400℉/204℃. Then, generously stuff the mushrooms, sprinkle with vegan Parmesan cheese, and bake for 15 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"Use caution when removing your mushroom stems . Don’t rush, especially if it’s your first time making stuffed mushrooms."],[null,"If it’s your first time making stuffed mushrooms , buy a few extra, just in case some break. Then, if you do end up with a couple of broken ones, finely chop them and add them to your stuffing. No waste."],[null,"Dry the excess liquid after the first round of baking your mushrooms. Don’t skip this step ."],[null,"Do NOT add all the broth at once , to your pan of arborio rice. When making Italian risotto, the slow way, is the best way for a perfectly creamy texture (without adding creams, vegan butter, or vegan cream cheese)."],[null,"Leftovers will keep in the refrigerator for 2-3 days in a sealed container."]]},"9390900":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 425 degrees F (218 degrees C) and line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Cut your cauliflower into small, bite sized pieces and set it aside. Then add the remaining cauliflower ingredients to a medium mixing bowl and whisk to combine, to make the batter. Place the cut up cauliflower bites into the batter and mix well to evenly coat the pieces."],[null,"Arrange the coated cauliflower on your baking sheet in a single layer, but do not dump everything from the bowl. You don't want excess batter on the tray or it may stick together and prevent crispiness."],[null,"Bake for 20-25 minutes, flipping once at the halfway point until desired crispiness is reached."],[null,"While the cauliflower is baking, prepare the sweet and sour sauce. Whisk all the sauce ingredients (except the pepper and pineapple) in a small bowl or measuring cup and set aside."],[null,"Then sauté the red pepper and pineapple chunks in a large skillet with a tablespoon of water or broth, to prevent sticking. Do so over medium high heat until slightly brown. Then reduce the heat to medium low and pour the sauce into the pan and simmer until slightly thickened, approx. 5 minutes."],[null,"By now, your cauliflower should be ready. Add it to the pan with the sauce and gently mix to evenly coat each piece."],[null,"Serve over rice or quinoa and garnish with sesame seeds and green onion."]],"h":[[null,"Do not dump the cauliflower onto the baking tray once coated with the batter. You don’t want any excess batter on the tray, or it will stick to the tray, and pieces may stick to one another, reducing its crispy exterior. Take the time to place the battered cauliflower in a single layer , one piece at a time, with plenty of space in between for the best results. Tastes best when freshly made but leftovers will keep refrigerated in a sealed container for 3-4 days."]]},"9794716":{"s":[[null,"In a small pot, add the cubed sweet potato, cover with water and bring to a boil. Cook until fork tender, approx. 10 minutes. Then drain and set aside."],[null,"Meanwhile, add diced onion, pepper and mushrooms to a large pan. Sprinkle with salt and pepper and dry sauté until softened, approx. 5 mins. (The mushrooms will release moisture, so you should not need any oil or water to sauté.)"],[null,"Add the cooked sweet potato, beans and seasoning to your food processor. Process until broken down, but not smooth. You want to keep some texture. Then add the sautéed veggies and the oats and pulse a few times to mix through. Do not puree."],[null,"Line a baking tray with parchment paper and use wet hands to form tennis sized balls from your batter. Then flatten into a patty shape and place on your tray. You should get 8 patties. Refrigerate for at least 30 minutes, or overnight if working ahead."],[null,"When ready to bake, heat your oven to 450 degrees F and bake for 25 minutes. Then carefully flip the burgers and bake another 15 minutes, until the edges are golden brown."]],"h":[[null,"Do not over process . You want a nice textured burger here, so make sure not to over do it in the food processor. Work in batches if you have a small processor. Don’t try and jam everything into a smaller appliance or the bottom will get pureed, and the top will stay chunky. This won’t give you the best texture. Use wet hands to make your patties ! The batter will be a little sticky, so using wet hands will prevent the patties from sticking to your hands. Taste the batter and adjust the seasoning if needed. Once your batter is processed, taste a sample and add more salt, pepper, garlic powder, cumin or cayenne, if needed. Always season to your taste. Make it smoky. If you want add a smoky flavour to your burgers, add a ½ teaspoon of smoked paprika to the batter. Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-4 days or freeze airtight for up to 3 months."]]},"9713201":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 450 degrees F roast and line a baking tray with parchment paper."],[null,"Add the cubed sweet potato, quartered onion and garlic (with the peel) to your baking tray. Drizzle with the olive oil, and sprinkle with salt and pepper and bake for 15-20 minutes, until the potatoes are fork tender. Remove from the oven."],[null,"Now peel the garlic, and place all the roasted veggies, along with the cashews, nutritional yeast, paprika, salt, thyme, milk, and veggie broth to your blende and process until smooth."],[null,"Meanwhile, bring a large pot of salted water to boil and cook your pasta according to package directions for al dente pasta. Drain and return to pot. Pour the sauce over the pasta and mix well."],[null,"Optional: Set the oven to broil and transfer the pasta and sauce to an oven safe dish. Place on top rack for 2-3 minutes until the top is golden and crispy, or to desired 'doneness'. Check often so it doesn't burn."]],"h":[[null,"The sauce will thicken as it cools so if preparing ahead, you will need to add more broth or milk when ready to serve. If you do not have a high speed blender, soak your cashews in boiling hot water for about 30 minutes first to soften them. Then drain and use as directed. For nut free: sub the raw cashews with sunflower seeds, and the cashew milk with soy, oat, or any milk you like. Sunflower seeds are a little less mild in flavour when compared to cashews, but definitely not overpowering. Especially when considering all the other flavours and seasoning in this dish. As an added bonus, sunflower seeds are budget friendly and lower in fat too! **For oil free: omit the oil for roasting the veggies. Instead you can spray or drizzle the veggies in water or broth to keep them from burning. Watch them carefully. For “nooch” free: if you don’t have, can’t find, or don’t want to use nutritional yeast, you may sub for 1-2 tablespoons of miso paste or soy sauce, but omit the teaspoon of salt from the sauce. Keep in mind this substitution will give you a nice umami flavour, but not the cheesiness that nutritional yeast offers. For more crunch : If you’re optionally baking your mac and cheese, you may also add half a cup of panko breadcrumbs on top before broiling. This will add even more flavour and added crunch to the top layer."]]},"9626419":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425℉/218℃ convection roast. If your oven does not have a convection feature, bake your potatoes longer."],[null,"Line a baking sheet with parchment, pierce your potatoes several times with a fork and place them on the tray. Then roast your sweet potatoes for 35-55 minutes, until soft and easily pieced with a fork. The cook time will vary according to the size of your potatoes, and whether or not you're using a convection oven."],[null,"Remove the sweet potatoes from the oven and let them cool for 2-3 minutes. Then slice each one in half, pull the peel back, and scoop the flesh into a bowl. Add the maple syrup, cinnamon, and salt to the same bowl, and use a large fork or potato mashed to mash the potatoes and combine with the other ingredients."],[null,"Serve warm."]],"h":[]},"9490339":{"s":[[null,"Add all the taco meat ingredients to your food processor and pulse until chopped, but still crumbly with lots of texture. Do not overprocess. Taste for salt and pepper, and add some if needed."],[null,"Transfer the \"meat\" to a large mixing bowl and add all the remaining salad ingredients to the same bowl. Mix well."],[null,"Choose a salad dressing from the options listed above, or anything else you'd prefer. If you plan to have leftovers, I recommend serving the dressing on each bowl, rather than mixing it into the salad, so you can store them separately to prevent sogginess."]],"h":[[null,"Do not overprocess the taco meat. You don’t want it blended, so pulse until crumbled and keep lots of texture for best results."],[null,"Store the salad and your dressing of your choice separately to keep the salad from getting soggy."],[null,"Leftovers will keep in the fridge for 3-4 days. The nutritional information includes the taco meat and the salad ingredients without the dressing or additional optional toppings. The nutritional information for the dressing will vary according to what you choose. You will find that nutritional information below each dressing recipe."]]},"9416487":{"s":[[null,"Add everything to the bowl of a food processor and process until smooth, scraping down the sides as needed."],[null,"Refrigerate for one hour or longer to chill and thicken."]],"h":[[null,"Make sure to drain and pat your tofu dry to avoid excess liquid in your tofu cream cheese. You want a thick spread to truly resemble the real deal. Use a food processor rather than a blender. It will be harder to blend smoothly in a blender due to limited liquid ingredients. Plus it’s more difficult to transfer thick spreads from a blender, where there is less space between the blades. Refrigerate for at least one hour before using . This will help it firm up and thicken. Storage Refrigerate your tofu cream cheese in a sealed container or glass jar for 5-7 days."],[null,"To keep longer , separate into smaller portions and freeze all but one in air-tight freezer-safe containers for up to 3 months. Keep 1 in the fridge for immediate use. Thaw the remaining portions as needed."]]},"9014896":{"s":[[null,"Melt the butter, if using, in a large pot and add the chopped onion, celery and garlic. Sauté, stirring often, until softened and the onions are translucent, about 5 minutes."],[null,"Add the smoked paprika and the salt and mix well. Lower the heat and add a splash of water and the flour and stir constantly for about 30 seconds or so."],[null,"Now add your chopped tomatoes to the pot and cook them, stirring often for 1-2 minutes. Then pour in your broth, the bay leaves, and the parsley. Mix well and bring to a medium boil, cooking for about 20-25 minutes, stirring occasionally."],[null,"Remove from the heat and remove and discard the bay leaves. Add the tofu and using an immersion blender, puree your tomato soup. Once smooth, taste and adjust for salt and pepper, if needed."],[null,"Serve garnished with fresh basil and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"For best results, let your cooked and pureed pot of soup rest for 10 minutes before serving. This quick rest time will thicken the soup a little more. If you don’t have a stick blender or immersion blender , you may carefully transfer the soup, in batches, to a stand blender. Use extreme caution when blending hot liquids, don’t fill the blender to the top, and work in as many batches as needed. Make it oil free by skipping the butter and using water or broth to sauté instead. Add more as needed, to prevent sticking. For a soy free version , skip the tofu and use 1.5 cups of cashew cream to stir in at the end. Keep in mind, this will increase the fat content. OR – Use a 15 oz can of drained and rinsed white cannellini beans if avoiding both soy and nuts. Tofu blocks vary in size, and I’m using a 454g block of medium/firm tofu this time, but anything from 350 to 454g will be fine for this recipe. Leftovers keep refrigerated for up to 3 days, or you may freeze for 2-3 months."]]},"9635144":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 400 degrees F (205 degrees C) and line two large baking sheets with parchment paper."],[null,"Stack the corn tortillas in an even pile on a cutting board. Then use a pizza cutter to slice them into four quarters. (If using larger wraps, slice into six pieces instead.)"],[null,"Arrange the cut tortilla chips in an even layer on your baking sheets. Then brush each one with lime juice and evenly sprinkle with salt and garlic powder, if using."],[null,"Bake for 8-10 minutes, checking often towards the end of cooking. You want them golden brown and crispy, but not overly done."]],"h":[[null,"I’m using six-inch corn tortilla wraps and sliced each one into four quarters to make perfectly sized restaurant-style chips. If you’re using larger wraps , you may slice them into six pieces. Check on your tortilla chips often towards the end of cooking . The chips will go from perfectly done, to overdone quickly, so use your oven timer to set reminders."]]},"9141850":{"s":[[null,"Add the potatoes to a pot of generously salted water and bring it to a boil. Cook the potatoes until fork tender, approx. 10-15 minutes depending on the potato size."],[null,"Drain the water and transfer the potatoes to a cutting board, or another work surface. Once cool enough to handle, you may press the potatoes down using a potato masher, or the bottom of a cup, OR cut them in half lengthwise."],[null,"Preheat your waffle iron (grease it if needed) and then place the potatoes inside. Sprinkle them with the seasoning and press the lid down hard, to force the potatoes into a waffle shape. Cook them for 5-8 minutes, or until desired crispiness is reached. This will vary according to your waffle iron, and the size of your potatoes."],[null,"Serve them with green onions and dipping sauce of your choice."]],"h":[]},"9604269":{"s":[[null,"Using a kettle or small pot, boil a cup or two of fresh water. (Since some will evaporate.)"],[null,"Add all the ingredients using only 3/4 cup of the hot water to your blender and process until smooth and creamy. It will take about a minute or so for the walnuts to fully break down and become smooth. If needed, turn off your blender and start again until desired texture is reached. Taste for seasoning and adjust if necessary. If you like a thinner sauce, add an additional 1-2 tablespoons of water and re-blend."]],"h":[[null,"No need to soak the walnuts if you’ve got a powerful blender. If not, soak them for 30 minutes in hot water and then drain before adding to your blender. If you’re not using a powerful blender , turn it off, wait 30 seconds and start again until your walnut cheese is smooth. (This will help prevent overheating in a less powerful blender.) Add 1-2 tablespoons of additional hot water , as needed to reach desired consistency, if you prefer a thinner sauce. Change it up ! If you’d like to switch up the flavours, sub the onion powder for garlic powder, paprika, smoked paprika, or any other spices you’d like. (Keep in mind darker seasoning will change the colour of your walnut cheese sauce.) Leftovers keep in a sealed container in the fridge for 3 days. Reheat before serving."]]},"9964071":{"s":[[null,"Mash the bananas in a large mixing bowl. Then add the peanut butter and maple syrup and mix well. Next, add the dry ingredients and mix until combined. The batter will be thick."],[null,"Stir in the shredded zucchini to the same bowl and set aside to let the batter rest for 10 minutes."],[null,"Preheat your oven to 350℉/176℃ and line a large baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Then scoop the batter onto your tray and shape and flatten the cookies, as they won't spread much in the oven."],[null,"Bake for 18-22 minutes until golden brown. Then remove them from the oven, and let them cool for 5-10 minutes to set."]],"h":[[null,"For picky eaters , peel the zucchini before shredding it to hide its bright green skin. Squeeze the shredded zucchini over a bowl or your kitchen sink before adding to your batter. The batter will be thick but the zucchini will add moisture to the cookies. For nut-free use soy butter or sunflower butter instead of peanut butter. Leftover cookies will keep at room temperature for 2 days, or refrigerated for up to 6 days. Freeze them airtight for up to 3 months AFTER cooling to room temperature first."]]},"9320396":{"s":[[null,"Spiralize your zucchini using a spiralizer. Place the noodles in a colander that sits in a large bowl and generously sprinkle the zucchini with salt. Toss them with your hands and set aside for 30 minutes or longer. (If working ahead, you may do this step several hours before cooking.)"],[null,"Meanwhile, add the walnuts and sundried tomatoes to your food processor and pulse until crumbly but don't overprocess. Keep it chunky. Transfer to a deep skillet."],[null,"Work in small batches and process the cauliflower and mushrooms next. Again, you want to keep the texture crumbly and not overprocessed. Transfer to the same pan as the walnut mixture and add all the seasoning."],[null,"Mix well and sauté for 5-7 minutes until the veggies are softened and reduced. Then pour in the tomato sauce and simmer for 10-15 minutes."],[null,"Lastly, gently heat the zucchini noodles in a pan for 1-2 minutes. Do NOT cook or they will get too soft. Just warm them up. Then serve with the bolognese sauce."]],"h":[[null,"Do not overprocess the veggies . The sauce tastes best with texture."],[null,"If you have some stubborn large pieces while processing the veggies , add those to the next batch, rather than continuing to process, so you don’t overprocess the rest."],[null,"Do NOT overcook your zucchini noodles . They taste best with a little bite to them."],[null,"Transfer your zoodles to bowls immediately after warming them . Don’t let them sit too long in the hot pan, or they may get too soft"],[null,"For nut-free , use pumpkin seeds/pepitas or sunflower seeds."],[null,"For oil-free , use sundried tomatoes that come in a vacuum-sealed bag, not jarred."],[null,"Store the leftover sauce and zoodles in separate containers to prevent sogginess for up to 3 days."]]},"9969110":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F (190 degrees C). Then grab a large baking sheet and line it with paper towels or a clean dishtowel."],[null,"Slice the zucchini lengthwise into 1/8 inch thick slices. Arrange the slices in a single layer on your baking sheet and sprinkle generously with salt. Set aside and let rest for 15 minutes. (The salt will soften the zucchini, release excess moisture and make them pliable for rolling.)"],[null,"Meanwhile, prepare your cheese by adding all the vegan ricotta ingredients to your food processor. Blend until smooth and set aside."],[null,"Now, combine the sauce ingredients in a small bowl and set aside."],[null,"By now, your zucchini should be ready for rolling. Pat the slices dry to remove the excess moisture. Then spread 1 cup of the prepared tomato sauce on the bottom of a baking dish or 10-inch cast iron pan. (Or another oven safe dish.)"],[null,"Add approx. one teaspoon of the ricotta mixture to a zucchini slice, and then starting at the bottom, roll it up. Place it in your baking dish, standing upright, on top of the tomato sauce layer. Repeat with remaining slices. Then top the zucchini roll ups with the remaining sauce, and sprinkle with vegan parm, if using."],[null,"Cover with a lid, or parchment paper, followed by aluminum foil, and bake for 20-25 minutes, until the zucchini are tender, but not overcooked. Remove from the oven and serve."]],"h":[[null,"If you don’t have a high-speed blender , soak your cashews in boiling hot water for 30 minutes, and then drain, before processing. Do not skip salting the zucchini . The step is what makes your zucchini soft enough for rolling while releasing excess moisture. Leftovers keep refrigerated for 2-3 days or frozen for up to 3 months."]]},"9627100":{"s":[[null,"Add all the ingredients to a soup pot, cover it with its lid, and bring it to a boil over high heat. Then reduce the heat to maintain a low boil and cook for 10-12 minutes until the potatoes are fork tender."],[null,"Use an immersion blender to puree your soup, or carefully transfer it to a stand blender and puree it in batches until smooth."]],"h":[[null,"Don't stress over uniform-sized veggie pieces . Since you'll be pureeing the soup, you don't need even sizes. This will save you time on prep."],[null,"Use an immersion blender to puree for less mess, ease, and fewer dishes to wash."],[null,"If you don't have an immersion blender , use extreme caution when blending hot liquids. Don't overfill your blender, and work in batches to prevent spills."],[null,"Taste for salt and pepper once cooked , and add more, if needed. Depending on the broth you're using, you may want more salt."],[null,"Store leftovers in the refrigerator for 3-4 days, or in the freezer airtight for up to 3 months."]]},"7449009":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a non-stick pan. Add the garlic, cumin, ginger and chilli powder, fry for 2 minutes until the spices are fragrant."],[null,"Add the vegetables to the pan and continue to fry for 2-3 minutes."],[null,"Pour over the stock and add the chickpeas, apricots and tomatoes, bring to the boil and simmer for 10-12 minutes, until the vegetables are just tender."],[null,"Stir in the harissa paste and season with plenty of black pepper."],[null,"Serve the vegetables over freshly prepared couscous, sprinkle with coriander and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Serve with couscous, rice or flat bread and plenty of salad."],[null,"If you don’t have harissa paste, you could use a little more chilli and/or garlic plus half tsp dried mint and a good squeeze of lemon."],[null,"In place of apricots, you could use raisins or sultanas."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat thoroughly until piping-hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"6041604":{"s":[[null,"Lay out the slices of whole grain or whole wheat bread."],[null,"Spread a generous layer of hummus on each slice."],[null,"Divide the mixed salad greens evenly and place them on two slices of bread."],[null,"Top the greens with cucumber slices, bell pepper slices, tomato slices, red onion slices, and Kalamata olives."],[null,"Drizzle extra virgin olive oil over the vegetable layers. Season with black pepper."],[null,"Place the remaining slices of bread, hummus-side down, on top of the vegetables to form sandwiches. Press down gently to secure the layers."]],"h":[]},"9898504":{"s":[[null,"Peel and quarter your onion and peel your carrots. Add them to a food processor and process until finely chopped. If you do not have a food processor, you may finely chop by hand. Then transfer them to a large pot."],[null,"Add all remaining ingredients except the spinach to the same pot and bring to a boil over high heat. Then lower the heat to medium-low and simmer with the lid on, but slightly askew for 30-40 minutes until the barley and beans are tender."],[null,"Turn off the heat and stir in the spinach. The spinach will wilt quickly and then serve."]],"h":[[null,"To soak your beans overnight , cover them with cool water two inches above the beans to allow room for them to grow. Drain when ready to use. If you did not soak the beans overnight , boil some water in a pot or kettle and cover the beans with the boiling hot water for 30 minutes. Then drain and use as directed. To make the soup gluten free , you may use brown rice instead of barley. Leftovers keep refrigerated for 3-4 days or freeze them airtight for up to 3 months."]]},"9518240":{"s":[[null,"Add all the ingredients to a small blender or food processor and blitz until a powder like consistency is reached, approx 20 seconds."],[null,"Store in a clean jar or sealed container in your pantry."],[null,"To make broth, combine 1 teaspoon of soup mix with 1 cup of hot water."]],"h":[[null,"For a low sodium vegetable bouillon powder , use 1 tablespoon of salt for 50% reduced sodium or use a half tablespoon of salt to reduce the sodium by 75%. Double, triple, quadruple the recipe as desired. I like to make a big batch at a time to always have some on hand ready to go for soups, casseroles, veggies, and more. Store your mix in a CLEAN and DRY jar or container. Store in a cool dark place, like your pantry, or if you live in a humid climate, you may store in the refrigerator to maintain freshness. Use your soup mix powder to replace veggie broth in any recipe . Just combine 1 teaspoon of your mixture with 1 cup of hot water for every cup called for. If you skip blending into a powder and mix the seasoning in a bowl, you'll need about a tablespoon of soup mix for every cup of hot water. When blended, the spices are more condensed, and 1 teaspoon to every cup of water works well. Use more or less to your taste. Also, make sure to omit the bay leaf if you choose to skip the blending. For a \"chicken\" broth version , add 1 teaspoon of poultry seasoning. Or ½ teaspoon of sage, and ¼ teaspoon each of thyme and rosemary."]]},"6563395":{"s":[[null,"Heat oil in a large skillet over medium heat."],[null,"Add diced onions and potatoes and cook until the onions are softened."],[null,"Stir in diced bell pepper and zucchini and season with black pepper and ¼ teaspoon salt. Cook for 5–7 minutes until vegetables are tender."],[null,"Add cherry tomatoes, minced garlic, smoked paprika, cumin, ¼ teaspoon salt, and pepper. Cook for an additional 3–5 minutes, allowing tomatoes to soften."],[null,"Create four wells in the vegetable mixture."],[null,"Crack one egg into each well. Season with ¼ teaspoon salt and black pepper."],[null,"Cover the skillet and cook for 5–7 minutes or until the eggs are cooked to your liking."]],"h":[]},"7854824":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a large pan, add the onions and cook 5–8 minutes until they start to brown."],[null,"Add the red pepper, carrots, courgette and mushrooms, and cook a further 10 minutes."],[null,"Next, add the chilli powder, cumin, oregano and tomatoes. Mix well, then cook for a further 10 minutes, stirring regularly."],[null,"Add the lentils and beans with their water and ketchup. Mix well and bring to a gentle bubble. Add a lid and simmer gently for 30 minutes, stirring regularly."]],"h":[[null,"Keep in the fridge for up to three days or freeze."],[null,"Be careful with chilli – you can always add more but you can't take it out! Add a little and allow time for the heat to infuse, taste it and only add more if you need to. If sharing with friends, make it mild and serve with some chilli sauce or flakes on the side, so people can spice it up if they want to."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat thoroughly until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"7943784":{"s":[[null,"Cook the noodles according to the packet instructions, usually around 2-4 minutes. Drain in a colander, rinse in cold water to stop them cooking and set aside."],[null,"Heat the oil in a wok or large frying pan, add the onion and red pepper and stir-fry for 2-3 minutes. Add the mushrooms, garlic and chilli flakes, if using, and stir for another minute."],[null,"Add the baby corn, spring onions, Chinese five-spice powder and pak choi and continue stirring for another 2-3 minutes."],[null,"Add the tomatoes and the noodles and mix well for 1-2 minutes until the noodles are hot."],[null,"Mix in the beansprouts and soy sauce, cook for another minute and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Use rice noodles for a gluten-free version."],[null,"Cut the spring onions at an angle for a more interesting shape."],[null,"When making stir-fries prep all your ingredients first and have everything ready to throw into the wok."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"3665":{"s":[[null,"Thaw and chop green beans. Grate carrots, cabbage and cilantro."],[null,"Soaked bread slices in water and drained by squeezing between the palms of your hands."],[null,"In a medium pan cover cabbage and carrots with water and boil for 10 minutes. Add the chopped green beans and cook until completely done. Drain excess water and cool."],[null,"Add spices, flour, bread slices, cilantro and lime juice to vegetables and mix well."],[null,"Make 12 balls and flatten each into a patty the size of a small burger."],[null,"Heat a saucepan over medium heat. Add the oil and place patties in the saucepan, two or three at a time without crowding. Flip patties over when cooked, about 2-3 minutes on each side."],[null,"Serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"Serving suggestions: Serve on a bun with mayonnaise, lettuce and onion or serve without bread and top with Cilantro Chutney or your favorite dipping sauce."],[null,"Freeze or refrigerate leftover cutlets for a quick meal or snack later."]]},"7032450":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4. Boil the sweet potato slices for 7-10 minutes until just tender. Drain and set aside."],[null,"Grill the aubergine slices for 4 minutes on each side and set aside."],[null,"Add the oil to a pan and add the onions. When they start to brown, add the peppers, courgettes and carrots. Cook for 5 minutes."],[null,"Add the garlic, lentils, tomatoes, oregano and thyme. Bring to the boil, turn down the heat, cover and simmer for 5 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, to make the topping mix the yogurt, Cheddar and cinnamon together."],[null,"In an ovenproof dish, place a layer of aubergine, add a spoonful of the lentil and tomato mixture, followed by a layer of sweet potato. Top with more of the lentil and tomato mixture, and layer alternately, finishing with the aubergine."],[null,"Spoon the yogurt mixture over the top and bake for 15 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"You could make individual moussaka in ovenproof dishes to serve direct to the table."],[null,"For the best flavour, allow to stand for 5-10 minutes before serving."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat thoroughly until piping-hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"4541672":{"s":[[null,"In a mug, whisk together eggs and milk."],[null,"Add onion, red pepper, cheese, spinach and basil. Mix to combine."],[null,"Place mug in a microwave and cook for 1 ½ to 2 minutes until egg is thoroughly cooked."],[null,"Serve immediately."]],"h":[[null,"Cooking times may vary based on microwave. It is recommended to stir the egg mixture after 1 minute of cooking."],["Breakfast: high-protein, low-potassium options","A healthy diet is an important part of your treatment for chronic kidney disease. As your kidneys fail, the amount of energy your body needs increases. Starting the day with a healthy breakfast can help provide nutrients your body needs. A good morning choice should include protein, but be low in salt, phosphorus and potassium. Plan ahead to ensure you have the right ingredients at home and try some of the following ideas for a nutrient-dense breakfast. Shakes: Start with a kidney-friendly oral nutritional supplement and blend with lower-potassium fruits such as blueberries, pineapple, or raspberries to create a delicious flavor. Breakfast Casseroles: Eggs are high in protein and a good breakfast choice. Limit additions of sausage and milk to lower salt and potassium intake. Improve egg flavor by adding small amounts of lower-potassium vegetables like onions, red peppers, and kale. Protein Bars: When eating on the road, a quick and portable breakfast is necessary. Protein bars can be eaten as part of your kidney diet. Pay attention to the nutrition facts label and ingredient list to avoid high-potassium selections. Ask your dietitian for recommendations."]]},"1838":{"s":[[null,"Chop bell pepper, zucchini and onion."],[null,"Prepare white rice according to instructions to make 4 cups."],[null,"Fill a 2-quart saucepan with enough water to cover asparagus and broccoli. Boil water and cook asparagus and broccoli for about 4 minutes or until crisp-tender; drain."],[null,"Heat oil in 10” skillet over medium-heat. Cook asparagus, broccoli, bell pepper, zucchini and onion in oil about 5 minutes, stirring occasionally until onion is crisp-tender."],[null,"Stir in remaining ingredients. Cook about 5 minutes, stirring frequently, until hot."]],"h":[[null,"If you are on a low potassium diet reduce portion to 3/4 cup ."],[null,"Portion leftovers into individual servings, place in freezer zip-top bags and freeze. Reheat in the microwave for a quick side dish later."],[null,"Substitute 1/4 teaspoon ground turmeric for saffron if desired."]]},"7492878":{"s":[[null,"Prepare all the vegetables. (When preparing the onion, peel and carefully trim only the ends, as leaving the root intact holds the wedges together.)"],[null,"In a dish, stir together all of the ingredients for the dip together and place in the fridge."],[null,"Mix together the gram flour, all the spices, chilli and bicarbonate of soda in a bowl, and then mix in the water. The batter should be the consistency of thick cream."],[null,"Heat the oil in a saucepan to 180°C. If you don’t have a thermometer, then test the oil with a small blob of batter. (If the oil is hot enough, the batter should start frying straight away and float to the top.)"],[null,"Add the vegetables to the batter and mix them around so they’re all coated. Pick them out with a spoon and carefully drop into the hot oil – a few at a time. Cook the pakoras for 3–4 minutes."],[null,"When golden brown, remove the pakoras with a slotted spoon and place on kitchen paper to drain. Repeat until all of the pakoras are cooked. Serve with the dip."]],"h":[[null,"Due to the fact that the pakoras are fried, they are meant as an occasional treat."],[null,"To make sure that the pakoras are not too fatty, the oil needs to be hot enough – in this case, 180ºC. This way, the cooking time will be less and the vegetables won’t be in the oil for very long. Using a cook’s thermometer is a good way of making sure the oil is at the right temperature."],[null,"It’s possible to use a recipe for baked pakoras to reduce the amount of fat, but you need bigger pieces of vegetable chunks and a thicker batter. This way, the pakoras will hold together better."],[null,"Make sure you use the right type of oil – and avoid ghee or dripping. Use rapeseed oil, as it’s better for the cooking process and is an unsaturated fat. Olive oil isn’t suited to frying."],[null,"You could use most vegetables in this batter – try broccoli, aubergine, carrot sticks, spring onions, asparagus, baby corn or mushrooms."]]},"2072":{"s":[[null,"In a bowl, wash rice under cold water and pour the water out. Repeat twice. Set aside."],[null,"Heat a large pan over high heat and add oil, cardamom, cinnamon and cloves."],[null,"Once the spices begin to change color, add uncooked rice and frozen vegetables to the pan. Stir rice, vegetables and spices together for about 2 minutes."],[null,"Add warm water to the pan. Stir in chili, ginger and salt."],[null,"When water starts to boil, turn the heat down to low and cover the pan. Cook 20 minutes or until rice is soft and fluffy."],[null,"Remove from heat and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Choose mixed vegetables with corn, green beans, peas, carrots."]]},"7066965":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200oC/ gas 6. Add the olive oil to the pan with the onion and cook for 2 minutes. Next, add the peppers and mushrooms, and stir regularly for 7–8 minutes, making sure they are evenly cooked."],[null,"Add the basil, oregano, garlic, a grind of black pepper, the sun-dried and fresh tomatoes. Mix well, bring to the boil, then turn down the heat, put a lid on and simmer gently for 5 minutes."],[null,"Place the naan breads onto a baking tray and spread the vegetables and mozzarella cheese evenly over the top. Bake in the oven for around 8–10 minutes (until the cheese has melted and the edges of the naan are lightly browned)."],[null,"Sprinkle with fresh basil leaves and black pepper before serving."]],"h":[[null,"By cooking your vegetables first, you can get far more onto your pizza. This makes for a healthier and tastier meal."],[null,"You can keep a couple of naan breads in the freezer and use different combinations of vegetables - even leftovers. If you don't have reduced-fat mozzarella, a reduced-fat Cheddar cheese works well."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Freeze in greaseproof paper. Defrost for 1 hour then bake as normal."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"6679419":{"s":[[null,"Coat large nonstick skillet with nonstick cooking spray and set over medium-high heat until hot. Reduce heat to medium-low and sauté onion until very soft and golden, about 20 minutes. Add the balsamic vinegar and sauté for another 5 minutes. Transfer to plate."],[null,"Preheat oven to 400°F. Mix flour, thyme, and 1/4 teaspoon salt in a large bowl. Stir in water and oil, just until a soft dough forms. Lightly sprinkle work surface with flour and roll out dough with a rolling pin into a 16 × 10-inch rectangle or 13-inch round. Fold in half and transfer to 12 × 6-inch tart pan or 9-inch round tart pan with removable bottom. Trim the edges. Spread the Dijon mustard evenly over the bottom of the tart with the back of a spoon."],[null,"Lightly coat skillet again with nonstick cooking spray and set over medium heat. Add zucchini to the skillet with 1/4 teaspoon black pepper and sauté until golden, 5–7 minutes."],[null,"Arrange a layer of tomatoes, followed by the zucchini, another layer of the remaining tomatoes, and the onion, overlapping them slightly on the bottom of the tart. Sprinkle with remaining 1/4 teaspoon salt, 1/4 teaspoon black pepper, and the Parmesan cheese. Bake for about 20 minutes until tart is a lightly golden brown. Remove from the oven and sprinkle the top with the basil and return to the oven for 3 more minutes. Let the tart cool for 5 minutes, then slice into wedges and serve."]],"h":[]},"7106956":{"s":[[null,"Put the oil in a pan and gently cook the onion until well browned, stirring regularly."],[null,"Add the diced pepper, carrot, courgette and mushrooms to the pan continue cooking gently for 5 minutes, stirring regularly."],[null,"Add the garlic and oregano. Stir for 1 minute, add the stock and the fresh and canned tomatoes, black pepper and tomato purée."],[null,"Boil a saucepan of water and cook the pasta according to the packet instructions."],[null,"Bring to a gentle simmer, cover and cook for 15 minutes, stirring occasionally, and add a little water if it starts to stick."],[null,"Finally, add the lentils, simmer for a further 5 minutes, and serve with the pasta."]],"h":[[null,"The secret to this dish is dicing all the vegetables really finely, so they’re the same size so they will coat your pasta evenly."],[null,"For a gluten free alternative this sauce is ideal served with polenta or baked sweet potatoes."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat thoroughly until piping-hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"5919422":{"s":[[null,"If using peas: Put the peas into a pan of water and boil for 5 minutes, then drain. If using broccoli: Remove the chunky stem and discard. Chop the florets evenly and boil in a pan of water for 5 minutes and drain. If using courgette: Cut the ends off the courgette and throw them away. Slice the courgette, boil in a pan of water for 5 minutes and drain."],[null,"Heat the oil in a large saucepan and add the onion and garlic, cook over a medium heat for 5 minutes, or until the onion is soft."],[null,"Take the pan off the heat and add the rice, stirring until the rice is coated with the oil."],[null,"In a jug, add 850ml boiling water to the stock cube and stir until dissolved."],[null,"Using a ladle, add one scoop of the stock to the rice mixture, and put back on the heat. Gently stir the rice until nearly all the liquid has been absorbed. Each time the stock is absorbed, add another ladleful."],[null,"About 15 minutes after you added the first stock, stir in the precooked vegetables. Keep adding ladles of stock and stirring them in, until the rice is creamy and just tender."],[null,"Take the pan off the heat and cover it with a lid. Leave it for 3 minutes, then stir in the parsley, parmesan and 2 pinches of pepper."]],"h":[]},"5608712":{"s":[[null,"Heat oil in a pan and fry the onions, garlic and ginger until soft."],[null,"Once softened add in the cumin, garam masala and coriander, mix together for 2 minutes."],[null,"Then add in the carrots, cauliflower, peppers, and peas, stir together, and cook until soft. Set aside."],[null,"In a small bowl mix together the flour and water until a paste forms."],[null,"Place a small spoonful of the vegetable mixture onto 1 spring roll wrapper, Fold over the mixture and continue to fold in opposite directions until a triangle has formed."],[null,"Spread a small amount of the flour mixture at the opening of the triangle and press together to seal."],[null,"Heat enough oil in a pan to shallow fry (usually ¼ inch up the side of the pan). Test the temperature with a small amount of pastry, if it turns golden brown and bubbles, the oil is ready to fry."],[null,"Place the sambusa into the pan and cook on both sides until golden brown, remove from the pan and place onto kitchen paper."],[null,"Once slightly cooled serve and enjoy!"]],"h":[]},"7497836":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180°C/gas 4. Put the oil onto a baking sheet, add the vegetables and sprinkle with the cumin and pepper and toss together well so all the vegetables are coated."],[null,"Bake for 30-40 minutes, jumbling around a couple of times throughout to ensure even cooking."],[null,"Meanwhile, to make the satay sauce add the onion to a pan with the garlic, chilli and 150ml water and bring to the boil. Simmer 5 minutes until the onion is soft. Gradually stir in the cornflour and keep stirring until it thickens. Add the peanut butter, soy sauce and sweetener and blend until smooth."],[null,"For the salad, mix together the cucumber and spring onion, sprinkle with coriander and a squeeze of lime to serve."]],"h":[[null,"The nutritional analysis above includes a serving suggestion of salad."],[null,"You could cut the vegetables into smaller pieces, thread onto skewers and grill or BBQ to serve with the satay sauce and salad."],[null,"Works well with roasted root vegetables, eg pumpkin, fennel, beetroot. The satay sauce is great with chicken."],[null,"Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat thoroughly until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"2190":{"s":[[null,"Chop cashew nuts. Dice onion, carrot and tomato. Chop cilantro and jalapeno pepper. Grate ginger root."],[null,"Heat vegetable oil in a wok on the stove top over medium to high heat. When oil starts changing its color, add mustard seeds. When mustard seeds start to pop, turn the heat to medium low and add split chick peas (Chana dahl) and black beans (urad dahl). Stir the ingredients with a wooden spoon and add chopped cashew nuts. Fry until the peas and cashew nuts turn golden brown. Add cumin."],[null,"Add onion and saute to golden brown. Add tomatoes, carrots, peas, curry leaves, cilantro and ginger and cook until tomatoes soften."],[null,"Add cream of wheat and cook for 2-3 minutes."],[null,"Heat water to a boil. Add salt and stir in boiling water without forming lumps. Mixture becomes semi-solid consistency. Keep stirring until the water evaporates. Turn the heat to low and close the lid and cook for 3-4 minutes."],[null,"Turn the heat off. Sprinkle lemon juice and fluff with a fork. Divide into 2 portions and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Chana dahl, Urad dahl, mustard seeds, cumin and curry leaves are available at an Indian grocery store."],[null,"Upma is a well known breakfast dish in South India. In addition to semolina (farina, Cream of Wheat®), upma contains seasonings and vegetables."]]},"7346125":{"s":[[null,"Warm the tortilla in a dry frying pan for 1 minute each side (this makes it more pliable). Next, put it on a board and spread the hummus over the bottom left-hand quarter, leaving a 2cm-margin at the edges of the wrap."],[null,"Place the carrot, onion, yellow pepper, alfalfa and lettuce on top of the hummus."],[null,"Roll up the tortilla tightly from the bottom up, tucking in the sides when you get a third of the way up."],[null,"Wrap in greaseproof paper or foil and twist the ends."]],"h":[[null,"Wholemeal tortilla is higher in fibre and keeps you feeling fuller longer. Wholegrains are beneficial for heart and gut health."],[null,"Wholemeal tortillas are a handy store cupboard item. They make a good super-thin pizza base."],[null,"If you can't find alfalfa, you can use watercress, rocket or extra lettuce instead."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"6523355":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F. Coat an 8-inch baking pan with cooking spray. Set aside."],[null,"Mix all the ingredients in a large bowl. Pour into prepared baking pan. Cover and bake for 45 minutes. Uncover and bake an additional 30 to 40 minutes or until thickened."]],"h":[]},"6556196":{"s":[[null,"Heat olive oil in a non-stick skillet over medium heat. Add spinach and sauté until wilted (about 2 minutes)."],[null,"Whisk eggs with cumin and paprika, then pour into the skillet with spinach. Scramble until cooked through."],[null,"Assemble the bowl. Divide cooked quinoa, black beans, tomatoes, avocado, and scrambled eggs among 4 bowls."],[null,"Drizzle with lime juice."]],"h":[]},"4128883":{"s":[[null,"To prepare the rice, bring water to a boil. Add rice. Simmer covered for 15–20 minutes until water is absorbed. Remove from heat."],[null,"To prepare tofu, heat oil over medium heat in a non-stick frying pan. Add diced tofu and brown, approximately 2–3 minutes per side. Remove tofu from pan and set aside. Reserve pan with residual oil."],[null,"To prepare the miso sauce, add the miso paste, rice wine vinegar, water, honey, and sesame oil to a small mixing bowl. Whisk well to combine. Refrigerate."],[null,"To prepare the stir fry, place the same non-stick frying pan over high heat, add celery, mushrooms, red peppers, bean sprouts, ginger and garlic. Sauté for 2–3 minutes until vegetables are tender crisp."],[null,"Add miso sauce and tofu. Simmer for 2–3 minutes until sauce reduces and stir fry is heated through."],[null,"Serve immediately on a bed of rice."]],"h":[[null,"* Miso should be used sparingly to add a burst of flavor to recipes because it is high in sodium. Compare labels and choose the lowest sodium miso available at your store. This recipe used a miso product with 140mg sodium per teaspoon."],[null,"Create your own chop suey recipes by trying different vegetable/protein combinations with our miso sauce."],["Asian take-out: what is kidney-friendly?","Eating away from home can be a challenge for those who have chronic kidney disease as there can easily be too much sodium, potassium and/or phosphorus added to the foods. When you’re busy or you just don’t feel like cooking, picking up a meal may be the solution. A common type of take-out food is Asian cuisine. Consider the following to make Asian dishes kidney-friendly: • Choose a restaurant where you know the menu and where foods can be prepared specifically for you. • Ask about ingredients in unfamiliar dishes so you know if they fit into your diet. • Ask for food to be cooked without soy sauce, fish sauce or monosodium glutamate (MSG). Most sauces are quite high in sodium so request that they be provided on the side. Use little of these or none at all. Do not add soy sauce. • Choose lower-potassium vegetables, such as asparagus, green beans, cabbage, carrots, onions or snow peas. • Order steamed white rice."]]},"2799":{"s":[[null,"Mince garlic and ginger root. Slice carrots. Dice yellow onion and tofu. Chop cilantro and green onions."],[null,"Beat eggs then sauté in a skillet like an omelet. Chop cooked eggs into pieces and set aside."],[null,"Heat oil in skillet over moderate heat. Stir in garlic, ginger, carrots, yellow onion, tofu, peas, and dry mustard."],[null,"When carrots are softened, add rice, chopped eggs and soy sauce. Mix, and turn off heat."],[null,"Stir in cilantro and green onions."]],"h":[[null,"Basmati rice has a better glycemic profile than other types of white rice. It is also lower in phosphorus than brown rice."],[null,"To reduce cholesterol you can use 1-1/2 cups low-cholesterol egg substitute to replace the 6 eggs."]]},"2001":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400° F. Set the vegetarian crumbles out to thaw."],[null,"Slice the spinach leaves. Dice the carrots and vegetarian chik’n strips. Mince the onion."],[null,"Place the thawed vegetarian crumbles on a clean dish towel, cover and press to remove extra liquid."],[null,"In a medium bowl add drained crumbles, beaten eggs, bread crumbs, cheese, basil and onion. Combine thoroughly."],[null,"Roll mixture into approximately 50 to 60 small veggie meatballs and set on a greased baking sheet. Bake for approximately 15 minutes, or until cooked through. Remove the veggie meatballs from the oven to cool."],[null,"In a large stockpot heat the vegetable broth to boiling. Stir in the spinach, carrots, pasta and veggie meatballs. Return to a boil; reduce heat to medium."],[null,"Cook at a slow boil for 10 minutes or until pasta is al dente. Stir frequently."],[null,"Add diced vegetarian chik’n to the soup. Heat thoroughly and serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"Chik’n and chick’n are terms used in vegetarian chicken substitute products. The primary ingredient is soy protein."]]},"6146820":{"s":[[null,"Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium heat. Sauté the onion until tender."],[null,"Stir in the veggie crumbles, water and Italian seasonings. Cover and cook until crumbles are cooked through, about 4 minutes."],[null,"Pour 2-1/2 cups vegetable broth into the mixture and bring to a boil. Add pasta and cook, stirring occasionally, over medium high heat until broth is absorbed, about 10 to 12 minutes."],[null,"Add remaining broth, kale and chili flakes and cook over medium heat until pasta is done, about 14 minutes."],[null,"Remove the pan from the heat and stir in the Greek yogurt. Serve hot."]],"h":[]},"7716059":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200°C/400°F/gas 6. To make the tomato sauce, heat the oil in a large saucepan and sauté the onions, garlic and tomato purée over a medium heat, stirring, for a couple of minutes."],[null,"Add the tomatoes, rinsing out the tins with a little extra water to stir through the sauce. Simmer for 20 minutes."],[null,"Discard the thick stem from the cabbage and roughly chop the leaves. Add to the sauce along with the basil and simmer for 5 minutes, then fold in the lentils and crème fraiche, and take off the heat."],[null,"Scoop a thin layer of the tomato sauce into the bottom of a 20cm x 30cm baking tray."],[null,"Add a layer of lasagne sheets, then a layer of tomato sauce and a sprinkling of grated cheese. Continue with lasagne sheets and repeat the layers until you run out of sheets and sauce. There should be a final layer of sauce with cheese on top."],[null,"Place in the oven and bake for 30 to 40 minutes, or until the lasagne is golden and the sheets are soft. Serve with a large salad."]],"h":[[null,"For lower-carb version of this dish, use sliced aubergines in place of the lasagne sheets."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"6675774":{"s":[[null,"Heat olive oil in a pot. Sauté onion until golden brown."],[null,"Add cumin seeds, bay leaf, cloves, turmeric, and chili powder. Stir for 1 minute. Add the rice and lentils, stir to coat in the seasoning."],[null,"Pour in vegetable broth, cover, and simmer for 25–30 minutes until rice and lentils are cooked."],[null,"Garnish with cilantro."],[null,"Serve with 1/2 cup steamed green beans"],[null,"Optional step: We recommend serving with a cucumber raita, which is not included in the nutritional analysis of this recipe."]],"h":[]},"6658081":{"s":[[null,"Heat olive oil in a pot. Sauté onions, garlic, and ginger until fragrant."],[null,"Add coriander, turmeric, chili powder, and garam masala. Stir for 1 minute."],[null,"Add cauliflower, carrots, and peas. Cook for 5 minutes."],[null,"Stir in yogurt and vegetable broth. Simmer for 10–15 minutes until vegetables are tender."],[null,"Optional step: Serve with 1/2 cup cooked brown rice or whole grain roti. The grams of carbohydrate will need to be added to the total carbs of the meal."]],"h":[]},"3483":{"s":[[null,"Dice onion; chop bell pepper."],[null,"Prepare Easy Pizza Dough and Red Pepper Tomato Sauce recipes."],[null,"Preheat oven to 425º F."],[null,"Shape pizza dough to make two flat 12″ pizza crusts."],[null,"Spread 1/2 cup Roasted Red Pepper Tomato Sauce over each pizza."],[null,"Top with red onion, mushrooms, bell pepper and pineapple."],[null,"Sprinkle mozzarella and Parmesan cheeses on top."],[null,"Bake for12 to 16 minutes until bubbly and browned."]],"h":[[null,"Red pepper tomato sauce and pizza dough can be made in advance and refrigerated or frozen until the day pizza is prepared."],[null,"To form 12″ pizza, turn a medium-sized bowl upside down and dust with flour. Gently stretch dough evenly over outside of the bowl; turn and place on pizza pan."],[null,"Makes two 12″ pizzas."]]},"2168905":{"s":[[null,"Mix all ingredients together, minus the toppings, leave for one hour."],[null,"Then cut the dough into 3 balls and roll the dough thin."],[null,"Chop tomato and green pepper. Spread sauce evenly across dough"],[null,"1 tablespoon of pizza sauce, then put on tomato, green pepper and mozzarella evenly on each pizza."],[null,"Place in the oven for 10 minutes at 180˚C."]],"h":[[null,"Portions: 3 Serving Size: 1 pizza"]]},"6793545":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F. Coat a 9x13-inch baking dish with cooking spray."],[null,"While the lentils are cooking, add the olive oil to a large sauté pan over medium-high heat. Add the mushrooms and sauté until cooked through and all the liquid is evaporated."],[null,"Add the onion, carrots, celery, green beans, and garlic, and sauté until the onions turn clear and the carrots start to soften."],[null,"Add one cup of the cooked lentils and any liquid into the vegetables and stir to combine. Reserve the remaining lentils. Pour 1 cup of the almond milk into the vegetables. Stir to combine. Add ½ teaspoon of salt (optional) and the pepper."],[null,"Pour the vegetable mixture into the 9x13-inch baking pan. Set aside."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine the remaining lentils with the rest of the almond milk, the remaining ½ teaspoon salt (optional), and parsley. Beat the mixture with an electric mixer until fluffy."],[null,"Spoon the lentils over the top of the lentil/vegetable mixture and gently spread to cover the entire top."],[null,"Cover with foil and bake for 45 minutes. Uncover and bake an additional 30 minutes or until the top starts to turn golden brown and the filling is bubbly."],[null,"Let the shepherd’s pie rest for 10 minutes out of the oven before serving."]],"h":[]},"7767641":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 200°C/ gas 6. For the topping, peel and roughly chop the sweet potatoes and add to a pan of boiling water, cooking for about 15–20 minutes, until soft."],[null,"Drain, then season with pepper, and beat in the mustard and milk with a wooden spoon until the mash is smooth and creamy."],[null,"To make the filling, add the oil to a pan, throw in the onion and cook for 5 minutes, stirring regularly."],[null,"Add the carrot and mushrooms and cook for a further 5 minutes until the onions are golden brown."],[null,"Now add the thyme, tomatoes, puy lentils, pepper, vegetable stock and soy sauce. Stir, then bring to a gentle boil, turn down the heat, cover and simmer gently for 5 minutes."],[null,"Put the lentil mixture into an ovenproof dish and top with the sweet potato."],[null,"Bake for 15-20 minutes until golden brown. Serve with green vegetables."]],"h":[[null,"It's easy to make this dish gluten free by using gluten-free soy sauce, or tamari, a gluten-free vegetable stock cube and a suitable mustard."],[null,"To get a crispy topping, use a fork to create lots of little peaks in the potato."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat thoroughly until piping hot throughout."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 3"]]},"6877159":{"s":[[null,"Cook the pasta according to the package directions. Drain."],[null,"In a large bowl, mix together the pasta, red bell pepper, cucumber, broccoli, carrots, and chicken."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the dressing ingredients. Pour the dressing over the pasta, vegetables, and chicken and mix well. Serve."]],"h":[]},"6200474":{"s":[[null,"Prepare pasta according to package instructions, omitting any added salt or fat. Preheat oven to 375°F."],[null,"Heat olive oil in a large skillet over medium heat. Add onion and saute for 4 minutes. Then add zucchini and red pepper and saute another 5-7 minutes or until veggies are cooked through."],[null,"While veggies are cooking, whisk together ricotta, egg, Parmesan, and pepper in a small bowl."],[null,"Add diced tomatoes to cooked veggie mixture and heat through. Stir in basil, pasta, and ricotta mixture."],[null,"Spray a 9x13-inch baking dish with cooking spray, pour in ziti mixture, and sprinkle mozzarella over the top. Bake for 25 minutes and serve immediately."]],"h":[]},"6158772":{"s":[[null,"Add olive oil to the skillet over medium heat. Add mushrooms and sauté until nicely brown at edges (about 3 minutes), set aside."],[null,"Beat eggs with egg whites or egg substitute in medium sized bowl, using a mixer or by hand, until blended."],[null,"Stir in shredded spinach, and scallions. You could also add fresh or dried herbs such as basil or parsley for more flavor."],[null,"Begin heating medium/large nonstick skillet over medium-low heat. Coat pan generously with cooking spray."],[null,"Pour in egg mixture and continue to scramble the mixture as it cooks using a spatula. When eggs are cooked to your liking, turn off the heat and stir in mushrooms."],[null,"Spread half of the egg mixture down the center of each tortilla. top each with 1 tablespoon fresh salsa or other sauce of your choice. Then roll it up to make a wrap."]],"h":[]},"7868675":{"s":[[null,"Heat a small frying pan and spray with 2 pumps of oil. Add ¼ of the beaten egg and tilt the pan so that the egg spreads to form a 15cm circle. Cook for 30 secs, carefully turn over and cook for a further 30 secs. Lift onto a plate and repeat to make 4 wraps in total."],[null,"Stir the chives and cheese together. Put the mushrooms on a plate, drizzle each with 1tsp vinegar, cover with clingfilm, pierce and microwave on full power for 2 mins. Thinly slice."],[null,"Spread the wraps with the cheese, arrange the mushrooms on top, scatter over the chopped tomatoes and onion, roll up loosely and serve. Delicious hot or cold."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"6081295":{"s":[[null,"Heat oil in a large soup pot over medium-high heat."],[null,"Add onion and carrots and sauté 5 minutes. Add green pepper and zucchini and sauté another 2 minutes."],[null,"Add garlic and sauté 30 seconds. Add chili powder and all remaining ingredients; bring to a boil."],[null,"Cover, reduce heat, and simmer 30-35 minutes or until the vegetables are tender."]],"h":[]},"7204791":{"s":[[null,"Spray a large, heavy-based, lidded, non-stick saucepan or flameproof casserole dish with a couple of pumps of cooking spray and put over a medium-low heat. Add the onion, celery and peppers. Cover and fry for 8-10 minutes until softened, stirring now and then (add a splash of water if the veg start to stick to the pan or dish)."],[null,"Add the garlic, paprika and cumin, and cook for 1 minute until fragrant. Stir in the tomatoes with 100ml water and bring to the boil. Lower the heat and simmer gently for 2-3 minutes until slightly thickened and reduced."],[null,"Stir in the mince and kidney beans, and simmer for a further 20 minutes until thick. Season with pepper."],[null,"Serve the chilli in bowls topped with the yoghurt. Add a twist of black pepper and the coriander, and serve with the lime wedges."]],"h":[[null,"You can use a plain yoghurt of your choice. However, this will change the nutritional information and the texture of the dish."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"2545":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 F."],[null,"Chop the onion, bell pepper and mushrooms."],[null,"In a small nonstick skillet heat the vegetarian crumbles with 2 tablespoons water and the Italian seasoning blend until hot and most of the water is evaporated."],[null,"Brush the bottom side or each pita with olive oil, then spread 1-1/2 tablespoons of pizza sauce on each pita."],[null,"Distribute the vegetables and vegetarian crumble evenly over both pitas."],[null,"Top each pita pizza with 1/4 cup of mozzarella cheese. Bake for 6-8 minutes until cheese is melted."]],"h":[[null,"Check labels on pitas and pizza sauce and select the lowest sodium brands."],[null,"Frozen vegetarian crumbles are a soy product that can be used as a replacement for ground beef. If desired you can substitute lean ground beef or turkey."],[null,"For a thin crust pizza open the pita and split into 2 round pieces. Carbohydrate is reduced to 22 grams."]]},"1982":{"s":[[null,"Chop the onion and kale."],[null,"In a large skillet heat the olive oil over medium heat. Sauté the onion until tender. Stir in the veggie crumbles, 1/3 cup water and Italian seasonings. Cover and cook until crumbles for 4 minutes."],[null,"Pour 2-1/2 cups chicken broth into the mixture and bring to a boil."],[null,"Add pasta and cook and stir over medium high heat until broth is absorbed, about 10 to 12 minutes. Add remaining broth, kale and chili flakes and cook over medium heat until pasta is done, about 14 minutes."],[null,"Remove skillet from heat and stir in Greek yogurt. Serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"This recipe was analyzed with Morningstar Farms® Grillers® Crumbles™. Soy protein products vary greatly in potassium content. Always check the label for potassium content if available."],[null,"Many soy-based vegetarian protein products contain a significant amount of sodium. To keep total sodium low try to use other low sodium ingredients in your recipes that include these products."],[null,"Use pasta of choice–whole wheat or refined, farfalle, fusilli, macaroni, orecchiette, rotini or shells."]]},"6378666":{"s":[[null,"In a medium bowl, combine buttermilk, yogurt, mayonnaise, parsley, dill, garlic powder, onion powder, salt, and pepper."],[null,"Pour 1/4 of the dip into a plastic or glass cocktail cup."],[null,"Arrange 1 cup of assorted vegetable sticks in the cup so all of them are touching the dip."],[null,"Repeat process for 3 more cups. If not serving immediately, store vegetable sticks separately and add to cups with dip before serving."]],"h":[]},"6633224":{"s":[[null,"Add the cooking spray and canola oil to a non-stick sauté pan over medium heat. Add the mushrooms, zucchini, and onion. Sauté until the mushrooms are dry and the onions turn clear, about 5-7 minutes. Stir in the bean sprouts. Sauté 2-3 more minutes. Set aside to cool."],[null,"In a medium bowl, whisk the egg substitute and egg together. Whisk in the flour and then stir in the vegetable mixture and salt (optional). Mix well."],[null,"Over medium-high heat, re-spray nonstick sauté pan with cooking spray and pour the batter by heaping 1/2 cup to form patties. Cook well on both sides until golden brown, about 4-5 minutes per side. Remove the patties from the pan and set aside."],[null,"In a small bowl, combine the cornstarch, low- or no-calorie sweetener, soy sauce, and chicken broth. Mix well. Add this mixture to the hot pan and bring to a boil; reduce heat and simmer 5 minutes to make a gravy."],[null,"Pour the gravy over patties and serve hot."]],"h":[]},"2838":{"s":[[null,"Grate ginger root. Cut snow peas into thirds and cut carrot into matchstick-size strips. Thinly slice scallions."],[null,"Combine soy sauce, sugar, vinegar and ginger in a small bowl; set aside."],[null,"Heat the oil in a large nonstick skillet or wok over medium-high heat."],[null,"Add the carrots and stir-fry for 2 minutes."],[null,"Add the snow peas, bean sprouts and 1 tablespoon of the soy sauce mixture. Stir-fry until the vegetable are almost tender but still crisp, about 2 minutes. Transfer to a bowl."],[null,"Return skillet to medium heat and add remaining sauce mixture, cooked rice and scallions."],[null,"Cook until warmed through, about 1 minute."],[null,"Lightly beat the eggs. Make a large space in the center of the rice and pour the eggs into it."],[null,"Scramble the eggs with a spatula until set."],[null,"Stir eggs into rice. Add vegetables and stir. Serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"Recipe works best with cooked rice that has been refrigerated."],[null,"For a higher protein meal add 2 cups of cooked chicken, shrimp or tofu."]]},"9727877":{"s":[[null,"Add the pumpkin seeds and sun dried tomatoes to the bowl of your food processor and pulse until crumbly, but do not over process. Set aside."],[null,"Shred all the remaining vegetables using a food processor or Veggie Bullet. Do not puree them! Transfer the shredded veggies to a deep, nonstick skillet."],[null,"Cook the veggies over medium high heat until reduced and cooked through, about 8 minutes. Stir often to prevent sticking. You won't need any oil or water since the veggies will produce their own liquid."],[null,"Add all the seasoning, pumpkin seeds and sun dried tomato mixture with the 1/3 cup of water and cook another 2-3 minutes, adding a little more water if needed to keep the mixture moist."],[null,"Serve your vegan meat crumbles as a taco salad, wrap it up in soft or crunchy shells or use lettuce wraps."]],"h":[[null,"Do not puree or over process the ingredients ! You want a crumble consistency of very finely chopped veggies, and not a pasty consistency. So a food processor or veggie bullet, using the shredder attachment works best. If using a food processor, work in smaller batches if needed, to avoid overly processing the ingredients. For picky eaters . If you need to hide the ingredients a little more from picky eaters, rather than process the sun dried tomatoes in the food processor, puree them separately in a blender along with all the seasoning and 1 cup of water. This makes a red sauce that you can pour over your veggie grounds and it will make the dish a more uniform colour of reddish brown, resembling ground meat or soy grounds. I made the veggie grounds this way when serving my nieces and nephews and they had no idea it was homemade! Seasoning! This recipe is generously seasoned and suits our family perfectly. However, feel free to adjust the seasoning to your preference. Leftover vegan crumble meat keeps refrigerated for up to 5 days. Just reheat and serve or enjoy cold. Optional toppings are not included in the nutritional information."]]},"6051058":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F."],[null,"In a large pot, heat the oil on medium heat. Add chopped onion, diced carrots, and diced celery. Sauté until the vegetables are softened, about 5 minutes."],[null,"Stir in tempeh and potato. Cook for an additional 3–4 minutes."],[null,"Sprinkle flour over the vegetable mixture and stir to coat evenly. Cook for 1–2 minutes to remove the raw taste of the flour."],[null,"Gradually pour in vegetable broth, stirring constantly to avoid lumps. Add dried thyme, pepper, and frozen peas. Bring the mixture to a simmer and cook until the sauce thickens, about 5 minutes."],[null,"Remove the pot from the heat and let the filling cool slightly."],[null,"Spoon the vegetable filling into a square baking dish."],[null,"Top filling with biscuits."],[null,"Bake in the preheated oven for 10–15 minutes until biscuits are golden brown. Cut into 4 pieces and serve."]],"h":[]},"6850173":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350°F. Spray 2 12-cup muffin tins with cooking spray."],[null,"Separate the egg whites from the egg yolks."],[null,"In a large bowl, beat the egg yolks and cottage cheese with a hand or stand mixer on medium high until creamy."],[null,"In another large bowl, beat the egg whites until stiff peaks form."],[null,"Mix the vegetables and spices into the egg yolk mixture and combine well."],[null,"Gently fold the egg whites into the egg yolk and vegetable mixture."],[null,"Using a scoop or large spoon, divide the egg mixture evenly between 18 of the muffin cups."],[null,"Place the tins in the preheated oven and bake for 25–30 minutes, until puffed and brown on the top."],[null,"Remove from the oven and cool for 5 minutes. Gently remove the muffins from the tins."]],"h":[]},"6698493":{"s":[[null,"In a medium bowl combine cabbage, carrots, cucumbers, 1/4 cup of the cilantro and green onion."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together peanut butter, soy sauce, vinegar, water, oil, pepper flakes, garlic, and remaining 2 tbsp cilantro."],[null,"Before using, soak spring roll skin in water for 10-15 seconds and shake off excess water. Place about 1/4 cup of vegetable mixture in the bottom of spring roll. Take the spring roll edge nearest to you and fold to cover the filling. Take the side edges and fold in tightly. Roll outward to seal. Repeat procedure for remaining 11 spring rolls."],[null,"Serve spring rolls with peanut sauce."]],"h":[]},"3227":{"s":[[null,"Cut bread into cubes. Place on a baking sheet and bake at 225° F for 15 minutes. Turn cubes over and continue baking 15 minutes or until dry and crisp."],[null,"Dice onion, mushrooms and bell pepper."],[null,"Melt butter in a small skillet and sauté onion, mushrooms and red peppers."],[null,"Grease a 9” square baking dish with nonstick cooking spray. Arrange half of the bread cubes in a single layer in the dish and sprinkle with half of the vegetable mixture. Arrange spinach leaves on top."],[null,"Form a second layer with remaining bread and vegetables on top."],[null,"Whisk together eggs, vinegar, half & half creamer, Worcestershire sauce, hot sauce and black pepper. Pour evenly over the bread."],[null,"Cover surface with plastic wrap and refrigerate at least 1 hour or overnight."],[null,"Allow strata to stand at room temperature for 20 minutes."],[null,"Pre-heat oven to 325° F. Remove plastic wrap and bake 50 minutes."],[null,"Remove from oven and sprinkle cheddar cheese over the top. Cook for an additional 10 minutes or until a knife inserted near the center comes out clean."],[null,"Cut into 9 servings and serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"Look for a rustic-style artisan white bread or a sourdough round loaf. Slice 1/2 inch thick. Compare breads and select the lower sodium choice."],[null,"Look for half and half without \"phos\" in the ingredient list, this would indicate a phosphate additive, which should be avoided."]]},"54930":{"s":[[null,"Roughly chop bell pepper and zucchini. Heat olive oil in skillet. Add chopped vegetables and heat for about 5 minutes. Add beans and cook and stir for about 5 to 8 minutes longer."],[null,"Spray a second pan with cooking spray and heat on medium. Slice the polenta into 8 slices and brown in the skillet. About 4 minutes per side."],[null,"To serve, place 2 slices of polenta on a plate and add approximately 3/4 cup of veggies on top. Tear apart, or cut up, fresh mozzarella, should be about 1 ounce per serving. Top with 1 tablespoon of dressing. Save the rest of the dressing for a salad or as a raw vegetable dip."]],"h":[[null,"The naturally occurring phosphorus in foods like fresh cheese are only partly absorbed by our bodies. Approximately 40-60%, each food and person is different."],[null,"Pre-cooked polenta usually comes in a 24-ounce tube. Use half for this recipe and save the rest for later use."],[null,"To make it more diabetes-friendly, you may cut back on the cheese to reduce the fat content."]]},"6935097":{"s":[[null,"Set your waffle iron to a low or medium setting and allow it to preheat. Lightly coat both the top and bottom plates with cooking spray."],[null,"Place the egg whites in a large bowl. Whisk vigorously until slightly frothy."],[null,"Add the shredded cheese, diced turkey sausage, bell peppers, onions, and black pepper to the eggs. Stir until all ingredients are evenly distributed."],[null,"Pour a portion of the egg mixture onto the center of the preheated waffle iron, ensuring not to overfill. Close the lid gently. Cook for approximately 3-5 minutes, or until the eggs are fully set and the surface is lightly golden. Cooking times may vary depending on your waffle iron; monitor closely to prevent overcooking."],[null,"Carefully remove the omelette from the waffle iron using a spatula. Repeat the process with the remaining egg mixture. Serve warm, garnished with chives."]],"h":[]},"6704193":{"s":[[null,"Bring a 4-quart pot filled with water to a boil. Boil the shrimp until they are pink outside and opaque inside, about 3 minutes. Remove from pot with slotted spoon. Toss with lemon juice, garlic, extra virgin olive oil, parsley, and salt."],[null,"Serve with some cooked polenta or top a green salad with this mixture."]],"h":[]},"9159147":{"s":[[null,"Add everything to your food processor or blender and process until smooth, scraping down the sides as needed."],[null,"For a chunky guasacaca, pulse in a food processor until you reach desired consistency, without over processing."],[null,"Taste and adjust to your taste, adding more salt, vinegar, or jalapeno to your preference."]],"h":[[null,"Jalapenos really vary in their level of spiciness . Start with 1, seeds removed, if you want a mild spice level to your guasacaca. Taste the dip once processed and add more, or add in the seeds until the desired spiciness level is reached."],[null,"If you don’t want any heat , you may skip the jalapeno OR replace it with half to one yellow or green bell pepper."],[null,"Do not sub the fresh herbs for dry . That just won’t work well for guasacaca. The freshness from the cilantro and parsley is what makes this dish so special."],[null,"For less tang , you may use lemon juice instead of lime juice and apple cider vinegar instead of rice vinegar. I urge you to try it the original tangy way first, though."],[null,"Make it a salad dressing . Add a little more lime juice, vinegar, or some olive oil or water to your guasacaca until the desired consistency is reached. It will add some lovely pizzazz to a fresh green salad."]]},"7288649":{"s":[[null,"Bring a pan of water to the boil, add the vermicelli and simmer for 2 minutes."],[null,"Drain. Return to the pan and add the milk."],[null,"Simmer for 15-20 minutes, stirring occasionally, until the vermicelli and milk have thickened."],[null,"Remove from the heat, sweeten with sweetener to your taste, and sprinkle over the pistachio nuts."]],"h":[[null,"You could use macaroni for this pudding in place of the vermicelli."],[null,"Try adding some dried fruits such as raisins, sultanas, prunes or apricots."],[null,"To add extra flavour, add a good pinch of nutmeg, cinnamon or mixed spice."]]},"4750582":{"s":[[null,"Press or pat the tofu dry to remove excess moisture, then cut into ½ inch cubes."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together all sauce ingredients until well combined."],[null,"In a nonstick skillet, heat the canola oil over medium-high heat. Add the tofu and cook, stirring occasionally, until crispy, about 8 minutes."],[null,"In a saucepan, bring water to a boil and cook the rice vermicelli according to the package directions. Drain in a strainer, then return the vermicelli to the pot and add a few drops of oil if the noodles are sticking."],[null,"Divide the rice vermicelli among four bowls. Top each bowl with carrot, cucumber, radishes, green onions, mint or cilantro, peanuts, and crispy tofu."],[null,"Spoon or drizzle the sauce over each bowl and season with black pepper to taste."]],"h":[["Use of Oils with Cooking","Including healthy fats as part of a diet for chronic kidney disease (CKD) is encouraged. Fat provides energy, but too much of certain types can be harmful for your heart and kidneys. Saturated fat and trans-fat are considered “bad” fats because they increase the risk for heart disease and inflammation. In comparison unsaturated fats, such as monounsaturated and polyunsaturated fats, are healthier choices that help lower blood cholesterol and reduce inflammation. Cooking oils are used frequently as an ingredient or coating in recipes and enhance texture, flavor, and moisture. Cost can vary depending on the type of oil, so storing oils in airtight containers in a dark, cool place can help save money by preventing spoiling. Moderation is key with using oil as each type offers a different nutrient profile. CANOLA OIL: This type of polyunsaturated oil offers the benefits of omega 3 and omega 6 fatty acids and is low in saturated fat. With a more neutral flavor, canola oil can be used in a variety of recipes. OLIVE OIL: Considered a heart healthy oil, this selection is a good source of antioxidants and monounsaturated fat. Olive oil has a stronger flavor and can boost taste in salad dressings, glazes, or marinades. SESAME OIL: Low in saturated fat and rich in omega 3 and omega 6 fatty acids, sesame oil is another good option. Often mild in flavor, this oil can work well for sauteing or in a recipe. COCONUT AND PALM OIL: Containing a high amount of saturated fat, use coconut and palm oil in moderation. Too much can contribute to risk for high cholesterol and heart disease."]]},"1829":{"s":[[null,"Finely chop the onion and celery. Place onion and olive oil in a small microwave-safe bowl and microwave for 2 minutes. Let cool for several minutes."],[null,"Drain tuna well and place in a mixing bowl. Pat with a paper towel to remove excess water."],[null,"Stir in the onion mixture, celery, mayonnaise, lemon juice and sugar. Mix until well blended."],[null,"Refrigerate to chill before serving."]],"h":[[null,"Make a tuna sandwich, spread on celery stalks or add to a lettuce salad."],[null,"Use low-fat mayonnaise to reduce fat to 13 grams per serving. Note sodium content will be higher."],[null,"If you need more protein try tuna salad and low-salt crackers for a snack."],[null,"See two variations for this recipe: Tarragon Apple Tuna Salad with Walnuts and Curried Tuna Salad with Grapes."]]},"2818":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 425° F. Thaw the pie dough and berries."],[null,"Roll the pie dough into a 12″ circle. Place on a baking sheet lightly coated with cooking spray."],[null,"In a medium bowl, combine the thawed berries and 2 tablespoons of sugar (or sugar substitute)."],[null,"Arrange the berry mixture in the center of the dough leaving a 2″ to 3″ border. Fold the edges of dough in towards the center, pressing gently to seal. (Dough will only partially cover the berries.)"],[null,"Melt the preserves by heating in the microwave 10 to 20 seconds."],[null,"Brush folded-in edges of the dough with melted preserves. Bake for 10 minutes; then reduce heat to 350° F. Bake an additional 20 minutes."],[null,"Remove galette from the oven and sprinkle with remaining 1/2 tablespoon sugar."],[null,"Serve warm or at room temperature. Cut into 6 wedges as you would a pie."]],"h":[[null,"Galette, a French dessert, is a round, flat cake made of pastry dough, often topped with jam or fruit."],[null,"Mixed berries may include a combination of blueberries, marion berries, blackberries or raspberries. Check the frozen food section at your local grocery store."],[null,"Other berry preserves may be substituted for blackberry preserves."],[null,"Reduce calories to 111 and carbohydrate to 12 grams (1 carbohydrate choice) by replacing sugar with low calorie sweetener of choice.."]]},"7071862":{"s":[[null,"Add the oats and 250ml water to a pan. Bring to the boil, then turn down the heat and stir regularly for 4–5 minutes."],[null,"Stir in three-quarters of the fruit and add the milk."],[null,"Bring the heat back up, mix well and put into a bowl."],[null,"Top with the rest of the fruit and the almonds, then serve."]],"h":[[null,"This porridge is also great made with chopped apples, a few raisins and a good pinch ground cinnamon."],[null,"You can use gluten-free oats or other rolled grains, such as millet, buckwheat or rice, which are available in health food shops."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"7006687":{"s":[[null,"Add the oil to a pan. Add the beef and cook for 4–5 minutes over a high heat, stirring regularly. Stir in the chilli flakes, garlic and ginger."],[null,"Next, add the red pepper, stirring for 2–3 minutes, followed by the baby sweetcorn. Stir for 1 minute."],[null,"Add the beansprouts and spring onions, mix well for 1 minute and remove from the heat. Allow to cool."],[null,"For the dressing, add the cucumber, coriander, lime juice and soy sauce to a small bowl."],[null,"Add the dressing to the noodles and mix in well. Next, add the cooled beef mixture, mix together and serve."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"7654528":{"s":[[null,"Cook noodles according to pack instructions (times vary – typically 4–6 minutes), drain and immediately plunge them into cold water to stop them cooking further. Drain again and then add to a bowl with the toasted sesame oil, mix well and reserve."],[null,"Meanwhile, add the rapeseed oil to a pan, then add the red pepper, ginger and chilli (if using), and stir for 2 minutes."],[null,"Next, add the spring onions and bean sprouts, toss for 1 minute and then remove from the heat."],[null,"Add the bean sprout mixture to the noodles, along with the coriander, cucumber, lime juice, and half the peanuts, and mix well."],[null,"Put into lunch boxes and sprinkle the rest of the peanuts on top, adding 1 tsp soy sauce to each, to flavour if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Choose reduced-salt soy sauce to lower the salt content in this recipe. Alternatively, to make the recipe healthier, leave out this ingredient altogether."],[null,"Use rice noodles and gluten-free tamari, instead of soy sauce, if using, for a gluten-free salad."],[null,"You could also try this recipe with a mix of walnuts, sunflower seeds and pumpkin seeds."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"7984576":{"s":[[null,"Divide the mint leaves and lime chunks between four individual glasses, giving each chunk a squeeze as you add it."],[null,"Add the sweetener and squash together with the handle of a wooden spoon to bring out the juice and flavours."],[null,"Add the ice cubes to each glass, top up with sparkling water, stir and serve with a sprig of mint, a couple of pieces of lime and a straw."]],"h":[[null,"You could use oranges, or try lemons instead."],[null,"Virgin mojito is also ideal served from a big jug."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"2465":{"s":[[null,"Plug in waffle iron to warm"],[null,"In a bowl, combine flour, cornmeal, sugar and baking powder."],[null,"In another bowl, combine eggs, almond milk and oil."],[null,"Stir dry ingredients into wet ingredients just until moistened."],[null,"Lightly spray hot waffle iron with cooking spray to prevent sticking. Fill with one cup of corn bread mix."],[null,"Follow waffle iron’s instructions to cook, approximately 3 minutes."],[null,"Repeat with remaining corn bread batter."],[null,"Tear apart each waffle into 4 sections and serve warm."]],"h":[[null,"Traditional corn bread requires preheating the oven and cooking for 20 minutes. Waffle iron cornbread is easy to make in minutes with a unique waffle pattern you can use for a drizzle of honey or butter. You may never make cornbread the old way again!"]]},"2263":{"s":[[null,"Plug in waffle iron to heat."],[null,"Finely chop onion and bell pepper. Melt the butter."],[null,"In a bowl, lightly beat 2 eggs. Add in finely chopped vegetables, melted butter and black pepper."],[null,"Spray waffle iron with cooking spray. Pour entire contents into waffle iron."],[null,"Cook for 2 minutes, or follow waffle iron directions if your waffle iron has a “ready” indicator light."]],"h":[[null,"It is important not to whip too much air into the eggs."]]},"9106033":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 350°F/176°C and line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"Combine all the ingredients in a mixing bowl and then use a 1-tablespoon cookie scoop to divide your batter into 12 cookies. Place the cookie balls on your baking sheet with plenty of space in between each one."],[null,"Use a fork to press each cookie down and make a crisscross pattern. Then bake for 8-10 minutes, remove from the oven and let rest until completely cooled to room temperature. They will be soft when you take them out of the oven but will harden as they cool."]],"h":[]},"4595502":{"s":[[null,"Place oven rack in middle position. Preheat oven to 350°F."],[null,"In a bowl, combine flour, oats, baking soda, nutmeg, and nuts."],[null,"In a larger bowl, with the help of an electric mixer, mix together the softened butter, sugar, egg, and vanilla extract. Add the dry ingredients from step 2. Mix everything together with a wooden spoon or use your hands."],[null,"Cover a baking sheet with parchment paper or use a silicone baking sheet. Distribute the batter to make 16 cookies (2 tablespoons of batter per cookie). Bake for 7–8 minutes, or until slightly browned. Remove cookies from the oven and let them cool on a wire rack. Note, they are still soft when removed from the oven. The cookies harden when they cool."]],"h":[["Nuts can be part of a kidney-friendly diet","Nuts are a rich source of protein, fiber, healthy fats, disease fighting antioxidants, and minerals such as potassium and phosphorus. The fiber and healthy fat content of nuts can help to lower cholesterol levels. Research also suggests that nuts may decrease inflammation that can lead to heart disease, cancer, and possibly kidney disease. While nuts can be a rich source of potassium and phosphorus, they can still be part of a kidney-friendly diet. The key here is portion size. Start by adding small amounts to your diet. Nibble on a few nuts as part of a healthful snack. Chop and sprinkle on hot cereal, a salad, or add to baked goods. Chop finely and use to coat fish or chicken for added flavor and texture. To maximize their health benefits, choose nuts without added salt and sugar. It can also be helpful to choose nuts that are lower in potassium and phosphorus content such as walnuts, pecans, and macadamia nuts. Ask your registered dietitian nutritionist which type of nuts and how much is right for you."]]},"6478767":{"s":[],"h":[]},"7406405":{"s":[[null,"Place the cardamom pods, mint, ginger syrup and 2 tbsp water into a pan. Bring to the boil."],[null,"Remove from the heat and cool for 15 minutes."],[null,"Pour over the prepared fruit, stand for 10 minutes and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Delicious with a little half-fat crème fraiche or non-dairy alternative."],[null,"If you don't have cardamom pods, you could use a good pinch of cinnamon or mixed spice."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"7310597":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the grill to high."],[null,"Place the peppers onto a foil-lined baking tray, skin side up, and grill for 7–8 minutes until the skins are blackened."],[null,"Place in a plastic bag, seal and set aside."],[null,"When cool enough to handle (approx 10 minutes), peel off the skins and slice the flesh."],[null,"Meanwhile, heat the oil in a non-stick frying pan."],[null,"Add the oregano, spring onions and the lentils and fry for 2 minutes."],[null,"Add the remaining ingredients, except the parsley, heat through, season then transfer to a serving dish."],[null,"Serve warm, sprinkled with the parsley."]],"h":[[null,"Feta cheese works well instead of goat’s cheese, if you prefer."],[null,"You could use puy lentils instead of green, look out for those tinned just in water rather than with added salt and sugar."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"7540559":{"s":[[null,"Finely grate the zest from the lime and set aside. Squeeze the lime juice into a large saucepan and add the pineapple juice, 200ml water, cinnamon stick and root ginger. Bring to the boil, take off the heat, cover and set aside for 10 minutes."],[null,"Pile the prepared fruit except the pomegranate seeds into individual serving bowls. Strain the pineapple juice mixture and pour equally over the fruit."],[null,"Serve with the yoghurt scattered with pomegranate seeds and lime zest."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"3056":{"s":[[null,"Cut the lime into slices. Cut the watermelon into large chunks and measure 2 cups."],[null,"Place the watermelon in a blender along with 2 lime slices and blend until smooth."],[null,"Use a sieve to strain the mixture and pour into 4 cups. Garnish with mint leaves and lime slices and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Replace sugar with stevia sweetener to reduce carbohydrates to 12 grams."]]},"2353":{"s":[[null,"Dice the watermelon and cucumber; chop the fresh basil."],[null,"Place watermelon and cucumber in a fine strainer and let sit for 20 to 30 minutes. Discard the juice."],[null,"Whisk together the balsamic vinegar, honey, lemon juice and olive oil. Drizzle over the watermelon and cucumber and mix."],[null,"Add basil and goat cheese and toss gently to combine."]],"h":[[null,"Watermelon and cucumbers hold a lot of water. Straining the liquid at the beginning of the process helps get rid of some of the fluid. Use a slotted spoon or strain again if needed if it is being eaten the next day."],[null,"Feta may be substituted in place of crumbled goat cheese. Feta has a higher sodium content. Sodium will be 55 mg higher per serving."],[null,"Goat cheese is made from 100% goat’s milk. Feta cheese is made from sheep’s milk but may contain some goat’s milk."]]},"6251897":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, mix together the tomatoes, watermelon, basil, and red onion."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the olive oil, sherry vinegar, salt, pepper, and chili powder. Add the dressing to the tomato-watermelon mixture. Cover and refrigerate for 30 minutes."],[null,"Before serving, top the salad with the chives. Pack in an airtight container for transport."],[null,"If you’re not serving it right away, store this juicy salad in the refrigerator. It’s best enjoyed within 24 hours."]],"h":[]},"6306338":{"s":[[null,"Place watermelon, cucumber, bell pepper, tomatoes, shallot, jalapeño, vinegar, olive oil, salt, and pepper in a blender. Blend until completely smooth. Taste and adjust seasonings if needed."],[null,"Refrigerate the gazpacho for at least an hour before serving."],[null,"To serve, divide gazpacho between bowls and top with basil. If desired, add a small drizzle of olive oil."]],"h":[]},"6457837":{"s":[[null,"Puree the watermelon, ice, lime juice, and mint in a blender until you get a slushie consistency. Pour into glasses and garnish with a sprig of mint (optional)."]],"h":[]},"6910724":{"s":[[null,"Bring broth to boil in a small saucepan. Add quinoa and cover, reduce heat to low. Cook for 15 minutes, or until broth is absorbed. Spread quinoa onto a large baking sheet pan into a thin layer to cool."],[null,"Once the quinoa has cooled to room temperature, arrange the arugula on a large serving platter. Top with quinoa, watermelon, avocado, pumpkin seeds, mint, and feta."],[null,"Combine the lime zest and juice, oil, and honey in a small bowl. Whisk to combine and drizzle the dressing over the salad. Add salt and pepper if desired."]],"h":[]},"6118904":{"s":[[null,"Add all ingredients to a pitcher. Refrigerate overnight before serving to infuse flavors."]],"h":[]},"4964931":{"s":[[null,"Dice watermelon into 1/2 inch cubes. Place cubes on a cookie sheet, in a single layer, and freeze for at least 2 hours or overnight."],[null,"In a food processor, add frozen watermelon and strawberries, lemon juice, water, and honey. Process until smooth."],[null,"Place in a serving dish and serve immediately."],[null,"Alternatively, cover and freeze for later use. Remove from freezer 5 minutes before serving."]],"h":[[null,"* People with weakened immune systems should not eat raw honey due to the risk of bacterial or fungal infection. Filtered honey, commonly found at local grocery stores, is a preferable substitute, however, always contact your healthcare team if you have any food concerns."],[null,"You can use lime juice in place of the lemon juice."],["Enjoy watermelon as a lower-potassium fruit","Fruits are part of a healthy diet for all. However, for those with chronic kidney disease, many fruits contain too much potassium to be enjoyed on a daily basis. Typically melons contain a lot of potassium, but watermelon has the least amount of all the melons. To compare, a ½ cup of diced watermelon contains 85 milligrams of potassium whereas the same amount of cantaloupe contains 208 milligrams and honeydew contains 194 milligrams of potassium.1 In other words, watermelon contains less than half the amount of potassium when compared to other melons. Always remember, a lower-potassium food can be too much potassium if you eat too much of it and a higher-potassium food may work in your diet if you have only a small amount of it. Ask your dietitian how much watermelon is right for you."]]},"3884":{"s":[[null,"Place all ingredients except garnish wedges in a blender and blend for 30 seconds."],[null,"Pour into 2 small glasses, garnish with wedges and enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Watermelons vary in sweetness. Adjust by adding more sweetener if needed."],[null,"For fluid restricted diets, enjoy a serving of Watermelon Summer Cooler now and freeze one serving for later. Remove from freezer 10 to 15 minutes before serving."],[null,"If sugar substitute is used instead of sugar, the carbohydrate is reduced to 6 grams and 26 calories per 6 ounce serving."]]},"6785856":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, toss together the watermelon, feta, arugula, and onion."],[null,"In a medium bowl, whisk together the balsamic vinegar, olive oil, salt, and pepper."],[null,"Drizzle the dressing over the salad and toss gently to coat."]],"h":[]},"7805342":{"s":[[null,"Cut the watermelon into small slices and set aside."],[null,"Scatter the rocket and mint leaves over a serving platter and drizzle with the olive oil. Arrange the melon over the leaves then scatter the butter beans and feta over the top."],[null,"Drizzle with lemon juice and black pepper to serve."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"3016":{"s":[[null,"Cut watermelon into cubes."],[null,"Add all ingredients to a pitcher."],[null,"Refrigerate overnight before serving."]],"h":[[null,"If you are on limited fluids, adjust the portion size to meet your needs."],[null,"After flavors develop you can pour into ice cube trays to make flavored ice."]]},"7023571":{"s":[[null,"Add the oil to a pan, then add the chopped leek and cook over a low to medium heat, stirring frequently, for 4 minutes until it is soft."],[null,"Remove the leek from the heat and allow it to cool for a few minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, turn on the grill to high and toast one side of the rye bread."],[null,"Add the egg to a bowl with the mustard, and beat lightly. Next, stir in half the grated cheese and all the leek."],[null,"Spread the mixture evenly over the untoasted side of the bread, sprinkle with the remaining cheese and grill for about 2–3 minutes until golden brown."]],"h":[[null,"Using a mature Cheddar means you can use less and still get a strong flavour."],[null,"Rye bread is an excellent wholegrain – it’s high in fibre and will keep you feeling fuller for longer, so is ideal for breakfast."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"2443":{"s":[[null,"To cook wheat berries, bring 1-1/2 cups water and 1/2 cup wheat berries to a boil. Turn down heat to simmer and put lid on pan. Simmer for 30 minutes. Check for doneness and add extra water if needed. Continue cooking for 15-20 minutes, checking every 5 minutes until done. Wheat berries should be al dente or chewy."],[null,"Thinly slice pear. Heat butter in sauté pan and add pear slices. Cook until tender."],[null,"Add cranberries and chopped crystallized ginger to pears. Cook until cranberries start to burst."],[null,"Add cooked wheat berries, orange zest, maple syrup and cinnamon. Stir until heated through. Serve and enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"Cook wheat berries the day before and refrigerate until ready to use. Cook extra to serve as a side dish or add to soups and salads."],[null,"Wheat berries may be labeled as hard white or red whole grain wheat, and is often available in bulk bins in the grocery store."],[null,"Add a splash of milk or milk substitute if desired."],[null,"Substitute 1/4 cup dried cranberries if fresh are not available."]]},"4248376":{"s":[[null,"Preheat conventional oven to 350°F. Line the muffin tins with paper cups."],[null,"In a mixing bowl, whisk the egg, sugar, oil and vanilla together. Add the rice beverage and mix to combine."],[null,"In a separate bowl, sift together the flour, wheat bran and baking soda."],[null,"Add the dry ingredients to the wet ingredients and mix thoroughly."],[null,"Fold the berries into the muffin mixture."],[null,"Divide the batter among the 12 muffin cups and bake for approximately 20 minutes or until the tops of the muffins spring back upon touch."]],"h":[["Wheat bran as a fiber choice","A healthy diet must contain ample fiber to promote bowel function and prevent diseases of the colon. It has also been shown to improve cholesterol, blood pressure and glucose levels for those with diabetes. Wheat bran can be a source of fiber in the diet. Wheat is a grain that is commonly ground to make flour. During this process, the shell, known as the bran is separated from the rest of the grain and available to be added to various foods to increase their fiber content. Typically, it is sold as pure wheat bran and available in bulk at grocery stores. Wheat bran cannot be stored in the cupboard like regular wheat flour. It tends to get rancid over time. Store in the refrigerator to ensure freshness. If it is bitter in taste, it is probably rancid and should be thrown away. In addition to adding fiber to the diet, wheat bran is also a good source of iron, magnesium and B vitamins. Wheat bran is easy to add to cereals or baked goods. Adding it to muffins is common, but it can also be added to pancakes, waffles, yeast breads or even cookies to increase the nutritional value of these foods. In a CKD diet, wheat bran should be enjoyed in moderation because it contains a higher amount of potassium and phosphorus. Ask your dietitian how much is right for you."]]},"6093808":{"s":[],"h":[]},"2000":{"s":[[null,"Peel potato and cut into small cubes. Soak or double-boil to reduce potassium if you are on a low potassium diet (see helpful hints below)."],[null,"In a medium-size pot, boil cauliflower and potatoes for 25 minutes. Drain and place in food processor or mixing bowl."],[null,"Add margarine, half & half and salt (optional). Process or mix on high speed until smooth. Serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"Potatoes are very high in potassium but you can remove part of the potassium by using one of these methods:"],[null,"Double cook method: Peel and dice potatoes. Place in a large pot of water and bring to a boil. Drain the water and add fresh water to the pot. Bring to a boil, cook for 10 minutes then drain and set aside."],[null,"Leaching method: Peel and dice potatoes. Place in a large pot of warm tap water and soak for 2 to 4 hours. Drain and set aside."],[null,"Skip step # 1 if you are not on a low potassium diet."],[null,"Omit salt if adding other sodium containing toppings such as gravy, salted butter, etc. Sodium content per portion is 37 milligrams prepared without salt."],[null,"Frozen cauliflower can be substituted for fresh."],[null,"Freeze extra portions for later meal. Reheat in microwave."]]},"6543489":{"s":[[null,"In a blender or food processor, combine the low-fat cottage cheese, Greek yogurt, fresh lemon juice, Worcestershire sauce, and minced garlic. Blend the ingredients until you achieve a smooth and creamy consistency. This may take a few minutes, depending on the power of your blender or food processor."],[null,"Once the mixture is smooth, transfer it to a bowl. Stir in the chopped fresh chives and season the whipped cottage cheese dip with pepper. Mix well to ensure the flavors are evenly distributed."],[null,"Refrigerate the dip for at least 30 minutes before serving to allow the flavors to meld and enhance the overall taste."]],"h":[]},"2761":{"s":[[null,"Place quart size bowl and mixers from a hand-mixer in the freezer for 15-20 minutes."],[null,"Pour whipping cream, vanilla extract and sugar into chilled bowl. Begin to beat on low speed. When cream begins to foam beat on high speed until stiff peaks are formed. Be careful not to overbeat."]],"h":[[null,"May use preferred sweetener to taste in recipe."],[null,"Use in recipes calling for whipped cream topping or Cool Whip® frozen dessert topping. Homemade whipped cream does not contain phosphate additives."]]},"3744":{"s":[[null,"Combine all of the ingredients in a bowl and whisk together."],[null,"Refrigerator for 30 minute to let the flavor blend."]],"h":[[null,"Add White BBQ Sauce while grilling poultry, meat, or vegetables; use as a marinade or serve as a side sauce."],[null,"Substitute lower fat mayonnaise and omit the 1/8 teaspoon of salt if desired."]]},"7067962":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180ºC/gas 4."],[null,"Heat a flameproof casserole dish over high heat, spray lightly with olive oil and fry the lamb in batches until browned all over. Set aside."],[null,"To the same casserole dish, add the onion, celery, carrots, garlic and rosemary and cook, adding a splash of water, until the vegetables have started to soften (approx. 10 minutes)."],[null,"Return the lamb to the casserole and add the Worcestershire sauce, tomatoes and bay leaves. Stir to combine and add 300ml water."],[null,"Cover and cook in the oven for 45 minutes. Stir in the beans and cabbage, adding extra water as necessary."],[null,"Return to the oven for a further 15 minutes."]],"h":[[null,"You could make this dish with lean beef."],[null,"Try other beans such as borlotti, cannellini or haricot."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Defrost in the fridge or microwave and reheat in the oven or microwave until piping hot."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 4"]]},"6007726":{"s":[[null,"In a large saucepan, heat the oil over medium heat. Add the onion and sauté for 5 minutes. Add the garlic, Italian seasoning, smoked paprika, and cayenne pepper and sauté for 2 minutes."],[null,"Add the carrots and yellow squash and sauté for 3 minutes. Pour in the broth and tomatoes and bring to boiling. Lower the heat and simmer for 30 minutes."],[null,"Add the beans and simmer for 5 minutes. Drizzle in the lemon juice. Season with the salt and pepper."],[null,"To serve, place a scant 1/4 cup of cooked farro in the bottom of each soup bowl. Ladle the soup over the farro. If desired, sprinkle with fresh parsley."]],"h":[]},"3951":{"s":[[null,"Mince the garlic clove. Place beans in a colander and rinse and drain well."],[null,"In a medium size pan, heat 2 tablespoons olive oil over low-medium heat. Add garlic and turn heat to low."],[null,"Add in red pepper flakes and dried rosemary. Stir together until garlic is fragrant, about 3 minutes."],[null,"Add beans and stir to combine."],[null,"Transfer bean mixture to a food processor and pulse. Add in 1 to 2 tablespoons of water as needed for preferred consistency."],[null,"Remove mixture from processor and place in a bowl."],[null,"Garnish with remaining olive oil and basil leaves."]],"h":[[null,"Serve with unsalted pretzels or baby carrots or use as a spread for burgers, wraps or sandwiches."],[null,"Replace the rosemary and basil with any other preferred herbs of choice."],[null,"Can be served warm, cold or at room temperature."],[null,"White beans include cannellini beans, great northern beans and navy beans."],[null,"Substitute boiled white beans for canned beans if desired."],[null,"A 15 ounce can of white beans yields 10.5 ounces after beans are rinsed and drained."]]},"9992749":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350℉/176℃ and line two large baking sheets with parchment paper."],[null,"Blend the beans and milk until smooth and then transfer the mixture to a large bowl."],[null,"Add all the dry ingredients and mix until you have a ball of dough. It will be firm, but softer and stickier than pizza dough."],[null,"Divide the dough roughly in half and place each half on your prepared trays, or work on your counter if easier. (Make sure the dough is on parchment paper, and not directly on your tray or counter to prevent sticking.)"],[null,"Place another sheet of parchment paper over the dough and use a rolling pin to flatten and stretch the dough as evenly and thinly as possible without breaking it. Then remove the parchment paper on top of your dough and smooth out any rough or rounded edges to make them straight with a silicone spatula or your fingers. (This will help with even, uniform crackers, but is not entirely necessary.)"],[null,"Cut the dough into a grid pattern with a cookie or pizza cutter. Slightly separate each row and column by pushing the edges over with your cutter. This will help crisp up the edges. Then use a fork to prick the dough all over."],[null,"Optional: Brush the dough with olive oil and sprinkle with rosemary and extra salt if you'd like."],[null,"Bake in your preheated oven for 30-35 minutes, until the edges of your crackers are golden. Remove from the oven, let cool to room temperature, and serve with a dip or as is."]],"h":[[null,"If you don’t have oat flour or chickpea flour on hand , you can make some by grinding oats and/or chickpeas in a high-speed blender. (I use my Vitamix )."],[null,"The dough will be firm, but softer and stickier than pizza dough. This is normal."],[null,"Use TWO sheets of parchment paper (1 below and 1 above the dough) when stretching, to prevent it from sticking to your rolling pin."],[null,"Separate the rows of protein crackers AND prick the dough with"],[null,"If you have leftovers, you may store them at room temperature in a sealed container for up to 5 days. Make sure they are completely cooled before storing."]]},"6630727":{"s":[[null,"Preheat a large pot over medium heat."],[null,"Once the pot is hot, add oil and swirl to coat the bottom. Add garlic, veggies, and spices and cook, stirring occasionally, until softened, 7–8 minutes."],[null,"Add beans, broth, and tomatoes to the pot. Stir to combine the chili and bring to a boil over high heat."],[null,"Once boiling, reduce heat to medium and simmer, stirring occasionally, until veggies and beans are soft, about 30 minutes."],[null,"To serve, divide chili between bowls and top with parsley."]],"h":[]},"7095780":{"s":[[null,"Mix together all the salad ingredients in a large bowl."],[null,"In a small bowl whisk together the dressing ingredients, season well. Pour over the salad and leave to infuse for at least 30 minutes. Serve with lemon wedges and a green salad."]],"h":[[null,"You could use a tin of salmon or crab for this dish instead of tuna."],[null,"This is great for a packed lunch or picnic."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"3924":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, mix sour cream and mayonnaise."],[null,"Cut grapes in half; coursely chop walnuts and dice chicken."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine turkey, grapes and walnuts."],[null,"Fold sour cream and mayonnaise into ingredients in large bowl."],[null,"Chill for at least one hour."],[null,"Serve cold on a lettuce leaf with low-sodium crackers or a crisp breadstick."]],"h":[[null,"Use turkey or chicken leftover from a holiday meal."],[null,"Make a meatless salad by replacing chicken or turkey with either diced extra firm tofu and coarsely diced mushrooms or diced cooked egg white and coarsely diced mushrooms."],[null,"In the egg white variation, use the whites of hardboiled eggs or cooked pasteurized liquid egg whites."],[null,"Nuts are high in phosphorus and potassium. By limiting portion to 1/2 cup the walnuts add 32 mg phosphorus and 50 mg potassium per serving. Omit if desired."],[null,"Use low-fat sour cream and mayonnaise to cut fat grams in half."]]},"3379":{"s":[[null,"Cook pasteurized liquid egg whites in microwave or on stovetop. Chop the egg whites after cooking and set aside."],[null,"Chop green onions."],[null,"Combine all ingredients except egg in a bowl and mix."],[null,"Combine cooked egg whites to the mixture. Blend well."]],"h":[[null,"Other ingredients may replace the chives and tarragon."],[null,"Try chilies, cumin and cilantro for a Mexican taste, curry and chutney for Indian, basil and oregano for Italian."],[null,"Try stuffing egg salad into a pita with a little chopped tomato and lettuce."],[null,"Use reduced-fat, low-sodium mayonnaise for a lower calorie, lower fat dish."]]},"2909":{"s":[[null,"Finesly chop onion and celery."],[null,"Melt margarine in a nonstick frying pan."],[null,"Saute onion and celery in margarine until soft. Stir in flour, poultry seasoning and pepper. Stir over low heat for one minute."],[null,"Add nondairy creamer, 1/4 cup at a time and stir until thickened. Ready for use in casserole or pot pie."]],"h":[[null,"Use this gravy instead of canned cream soup, as the sodium content is much lower. Change the flavor by adding various herbs and spices."]]},"6606213":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6056779":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F. Coat a 9x13-inch baking dish with cooking spray and set aside."],[null,"In a large bowl, sift together the whole wheat flour and baking powder. Cut in the margarine and then add the parsley and 1 cup milk, and gently stir to combine. Refrigerate until needed."],[null,"Add the olive oil and a generous amount of cooking spray to a large nonstick sauté pan over medium-high heat. Add the carrots, celery, onion and mushrooms. Sauté for 10 minutes or until the vegetables are soft but not mushy."],[null,"Stir in the cooked chicken."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the flour, 1 1/2 cup milk, salt and ground black pepper. Add to the vegetable mixture and bring to a boil. Reduce to a simmer for 2 minutes. Remove from heat."],[null,"Pour the chicken and vegetable mixture into the baking dish. Drop clumps of the whole wheat crust mixture on top of the chicken and vegetable mixture (the topping will be very sticky). Use a spoon to gently spread the topping."],[null,"Bake for 20 minutes and serve."]],"h":[]},"6673785":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6607709":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6160768":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6311769":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6840452":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 425°F."],[null,"In a small bowl mix together 2 tbsp of the olive oil and salt. Place cauliflower, cut side down, in a large baking dish. Pour olive oil evenly over cauliflower and use your hands to rub the oil and salt mixture into the cauliflower."],[null,"Place on the middle oven rack, and roast 1 hour (if cauliflower starts getting too dark, then cover with aluminum foil)."],[null,"While cauliflower is roasting, whisk together the lemon juice, remaining 2 tbsp olive oil, parsley, and black pepper in a small bowl."],[null,"When cauliflower is finished roasting, pour vinaigrette evenly over entire head."],[null,"To serve, cut whole cauliflower in half, then cut each half into 4 pieces."]],"h":[]},"6159236":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F."],[null,"In a small nonstick skillet, heat the margarine over medium heat until melted, swirling to coat the bottom. Cook the green onions, mushrooms, and bell pepper over medium-high heat for 3 minutes, or until tender, stirring frequently."],[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the egg substitute and milk. Pour over the vegetables. Reduce the heat to medium."],[null,"Cook without stirring until the mixture begins to set on the bottom and around the edge. As it sets, push the mixture toward the center of the skillet and tilt the skillet so the uncooked portion flows to the edge and all the egg substitute is fully cooked, 3 to 4 minutes. (A rubber scraper works well for this.)"],[null,"Put the English muffin halves with the cut side up on a baking sheet. Sprinkle each with 1 Tbsp. Colby and Monterey Jack mixture. Spoon the egg mixture over the cheese. Top with the remaining cheese. Sprinkle with the tomato."],[null,"Bake for 5 to 8 minutes, or until the cheese is melted."]],"h":[]},"6624712":{"s":[],"h":[]},"9005196":{"s":[[null,"Line a 5-inch x 9-inch loaf pan with parchment paper and set it aside."],[null,"Add the flour, instant yeast, and salt to a large bowl and mix well."],[null,"Then add the maple syrup to a bowl of warm water and mix to dissolve. Then pour the water into your bowl of flour and mix using a silicone spatula, without overmixing, and DO NOT KNEAD."],[null,"Fold in the chopped figs and walnut pieces and then transfer the dough to your prepared loaf pan. Cover the pan with plastic wrap and let it rest for 20 minutes. It will rise to approximately double its size, and the bread will reach the top of your loaf pan. (see notes)"],[null,"Meanwhile, preheat the oven to 400°F/204°C and then bake your risen fig and walnut bread for 40 minutes. Remove from the oven and let cool before slicing."]],"h":[[null,"Weigh your flour for the best results . Flour volume will vary depending on measuring methods, such as the scoop and sweep, vs spooning your flour into the measuring cup. Use a kitchen scale for the most accurate flour measurement. Make sure to use warm water to mix with the maple syrup, and NOT cold. You need warm water to activate the yeast. DO NOT KNEAD the dough . Mix until no floury bits remain, without overmixing. When the bread reaches the top of the loaf pan, it’s ready to bake . Don’t let the bread rise above the loaf pan edges or you’ll end up with a muffin top. This normally takes 20 minutes, but if it’s not quite there yet, leave it for an additional 5 minutes. Freshly baked bread tastes best the same day it’s made, but you may store it at room temperature for 3-4 days. To freeze , make sure the bread is completely cooled to room temperature first. Then wrap it tightly in plastic wrap, and place it in a freezer-safe airtight container. You want to keep air away from the bread in your freezer to prevent freezer burn."]]},"6525164":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F. Grease a 9x5-inch loaf pan."],[null,"In a large bowl, whisk together the whole wheat flour, brown sugar substitute, baking soda, baking powder, salt, cinnamon, ginger, nutmeg, and cloves."],[null,"In another bowl, combine the applesauce, maple syrup, vegetable oil, freshly grated ginger, eggs, and vanilla extract. Mix until well combined."],[null,"Gradually add the wet ingredients to the dry ingredients, stirring until just combined. Do not overmix."],[null,"Slowly pour in the hot water while gently stirring the batter. The batter will be thin."],[null,"Pour the batter into the prepared loaf pan."],[null,"Bake in the preheated oven for about 45–50 minutes, or until a toothpick inserted into the center of the bread comes out clean."],[null,"Once baked, remove the gingerbread from the oven and allow it to cool in the pan for about 10 minutes. Then, carefully remove it from the pan and transfer it to a wire rack to cool completely."]],"h":[]},"6794979":{"s":[[null,"Set up a mixer fitted with the dough hook attachment. If you do not have a mixer, set up a food processor."],[null,"Add warm water, brown sugar substitute, and yeast to the mixing bowl or food processor bowl and let the yeast bloom for 5 minutes. The yeast should begin to get frothy."],[null,"Add the flour and 1 tsp coarse salt and mix on low until flour is incorporated. If using a mixer with the dough hook attachment, turn the speed up to medium and knead the dough for 5 minutes. If using a food processor, turn the dough onto a clean, floured board or countertop and knead by hand for 5-7 minutes. If the dough is too sticky, add one Tbsp. of flour at a time until it forms a smooth dough."],[null,"Add kneaded dough to a large bowl coated with cooking spray, cover and put in a warm place for one hour to rise."],[null,"While the dough is rising, preheat the oven to 400 degrees F. Coat a baking sheet with cooking spray. Set aside."],[null,"In a medium sauté pan, heat olive oil over medium-high heat. Add mushrooms and sauté until softened and all of the liquid from them is evaporated."],[null,"In a medium bowl, combine mushrooms, spinach, garlic, 1/2 tsp coarse salt, pepper and mozzarella cheese. Set aside."],[null,"Divide the dough into eight balls and let rest, covered with plastic wrap, for about 15 minutes."],[null,"Roll out each dough round to 1/4 inch thickness. Add 1/8 of filling (about 1/2 cup) to each round. Fold over to form a hand pie and press the edges to seal. Repeat this process for the remaining 8 dough rounds and place on the baking sheet."],[null,"Brush each pie with egg wash and bake for 25 minutes or until golden brown."]],"h":[]},"6589479":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F and line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"In a large mixing bowl, combine whole wheat flour, all purpose flour, baking soda, salt, and raisins."],[null,"Make a well in the center of the dry ingredients and buttermilk all at once. Fold the ingredients with a rubber spatula until just combined. Do not overmix."],[null,"Turn the dough out onto the parchment paper and form into a round loaf. Cut an X into the top of the dough with a sharp knife about 1/2 inch deep."],[null,"Place on the middle rack to bake for 30 min or until firm and golden brown."]],"h":[]},"9605778":{"s":[["Preparation Directions","Lightly grease a 9 inch pie plate or cut a circular piece of parchment paper to rest inside. Set aside."],["Preparation Directions","Add all the ingredients EXCEPT water to your food processor and process until combined, without over mixing."],["Preparation Directions","Lightly flour a sheet of parchment paper on your counter top, and gather the mixture from your processor with your hands to form a ball. If the mixture is very dry or crumbly add a tablespoon of water to your dough and mix it in very well, using your hands. (You shouldn't need the water if you weigh your flour using a kitchen scale.) You want a ball of dough, resembling a playdough consistency. Not too dry, and not so wet, that it's sticky."],["Preparation Directions","Place the dough on your floured parchment paper and sprinkle a touch of flour on top of your ball of dough, and on your rolling pin. Then use the rolling pin to stretch the dough into a circle that is roughly 10-11 inches wide. (A little wider than your plate.) The dough should be about 1/4 inch thick and do your best to stretch it as evenly as possible."],["Preparation Directions","Now, use the parchment paper to flip the dough over top your pie plate. Then gently remove the parchment paper. Use your hands to press the crust into the plate, along the bottom and edges. If you have any tears, use damp fingers to press and seal the dough back together."],["Preparation Directions","Then go around the edges and use a knife to trim any excess dough."],["Preparation Directions","Optional: Use your fingers to make a decorative design around the edges, if desired. (See process shots above.) It doesn't need to be perfect!"],["Preparation Directions","Prick the bottom of your pie crust with a fork, all over to allow steam to escape and then bake."],["Baking Directions","If you're making a pie with a no bake filling: Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F and blind bake the pie crust for 15-20 minutes, until the edges are golden and then remove from the oven. Let cool completely before filling for a pie that doesn't require further baking. For example my lemon pie, key lime, or strawberry pie."],["Baking Directions","If you're making a pie that has a long cook time: Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (For example, a blueberry or apple pie) and blind bake the pie crust for 10-15 minutes. Then remove from the oven and fill (no need to let cool first) and continue baking the recommended time for that recipe. (Typically anywhere between 40-60 minutes.) OR for a pie with a long cook time that doesn't require a blind bake, just fill it from raw and bake according to the directions of your pie. For example, my pecan pie does not require a blind bake."]],"h":[[null,"***Check out the pie crust in action with the above video for our Vegan Lemon Pie*** For best results, use a kitchen scale and weigh your flour . Relying on measurements is not as accurate as weight. Try not to overprocess your mixture in the food processor . Pulse until combined and then transfer to a clean surface to continue by hand. Make sure to lightly flour your work surface and rolling pin , to prevent sticking. As you’re stretching the dough, it helps to pick it up and move it around between rolling, so it doesn’t get overly stuck. Do not add water, unless needed. If you use a kitchen scale, you shouldn’t need any water. If you’re working ahead , you may prep the dough into a ball, wrap well and refrigerate. Then remove from the fridge about 20 minutes before rolling it out. If you’re making a pie with a long bake time (like apple or blueberry) cover your pie edges with a foil ring (cut a ring from aluminum foil) or a pie shield, if you have one, to prevent the edges from burning."]]},"6326662":{"s":[[null,"Bring a large pot of water to a boil. Add pasta and cook until al dente, according to package directions. Reserve ½ cup of the pasta water before draining."],[null,"While pasta cooks, heat olive oil in a large skillet over medium heat. Add mushrooms and cook, stirring occasionally, until softened and browned, about 5-7 minutes."],[null,"Stir in garlic, red pepper flakes (if using), salt, and black pepper. Cook for 30 seconds until fragrant."],[null,"Add kale and vegetable broth, stirring occasionally, until the greens are tender, about 3-4 minutes."],[null,"Reduce heat to low and add the drained pasta to the skillet. Toss everything together, adding a splash of reserved pasta water if needed to coat the noodles evenly."],[null,"Remove from heat, stir in Parmesan cheese and lemon juice, and toss again."]],"h":[]},"6499693":{"s":[],"h":[]},"6379941":{"s":[[null,"In a medium bowl, combine oats, wheat germ, and yogurt. Let stand until oats soften. Mix in egg, egg whites, vanilla, skim milk and mashed sweet potato."],[null,"In a large bowl, mix together whole-wheat flour, baking powder, baking soda, salt, cinnamon, and low- or no-calorie sweetener."],[null,"Make a well in the center of the dry ingredients. Pour entire wet mixture into the well and fold together until completely incorporated."],[null,"Coat a griddle or non-stick skillet with cooking spray and heat over medium heat. Use 1/3 cup batter for each pancake and cook until brown on bottom and some bubbles begin to break around edges. Turn pancake over and cook until brown and slightly firm to the touch in the center."],[null,"Repeat procedure for remaining 9 pancakes."]],"h":[]},"9508489":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F and line a baking tray with parchment paper."],[null,"Sift all the dry ingredients into a large mixing bowl. Then add the wet ingredients to the same bowl and stir until you have a ball of dough. It will be a little sticky."],[null,"Sprinkle some flour on a clean cutting board or countertop. Then place your ball of dough on top and knead for 30-45 seconds, sprinkling more flour, as needed. Do not over knead."],[null,"Now divide your dough into 6 equal pieces and shape each piece into a round, flattened disk and place them on your prepared tray."],[null,"OPTIONAL: Combine the 2 tablespoons of plant milk with the maple syrup in a small bowl and brush each of your vegan burger buns. Then sprinkle the buns with the seeds."],[null,"Bake in your preheated oven for 22-25 minutes, until golden brown. Then remove from the oven, let cool slightly and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Weigh your flour for the most accurate results . Scooping flour out of a bag with measuring cups usually results in too much being used, and will produce dry and dense results. Do not over knead the dough . Over kneading can cause dense and chewy results. For a softer bun , use white whole wheat flour also known as whole wheat pastry flour. Or try 50 percent whole wheat flour and 50 percent unbleached white all-purpose flour. These vegan hamburger buns taste best on the same day they’re made, but you may keep them at room temperature in a zip-top bag for 2-3 days. Or freeze airtight for up to 3 months and thaw as needed."]]},"6713059":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, dissolve yeast with 1/4 cup lukewarm water."],[null,"Place the flour, pepper, fennel seeds, chile flakes, and salt in a large bowl. Add the yeast mixture, an additional 1/2 cup lukewarm water, and 3 tablespoons. olive oil. Mix well to combine and form a dough."],[null,"Turn dough out onto a lightly floured surface. Knead energetically, adding a little more flour if needed, for about 8–10 minutes, until the dough is smooth and elastic."],[null,"Oil a large bowl with remaining 1/2 teaspoon olive oil and place the dough inside. Turn dough to coat with oil, and cover with plastic wrap and clean kitchen towels. Allow to rise until doubled in size, approximately 1 ½ hours."],[null,"Preheat oven to 375°F."],[null,"Remove dough from bowl and break off a small chunk. Roll into a 6-inch rope that is approximately the width of a pencil, and form into a circle. Pinch the ends together tightly, and place ring on an ungreased baking sheet. Repeat with the rest of the dough. Cover rings with a clean kitchen towel and allow to rise until doubled in size, approximately 1 hour."],[null,"Brush tops of the rings with the egg white and bake until light golden, 15–20 minutes. Remove, cool on a rack, and store in a tightly covered container for up to a month."]],"h":[]},"6540545":{"s":[[null,"In a heavy-bottomed pan, heat 1 tsp oil over medium-high heat. Add the ajwain seeds, gingerroot, and chile. Cook for about 1 minute, stirring frequently."],[null,"Add the spinach and ¼ tsp salt. Cook for 3 minutes, or until the moisture released from the spinach is absorbed and the base becomes dry. Add the amchoor powder and cumin, stirring well. Remove from the heat. Set aside to cool."],[null,"To make the dough for the paratha: mix 2 cups flour and the remaining ¼ tsp salt in a shallow dish. Add the spinach mixture to the flour mixture. Add water, little by little, to form a smooth dough (similar to the consistency of a pizza dough). Knead the dough until smooth. Transfer to a glass bowl. Cover with a damp towel. Set aside for 30 minutes to an hour at room temperature."],[null,"After the standing time, knead the dough once again. Shape into 8 balls. Lightly dust your work surface with the remaining 1 Tbsp flour. Using a rolling pin, flatten each dough ball so it’s 6 inches in diameter."],[null,"Preheat a cast iron griddle or flat skillet over medium-high heat. Place one piece of dough in the skillet. Cook for about 1 minute, or until it begins to bubble."],[null,"Turn the paratha. Brush with ¼ tsp of the remaining oil. Continue cooking for about 3–4 minutes per side, turning as necessary, until the edges are brown on both sides. Using a flat spatula, press the middle of the paratha as it’s cooking so it cooks evenly."],[null,"Remove from the skillet. Repeat the cooking process with the remaining pieces of dough and remaining oil. Serve hot."]],"h":[]},"7052242":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 180ºC/gas 4 and lightly grease a 19cm x 28cm baking tray."],[null,"Place the raisins, sugar, spread and mixed spice into a medium pan with 200ml of water."],[null,"Bring to the boil, then remove from the heat and cool."],[null,"In a separate dish, stir together the remaining ingredients then stir into the raisin mixture. Spoon into the prepared tin, smooth out to 1½ cm thick then bake for 25–30 minutes."],[null,"Immediately after removing from the oven mark into 25 bars."],[null,"Allow to cool, and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Try adding different spices such as cinnamon or ground ginger."],[null,"You can also use dried fruits such a mixed dried fruit, sultanas, prunes or apricots."],[null,"Freezing instructions: Suitable for freezing once cooked. Freeze in portions then defrost and serve cold or warm."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"7037421":{"s":[[null,"Add 1 tsp of oil to a saucepan over a low to medium heat, then add the onion. Cook for 3-4 minutes, stirring regularly until softened, then remove from the heat."],[null,"Beat the egg into the milk, then place the flour in a bowl and gradually stir in the milk mixture until smooth. Next, add the spinach, onion, cheese and pepper then mix."],[null,"Heat a non-stick pan over a medium to low heat. Add the remaining teaspoon of oil and wipe it around the pan with kitchen paper, before adding ¼ of the mixture. Spread it around the pan with the back of a spoon, about 12-15cm diameter and ½cm thick."],[null,"Cook for 2-3 minutes, then flip over with a spatula and cook for another minute or two on the other side.Serve topped with fresh tomatoes sprinkled with basil and black pepper."]],"h":[[null,"Try adding other vegetables to the pancakes such as grated courgette, cooked leeks or mushrooms."],[null,"Keep the pancakes warm between two plates, over a saucepan of gently simmering water, until they are all cooked."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 1"]]},"6059033":{"s":[[null,"Add the oil to a soup pot over medium-high heat. Add the onion and celery and sauté until the onions turn clear, about 5 minutes."],[null,"Add the mushrooms and sauté until soft and all the liquid is evaporated, about 10 to 12 minutes. Add the garlic and sauté 1 more minute."],[null,"Add the flour to the mushrooms and sauté for 2 minutes, then add the broth and stir well, scraping up the bits at the bottom of the pan."],[null,"Add the bay leaf, salt (optional), and ground black pepper. Bring to a boil, then reduce it to a simmer for 10 minutes."],[null,"Add the evaporated milk and simmer for 1 minute. Remove the bay leaf and then puree the soup with an immersion blender or in batches in a stand blender. Ladle into bowls and garnish with additional sauteed sliced mushrooms, if desired."]],"h":[]},"6089264":{"s":[[null,"In a medium saucepan, bring 4 cups of water to boiling. Add the rice and salt and return to boiling. Lower the heat, cover, and simmer for about 1 hour, or until the rice is tender."],[null,"Meanwhile, in a large skillet, heat the oil over medium heat. Sauté the onion for 7 to 8 minutes, until soft. Add the celery and carrots and sauté for 5 to 6 minutes. Add the garlic, thyme, and marjoram and sauté for 1 minute; set aside until the rice is cooked."],[null,"Toss the cooked rice with the vegetable mixture. Stir in the cherries, pepper, parsley, and almonds. Serve warm or at room temperature."]],"h":[]},"6320059":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a large pot over medium heat. Add the onion and cook for 3 to 4 minutes."],[null,"Add the water and chicken broth to the pan and bring to a boil."],[null,"Add the rice; cover and cook according to package directions; usually about 50-60 minutes."],[null,"Remove the lid and add in the toasted almonds and cranberries; use a fork to mix together."]],"h":[]},"6444169":{"s":[[null,"Start by washing and preparing a variety of winter non-starchy vegetables like carrots, radishes, celery, broccoli, cauliflower, cherry tomatoes, and bell pepper strips. Cut them into bite-sized sticks or florets for easy dipping."],[null,"Once the vegetables are ready, arrange them beautifully on a serving platter, creating an inviting display. To enhance their flavors, lightly drizzle a small amount of olive oil over the vegetables and season them with a pinch of salt and pepper."],[null,"Take a small bowl and combine 1/2 cup of mayonnaise with fresh lemon juice, maple syrup, grated garlic, salt and pepper and finely chopped fresh herbs, such as rosemary, chives, and parsley. Stir the mixture until the herbs are evenly distributed throughout the aioli. Season the herb aioli with salt and pepper, adjusting the herbs to your preference."]],"h":[]},"4704874":{"s":[[null,"In a small saucepan, combine water, sugar, mint and cinnamon and bring to a boil. Reduce to medium heat and let simmer until liquid is reduced by about half."],[null,"Remove the syrup from the stove and let cool."],[null,"Arrange the fruits on a serving plate and add the syrup on top. Garnish with mint leaves."]],"h":[[null,"* You can also use canned mandarin oranges if fresh clementines are not available."],["Kidney-friendly fruit salad","When planning your meals consider adding a fruit salad to the menu. Fruit is a good source of vitamins and fiber as well as other disease fighting nutrients, making it an important part of a healthy diet. Fruits also contain potassium, which can be a concern for many who have chronic kidney disease. To lower the potassium content of your fruit salad, choose lower-potassium fruits such as apples, blueberries, raspberries, clementine or mandarin orange slices, grapes, pear, pineapple, plum and dried cranberries. Even though you choose lower-potassium fruits, portion size is still very important. Ask your dietitian how much fruit you should include in your diet every day. When preparing a fruit salad, use a variety of colors of fruit for added appeal. Use seasonal fruits when possible to allow you to have fresh options, but when they are not available, fruit that has been canned in its own juice is a good choice as well. Like vegetable salads, you can add a dressing to your fruit salad for additional flavor. Create your own fruit salad dressing from honey and fruit juice such as lemon, lime and pineapple. Other ingredients to add more flavor and visual appeal include poppy seeds, vanilla extract, and cinnamon. Experiment until you find the right combination for you."]]},"6101914":{"s":[[null,"In a small bowl, whisk together the walnut oil, vinegar, lemon juice, chives, honey and salt and pepper to make the dressing. Set aside."],[null,"For the salad, divide the greens among 6 serving plates. Sprinkle the greens with the pomegranate seeds, blue cheese, and pistachios. Drizzle with the vinaigrette."]],"h":[]},"6607536":{"s":[[null,"Combine the dressing ingredients in a bowl."],[null,"Combine the greens, grapefruit, oranges, onion and walnuts. Add dressing and toss to coat."]],"h":[]},"6198260":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F."],[null,"In a small bowl mix together the squash and cinnamon."],[null,"In another small bowl, mix together the crumble topping, using your hands."],[null,"Pour the squash into a round baking dish. Spread the crumble topping evenly over the squash."],[null,"Bake for 20 minutes."]],"h":[]},"6057764":{"s":[[null,"In a large saucepan, heat the olive oil over medium-high heat. Add the onions and sauté for 4 minutes. Add the carrots and fennel and season with the salt and black pepper. Sauté for 3 minutes. Add the garlic and sauté for 1 minute."],[null,"Add the broth, cabbage, and rutabaga to the pan. Bring to boiling. Reduce the heat to low, cover, and simmer for 45 minutes to 1 hour. Add the pasta, raise the heat to medium, and cook for 7 minutes, or until the pasta is tender. Ladle the soup into bowls and garnish each bowl with the chives."]],"h":[]},"5648383":{"s":[[null,"Place a pan over a medium heat and add all the ingredients."],[null,"Stir continuously to warm gently, do not boil."],[null,"Remove from the heat and whisk with a hand or electric whisk to make a frothy drink."],[null,"Serve warm."]],"h":[[null,"Serve with suitable biscuits such as gingerbread."],["Renastep note","Renastep is a Food for Special Medical Purposes and must be used under medical supervision."],["Renastep note","Renastep is a ready to use feed for the dietary management of kidney disease from 3 years of age onwards. Renastep contains milk and fish. Refer to labels for allergen and other product information."],["Renastep note","This recipe has been specifically designed for the dietary management of kidney disease."]]},"7313285":{"s":[[null,"Cook the gnocchi as per packet instructions (usually about 1-2 minutes in boiling water). They're ready as soon as they float to the top."],[null,"Drain and lightly toss in the oil. Sprinkle with the poppy seeds, ensuring they're evenly coated. Set aside."],[null,"To make the swamp juice, add the peas, spinach, mint and milk to a pan, bring to boiling point and cook for 3.4 minutes. Remove from the heat and blend to a smooth sauce."],[null,"Place the sauce into a dish and add the gnocchi. Use cocktail sticks to serve."]],"h":[[null,"You could use other herbs, such as basil or parsley, if you don’t have mint. Add a little chilli or curry paste if you want to spice it up a bit."],[null,"This makes excellent canapes to pass around. There are usually around 30 gnocchi in a pack. Serve with cocktail sticks."],[null,"You can serve the sauce hot or cold. A tomato sauce would also work well with the gnocchi, too."],["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 0"]]},"6998435":{"s":[[null,"Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F."],[null,"Place the CAULIPOWER chicken tenders on a baking sheet that has been sprayed with nonstick cooking spray."],[null,"Heat for 17 to 19 minutes for a conventional oven, 15 to 17 minutes for a convection oven, or until the tenders reach an internal temperature of 165 degrees F."],[null,"Remove the tenders from the oven and place the hot tenders on the lettuce."],[null,"Top with carrots, green onions, avocado, red cabbage and pico de gallo."]],"h":[]},"6931629":{"s":[[null,"Heat oil in medium frying pan over medium heat. Sauté pepper and green beans for 2 minutes."],[null,"Add remaining ingredients except lima beans and artichoke hearts and bring to a boil. Cover, reduce heat, and simmer 20 minutes."],[null,"Add lima beans and artichokes, stir, cover, and cook 5 more minutes."]],"h":[]},"6824681":{"s":[[null,"Whisk all ingredients together in a small bowl. Cover and refrigerate for up to 3 days."]],"h":[]},"6475917":{"s":[[null,"In a medium-sized bowl, combine the Greek yogurt, chives, parsley, garlic, onion powder, dried dill, Dijon mustard, apple cider vinegar, salt, and pepper."],[null,"Allow the dressing to sit in the refrigerator for at least 10 minutes to allow the flavors to meld."]],"h":[]},"2891":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400º F."],[null,"Finely chop onion and cilantro and mince garlic cloves. Thinly slice chili peppers. Cut tomato in half and remove skin and seeds. Shred chicken."],[null,"Cut tortillas into thin strips. Arrange the tortilla strips on a baking sheet and spray with cooking spray. Bake for 3 minutes or until lightly toasted. Remove from oven and place onto a plate to cool."],[null,"Heat oil in a large saucepan over medium heat. Add onion, garlic and chili peppers. Cook until the onions are translucent."],[null,"Add tomato, broth, chicken, salt and bay leaf. Simmer for 8 to 10 minutes."],[null,"Add lime juice and cilantro. Season with black pepper."],[null,"Taste, and add more lime juice if desired."],[null,"Serve with tortilla strips sprinkled on top."]],"h":[[null,"Twelve unsalted tortilla chips can be substituted for the tortillas. Skip step #2 in preparations."],[null,"Homemade chicken stock contains 30 to 60 mg sodium per cup, if no salt or bouillon is added. No-salt added broth or low-sodium broth contains less than 140 mg sodium per cup. Reduced sodium broth contains 450 to 600 mg sodium per cup."],[null,"If reduced sodium broth is used in this recipe, decrease broth portion to 2 cups, omit the 1/4- teaspoon salt and add 2 cups of water to keep sodium low."]]},"2051":{"s":[[null,"Mix ingredients with hand mixer in medium mixing bowl until smooth."],[null,"Refrigerate until ready to serve."]],"h":[[null,"Serve with cut-up low potassium fruit of your choice or low sodium crackers."],[null,"The yogurt used in this dip does not have to be vanilla flavor; plain yogurt will also work. If you use other flavored yogurt, nutrient contents may change, as well as the color of dip. The same is true if you use any flavor of Polaner All Fruit: the flavor and color of the dip will vary."],[null,"This dip contains dairy; small amounts are appropriate for dialysis patients when potassium, phosphorus and calcium are well controlled. Consult your renal dietitian if needed and stick to the recommended portion."],[null,"Greek yogurt has higher protein content per serving than other yogurts."]]},"6055782":{"s":[[null,"Prepare the ingredients: Place an oven rack in the center of the oven, then preheat to 450°F. Fill a medium pot 3/4 of the way up with water; cover and heat to boiling on high. Wash and dry the fresh produce. Cut off and discard the stem ends of the Brussels sprouts; halve lengthwise. Halve and peel the onion; cut into 1-inch-wide wedges, separating the layers. Halve the grapes. Peel and roughly chop 2 cloves of garlic."],[null,"Cook the farro: Add the farro to the pot of boiling water and cook, uncovered, 18 to 20 minutes, or until tender. Turn off the heat. Drain thoroughly and return to the pot. Cover to keep warm."],[null,"Roast the vegetables & grapes: Meanwhile, place the prepared brussels sprouts, onion, and grapes on a sheet pan. Drizzle with 1/2 teaspoon of olive oil and season with salt (optional) and pepper; toss to coat. Arrange in an even layer. Roast 15 to 17 minutes, or until browned and tender when pierced with a fork. Remove from the oven."],[null,"Cook the chicken: Meanwhile, pat the chicken dry with paper towels; season on both sides with salt (optional), pepper, and enough of the za’atar to coat (you may have extra). In a medium pan (nonstick, if you have one), heat 1/2 teaspoon of olive oil on medium-high until hot. Add the seasoned chicken. Cook 6 to 7 minutes per side, or until browned and cooked through (an instant-read thermometer should register 165°F). Leaving any browned bits (or fond) in the pan, transfer to a cutting board."],[null,"Make the pan sauce: In the pan of reserved fond, heat 1/2 teaspoon of olive oil on medium high until hot. Add the chopped garlic. Cook, stirring frequently, 30 seconds to 1 minute, or until slightly softened. Add the vinegar (carefully, as the liquid may splatter), 1/4 cup of water, and as much of the red pepper flakes as you’d like, depending on how spicy you’d like the dish to be. Season with salt (optional) and pepper. Cook, stirring occasionally, 1 to 2 minutes, or until the sauce is slightly thickened. Turn off the heat."],[null,"Finish & serve your dish: To the pot of cooked farro, add the roasted vegetables and grapes and pan sauce. Stir to combine. Slice the cooked chicken crosswise. Serve the sliced chicken over the finished farro. Enjoy!"]],"h":[]},"4120739":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350°F."],[null,"Pour the melted butter and the lemon juice into a 9 × 9\" cake pan, making sure the bottom is covered with the liquid. Sprinkle the brown sugar on top and place the apple slices following a pattern. Set aside."],[null,"In a bowl, mix the flour, cream of tartar, baking soda and allspice. Set aside."],[null,"In another bowl, with the help of an electric mixer, mix the soft butter and the sugar for 2 minutes. Add the eggs, peanut butter, and vanilla extract. Mix for another 2 minutes. Reduce mixing speed to low and incorporate the dry ingredients from step 3, alternating with the milk."],[null,"Pour the batter into the cake pan over the apple slices. Bake in the oven for 40 minutes or until a toothpick inserted in the middle comes out clean."],[null,"Let cool for about 20 minutes. Place serving plate on top of cake pan and flip. Remove the pan and enjoy!"]],"h":[[null,"* choose firm apples that hold their shape, e.g. Honeycrisp"],[null,"* For Transplant: This recipe is higher in saturated fat. Check with your registered dietitian to see how this recipe can be included in your diet."],["Including nuts and seeds in a low-phosphorus diet","Nuts, nut butter and seeds add protein and fiber to meals and snacks as well as distinct flavor and texture. These foods are a natural source of phosphorus and potassium and can be included in a kidney-friendly diet in the correct portion size. Another benefit with these plant-based foods is that phosphorus absorption is lower compared to meat or foods with phosphorus additives. Incorporating nuts and seeds into your diet can be simple. For example, try adding an ounce of almonds or walnuts or a tablespoon of flax seeds to hot cereal for breakfast. Spreading a thin layer of peanut or almond butter on a bagel or English muffin can offer a flavorful, quick morning meal. A small amount of roasted pumpkin seeds, pecans or cashews make a great topping for a green salad. Or try them with a home-made tuna or chicken salad for lunch. Mix nuts and seeds with oil and herbs, blend them into a sauce, and include them in a poultry dish or as flavor on pasta. An ounce of nuts, especially unsalted nuts, and sunflower seeds are a low phosphorus, high protein snack. If craving a sweet snack, combine chia seeds, rice or almond milk, nut butter and fresh berries to create a pudding."]]},"6324312":{"s":[[null,"Toast the whole grain bread until it reaches your preferred level of golden-brown crispness."],[null,"While the bread toasts, scoop 1/4 of an avocado into a small bowl. Add the lemon juice and mash with a fork until chunky or smooth, depending on your preference."],[null,"Spread the mashed mixture evenly across the warm toast."],[null,"Serve immediately while the toast is still crunchy."]],"h":[]},"3360":{"s":[[null,"Finely chop onion."],[null,"Combine vinegars, water, black pepper, ketchup, chili powder, onion and Tabasco sauce."],[null,"Add seasonings: poultry seasoning, dry mustard, onion powder, garlic powder, ginger, ginger ale and lemon juice."],[null,"Add brown sugar and Liquid Smoke."],[null,"In a separate container, mix flour and oil to make a paste until all lumps of flour have disappeared. Add paste to sauce."],[null,"Cook for 15 minutes on low heat."],[null,"Pour or brush on baked or grilled meats."]],"h":[[null,"Use on hamburgers, beef ribs, chicken, short ribs and steaks."]]},"6991775":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil over medium-low heat. Add the garlic and sauté for about 5 to 6 minutes, or just until the garlic starts to brown."],[null,"Add in the broccolini, broth, and crushed red pepper. Cover the pan and let it steam on medium-high heat until the broccolini turns bright green and is tender, about 5 to 6 minutes."],[null,"Add in the lemon juice and zest, and serve immediately."]],"h":[]},"3274":{"s":[[null,"In measuring cup, whisk balsamic vinegar and olive oil."],[null,"Chop green onion and add to herbs and seasonings. Whisk to combine."],[null,"Cut chicken into 2 pieces. Pour marinade over chicken in leak-proof bowl or plastic storage bag. Refrigerate and marinate from 30 minutes up to 24 hours."],[null,"Remove chicken from marinade. Pan fry in medium-hot, non-stick or greased skillet for several minutes on each side until thoroughly cooked. (Using a thermometer, the internal temperature of the chicken breast should be 170º F)."]],"h":[[null,"For a lower protein diet adjust portion of chicken to meet your meal plan."],[null,"Marinate and cook extra chicken to add to a salad or for a sandwich the next day."]]},"3612":{"s":[[null,"Chop green onions."],[null,"Mix all ingredients except the chicken wings. Set aside 3/4 cup of marinade."],[null,"Place chicken wings into a container, or large re-sealable plastic bag. Pour the extra marinade over wings."],[null,"Cover and marinate in the refrigerator 4 to 6 hours."],[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Place chicken wings on a baking sheet, and bake for 20 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile, in a small sauce pan, bring reserved 3/4 cup marinade to a boil. Reduce by 1/3 until it thickens slightly to a glaze (approximately 10 minutes)."],[null,"After 20 minutes remove chicken from the oven, and brush wings with the glaze."],[null,"Raise oven temperature to 400° F and cook chicken wings about another 20 minutes, until done."]],"h":[[null,"Seven pounds whole chicken wings yields about 36 wings."],[null,"Chicken wing drummettes or boneless chicken pieces may be substituted for whole chicken wings. Adjust cooking time to avoid overcooking."]]},"4177552":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, let the chickpeas soak in 4 quarts of water for 12 hours to reduce potassium content. Drain, rinse and dry them on a kitchen towel."],[null,"In a large non-stick frying pan or heavy-bottom pot, heat oil over medium heat. Add the chickpeas, turmeric, and garlic powder. Cook for 7-8 minutes, stirring occasionally until the chickpeas are slightly browned. Add additional oil if necessary. Remove them from the pan and set aside."],[null,"Add onions and sugar to the pan. Cook for 5 minutes, stirring occasionally until slightly browned. Crush half of the chickpeas and add them to the pan. Add lime juice, jalapeno, rice, and chicken broth. Bring to a boil, then reduce temperature to low and let simmer for 15 minutes. Add the chicken to heat through."],[null,"Take the pan off the stove and add the yogurt, spinach, and parsley. Stir to combine."],[null,"Distribute into 4 bowls and garnish with the remaining chickpeas and parsley. Add pepper to taste."]],"h":[[null,"* Look for low- or reduced sodium broth containing 200 mg or less sodium per 1 cup serving. Avoid low-sodium broth that contains potassium chloride."],[null,"Note: If you like it spicy, do not remove the seeds from the jalapeno pepper."],[null,"*Can be lower with soaking"],["Reducing potassium content in legumes (beans)","Dietary protein can come from plants or animals with each offering different health benefits. The daily amount needed depends on how well your kidneys are functioning. Too much dietary protein puts extra stress on the kidneys while too little prevents the building of muscle mass and may not be enough for your body’s everyday needs. Working with a registered dietitian nutritionist can help you figure out the amount of protein you need based on your stage of kidney disease, and any other health issues you are managing. Legumes (beans) are a great source of protein but also contain some potassium. Consuming the right portion size, on average half a cup, can limit how much potassium you are eating. With the correct preparation and cooking method, the potassium content of legumes can also be lowered. Consider the following tips when including legumes in a low-potassium diet. 1. Soak (leech) raw or canned legumes overnight (~ 12 hours) in a large pot of water. 2. After soaking, drain, add fresh water, and simmer or boil the legumes for at least 30 minutes. If using a pressure cooker, legumes should be cooked for at least 15 minutes. This step is only necessary when using raw legumes."]]},"4189204":{"s":[[null,"For mayonnaise: whisk together yolks, lemon juice and mustard. Drizzle oil into the mixture and whisk until blended and creamy. Season to taste with black pepper. The extra may be stored in a clean glass jar (closed with a lid) in the fridge for up to 1 week."],[null,"Mix all ingredients for the crabmeat mixture in a bowl. Divide filling between fresh rolls, add lettuce leaf, sprinkle with paprika and serve."]],"h":[[null,"* Instead of using raw eggs the FDA recommends to use either shell eggs that have been treated to destroy Salmonella, by pasteurization or another approved method, or pasteurized egg products."],[null,"The easy mayonnaise recipe is a great base for many lunch salads! Try it with leftover cold salmon or chicken breast!"]]},"3036":{"s":[[null,"Peel and seed cucumbers; slice onion."],[null,"Mix all ingredients in a large bowl."],[null,"Cover and refrigerate at least 30 minutes to marinate."],[null,"Serve chilled."]],"h":[[null,"Decrease carbohydrate to 4 grams by using sugar substitute instead of sugar."],[null,"Leftovers will keep in the refrigerator up to one week."]]},"1745":{"s":[[null,"Drain and rinse kidney beans, corn and hominy."],[null,"Chop onion and green peppers; dice garlic and seed jalapeño pepper."],[null,"Place chicken in the bottom of a large crock-pot and top with all remaining ingredients."],[null,"Cover crock-pot and cook on high for 1 hour. Turn heat to low and cook for an additional 6 hours."],[null,"Shred chicken with a fork and mix to combine ingredients."],[null,"Portion into 1 cup servings and enjoy."]],"h":[[null,"Sodium content varies between brands. Compare several cans and select the products with the lowest amount of sodium per serving."],[null,"This is a thick soup, so you may need to add some low sodium chicken broth when reheating leftovers. Serve over steamed rice if desired."]]},"3762":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F."],[null,"Arrange pear slices in an 11” x 7” x 2” baking dish."],[null,"Combine Splenda brown sugar blend, ginger, rum extract, cinnamon and allspice."],[null,"Sprinkle brown sugar mixture over pears."],[null,"Dot with margarine."],[null,"Bake for 20 minutes."],[null,"Serve hot or refrigerate at least 1 hour to serve chilled."]],"h":[[null,"Bartlett amd Bosc pears are the best varieties for baking."],[null,"People without diabetes may prefer to use regular brown sugar."],[null,"Replace allspice with pumpkin pie spice if desired."]]},"7523365":{"s":[[null,"Toss the tomatoes, balsamic vinegar, lime juice, mint and basil together and tip onto a serving plate. Scatter over the watermelon and strawberries."],[null,"Using a vegetable peeler, peel long strips of cucumber and arrange over the salad. Scatter over the edamame beans and toasted pine nuts to serve."]],"h":[["Fruit/veg portions","Fruit/veg portions per serving: 2"]]},"6954369":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, combine the cucumbers, salt, and ice water. Cover and chill for 1 hour, then drain and return the cucumbers to the bowl."],[null,"Add the remaining ingredients and mix until well combined. Cover and chill for at least 2 hours before serving."]],"h":[]},"3280":{"s":[[null,"Cut zucchini into chunks. Thinly slice onion."],[null,"Place zucchini and onion in 10” x 6” x 2” dish. Cover with plastic wrap, turning one edge back slightly to vent. Microwave on high for 7 minutes. Drain liquid."],[null,"In large bowl, mix together beaten eggs, cheese, drained pimento, salt and pepper. Add zucchini and onions, stirring well."],[null,"Grease dish in which vegetables were microwaved."],[null,"Pour mixture into dish and cover with paper towel. Microwave on medium-high for 4 minutes. Remove paper towel and stir."],[null,"Continue to microwave uncovered for 4 to 6 minutes until center is set."]],"h":[[null,"Prepare this dish in the oven instead of microwave if desired. Bake at 350º F for 30 minutes or until set."],[null,"The amount of cheese per portion is 1 tablespoon."]]},"1894":{"s":[[null,"Dice peppers and squash; chop onion and slice mushrooms."],[null,"Crack 2 large eggs and pour into a ziptop bag. Shake the bag to combine eggs."],[null,"Add your choice of vegetables."],[null,"Close bag. Be sure to get all the air out of the bag. Shake to mix ingredients."],[null,"Repeat above steps to make 6 servings with remaining ingredients."],[null,"Place the bags in boiling water for 10-15 minutes. Remove and carefully open the bag and the omelet will roll out."]],"h":[[null,"Add black pepper or Mrs. Dash® herb seasoning for extra flavor."],[null,"Works great for a group, since each person can pick what ingredients they want in their omelet."],[null,"Serve with English muffin, bagel, fruit, or toast."],[null,"Cook up to 6 omelets in a large pot."],[null,"For a lower cholesterol omelet use 3 egg whites or 1/2 cup low cholesterol egg product instead of whole eggs."],[null,"If you are on a lower protein diet make the omelot with one egg. Count as 7 grams protein."],[null,"Research on cooking with plastics shows the safest plastic for use with food is polypropylene. Avoid polyvinyl chloride (PVC), which can leach into the food. If you are still concerned you can make this recipe in a skillet without using the zip-top bags."]]},"9240928":{"s":[[null,"Place the spiralized zucchini in a skillet and heat over medium heat until warmed up, but DO NOT over cook, or they will get too soft."],[null,"Transfer to a dish and top with the veggies and vegan parmesan cheese."],[null,"Enjoy!"]],"h":[]},"6694475":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl, combine the grated zucchini, corn kernels, whole wheat flour, chopped green onions, minced garlic, beaten eggs, baking powder, ground cumin, salt, and black pepper. Mix until well combined."],[null,"Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium heat."],[null,"Scoop a spoonful of the zucchini and corn mixture and carefully drop it into the hot skillet, flattening it slightly with the back of the spoon to form a fritter. Repeat to make more fritters, ensuring not to overcrowd the skillet."],[null,"Cook the fritters for 3–4 minutes on each side or until they are golden brown and cooked through."],[null,"Remove the fritters from the skillet and place them on a paper towel-lined plate to absorb any excess oil."],[null,"Repeat the process until all the batter is used."],[null,"Serve warm."]],"h":[]},"6671815":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350 degrees F. Lightly spray a muffin tin or line with paper muffin cups. Set pan aside."],[null,"In a medium bowl, combine brown sugar substitute, unsweetened applesauce, oil, egg whites and vanilla; mix well. Set aside."],[null,"In a large bowl, combine flour, oats, baking powder, baking soda, salt, cinnamon and dates."],[null,"Make a well in the center of the dry ingredients. Add sugar (wet) mixture to dry ingredients all at once and mix well."],[null,"Stir in zucchini. Equally portion batter among the 12 muffin cups."],[null,"Bake for 30 minutes or until toothpick inserted in center comes out clean."]],"h":[]},"6511716":{"s":[[null,"Add the olive oil to a large skillet over medium-high heat. Add the onion and sauté for 5-6 minutes or until the onions start to turn clear."],[null,"Add the garlic and zucchini and sauté for 4-5 more minutes until the zucchini is just starting to soften."],[null,"Add the corn and sauté for 2-3 minutes. Then add remaining ingredients until heated through."]],"h":[]},"3596":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 325° F."],[null,"Grease two 8-1/2″ x 4-1/2″ loaf pans."],[null,"In a large bowl, mix flour, sugar, pumpkin pie spice, baking soda and salt."],[null,"In medium bowl, beat eggs slightly. Stir in zucchini, honey, oil, applesauce, lemon juice and vanilla."],[null,"Stir liquid mixture into flour mixture just until flour is moistened. Spread evenly in loaf pans."],[null,"Bake 1 hour or until toothpick comes out clean."],[null,"Cool in pan on wire racks for 10 minutes, then remove from pans."],[null,"Cut each loaf into 12 slices."]],"h":[[null,"Boost protein content to 4 grams by adding 7 tablespoons of your favorite protein powder to dry ingredients."],[null,"If Splenda® is used instead of sugar, carbohydrate is decreased to 22 grams and 1-1/2 carbohydrate choices."],[null,"Zucchini bread freezes well. Wrap in plastic wrap, then place in a freezer bag."],[null,"If desired, use 2/3 cup applesauce and omit the oil, or use 2/3 cup oil and omit the applesauce."]]},"2522":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 325° F."],[null,"Chop onion. Grate or chop zucchini. Cut cream cheese and bread into cubes."],[null,"Combine eggs, nondairy creamer, onion, salt, pepper and Mrs. Dash® seasoning. Mix well."],[null,"Add zucchini, cream cheese and bread cubes. Stir and let stand for 10 minutes."],[null,"Spray a small casserole dish with nonstick cooking spray. Pour mixture into dish and bake 45 minutes until casserole is lightly browned and puffy."]],"h":[[null,"Suggested casserole dish size is 6″ x 7-1/2″ or 7″ round."],[null,"For variation, prepare with any summer squash."]]},"6706835":{"s":[[null,"Preheat your oven to 425 degrees F and line a baking sheet with parchment paper."],[null,"In a mixing bowl, combine the grated Parmesan cheese, breadcrumbs, garlic powder, paprika, salt, and pepper. Mix these dry ingredients well to create a flavorful coating for the zucchini chips."],[null,"Thinly slice the zucchinis into rounds. You can use a knife or a mandoline for evenly sliced rounds."],[null,"Toss the zucchini slices with the olive oil until they are lightly coated."],[null,"Dip each zucchini slice into the prepared coating mixture, making sure both sides are coated evenly."],[null,"Place the coated zucchini slices on the baking sheet in a single layer."],[null,"Bake in the preheated oven for approximately 20 minutes or until the zucchini chips are golden brown and crispy."]],"h":[]},"6245458":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oven to 425°F. Spray a large baking sheet with nonstick cooking spray. Cut the ends off of the zucchini and slice them in quarters lengthwise (so you have 8 long strips), then cut each strip into 3 shorter pieces."],[null,"Beat the egg whites in a shallow bowl until they are frothy. In another shallow bowl, combine the panko, cornmeal, cheese, oregano, and basil. Dip each zucchini strip into the egg whites, then into the panko mixture. Place the zucchini strips on the baking sheet, spray the tops with nonstick cooking spray, and bake for 20 minutes, flipping once, until they are browned. Serve with marinara sauce."]],"h":[]},"2953":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 350° F. Grate the zucchini; chop onion and parsley; mince garlic. Slightly beat the eggs."],[null,"In a large bowl combine all ingredients together and mix well."],[null,"Pour into a greased 11 x 7-inch pan or a 9-inch cast iron skillet. Bake for 30 to 35 minutes until set and light brown."],[null,"Cut into 9 pieces and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Leftovers still taste great the next day! Refrigerate and reheat in the oven or microwave."],[null,"Good hot or cold!!"]]},"6152434":{"s":[[null,"In a bowl, combine the grated and squeezed zucchini, crumbled feta, chopped dill, flour, salt, pepper, and beaten egg."],[null,"Form the mixture into 12 small patties and cook them in a skillet with olive oil until golden brown on both sides, about 3 to 5 minutes per side."],[null,"Serve with Greek yogurt."]],"h":[]},"2911":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 375°F."],[null,"In a large bowl, mix flour, sugar, pumpkin pie spice, baking soda and salt."],[null,"In medium bowl, beat eggs slightly. Stir in zucchini, honey, oil, applesauce, lemon juice and vanilla."],[null,"Stir liquid mixture into flour mixture just until flour is moistened."],[null,"Grease muffin tins or use paper liners. Fill each cup 3/4 full."],[null,"Bake for 15 to 20 minutes or until toothpick comes out clean."]],"h":[[null,"Boost protein content to 3 grams by adding 7 tablespoons of your favorite protein powder to dry ingredients."],[null,"If Splenda is used instead of sugar carbohydrate is decreased to 18 grams and 1 carbohydrate choice."],[null,"Top muffins with cream cheese frosting and serve for dessert if higher calories are desired."],[null,"If desired use 2/3 cup applesauce and omit the oil or use 2/3 cup oil and omit the applesauce."]]},"3031":{"s":[[null,"Grate onion and zucchini into a bowl and stir to combine. Place the zucchini mixture on a clean kitchen towel. Twist and squeeze out as much liquid as possible. Return to bowl."],[null,"Mix flour, salt, and Mrs. Dash® herb seasoning in a small bowl. Add egg product and mix; stir into zucchini and onion mixture. Form 4 patties."],[null,"Heat oil over high heat in a large nonstick frying pan. Lower heat to medium and place zucchini patties into pan. Sauté until brown, turning once."]],"h":[[null,"Serve with 1 tablespoon applesauce or cranberry sauce."]]},"2809":{"s":[[null,"Peel and slice zucchini and onion. Chop cillantro."],[null,"Heat butter and olive oil in a nonstick skillet over medium heat."],[null,"Sauté cumin seeds to brown."],[null,"Add zucchini and onion and sprinkle with black pepper. Stir a few times to mix."],[null,"Cover and cook for approximately 5 minutes to medium tenderness, stirring a few times."],[null,"Add lemon juice and chopped cilantro. Mix, cook another minute and serve."]],"h":[[null,"Cilantro leaves are also known as coriander, dhania, Chinese parsley and Mexican parsley."]]},"2897":{"s":[[null,"Drain the grated zucchini in a colander or strainer to remove as much water as possible. Use a paper towel to press out some of the water through the strainer."],[null,"Mix all ingredients together in a large bowl. Heat a waffle iron to medium heat."],[null,"Spray waffle iron with cooking spray, drop about 1/3 cup of mixture in the center and close the iron. Cook for 4-5 minutes and remove to a plate to keep warm. Repeat with remaining mixture."]],"h":[[null,"Two medium or 3 small zucchini will yield about 3 cups of grated zucchini."],[null,"Serve these tasty zucchini waffles as a side dish with fish or your favorite chicken dish."],[null,"Serve savory with sour cream or add some sweetness with maple syrup. You may also enjoy these waffles as a snack or unique breakfast."]]},"6664392":{"s":[[null,"In a large skillet, heat the oil over medium heat. Add the onion and sauté for 5 minutes. Add the garlic and red and jalapeño peppers and sauté for 2 minutes."],[null,"Add the zucchini and sauté for 3 to 4 minutes. Add the corn to the skillet and sauté for 2 to 4 minutes. Season with the salt and black pepper."]],"h":[]},"3776":{"s":[[null,"In a large skillet, heat oil over medium-high heat."],[null,"Slice zucchini lengthwise and chop."],[null,"Add zucchini to skillet and sauté until tender, stirring often."],[null,"Drain and rinse black beans from the can, then add beans to the skillet."],[null,"Chop tomato and add to skillet along with water."],[null,"Increase heat and bring to a boil."],[null,"Add rice; stir well."],[null,"Remove from heat and let stand 7 minutes or until liquid is absorbed."],[null,"Sprinkle each portion with 1 tablespoon cheese blend, if desired."]],"h":[[null,"Add freshly squeezed lemon juice, if desired for added flavor."],[null,"Instant brown rice can be substituted for instant white rice, if desired for whole grain option."],[null,"Cheese blend is optional,; omit if your phosphorus level is high."],[null,"Although beans are high in potassium and phosphorus, you can still include in a kidney diet when substituted for a meat entree. Beans are an excellent source of fiber."]]},"1719":{"s":[[null,"Grate zucchini and chop onion."],[null,"In a medium bowl beat the eggs; add flour and mix well."],[null,"Add the zucchini and onion and stir into the egg mixture until well mixed."],[null,"Coat a frying pan with olive oil and heat. When oil is heated, drop the mixture by spoonfuls into the oil, making 16 equal portions."],[null,"Using a spatula, flatten the latkes and fry until brown on both sides."],[null,"Drain on a paper towel to soak up extra oil."],[null,"Serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"The latkes taste best if eaten immediately."],[null,"Potato latkes (pancakes) are a classic Eastern European dish. Zucchini-Onion Latkes are a good low-potassium alternative."],[null,"Potato latkes contain over 600 mg potassium for a comparable serving unless the potatoes are soaked or boiled to reduce potassium."]]},"5499172":{"s":[[null,"Boil the rice until it becomes mushy, drain the water and blend until smooth. Place into a bowl."],[null,"Add the breadcrumbs to the bowl of rice and stir together until well combined."],[null,"Add grated onion, harissa, garlic, olive oil, tomato puree, chipotle paste, chili flakes, and black pepper, cumin to the mixture and knead together."],[null,"Sprinkle with spring onions, parsley and lemon juice."],[null,"Roll the mixture into 20 small balls and place on a plate. Serve and enjoy!"]],"h":[["Renastep note","Always check with your dietitian or doctor that this recipe is suitable for you."]]},"8582981":{"s":[[null,"Trim visible fat from the meat. Heat the tablespoon of oil in a pot and cook the onion until golden."],[null,"Add the meat and turn until browned on all sides, then add the tomato, paste, spices, cumin, dried lime and 500 ml hot water."],[null,"Cover and simmer for about 1 hour until the meat is nearly tender, adding a little water if needed."],[null,"For the fry: heat the oil in a pan and stir the garlic for 30 seconds, add the fresh and ground coriander, then the okra, and toss for 3–4 minutes."],[null,"Add the okra mixture to the meat with the salt and simmer for 15–20 minutes until the okra is tender and the sauce has thickened."],[null,"Add the lemon juice and serve hot with rice."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: lean, trimmed lamb, much less oil than usual, okra tossed in the garlic fry rather than fried, and no-salt tomato paste with no stock cubes."],[null,"Kidney tip: okra, tomato and tomato paste are high in potassium; use only 2 tomatoes, boil the okra and discard the water before the fry, and keep to a small plate with white rice."],[null,"Diabetes tip: the stew itself has about 20 g carbohydrate; serve it with 150 g cooked rice, ideally brown rice or half bulgur."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Sayidaty Kitchen, WebTeb"]]},"8420839":{"s":[[null,"Soak the potato cubes in warm water for at least 2 hours, changing the water once, then drain."],[null,"Heat the olive oil in a pot and cook the onion until soft, then add the garlic."],[null,"Add the tomatoes, tomato paste, spices and dried lime and stir for 5 minutes until thick."],[null,"Add the potatoes, carrot, green beans and eggplant, stir, then cover for 10 minutes on low heat."],[null,"Add the zucchini, bell pepper, hot water and salt, bring to the boil, then cook covered for 15–20 minutes until the vegetables are tender and the sauce has thickened."],[null,"Remove the dried lime, sprinkle with coriander and serve hot with white or brown rice."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: fewer potatoes and more mixed vegetables, only 1 tbsp olive oil, no frying of the vegetables, and no-salt-added tomato paste with less salt."],[null,"Kidney tip: potatoes, tomatoes, tomato paste and eggplant are high in potassium; soak the potatoes as in the steps or swap them for cauliflower, use less tomato paste, and keep to one serving."],[null,"Diabetes tip: the idam itself is low in carbohydrate and high in fibre; serve it with about 100 g cooked brown rice."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, vegetarians, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Sayidaty, Cookpad Saudi Arabia"]]},"8072056":{"s":[[null,"Boil the lentils in 500 ml water for about 20 minutes until tender, then drain and keep the cooking water."],[null,"Heat the oil in a pot and cook the onion and garlic over medium heat until soft but not browned."],[null,"Add the chicken and spices and stir until the chicken changes colour and its juices are absorbed."],[null,"Add the tomato and cook for 5 minutes until it breaks down, then add the cooked lentils."],[null,"Add the purslane and salt, stir, cover and cook on low heat for 10–15 minutes; if it gets dry add a little of the lentil water."],[null,"Squeeze over the lemon and serve with whole-wheat bread or a small portion of rice."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: skinless chicken breast, 2 tbsp olive oil instead of about 120 ml vegetable oil, and less salt with no stock cubes."],[null,"Kidney tip: purslane is very high in potassium and oxalate, and lentils are high in potassium and phosphorus; boil the purslane for 5 minutes and throw away the water before adding it, halve the lentils, and have half a portion if you must limit potassium."],[null,"Diabetes tip: the stew alone has about 26 g carbohydrate; if you add rice keep it to half a portion (about 75 g cooked) or use whole-wheat bread."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Cookpad, Food2Mins"]]},"8423933":{"s":[[null,"Leave the laban out of the fridge for a few hours if you like a sourer taste."],[null,"Put the laban in a pot over very low heat without boiling, stirring gently now and then, until it curdles and the yellow whey separates from the curd (30–45 minutes)."],[null,"Strain the curd through muslin or a fine sieve and discard the whey, then return the curd to a clean pot over low heat, stirring constantly, until most of the liquid has evaporated and it no longer sticks."],[null,"Mix in the salt and let it cool until easy to shape."],[null,"Shape into small balls or discs the size of a walnut (about 20 pieces) and lay them on muslin or a clean towel to absorb moisture."],[null,"Cover with light muslin and leave in the sun or a dry, airy place for 1–2 days until firm and dry, then keep in an airtight box in the fridge."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: low-fat laban and very little salt (about 0.2 g per portion) instead of the large amount used for long storage, so keep it in the fridge and eat it within two weeks."],[null,"Kidney tip: aqit is rich in protein and phosphorus like other dairy foods; keep to 1–2 pieces a day and avoid salty shop-bought aqit."],[null,"Diabetes tip: aqit is very low in carbohydrate (about 2 g per portion); serve it with just one date or with cucumber rather than many dates."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Arabic Wikipedia (Aqit), Cookpad Saudi Arabia"]]},"8388701":{"s":[[null,"Mix both flours with the salt and oil, add the water little by little and knead to a firm, slightly stiff dough; cover and rest for 1 hour."],[null,"Put the meat in a non-stick pan over medium heat and stir, breaking it up, until its juices evaporate; add the onion and stir for 5 minutes until soft."],[null,"Add the spices and salt and stir for 1 minute, then take off the heat, let it cool and mix in the parsley and chopped egg."],[null,"Heat the oven to 200 °C and line a tray with baking paper."],[null,"Divide the dough in two, roll the first half into a thin rectangle (about 30×20 cm) and spread the filling over it in a thin layer, then roll out the second half and lay it on top."],[null,"Cut into 12 squares, press the edges of each square with a fork to seal, place them on the tray and brush with the oil."],[null,"Bake for 20–25 minutes until puffed and golden, and serve hot with salad."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: baked instead of deep-fried, half whole-wheat flour, extra-lean minced meat, no custard powder or starch, and limited salt."],[null,"Kidney tip: meat and egg yolk contain phosphorus; you can use 1 whole egg plus 1 egg white, and keep to 2 pieces with a cucumber and lettuce salad."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion (3 pieces) has about 49 g carbohydrate; have 2 pieces with a large salad or vegetable soup."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Arabic Wikipedia (Saudi cuisine: Madini buff), Cookpad Saudi Arabia"]]},"8856991":{"s":[[null,"Drain and rinse the chickpeas, then put them in a pot with water to cover by 5 cm, the bay leaves and the mint."],[null,"Bring to the boil and skim off the foam, then add a splash (about 100 ml) of cold water and skim again; repeat twice."],[null,"Turn the heat right down and simmer for 2–3 hours until the chickpeas are tender but whole, adding the salt in the last 30 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile boil the beetroot for 25–30 minutes until tender, then peel and dice it, keeping 3 tbsp of the cooking water."],[null,"Mix the beetroot and carrot with the diluted vinegar, lemon juice, beet water and chilli and leave 20 minutes; add the cucumber just before serving."],[null,"Ladle the chickpeas with a little of their liquid into small bowls, add the cumin and olive oil, and top with a spoonful of the salad."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: no baking soda in the soak, fresh beetroot instead of canned, fresh chilli instead of salty bottled hot sauce, and little salt."],[null,"Kidney tip: chickpeas and beetroot are high in potassium, and chickpeas in phosphorus; keep to one small bowl, drain the chickpeas from their liquid, and you can use less beetroot and more cucumber."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one bowl has about 39 g carbohydrate with 8 g fibre and raises blood sugar slowly; have it as an evening snack in place of sweets."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, vegetarians, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Mawdoo3 Sufrati, JustFood"]]},"8924859":{"s":[[null,"Mix both flours with the sugar, yeast, nigella seeds and salt."],[null,"Add the egg, oil and warm laban and knead to a soft, smooth dough, adding a spoon of water if needed; cover and leave to rise for 1 hour."],[null,"Heat the oven to 240 °C with a cast-iron tray or baking stone inside."],[null,"Divide the dough into 16 small balls and press each one by hand into a thin round about 10 cm wide."],[null,"Brush the rounds lightly with oil and bake on the hot tray for 5–6 minutes, turning halfway, until puffed and golden. (You can also cook them in a covered non-stick pan over medium heat for 2 minutes per side.)"],[null,"Stack the rounds on a plate, pour the honey over and serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: baked or pan-cooked instead of deep-fried, two-thirds whole-wheat flour, low-fat laban, half the usual sugar in the dough, and limited honey (about 2 tsp per portion)."],[null,"Kidney tip: whole-wheat flour and laban contain phosphorus and potassium; you can use more white flour and keep to 2 rounds."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion (2 rounds) has about 37 g carbohydrate; skip the honey and serve with a boiled egg or low-fat labneh and cucumber."],[null,"Suitable for: heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Arabic Wikipedia (Saudi cuisine: tawa), Cookpad Saudi Arabia"]]},"8364233":{"s":[[null,"Heat the olive oil in a heavy pot and cook the chopped onion until soft and lightly golden."],[null,"Add the meat and stir for 5 minutes until browned, then add the spices and chillies and stir for 1 minute."],[null,"Add the tomatoes and tomato paste and stir until they break down, then add the pumpkin, zucchini and eggplant and cover for 5 minutes."],[null,"Pour in 1.5 l hot water and bring to the boil, then add the washed (unsoaked) rice and the salt and stir."],[null,"Cover and cook on very low heat for about 3 hours, stirring now and then and adding hot water as needed, until the rice and vegetables melt together into a thick, soft texture."],[null,"Fry the sliced onion in the ghee with the dried lime until golden, stir the tamman briefly, spoon it into a serving dish and top with the onion."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: lean, trimmed meat, more vegetables, only 1 tbsp olive oil and 1 tsp ghee, and no-salt-added tomato paste with no stock cubes."],[null,"Kidney tip: tomatoes, tomato paste, pumpkin, eggplant and meat contain potassium and phosphorus; you can use less tomato paste and pumpkin, add more zucchini, and keep to one serving."],[null,"Diabetes tip: short-grain rice cooked this long raises blood sugar quickly; keep to one serving and eat it with a green salad or low-fat laban."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Mawdoo3, Saraya News"]]},"8184629":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a pot and cook the onion until soft, then add the garlic and lamb and stir until browned."],[null,"Add the spices, dried lime, tomato paste and blended tomato and stir for 5 minutes."],[null,"Add 1.5 l water, cover and simmer for about 1 hour until the lamb is nearly tender, skimming off any fat."],[null,"Meanwhile knead the flour, salt and water into a soft dough, divide into 4 balls, roll thin and cook on a hot griddle for 1 minute per side."],[null,"Add the carrots and pumpkin to the stew; after 10 minutes add the zucchini, eggplant and chilli and cook 15–20 minutes until tender, then add the salt."],[null,"For the topping: cook the onion in the ghee over medium heat until golden, then add the ground dried lime and turmeric."],[null,"Tear the bread into a deep dish, soak it with broth layer by layer, then top with the lamb and vegetables and finish with the onion topping."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: boneless trimmed lamb, homemade whole-wheat bread instead of shop bread, more vegetables, no stock cubes, and only a little ghee for the onion topping."],[null,"Kidney tip: the broth, tomatoes, pumpkin and carrots are high in potassium, and meat and whole-wheat flour are high in phosphorus; take less broth, keep to about 100 g cooked meat, and you can boil the vegetables in separate water and drain them to cut potassium."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one bowl has about 54 g carbohydrate, mostly from the bread; eat the vegetables and meat first, and whole-wheat bread raises blood sugar more slowly than white bread."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Mawdoo3, Sayidaty Kitchen"]]},"8022034":{"s":[[null,"Mix both flours with the yeast, sugar and salt, then add the cream cheese and evaporated milk and knead, adding the water little by little, to a soft, smooth dough that does not stick to your hands."],[null,"Cover the dough and leave to rise for 1 hour or until doubled."],[null,"Dust the worktop with a little flour, roll the dough about ½ cm thick and cut 12 rounds with a glass or cutter."],[null,"Place the rounds on a tray lined with baking paper, brush with the oil and leave for 15 minutes to puff; heat the oven to 200 °C."],[null,"Bake the rounds for 12–15 minutes until puffed and golden."],[null,"Brush them while hot with the thinned honey, sprinkle with pistachios and serve warm."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: baked instead of fried, low-fat cream cheese instead of full-fat cheese, fat-free evaporated milk, half whole-wheat flour, and 40 g honey for the whole batch instead of a glass of syrup."],[null,"Kidney tip: cheese, evaporated milk and pistachios contain phosphorus; keep to one piece, and you can skip the pistachios and use only white flour."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one piece has about 21 g carbohydrate; have one piece without the honey glaze, with Arabic coffee or unsweetened tea."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Arabic Wikipedia (Saudi cuisine), Cookpad Saudi Arabia"]]},"8209870":{"s":[[null,"Put the chicken in a large pot with the grated onion, whole spices and water, bring to the boil and cook on low heat for 25 minutes until done, skimming off the foam."],[null,"Lift out the chicken and shred it, and remove the whole spices from the broth."],[null,"Drain the jareesh and add it to the broth with the cumin and chilli, bring to the boil, then turn the heat right down, cover and cook for 2 hours, stirring every 10 minutes so it does not stick (or 40 minutes in a pressure cooker), adding hot water if it dries out."],[null,"Add the shredded chicken, laban, salt and lemon juice, stir well and leave on low heat for 20–30 minutes."],[null,"Mash the jareesh with the back of a heavy ladle or a jareesh masher until smooth and thick."],[null,"For the kushna: heat the oil and ghee and cook the onion on medium heat until soft and lightly browned, then add the tomato paste, dried lime, cinnamon and a splash of water and stir for 2 minutes."],[null,"Spoon the jareesh into bowls, top with the kushna and serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: no stock cubes, cream, milk powder or lamb fat, skinless chicken, laban made from low-fat yoghurt, only 1 tsp ghee in the kushna and about half the usual salt."],[null,"Kidney tip: whole wheat, laban and chicken are high in phosphorus and potassium; keep to one bowl, and you can halve the laban and replace it with water plus lemon juice. Ask your dietitian about your own portion."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one bowl has about 50 g carbohydrate with 7 g fibre from the whole wheat; do not add rice or bread, and serve it with a green salad."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Arabic Wikipedia (Jareesh), The National News (jareesh as a national dish)"]]},"8217561":{"s":[[null,"Whisk the flour with the milk and baking powder to a smooth, pourable batter like pancake batter."],[null,"Heat a non-stick pan over medium heat, pour in half the batter and spread it thin; cook for 4–5 minutes per side until cooked and browned. Repeat with the rest."],[null,"If the dates are firm, soak them in a little hot water for 5 minutes and drain."],[null,"Cut up the bread and mince it with the dates, alternating pieces, in a meat grinder or food processor until evenly mixed."],[null,"Melt the ghee in a pan over low heat, add the hunaini mixture with the cardamom, cinnamon, saffron and pepper and stir for 5 minutes until hot and cohesive."],[null,"Serve warm in small bowls with Arabic coffee."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: whole-wheat bread made with low-fat milk and cooked without fat, a little ghee instead of sticks of butter, no added sugar, and a small portion."],[null,"Kidney tip: dates are rich in potassium, and milk and whole-wheat flour contain phosphorus; you can use water instead of milk and have half a portion."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has about 51 g carbohydrate; have half a portion after a meal with protein and vegetables, and do not add honey or sugar."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Sayidaty Kitchen, WebTeb"]]},"8973451":{"s":[[null,"Mix the sorghum flour, wheat flour, yeast, grated onion and garlic, then whisk in the warm water gradually to a pourable batter like cake batter."],[null,"Cover and leave in a warm place for 3–4 hours until bubbly and slightly sour."],[null,"Meanwhile heat the oil in a pot and cook the sliced onion until soft and golden, then add the garlic and tomatoes and stir for 3 minutes."],[null,"Add the lamb and turn until it changes colour, then add the whole and ground spices and the water. Bring to the boil, lower the heat, cover and simmer 1½ hours until tender, skimming off foam and fat."],[null,"Add the salt during the last 10 minutes of cooking."],[null,"Heat a non-stick pan over medium heat without oil, pour in a small ladle of batter and spread it into a round. Cook until covered with holes and dry on top, without flipping (about 2 minutes). Repeat to make about 8 rounds."],[null,"Tear 2 lahoh rounds into each bowl, ladle the hot broth over them until soaked, then place the meat on top."],[null,"Melt the ghee and drizzle ½ tsp over each bowl, sprinkle with parsley and serve hot with a green salad."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: trimmed lamb leg instead of fatty meat, the fat is skimmed from the broth, only 2 tsp ghee for the whole pot instead of a generous pour, little salt with no stock cubes or salted spice mixes, and the lahoh is made from whole grains."],[null,"Kidney tip: tomato, meat and whole grains add potassium and phosphorus; keep to one bowl, use one ladle of broth rather than drinking the extra, and you can swap half the whole wheat flour for white flour to lower phosphorus."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one bowl has about 45 g carbohydrate from the lahoh; whole sorghum and wheat raise blood sugar more slowly than white bread, so serve it with a large salad."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (Mawsouat Al Tabkh), Sayidaty Kitchen, Yummy (Layalina)"]]},"8678841":{"s":[[null,"Beat the eggs and sugar with an electric mixer until pale and fluffy."],[null,"Add the milk and saffron rose water, then both flours, milk powder, baking powder and cardamom, and beat until thick and creamy."],[null,"Cover and rest the batter for 10–15 minutes."],[null,"Heat a non-stick pan over low to medium heat and brush with a very thin layer of oil."],[null,"Drop one tablespoon of batter per round (or use a squeeze bottle), leaving space between them."],[null,"Cook until bubbles appear and the base is golden (1–2 minutes), then flip and cook 1 minute on the other side. Brush the pan again between batches (makes about 16 rounds)."],[null,"Serve warm with tea or unsweetened Saudi coffee."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: 60 g sugar instead of about 200 g, cooked in a brushed pan instead of fried in oil, low-fat milk and nonfat milk powder, and no syrup poured over."],[null,"Kidney tip: milk and baking powder (which contains phosphate) add phosphorus; you can use water instead of milk and an extra spoon of flour instead of the milk powder, and keep to two rounds."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one serving has about 30 g carbohydrate, about 8 g of it added sugar; keep to two rounds with an unsweetened drink."],[null,"Suitable for: heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (Mawsouat Al Tabkh), Mawdoo3, Al Jawhara Magazine"]]},"8302643":{"s":[[null,"Soak the qamar al-din in the hot water for at least 1 hour until soft, and soak the apricots, figs and raisins in more hot water for 30 minutes, then drain them."],[null,"Soak the almonds and pistachios in boiling water for 10 minutes and slip off the skins; toast the pine nuts in a dry pan until golden."],[null,"Mash the qamar al-din with its soaking water with a spoon or blender until smooth and liquid."],[null,"Melt the ghee in a pot, add the cardamom, cinnamon and cloves and stir for 1 minute until fragrant."],[null,"Add the qamar al-din mixture, bring to the boil, then lower the heat and cook for 15–20 minutes, stirring, until it thickens a little."],[null,"Add the apricots, figs, raisins and dates and cook gently for another 10–15 minutes, stirring, until thick like a soft jam."],[null,"Turn off the heat, stir in the almonds, pistachios and pine nuts and remove the cinnamon sticks."],[null,"Serve warm or cold in small dishes; it keeps in a sealed box in the fridge for up to 2 weeks."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: no sugar added beyond the qamar al-din (the traditional recipe uses about 3 glasses of sugar), 12 g ghee instead of 2 glasses, a moderate amount of nuts, and a small portion."],[null,"Kidney tip: dried fruit (apricots, figs, dates, raisins) and nuts are very high in potassium; keep to 2 tablespoons on the day, and avoid it if you are on a low-potassium diet."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has about 30 g carbohydrate, mostly fruit sugar; have half a portion with an egg or low-fat cheese at the Eid breakfast rather than on its own."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Arabic Wikipedia (Dibyaza), English Wikipedia (Saudi Arabian cuisine)"]]},"8948148":{"s":[[null,"Mix both flours with a quarter of the salt, add the warm water gradually and knead to a firm, smooth dough. Cover and rest for 30 minutes."],[null,"Heat the oil in a wide pot, add the cumin, cardamom pods and cinnamon, then the lamb, and brown it on all sides."],[null,"Add the onion and garlic and stir for 3 minutes, then the tomatoes, black pepper, turmeric and black lime."],[null,"Pour in the hot water, cover leaving a small gap and simmer for 1 hour until the meat is nearly tender, skimming off foam and fat."],[null,"Add the zucchini, carrot and the rest of the salt."],[null,"With wet hands divide the dough into 12 balls and flatten each in your palm into a thick oval."],[null,"Lower the discs into the simmering broth one at a time, leaving a minute between each so they do not stick together."],[null,"Cover and simmer 25–30 minutes, gently shaking the pot every 5 minutes, until the dumplings and meat are cooked."],[null,"Arrange the daghabees and meat on a platter with the broth and vegetables in a bowl, and dip the dumplings into the broth to eat."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: no stock cubes (common recipes add two and a half), lean lamb with the fat skimmed off the broth, more whole wheat than white flour, and vegetables added to the broth."],[null,"Kidney tip: tomato, brown flour and meat add potassium and phosphorus; use more white flour if you need to limit phosphorus, and keep to three dumplings with a little broth."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one plate has about 57 g carbohydrate, mostly from the dough; keep to three small dumplings and serve with a green salad."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (Mawsouat Al Tabkh), Arabic Wikipedia, Al Jawhara Magazine"]]},"8115611":{"s":[[null,"Toast the coriander seeds in a dry pan over low heat for 5–6 minutes, stirring, until they darken slightly and smell fragrant, then tip onto a plate."],[null,"Toast the cumin in the same pan for just 2–3 minutes until fragrant, then the sesame until golden, and let everything cool."],[null,"Grind the coriander, cumin, black pepper, dried rose, citric acid and salt to a fine powder in a spice grinder."],[null,"Stir the whole toasted sesame into the powder and mix well."],[null,"Keep the dagga in a sealed jar in a cool, dry place for up to 3 months; serve 1 tbsp over low-fat yoghurt, eggs or salad."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: 3 g salt for the whole batch (about 1.4%) instead of table salt plus kamrani salt at around 5% in the traditional blend; the sour citric acid and toasted spices make up for the salt."],[null,"Kidney tip: sesame and cumin contain phosphorus and potassium; one tablespoon is fine, but watch what you serve it with: yoghurt is a source of phosphorus, so keep it to half a pot."],[null,"Diabetes tip: the dagga itself is low in carbohydrate (about 4 g per tablespoon); serve it with eggs, vegetables and salad for strong flavour without sugar."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Mawdoo3, Tawabel7 spice shop"]]},"8556931":{"s":[[null,"Blend the tomatoes, chillies and garlic until smooth."],[null,"Pour into a small pan over medium heat, add the tomato paste, cumin, kabsa spices and water, bring to the boil, then simmer for 10 minutes until slightly thick."],[null,"Add the olive oil, lemon juice, vinegar and salt and stir for 3 minutes over low heat."],[null,"Take off the heat, stir in the parsley and serve warm or cold beside kabsa. Keep in a closed jar in the fridge for up to 4 days."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: no ketchup (high in sugar and salt) and no stock cubes, no-salt-added tomato paste, one spoon of oil instead of a lot, and sourness from lemon and vinegar instead of salt."],[null,"Kidney tip: tomatoes are high in potassium; keep to 2 tablespoons of dagoos with the meal, and you can replace half the tomatoes with roasted red sweet pepper."],[null,"Diabetes tip: dagoos is low in carbohydrate (about 7 g per portion) and its flavour helps you eat a smaller amount of rice."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Sayidaty Kitchen (Saudi dagoos), Atyab Tabkha (spicy dagoos for kabsa)"]]},"8882310":{"s":[[null,"Heat 1 tbsp of the oil in a pot and cook the onion with the whole spices until soft and lightly golden, then add the garlic and orange peel and stir."],[null,"Add the chicken and turn it until it changes colour, then add the tomato, tomato paste and a quarter of the carrots and stir for 2 minutes."],[null,"Add 800 ml hot water, bring to the boil, then simmer for 25–30 minutes, adding the ground spice for the last 5 minutes."],[null,"Lift the chicken onto an oven tray, strain the broth and measure 400 ml."],[null,"Return the broth to the pot with the salt; when it boils add the drained rice and half of the remaining carrots. Cook on high until the liquid is absorbed, then cover tightly and leave on very low heat for 20 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile mix 3 tbsp of broth with the turmeric and 1 tsp of the oil, brush it over the chicken and grill at 220°C (top heat) for 10–15 minutes, brushing once or twice, until browned."],[null,"Heat the rest of the oil in a frying pan and stir the remaining carrots until soft, then add the raisins for a minute."],[null,"Spoon the rice onto a platter, scatter the carrots and raisins around the edge, set the chicken in the middle and serve with a tomato and cucumber salad."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: skinless chicken instead of a whole bird with skin, only 2 tbsp oil, no-salt-added tomato paste, no seasoning powder, soy sauce or sugar on the carrots, and orange peel and black lime for flavour instead of extra salt."],[null,"Kidney tip: tomato, tomato paste, raisins and carrots add potassium; use one tomato, cut the raisins to 15 g, and keep to about 90 g cooked chicken per portion."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has about 59 g carbohydrate; keep to 150 g cooked rice, you can make half of it brown rice, and serve with a large salad."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Hia Magazine, Sayidaty Kitchen"]]},"8732321":{"s":[[null,"Wash the Hasawi rice and soak it in warm water for 1 hour."],[null,"Put the chicken in a pot with the quartered onion, tomato, carrot, whole spices and water. Bring to the boil, lower the heat, skim, and simmer 30–35 minutes until cooked."],[null,"Lift out the chicken, rub it with the bezar, turmeric and a little broth, and brown it in a 220 °C oven for 15–20 minutes."],[null,"Strain the broth and keep about 700 ml; mash the tomato and carrot into it if you like."],[null,"Return the broth to the pot with the tomato paste and garlic, add the drained rice and the salt, bring to the boil, then cover and cook on low heat 35–40 minutes until the red rice is tender and has absorbed the broth; add a little hot water if needed."],[null,"For the topping: warm the olive oil in a pan and cook the sliced onion, covered, on low heat for 15 minutes until soft and golden; add the curry, dried lime, cardamom, cinnamon and raisins and stir for 2 minutes."],[null,"Lay the browned chicken on the rice, set a small heatproof bowl with the ghee in the middle of the pot, drop the hot charcoal into it, close the lid at once and leave 10 minutes."],[null,"Remove the bowl and charcoal, spoon the rice onto a platter, top with the chicken and onion topping, sprinkle with the almonds, and serve with a green salad and daqoos."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: skinless chicken, homemade broth without stock cubes, 1 tbsp oil instead of about 80 ml, ghee only for smoking, fewer raisins, dry-toasted almonds instead of fried nuts, and under ¼ tsp salt per serving."],[null,"Kidney tip: red rice, almonds, raisins and tomato paste add potassium and phosphorus; you can swap half the red rice for white basmati, cut or skip the raisins and almonds, and keep to one serving."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one serving has about 150 g cooked rice; red Hasawi rice is high in fibre, so serve it with a large salad and go light on the raisins."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Mawdoo3, Hia Magazine, Dawan"]]},"8795911":{"s":[[null,"Put the lamb in a pot with the onion, garlic, cardamom, cloves, cinnamon, bay leaf, black pepper and water. Bring to the boil, skim, then cover and simmer for 60–75 minutes until tender."],[null,"Lift out the lamb and keep it covered. Strain the broth and measure 400 ml for the rice (top up with water if needed)."],[null,"In a frying pan, heat 1 tbsp of the oil, toast the almonds for a minute and lift them out. Add the carrots and stir for 5 minutes, sprinkle in the sugar and stir until glossy and lightly caramelised, add 3 tbsp water and cover for 5 minutes until tender, then add the raisins for a minute."],[null,"In the pot, heat the rest of the oil and toast the cumin seeds for half a minute. Add the measured broth and the salt; when it boils add the drained rice and cook over high heat until most of the liquid is absorbed."],[null,"Arrange the lamb and half of the carrots on the rice, cover tightly (you can wrap the lid in a cloth) and leave on very low heat for 20–25 minutes."],[null,"Spoon the rice and lamb onto a platter, top with the remaining carrots, raisins and almonds, sprinkle with lemon juice and serve with lemon wedges and a green salad."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: 2 tbsp oil instead of the large amount used in traditional recipes, only 10 g sugar for the carrots instead of a heavy caramel, trimmed leg of lamb, 150 g cooked rice per portion with more carrots, and no stock cubes."],[null,"Kidney tip: raisins, almonds, carrots and meat add potassium and phosphorus; cut the raisins to 20 g and the almonds to 10 g, keep to about 60–90 g cooked meat per portion, and boil and drain the carrots before glazing them."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has about 63 g carbohydrate; keep to 150 g cooked rice, you can make half of it brown rice, and start the meal with a large salad."],[null,"Suitable for: a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Layalina Yummy, Duyoufi Foods"]]},"8855503":{"s":[[null,"Boil the water with the grated ginger and cardamom over medium heat for 15–20 minutes, then strain and keep the ginger water."],[null,"In another pan whisk the cold milk with the rice flour and sugar until there are no lumps."],[null,"Add the ginger water and cook over low heat, stirring all the time, until it boils and starts to thicken, about 8–10 minutes."],[null,"Add the ground almonds and rose water and stir for 2 more minutes until creamy."],[null,"Pour into warm mugs, top with the chopped almonds and a pinch of cinnamon or ginger and serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: liquid low-fat milk instead of full-fat milk powder, 40 g sugar instead of about 100 g, and 30 g almonds instead of about 140 g."],[null,"If you can get pure salep powder (orchid root) from a spice seller, use 1 tbsp of it instead of the rice flour and sprinkle it slowly over the hot milk while whisking so it does not form lumps."],[null,"Kidney tip: milk and almonds are sources of phosphorus and potassium; you can replace half the milk with water or a plant milk without added phosphate, and keep to half a mug."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one mug has about 22 g carbohydrate; cut the sugar to 1 tbsp or use a zero-calorie sweetener, and drink it with a meal rather than on its own."],[null,"Suitable for: heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Sayidaty Kitchen, Sahha wa Hana"]]},"8510512":{"s":[[null,"Put the chicken in a pot with the water, bring to the boil and skim off the foam."],[null,"Add the onion and whole spices and simmer 30 minutes until the chicken is cooked, then lift it out and strain the broth."],[null,"Measure about 1 l of broth back into the pot, add the drained rice and half the salt and simmer 30–40 minutes until the rice is very soft; add a little boiling water if it dries."],[null,"Add the hot milk little by little and beat the rice with a wooden spoon until creamy and smooth, then leave 10 minutes on very low heat."],[null,"Brush the chicken with the oil, turmeric, spices and remaining salt and brown it under the oven grill at 220°C for 10 minutes."],[null,"Blend the dagoos ingredients and serve chilled."],[null,"Warm the ghee with the mastic for a few seconds, pour it over the saleeq in the serving dish, top with the chicken and serve at once with the dagoos and a green salad."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: skinless chicken browned under the grill instead of fried, low-fat milk instead of full-fat milk powder, very little ghee, no bouillon and much less salt."],[null,"Kidney tip: milk and chicken are high in phosphorus and tomato in potassium; keep to one portion (90–120 g cooked chicken), and you can swap half the milk for broth. Ask your dietitian."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one plate has about 51 g carbohydrate from soft, quickly absorbed rice; do not go beyond it, and start with the salad and dagoos."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Arabic Wikipedia (Saleeq Taifi), Sayidaty Kitchen"]]},"8827618":{"s":[[null,"Put the lamb in a pot with the water, bring to the boil and skim off the foam."],[null,"Add the onion and whole spices and simmer 1 to 1½ hours until the lamb is tender, then lift it out and strain the broth."],[null,"Measure about 1 l of broth back into the pot, add the drained rice and half the salt and simmer 30–40 minutes without much stirring until the rice is very soft; add a little broth if it dries."],[null,"Add the hot milk little by little, stirring and beating the rice with a wooden spoon until creamy and smooth, then leave 10 minutes on very low heat."],[null,"Brush the lamb with the oil, turmeric, spices and remaining salt and brown it under the oven grill at 220°C for 10–15 minutes."],[null,"Blend the dagoos ingredients and serve chilled."],[null,"Warm the ghee with the mastic for a few seconds, pour it over the saleeq in the serving dish, top with the lamb and serve at once with the dagoos and a green salad."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: lean, trimmed lamb, low-fat milk instead of full-fat or powdered milk, very little ghee, no bouillon and much less salt; the flavour comes from cardamom and mastic."],[null,"Kidney tip: milk and meat are high in phosphorus and tomato in potassium; keep to one portion (90–100 g cooked meat), and you can swap half the milk for broth. Ask your dietitian."],[null,"Diabetes tip: long-cooked soft rice raises blood sugar quickly; one plate has about 51 g carbohydrate, so do not go beyond it and start with the salad."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Arabic Wikipedia (Saleeq Taifi), Sayidaty Kitchen"]]},"8026159":{"s":[[null,"Heat the teaspoon of oil in a non-stick pan and soften the onion, then add the meat and stir until browned and dry."],[null,"Add the garlic, chilli, spices and salt and stir for 2 minutes, then take off the heat, add the coriander and parsley and let the filling cool completely."],[null,"Heat the oven to 200 °C and line a tray with baking paper."],[null,"Put a spoonful of filling at one end of a pastry strip, fold it over and over into a triangle to the end, and seal the edge with the flour paste."],[null,"Arrange the triangles on the tray and brush the tops lightly with the oil."],[null,"Bake for 15–18 minutes, turning halfway, until golden and crisp, and serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: baking instead of deep-frying saves most of the fat, with lean meat and less salt."],[null,"Kidney tip: ready samboosa pastry contains sodium and the meat contains phosphorus; keep to 4 pieces, and you can replace some of the meat with grated zucchini."],[null,"Diabetes tip: 4 pieces have about 21 g carbohydrate; eat them with a vegetable soup or salad rather than adding more pieces."],[null,"You can freeze the triangles before baking and bake them straight from frozen, adding 5 minutes."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (Saudi cooking book), Sayidaty Kitchen, Arab News, Foodie Atlas"]]},"8795821":{"s":[[null,"Melt the ghee in a wide pot over medium heat, add the broken vermicelli and stir constantly for 4–5 minutes until evenly golden but not dark."],[null,"Add the sugar and cardamom and stir for 1 minute."],[null,"Add the hot water and the saffron in rose water and stir, then cover, lower the heat and cook for 8–10 minutes until the water is absorbed and the vermicelli is tender."],[null,"Fluff with a fork to separate the strands and serve warm."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: less ghee and less than half the usual sugar, no salt, and flavour from cardamom, saffron and rose water."],[null,"Kidney tip: this dish is relatively low in potassium, sodium and phosphorus, so it is a suitable sweet in one portion; avoid adding nuts or milk."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has about 47 g carbohydrate; have half a portion with a boiled egg or a vegetable omelette (balaleet style) to slow the rise in blood sugar, and choose whole-wheat vermicelli."],[null,"Suitable for: heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Cookpad Saudi Arabia, WebTeb"]]},"8892072":{"s":[[null,"Heat the olive oil in a wide pan and cook the onion until soft, then add the garlic, chillies and bell pepper and stir for 2 minutes."],[null,"Stir in the cumin and bezar, then add the tomatoes, tomato paste and 50 ml water and cover for 8–10 minutes until the sauce is thick."],[null,"Whisk the whole eggs with the egg whites, salt and black pepper and pour them over the sauce."],[null,"Stir gently on low heat now and then until the eggs are set as you like, then sprinkle with coriander and serve hot with whole-wheat bread."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: 1 tbsp olive oil for the whole pan, less salt, 2 of the eggs replaced by whites to lower cholesterol, and more vegetables."],[null,"Kidney tip: tomatoes and tomato paste are high in potassium and egg yolk contains phosphorus; you can cut the tomatoes to 2 with more peppers, and use more egg whites."],[null,"Diabetes tip: shakshouka is low in carbohydrate and high in protein; the carbohydrate comes from the bread, so have half a whole-wheat flatbread."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, vegetarians, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Sayidaty, Layalina Yummy"]]},"8372036":{"s":[[null,"Drain the soaked wheat and put it in a pot with the water, cinnamon, cardamom pods and cloves; cover and simmer for about 1½ hours until the grains are soft, adding hot water as needed."],[null,"Rinse the rice, add it to the wheat and cook 25–30 minutes until soft and thick, then take out the cinnamon, cloves and cardamom pods."],[null,"Dissolve the cornstarch in a little cold milk, add it with the rest of the milk, the sugar and ground cardamom, and stir constantly for 5–7 minutes until thick like a pudding."],[null,"Add the rose water and half the raisins and apricots, stir for 1 minute and take off the heat."],[null,"Spoon into 10 small bowls, top with the rest of the dried fruit and the chopped nuts, and serve warm or chilled."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: less than half the traditional sugar (80 g instead of about 200 g for the same amount of grain), skimmed instead of full-fat milk, and a moderate amount of nuts and dried fruit in small portions."],[null,"Kidney tip: whole wheat, milk, nuts, dried apricots and raisins contain phosphorus and potassium; keep to one small bowl and cut down the apricots and raisins or swap them for a little grated apple."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one bowl has about 37 g carbohydrate, including 8 g added sugar; eat it after a meal with protein and vegetables, and you can reduce the sugar further or use a sweetener."],[null,"Suitable for: heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Hia Magazine (Chef Fahad Bukhari), Cookpad Saudi Arabia"]]},"8563508":{"s":[[null,"Toast the whole-wheat flour in a dry pot over low heat for 3–4 minutes, stirring, until it smells nutty, then let it cool a little."],[null,"Add the salt, then the warm water gradually, and mix to a soft dough a little thicker than cake batter; rest it for 15 minutes."],[null,"Grease a non-stick pan or tray with the first teaspoon of ghee, spread the dough in it and bake in an oven heated to 200 °C for about 30 minutes, or cook over low heat, turning once, until done on both sides."],[null,"While it is hot, put the bread in a clean bag or bowl and knead it with your hands (protected with a cloth) until smooth and cohesive. Add a spoonful of hot water if it gets dry."],[null,"Shape it in a serving bowl, make a well in the centre, pour the melted ghee into it, drizzle the honey around the edge and decorate with the dates."],[null,"Divide into 6 small portions and serve warm with Arabic coffee."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: whole-wheat flour instead of white, about 2.5 g ghee per portion instead of large amounts, half the usual honey with dates for sweetness, and small portions."],[null,"Kidney tip: whole-wheat flour and dates have more phosphorus and potassium than white flour; keep to one portion, and you can swap half the whole-wheat flour for white flour and use one date per portion."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has about 42 g carbohydrate; count it in your meal, have it with unsweetened coffee and do not add extra honey."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Yummy Layalina, Bayut"]]},"8931533":{"s":[[null,"Put the meat in a pot with the water, onion, garlic, chilli and whole spices, bring to the boil and skim off the foam."],[null,"Lower the heat, cover and cook for 1½ hours until nearly tender, then add the carrots, zucchini, tomato and salt and cook for 20 minutes more."],[null,"For the aseeda: boil the 300 ml water with the pinch of salt in a non-stick pot, add the flour all at once and stir fast with a wooden stick or spoon until it forms one mass."],[null,"Add 100 ml of the hot broth gradually and keep beating (folding and pressing from the bottom up) on low heat for 10 minutes until smooth and firm."],[null,"Shape it in serving bowls, make a well in the centre and put a little ghee in it."],[null,"Serve at once with the meat, vegetables and broth, and sprinkle the spices over the broth to taste."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: lean meat instead of fatty ribs and shoulder, vegetables in the broth, and less ghee and salt; the honey-and-ghee version is best kept for occasions and small amounts."],[null,"Kidney tip: whole-wheat flour and meat contain phosphorus (about 520 mg per portion) and the broth carries potassium; drink only a little broth, and you can make the aseeda with half white flour to lower phosphorus."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has about 54 g carbohydrate with 9 g fibre from the whole wheat; serve it with green salad and avoid adding honey."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, WebTeb, Food2mins"]]},"8595227":{"s":[[null,"Mix the flour with the nigella seeds and salt, then whisk in the water gradually to a batter slightly thicker than cake batter. Leave it to rest for 30 minutes."],[null,"Heat a griddle or non-stick pan over medium heat and wipe it with a little of the oil on kitchen paper."],[null,"Pour in a ladle of batter and spread it into a thin round. Cook until browned underneath, flip and brown the other side. Repeat with the rest of the batter."],[null,"For the basil ghee: toast the spoon of flour in a small pan over low heat until golden and fragrant. Add the ghee; when it melts and starts to foam, add the basil, cover for under a minute, then turn off the heat, let it cool a little and strain."],[null,"Tear the warm breads by hand into medium pieces in a serving dish."],[null,"Pour the basil ghee and then the honey over the bread and serve warm with low-fat milk, tea or coffee."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: all the flour is wholewheat, the sugar in the dough is gone, 25 g ghee serves six instead of a whole block of butter, and the honey is cut to 10 g per serving."],[null,"Kidney tip: wholewheat flour has more phosphorus and potassium than white flour; you can use half wholewheat and half white flour, keep to one portion, and drink tea or light coffee instead of milk."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has about 45 g carbohydrate including 8 g added sugar; serve the honey on the side and use little, and eat a boiled egg or low-fat laban with it to slow the rise in blood sugar."],[null,"Suitable for: heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Saudipedia (Asir folk foods), Mawdoo3"]]},"8627840":{"s":[[null,"Spread the bread squares on a tray and toast them in a 200 °C oven for 8–10 minutes until crisp."],[null,"Put the lettuce, cucumber, tomato, peppers, radishes, spring onions, parsley and mint in a large bowl."],[null,"Whisk the olive oil with the lemon juice, vinegar, sumac, cumin, garlic and salt until slightly thick."],[null,"Pour the dressing over the vegetables and toss, then add the toasted bread just before serving and dust with a little sumac."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: the bread is whole wheat and oven-toasted instead of fried, olive oil is 5 g per serving, and salt is ½ g per serving, with sumac and lemon carrying the flavour."],[null,"Kidney tip: tomatoes and parsley contain potassium; you can replace half the tomatoes with cucumber and peppers, and use white bread instead of whole wheat to lower phosphorus."],[null,"Diabetes tip: fattoush is low in carbohydrate and high in fibre, a good way to fill half the plate next to rice or grilled meat."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, vegetarians."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Arabic Wikipedia, Sayidaty"]]},"8874214":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oven to 190°C with top and bottom heat and line two trays with baking paper."],[null,"Whisk the egg with the sugar, oil, soaked saffron, cardamom, ginger and salt."],[null,"Mix the flour with the milk powder and baking powder, add it to the egg mixture with the water a little at a time, and knead to a firm dough that is easy to shape and does not stick."],[null,"Divide the dough into 16 balls and flatten each into a round about 1 cm thick. Press it with a wooden fatit mould, or with a basket or sieve, to make the pattern."],[null,"Bake for 15–20 minutes until the edges and bottoms are golden, then cool on a rack."],[null,"For the syrup: simmer the water with the honey, cinnamon, cardamom and black lime for 2 minutes until slightly thick, then strain."],[null,"Serve each round with 1 tsp of syrup spooned over it or on the side for dipping."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: 60 g sugar instead of about 200 g, 60 ml oil instead of about 180 ml, skimmed milk powder, and a lighter honey syrup in a small amount per round."],[null,"Kidney tip: wholewheat flour, milk powder and baking powder contain phosphorus; keep to one round, and you can use low-sodium baking powder and half white flour."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one round has about 20 g carbohydrate including 6 g added sugar; have one with unsweetened Arabic coffee and skip the syrup if you can."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Arabic Wikipedia (Fatit), Khaleej Kitchen (Qassim kleicha)"]]},"8813736":{"s":[[null,"Mix the flour with the milk powder, yeast, salt, ginger and cinnamon, add the water gradually and knead a soft, firm dough."],[null,"Oil a sheet of foil with 1 tsp of the oil, shape the dough on it into a thick round (about 3 cm), wrap it up and leave 30 minutes."],[null,"Bake at 180 °C for 50–60 minutes until cooked through, then open the foil and leave 10 more minutes to brown."],[null,"Cook the onion in the rest of the oil over medium heat until soft and golden, then add the cinnamon and dried lime."],[null,"Crumble the hot loaf coarsely by hand or in a food processor, removing any hard edges."],[null,"Rub the crumbs with the warm ghee and chopped dates until evenly mixed, then fold in the onion and serve warm with lemon."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: much less ghee than usual with a little olive oil, dates for sweetness instead of icing sugar or honey, and a whole-wheat loaf."],[null,"Kidney tip: whole-wheat flour and dates are high in potassium and phosphorus; keep to one small bowl, and you can swap a third of the whole-wheat flour for white flour and use fewer dates."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one bowl has about 48 g carbohydrate, including the sugar from the dates; eat it with laban or unsweetened Arabic coffee and stop at one bowl."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, WebTeb, Cookpad"]]},"8806717":{"s":[[null,"Soak the truffles in water for an hour, then scrub them one by one, scrape off the thin skin with a knife, peel the base where the sand collects, and rinse several times until no sand is left."],[null,"Cut the truffles into medium cubes."],[null,"Heat the oil in a pan over medium heat and soften the onion without browning it. Add the garlic, then the bell pepper and chilli, and stir for a minute."],[null,"Add the truffles, bezar, turmeric and black pepper and stir well. Lower the heat, cover and cook for 30 minutes, stirring now and then; the truffles will release their water."],[null,"Uncover and raise the heat a little for the last 10 minutes until the liquid evaporates and the truffles brown slightly, then add the salt."],[null,"Sprinkle with fresh coriander and serve with rice or wholewheat bread."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: olive oil instead of butter and ghee, no seasoning powder or stock cubes, and only ½ tsp salt for four people. The nutrition is calculated using white mushrooms as an approximate stand-in for faqa."],[null,"Kidney tip: truffles and mushrooms are high in potassium; keep to half a portion (about 150 g truffles) with more onion and bell pepper, and you can boil the cut truffles for 10 minutes and drain them before cooking to lower the potassium."],[null,"Diabetes tip: the dish is low in carbohydrate; serve it with 150 g cooked rice (basmati, or half brown) or a quarter of a wholewheat flatbread, with a salad."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, vegetarians, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Mawdoo3, Sayidaty Kitchen"]]},"8488762":{"s":[[null,"Drain the soaked beans, cover with water by about 5 cm and cook over medium heat for 30 minutes (or 30 minutes in a pressure cooker)."],[null,"Add the lentils and date and cook on very low heat for 1–2 hours (or 30 more minutes under pressure) until the beans are soft and the lentils have melted, adding boiling water if needed."],[null,"For the dakous: finely chop or briefly blend the tomato, garlic, coriander and chilli, then add the lemon juice."],[null,"Mash the beans lightly and stir in the salt, cumin, tahini and 3 tbsp of the dakous."],[null,"For a smoky flavour (optional): set a small bowl with a hot piece of charcoal in the middle of the beans, add a drop of oil, cover for 1 minute, then remove it."],[null,"Spoon into bowls, top with the remaining dakous, a pinch of cumin and the olive oil, and serve with whole-wheat bread."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: no ghee and no stock cubes, less tahini and oil, and less than half the salt of a typical fool shop."],[null,"Kidney tip: fava beans, lentils and tahini are very high in potassium and phosphorus; take half a bowl with bread and vegetables, and soaking the beans, changing the water several times and cooking them in fresh water lowers potassium a little."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one bowl has about 49 g carbohydrate and plenty of fibre (about 18 g); eat it with a small whole-wheat flatbread instead of tamees, with cucumber and tomato."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, vegetarians, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Sayidaty Kitchen, Mawdoo3"]]},"8547419":{"s":[[null,"For the qursan bread: knead the flour, salt and water until smooth, rest for 30 minutes, then divide into 4 balls and roll each out very thin."],[null,"Cook each sheet on a hot dry saj or pan for 1–2 minutes per side until dry and speckled, then let it cool and break it into pieces about half the size of your palm."],[null,"For the broth: heat the oil in a pot and soften the onion, then add the meat and stir until it changes colour; add the spices, tomatoes and tomato paste and let it thicken for 5 minutes."],[null,"Pour in the boiling water, add the dried limes and chillies and simmer on medium heat for 45 minutes until the meat is almost tender (or 25 minutes in a pressure cooker)."],[null,"Add the carrot, then after 5 minutes the rest of the vegetables and the salt, and cook for 15–20 minutes until tender; then lift the meat out and set aside."],[null,"Heat the oven to 180°C. In an ovenproof pot or deep dish put a little broth, then a layer of qursan, then broth with vegetables, then some of the onion and dried lime; repeat until everything is used."],[null,"Push a spoon down into the layers in several places so the broth reaches all the bread, arrange the meat in the centre, cover with foil and bake for 25–30 minutes until the broth is absorbed."],[null,"Sprinkle with spring onion and serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: homemade fat-free whole-wheat qursan, no sugar, apricot paste or browned butter on top, lean meat, little oil, more vegetables and about half the usual salt; dried lime, cinnamon and cardamom replace the date-based masmana spice."],[null,"Kidney tip: whole-wheat flour, pumpkin, tomatoes, tomato paste, carrot and meat are high in potassium and phosphorus; keep to one plate, and you can halve the pumpkin and tomatoes and use more zucchini and green beans. Ask your dietitian about your own portion."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one plate has about 57 g carbohydrate with 11 g fibre; the qursan is the starch of the meal, so do not add bread or rice, and add a green salad."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Arabic Wikipedia (Qursan), Saudipedia (Qursan)"]]},"8447746":{"s":[[null,"Toast the flour in a dry non-stick pan over low heat, stirring all the time, for 8–10 minutes until golden and fragrant."],[null,"Add the butter and stir it into the flour until melted and slightly crumbly."],[null,"Add the dates and stir and press with the spoon for 5 minutes until soft and mixed with the flour; add a little hot water if it gets dry."],[null,"Add the cardamom, cinnamon and ginger, then the yoghurt, and stir for 2 minutes over low heat until smooth."],[null,"Spread it in a serving dish, mark into 8 portions and serve hot with Arabic coffee."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: 25 g butter instead of 100–150 g, low-fat yoghurt instead of cream, no added sugar, and a small fixed portion (55 g) instead of a full bowl."],[null,"Kidney tip: dates are very high in potassium, and wholewheat flour and yoghurt contain phosphorus; keep to one small portion on special occasions and ask your dietitian."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has about 30 g carbohydrate, mostly date sugar; eat it after a balanced meal rather than as a snack on its own, and do not have more than one portion."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Sayidaty Kitchen (qishd), Atyab Tabkha (Qassimi qishd)"]]},"8543483":{"s":[[null,"Bring the water to the boil in the coffee pot (mulgama), then turn the heat down to low."],[null,"Add the coffee, stir once and let it simmer gently for 12–15 minutes without boiling over."],[null,"Turn off the heat, cover and leave 3–5 minutes so the grounds settle to the bottom."],[null,"Put the cardamom, saffron and cloves in the dallah or flask, then pour the coffee over them slowly, leaving the grounds behind."],[null,"Leave 2 minutes to infuse, then serve in finjans with the dates."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: no sugar, coffee creamer or milk powder (which some modern versions add), and the portion is 3 finjans with 2 small dates instead of sweets on the side."],[null,"Kidney tip: the coffee itself is low in potassium at this amount, but dates are high in potassium; keep to 2 dates at most and count the coffee in your daily fluid allowance if you have one."],[null,"Diabetes and blood pressure tip: one serving has about 13 g carbohydrate, all from the dates; do not go above 2 dates, and limit yourself to 3–4 finjans a day as caffeine can raise blood pressure for a while."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (Mawsouat Al Tabkh), Saudipedia, Sayidaty Kitchen"]]},"8861015":{"s":[[null,"Trim visible fat from the meat, put it in a pot with 1.5 l water, the onion, garlic, carrot and whole spices, bring to the boil skimming the foam, then simmer 1½ hours until tender."],[null,"Rinse the rice and soak it for 30 minutes. Lift out the meat, strain the stock and skim the fat off the top."],[null,"Heat the oven to 220 °C. Mix the tomato paste with the oil and half the saffron, brush it over the meat, and roast on a tray for 15–20 minutes until browned."],[null,"Bring 400 ml of the stock to the boil with the ghee, spices, turmeric and salt, add the drained rice and cook on high heat until the stock is absorbed, then cover and cook on low heat for 20 minutes and drizzle the rest of the saffron on top."],[null,"Boil the spaghetti in the remaining stock (or water) until tender and drain."],[null,"Toast the almonds in a dry pan until lightly golden."],[null,"Spread the rice on a serving platter, arrange the pasta around the edges and the sliced meat in the centre, top with the almonds, raisins and boiled eggs, and serve with the tomato, cucumber and lemon."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: lean, trimmed lamb leg, rice and whole-wheat pasta at about 150 g cooked per person, almonds toasted without oil, less ghee, and homemade stock instead of stock cubes."],[null,"Kidney tip: meat, egg and almonds contain phosphorus and raisins and tomato paste add potassium; keep to 90 g meat, leave out the raisins, and you can use only the egg whites."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one plate has about 56 g carbohydrate; start with the salad, and you can swap half the rice for brown rice or bulgur."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Fatafeat, Wikipedia (Quzi)"]]},"8606692":{"s":[[null,"Grind the soaked wheat in a food processor or mincer until fine, then add the flour, cumin, turmeric and salt and knead into a sticky, firm dough."],[null,"Mix the filling ingredients."],[null,"Divide the dough into 12 balls, flatten each by hand on a floured surface, put a tablespoon of filling in the centre, gather the edges to seal, then flatten again into a thick disc about 9 cm across."],[null,"Bring a large pot of unsalted water to the boil, drop the discs in one at a time and lift them out with a slotted spoon once they float (about 1 minute); leave to dry on a rack."],[null,"Heat a griddle or non-stick pan, brush the discs lightly with oil and brown for 3–4 minutes on each side until golden and crisp (or bake at 220 °C for 15–20 minutes, turning once)."],[null,"Serve hot with lemon and a green salad. The boiled discs can be frozen, each wrapped separately, and browned when needed."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: browned with a brush of oil on a griddle or in the oven instead of deep frying, boiled in unsalted water, and no processed or cheddar cheese in the dough, with little salt."],[null,"Kidney tip: whole wheat is high in phosphorus and potassium; you can replace part of the wheat with extra white flour, and keep to one or two patties with a low-protein meal."],[null,"Diabetes tip: two patties have about 47 g carbohydrate from fibre-rich whole grain; count them instead of bread or rice in the meal and serve with salad and low-fat laban."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Atyab Tabkha (Hasawi kubba), Al-Yaum newspaper (making Hasawi kubba)"]]},"8771457":{"s":[[null,"Rinse the liver, remove the membranes and veins, pat it dry and cut it into long thin strips."],[null,"Heat the oil in a wide pan or saj over high heat. Add the bay leaves, chilli and onion and stir until the onion softens and starts to brown, then add the garlic for half a minute."],[null,"Add the liver in two batches so the pan stays hot, and stir for 3–4 minutes until browned on all sides."],[null,"Sprinkle in the cumin, dried coriander, turmeric and black pepper and stir."],[null,"Add the tomato and then the bell pepper, stir for 2 minutes, then cover for 2 minutes over medium heat so the liver stays moist in the tomato juices. Do not overcook or it will dry out."],[null,"Turn off the heat, add the salt, lemon juice and fresh coriander, stir and serve hot straight away."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: no suet, heart or kidneys, only 2 tbsp olive oil for four people, and a small amount of salt added at the end, with lemon and spices for flavour."],[null,"Heart tip: liver is very high in cholesterol (about 460 mg per serving), so people with heart disease or high cholesterol should eat it once a week or less; half a portion is enough."],[null,"Kidney tip: liver is high in phosphorus and protein, and tomato and peppers add potassium; keep to half a portion (about 60 g cooked liver), use one tomato only and more onion and bell pepper."],[null,"Diabetes tip: the dish itself is low in carbohydrate; serve it with a quarter of a wholewheat flatbread (about 30 g) and a green salad instead of white bread."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, House of Saud (Saudi breakfast guide), Sayidaty Kitchen"]]},"8273097":{"s":[[null,"Wash the rice, soak it for 30 minutes, then drain."],[null,"Mix two thirds of the onion with the ground loomi, turmeric and mixed spice."],[null,"Heat 3 tsp ghee in a pot, add the spiced onion and whole spices and cook until soft and lightly browned, then add the garlic."],[null,"Add the tomato paste and toast it for 1 minute, then the tomatoes, bell pepper and half the coriander, and cook 5 minutes until thick."],[null,"Add the lamb and turn it in the mixture for 5 minutes, then the hot water and ground cardamom; cover and simmer 1½ hours until tender (or 35 minutes in a pressure cooker). Skim off the fat and add the salt."],[null,"Lift out the lamb, keep about 375 ml broth in the pot, add the rice and boil on high heat until the broth drops."],[null,"For the topping: cook the remaining onion in 1 tsp ghee with a splash of water until golden, then spread it over the rice with the lamb."],[null,"Cover and cook on the lowest heat for 25 minutes, then serve sprinkled with the rest of the coriander, with green salad."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: ghee limited to one teaspoon per person instead of pouring it over the top, trimmed meat, no stock cubes, and much less salt, relying on black lime and coriander for flavour."],[null,"Kidney tip: tomatoes and tomato paste raise potassium and the meat is high in phosphorus; on a low-potassium diet cut the paste to 1 tbsp and keep to the meat portion (about 100 g cooked). Skip a large yoghurt salad on the side if your phosphorus is high."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one plate has about 54 g carbohydrate; serve with a large green salad, and you can mix in half brown rice."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (Mawsouat Al Tabkh), Chef Hessa (Cookinsta), Food2mins"]]},"8282733":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a wide pan over medium heat, add the onion and cook for 12–15 minutes until caramelised and deep golden; add a spoon of water if it starts to stick."],[null,"Add the garlic and spices and stir for 1 minute until fragrant."],[null,"Add the tomatoes and tomato paste, stir and simmer gently for 8–10 minutes until thick."],[null,"Add the salt and spring onion, stir for 30 seconds, then take off the heat and serve hot over maraheef or jareesh, or beside rice."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: a little olive oil instead of a finjan (about 60 ml) of oil or ghee, no-salt-added tomato paste, no stock cubes, and flavour from dried lime and spices instead of salt."],[null,"Kidney tip: tomatoes and tomato paste are high in potassium; use only 2 tomatoes with more onion, and keep to 2 tablespoons of kishna."],[null,"Diabetes tip: kishna is low in carbohydrate (about 13 g per portion) and adds flavour without needing more rice or bread. In the Gulf another version with raisins is called hashwa; raisins raise sugar and potassium, so use no more than a teaspoon if you add them."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Qassimy Kitchen (onion and tomato kishna), Sayidaty Kitchen (tomato kishna)"]]},"8424937":{"s":[[null,"Mash the dates with the black lime, cinnamon and cardamom (warm them 2 minutes with a spoonful of water to soften), and divide into 20 small balls."],[null,"Mix both flours, sugar, baking powder, salt and spices, then rub in the ghee with your fingertips until evenly spread."],[null,"Add the milk gradually and knead to a soft, firm dough that does not stick to your hands, then cover and rest 15 minutes."],[null,"Heat the oven to 180 °C and line a tray with baking paper."],[null,"Divide the dough into 20 balls, flatten each in your palm, put a date ball in the middle and seal well."],[null,"Sprinkle the kleeja mould with a little sesame, press the ball into it to take the pattern, then turn it out onto the tray. (Without a mould: flatten into a thick disc and mark the top with a fork.)"],[null,"Bake on the middle shelf for 15 minutes until golden underneath, then switch to top heat for 2–3 minutes to colour the tops."],[null,"Let them cool completely and store in an airtight tin."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: 2 tbsp sugar (25 g) instead of about 200 g, 40 g ghee instead of 200 g butter or tail fat, a date filling with no added sugar or syrup, and at least half the flour is whole wheat."],[null,"Kidney tip: dates, brown flour and baking powder (which contains phosphate) add potassium and phosphorus; keep to one piece, and you can use only white flour to lower phosphorus."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one piece has about 19 g carbohydrate; have one piece with unsweetened Saudi coffee in place of dates, not alongside other sweets."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (Mawsouat Al Tabkh), Saudipedia, Arab News"]]},"8621099":{"s":[[null,"Wash the tripe well, cover it with water in a pot with the vinegar, lemon juice and cumin seeds, boil for 10 minutes and discard the water."],[null,"Return it to the pot with fresh water, the cinnamon, bay leaves, turmeric and garlic and simmer until tender (about 30 minutes, or 15 minutes in a pressure cooker), then drain and cut into thin strips."],[null,"Heat the oil in a pot and cook the onion until soft, then add the tripe and crushed garlic and stir for 3 minutes."],[null,"Add the spices, tomatoes and chillies and stir until the tomatoes break down."],[null,"Add the lentils, 300 ml hot water and the salt, cover and cook on very low heat for 30 minutes until the tripe and lentils are soft and the sauce thickens."],[null,"Stir in the fresh coriander for the last 2 minutes and serve with lemon, spring onion, rocket and whole-wheat bread."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: no lamb fat and no stock cubes, a single spoon of olive oil, trimmed tripe, and little salt with plenty of cumin and coriander."],[null,"Kidney tip: tripe has less phosphorus than liver or heart, but offal is high in cholesterol and purines; leave out the liver, keep to one portion, and you can omit the lentils to lower potassium and phosphorus."],[null,"Diabetes and heart tip: the dish is low in carbohydrate (about 18 g); pick one small whole-wheat bread, and have it no more than once a week because of its cholesterol."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Mawdoo3, Elwasfa"]]},"8264162":{"s":[[null,"Singe the trotters over an open flame to remove any remaining hair, then rub with lemon and wash well."],[null,"Boil them in water for 5 minutes, then discard the water and rinse again."],[null,"Heat the oil in a large pot (or pressure cooker) and cook the onion until soft, then add the garlic and tomato and stir 3 minutes."],[null,"Add the trotters, the whole and ground spices and the drained wheat, and cover with the water."],[null,"Bring to the boil, lower the heat and simmer covered for 2–2½ hours until the meat falls off the bone (or 45–60 minutes in a pressure cooker)."],[null,"Strain the broth into a bowl and chill it for a few hours or overnight, then lift off and discard the layer of set fat."],[null,"Return the broth to the pot with the trotters and wheat, add the chickpeas and salt, and simmer gently for 15 minutes."],[null,"Serve 2 trotters per bowl with chickpeas, wheat and a little broth, sprinkled with lemon juice and parsley, with a rocket (jarjeer) salad."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: the broth is chilled and the set fat removed (the key step, as trotters are rich in saturated fat), only 1 tsp oil, no stock cubes or salted curry mix, and chickpeas and whole wheat are added for fibre instead of lots of bread."],[null,"Kidney tip: chickpeas and whole wheat add potassium and phosphorus and the concentrated broth is rich in protein; rinse the canned chickpeas well or use fewer, and keep the broth in the bowl to a little."],[null,"Diabetes and heart tip: one bowl has about 32 g carbohydrate from the chickpeas and wheat, so little extra bread is needed; for heart patients trotters are an occasional dish, not a daily breakfast, because of their cholesterol."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (Mawsouat Al Tabkh), Asharq Al-Awsat, Khiyam"]]},"8092380":{"s":[[null,"In a blender mix the egg, warm water and yeast for 1 minute, then add both flours, milk powder and salt gradually while blending to a smooth batter thinner than cake batter."],[null,"Cover and leave in a warm place for 1 hour until bubbles appear on top."],[null,"Heat a non-stick pan over medium heat and wipe it with a paper towel dipped in a little oil."],[null,"Stir the batter, pour a small ladle into the pan and swirl to cover the base thinly."],[null,"Cook until the top is full of holes and dry and the base is golden (1–2 minutes), then flip for a few seconds if you like. Repeat to make about 12 rounds."],[null,"Stack the rounds on a plate, brushing each with a thin layer of ghee and sprinkling with a little of the sugar and cardamom."],[null,"Serve warm with tea or a glass of low-fat laban."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: 12 g ghee instead of 80 g butter, 16 g sugar instead of 3 tbsp or a heavy dusting of icing sugar, about 40% of the flour is whole wheat, the milk powder is nonfat, and the pan is only wiped with oil."],[null,"Kidney tip: milk powder and brown flour add phosphorus and potassium; you can use only white flour and leave out the milk powder, and keep to three rounds."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one serving has about 44 g carbohydrate; you can skip the sugar on top and keep just the cardamom, and eat it with an egg or low-fat cheese to slow the rise in blood sugar."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (Mawsouat Al Tabkh), Mawdoo3, Al Jawhara Magazine"]]},"8749249":{"s":[[null,"Mix the meat with the grated onion, spices, 1 tsp oil and the salt, knead well, cover and chill for at least 1 hour."],[null,"For the garlic yoghurt: stir the crushed garlic into the yoghurt and keep it in the fridge."],[null,"For the sauce: blend the tomatoes, onion and garlic, then simmer with the oil, paprika and salt over low heat for 10–15 minutes until thick."],[null,"For the rice: bring 400 ml water to the boil with the cardamom, oil and salt, add the drained rice, cover and cook on low heat for 15 minutes."],[null,"Shape the meat into walnut-sized balls, brush a griddle or iron pan with the remaining teaspoon of oil and cook the balls over medium-low heat, turning, until the juices dry and they are cooked through (8–10 minutes), or grill them over charcoal."],[null,"Serve the Makkah way in three parts: on the garlic yoghurt, in the red sauce and over the rice, with a green salad."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: lean minced leg meat instead of meat with added fat, 2 tbsp oil for the whole dish instead of about 250 ml of oils, low-fat yoghurt and much less salt."],[null,"Kidney tip: yoghurt, tomato and meat are high in phosphorus and potassium; halve the yoghurt, keep the sauce to 2 tbsp per person and stick to one portion of meat (about 90 g cooked)."],[null,"Diabetes tip: the plate has about 57 g carbohydrate, mostly from the rice; you can serve the mabshoor with the yoghurt and salad and halve the rice."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Sayidaty Kitchen, Elwasfa"]]},"8189464":{"s":[[null,"Mash the soaked dates with a fork in their soaking water to a smooth paste."],[null,"In a large bowl mix the flour, spices, cinnamon, salt and sesame, then add the spring onion, onion, mashed dates, egg and saffron."],[null,"Add the water gradually while mixing to a thick, soft batter similar to luqaimat batter, then let it rest for 10 minutes."],[null,"Heat a non-stick pan over medium heat and brush it lightly with oil."],[null,"Pour in a small ladle of batter and spread it with the back of the spoon into a round about 12 cm wide; cook for 2–3 minutes until browned underneath, then flip and brown the other side. Repeat with the rest of the batter to make 8 rounds, brushing the pan with oil between batches."],[null,"Cut the rounds as you like, drizzle with the date syrup and serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: whole-wheat flour, a brush of olive oil instead of plenty of oil, little salt and no salted seasoning mixes, and about half the usual date syrup."],[null,"Kidney tip: dates, date syrup and whole-wheat flour contain potassium and phosphorus; you can eat one round, swap half the flour for white flour and use less syrup."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion (2 rounds) has about 64 g carbohydrate; have one round with an egg or low-fat labneh and cucumber, and skip the syrup or use just 1 tsp."],[null,"Suitable for: heart health and blood pressure, people on dialysis, vegetarians."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Sayidaty Kitchen, Cookpad Saudi Arabia"]]},"8010105":{"s":[[null,"Prick the eggplants with a fork and roast them whole, without oil, in a 220 °C oven (or over a gas flame) for 40–45 minutes, turning, until completely soft and charred."],[null,"Let cool a little, peel, and drain the flesh in a sieve for 10 minutes."],[null,"Mash the eggplant with a fork or chop it finely with a knife."],[null,"Add the garlic, vinegar, lemon juice, yoghurt, tahini and salt and mix with a spoon until even."],[null,"Spread it in a serving dish, drizzle the olive oil in a circle, garnish with lemon, parsley and cumin, and serve cold."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: the eggplant is roasted without being coated in oil, only 2 tbsp tahini, low-fat yoghurt, and 1 tsp olive oil on top."],[null,"Kidney tip: eggplant, tahini and yoghurt contain potassium and phosphorus; keep to one serving (4 tbsp) and you can cut the tahini to 1 tbsp."],[null,"Diabetes tip: mutabbal is low in carbohydrate; watch the bread eaten with it and use cucumber and carrot sticks instead."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Mawdoo3, Sayidaty"]]},"8158001":{"s":[[null,"Bring 800 ml water with the salt to the boil in a pot over medium heat."],[null,"Spread the flour in a wide dish, sprinkle the remaining water over it a little at a time and rub it with your fingertips until it forms small crumbs like coarse sand."],[null,"Add the crumbs to the boiling water gradually, stirring all the time, until it reaches the thick texture you like."],[null,"Lower the heat and cook for 20–30 minutes, stirring now and then, until the raw flour taste is gone."],[null,"Spoon it into 4 small bowls, make a small hollow in the middle, add 3 g ghee and 1 tsp honey to each and serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: whole-wheat flour, very little salt (usual recipes use a whole tablespoon), and about half the usual ghee and honey."],[null,"Kidney tip: whole-wheat flour has more phosphorus and potassium than white flour; you can use half whole-wheat and half white flour, and keep to one portion."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has about 42 g carbohydrate; you can skip the honey and sprinkle a little cinnamon, and have it with a boiled egg or low-fat laban to slow the rise in blood sugar."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Elbalad News, Just Food"]]},"8307084":{"s":[[null,"Soak the dates in 500 ml of boiling water for 10 minutes, then blend them with the rest of the water until smooth and liquid."],[null,"Pour the date mixture into a heavy pot and add the flour gradually while whisking so no lumps form, then add the salt and half the pepper and cinnamon."],[null,"Cook over medium heat, stirring constantly, for 15–20 minutes until it boils and thickens."],[null,"Add half the ghee, cover and leave on very low heat for 1 hour to 1 hour 15 minutes, stirring every 10–15 minutes, until thick, glossy and dark."],[null,"Spoon the muhalla into a serving dish; melt the remaining ghee with the black lime and the rest of the pepper and cinnamon, pour it over the top and serve warm."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: fewer dates and a higher share of whole-wheat flour, no added sugar, much less fat than the usual butter, and a small portion."],[null,"Kidney tip: dates are rich in potassium; keep to half a portion (60 g) if your potassium is restricted, and ask your dietitian."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has about 46 g carbohydrate from date sugar; count it as part of your meal, not an extra, and preferably have half a portion after a meal with protein and vegetables."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Qassimy.com, Al Bilad newspaper"]]},"8888089":{"s":[[null,"Put the onions in a wide heavy pot over medium heat with a splash of water and stir until soft and the water has evaporated."],[null,"Add the oil and keep stirring for 25–30 minutes, adding a splash of water whenever it starts to stick, until the onions are very dark brown but not burnt."],[null,"Add the whole and ground spices and the garlic and stir for 2 minutes, then add a splash of water and cover for 3 minutes."],[null,"Add the chicken and turn it for 10 minutes until coated brown from the onions."],[null,"Add the hot water, loomi and salt, cover and simmer for 30 minutes until the chicken is cooked."],[null,"Lift the chicken onto a tray and brown it in an oven preheated to 220 °C for 10 minutes without added fat."],[null,"Measure the broth: you need about 375 ml. Add the drained rice and boil uncovered without stirring until the broth is absorbed."],[null,"Turn the heat to the lowest setting, cover and cook 20 minutes until the rice is done."],[null,"Spoon the rice onto a platter, top with the chicken and serve with a green salad and cucumber."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: the onions are roasted in 2 tbsp oil with splashes of water instead of being covered in oil, the chicken is skinless and browned in the oven, there are no stock cubes, and the rice portion is about 150 g cooked per person."],[null,"Kidney tip: chicken is high in phosphorus and potassium; keep to one plate (about 100 g cooked chicken). The dish has no tomato or potato, so it is lighter in potassium than many rice dishes."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one plate has about 54 g carbohydrate; serve with a large salad, and you can mix in a quarter brown rice."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (Mawsouat Al Tabkh), Wikipedia, Cookinsta"]]},"8737541":{"s":[[null,"Mix the flour, yeast and a quarter of the salt, add the warm water gradually and knead to a very soft, slightly sticky dough; cover and rest for 1 hour."],[null,"Divide the dough into 16 walnut-sized balls and oil your hands lightly."],[null,"Heat a saj or non-stick pan over medium heat, press each ball with your palm straight onto the hot surface into a thin round, cook 1 minute, then flip until browned in spots. Keep the marasee covered."],[null,"For the balool: heat the oil and ghee and cook the onion until soft and golden, then add the cardamom, dried lime, turmeric and spices for 1 minute."],[null,"Add the tomato and zucchini and stir 5 minutes, then pour in the boiling water and the remaining salt and simmer 10 minutes."],[null,"Tear the marasee into pieces in a deep dish, pour the hot balool over, leave 2 minutes to soak in, and serve at once with low-fat laban or a salad."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: no sugar in the broth, olive oil with one teaspoon of ghee instead of plenty of butter, no bouillon, and tomato and zucchini for more vegetables."],[null,"Kidney tip: whole-wheat flour is higher in phosphorus and potassium than white flour; you can use half and half and less tomato, and keep to one plate. Ask your dietitian."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one plate has about 51 g carbohydrate with 8 g fibre; add a protein such as a boiled egg or some grilled chicken, and skip the honey."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, vegetarians."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Arabic Wikipedia (Marasee), Mawdoo3 (marasee), Qassimy.com (marasee recipes)"]]},"8950951":{"s":[[null,"Mix both flours with the salt and oil, add the water gradually and knead to a soft dough; rest it for 15 minutes."],[null,"Divide the dough into 3 pieces, roll each thin and cook in a non-stick pan over medium heat on both sides until golden and slightly crisp."],[null,"While hot, chop the breads very fine or pulse them in a food processor."],[null,"Mash the bananas with a fork in a bowl, add the chopped bread and knead together until even."],[null,"Press the marsa into a serving dish and smooth the top, pour over the melted ghee, drizzle with the honey and divide into 4 portions."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: part whole-wheat flour, a little oil in the dough instead of lots of fat, about half the usual ghee and honey, and the banana gives most of the sweetness."],[null,"Kidney tip: banana is high in potassium (about 90 g banana per portion); you can use one banana only, or all white flour, and keep to one portion."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has about 56 g carbohydrate; serve it with a piece of grilled fish (it is traditionally eaten with fish) and a green salad, and you can reduce or skip the honey."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Al-Madina newspaper, Cookpad"]]},"8659511":{"s":[[null,"Mix the flour with the salt and spices, add the water gradually and knead until the dough holds together, then cover for 20 minutes and divide into 8 balls."],[null,"Soak the potato cubes in warm water for 2 hours, then drain (to lower the potassium)."],[null,"Heat the oil in a wide pot and cook the onion until soft and lightly coloured, then add the whole spices and garlic for 1 minute."],[null,"Add the chicken and stir until it turns white and the edges colour, then add the carrot, eggplant, bell pepper, tomato paste, bezar and turmeric and stir for 3 minutes."],[null,"Pour in the boiling water and simmer on medium heat for 20 minutes."],[null,"Roll each ball very thin on a floured surface and add the sheets to the boiling broth one at a time, stirring gently after each so they do not stick."],[null,"Add the zucchini, potato and salt, cover and cook on low heat for 25 minutes until the dough and vegetables are tender, then serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: no stock cubes, skinless chicken, little oil, a small amount of soaked potato and about half the usual salt with more vegetables."],[null,"Kidney tip: whole-wheat flour, potato, carrot, tomato paste and chicken are high in potassium and phosphorus; soak the potato as in the steps or replace it with zucchini, and keep to one plate with only a little broth. Ask your dietitian about your own portion."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one plate has about 62 g carbohydrate; you can leave out the potato to lower it, do not add bread or rice, and start with a green salad."],[null,"Best kept as an occasional dish for kidney, diabetes and heart diets; keep to one serving."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), WebTeb (chicken marqooq), Arabic Wikipedia (Marqooq)"]]},"8178564":{"s":[[null,"Mix the flour, salt and turmeric, add the water gradually and knead to a firm dough slightly stiffer than pastry dough, then cover for 30 minutes, knead again and divide into 8 balls."],[null,"In a heavy pot heat the oil and cook the onion until soft, then add the tomato paste and tomatoes and stir for 2 minutes."],[null,"Add the meat, cumin and bezar and stir for 10 minutes, then pour in the boiling water, add the dried limes and simmer on medium heat for 45 minutes until the meat is almost tender (or 20 minutes in a pressure cooker)."],[null,"Roll each ball on a floured surface into a very thin round about 25 cm across."],[null,"With the stew boiling, lay one sheet on the surface and cover the pot for 1 minute, then push it aside with a spoon and add the next sheet; repeat until all the dough is used."],[null,"Add the zucchini, eggplant, chilli and salt around the sides, cover and cook on low heat for 40 minutes, stirring gently from the bottom, and add hot water if it gets too thick."],[null,"Add the pumpkin for the last 15 minutes until tender, then serve the marqooq hot topped with the onion and dried lime."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: no stock cubes and no browned butter or ghee, lean meat, a little olive oil, more vegetables and about half the usual salt."],[null,"Kidney tip: whole-wheat flour, tomatoes, tomato paste, pumpkin and meat are high in potassium and phosphorus; keep to one plate, you can swap half the whole-wheat flour for white flour, halve the tomatoes and drink only a little of the broth. Ask your dietitian about your own portion."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one plate has about 59 g carbohydrate with 10 g fibre from the whole-wheat flour and vegetables; do not add bread or rice, and add a green salad."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Arabic Wikipedia (Marqooq), Mawdoo3"]]},"8866678":{"s":[[null,"Soak the potato cubes in warm water for 30 minutes, then drain and pat dry."],[null,"Heat the oven to 220 °C. Toss the eggplant, potato and carrot with 1 tbsp of the oil and spread them on a lined tray."],[null,"Roast for 25–30 minutes, turning once, until browned and tender."],[null,"In a pot heat the rest of the oil and soften the onion and chilli without browning, then add the garlic."],[null,"Add the tomato, tomato paste, spices, salt and 100 ml water and cook for 10 minutes until thick."],[null,"Add the roasted vegetables, stir gently, cover and simmer 10 minutes to absorb the sauce. Serve hot or warm."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: the vegetables are roasted with a spoon of oil instead of deep-fried, with no-salt tomato paste and little salt."],[null,"Kidney tip: potato, tomato and eggplant contain potassium; cut the potatoes small and boil them in plenty of water for 10 minutes, discarding the water, before roasting, or replace them with more eggplant and carrot, and keep to a small plate."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one plate has about 30 g carbohydrate from the potatoes; if you serve it with rice or bread, halve the rice or bread."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, vegetarians, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Sayidaty Kitchen, Mawdoo3"]]},"8260973":{"s":[[null,"Blend the milk, egg and one teaspoon of oil, then add the flour, yeast, sugar, salt and cardamom and blend to a smooth batter like a thick crêpe batter."],[null,"Stir in the nigella seeds, cover and leave in a warm place for 30 minutes."],[null,"Heat a griddle or non-stick pan over medium heat and wipe it with the oil on a paper towel."],[null,"Pour a small ladle of batter into a round, cook until bubbles appear, then flip until golden. Repeat to make 12 rounds, keeping them covered so they stay soft."],[null,"Serve 2 rounds per person with 1 tsp honey (5 g) and unsweetened tea or Arabic coffee."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: whole-wheat flour instead of white, half the sugar or less, low-fat milk, yeast instead of baking powder (less sodium and phosphorus), and a measured amount of honey with no ghee."],[null,"Kidney tip: milk and whole-wheat flour contain phosphorus; keep to 2 rounds, and you can replace half the milk with water and half the flour with white flour. Ask your dietitian."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one serving has about 27 g carbohydrate, about 6 g of it added sugar; you can skip the honey and serve with low-fat laban or an egg."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Al Ain News (musabeeb), Arabic Wikipedia (Marasee)"]]},"8454387":{"s":[[null,"Mix both flours with the yeast, sugar, cardamom, saffron and a pinch of salt, then add the egg and warm water gradually and whisk to a thick pourable batter like pancake batter."],[null,"Cover and leave in a warm place for 45 minutes until bubbly."],[null,"For the kashna: heat the oil and cook the onion until soft, add the garlic and spices for 1 minute, then the tomatoes, pepper and remaining salt, and cook 8–10 minutes until thick; turn off the heat and add the spring onions."],[null,"Heat a griddle or non-stick pan over medium heat and wipe it once with the oil on a paper towel."],[null,"Pour a small ladle of batter, spread it a little, and cook until bubbles appear and the underside is golden, then flip for 1 minute. Repeat to make 12 rounds."],[null,"Arrange the musabeeb on a plate, top with the hot kashna and serve with a green salad or cucumber."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: two-thirds whole-wheat flour, yeast instead of baking powder and milk powder (less sodium and phosphorus), only one teaspoon of sugar, and kashna made with olive oil instead of butter and ghee."],[null,"Kidney tip: whole-wheat flour is higher in phosphorus and potassium than white, and tomatoes are high in potassium; you can use half and half flour, use less tomato and more onion and pepper. Ask your dietitian."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion (3 rounds) has about 44 g carbohydrate; the kashna and salad add fullness, and you can have a boiled egg instead of the third round."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Yummy Layalina (musabeeb with kashna), Sayidaty Kitchen (musabeeb with onion and sauce)"]]},"8655008":{"s":[[null,"Mix the meat with the lemon juice, garlic, olive oil, spices and the ¼ tsp salt, and leave for at least 30 minutes."],[null,"Put the coarse salt in a heavy, thick pot to a depth of 3–4 cm and heat it over medium-low heat for about 15 minutes until very hot and lightly crackling."],[null,"Lay a double sheet of foil with a few small holes over the salt, then arrange the meat on it so it touches neither the salt nor the sides of the pot."],[null,"Seal the top of the pot tightly with foil and then the lid, and cook on low heat for about 1½ hours without opening, until the meat is tender and browned."],[null,"Meanwhile heat the oil and ghee in another pot, cook the onion until soft, then add the whole spices, tomato and chilli and stir for 3 minutes."],[null,"Add the boiling water and salt, then the drained rice; boil until the water drops to the level of the rice, then cover and cook on low heat for 15 minutes."],[null,"Lift the meat gently off the foil and place it on the rice; discard the salt once cool (it can be reused for cooking only). Serve with a green salad."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: traditionally the meat sits directly on the salt and absorbs some of it; here foil separates them so the salt only supplies heat, and the meat is trimmed of visible fat, with olive oil instead of fat."],[null,"Kidney tip: meat and tomato provide potassium and phosphorus; keep to one portion (about 110 g cooked meat and 150 g cooked rice), and you can leave the tomato out of the rice. Ask your dietitian about your own portion."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has about 45 g carbohydrate; start with the salad, and you can replace a quarter of the rice with soaked brown rice."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Sayidaty Kitchen (madhbi lahm), Khaleej Kitchen (stone madhbi), Elbalad (salt madhbi)"]]},"8773393":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil and ghee in a pot and cook the onion 5 minutes until golden, then add the garlic, tomato, tomato paste, spices and half the parsley and coriander and stir for 5 minutes."],[null,"Add the chicken and turn it in the sauce, then pour in the boiling water and simmer 25 minutes until cooked."],[null,"Meanwhile blanch the chard in boiling water for 3 minutes, drain and discard the water."],[null,"Add the drained rice, cooked mung beans and salt, cover and cook 15 minutes on medium heat then 20 minutes on low until the rice is very soft; add a little boiling water if it dries."],[null,"Stir in the chard until wilted, then beat the mixture with a wooden masher or potato masher until smooth, leaving a little of the chicken in shreds."],[null,"Add the lemon juice and the rest of the parsley and coriander and serve hot with a cucumber salad."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: no stock cubes, olive oil and a little ghee instead of 60 g butter, skinless chicken, and no fried onion garnish."],[null,"Kidney tip: chard and mung beans are very high in potassium and phosphorus; blanching the chard and soaking and boiling the mung beans, then discarding the water, lowers the potassium, and you can halve the chard. Keep to one plate and ask your dietitian."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one plate has about 56 g carbohydrate; the mung beans and chard add fibre that slows sugar absorption, and you can swap a quarter of the rice for soaked brown rice."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Hia Magazine, Cookpad Saudi Arabia (Hasawi madrouba)"]]},"8434519":{"s":[[null,"Mix the flour, salt and oil, add the water gradually and knead to a slightly stiff dough, then cover for 30 minutes and knead again."],[null,"Shape the dough into walnut-size balls and roll each into a disc 6–7 cm across and 2–3 mm thick; dust with a little flour so they do not stick."],[null,"In a heavy pot heat the oil and cook the onion until golden, then add the garlic, tomato paste, bezar, cumin and turmeric and stir for 1 minute."],[null,"Add the blended tomato and pepper and the meat and stir for 10 minutes, then pour in the boiling water, add the dried limes and simmer for 40 minutes (or 20 minutes in a pressure cooker)."],[null,"Add the salt, then drop in the dough discs in batches while the broth boils, stirring gently between batches."],[null,"Place the zucchini, pumpkin and chillies around the sides of the pot so the discs do not break, cover and cook for 15 minutes on high heat and then 45 minutes on low heat, adding hot water if needed."],[null,"Spoon the mutazeez into a serving dish and top with the onion, dried lime and cinnamon."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: no ghee or browned butter on top and no sweetened masmana spice or apricot paste, lean meat, little oil and about half the usual salt with more vegetables."],[null,"Kidney tip: whole-wheat flour, tomatoes, tomato paste, pumpkin and meat are high in potassium and phosphorus; keep to one plate, you can swap half the whole-wheat flour for white flour, halve the tomatoes and drink only a little of the broth. Ask your dietitian about your own portion."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one plate has about 60 g carbohydrate with 10 g fibre; the dough discs are the starch of the meal, so do not add bread or rice, and add a green salad."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Arabic Wikipedia (Mutazeez), Atyab Tabkha"]]},"8250747":{"s":[[null,"Mix both flours with the salt and half the oil, add the water little by little and knead for 5 minutes into a soft, smooth dough."],[null,"Divide the dough into 4 balls, coat them with the rest of the oil, cover and rest for at least 30 minutes."],[null,"Brown the minced beef with the onion in a non-stick pan without oil until cooked and dry, then add the cumin, spices and pepper and let it cool."],[null,"Mix the meat with the leek, spring onion, tomato and salt, and beat the eggs separately."],[null,"Stretch one dough ball on a smooth surface with lightly oiled hands until it is very thin and almost see-through."],[null,"Put a quarter of the filling in the centre, pour a quarter of the egg over it, then fold the sides over to make a closed square parcel."],[null,"Heat a non-stick griddle over medium heat, wipe it with a little oil and cook the parcel until golden underneath, then turn and cook the other side until the egg is set (about 4 minutes per side)."],[null,"Repeat with the remaining dough, cut each mutabbaq into squares and serve hot with lemon."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: half the flour is whole wheat, the lean meat is browned without oil, the parcel is cooked with a wipe of oil instead of a lot of oil, and the ready samboosa sheets and cheese are left out to cut sodium."],[null,"Kidney tip: egg, meat and whole-wheat flour contain phosphorus and tomato adds potassium; keep to one mutabbaq, and you can use egg whites for one of the eggs and use less tomato."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one mutabbaq has about 53 g carbohydrate; serve it with a large green salad rather than sweet drinks."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Layalina Yummy, Arabizi Translations"]]},"8146164":{"s":[[null,"Wash the lentils and rice well, soak them in hot water for 30 minutes and drain."],[null,"Heat the oil in a pot and cook the onion over medium heat until soft and starting to colour, then add the garlic for 1 minute."],[null,"Add the lentils, rice, cumin, turmeric and pepper and stir for 2 minutes, then pour in 1.2 l of the hot water."],[null,"Bring to the boil, then lower the heat and cook for 35–40 minutes, stirring every few minutes and adding the remaining water as needed, until thick and smooth."],[null,"Add the salt in the last 5 minutes of cooking."],[null,"For the topping: toss the sliced onion with the teaspoon of oil and bake at 200 °C for 15–20 minutes until browned, or brown it in a non-stick pan."],[null,"For the salad: mix the yoghurt with the cucumber, dill and pinch of salt."],[null,"Ladle out the ma'doos, drizzle with the melted ghee, top with the browned onions and serve with the yoghurt salad, radishes and leafy greens."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: no stock cubes, more lentils than rice, oven-browned instead of deep-fried onions, 1 tsp ghee for the whole pot, and less than half the usual salt."],[null,"Kidney tip: lentils and yoghurt are high in potassium and phosphorus; soak and rinse the lentils well, use equal amounts of rice and lentils, and keep the yoghurt salad to 2 tbsp."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has about 57 g carbohydrate but plenty of fibre and protein from the lentils; serve it with grilled fish and a large salad rather than a bigger portion."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, vegetarians, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Cookpad, Yummy (Layalina)"]]},"8946423":{"s":[[null,"Knead the flour with the yeast, salt and water to a soft dough; cover and let it rise for 30 minutes."],[null,"Divide the dough into 3 balls, roll each one thin and cook in a dry non-stick pan or on a hot saj for 1–2 minutes per side until cooked and spotted."],[null,"Cut up the bread and pulse it in a food processor to fine crumbs."],[null,"Melt the ghee in a pot over low heat, add the dates and mash until they melt, then add the bread crumbs and toss for 5 minutes."],[null,"Add the sliced bananas and cardamom and mash with the spoon while stirring for 3–5 minutes until the mixture is even and soft."],[null,"Spoon the ma'soub into serving plates and top each with a teaspoon of cream and a little honey; serve warm."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: home-made whole-wheat bread, much less ghee, a small amount of light cream, and sweetness mainly from bananas and dates with only one spoon of honey for the whole dish."],[null,"Kidney tip: bananas and dates are rich in potassium and whole-wheat flour contains phosphorus; use 2 bananas instead of 3 plus a cooked grated apple, and have half a portion."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has about 65 g carbohydrate; have half a portion with a boiled egg or low-fat laban and skip the honey."],[null,"Suitable for: heart health and blood pressure, vegetarians."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Mawdoo3, Khaleeji Food"]]},"8141151":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oven to 180 °C. Brush a stone maghash pot, or a heavy ovenproof pot or clay casserole, with the oil."],[null,"Crush the garlic with the cumin, coriander, black pepper, cardamom and salt, and rub the mixture into the meat."],[null,"Drain the potato. Layer the onion in the pot, then the okra and meat, then the tomato, potato, zucchini and peppers."],[null,"Add the hot water and cover tightly with a lid or foil."],[null,"Cook in the oven for 2 hours until the meat is very tender; check after an hour and add a little water if it looks dry."],[null,"Serve it bubbling in the same pot."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: lean meat, one spoon of oil for the whole pot, no stock cubes, less than ¼ tsp salt per portion, and more vegetables."],[null,"Kidney tip: the tomato, potato and okra contain potassium and the meat contains phosphorus; boil the cut potato or soak it in hot water for 2 hours and discard the water, or replace it with more zucchini, and keep to one portion."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has only about 20 g carbohydrate; it is traditionally served with rice or bread, so keep to 150 g cooked rice (basmati or brown) or half a whole-wheat flatbread with a green salad."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Yummy Layalina, Cookinsta, Saudi Press Agency"]]},"8409501":{"s":[[null,"Toast the jareesh in a dry pan over medium heat, stirring, until golden, then rinse it, soak in boiling water for 1 hour and drain."],[null,"Heat the oil in a pot and cook the onion until soft, then add the garlic, whole spices and chillies for 1 minute."],[null,"Add the shrimp and ground spices and stir for just 2 minutes, then lift the shrimp out and set aside so it stays tender."],[null,"Add the tomatoes and tomato paste to the pot and cook for 5 minutes until saucy."],[null,"Add the jareesh, boiling water and salt, cover and simmer for 35–40 minutes, stirring now and then, until the jareesh is tender and has absorbed the water."],[null,"Return the shrimp to the pot for 5 minutes on low heat, then serve topped with coriander and a squeeze of lemon."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: a little olive oil instead of butter, fresh shrimp instead of salt-treated frozen shrimp, little salt, and no fried onion or nuts."],[null,"Kidney tip: jareesh and shrimp are high in phosphorus, and tomatoes in potassium; keep to one plate and you can halve the tomatoes. Frozen shrimp often has added phosphate and sodium, so read the label."],[null,"Diabetes and heart tip: one plate has about 43 g carbohydrate from fibre-rich whole grain; serve with a green salad. Shrimp is low in fat but high in cholesterol (about 160 mg per plate), so do not add more."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Supermama, 7elwa"]]},"8715906":{"s":[[null,"Mix both flours with the yeast, baking powder, sugar, salt and cardamom in a large bowl."],[null,"Whisk the egg with the laban, then add it to the flour little by little, mixing until you have a soft batter a little thicker than luqaimat batter."],[null,"Cover and leave in a warm place for 1 to 3 hours until puffed and slightly sour."],[null,"Heat the oven to 200 °C with the top element on. Heat a non-stick griddle over medium heat and wipe it with a little oil."],[null,"Drop coin-sized rounds of batter onto the griddle with a wet spoon and cook until the bottoms are golden."],[null,"Move the griddle to the oven for 5–7 minutes until the tops brown, then put the pieces in a covered container to stay soft. Repeat with the rest of the batter."],[null,"Warm the honey with the ghee and spices, pour it over the muqashqash, shake the container to coat, and serve warm."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: more than half the flour is whole wheat, the laban is low-fat, honey and ghee are less than half the traditional amount, and less baking powder keeps sodium down."],[null,"Kidney tip: laban, baking powder and whole-wheat flour contain phosphorus; keep to one portion (4 small pieces), and you can use low-sodium baking powder or rely on the yeast alone."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has about 29 g carbohydrate, including 7 g added sugar; serve the honey on the side and eat it with unsweetened laban or milk."],[null,"Suitable for: heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, M3aarf, Dlwaqty, Layalina Yummy"]]},"8673518":{"s":[[null,"Melt the ghee in a pot over medium heat, add the mastic and let it melt, then add the chicken and stir until it turns white."],[null,"Add the onion, cardamom, bay leaf, ground coriander, cumin, black pepper and 800 ml water, bring to the boil skimming the foam, then simmer for 20 minutes until the chicken is cooked."],[null,"Remove the onion pieces and bay leaf, add the molokhia and salt, stir well and let it come to the boil once or twice only, without a lid."],[null,"In a small pan heat the oil and cook the garlic until pale golden, then add the fresh coriander for a few seconds."],[null,"Stir the garlic fry into the molokhia, take off the heat and serve with lemon."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: skinless chicken breast, homemade stock with no stock cubes, and much less ghee and oil than the usual butter and ghee."],[null,"Kidney tip: molokhia is very high in potassium (about 1000 mg per bowl); keep to half a bowl, cut the molokhia to 250 g with more stock, and check with your dietitian before eating it."],[null,"Diabetes tip: the dish is low in carbohydrate (about 10 g); serve it with 150 g cooked rice, preferably basmati or brown."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Saudi Encyclopedia (ksaency), Sayidaty Kitchen"]]},"8872488":{"s":[[null,"Mix both flours with the salt and egg, add the water a little at a time and knead to a soft, smooth dough that does not stick. Cover and rest for 30 minutes."],[null,"Mix the meat well with the squeezed onion, cumin, black pepper, chilli and salt."],[null,"Roll the dough out thinly and cut it into 24 squares (about 8 cm). Put a spoon of filling in the middle of each, bring the four corners up over it and pinch well to seal."],[null,"Grease the steamer trays with the oil, arrange the mantu with space between them, set them over boiling water, cover and steam for 35–40 minutes until the filling is cooked."],[null,"For the yoghurt sauce: mix the yoghurt with the garlic and mint."],[null,"For the hot sauce: pulse the tomatoes, chilli, garlic, lemon juice and coriander in a blender until coarse."],[null,"Serve the mantu hot with both sauces and a light sprinkle of cumin and black pepper."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: the mantu are steamed, not fried, half the flour is wholewheat, 90% lean meat replaces fatty meat and ghee, the yoghurt is low-fat, and the hot sauce is fresh tomato with no added salt."],[null,"Kidney tip: meat, yoghurt and tomato add phosphorus and potassium; eat 4 dumplings instead of 6, have just 2 tbsp of the yoghurt sauce, and swap the tomato in the hot sauce for roasted red pepper."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion (6 dumplings) has about 48 g carbohydrate; serve it with a large green salad and no extra rice or bread."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Layalina Yummy, Mawdoo3"]]},"8879817":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a large heavy pot and cook the onion until soft, then add the meat and spices and brown for 8–10 minutes."],[null,"Add the grated tomato and tomato paste and stir for 5 minutes until thick."],[null,"Add the drained wheat and boiling water, bring to the boil, then turn the heat very low, cover and cook for 3½–4 hours, stirring now and then and adding boiling water when needed (or 1½ hours in a pressure cooker)."],[null,"Add the salt in the last hour, then beat the hareis while hot with a wooden masher or hand blender until the meat falls apart and blends with the wheat."],[null,"For the kishna: heat the ghee in a small pan and fry the onion until golden, then add the chilli and dried lime for 1 minute."],[null,"Spread the hareis in a serving dish, spoon the kishna over the top and serve hot with a green salad."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: lean meat, 1 tbsp oil and 2 tsp ghee for the whole pot instead of plenty of butter and ghee, no-salt-added tomato paste instead of a whole can of tomato sauce, and less salt."],[null,"Kidney tip: whole wheat and meat are high in phosphorus, and tomato and tomato paste in potassium; use half the tomato paste, keep to one portion (about 100 g cooked meat) and ask your dietitian about whole grains."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one bowl has about 53 g carbohydrate from fibre-rich whole grain; eat it with salad and do not add sugar on top."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Sayidaty Kitchen (hareis with meat and onion), Saudipedia (popular foods of Hail)"]]},"8775002":{"s":[[null,"Put the chicken in a pot with water to cover, boil for 5 minutes, then discard the water and foam."],[null,"Return the chicken to the pot with the drained wheat, cinnamon, cardamom, onion and water; the water should be about 3 cm above the grain."],[null,"Bring to the boil, then cover and cook on very low heat for 4–5 hours, stirring now and then and adding hot water when needed, until the grains burst and the chicken falls apart (or 1½ hours in a pressure cooker)."],[null,"Remove the cinnamon, cardamom and onion, add the salt and beat at once while hot with a wooden masher or hand blender until smooth and stretchy; add hot water if it is too thick."],[null,"Spread it in bowls, make a small well in the centre, add about a teaspoon of melted ghee to each, and dust with a little cinnamon if you like."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: skinless chicken boiled first to remove fat, about a teaspoon of ghee per bowl instead of pouring plenty, and less salt with flavour from cinnamon and cardamom."],[null,"Kidney tip: whole wheat and chicken are high in phosphorus and protein; keep to one portion (about 100 g cooked chicken) or smaller as your dietitian advises."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one bowl has about 44 g carbohydrate from whole grain; do not sprinkle sugar on top as some people do, and serve with a green salad."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Al-Madina newspaper (hareis on the Hasawi Ramadan table), Cookpad (Hasawi hareesa)"]]},"8388223":{"s":[[null,"Mix both flours with the salt, then add the yoghurt, oil and two thirds of the beaten egg, and knead while adding the warm water little by little until you have a soft, smooth dough."],[null,"Divide the dough into 12 balls, cover and leave to rest for 30 minutes."],[null,"Cook the minced beef in a non-stick pan without oil over medium heat until it changes colour and its liquid evaporates, then add the onion, spices and salt and cook for 5 minutes."],[null,"Take the filling off the heat and let it cool, then stir in the tomato, chilli and parsley."],[null,"Heat the oven to 200 °C and line a tray with baking paper."],[null,"Roll each ball into a thin circle about 15 cm across, put a heaped tablespoon of filling in the middle, fold in two opposite sides and then the ends to make a closed square parcel."],[null,"Place the parcels seam-side down on the tray and brush the tops with the rest of the egg."],[null,"Bake for 20–25 minutes until golden on top and underneath, and serve warm with a green salad."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: half whole-wheat flour, lean mince instead of fatty meat, a little olive oil instead of vegetable shortening, about a third of the usual salt, and oven-baked, never fried."],[null,"Kidney tip: meat, yoghurt and whole-wheat flour supply phosphorus and potassium; keep to 2–3 pieces, and use all white flour if your dietitian has asked you to limit phosphorus."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one serving (3 pieces) has about 65 g carbohydrate; have 2 pieces with a large salad if it is part of the Ramadan iftar meal."],[null,"Best kept as an occasional dish for kidney, diabetes and heart diets; keep to one serving."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Arabic Wikipedia (Yaghmish), Cookpad"]]},"8448083":{"s":[[null,"Peel the potatoes, cut each in half lengthways, then cut each half into 3 thick fingers."],[null,"Boil the fingers for 5 minutes, drain and discard the water, and pat them very dry with a towel."],[null,"Heat the oven to 220 °C. Toss the potatoes with the oil and black pepper and spread them in one layer on a tray lined with baking paper."],[null,"Bake for 30–35 minutes, turning once, until golden and crisp (or air-fry at 200 °C for 18–20 minutes), then sprinkle with the salt."],[null,"For the humar sauce: strain the tamarind, keeping the liquid and pulp and discarding the seeds, then blend it with the paste, chillies, garlic, coriander, cumin and salt until smooth; thin with water to taste."],[null,"For the garlic sauce: whisk the yoghurt with the garlic, lemon juice and salt."],[null,"Arrange the potatoes on plates and drizzle with both sauces, or serve the sauces in small dishes on the side."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: potatoes baked with one spoon of oil instead of deep fried, a low-fat yoghurt garlic sauce instead of oil and starch or mayonnaise, and much less salt in the sauces (usual recipes add a spoon of salt to the humar sauce)."],[null,"Kidney tip: potatoes, tamarind and tomato paste are high in potassium and yoghurt contains phosphorus; after cutting, soak the potatoes in hot water for 2 hours, then boil them in fresh water and discard it, so the real potassium is lower than calculated here, and use only a teaspoon of each sauce."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has about 38 g carbohydrate; serve it with a protein such as grilled chicken or fish and a green salad rather than as a meal on its own."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, vegetarians, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Elbalad News, Yummy Layalina"]]},"8307784":{"s":[[null,"Mix both flours, the milk powder, yeast, sugar, baking powder and salt in a bowl."],[null,"Add the egg and the dough oil, then the warm water little by little, and knead for 8 minutes to a soft dough that does not stick to your hands."],[null,"Cover the dough and leave it in a warm place for 1 hour until doubled."],[null,"Heat the oven to 200 °C and oil a baking tray with the tray oil or line it with baking paper."],[null,"Roll the dough 1 cm thick and cut small 4 cm rounds (or roll small balls), set them on the tray and rest them for 10 minutes."],[null,"Bake the makhamir for 12–15 minutes until puffed and golden, using the top grill for the last 2 minutes if you like."],[null,"For the bulool: put the water on the heat, add the cinnamon, dried limes, sugar and salt and stir until the sugar dissolves."],[null,"Add the ghee and simmer the bulool gently for 15 minutes, then lift out the dried limes and pour the bulool into a deep dish."],[null,"Serve the warm makhamir next to the hot bulool so each piece can be dipped, or pour the bulool over them just before serving."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: the makhamir are baked, not fried; half the flour is whole wheat; the bulool uses 45 g sugar instead of about 150 g, 2 tsp ghee instead of 50 g butter, and a pinch of salt instead of 2 tsp."],[null,"Kidney tip: whole-wheat flour and milk powder add some phosphorus; you can use all white flour and leave out the milk powder, and keep to one portion."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has about 48 g carbohydrate; dip the makhamir lightly rather than soaking them, and have 3 pieces with unsweetened Arabic coffee."],[null,"Suitable for: heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Sahha wa Hana, Mhtwyat"]]},"8822185":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a pot and cook the onion until soft and lightly golden, then add the garlic, ginger, cinnamon stick and whole dried limes for 1 minute."],[null,"Add the tomatoes, tomato paste, turmeric, curry powder, cardamom and ground dried lime, and stir for 5 minutes until the sauce thickens."],[null,"Add the shrimp and stir for 2 minutes until coated and just pink, then lift it out onto a plate."],[null,"Pour in the boiling water, add the bell pepper, chilli and half the coriander, and bring to the boil."],[null,"Add the drained jareesh and the salt, cover and simmer on low heat for 35–40 minutes, stirring now and then, until the grains are swollen and tender; add a little boiling water if it dries out."],[null,"Return the shrimp with the lemon juice and simmer just 5 minutes more so it stays tender."],[null,"Garnish with the rest of the coriander and serve with a green salad and cucumber."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: about half the usual shrimp, no stock cubes, olive oil instead of a ghee or fat topping, less salt and extra bell pepper."],[null,"Kidney tip: jareesh (a whole grain), shrimp, tomatoes and tomato paste are rich in phosphorus and potassium; keep to one plate and you can halve the tomatoes. Ask your dietitian about your portion."],[null,"Diabetes and heart tip: one plate has about 49 g carbohydrate with plenty of fibre from the jareesh; start with the salad. Shrimp is high in cholesterol, so keep to this portion and do not have it every day."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Zahrat Al Khaleej, Maggi Arabia (jareesh with prawns)"]]},"8345144":{"s":[[null,"Mix the flour with the yeast and salt, add the warm water little by little and knead to a soft dough; cover and leave to rise for 1 hour."],[null,"Meanwhile heat the ghee in a pot, add the onion and stir until soft, then add the garlic and meat and stir until the meat changes colour."],[null,"Add the tomatoes, tomato paste, spices, black lime and cardamom, then the water; cover and simmer gently for about 1¼ hours, skimming off the foam."],[null,"Add the carrot and courgettes for the last 25 minutes, then the salt at the end."],[null,"Heat the oven to 230 °C, press the dough by hand into a thick round on a sheet of foil lightly dusted with flour, and bake for 20–25 minutes, turning once, until cooked and browned. (Outdoors the round is set in foil on the embers and covered with a few hot coals.)"],[null,"Let the jamriyya cool a little, then break it into small pieces in a pot or deep dish."],[null,"Pour the broth over the pieces a little at a time and press with the ladle until soaked, then move it to the serving dish, arrange the meat and vegetables in the centre and serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: lean meat with visible fat trimmed, little ghee (1 tsp per 2 portions), homemade broth with no stock cubes, more vegetables in the broth, and whole-wheat bread."],[null,"Kidney tip: whole-wheat flour, tomato and broth contain potassium and phosphorus; swap half the whole-wheat flour for white flour, pour less broth, and keep to 90–100 g cooked meat."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has about 63 g carbohydrate from whole-wheat bread; you can cut the bread to two-thirds of a portion and serve it with a large green salad."],[null,"Suitable for: heart health and blood pressure."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Cookpad Saudi Arabia (jamriyya), Arabic Wikipedia (thareed)"]]},"8828126":{"s":[[null,"Brush a small tray (20 × 15 cm) very lightly with ghee or line it with baking paper."],[null,"Put the sugar and water in a small pot and stir until the sugar dissolves, then boil over high heat for 5–6 minutes without stirring until the syrup thickens slightly."],[null,"Turn off the heat and stir in the ghee, cardamom and rose water."],[null,"Add half the milk powder and stir quickly with a wooden spoon, then add the rest and keep stirring until a soft, cohesive dough forms. (If it stays too soft, return it to low heat for a minute while stirring.)"],[null,"Press the dough into the tray 1.5 cm thick, sprinkle the pistachios on top and press them in lightly."],[null,"Let it cool completely, then chill for 2 hours and cut into 12 pieces."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: skimmed instead of full-cream milk powder, less than half the usual sugar, and a little ghee; it stays soft like traditional labaniya but is less sweet."],[null,"Kidney tip: milk powder is very high in phosphorus and potassium; have one piece on special occasions only, and on dialysis take it with your phosphate binder as your doctor advises."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one piece has about 15 g carbohydrate (6 g of it added sugar); stick to one piece with Arabic coffee and no other sweets."],[null,"Suitable for: heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Arabic Wikipedia, WebTeb"]]},"8806052":{"s":[[null,"Put the sago and hot water in a pot over low heat and stir constantly until the pearls turn from white to almost clear (about 10 minutes)."],[null,"Add the milk gradually, raise the heat to medium and keep stirring for 10 minutes until the mixture thickens."],[null,"Add the sugar and cardamom and stir over low heat for 5 minutes, then turn off the heat and add the rose water."],[null,"Divide between 6 small glasses or bowls, cover and let cool, then chill for 4 hours."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: low-fat milk instead of full-cream milk powder, and 60 g sugar instead of about 200 g, in small portions."],[null,"Kidney tip: milk is a source of phosphorus and potassium; keep to one small glass, and you can replace a third of the milk with water or a plant milk without added phosphate."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one glass has about 31 g carbohydrate including 10 g added sugar; eat it after a meal rather than on its own, or use a sugar substitute."],[null,"Suitable for: heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Sayidaty Kitchen, Cookpad"]]},"8535403":{"s":[[null,"Heat the olive oil in a wide pan over high heat, add the onion and chilli and stir until the onion softens."],[null,"Add the chicken and garlic and stir for 5–6 minutes until the chicken is white on all sides."],[null,"Add the bell pepper, cabbage and carrot and stir for 4–5 minutes until slightly soft but still crisp."],[null,"Add the spices and salt and stir, then add the parsley."],[null,"Add the soy sauce and lemon juice and stir for 3 minutes until the chicken is fully cooked; serve hot with whole-wheat bread."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: skinless chicken breast, only 1 tbsp olive oil, no Maggi cube, and a small amount of reduced-sodium soy sauce instead of sweet soy sauce."],[null,"Kidney tip: chicken supplies phosphorus and potassium, so keep to one serving; cabbage, peppers and carrot are relatively low-potassium vegetables, and you can leave out the soy sauce."],[null,"Diabetes tip: the dish itself is low in carbohydrate; serve it with 1 small whole-wheat flatbread or 100 g brown rice."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Cookinsta (Hani Al-Dosari), Cookpad Saudi Arabia"]]},"8052626":{"s":[[null,"Mix the ground spices, garlic, lemon juice and ¼ tsp of the salt and rub it well into the lamb."],[null,"Brush a deep oven dish (or pressure cooker) with the olive oil, spread the onions with the cinnamon, cardamom and cloves on top, then lay the lamb over them."],[null,"Seal tightly with foil and cook at 160°C for 3 hours until the lamb falls apart (or 40 minutes after the whistle on low heat in a pressure cooker, with no added water)."],[null,"Uncover, raise the oven to 220°C and brown the lamb for 10–15 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile boil the water with the ghee and the rest of the salt, add the rice and simmer covered for 15 minutes, then drizzle the saffron on top and rest 5 minutes."],[null,"Spread the rice on a platter, arrange the lamb on top and spoon over the cooking juices after skimming off the fat."],[null,"Serve with green salad or a light lemony tahini salad."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: trimmed lean lamb instead of fatty cuts, fat skimmed from the juices, measured oil and ghee and much less salt."],[null,"Kidney tip: lamb provides phosphorus and potassium; keep to 90–100 g cooked meat and go easy on tahini salad, which is high in phosphorus."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one plate has about 48 g carbohydrate; start with the salad and reduce the rice if you need a lighter meal."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), English Wikipedia (Haneeth), Sayidaty Kitchen"]]},"8946205":{"s":[[null,"Melt the ghee in a non-stick pot over low heat, add the flour and stir constantly for 6–8 minutes until toasted, golden and fragrant."],[null,"Stir in the cardamom, then add the dates and mash them into the flour with a wooden spoon or masher over very low heat until evenly blended (about 5 minutes)."],[null,"Add the sesame and nigella seeds and stir for 1 minute."],[null,"Let it cool slightly, then shape into 12 small balls or squares with damp hands and serve warm with Arabic coffee."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: 25 g ghee instead of 100 g butter plus oil, whole-wheat flour, no added sugar or cream, and small fixed pieces."],[null,"Kidney tip: dates are high in potassium (about 170 mg per piece) and sesame and whole-wheat flour contain phosphorus; have one piece, and you can use white flour and skip the sesame."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one piece has about 22 g carbohydrate from dates and flour; keep to one piece with coffee after a meal."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Al Bilad Daily, Cookpad"]]},"8352970":{"s":[[null,"Mix both flours with the yeast and salt, add the warm water gradually and knead for 8–10 minutes until smooth and elastic."],[null,"Cover and leave in a warm place for an hour until doubled."],[null,"Divide into 8 equal balls, rest for 15 minutes, then roll each into a long oval about half a centimetre thick."],[null,"Heat the oven to its highest setting (250 °C) with a baking stone or an upturned tray inside for 20 minutes."],[null,"Brush the breads with egg, sprinkle with the seeds, place them on the hot stone and bake for 6–8 minutes until puffed and golden. In a traditional tannour they are slapped onto the hot wall until cooked."],[null,"Wrap them in a clean cloth to keep them soft and serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: mostly whole-wheat flour instead of white, little salt, and no sugar or ghee in the dough; serve it with broth, stew or laban instead of ghee and honey."],[null,"Kidney tip: whole-wheat flour has more phosphorus and potassium than white flour; you can reverse the ratio (two thirds white flour) and keep to one bread with a meal."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one bread has about 33 g carbohydrate; let it replace rice in the meal, or eat half with a vegetable stew or broth."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Sayidaty Kitchen, M3aarf"]]},"8147000":{"s":[[null,"For the bread: mix both flours with the yeast and salt, add the warm water gradually and knead to a soft dough. Cover and leave to rise for 45–60 minutes."],[null,"For the marag: heat the oil in a pot and cook the onion until soft, then add the meat and garlic and stir until the meat changes colour."],[null,"Add the tomatoes, tomato paste, spices and cinnamon and simmer for 10 minutes."],[null,"Add the hot water and salt, cover and simmer for 50 minutes until the meat is almost tender."],[null,"Drain the potato, add it with the beans, carrots, zucchini and peppers, and cook for 20–25 minutes until the vegetables are tender. Ladle some clear broth into small bowls and keep the rest as a thicker idam."],[null,"While the marag cooks, heat the oven to 230 °C with a tray inside. Divide the dough into 4 pieces, flatten them with wet hands and sprinkle with the sesame and nigella seeds."],[null,"Bake the breads on the hot tray with bottom heat for 8–10 minutes, then switch to top heat until golden."],[null,"Serve each hot bread with a bowl of broth and idam."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: lean meat, no stock cubes, less than ¼ tsp salt per portion, one spoon of oil for the whole pot, more vegetables, and a whole-wheat bread instead of white bread with ghee and honey."],[null,"Kidney tip: the meat and whole-wheat flour contain phosphorus, and the tomatoes, tomato paste and potato add potassium; soak the cut potato in hot water for 2 hours or boil it and discard the water, or leave out the potato and paste, and keep to one portion."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has about 66 g carbohydrate, mostly from the bread; you can eat half the bread with more vegetables and a green salad."],[null,"Best kept as an occasional dish for kidney, diabetes and heart diets; keep to one serving."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Sayidaty Kitchen, M3aarf"]]},"8264405":{"s":[[null,"Coat the chicken with the yoghurt, lemon juice, half the curry powder and half the garlic, and chill for at least 30 minutes."],[null,"Soak the potato cubes in warm water for at least 2 hours, changing the water once, then drain."],[null,"Heat the olive oil in a pot and toast the whole spices for 1 minute, add the onion and cook until soft, then the rest of the garlic and the ground spices."],[null,"Add the chicken with its marinade and stir for 5 minutes, then add the tomatoes and tomato paste and cover for 10 minutes until the sauce thickens, adding a little water if needed."],[null,"Add the carrots, green beans, potatoes, 100 ml water and the salt, and cover for 15 minutes."],[null,"Add the zucchini and bell pepper and cook 10 more minutes until the vegetables are tender and the sauce is thick, then sprinkle with coriander and serve with rice or whole-wheat bread."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: no soy sauce, ketchup, mayonnaise or stock cubes; the marinade is low-fat yoghurt, lemon and no-salt-added tomato paste. You can also bake it covered in a tray at 200 °C for 1 hour, as in the first reference."],[null,"Kidney tip: potatoes, tomatoes, tomato paste and yoghurt are high in potassium or phosphorus; soak the potatoes as in the steps or replace them with cauliflower or cabbage, and use less tomato paste."],[null,"Diabetes tip: the dish itself is low in carbohydrate; add only about 100 g cooked rice or 1 small whole-wheat flatbread."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Cookpad Saudi Arabia, Sayidaty"]]},"8730983":{"s":[[null,"Rub the meat with the turmeric, mixed spices and red pepper, and put it in a wide pot with the onion, tomato, cardamom and loomi."],[null,"Pour the boiling water over the meat, skim the foam when it boils, then simmer for about 1½ hours until tender."],[null,"In a small pot boil the small onions and eggplant in water with the vinegar and turmeric for about 10 minutes until tender, then drain."],[null,"Strain the broth and skim the fat off the top; you need about 450 ml for the rice."],[null,"Heat the olive oil in the rice pot and cook the onion, tomato and tomato paste for 5 minutes, then add the broth and salt; when it boils add the drained rice."],[null,"Cook the rice on high heat until it absorbs most of the broth, then squeeze over the lemon, cover and cook on low heat for 15–20 minutes. Put the meat on top for the last 10 minutes to warm through."],[null,"For the kashna: heat the ghee in a frying pan and cook the sliced onion gently until soft and golden, then add the raisins and ground loomi for 2 minutes."],[null,"Spread the rice on a serving platter with the meat in the centre, arrange the eggplant, boiled onions, eggs and lemon slices around it, and spoon the kashna on top."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: a home batch with about 600 g meat instead of a whole lamb, trimmed meat with the fat skimmed off the broth, 2 tsp ghee instead of plenty of butter and oil, no-salt tomato paste instead of a can of regular paste, and no citric-salt seasoning or stock cubes."],[null,"Kidney tip: tomato, tomato paste, eggplant, raisins, meat and eggs provide potassium and phosphorus; keep to one portion (about 100 g cooked meat and 150 g cooked rice), and you can leave out the raisins and the half egg. Ask your dietitian about your own portion."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has about 60 g carbohydrate; take more of the eggplant and boiled onions, go easy on the raisins, and serve with a salad."],[null,"Suitable for: a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Arabic Wikipedia (Mufattah), Mawdoo3 (Hail tamn)"]]},"8366850":{"s":[[null,"Whisk the flour with the yeast, salt, milk and water by hand or with a mixer until you have a smooth, pourable batter slightly thicker than pancake batter."],[null,"Cover and leave to rise for about 30–45 minutes until bubbles appear on the surface."],[null,"Heat a saj or non-stick pan over medium heat and wipe it with a few drops of oil."],[null,"Pour a small ladle of batter into a medium round and leave it until holes appear on top and the base is cooked, then turn it and cook until lightly golden on both sides."],[null,"Repeat with the rest of the batter to make 12 rounds, brush them with the rest of the olive oil and serve warm."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: whole-wheat flour, low-fat milk instead of evaporated milk, little salt, and served with a little olive oil instead of ghee, honey and date syrup."],[null,"Kidney tip: whole-wheat flour and milk contain phosphorus; you can replace the milk with water and use half whole-wheat and half white flour, and keep to 2 rounds."],[null,"Diabetes tip: 2 rounds have about 30 g carbohydrate; serve them with eggs or low-fat labneh and vegetables such as cucumber and tomato instead of honey or date syrup."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Cookpad, Qassimy"]]},"8861033":{"s":[[null,"Peel and halve the potatoes, soak them in hot water for 1 hour, then boil them in fresh water for 5 minutes and drain (this lowers the potassium)."],[null,"Mix the yoghurt with the grated onion, garlic, ginger, vinegar, ground spices and half the salt, and marinate the meat in it for at least 1 hour."],[null,"Heat the olive oil in a heavy pot and cook the sliced onion over medium heat until soft and golden brown; lift out half for the topping."],[null,"Lift the meat out of the marinade, add it to the pot and stir for 10 minutes until browned, then add the marinade, 250 ml hot water and the rest of the salt."],[null,"Cover and simmer for 50–60 minutes until the meat is tender, laying the potatoes on top of the meat for the last 20 minutes. A little thick sauce should remain."],[null,"Meanwhile wash the rice and soak it for 20 minutes, then boil it in water with the cardamom, cloves, cinnamon, bay leaf and the pinch of salt for 6–7 minutes until half cooked, and drain."],[null,"Spread the rice over the meat and potatoes and sprinkle with the soaked saffron and the remaining browned onion."],[null,"Cover the pot tightly and leave on very low heat for 15–20 minutes until the rice is done."],[null,"Fold the layers gently when serving and serve with a green salad or a cucumber and low-fat yoghurt salad."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: no stock cube and no salty ready curry spice, 5 g salt for the whole pot, lean meat, low-fat yoghurt, only 2 tbsp oil instead of a lot for frying the onions, and 150 g cooked rice per portion."],[null,"Kidney tip: potatoes, meat and yoghurt are sources of potassium and phosphorus; soak and boil the potatoes as in step 1 or swap them for pumpkin or courgette, and keep to one portion."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has about 66 g carbohydrate from rice and potatoes; you can swap half the potatoes for courgette or carrot or mix in some brown rice, and start with the salad."],[null,"Suitable for: a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Arabic Wikipedia (Zurbian), Sayidaty Kitchen"]]},"8549296":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a non-stick pot over medium-high heat, add the grated onion and stir for 4–5 minutes until soft and lightly golden."],[null,"Add the garlic and green chilli and stir for 1 minute, then add the cumin, black pepper, turmeric and spices and stir for 30 seconds until fragrant."],[null,"Add the lamb and stir over high heat until it changes colour and its juices have almost evaporated (about 10 minutes)."],[null,"Add the boiling water and the small onions, cover, lower the heat and simmer gently for 1–1¼ hours, stirring now and then, until the meat is tender and the sauce has reduced and thickened."],[null,"Add the salt at the end and taste; if the sauce is still thin, uncover and cook 10 more minutes."],[null,"Toss the cucumber and tomato with the lemon juice and pinch of salt, and serve the sulat hot with the thin bread and salad."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: lean lamb leg instead of rendering pieces of fat, 2 tsp olive oil for the whole pot, little salt added at the end, and whole-wheat bread with a fresh salad."],[null,"Kidney tip: meat and tomato contain phosphorus and potassium; keep to 90–100 g cooked meat, spoon less sauce onto the bread, and you can replace the tomato with extra cucumber."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has about 34 g carbohydrate, mostly from the bread; keep to one small flatbread and fill up on salad."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Sayidaty Kitchen, Cookpad Saudi Arabia"]]},"8223689":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a pot and cook the onion until soft, then add the chicken and stir until it changes colour."],[null,"Add the garlic, tomato, carrot, spices and bay leaves and stir for 3 minutes."],[null,"Pour in the water, bring to the boil and simmer 20 minutes until the chicken is cooked, then lift the chicken out onto a plate."],[null,"Add the drained jareesh to the broth and simmer, covered, for 40 minutes, stirring now and then; then add the oats and salt and cook 10 minutes more until thick."],[null,"Return the chicken to the pot, loosen with a little boiling water if needed, and remove the bay leaves."],[null,"Serve hot with lemon and fresh coriander."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: no stock cubes or butter, skinless chicken, little salt and extra carrot for flavour and fibre."],[null,"Kidney tip: jareesh and oats are whole grains rich in phosphorus and potassium; keep to one bowl and you can reduce the tomato and carrot. Ask your dietitian."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one bowl has about 34 g carbohydrate with good fibre; count it in place of bread or rice at the same meal."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Sayidaty Kitchen, Fatafeat"]]},"8141965":{"s":[[null,"Put the drained wheat in a pot with 2 l water and the spice bag, bring to the boil, then lower the heat and cook for 2 hours, adding water whenever it runs low."],[null,"In a pan, soften the onion in the ghee, then add the meat and stir until it changes colour."],[null,"When the wheat is soft and split, pulse it briefly with a hand blender to thicken, then add the meat and onion, tomato juice and paste."],[null,"Add the cumin, pepper and salt and simmer for another hour, stirring now and then so it does not stick, until the meat is tender."],[null,"Remove the spice bag, adjust the thickness with a little hot water, sprinkle with coriander and serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: lean meat instead of fatty meat on the bone, no stock cubes, a little ghee and less than half the usual salt; the white version is made the same way with low-fat milk instead of tomato."],[null,"Kidney tip: whole wheat and meat contain phosphorus and the tomato adds potassium; keep to one bowl, and you can halve the tomato."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one bowl has about 27 g carbohydrate with 5 g fibre; if you have the soup, cut down on rice or bread in the same meal."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Al Bayan, WebTeb"]]},"8855907":{"s":[[null,"Dice the potato small, soak it in warm water for 2 hours, then boil it for 5 minutes in plenty of water and drain."],[null,"Heat the oil in a pressure cooker and soften the garlic, then the onion, chillies and bell pepper."],[null,"Add the spices and coriander seeds, then the lentils, and stir over low heat for 5 minutes."],[null,"Add the pumpkin, carrots, tomato, potato, stock and salt, close the cooker and cook for 20–25 minutes on medium heat (or 40 minutes in an ordinary pot)."],[null,"Take out the chillies if you like, blend the soup until smooth and adjust the thickness with hot water."],[null,"Serve hot with a squeeze of lemon."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: olive oil instead of butter, water or unsalted homemade vegetable stock instead of ready stock, and more pumpkin and carrot with only a little leached potato."],[null,"Kidney tip: lentils, potato and tomato are sources of potassium and phosphorus; leach the potato as in the first step or replace it with pumpkin, and keep to one bowl."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one bowl has about 36 g carbohydrate and 6 g fibre; serve it with salad and go easy on bread."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, vegetarians, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Sayidaty Kitchen, Mawdoo3"]]},"8439097":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a pot and soften the onion and garlic for 2 minutes, then add the chicken and stir until it turns white."],[null,"Add the cabbage and water and bring to the boil until the cabbage wilts."],[null,"Add the tomato, paste, spring onions, dill, sugar, salt and pepper and simmer for 30 minutes."],[null,"Stir in the flour mixture and the vinegar and cook for 5 minutes until slightly thickened."],[null,"Serve hot; it should taste lightly sour."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: fresh chicken breast instead of salty smoked chicken, a pinch of sugar instead of a full spoon, and little oil."],[null,"Kidney tip: one bowl has about 700 mg potassium from the cabbage, tomato, dill and chicken; you can leave out the fresh tomato and dill to lower it, and cut the chicken to 40 g per portion if you need less protein."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one bowl has only about 18 g carbohydrate and plenty of fibre; serve it with a slice of wholemeal bread instead of white baguette."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, WebTeb, Sayidaty Kitchen"]]},"8401822":{"s":[[null,"Season the fish with the lemon juice and half the cumin and pepper and set aside."],[null,"Brown the onions in the pot with the oil over medium heat for 20–25 minutes, adding a spoon of water whenever they stick, until deep brown but not burnt."],[null,"Blend the browned onions with the garlic, tomato and a little water until smooth, then return to the pot with the tomato paste, whole spices, turmeric and the rest of the cumin and pepper."],[null,"Add the water and half the salt, boil for 10 minutes, then add the fish and simmer gently for 8–10 minutes until just cooked."],[null,"Lift the fish onto a tray and put it, uncovered, in a 180 °C oven for 10 minutes before serving so the top colours a little."],[null,"Strain the broth, measure 450 ml back into the pot, add the drained rice and the rest of the salt, bring to the boil, then cover and cook on very low heat for 20 minutes until tender."],[null,"Spoon the brown rice onto a platter, set the fish on top and serve with green salad and lemon wedges."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: the fish is poached in the broth instead of fried, the onions are browned in just 4 tsp oil, there are no stock cubes, and the rice is 50 g raw per person."],[null,"Kidney tip: the fish and tomato raise potassium and phosphorus (about 1000 mg potassium per portion); swap the tomato for a little vinegar, and eat only 100 g fish if your doctor limits protein or potassium."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has about 53 g carbohydrate; you can make half the rice brown rice (it needs more water and time), and fill half the plate with salad."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Cookinsta, Mawdoo3"]]},"8047539":{"s":[[null,"Soak the dates in half the water (hot) for 15 minutes, then blend until smooth."],[null,"Toast the flour in a heavy pot over medium heat, stirring, until it colours slightly and smells nutty."],[null,"Gradually whisk in the date mixture, the rest of the water, the spices and the salt so no lumps form."],[null,"Cook on low heat for at least 1 hour, stirring every 10–15 minutes, until the flour is cooked and the mixture is smooth and glossy."],[null,"Divide into 8 small bowls, sprinkle with a little black pepper and drizzle about ¼ tsp ghee on each, and serve warm."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: about half the traditional dates per gram of flour (300 g dates to 150 g flour), no added sugar, a little ghee instead of butter, and a small portion."],[null,"Kidney tip: dates and whole-wheat flour contain potassium and phosphorus (about 310 mg potassium per portion); keep to one small bowl and skip the nuts."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has about 42 g carbohydrate, mostly from the dates; count it as part of the meal's carbs and have it after a meal with protein and vegetables."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Cookpad, Sotor"]]},"8789912":{"s":[[null,"Mix both flours with the yeast, sugar, salt, nigella and fennel, then add the dough oil and the warm water little by little and knead for 8–10 minutes until soft and elastic. Cover and leave to rise for 45 minutes."],[null,"Cook the onion and minced beef in a non-stick pan without oil over medium heat, breaking up the meat with a spoon, until the liquid has evaporated and the meat has changed colour, about 10 minutes. Add the cumin, black pepper and the filling salt."],[null,"Whisk the tahini with the vinegar, water and garlic to a creamy sauce, then mix it with the cooked meat and the chopped leeks."],[null,"Heat the oven to 200 °C and oil a 30 cm round tray with the tray oil."],[null,"Press the dough into the tray, raising the edges a little, and spread the meat mixture over it, leaving a 2 cm border."],[null,"Fold the border slightly over the filling and brush it with beaten egg, pour the rest of the egg over the filling, then lay the tomato slices on top and sprinkle with sesame."],[null,"Rest the tray for 10 minutes, then bake on the middle shelf for 25–30 minutes until the base and edges are browned, browning the top for the last 2 minutes."],[null,"Leave for 5 minutes, cut into four and serve with a green salad or rocket."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: half the flour is whole wheat, 5%-fat mince cooked without oil, 40 g tahini instead of ¾ of a glass, only 20 ml oil instead of half a glass in the dough, and 4 g salt for the whole tray instead of plenty of salt and a stock cube."],[null,"Kidney tip: meat, tahini and whole-wheat flour are sources of phosphorus, and tomato and leeks contain potassium; you can use all white flour and cut the meat to 350 g with more leeks, and keep to a quarter of the tray."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has about 70 g carbohydrate; cut the tray into six pieces instead and have one piece with a large plate of salad."],[null,"Best kept as an occasional dish for kidney, diabetes and heart diets; keep to one serving."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Sayidaty Kitchen, Maw9i3i"]]},"8495864":{"s":[[null,"Drain the cooked beans, keeping a little of the cooking water, and lightly mash half of them."],[null,"Heat the oil in a wide pan and cook the onion until soft and lightly golden, then add the garlic and chillies for 2 minutes."],[null,"Add the tomatoes, tomato paste, cumin and pepper and cook for 7 minutes until thick."],[null,"Add the beans, salt and a splash of the cooking water and toss over low heat for 5 minutes to absorb the flavours."],[null,"Spoon into a dish, drizzle with the tahini thinned with lemon, and serve with a rocket and cucumber salad."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: home-cooked unsalted beans instead of canned, no stock cubes, and only a little oil and tahini."],[null,"Kidney tip: fava beans, tahini and tomatoes are high in potassium and phosphorus; take half a portion and ask your dietitian about your amount. If you use canned beans, choose no-salt-added and rinse them well."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one bowl has about 39 g carbohydrate and about 15 g fibre; eat it with a small whole-wheat flatbread instead of white tamees."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, vegetarians, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Sayidaty Kitchen, Elwasfa"]]},"8546041":{"s":[[null,"Mix the flour with the salt, add the water little by little and knead for 8–10 minutes to a firm dough that does not stick to your hands; cover and rest for 15 minutes."],[null,"Heat the oven to 230 °C with a cast-iron tray or baking stone inside for at least 20 minutes."],[null,"Press the dough by hand into a thick round about 22–25 cm wide and 2 cm thick and prick it with a fork."],[null,"Put the round on the hot tray and bake for 35–40 minutes, turning it halfway, until browned on both sides and hollow-sounding when tapped. (Outdoors it is traditionally buried in ash and embers for about an hour, then brushed clean.)"],[null,"Brush off any burnt crust, then crumble the hot bread by hand or cut it into small pieces in the serving dish."],[null,"Melt the ghee and pour it over the crumbs while tossing, drizzle with honey if you like and serve warm."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: whole-wheat flour, limited salt (½ g per portion), far less ghee than usual (under 1 tsp per portion), and a little optional honey instead of sugar."],[null,"Kidney tip: whole-wheat flour has more phosphorus and potassium than white flour; you can swap half of it for white flour and keep to one portion."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has about 40 g carbohydrate; skip the honey and serve it with low-fat laban or a boiled egg and salad."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Al Watan (Saudi newspaper), Al Khaleej magazine"]]},"8546606":{"s":[[null,"In a large bowl mix the chicken with the onion, tomatoes, pepper, frozen vegetables, chickpeas and garlic."],[null,"Whisk the lemon juice, oil, spices and salt into the stock, pour it over the chicken and vegetables and toss well to coat."],[null,"Lay two sheets of foil crosswise in a wide pot or tray, pile the mixture in the centre and seal the foil tightly on all sides so no steam escapes."],[null,"Cook the parcel in the pot over low heat for 50–60 minutes (or in the oven at 200 °C for 45–50 minutes, or on embers) until the chicken is fully cooked."],[null,"Open the foil carefully to avoid the steam, check the chicken is cooked through, and serve hot with salad or a small amount of basmati rice or bread."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: no Maggi cube (homemade unsalted stock and spices instead), skinless chicken, one spoon of oil for the whole dish, and rinsed canned chickpeas to cut sodium."],[null,"Kidney tip: chickpeas, tomato and peas contain potassium and phosphorus; you can leave out or halve the chickpeas, swap the tomato for courgette or cabbage, and keep to 90–120 g chicken."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has only about 22 g carbohydrate; if serving with rice, keep to about 75 g cooked basmati rice with salad."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Cookpad Saudi Arabia, Sayidaty Kitchen"]]},"8088682":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oven to 220 °C, line a tray with baking paper and brush it with half the oil."],[null,"Knead the meat with the millet flour, onion, garlic, egg, spices and salt until the mixture holds together."],[null,"With wet hands, roll the mixture into small walnut-sized balls (about 40) and set them on the tray."],[null,"Brush the balls with the rest of the oil and bake for 12–15 minutes, turning once, until browned outside and still juicy inside, or air-fry at 200 °C for 10–12 minutes."],[null,"For the salad: whisk the tahini with the lemon juice, vinegar and a little water to a thin sauce, then add the salt, cumin, pepper, cucumber and tomato."],[null,"Serve the kebab hot with the tahini salad."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: extra-lean mince, baking or air-frying instead of deep frying, no stock cubes, and less salt and tahini."],[null,"Kidney tip: the meat, tahini and millet flour contain phosphorus and the tomato adds potassium; keep to one portion (10 balls) and you can replace the tomato with more cucumber."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has only about 19 g carbohydrate; serve it with green salad and half a wholemeal flatbread instead of white rice."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Hia Magazine, Al Sayaha Al Arabia"]]},"8122925":{"s":[[null,"Wash the rice, soak it for 30 minutes, then drain."],[null,"Heat the oil in a pot and cook the onion until soft, then add the garlic and tomatoes and cook 5 minutes until thick."],[null,"Add the pigeons and turn them in the mixture until they change colour, then add the cinnamon, cardamom, cumin, kabsa spice, chilies and salt and stir for 5 minutes."],[null,"Pour in the hot water, cover and simmer 30–40 minutes until the pigeons are tender."],[null,"Lift the pigeons onto a tray, brush with the lemon juice and a pinch of turmeric and brown them in an oven preheated to 220 °C for 10–15 minutes."],[null,"Skim the fat off the broth, keep about 375 ml in the pot, add the rice and loomi and boil on high heat until the broth drops."],[null,"Cover and cook on the lowest heat for 20 minutes."],[null,"Spread the rice on a platter, place the pigeons on top and serve with green salad."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: the pigeon skin and most of its fat are removed, one tablespoon of oil replaces the usual generous amount, the pigeons are browned in the oven instead of fried, and no stock cubes are used."],[null,"Kidney tip: pigeon meat is high in phosphorus and protein and tomatoes add potassium; one small pigeon per person is enough, and do not drink the extra broth."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one plate has about 50 g carbohydrate; serve with a large salad, and you can mix in half brown rice."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (Mawsouat Al Tabkh), Cookpad, Cookinsta"]]},"8731069":{"s":[[null,"Soak the potato slices in warm water for 2 hours (change the water once) to reduce potassium, then drain. Wash the rice and soak it for 30 minutes."],[null,"Heat the oven to 220 °C. Toss the potato, carrot, cauliflower, peppers and zucchini with 1 tbsp oil and half the paprika, spread in a tray and roast for 20 minutes, turning once."],[null,"Heat the teaspoon of oil in a non-stick pan and cook the chicken 6–8 minutes until cooked and golden, then remove. Soften the onion and garlic in the same pan with a splash of water."],[null,"Boil the rice in plenty of unsalted water for 8 minutes until half-cooked, then drain."],[null,"In a deep ovenproof dish layer the onion and garlic, then the roasted vegetables and chicken, then the rice on top."],[null,"Bring the blended tomato, water, spices, remaining paprika, loomi and salt to the boil and pour over the rice."],[null,"Cover with foil and bake at 200 °C for 25 minutes until the rice is tender and has absorbed the liquid."],[null,"Turn out onto a platter or serve straight from the dish, with green salad."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: the vegetables are roasted with one tablespoon of oil instead of fried in lots of oil, the chicken is skinless breast in a moderate amount, there is less rice and more vegetables, and no stock cubes."],[null,"Kidney tip: potato, tomato and cauliflower are high in potassium; soak the potato as in the first step or replace it with extra zucchini and pepper, and keep to one plate."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one plate has about 68 g carbohydrate, part of it from the potato; you can leave out the potato to cut starch, and mix in half brown rice."],[null,"Suitable for: heart health and blood pressure, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (Mawsouat Al Tabkh), Sayidaty Kitchen, Hia Magazine"]]},"8681642":{"s":[[null,"Wash the rice until the water runs clear, soak it for 30 minutes, then drain."],[null,"Heat the oil in a wide pot, add the whole spices and onion and cook 5–6 minutes until soft and golden, then add the garlic for 1 minute."],[null,"Add the chicken and turn it for 5 minutes until it changes colour."],[null,"Stir in the tomato paste for 1 minute, then add the grated tomato, carrot, kabsa spice, black pepper, turmeric and loomi and cook 5 minutes until thick."],[null,"Add the hot water and salt, cover and simmer 25–30 minutes until the chicken is cooked."],[null,"Lift the chicken onto a tray and brown it in an oven preheated to 220 °C for 10 minutes, with no added fat."],[null,"Measure the broth: you need about 375 ml for the rice; top up with water or boil to reduce. Add the drained rice, bell pepper and chilies and boil uncovered on high heat until the liquid drops to the level of the rice."],[null,"Cover tightly and cook on the lowest heat for 20 minutes, then turn off the heat and leave covered for 10 minutes."],[null,"Fluff the rice with a fork, spread it on a serving platter, top with the chicken and garnish with almonds and coriander. Serve with green salad and homemade salt-free daqqus (tomato-chili sauce)."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: no stock cubes or ready kabsa mix (the main source of salt in traditional kabsa), skinless chicken, one tablespoon of olive oil instead of butter, chicken browned in the oven instead of fried, and about 150 g cooked rice per person."],[null,"Kidney tip: tomatoes, tomato paste and almonds add potassium and phosphorus; on a low-potassium diet use 1 tbsp paste and skip the almonds. Keep to one plate and ask your dietitian about the right protein portion for you (before or on dialysis)."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one plate has about 56 g carbohydrate; fill half your plate with salad, and you can swap half the rice for brown rice (add 100 ml more water and 10 minutes more cooking)."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (Mawsouat Al Tabkh), Sayidaty Kitchen, Wikipedia (Kabsa)"]]},"8786062":{"s":[[null,"Mix the lemon juice, garlic, cumin, coriander, turmeric, black pepper and the pinch of salt; coat the fish and chill for 20 minutes."],[null,"Wash the rice, soak it for 30 minutes, then drain."],[null,"Heat the oil in a pot, add the whole spices and onion and cook until golden, then the garlic for 1 minute."],[null,"Stir in the tomato paste for 1 minute, then the tomatoes, half the coriander, chilies, loomi and kabsa spice, and cook 5 minutes until thick."],[null,"Add the hot water and the rest of the salt and simmer 10 minutes, then add the rice and boil on high heat until the liquid drops to the level of the rice."],[null,"Sprinkle the saffron over the rice, cover and cook on the lowest heat for 20 minutes."],[null,"Meanwhile place the fish in a tray brushed with the teaspoon of oil and bake in an oven preheated to 200 °C for 12–15 minutes until it flakes easily."],[null,"Spread the rice on a platter, top with the fish, sprinkle with the remaining coriander and serve with lemon wedges and green salad."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: the fish is baked instead of fried, the rice is cooked with one tablespoon of oil instead of butter, and there are no stock cubes or salted spice mixes."],[null,"Kidney tip: fish, tomatoes and tomato paste add potassium and phosphorus; keep to one piece of fish (about 110 g cooked), and cut the paste to 1 tbsp on a low-potassium diet."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one plate has about 52 g carbohydrate; serve with a large green salad, and you can mix in half brown rice."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (Mawsouat Al Tabkh), WebTeb, Elbalad"]]},"8528722":{"s":[[null,"Wash the rice, soak it for at least 30 minutes, then drain."],[null,"Heat 1 tbsp oil in a pot, add the chopped onion, whole spices, whole loomi and chilies and cook until the onion is golden."],[null,"Add the lamb and brown it lightly on all sides."],[null,"Add the garlic, bell pepper, tomatoes, tomato paste and ground spices and stir for 5 minutes."],[null,"Pour in the hot water, cover and simmer for 1½ hours until the lamb is tender (or 35 minutes in a pressure cooker). Skim the fat from the surface, then add the salt."],[null,"Lift out the lamb and loomi, keep about 375 ml of broth in the pot, add the drained rice and boil on high heat until most of the broth is absorbed."],[null,"Return the lamb and loomi on top of the rice, cover and cook on the lowest heat for 25 minutes."],[null,"For the topping: heat 1 tsp oil in a non-stick pan and cook the sliced onion with a splash of water until soft and golden, then add the raisins and ground loomi for 1 minute."],[null,"Spread the rice on a platter, top with the lamb and the onion-raisin topping, and serve with green salad."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: trimmed lamb leg instead of fatty cuts, fat skimmed from the broth, far less oil, no stock cubes, and limited salt with more flavour from loomi and spices."],[null,"Kidney tip: tomatoes, tomato paste and raisins are high in potassium and the meat is high in phosphorus; you can cut the paste to 1 tbsp, skip the raisins and keep to the meat portion (about 100 g cooked)."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one plate has about 60 g carbohydrate; serve with a large salad, and you can mix in half brown rice."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (Mawsouat Al Tabkh), Munaty Cooking, Wikipedia (Kabsa)"]]},"8537975":{"s":[[null,"Put the meat and water in a pot, bring to the boil and skim off the foam as it rises for 10 minutes."],[null,"Add the onion quarters, tomato, bell pepper, whole spices and ground coriander, cover and simmer 2–2½ hours until the meat is very tender (or 50–60 minutes in a pressure cooker)."],[null,"Wash the rice, soak it for 45 minutes, then drain."],[null,"Add the salt to the broth, lift out the meat, strain the broth to remove the spices and vegetables, and skim off the fat."],[null,"Return the meat to the pot, spread the rice over it and add about 375 ml broth so it sits less than 1 cm above the rice; boil on high heat until the broth is absorbed."],[null,"Lay the garlic cloves and chilies on the rice, cover and cook on very low heat for 25 minutes."],[null,"For the topping: heat the ghee and oil in a non-stick pan and cook the sliced onion with the turmeric and a splash of water until golden, then add the raisins for 1 minute. Spread over the rice and leave covered for 10 minutes."],[null,"Serve the rice on a platter with the meat on top or buried underneath in the traditional way, with green salad."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: no hump fat (traditionally added), lean meat with the fat skimmed off the broth, whole spices instead of a stock cube, and only two teaspoons of ghee for flavour."],[null,"Kidney tip: camel meat is rich in protein and phosphorus and raisins are high in potassium; keep to the meat portion (about 100 g cooked) and you can skip the raisins. White kabsa without tomato paste is lower in potassium than the red version."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one plate has about 56 g carbohydrate; serve with a large green salad, and you can mix in half brown rice."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (Mawsouat Al Tabkh), Meat and More, Hawaa World"]]},"8382826":{"s":[[null,"Wash fresh grape leaves in cold water and drain; if using jarred leaves, soak them in boiling water for 10 minutes, then rinse well to remove the brine."],[null,"Mix all the filling ingredients (rice, onion, spring onion, tomato, parsley, tomato paste, oil, spices and half the salt)."],[null,"Put a teaspoon of filling on the rough side of each leaf, fold in the sides and then the ends over them to make a small square or hexagonal parcel."],[null,"Lay the lamb in the bottom of the pot, then the onion and tomato slices, garlic and chilli, and pack the kubayba tightly on top."],[null,"Place an upside-down plate on the kubayba, mix the boiling water with the rest of the salt and a pinch of spices and turmeric, and pour it over the plate until it just covers the parcels."],[null,"Boil for 15 minutes over medium heat, then cover and cook on very low heat for about 2 hours until the meat and rice are tender, adding a little boiling water if it dries out."],[null,"Pour the lemon juice over, leave for 10 minutes, then turn the pot out onto a serving dish and serve with cucumber salad and low-fat laban."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: lean lamb instead of fatty meat, a little olive oil instead of a finjan (about 60 ml) of oil plus ghee, no stock cubes, much less salt and more vegetables in the filling."],[null,"Kidney tip: tomatoes, tomato paste, parsley and meat are high in potassium and phosphorus, and jarred grape leaves are high in sodium; use fresh leaves or soak jarred ones well, and keep to one portion (about 100 g cooked meat)."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one plate has about 63 g carbohydrate from the rice and grape leaves; start with the salad, and you can replace a quarter of the rice with brown rice or coarse bulgur."],[null,"Suitable for: heart health and blood pressure, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Sayidaty Kitchen (Kubayba Hail), Saudipedia (Kubayba Hail ingredients)"]]},"8980893":{"s":[[null,"Boil the pumpkin in a little water for 12–15 minutes until soft, then drain well and let it cool slightly."],[null,"Blend the pumpkin with the yoghurt and water until smooth."],[null,"In a large bowl mix both flours, the cornflour, yeast, salt, cardamom and saffron, then add the pumpkin mixture and beat hard by hand or with a spoon to a soft, sticky dough."],[null,"Cover and leave in a warm place for 1 to 1½ hours until doubled."],[null,"Heat an aebleskiver (round pancake) pan over medium heat, brush the hollows lightly with oil and drop a small ball of dough into each with two wet spoons; turn until browned all over and cooked through (4–5 minutes). Or air-fry in an oiled basket at 190 °C for 8–10 minutes, shaking once."],[null,"Pile the luqaimat on a plate, drizzle with the date syrup, sprinkle with sesame and serve at once."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: no deep frying (one spoon of olive oil for the whole batch), half whole-wheat flour, low-fat yoghurt, and a little date syrup instead of sugar syrup."],[null,"Kidney tip: pumpkin, date syrup, yoghurt and whole-wheat flour contain potassium and phosphorus; keep to 6 pieces, and you can use all white flour and less syrup."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has about 47 g carbohydrate; have 3 pieces with no syrup or just 1 tsp, with Arabic coffee instead of sweet tea."],[null,"Suitable for: heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Fatafeat, Cookpad Saudi Arabia"]]},"8531902":{"s":[[null,"Season the fish with the lemon juice, turmeric, cumin, coriander and black pepper and leave for 20 minutes."],[null,"Heat the fish oil in a non-stick pan and sear the fish for 3 minutes per side until golden but not fully cooked, then set aside."],[null,"Heat the second spoon of oil in a pot and cook the onion until soft, then add the garlic, ginger and whole spices for 1 minute."],[null,"Add the tomato, chilli and half the coriander and stir for 5 minutes until the sauce thickens."],[null,"Add the stock and salt; when it boils add the drained rice and cook until it absorbs most of the liquid."],[null,"Lay the fish on the rice, cover and cook on low heat for 15 minutes until the rice and fish are done."],[null,"Sprinkle with the rest of the coriander and serve with a green salad and lemon wedges."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: the fish is seared in one spoon of oil instead of being floured and deep-fried, homemade fish stock replaces stock cubes, and there is about half the usual salt."],[null,"Kidney tip: fish and tomato are high in potassium and phosphorus; keep to one portion (about 110 g cooked fish and 150 g cooked rice), and you can halve the tomato. Ask your dietitian about your own portion."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has about 50 g carbohydrate; start with the salad, and you can replace a quarter of the rice with soaked brown rice."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Sayidaty Kitchen (Kuwaiti fish majbous), Khaleej Kitchen (fish majbous)"]]},"8274562":{"s":[[null,"Heat the olive oil in a wide pot and cook the onion until soft, then add the garlic and meat and stir until the meat changes colour."],[null,"Add the ground and whole spices, the tomato and the chilli and stir for 5 minutes."],[null,"Pour in the boiling water and simmer for about 1¼ hours until the meat is tender, skimming the foam and fat from the surface."],[null,"Lift out the meat and leave about 450 ml broth in the pot, then add the salt and the drained rice."],[null,"Boil the rice until it absorbs most of the broth, then sprinkle with the saffron, return the meat on top, cover and cook on low heat for 15–20 minutes."],[null,"Warm the ghee in a small pan and toss the raisins for 1 minute, then scatter them with the almonds over the rice and meat; serve with salad and vegetables."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: 2 tsp ghee plus 1 tbsp olive oil instead of a large amount of ghee, trimmed meat with the fat skimmed off the broth, no stock cubes, and about half the usual salt."],[null,"Kidney tip: tomato, raisins, almonds and meat are high in potassium or phosphorus; you can leave out the raisins and almonds, and keep to one portion (about 100 g cooked meat and 150 g cooked rice). Ask your dietitian about your own portion."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has about 55 g carbohydrate; start with the salad, and you can replace a quarter of the rice with soaked brown rice."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Sayidaty Kitchen (majbous lahm), Mawdoo3 (majbous lahm)"]]},"8758649":{"s":[[null,"Soften the onion, garlic and chilli in the tablespoon of oil, then add the chopped tomatoes and cook for 2 minutes."],[null,"Add the rice and spices and stir for 3 minutes, then turn off the heat, add the herbs and mix well."],[null,"Line the bottom of the pot with the onion rings, tomato slices and a few grape leaves."],[null,"Lay each leaf shiny side down, put a heaped tablespoon of filling on it, fold in the sides and roll tightly, then pack the rolls close together in the pot."],[null,"Mix the cooking-liquid ingredients, pour over the rolls to cover them, and weigh them down with an upside-down plate."],[null,"Cook on high heat for 10 minutes, then on very low heat for 1½ to 2 hours until the rice and leaves are tender."],[null,"Leave it in the pot to cool completely, then turn it out onto a serving plate and garnish with pomegranate seeds."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: fresh or frozen leaves instead of brined ones (brined leaves are very salty; if you use them, soak in hot water, change the water twice and add no salt), 2 tbsp oil instead of a large amount, and no sugar or stock cubes."],[null,"Kidney tip: grape leaves are rich in calcium with moderate potassium, and tomato and herbs add more potassium; keep to 8 rolls and you can use less tomato in the cooking liquid."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has about 49 g carbohydrate from the rice; serve it with low-fat laban or salad and have it instead of rice in that meal, not as well as rice."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Sayidaty Kitchen, Cookpad"]]},"8217835":{"s":[[null,"Trim visible fat from the meat, put it in a pot with 1 litre of water and the whole spices, bring to the boil skimming the foam, then simmer about 1 hour until tender. Strain and keep about 400 ml of the stock."],[null,"Heat the oil and ghee in a pot and cook the onion over medium heat until golden, then add the garlic and chilli and stir for 1 minute."],[null,"Add the grated tomato, tomato paste, cumin, ground coriander, black pepper and salt and cook for 10 minutes until thick."],[null,"Add the okra, meat and 300 ml of the stock, cover and simmer for 20–25 minutes until the okra is tender, keeping the sauce fairly thick."],[null,"Whisk the yogurt with the cornstarch, spices, saffron and a little warm stock, then stir it gently into the pot and cook 5 minutes on very low heat without boiling hard."],[null,"Turn off the heat, add the fresh coriander and lemon juice and serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: lean, trimmed lamb, fat-free yogurt, okra cooked in the sauce instead of fried, and homemade stock instead of stock cubes, with less salt."],[null,"Kidney tip: okra and tomato are high in potassium, and yogurt and meat contain phosphorus; use 2 tomatoes instead of 3, boil the okra in water and discard the water before adding it, and keep to a small plate."],[null,"Diabetes tip: the stew itself is low in carbohydrate (about 26 g); serve it with 150 g cooked basmati or brown rice rather than rice with vermicelli."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Chef Hessa (Cookinsta), Cookpad Saudi Arabia"]]},"8212604":{"s":[[null,"Soak the potato slices in warm water for at least 1 hour, then drain (this lowers the potassium)."],[null,"Rub the chicken with the turmeric, ground spices and tomato paste and leave for 20 minutes."],[null,"Brush the bottom of the pressure cooker with the olive oil and layer the onion, garlic, potato, carrot and bell pepper, then put the chicken on top without water."],[null,"Close the cooker and cook on low heat for 10–12 minutes after it whistles, then release the steam."],[null,"Meanwhile boil the rice in plenty of water with the cardamom, cloves, salt and the teaspoon of oil for 6 minutes until half cooked, then drain."],[null,"Spread the rice over the chicken, close the pot and leave on low heat for 15 minutes."],[null,"To smoke: put the lit charcoal in a small foil tray on the rice, drip the oil onto it and close the pot for 5 minutes. Remove the charcoal and turn the madfoona out onto a platter."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: skinless chicken, no stock cubes or colouring, less oil, and about half the usual salt."],[null,"Kidney tip: potato, tomato paste, carrot and chicken are high in potassium and phosphorus; soak the potato as in the first step or swap it for zucchini, and keep to one portion (about 100 g cooked chicken and 150 g cooked rice). Ask your dietitian about your own portion."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has about 60 g carbohydrate from the rice and potato; take less rice and more salad."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Cookinsta (chicken madfoona), Sayidaty Kitchen (madfoon lahm)"]]},"8447456":{"s":[[null,"Soak the potato slices in warm water for at least 1 hour, then drain (this lowers the potassium)."],[null,"Season the meat with the ground spices and tomato paste and leave for 20 minutes."],[null,"Brush the bottom of the pressure cooker with the olive oil and layer the onion, then the garlic, bell pepper, carrot and potato, and put the meat on top without adding water."],[null,"Close the cooker and cook on low heat for 30 minutes after it whistles until the meat is tender, then release the steam and open it."],[null,"Meanwhile boil the rice with the whole spices and salt in plenty of water for 6 minutes until half cooked, then drain."],[null,"Scatter the parsley over the meat, cover with the rice and dot the ghee on top, then close the cooker, bring to a whistle on high heat and cook 10 minutes on low heat."],[null,"To smoke: put the lit charcoal in a small foil tray on the rice, drip the oil onto it and close the pot for 5 minutes. Remove the charcoal, turn the pot out onto a platter and serve with salad."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: no stock cubes, trimmed lean meat, 2 tsp ghee instead of butter pieces, carrot for more vegetables, and about half the usual salt."],[null,"Kidney tip: potato, tomato paste, carrot and meat are high in potassium and phosphorus; soak the potato as in the first step or swap it for zucchini, and keep to one portion (about 100 g cooked meat and 150 g cooked rice). Ask your dietitian about your own portion."],[null,"Diabetes tip: rice and potato together raise the carbohydrate (about 60 g per portion); take less rice when you eat the potato, and start with the salad."],[null,"Suitable for: a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Sayidaty Kitchen (madfoon lahm), Yummy Layalina (madfoon lahm)"]]},"8936981":{"s":[[null,"Blend the maraheef ingredients (both flours, egg, milk powder, yeast, salt and water) until smooth and pourable like a thick soup; add a little water if it is too heavy."],[null,"Cover the batter and leave it to rest for 30 minutes in a warm place."],[null,"For the kishna: heat the olive oil and ghee in a pan and cook the onion over medium heat for 8–10 minutes until soft and golden."],[null,"Add the chilli and spices, then the tomatoes and tomato paste; stir and simmer gently for 10 minutes until thick without adding water, then add the salt and spring onion and take off the heat."],[null,"Heat a griddle or non-stick pan and wipe it with a little oil on kitchen paper, then pour a small ladle of batter and spread it thinly in a circle with the back of the ladle."],[null,"Cook until the top is dry and full of holes (about 1 minute), then turn for 30 seconds; repeat with the rest of the batter (16–20 rounds)."],[null,"Layer the maraheef in a dish with the hot kishna between and on top, and serve straight away."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: wholewheat instead of white flour, yeast instead of baking powder (which is high in sodium), no sugar in the batter, and a kishna made with 1 tbsp oil and 1 tsp ghee instead of plenty of ghee, with little salt."],[null,"Kidney tip: wholewheat flour, tomatoes, tomato paste and milk powder add phosphorus and potassium; you can use half white and half brown flour, cut the tomatoes to 200 g and keep to one portion."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has about 48 g carbohydrate; eat it with a green salad or low-fat laban and avoid adding honey or sugar on top."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, vegetarians."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Saudipedia (popular foods of Qassim), Qassimy Kitchen (maraheef recipe)"]]},"8190598":{"s":[[null,"Soak the truffles in warm water for 2 hours, then scrape the skin with a knife (do not peel them like potatoes), remove all sand and grit, rinse well and halve the large ones."],[null,"Knead the flour with the salt and water to a soft, smooth dough, cover for 30 minutes and divide into 8 balls."],[null,"Heat the oil in a heavy pot and soften the onion and garlic with the cinnamon and cardamom, then add the meat and bezar and stir for 5 minutes."],[null,"Add the grated tomatoes and tomato paste and stir until thick, then pour in the boiling water and simmer for 40 minutes until the meat is almost tender."],[null,"Add the truffles and carrots and cook for 15 minutes until tender, then lift them out with a slotted spoon and set aside."],[null,"Roll the balls very thin to the size of a small flatbread and add them to the boiling broth one at a time, tearing each sheet with a fork as it goes in so the dough cooks light."],[null,"Add the zucchini and salt, cover and cook on medium-low heat for 30–40 minutes, stirring now and then so it does not stick."],[null,"Return the truffles and carrots to the pot with the coriander, leave for 5 minutes, then serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: no vegetable stock cubes, lean meat, little oil and about half the usual salt; the truffles give a rich flavour so the dish does not need more salt."],[null,"Kidney tip: truffles, whole-wheat flour, tomatoes, carrots and meat are high in potassium and phosphorus; keep to one plate with only a little broth, and you can halve the tomatoes. The truffle values are estimated (calculated from white mushrooms). Ask your dietitian about your own portion."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one plate has about 58 g carbohydrate with 10 g fibre; do not add bread or rice, and add a green salad."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Cookpad (marqooq with meat and faqa), Al Eqtisadiah newspaper"]]},"8207050":{"s":[[null,"Put the apple, orange and lemon slices and the mint sprigs in a large jug and press the mint lightly with a spoon to release its aroma."],[null,"Add the apple juice, stir gently and chill the jug for 30 minutes so the flavours infuse."],[null,"Just before serving add the chilled sparkling water and ice and stir very gently so the bubbles stay."],[null,"Pour into glasses with some fruit slices and mint leaves and serve at once."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: unsweetened apple juice for only a third of the jug, and plain sparkling water instead of sweet fizzy drinks and sweetened flavoured malt drinks, so there is no added sugar in the glass."],[null,"Kidney tip: orange and apple juice contain potassium; for a low-potassium diet leave out the orange and use more apple and lemon slices, keep to one glass and count it in your daily fluid allowance."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one glass has about 14 g carbohydrate from fruit sugar; you can make the juice only a quarter of the jug and add more sparkling water."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, kidney disease (not on dialysis), people on dialysis, vegetarians, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking, Rauch Fruchtsäfte (story of the drink), Chocolates & Chai"]]},"8269245":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in the pressure cooker over medium heat and cook the onion until soft, then add the garlic and whole spices for 1 minute."],[null,"Add the grated tomato, tomato paste and ground spices and stir for 3 minutes until the sauce thickens."],[null,"Add the chicken and turn it in the sauce, then add the carrot, zucchini and chilli."],[null,"Pour in 300 ml boiling water, close the pressure cooker and cook for 10 minutes after it whistles, then release the steam and open it."],[null,"Measure the liquid in the pot to about 400 ml (top up with boiling water or boil it down), then add the drained rice and the salt; the liquid should sit about 1 cm above the rice."],[null,"Close the lid and cook on low heat for 7 minutes after the whistle, then turn off the heat and leave 10 minutes before opening."],[null,"Fluff the rice with a fork and serve with a cucumber and leafy salad."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: no stock cubes, skinless chicken, less oil, roughly half the usual salt and more vegetables in the pot."],[null,"Kidney tip: tomatoes, tomato paste, carrots and meat are high in potassium and phosphorus; keep to one portion (90–100 g cooked meat and about 150 g cooked rice) and you can halve the tomatoes. Ask your dietitian about your own portion."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one plate has about 50 g carbohydrate; eat the salad first, and you can swap a quarter of the rice for brown rice soaked for an hour."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Sayidaty Kitchen, Tefal Middle East (chicken madghout)"]]},"8509390":{"s":[[null,"Soak the truffles in cold water, then scrub them with a brush and rinse several times until all the sand is gone."],[null,"Blend the tomatoes, chilli and black pepper until smooth."],[null,"Heat the oil in the pressure cooker, stir the truffles for 2 minutes, then pour in the tomato mixture and cook 3 minutes."],[null,"Add 300 ml hot water, close the cooker and cook 10 minutes after the whistle, then release the steam."],[null,"Add the drained rice and the salt and top up with water to about 400 ml of liquid, about 1 cm above the rice."],[null,"Close and cook on low heat for 7 minutes after the whistle, rest 10 minutes before opening and serve hot."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: a measured amount of olive oil instead of a lot of oil and much less salt, keeping the traditional simple style without onion or heavy spicing."],[null,"Kidney tip: truffles and tomatoes contain potassium; keep to one portion and you can use only 2 tomatoes. The dish has no meat, so it is lower in phosphorus."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one plate has about 47 g carbohydrate; serve with a green salad and a glass of low-fat laban to add protein."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, vegetarians, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Arab News (Saudi truffle season), Tareekaa (truffle kabsa)"]]},"8162919":{"s":[[null,"Soak the potato cubes in warm water for 2 hours (change the water once), then drain. Wash the rice, soak it for 30 minutes and drain."],[null,"Heat the oil in the pressure cooker and cook the onion with the loomi, cinnamon, cardamom, cumin and black pepper until soft."],[null,"Add the lamb and brown it lightly, then add the tomato paste, tomatoes, kabsa spice and garlic and stir for 3 minutes."],[null,"Pour in the hot water, close the pressure cooker and cook 30–35 minutes after it comes to pressure on medium heat."],[null,"Release the steam, open the pot, skim off the fat and add the salt. You need about 400 ml broth; top up with water or boil to reduce."],[null,"Add the potato, rice and chilies and boil uncovered until the broth drops, then close the lid and cook on very low heat for 12–14 minutes."],[null,"Turn off the heat and leave the pot closed for 10 minutes before opening."],[null,"Spoon the madghoot onto a platter with the lamb on top and serve with a tomato, onion and cucumber salad."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: trimmed lamb leg with the fat skimmed from the broth, less than half the usual oil, no stock cubes, and limited salt."],[null,"Kidney tip: potato, tomatoes and tomato paste are high in potassium and the meat is high in phosphorus; soak the potato as in the first step or leave it out, and keep to the meat portion (about 100 g cooked)."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one plate has about 58 g carbohydrate; serve with a large salad, and you can leave out the potato or mix in half brown rice."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (Mawsouat Al Tabkh), Layalina, Meat and More"]]},"8557472":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil and ghee in a pot over medium heat with the cardamom and mastic until fragrant."],[null,"Add the meat and stir until it browns, releases its juices and they dry up."],[null,"Add the onion, garlic and tomato paste and stir for 3 minutes, then add the blended tomatoes and cook until most of their liquid has evaporated."],[null,"Add the spices, salt and hot water, cover and simmer on low heat for 1 hour until the meat is tender and the sauce is thick."],[null,"Meanwhile bring the rice water and salt to the boil, add the drained rice, cover and cook on low heat for 15 minutes."],[null,"Serve the mu'arraq on or beside the rice with a green salad."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: lean leg meat instead of fatty meat on the bone, 1 tsp ghee instead of 2 tbsp, half the tomato paste and no salt added, and a set rice portion."],[null,"Kidney tip: tomato paste, tomatoes and meat are high in potassium and phosphorus; you can leave out the paste, and keep to one portion of meat (about 90 g cooked) with a little sauce."],[null,"Diabetes tip: the plate has about 48 g carbohydrate from the rice; start with the salad, and you can swap a third of the rice for brown rice or serve it with whole-wheat bread."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Yummy (Layalina), Sho Tabkha"]]},"8908761":{"s":[[null,"Put the goat in a pot with the water, bring to the boil and skim, then add the onion, tomato, whole spices, bezar and ¼ tsp of the salt."],[null,"Simmer for 1½–2 hours until tender (or 45 minutes in a pressure cooker)."],[null,"Lift the meat onto an oven tray, strain the broth, let it settle and skim off the fat."],[null,"Beat the egg with 3 tbsp broth, saffron and turmeric, brush it over the meat and brown under the top heat of the oven at 220°C for 15 minutes."],[null,"In a pot, soften the onion in the oil and ghee, add the tomato and carrot, then the drained rice, the rest of the salt and 450 ml of the strained broth."],[null,"When it boils, cover and simmer 15–20 minutes until done. You can smoke the rice and meat with a glowing piece of charcoal in a metal bowl for 3 minutes."],[null,"Toss the salad ingredients with the lemon juice and sumac, without salt or fried bread."],[null,"Spread the rice on a large platter, place the meat on top and serve with the salad."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: a home version with about 600 g meat instead of a whole goat, no stock cubes, fat skimmed from the broth, little ghee, a salad without fried bread and no fried liver or offal."],[null,"Kidney tip: with its salad this plate is high in potassium (meat, tomato, carrot, leafy greens); use less tomato and rocket and keep to 90–100 g cooked meat."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one plate has about 54 g carbohydrate; start with the salad and skip dessert after the meal."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Saudipedia (Kabsa and Mufattah), Sayidaty Kitchen"]]},"8677197":{"s":[[null,"Heat the oil in a thick saj or wide pan over medium-high heat and stir the onion until soft and starting to brown."],[null,"Add the chicken and toss for 5 minutes until it changes colour on all sides, then add the garlic."],[null,"Add the tomatoes and spices and stir for 3 minutes, then the bell pepper, chilli and tomato paste."],[null,"Add the salt and 100 ml boiling water and stir, then cover and cook on medium-low heat for 15–20 minutes until the chicken is cooked through and the sauce thickens."],[null,"Uncover for the last 2 minutes to cook off extra liquid, sprinkle with coriander and serve hot with a green salad."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: no Maggi or stock cubes, skinless chicken, little oil, and no-salt-added tomato paste with about half the usual salt."],[null,"Kidney tip: chicken, tomatoes and tomato paste are high in potassium and phosphorus; keep to one plate (about 100 g cooked chicken), and you can leave out the tomato paste and halve the tomatoes. Ask your dietitian about your own portion."],[null,"Diabetes tip: the nutrition values are for the muqalqal alone, without rice or bread; serve it with 150 g cooked rice (adds about 40 g carbohydrate) or one small whole-wheat bread and a large salad."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Mawdoo3 (chicken muqalqal), Al Bawaba News"]]},"8925350":{"s":[[null,"Heat a heavy deep pan or saj over high heat, add half the oil and toss half the meat for 3–4 minutes until browned, then take it out and repeat with the rest."],[null,"Add the remaining oil and the onion and stir until soft, then the garlic, cumin, bezar, turmeric and black pepper for 1 minute."],[null,"Return the meat to the pan, add the tomatoes and stir until they start to break down."],[null,"Cover and cook on low heat for 30–35 minutes until the meat is tender, stirring now and then and adding 50–100 ml hot water if needed."],[null,"Add the bell pepper, chilli and salt and toss over high heat for 4–5 minutes until most of the sauce has cooked down and the pepper is still slightly crisp."],[null,"Blend the dip ingredients, then serve the muqalqal sprinkled with coriander, with the dip and a green salad."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: no lamb fat, liver or kidneys (high in cholesterol and phosphorus), lean meat, a little olive oil, about half the usual salt and more peppers and tomato."],[null,"Kidney tip: meat and tomatoes are high in potassium and phosphorus; keep to the portion (about 90–100 g cooked meat), and you can halve the tomatoes and add more bell pepper. Ask your dietitian about your own portion."],[null,"Diabetes tip: the nutrition values are for the muqalqal alone, without rice or bread; serve it with 150 g cooked rice (adds about 40 g carbohydrate) or one small whole-wheat bread and a large salad."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Sayidaty Kitchen, Eeina (Saudi mugalgal)"]]},"8064883":{"s":[[null,"Soak the potato slices in warm water for at least 1 hour, then pat dry (this lowers the potassium). Heat the oven to 220°C."],[null,"Brush the eggplant, potato and zucchini slices with the tablespoon of oil, spread them on a lined tray and roast for 20–25 minutes, turning once, until golden."],[null,"Meanwhile heat the teaspoon of oil in a pot and cook the onion until soft, then add the chicken, garlic and spices and stir for 5 minutes."],[null,"Add boiling water to cover the chicken (about 600 ml) and cook for 20 minutes, then strain and keep the broth."],[null,"In a deep pot, lay the tomato slices on the bottom, then the chicken, then the roasted vegetables, then the drained rice, and level it."],[null,"Dissolve the salt in the hot broth and pour it in gently until it is about 1 cm above the rice, then put a small plate on the rice and bring to the boil; cover and cook on low heat for 25–30 minutes."],[null,"Rest for 10 minutes, then put the serving platter on top, turn the pot over firmly and lift it off gently; sprinkle with the parsley. Serve with salad and low-fat yoghurt."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: the vegetables are oven-roasted with one spoon of oil instead of deep-fried, the chicken is skinless, there are no stock cubes, and about half the usual salt."],[null,"Kidney tip: potato, tomato, eggplant and chicken provide potassium and phosphorus; soak the potato as in the first step or swap it for cauliflower, and keep to one portion (about 100 g cooked chicken and 150 g cooked rice). Ask your dietitian about your own portion."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has about 60 g carbohydrate from the rice and potato; swap the potato for cauliflower to lower it, and serve with salad."],[null,"Suitable for: a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Wikipedia (Maqluba), Sayidaty Kitchen (maqluba with eggplant, cauliflower and potato)"]]},"8621621":{"s":[[null,"Season the fish with the lemon juice and spices and leave for at least 30 minutes. Heat the oven to 200°C."],[null,"Brush a tray with the teaspoon of oil, lay the fish on it and bake for 10 minutes until firm but not fully cooked."],[null,"Heat the tablespoon of oil in a deep pot and cook the onion until soft, then add the tomato and spices and stir for 2 minutes."],[null,"Add the carrot and bell pepper, cover and cook on low heat for 5 minutes until soft, then spread them over the bottom of the pot."],[null,"Lay the fish over the vegetables, then spread the drained rice and whole spices on top."],[null,"Dissolve the salt in the boiling water or stock and pour it in gently until it is about 1 cm above the rice; bring to the boil, then cover and cook on low heat for 20–25 minutes."],[null,"Rest for 10 minutes, then turn it out onto a platter and scatter the almonds on top. Serve with a green salad."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: the fish is baked instead of fried, there is less oil in the vegetable base, no stock cubes, and about half the usual salt."],[null,"Kidney tip: fish, tomato, carrot and almonds provide potassium and phosphorus; you can leave out the almonds and use less tomato, and keep to one portion (about 110 g cooked fish and 150 g cooked rice). Ask your dietitian about your own portion."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one portion has about 50 g carbohydrate; start with the salad, and you can replace a quarter of the rice with soaked brown rice."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Wikipedia (Maqluba), Elbalad (fish fillet maqluba)"]]},"8567106":{"s":[[null,"Rub the goat with the spices and ¼ tsp of the salt, sprinkle with the saffron water and leave 30 minutes."],[null,"Heat the oven to 170°C. In an ovenproof pot, soften the onion in the oil and ghee, then add the tomato, bell pepper, chilli and whole spices."],[null,"Add the drained rice, the rest of the salt and the water, stir once, then seal the pot with foil and pierce several holes in it."],[null,"Start the meat alone: put it on the oven rack over a tray, tent with foil and cook 1¼ hours, then set the rice pot on the lowest shelf right under the meat so its juices drip through the pierced foil."],[null,"Cook 45 minutes more until the meat is tender and the rice has absorbed the water, then uncover the meat and brown it for 10 minutes."],[null,"For the Hasawi flavour: place the lit charcoal or palm-frond piece in a metal bowl inside the switched-off oven with the rice and meat, close for 5 minutes, then open the door carefully to let the smoke out."],[null,"Serve the rice topped with the goat, with green salad and low-fat laban."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: goat is naturally lean and visible fat is trimmed, only 2 tsp ghee, no stock cubes and much less salt."],[null,"Kidney tip: goat, tomato and peppers add potassium; keep to 90–100 g cooked meat and you can halve the tomato."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one plate has about 46 g carbohydrate; serve with a large salad and you can mix a quarter brown rice into the rice."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Al-Madina newspaper (Hasawi mandi), Arabic Wikipedia (Mandi)"]]},"8672714":{"s":[[null,"Mix the lemon juice, garlic, ground spices, the chicken oil and ¼ tsp of the salt; rub the chicken inside and out and leave 30 minutes."],[null,"Heat the oven to 180°C. In a pot, soften the onion in the rice oil, then add the whole spices, chilli, the rest of the salt and the boiling water and boil 5 minutes."],[null,"Spread the drained rice in a deep oven tray, pour the spiced liquid with the onion over it and level without pressing."],[null,"Seal the tray with two layers of foil and pierce several holes, then lay the chicken on the foil and cover it with another sheet of foil."],[null,"Bake 1¼–1½ hours until the chicken is cooked (75°C at the thickest part) and the rice is tender, then uncover the chicken and brown it under the grill for 5 minutes."],[null,"To smoke: put the glowing charcoal in a small metal bowl beside the chicken, cover the tray for 3 minutes, then remove the charcoal."],[null,"Serve the rice topped with the chicken, with salad and a homemade unsalted hot tomato salsa."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: skin removed, a lemon and garlic marinade instead of salty paste, no stock cubes and only 2 tbsp oil for the whole dish."],[null,"Kidney tip: chicken and rice provide phosphorus; keep to 90–100 g cooked chicken and avoid salty ready sauces. This dish is moderate in potassium."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one plate has about 46 g carbohydrate; fill up on salad and vegetables and skip raisins and fried nuts on top."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Arabic Wikipedia (Mandi), Sayidaty Kitchen"]]},"8742903":{"s":[[null,"Rinse and dry the fish, rub it with the lemon juice, spices, turmeric and ¼ tsp salt and leave 20 minutes."],[null,"For the stuffing: cook the onion and garlic in the teaspoon of oil for 3 minutes, then add the tomato, coriander and vinegar and cook 2 minutes until thick."],[null,"Fill the fish with the stuffing (or spread it between the steaks) and close it."],[null,"Heat the oven to 200°C. In a pot, soften the rice onion in the oil, add the spices, chilli, salt and water; when hot add the rice, stir and pour into an oven tray."],[null,"Cover the tray with pierced foil, lay the fish on top and cover it with more foil."],[null,"Bake 40–45 minutes until the rice is tender and the fish flakes easily, then uncover the fish and brown it under the grill for 5 minutes."],[null,"Optionally smoke it with a piece of charcoal for 3 minutes, then serve with lemon wedges and salad."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: the fish is baked, not fried, less than 2 tbsp oil for the whole dish, no stock cubes and much less salt."],[null,"Kidney tip: grouper is rich in potassium and phosphorus; keep to 100–120 g cooked fish and use less tomato in the stuffing if you must limit potassium."],[null,"Diabetes and heart tip: fish is a lean, heart-friendly protein; one plate has about 48 g carbohydrate, so add plenty of salad."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Sayidaty Kitchen, Elbalad News (fish mandi)"]]},"8485563":{"s":[[null,"Mix the yoghurt, spices, turmeric, saffron, garlic and ¼ tsp of the salt; coat the lamb and chill for at least 1 hour."],[null,"Heat the oven to 170°C. In a pot, soften the onion in the oil and ghee, then add the tomato and whole spices and stir 2 minutes."],[null,"Add the drained rice, the rest of the salt and the lukewarm water, and pour everything into a deep oven tray."],[null,"Seal the tray with two layers of foil and pierce holes, then arrange the lamb on top and cover it with more foil."],[null,"Cook for 2–2½ hours until the lamb is tender, then uncover the meat and brown it for 10 minutes on the top shelf."],[null,"Smoke the rice and lamb with a glowing piece of charcoal in a small metal bowl for 3–5 minutes under cover."],[null,"Serve the rice topped with the lamb and sprinkled with raisins, with a green salad."]],"h":[[null,"What changed: lean leg instead of fatty ribs, only 2 tsp ghee instead of a lot of butter, no stock cubes and much less salt."],[null,"Kidney tip: lamb, yoghurt and raisins add phosphorus and potassium; you can leave out the raisins and keep to 90–100 g cooked meat."],[null,"Diabetes tip: one plate has about 50 g carbohydrate; for a lower-carb meal halve the rice and add roasted vegetables."],[null,"Suitable for: people with diabetes, heart health and blood pressure, a gluten-free diet."],[null,"References: Encyclopedia Cooking (encyclopediacooking.com), Arabic Wikipedia (Mandi), Sayidaty Kitchen"]]},"2430":{"s":[[null,"Preheat oven to 400° F and place muffin papers in muffin pan. peel and cut apple into small pieces."],[null,"Beat eggs in a large bowl. Add sugar, oil and water; mix well. Add vanilla."],[null,"In a separate bowl, combine flour, baking soda and 1 teaspoon cinnamon."],[null,"Stir flour mixture into egg mixture. Batter will be lumpy. Fold in apple pieces."],[null,"Fill muffin cups 3/4 full. Mix remaining 1/2 teaspoon cinnamon with 1 teaspoon sugar. Sprinkle on top of muffins."],[null,"Bake for 20 minutes or until lightly browned."]],"h":[[null,"Try freezing leftover muffins and reheating in the microwave for 30 to 60 seconds for a quick snack."],[null,"Sugar can be replaced with Splenda® sugar-free sweetener. Be aware muffins will not rise as high and may cook 3 to 5 minutes faster than the recipe’s expected baking time."]]}});